-- Generated from the sanitized recipe catalog snapshot by scripts/build-recipe-catalog.py.



















































Once the griddle is hot, place the paratha over it and cook on medium flame until brown spots appear on the base of the paratha. Flip the paratha and add 1 teaspoon ghee on it, spread it evenly and flip it again. Add 1 ghee oil on each side, press the paratha with a ladle and cook it well on both sides until it is nice and brown.','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5d5a6deb3ec4ec0ae14a3e2a','5d5a6d82d5b157eee236f600',1,'Soak Rice(p1)','Wash and soak 1 cup long grain Basmati rice in 2 cups water for 15 minutes.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('5d5a6f85d5b157eee236f606','5d5a6d82d5b157eee236f600',2,'Chopping(p2)','Wash, peel and cube 1/4 cup potatoes, finely chop 1 cup onions, 1/4 cup carrot, 1/4 cup beans, 1 inch piece ginger, and 1 tablespoon garlic. Wash and chop 1/2 cup cauliflower in medium chunks, peel 1/4 cup green peas, slit 2 nos green chilies in halves and squeeze 1 teaspoon lemon juice.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('5d5a70cf3ec4ec0ae14a3e2c','5d5a6d82d5b157eee236f600',3,'Make pulao(m1)','Heat 1 tablespoon Ghee in a pan. Add 1 teaspoon cumin seeds, 1 inch cinnamon stick, 2 nos black cardamom, 2 nos green cardamom,  3 nos cloves and saute for 30 seconds. Add 1 cup finely chopped onion and saute on medium flame for 2-3 minute. Now add 2 nos bay leaves, 1 inch piece finely chopped ginger, 1 tablespoon finely chopped garlic and 2 nos slit green chilies and cook them for another 3-4 minute on medium heat till onions turn slightly golden brown.','cook_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":4,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5d5a726f3ec4ec0ae14a3e2d','5d5a6d82d5b157eee236f600',4,'Make pulao(m2)','To the fried onions, Now add 1/4 cup chopped  carrot, 1/4 cup chopped  beans, 1/2 cup chopped cauliflower chunks, 1/4 cup green peas, 1/4 cup cubed potatoes and give them a good toss. Now add 1 cup soaked basmati rice into the vegetables and saute them together.Now add 2 cup water to the rice, give it a stir. Add 1.5 t salt, 1/2 t garam masala and 1 teaspoon lemon juice into the rice to make rice more fluffy. Cover it with a lid and cook on medium-low flame for 12-15 minutes. If you are cooking pulav in a pressure cooker, cook on high flame till the first whistle. After the first whistle, reduce to flame to low and continue to cook for 8 minutes and then switch off the flame and allow the pressure cooker to depressurize naturally. After the pressure has been released, open the lid and give the pulav a gentle mix and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":8,"flame":2}'),('5d5b91453ec4ec0ae14a3e41','5d5b9025800fa4ef25af92a8',1,'Chopping(p1)','Wash, peel and finely chop 1/2 cup onion, 2 teaspoons garlic and 1-inch piece ginger. Wash and finely chop 1/2 cup carrot, 1/2 cup cabbage, 1/2 cup capsicum, and 1/4 cup spring onion greens. Keep the chopped vegetables aside. Next, to make the slurry, take 2 teaspoons of all-purpose flour in a bowl and add 2 tablespoons water into it, give it a good whisk to avoid any lumps and blend well till flour is well mixed with water to pouring consistency.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('5d5b938b3ec4ec0ae14a3e42','5d5b9025800fa4ef25af92a8',2,'Make filling(m1)','To make the spring rolls filling, in a pan, heat 1 tablespoon oil on medium flame. Into the hot oil, add 1-inch piece chopped ginger, 2 teaspoons chopped garlic and saute them on high flame for 1 minute. Next, add 1/2 C chopped onion into this and saute on medium-high flame for 2-3 minutes until it turns slightly golden.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5d5b95d3800fa4ef25af92ac','5d5b9025800fa4ef25af92a8',3,'Make Filling(m2)','After stir-frying onions for 2-3 minutes, add 1/2 cup chopped cabbage,1/2 cup chopped capsicum,1/2 cup chopped carrot,1/4 teaspoon black pepper powder, 1 teaspoon salt, 1 teaspoon soy sauce,1 teaspoon vinegar, and 2 teaspoons red chili sauce into this and saute them together on high flame to keep the crunch of the vegetables intact. Continue to stir fry the vegetables for 2-3 minutes on high flame. Then add 1/4 cup chopped spring onion greens and give it a final toss. Turn off the heat and keep the filling aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":1,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5d5b97ecd5b157eee236f61e','5d5b9025800fa4ef25af92a8',4,'make spring rolls(m3)','To shallow fry the spring rolls, take 1 cup oil in a pan and let it heat on medium flame for 3-4 minutes. While the oil is heating, to wrap the spring rolls, on the counter place one spring roll wrapper, keep 1 tablespoon of the vegetable filling slightly off the corner, take the edge and tuck it inwards, rolling the filling inside the sheet. Fold the edges inwards and roll the sheet further. Apply the flour slurry to the edge of the sheet using the index finger, continue to roll till the end and seal the spring roll. Prepare all the spring rolls similarly. After heating the oil for 3-4 minutes, drop the prepared spring rolls one by one into it and shallow fry them for 3-4 minutes on medium high flame until they turn slightly golden and crisp. After shallow frying the rolls for 3-4 minutes, take them out on a kitchen towel and dab to remove the excess oil. Serve Hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":1,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5d5b9f6ad5b157eee236f622','5d5b9cea3ec4ec0ae14a3e47',1,'Chopping(p1)','Wash,peel and chop 2 cup bottle gourd into 1 inch cubes. Finely chop 1 cup  tomatoes, 2 tablespoon fresh coriander leaves and slit 2 nos green chilies lengthwise.Squeeze 1/2 tablespoon lemon juice and keep aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('5d5ba0413ec4ec0ae14a3e4b','5d5b9cea3ec4ec0ae14a3e47',2,'Make curry(m1)','In a pressure cooker, heat 1 tablespoon ghee. Into the hot ghee,add 1/4 teaspoon hing and 1 teaspoon cumin seeds, saute it for a few seconds until it crackles. Then add 1 teaspoon cumin powder,1/2 teaspoon turmeric powder,1 teaspoon red chili powder and saute for a few seconds. Add 1 cup chopped tomatoes into this and give it a good mix. Then add 2 nos green chilies slit lengthwise and 1/4 cup water. Give it a stir and  allow it to cook for 2-3 minutes on medium flame.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5d5bb86038d3cf07e240e0bc','5d5b9cea3ec4ec0ae14a3e47',3,'Make curry(m2)','Next, add 2 cup cubed bottle gourd, 1/2 teaspoon salt and 1 cup water. Mix everything well, cover it with the lid and pressure cook it on high flame till one whistle. After the first whistle,reduce to low flame and continue to cook for another 5 minutes and then switch off the flame. Keep the cooker aside and allow the pressure to release naturally. After the pressure has been released, take off the lid, give it a good stir and garnish it with 2 tablespoon chopped coriander leaves and serve','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":5,"flame":3}'),('5d5bd16d2e84eba0c8d8b87d','5d5bd0742e84eba0c8d8b87a',1,'Make Sugar Syrup(p1)','To make the sugar syrup, Heat 3/4 cup water in a deep bottom pan on medium flame for 1 minute, add 1/2 cup sugar, 3 nos green cardamom into the hot water, give it a good stir to dissolve the sugar well with water and bring it to a boil on high flame. After it has come to a boil, reduce to low flame and continue to boil it for another 6-7 minutes and keep stirring occasionally. Then turn off the heat and set aside. While the sugar syrup is boiling, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5d5bd2232e84eba0c8d8b880','5d5bd0742e84eba0c8d8b87a',2,'Chopping(p2)','On a chopping board take a bread slice and trim it''s sides using a knife,removing the brown edges completely and then cut it diagonally. Similarly trim the slices for the rest of the three bread slices. Finely slice 4 nos almonds and 4 nos pistachios using a knife.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),
('5d5bd340df3ea8cb34948e64','5d5bd0742e84eba0c8d8b87a',3,'Make Saffron Milk(m1)','Heat 3 cup full cream milk in a deep bottom pan on medium flame for a minute,then add 1 teaspoon saffron strands and 1/2 teaspoon rose water into it and give it a good stir. Bring it to a boil on high flame. After it has come to a boil, reduce to low flame and continue to cook the milk  for another 10-12 minutes while stirring in between,until milk thickens and turns slightly yellow in color. After boiling the milk for 10-12 minutes, add 1/4 cup sugar into it and keep stirring on low flame until the sugar is dissolved in the milk. Once the sugar is well dissolved in the milk, turn off the heat and set aside. While the milk is boiling, Please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5d5bd3d4789932e6d6c05204','5d5bd0742e84eba0c8d8b87a',4,'Fry Bread Slices(m2)','To fry the bread slices, heat 1/4 cup ghee in a pan on medium flame for 1 minute. Then drop the bread slices one by one and shallow fry them on medium-high heat for 2-3 minutes until they turn golden and crisp. After frying the bread slices for 2-3 minutes, take them out leaving the extra ghee behind.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":1,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5d5bd4672e84eba0c8d8b883','5d5bd0742e84eba0c8d8b87a',5,'Make shahi tukda(m3)','Next, Take the fried bread slices and dip them completely in the sugar syrup one by one using a tong, then instantly take them out on a plate or they will turn soggy. Add saffron milk on top of the sugar syrup soaked bread slices and Garnish with sliced almonds and pistachios on top. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('5d5e6d3b0e84bacce5d4bb32','5d5ce84847dcf776dc68019e',1,'Peel&Pressure cook potatoes(p1)','Wash and peel 2 cup of baby potatoes. Add the washed and peeled potatoes into a pressure cooker along with 1.5 cup water and 1 teaspoon salt. Cover it with a lid and pressure cook it on high flame till one whistle, after the first whistle,reduce to low flame and continue to cook for another 7 minutes and then switch off the flame. Keep the pressure cooker aside and allow the pressure to release naturally. After the pressure from the cooker has been released, take off the lid and keep aside. While the potatoes are cooking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":9,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":7,"flame":3}'),('5d5e710f373221adb7a15318','5d5ce84847dcf776dc68019e',2,'Chop-Coriander-cumin powder(p2)','Meanwhile,wash and finely chop 2 nos green chilies and 2 tablespoon fresh coriander leaves. Squeeze 2 teaspoon lemon juice and keep aside. To make coriander powder-Take 2 teaspoon coriander seeds in a spice grinder and grind it into a coarse powder. To make the roasted cumin powder- In a pan, dry roast 1 teaspoon cumin seeds on medium flame for 1-2 minutes till it releases nice aroma. Keep stirring it while roasting. After roasting it for 1-2 minute, cumin seeds will turn slightly dark in color. Then turn off the flame and grind the roasted cumin seeds in a spice grinder to make it a fine powder.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":1,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),
('5d5e7327373221adb7a1531b','5d5ce84847dcf776dc68019e',3,'Make Jeera Aloo(m1)','To make the jeera aloo- In a pan heat 1 tablespoon oil on medium flame for 1 minute. Add 1 teaspoon cumin seeds into the hot oil and let it crackle for a few seconds. Next add 2 nos chopped green chilies, 2 teaspoon crushed coriander seeds, 1 teaspoon red chili flakes, 1/2 teaspoon turmeric powder, 2 teaspoon dry mango powder, 1/2 teaspoon roasted cumin powder, 1 teaspoon salt into it and saute everything together on medium flame for 1 min. After 1 min add (2 C) boiled baby potatoes into the masala and give it a good toss. Then cover the potatoes with a lid and continue to cook the potatoes with masala on medium flame for another 3 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5d5e7400373221adb7a1531c','5d5ce84847dcf776dc68019e',4,'Make Jeera Aloo(m2)','After cooking the potatoes for 3 minutes, take off the lid, give it a gentle stir and add 2 teaspoon lemon juice into it. Mix the lemon juice well with the potatoes and stir fry on medium flame for 1 minute. Then turn off the heat and garnish the  potatoes with 2 tablespoon chopped coriander leaves. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5d5e828fa894cb6b9682ffa0','5d5e8106bad6cf570694749f',1,'Boil Dal(p1)','For Punjabi Dal Tadka, wash 1/2 cup arhar dal and 1/2 cup moong dal well with water. In a pressure cooker, add the washed arhar dal and moong dal along with 2 cups of water. Add 1 teaspoon salt into it, cover it with the lid and pressure cook it on high flame till one whistle. After the first whistle, reduce to low flame and continue to cook for another 8 minutes. After cooking the dal for 8 minutes on low flame, turn off the heat, keep the cooker aside and allow the pressure to release naturally. While the dal is cooking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":8,"flame":3}'),('5d5f76fdda551d04d3dc0057','5d5e8106bad6cf570694749f',2,'Chopping(p2)','For the Punjabi Dal Tadka, wash, peel and finely chop 1/2 cup onion, 1-inch piece of ginger and 2 teaspoons garlic. Wash and finely chop 1/2 cup tomatoes, 2 nos green chilies, and 2 tablespoons fresh coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('5d5f7970da551d04d3dc005a','5d5e8106bad6cf570694749f',3,'Cook dal(m1)','To make the Punjabi Dal Tadka, heat 1 tablespoon ghee in a pan on medium flame for a minute, add 1/2 cup finely chopped onions into it and saute it for 2-3 minutes on medium-high flame until it turns slightly golden. To the stir-fried onion, add a 1-inch piece of chopped ginger and 1 teaspoon chopped garlic and saute them together on high flame for another 1 minute. Next, add 2 nos chopped green chilies,1/2 cup chopped tomatoes into it. Saute and cook the tomatoes on medium-low flame for 3-4 minutes until they turn soft. Keep stirring the tomatoes occasionally.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('5d5f7adaa894cb6b9682ffa6','5d5e8106bad6cf570694749f',4,'Cook dal(m2)','After cooking the tomatoes for 3-4 minutes, add 1/2 teaspoon turmeric powder,1 teaspoon red chili powder and cooked dal into it. Combine everything well. Stir in 1 cup water to adjust the consistency of the dal, if it gets too thick. Stir and bring it to a boil. Add 1 tablespoon lemon juice, in the end, to give a nice tangy flavor to the dal. Then, turn off the heat.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5d5f7e81bad6cf57069474ac','5d5e8106bad6cf570694749f',5,'Make Tempering(m3)','To make the tempering for the Punjabi Dal Tadka, heat 1 tablespoon ghee in a pan on medium flame, add 1/4 teaspoon hing and 1 teaspoon cumin seeds into it and let it crackle, add 2 nos dried red chilies and 1 teaspoon chopped garlic into this and saute on medium flame for 2 minutes till garlic turns slightly golden and aromatic. Next, add this tempering on top of the cooked dal and give it a gentle stir. Garnish with 2 tablespoons chopped coriander leaves and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5d5fce41ab82f8570dd3735c','5d5fc6c3ab82f8570dd37357',1,'Boil water &chop(p1)','Place 3 cup of water in a deep dish on high flame and let it come to a boil. While the water is heating, wash and cut 2 cup cauliflower into medium sized florets. Finely chop 1/2 cup onion. Next cut 1/2 cup capsicum in 1 inch pieces. Chop 3 tablespoon spring onion greens and 2 nos green chilies. Finely chop 1 inch ginger and 1 tablespoon garlic.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5d5fcfadab82f8570dd3735d','5d5fc6c3ab82f8570dd37357',2,'Blanch cauliflower(p2)','Once the water comes to boil, add 2 cup cauliflower florets and cook them only for 2 minutes on high flame. After 2 mins, drain off the hot water carefully and wash the blanched cauliflower florets with cold water and keep aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5d5fd39e28bff0c54286830c','5d5fc6c3ab82f8570dd37357',3,'Coat cauliflower in cornflour paste(p3)','Heat 1 cup of cooking oil in a kadai on medium flame. While the oil is heating, take 5 tablespoon all purpose flour in a bowl. Add 3 tablespoon cornflour and crack 1 nos egg into this. Next add 1 teaspoon ginger garlic paste, 1/2 teaspoon salt, 1/2 teaspoon soy sauce, 1/2 teaspoon black pepper powder, 1/4 cup water and whisk them together to make a smooth and lump free paste. To this paste, add blanched cauliflower florets and mix well to make sure all pieces are coated well.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('5d5fd916ab82f8570dd3735f','5d5fc6c3ab82f8570dd37357',4,'Fry cauliflower florets(p4)','Once the oil is hot, carefully drop the cauliflower florets one by one into it and shallow fry them for 3-4 minutes on medium high flame till they turn golden and crisp. Once they turn crisp take them out on kitchen towel to remove the excess oil.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":1,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5d5fded34cb2b1aa30376ae3','5d5fc6c3ab82f8570dd37357',5,'Make manchurian(m1)','In a wok, heat 2 tablespoon oil, add 1 teaspoon finely chopped ginger, 1 teaspoon finely chopped garlic and saute for a minute on medium flame. Now add 2 nos chopped green chilies, 1/2 cup chopped onion, and saute for 2-3 minutes till onions turn slightly golden then add 1/2 cup chopped capsicum and toss them together.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5d5fdf4f4cb2b1aa30376ae4','5d5fc6c3ab82f8570dd37357',6,'Make Gobhi manchurian(m2)','Now add 1.5 tablespoons dark soy sauce, 1 teaspoon vinegar, 2 teaspoons red chili sauce, 2 teaspoon tomato sauce, 1/2 teaspoon black pepper powder, 1 teaspoon salt and saute everything together on high flame for 30 seconds. Add fried cauliflower chunks into this sauce and combine them well with the sauce. Garnish with 3 tablespoon chopped spring onions and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5d61217739613718ed7d8450','5d611e1c39613718ed7d844e',1,'Roast Eggplant(p1)','Peel 8 cloves garlic. Wash the eggplant and make 1 inch slits all over it using a knife. Insert 1 clove garlic into each slit. Next, roast the eggplant, by keeping it directly on high flame on the cook top. Keep roasting the eggplant till it''s skin turns black. Keep flipping it occasionally while roasting to make sure that all the sides are cooked evenly. Once cooked take it off the flame and let it cool down. Once cool, peel off the burned skin. Next, Mash the roasted eggplant pulp using a vegetable masher or a fork. Keep this mashed pulp aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":3,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5d61286739613718ed7d8452','5d611e1c39613718ed7d844e',2,'Boil Peas(p2)','Wash and peel 1/4 cup green peas and put them to boil in a pan with 2 cup water and 1/2 teaspoon salt. Boil the green peas on high flame for 3-4 minutes,then drain off the excess water and keep aside. While the peas are boiling please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":4,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5d61292709e1dd5a7f423814','5d611e1c39613718ed7d844e',3,'Chopping(p3)','Wash and finely chop 1 cup onion, 1 cup tomatoes, 2 nos green chilies, and 2 tablespoon fresh coriander leaves and finely grate 1 inch piece ginger.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5d612f5839613718ed7d8453','5d611e1c39613718ed7d844e',4,'Make Bharta(m1)','Heat 4 tablespoon mustard oil, add 1 inch piece grated ginger, 2 nos finely chopped green chilies into it and give it a quick saute. Add 1 cup finely chopped onion and saute it on medium flame for 3-4 minutes until it turns slightly golden.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5d6131331710a053f6cd1249','5d611e1c39613718ed7d844e',5,'Make Bharta(m2)','Once the onions turn slightly translucent, add 1 cup finely chopped tomatoes and give it a good toss. Into this, add 2 teaspoon coriander powder, 1 teaspoon turmeric powder, 1 teaspoon red chili powder, (1/2 teaspoon garam masala powder, 1 teaspoon amchoor powder, 1.5 teaspoon salt and saute everything together. Cook for 2-3 minutes on medium flame','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":1,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5d6131f41710a053f6cd124a','5d611e1c39613718ed7d844e',6,'Make Bharta(m3)','Next add mashed eggplant pulp and 1/4 cup boiled green peas into the fried masala and combine everything well. Saute and cook on high flame for 2-3 minutes. Garnish the baingan bharta with 2 tablespoon finely chopped coriander leaves and Serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5d62cd4209e1dd5a7f423815','5d62c8c139613718ed7d8455',1,'Boil Potatoes(p1)','To boil the potatoes- Wash 3 nos potatoes well with water and keep them in a pressure cooker with 2 cup water, enough to cover them. Add 1/2 teaspoon salt into this and pressure cook on high flame till one whistle, then cook on low flame for 8 minutes and then turn off the flame. Keep the cooker aside and let the pressure release naturally. While the potatoes are boiling,please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":8,"flame":4}'),
('5d62cfab39613718ed7d8456','5d62c8c139613718ed7d8455',2,'Chopping & mash potatoes(p2)','Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup onion, 1/4 cup tomatoes, 1/4 cup capsicum, 2 nos green chilies and 2 tablespoon fresh coriander leaves. Once the potatoes are boiled, take them out and let them come to room temp, then gently peel the skin off and mash them with the help of a potato masher or a fork.','prep_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":4,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5d62d0b539613718ed7d8457','5d62c8c139613718ed7d8455',3,'Potato mixture(p3)','To make the sandwich filling-Take 3/4 cup boiled and mashed potatoes in a bowl. Add 1/4 cup finely chopped tomatoes, 1/4 cup chopped onion, 1/4 cup chopped capsicum, 2 nos finely chopped green chilies and 2 tablespoon fresh coriander leaves into it. Next add 1 teaspoon salt, 1/2 teaspoon black pepper powder, 1/2 teaspoon chat masala into it and combine the mixture well.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5d62d11a09e1dd5a7f423816','5d62c8c139613718ed7d8455',4,'Make Sandwich(m1)','To make the sandwich- Take a bread slice and spread 1 tablespoon potato mixture to cover it evenly. Top it up with a cheese slice. Take another bread slice and spread 1 tablespoon potato mixture on this evenly. Then cover the sandwich with this bread slice.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5d62d18639613718ed7d8458','5d62c8c139613718ed7d8455',5,'Make Sandwich(m2)','Heat a pan and grease it with 1 teaspoon ghee or butter. Place the sandwich on it, cover it with a lid and cook it for 3 minutes on medium low flame until it turns crisp and slightly golden. Flip the sandwich and cook the other side similarly. When both the sides are cooked evenly, slice the sandwich diagonally and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":1,"idle_time":4,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5d62d74339613718ed7d845b','5d62d65539613718ed7d845a',1,'Chopping(p1)','Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup onion, 1/4 cup carrots, 1/2 cup cabbage, 1/2 cup capsicum, 2 tablespoon spring onion greens and 1 inch ginger piece. Wash and chop 1/4 cup mushrooms in medium chunks','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5d62d79709e1dd5a7f423818','5d62d65539613718ed7d845a',2,'Cornflour slurry(p2)','To make cornflour slurry, Take 1 tablespoon cornflour in a bowl, add 1/4 cup water into it and mix well to avoid any lumps.','prep_method','{"active_time":1,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5d62d94109e1dd5a7f423819','5d62d65539613718ed7d845a',3,'Make soup(m1)','To make the soup-In a saucepan, heat 1 tablespoon oil on medium heat for a minute. Add 1 inch piece finely chopped ginger into the hot oil and saute for 30 seconds. Add 1/4 cup chopped onion into this and saute for 2-3 minute until they turn slightly translucent. Next add 1/4 cup chopped carrot, 1/2 cup chopped cabbage, 1/4 cup chopped capsicum and 1/4 cup chopped mushroom into this and stir fry the vegetables on high flame for 1-2 minutes. Then add 2 cup water to the vegetables, give it a good stir, cover it with a lid and bring it to a boil.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5d62db7c39613718ed7d845c','5d62d65539613718ed7d845a',4,'Make Soup(m2)','Once it has come to a boil, remove the lid and add 2 tablespoon soy sauce and 1 teaspoon salt. Be careful while adding salt as soy sauce itself is salty. Add 1/4 teaspoon black pepper powder and stir in the cornflour slurry to thicken the soup. Keep stirring on high flame until the slurry is well combined with the soup. Boil the soup on high flame for 4-5 minutes. Then add 1 tablespoon vinegar and stir well for 1 minute. Garnish the soup with 2 tablespoon chopped spring onions and Serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5d636fd81710a053f6cd124d','5d636c441710a053f6cd124c',1,'First Marinate(ap1)','To marinate the chicken for the Hyderabadi Chicken Biryani, wash 600-gram chicken well with water. Take the washed chicken in a bowl, add 1/2 teaspoon shahi jeera, 1 tablespoon ghee, 1 teaspoon ginger garlic paste, 1/2 teaspoon garam masala powder, 1 teaspoon coriander powder, 1/2 teaspoon cumin powder, 1.5 teaspoons of red chili powder, 1 teaspoon turmeric powder, 2 teaspoons of salt, 2 tablespoons of cooking oil, 4 nos chopped green chilies and 2 tablespoons of lemon juice to the chicken. Combine the chicken well with the spices using a spatula. Cover the chicken with a lid. Set it aside and let it marinate for 10-12 hours.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":720,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5d6370a139613718ed7d8460','5d636c441710a053f6cd124c',2,'Soak Rice(p1)','For the Hyderabadi Chicken Biryani, wash 1.5 cups of basmati rice well with water. Soak the washed rice in 1 cup water and set it aside for 45 minutes. While the rice is soaking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":45,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":45,"flame":0}'),
('5d63724439613718ed7d8463','5d636c441710a053f6cd124c',3,'Chopping&fry onion(p2)','For Hyderabadi Chicken Biryani, wash and finely chop 4 nos green chilies, 3 tablespoons of mint leaves, 3 tablespoons of coriander leaves. Wash, peel and finely slice 1 cup onion. Whisk 1 cup curd in a bowl using a whisker till it''s smooth and lump-free. To fry the onions- In a pan, heat 1 tablespoon ghee on medium flame for 1 minute. Add 1 cup sliced onion into the hot ghee and saute on medium flame. Continue to stir fry the onions on medium flame for 8 minutes until they turn crisp and golden. After frying the onions for 8 minutes, turn off the heat and take them out in a bowl leaving the extra ghee behind. Dab them on a kitchen towel to remove extra ghee.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5d63739909e1dd5a7f423822','5d636c441710a053f6cd124c',4,'Second Marinate & soak saffron(p3)','After marinating the chicken for 10-12 hours, add 1 cup whisked curd, 2 tablespoons chopped fresh coriander and mint leaves into it. Then, add 1/4 cup golden fried onion to it and give it a good mix. After combining the chicken well with the second marinate, set it aside for 30 minutes. In a bowl, take 1 teaspoon saffron strands and soak it in 2 tablespoons of milk for 30 minutes. While the chicken is resting, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":30,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":30,"flame":0}'),('5d63768139613718ed7d8467','5d636c441710a053f6cd124c',5,'Make spice potli (p4)','To make the spice potli for the Hyderabadi Chicken Biryani, take a muslin cloth, keep 2 nos black cardamoms, 3 nos green cardamoms, 4 nos cloves, 1/2 teaspoon shahi jeera, 6 nos black peppercorns, 2-inch cinnamon stick and 1 nos bay leaf inside it and tuck it well to make a potli.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5d638be809e1dd5a7f423829','5d638a5b1710a053f6cd1253',1,'Chopping & soak cahsew(p1)','For Paneer Lababdar, In a bowl, soak 10 nos cashew nuts in 1/4 cup water for 10 minutes. Meanwhile, wash, peel and roughly chop 1 cup onion. Wash and roughly chop 1 cup tomatoes, 2 nos green chilies and squeeze 2 teaspoons lemon juice. Next, cut 2 cups of paneer into 1-inch cubes and grate 1/2 cup paneer using a grater in a bowl.','prep_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":1,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5d638e1309e1dd5a7f42382c','5d638a5b1710a053f6cd1253',2,'Make paste(p2)','For Paneer Lababdar, heat 2 tablespoons oil in a pan on medium flame for a minute. Add 1 tablespoon butter into it and melt it together. Next, add 1/2 teaspoon cumin seeds, 1-inch cinnamon stick and 2 nos green cardamoms into the hot oil and saute them for a minute on medium flame. Next, add 1 cup chopped onions and saute it on medium flame for 2-3 minutes till it turns slightly translucent. Then, add 1 teaspoon ginger-garlic paste to it and saute them together on high flame for a minute. Add 2 nos chopped green chilies and 1 cup chopped tomatoes into this and continue to saute for another 3-4 minutes on low flame till tomatoes turn soft. Once the tomatoes are cooked, turn off the heat, and let the mixture cool down completely.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":4,"idle_time":7,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('5d638f4a39613718ed7d8473','5d638a5b1710a053f6cd1253',3,'Blend & Make Paste(p3)','After the prepared mixture for Paneer Lababdar has come to room temperature, transfer it into a blender jar, add 10 nos soaked cashew nuts into it and blend together to make a fine paste.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5d6391b909e1dd5a7f42382d','5d638a5b1710a053f6cd1253',4,'Make Paneer Lababdar(m1)','To make Paneer Lababdar, transfer the onion-tomato paste from the blender jar in a heavy bottom pan and saute on medium flame for a minute. Then, add 2 teaspoons of coriander powder, 1/2 teaspoon turmeric powder, 1/2 teaspoon garam masala powder, 1 teaspoon red chili powder and 1 teaspoon salt into the paste and mix everything together. Keep stirring the masala on medium flame for another 2-3 minutes until the flavor comes out. After cooking the masala for 2-3 minutes, add 2 cups of cubed paneer, 1/2 cup grated paneer and 1.5 cups of milk into this. Gently combine everything together and continue to stir on low flame for 1 minute. Cover it with a lid and cook on low flame for 4-5 minutes. After cooking the paneer with curry for 4-5 minutes, take off the lid and give it a gentle stir. Turn off the heat, sprinkle 2 tablespoons of Kasuri methi on top and add 2 teaspoons of lemon juice to it. Give it a final stir and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":2,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5d63a92d39613718ed7d8478','5d63a8271710a053f6cd125c',1,'Wash mint(p1)','Wash 1/4 cup of mint leaves and squeeze 2 teaspoon lemon juice.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5d63aa6139613718ed7d847b','5d63a8271710a053f6cd125c',2,'Make Tea(m1)','To make the tea- Boil 1 cup water in a deep vessel on high flame for 1 min. Then add 1 teaspoon tea leaves, 8 nos fresh mint leaves and 2 teaspoon sugar into the boiling water.Give it a good stir and continue to boil it for another 2-3 minutes on medium flame till the tea leaves releases aroma. Keep stirring occasionally. After boiling the tea for 2-3 minutes, turn off the heat, take it down and strain it into a jar using a tea strainer. Allow it cool down for 10 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5d63ab3309e1dd5a7f423834','5d63a8271710a053f6cd125c',3,'Make Tea(m2)','After the tea has cooled down, take 4 nos ice cubes in a glass mug or a glass tumbler. Add 4 nos fresh mint leaves into it, then pour 1/2 cup orange juice and 1/2 cup prepared mint tea into this. Add 1 teaspoon lemon juice on top and serve right away. Make another cup of mint iced tea similarly.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5d63afef39613718ed7d847e','5d63adae09e1dd5a7f423835',1,'P1: Chopping','Peel and grate the radish and finely chop green chilli and coriander leaves. Make a roasted cumin powder by dry roasting cumin seeds and then grinding them into a coarse powder with a mortar and pestle.','prep_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5d63b1bd1710a053f6cd1261','5d63adae09e1dd5a7f423835',2,'M1: Make Raita','In a bowl, whisk fresh curd and remove all lumps. To this add the grated raddish, salt, roasted cumin powder, green chillies, and coriander leaves, mix this well.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5d63b30e1710a053f6cd1264','5d63adae09e1dd5a7f423835',3,'M2: Make Tempering','Heat oil in a tempering pan and then add cumin seeds, mustard seeds, dry red chilli, and curry leaves. Let this cook for half a minute and then pour it over the raita. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5d63c2f11710a053f6cd1266','5d63c17b39613718ed7d8484',1,'Cook dal(p1)','For Vegetable Kootu, wash 1 cup toor dal well with water. To cook the dal, In a pressure cooker, add 1 cup of washed toor dal, 2 tablespoons of peanuts and 1 cup water along with 1 teaspoon salt. Give it a stir, cover it with a lid and pressure cook it on high flame till one whistle, after the first whistle, reduce to low flame and continue to cook for another 8 minutes on low flame. After cooking the dal for 8 minutes, turn off the heat, keep the pressure cooker aside, and allow the pressure to release naturally. Once the pressure from the dal cooker has been released, take off the lid and mash the dal and peanuts well using a hand blender till smooth consistency. While dal is cooking please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":8,"flame":3}'),('5d63c48409e1dd5a7f42383d','5d63c17b39613718ed7d8484',2,'Chopping(p2)','For Vegetable Kootu, wash, peel and cube 1/2 cup potatoes,1/2 cup pumpkin, and 1/2 cup cucumber. Wash and chop 1/2 cup carrot and 1/2 cup beans. Peel and wash 1/4 cup green peas. Grate 1/4 cup fresh coconut and wash 10 nos curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5d63c6411710a053f6cd1267','5d63c17b39613718ed7d8484',3,'Pressure cook vegetables(p3)','To cook the vegetables for Vegetable Kootu, in a pressure cooker, add 1/2 cup cubed potatoes, 1/2 cup pumpkin,1/2 cup cucumber, 1/2 cup chopped carrot, 1/2 cup beans and 1/4 cup peeled and washed green peas. Next, add 1 teaspoon salt, 1/2 teaspoon turmeric powder, and 1/2 cup water into the vegetables. Give it a good stir, cover it with a lid and pressure cook the vegetables on high flame till one whistle. After the first whistle, reduce to low flame and continue to cook for another 8 minutes on low flame. After cooking the vegetables for 8 minutes, turn off the flame, keep the pressure cooker aside, and allow the pressure to release naturally. While the vegetables are cooking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":8,"flame":3}'),('5d63c7ef39613718ed7d8489','5d63c17b39613718ed7d8484',4,'Make coconut paste(p4)','To make the coconut paste for Vegetable Kootu, heat 2 teaspoons of oil in a pan on medium flame. Add 1 tablespoon coriander seeds, 1/4 teaspoon fenugreek seeds, 1/2 teaspoon cumin seeds, 3 nos dry red chilies and 2 teaspoon chana dal into the hot oil. Saute everything together on a medium flame for 1-2 minutes till the whole spices turn aromatic. After 2 minutes, turn off the flame, take it down and let it cool for 10 minutes. After the spices have come to room temperature, transfer them in a blender jar, add 1/4 cup freshly grated coconut along with 1/2 cup water and blend them well to make a smooth paste.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5d63c88439613718ed7d848a','5d63c17b39613718ed7d8484',5,'Make veg kootu(m1)','To make the Vegetable Kootu, Once the pressure from the cooker has been released and vegetables are cooked completely, take off the lid and transfer the cooked vegetables in a heavy bottom saucepan. Add mashed dal into it along with the prepared coconut paste. Combine everything well and cook it on medium-low flame for 3-4 minutes while stirring in between. After cooking for 3-4 minutes, turn off the heat and take it down.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":4,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5d63c99839613718ed7d848d','5d63c17b39613718ed7d8484',6,'Make Tempering(m2)','To make the tempering for Vegetable Kootu, heat 2 teaspoons of oil in a tadka pan on medium flame for 1 minute, add 1 teaspoon urad daal, 1/2 teaspoon mustard seeds, 3 nos dried red chilies and 10 nos curry leaves into the hot oil and saute it on medium flame for 1 minute. After 1 minute, turn off the heat and pour this tempering on top of the prepared vegetable kootu. Give it a gentle stir and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5d63ccca39613718ed7d8490','5d63cc2809e1dd5a7f423842',1,'Chop(p1)','For Methi Laccha Partha, wash 1 cup fenugreek leaves well with water and dab them on a kitchen towel to remove extra water. Next, finely chop the fenugreek leaves and keep aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5d63ce2109e1dd5a7f423845','5d63cc2809e1dd5a7f423842',2,'Knead Dough(p2)','To make the dough for Methi Laccha Paratha, take 2 cups of all-purpose flour in a bowl. Add 1 cup wheat flour, 1 cup finely chopped fenugreek leaves, 2 teaspoon sugar, 1 teaspoon salt and 1 tablespoon oil into it. Combine all the dry ingredients well using a spoon. Add 1.5 cup water slowly into the flour. Combine and constantly knead for 3-4 minutes to make a soft dough. Cover the dough with a cloth and set it aside for 20 minutes.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":20,"flame":0}'),('5d63cf1839613718ed7d8494','5d63cc2809e1dd5a7f423842',3,'Make paratha(m1)','After resting the dough for 20 minutes, divide it into four equal ball sized portions. Take one ball, dust some flour on it and roll it using a rolling pin in a 7-inch diameter circle. Apply 1 teaspoon ghee all over it and pleat it completely into a 7-inch strip. Take one edge of the strip and roll it to across the length of the strip, tuck the edge in the center, press it with the palms and flatten it. Dust some flour and roll it again into a 7-inch circle. Heat a pan on medium flame for 1 minute, place the paratha on it and continue to roast it for 1 minute on medium flame, flip it and apply 1 teaspoon oil all over it evenly. Flip the paratha and roast on medium-high flame till it turns slightly golden. Apply oil to the other side of the paratha and cook both the sides evenly for 2-3 minutes on medium-high flame. Once the paratha is crisp and golden, take it out on a serving dish and serve. Make the rest of the parathas similarly.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5d64c82b09e1dd5a7f42384b','5d64c72039613718ed7d8499',1,'Cook Rice(p1)','Wash 1 cup short grain rice well with water. In a deep bottom pan, add 1 cup washed rice along with 2 cup water and bring it to a boil on high heat, then reduce to low flame,cover it with a lid and continue to cook on low flame for another 10-12 minutes until rice absorbs all the water and is completely cooked. After cooking the rice for 10-12 minutes, turn off the heat and set aside. If cooking rice in a pressure cooker,after adding water to the rice,cover it with a lid and pressure cook it on high flame till one whistle,then reduce to low flame and continue to cook for another 8 minutes on low flame. After 8 minutes,turn off the heat and allow the pressure to release naturally. While the rice is cooking, Please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":8,"flame":3}'),('5d64c90539613718ed7d849c','5d64c72039613718ed7d8499',2,'Chopping(p2)','Wash, peel and grate 1/4 cup carrot and 1/2 inch ginger using a grater. Finely chop 2 nos green chilies and 1 tablespoon fresh coriander leaves. Wash and peel 2 tablespoon pomegranate seeds. Wash 10 nos curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5d64c9ff09e1dd5a7f423851','5d64c72039613718ed7d8499',3,'Make Curd Rice(m1)','To make the curd rice- Take cooked rice in a bowl. Add 1/2 cup curd into it and combine the rice well with the curd using a spoon. Then add 1/4 cup grated carrot and 1 teaspoon salt into the rice and mix well.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5d64cbc41710a053f6cd1277','5d64c72039613718ed7d8499',4,'Make Tempering(m2)','To make the tempering for curd rice- Heat 2 tablespoon oil in a pan on medium heat for 1 minute. Add 1/2 teaspoon mustard seeds and 10 nos curry leaves into the hot oil and let it crackle for a minute. Then add 1 teaspoon urad daal, 1/2 inch grated ginger,1 nos dried red chili and give it a quick saute. Add 2 nos chopped green chilies into it and saute for a minute. Then turn off the heat and pour this tempering on top of the curd rice. Garnish with 1 tablespoon chopped coriander leaves and Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5d64d0d439613718ed7d84a6','5d64cdf709e1dd5a7f423856',1,'Boil&Make onion paste(p1)','For Chicken Kali Mirch, wash, peel and finely chop 1 cup onion. Wash and finely chop 2 nos green chilies. Boil 1.5 cups of water in a deep bottom pan on high flame for 1 minute. Once it has come to a boil, add 1 cup chopped onion, 10 nos cashew nuts, and 2 nos chopped green chilies into it, give it a stir and continue to boil it on medium flame for 2-3 minutes until the raw smell of onion is gone. After boiling onions for 2-3 minutes, turn off the flame and let it cool completely. Once the onions have come to room temperature, transfer them into a blender jar and blend well to make a smooth paste. While the onions are cooling down, please go to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5d64d2061710a053f6cd1280','5d64cdf709e1dd5a7f423856',2,'Wash Chicken&pepper powder(p2)','For Chicken Kali Mirch, wash 500 grams of chicken well with water. Whisk 1/4 cup curd in a bowl using a hand whisker till smooth. Squeeze 1 tablespoon lemon juice. Take 2 tablespoons of black peppercorns in a pepper grinder and grind it into a coarse powder or use a mortar pestle to crush the peppercorns into a coarse powder.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5d64d38d1710a053f6cd1284','5d64cdf709e1dd5a7f423856',3,'Make chicken kalimirch(m1)','To make the Chicken Kalimirch, heat 3 tablespoons of cooking oil in a heavy bottom saucepan on medium flame for 1 minute. Add 4 cloves, 4 green cardamoms, 1-inch cinnamon stick into the hot oil and saute for a minute. Next, add the boiled onion cashew paste into this and continue to saute on medium-low flame for another 3-4 minutes until the masala is well combined with the oil. After cooking the masala for 3-4 minutes, add 2 teaspoons of ginger-garlic paste into it and saute for a minute until garlic releases the aroma. Next, add 500 gram washed chicken into it and combine everything well.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":3,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5d64d6a809e1dd5a7f42385c','5d64cdf709e1dd5a7f423856',4,'Make chicken kalimirch(m2)','Next, add 1/4 cup whisked curd into the chicken and mix it well. Then add 2 teaspoons of coriander powder, 1/2 teaspoon cumin powder, and 2 teaspoon salt into the chicken and give it a quick mix. Add 1/2 cup water along with 1 tablespoon black pepper powder into it and stir well. Let the curry cook for another 4-5 minutes on medium flame till oil separates. After cooking the curry for 4-5 minutes, add 1/2 cup of water into the chicken, cover it with a lid and allow it to cook on low flame for 20-25 minutes until the chicken is completely cooked. After cooking the chicken for 20-25 minutes, take off the lid, add 1 tablespoon lemon juice, 1 teaspoon honey, 1 teaspoon Kasuri methi and 1 tablespoon freshly grounded black peppercorns into it. Saute everything together on medium flame for a minute. Then add 1/4 cup fresh cream into the curry and give it a final stir. Turn off the flame and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":28,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5d64daf909e1dd5a7f42385d','5d64da5f1710a053f6cd1285',1,'Soak Chana Dal(p1)','For Lauki Chana Dal, wash 1 cup chana dal well with water and soak it in 1/2 cup water for 20 minutes. While the dal is soaking please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":20,"flame":0}'),('5d64eebd1710a053f6cd1289','5d64da5f1710a053f6cd1285',2,'Chopping(p2)','For Lauki Chana Dal, wash, peel, and cube 2 cups of bottle gourd. Wash, peel and finely chop 1/2 cup onion and 1-inch piece ginger. Wash and finely chop 1/2 cup tomatoes, 3 nos green chilies, 2 teaspoons of garlic and 2 tablespoons of fresh coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5d64f1251710a053f6cd128a','5d64da5f1710a053f6cd1285',3,'Make lauki chana(m1)','To make Lauki Chana Dal, heat 1.5 tablespoons of ghee in a pressure cooker on a medium flame for 1 minute. Add 1/2 cup chopped onions into the hot ghee and saute it on medium flame for 2-3 minutes till it turns slightly translucent. After stir-frying the onions for 2-3 minutes, add 1-inch piece chopped ginger, 2 teaspoons chopped garlic and 3 nos chopped green chilies into it and saute them together for another 1 minute on medium flame. Next, add 1/2 cup chopped tomatoes into it, give it a quick toss and add 1 cup soaked chana daal along with 2 cups of cubed bottle gourd into it. Add 1/2 teaspoon turmeric powder, 1 teaspoon salt along with 2 cups of water into it. Give it a good stir and mix everything well. Cover it with a lid and pressure cook it on high flame till one whistle. After the first whistle, reduce to low flame and continue to cook for another 8 minutes on low flame. After 8 minutes, turn off the flame and allow the pressure to release naturally. Once the pressure has been released. Take off the lid and give it a stir.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":8,"flame":3}'),('5d64f1fa1710a053f6cd128d','5d64da5f1710a053f6cd1285',4,'Make Tempering(m2)','To make the tempering for Lauki Chana Dal, heat 2 teaspoons of ghee in a tadka pan on medium flame for 1 minute. Add 1 teaspoon cumin seeds and 1/4 teaspoon hing into it and let it crackle for a few seconds. Next, add 1 teaspoon red chili powder, give it a stir and turn off the flame. Pour this tempering instantly on top of the Lauki Chana Dal and stir. Garnish with 2 tablespoons chopped coriander leaves and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5d64fa691710a053f6cd1293','5d64f9b01710a053f6cd1290',1,'Boil&shred chicken(p1)','Wash the boneless chicken well with water. To cook the boneless chicken, Heat 1 cup water in a pan on medium heat for a minute. Add 1 cup boneless chicken into the hot water along with 1 teaspoon salt and bring it to a boil. After it has come to a boil, cover it with a lid and continue to cook on medium-low flame for 12-15 minutes until the chicken is no longer pink. After cooking it for 15 minutes, take off the lid, drain off the excess water if any and take out the cooked chicken on a chopping board. Shred the cooked chicken using a fork or knife. While the chicken is cooking, Please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5d64fbd31710a053f6cd1296','5d64f9b01710a053f6cd1290',2,'Boil Egg Noodles(p2)','To boil the noodles- Heat 3 cup water in a deep and wide pan on medium heat for 1-2 minutes. Add 200-gram egg noodles into the hot water along with 1 teaspoon salt and 1 teaspoon oil to prevent them from sticking together. Bring the noodles to a boil on high flame. After a boil, reduce to medium flame and continue to boil them for another 5-6 minutes while stirring in between until they are completely cooked. After boiling the noodles for 6 minutes, turn off the heat, drain off the extra water and wash them with cold water. Keep aside. While the noodles are boiling, Please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5d64fe1c1710a053f6cd1299','5d64f9b01710a053f6cd1290',3,'Chopping(p3)','Wash, peel and cube 1 cup onion. Wash and slit 3 nos green chilies lengthwise. Wash and julienne 1/4 cup capsicum, 1/4 cup carrot and 1/4 cup cabbage. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoon celery, finely chop 2 tablespoon spring onion greens and 2 teaspoon garlic. Wash and finely slice 1/4 cup spring onion whites. In a bowl, crack 2 nos eggs and whisk them well using a hand blender or a fork.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5d65003f39613718ed7d84ba','5d64f9b01710a053f6cd1290',4,'Make hakka noodles(m1)','To make the chicken hakka noodles- Heat 2 tablespoon sesame oil in a pan on medium heat for 1 minute. Add 2 teaspoon minced garlic into the hot oil and saute it for a minute. Add 1/2 cup cubed onion, 3 nos slit green chilies, 1/4 cup spring onion whites and 2 tablespoon chopped celery into it and saute them together on high flame for 2-3 minutes until onion turns slightly translucent. Then add 1/4 cup carrot, 1/4 cup capsicum and 1/4 cup cabbage into it and stir fry the vegetables for another 1-2 minutes on high flame. After stir frying the vegetables, gather them to one side of the pan using the spatula and pour 2 nos whisked eggs to the vacant side of the pan. Keep stirring the eggs on high flame for 1-2 minutes, then mix the eggs with vegetables and toss them together.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5d65019809e1dd5a7f423868','5d64f9b01710a053f6cd1290',5,'Make Hakka Noodles(m2)','Next add 1 cup shredded boneless chicken into the stir fried vegetables and egg. Add 1 tablespoon soy sauce, 1 teaspoon red chili sauce, 1 teaspoon green chili sauce and 1 teaspoon vinegar along with the boiled noodles into it. Combine everything together and saute on high flame for 1-2 minutes. Turn off the heat and garnish with 2 tablespoon chopped spring onion greens. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5d650bf709e1dd5a7f42386a','5d650b8f1710a053f6cd129f',1,'Slice Brinjal(p1)','Wash 1 nos large brinjal and cut it into 1/2 inch slices.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5d650ce51710a053f6cd12a0','5d650b8f1710a053f6cd129f',2,'Coat slices(m1)','To make the spice mix- On flat dish or a plate, Take 1/2 teaspoon turmeric powder, 1 teaspoon red chili powder and 1/2 teaspoon salt. Mix the spices well using a spoon or with fingers. Next coat 1.5 cup brinjal slices with the spices well. Coat both the sides of the slices evenly with the spices. Take 1/4 cup rice flour in a separate plate. Next coat the brinjal slices one by one with the rice flour evenly. Coating the brinjal slice with the rice flour will give it a nice crunch.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5d650d521710a053f6cd12a1','5d650b8f1710a053f6cd129f',3,'Fry brinjal slices(m2)','To shallow fry the brinjal slices- Heat 1/2 cup mustard oil in a pan on medium heat for 1 minute. Add brinjal slices into the hot oil one by one and shallow fry them for 2-3 minutes on medium high heat till they turn slightly golden and crisp. After frying the slices for 2-3 minutes, take them out on a plate leaving the extra oil behind. Serve','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":1,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":1,"flame":3}'),('5d679a0e39613718ed7d84ed','5d6797b709e1dd5a7f423880',1,'Boil Potatoes(p1)','To boil the potatoes- Wash 3 nos medium sized potatoes well with water. Put the washed potatoes in a pressure cooker. Add 2 cup water into it, enough to cover them. Cover it with a lid and pressure cook it on high flame till one whistle. After the first whistle, reduce to low flame and continue to cook to for another 8 minutes.  After cooking the potatoes for 8 minutes, turn off the heat and allow the pressure to release naturally. Once the pressure has been released, take off the lid, take out the potatoes and let them come to room temperature. Once the potatoes have come to room temperature, gently peel off the skin and cut them into 1 inch cubes. While the potatoes are boiling, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":8,"flame":3}'),('5d679b6b09e1dd5a7f423883','5d6797b709e1dd5a7f423880',2,'Make Green Chutney(p2)','For the mint chutney- Wash and chop 1 cup coriander leaves and 1/2 cup mint leaves. Peel 1 inch piece ginger and 4 cloves garlic. Slit 3 nos green chilies. Then transfer chopped coriander leaves, mint leaves, ginger and garlic cloves  into a blender jar. Add 1/2 teaspoon cumin seeds, 1 teaspoon salt and squeeze 2 tablespoon lemon juice into it along with 2 tablespoon water and blend smooth to make the coriander chutney.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5d679d0b39613718ed7d84ee','5d6797b709e1dd5a7f423880',3,'Make Tamarind Chutney(p3)','To make the tamarind chutney- In a pan, take 1/4 cup seedless tamarind. Add 1/4 cup dates and 1/4 cup jaggery into it along with 1.5 cup water. Stir everything well for a minute on medium flame till jaggery is well dissolved in water. Continue to boil it for 10 minutes on medium high flame. Then add 1/2 teaspoon fennel powder, 1 teaspoon coriander powder, 1/2 teaspoon cumin powder, 1 teaspoon red chili powder 1/2 teaspoon dry ginger powder and 1 teaspoon salt into. Stir them together for a minute mashing the dates and tamarind well with the spatula. Then reduce to low flame and continue to cook for another 2-3 minutes. After cooking it for 2-3 minutes, turn off the heat and allow it cool completely. Once it has come to room temperature, transfer it in a blender jar and blend smooth to make the tamarind chutney.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5d679de51710a053f6cd12c1','5d6797b709e1dd5a7f423880',4,'Chopping(p4)','Wash and chop 2 tablespoon fresh coriander leaves, wash and peel 2 tablespoon pomegranate seeds. Whisk 1/4 cup curd in a bowl using a hand whisker to avoid any lumps.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5d679e8d09e1dd5a7f423885','5d6797b709e1dd5a7f423880',5,'Fry potatoes(m1)','To fry the potatoes, heat 1/2 cup ghee in a pan on medium high flame for 1-2 minutes. Once the ghee is hot, carefully drop boiled potato cubes one by one into the hot ghee and shallow fry them on medium high flame for 3-4 minutes until they turn golden and crisp. After frying the potato cubes, take them out on kitchen towel and dab to remove the extra ghee.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5d679fd61710a053f6cd12c2','5d6797b709e1dd5a7f423880',6,'Make chat(m2)','To make the aloo chaat- Take the fried potato cubes in a bowl. Sprinkle 1/4 teaspoon salt, 1/4 teaspoon red chili powder, 1/4 teaspoon cumin powder, 1/4 teaspoon chaat masala powder and add 1 tablespoon lemon juice into it and give it a good mix using a spoon. Next add 3 tablespoon coriander chutney, 3 tablespoon tamarind chutney and 3 tablespoon whisked curd on top of the potatoes. Garnish the aloo chaat with 2 tablespoon nylon sev, 2 tablespoon pomegranate seeds and 2 tablespoon fresh coriander leaves and Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5d67ab6e1710a053f6cd12c4','5d67aac11710a053f6cd12c3',1,'Soak rice&dal (ap1)','In a bowl, take 1.5 cup rice, add 1 tablespoon poha into it and soak it in 3 cup water for 5 hours. In a separate bowl, take 1/2 cup urad daal, add 1 teaspoon fenugreek seeds into it and soak it in 1 cup water for 5 hours.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":300,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5d67ac201710a053f6cd12c5','5d67aac11710a053f6cd12c3',2,'Make Batter(ap2)','After soaking the rice and urad daal in water for 5 hours, first transfer the soaked rice into a blender jar, add 1/4 cup water into it and blend well to make a smooth batter. Transfer the rice batter in a bowl and empty the blender jar. Next transfer the soaked urad daal and methi into the same blender jar along with 1/4 cup water and blend well to make a smooth batter. Transfer the urad daal batter into the rice batter bowl and combine them together using a spatula. Cover it with a plate and let the batter rest and ferment for 7-8 hours.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":480,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5d67ba2739613718ed7d84f2','5d67aac11710a053f6cd12c3',3,'Make Dosa(m1)','After resting the dosa batter for 8 hours, batter will rise, give it good stir. Add 1 teaspoon salt and 1/2 cup water into it to adjust the consistency. Heat a nonstick tawa on medium flame for 1 minute. Then pour 1 ladle full of dosa batter on the tawa and spread it into a 9 inch thin circle. Apply 1 teaspoon oil all over it using a oil brush and cook it on medium low flame for 1-2 minutes until tiny bubbles start to appear on it and dosa turns crispy and golden. After cooking it for 2-3 minutes, fold the dosa from center and take it out on a plate and serve. Make the rest of the paper dosa similarly.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5d68d5661710a053f6cd12d0','5d68d23d09e1dd5a7f42388c',1,'Make Batter','To make aloo pakora batter- In a mixing bowl, take 1 cup gram flour. Add 1 teaspoon carom seeds, 1 teaspoon red chili powder, 1/2 teaspoon turmeric powder, 1/2 teaspoon coriander powder, 1 teaspoon salt, 1 teaspoon chat masala and 1/4 teaspoon hing into the gram flour and mix all the dry ingredients well. Then, into this, add 1 cup water or more, enough to make a batter of flowy thick consistency. Give the batter a good whisk to avoid any lumps.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5d68e53909e1dd5a7f42388d','5d68d23d09e1dd5a7f42388c',2,'Slice Potato(p2)','Wash, peel and cut thin and round slices of 1 cup potatoes using a vegetable slicer or a knife. Wash the potato slices with water to remove the extra starch and dab them on a kitchen towel to remove the extra water and keep them aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5d68e60d1710a053f6cd12d1','5d68d23d09e1dd5a7f42388c',3,'Make Pakora(m1)','To make aloo pakora- Heat 2 cups of oil in a kadai or a pan, while the oil is heating, add potato slices to the the gram flour batter and coat the slices well with the mixture. Next, to the heated oil carefully drop the coated potato slices one by one and shallow fry them on medium high flame for 3-4 minutes until they turn crisp and slightly golden. After frying them for 2-3 minutes, take them out on a kitchen towel to remove extra oil. Serve Hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":1,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5d68f09c09e1dd5a7f42388f','5d68eebc09e1dd5a7f42388e',1,'Knead dough(p1)','To make the dough- In a bowl take 2 cups of all purpose flour. Add 1 teaspoon salt and 2 teaspoon oil into this. Add about 3/4 cup water into this gradually and knead to make a soft dough. Add more water if required. Cover the dough with a cloth and let it rest for 15-20 minutes. While the dough is resting,please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":25,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5d68f0f639613718ed7d8500','5d68eebc09e1dd5a7f42388e',2,'Chop(p2)','Meanwhile, Wash and slice 1 cup onion and shred 1/2 cup cabbage.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5d68f20f09e1dd5a7f423890','5d68eebc09e1dd5a7f42388e',3,'Make filling(p3)','To make the filling- In a pan, heat 1 tablespoon oil on medium flame for a minute. Add 1 cup sliced onion into the hot oil and saute for 1-2 minutes on high flame till the onions turn slightly translucent. Then add 1/2 cup shredded cabbage into it and stir fry the vegetables on high flame for another 2-3 minutes. Next add 1/4 teaspoon salt, 1/4 teaspoon red chili flakes and give it a good toss.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":1,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5d68f33c09e1dd5a7f423891','5d68eebc09e1dd5a7f42388e',4,'Make paratha(p4)','After resting the dough for 15-20 minutes, knead it again and split it into 4 equal portions. Make round balls of each portion. Apply some oil on the rolling  platform, put one ball on it and spread it using fingers. Then roll it flat in a 6 inch diameter circle. Keep the edges thin while rolling. Place the paratha on a heated pan and roast it for 1 min on medium low flame. Flip it and apply 1 teaspoon oil all over the surface and roast it on medium low flame till it turns golden. Flip the paratha and cook the other side similarly. Once it''s slight golden take it out and keep aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":1,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5d68f3d31710a053f6cd12d5','5d68eebc09e1dd5a7f42388e',5,'Make Egg Paratha(m1)','In a bowl, crack 4 nos eggs. Add 1/2 teaspoon red chili powder and 1/4 teaspoon salt into the eggs and give it a good whisk. In a pan, heat 1 teaspoon oil and pour half of the egg mixture (for 1 paratha) and spread it. Next, place the ready paratha on this egg mixture and cook on medium low flame for 2-3 minutes. Flip the egg paratha and cook the other side for 1-2 minute. Then turn off the heat and take out the paratha on a dish.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5d6a87821710a053f6cd12de','5d6a83fd1710a053f6cd12dd',1,'Activate yeast&chop(p1)','In a pan, add 3/4 cup milk and heat it on low flame for 40 seconds till it''s lukewarm. Make sure not to boil the milk. Pour this lukewarm milk in a bowl. Add 1 teaspoon sugar and 1 teaspoon dry yeast into it, stir in well and let it rest for 10 minutes. Meanwhile, Wash and finely chop  2 tablespoon coriander leaves. Peel and finely chop 2 teaspoon garlic. Wash and slice 1/4 cup onion and 1/4 cup capsicum. Grate 1/4 cup mozzarella cheese.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":7,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5d6a883b1710a053f6cd12df','5d6a83fd1710a053f6cd12dd',2,'Knead dough(p2)','After 10 minutes, yeast activates. Add 1.5 cup all purpose flour, 1 teaspoon chopped garlic, 1/2 teaspoon mixed herbs, 1/2 teaspoon chili flakes and 1/2 teaspoon salt into the activated yeast and knead for 2-3 minutes until it is well combined. Apply 1 teaspoon oil all over the dough and knead it again. Then cover it with a cloth and let it rest in a warm place for 45-60 minutes.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":60,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5d6a889c39613718ed7d8509','5d6a83fd1710a053f6cd12dd',3,'Garlic Butter(m1)','To make the Garlic butter- Heat 3 tablespoon butter in a pan on medium flame for a minute. Pour it in a bowl, Into this add 1 teaspoon chopped garlic and 2 tablespoon chopped coriander leaves. Give it a good whisk.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5d6a89911710a053f6cd12e0','5d6a83fd1710a053f6cd12dd',4,'Make garlic bread(m2)','After 45-60 minutes, dough will rise and doubles in size, give it a quick knead again. Then make a ball of the complete dough, place it on a platter and flatten it using fingers. Spread it into a 9 inch circle. Apply the garlic butter mixture on the rolled out dough surface evenly using a oil brush. Add 1/4 cup grated mozzarella cheese, 1/4 cup sliced onion, 1/4 cup sliced capsicum on half of the surface. Sprinkle 1/4 teaspoon oregano on top and fold it from the center packing the cheese and vegetables inside. Brush 1 teaspoon garlic butter and sprinkle 1/4 teaspoon chili flakes and 1/4 teaspoon mixed herbs on top. Make small slits over the surface using a knife.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5d6a89d939613718ed7d850a','5d6a83fd1710a053f6cd12dd',5,'Make garlic bread(m3)','Preheat the oven at 200 degree C. Place the garlic bread dough inside it and bake at 180 degree C for 20-22 minutes, till it turns slightly golden and crisp. Serve Hot','cook_method','{"active_time":1,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":20,"flame":2}'),('5d6a8c5909e1dd5a7f42389e','5d6a8bfd39613718ed7d850b',1,'Chopping(p1)','Wash, peel and finely chop 2 cup bottle gourd and 2 nos green chilies. In a bowl take 1 cup curd and whisk it well to avoid any lumps.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5d6aa24139613718ed7d850c','5d6a8bfd39613718ed7d850b',2,'Make Raita(m1)','Heat 1 tablespoon ghee in a saucepan on medium heat for 1 minute. Add 1 teaspoon cumin seeds into it and let it crackle. Add 2 nos finely chopped green chilies and give it a quick saute. Next add 2 cup finely chopped bottle gourd into this and saute on medium flame for 1-2  minutes, add 1 teaspoon salt and saute well. Next stir in 3/4 cup water into the bottle gourd, cover it with a lid and cook on low flame for 7-8 minutes until bottle gourd turns tender. After cooking it for 7-8 minutes remove the lid, take out some bottle gourd in a spoon, mash it and check if it is completely cooked. Once it''s cooked,turn off the heat and let it cool down completely.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5d6aa2ae1710a053f6cd12e1','5d6a8bfd39613718ed7d850b',3,'Make raita(m2)','To make bottle gourd raita- Once the bottle gourd has come to room temperature, add 1 cup whipped curd into it and combine well. Add 2 tablespoon chopped coriander leaves into the raita and mix everything well. Serve','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5d76a7cf39613718ed7d852c','5d636c441710a053f6cd124c',6,'Par boil rice(p5)','To parboil the rice for the Hyderabadi Chicken Biryani, after soaking the rice in water for 45 minutes, drain off the extra water. Heat 4 cups of water in a deep bottom pan on medium heat for 2 minutes. Once the water has come to a boil, add spices potli, 1/2 teaspoon cumin seeds, 1 teaspoon ginger garlic paste and 1 teaspoon salt into it and bring it to boil. After the water has come to a boil, add soaked rice to it and let it boil for another 4-5 minutes on medium flame while stirring in between. Once the rice is partially cooked, drain off the extra water, Cover it with a lid and keep it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5d76a88409e1dd5a7f4238bf','5d636c441710a053f6cd124c',7,'Make biryani(m1)','To assemble the Hyderabadi Chicken Biryani, transfer the chicken to a heavy bottom pan and place it on low heat. Next, spread a thick layer of parboiled rice over the chicken layer, evenly. Sprinkle the soaked saffron milk on top of the rice along with 3/4 cup of golden fried onions. Add 1 tablespoon chopped fresh coriander leaves and mint leaves along with 1 tablespoon ghee on top of the rice. Cover it with a lid tightly and continue to cook on low flame for 40 minutes. After cooking the biryani for 40 minutes, turn off the heat, take off the lid and give it a final stir with light hands. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":40,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":40,"flame":2}'),('5d842cb41710a053f6cd1359','5d842c7339613718ed7d857a',1,'P1: Rinse the rice','First, wash 1 cup of Thai jasmine rice well with water for 2 times.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5d842cf91710a053f6cd135a','5d842c7339613718ed7d857a',2,'M1: Simmer the rice','In a saucepan boil 2 cups of water, as soon as its boiling add the rice and cover it, simmer for 15 mins. Once this is done let the rice rest for another 5 mins, then take the lid off and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":15,"flame":3}'),('5d9f5cb21710a053f6cd13a5','5d9f5b9a39613718ed7d85a9',1,'p1-Cut tofu and eggplant','To prepare ingredients for the Thai Green Curry. First, Cut 200 grams of tofu into 1 inch cubes as shown. Wash and cut 1 cup of small eggplants into quarters as shown.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5d9f5d0f39613718ed7d85ab','5d9f5b9a39613718ed7d85a9',2,'p2-cut mushroom and baby corn','Wash and chop 1 cup of white button mushrooms into 4 pieces as shown. Cut 1 cup of baby corn into smaller pieces as shown.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5d9f5d4b39613718ed7d85ac','5d9f5b9a39613718ed7d85a9',3,'p3-cut thai chilli, lime leaves and basil','Wash and chop 4 Thai bird''s eye chilies. Wash and roughly tear 5 Kaffir lime leaves into halves. Wash 10 individual Thai basil leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5d9f5d9039613718ed7d85ad','5d9f5b9a39613718ed7d85a9',4,'m1-Cook curry paste and coconut milk','To make Thai green curry with tofu- Heat 2 tablespoon of coconut oil in a pan on medium heat for a minute. Add 4 tablespoons of Thai green curry paste and half a teaspoon of Turmeric powder into the pan and saute it on medium high heat for 4 to 5 minutes. Be careful as the oil might splutter. After the paste has been cooked for 4-5 minutes, add 1 cup of coconut milk to the pan and mix it well with the green curry paste. Then reduce the flame to low and let the gravy simmer for 8 to 10 minutes till the coconut milk becomes thick and the oil starts to separate. While the gravy simmers, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('5d9f5ded09e1dd5a7f423954','5d9f5b9a39613718ed7d85a9',5,'m2-Add tofu, palm sugar, kaffir lime, chili','After simmering the curry for 8 to 10 minutes, oil will separate from the coconut milk. Then add 200 grams of tofu cubes into it and mix well. Next, Add 1 cup of coconut milk along with 2 cups of water, 1 tablespoon palm sugar, 5 Kaffir lime leaves, and 4 chopped Thai bird''s eye chili and mix well.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5d9f5e321710a053f6cd13a9','5d9f5b9a39613718ed7d85a9',6,'m3-Add veggies and cook on low','Next add 1 cup cut eggplant, 1 cup cut mushrooms, 1 cup cut baby corn and mix well. Bring the curry to a boil on medium heat. As soon as the curry comes to a boil, cover the pan, reduce the flame to low and continue to simmer till the egg plant is cooked through. This will take 8 to 10 minutes. Please remember to keep stirring the curry occasionally to prevent the coconut milk from splitting or from overflowing from the vessel.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5d9f5eb91710a053f6cd13aa','5d9f5b9a39613718ed7d85a9',7,'m4-Add lime juice, season and serve','After simmering the curry for 8 to 10 minutes, add the 1 tablespoon of lime juice and 10 individual Thai basil leaves to the curry and mix well.  Cook the curry for another 1-2 minutes on medium high heat. Check the gravy for seasoning and add salt as per taste. Finally, turn off the flame and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5dc5588439613718ed7d85e8','5dc557f51710a053f6cd13e9',1,'chop (p1)','For Greek Omelette, wash, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Wash and chop 1/4 cup of spinach leaves. Crumble 2 tablespoons of feta cheese using a fork.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('5dc558f909e1dd5a7f4239c1','5dc557f51710a053f6cd13e9',2,'beat eggs(p2)','For the Greek Omelette, crack 2 eggs in a bowl. Add 1 tablespoon of milk, 1/4 teaspoon of salt and 1/4 teaspoon of black pepper powder into the eggs and give it a good whisk using a spoon or a fork.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),
('5dc5595c09e1dd5a7f4239c2','5dc557f51710a053f6cd13e9',3,'make greek omelette (m1)','To make the Greek Omelette, heat 1 tablespoon of olive oil in a pan on medium flame for a minute. Then, add 1/4 cup of chopped spinach leaves, 1/4 cup of chopped onions and 1 tablespoon of kalamata olives into the hot oil and stir fry the vegetables on high flame for a minute.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5dc559cb09e1dd5a7f4239c3','5dc557f51710a053f6cd13e9',4,'make greek omelette(m2)','After stir-frying the vegetables add 1/4 cup of tomatoes and fry it on high flame for another 2 minutes. Then, pour the beaten egg mixture over the vegetables evenly. Add 2 tablespoons of crumbled feta cheese over the egg mixture and cook the omelette on medium-low flame for 2 minutes. Once the omelette is evenly cooked, turn off the flame and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5dc931ce39613718ed7d85f0','5dc92f5639613718ed7d85ef',1,'Chopping and pomegranate juice-p1','For Persian Chicken, wash 500 grams of chicken well with water. Peel and separate 1.5 cups of pomegranate seeds. Squeeze 1 tablespoon of lemon juice. Wash, peel and finely chop 1 cup of onion. To make the pomegranate juice, in a juicer take 1.5 cups of pomegranate seeds and blend it well to make the juice.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('5dc9326309e1dd5a7f4239d0','5dc92f5639613718ed7d85ef',2,'Make pomegranate molasses-p2','To make pomegranate molasses for Persian Chicken, heat a deep bottom pan on medium flame and add 1 cup of freshly prepared pomegranate juice. Next, add 1 tablespoon of lemon juice and 3 tablespoons of sugar to the juice and stir it well. Keep stirring it continuously on medium flame until the sugar dissolves completely. Continue to boil the syrup on medium flame for another 10-12 minutes until the syrup is reduced to 1/4 cup. While the molasses is cooking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":12,"flame":3}'),('5dc9330a1710a053f6cd13f0','5dc92f5639613718ed7d85ef',3,'Make walnut paste-p3','To make the walnut paste for Persian Chicken, heat 1 teaspoon of ghee in a pan on medium flame for a minute. Then, add 3/4 cup of walnuts and roast the walnuts on low flame for 5 minutes. Keep tossing the walnuts continuously while roasting it. Once the walnuts turn light brown, turn off the flame and let it cool down. Then, transfer it to a blender jar and grind it well to make a walnut paste. Next, after the pomegranate syrup is reduced to 1/4 cup, it will thicken. Then, turn off the flame and take out the pomegranate molasses in a bowl.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5dc9358609e1dd5a7f4239d1','5dc92f5639613718ed7d85ef',4,'fry chicken and spices- m1','To make the Persian Chicken, heat 3 tablespoons of butter in a kadai on medium flame for 30 seconds. Then, add 1 cup of finely chopped onions and stir fry the onions on medium-high flame for 3-4 minutes till it turns slightly golden brown. After frying the onions for 3-4 minutes, add 500 grams of chicken. Next, add 1/2 teaspoon of turmeric powder, 1/2 teaspoon of black pepper powder, 1/4 teaspoon of nutmeg powder, 1 teaspoon of salt, 1 teaspoon of sugar and 1/4 teaspoon of cinnamon powder. Then, saute it together, ensure to mix all the spices well with the chicken. Keep frying the chicken on medium-high flame for 4-5 minutes till the chicken is cooked.','cook_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5dc9365909e1dd5a7f4239d2','5dc92f5639613718ed7d85ef',5,'Simmer Chicken-m2','After frying the chicken for 5 minutes, add 1.5 cups of water and bring it to a boil on high flame. After the boil, cover the chicken with a lid and cook it on medium flame for 10 minutes. While the chicken is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":10,"flame":3}'),('5dc936ec1710a053f6cd13f1','5dc92f5639613718ed7d85ef',6,'make persian chicken-m3','For Perisan Chicken, after simmering the chicken, take off the lid and add the prepared walnut paste to it. Give it a stir. Then, add 1/4 cup of the prepared pomegranate molasses and stir well. Then cover the chicken with a lid, reduce to low flame and continue to simmer the chicken for an hour. After simmering the chicken for 1 hour, the oil will separate from the curry. Then, turn off the flame and garnish the chicken with 1 tablespoon of pomegranate seeds and 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":60,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":46,"flame":3}'),('5dc945171710a053f6cd13f2','5dc9444e39613718ed7d85f1',1,'wash and blanch spinach leaves-p1','For Palak Paneer, wash a bunch of spinach leaves well with water. Remove the stems of 1 cup of spinach leaves. To blanch the spinach leaves, boil 2 cups of water in a deep bottom pan on high flame for 1-2 minutes. Then, add 1 cup of washed spinach leaves along with 1/2 teaspoon of salt to the boiling water and let it boil on medium flame for 2-3 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and drain the excess water from the spinach leaves. Then, wash the blanched spinach leaves with regular water to prevent it from cooking further. While the spinach leaves are boiling, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":3,"flame":3}'),('5dc945d609e1dd5a7f4239d3','5dc9444e39613718ed7d85f1',2,'chopping-p2','For Palak Paneer, wash, peel and finely chop 1/2 cup of onion. Wash and finely chop 1/2 cup of tomatoes. Wash and finely chop 2 nos green chilies. Peel and finely chop 2 teaspoons of garlic and 1-inch piece of ginger. Finely cut 1-inch piece of ginger into juliennes. Cut 1 cup of paneer into 1-inch cubes.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),
('5dc946791710a053f6cd13f3','5dc9444e39613718ed7d85f1',3,'make spinach puree-p3','To make the spinach puree for Palak Paneer, in a blender jar, add the blanched spinach leaves, 1 teaspoon of chopped garlic, 1/2 inch piece of chopped ginger and 2 nos chopped green chilies. Blend it well to make a smooth puree.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5dc9477339613718ed7d85f2','5dc9444e39613718ed7d85f1',4,'make palak paneer-m1','To make Palak Paneer, heat 2 tablespoons of ghee in a deep bottom pan on medium flame for a minute. Then, add 1/2 teaspoon of cumin seeds, 1 nos bay leaf, 1 teaspoon of chopped garlic and 1/2 inch piece of chopped ginger. Saute it for a minute till the garlic turns aromatic. Then, add 1/2 cup of chopped onions and saute it for 2-3 minutes on medium-high flame till the onions turn slightly translucent. After frying the onions, add 1/2 cup of chopped tomatoes to it. Saute and cook the tomatoes on medium-low flame for 3-4 minutes, until it turns tender. Keep stirring the tomatoes occasionally while cooking, to prevent it from sticking to the bottom of the pan.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5dc9483939613718ed7d85f3','5dc9444e39613718ed7d85f1',5,'Simmer Paneer-m2','After cooking the tomatoes for 3-4 minutes, add 1/4 teaspoon of hing, 1/2 teaspoon of red chili powder, 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, 1 teaspoon of kasuri methi and 1 teaspoon of salt. Give it a stir and mix well. Next, add the prepared spinach puree to the masala and stir it continuously on medium-high flame for 1-2 minutes. Then, add 1/4 cup of water and mix it well. Reduce it to low flame and simmer the gravy for 8-10 minutes. While the gravy is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":10,"flame":3}'),('5dc948e039613718ed7d85f4','5dc9444e39613718ed7d85f1',6,'make palak paneer-m3','After simmering the gravy for 10 minutes, add 1 teaspoon of fresh cream and 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala to it. Stir it on medium flame for a minute. Then, add 1 cup of cubed paneer along with 1/2 cup of water and stir everything well. Continue to cook it for 1-2 minutes on medium flame, then turn off the heat. Transfer the palak paneer in a bowl, add 1 teaspoon of lemon juice and garnish it with ginger juliennes. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5dc94e1c39613718ed7d85f5','5d7d5bc21710a053f6cd1314',1,'P1: Soak the cashews & boil green peas','For Chicken Stew, soak 15 nos cashew nuts in a bowl along with 1/4 cup of water for 10 minutes. Wash and peel 1/2 cup of green peas, boil the peas in a deep bottom pan with 2 cups of water and 1/2 teaspoon of salt. Boil it on high flame for 3-4 minutes. Then, turn off the flame, drain the excess water from it and keep the boiled peas aside. While the peas are boiling, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5dc94ec21710a053f6cd13f4','5d7d5bc21710a053f6cd1314',2,'P2: Ground Spices','For Chicken Stew, in a mortar, add 1/2 teaspoon of black peppercorns, 2-inch piece of cinnamon stick, 1/4 teaspoon of fennel seeds, 3 nos green cardamoms and 3 nos cloves. Next, crush it into a coarse powder using a pestle.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5dc9529539613718ed7d85f6','5d7d5bc21710a053f6cd1314',3,'P3: Chop & prep the ingredients','For Chicken Stew, wash 600 grams of chicken well with water. Wash, peel and cube 1/2 cup of potatoes. Peel and dice 1/2 cup of carrot. Wash, peel and finely slice 1 cup of onion. Peel and finely chop 2 teaspoons of garlic and 2-inch piece of ginger. Wash and finely chop 3 nos green chilies. Wash 10 nos curry leaves. To make the cashew paste, add the soaked cashew nuts in a blender jar along with 2 tablespoons of water and blend it well to make a smooth paste.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5dc9541639613718ed7d85f7','5d7d5bc21710a053f6cd1314',4,'M1: Sear Chicken','To make Chicken Stew, heat 2 tablespoons of coconut oil in a pan on medium flame for a minute. Next, add freshly ground spices to the hot oil and saute for a minute. Then, add 1 cup of sliced onions, 2 teaspoons of chopped garlic, 2-inch piece of chopped ginger, 3 nos chopped green chilies and 10 nos curry leaves. Mix it well and fry the onions for 3-4 minutes on medium-high flame until it turns slightly golden. Then, add 600 grams of washed chicken into the onions and saute it together. Stir fry the chicken on medium-high flame for 8-10 minutes. Keep stirring continuously while frying the chicken with the onions. Add 1/4 cup of water to the chicken while cooking if it gets too dry.','cook_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5dc954cb39613718ed7d85f8','5d7d5bc21710a053f6cd1314',5,'M2: Simmer chicken with the curry','After cooking the chicken for 10 minutes, add 1/2 cup of cubed potatoes, 1/2 cup of diced carrots and 1/2 teaspoon of salt. Give it a good mix and stir fry the vegetables for 1-2 minutes on medium flame. Then, add 3/4 cup of coconut milk and 2 cups of water and stir well. Be careful while adding the coconut milk as it might splutter. Cover it with a lid and cook the chicken on low flame for 40-45 minutes, till the chicken is completely cooked.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":45,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":45,"flame":3}'),('5dc9555339613718ed7d85f9','5d7d5bc21710a053f6cd1314',6,'M3: Add cashew paste & coconut milk. Simmer the stew.','After cooking the chicken for 45 minutes, take off the lid and add 1 tablespoon of prepared cashew nut paste to it. Combine it well with the stew. Then, add 1/2 cup of boiled green peas along with 1/4 cup of coconut milk into it and give it a good stir. Simmer the stew for 1-2 minutes. Then turn off the flame and garnish the chicken stew with curry leaves and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5dca540d39613718ed7d85fc','5d7d47ce39613718ed7d8542',1,'roast vermicelli-p1','For Semiya Upma, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a pan on medium flame for a minute. Then, add 1 cup of vermicelli to it and roast it on low flame for 3-4 minutes until it turns slightly golden. After roasting the vermicelli, turn off the flame and let it cool down completely. While the vermicelli is cooling down, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5dca54a739613718ed7d85fd','5d7d47ce39613718ed7d8542',2,'Boil vermicelli-p2','For Semiya Upma, add 4 cups of water into a deep bottom pan and boil it on high flame for 2-3 minutes. Then, add roasted vermicelli to the boiling water along with 1/2 teaspoon of salt and give it a stir. Boil the vermicelli on high flame for 3 minutes. Keep stirring the vermicelli while it boils, to prevent it from sticking together. After boiling the vermicelli, turn off the flame and drain the excess water. While the vermicelli is boiling, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5dca55a71710a053f6cd13f6','5d7d47ce39613718ed7d8542',3,'chopping-p3','For Semiya Upma, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash, peel and finely chop 1-inch piece of ginger. Slit 2 nos green chilies. Peel 1/4 cup of green peas. Wash, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of carrot. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of capsicum and finely chop 1/4 cup of beans. Finely chop 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves. Squeeze 1 teaspoon of lime juice.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5dca57921710a053f6cd13f7','5d7d47ce39613718ed7d8542',4,'fry onions-m1','To make Semiya Upma, heat 3 teaspoons of cooking oil in a pan on medium flame for a minute. Add 1 teaspoon of mustard seeds, 1/2 teaspoon of urad dal, 1 teaspoon chana dal, 1 nos dry red chili, and 6 nos curry leaves to it. Give it a quick stir and let it splutter for a few seconds. Then, add 1 tablespoon of peanuts and stir fry the peanuts on high flame for a minute. Next, add 1-inch piece of finely chopped ginger and 2 nos slit green chilies and saute it on low flame for a minute. Then, add 1/4 cup of finely chopped onions and fry the onions on medium-high flame for 2-3 minutes till they turn slightly golden.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5dca582239613718ed7d85fe','5d7d47ce39613718ed7d8542',5,'simmer vegetables-m2','After frying the onions, add 1/4 cup of green peas, 1/4 cup of chopped carrot, 1/4 cup of chopped capsicum and 1/4 cup of chopped beans to the pan and stir fry the vegetables on high flame for 1 minute. Next, add 1/2 teaspoon of turmeric powder and 1/2 teaspoon of salt into the vegetables and continue to stir fry it for another minute on high flame. Then, cover the pan with a lid, reduce it to low flame and simmer the vegetables for 2 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":2,"flame":2}'),
('5dca58b909e1dd5a7f4239d8','5d7d47ce39613718ed7d8542',6,'garnish vermicelli-m3','After cooking the vegetables for Semiya Upma, remove the lid and give it a stir. Then, add the boiled vermicelli to the pan and gently mix everything together. Turn off the flame and garnish the semiya upma with 2 tablespoons of chopped coriander leaves and 1 teaspoon of lime juice. Give it a gentle mix and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5de7522a9a8ae0afdd4e2df6','5d68eebc09e1dd5a7f42388e',6,'Make egg roll(m2)','Keep the egg paratha on a plate. Spread 1 teaspoon mayonnaise on it evenly and keep 2 tablespoon cabbage onion filling on the paratha in the center lengthwise. Roll the paratha and Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5df8bc8608521ebca34d0f4f','5df8b93408521ebca34d0f4d',1,'P1: Soak boondi and prep the ingredients','To prepare the boondi for Boondi Raita, first, heat 1 cup of water over medium flame for a minute. Next, in a bowl, add half a cup of boondi and soak it in the hot water for 5 minutes, so it can absorb the water and become soft and moist. Next, wash and finely chop a tablespoon of coriander leaves. While the boondi is soaking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5df8bd420c3e3faf6f3cb81e','5df8b93408521ebca34d0f4d',2,'M1: Make the raita. Garnish and serve.','To make the Boondi raita, after soaking the bondi, drain off the water and set it aside. Next, in a large bowl, add 1 cup of curd followed by half a teaspoon of cumin powder and 1/4 teaspoon of red chili powder. Add 1/4 teaspoon of salt and mix it well using a whisk. Next, add in the soaked boondi and mix it well. Add a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and garnish the raita with some boondi and chopped coriander leaves. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e01b991e01e9c8010f00553','5e01b204e01e9c8010f00551',1,'P1','Wash and slice green chillies. Then wash, peel, and grate the bottle gourd into a large bowl. Add 1 tsp of salt to the grated gourd and squeeze the water out of it by hand. To this add garam masala, green chillies, coriander powder, dry mango powder, red chilli powder, and gram flour. Mix it well.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e01bb0314ac1f9a62ab361f','5e01b204e01e9c8010f00551',2,'P2','Coat a baking tray in ghee. Then divide the bottle gourd mixture into six equal parts and make small balls from it. Arrange these balls on the baking tray and coat them in ghee. Place them in the oven for 15-20 mins at 175°C.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":20,"flame":0}'),('5e01bd2b14ac1f9a62ab3620','5e01b204e01e9c8010f00551',3,'P3','Wash and chop onions, tomatoes, ginger, garlic, and coriander leaves. Make an onion puree by putting the onions, ginger, and garlic in a blender and blend it well. Then make a tomato puree, by blending the chopped tomatoes until smooth.','prep_method','{"active_time":14,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e01bf6614ac1f9a62ab3621','5e01b204e01e9c8010f00551',4,'M1','In a frying pan heat ghee, add red chillies and saute. Then add the onion puree, salt, coriander powder, garam masala, turmeric, red chilli powder, and green chillies. Saute these together on a medium flame for 1-2 mins.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e01c0c114ac1f9a62ab3622','5e01b204e01e9c8010f00551',5,'M2*','Then add the tomato puree and saute for 3-4 mins. Stir continuously while cooking. Then add 3/4 cups of water and bring it to a boil. Then add the baked kofta and simmer for 6-7 mins.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":7,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e01c18de01e9c8010f00557','5e01b204e01e9c8010f00551',6,'M3','Next, add 2Tbsp of fresh cream and stir it continuously for 1-2 mins on low flame. Turn off the flame, garnish this with coriander leaves, and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),
('5e01cd8a68ba1939423b3760','5e01caf1e01e9c8010f00564',1,'AP1','To make Chana Masala you need to soak the Chickpeas overnight or for 8-10 hours before you begin cooking.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":600,"advanced_prep_time":480,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e01ce27e01e9c8010f00568','5e01caf1e01e9c8010f00564',2,'P1','First, you need to cook the chickpeas in a pressure cooker along with baking soda and salt. Cook for 4 whistles on high flame and then for 8 mins on low flame. Set the pressure cooker aside to cool.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":18,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e01cefd68ba1939423b3761','5e01caf1e01e9c8010f00564',3,'P2','Then wash, peel, and chop onions, tomatoes, green chillies, lemon, and coriander.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e01cf7668ba1939423b3762','5e01caf1e01e9c8010f00564',4,'P3','Make a tomato puree by putting the chopped tomatoes into a blender. Then take the lid off the pressure cooker and strain the chickpeas, save the chickpea stock to use in the gravy later.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e01d0ac14ac1f9a62ab3626','5e01caf1e01e9c8010f00564',5,'M1','Start by heating a pan then add 1 Tbsp of Ghee or Oil. Once it is warm add the cumin seeds, black cardamom, cinnamon stick, and green chillies. After 2 mins add the ginger garlic paste to the pan.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e01d21c68ba1939423b3764','5e01caf1e01e9c8010f00564',6,'M2','Then add the onions and cook until they become translucent. Add 2 Tbsp of water to prevent burning and then add the dry spices: red chilli powder, turmeric, mango powder, garam masala, and salt. Cook this for 1 min.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e01d34614ac1f9a62ab3628','5e01caf1e01e9c8010f00564',7,'M3','Next, add the tomato puree and saute until the oil separates. Then add the chickpeas followed by the chickpea stock and mix well. Cover the pan with a lid and allow it to simmer for 8-10 mins.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e01d3ca14ac1f9a62ab3629','5e01caf1e01e9c8010f00564',8,'M4','Take the lid off and add 1/2 tsp of chana masala to the pan and mix well. If required, water can be added to adjust the consistency. The dish is ready, you can garnish it with fresh coriander, and onion and lemon slices','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e048ed114ac1f9a62ab362a','5e048c5ee01e9c8010f0056b',1,'P1','Start by washing and chopping cabbage, onion, and green chilli. Then grate 1/4 cup of coconut and wash 10 curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e04906168ba1939423b3765','5e048c5ee01e9c8010f0056b',2,'M1','In a pan heat coconut oil on a medium flame. Once it''s warm add mustard seeds, cumin seeds, and peanuts. Let them cook got 3-4 mins.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e04932768ba1939423b3768','5e048c5ee01e9c8010f0056b',3,'M2','After the peanuts are slightly brown add curry leaves, hing, green chillies, and onions. Cook until onions become translucent and then add salt and turmeric, mix well. Then add the cabbage and saute for 10-12 mins.','cook_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":4}'),('5e0493e368ba1939423b3769','5e048c5ee01e9c8010f0056b',4,'M3','To this add the grated coconut and mix well. Cook for another 1-2 mins and the dish is ready to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e18350e057fd3f6fc80ee4d','5e183327057fd3f6fc80ee4c',1,'P1: Making Coffee Decoction','Make the coffee decoction by combining instant coffee and hot water, until the coffee is dissolved completely.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e18363d985ffca18ae8fa40','5e183327057fd3f6fc80ee4c',2,'M1: Making the Drink','Put ice cubes in the serving glass and then add the cinnamon powder, almond essence, coffee decoction, milk, and powdered sugar. Mix it well and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e183fd3985ffca18ae8fa41','5e183f43057fd3f6fc80ee50',1,'P1: Make the Coffee Decoction','In a bowl combine instant coffee and hot water to make the coffee decoction, mix it well, until all the coffee is dissolved.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e940e4cd949647f48b3b2fe','5cfe511eecb2cc7ee630e3d6',1,'P1: Chopping the vegetables','For Roasted Vegetable Salad, first, wash and roughly chop 1/4 cup of capsicum, 1/4 cup of eggplant, 1/4 cup of zucchini, and 1 tbsp of parsley. Peel and roughly chop 1/4 cup of carrots, 1/4 cup of onions, and 1/4 cup of baby potato. Wash and chop 1/4 cup of cherry tomatoes into halves. Once all the ingredients are prepped, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":14,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e940f9b9d1b9abbdc2123f7','5cfe511eecb2cc7ee630e3d6',2,'M1: bake vegetables','For Roasted Vegetable Salad, preheat the oven to 180°C and then in a large bowl add 1/4 cup of capsicum, 1/4 cup of carrot, 1/4 cup of onions, 1/4 cup of eggplant, 1/4 cup of baby potatoes, 1/4 cup of zucchini, 5 pods of unpeeled garlic, 2 tbsp of olive oil, 1/2 tsp of salt, and 1/4 tsp of black pepper. Mix all these ingredients well, place them on a baking tray and let them bake for 15-20 mins. While the vegetables are cooking, please move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":20,"flame":0}'),('5e94103846ec6844c77d834a','5cfe511eecb2cc7ee630e3d6',3,'M2: make dressing for salad','Next, make the salad dressing, in a small bowl add 2 tbsp of mustard sauce, 1 tbsp of honey, 1 tsp of vinegar, 1 tsp of oregano, 2 tbsp of olive oil, and 1.5 tbsp of water, mix well. Once the vegetables are cooked, remove the skin of the roasted garlic and add it to a large bowl followed by the roasted vegetables, 1/4 cup of cherry tomatoes, and the prepared salad dressing. Toss all these ingredients together and the dish is ready to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e941422d173e07a0ad50a04','5d10752c7aa86e5274a85e0a',2,'m1: make tomato onion puree','To make Shahi Paneer, in a kadai, heat 1/2 tbsp of butter and then add 1/2 inch of cinnamon, 1 green cardamom, and 1 black cardamom. Let this splutter for a fews econds and then add 1/4 cup of chopped onions, 1/2 an inch of chopped ginger, and 2 cloves of chopped garlic, saute for 2-3 mins. Once the onions are translucent, add 1/4 cup of tomatoes and saute for 2 mins. Next, add 1/2 cup of water and 1/2 tsp of salt, mix well, then cover the kadai, and cook for 20 mins. After this, let the vegetable mixture cool down completely, and then blend it into a smooth puree. Once blended, pass it through a seave to make sure the puree is smooth and silky. Once this is ready set it aside and please move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e94157bd173e07a0ad50a05','5d10752c7aa86e5274a85e0a',3,'M2: cook the gravy with spices and paneer','Next, heat 1/2 tbsp of butter in a kadai on low flame and then add 1/4 tsp of shahi jeera, 1 bay leaf, 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder, and 1/2 tsp of red chilli powder saute for a few seconds. Next, add the prepared vegetable puree, mix well, and then add 2.5 tbsp of fresh cream, 1 cup of paneer, and 1/4 tsp of saffron. Combine all the ingredients, cover the kadai, and simmer for 5 mins. After this, add 1/4 tsp of kasuri methi and 1/4 tsp of garam masala, mix well, and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e941690d173e07a0ad50a06','5d10a746860ce8727dcd4ba8',1,'P1: blanch beans','To boil the beans for Basil Ground Chicken, first, wash 1/2 cup of beans well with water. Cut the edges of the beans using a knife. Then, cut the beans in half, into equal-sized pieces. Next, put 2 cups of water in a pan and bring it to a rolling boil on high flame. As the water comes to a boil, add 1/4 teaspoon of salt and 1/2 cup of chopped beans. Boil the beans on high flame for 3-4 minutes, till it turns tender. After boiling the beans, turn off the flame and drain off the water. Next, dip it in the chilled water, to prevent it from cooking further. After a minute, take it out and set it aside. While the beans are boiling, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":4,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e94177dd173e07a0ad50a07','5d10a746860ce8727dcd4ba8',2,'P2: chop the vegetables','For Basil Ground Chicken, wash 1 cup of minced chicken well with water. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of chopped red capsicum. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of green capsicum. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of yellow capsicum. Wash and finely chop 2 nos Thai red chilies. Wash and finely chop 1 nos green chili. Wash 1/2 cup of basil leaves. Wash and finely slice 1/2 cup of onions. Peel and finely chop 2 teaspoons of garlic.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9418066006438db3f96106','5d10a746860ce8727dcd4ba8',3,'M1: stir-fry vegetables','To make the Basil Ground Chicken, heat 1 tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan on medium flame for a minute. Add 2 teaspoons of chopped garlic and fry it on medium flame for 1-2 minutes, till it turns aromatic. Next, add 1 nos chopped green chili, 2 nos chopped Thai red chilies, 1/4 cup of chopped yellow capsicum, 1/4 cup of chopped red capsicum and, 1/4 cup of chopped green capsicum. Stir fry the vegetables on high flame for 2-3 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9418bac93a5a6f47718b7a','5d10a746860ce8727dcd4ba8',4,'M2: cook minced chicken with sauteed vegetables','After frying the vegetables for Basil Ground Chicken, add 2 teaspoons of palm sugar along with 1/2 teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Keep stirring it on medium flame for 1-2 minutes, until the sugar is completely dissolved. Then, add 1 cup of minced chicken and mix it well. Saute and cook the chicken on medium-low flame for 6-7 minutes till it is no longer pink. While the chicken is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":7,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e94196cc93a5a6f47718b7b','5d10a746860ce8727dcd4ba8',5,'M3: simmer the minced chicken with the sauce','After simmering the chicken for Basil Ground Chicken, add 1/2 cup of sliced onions and 1/2 cup of boiled beans and mix it well. Next, add 1/2 teaspoon of soy sauce and 1 teaspoon of fish sauce and saute it on medium-high flame for 1-2 minutes. Then, reduce it to low flame and continue to cook the chicken for another 8-10 minutes, until it is completely cooked. After simmering the chicken, add 1/2 cup of basil leaves and fry it on high flame for a minute. Then, turn off the flame and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('5e941b6aee8685d4ec57a097','5d11a1fd9243f874d7810f64',1,'P1: marinate the chicken','To make Chicken Tikka Masala, first marinate 250 g of chicken, in a large bowl with the chicken add 3 tbsp of curd, 1 tsp of red chili powder, 1 tsp of chicken masala powder, 3 tsp of ginger-garlic paste, and 1/2 tsp of salt, then mix well. Let this rest for 10 mins and while it''s resting, blend 1/4 cup of onions to make an onion puree and then set it aside. Wash and roughly chop 2 tbsp of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e941c366cf0a2f22f769b4f','5d11a1fd9243f874d7810f64',2,'m1: cook the chicken and simmer the curry','For Chicken Tikka Masala, heat a pan and then dry cook the marinated chicken for 8-10 mins, stirring occasionally. After this, take the chicken off the flame and keep it aside. Next, in another pan heat 2 tbsp of cooking oil and fry 1 tsp of ginger-garlic paste for 1 min. Then, add 1/4 cup of prepared onion puree, 1 tbsp of coriander leaves, 1 tsp of red chilli powder, 1 tsp of garam masala, and 3 tbsp of cashew powder, mix well. Next, add 1/2 cup of water and 1 tbsp of kitchen king masala, mix well, then cover the pan with a lid and let it simmer for 15 mins. While the curry is simmering, please move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":21,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e941c9ff1ae018d39b794fb','5d11a1fd9243f874d7810f64',3,'M2: thread and roast the chicken pieces, then simmer with gravy.','Next,  Put the cooked chicken pieces on skewers and roast them on a medium open flame until the chicken has charred. Remove the chicken from the skewers and then add it to the curry along with 3 tbsp of water. Cover the pan once more and cook for 5 mins. After that garnish the curry with 1 tbsp of coriander leaves and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e9422cbee8685d4ec57a09d','5d1f0781983ba767c7439c62',1,'P1: dry roast the spices and grind it to a coarse powder','In a pan, dry roast coriander seeds, dry red chillies, and cardamom for 2-3 mins. Next, grind them with a mortar and pestle to make a coarse powder. (This can also be done in a blender)','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e94239dee8685d4ec57a09e','5d1f0781983ba767c7439c62',2,'P2: Chop the vegetables','Finely chop half an onion and cut the other half into petals. Finely chop tomatoes. Chop red and green capsicum, peel and cut ginger, finely chop coriander leaves, and cut paneer into 1-inch cubes.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9424676cf0a2f22f769b57','5d1f0781983ba767c7439c62',3,'M1: Temper the ground spices and fry onions','Heat ghee in a kadai, then add finely chopped onions and fry it for 2-3 mins. Once the onions are slightly translucent, add garlic and ginger paste, saute this for 3-4 mins.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":2,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9425316cf0a2f22f769b58','5d1f0781983ba767c7439c62',4,'M2: saute & cook the tomatoes with spices','Once the ghee separates from the masala, add salt, red chili powder, and tomatoes,  saute this for 3-4 mins, stirring frequently.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":1,"flame":3}'),('5e9425c96cf0a2f22f769b59','5d1f0781983ba767c7439c62',5,'M3:  Fry the vegetables with the masala','Once the tomatoes are tender, stir in the tomato puree and saute for 1 min. Next, add red and green capsicum, and onion petals, mix this well. Crush the kasuri methi in your palms and add it to the pan, mix well.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e94263fee8685d4ec57a0a1','5d1f0781983ba767c7439c62',6,'M4: Add paneer to the gravy and simmer','Add the paneer along with 1/4 cup of water, cook for 1 min. Next, stir in fresh cream and cook for another minute. Turn off the flame, garnish with ginger, and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":1,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e942ad2f1ae018d39b79506','5e70933c91cde451322c517b',1,'P1: Making the Rice','To make Schezwan Egg Fried Rice, first, wash basmati rice and then add it to a pressure cooker along with double the amount of water. Cook on high flame for 1 whistle and then on low flame for 8 mins. Once this is done, allow the pressure to release naturally before you open the lid. While the rice is cooking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":10,"flame":3}'),
('5e942cb3ee8685d4ec57a0a5','5e70933c91cde451322c517b',2,'P2: Prepping Ingredients','Next, peel and finely chop garlic, ginger, and carrots. Wash and finely chop beans, spring onions, capsicum, and cabbage.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e942fb0ee8685d4ec57a0a6','5e70933c91cde451322c517b',3,'M1: Cook the Vegetables','To make Schezwan Egg Fried Rice, heat oil in a pan on medium flame and then add ginger, garlic, and capsicum, saute for 2 mins. Next, add beans, carrot, spring onion whites, and cabbage, saute for 3 mins. Then, add salt, pepper, soy sauce, vinegar, ketchup, and schewzan sauce, mix well.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e943166f1ae018d39b79508','5e70933c91cde451322c517b',4,'M2: Making the Fried Rice','Next, move the vegetables to the edge of the pan, creating space in the center and then add oil then crack the eggs into the center. Quickly scramble the eggs and once they have cooked well mix them with the vegetables. Next, add the spring onion greens and cooked basmati rice, and gently mix all the ingredients together. Once the ingredients are combined the dish is ready to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e943205f1ae018d39b79509','5d2829b37b8ec859d333b6d1',1,'P1: Marinate the Fish','To make Fish Molee, first marinate the fish, in a bowl combine 400 g of seer fish, 1/2 tsp of turmeric powder, 1/2 tsp of red chili powder, and 1/2 tsp of salt. While the fish is marinating, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9432936cf0a2f22f769b5c','5d2829b37b8ec859d333b6d1',2,'P2: Chop the vegetables','Next, peel and slice 1/2 cup of onions, wash and slit 3 green chilies, wah 12 curry leaves, and peel and finely chop 1 inch of ginger.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9433cff1ae018d39b7950a','5d2829b37b8ec859d333b6d1',3,'M1: Pan sear the fish and simmer the onions with coconut milk.','For Fish Molee, heat a pan with 3 tbsp of oil and then add the marinated fish, then shallow fry the fish for 5 mins until it is evenly browned on all sides. Take this off the pan once it is cooked and set it aside. Next, add 1/2 cup of onions to the same pan and saute for 2 mins. Then, add 1 tbsp of all-purpose flour and 1/4 tsp of black pepper, mix well. Next, add 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder and 12 curry leaves, mix well. To this, add 1.5 cups of coconut milk, 3 slit green chilies, 1 inch of chopped ginger, 1 tsp of salt, 1 pinch of cinnamon, 3 cloves, and 2 tsp of vinegar, mix well. Next, reduce the flame to low, cover the pan with a lid and simmer for 10 mins.','cook_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9434366cf0a2f22f769b5d','5d2829b37b8ec859d333b6d1',4,'M2: simmer the seared fish with coconut curry.','Next, add the cooked pieces of fish and close the lid once more, cook for 5 mins. Pour in 1/4 cup of thick coconut milk and simmer for another 3 mins. The dish is ready to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e94353af1ae018d39b7950b','5e70906c91cde451322c517a',1,'P1: Prepping the Ingredients','For Chicken Noodle Soup, peel and finely chop onions, carrots, and garlic. Wash and finely chop celery and parsley.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9436776cf0a2f22f769b5e','5e70906c91cde451322c517a',2,'M1: Cooking the Chicken','To make Chicken Noodle Soup, heat butter in a pot on medium heat and then add onions, carrots, and celery, saute for 3 mins. Once the vegetables are soft, add garlic, a bay leaf, and 1 spring of fresh thyme, mix well. Next, add a chicken stock cube, water, black pepper and salt, mix well. Once the water is boiling add chicken thighs, reduce the flame to low, cover the pot and let the soup simmer for 20 mins.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":20,"flame":2}'),('5e9437e7f1ae018d39b7950c','5e70906c91cde451322c517a',3,'M2: Cooking the Noodles','Next, take the pieces of chicken out of the soup and onto a plate. Add egg noodles to the pot, cover it, and cook it for 8-10 mins. While the noodles are cooking, with 2 forks shred the chicken into small bite-size pieces, then add the shredded chicken back to the soup. Garnish the soup with parsley and the dish is ready to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":8,"flame":3}'),
('5e943899ee8685d4ec57a0a7','5d285e3e983ba767c7439c92',1,'P1: Soak the lentils','For Panchmel dal, in a mixing bowl, add 1/4 cup of yellow moong dal, 1/4 cup of masoor dal and 1/4 cup of toor dal. Next, add 1/4 cup of chana dal followed by 1/4 cup of black urad dal and soak it in 3 cups of water for 30 minutes. While the dals are soaking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":30,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e943910ee8685d4ec57a0a8','5d285e3e983ba767c7439c92',2,'P2: Chop & prep the ingredients','For Panchmel dal, peel, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash 6 nos curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e943953f1ae018d39b7950d','5d285e3e983ba767c7439c92',3,'M1: Pressure cook the soaked lentils.','To make Panchmel Dal, add the soaked dals to a pressure cooker along with 3 cups of water and cover it with a lid. Pressure cook the dal over high flame until two whistles. Then, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook it for another 8 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the dal is cooking, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9439fe6cf0a2f22f769b5f','5d285e3e983ba767c7439c92',4,'M2: Fry the onions with ginger garlic paste for tempering.','To make Panchmel dal, heat 1 tablespoon of ghee in a kadai over medium flame for a minute. Temper it with 1/4 teaspoon of mustard seeds and half a teaspoon of cumin seeds. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions and fry it over medium-high flame for 2-3 minutes, until translucent. Next, add 1 teaspoon of ginger-garlic paste and fry it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e943aa8f1ae018d39b7950e','5d285e3e983ba767c7439c92',5,'M3: Add tomatoes and spices, then cook the masala.','After frying the ginger-garlic paste, add 1 nos dry red chili along with 6 nos curry leaves and mix it well. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes and mix it well. Saute and cook the tomatoes over medium-low flame for 4-5 minutes, until it turns tender. After cooking the tomatoes, add 1/4 teaspoon of red chili powder and 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder followed by half a teaspoon of coriander powder and mix it well. Saute and fry the masala for another 1-2 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e943b29f1ae018d39b7950f','5d285e3e983ba767c7439c92',6,'M4: Simmer the cooked lentils with the masala.','After frying the masala, add the prepared panchmel dal and mix it well. Add half a teaspoon of salt and allow it to cook over medium flame for 5 minutes. Keep stirring in between. After cooking the dal, add 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala followed by half a teaspoon of Kasuri methi and mix it well. Turn off the flame and add 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves. Mix it well and take it out into a serving bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9441e7f595ed1902ef80ae','5d3ab481f19f3410efefc440',1,'P1: Chop & prep the ingredients.','For Avocado Toast, wash and cut a small avocado into halves and remove the seed. Then, gently scoop out the pulp and put it into a bowl. Next, peel, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Peel, wash and finely chop 1 teaspoon of garlic. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash and cut a lemon into halves. Then, squeeze 1 teaspoon of lemon juice using a squeezer.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e944232f595ed1902ef80af','5d3ab481f19f3410efefc440',2,'P2: Prepare the avocado mixture','To prepare the avocado mixture for Avocado Toast, first, mash the avocado pulp well using a fork. Next, add 1 teaspoon of chopped garlic, and half a teaspoon of black pepper powder followed by half a teaspoon of salt. Add a teaspoon of lemon juice along with 1/4 cup of chopped onions and a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and mix it well to prepare a mixture.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e94428834cb09f78913f797','5d3ab481f19f3410efefc440',3,'M1: Toast the bread slices','To toast the bread slices, first, apply half a teaspoon of butter over a bread slice and place it onto a tawa. Toast the bread slice over medium flame for 2-3 minutes. Apply half a teaspoon of butter to the other side. Then, flip the bread slice and toast the other side for 1-2 minutes, until it turns slightly golden. Then, Take it out onto a plate and slice it diagonally. Toast the rest of the bread slices similarly.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9442c2a1c86f05ef13a66a','5d3ab481f19f3410efefc440',4,'M2: spread the avocado mixture over the toasted slices & serve.','To make the Avocado Toast, spread a thick layer of the prepared avocado mixture over the toasted bread slice. Sprinkle 1/4 teaspoon of mixed herbs and 1/4 teaspoon of chili flakes over it and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9448d534cb09f78913f799','5d3ab5ea6c7e050b497dc4a5',1,'P1: Flake the canned tuna and prep the ingredients','To make Tuna Celery Salad, first, drain the water from the can of tuna and then using 2 forks shred the tuna into smaller pieces. Next, wash and dice 1/2 cup of celery. Peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and roughly chop 2 tbsp of dill leaves. Squeeze 1 tbsp of lime juice.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9449aef595ed1902ef80b2','5d3ab5ea6c7e050b497dc4a5',2,'M1: Combine the ingredients and make the salad','For Tuna Celery Salad, in a large bowl add 1.5 cups of tuna, 1/2 cup of chopped celery, 1/4 cup of chopped onion, 2 tbsp of chopped dill, 2 tbsp of lime juice, 1/2 cup of mayonnaise, 1/4 tsp of salt, and 1/4 tsp of black pepper. Combine all the ingredients well and the dish is ready to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e953cb69f193732ef051067','5e575532f7851cecaf7c5088',1,'P1- prep ingredients','For Achari Bhindi, wash 1 cup of lady''s fingers well with water and spread it over a kitchen towel to wipe off the extra water. Allow it to dry completely and make sure there is no moisture left in the lady''s fingers. Then, cut it into 1-inch pieces. Next, peel, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash and roughly chop 1 nos medium-sized tomato. Then, add the chopped tomato to a blender jar and blend it well into a smooth puree.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e953d1bbf3f392645fdcc49','5e575532f7851cecaf7c5088',2,'M1- Fry bhindi','To make Achari Bhindi, heat 2 tablespoons of oil in a kadai and then fry 1 cup of lady''s finger along with 1/2 teaspoon of salt for 3-5 mins. Once the bhindi is fried cooked take it off the flame and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e953d759f193732ef051068','5e575532f7851cecaf7c5088',3,'m2 - temper spices','To make Achari Bhindi, heat 2 tablespoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Temper it with half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, half a teaspoon of fennel seeds and half a teaspoon of black caraway seeds. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions and fry it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes, until it turns translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e953dafbf3f392645fdcc4a','5e575532f7851cecaf7c5088',4,'m3 - cook masala','After frying the onions, add a teaspoon of ginger-garlic paste followed by half 1/4 cup of the prepared tomato puree and mix it well. Saute and cook the masala over medium-low flame for 4-5 minutes, until oil separates. After the masala releases oil, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder along with half a teaspoon of red chili powder and half a teaspoon of salt. Mix it well and fry the masala over medium flame for a minute.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e953de1bf3f392645fdcc4b','5e575532f7851cecaf7c5088',5,'m4 - garnish and serve','Next, add about 1/4 cup of water to the masala and stir it well. Add 1 cup of fried ladies fingers and mix it well the masala. Then, saute it with light hands over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Next, add 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and mix it well. Turn off the plate and take it out into a serving bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e953ee9bf3f392645fdcc4c','5e708a1591cde451322c5179',1,'P1: Prepping the Ingredients','To make Shakshuka, first, peel and finely chop onions. Wash and slice mushrooms. Wash and finely dice red capsicum. Wash and blend tomatoes into a smooth puree. Crumble feta cheese. Wash and roughly chop parsley.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e953fe6bf3f392645fdcc4d','5e708a1591cde451322c5179',2,'M1: Cooking the Vegetables','For Shakshuka, heat olive oil in a pan on medium-high flame and then add onions, mushroom, and salt, then saute for 2-3 mins. Next, add capsicum and jalapenos, then saute for 3 mins. Then, add cumin powder, paprika, turmeric powder, black pepper, cayenne powder, and mix well. Next, add the prepared tomato puree, mix well, and then saute for 2 mins. Next, add 3 tbsp of water and let this simmer for 15 mins.','cook_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e95414471a4dfd0d1b65dc2','5e708a1591cde451322c5179',3,'M2: Cooking the Eggs','Next, check the seasoning in the dish, adding any salt if necessary and then make small dents in the curry for the eggs. Then, gently crack 4 eggs into the pan, cover the pan, and let it cook for 6 mins. Next, take off the lid, garnish the dish with 1 tbsp of parsley and 1 tbsp of feta cheese, and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('5e954368b8df13802c95a090','5e7087b6a04de0b99a30032f',1,'P1: Prepping the Ingredients','For Ambur Biryani, first, soak dry red chillies in water for 20 mins. While the chillies are soaking, peel and finely slice onions, wash and slice tomatoes, peel and finely chop garlic, squeeze lime juice, and wash and roughly chop coriander leaves. Wash samba rice and keep aside. Once the chillies are done soaking, blend them into a smooth chilli paste and keep it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e954492b8df13802c95a091','5e7087b6a04de0b99a30032f',2,'M1: Cooking the Whole Spices','To make Ambur Biryani, heat oil in a deep pan on medium flame, then add cinnamon, cloves, and green cardamom, saute this for a few seconds. Next, add onions, garlic, and ginger paste, and saute this for 5 mins. Once the onions are golden, add tomato, and saute for 6-8 mins.','prep_method','{"active_time":14,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e95482eacd25afedeb1f6d2','5e7087b6a04de0b99a30032f',3,'M2: Making the Biryani','Once the tomatoes are soft, add the prepared chilli paste and saute for 2 mins. Next, add fresh curd and lime juice, mix well, then add chicken and salt, and cook for 5 mins stirring frequently. Next, add coriander leaves, water, and samba rice, mix well. Cook this for 5 mins, stirring occasionally, and then reduce the flame to low, cover the pan, and cook fro 15 mins. Once this is done, let the biryani rest for 5 mins before you open the lid. This dish is ready to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":14,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e954952ab62d52ee6dc4259','5e708618378bf22ba423187c',1,'P1: Soaking the Rice','For Masala Bath, first, wash 1 cup of sona masuri and then soak it in 2 cups of water for 20 mins. While the rice is soaking please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":20,"flame":0}'),('5e9549a4acd25afedeb1f6d4','5e708618378bf22ba423187c',2,'P2: Making the Masala Powder','Next, heat 1 tsp of oil in a pan on low flame for 1 min, then add 1 tbsp of coriander seeds, 1/2 tsp of cumin seeds, 1/2 tsp of sesame seeds, 1 star anise, 1/4 tsp of poppy seeds, 1 black cardamom, 1/2 an inch of cinnamon, 4 cloves, 1 tbsp of dry coconut, and 1/4 tsp of black peppercorns, roast these whole spices for 2-3 mins. Then, turn off the flame, allow the spices to cool and then blend them into a coarse masala powder. Keep this aside and then move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),
('5e9549d8b8df13802c95a092','5e708618378bf22ba423187c',3,'P3: Chopping','Next, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions, 1/4 cup of carrots, and 1/4 cup of potatoes. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes and 2 tbsp of coriander leaves. Wash and slit 2 green chillies. Wash and chop 1/4 cup of cauliflower into small florets. Grate 2 tbsp of fresh coconut.','prep_method','{"active_time":13,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e954b43acd25afedeb1f6d5','5e708618378bf22ba423187c',4,'M1: Cooking','To make Masala Bath, heat 1 tbsp of ghee in a pan on medium flame, then add 1/2 tsp of mustard seeds, 1/2 tsp of cumin seeds, 1 bay leaf, and 1/4 tsp of hing, let this splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions and 2 slit green chillies, saute for 2-3 mins. Once the onions are translucent, add 1 tsp of ginger-garlic paste, mix well, then add 1/4 cup of tomatoes and 15 cashew nuts, and mix well. Next, add 1/4 cup of green peas, 1/4 cup of cauliflower, and 1/4 cup of potatoes, saute for 1 min.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e954b76ab62d52ee6dc425a','5e708618378bf22ba423187c',5,'M2: Cooking','Then, add 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder, 1/2 tsp of red chilli powder, and the prepared masala powder, mix well. Reduce the flame to low, add 1 cup of soaked rice, saute for 1 min, then add 2.5 cups of water and 1 tsp of salt. Mix everything well, cover the pan with a lid, and simmer for 20 mins. After this, add 2 tbsp of grated coconut and 2 tbsp of coriander leaves, mix well, and this dish is ready to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e954dc4acd25afedeb1f6d6','5d4d03d7f845a829dca1141c',1,'P1: Knead the dough','To make Cabbage thepla, first, blend 1 green chilli and 1 inch of ginger into a smooth paste. Wash and grate 1/4 cup of cabbage. Then, in a large bowl, add 2 cups of flour, 1.5 tbsp of gram flour, 1 tsp of red chilli powder, 1/2 tsp of turmeric powder, 1/4 tsp of salt, the prepared ginger-green chilli paste, 2 tbsp of coriander leaves, 1 tsp of sesame seeds, 1/4 cup of grated cabbage, 1/2 cup of curd, and 1 tbsp of oil, mix these ingredients together. Knead the dough for 5 mins until you have a smooth soft dough.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e954dfab8df13802c95a093','5d4d03d7f845a829dca1141c',2,'M1: Roll out the dough ball','For Cabbage Thepla, make small lemon sized balls from the dough. Take one of these dough balls, flatten it with your palm on a rolling board, and dust it with flour. Next, using a rolling pin roll the dough into a disk shape, allowing it to remain slightly thick. Repeat this process with the remaining dough and move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e954e2eb8df13802c95a094','5d4d03d7f845a829dca1141c',3,'M2: Cook cabbage thepla','Next, heat a tawa on medium flame for 1 min. Then, drizzle 1/2 tbsp of oil on the tawa, then place a roti on top followed by another 1/2 tbsp of oil. Let the roti cook on each side for 2-3 mins. Once both sides have browned evenly, take them off the tawa. Repeat this with the remaining raw rotis and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e954ecaab62d52ee6dc425b','5d4d06b2f845a829dca1141e',1,'AP1: Soak kidney beans','For Kidney Bean Salad, first, soak 1/4 cup of kidney beans in 3/4 cup of water for 12 hours or overnight.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":480,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e954eefab62d52ee6dc425c','5d4d06b2f845a829dca1141e',2,'P1: Pressure cook kidney beans','To make Kidney Beans Salad, in a pressure cooker add 1/4 cup of soaked kidney beans, along with 2 cups of water and 1/4 tsp of salt, and 1/4 tsp of oil. Cook this on high flame for 1 whistle and then on low flame for 8 mins. Once this is done, allow the pressure to release naturally before you take off the lid. While the kidney beans are cooking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":1,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e954f28b8df13802c95a095','5d4d06b2f845a829dca1141e',3,'P2: Chop & prep the ingredients','Next, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of capsicum, 1 tsp of green chili, and 2 tbsp of coriander leaves. Wash and chop 1/4 cup of cherry tomatoes into halves. Squeeze 2 tbsp of lime juice.','prep_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e954f5fb8df13802c95a096','5d4d06b2f845a829dca1141e',4,'M1: Combine the ingredients & Make salad','For Kidney Bean Salad, make a salad dressing, in a small bowl add 2 tbsp of lime juice, 1 tbsp of olive oil, 1/2 tsp of salt, 1/2 tsp of black pepper, and 1 tbsp of honey and mix well. Once the kidney beans have cooked completely, add them to a large bowl and into the same bowl, add 1/4 cup of sweet corn kernels, 1/4 cup of onions, 1/4 cup of capsicum, 1 tsp of green chili, 1/4 cup of cherry tomatoes, 2 tbsp of coriander leaves, and the prepared salad dressing. Combine all these ingredients well and the salad is ready to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e954ff0ab62d52ee6dc425d','5d4d012cacc6496253ae8238',1,'P1: Chop & prep the ingredients','To make Potato, Carrot, Green Peas Sabzi, peel and finely chop 1 tsp of garlic, 1 inch of ginger, 1/4 cup of onion, 1 cup of carrot, and 1 cup of potato. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes, 2 green chilies, and 1 tbsp of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e955063acd25afedeb1f6d7','5d4d012cacc6496253ae8238',2,'M1: Temper the oil and simmer the vegetables with the masala','To make Potato, Carrot, Green Peas Sabzi, heat 1.5 tbsp of mustard oil in a pan and then add 1/4 tsp of carom seeds, 1/2 tsp of cumin seeds, 1 tsp of garlic, 1 inch of ginger, and 2 green chilies, let this splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 1/4 cup of onions, saute for 2-3 mins, then add 1/4 cup of tomatoes, and saute for 3 mins. Then, add 1 cup of carrots, 1/2 tsp of salt, 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder, 1/2 tsp of red chili powder, 1/2 tsp of coriander powder, and 1/4 tsp of garam masala, saute for 3 mins. Close the pan and cook the vegetables for 5 mins.','cook_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e95509bb8df13802c95a097','5d4d012cacc6496253ae8238',3,'M2: Simmer the vegetables. Then, garnish and serve','Next, add 1 cup of potatoes and 1/2 cup of green peas, cover the pan and cook for another 10 mins. Once this is done, garnish the dish with 1 tsp of kasuri methi, 1 tbsp of coriander leaves, and the dish is ready to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9550e0ab62d52ee6dc425e','5e7082bfa04de0b99a30032e',1,'P1: Chopping','For Beetroot Carrot Poriyal, wash and finely chop 3/4 cup of beetroots. Wash, peel and finely chop half a cup of carrots. Wash and finely chop 2 nos green chilies. Peel, wash and finely chop half a cup of onions. Wash, peel and finely chop 1 teaspoon of garlic. Wash 7 nos curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e95510aab62d52ee6dc425f','5e7082bfa04de0b99a30032e',2,'M1: Tempering','To make Beetroot Carrot Poriyal, heat 1 tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Next, add a teaspoon of chopped garlic followed by half a teaspoon of urad dal and half a teaspoon of cumin seeds. Add 2 nos chopped green chilies and saute it over medium flame for a minute.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e95513fb8df13802c95a099','5e7082bfa04de0b99a30032e',3,'M2: Cooking the Vegetables','Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped carrots followed by 3/4 cup of chopped beetroot and half a cup of chopped onions. Add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder along with half a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Then, stir fry the vegetables over medium flame for 6-7 minutes until tender-crisp.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e955184b8df13802c95a09a','5e7082bfa04de0b99a30032e',4,'M3: Adding the Masalas','After frying the vegetables, add half a teaspoon of red chili powder and half a teaspoon of coriander powder and mix it well. Then, saute and fry it for another 3-4 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and take it out into a bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e955244acd25afedeb1f6d9','5d4d1d79acc6496253ae823c',1,'P1: Chop & prep the ingredients','To make Masala Omelette, first, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 2 green chilies. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Wash and roughly chop 1 tbsp of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e955274b8df13802c95a09b','5e7081be378bf22ba423187b',1,'P1: Prepping Ingredients','To make Green Peas Sundal, first, peel and finely chop 1/2 cup of onions. Grate 1/4 cup of fresh coconut. Wash 7 curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e955290b8df13802c95a09c','5d4d1d79acc6496253ae823c',2,'M1: Prepare the omelette mixture and cook the omelette','For Masala Omelette, in a large bowl, whisk 4 eggs together well. Then, add 1/4 cup of onions, 2 chopped green chili, 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes, 1 tbsp of coriander leaves, 1/2 tsp of salt, and 1/2 tsp of black pepper. Whisk all the ingredients together well and then heat a frying pan with 1 tsp of oil. Next, add 1/2 the whisked egg mixture and let it cook for 2 mins. Once the edges are cooked well, flip the omelette carefully and cook for another 2 mins. Next, fold the omelette in half and cook on each side for 1 min. Repeat this process to make another omelette and enjoy.','cook_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e955378acd25afedeb1f6da','5e7081be378bf22ba423187b',2,'M1: Making Sundal','For Green Peas Sundal, heat 1 tbsp of coconut oil in a pan and then add 1/2 tsp of urad dal, 1/2 tsp of chana dal, 1/2 tsp of mustard seeds, 1/4 tsp of hing, and 1 broken dry chilli, let this splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 1/2 cup of chopped onion, 1/2 tsp of salt, and 7 curry leaves, saute for 2-3 mins. Once the onions are translucent, add 1.5 cups of green peas and saute for 2 mins. Then, add 1/4 cup of grated coconut, mix well, and this dish is ready to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9553efacd25afedeb1f6db','5e707f7391cde451322c5178',1,'P1: Prepping the Ingredients','To make Groundnut Sundal, boil 2 cups of peanuts in a pot for 15 mins. When these have boiled drain the excess water ad then set them aside. While the peanuts are boiling, prep all the other ingredients. Wash and finely chop 1 green chilli, wash 7 curry leaves, grate 3 tbsp of fresh coconut, and wash and finely chop 2 tbsp of raw mango.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e955471acd25afedeb1f6dc','5e707f7391cde451322c5178',2,'M1: Making Sudal','For Ground Nut Sundal, heat 2 tsp of coconut oil in a pan and then add 1/2 tsp of mustard seeds, 1 tsp of urad dal, 1 slit green chilli, 7 curry leaves, and 1/4 tsp of hing, let this splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 2 cups of groundnuts and 2 tbsp of raw mango, mix well. Then add 3 tbsp of grated coconut, mix well, and turn off the flame. Serve and Enjoy!','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e955539b8df13802c95a09d','5e707ae4a04de0b99a30032c',1,'AP1: Soaking the Dal','For Kollu Rasam, wash 1/4 cup of horse gram well with water. In a large mixing bowl, add 1/4 cup of rinsed horse gram and soak it in 2 cups of water for 2 hours. While it is soaking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":120,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e95553bacd25afedeb1f6dd','5d4d1e0424ade8297f194abd',1,'P1: Prepare the coffee decoction','For Filter Coffee, first, add 1 tbsp of coffee powder in the top half of the coffee filter, cover it with the press, and then pour 1/2 cup of hot water into the coffee filter. Let this rest for 15 mins.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e95556eb8df13802c95a09e','5e707ae4a04de0b99a30032c',2,'P1: Cook the Dal','For Kollu Rasam, soak 2 teaspoons of tamarind in 1/2 cup of water for 15 minutes. To cook horse gram, add the soaked horse gram to a pressure cooker along with 2 cups of water. Cover it with a lid and pressure cook it on high flame untill 4 whistles. After the fourth whistle, reduce it to low flame and continue to cook it for another 8 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the horse gram is cooking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e95559eacd25afedeb1f6de','5e707ae4a04de0b99a30032c',3,'P2: Prepping the Ingredients','For Kolllu Rasam, wash and finely chop 1/2 cup of tomatoes. Peel 2 cloves of garlic. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash 7 nos curry leaves. Next, after soaking the tamarind, mash it and mix it well with the water. Strain it using a strainer to remove the residue from it.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9555adacd25afedeb1f6df','5d4d1e0424ade8297f194abd',2,'M1: Pour in milk to the decoction. Stir in sugar and serve','For Filter Coffee, boil 1.5 cups of milk in a sauce pan. In a serving cup pour 2 tbsp of prepared coffee decoction or your preferred amount, then add 2 tsp of sugar and mix well. Next, pour in 1/2 cup of hot milk, mix well, and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9555c6ab62d52ee6dc4260','5e707ae4a04de0b99a30032c',4,'P3: Making a Paste','To make the horse gram paste for the Kollu Rasam, after the pressure from the cooker has been released, take off the lid and drain the water from the cooked horse gram using a strainer. Keep the horse gram extract aside to be further used while cooking the rasam. Next, in a blender jar, add 2 cloves of garlic, 1/2 teaspoon of cumin seeds, 1/4 teaspoon of black peppercorns and 1 tablespoon of cooked horse gram. Blend it to a coarse paste.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e955609acd25afedeb1f6e0','5e707ae4a04de0b99a30032c',5,'M1: Tempering','To make the Kollu Rasam, heat 1.5 teaspoons of cooking oil in a deep bottom pan on a medium flame for a minute. Add 1/2 teaspoon of mustard seeds, 1/4 teaspoon of fenugreek seeds, 1/4 teaspoon of cumin seeds, 7 curry leaves and 1 nos dry red chili. Saute and let it splutter on medium flame for a few seconds. Then, add the prepared horse gram paste and fry it on low flame for 1-2 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e955650ab62d52ee6dc4261','5e707ae4a04de0b99a30032c',6,'M2: Cooking','After frying the masala for Kollu Rasam, add 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes along with 1/2 cup of prepared tamarind extract. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, 1/4 teaspoon of jaggery, and 1/2 teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Cover it with a lid and allow it to simmer for 10 minutes. While the rasam is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e955679acd25afedeb1f6e1','5e707ae4a04de0b99a30032c',7,'M3: Cooking','After simmering the rasam, take off the lid and give it a stir. Next, add the prepared horse gram extract and stir it well. Boil the rasam on a medium flame for 2 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and garnish it with 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e95573dacd25afedeb1f6e2','5e7079a2378bf22ba423187a',1,'P1: Cooking the Dal','For Dal Rasam, wash 3/4 cup of toor dal well with water. Then, add it to a pressure cooker along with 1.5 cups of water and stir it well. Then, cover it with a lid and pressure cook the dal over high flame until one whistle. After that, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook it for another 8 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the dal is simmering, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e955769ab62d52ee6dc4262','5e7079a2378bf22ba423187a',2,'P2: Prepping the Ingredients','For dal rasam, soak 1 teaspoon of tamarind in 1/4 cup of water for 10 minutes. Nex, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Wash, peel and crush 2 nos cloves of garlic using the back of knife. Wash and finely chop 1 nos chopped green chili. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash 7 nos curry leaves. After soaking the tamarind mash it and mix it wel with water. Then, strain it to remove any solid residue.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9557b4ab62d52ee6dc4263','5e7079a2378bf22ba423187a',3,'M1: Tempering','To make Dal Rasam, heat a tablespoon of ghee in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, half a teaspoon of cumin seeds, 1/4 teaspoon of hing, 1 dry red chili and 7 nos curry leaves followed by 2 nos cloves of garlic. Saute it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Next, add a tablespoon of rasam powder and mix it well. Fry the masala over low flame for 1-2 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),
('5e9557faab62d52ee6dc4264','5e7079a2378bf22ba423187a',4,'M2: Cooking','Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes followed by 1/4 cup of prepared tamarind extract and 1 slit green chili. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder along with half a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Then, cover it with a lid and cook it over medium flame for 10 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":10,"flame":0}'),('5e95582aab62d52ee6dc4265','5e7079a2378bf22ba423187a',5,'M3: Cooking','After cooking the masala for Dal Rasam take off the lid and add the prepared toor dal followed by 3/4 cup of water and mix it well. Then, boil the rasam over high flame for 2 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and garnish it with a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":4}'),('5e9558c8ab62d52ee6dc4266','5d7b7ca939613718ed7d8532',1,'P1: Chop & prep the ingredients','To make Aloo Matar Sabzi, first, peel and chop 1 cup of potatoes in cubes. Peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1/2 cup of tomatoes. Wash and slit 1 green chili. Wash and roughly chop 1 tbsp of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e955919acd25afedeb1f6e3','5d7b7ca939613718ed7d8532',2,'M1: Temper the oil and saute onions with tomatoes','For Aloo Matar Sabzi, heat 1 tbsp of oil on low flame in a pressure cooker and then add 1/2 inch of cinnamon, 1 green cardamom, 1/2 tsp of Kasuri methi, and 1/4 tsp of cumin seeds. Let this splutter for a few seconds and then add 1/4 tsp turmeric powder, 1/2 tsp of red chili powder, and 1/4 tsp of coriander powder and saute this for 30 seconds. Next, add 1/4 cup of onions and 1/2 tsp of ginger-garlic paste, and saute for 2-3 mins. Once the onions are translucent, add 1/2 cup of tomatoes and saute for 2-3 mins.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e955967ab62d52ee6dc4267','5e70788691cde451322c5177',1,'P1: Cook the Dal','For Kalyana Rasam, soak 2 teaspoons of tamarind in 1/2 cup of water for 15 minutes. Next, to cook the dal, wash 1/2 cup of toor dal well with water. Put the washed dal into a pressure cooker with 1 cup of water and cover it with a lid. Pressure cook the dal on high flame till the first whistle. After the whistle, reduce it to low flame and continue to cook it for another 8 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the dal is cooking and tamarind is soaking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('5e955985ab62d52ee6dc4268','5d7b7ca939613718ed7d8532',3,'M2:  Add spices and pressure cook the vegetables.  Garnish & Serve','Next, once the tomatoes are soft, add 1 cup of chopped potatoes and 1/2 tsp of salt, mix well. Next, add 1/4 cup of green peas, 1/2 cup of water, and 1 slit green chili and mix well. Then, close the pressure cooker and cook on high flame for 1 whistle and then on low flame for 8 mins. Once this is complete, allow the pressure to release naturally before you open the cooker. After you open the lid, mash a few pieces of the potato and then add 1/4 tsp of garam masala and 1 tbsp of coriander leaves. Give it one final mix and the dish is ready to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9559a5acd25afedeb1f6e4','5e70788691cde451322c5177',2,'P2: Make Rasam Powder (optional)','To make the rasam powder for Kalyana Rasam, wash 18 nos curry leaves. Next, in a pan, add 2 teaspoons of toor dal, 2 teaspoons of coriander seeds, 1 teaspoon of cumin seeds, 1/2 teaspoon of black peppercorns, 1 dry red chili, and 6 nos curry leaves. Dry roast the spices on low flame without adding oil for 2-3 minutes, till it turns aromatic. Keep stirring the spices continuously while roasting to prevent it from burning. After roasting the spices, turn off the flame and allow it to cool down completely. Then, transfer it to a blender jar and blend it into a fine powder.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('5e9559dbacd25afedeb1f6e5','5e70788691cde451322c5177',3,'P3: Prepping Vegetables','For Kalyana Rasam, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Peel and slice 1 teaspoon of garlic. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Next, after soaking the tamarind, mash it and mix it well with the water and strain it using a strainer to remove the residue.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9559f8ab62d52ee6dc4269','5d7b875d39613718ed7d8534',1,'P1: Whisk the curd & prep the ingredients','For Makhana Raita, in a bowl, add 1 cup of curd and whisk it well using a whisk to avoid any lumps. Wash 8 nos curry leaves well with water.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e955a1ab8df13802c95a0a0','5e70788691cde451322c5177',4,'M1: Cooking','To make the Kalyana Rasam, in a saucepan, add 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes, 6 nos curry leaves and 1 teaspoon of sliced garlic. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, 1/4 teaspoon of jaggery, 1/2 teaspoon of salt, and 1/2 cup of tamarind extract along with 1.5 cups of water and give it a stir. Cover it with a lid and simmer it on a medium flame for 15 minutes. While the rasam is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e955a28ab62d52ee6dc426a','5d7b875d39613718ed7d8534',2,'P2: Fry the fox nuts','To roast the fox nuts for Makhana Raita, first, in a pan, add half a cup of fox nuts. Next, add a teaspoon of cooking oil and roast it on medium flame for 7-8 minutes, until it turns slightly golden and crisp. Keep stirring the fox nuts to prevent it from getting brown. After roasting it, turn off the flame and take it out on a plate and set it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e955a48b8df13802c95a0a1','5e70788691cde451322c5177',5,'M2: Cooking','After simmering the rasam, take off the lid and give it a stir. Next, add 1/2 cup of cooked toor dal and 1.5 cups of water. Mix it well and boil the rasam on medium-high flame for 2 minutes. Then, add the prepared Kalyana rasam powder and 1/4 teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Continue to boil the rasam on medium-high flame for another 2 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":4,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e955a63acd25afedeb1f6e6','5d7b875d39613718ed7d8534',3,'M1: Combine the ingredients & make the raita','To make the Makhana Raita, take the whisked curd in a large mixing bowl. Add 1/4 teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Next, add half a cup of roasted fox nuts and mix it well.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e955a6eb8df13802c95a0a2','5e70788691cde451322c5177',6,'M3: Cooking','To make the tempering for Kalyana Rasam, heat 1/2 teaspoon of ghee in a tadka pan on a medium flame for a minute. Add 1/2 teaspoon of mustard seeds, 1/4 teaspoon of hing, 1 dry red chili, and 6 nos curry leaves, roughly torn. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Then, turn off the flame and pour this tempering instantly over the prepared Kalyana Rasam. Garnish the rasam with 1/2 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and mix it well. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e955a90b8df13802c95a0a3','5d7b875d39613718ed7d8534',4,'M2: Prepare the tempering & add it to the raita.','To make the temper for Makhana Raita, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a pan on medium flame for a minute. Add 1/4 teaspoon of cumin seeds followed by 8 nos curry leaves and let it splutter for a few seconds. After that, turn off the flame and add the tempering to the prepared raita. Mix it well and sprinkle 1/4 teaspoon of red chili powder over it and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e955afcb8df13802c95a0a4','5d7c96fd39613718ed7d8537',1,'P1: Grate paneer & prep the ingredients','To make Besan Matar Chilla, first, grate 1/2 cup of paneer, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions, peel and roughly chop 1/2 an inch of ginger, and wash and roughly chop 1 green chilli and finely chop 1 green chilli.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e955b1dacd25afedeb1f6e7','5e70772091cde451322c5176',1,'P1: Prepping the Ingredients','For Tomato Rasam, first, soak 1 teaspoon of tamarind in 1/4 cup of water for 10 minutes Meanwhile, wash and roughly chop 1 cup of tomatoes. Peel and wash 2 cloves of garlic and crush it using the back of the knife. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves. Wash and 7 curry leaves. After soaking the tamarind, mash and mix it well with water and strain it to remove any solid residue.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e955b3eb8df13802c95a0a5','5d7c96fd39613718ed7d8537',2,'M1: Puree green peans annd combine with gram four to prepare the batter','To make Besan Matar Chilla, blend 1.5 cups of green peas, 1 green chilies, and 1/2 an inch of ginger into a smooth puree. Pour this into a large bowl, then add 1/2 tsp of salt and1/4 cup of gram flour, and mix well. Once all these ingredients are combined, the chilla batter is ready.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e955b44b8df13802c95a0a6','5e70772091cde451322c5176',2,'M1: Tempering','To make the Tomato Rasam, heat 1 tablespoon of cooking oil in a Kadai over medium flame for a minute. Add half a teaspoon of mustard seeds followed by half a teaspoon of cumin seeds and 1 nos dry red chili. Next, add 2 cloves of crushed garlic, 1/4 teaspoon of hing and 7 nos curry leaves. Saute it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e955b70ab62d52ee6dc426b','5e70772091cde451322c5176',3,'M2: Cooking','Next, add 1 cup of chopped tomatoes and mix it well. Add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder followed by half a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Next, add the prepared tamarind extract and mix it well. Then, cover it with a lid and simmer it for 5 minutes. While the tomatoes are simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e955b86ab62d52ee6dc426c','5d7c96fd39613718ed7d8537',3,'M2:  Pour the batter to the tawa followed by the toppings and make the chillas','Next, heat a tawa with 1/2 tbsp of oil and then pour 1/4 cup of batter spreading it in a circular motion to create the chilla shape. Then, sprinkle 1 tbsp of paneer, 1 tbsp of onions, 1 tbsp of tomatoes, 1/4 tsp of green chili, and 1/4 tsp of salt on top of the cooking chilla. Press these fresh ingredients into the chilla, then flip it, and cook for 2 mins. Flip it once more, then take it off the tawa and put it on a serving plate. Make the desired number of chillas with the remaining batter and enjoy.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e955be9ab62d52ee6dc426d','5e70772091cde451322c5176',4,'M3: Cooking','After simmering the tomatoes for Tomato Rasam, take off the lid and saute the tomatoes over medium flame for a minute. Next, add 1.5 tablespoons of rasam powder and mix it well. Add 2 cups of water and stir it well. Bring it to a boil over a high flame and continue to cook it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and add 1.5 tablespoons of chopped coriander leaves followed by half a teaspoon of ghee. Cover it with a lid and allow it to sit for 5 minutes. Then take it out into a bowl and garnish it with chopped coriander leaves and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e955c1bb8df13802c95a0a7','5d7c9f031710a053f6cd130b',1,'P1: Knead & prepare chapati dough','To make Masala Chapati, in a large bowl mix 1.5 cups of wheat flour along with 1/2 tsp of salt, 1 tsp of kasuri methi, 1/4 tsp of garam masala, 1/2 tsp of red chili powder, 1/4 tsp of cumin powder, and 1/4 tsp of black pepper powder. Mix the dry ingredients well and then gradually add 1/4 cups of water and knead the dough for 5 mins. Once the dough is smooth and soft, coat the dough in 1/2 tsp of oil, cover it and let it rest for 20 mins.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e955c57acd25afedeb1f6e8','5d7c9f031710a053f6cd130b',2,'M1: Divide the dough into dough balls and roll out the chapatis','For Masala Chapati, make small lemon sized balls from the rested dough. Place one of these balls on a rolling board and dust it with flour. Next, with a rolling pin begin rolling it gently into a disk shape and allow it to remain slightly thick. Repeat this process for the remaining dough balls and then move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e955c8fb8df13802c95a0a8','5d7c9f031710a053f6cd130b',3,'M2: Cook the chapati and serve','Next, heat a tawa on medium flame for 1 min then place the rolled dough on the tawa, let it cook on one side for 1 min, then flip it, and let it cook for another minute. Next, coat the chapati with 1/4 tsp of oil, flip it, and then coat the other side with 1/4 tsp of oil. Once the chapati has browned evenly on both sides transfer it to a serving plate. Repeat this process with the remaining chapatis and then serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e955cdbab62d52ee6dc426e','5e707561378bf22ba4231879',1,'P1: Cook the Dal','To make Mulangi Soppu Saaru, first, wash 1/2 cup of toor dal and cook it in a pressure cooker with 1 cup of water on high flame for 1 whistle and then on low flame for 8 mins. Once this is done, allow the pressure to release naturally before you open the cooker. While the dal cooks, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e955ceeb8df13802c95a0a9','5d7ca4711710a053f6cd130c',1,'P1: Knead & prepare the dough','To knead the dough for Plain Paratha, first, add 1.5 cups of whole wheat flour in a large mixing bowl. Add 1/4 teaspoon of salt along with half a teaspoon of cooking oil and mix it well. Next, gradually add about half a cup of water and knead it well into a smooth dough. Then, cover it with a cloth and allow it to rest for 20 minutes. While the dough is resting, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e955d2dab62d52ee6dc426f','5d7ca4711710a053f6cd130c',2,'M1: Divide the dough into dough balls & roll out the paratha','To make Plain Paratha, first, divide the prepared into small equal-size balls. Take a dough ball and dust it into some flour. Then, roll it into a small circle. Apply 1/4 teaspoon of cooking oil and dust some flour over it. Then, fold it into a semicircle and again apply a 1/4 teaspoon of cooking oil over it. After that, gently fold it into a triangle and roll it into a 7-inch triangular paratha. Make sure to roll out the edges thin.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e955d48acd25afedeb1f6e9','5e707561378bf22ba4231879',2,'P2: Prepping Ingredients','Next, wash and chop 3/4 cup of radish leaves. Wash and slice 1/2 cup of tomatoes. Peel and slice 1/4 cup of onions. Wash 12 curry leaves. Peel 1 clove of garlic.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e955d57b8df13802c95a0aa','5d7ca4711710a053f6cd130c',3,'M2: Cook the Paratha until browned and serve','To toast the Plain Paratha, place the rolled out paratha over a hot tawa and cook it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Then, gently flip it and apply half a teaspoon of cooking oil. Cook the paratha over medium-high flame for 2-3 minutes, until golden brown on both sides. After that, take it out onto a plate and serve. Make the rest of the parathas similarly.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e955db9b8df13802c95a0ab','5e707561378bf22ba4231879',3,'M1: Cooking','To make Mulangi Soppu Saaru, heat a pan on medium flame, then add 3/4 cup of radish leaves, 1/2 cup of tomatoes, 1/4 cup of onions, 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder, and 1/4 tsp of salt, and 1 cup of water, mix well. Close the pan with a lid and let this cook for 6 mins. While these vegetables are cooking, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e955deeab62d52ee6dc4270','5e707561378bf22ba4231879',4,'M2: Make Masala Powder','Next, heat 1/2 tsp of oil in another pan and then add 1/2 tsp of coriander seeds, 1/4 tsp of cumin seeds, 1/2 tsp of urad dal, 1/4 tsp of fenugreek seeds, 2 dry red chillies, and 6 curry leaves, saute this for 2-3 mins. Then, turn off the flame, allow the whole spices to cool down completely, then add them to a blending jar along with 1/4 cup of desiccated coconut, 2 tsp of tamarind, 1 clove of garlic, and 1/4 cup of water, and blend this into a smooth masala paste.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e955e36acd25afedeb1f6eb','5e707561378bf22ba4231879',5,'M3: Making a Tadka','Next, add the prepared masala paste to the cooking vegetables along with 1/4 tsp of jaggery and 1/4 tsp of salt, mix well. Cook this for 5 mins and then add 1/2 cup of cooked toor dal, mix well and boil for 2 mins. While the saaru is boiling, in a tadka pan heat 1 tsp of oil, then add 1/2 tsp of mustard seeds, 1 dry red chilli, and 6 curry leaves, saute this for a few seconds, and then pour it over the boiling saaru. Give the dish a quick stir and it is ready to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":7,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e955ed2ab62d52ee6dc4271','5e7072a8378bf22ba4231878',1,'P1: Prepping Ingredients','To make Coorgi Gawti Chicken, peel and finely slice 1/2 cup of onions. Wash and roughly chop 4 green chillies and 1/4 cup of coriander leaves. Wash 8 curry leaves. Soak 1 tsp of tamarind in 3 tbsp of hot water for 4 mins and then mash the two together to make a tamarind pulp.','prep_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e955f4ab8df13802c95a0ac','5e7072a8378bf22ba4231878',2,'M1: Making a Masala Paste','To make Coorgi Gawti Chicken, heat 1 tbsp of ghee in a Kadai and then add 1 inch of cinnamon, 3 green cardamoms, 1 star anise, 3 cloves, 1/2 tsp of black peppercorns, 1 tsp of mustard seeds, 1 tsp of cumin seeds, and 4 chopped green chillies, saute on high flame for 1 min. Next, add 1/2 cup of onion and 1/2 tbsp of coriander powder, saute on high flame for 2 mins. Then, add 1/4 cup of coriander leaves and saute on high flame for 3 mins. Next, allow this to cool completely and then blend along with 1/2 tsp of salt and 1/4 cup of water into a smooth paste.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('5e956093b8df13802c95a0ad','5e7072a8378bf22ba4231878',3,'M2: Cooking','Next, in the same Kadai heat 1 tbsp of ghee, then add 8 curry leaves and 2 tsp of ginger-garlic paste, saute for 1 min. Then, add 500 g of chicken and fry it for 3 mins on medium flame. Next, add the prepared masala paste, mix well, then cover the Kadai and cook for 10-15 mins on medium flame.  After this, add the prepared tamarind pulp and 1 tbsp of coriander leaves, cover the Kadai and cook for another 2 mins. Once this is done, the dish is ready to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":17,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e956100ab62d52ee6dc4272','5e706fae378bf22ba4231877',1,'P1: Prepping the Ingredients','To make Meen Muringakka Curry, clean 500 g of sardine. Wash and slice 1/2 cup of tomatoes. Wash and slit 2 green chillies. Wash and chop 2 drumsticks into 2-inch pieces. Peel 6 shallots, 1 inch of ginger, and 4 cloves of garlic. Wash 8 curry leaves. Soak 1 tbsp of tamarind in 1/4 cup of hot water for 2 mins and then mash the two together to make a tamarind pulp.','prep_method','{"active_time":11,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e956138acd25afedeb1f6ed','5e706fae378bf22ba4231877',2,'M1: Cooking','For Meen Munringakka Curry, heat a Kadai and then add 500 g of sardines, 1/2 cup of sliced tomatoes, 2 slit green chillies, 2 chopped drumsticks, the prepared tamarind extract, 1/2 tsp of turmeric powder, 1/2 tsp of red chilli powder, and 1 tsp of salt, cover the Kadai and cook the fish for 10 mins.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e95615cab62d52ee6dc4273','5e706fae378bf22ba4231877',3,'M2: Cooking','Next, in a blending jar add 1/2 cup of fresh coconut, 1.5 tsp of red chilli powder, 6 shallots, 4 cloves of garlic, 1 inch of ginger, and 3 tbsp of water, blend into a smooth paste. Add the prepared masala paste to the Kadai, reduce the flame to low, and then add 8 curry leaves. Mix the curry well and let it cook for another 4-5 mins stirring occasionally. Then, add 1 tsp of coconut oil over the curry, give it a quick stir, and then serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e9561d8ab62d52ee6dc4274','5e706d19a04de0b99a30032b',1,'P1: Prepping Ingredients','For Puli Kolambu, peel and finely chop 3/4 cup of shallots. Wash 8 curry leaves. Wash and slit 5 small eggplants with an X. Peel and roughly chop 20 cloves of garlic. Soak 1 tbsp of tamarind in 1/4 cup of hot water for 4 mins and then mash the two together to make a tamarind pulp. Blend 1/2 cup of fresh coconut with 2 tbsp of water to make a coconut paste.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e95625dab62d52ee6dc4275','5e706d19a04de0b99a30032b',2,'M1: Cooking','To make Puli Kolambu, heat 2 tbsp of sesame oil in a pan and then add 3/4 tsp of mustard seeds, 3/4 tsp of fennel seeds, 1/4 tsp of fenugreek seeds, 8 curry leaves, 3/4 cup of shallots, and 20 cloves of garlic, saute for 3-4 mins. Once the onions are translucent, add 5 slit brinjals, 1/2 tsp of turmeric powder, 1 tbsp of red chilli powder, and 1.5 tbsp of coriander powder, saute for 1 min. Next, add the prepared tamarind extract and 1/2 tsp of salt, mix well, cover the pan and cook for 10 mins on medium flame.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e95628eab62d52ee6dc4276','5e706d19a04de0b99a30032b',3,'M2: Cooking','Next, add the prepared coconut paste, 1 cup of water, and 1/2 tsp of red chilli powder, mix well. Cover the pan once more and cook for 10-15 mins on medium flame. After this add 3/4 tsp of jaggery, mix well, then drizzle 1/2 tbsp of sesame oil, turn off the flame, and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e956361ab62d52ee6dc4277','5e706af891cde451322c5175',1,'P1: Prepping Ingredients','To make Kara Kuzhambu, first, Soak 1 tbsp of tamarind in 1/4 cup of hot water for 4 mins and then mash the two together to make a tamarind pulp. Peel 1.25 cups of shallots. Wash and roughly chop 1/2 cup of tomatoes. Wash 8 curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e956396b8df13802c95a0ae','5e706af891cde451322c5175',2,'M1: Making the Masala Paste','For Kara Kazhambu, heat 1 tsp of oil in a pan and then1 tbsp of coriander leaves, 1 tbsp of chana dal, 4 dry red chillies, 1/4 tsp of cumin seeds, 1/2 tsp of fennel seeds, 6 shallots, and 1/4 cup of tomatoes,  saute this for 4 mins. Next, add 5.5 tbsp of desiccated coconut and saute for 2 mins. Allow the mixture to cool down completely, then blend it into a smooth masala paste.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e9563ccacd25afedeb1f6ee','5e706af891cde451322c5175',3,'M2: Cooking','Next, heat 1 tsp of sesame oil in a pan and then roast 1 tbsp of turkey berries for 1 min. Then take them off the flame and set aside. Next, heat 2 tsp of sesame oil in the same pan and then add 1 tsp of mustard seeds, 1 tsp f chana dal, 2 dry red chillies, and 8 curry leaves, let this splutter for a few seconds. Then, add 15 shallots, saute them for 2 mins and then add 1/4 cup of tomatoes, saute for another 2 mins. Once the tomatoes are soft, add the prepared tamarind extract and 1/2 tsp of salt, let this cook for 5 mins. Next, add the prepared masala paste, adjust the consistency of the gravy, then take it off the flame, and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e9564a9acd25afedeb1f6ef','5e70686ba04de0b99a30032a',1,'P1: Cook the Dal','For Spinach Moong Dal, wash 3/4 cup of moong dal well with water. Next, add the rinsed moong dal in a pressure cooker along with 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder and half a teaspoon of cooking oil. Add 1.5 cups of water and stir it well. Cover it with a lid and pressure cook the dal over a high flame until one whistle. After that, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook it for another 8 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the dal is simmering, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e9564ebb8df13802c95a0af','5e70686ba04de0b99a30032a',2,'P2: Making a Masala Paste','For Spinach Moong Dal, wash and finely chop 1 cup of spinach leaves. Wash, peel and crush 2 cloves of garlic using the back of a knife. Next, to make the masala paste, add 1/4 cup desiccated coconut to a blender jar. Next, add half a teaspoon of cumin seeds, 1/4 teaspoon of black peppercorns and 2 nos dry red chillies along with 1/4 cup of water and blend it well into a smooth paste.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e956541ab62d52ee6dc4278','5e70686ba04de0b99a30032a',3,'M1: Cooking','To make Spinach Moong Dal, add 1 cup of chopped spinach leaves in a Kadai. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder followed by half a teaspoon of salt and 2 cloves of crushed garlic. Add 1/4 cup of water and mix it well. Then, cover it with a lid and cook it over medium flame for 5 minutes. While it is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e95657dacd25afedeb1f6f0','5e70686ba04de0b99a30032a',4,'M2: Cooking','After simmering the spinach leaves for spinach moong dal, take off the lid and stir it well. Then, add the prepared coconut paste and mix it well. Add about 1/4 cup of water to adjust the consistency and allow it to boil over medium-high flame for 3 minutes while stirring in between. After that, add the prepared moong dal and mix it well. Then, simmer the dal for 5 minutes. After that turn off the flame and set it aside. While the dal is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":3,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('5e9565adab62d52ee6dc4279','5e70686ba04de0b99a30032a',5,'M3: Making a Tadka','To make the tempering for Spinach Moong Dal, heat a teaspoon of coconut oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, half a teaspoon of urad dal and 1/4 teaspoon of hing. Add 1 dry red chili and saute it over low flame for a minute. Then, turn off the flame and pour the tempering to the prepared dal. Mix it well and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e956644b8df13802c95a0b0','5e7062bd91cde451322c5172',1,'P1: Prepping Ingredients','For Vendekkai Gojju, soak 1 tsp of tamarind in 1/4 cup of water for 10 minutes. Wash 1 cup of the lady''s fingers well with water and then spread them over a kitchen towel and allow it to dry completely. Make sure there is no moisture left in the lady''s fingers, or it will stick together while cooking. Grate 3/4 cup of fresh coconut using a grater. After soaking the tamarind, mash it and mix it well with water and then strain it to remove any extra residue.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e95669aacd25afedeb1f6f1','5e7062bd91cde451322c5172',2,'P2: Make a Masala Paste','Prepare the masala paste for Vendekkai Gojju, in a blender jar, add 4 dry red chillies, 1 tsp of coriander seeds, 1 teaspoon of raw rice, 1 teaspoon of mustard seeds, 1 teaspoon of roasted gram, 1/4 teaspoon of hing, and 3/4 cup of grated coconut. Next, add 1 cup of water and blend it well into a smooth paste.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9566ceb8df13802c95a0b1','5e7062bd91cde451322c5172',3,'M1: Cooking','To make Vendekkai Gojju, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a Kadai for a minute over medium flame. Next, add half a teaspoon of mustard seeds and let it splutter for a few seconds. Then add 2 nos red chillies along with 8 nos curry leaves and saute it for a minute. Next, add 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder followed by 1 cup of sliced lady''s fingers saute it for 4-5minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e95670cacd25afedeb1f6f2','5e7062bd91cde451322c5172',4,'M2: Cooking','As the lady''s fingers turn slightly dark in color, add the 1/4 cup of prepared tamarind extract and mix it well. Then, saute and cook it over medium flame for 2 mins. Next, add 1/4 tsp of salt and mix it well. After that, add the prepared paste followed by 1/2 a cup of water and 1 teaspoon of jaggery and mix it well. Then, cook the curry for 5 minutes over medium flame. Then, turn off the flame and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9567d2ab62d52ee6dc427a','5e705f27a04de0b99a300328',1,'P1: Prepping Ingredients','For Aviyal, wash and peel 1 medium-sized potato and cut it into rectangular sticks. Wash and peel 1 raw banana and cut it into rectangular sticks. Wash, peel and cut 1/4 cup of carrot into rectangular sticks. Wash and cut 1/4 cup of beans into 3 inch long pieces. Wash and cut 1/4 cup of drumstick into 3 inch long pieces. Grate 1/4 cup of fresh coconut. Wash 10 nos curry leaves. Wash 1 nos green chili. Next, in a bowl, add 1/4 cup of curd and whisk it well using a whisk.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9567f5b8df13802c95a0b2','5e705f27a04de0b99a300328',2,'P2: Make a Coconut Paste','To make the coconut paste for Aviyal, in a blender jar, add 1/4 cup of fresh coconut, 1/2 teaspoon of cumin seeds, and 1 nos green chili. Next, blend it to a coarse paste.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e956837ab62d52ee6dc427b','5e705f27a04de0b99a300328',3,'M1: Cooking','To make the Aviyal, in a deep bottom pan, add 1/4 cup of chopped banana sticks, 1/4 cup of chopped potato sticks, 1/4 cup of chopped beans, 1/4 cup of chopped carrot sticks, and 1/4 cup of chopped drumsticks along with 1 cup of water. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, 1/2 teaspoon of red chili powder, and 1/2 teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Cover it with a lid and simmer the vegetables for 10-12 minutes. While the vegetables are simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e95685fb8df13802c95a0b3','5e705f27a04de0b99a300328',4,'M2: Cooking','After simmering the vegetables for Aviyal, take off the lid and add the prepared coconut paste and mix it well. Then, cover it with a lid and continue to simmer the vegetables for another 5 minutes. While the vegetables are simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('5e95689bb8df13802c95a0b4','5e705f27a04de0b99a300328',5,'M3: Cooking','After simmering the vegetables for Aviyal, take off the lid and stir the vegetables on a medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Next, in a bowl, pour 1/4 cup of whisked curd and add a ladle full of prepared vegetable stock to it and mix it well. Turn off the flame and add the curd mixture to the vegetables and mix it well. Keep the flame off while mixing the curd as it might split. After mixing the curd well with the curry, turn on the flame and cook the Aviyal on medium-low flame for 5-6 minutes. While the Aviyal is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e9568d0ab62d52ee6dc427c','5e705f27a04de0b99a300328',6,'M4: Cooking','After simmering the Aviyal, turn off the flame and take it out in a serving bowl. Next, to make the tempering, heat 1 tablespoon of coconut oil in a pan on a medium flame for a minute. Add 1/2 teaspoon of mustard seeds, 1 nos dry red chili, and 10 nos curry leaves. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Then, turn off the flame and pour this tempering instantly over the prepared Aviyal. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e956ddab8df13802c95a0b5','5e705b7ea04de0b99a300327',1,'M1: Cooking','To make Ragi Balls, add 2 cups of water in a pan and heat it over medium flame. Add 1/4 teaspoon of salt followed by a teaspoon of ghee and mix it well. Then, bring it to a boil over high flame. Meanwhile, add 2 tablespoons of ragi flour in a bowl. Add 1/4 cup of water and mix it well to prepare the slurry.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e956e02b8df13802c95a0b6','5e705b7ea04de0b99a300327',2,'M2: Cooking','As the water comes to a boil, add the prepared ragi flour slurry and mix it well. Then bring it to a boil while stirring in between. Then, add 1 cup of ragi flour and let it boil for a minute. After that, mix it well and keep stirring it continuously over a low flame until it comes together and the dough separates the pan. Then, add a teaspoon of ghee over the dough and cover it with a lid. Allow it to simmer for a minute.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e956e27b8df13802c95a0b7','5e705b7ea04de0b99a300327',3,'M3: Cooking','Next, grease a plate with half a teaspoon of ghee. After simmering the ragi dough, turn off the flame and divide it into halves. Next, place one half of the dough to the greased plate and carefully shape it into a round ball while the dough is still hot. Don''t let the dough sit, as it will become stiff after resting and shaping the balls will be difficult. Prepare the other ragi ball similarly and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e957ff5b8df13802c95a0b8','5d7cab6a09e1dd5a7f4238c4',1,'P1: Chop & prep the ingredients','For Masoor Dal, wash 3/4 cup of pink masoor dal well with water and set it aside. Peel, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Wash and slit 1 nos green chili. Wash 8 nos curry leaves. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e958037b8df13802c95a0b9','5d7cab6a09e1dd5a7f4238c4',2,'M1: Temper the ghee and saute onions with tomatoes','To make Masoor Dal, heat 1 tablespoon of ghee in a pressure cooker over medium flame for a minute. Add 1 nos bay leaf followed by 1/4 cup of chopped onions and fry it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes, until it turns slightly translucent. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of ginger-garlic paste along with 1 nos slit green chili and fry it with the onions for 1-2 minutes. Then, add 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes and mix it well. Saute and cook the tomatoes over medium-low flame for 4-5 minutes until it turns tender.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e95806bb8df13802c95a0ba','5d7cab6a09e1dd5a7f4238c4',3,'M2: Pressure cook the dal with masala','As the tomatoes turn tender, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder followed by half a teaspoon of Kashmiri red chili powder and half a teaspoon of salt. Mix it well and fry the masala over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. After that, add 3/4 cup of masoor dal along with 2 cups of water and mix it well. Then, cover it with a lid and pressure cook the dal over high flame until one whistle. Then, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook it for another 8 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the dal is cooking, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e95809fab62d52ee6dc427d','5d7cab6a09e1dd5a7f4238c4',4,'M3: Prepare the tempering and garnish the dal','To make Masoor Dal, after the pressure from the cooker is released, remove the lid and give it a stir. Add some water, if required to adjust the consistency of the dal and set it aside. To make the tempering for Masoor dal, heat 2 teaspoons of ghee in a small tempering pan over medium flame for a minute. Add 1/4 teaspoon of mustard seeds, 1/4 teaspoon of cumin seeds and 1/4 teaspoon of hing followed by 1/4 teaspoon of Kashmiri red chili powder and 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala. Mix it well and allow it to splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 8 nos curry leaves along with 1 nos dry red chili. Saute it over medium flame for a minute. Then, turn off the flame and the tempering to the prepared masoor dal. Garnish it with a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves. Mix it well and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e958128acd25afedeb1f6f3','5d7cad901710a053f6cd130e',1,'P1: Chop & prep the ingredients','For Green Chutney, rinse 1 cup of coriander leaves well with water and remove the root ends. Wash and separate 1/4 cup of mint leaves. Peel and wash 3 cloves of garlic. Wash, and peel a 1-inch piece of ginger. Wash and slit 3 nos green chilies. Wash and cut a lemon into halves. Then, squeeze 1 tablespoon lime juice.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e958181acd25afedeb1f6f4','5d7cad901710a053f6cd130e',2,'M1: Blend the ingredients to prepare the chutney. Add a dash of lime juice & serve','To make the Green Chutney, in a blender jar, add 1 cup of coriander leaves and 1/4 cup of mint leaves. Next, add 3 cloves of garlic, a 1-inch piece of ginger and 3 nos slit green chilies followed by 2 tablespoons of roasted gram dal and half a teaspoon of cumin powder. Next, add half a teaspoon of chat masala, half a teaspoon of sugar and half a teaspoon of salt along with 1/4 teaspoon of hing and 3 tablespoons of water. Blend it well into a smooth chutney. Take it out into a bowl and add a tablespoon of lime juice. Mix it well and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e958218ab62d52ee6dc427e','5d7cb01a09e1dd5a7f4238c7',1,'P1: Rinse and dry the ladies fingers','Wash and properly dry the okra. Spread them on a kitchen towel to absorb excess water. Let this rest for 15 mins.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e958251ab62d52ee6dc427f','5d7cb01a09e1dd5a7f4238c7',2,'P2: Prepare the spice mix to stuff the ladies fingers','In a bowl, combine coriander powder, turmeric powder, Kashmiri red chili powder, cumin powder, dry mango powder, garam masala, salt, and mustard oil.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e958288ab62d52ee6dc4280','5d7cb01a09e1dd5a7f4238c7',3,'P3: Slit & stuff the ladies fingers','Slit the okra lengthwise and stuff them with the masala mixture that was prepared earlier.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9582ecab62d52ee6dc4281','5d7cb01a09e1dd5a7f4238c7',4,'M1: Stir fry the ladies fingers','Heat oil in a pan, then add the okra and let it cook for 10-12 mins. Once sightly golden and cooked on all sides turn off the heat and squeeze lime juice on top. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e958373b8df13802c95a0bb','5d7cb10739613718ed7d853b',1,'P1: Rinse the lentil and prep the ingredients','For Toor dal, wash 1 cup of toor dal well with water. Wash, peel and cut 1/4 cup of raw mango into wedges. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9583a0b8df13802c95a0bc','5d7cb10739613718ed7d853b',2,'M1: Pressure cook the dal','To make the Toor Dal, add 1 cup of rinsed toor dal to a pressure cooker along with half a teaspoon of salt and half a teaspoon of turmeric powder. Add 1/4 cup of chopped raw mango wedges followed by 2 cups of water. Mix it well and cover it with a lid. Pressure cook the dal over high flame till one whistle. Then, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook it for another 8 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and set the cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the dal is cooking, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e9583ecacd25afedeb1f6f5','5d7cb10739613718ed7d853b',3,'M2: Prepare the tempering & add it to the dal. Garnish & serve','For Toor Dal, after the pressure from the cooker is released, take off the lid and gently mash it. Next, to prepare the tempering for the dal, heat a tablespoon of ghee in a small pan over medium flame for a minute. Temper it with 1/4 teaspoon of mustard seeds, half a teaspoon of cumin seeds and 1/4 teaspoon of hing. Add 1 nos dry red chili and saute it for a minute. Then, turn off the flame and mix it well. Add this tempering instantly to the prepared dal. Garnish it with 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e958452b8df13802c95a0bd','5d7d2eb739613718ed7d853d',1,'P1: Chop & prep the ingredients','To make Palak Chicken, peel and finely chop 3/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely slice 2 green chilies. Wash and roughly chop 1/2 cup of tomatoes into quarters. Clean 400 g of chicken. Wash and finely chop 2 cups of spinach leaves. Wash and roughly chop 1 tbsp of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e95849bab62d52ee6dc4282','5d7d2eb739613718ed7d853d',2,'M1: Cook the masala','For Palak Chicken, in a kadai heat 1 tbsp of ghee and then add 2 sliced green chilies, 3/4 cup of chopped onions, and 1/2 tsp of salt. Saute this for 2-3 mins until the onions become golden brown. Next, add 2 tsp of ginger-garlic paste, 1 tsp red chili powder, 1/2 tsp of coriander powder, 1/2 tsp of turmeric powder, 1/2 tsp of cumin powder, and mix well. Saute this for 2 mins and cook the masala.','cook_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e958503acd25afedeb1f6f6','5d7d322d39613718ed7d853e',1,'P1: Chop & prep the ingredients','To make Missi Roti, wash and finely chop 1 tbsp of coriander leaves and 1 green chili. Next, peel and finely chop 1/4 C of onions.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e958e46acd25afedeb1f6f7','5e6f5903378bf22ba4231872',1,'P1: Prepping Ingredients','For Ragi Roti, peel, wash and finely chop half a cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1 nos green chili. Wash, peel and finely chop a 1-inch piece of ginger. Grate 1 teaspoon of coconut using a grater. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash and roughly chop 8 nos curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e958ea4b8df13802c95a0be','5d7d322d39613718ed7d853e',2,'P2: Knead & prepare the dough','Next, in a large mixing bowl combine 1 cup of wheat flour, 1/2 cup of gram flour, 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder, 1/4 tsp of black pepper, 1/2 tsp of carom seeds, 1/2 tsp of dry mango powder, 1/4 tsp of asafoetida, 1/2 tsp of Kasuri methi, 1/2 tsp of ginger-garlic paste, 1 finely chopped green chili, 1/4 cup of finely chopped onions, 1 tbsp of finely chopped coriander leaves, 1/2 tsp of salt, and mix this well. Next, gradually add 1/4 C of water to this dry mixture. Knead the dough for 5 mins until all the ingredients are combined. Once the dough is smooth and soft, add 1/2 tsp of cooking oil and knead the dough for another minute.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e958ea6b8df13802c95a0bf','5e6f5903378bf22ba4231872',2,'P2: Making the Dough','To knead the dough for Ragi Flour, first, heat half a cup of water in a saucepan over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Then pour it into a cup and set it aside. Next, in a mixing bowl, add half a cup of chopped onions followed by a 1-inch piece of chopped ginger and 1 chopped green chili. Next, add 8 nos chopped curry leaves, 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves, and 1/4 teaspoon of salt along with 1 teaspoon of cumin seeds. Mix it well. Next, add 1 cup of ragi flour and mix it well. Then, gradually add half a cup of hot water and knead it well into a smooth dough.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('5e958ef6acd25afedeb1f6f8','5e6f5903378bf22ba4231872',3,'M1: Rolling the Dough','To roll the Ragi Roti, first, divide the prepared dough into small equal-sized dough balls. Next, take a small sheet of aluminum foil and grease it well with 1/4 teaspoon of cooking oil. Then, carefully place the dough ball over it and roll it into a thin roti round while patting it gently in a circular motion. Apply some water on fingers in between, while rolling it, to avoid it from sticking. Make a small hole in the center of the rolled roti as shown.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e958f27b8df13802c95a0c0','5e6f5903378bf22ba4231872',4,'M2: Making the Roti','To make the Ragi Roti, apply half a teaspoon of cooking oil over a Tawa and heat it over medium flame for a minute. Then, carefully place the rolled out ragi roti onto the hot Tawa and cook it over low flame for 1-2 minutes. Gently remove the aluminum foil and apply half a teaspoon of cooking oil over it. Flip the roti and continue to cook it on low flame for 2-3 minutes, until it is evenly cooked on both sides. Then, take it out onto a plate and serve. Make the rest of the rotis similarly.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e959026acd25afedeb1f6f9','5e6f5437a04de0b99a300326',1,'P1: Prepping Ingredients','For Gojju Avlakkai, soak 2 teaspoons of tamarind in 1.5 tablespoons of water for 10 minutes. Wash and slit 1 nos green chili lengthwise. Wash 5 nos curry leaves. Grate 1/4 cup of fresh coconut using a grater. Next, add 3/4 cups of poha to a blender jar and blend it to a coarse powder. After soaking the tamarind, mix it well with water.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e95903bacd25afedeb1f6fa','5d7d322d39613718ed7d853e',3,'M1: Divide the dough into dough balls and roll out the rotis','For Missi Roti, make lemon sized balls from the dough. Place one of these balls on the rolling board and dust it with some flour. Then, with a rolling pin begin gently rolling out the dough ball into a disk shape allowing it to remain slightly thick. Repeat this process for the remaining dough balls and then move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e95905fab62d52ee6dc4283','5e6f5437a04de0b99a300326',2,'P2: Make a Batter','To make the poha batter for Gojju Avlakkai, in a large mixing bowl, add 1.5 tablespoons of tamarind pulp, 2 teaspoons of jaggery, 2 teaspoons of puliyogare powder, and 1 teaspoon of salt along with 1/2 cup of water. Mix it well. Next, add the prepared poha powder and mix it well. Set it aside and let it rest for 10 minutes. While the batter is resting, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e95907ab8df13802c95a0c1','5d7d322d39613718ed7d853e',4,'M2: Cook the rolled out missi rotis','Next, heat a tawa for 1 min and then place the rolled dough on it. Let it cook on one side for 1 min and then flip the roti and let it cook for another minute. Then drizzle the roti with 1/2 tsp of oil on one side and let it cook for 1 min. Next, flip the roti again, drizzle 1/2 tsp of oil on the other side, and let it cook for 1 min. Once both sides are roasted evenly and have a nice brown color, take the roti off the tawa. Repeat this procedure with the remaining rotis and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e95909cb8df13802c95a0c2','5e6f5437a04de0b99a300326',3,'M1: Tempering','To make the Gojju Avlakkai, after resting the poha batter, the poha will absorb the water and form a stiff lump. Mix it well and separate it into fine crumbles using a spoon. Next, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a pan on a medium flame for a minute. Add 1/2 teaspoon of mustard seeds, 1/2 teaspoon of urad dal, 1/2 teaspoon of chana dal, 1 nos dry chili, 1 slit green chili, and 5 nos curry leaves. Saute it on medium-high flame for a minute.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9590c8b8df13802c95a0c3','5e6f5437a04de0b99a300326',4,'M2: Cooking','Next, add the prepared poha mixture along with 1/4 cup of grated coconut. Mix it well and cover it with a lid. Reduce it to low flame and simmer it for 5 minutes. After simmering it, take off the lid and saute it on medium-high flame for a minute. Garnish with 1 teaspoon of grated coconut and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('5e9590fdab62d52ee6dc4284','5d7d341309e1dd5a7f4238ca',1,'P1: Prepare the batter for chillas','To prepare the batter for Besan Chilla, in a mixing bowl, add 1/2 cup of gram flour. Add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, and 1/4 teaspoon of carom seeds. Next, season it with 1/4 teaspoon of salt and add 1/4 cup of water. Mix it well and whisk it until the batter is smooth and lump-free. Set it aside and allow it to rest for 30 minutes. While the chilla batter is resting, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":30,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e959136ab62d52ee6dc4285','5d7d341309e1dd5a7f4238ca',2,'P2: Chop & prep the ingredients','For Besan Chilla, peel, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Wash, peel and finely chop a 1/4-inch piece of ginger. Wash and finely chop 1 nos green chili. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e959179ab62d52ee6dc4286','5d7d341309e1dd5a7f4238ca',3,'P3: Add the chopped ingredients to prepare the batter','To make the batter for Besan Chilla, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions to the prepared gram flour batter. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes, 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and a 1/4-inch piece of chopped ginger followed by 1 nos chopped green chili. Mix it well and add a little water if required, to adjust the consistency of the batter. The batter should be of flowing consistency.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9591aeab62d52ee6dc4287','5e6f3b35a04de0b99a300324',1,'P1: Prepping Ingredients','For Red Garlic Chutney, first, add half a cup of water in a saucepan and heat it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. As it comes to a boil, turn off the flame and take it out into a cup. Next, in a bowl, add 5 Kashmiri dry red chilies and soak it in half a cup of hot water for 15 minutes. Meanwhile, peel and wash 5 cloves of garlic. Squeeze 1 tablespoon of lemon juice using a squeezer. Wash and peel a half-inch piece of ginger. While the red chilies are soaking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9591cdab62d52ee6dc4288','5e6f3b35a04de0b99a300324',2,'M1: Making the Chutney','To make the Red Garlic Chutney, add the soaked Kashmiri red chilies to a blender jar followed by 5 cloves of garlic and a half-inch piece of ginger. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of cumin powder, 1 teaspoon of chat masala, 1/4 a teaspoon of sugar and 1/4  teaspoon of salt. Add 1/4 cup of water and blend it well into a smooth chutney. Take it out into a bowl and add a tablespoon of lemon juice into it. Mix it well and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9591dcab62d52ee6dc4289','5d7d341309e1dd5a7f4238ca',4,'M1: Pour & spread the batter onto the tawa & cook it to make chillas','To make the Besan Chilla, pour a ladle full of the prepared batter over the hot tawa and gently spread it into a slightly thick 5-inch circle. As the small bubbles start to appear, add a teaspoon of cooking oil over it and cook it over medium-low flame for 3-4 minutes, until it turns golden and crisp. Next, carefully flip it and cook the other side for a minute. Then, gently fold it into a triangle and take it out onto a plate and serve. Make the rest of the besan chillas from the batter similarly.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e959272ab62d52ee6dc428a','5d7d36331710a053f6cd130f',1,'P1: Chop & prep the ingredients','Soak 2 tsp tamarind in 1 cup of warm water. Peel and cut potatoes into wedges, chop beans, peel and dice pumpkin, peel and cut carrots into 3 inch long verticals, cut drumsticks, peel and chop ginger, green chilies, coriander leaves, and wash curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e959277b8df13802c95a0c4','5e6f3a1da04de0b99a300322',1,'P1: Prepping Ingredients','For Onion Chutney, peel, wash and finely chop half a cup of onions. Wash 8 nos curry leaves well with water.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9592bfacd25afedeb1f6fb','5e6f3a1da04de0b99a300322',2,'M1: Cooking','To make Onion Chutney, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add 1 teaspoon of urad dal, 1 teaspoon of chana dal, and 3 nos dry red chilies. Saute and roast it on low flame for 1-2 minutes. Next, add half a cup of chopped onions. Stir and fry the onions over medium-high flame for 4-5 minutes until it turns golden brown. After frying the onions, turn off the flame and allow the mixture to cool down completely. While the onion mixture is cooling down, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9592dcab62d52ee6dc428b','5d7d36331710a053f6cd130f',2,'M1: Temper the oil with the spices and cook the gram flour','Heat cooking oil in a pan, then fry cumin seeds, fenugreek seeds, hing, ginger, green chili, and curry leaves. Next, add gram flour and stir continuously on low flame for 8 mins, until the flour and oil have combined.','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e9592e5acd25afedeb1f6fd','5e6f3a1da04de0b99a300322',3,'M2: Blending','To make the Onion Chutney, after the prepared onion mixture cools down, transfer it to a blender jar. Add a teaspoon of tamarind followed by half a teaspoon of jaggery and half a teaspoon of salt. Add 1/4 cup of water and blend it well into a smooth chutney. Then, take it out into a bowl and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e959303acd25afedeb1f6fe','5e6f3a1da04de0b99a300322',4,'M3: Tempering','To make the tempering for Onion Chutney, heat a teaspoon of cooking oil in a small tempering pan over medium flame for a minute. Add a teaspoon of mustard seeds followed by a teaspoon of urad dal and 1/4 teaspoon of hing. Next, add 1 nos dry red chili along with 8 nos curry leaves. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Then, turn off the flame and add the tempering instantly to the prepared onion chutney. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e95930ab8df13802c95a0c5','5d7d36331710a053f6cd130f',3,'M2: Add vegetables and simmer the kadhi','Once combined gradually add 2 cups of hot water to make a thick paste. Once all lumps are removed add turmeric, red chili powder, and salt. Next, add potatoes, beans, carrot, pumpkin, drumsticks and mix it well. Cover the pan with a lid and let it simmer for 8-10 mins on low flame.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e95934eacd25afedeb1f6ff','5d7d36331710a053f6cd130f',4,'M3: Add tamarind extract and simmer the kadhi. Garnish & serve','Next, mash and mix the tamarind and water. Add this to the Kadhi followed by jaggery and mix it well. Cook the kadhi for another 4-5 mins. Once the gravy is thick turn off the flame and garnish with coriander leaves. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9593e1b8df13802c95a0c6','5e6f369c91cde451322c5169',1,'P1: Prepping Ingredients','For Coriander Chutney, wash 3/4 cup of coriander leaves and remove the root ends. Wash, peel and roughly chop a 1/2-inch piece of ginger. Wash and roughly chop 2 green chilies. Grate 1/4 cup of fresh coconut using a grater. Peel and wash 3 cloves of garlic. Wash 7 curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9593f9ab62d52ee6dc428c','5d7d3c2d39613718ed7d8540',1,'P1: Chop & prep the vegetables','For Kachumbar Salad, wash and dice 1/2 cup of cucumber. Wash and chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Wash, peel and dice 1/4 cup of carrots. Peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of cabbage. Wash and finely chop 1 nos green chili. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of mint leaves. Squeeze 1 tablespoon of lime juice. Crush 1 teaspoon of black peppercorns using a pepper grinder.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e959431ab62d52ee6dc428d','5d7d3c2d39613718ed7d8540',2,'M1: Add the chopped vegetables to a mixing bowl','To make Kachumbar Salad, in a large mixing bowl, add 1/2 cup of diced cucumber, 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes, 1/4 cup of diced carrot, 1/4 cup of chopped onions, 1/4 cup of chopped cabbage and 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e95946eab62d52ee6dc428e','5d7d3c2d39613718ed7d8540',3,'M2: Season the salad and garnish with mint leaves','Next, add 1/2 teaspoon of crushed black pepper, 1 nos finely chopped green chili, 1/2 teaspoon of chat masala and 1/4 teaspoon of salt to the salad along with 1 tablespoon of lime juice. Mix the salad well. Garnish with 1 tablespoon chopped mint leaves and serve.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9594e7b8df13802c95a0c7','5d7d3e1909e1dd5a7f4238ce',1,'P1: Rinse & soak rice','Wash then soak Basmati Rice in 2 cups of water for 20 mins.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e95950cacd25afedeb1f700','5d7d3e1909e1dd5a7f4238ce',2,'P2: Prep the ingredients','Wash and chop onions and green chilies. Squeeze 1 tsp of lime juice.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e959543ab62d52ee6dc428f','5d7d3e1909e1dd5a7f4238ce',3,'M1: Roast the nuts','In pan heat ghee, then add cashew nuts and raisins. Let them cook for 3-4 mins. Stir this continuously to prevent burning.  Once this is done set it aside leaving the ghee in the pan.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e95958db8df13802c95a0c8','5d7d3e1909e1dd5a7f4238ce',4,'M2: Temper the ghee with whole spices and fry the onions','Once the cashews are golden brown, add a bay leaf, a cinnamon stick, green cardamom, cloves, and black peppercorn. Saute this for a few seconds then add onions, green chilies and saute for 3-4 mins.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9595c0ab62d52ee6dc4290','5d7d3e1909e1dd5a7f4238ce',5,'M3: Add water & simmer the rice','Once the onions are slightly golden, add the soaked basmati rice, 2 cups of water, lime juice, and salt. Mix well and cover with a lid. Let this simmer for 20 mins.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e9595efacd25afedeb1f701','5d7d3e1909e1dd5a7f4238ce',6,'M4: Gently mix the rice. Garnish & serve','Once the rice has cooked, remove the lid and add the roasted nuts. Gently mix the rice and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e959688b8df13802c95a0c9','5e6f369c91cde451322c5169',2,'M1: Tempering','To make the Coriander Chutney, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a Kadai over medium flame for a minute. Add 1 teaspoon of urad dal along with 1 teaspoon of cumin seeds. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 2 nos chopped green chilies followed by a 1/2-inch piece of chopped ginger and fry it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e9596d3ab62d52ee6dc4291','5e6f369c91cde451322c5169',3,'M2: Cooking','Next, add 1 teaspoon of tamarind followed by 3/4 cup of coriander leaves and mix it well. Saute and fry the coriander leaves with the tempering over low flame for 2-3 minutes. Make sure not to fry it over the high flame as it may turn dark if exposed to heat for long. Next, add 1/4 cup of grated coconut and mix it well. Add 1/4 teaspoon of jaggery and saute it until it dissolves completely. Then, turn off the flame and allow the mixture to cool down completely. While it is cooling down, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e959715b8df13802c95a0ca','5e6f369c91cde451322c5169',4,'M3: Blending','To make the Coriander Chutney, after the prepared coriander leaves mixture cools down, transfer it to a blender jar along with 1/4 cup of water and blend it well into a smooth chutney. Then transfer it to a bowl and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e959768b8df13802c95a0cb','5e6f369c91cde451322c5169',5,'M4: Making a Tadka','To make the tempering for the Coriander Chutney, heat 1 teaspoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add half a teaspoon of urad dal, 1/4 teaspoon of mustard seeds and 1/4 teaspoon of cumin seeds followed by 1 dry red chili and 1/4 teaspoon of hing. Next, add 7 nos curry leaves along with 3 nos cloves of crushed garlic and saute it for a minute over medium flame. Then, turn off the flame and add the prepared coriander chutney into the tempering and mix it well. Take it out into a serving bowl and mix it well.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9597d6acd25afedeb1f702','5d7d4d7f09e1dd5a7f4238d4',1,'P1: Grate coconut & prep the ingredients','For Coconut Chutney, Finely chop half a cup of fresh coconut. Wash, peel and finely chop a 1/2-inch piece of ginger. Wash and roughly chop 1 nos green chili. Wash 12 nos curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e959808ab62d52ee6dc4292','5d7d4d7f09e1dd5a7f4238d4',2,'M1: Blend the ingredients to a prepare the chutney','To make the Coconut Chutney, in a blender jar, add half a cup of chopped coconut. Add 1 nos chopped green chili, and 1/2- inch piece of chopped ginger followed by 1/4 cup of roasted Bengal gram and 1/4 teaspoon of salt. Cover the blender jar with a lid and blend it well into a smooth chutney. Add 3 tablespoons of water, while blending the chutney. Then, take it out into a bowl and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e95982cab62d52ee6dc4293','5d7d4d7f09e1dd5a7f4238d4',3,'M2: Prepare the tempering & add it to the chutney','To make the tempering for Coconut Chutney, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a small pan over medium flame for a minute. Add 12 nos curry leaves and saute it over medium flame for a minute. Then, turn off the flame and add the tempering instantly over the prepared chutney. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e959846acd25afedeb1f703','5e6f32ee91cde451322c5168',1,'P1: Roasting Rava','To roast the semolina for Khara bath, add 3/4 cup of semolina to a frying pan and saute it over low flame. Saute and dry roast the Rava for 4-5 minutes until it turns slightly golden. Keep stirring it continuously while roasting, as it might burn easily. As the rava turns aromatic and slightly changes color, turn off the flame and set it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e95986cab62d52ee6dc4294','5e6f32ee91cde451322c5168',2,'P2: Prepping Ingredients','For Khara Bhath, peel, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of green capsicum. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of beans. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of carrots. Wash and chop 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves. Wash 8 nos curry leaves. Wash and cut a lemon into halves and squeeze 1 tablespoon of lemon juice. Wash and slit 1 nos green chili. Wash, peel and finely chop a 1-inch piece of ginger.','prep_method','{"active_time":18,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e959891ab62d52ee6dc4295','5d7d50621710a053f6cd1311',1,'P1: Soak rice & prep the ingredients','Soak sona masuri in 1/4 cup of water for 15 mins. Wash and slice ivy gourd, wash green chilies and curry leaves, grate fresh coconut, and whisk 1/2 a cup of curd, removing all lumps.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9598adacd25afedeb1f704','5e6f32ee91cde451322c5168',3,'P3: Frying Nuts for Sheera','To fry the nuts for sheera, heat 2 tablespoons of ghee in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add 4 nos cashews followed by a tablespoon of raisins and saute it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes, until cashews turn slightly golden. Then, take it out into a bowl and set it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('5e9598cbacd25afedeb1f705','5d7d50621710a053f6cd1311',2,'P2: Prepare the coconut paste','In a blending jar, blend grated coconut, green chili, curry leaves, soaked rice, and 1/2 cup of water.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9598f6ab62d52ee6dc4296','5e6f32ee91cde451322c5168',4,'P4: Roasting Rava','Next, add 3/4 cup of semolina to the same pan. Saute and roast the rava for 4-5 minutes until it turns slightly golden. Keep stirring it continuously while roasting, as it might burn easily. As the rava turns aromatic and slightly changes color, turn off the flame and set it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e95990dacd25afedeb1f706','5d7d50621710a053f6cd1311',3,'M1: Simmer the ivy gourds with salt 7 curry leaves','In a pan, add the ivy gourd along with 1 cup of water. curry leaves and salt, stir this, cover it, and let it cook for 10 mins.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e959930acd25afedeb1f707','5e6f32ee91cde451322c5168',5,'M1: Cooking Khara Bath','To make khara bhath, heat a tablespoon of ghee in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add a teaspoon of mustard seeds, a teaspoon of urad dal, a teaspoon of chana dal and 10 nos cashews followed by 8 nos curry leaves. Saute the tempering over low flame for a minute. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions followed by 1  slit green chili and fry it over medium flame for 3-4 minutes until translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e959968ab62d52ee6dc4297','5d7d50621710a053f6cd1311',4,'M2: Add the coconut paste & curd, then cook the curry','Next, add the prepared coconut paste, season with salt, mix well, cook for 5 mins, and stir occasionally. After this, add the whisked curd and combine it.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e959986ab62d52ee6dc4298','5e6f32ee91cde451322c5168',6,'M2: Cooking Khara Bath','After frying the onions, add 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes and mix it well. Saute and cook the tomatoes over medium flame for 4-5 minutes until tender. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped  green capsicum, 1/4 cup of chopped beans, 1/4 cup of chopped carrots and 1/4 cup of green peas followed by half a teaspoon of salt. Mix it well and stir-fry the vegetables over high flame for 2-3 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9599dbbd28bae9388e5318','5d7d50621710a053f6cd1311',5,'M3: Prepare the tempering & add it to the curry.','Make a tadka, heat oil in a tempering pan and then add mustard seeds, cumin seeds, dry red chili, and curry leaves. Saute this for a few seconds and immediately pour the tadka into the Majjiga Huli. Give it a final stir and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e959a96bf34cc9c0d0dc29f','5e6f32ee91cde451322c5168',7,'M3: Cooking Khara Bath','After frying the vegetables, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder followed by 1 teaspoon of vangi bath masala. Mix it well and saute the masala for a minute. Next, add 1 cup of water and stir it well. Then, bring it to a boil over a high flame. As it comes to a boil, add 3/4 cup of roasted semolina while continuously stirring it over a low flame until well combined. Then, cover it with a lid and simmer it for 5 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e959aadbf34cc9c0d0dc2a1','5d7d549839613718ed7d8545',1,'P1: Slice the raw bananas &  coat the slices with spices','Peel and slice the bananas and crush black peppercorns. In a large bowl, combine the banana with turmeric powder, sambar powder, black pepper, and salt. Mix this with your hands, coating the slices evenly.','prep_method','{"active_time":11,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e959ae32f7a2b2b07c1b3c2','5d7d549839613718ed7d8545',2,'M1: Temper the oil with mustard seeds & curry leaves','Heat cooking oil in a pan, then add mustard seeds, urad dal, cumin seeds, fennel seeds, dry red chili, hing, and curry leaves. Saute for a few seconds.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e959ae394ac7444f444809c','5e6f32ee91cde451322c5168',8,'M4: Cooking Khara Bath','After simmering the khara bhath, take off the lid and saute it for a minute. Next, add 2 tablespoons of desiccated coconut followed by 2 tablespoons of chopped coriander leaves and a tablespoon of lemon juice. Mix it well and turn off the flame.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e959b122f7a2b2b07c1b3c3','5d7d549839613718ed7d8545',3,'M2: Add the banana slices and simmer','Next, add the marinated banana slices and cook for 2 mins, spread evenly and cook on all sides. Sprinkle 2 Tbsp of water on the pan, cover it and let it simmer for 10 mins.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e959b42bf34cc9c0d0dc2a2','5d7d549839613718ed7d8545',4,'M3: Stir-fry the banana slices','After the banana has cooked, cook for another 2 mins without the lid to remove excess water, stir continuously to prevent burning. Next, turn off the flame and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":4}'),('5e959b47bf34cc9c0d0dc2a3','5e6f32ee91cde451322c5168',9,'M5: Cooking Sheera','To make Sheera, add 1.5 cups of water to a pan and bring it to a boil. As the water comes to a boil, add 3/4 cup of roasted semolina while continuously stirring it over a low flame until well combined. Then, add 1/4 cup of sugar and mix it well. Next, add 2 tablespoons of ghee and mix it well. Then, cover it with a lid and simmer it for 5 minutes. While the sheera is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e959b6a94ac7444f444809d','5e6f32ee91cde451322c5168',10,'M6: Cooking Sheera','After simmering the Sheera, take off the lid and the fried nuts followed by 1/4 teaspoon of cardamom powder and mix it well. Turn off the flame and take it out into a bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('5e959c3368027665d3f6b69e','5d7d565f39613718ed7d8546',1,'P1: Chop & prep the ingredients','To make Coriander Mint Chutney, first, wash and roughly chop 2 tbsp of mint leaves, 2 green chilies, and 1.5 tbsp of coriander leaves. Peel 2 cloves of garlic and 1/2 an inch of ginger. Grate 1/2 cup of fresh coconut. Wash 8 curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e959c90d976833a72d62cdf','5d7d565f39613718ed7d8546',2,'M1: stir-fry the coriander & mint leaves & blend all the ingredients to prepare a chutney','For Coriander Mint Chutney, heat 1.5 tsp of oil in a pan and then add 1/2 tsp of cumin seeds, 2 cloves of garlic, and 1/2 an inch of ginger and let this splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 2 tbsp of mint leaves and 1.5 tbsp of coriander leaves, saute this for 1 min. Once the leaves shrink, turn off the flame, allow the mixture to cool and then add it to a blending jar along with 1/2 cup of grated coconut, 2 tbsp roasted gram, 1 tsp of tamarind, 2 green chili, 1/2 tsp salt, and 5 tbsp of water. Blend this into a smooth chutney and transfer it to a serving bowl.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e959cd468027665d3f6b69f','5d7d565f39613718ed7d8546',3,'M2: Prepare the tempering & add it to the chutney','Next, in a tadka pan, heat 1.5 tsp of oil and then add 1/2 tsp of mustard seeds and 8 curry leaves. Let them splutter for a few seconds and then pour the tadka over the chutney. Give it a final mix and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e959d4b68027665d3f6b6a0','5e6f2ffa378bf22ba423186e',1,'AP1: Soaking Urad Dal','For Bonda Soup, soak 3/4 cup of urad dal in 2 cups of water for 2 hours. While the dal is soaking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":120,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e959d85d976833a72d62ce0','5e6f2ffa378bf22ba423186e',2,'P1: Prepping Ingredients','For Bonda Soup, peel, wash and finely chop half a cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Wash, peel and finely chop a 1-inch piece of ginger. Wash and finely chop 1 green chilies. Wash and slit 1 green chili. Wash and finely chop 3 tablespoons of coriander leaves. Wash 12 curry leaves. Finely chop a tablespoon of coconut. Wash and cut a lemon into halves. Then, squeeze 1 tablespoon of lemon juice.','prep_method','{"active_time":14,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e959db9d976833a72d62ce1','5e6f2ffa378bf22ba423186e',3,'P2: Cook Moong Dal','To cook the dal for Bonda Soup, wash half a cup of yellow moong dal and add it to a pressure cooker. Next, add a half-inch piece of chopped ginger, 1 slit green chili and 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes. Add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder along with a teaspoon of cooking oil and 1/4 teaspoon of salt. Mix it well. Add 1 cup of water and cover it with a lid. Then, pressure cook the dal over a high flame until one whistle. After that, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook it for another 8 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the dal is simmering, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e959ddf68027665d3f6b6a1','5d7d58161710a053f6cd1313',1,'P1: Chop & prep the ingredients','Wash yellow moong dal with water, peel and finely chop ginger, slit green chilies, finely chop tomatoes, grate fresh coconut, finely chop coriander leaves, squeeze 1 Tbsp of lemon juice, and wash curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e959df368027665d3f6b6a2','5e6f2ffa378bf22ba423186e',4,'P3: Make a Bonda Batter','To prepare the bonda batter for Bonda Soup, add the soaked urad dal to a blender jar and blend it well into a smooth and thick batter. Then, transfer it to a large mixing bowl and beat the dal for 3-4 minutes until it becomes light and fluffy. Next, add 1 chopped green chili, a half-inch piece of chopped ginger, 6 curry leaves and 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves followed by 1/4 teaspoon of crushed black peppercorns and a tablespoon of chopped coconut and mix it well.','prep_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e959e03d976833a72d62ce2','5d7d58161710a053f6cd1313',2,'M1: Pressure cook the moong dal','Cook the moong dal in a pressure cooker with ginger, green chilies, tomatoes, turmeric powder, cooking oil, salt, and 2.5 cups of water. Cook this on high flame for 1 whistle and then on low flame for 8 mins. Once this is done set the cooker aside to cool down before you take off the lid.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e959e2f68027665d3f6b6a3','5e6f2ffa378bf22ba423186e',5,'M1: Make Bonda','For Bonda Soup, heat 1.5 cups of cooking oil in a Kadai over medium-high flame for 2-3 minutes. Then, make small balls from the prepared urad dal batter with wet hands as shown and carefully drop it one by one into the hot oil. Then deep the bondas over medium-high flame for 5-6 minutes, until it turns crisp and golden brown. After that, carefully take it out onto a kitchen napkin to wipe off the excess oil and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e959e413dcc9d934824bbac','5d7d58161710a053f6cd1313',3,'M2: Mash the cooked dal & prepare tempering','Take off the lid, whisk the dal and remove any lumps. Heat oil in a pan and temper mustard seeds, cumin seeds, hing, curry leaves and let this splatter for a few seconds.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e959e5e68027665d3f6b6a4','5e6f2ffa378bf22ba423186e',6,'M2: Make the Soup','To make Bonda Soup, after cooking the moong dal, take off the lid and mash it well using a whisk. Next, heat a tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium for a minute. Add half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, half a teaspoon of cumin seeds, 1/4 teaspoon of hing and 6 nos curry leaves. Saute it over low flame for a minute.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e959e8668027665d3f6b6a5','5e6f2ffa378bf22ba423186e',7,'M3: Make the Soup','Next, add the prepared moong dal and mix it well. Add 1/4 teaspoon of salt followed by 1 cup of water and stir it well. Allow it to boil over medium-high flame for 1-2 minutes while stirring in between. After that, add 1 tablespoon of desiccated coconut followed by 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and a tablespoon of lemon juice and mix it well. Then, in a bowl, add a prepared bonda. Pour the dal soup over it and garnish it with chopped onions and coriander leaves. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e959ee322360f5517909864','5d7d58161710a053f6cd1313',4,'M3: Add the cooked dal to the tempering & cook the rasam.  Garnish & serve','Add the mashed dal to the tadka and mix. Add 2 cups of water and salt, mix well. Bring the rasam to a boil and then add grated coconut, coriander leaves, and lemon juice. Stir the rasam once more, take it off the flame, and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e959f73cf4ec3ed4b5aafb6','5d7d599339613718ed7d8547',1,'P1: Shred cabbage & prepare the coconut paste','Finely chop cabbage, wash curry leaves, and grate fresh coconut. In a blending jar, add grated coconut, dry red chili, cumin seeds, blend this into a coarse powder.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e959f779e934d26fb80cf7d','5e6f299ba04de0b99a30031c',1,'AP1: Prepping the Ingredients','For Mangalore Bonda, peel, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1 nos green chili. Wash, peel and finely chop a 1/4-inch piece of ginger. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coconut. Wash and finely chop 8 nos curry leaves. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e959fa7cf4ec3ed4b5aafb7','5e6f299ba04de0b99a30031c',2,'AP2: Prepare the Batter','To prepare the batter for Mangalore Bonda, add 1/4 cup of sour curd to a large mixing bowl. Add 1 chopped green chili, 1/4-inch piece of ginger, 8 chopped curry leaves and 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves followed by 1 tablespoon of chopped coconut and 1/4 cup of chopped onions. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of salt, 1/4 teaspoon of baking soda and 1/4 teaspoon of hing. Mix it well.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e959fc922360f5517909865','5d7d599339613718ed7d8547',2,'M1: Fry the cabbage with spices then simmer','Heat oil in a pan, add mustard seeds, urad dal, chana dal, and curry leaves. Saute for a few seconds and then add cabbage and cook for 1 min. Next, add turmeric powder, jaggery, salt, and water. Cover with a lid, simmer for 5 mins.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e959fe222360f5517909866','5e6f299ba04de0b99a30031c',3,'AP3: Prepare the Batter','Next, add 1/4 cup of all-purpose flour followed by 2 tablespoons of rice flour. Then, mix it well and combine the batter. The batter should be thick and moist. Then set it aside and allow it to rest for 3 hours. While the batter is resting, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":180,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e95a0059e934d26fb80cf7e','5e6f299ba04de0b99a30031c',4,'M1: Make the Bonda','To make Mangalore Bonda, heat 1.5 cups of cooking oil in a Kadai over medium-high flame for 2-3 minutes. Next, gently mix the prepared vada batter and take a small scoop of the batter as shown, then carefully drop it into the hot oil. Drop the vada batter scoops one by one to the oil and deep fry it over medium-high flame for 5-6 minutes, until it turns crisp and golden brown. After that, carefully take it out onto a kitchen napkin to wipe off the excess oil. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e95a0069e934d26fb80cf7f','5d7d599339613718ed7d8547',3,'M2: Add the coconut paste & simmer. Garnish & serev','Add the coconut masala and then cook for another 2 mins, stirring occasionally. Next, take off the lid and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e95a0a99e934d26fb80cf80','5e6f26a1a04de0b99a30031a',1,'AP1: Soaking Rice','For Curd Dosa, add 3/4 cup of sona-masuri rice in a mixing bowl. Add 1/4 teaspoon of fenugreek seeds and then soak the rice in 2 cups of water for 5 hours. While the rice is soaking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":300,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e95a0f722360f5517909867','5e6f26a1a04de0b99a30031a',2,'AP2: Resting the Batter','To prepare the batter for Curd Dosa, first, rinse half a cup of poha with water. Next, add the soaked sona masuri rice to a blender jar along with half a cup of rinsed poha and blend it well into a smooth batter. Then, transfer it to a large bowl. Add 1/4 cup of curd and mix it well. Then, set the batter aside and allow it to ferment for 8 hours. While the batter is fermenting, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":480,"advanced_prep_time":480,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e95a117cf4ec3ed4b5aafb8','5e6f26a1a04de0b99a30031a',3,'M1: Make Dosa','To make Curd Dosa, after resting the rice batter, it will rise and turns frothy. Then, add 1/4 teaspoon of salt into it and gently mix it. Next, add half a teaspoon of cooking oil to a tawa and wipe it with a tissue to apply it evenly across the tawa. Next, pour a ladle full of the prepared batter over it and spread it across into a slightly thick round dosa. Then, cover it with a lid and simmer it for 2-3 minutes. After that, take off the lid gently, take it out onto a plate. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e95a18322360f5517909868','5d7d5cfa1710a053f6cd1315',1,'AP1: Rinse  & soak rice','Wash and soak 1 cup of sona masuri in 4 cups of water for 5 hours.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":300,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e95a255268f112893076973','5e6f247b378bf22ba4231869',1,'AP1: Soaking','For Mixed Dal Dosa, in a large bowl, add 1/4 cup of moong dal,1/4 cup of toor dal, 1/4 cup of masoor dal, 1/4 cup of chana dal, and 1/4 cup of urad dal along with 1/4 cup of green whole moong dal. Next, add 1/4 cup of sona masuri rice and then soak it in 3 cups of water for 5 hours. While the dals are soaking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":300,"advanced_prep_time":300,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e95a26a9b3b38fb374fbdfb','5d7d5cfa1710a053f6cd1315',2,'AP2: Blend the soaked rice with grated coconut','Grate fresh coconut. In a blending jar add the soaked rice, grated coconut and blend it until smooth. Then transfer this into a large mixing bowl.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e95a28a268f112893076974','5e6f247b378bf22ba4231869',2,'P1: Prepping Ingredients','For Mixed Dal Dosa, peel, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and peel a half-inch piece of ginger. Peel and wash 2 cloves of garlic. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves. Wash 8 nos curry leaves','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e95a2a49b3b38fb374fbdfc','5d7d5cfa1710a053f6cd1315',3,'AP3: Prepare the appam batter','In a pan, mix 2 Tbsp of the rice batter with 1/2 cup of water with the flame off. Then turn on the flame and stir the batter continuously to form a thick paste. Let this cool. Once it is cool transfer it to the bowl with the rest of the batter and leave it for 8 hours to ferment.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":480,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e95a2ba268f112893076975','5e6f247b378bf22ba4231869',4,'P3: Prepare the Batter','Then, transfer the prepared batter to a large mixing bowl. Add 8 nos curry leaves followed by 2 tablespoons of chopped coriander leaves. Mix it well and prepare the batter.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e95a2ba9b3b38fb374fbdfd','5e6f247b378bf22ba4231869',3,'P2: Prepare the Batter','To prepare the batter for Mixed Dal Dosa, add the soaked dals to a blender jar. Add a 1-inch piece of cinnamon stick, 1 dry red chili and a half-inch piece of ginger followed by 2 cloves of garlic and 1/4 cup of chopped onions. Next, add a teaspoon of fennel seeds, half a teaspoon of salt along with 1/4 cup of water and blend it well into a smooth batter.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e95a2f0268f112893076976','5d7d5cfa1710a053f6cd1315',4,'P1: Add baking soda & water to the batter','After 8 hours the batter will ferment and rise. Give it a quick stir and then add sugar, salt, and baking soda along with 3 Tbsp of water. Mix well.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e95a312268f112893076977','5e6f247b378bf22ba4231869',5,'M1: Make Dosa','To make Mixed Dal Dosa, add half a teaspoon of cooking oil to a tawa and wipe it with a tissue to apply it evenly across the tawa. Next, pour a ladle full of the prepared batter over it and spread it across into a thin round dosa. Add half a teaspoon of cooking oil over it. Then, cover it with a lid and simmer it for 1-2 minutes. After that, take off the lid and cook the other side. Cook the dosa until golden and crisp. Then, take it out onto a plate. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e95a329268f112893076978','5d7d5cfa1710a053f6cd1315',5,'M1: Make the appams from the batter','To make an Appam, heat the tawa, then pour a ladle full of batter on the hot tawa. Hold the tawa on both sides and swirl the batter in a clockwise motion to spread it. Reduce the flame to low and let it cook for 2 mins with the lid on. When bubble appears on the surface remove the appam from the tawa. It is ready to eat!','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e95a38a268f112893076979','5d7d5f6a39613718ed7d8548',1,'P1: Soak tamarind & pressure cook the rice','Soak 1 Tbsp of tamarind in 1/4 cup of water for 15 mins. Cook 1 cup of rice in a pressure cooker with 2 cups of water, on high flame for 1 whistle and then on low flame for 8 mins. Once this is done set the cooker aside to cool before you take off the lid. (You can use leftover rice to make this dish.)','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e95a3b31acac57963d6f814','5d7d5f6a39613718ed7d8548',2,'P2: Prep the ingredients','Wash curry leaves, set them aside. Mash and mix the tamarind with the water, remove the pulp with a strainer, and set the extract aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e95a3f21acac57963d6f815','5d7d5f6a39613718ed7d8548',3,'M1: Boil the tamarind slurry','Heat oil in a pan and then add mustard seeds, urad dal, chana dal, dry red chilli, curry leaves, and peanuts. Saute this for a few seconds adn then add the tamarind extract, jaggery, turmeric powder, and salt. Stir and cook on high flame for 10 mins, stir occasionally.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e95a3f99b3b38fb374fbdfe','5e6f22b8a04de0b99a300316',1,'AP1: Soaking Rice','For Neer Dosa, wash and soak 3/4 cup of sona masuri rice in 2 cups of water for 5 hours. While the rice is soaking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":300,"advanced_prep_time":300,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e95a3ff268f11289307697a','5e6f22b8a04de0b99a300316',2,'P1: Prepare the Batter','To prepare the batter for Neer Dosa, add the soaked sona masuri rice to a blender jar and blend it well into a smooth batter. Then, transfer it to a bowl and add half a teaspoon of salt. Mix it well. Then, add about 3/4 cup of water and stir it well to prepare a thin and flowy batter.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e95a44e1acac57963d6f816','5e6f22b8a04de0b99a300316',3,'M1: Make Dosa','To make Neer Dosa, pour a ladle full of the prepared rice batter over a hot tawa and spread it across. Then, cover and cook it over low flame for a minute. After that, take off the lid and gently fold it into a triangle. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":1,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e95a454268f11289307697b','5d7d5f6a39613718ed7d8548',4,'M2: Add puliyogare powder, rice & cook. Garnish & serve','Next, add puliyogare powder and mix until all lumps are gone. Add the cooked rice and gently combine the masala and rice. Saute the rice for 1 min, turn off the flame, and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e95a500268f11289307697c','5e6f212a378bf22ba4231866',1,'AP1: Soaking Rice and Dal','For Ghee Roast Dosa, soak 3/4 cup of sona masuri rice in 2 cups of water for 5 hours. Next, in a separate bowl, add 1/4 cup of urad dal and soak it in 1 cup of water for 3 hours. While the dal and rice are soaking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":180,"advanced_prep_time":180,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e95a5449b3b38fb374fbdff','5d7f1ac639613718ed7d8549',1,'AP1: Soak the green moong beans','For Hesaru Kaal Palya, soak 1 cup of green moong beans in 2 cups of water for 8 hours. While the moong beans are soaking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":2160,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e95a55f9b3b38fb374fbe00','5e6f212a378bf22ba4231866',2,'AP2: Prepare the Batter','To prepare the batter for Ghee Roast Dosa, add the soaked urad dal to a blender jar and blend it well into a smooth batter. Transfer it to a large bowl and set it aside. Next, add the soaked rice to the blender jar and blend it into a slightly coarse batter. Then, transfer it to the urad dal batter.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e95a5929b3b38fb374fbe01','5d7f1ac639613718ed7d8549',2,'AP2: Sprout the soaked moong beans','For Hesaru Kaal Palya, after soaking the moong beans for 8 hours, it will absorb the water and increase in size. Drain the water and rinse it with fresh water. Next, to sprout the moong beans, add the soaked moong beans to a colander and cover it with a damp cloth. Allow the moong beans to rest for another 12 hours.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":2160,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e95a5a9268f11289307697d','5e6f212a378bf22ba4231866',3,'AP3: Prepare the Batter','Next, rinse 2 tablespoons of poha with water and squeeze the excess water from it. Then, add it to the blender jar and blend it well into a smooth paste. Add the prepared poha paste to the urad dal batter and mix it well. Then, set it aside and allow the batter to ferment for 8 hours. While the batter is fermenting, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":480,"advanced_prep_time":480,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e95a5b51acac57963d6f817','5d7f1ac639613718ed7d8549',3,'P1: Chop & prep the ingredients','Rinse the green moong sprouts well. Finely chop onions, garlic, coriander leaves, and tomatoes. Slit a green chili and wash curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e95a5cd1acac57963d6f818','5e6f212a378bf22ba4231866',4,'M1: Make Dosa','To make Ghee Roast Dosa, after resting the prepared dosa batter, it will rise and turns frothy. Then, add 1/4 teaspoon of salt and gently mix it. Next, pour a ladle full of the dosa batter over a hot Tawa and spread it across into a thin round dosa. Then, add a teaspoon of ghee to it and cover it with a lid. Allow it to simmer for 1-2 minutes until crisp and golden. Then, take off the lid and carefully take it out onto a plate. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e95a6031acac57963d6f819','5d7f1ac639613718ed7d8549',4,'M1: Fry onions & cook tomatoes','Heat cooking oil in a pan and then add mustard seeds, cumin seeds, and curry leaves. Saute this for a few seconds, then add garlic, ginger paste, and green chili, cook this for 1 min. Next, add onions and saute them for 2-3 mins. Once they are slightly translucent, add tomatoes and cook them for 3-4 mins, stirring continuously, until tender.','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e95a63a9b3b38fb374fbe02','5d7f1ac639613718ed7d8549',5,'M2: Add the spices & simmer the moong sprouts','Once the tomatoes have cooked, add turmeric powder, Kashmiri red chilli, jaggery, and salt, saute 2-3 mins. Next, add the moong sprouts with 1 cup of water and mix it well. Cover the pan and simmer for 15 mins, until water has absorbed. Once this is done, garnish with coriander leaves and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e95a6ac1acac57963d6f81a','5e6f1ff9378bf22ba4231865',1,'AP1: Soaking','For Adai, in a large bowl, add 1/4 cup of chana dal followed by 1/4 cup of toor dal and 1/4 cup of urad dal. Add 5 dry red chilies and rinse it thoroughly with water. Next, add 2 cups of water and soak it for 3 hours. Next, in a separate bowl, soak half a cup of rice in 2 cups of water. While the dals are soaking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":180,"advanced_prep_time":180,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e95a6da1acac57963d6f81b','5e6f1ff9378bf22ba4231865',2,'P1: Prepare Batter','To prepare the Batter for Adai, add the soaked dals to a blender jar along with the soaked rice. Add 1 teaspoon of salt followed by half a teaspoon of hing. Add 1/4 cup of water and blend it well into a smooth batter. Then, take it out into a bowl and set aside. Next, peel, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions.','prep_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e95a70d1acac57963d6f81c','5e6f1ff9378bf22ba4231865',3,'M1: Make Dosa','To make Adai, pour a ladle full of the prepared adai batter over a hot tawa and spread it into a thick round circle. Add a teaspoon of cooking oil and cook it over medium flame. Add 2 tablespoons of chopped onions and gently press it using a flat turner. Then, flip and cook both sides of adai for 2-3 minutes, until it turns slightly golden. Then, carefully take it out onto a plate. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e95a7681acac57963d6f81d','5d7f1cef09e1dd5a7f4238d8',1,'P1: Soak tamarind & pressure cook the toor dal','Soak tamarind in 1/4 cup of water for 15 mins. Cook toor dal in a pressure cooker with 1.5 cups of water and cook this on high flame for 1 whistle and then on low flame for 8 mins. Once the dal is cooked let the pressure cooker cool completely before you take off the lid.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e95a7969b3b38fb374fbe03','5d7f1cef09e1dd5a7f4238d8',2,'P2: Chop & prep the ingredients','Cut shallots in half, finely chop tomatoes and coriander leaves, cut drumsticks into 3-inch pieces, and wash curry leaves. Mash and mix the tamarind with the water and then remove the pulp with a strainer. Keep the tamarind water aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e95a7d3268f11289307697e','5d7f1cef09e1dd5a7f4238d8',3,'M1: Temper the oil.  Fry the shallots and tomatoes','Heat oil in a pan and then add mustard seeds, dry red chili, hing, curry leaves and let them splatter for a few seconds. Next. add the sliced onions and cook them for 2 mins. Once they are translucent add the tomatoes and saute them for 2-3 mins.','cook_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e95a80f268f11289307697f','5d7f1cef09e1dd5a7f4238d8',4,'M2: Add spices and simmer the drumsticks','Once the tomatoes are tender, add turmeric powder, sambar powder, salt and cook the masalas for 1 min. Next, add the drumstick, fry them for 2 mins and then add 3/4 cup of water. Stir this and cover the pan with a lid. Let this cool for 10 mins.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e95a8471acac57963d6f81e','5d7f1cef09e1dd5a7f4238d8',5,'M3: Add the cooked dal & simmer the sambar. Garnish & serve','Take off the lid and stir the sambar, add the cooked dal and cook this for 5 mins. Next, add the tamarind extract and cook for another 5 mins. After this, garnish with coriander leaves and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e95aa231acac57963d6f81f','5d7f228639613718ed7d854a',1,'P1: Chop & prep the ingredients','Finely chop onions and tomatoes. Dice carrots and potatoes. Cut the cauliflower into small florets. Wash and peel green peas.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e95aa57268f112893076980','5d7f228639613718ed7d854a',2,'M1: Fry the onions & cook the tomatoes','Heat cooking oil in a pan and then add a bay leaf, cinnamon stick, green cardamom, and cloves. Saute this for a few seconds and then add onions and saute them for 2-3 mins. Once they are slightly translucent, add the tomatoes and saute them for 3-4 mins.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e95aa7a268f112893076981','5d7f228639613718ed7d854a',3,'M2: Simmer the vegetables','Once the tomatoes are tender, add the carrots, cauliflower, green peas, potatoes, beans, and salt. Saute this for 2 mins on medium flame. Next, add 2 cups of water, stir, cover it with a lid, and cook for 10 mins.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e95aaa89b3b38fb374fbe04','5d7f228639613718ed7d854a',4,'M3: Prepare coconut paste','Make a coconut,  in a blending jar add grated coconut, cashew nuts, ginger, garlic, green chili, poppy seeds, coriander seeds, fennel seeds, coriander leaves, and 1/4 cups of water. Blend this into a smooth paste.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e95aacc268f112893076982','5d7f228639613718ed7d854a',5,'M4: Add coconut paste and simmer the kurma','After cooking the vegetables for 10 mins, take off the lid and pour in the coconut paste. Mix this well and saute on medium flame for 2 mins. Next, add a cup of water, stir, cover it with the lid, and cook for another 10 mins. Once that is done, take off the lid, stir the Kurma and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e969736d939a7cdada21609','5e6f1b4ba04de0b99a300312',1,'P1: Prepping Ingredients','For Onion Rava Dosa, peel, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of curry leaves. Wash, peel and finely chop 1/4 inch piece of ginger. Wash and finely chop 1 nos green chili.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9697bba6a04af56e443ee3','5e6f1b4ba04de0b99a300312',2,'P2: Prepare the Batter','To prepare the batter for Onion Rava Dosa, in a large mixing bowl, add 1/4 cup of semolina followed by 1/4 cup of rice flour and a tablespoon of all-purpose flour. Next, add 2 tablespoons of curd and 1/4 teaspoon of salt. Add 1/2 a cup of water and mix it well using a whisk to avoid any lumps.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9698183e1749fedf549a8d','5e6f1b4ba04de0b99a300312',3,'P3: Prepare the Batter','Next, add 1 nos chopped green chili, 1/4-inch piece of chopped ginger, and 1/4 teaspoon of crushed black peppercorns and 1/4 teaspoon of cumin seeds followed by 1 tablespoon of chopped curry leaves and 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves. Add 1/4 cup of chopped onions and mix them well. Add about 3/4 cup of water and stir it well. The batter should be thin and flowy consistency. Then, allow it to rest for 20 minutes. While the batter is resting, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":20,"flame":0}'),('5e969863d939a7cdada2160a','5e6f1b4ba04de0b99a300312',4,'M1: Make Dosa','To make Onion Rava Dosa, after resting the prepared batter gently mix it. Then, pour a ladle full of the batter over the hot Tawa and spread it across. Add half a teaspoon of cooking oil and cook it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until it turns golden and crisp. Then, fold the dosa and take it out onto a plate. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9699d7d939a7cdada2160b','5e6f176ba04de0b99a300311',1,'P1: Prepping Ingredients','For Oats Dosa, wash, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash, peel and finely chop 1/4 inch piece of ginger. Wash and finely chop 1 nos green chili. Wash and finely chop 2 teaspoons of coriander leaves. Wash and finely chop 1 teaspoon of curry leaves. Crush 1/4 teaspoon of black peppercorns to a coarse powder using a pepper grinder. Next, add 1/4 cup of rolled oats to a blender jar and grind it well to a fine powder.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e969a2ed939a7cdada2160c','5e6f176ba04de0b99a300311',2,'P2: Make Batter','To make the batter for Oats Dosa, transfer the prepared oats powder to a large mixing bowl. Add 2 tablespoons of rice flour, 1 tablespoon of semolina and 2 tablespoons of curd. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of cumin seeds, 1/4 inch piece of chopped ginger, 1 chopped green chili, 1 teaspoon of chopped curry leaves, 1/4 teaspoon of crushed black pepper, 2 teaspoons of chopped coriander leaves and 1/4 cup of chopped onions along with 1/4 teaspoon of salt. Add 3/4 cup of water and mix it well, keeping the consistency of the batter thin and runny.  Set it aside for 20 minutes. While the batter is resting, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e969a703e1749fedf549a8e','5e6f176ba04de0b99a300311',3,'M1: Make Dosa','To make the Oats Dosa, after resting the prepared batter, give it a stir. Next, heat a tawa on a medium flame for a minute. Then, pour a ladleful of batter on the tawa and spread it across. Drizzle 1 teaspoon of oil over it and cook the dosa on medium-high flame for 1-2 minutes, until it is golden and crisp. Then, carefully take out the dosa scraping the sides. Similarly, make the rest of the dosas from the batter. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e969b374d5574fef5a830a6','5e6b6cec378bf22ba4231860',1,'AP1: Soak Millet and Dal','For Thinai Idli, wash 1 cup of foxtail millet well with water and then soak it int 2 cups of water for 5 hours. Next, in a separate bowl, add 1/4 cup of urad dal and soak it in 1 cup of water. While the dal is soaking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":300,"advanced_prep_time":300,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e969bb73e1749fedf549a8f','5e6b6cec378bf22ba4231860',2,'AP2: Prepare Batter','To prepare the batter for Thinai Idli, add the soaked urad dal to a blender jar and blend it well into a smooth batter. Then, transfer it to a large bowl. Next, add the soaked foxtail millet to a blender jar along with 1/4 cup of water and blend it well into a smooth batter. Then, add it to the urad dal batter. Next, add a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Then, set it aside and allow the batter to ferment for 8 hours. While the batter is fermenting, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":480,"advanced_prep_time":480,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e969be901682d9fca89ae1c','5e6b6cec378bf22ba4231860',3,'M1: Make Dosa','To make Thinail Idli, grease an idli plate with a teaspoon of cooking oil using an oil brush. Next, after fermenting the batter, mix it gently. The batter will rise and turns slightly frothy.  Then,  pour the prepared batter to the molds of the idli plate. Then, carefully keep it in the steamer and steam the idlis for 15 minutes. After that, take it out from the steamer and gently take out the idlis. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e969c783e1749fedf549a90','5e6b5f6e378bf22ba4231854',1,'P1: Prepping Ingredients','For Ragi Dosa, wash, peel and finely chop 1/4 inch piece of ginger. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Peel, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 8 nos curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e969cb34d5574fef5a830a7','5e6b5f6e378bf22ba4231854',2,'P2: Prepare the Batter','To prepare the batter for Ragi Dosa, in a large mixing bowl, add1/4 cup of ragi flour followed by 1/4 cup of semolina and 1.5 tablespoons of rice flour. Next, add 1.5 tablespoons of curd, 1/4-inch piece of chopped ginger, 1 green chili, 8 chopped curry leaves and 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e969d7d4d5574fef5a830a8','5e6b5f6e378bf22ba4231854',3,'P3: Prepare the Batter','Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions, 1/4 teaspoon of cumin seeds, 1/4 teaspoon of crushed black peppercorns, and 1/4 teaspoon of salt. Add 1 cup of water and mix it well to avoid any lumps. Then, set it aside and allow the batter to rest for 15 minutes. While the batter is resting, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e969d9701682d9fca89ae1d','5e6b5f6e378bf22ba4231854',4,'M1: Make Dosa','To make Ragi Dosa, after resting the prepared ragi batter, add about 1/4 cup of water and mix it well.  Next, pour a ladle full of the dosa batter over a hot tawa and spread it across into a thin round dosa. Then, add a teaspoon of oil to it and cook it for 2-3 minutes. Flip and cook the dosa over medium flame until crisp and golden. Then, carefully take it out onto a plate. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e969ee04d5574fef5a830a9','5e6b5c36378bf22ba4231852',1,'AP1: Soak Urad Dal','For Medu Vada, soak 3/4 cup of urad dal in 2 cups of water for 4 hours. While the dal is soaking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":240,"advanced_prep_time":480,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e969ee13e1749fedf549a91','5e6b5c36378bf22ba4231852',2,'AP2: Prepare the Batter','To prepare the batter for Medu Vada, first, rinse the soaked urad dal well with water. Then, add it to a blender jar along with 1/4 cup of water and blend it well into a smooth and thick batter. Transfer it to a blender jar and allow it to refrigerate for 2 hours. While the batter is refrigerating, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":120,"advanced_prep_time":240,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e969ee14d5574fef5a830aa','5e6b5c36378bf22ba4231852',3,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Medu Vada, peel, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1 nos green chili. Wash and finely chop 8 nos curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}');
























































































































