('629bc4a0e7e5902eb9ac37d5','Mutton Mince','5d0b0b77487bb10e33c455cb','5cd2a32869dc751f8327be70','{"sku":"40227667","min_order_qty":250,"min_order_unit":"Gram","main_unit":"Cup","weight_per_unit":0,"cooking_units":[{"unit":"Cup","wpu":135},{"unit":"Gram","wpu":1}],"description":"Fresho Mutton Goatkid - Mince, Fresh & Tender, 250 g","other_name":["Goat Mince","Minced Mutton","Minced Mattan","Minced Muton","Muton Mince","Mutan Mince"]}'),('629c8b3eaf0117ae76ffd141','Pomegranate Juice','5d49254ce515864797591162','5cd2a32869dc751f8327be70','{"sku":"40104279","min_order_qty":180,"min_order_unit":"Millilitre","main_unit":"Cup","weight_per_unit":0,"cooking_units":[{"unit":"Cup","wpu":200},{"unit":"Tablespoon","wpu":15},{"unit":"Teaspoon","wpu":5}],"description":"Real India''s No.1 Juice - Pomegranate, 180 ml","other_name":["Anar ka Juice","Anar Juice","Pomogranate Juice","Pomogranite Juice","Anaar ka Juice","Dalimbri Juice","Dalambri Juice"]}'),('629d7db8af0117ae76ffd156','Bean Sprouts','5d0b0b7e487bb10e33c455cc','5cd2a32869dc751f8327be70','{"sku":"40025927","min_order_qty":200,"min_order_unit":"Gram","main_unit":"Cup","weight_per_unit":0,"cooking_units":[{"unit":"Cup","wpu":200},{"unit":"Tablespoon","wpu":10},{"unit":"Teaspoon","wpu":3}],"description":"Fresho Beans Sprouts/Modache Mug, 200 g","other_name":["Mung Bean Sprouts","Been Sprouts","Mung Been Sprouts","Fresh Bean Sprouts","Mudachi Mag","Mudachi Mug"]}'),('629ddaae29fb46b3cfbc50ff','Chicken Breast (Skinless)','5d0b0b77487bb10e33c455cb','5cd2a32869dc751f8327be70','{"sku":"40085971","min_order_qty":1,"min_order_unit":"Kilo","main_unit":"Cup","weight_per_unit":0,"cooking_units":[{"unit":"Cup","wpu":150},{"unit":"Gram","wpu":1}],"description":"Fresho Chicken - Breast Boneless, Without Skin, 1 kg","other_name":["Chicken Breast- Boneless and Skinless","Skinless Chicken Breast","Boneless Chicken Breast","Boneless and Skinless Chicken Breast","Boneless & Skinless Chicken Breast","Skinless and Boneless Chicken Breast","Skinless & Boneless Chicken Breast"]}'),('629e4c8629fb46b3cfbc510f','Amarantha Flour','5d3ea8de6c7e050b497dc4b6','5d159bbfe73520e9a610389e','{"sku":"40252007","min_order_qty":500,"min_order_unit":"Gram","main_unit":"Cup","weight_per_unit":0,"cooking_units":[{"unit":"Cup","wpu":230},{"unit":"Tablespoon","wpu":10}],"description":"Graminway Rajgira Atta / Amaranth Flour - Gluten Free , High Protein, For A Healthy Lifestyle, 500 g","other_name":["Rajgira Atta","Rajagira Atta","Rajgira Ata","Rajagira Ata","Amarantha Floor","ramadana flour","amaranth flour","rajgira ka atta","Amaranthus Flour","Amaranthus Floor"]}'),
('62a00f315e33e0a4df83145d','Vanilla Yogurt','5d4923a6eac6bd0a9b1d58b9','5cd2a32869dc751f8327be70','{"sku":"40200836","min_order_qty":75,"min_order_unit":"Gram","main_unit":"Cup","weight_per_unit":0,"cooking_units":[{"unit":"Cup","wpu":150},{"unit":"Tablespoon","wpu":12}],"description":"Epigamia Fruit Yogurt - Vanilla Bean, 75 g Cup","other_name":["Vanilla Curd","Vanilla Dahi","Vanila Yogurt","Vanila Yoghurt","Vanilla Doi","Sweet Dahi","Sweet Dai","Sweet Doi","Vanilla Kurd"]}'),('62a034b85511d9e71bcc7da2','Muskmelon','5cff5d4598efbc46349fa581','5cd2a32869dc751f8327be70','{"sku":"10000141","min_order_qty":500,"min_order_unit":"Gram","main_unit":"Cup","weight_per_unit":0,"cooking_units":[{"unit":"Cup","wpu":180},{"unit":"Tablespoon","wpu":10},{"unit":"Nos","wpu":500}],"description":"Fresho Muskmelon - Netted Small, 1 pc 500g-900g","other_name":["Cantaloupe","Chibdu","Chibud","Chibad","Kantaloupe","Musk Melon","Musk Melan","Muskmelan"]}'),('63b69a9ef2d4a37dfeaa3da6','Vanilla Ice Cream','5d4923bbe51586479759115d','5cd2a32869dc751f8327be70','{"sku":"40008509","min_order_qty":125,"min_order_unit":"Millilitre","main_unit":"Cup","weight_per_unit":0,"cooking_units":[{"wpu":15,"unit":"Tablespoon"}],"description":"Vanilla Ice Cream","other_name":["Vanila Ice Cream","Vanilla Icecream"]}');
INSERT INTO catalog_recipe_steps VALUES
('5d0a2295487bb10e33c455c0','5d0a1fcc828e55e31ee1151d',1,'Rinse the rice and lentil, then lightly roast them','For Kara Pongal, first, rinse half a cup of rice well with water. Rinse half a cup of yellow moong dal with water. Next, heat 1 tablespoon of ghee in a pressure cooker over medium flame for a minute. Add half a cup of rinsed rice and half a cup of yellow moong dal to it and saute it over medium flame for a minute.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"timer":2,"flame":0}'),('5d0a2313487bb10e33c455c2','5d0a1fcc828e55e31ee1151d',2,'Pressure cook dal and rice','Next, add 2.5 cups of water followed by half a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Cover it with a lid and pressure cook it on high flame until two whistles. Then, reduce the flame to low and simmer it for 5 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the Pongal is cooking, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"timer":2,"flame":0}'),('5d107713400c0513f5806a80','5d10752c7aa86e5274a85e0a',1,'P1: chop the vegetables','To make Shahi Paneer, first, peel and slice 1/4 cup of onions, 1/2 an inch of ginger, and 2 cloves of garlic. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Chop 1 cup of paneer into cubes.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5d1de7f37b8ec859d333b6a7','5d0a1fcc828e55e31ee1151d',3,'Chop and prep the ingredients','For Kara Pongal, wash and slit 2 nos green chilies. Wash, peel and finely chop a 1-inch piece of ginger. Wash 7 nos curry leaves','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":2,"flame":0}'),('5d52af01acc6496253ae824b','5d52acaaacc6496253ae8249',1,'Chopping (p1)','For Alleppey Fish Curry, wash 500 grams of fish well with water and slice it in 1/2 inch slices. Wash, peel and slice 1.5 cups of onion. Wash and finely chop 1 cup of tomatoes, 1-inch piece ginger, and 1 teaspoon garlic. Wash 1/2 cup raw mango and cut it into wedges. Slit 3 nos green chilies lengthwise. Wash 10 nos curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5d5398ed24ade8297f194acb','5d52acaaacc6496253ae8249',2,'Cook Curry(m1)','To make the Alleppey Fish Curry, heat 2 tablespoons of coconut oil in a saucepan on medium flame for 1 minute. Add 1 teaspoon mustard seeds into the hot oil and let it crackle for a few seconds. Add 3 nos slit green chilies, 10 nos curry leaves and give it a quick saute on medium flame. Next, add 1.5 cups sliced onion, 1-inch piece chopped ginger,1 teaspoon chopped garlic into it and saute them together on a medium flame for 2-3 minutes till onion turns slightly translucent. After frying the onions for 2-3 minutes, add 1 cup chopped tomatoes to it, Give it a saute and cook the tomatoes on low flame for 4 minutes until they turn soft. After cooking the tomatoes for 4 minutes. Add 1/2 cup raw mango wedges along with 1/2 cup water into it. Give it a good stir, cover it with a lid, and continue to cook on low flame for another 3-4 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5d539bd2acc6496253ae824e','5d52acaaacc6496253ae8249',3,'Cook curry (m2)','After cooking the curry for 3-4 minutes, the raw mango will turn soft. Take off the lid and give it a stir. Next, add 1 teaspoon salt,1/2 teaspoon turmeric powder, 2 teaspoons Kashmiri red chili powder and saute everything together on a medium flame for a minute. Next, add 2 cups of sliced fish along with 1 cup of coconut milk into the masala. Combine everything well. Cover it with a lid and continue to cook it on low flame for another 6-7 minutes until the fish is completely cooked. After cooking the fish for 6-7 minutes. Turn off the heat, give it a final stir and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":7,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":7,"flame":2}'),('5d5a31b424ade8297f194ad7','5d5a30d924ade8297f194ad5',1,'Boil Potatoes(p1)','To boil the Potatoes, Wash the 3 nos medium sized potatoes well in water. Take a pressure cooker and add washed potatoes into it. Add 1 teaspoon salt and 3 cups water into it, enough to cover the potatoes. Close the pressure cooker and cook on high flame till one whistle. After one whistle, reduce the flame to low and continue cooking for 8 minutes and then turn off the flame. Keep the cooker aside and let the pressure release naturally. While the potatoes are boiling, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":8,"flame":3}'),('5d5a346cf845a829dca11446','5d5a30d924ade8297f194ad5',2,'Make dough(p2)','To make the dough,take 2 cups of wheat flour in a bowl. Add 1/2 teaspoon salt and mix 3/4 cup water slowly to knead a smooth dough.Add more water if required. Knead the dough for 2-3 minutes until it is soft.Then cover the dough with a plate or wet cloth and keep aside for 30 mins.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('5d5a3ce2acc6496253ae8259','5d5a30d924ade8297f194ad5',3,'Chopping(p3)','Finely chop 1/4 cup onion, 2 nos green chilies, 2  fresh coriander leaves, and grate 1 inch piece of ginger. Once the potatoes are boiled, release the pressure from the cooker using a spoon, take out the potatoes and peel off the skin.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),
('5d5a4b05acc6496253ae825c','5d5a30d924ade8297f194ad5',4,'Make Potato mixture(p4)','Take the boiled and peeled potatoes in a bowl and mash them with a potato masher or a fork. To the mashed potatoes add 2 teaspoon chopped green chili, 2 tablespoon chopped coriander leaves,1 inch piece grated ginger, and 1/4 cup finely chopped onion,1/2 teaspoon salt, 1/2 teaspoon red chili powder, 2 teaspoon dry mango powder,1 teaspoon anardana powder, 1/2 teaspoon cumin powder and 1/2 teaspoon garam masala powder and mix everything together and make sure the potato mixture is well combined.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('5d5a4e0624ade8297f194adc','5d5a30d924ade8297f194ad5',5,'Make Paratha(m1)','Heat a griddle or tawa on medium flame. Next, take the dough and knead it once again and divide it into 4 equal portions and make equal sized balls. Take one dough ball, dust some flour and roll it into a 4 inch circle. Take ball sized potato mixture and place it in the middle of the rolled out circle, bring the edges together to seal it, remove the extra dough if any. The filling should be approximately the same size as the dough ball. Press the dough slightly, dust and roll it once again. Roll it gently to make it into a 6 inch size paratha. Make sure you roll the dough out evenly so that the filling is equally distributed to all sides and edges of the dough.  
INSERT INTO catalog_recipe_steps VALUES
('5e969f9a01682d9fca89ae1e','5e6b5c36378bf22ba4231852',4,'P2: Prepare the Batter','To prepare the batter for Medu Vada, after refrigerating the prepared urad dal, add 1/4 teaspoon of salt, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions and 1 chopped green chili along with 8 nos chopped curry leaves. Mix it well and set it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e969fc601682d9fca89ae1f','5e6b5c36378bf22ba4231852',5,'M1: Make the Vada','To make Medu Vada, heat 1.5 cups of cooking oil in a Kadai over medium-high flame for 2-3 minutes. Next, apply some water over a small piece of banana leaf, and carefully place a small ball-sized portion of the batter over it. Then, gently press it to slightly flatten it and make a small hole in the center as shown. Next, carefully drop it into the hot oil and deep fry it over medium flame for 4-5 minutes until it turns golden and crips. Then, take it out onto a plate and serve. Make the rest of the vadas similarly.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96a0ac4d5574fef5a830ab','5e6b571fa04de0b99a3002f7',1,'P1: Prepare Ingredients','For Kanchipuram idli, wash 6 nos curry leaves well with water. Next, crush 6 nos cashews coarsely.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96a10d01682d9fca89ae21','5e6b571fa04de0b99a3002f7',2,'P2: Prepare the Batter','To prepare the batter for Kanchipuram idli, pour 2 cups of readymade idli batter in a large mixing bowl. Add 1/4 cup of water and mix it well to adjust the consistency of the batter. Next, to prepare the tempering, heat 2 teaspoons of gingelly oil in a small tempering pan over medium flame for a minute. Add 1/4 teaspoon of cumin seeds, 1/4 teaspoon of crushed black peppercorns and 1/4 teaspoon of hing followed by 6 crushed cashew nuts. Saute it over low flame for 1 to 2 mins. Next, add 6 nos curry leaves and mix it well. Turn off the flame and add the tempering to the idli batter.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96a1114d5574fef5a830ac','5e6b571fa04de0b99a3002f7',3,'P3: Prepare the Batter','Next, add 1/2 teaspoon of ginger powder along with 1/4 teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Then set the batter aside. Next, slightly heat a small piece of banana leaf over a direct flame as shown. Then fold it and place it inside a small bowl as shown and brush it with 1/4 teaspoon of gingelly oil using an oil brush. Prepare the rest of the idli bowls similarly.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e96a1ce01682d9fca89ae22','5e6b571fa04de0b99a3002f7',4,'M1: Make Idli','To make Kanchipuram idli, pour a ladle full of the prepared idli batter into the lined bowls. Then carefully place it into the steamer. Cover it with a lid and allow it to steam for 20 minutes. While the idlis are steaming please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96a1ce01682d9fca89ae23','5e6b571fa04de0b99a3002f7',5,'M2: Make Idli','After simmering the Kanchipuram idli, take off the lid and insert a toothpick inside an idli to check if it is cooked through. The toothpick should come out clean. Then carefully take the idlis out of the steamer and server.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('5e96a3615decc44971684d73','5e69e04ea5f34a91db916323',1,'P1: Make Idli','For Masala Idli, you may use leftover Idlies or make fresh ones with a ready-made idli batter. Pour the idli batter into the cavities of the greased idli plate. Next, carefully place it inside the steamer and cover it with a lid. Allow the idlis to steam for 12 minutes. After steaming the idlis, remove the lid of the steamer and carefully take out the idli plate. Gently, take out the idlis from the plate and serve.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96a38801682d9fca89ae25','5e69e04ea5f34a91db916323',2,'P2: Prep Ingredients','For Masala Idli, slice 6 nos idlis into long and thick slices as shown. Next, wash 8 nos curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96a3e45decc44971684d74','5e69e04ea5f34a91db916323',3,'M1: Cook Masala Idli','To make Masala Idli, heat a teaspoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add a teaspoon of cumin seeds and a teaspoon of mustard seeds. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 8 curry leaves and saute it for a minute. Then, add 6 nos sliced idlis and mix it well with the tempering. Saute and fry the idli over medium flame for 2-3 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e96a413b431d12afe583c56','5e69e04ea5f34a91db916323',4,'M2: Cook Masala Idli','Next, add half a teaspoon of sambar powder, 1/4 teaspoon of red chili powder, 1/4 teaspoon of dry mango powder and half a teaspoon of salt. Mix it well and fry the idlis over medium-low flame for 5-6 minutes until it turns crisp and slightly golden. Then, turn off the flame and take it out onto a plate. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e96a542b431d12afe583c57','5e69d272a5f34a91db916320',1,'P1: Roast Oats','To roast the rolled oats for Oats Idli, add half a cup of rolled oats to a pan. Saute and dry roast it over medium flame for 5-6 minutes until it turns crisp and slightly golden. Then, turn off the flame and allow it to cool down completely. While it is cooling down, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e96a56f5decc44971684d75','5e69d272a5f34a91db916320',2,'P2: Prep Ingredients','For Oats Idli, wash, peel and grate 1/4 cup of carrot. Wash and finely chop 1 nos green chili. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash 6 nos curry leaves. Next, after the roasted oats cool down, transfer it to a blender jar and blend it well into a fine powder. Next, grease an idli plate with a teaspoon of cooking oil using an oil brush.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96a5a65decc44971684d76','5e69d272a5f34a91db916320',3,'M1: Cooking','For Oats Idli, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add 1/4 teaspoons of mustard seeds, 1/4 teaspoon of urad dal 1/4 teaspoon of chana dal and 1/4 teaspoon of cumin seeds followed by 6 nos curry leaves. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Then, add 1/4 teaspoon of ginger paste along with 1 nos chopped green chili and saute it for a minute.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e96a5cd5decc44971684d77','5e69d272a5f34a91db916320',4,'M2: Cooking','Next, add 1/4 cup of grated carrots followed by 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder and mix it well. Stir and fry the carrot over medium flame for 2 minutes. Next, add 1/4 cup of semolina and mix it well. Saute and roast the semolina over medium flame for 2-3 minutes. Next, add half a cup of prepared oats powder and mix it well. Then, saute it over low flame for 4-5 minutes until it slightly changes color. Then, transfer it to a large bowl and allow it to cool down completely.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e96a5f301682d9fca89ae26','5e69d272a5f34a91db916320',5,'M3: Prepare the Batter','To prepare the batter for Oats Idli, after the prepared oats mixture cools down, add 1/4 cup of curd along with 1/4 cup of water and mix it well. Next, add a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves followed by half a teaspoon of salt and 1/4 cup of water. Mix it well to avoid any lumps. Then, set it aside for 20 minutes. While the batter is resting, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96a63501682d9fca89ae27','5e69d272a5f34a91db916320',6,'M4: Make Idli','To make Oats Idli, after resting the prepared batter, mix it well. if required add some water to adjust the consistency. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of Eno fruit salt to the batter and gently it. The batter will rise and turns slightly frothy. Add the cashew nuts to each mold of the greased plate. Then, instantly pour the prepared batter to the molds of the idli plate without further resting it. Resting the batter after adding the fruit salt will reduce the rise of the batter and idlis may not come out spongy. Then, carefully keep it in the steamer and steam the idlis for 15 minutes. After that, take it out from the steamer and gently take out the idlis. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e96a732b431d12afe583c58','5e69cc89a5f34a91db91631f',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Rava Idli, wash, peel and grate 1/4 cup of carrots. Wash, peel and finely chop a half-inch piece of ginger. Wash and finely chop 1 nos green chili. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Next, grease an idli plate with a teaspoon of cooking oil using an oil brush.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96a75d5decc44971684d78','5e69cc89a5f34a91db91631f',2,'M1:  Prepare the tempering','For Rava Idli, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add 1/4 teaspoon of mustard seeds, 1/4 teaspoon of cumin seeds, 1/4 teaspoon of chana dal and 1/4 teaspoon of hing followed by 6 nos curry leaves. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 1 nos chopped green chili along with a half-inch piece of chopped ginger and saute it over medium flame for a minute.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96a78201682d9fca89ae28','5e69cc89a5f34a91db91631f',3,'M2:  Add the semolina & roast','Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped carrot followed by 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder and mix it well. Stir and fry it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Next, add half a cup of semolina and mix it well. Keep stirring it continuously and roast the semolina over low flame for 5 minutes until it slightly changes color. Then, turn off the flame and allow it to cool down completely. While it is cooling down, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('5e96a7bd5decc44971684d79','5e69cc89a5f34a91db91631f',4,'M3: Prepare the Batter','After the semolina mixture for Rava Idli cools down, transfer it to a large bowl. Add 1/4 cup of curd followed by 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and 1/4 teaspoon of salt. Mix it well to prepare a thick batter. Next, add half a cup of water and mix it well to avoid any lumps. Then, set it aside and allow it to rest for 15 minutes. While the batter is resting, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96ad8bfe919dd663d223a9','5e69cc89a5f34a91db91631f',5,'M4: Steam the  idlis & serve','To make Rava Idli, after resting the prepared batter semolina absorbs water. Then, add about 3 tablespoons of water and mix it well to adjust the consistency of the batter. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of Eno fruit salt to the batter and gently mix the batter. The batter will rise and turns slightly frothy. Add the cashew nuts to each mold of the greased plate. Then, instantly pour the prepared batter to the molds of the idli plate without further resting it. Resting the batter after adding the fruit salt will reduce the rise of the batter and idlis may not come out spongy. Then, carefully keep it in the steamer and steam the idlis for 13 minutes. After that, take it out from the steamer and gently take out the idlis. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e96ae185decc44971684d7a','5e60e0897b824f089995fd20',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','To make Moong Dal Sundal, heat 3 cups of water in a pot, once boiling reduce the flame to low, then add 3/4 cup of green moong dal, cover the pot, and cook for 5-7 mins. After this is done, drain the excess water and keep it aside. While the dal is cooking, peel and finely chop 1/2 cup of onions, wash 8 curry leaves, wash and slit 2 green chillies, peel and grate 1 tsp of ginger, and wash and roughly chop 1 tbsp of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e96ae3cfe919dd663d223aa','5e60e0897b824f089995fd20',2,'M1: Make Sundal','To make Moong Dal Sundal, heat1 tbsp of oil in a pan and then add 1/2 tsp of mustard seeds, 1 tsp of chana dal, 1/2 tsp of urad dal, and 8 curry leaves, let this splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 1/2 cup of chopped onions, saute for 1 min, and then add 2 slit green chillies and 1 tsp of grated ginger. Saute this for 2-3 mins, once the onions are translucent, add 1/4 tsp of hing and 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder. Next, add the cooked moong dal and 1/2 tsp of salt, mix well, cover the pan with a lid and cook for 2 mins. Then, add 1/4 cup of desiccated coconut and 1 tbsp of coriander leaves, mix well, and then serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e96aeb9fe919dd663d223ab','5e60deb1a342c0f170bd9a47',1,'AP1: Soak Chickpeas','For Chickpea Sundal, soak 1 cup of chickpeas in water for 12 hours or overnight.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":720,"advanced_prep_time":720,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e96aedd5decc44971684d7b','5e60deb1a342c0f170bd9a47',2,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Chickpea Sundal, cook 1 cup of soaked chickpeas in a pressure cooker along with 1 tsp of salt on high flame for 1 whistle and then on low flame for 8 mins. Once this is complete let the pressure release naturally before you open the lid. While the chickpeas are cooking, peel and finely chop 1/2 cup of onions and wash 8 curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":4}'),('5e96af025decc44971684d7c','5e60deb1a342c0f170bd9a47',3,'M1: Make Sundal','To make Chickpea Sundal, heat 1 tbsp of oil in a pan and then add 1/2 tsp of mustard seeds, 1 tsp of urad dal, 1 tsp of chana dal, 1 broken dry red chili, and 8 curry leaves, let this splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 1/2 cup of chopped onions and saute for 2-3 mins. Once the onions are translucent, add the cup of cooked chickpeas and 1 tsp of salt, saute for 2 mins. Next, add 1/2 cup of desiccated coconut, mix well, and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96af6a5decc44971684d7d','5e60dd897b824f089995fd1f',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','To make Chana Dal Sundal, first, wash 1 cup of chana dal and then cook it in a pressure cooker with 1.5 cups of water on high flame for 1 whistle and then on low flame for 8 mins. Once this is done, allow the pressure to release naturally before you open the lid of the cooker. While the dal is cooking, wash and finely chop 1 green chilli, was 8 curry leaves, and 1/4 cup of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96af875decc44971684d7e','5e60dd897b824f089995fd1f',2,'M1: Make Sundal','For Chana Dal Sundal, heat 1 tbsp of oil in a pan and then add 1/4 tsp of hing, 1 tbsp of mustard seeds, 8 curry leaves, and 1 chopped green chilli, let this splutter for a few seconds. Next, add the cooked cup of chana dal and saute for 2 mins. Then, add 1/4 cup of desiccated coconut, 1/4 cup of coriander leaves, 1 tbsp of lime juice and 1/2 tsp of salt, saute for another 2 mins. Turn off the flame, this dish is ready to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e96b00f5decc44971684d7f','5e60dbe77b824f089995fd1e',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Green Moong Sprouts Kosambari, wash, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of cucumber. Wash, peel and grate 1/4 cup of carrots. Wash and grate 1/4 cup of cauliflower. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves. Wash and cut a lemon into halves, then squeeze a teaspoon of lemon juice. Wash and finely chop 1 nos green chili. Wash 7 curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e96b0d75decc44971684d80','5e60dbe77b824f089995fd1e',2,'M1: Mix Ingredients','To make the Green Moong Sprouts Kosambari, add 1 cup of green moong sprouts to a large mixing bowl. Add 1/4 cup of chopped cucumber 1/4 cup of grated carrot, 1/4 cup of grated cauliflower and 2 tablespoons of chopped coriander leaves. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of salt followed by a teaspoon of lemon juice and mix it well.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96b181fe919dd663d223ac','5e60dbe77b824f089995fd1e',3,'M2: Make Tadka','To make the tempering for Green Moong Sprouts Kosambari, heat a teaspoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add a 1/4  teaspoon of mustard seeds, half a teaspoon of chana dal, 1/4 teaspoon of cumin seeds and 7 nos curry leaves. Next, add 1 chopped green chili along with 1/4 teaspoon of hing. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Then, turn off the flame and add the tempering to the prepared kosambari. Mix it well and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96b31501682d9fca89ae29','5e60daaa7b824f089995fd1d',1,'P1:  Prep Ingredients','For Moroccan Carrot Salad, wash, peel and cut 1.5 cups of carrot into thick slices. Next, add 2 cups of water to a saucepan and bring it to a boil. Then, add 1/4 teaspoon of salt along with 1.5 cups of sliced carrots and let it boil over medium flame for 5 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and drain off the hot water from the blanched carrots and set it aside. While the carrots are blanching, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e96b34901682d9fca89ae2a','5e60daaa7b824f089995fd1d',2,'P2: Prep Ingredients','For Moroccan Carrot Salad, wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of fresh parsley. Peel, wash and finely chop 1 teaspoon of garlic. Wash and cut a lemon into halves, and squeeze 1.5 tablespoons of lime juice.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96b371fe919dd663d223ad','5e60daaa7b824f089995fd1d',3,'M1: Make Salad','To prepare the dressing for Moroccan Carrot Salad, in a bowl, add 2 tablespoons of chopped parsley followed by a teaspoon of chopped garlic and 1/4 teaspoon of black pepper powder. Next, add half a teaspoon of cumin powder, 1/4 teaspoon of paprika and 2 tablespoons of olive oil followed by 1.5 tablespoons of lemon juice and mix it well. Next, to make the salad, add 1.5 cups of blanched carrots to the prepared dressing and mix it well. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e96b45401682d9fca89ae2b','5e60d99da342c0f170bd9a46',1,'P1: Blanch Beetroot','For Beetroot Raita, wash, peel and grate 1 cup of beetroot. To blanch the beetroot, add the grated beetroots in a kadai along with 1/4 cup of water and 1/4 teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Cover it with a lid and allow it to boil over medium flame for 10 minutes. While the beetroot is boiling, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e96b51a01682d9fca89ae2c','5e60d99da342c0f170bd9a46',2,'P2: Prep Ingredients','For Beetroot Raita, grate 1/4 cup of fresh coconut using a grater. Wash and slit 1 nos green chili. Wash and peel a half-inch piece of ginger. Wash 7 nos curry leaves. Next, to make the coconut paste, add 1/4 cup of grated coconut to a blender jar. Add half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, half a teaspoon of cumin seeds and 1 slit green chili along with a half-inch piece of ginger. Add 1/4 cup of water and blend it well into a smooth paste.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96b6ee01682d9fca89ae2d','5e60d99da342c0f170bd9a46',3,'M1: Cooking','To make the Beetroot Raita, add the prepared coconut paste to the simmered beetroots and mix it well. Add some water if required to adjust the consistency and allow it to cook over medium flame for 7 minutes. Keep stirring in between. While the beetroot is cooking, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":7,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e96b75f5decc44971684d81','5e60d99da342c0f170bd9a46',4,'M2: Adding Curd','After simmering the beetroot for Beetroot Raita, mix it well and turn off the flame. Then, add 1/4 cup of curd followed by half a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Make sure to add the curd only while the flame is off, or it might split.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96b788fe919dd663d223ae','5e60d99da342c0f170bd9a46',5,'M3: Make Tadka','To make the tempering for Beetroot Raita, heat half a teaspoon of coconut oil in a small tempering pan over medium flame for a minute. Add half a teaspoon of mustard seeds followed by 1 nos dry red chili and 7 nos curry leaves. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Then, turn off the flame and add the tempering instantly over the prepared chutney. Mix it well and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e96b82e5decc44971684d82','5e60d5e8a342c0f170bd9a45',1,'P1: Soak Rice','For Aloo Dum Biryani, wash and soak 1 cup of basamati rice in 2 cups of water for 30 minutes. Next, soak half a teaspoon of saffron on 1/4 cup of milk for 15 minutes. While the rice is soaking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":30,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":30,"flame":0}'),('5e96b852fe919dd663d223af','5e60d5e8a342c0f170bd9a45',2,'P2: Fry Potatoes','To fry the potatoes for Aloo Dum Biryani, wash and peel 1 cup of baby potatoes. Next, heat  2 tablespoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Next, add 1 cup of baby potatoes to the hot oil. Saute and fry the potatoes over medium-high flame for 5-6 minutes until golden brown. Then, turn off the flame and take it out onto a plate.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96b8775decc44971684d83','5e60d5e8a342c0f170bd9a45',3,'P3: Make the Marinate','To make the mint-coriander paste for Aloo Dum Biryani, wash and roughly chop 1/4 cup of coriander leaves. Wash and roughly chop 1/4 cup of mint leaves. Wash and peel a 1-inch piece of ginger. Peel and wash 3 nos cloves of garlic. Wash and slit 2 nos green chilies. Next, to a blender jar, add 1/4 cup of chopped mint leaves, 1/4 cup of chopped coriander leaves and 3 cloves of garlic along with a 1-inch piece of ginger and 1 slit green chili. Add 1/4 cup of water and blend it well into a smooth paste.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96b8ad5decc44971684d84','5e60d5e8a342c0f170bd9a45',4,'P4: Marinate the Potatoes','To marinate the baby potatoes for Aloo Dum Biryani, in a large mixing bowl, add the prepared masala paste along with half a cup of curd. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of coriander powder, 1/4 teaspoon of red chili powder and 3/4 teaspoon of Kasuri methi followed by a tablespoon of biryani masala. Squeeze a tablespoon of lemon juice into this and add half a teaspoon of salt. Mix it well and prepare the marinade. Next, add the fried baby potatoes and coat it well with the marinade. Then set it aside for 30 minutes. While the potatoes are marinating, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":30,"flame":0}'),('5e96b8defe919dd663d223b0','5e60d5e8a342c0f170bd9a45',5,'P5: Prep Ingredients','For Aloo Dum Biryani, peel, wash and finely slice 3/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes.  To fry the onions, heat 2 tablespoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add 1/4 cup of chopped onions and fry it over medium-high flame for 6-7 minutes until it turns crisp and golden brown. After that, turn off the flame and take it out into a bowl and set it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e96b99401682d9fca89ae2e','5e60d5e8a342c0f170bd9a45',6,'M1: Boil Water','To boil the rice for Aloo Dum Biryani, add 6 cups of water in a deep bottom pan and heat it over medium flame. Add 2 nos green cardamoms, 3 nos cloves, a half-inch piece of cinnamon stick, and 1 nos bay leaf. Next, add 3/4 teaspoons of black peppercorns followed by half a teaspoon of salt, a teaspoon of cooking oil and 1 slit green chili. Stir it well and bring it to a boil over a high flame.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96ba0001682d9fca89ae2f','5e60d5e8a342c0f170bd9a45',7,'M2: Partially Cook the Rice','As it comes to a boil, add 1 cup of soaked basmati rice and stir it well. Then, boil the rice over medium-high flame for 3 minutes. Keep stirring it in between. Make sure not to cook the rice completely as it will be cooked later. After parboiling the rice, turn off the flame and drain off the water from it. Then, set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":3,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e96ba5501682d9fca89ae30','5e60d5e8a342c0f170bd9a45',8,'M3: Temper the Whole Spices','To make Aloo Dum Biryani, heat 2 tablespoons of ghee in a kadai over medium flame for a minute. Add 1 bay leaf, 3 cloves, 1 mace, 2 green cardamoms and 1 black cardamom followed by half-inch piece of cinnamon stick and 1 nos star anise. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of shai jeera along with 1/4 teaspoon of hing and saute it over low flame for a minute.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96ba8201682d9fca89ae31','5e60d5e8a342c0f170bd9a45',9,'M4: Cook the Onions and Tomatoes','Next, add half a cup of sliced onions followed by 3/4 teaspoon of ginger garlic paste and fry it over medium flame for 4-5 minutes until onion turns golden brown. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes and mix it well. Saute and cook the tomatoes for 4-5 minutes until tender.','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96baba01682d9fca89ae32','5e60d5e8a342c0f170bd9a45',10,'M5: Add the Marinated Potatoes','After cooking the tomatoes, add the marinated potatoes along with the marinade. Add 1/4 cup of green peas followed by half a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Then, cover it with a lid and allow it to simmer for 8 minutes until oil separates. While it is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('5e96baf001682d9fca89ae33','5e60d5e8a342c0f170bd9a45',11,'M6: Add the Rice','After simmering the potatoes for Aloo Dum Biryani, take off the lid and stir it well. Masala releases the oil. Then, add 2 tablespoons of fried onions followed by 1 cup of parboiled basmati rice and spread it evenly over the prepared masala. Next, add 2 tablespoons of chopped coriander and 2 tablespoons of chopped mint leaves. Sprinkle a tablespoon of biryani masala along with 1/4 cup of soaked saffron milk. Add 2 tablespoons of fried onions on top and then cover it with a sheet of aluminium foil. Cover it with a lid and seal it tight so there is no room for the air to escape. Then, simmer the biryani for 20 minutes. While the Biryani is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":20,"flame":2}'),('5e96bb1601682d9fca89ae34','5e60d5e8a342c0f170bd9a45',12,'M7: Final Touches','After simmering the Aloo Dum Biryani, take off the lid and remove the foil. Then, gently mix the rice with light hands and take it out onto a serving plate. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96be6ffe919dd663d223b3','5e60cfc5a342c0f170bd9a44',1,'P1: Soak Rice','For Navratan Pulao, wash and soak 1 cup of basmati rice in 2 cups of water for 20 minutes. Next, in a small bowl, add 1/4 teaspoon of saffron and soak it in 2 tablespoons of milk for 15 minutes. While the rice and saffron are soaking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96be725decc44971684d88','5d7f23e41710a053f6cd1319',1,'P1: Soak Rice','Soak basmati rice in 2 cups of water for 20 mins. Wash and finely chop coriander.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96be9f01682d9fca89ae37','5e60cfc5a342c0f170bd9a44',2,'P2: Prep Ingredients','For Navratan Pulao, peel, wash and finely slice 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and slit 2 nos green chilies. Wash, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of carrots. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of green capsicum. Wash, peel and dice 1/4 cup of potatoes.  Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of beans.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e96bea101682d9fca89ae38','5d7f23e41710a053f6cd1319',2,'M1: Pressure cook the rice','Heat ghee in a pressure cooker and then add cumin seeds, saute this for a few seconds. next, add the soaked rice and saute for 1 min then add 2 cups of water and a pinch of salt. Give it a nice stir and then cover it with the lid. Cook this on high flame for 1 whistle and then on low flame for 8 mins. Once this is done let the pressure cooker cool completely before you take off the lid.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96bec3fe919dd663d223b4','5e60cfc5a342c0f170bd9a44',3,'P3: Prep Ingredients','Next, wash and cut 1/4 cup of cauliflower into small florets. wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves. Deseed 3 nos dates and roughly slice it. Cut 1/4 cup of paneer into small cubes.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96bee05decc44971684d89','5d7f23e41710a053f6cd1319',3,'M2: Garnish & serve','Once the cooker has cooled take off the lid and gently mix the rice. Garnish it with coriander leaves and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":1,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96befffe919dd663d223b5','5e60cfc5a342c0f170bd9a44',4,'P4: Cook Rice','To cook the rice for Navaratan Pulao, add the soaked basmati rice to a pressure cooker along with 2 cups of water. Then, cover it with a lid and pressure cook the rice over a high flame until one whistle. After that, reduce the flame to low and continue to simmer it for another 8 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the rice is cooking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96bf2601682d9fca89ae39','5e60cfc5a342c0f170bd9a44',5,'P5: Fry Nuts','To fry the nuts for Navratan Pulao, heat 2 tablespoons of ghee in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add 7 nos cashews, 10 nos almonds, 3 nos walnuts, 2 tablespoons of raisins and 3 nos sliced dates followed by a teaspoon of pumpkin seeds and 10 nos pistachios. Next, add 1/4 cup of cubed paneer and mix it well. Saute and fry the nuts over medium-low flame for 4-5 minutes until golden brown. Then, turn off the flame and set it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e96bf465decc44971684d8a','5d7f4ce909e1dd5a7f4238dd',1,'P1: Chop & prep the ingredients','Finely chop onions, tomatoes, peel garlic, and wash curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96bf85fe919dd663d223b6','5d7f4ce909e1dd5a7f4238dd',2,'M1:  Prepare the chutney mixture','Heat cooking oil in a pan, then add chana dal, urad dal, dry red chilli, and saute for a few seconds. Next, add onions and garlic, saute this for 2-3 mins. Once the onions are slightly golden, add tomatoes and cook them for 3-4 mins stirring occasionally.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":3,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96bf95fe919dd663d223b7','5e60cfc5a342c0f170bd9a44',6,'M1: Cooking','To make Navaratan Pulao, heat 1 tablespoon of cooking oil in a Kadai over medium flame for a minute. Add 1 teaspoon of cumin seeds, a 1-inch piece of cinnamon stick, 1 nos bay leaf and 3 nos green cardamoms followed by 3 nos cloves and half a teaspoon of crushed black peppercorns. Saute it over low flame for a minute. Next, add 1/4 cup of sliced onions followed by a teaspoon of ginger-garlic paste. Saute and fry the onions over medium flame until onions turn golden brown.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96bfb701682d9fca89ae3a','5e60cfc5a342c0f170bd9a44',7,'M2: Cook Vegetables','After frying the onions, add 1/4 cup of chopped carrots, 1/4 cup of chopped potatoes, 1/4 cup of chopped beans and 2 tablespoons of sweet corn kernels. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped green capsicum, 1/4 cup of chopped cauliflower florets, 1/4 cup of green peas and 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes followed by 2 tablespoons of chopped coriander leaves. Stir and fry the vegetables over high flame for 2-3 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96bfd8fe919dd663d223b8','5e60cfc5a342c0f170bd9a44',8,'M3: Cooking','Next, add 2 tablespoons of water along with half a teaspoon of salt and half a teaspoon of garam masala. Mix it well and cover it with a lid and simmer the vegetables for 5 minutes until tender. While the vegetables are simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e96bfdbfe919dd663d223b9','5d7f4ce909e1dd5a7f4238dd',3,'M2: Blend the chutney mixture to a smooth chutney','Once the tomatoes are tender, turn off the flame and let the mixture cool completely. Once cool, transfer it to a blending jar and blend into a smooth chutney.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96c002fe919dd663d223ba','5e60cfc5a342c0f170bd9a44',9,'M4: Add Rice','After simmering the vegetables for Navratan Pulao, take off the lid and stir it well. Next, add the cooked basmati rice followed by half a teaspoon of salt and gently mix it. Then, add the fried nut and paneer cubes. Next, sprinkle 2 tablespoons of soaked saffron milk over the rice and cover it with a lid. Simmer the pulao for 10 minutes. While the pulao is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('5e96c00efe919dd663d223bb','5d7f4ce909e1dd5a7f4238dd',4,'M3: Prepare the tempering & add it to the chutney','Make a tadka, heat cooking oil in a tempering pan and then add mustard seeds, urad dal, curry leaves, and saute this for a minute. Immediately pour it over the chutney, give it a quick stir and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96c0255decc44971684d8b','5e60cfc5a342c0f170bd9a44',10,'M5: Final Touches','After simmering the Navratan Pulao, take off the lid and gently mix the rice with light hands. Then, take it out into a serving bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96c09efe919dd663d223bc','5d7f5d0e1710a053f6cd131c',1,'P1: Chop & prep the ingredients','Finely chop onions, carrots, and beans. Slit green chilies, grate fresh coconut and wash curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e96c0d501682d9fca89ae3b','5d7f5d0e1710a053f6cd131c',2,'M1: Temper the oil & fry the onions','Heat cooking oil in a pan and then add mustard seeds, urad dal, chana dal, curry leaves, and dry red chili. Saute this for a few seconds and then add onions and let them cook for 2-3 mins.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96c0fc01682d9fca89ae3c','5d7f5d0e1710a053f6cd131c',3,'M2: Simmer the carrot & beans','Once the onions are slightly golden, add the carrots, beans, turmeric powder, and salt. Saute this on high flame for 2 mins. Next, add 1/4 cup of water and cover the pan with a lid. Let this simmer for 10 mins.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96c125fe919dd663d223bd','5d7f5d0e1710a053f6cd131c',4,'M3: Garnish & serve','After simmering for 10 mins, remove the lid, add grated coconut and mix well. Cook on high flame for another minute and then turn off the flame. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e96c14201682d9fca89ae3d','5e60ae387b824f089995fd13',1,'AP1: Soak Chana Dal','For Bengali Chana Dal, wash and soak 1 cup of chana dal in 2 cups of water for 2 hours. While the dal is soaking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":120,"advanced_prep_time":120,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96c18cfe919dd663d223be','5d7f642909e1dd5a7f4238df',1,'P1: Soak the lentil & prep the ingredients','Soak toor dal in 2 cups of water for 20 mins. Soak 1 tsp of tamarind in 2 Tbsp of water. Roughly chop onions and tomatoes. Finely chop garlic, slit green chili, and wash curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e96c1c65decc44971684d8c','5d7f642909e1dd5a7f4238df',2,'M1: Pressure cook the dal','Cook toor dal in a pressure cooker along with tomatoes, tamarind extract, onions, turmeric powder, Kashmiri red chili powder, green chili, cooking oil, and 2 cups of water. Cook this on high flame for 2 whistles and then cook on low flame for 8 mins. Once this is done set the cooker aside to cool down completely before you open the lid.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96c1edfe919dd663d223bf','5d7f642909e1dd5a7f4238df',3,'M2: Prepare the tempering','Heat cooking oil in a deep pan, then add garlic and saute for 1-2 mins until golden. Next, add mustard seeds, urad dal, cumin seeds, hing, dry red chili, and curry leaves. Fry this for 1 min.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96c2225decc44971684d8d','5d7f642909e1dd5a7f4238df',4,'M3: Simmer the dal with  tempering. Garnish & serve','Take off the pressure cookers lid and whisk the dal and then transfer it to the pan with the tadka. Simmer the dal in this pan for 2 mins and then turn off the flame. Garnish with coriander leaves and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e96c2e65decc44971684d8e','5d7f670009e1dd5a7f4238e0',1,'P1: Soak tamarind & prep the ingredients','Soak 1Tbsp of tamarind in 1 cup of water for 15 mins. Chop tomatoes and coriander leaves, slit green chilies, wash curry leaves, and crush the black peppercorns.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96c311fe919dd663d223c0','5d7f670009e1dd5a7f4238e0',2,'M1: Simmer the tomatoes','In a saucepan, add tomatoes, green chili, curry leaves, and turmeric powder. Next, add the tamarind extract, salt, and bring this to a boil. Cover with a lid and let it simmer for 8 mins.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e96c3375decc44971684d8f','5d7f670009e1dd5a7f4238e0',3,'M2: Add water & boil the rasam','Once the tomatoes are tender, take off the lid and add 2 cups of water. Let this boil for 2 mins, add black pepper and mix it well. Turn off the flame.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96c3675decc44971684d90','5d7f670009e1dd5a7f4238e0',4,'M3: Prepare the tempering & add it to the rasam','Heat oil in a tempering pan and fry mustard seeds, cumin seeds, hing, dry red chili, and curry leaves. Let this splutter for a few seconds then immediately pour it into the rasam. Garnish with coriander leaves, give it a quick stir, and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96c3e501682d9fca89ae3e','5d7f694509e1dd5a7f4238e1',1,'P1: Rinse the rise','Wash 1 cup of rice well with the water.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96c40601682d9fca89ae3f','5d7f694509e1dd5a7f4238e1',2,'M1: Pressure cook the rice','Cook the rice in a pressure cooker with 2 cups of water and a pinch of salt. Cook on high flame for 1 whistle and then cook on low flame for 8 mins. Let the pressure cooker cool down completely before you take off the lid and serve the rice.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96c5d0fe919dd663d223c1','5e19672e985ffca18ae8fa59',1,'P1: Chop & prep the ingredients','Finely chop onions, finely slice the ivy gourd and green chilies, and wash curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e96c602fe919dd663d223c2','5e19672e985ffca18ae8fa59',2,'M1: Temper the oil & fry the onions','Heat oil in a pan and then add the chana dal, urad dal, mustard seeds, and hing, Saute for a few seconds. Next, add the green chilies and saute for a few seconds. Then add the onions and curry leaves, and cook them for 2-3 mins.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96c62cfe919dd663d223c3','5e19672e985ffca18ae8fa59',3,'M2: Simmer the ivy gourds','Once the onions are slightly translucent, add the ivy gourd, mix well, cover the pan, and cook for 15-20 mins.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":20,"flame":2}'),('5e96c67101682d9fca89ae40','5e19672e985ffca18ae8fa59',4,'M3: Season & stir-fry the ivy gourds','Next, add turmeric powder, red chili powder, coriander powder, and salt, mix well. Once the vegetables are cooked, add the Andra masala powder, mix well, and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96c70ffe919dd663d223c4','5e183f43057fd3f6fc80ee50',2,'M1: Make the cold coffee','Put ice cubes in a serving glass and then pour the coffee in followed by milk, powdered sugar, and vanilla essence. Stir this well and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96c7935decc44971684d91','5e19695c4f28558c29df63e9',1,'P1: Chop & prep the ingredients','Wash and chop cauliflower into small florets. Peel and julienne ginger, crush the black peppercorns, and taw frozen peas.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e96c7f35decc44971684d92','5e19695c4f28558c29df63e9',2,'M1: Fry and simmer cauliflower florets with green peas','For Gobi Matar Sabzi, heat 1 tbsp of ghee in a kadai and then add 1/4 tsp of cumin seeds and let them splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 1/2 cup of cauliflower, 1/4 tsp of salt, 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder and mix well. Sprinkle 2 tbsp of water and cover the pan with a lid and cook for 3 mins over low flame. Next, add 1/2 cup of green peas, mix well, cover the pan and cook for another 5 mins. While it simmers, please move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96c8975decc44971684d93','5e196c174f28558c29df63ec',1,'P1: Chop fenugreek leaves & potatoes','Clean, wash and chop fenugreek leaves. Wash baby potatoes and cut into quarters. Wash, peel, and chop onions and ginger.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96c8bdfe919dd663d223c5','5e196c174f28558c29df63ec',2,'M1: Fry the onions','In a pan, heat mustard oil and add cumin seeds, ginger, and saute it for 1-2 mins. Next, add onions and fry them for 3-4 mins.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96c8ea01682d9fca89ae41','5e196c174f28558c29df63ec',3,'M2: Simmer the potatoes','Once the onions become translucent, add salt, red chili powder, and saute well. Then, add the baby potatoes and cover the pan to let them cook. Stir occasionally to avoid burning.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e96c92afe919dd663d223c6','5e196c174f28558c29df63ec',4,'M3: Add the fenugreek leaves & simmer the sabzi','Next, take off the lid and add the chopped fenugreek leaves. Mix it well, cover with the lid, and let it cook for 15 mins.  Stir occasionally while cooking. Take off the lid and cook on high flame for 1-2 mins. Turn off the heat and serve the dish.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e96ca7afe919dd663d223c7','5e196e2e057fd3f6fc80ee6b',1,'P1: Boil the potatoes & prep the ingredients','To make masala dosa, first, peel and roughly dice 2 potatoes. Next boil 1 cup of water, once boiling, add 2 chopped potatoes and let it cook for 10 mins. While the potatoes are cooking prep the other vegetables. Next, peel and finely chop 1 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1 green chili. Wash and roughly chop 1 tbsp of coriander leaves. Peel 6 cloves of garlic. Wash 6 curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96cab501682d9fca89ae43','5e196e2e057fd3f6fc80ee6b',2,'M1: Make the chutney','To make masala dosa, first make the chutney, in a pan heat 2 tsp of oil, and then add 2 tbsp of chana dal, 1 tsp of cumin seeds and saute for 1 min. Then, add 1/2 cup of onions, 6 cloves of garlic, 15 dry red chilies, and saute for 2-3 mins. Once the onions have browned, turn off the heat and let the mixture cool down completely. Next, add the cooked ingredients to a blending jar with 1/2 tsp of salt and 1/4 cup of water. Blend this into a smooth chutney, set this aside, and move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96cadffe919dd663d223c8','5e196e2e057fd3f6fc80ee6b',3,'M2: Prepare the potato stuffing','Next, prepare the aloo filling, in the same pan heat 1 tbsp of oil and then add 1/4 tsp of mustard seeds, 1/4 tsp of urad dal, 1/4 tsp of cumin seeds, 1/4 tsp of hing, 6 curry leaves, and let this splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 1/2 cup of onions, 1 chopped green chili, and saute this for 2-3 mins. Then, add 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder, 1 tsp of salt, and mix well. To this, add 2 boiled potatoes, mix well, and with a masher, lightly mash the potatoes into smaller pieces. Garnish with 1 tbsp of coriander leaves and then keep the filling aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96cb0a5decc44971684d95','5e196e2e057fd3f6fc80ee6b',4,'M3: Make the masala dosa','Next, assemble the masala dosa, heat a tawa for 1 min and then pour 1 ladle of dosa batter on the tawa and spread it in a circular manner to make the dosa shape. Then, drizzle 1/2 tsp of oil around the edges and center of the dosa. Let it cook on one side for 2 mins and then flip the dosa and let it cook for another 2 mins. Flip the dosa again and spread 1 tsp of chutney in the center, then place 2 tbsp of the potato filling on one half, and drizzle 1 tsp of ghee over the whole dosa. Close the dosa and take it off the tawa and onto a plate to serve. Make the desired amount of dosa and Enjoy.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96cb8cfe919dd663d223c9','5e19714c057fd3f6fc80ee6e',1,'P1: Peel & slice the ripe bananas','For Chocolate Banana Smoothie, wash, peel and roughly slice 2 nos ripe banana.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e96cbcd01682d9fca89ae44','5e19714c057fd3f6fc80ee6e',2,'M1: Blend the bananas with milk & other ingredients to make a smoothie','To make Chocolate Banana Smoothie, add 2 nos sliced banana to a blender jar, followed by 3 tablespoons of cocoa powder and 2 tablespoons of honey. Add 2 teaspoons of vanilla essence along with 1.5 cups of chilled milk and blend it smooth. Pour the prepared smoothie into glasses and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96cd73fe919dd663d223ca','5e1972d94f28558c29df63ed',1,'P1:  Prepare the Coffee  Decoction','To prepare the coffee base for Chocolate Cold Coffee, first, add 3/4 cup of water to a saucepan and bring it to a rolling boil. After it has come to a boil, turn off the flame and pour it into a large mixing bowl. Add 1 tablespoon of instant coffee granules to the hot water and mix it well until it is completely dissolved. Set the prepared coffee base aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96cd9ffe919dd663d223cb','5e1972d94f28558c29df63ed',2,'M1: Make the cold coffee','To make the Chocolate Cold Coffee, first, add some ice cubes to a mason jar followed by 1 tablespoon of chocolate syrup. Next, add 1/4 cup of the prepared coffee base along with 1 cup of boiled and chilled milk. Add a teaspoon of powdered sugar along with a teaspoon of cocoa powder and mix it well. Serve. Make another glass of Chocolate Cold Coffee similarly.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96cf07fe919dd663d223cc','5e1974824f28558c29df63f0',1,'M1: Boil the tea leaves with chai masala','To make the masala tea- Heat 1 cup water on medium flame for a minute, add 1 teaspoon tea masala powder into the hot water, and give it stir. Next, add 2 teaspoon sugar and 2 teaspoon tea leaves into it and bring it to a boil on medium flame until the flavor comes out. After it has come to a boil, add 1 cup milk into it, give it a stir and boil it on low flame for 1 minute. Then turn off the heat and strain the tea in a cup using a tea strainer. Serve','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96d036fe919dd663d223cd','5e19757c057fd3f6fc80ee70',1,'P1: Slice the bananas','For Banana Shake, wash, peel and roughly slice 2 nos banana.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e96d0685decc44971684d97','5e19757c057fd3f6fc80ee70',2,'M1: Blend the banana with milk & other ingredients to make the shake','To make the Banana Shake, add 2 nos sliced bananas into a blender jar. Add 1.5 cups of milk followed by 1/4 teaspoon of cinnamon powder. Next, add 2 teaspoons of honey and blend it smooth. Pour the prepared banana shake into glasses and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96d1115decc44971684d98','5e19760d057fd3f6fc80ee72',1,'M1: Make the ginger flavored tea decoction','To make Adrak Chai, heat 2 cups of water in a saucepan over medium flame for a minute. Grate a 1-inch piece of ginger into it. Next, add 2 nos green cardamoms followed by 1/2 inch piece of cinnamon stick and allow it to boil over medium-high flame for 5 minutes and let the ginger and whole spices infuse the flavor into the water. After boiling it, add 3 teaspoons of tea powder and continue to boil it for another 5 minutes and keep stirring in between. While the tea is boiling, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96d14701682d9fca89ae46','5e19760d057fd3f6fc80ee72',2,'M2: Stir in milk & sugar, and simmer tea. Strain & serve','After preparing the tea decoction for Adrak Chai, stir it well and add half a cup of milk into it. Add 2 teaspoons of sugar and continue to boil it for another 2 minutes, until all the flavor is infused in the tea. Keep stirring in between. As the tea gets the right amount of color and flavor, turn off the flame and strain the prepared tea into cups. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96d79d5decc44971684d99','5e60ae387b824f089995fd13',2,'P1: Cook the Dal','To cook the dal for Bengali Chana Dal, add 1 cup of soaked chana dal to a pressure cooker along with 2 cups of water. Add half a teaspoon of salt along with 2 nos bay leaves. Then, cover it with a lid and pressure cook the dal over a high flame until two whistles. After that, reduce the flame to low and continue to simmer it for another 5 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the dal is cooking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96d7bffe919dd663d223d0','5e60ae387b824f089995fd13',3,'P2: Prep Ingredients','For Bengali Chana Dal, chop 2 tablespoons of coconut into small dices. Wash and slit 3 nos green chilies. To make the spice for the dal, in a small bowl, add a teaspoon of ginger paste. Add half a teaspoon of cumin powder, half a teaspoon of coriander powder and 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder. Add 3 tablespoons of water and mix it well to prepare a solution of spices.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e96d7eefe919dd663d223d1','5e60ae387b824f089995fd13',4,'M1: Fry Coconut','To make Bengali Chana Dal, heat a tablespoon of mustard oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add 2 tablespoons of chopped coconut pieces and fry it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes until golden. Then, take it out into a bowl and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96d84901682d9fca89ae47','5e60ae387b824f089995fd13',5,'M2: Temper the Whole Spices','Next, to the same oil, add 2 dry red chilies and saute it over low flame for a minute. Next, add 3 green cardamoms followed by 3 cloves and a 1-inch piece of cinnamon stick. Next, add half a teaspoon of cumin seeds and 1/4 teaspoon of hing. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Next, add the prepared solution of spices and mix it well. Saute and cook the masala over medium-low flame for 5-6 minutes until the raw smell of spices fades away.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96d87701682d9fca89ae48','5e60ae387b824f089995fd13',6,'M3: Cooking the Dal','After cooking the masala, add 3 nos slit green chilies and fry the masala over medium flame until oil separates. Then, add the prepared chana dal followed by half a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Then, simmer the dal over medium flame for 8 minutes, until the dal thickens. While the dal is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e96d89f5decc44971684d9a','5e60ae387b824f089995fd13',7,'M4: Cooking the Dal','After simmering the Bengali Chana Dal, add half a teaspoon of sugar and mix it well. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala followed by half a teaspoon of ghee and 2 tablespoons of fried coconut pieces. Mix it well and turn off the flame. Cover the dal with a lid and let it sit for 2 minutes. Then, take it out into a serving bowl and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e96d9a55decc44971684d9b','5e60aa8ba342c0f170bd9a3e',1,'P1: Soak Dal','For Palak Chana dal, wash and soak 1 cup of chana dal in 2 cups of water for 1 hour. While the dal is soaking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":60,"advanced_prep_time":60,"timer":60,"flame":0}'),
('5e96d9d1fe919dd663d223d2','5e60aa8ba342c0f170bd9a3e',2,'P2: Prep Ingredients','For Palak Chana Dal, peel, wash and finely chop 1.5 cups of spinach leaves. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Peel, wash and finely chop 1 teaspoon of garlic. Wash, peel and finely chop a 1-inch piece of ginger. Wash and finely chop 1 green chili.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96d9fa01682d9fca89ae49','5e60aa8ba342c0f170bd9a3e',3,'M1:  Pressure Cook the Dal','To cook the dal for Palak Chana Dal, add 1 cup of soaked chana dal to a pressure cooker along with 2 cups of water. Then, cover it with a lid and pressure cook the dal over a high flame until two whistles. After that, reduce the flame to low and continue to simmer it for another 5 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the dal is cooking, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96da2afe919dd663d223d3','5e60aa8ba342c0f170bd9a3e',4,'M2: Temper Spices','To make Palak Chana Dal, heat a tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add 1 teaspoon of cumin seeds, 1/4 teaspoon of hing and 1 nos dry red chili. Saute an allow it to splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 1 teaspoon of chopped garlic followed by a 1-inch piece of chopped ginger and 1 nos chopped green chili. Saute it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96daa1fe919dd663d223d4','5e60aa8ba342c0f170bd9a3e',5,'M3: Cook the Dal','Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions and fry it over medium flame for 3-4 minutes until translucent. After frying the onions, add 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes and mix it well. Saute and cook the tomatoes over medium flame for 4-5 minutes until tender. Next, add half a teaspoon of salt along with 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder and mix it well. Then, add 1.5 cups of chopped spinach leaves and fry it with the masala for a minute. Then, cover it with a lid and simmer it for 5 minutes. While it is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e96dac0fe919dd663d223d5','5e60aa8ba342c0f170bd9a3e',6,'M4: Cook the Dal','After simmering the spinach leaves for Palak Chana Dal, take off the lid and add half a teaspoon of red chili powder followed by half a teaspoon of garam masala. Mix it well and saute the masala over low flame for a minute. Next, add the prepared chana dal and mix it well. Add about 1/4 cup of water and stir it well. Then, cover it with a lid and simmer the dal for 3 minutes. While the dal is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),
('5e96dae901682d9fca89ae4a','5e60aa8ba342c0f170bd9a3e',7,'M5: Garnish','To make the tempering for Palak Chana Dal, heat a tablespoon of butter in a pan over low flame for a minute. Add a teaspoon of paprika and saute it over low flame for a minute. Then, turn off the flame and add the tempering to the dal. Mix it well and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96e19f5decc44971684d9c','5e60a8dda342c0f170bd9a3d',1,'AP1: Soak the Dal','For Navrang Dal, in a large bowl, add 1/4 cup of green moong dal, 1/4 cup of kidney beans, 1/4 cup of black urad dal and 1/4 cup of black-eyed peas. Next, add 1/4 cup of the mix of 5 dals and soak it in 3 cups of water for 8 hours. While the dals are soaking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":480,"advanced_prep_time":480,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96e1d0fe919dd663d223d6','5e60a8dda342c0f170bd9a3d',2,'P1: Cool the Dal','To cook the Navrang Dal, add the soaked dal to a pressure cooker along with 3 cups of water. Add half a teaspoon of salt followed by 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder and mix it well. Then, cover it with a lid and pressure cook the dal over a high flame until two whistles. After that, reduce the flame to low and continue to simmer it for another 5 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the dal is cooking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96e1ff2f30df0f66c9344c','5e60a8dda342c0f170bd9a3d',3,'P2: Prep Ingredients','For Navrang Dal, peel, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Wash and 1 nos green chili. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96e2345decc44971684d9d','5e60a8dda342c0f170bd9a3d',4,'M1: Temper','For Navrang Dal, heat a teaspoon of cooking oil and a tablespoon of ghee in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add 1 nos bay leaf followed by half a teaspoon of cumin seeds and saute it over medium flame for a minute. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions and fry it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e96e2592f30df0f66c9344d','5e60a8dda342c0f170bd9a3d',5,'M2: Cooking','After frying the onions, add a teaspoon of ginger-garlic paste along with 1 nos chopped green chili and saute it over medium flame for a minute. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder followed by half a teaspoon of red chili powder and mix it well. Then, add half a cup of chopped tomatoes and mix it well. Saute and cook the tomatoes over medium for 1- 2 minutes. Then, cover it with a lid and simmer it for 2-3 minutes, until tomatoes turn tender. While the masala is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96e27b5decc44971684d9e','5e60a8dda342c0f170bd9a3d',6,'M3: Cooking','After simmering the tomatoes, take off the lid and saute the masala for a minute. Next, add half a teaspoon of coriander powder along with half a teaspoon of cumin powder and mix it well. Then, add the prepared Navrang Dal and stir it well with the masala. Then, bring it to a boil over high flame. Add half a teaspoon of salt followed by a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and mix it well. Cook the dal over medium flame for another 5 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":5,"flame":2}'),('5e96e342fe919dd663d223d7','5e60a757a342c0f170bd9a3c',1,'P1: Cook Dal','To cook the dal for Rajasthani Dal, wash half a cup of toor dal well with water. Next, rinse 1/4 cup of chana dal well with water. Rinse 1/4 cup of yellow moong dal well with water. To cook the dal add the rinsed dal to a pressure cooker along with 2 cups of water and cover it with a lid. Pressure cook the dal over a high flame until one whistle. After that, reduce the flame to low and continue to simmer it for another 8 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the dal is cooking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96e3625decc44971684d9f','5e60a757a342c0f170bd9a3c',2,'P2: Prep Ingredietns','For Rajasthani Dal, wash and finely chop half a cup of tomatoes. Wash and finely chop 1 nos green chili. Wash, peel and grate a 1-inch piece of ginger. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash 6 nos curry leaves well with water.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96e39c5decc44971684da0','5e60a757a342c0f170bd9a3c',3,'M1: Adjust the Dals Consistency','To make Rajasthani Dal, after the pressure from the cooker is released, take off the lid and mash the dal using a whisk. Next, add about half a cup of water to adjust the consistency of the dal. Bring it to a boil over a high flame. Then, turn off the flame and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":4}'),
('5e96e3bbfe919dd663d223d8','5e60a757a342c0f170bd9a3c',4,'M2: Temper Spices','To make the tempering for Rajasthani Dal, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Temper it with half a teaspoon of mustard seeds and half a teaspoon of cumin seeds. Next, add 1 nos chopped green chili, 6 nos curry leaves and 1/4 teaspoon of hing followed by a 1-inch piece of grated ginger. Saute it for a minute.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e96e3e1fe919dd663d223d9','5e60a757a342c0f170bd9a3c',5,'M3: Cooking the Dal','Next, add half a cup of chopped tomatoes and mix it well. Saute and cook the tomatoes over medium flame for 4-5 minutes until tender. After that, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder followed by 1/4 teaspoon of red chili powder and mix it well. Saute the masala over low flame for a minute. Next, add the prepared dal and mix it well. If required add about 1/4 water to adjust the consistency of the dal. Next, add half a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Then, cover it with a lid and allow it to simmer for 5 minutes. While the dal is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e96e518fe919dd663d223db','5e60a648a342c0f170bd9a3b',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Gujarati Dal, first, wash and soak 3/4 cup of toor dal in 2 cups of water for 20 minutes. Meanwhile, wash and chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Wash and slit 1 nos green chili. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash 8 nos curry leaves well with water. While the dal is soaking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96e557fe919dd663d223dc','5e60a648a342c0f170bd9a3b',2,'M1: Making Dal','To make Gujarati Dal, add 3/4 cup of soaked toor dal to a pressure cooker. Add 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes along with 2 nos pieces of kokum. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, 1/4 teaspoon of Kashmiri red chili powder, 1/4 teaspoon of coriander powder and 1/4 teaspoon of cumin powder followed by 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96e591fe919dd663d223dd','5e60a648a342c0f170bd9a3b',3,'M2: Making Dal','Next, add 1 nos green chili, half a teaspoon of ginger paste and half a teaspoon of salt along with half a teaspoon of jaggery. Next, add half a teaspoon of cooking oil followed by 1.5 cups of water and mix it well. Then, place a small bowl in the pressure cooker as shown, and add a tablespoon of peanuts into it. Then, cover the pressure cooker with a lid and pressure cook the dal over a high flame until one whistle. After that, reduce the flame to low and continue to simmer it for another 8 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the dal is cooking, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('5e96e5c02f30df0f66c9344e','5e60a648a342c0f170bd9a3b',4,'M3: Making Dal','After cooking the Gujarati Dal, take off the lid and carefully take out the peanut bowl and set it aside. Then, whisk them well until smooth. Add about half a cup of water to adjust the consistency of the dal. Add the boiled peanuts and mix it well. Then, simmer the dal for 5 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and set it aside. While the dal is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":5,"flame":1}'),('5e96e656fe919dd663d223de','5e60a648a342c0f170bd9a3b',5,'M4: Make Tadka','To make the tempering for Gujarati Dal, heat half a teaspoon of ghee in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, 1/4 teaspoon of cumin seeds, and 1/4 teaspoon of fenugreek seeds. Next, add a half-inch piece of cinnamon stick and 1 dry red chili followed by 8 curry leaves. Saute and let it splutter over medium flame for a few seconds. Then, turn off the flame and add the tempering over the prepared dal. Add 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and mix it well. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96e970fe919dd663d223e1','5e60a2e90396dd8109153a82',1,'P1: Blanch Spinach','To blanch the spinach leaves for Murgh Saagwala, wash and roughly chop 3/4 cup of spinach leaves. Then, add 3 cups of water in a saucepan and bring it to a boil over a high flame. As the water comes to a boil, add 3/4 cup of spinach leaves and dip it completely in the water. Then, boil it over medium-high flame for 2 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and take it out of the water. Then, dip the blanched spinach leaves immediately in a cold bath. This will prevent the spinach leaves from cooking further while retaining the color.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96e9ba2f30df0f66c93453','5e60a2e90396dd8109153a82',2,'P2: Prep Ingredients','For Murgh Saagwala, to make the spinach puree, transfer 3/4 cup of blanched spinach leaves to a blender jar and blend it well into a smooth puree. Next, peel, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop half a cup of tomatoes. Wash 400 grams of chicken thoroughly with water and set it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96e9da5decc44971684da1','5e60a2e90396dd8109153a82',3,'M1: Cook Onions','To make Murgh Saagwal, heat 1 tablespoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add 1/4 cup of chopped onions and fry it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until it turns translucent. After that, add a teaspoon of ginger-garlic paste and saute it for a minute.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e96e9fbfe919dd663d223e2','5e60a2e90396dd8109153a82',4,'M2: Add Masala Powders','Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, half a teaspoon of red chili powder, half a teaspoon of cumin powder and half a teaspoon of coriander powder. Mix it well and fry the masala over low flame for a minute. Next, add half a cup of chopped tomatoes along with half a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Saute and cook the tomatoes for 2-3 minutes. Then, cover it with a lid and simmer the masala for 5 minutes, until oil separates. While the masala is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96ea1bfe919dd663d223e3','5e60a2e90396dd8109153a82',5,'M3: Cook Chicken','After simmering the masala for Murg Saagwala, take off the lid and fry the masala over medium-high flame for 1-2 minutes. Next, add 400 grams of chicken pieces and mix it well with the masala. Then, fry the chicken over medium flame for 5-6 minutes, until it is no longer pink. After that, add 1/4 teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Then, cover it with a lid and simmer it for 10 minutes. While the chicken is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e96ea4bfe919dd663d223e4','5e60a2e90396dd8109153a82',6,'M4: Continue Cooking the Curry','After simmering the chicken for Murgh Saagwala, take off the lid and stir it well. Next, add half a teaspoon of garam masala followed by a teaspoon of Kasuri methi and mix it well. Then, add 3/4 cup of the prepared spinach puree and mix it well. Bring it to a boil over a high flame. After that, reduce the flame to low and cover it with a lid. Then, simmer the chicken for 10 minutes, until it is cooked through. While the chicken is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('5e96ea73fe919dd663d223e5','5e60a2e90396dd8109153a82',7,'M5: Final Touches','After simmering the Murgh Saagwala, take off the lid and stir it well. Then, turn off the flame and take it out into a serving bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96eb395decc44971684da2','5e609b86a342c0f170bd9a3a',1,'P1: Marinate the Fish','To marinate the fish fillets for Methi Machi, first wash 400 grams of basa fillets thoroughly with water and put the fillets in a large mixing bowl. Next, add a teaspoon of white pepper powder followed by half a teaspoon of salt. Squeeze a tablespoon of lemon juice into this and mix it well. Coat the fillets well with the marinade and allow it to marinate for 1 hour. While it is marinating, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":60,"advanced_prep_time":60,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e96eb6a2f30df0f66c93454','5e609b86a342c0f170bd9a3a',2,'P2: Prep Other Ingredients','For Methi Machi, peel, wash and finely chop half a cup of onions. Wash, peel and finely chop a 1-inch piece of ginger. Peel, wash and finely chop 1 teaspoon of garlic. Wash and finely chop 3/4 cups of fenugreek leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96eb9a5decc44971684da3','5e609b86a342c0f170bd9a3a',3,'M1: Cook Fish','To fry the fish fillets for Methi Machi, heat 1/4 cup of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Then, add the marinated fish fillets one by one to the hot oil and sear it over medium flame for 5-6 minutes. Flip and fry the fish fillets until it is cooked through and evenly browned on both sides. Then, turn off the flame and take it out onto a plate.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96ebb9fe919dd663d223e6','5e609b86a342c0f170bd9a3a',4,'M2: Tempering and Sauteing','To make Methi Machi, heat 2 tablespoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add 1 teaspoon of chopped garlic followed by a 1-inch piece of chopped ginger and saute it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes until aromatic. Next, add half a cup of chopped onions and fry it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96ec5efe919dd663d223e7','5e609b86a342c0f170bd9a3a',5,'M3: Cooking','After frying the onions, add half a teaspoon of cumin powder, half a teaspoon of red chili powder and half a teaspoon of salt. Mix it well and saute the masala over medium flame for a minute. Next, add 3/4 cup of tomato puree and mix it well. Saute and cook the tomato puree over medium flame for 2-3 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96ec865decc44971684da4','5e609b86a342c0f170bd9a3a',6,'M4: Cooking','Next, add 3/4 cup of chopped fenugreek leaves and mix it well. Saute the fenugreek leaves with the gravy over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Add half a cup of water and stir it well. Then, bring it to a boil over a high flame. After that, add the fried basa fillets and gently mix it. Allow it to simmer for 2-3 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('5e96ed3c2f30df0f66c93455','5e5f92a77b824f089995fd0c',1,'P1: Marinate the Chicken','To marinate the chicken for Butter Chicken, first, wash 300 grams of boneless chicken thoroughly with water and put it in a large mixing bowl. Add a teaspoon of ginger-garlic paste, 2 tablespoons of curd, and squeeze a teaspoon of lemon juice into it. Next, add a teaspoon of Kashmiri red chili powder followed by a teaspoon of garam masala and half a teaspoon of salt. Mix it well and coat the chicken pieces well with the marinade. Then, allow it to marinate for 30 minutes. While the chicken is marinating, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":30,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96ed5d5decc44971684da5','5e5f92a77b824f089995fd0c',2,'P2: Prep Ingredients','For Butter Chicken, peel, wash and finely chop half a cup of onions. Wash and finely chop half a cup of tomatoes. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. .','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96ed885decc44971684da6','5e5f92a77b824f089995fd0c',3,'P3: Prepare a Masala Paste','To prepare the masala paste for Butter Chicken, heat 1 tablespoon of butter in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add a tablespoon of cooking oil and mix it well. Add half a cup of chopped onions and fry it over medium flame for 3-4 minutes until it turns slightly golden. Next, add a teaspoon of ginger-garlic paste and saute it for a minute.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96edd2fe919dd663d223e8','5e5f92a77b824f089995fd0c',4,'P4: Prepare the Masala Paste','Next, add half a cup of chopped tomatoes and mix it well. Saute and cook the tomatoes over medium flame for 4-5 minutes until tender. Add 3 nos dry red chilies and saute it for a minute. Next, add a teaspoon of salt followed by a teaspoon of cumin powder and half a teaspoon of coriander powder. Next, add a teaspoon of garam masala and mix it well. Saute and cook the masala over medium flame for 2-3 minutes.','prep_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96ee29fe919dd663d223e9','5e1977634f28558c29df63f3',1,'P1: Grate ginger & squeeze lime juice','For Sulaimani Chai, wash, peel and grate a 1-inch piece of ginger. Wash and cut a lime into halves and squeeze 1 teaspoon of lime juice using a lemon squeezer.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e96ee53fe919dd663d223ea','5e5f92a77b824f089995fd0c',5,'P5: Prepare Masala Paste','Next, add 1/4 cup of water and mix it well. Add 10 nos cashews and saute the masala over medium flame for 5 minutes until oil separates. After that, turn off the flame and allow it to cool down for some time. Then, transfer it to a blender jar and blend it well into a smooth paste.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e96ee5ffe919dd663d223eb','5e1977634f28558c29df63f3',2,'M1: Simmer the tea with ginger & whole spices. Strain & serve','To make Sulaimani Chai, first, add 1.5 cups of water into a saucepan. Add 3 nos cloves, and 2 nos green cardamoms followed by a 1-inch piece of grated ginger. Mix it well and bring it to a rolling boil over high flame. As it comes to a boil, reduce the flame to low and add 2 teaspoons of tea powder along with 2 teaspoons of jaggery. Then, allow it to simmer for a minute and let the spices infuse the flavor in the tea. Then, turn off the flame and a teaspoon of lime and mix it well. Strain the tea into cups and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96ee792f30df0f66c93456','5e5f92a77b824f089995fd0c',6,'M1: Fry the Chicken','To fry the chicken for Butter chicken, heat a tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add the marinated boneless chicken pieces and sear it over medium flame for 8-10 minutes, until it turns slightly tender and golden. Then, turn off the flame and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":4}'),('5e96eea5fe919dd663d223ec','5e5f92a77b824f089995fd0c',7,'M2: Cooking the Curry','To make Butter Chicken, heat 2 tablespoons of butter in a pan over low flame for a minute. Next, add a teaspoon of Kashmiri red chili powder and saute it over low flame for a minute. Next, add the prepared masala paste and mix it well. Saute and cook the masala over medium flame for 2-3 minutes. Add 1/4 cup of water and stir it well.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96eec7fe919dd663d223ed','5e1977f04f28558c29df63f5',1,'AP1: Soak the lentils','To make Dal Makhani, first, wash then soak 1/2 cup of black urad dal, 1/4 cup of chana dal, 1/4 cup of kidney beans in 1 cup of water for 8 hours or overnight.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e96eed25decc44971684da7','5e5f92a77b824f089995fd0c',8,'M3: Cooking the Curry','Next, add the fried chicken pieces and mix it well with the gravy. Then, reduce the flame to low and add 1/4 cup of fresh cream. Keep stirring it over low flame until it is well combined. Then, cover it with a lid and simmer the chicken for 10 minutes until it is cooked through. While the chicken is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('5e96eef7fe919dd663d223ee','5e5f92a77b824f089995fd0c',9,'M4: Garnish','After simmering the butter chicken, stir it well. Add a tablespoon of Kasuri methi followed by a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves. Then, turn off the flame and take it out into a serving bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('5e96ef19fe919dd663d223ef','5e1977f04f28558c29df63f5',2,'P1: Pressure cook the soaked lentils','To make Dal Makhai, in a pressure cooker add the soaked dal with 1 tbsp of ghee, 3/4 tsp of ginger-garlic paste, 1/2 tsp of red chili powder, 1/2 tsp of salt, and 2 cups of water. Cook this on high flame for 2 whistles and then on low for 8 mins. Once this is done allow the pressure to release naturally before you open the lid. While the dal is cooking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96ef43fe919dd663d223f0','5e1977f04f28558c29df63f5',3,'P2: Chop & prep the ingredients','Next, prep the vegetables, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions and 1/2 inch of ginger. Wash and roughly chop 1 tbsp of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96ef802f30df0f66c93457','5e1977f04f28558c29df63f5',4,'M1: cook the masala','For Dal Makhani, in a kadai heat 1/2 tbsp of ghee and then add 1/2 tsp of cumin seeds, let them splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped onion and saute for 2-3 mins. Once the onions are translucent, add 3 tbsp of tomato puree, and saute for 2-3 mins. Next, add 1/2 inch of chopped ginger, 1/4 tsp of garam masala, and cook for another 2 mins. Next add the cooked dal to the pan, 2 tbsp of fresh cream, 1 tbsp of butter, and mix well. Cook this for 2 mins and then garnish with 1 tbsp of coriander leaves and 1 tsp of fresh cream. The dish is ready to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e96f04a2f30df0f66c93458','5e5f888a7b824f089995fd09',1,'P1: Blanch Spinach Leaves','To blanch the spinach leaves for Lasooni Palak, wash and roughly chop 1 cup of spinach leaves. Add 3 cups of water in a saucepan and bring it to a rolling boil over a high flame. As the water comes to a boil, add 1 cup of spinach leaves and dip it completely in the water. Then, boil it over medium-high flame for 2 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and take it out of the water. Then, dip the blanched spinach leaves immediately in a cold bath. This will prevent the spinach leaves from cooking further while retaining the color.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":5}'),('5e96f06ffe919dd663d223f1','5e5f888a7b824f089995fd09',2,'P2: Prep Ingredients','For Lasooni Palak, wash and peel a half-inch piece of ginger. Wash and peel 1 clove of garlic. Wash, peel and finely slice 1 teaspoon of garlic. Peel, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and slit 2 nos green chilies. Wash and cut a lemon into halves. Then, squeeze 1 teaspoon of lemon juice.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96f08ffe919dd663d223f2','5e202bb14f28558c29df640d',1,'P1: Boil the pasta','To make Spaghetti Aglio e Olio, boil a pot of water with 1/2 tsp of olive oil, 1/2 tsp of salt and 200 g of spaghetti. Let this cook for 8-12 mins, until the pasta is 3/4th cooked or al dente. Once this is done, drain the water, preserve 1/2 cup of the water for later, and set the pasta aside. While the pasta is cooking please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96f0955decc44971684da8','5e5f888a7b824f089995fd09',3,'P3: Make Spinach Puree','To prepare the spinach puree for Lasooni Palak, add the blanched spinach leaves to a blender jar along with a half-inch piece of ginger and 2 nos slit green chilies. Then, cover the jar with a lid and blend it well into a smooth puree.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96f0c25decc44971684da9','5e202bb14f28558c29df640d',2,'P2: Chop & prep the ingredients','Next, wash and roughly chop 2 tbsp of parsley leaves. Peel and finely chop 15 cloves of garlic. Grate 2 tbsp of parmesan cheese.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e96f0e5fe919dd663d223f3','5e5f888a7b824f089995fd09',4,'M1: Temper the Spices','To make Lasooni Palak, heat 1 tablespoon of ghee in a Kadai over medium flame for a minute. Add 1 no bay leaf, a half-inch piece of cinnamon stick, 1 nos green cardamom, half a teaspoon of cumin seeds and half a teaspoon of Kasuri methi. Saute and let it splutter over medium flame for a minute. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions and fry it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96f1055decc44971684daa','5e5f888a7b824f089995fd09',5,'M2: Making the Curry','After frying the onions, add 2 teaspoons of gram flour and mix it well. Saute it over low flame fr 2-3 minutes, until gram flour turns aromatic. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of cumin powder, 1/4 teaspoon of coriander powder and 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala followed by half a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Saute and fry the masala over medium flame for 1-2 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96f1295decc44971684dab','5e5f888a7b824f089995fd09',6,'M3: Making the Curry','Next, add the prepared spinach puree and mix it well with the masala. Then, saute and cook the gravy over medium flame for 2-3 minutes. Add 1/4 cup of water to adjust the consistency and mix it well. Then, continue to simmer it for 3 minutes. While lasooni palak is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e96f142fe919dd663d223f5','5e202bb14f28558c29df640d',3,'M1: Combine the pasta with garlic flavored chili oil. Garnish with parmesan cheese','For Spaghetti Aglio e Olio, heat 3 tbsp of olive oil in a pan and then add 15 cloves of chopped garlic. Let this fry for 4-5 mins, until the garlic is golden. Next, add 1 tsp of red chili flakes and cook for another minute. Once this is done, turn off the flame and pour the olive oil mixture on top of the cooked pasta along with 1/2 cup of reserved pasta water, 1 tbsp of parmesan cheese. Gently combine all the ingredients and then garnish with 1 tbsp of parmesan cheese. The dish is ready to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96f1555decc44971684dac','5e5f888a7b824f089995fd09',7,'M4: Making the Curry','After simmering the Lasooni Palak, add a teaspoon of lemon juice and mix it well. Then, turn off the flame and set it aside. To make the tempering, heat a tablespoon of ghee in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add 1 teaspoon of sliced garlic and saute it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until it turns slightly golden brown. Then, add 1 dry red chili and saute it for a few seconds. After that, turn off the flame and add the tempering to the prepared lasooni palak. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('5e96f1b05decc44971684dad','5e202fa94f28558c29df640e',1,'P1: Knead & rest the dough','To make the dough for Paneer Paratha, add 1 cup of wheat flour in a large mixing bowl. Add 1/4 teaspoon of salt along with half a cup of water and mix it well. Knead the flour for 4-5 minutes. Add more water if required and knead it well into a smooth dough. Apply half a teaspoon of cooking oil over it and cover it with a damp cloth. Set it aside and allow the dough to rest for 20 minutes. While the dough is resting, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96f1d42f30df0f66c93459','5e202fa94f28558c29df640e',2,'P2: Grate paneer & prep other ingredients','For Paneer Paratha, grate 3/4 cup of paneer using a grater. Wash, peel and finely chop a 1/2-inch piece of ginger. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96f1fffe919dd663d223f6','5e202fa94f28558c29df640e',3,'P3: Prepare paneer stuffing','To make the stuffing for Paneer Paratha, in a mixing bowl, add 3/4 cup of grated paneer. Add half a teaspoon of Kashmiri red chili powder followed by 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala and 1/4 teaspoon of salt. Next, add a 1/2-inch piece of chopped ginger along with 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves and mix it well. Set the prepared stuffing aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96f2272f30df0f66c9345a','5e202fa94f28558c29df640e',4,'M1: Stuff & roll out the paneer paratha','To make the Paneer Paratha, first, divide the prepared dough into equal-sized balls. Next, take one dough ball and dust some flour over it and roll it into a 5-inch circle. Next, take 2-3 tablespoons of the prepared paneer stuffing and shape it into a small ball. Place the paneer stuffing ball onto the rolled out dough circle and pleat it as shown to stuff it inside. Remove the extra dough and press it to seal the dough ball. Dust some flour over it and roll it into a 7-inch round paratha. Make sure to roll the edges thin.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96f24b2f30df0f66c9345b','5e202fa94f28558c29df640e',5,'M2: Cook the stuffed paneer paratha','To toast the Paneer Paratha, place the prepared paratha over the hot tawa and toast it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes until small brown spots start to appear on its surface. Flip and toast the other side similarly. Then, add a teaspoon of cooking oil to each side and cook the paratha over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until it turns golden brown. As it turns slightly golden and crisp, take it out onto a plate and serve. Make the rest of the parathas similarly.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e96f2b12f30df0f66c9345c','5e5f8680a342c0f170bd9a38',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Veg Handi, peel, wash and roughly chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash, peel and chop a half-inch piece of ginger. Peel, wash and chop 1 teaspoon of garlic. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Wash, peel and chop 1/4 cup of carrots.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96f2b1fe919dd663d223f7','5e5f8680a342c0f170bd9a38',2,'P2: Make a Masala Paste','To prepare the masala paste for Veg Handi, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add 1/4 cup of chopped onions and fry it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until translucent. Next, add 1 teaspoon of chopped garlic followed by a half-inch piece of chopped ginger and saute it for a minute.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96f3072f30df0f66c9345d','5e5f8680a342c0f170bd9a38',3,'P3: Make a Masala Paste','Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes and mix it well. Saute and cook the tomatoes over medium flame for 4-5 minutes until tender. Add 4 nos cashews and saute it for a minute. Then, turn off the flame and allow the mixture to cool down completely. While the mixture is cooling down, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e96f3392f30df0f66c9345e','5e5f8680a342c0f170bd9a38',4,'P4: Prep other Ingredients','Next, wash and cut 1/4 cup of cauliflower into small florets. Wash and slice 1/4 cup of green capsicum. Wash, peel and cube 1/4 cup of potatoes. Wash and chop 1/4 cup of beans. Next, to make the masala paste, after the prepared mixture cools down, transfer it to a blender jar and blend it well into a smooth paste.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96f35cfe919dd663d223f8','5e5f8680a342c0f170bd9a38',5,'M1: Temper Spices','To make Veg Handi, a tablespoon of cooking oil in a Kadai over medium flame for a minute. Add 1 nos bay leaf followed by a half-inch piece of cinnamon stick and 3 nos cloves. Saute it over low flame for a minute. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder along with half a teaspoon of Kashmiri red chili powder and saute it over low flame for a minute','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),
('5e96f36dfe919dd663d223f9','5e203487057fd3f6fc80ee8c',1,'P1: Chop & prep the ingredients','Wash and slice button mushrooms, finely chop onions, tomatoes, slice garlic, slit green chili, chop coriander leaves, wash curry leaves, squeeze 1 Tbsp of lemon juice, and crush the black peppercorns.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96f379fe919dd663d223fa','5e5f8680a342c0f170bd9a38',6,'M2: Making the Curry','Next, add the prepared masala paste and mix it well. Saute and cook the masala over medium flame for 4-5 minutes until it comes together. Add 1/4 teaspoon of coriander powder followed by 1/4 teaspoon of cumin powder and half a teaspoon of salt. Mix it well ad saute the masala over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Then, reduce the flame to low and add 1/4 cup of curd. Keep stirring it continuously over a low flame until well combined, to prevent the curd from splitting.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e96f3a2fe919dd663d223fb','5e5f8680a342c0f170bd9a38',7,'M3: Making the Curry','Once the curd is well combined with the masala, add 1/4 cup of chopped carrots followed by 1/4 cup of chopped cauliflower florets and 1/4 cup of chopped capsicum. Next, add 1/4 cup of green peas, 1/4 cup of cubed potatoes and 1/4 cup of chopped beans. Add half a cup of water and mix it well. Then, cover it with a lid and simmer it for 15 minutes. While the vegetables are simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('5e96f3a2fe919dd663d223fc','5e203487057fd3f6fc80ee8c',2,'M1: Temper oil and fry onions','To make Mushroom Poriyal, heat 2.5 teaspoons of cooking oil in a pan on medium flame for a minute. Then, add 1/2 teaspoon of mustard seeds, 1/2 teaspoon of cumin seeds, 5 nos curry leaves, 2 cloves of sliced garlic and 1 nos slit green chili. Saute it on medium flame for 1-2 minutes till the garlic turns aromatic. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions and 1/2 teaspoon of ginger paste and stir fry it on medium-high flame for 3-4 minutes, until it turns slightly golden.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96f3c22f30df0f66c9345f','5e5f8680a342c0f170bd9a38',8,'M4: Garnish','After simmering the Veg Handi, take off the lid and stir it well. Add half a teaspoon of Kasuri methi and 2 teaspoons of fresh cream followed by 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala and a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves. Mix it well and turn off the flame. Take it out into a serving bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),
('5e96f443fe919dd663d223fd','5e203487057fd3f6fc80ee8c',3,'M2: Simmer the mushrooms','Once the onions are slightly brown, add the tomatoes and saute them for 3-4 mins Once the tomatoes are tender add the mushrooms along with salt. Saute this on high flame for 2 mins then cover the pan with a lid, reduce the flame to low and simmer for 10 mins.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96f49cfe919dd663d223fe','5e203487057fd3f6fc80ee8c',4,'M3:  Simmer the mushrooms with the spices. Garnish & serve','Take the lid off, add turmeric, Kashmiri red chili powder, garam masala, black pepper, and mix well. Cook for another 2-3 mins then turn off the flame, garnish with coriander leaves, and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e96f5862f30df0f66c93460','5e204811057fd3f6fc80ee8e',1,'P1: Boil the sweet corn kernels','Boil sweet corn kernels in 2 cups of boiling water for 4-5 mins. Once this is done, drain the water and set the kernels aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96f5af2f30df0f66c93461','5e204811057fd3f6fc80ee8e',2,'P2: Chop & prep the ingredients','Finely chop onions, tomatoes, cucumbers, capsicum, green chili, and coriander leaves.  Squeeze 1 Tbsp of lime juice.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96f607fe919dd663d223ff','5e204811057fd3f6fc80ee8e',3,'M1: Combine the chopped vegetables with corn kernels. Season the salad & serve','In a large bowl, add sweet corn kernels, cucumber, tomatoes, onions, capsicum, green chili, coriander leaves, black pepper, salt, lime juice, and olive oil. Toss this together and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e96f687fe919dd663d22400','5e204b534f28558c29df6410',1,'P1: Soak the soya chunks','To make Soya Chunk Curry, First, in a covered bowl soak 1 cup of soya chunks in 1.5 cups of hot water for 8 mins. Once this is done, transfer the soya chunks into an ice bath and let them rest for 10 mins.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":18,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96f6b32f30df0f66c93462','5e204b534f28558c29df6410',2,'P2: Chop & prep the ingredients','Next, peel and slice 1/4 cup of onions and another 1/4 cup of onion finely chopped, wash and roughly chop 1/2 cup of tomatoes, peel 2 cloves of garlic, and peel and roughly chop 1/2 inch of ginger.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96f7025decc44971684dae','5e204b534f28558c29df6410',3,'M1: Prepare the masala paste','For Soya Chunk Curry, in a kadai heat 1 tsp of oil and then add 1/4 cup of onions, 2 cloves of garlic, 1/2 inch of ginger, and saute for 2-3 mins. Next, add 1/2 cup of tomatoes and saute for 2 mins. Add 4 cashew nuts to this and mix well. Allow this to cool down completely and then blend it into a smooth puree.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96f74dfe919dd663d22401','5e204b534f28558c29df6410',4,'M2:  Cook the masala','Next, in the same kadai heat 1.5 tsp of oil and then add 1/2 inch of cinnamon, 1 bay leaf, and 1/2 tsp of cumin seeds. Let this splutter for a few seconds and then add 1/4 cup of onion, saute for 2-3 mins. Add 1/2 tsp of red chili powder and 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder to this, and mix well. Next, pour in the prepared masala paste and saute for 5 mins. Then, add 1/2 tsp of coriander powder and 1 tsp of salt, and saute for 2 mins.','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96f77ffe919dd663d22402','5e204b534f28558c29df6410',5,'M3: Simmer the soya chunks gravy','Next, add 1/2 cup of water and 2 tbsp of curd, and mix well. Once the curry comes to a boil, add 1 cup of soya chunks, ensure you squeeze out any excess water before adding it to the kadai. Mix well, cover the kadai with a lid and let it simmer for 10 mins. Once this is done, add 1/2 tsp of Kasuri methi, 1/4 tsp of garam masala, and mix well. The dish is ready to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('5e96f82d2f30df0f66c93463','5e204daf057fd3f6fc80ee8f',1,'P1: Soak the fox nuts in  milk & blend into a coarse paste','Soak the makhana in milk for 30 mins and then blend it into a coarse paste. Slice the almonds. Toast a few Makhana in ghee as a garnish.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":30,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e96f875fe919dd663d22403','5e204daf057fd3f6fc80ee8f',2,'M1: Simmer the kheer. Garnish & serve','Heat milk in a saucepan, then add the saffron, stir and let the milk come to a boil. Once it starts boiling, pour in the milk-makhana paste and mix well. Next add sugar, cardamom powder, sliced almonds, and nutmeg, mix well. Let it cook for another minute and take it off the heat, pour into bowls, garnish with toasted makahana, and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96f92d2f30df0f66c93464','5e213a24057fd3f6fc80ee91',1,'AP1: Soak kidney beans','To make Rajma Masala, first, soak 1/2 cup of kidney beans in 1.5 cups of water for 12 hours or overnight.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":720,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96f9605decc44971684daf','5e213a24057fd3f6fc80ee91',2,'P1: Pressure cook the soaked kidney beans','To make Rajma Masala, in a pressure cooker add 1/2 cup of soaked kidney beans, 1 bay leaf, 1 black cardamom, 1/2 tsp of salt, and 2 cups of water. Give it a quick stir and let it cook on high flame for 2 whistles and then on low flame for 8 mins. Once this is done the kidney beans should be well cooked, allow the pressure to release naturally before you take off the cooker''s lid.  While the rajma is cooking, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e96f9902f30df0f66c93465','5e213a24057fd3f6fc80ee91',3,'P2: Chop & prep the ingredients','Next, peel and finely chop 1/2 cup of onions. Wash and slit 1 green chili. Wash and roughly chop 1 tbsp of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e96f9bbfe919dd663d22404','5e213a24057fd3f6fc80ee91',4,'M1: Simmer the gravy','For Rajma Masala, in a pan heat 1 tbsp of ghee and then 1/2 tsp of cumin seeds, 1/2 inch of cinnamon, and 3 cloves, let this splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 1/4 cup of onions and then saute for 2-3 mins. Once the onions have browned, add 1/2 tsp of ginger-garlic paste, 1 slit green chili, and mix well. Next, add 1 cup of tomato puree, mix well, cover the pan with a lid, reduce the flame to low and cook for 10 mins, stirring occasionally.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e96f9f35decc44971684db0','5e213a24057fd3f6fc80ee91',5,'M2: Simmer the kidney beans with the gravy','Once the curry is thick, add 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder, 1/2 tsp of red chili powder, 1/2 tsp of coriander powder, 1/2 tsp of cumin powder, 1/4 tsp of dry mango powder, 1/4 tsp of garam masala, and 1/4 tsp of salt, mix well. Then, add 1/2 cup of cooked kidney beans, mix well, close the pan again, let it simmer for 15 mins. Garnish the curry with 1/2 tsp of Kasuri methi and 1 tbsp of coriander leaves. Give it a final mix and this dish is ready to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e96fa935decc44971684db1','5e213c2f985ffca18ae8fa85',1,'P1: Slice the ladies fingers & prep other ingredients','For Bhindi Pyaaz Crispy Fry, wash 1.5 cups of ladies'' finger well with water and dab it on a kitchen towel to dry off the water. Then, allow it to rest for some time. Make sure there is no moisture left on the ladies'' fingers, to prevent it from sticking together, while cooking. Then, stack it together and remove the cap and bottom part of the ladies'' fingers. Next, finely cut it into thin diagonal slices as shown. Wash, peel and finely slice 1/2 cup of onions. Squeeze 1 tablespoon of lime juice.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96fadbfe919dd663d22405','5e213c2f985ffca18ae8fa85',2,'P2: Season  & coat the sliced ladies fingers with turmeric powder','To prepare the ladies finger for Bhindi Pyaaz Crispy Fry, put the sliced ladies fingers in a bowl. Add 1/2 teaspoon of salt and 1/2 teaspoon of turmeric powder and mix it well.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e96fb0bfe919dd663d22406','5e213c2f985ffca18ae8fa85',3,'M1: Make brown onions','To fry the onions for Bhindi Pyaaz Crispy Fry, heat 1/4 cup of cooking oil in a pan on medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Add 1/2 cup of sliced onions and fry it on medium-high flame for 5-6 minutes, until it turns crisp and golden brown. Keep stirring the onions, while frying to prevent it from getting burnt. After frying the onions, turn off the flame and carefully remove it on a kitchen towel to absorb excess oil.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e96fb4c2f30df0f66c93466','5e213c2f985ffca18ae8fa85',4,'M2: Fry the ladies fingers. Top them with brown onions & serve','Next, to fry the ladies finger for Bhindi Pyaaz Crispy Fry, add 1.5 cups of sliced ladies finger to the same pan, and fry it on medium flame for 6-7 minutes, till it turns crisp and golden brown. Keep stirring it while frying, to ensure that ladies fingers are evenly fried. After frying, turn off the flame and carefully remove it on a kitchen towel to absorb excess oil. Next, place the fried ladies finger over a serving plate. Add the fried onions and drizzle 1 tablespoon of lime juice as a garnish. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e97e5125decc44971684db2','5e5f8439a342c0f170bd9a37',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Lasuni Methi Paneer, cut 1 cup of paneer into cubes. Wash and roughly chop 1 cup of fenugreek leaves. Peel, wash and finely slice half a cup of onions. Wash and finely chop half a cup of tomatoes. Wash and finely chop 2 nos green chilies. Peel, wash and finely chop 2 teaspoons of garlic.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e97e54dfe919dd663d22407','5e5f8439a342c0f170bd9a37',2,'P2: Fry the Paneer','To fry the paneer for Lasuni Methi Paneer, heat 1 tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Next, add 1 cup of cubed paneer pieces one by one and fry it over medium flame for 4-5 minutes. Flip and fry the paneer pieces until it is evenly browned on all the sides. Then, turn off the flame and take it out onto a plate.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e97e7d75decc44971684db3','5e5f8439a342c0f170bd9a37',3,'M1: Prepare a Masala Paste','To prepare the masala paste for Lasuni Methi Paneer, heat 2 tablespoons of butter in a pan over low flame for a minute. Add 1/4 cup of sliced onions followed by 2 teaspoons of chopped garlic. Saute and fry the onions over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e97e8505decc44971684db4','5e5f8439a342c0f170bd9a37',4,'M2: Prepare a Masala Paste','After frying the onions, add 2 nos chopped green chilies followed by half a cup of chopped tomatoes and mix it well. Saute and cook the tomatoes over medium flame for 4-5 minutes until tender. Next, add half a teaspoon of turmeric powder along with 1 cup of chopped fenugreek leaves and mix it well. Then, cover it with a lid and simmer it for 3 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and allow the mixture to cool down completely. While the mixture is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e97e8abfe919dd663d22408','5e5f8439a342c0f170bd9a37',5,'M3: Make a Masala Paste','To prepare the masala paste for Lasuni Methi Paneer, after the prepared mixture cools down, transfer it to a blender jar and blend it into a slightly coarse paste.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e97e8defe919dd663d22409','5e5f8439a342c0f170bd9a37',6,'M4: Cooking the Gravy','To make Lasuni Methi Paneer, heat a tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add half a teaspoon of garam masala and saute it over low flame for a minute. Next, add the prepared fenugreek paste and mix it well. Add half a cup of water and stir it well. Then, add 1 cup of fried paneer pieces and gently mix it with the gravy. Next, cover it with a lid and simmer it for 5-6 minutes, until the gravy thickens. While it is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e97e8fffe919dd663d2240a','5e5f8439a342c0f170bd9a37',7,'M5: Garnish','After simmering the Lasuni Methi Paneer, take off the lid and reduce to low flame. Then, add 1.5 tablespoons of fresh cream and keep stirring it continuously until it is well combined. Then, turn off the flame and take it out into a serving bowl. Garnish it with a teaspoon of fresh cream and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('5e97ed1a2f30df0f66c93468','5e5f825f88bd74342682d6ad',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Methi Matar Malai, soak 1/4 cup of cashews in 1 cup of water for 20 minutes. Meanwhile, wash and finely chop 1 cup of fenugreek leaves. Peel, wash and slice 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and slit 1 nos green chili. While the cashews are soaking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":20,"flame":0}'),('5e97ed425decc44971684db5','5e5f825f88bd74342682d6ad',2,'P2: Prepare the Masla Paste','For Methi Matar Malai, heat a tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add 1/4 cup of sliced onions and fry it over medium flame for 4-5 minutes until it turns slightly golden. Add 1 slit green chili followed by half a teaspoon of ginger-garlic paste and mix it well. Saute and fry the onions for another 1-2 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and allow the mixture to cool down completely.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e97ed73fe919dd663d2240b','5e5f825f88bd74342682d6ad',3,'P3: Prepare the Masala Paste','To prepare the masala paste for Methi Matar Malai, add the prepared onion mixture to a blender jar. Next, add 1/4 cup of soaked cashews and cover the jar with a lid. Then, blend it well into a smooth paste.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e97eda82f30df0f66c93469','5e5f825f88bd74342682d6ad',4,'M1: Make the Curry','To make Methi Matar Malai, heat a tablespoon of cooking oil over medium flame for a minute. Temper it with half a teaspoon of cumin seeds and saute it for few seconds. Next, add the prepared masala paste and saute it over medium flame for 4-5 minutes. Saute and cook the masala until it comes together and oil separates.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e97eddb2f30df0f66c9346a','5e5f825f88bd74342682d6ad',5,'M2: Cooking the Curry','As the masala separates the pan, add 1 cup of chopped fenugreek leaves and mix it well. Then, saute and fry the fenugreek leaves with the masala over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until it slightly shrivels up. After that, add 3/4 cup of water followed by half a cup of fresh cream and mix it well. Keep stirring it over a low flame until it is well combined. Then, add half a cup of frozen green peas along with 1/4 teaspoon of sugar and half a teaspoon of salt. Mix it well and cover it with a lid. Then, allow it to simmer for 8 minutes. While it is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('5e97ee0c2f30df0f66c9346b','5e5f825f88bd74342682d6ad',6,'M3: Garnish','After simmering the Methi Matar Malai, take off the lid and stir it well. Once the gravy thickens and turns creamy, add 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala and mix it well. Then, turn off the flame and take it out into a serving bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('5e97eeb85decc44971684db6','5e5f810399c5da6a770f7997',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Gujarati Kadhi, wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash and slit 1 nos green chili. Wash 7 nos curry leaves well with water. Next, to prepare the batter for kadhi, in a large bowl, add 3/4 cup of curd Add 2 tablespoons of gram flour followed by 1/4 teaspoon of ginger paste and 3/4 teaspoon of sugar. Add 2 cups of water and whisk it well until smooth to avoid any lumps.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e97f5a0209693d6562f917d','5e5f810399c5da6a770f7997',2,'M1: Making the Kadhi','To make Gujarati Kadhi, heat 1 tablespoon of ghee in a kadai over medium flame for a minute. Add 1/4 teaspoon of mustard seeds, 1/4 teaspoon of cumin seeds, and 1/4 teaspoon of fenugreek seeds. Next, add 2 nos cloves, a half-inch piece of cinnamon stick and 1 dry red chili followed by 1/4 teaspoon of hing and 7 curry leaves. Add 1 slit green chili and saute it over medium flame for a minute.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e97f6c1de86da3ab20984a0','5e5f810399c5da6a770f7997',3,'M2: Adding Gram Flour','Next, add the prepared gram flour batter and keep stirring it continuously over a low flame to avoid it from splitting. Keep stirring the batter until it is well combined. Then, allow it to simmer over medium flame for 15 minutes while stirring in between. While the kadhi is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":15,"flame":1}'),('5e97f6e2c437aa13304ab0a5','5e5f810399c5da6a770f7997',4,'M3: Garnish','After simmering the Gujarati Kadhi, add 1/4 cup of water to adjust the consistency and stir it well. Next, add half a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Then, allow it cook over low flame for another 2 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and add 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves. Mix it well and take it out into a serving bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('5e97f809de86da3ab20984a1','5e5f7f5199c5da6a770f7996',1,'P1: Prep Ingrdients','For Punjabi Boondi Kadhi, peel, wash and slice 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Next, to prepare the batter, in a large mixing bowl, add half a cup of curd. Add 1/4 cup of gram flour and whisk it well until smooth to avoid any lumps. Add 1 cup of water and mix it well to prepare a thin and flowy batter.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e97f85bc437aa13304ab0a6','5e5f7f5199c5da6a770f7996',2,'M1: Making the Kadhi','To make Punjabi Boondi Kadhi, heat 1 tablespoon of mustard oil in a pressure cooker over medium flame for a minute. Add half a teaspoon of fenugreek seeds and saute it for a minute. Next, add 1/4 cup of sliced onions and fry it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e97f88fc437aa13304ab0a7','5e5f7f5199c5da6a770f7996',3,'M2: Adding the Gram Flour','After frying the onions, add a teaspoon of red chili powder followed by half a teaspoon of turmeric powder and half a teaspoon of garam masala and mix it well. Then, fry the masala over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Next, add the prepared gram flour batter and keep stirring it over a low flame until well combined. Make sure to stir the batter over a low flame to prevent the curd from splitting.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e97f8b8c437aa13304ab0a8','5e5f7f5199c5da6a770f7996',4,'M3: Cooking in the Pressure Cooker','Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Then, cover it with a lid and pressure cook the kadhi until two whistles. After that, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the kadhi is cooking, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e97f8e6de86da3ab20984a2','5e5f7f5199c5da6a770f7996',5,'M4: Final Touches','After cooking the Punjabi Boondi Kadhi, take off the lid and stir it well. Then, add 1/4 cup of boondi and mix it well. Continue to cook the kadhi over medium flame for 2 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set it aside. Next, to make the tempering, heat a teaspoon of mustard oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add a teaspoon of red chili powder and saute it over low flame for a few seconds. Then, turn off the flame and pour the tempering over the prepared kadhi. Garnish it with a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e97faafc437aa13304ab0a9','5e5f7e0688bd74342682d6ac',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Paneer Butter Masala, peel, wash and roughly chop half a cup of onions. Wash and roughly chop 3/4 cups of tomatoes. Cut 1 cup of paneer into medium cubes. Wash and finely chop 1.5 tablespoons of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e97fad8d4c21142148b36b6','5e5f7e0688bd74342682d6ac',2,'P2: Prepare a Masala Paste','To prepare the masala paste for Paneer Butter Masala, heat a tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add half a cup of roughly chopped onions and fry it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until translucent. Next, add 2 nos dry red chilies and saute it for a minute. Add 3/4 cup of chopped tomatoes along with 1/4 cup of cashews and mix it well. Saute and cook the tomatoes for 4-5 minutes until tender.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e97faf9c437aa13304ab0ab','5e5f7e0688bd74342682d6ac',3,'P3: Prepare a Masala Paste','After cooking the tomatoes, add half a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Then, saute and fry the masala over medium flame for 2-3 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and allow it to cool down completely. Once cool, blend this into a smooth masala paste. While the mixture is cooling down, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e97fb9ad4c21142148b36b7','5e5f7e0688bd74342682d6ac',4,'P4: Prepare a Khova Paste','Next, add 2 tablespoons of khova to a blender jar followed by 2 tablespoons of milk. Cover the jar with a lid and blend it well into a smooth paste. Take it out into a bowl and set it aside. Next, after the prepared masala mixture cools down, transfer it to a blender jar and blend it well into a smooth paste.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e97fbc5c437aa13304ab0ac','5e5f7e0688bd74342682d6ac',5,'M1: Making the Curry','To make Paneer Butter Masala, heat a tablespoon of ghee in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add a teaspoon of Kashmiri red chili powder and saute it over low flame for a minute. Next, add the prepared masala paste and mix it well. Saute and cook the masala over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until it comes together. Add some water and mix it well.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e97fbf1c437aa13304ab0ad','5e5f7e0688bd74342682d6ac',6,'M2: Simmering the Curry','Next, add half a teaspoon of garam masala followed by half a teaspoon of kasuri methi and a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and mix it well. Then cover it with a lid and simmer the masala for 10 minutes. While the masala is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":10,"flame":2}'),('5e97fc49de86da3ab20984a3','5e5f7e0688bd74342682d6ac',7,'M3: Cooking the Curry','After simmering the masala for Paneer Butter Masala, take off the lid and add the prepared khoya paste along with half a teaspoon of sugar. Mix it well and keep stirring it over a low flame until it comes together. Next, add 1/4 cup of water and mix it well. Add half a teaspoon of salt followed by 1 cup of cubed paneer and gently mix it. Then, cover it with a lid and simmer the paneer for 10 minutes. While Paneer Butter Masala is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('5e97fcc9c437aa13304ab0ae','5e5f7e0688bd74342682d6ac',8,'M4: Garnish','After simmering the Paneer Butter Masala, take off the lid and stir it well. Turn off the flame and take it out into a serving bowl. Garnish it with a teaspoon of butter and a teaspoon of chopped coriander leaves. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e97fe16de86da3ab20984a4','5e5f7ca1d6596e61e3deda66',1,'AP1: Soak Chickpeas','For Pindi Chana Masala, soak 3/4 cups of chickpeas in 2 cups of water for 8 hours. While the chickpeas are soaking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":480,"advanced_prep_time":480,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e97fe5ad4c21142148b36b8','5e5f7ca1d6596e61e3deda66',2,'P1: Pressure Cook the Chickpeas','To boil the chickpeas for Pindi Chana Masala, add the soaked chickpeas to a pressure cooker along with 1 tea bag and a half-inch piece of the cinnamon stick along with 1 bay leaf. Next, add 2 green cardamoms, 2 cloves, 1/4 teaspoon of baking soda and 1/4 teaspoon of salt. Add 2.5 cups of water and cover it with a lid. Then, pressure cook the chickpeas over a high flame until 4 whistles. After that, continue to simmer it over low flame for 5 minutes. After that, take off the lid and remove the tea bags. Then, turn off the flame and set it aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the chickpeas are boiling, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e97fe83c437aa13304ab0af','5e5f7ca1d6596e61e3deda66',3,'P2: Prep Other Ingredients','For Pindi Chana Masala, peel, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Wash, peel, and julienne a 1-inch piece of ginger. Wash and slit 2 nos green chilies. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e97fec4c437aa13304ab0b0','5e5f7ca1d6596e61e3deda66',4,'M1: Cook the Onions','To make Pindi Chana Masala, heat 1 tablespoon of cooking oil in a Kadai over medium flame for a minute. Add 1 nos bay leaf and saute it for a few seconds. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions and fry it over medium flame for 3-4 minutes, until translucent. After frying the onions, add half a teaspoon of ginger-garlic paste followed by 2 nos slit green chilies and saute it for 2-3 minutes until onions turn golden brown.','cook_method','{"active_time":0,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e97feeed4c21142148b36b9','5e5f7ca1d6596e61e3deda66',5,'M2: Making the Curry','After the onions are browned, add 1 tablespoon of chana masala and mix it well. Saute and fry the masala over low flame for 1-2 minutes. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes and mix it well. Saute and cook the tomatoes over medium flame 4-5 minutes until tender. Then, fry and cook the masala until oil separates.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e97fef0c437aa13304ab0b1','5e5f7ca1d6596e61e3deda66',6,'M3: Making the Curry','After cooking the masala, add the boiled chickpeas along with the stock and stir it well. Add half a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. If required, add some water to adjust the consistency. Then, cover it with a lid and simmer it for 15 minutes. While the chickpeas are simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":15,"flame":1}'),('5e97ff35de86da3ab20984a5','5e5f7ca1d6596e61e3deda66',7,'M4: Final Touches','After simmering the Pindi Chana Masala, take off the lid and stir it well. Mash a few chickpeas to thicken the gravy. Then, turn off the flame and set it aside. To make the tempering, heat a tablespoon of ghee in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add 1 slit green chili along with a half-inch piece of sliced ginger and 1/4 teaspoon of red chili powder. Saute it over low flame for a minute and then, turn off the flame. Add the tempering to the prepared chana masala. Garnish it with a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e97ffc5d4c21142148b36ba','5e5f7b21d6596e61e3deda65',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Mushroom Hara Pyaza, wash and finely chop 1.5 cups of spring onions. Wash and quarter 1.5 cups of button mushrooms.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e97fff2c437aa13304ab0b2','5e215081985ffca18ae8fa8b',1,'P1: Chop & prep the ingredients','To make carrot soup, first, peel and roughly chop 1/2 cup of carrot, 1/4 cup of potato,soak 1/4 cup of chopped potatoes in 1/2 cup of water until use. Roughly chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and roughly chop 1 tbsp of coriander leaves. Crush 1 tsp of black peppercorns with a mortar and pestle.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e980013c437aa13304ab0b3','5e5f7b21d6596e61e3deda65',2,'M1: Cook the Green Vegetables','To make Mushroom Hara Pyaza, heat a tablespoon of mustard oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add half a teaspoon of cumin seeds and let it splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 1.5 cups of chopped spring onions and fry it over low flame for 2-3 minutes until it slightly changes color. Next, add 1/4 cup of green peas and mix it well. Stir and fry the green peas over medium flame for 1-2 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e980027c437aa13304ab0b4','5e215081985ffca18ae8fa8b',2,'M1:  Pressure cook carrots & potatoes','For Carrot Soup, in a pressure cooker add 1/2 cup of carrots, 1/4 cup of soaked potatoes, 1/4 cup of onions, 1 tsp of salt, 1 tsp of black peppercorns, 1 vegetable stock cube and 2.5 cups of water. Let this cook on high flame for 1 whistle and then on low for 8 mins. Once this is done, allow the pressure to release naturally before you open the lid. While this is cooking please move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e980051c437aa13304ab0b5','5e215081985ffca18ae8fa8b',3,'M2: Simmer the soup. Garnish & serve','For carrot soup, once the vegetables in the cooker have cooled completely, blend them into a smooth puree. Next, pour the puree into the cooker and cook it for 2 mins without the lid. Adjust the consistency of the soup and then garnish with 1 tbsp of coriander leaves. The dish is ready to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e980056c437aa13304ab0b6','5e5f7b21d6596e61e3deda65',3,'M2: Cooking the Mushrooms','Next, add half a teaspoon of salt followed by 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder and half a teaspoon of crushed black peppercorns. Mix it well and fry it over medium flame for a minute. After that, add 1/5 cups of chopped button mushrooms and mix them well. Stir and fry the mushrooms over medium flame for 2-3 minutes. Then, cover it with a lid and simmer the mushrooms for 5-6 minutes until tender. While the mushrooms are simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e980074d4c21142148b36bb','5e5f7b21d6596e61e3deda65',4,'M3: Final Touches','After simmering the Mushroom Hara Pyaza, take off the lid and fry the mushrooms over a medium-high flame to reduce the extra water. Next, add half a teaspoon of garam masala and mix it well. Then, turn off the flame and take it out into a bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":4}'),
('5e980312d4c21142148b36be','5e5f79b288bd74342682d6ab',1,'P1: Blanch Cauliflower','To blanch the cauliflower for Veg Jalfrezi, wash and cut 1/4 cup of cauliflower into small florets. Then, add 1 cup of water in a saucepan and bring it to a rolling boil over a high flame. Add 1/4 teaspoon of salt and mix it well. As the water comes to a boil, add 1/4 cup of cauliflower florets and let it boil over medium-high flame for 2-3 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and drain off the water from the cauliflower and set it aside. While the cauliflower is blanching, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e980341de86da3ab20984aa','5e5f79b288bd74342682d6ab',2,'P2: Blanch Baby Corn','To blanch the baby corns for Veg Jalfrezi, slice 1/4 cup of baby corns. Then, add 1 cup of water along in a saucepan and bring it to a boil over a high flame. Add 1/4 cup of baby corns and let it boil over medium-high flame for 3-4 minutes. While it is blanching, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":4,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e98036bde86da3ab20984ab','5e5f79b288bd74342682d6ab',3,'P3: Chop Ingredients','For Veg Jalfrezi, wash, peel and julienne a half-inch piece of ginger. Peel, wash and cut 1/4 cup of onions into petals. Wash and slit 2 nos green chilies. Peel, wash and finely chop 1 teaspoon of garlic. Wash and finely slice 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Wash and chop 1/4 cup of beans.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e980398de86da3ab20984ac','5e5f79b288bd74342682d6ab',4,'P4: Chop Ingredients','Next, wash and finely slice 1/4 cup of red capsicum. Wash and finely slice 1/4 cup of green capsicum. Wash and finely slice 1/4 cup of yellow capsicum. Wash, peel and cut 1/4 cup of carrot into 2-inch sticks. Wash and roughly chop 1/4 cup of button mushrooms. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9803bbc437aa13304ab0b8','5e5f79b288bd74342682d6ab',5,'M1: Cook Spices and Onions','To make Veg Jalfrezi, heat 1 tablespoon of ghee in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add half a teaspoon of cumin seeds followed by a half-inch piece of ginger juliennes and 2 nos dry red chilies. Saute it over medium flame for a minute. Next, add 1/4 cup of onion petals along with 2 nos slit green chilies and fry the onions over medium flame for 3-4 minutes until it turns slightly golden.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e9803f5c437aa13304ab0ba','5e5f79b288bd74342682d6ab',6,'M2: Continue Cooking','Next, add 1 teaspoon of chopped garlic and saute it for a minute. Add half a teaspoon of red chili powder followed by a teaspoon of coriander powder and half a teaspoon of turmeric powder. Mix it well and fry the masala over low flame for 1-2 minutes. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped carrots, 1/4 cup of blanched cauliflower florets, 1/4 cup of blanched baby corns, 1/4 cup of chopped french beans, and 1/4 cup of green peas.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e98041dc437aa13304ab0bb','5e5f79b288bd74342682d6ab',7,'M3: Continue Cooking','Next, add 1/4 cup of sliced red capsicum followed by 1/4 cup of sliced green capsicum and 1/4 cup of sliced yellow capsicum. Next, add 1/4 cup of sliced tomatoes along with 1/4 cup of chopped mushrooms. Stir and fry the vegetables over high flame for 2-3 minutes until tender-crisp. After frying the vegetables, add half a cup of tomato puree and mix it well. Then, cook it over low flame for 1-2 minutes. Next, add a teaspoon of vinegar followed by a teaspoon of tomato ketchup and mix it well. Then, allow it to simmer for 5-6 minutes while stirring in between. While the veg jalfrezi is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e980442c437aa13304ab0bc','5e5f79b288bd74342682d6ab',8,'M4: Final Touches','After simmering the Veg Jalfrezi, add half a teaspoon of garam masala followed by half a teaspoon of Kasuri methi and mix it well. Add a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and mix it well. Then, turn off the flame and take it out into a serving bowl. Garnish it with half a teaspoon of fresh cream and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('5e980592de86da3ab20984ae','5e5f774988bd74342682d6aa',1,'AP1: Soak Urad Dal','For Sukhi Urad Dal Sabzi, wash and soak 3/4 cup of urad dal in 2 cups of water for 4 hours. While the dal is soaking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":420,"advanced_prep_time":240,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9805d0de86da3ab20984b0','5e5f774988bd74342682d6aa',2,'P1: Chop Ingrdients','For Sukhi Urad Dal Sabzi, peel, wash and finely slice 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Wash, peel and finely slice a half-inch piece of ginger. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash and cut a lemon into halves. Then, squeeze 1 teaspoon of lemon juice.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9805f5d4c21142148b36bf','5e5f774988bd74342682d6aa',3,'M1: Temper Spices','To make Sukhi Urad Dal Sabzi, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add 1 teaspoon of cumin seeds, 1/4 teaspoon of hing, 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, 1/4 teaspoon of red chili powder and half a teaspoon of salt. Next, add a half-inch piece of sliced ginger and saute it over low flame for a minute.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e980619de86da3ab20984b1','5e5f774988bd74342682d6aa',4,'M2: Add the Soaked Dal','Next, add the soaked urad dal followed by 1 cup of water and mix it well. Then, cover it with a lid and simmer the dal for 6-7 minutes. Make sure not to overcook the dal. While the dal is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":7,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e980658c437aa13304ab0c1','5e5f774988bd74342682d6aa',5,'M3: Cook Onions','After simmering the sukhi urad dal, take off the lid and saute it over medium-high flame for 2-3 minutes to reduce the excess water from the dal. Then, turn off the flame and set it aside. Next, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add 1/4 cup of sliced onions and saute it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e98068cd4c21142148b36c2','5e5f774988bd74342682d6aa',6,'M4: Continue Cooking','After frying the onions, add half a teaspoon of salt followed by 1/4 teaspoon of red chili powder and mix it well. Saute it over low flame for a minute. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes and mix it well. Saute and cook the tomatoes over medium flame for 4-5 minutes until tender. After that, add the cooked urad dal and mix it well. Then, cover it with a lid and allow it to simmer for 2-3 minutes. While the dal is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9806b0c437aa13304ab0c2','5e5f774988bd74342682d6aa',7,'M5: Final Touches','After simmering the sukhi urad dal, take off the lid and saute it over medium flame for a minute. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala followed by 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and a teaspoon of lemon juice. Mix it well and turn off the flame. Take it out into a serving bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('5e980773c437aa13304ab0c5','5e5f762b98151ea9068f5bde',1,'P1: Chop Ingredients','For Kasuri Methi Paneer Sabzi, cut 1 cup of paneer into medium cubes. Peel, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Wash, peel and grate a half-inch piece of ginger. Peel, wash and grate 1 teaspoon of garlic.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9807a5c437aa13304ab0c6','5e5f762b98151ea9068f5bde',2,'M1: Cook Spices and Onions','To make Kasuri Methi Paneer Sabzi, heat a tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Temper it with half a teaspoon of cumin seeds and allow it to splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions and fry it over medium flame for 3-4 minutes until translucent. After frying the onions add 1 teaspoon of grated garlic followed by a half-inch piece of grated ginger and saute it over medium flame for a minute.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9807c6de86da3ab20984b2','5e5f762b98151ea9068f5bde',3,'M2: Continue Cooking','Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes and mix it well. Saute and cook the tomatoes over medium flame for 4-5 minutes until tender. Then, add a teaspoon of red chili powder, followed by half a teaspoon of turmeric powder and half a teaspoon of garam masala. Mix it well and fry the masala for 1-2 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9807e9de86da3ab20984b3','5e5f762b98151ea9068f5bde',4,'M3: Final Touches','After frying the masala, add 1 cup of cubed followed by half a teaspoon of salt and a tablespoon of crushed Kasuri methi. Then, gently mix the paneer with the masala. Next, cover it with a lid and simmer the paneer for 4-5 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and take off the lid. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e980867c437aa13304ab0c7','5e2263124f28558c29df642f',1,'P1: Chop  & prep the ingredients','To make Avarekalu Saaru, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions and peel and roughly chop another 1/4 cup of onions. Peel and chop 1/4 cup of potatoes into cubes. Wash and roughly chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes and 1 tbsp of coriander leaves. Wash 8 curry leaves. Peel 4 cloves of garlic. Peel and roughly chop 1/2 inch of ginger. Roughly chop 1/4 cup of fresh coconut. Wash 8 curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":14,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e980899de86da3ab20984b4','5e2263124f28558c29df642f',2,'P2: Prepare onion & coconut paste','Next, make an onion paste, in a blending jar add 1/4 cup of roughly chopped onions, 1/2 inch of ginger, and 4 cloves of garlic. Blend this into a smooth puree and keep it aside. Next, make a coconut paste, in a blending jar add 1/4 cup of roughly chopped coconut and 3 tbsp of water, blend into a smooth paste and keep it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9808e8de86da3ab20984b5','5e2263124f28558c29df642f',3,'M1: Fry the vegetables with onion paste','To make Avarekalu Saaru, in a pressure cooker, heat 2 tsp of oil, and then add 1/4 cup of finely chopped onions and 8 curry leaves. Saute this for 2-3 mins, then add 1/4 cup of potatoes, and saute for another 2-3 mins. Next, add 1/4 cup of lima beans and 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder, and saute this for 1 min. Then, add the prepared onion puree nad cook the masala over medium flame for 5-6 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e980a13d4c21142148b36c6','5e5f7483437cb032ff003876',1,'P1: Chop Ingredients','For Paneer Jalfrezi, cut 1 cup of paneer into 2-inch long rectangular pieces. Peel, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Peel, wash, and finely slice 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1/4  cup of tomatoes. Wash and finely slice 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Wash, peel, and julienne a half-inch piece of ginger. Wash and finely slice 1/4 cup of red capsicum. Wash and cut a lemon into halves and squeeze 1.5 teaspoons of lemon juice.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e980a59c437aa13304ab0c9','5e5f7483437cb032ff003876',2,'P2: Prepare a Masala Paste','To prepare the masala paste for Paneer Jalfrezi, heat 1 tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add 1/4 cup of chopped onions and fry it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until translucent. Next, add a teaspoon of ginger-garlic paste and saute it for a minute. After that, add 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes and mix it well. Saute and cook the tomatoes over medium flame for 4-5 minutes, until tender.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e980a9ade86da3ab20984b7','5e5f7483437cb032ff003876',3,'P3: Make the Masala Paste','After cooking the tomatoes, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder followed by 1/4 teaspoon of Kashmiri red chili powder and 1/4 teaspoon of coriander powder. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of cumin powder and mix it well. Saute the masala over a low flame until oil separates. Then, turn off the flame and allow the mixture to cool down for some time. After that, transfer it to a blender jar and blend it well into a smooth paste.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('5e980aebd4c21142148b36c7','5e5f7483437cb032ff003876',4,'M1: Cook Spices and Onions','To make Paneer Jalfrezi, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a kadai over medium flame for a minute. Add 1 nos dry red chili, followed by a half-inch piece of ginger juliennes and 1/4 teaspoon of cumin seeds. Saute it over medium flame for a minute. Next, add 1/4 cup of sliced onions and saute it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e980affc437aa13304ab0ca','5e2554b4057fd3f6fc80eec2',1,'P1: Chop & prep the ingredients','To make Aloo Gobi Masala, first, peel and dice 1/2 cup of potatoes. wash and chop 1/2 cup of cauliflower. peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. wash and chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. peel and finely chop 1 teaspoon of garlic and 1/2 inch of ginger. wash and roughly chop 1 tbsp of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":11,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e980b11c437aa13304ab0cb','5e5f7483437cb032ff003876',5,'M2: Continue Cooking the Curry','After frying the onions, add 1/4 cup of sliced red capsicum and fry it over high flame for a minute. Next, add the prepared masala along with a teaspoon of tomato sauce and half a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Saute and fry the masala over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Next, add 1 cup of paneer pieces followed by 1/4 cup of sliced tomatoes and mix it well. Then, cover it with a lid and allow it to simmer for 2 minutes until tomatoes turn tender. While the paneer is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":4}'),('5e980b2dd4c21142148b36c8','5e5f7483437cb032ff003876',6,'M3: Garnish','After simmering the Paneer Jalfrezi, take off the lid and add 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala followed by 1.5 teaspoons of lemon juice. Then, gently mix it and turn off the flame. Take it out into a serving bowl and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e980b39de86da3ab20984b9','5e2554b4057fd3f6fc80eec2',2,'P2: Blanch cauliflower & potatoes','Next, in a pot boil 1 cup of water and then add 1/2 cup of chopped potatoes and 1/2 cup of chopped cauliflower. Let them cook for 5-6 mins and then drain the excess water and set them aside. Next, boil 1/4 cup of frozen green peas in 1 cup of water for 4-5 minutes. Then, drain and remove the boiled green peas in a bowl and set aside. While the vegetables are boiling, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":4}'),
('5e980b7cc437aa13304ab0cc','5e2554b4057fd3f6fc80eec2',3,'M1: Cook the masala','For Aloo Gobi Masala, heat 2 tbsp oil in a pan, add 1 tsp of cumin seeds and let them splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 1/2 tsp of hing and  1/4 cup of chopped onions, saute this for 2-3 mins. Once the onions have browned, add 1/2 inch of chopped ginger and 1 teaspoon of chopped garlic, and mix well. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes, and saute for 2 mins.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e980c0cc437aa13304ab0cd','5e2582874f28558c29df6434',1,'P1: Scoop out the avocado pulp & prep the ingredients','For Avocado Sandwich, wash and cut a small avocado into halves and remove the seed. Then, gently scoop out the pulp and put it into a bowl. Next, peel, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and cut 1/4 cup of tomatoes into round slices. Peel, wash and finely chop 1 teaspoon of garlic. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash and cut a lemon into halves. Then, squeeze 1 teaspoon of lemon juice using a squeezer.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e980c2ede86da3ab20984ba','5e2582874f28558c29df6434',2,'P2: Prepare the avocado mixture','To prepare the avocado mixture for Avocado Toast, first, mash the avocado pulp well using a fork. Next, add 1 teaspoon of chopped garlic, and half a teaspoon of black pepper powder followed by half a teaspoon of salt. Add a teaspoon of lemon juice along with 1/4 cup of chopped onions and a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and mix it well to prepare a mixture.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e980c63d4c21142148b36c9','5e2582874f28558c29df6434',3,'P3: Prep the ingredients for green chutney','For Green Chutney, rinse 1 cup of coriander leaves well with water and remove the root ends. Wash and separate 1/4 cup of mint leaves. Peel and wash 3 cloves of garlic. Wash, and peel a 1-inch piece of ginger. Wash and slit 3 nos green chilies. Wash and cut a lemon into halves. Then, squeeze 1 tablespoon lime juice.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e980c87c437aa13304ab0ce','5e2582874f28558c29df6434',4,'P4: Blend & make the green chutney','To make the Green Chutney, in a blender jar, add 1 cup of coriander leaves and 1/4 cup of mint leaves. Next, add a 1-inch piece of ginger, 3 cloves of garlic and 3 nos slit green chilies followed by 2 a tablespoon of lemon juice. Next, add half a teaspoon of cumin seeds, chat masala, half a teaspoon of sugar and half a teaspoon of salt along with 3 tablespoons of water. Blend it well into a smooth chutney. Take it out into a bowl and add a tablespoon of lime juice. Mix it well and set it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e980ce2de86da3ab20984bb','5e2582874f28558c29df6434',5,'M1:  Assemble & stuff the sandiwiches with avocado mixture','To prepare the Avocado Sandwich, take 2 bread slices and add a tablespoon of the prepared green chutney over each slice. Spread the chutney over the bread slice evenly. Next, spread 2 tablespoons of the prepared avocado mixture over one of the bread slices. Add 3 slices of tomato and sprinkle 1/4 teaspoon of mixed herbs followed by 1/4 teaspoon of chili flakes over it. Cover the sandwich with another bread slice and apply half a teaspoon of butter over it. Prepare the other sandwich similarly.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e980d06d4c21142148b36ca','5e2582874f28558c29df6434',6,'M2: Grill & make the avocado sandwiches','To grill the Avocado Sandwich, place the prepared sandwich inside the grill, with butter side on the bottom. Apply half a teaspoon of butter over it and grill the sandwich for 3-4 minutes until both sides are evenly browned. Then, carefully take it out onto a plate and slice it into halves. Serve. Make the other sandwich similarly.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":4,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e980d8cd4c21142148b36cb','5e258a1d057fd3f6fc80eec5',1,'P1: Pressure cook the dal & rice','To make Bisi Bele Bath, wash 1/2 cup of toor dal and 1 cup of rice. Cook the dal and rice together in a pressure cooker with 3 cups of water, cook on high flame for 1 whistle and then on low flame for 8 mins. Once this is done let the pressure release naturally before you open the cooker. While this is cooking move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e980dbac437aa13304ab0cf','5e258a1d057fd3f6fc80eec5',2,'P2: Soak the tamarind & prep the ingredients','Next, in a small bowl add 1 tbsp of tamarind and 1/4 cup of hot water. Let this rest for 2 mins and then mash the tamarind and water together to make a tamarind pulp. Peel and roughly slice 1/4 cup of carrots. Wash and chop 4 green beans into 1-inch pieces. Peel and roughly dice 1/4 cup of potatoes. Peel and chop 1/4 cup of onions into petals. Wash 8 curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e980df1c437aa13304ab0d0','5e258a1d057fd3f6fc80eec5',3,'M1: Simmer cooked dal & rice with vegetables','For Bisi Bele Bath, in a pan add 1/4 cup of carrots, 4 chopped green beans, 2 tbsp of green peas, 1/4 cup of potatoes, 2 tbsp of peanuts, 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder, 1/2 tsp of salt, and 1 cup of water. Mix well, cover the pan with a lid and let it cook for 8 mins. Once this is done, add the prepared tamarind pulp, 1/4 tsp of jaggery, 1/4 cup of onion petals, and let it boil for 10 mins. Next, add the cooked dal and rice and gently mix all the ingredients together. Once they are combined well, add 3/4 cup of water to adjust the consistency, then add 3 tbsp of bisi bele bath masala, 1/4 tsp of salt, 1 tbsp of ghee, and mix well. Cover the pan with a lid and simmer for 20 mins.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":38,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('5e980e2ade86da3ab20984bc','5e258a1d057fd3f6fc80eec5',4,'M2: Prepare the tempering & add it to the bhath. Garnish & serve','Next, in a tadka pan, heat 1 tbsp of ghee and then add 1/2 tsp of mustard seeds, 1 broken dry red chili, 1/4 tsp of hing, 8 curry leaves, and 7 cashew nuts and let them splutter for a few seconds. Pour this tadka over the cooked bisi bele bath and give the dish a good mix. Put the Bisi Bele Bath in a serving dish and enjoy.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e980e93d4c21142148b36cc','5e2591a2057fd3f6fc80eec8',1,'P1: Heat the milk to knead the dough','For Plain Laccha Paratha, first, add half a cup of milk to a saucepan and heat it over a medium flame for a minute. Make sure not to boil it, only let it warm. Before it comes to a boil, turn off the flame and take it out into a cup.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e980eb2d4c21142148b36cd','5e2591a2057fd3f6fc80eec8',2,'P2: Knead & rest the dough','To prepare the dough for Plain Laccha Paratha, in a large mixing bowl, add 3/4 cup of wheat flour and 3/4 cup of all-purpose flour. Next, add 3/4 teaspoon of sugar, half a teaspoon of salt and 1/4 teaspoon of baking soda followed by a teaspoon of cooking oil. Mix it well and crumble the flour with fingers so it holds shape. Next, add half a cup of warm milk and knead it well into a smooth dough. Cover the dough with a damp cloth and allow it to rest for 30 minutes.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":30,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e980eddc437aa13304ab0d1','5e2591a2057fd3f6fc80eec8',3,'M1: Divide the dough into dough balls & roll','To make the Plain Laccha Paratha, after resting the dough, knead it again and roll it into a long cylindrical shape. Then, divide it into small equal-sized balls. Next, take a dough ball and dust it into some flour. Then, gently press it and roll it into an 8-inch round paratha.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e980f04c437aa13304ab0d2','5e2591a2057fd3f6fc80eec8',4,'M2: Make pleats & roll the laccha paratha','Next, apply a teaspoon of cooking oil over it and dust some wheat flour. Then, gently pleat it as shown. Stretch it lengthwise and roll it into a circle, securing the end tight. Make the rest of the pleated dough balls similarly. Dust the pleated dough ball into the wheat flour and pat it gently. Then, roll it into a 7-inch round paratha. Make sure to roll the edges thin.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e980f1fc437aa13304ab0d3','5e2591a2057fd3f6fc80eec8',5,'M3: Toast the paratha','To toast the Plain Laccha Paratha place the rolled laccha paratha onto a hot tawa and cook it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Flip and cook both the sides of paratha until slightly golden. Then, apply half a teaspoon of cooking oil to each side of the paratha and continue to cook it for another 2-3 minutes, until it turns golden and crisp. As the paratha is evenly cooked from both the sides, take it out onto a plate and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e98102bde86da3ab20984bd','5e579b395fc0995ffcc4140b',1,'P1: Marinate the Paneer','To marinate the Paneer for Tawa Paneer, first, cube 1 cup of paneer and put it into a large bowl. Add 2 tablespoons of curd, half a teaspoon of Kashmiri red chili powder and 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala followed by half a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Coat the paneer pieces well with the marinade and allow it to rest for 10 minutes. While the paneer is marinating, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e98104dde86da3ab20984be','5e579b395fc0995ffcc4140b',2,'P2: Chop Ingredietms','For Tawa Paneer, peel, wash and finely chop half a cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Wash and dice 1/4 cup of green capsicum. Wash and finely chop 2 nos green chilies. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e98107ac437aa13304ab0d4','5e579b395fc0995ffcc4140b',3,'M1: Cook Spices and Onions','To make Tawa Paneer Masala, heat 2 tablespoons of cooking oil over a tawa for a minute. Add half a cup of chopped onions and fry it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Add 2 nos chopped green chilies and saute it for 2-3 minutes until onion turns golden brown. Add a teaspoon of ginger-garlic paste and fry it with the onions for a minute. Add 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes and saute it over medium flame for 3-4 minutes, until it turns tender.','cook_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e98109ed4c21142148b36d2','5e579b395fc0995ffcc4140b',4,'M2: Continue Cooking','After cooking the tomatoes, add 1/4 cup of diced green capsicum. Stir and fry the capsicum over medium flame for 2-3 minutes, until tender-crisp. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, half a teaspoon of Kashmiri red chili powder and half a teaspoon of coriander powder followed by half a teaspoon of cumin powder and half a teaspoon of chat masala. Add half a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Saute and fry the masala for 2-3 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e9810a0c437aa13304ab0d5','5e269321057fd3f6fc80eecc',1,'P1: Chop & prep the ingredients','For Red Coconut Chutney, grate half a cup of fresh coconut using a grater. Wash, peel and roughly chop a 1/2-inch piece of ginger. Peel and wash 2 cloves of garlic. Wash 6 nos curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9810bede86da3ab20984bf','5e579b395fc0995ffcc4140b',5,'M3: Cook Gravy','After frying the masala, add 1/4 cup of water to it and mix it well. Then, cook the masala over medium-low flame for 6-7 minutes while stirring in between. As the masala releases oil, add the marinated paneer pieces and mix it well. Saute and cook the paneer pieces with the masala over medium-low flame for 5 minutes. While it is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('5e9810c9de86da3ab20984c0','5e269321057fd3f6fc80eecc',2,'M1: Blend the ingredients & make the chutney','To make the Red Coconut Chutney, in a blender jar, add half a cup of grated fresh coconut. Add 2 teaspoons of roasted Bengal gram, 2 nos Kashmiri dry red chilies and 1 tablespoon of tamarind. Next, add a 1/2-inch piece of chopped ginger followed by a garlic clove and half a teaspoon of salt. Add 1/4 cup of water and blend it well into a smooth chutney. Then, transfer it into a bowl and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9810d8de86da3ab20984c1','5e579b395fc0995ffcc4140b',6,'M4: Garnish','For Tawa Paneer, after frying the paneer pieces well with the masala, add a teaspoon of Kasuri methi and a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves. Mix it well and take it out into a bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('5e9810f0de86da3ab20984c2','5e269321057fd3f6fc80eecc',3,'M2: Prepare the tempering & add it to the chutney','To make the tempering for Red Coconut Chutney, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a small tempering pan over medium flame for a minute. Add half a teaspoon of mustard seeds and 1/4 teaspoon of urad dal followed by a dry red chili and 6 nos curry leaves. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Then, turn off the flame and add this tempering instantly over the prepared chutney. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e98114ac437aa13304ab0d6','5e579a205fc0995ffcc4140a',1,'P1: Chop Ingredients','For Lauki Sabzi, wash, peel and cube 1.5 cups of bottle gourd. Wash, peel and finely chop a 1-inch piece of ginger. Wash and finely chop 1 nos green chili. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e98117ad4c21142148b36d3','5e269c2f4f28558c29df6438',1,'P1: Knead & rest the chapathi dough','To make Paneer Kaati Roll, first make the chapati dough, in a bowl mix 1/2 cup of whole wheat flour, 1/4 tsp of salt, and 1/2 tsp oil. Next, gradually add 1/4 cup of water and knead the dough for 5 mins. Once the dough is smooth and soft, coat it with oil, cover it, and let it rest for 20 mins. While the dough is rest move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e98117bde86da3ab20984c3','5e579a205fc0995ffcc4140a',2,'M1: Temper Spices','To make Lauki Sabzi, heat 1 teaspoon of mustard oil in a Kadai over medium flame for a minute. Add half a teaspoon of mustard seeds followed by half a teaspoon of cumin seeds and 1/4 teaspoon of hing. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 1 chopped green chili along with a 1-inch piece of chopped ginger. Add 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and saute it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9811a3d4c21142148b36d4','5e269c2f4f28558c29df6438',2,'P2: Marinate the paneer','Next, chop 200 g of paneer into cubes and then place in a large bowl and add 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder, 1 tsp of red chili powder, 1 tsp of coriander powder, 1/2 ts of garam masala, 1 tsp of cumin powder, 1/2 tsp of chaat masala, 1/2 tsp of salt, 1 tbsp of curd, and 1/2 tsp of lime juice. Combine all ingredients well and let the paneer marinate for 20 mins.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9811a5d4c21142148b36d5','5e579a205fc0995ffcc4140a',3,'M2: Cook Vegetables','Next, add 1.5 cups of cubed bottle gourd followed by half a teaspoon of salt and 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder and mix it well. Stir and fry the bottle gourd over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Then, cover it with a lid and allow it to simmer for 7-8 minutes until it turns tender. While the bottle gourd is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e9811bcd4c21142148b36d6','5e579a205fc0995ffcc4140a',4,'M3: Final Touches','After simmering the Lauki Sabzi, take off the lid and stir it well. Then, fry the bottle gourd over medium-high flame for 3-4 minutes to reduce the extra water. Then, turn off the flame and take it out into a serving bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e9811ccd4c21142148b36d7','5e269c2f4f28558c29df6438',3,'P3: Make the green chutney','Next, make the green chutney, in a blending jar add, 1/4 cup of mint leaves, 1/4 cup of coriander leaves, 1 green chili, 2 cloves of garlic, 1/2 inch of ginger, 1/2 tsp of lime juice, 1/4 tsp of cumin seeds, 2 tsp of curd, 1/4 tsp of black salt. Blend this and make a smooth chutney. Once this is ready, set it aside, and move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9811f2d4c21142148b36d8','5e269c2f4f28558c29df6438',4,'P4: Prepare the vegetable stuffing','Next, prep the vegetable filling, wash and julienne 1/4 cup of green capsicum, peel and julienne 1/4 cup of onions and 1/4 cup of carrots, and wash and julienne 1/2 cup of cabbage. In a large bowl combine all the chopped vegetables with 1 tsp of chaat masala. Once the ingredients are combined, set them aside and move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e981217c437aa13304ab0d7','5e269c2f4f28558c29df6438',5,'M1: Cook the marinated paneer','For Paneer Kaati Roll, in a pan heat 2 tsp of oil and then add the marinated paneer. Cook it on high flame for 5 mins, occasionally stirring and once this is done, set it aside. Move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":4,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e981243d4c21142148b36d9','5e269c2f4f28558c29df6438',6,'M2: Make the chapathis','Next, take the rested dough, and make 2 small lemon sized balls from it. Flaten them slightly with your palms, dush them in flour, and with a rolling pin roll them into large circular shapes. Next, heat a tawa and once hot place the rolled chapati on it. Let it cook on each side for 2 mins, then coat both sides in 1/4 tsp of oil each, and cook them for another 2 mins on each side. Once the chapati has browned evenly on both sides take it off the tawa and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e98128cde86da3ab20984c4','5e269c2f4f28558c29df6438',7,'M3: Assemble the kathi roll & serve','Now we will assemble the kathi roll with the ingredients we have prepared. On a roti spread 2 tsp of green chutney, add 1/4 cup of the vegetable filling, 3 tsp of the cooked paneer, and then roll the chapati shut. Prepare another roll in the same way and enjoy.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e98132cd4c21142148b36da','5e269e73057fd3f6fc80eecd',1,'P1: Soak the onions in vinegar & prep the ingredients','For the Greek Salad, wash, peel and finely slice 1/4 cup of onion. Soak the onions in 1 cup of cold water with 1 teaspoon of vinegar for 10 minutes to reduce the raw and pungent flavor of the onions. Meanwhile, wash and cube 1/2 cup of cucumber. Wash and slice 1/4 cup of green capsicum. Wash and cut 1/2 cup of cherry tomatoes into halves. Cut 1/2 cup of feta cheese into cubes. Wash 5 nos oregano leaves. After soaking the onion for 10 minutes, squeeze it well and rinse it with water.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e98134dde86da3ab20984c5','5e269e73057fd3f6fc80eecd',2,'M1: Make the salad dressing','To make the dressing for the Greek Salad, pour 3 tablespoons of olive oil into a mixing bowl. Next, add 1.5 tablespoons of red wine vinegar, 1/4 teaspoon of salt, 1/2 teaspoon of black pepper powder and 1/2 teaspoon dried oregano and mix well.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e981382d4c21142148b36db','5e269e73057fd3f6fc80eecd',3,'M2: Add the dressing to the salad.  Garnish & serve','To make the Greek Salad, take a large mixing bowl, add 1/2 cup of cubed cucumber, 1/4 cup of sliced green capsicum, 1/2 cup of halved cherry tomatoes. Next, add 3 tablespoons of pitted kalamata olives and 1/4 cup of sliced and rinsed onions. Next, pour the prepared dressing over the salad and mix well. Add 1/2 cup of cubed feta cheese to the salad. Garnish it with 5 nos of fresh oregano leaves and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e981436c437aa13304ab0d8','5e26a863057fd3f6fc80eece',1,'P1: Preheat the oven & prep the ingredients','For Roasted Tomato and Red Pepper Soup, preheat the oven to 200 degrees C. Meanwhile, wash and cut 1.5 cups of tomatoes into quarters. Wash and roughly chop 1/2 cup of red capsicum. Peel 4 cloves of garlic. Wash, peel and slice 1/4 cup of onions. Wash 7 nos basil leaves. Crush 1/2 teaspoon of black peppercorns to a coarse powder using a pepper grinder.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e981466de86da3ab20984c6','5e26a863057fd3f6fc80eece',2,'M1: Bake the vegetables','To bake the vegetables for Roasted Tomato and Red Pepper Soup, line a baking tray with parchment paper. Next, add 1.5 cups of quartered tomatoes, 1/2 cup of chopped red capsicum, 4 cloves of garlic and 1/4 cup of sliced onions to the tray. Sprinkle 1/4 teaspoon of salt, 1/4 teaspoon of crushed black pepper and drizzle 1 teaspoon of olive oil over it. Place the baking tray in the preheated oven and bake it at 200 degrees C for 40-45 minutes. While the vegetables are baking, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":45,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":45,"flame":0}'),('5e981495d4c21142148b36dc','5e26a863057fd3f6fc80eece',3,'M2: Puree the roasted vegetables','After baking the vegetables, take it out from the oven and let it cool down completely. After it cools down, transfer it to a blender jar, add 5 nos basil leaves, 1/2 teaspoon of oregano and blend it to a smooth puree.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9814b5d4c21142148b36dd','5e26a863057fd3f6fc80eece',4,'M3: Simmer the soup. Garnish & serve','To make the Roasted Tomato and Red Pepper Soup, pour the prepared red pepper puree in a deep bottom pan, add 1 cup of water and stir it well. Bring the soup to a boil on medium-high flame. After a boil, turn off the flame. Add 2 teaspoons of fresh cream to the soup and garnish it with 2 nos basil leaves. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e98153cd4c21142148b36de','5e26ab7c985ffca18ae8faae',1,'AP1: Soak the rolled oats','To make Apple Cinnamon Overnight Oats, first wash and then grate 1/2 cup of apple. Next, in a bowl add 1 cup of rolled oats, 2 tbsp of chia seeds, 1/2 tsp of salt, 1/2 cup of greek yogurt, 1 cup of milk, 1/2 cup of grated apple, 4 tsp of honey, and mix well. Once the ingredients are combined, place then in the fridge overnight or for at least 4 hours.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":240,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e981567de86da3ab20984c7','5e26ab7c985ffca18ae8faae',2,'M1: Garnish with chopped walnuts & serve','For Apple Cinnamon Overnight Oats, Roughly chope 1 tbsp of walnuts and garnish your bowl of oats with it. Your dish is ready to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9815c8de86da3ab20984c9','5e26ad6d985ffca18ae8faaf',1,'P1: Pressure cook the rice','To cook the rice for Coconut Rice, wash 1.5 cups of sona masuri rice well with water. Next, put the washed rice in a pressure cooker with 3 cups of water. Cover it with a lid and pressure cook it on high flame till one whistle. After the first whistle, reduce it to low flame, and continue to cook it for another 8 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the rice is cooking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9815f0de86da3ab20984cb','5e26ad6d985ffca18ae8faaf',2,'P2 Chop & prep the ingredients','For Coconut Rice, wash, peel and finely chop a 1-inch piece of ginger. Wash and slit 2 nos green chilies. Wash 5 nos curry leaves. Grate 3/4 cup of fresh coconut using a grater.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e981625d4c21142148b36e0','5e26ad6d985ffca18ae8faaf',3,'M1: Temper the oil & fry the cashews','To make Coconut Rice, heat 3 teaspoons of cooking oil in a pan on medium flame for a minute. Add 1 teaspoon of mustard seeds, 1/2 teaspoon of urad dal, 1 teaspoon of chana dal, 5 nos curry leaves and 1 nos dry red chili to it. Saute and let it splutter on medium flame for a few seconds. Next, add 2 nos slit green chilies and 1 inch piece of chopped ginger and saute it on medium flame for another 1-2 minutes. Then, add 10 cashew nuts and fry it for 3-4 minutes till it turns slightly golden.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e98164ed4c21142148b36e2','5e26ad6d985ffca18ae8faaf',4,'M2: Simmer the rice with coconut. Garnish & serve','After frying the cashew nuts, add 3/4 cup of grated coconut and saute it on medium-low flame for a minute. Then, add 2 cups of cooked rice along with 1/2 teaspoon of salt and mix it gently. Cover it with a lid and simmer the rice for 2 minutes. After simmering the rice, take off the lid and give it a stir. Turn off the flame and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e9816d4c437aa13304ab0d9','5e26bde4985ffca18ae8fab2',1,'P1: Pressure cook the dal','To cook toor dal for Methi Dal Fry, wash 3/4 cups of toor dal well with water. Transfer the washed dal to a pressure cooker with 1.5 cups of water and cover it with a lid. Pressure cook it on high flame till one whistle. After the first whistle, reduce it to low flame and continue to cook the dal for another 8 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the dal is cooking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e9816fcc437aa13304ab0db','5e26bde4985ffca18ae8fab2',2,'P2: Chop fenugreek leaves & prep the ingredients','For Methi Dal Fry, wash half a bunch of fenugreek leaves well with water, dab it on a kitchen towel to remove excess water and let it dry completely. Then, remove the stems and finely chop 1/2 cup of fenugreek leaves. Wash, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Peel and roughly chop 2 cloves of garlic. Wash and slit 1 nos green chili lengthwise. Wash 5 nos curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e981730de86da3ab20984cf','5e26bde4985ffca18ae8fab2',3,'M1: Temper the oil and fry the garlic','To make Methi Dal Fry, heat 1.5 teaspoons of cooking oil in a deep bottom pan on medium flame for a minute. Add 1/2 teaspoon of mustard seeds, 1/2 teaspoon of cumin seeds, 1 nos dry red chili, 1/2 teaspoon of hing and 5 nos curry leaves. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 2 cloves of chopped garlic and saute it on medium-high flame for 1-2 minutes till the garlic turns aromatic.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e981765de86da3ab20984d0','5e26bde4985ffca18ae8fab2',4,'M2: Fry the onions & cook the tomatoes','After frying the garlic, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions and 1 nos slit green chili. Stir fry the onions on medium-high flame for 2-3 minutes, till it turns slightly translucent. After frying the onions, add 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes to it. Saute and cook the tomatoes on medium-low flame for 3-4 minutes, till it turns tender.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9817a3d4c21142148b36e4','5e26bde4985ffca18ae8fab2',5,'M3: Simmer the dal with fenugreek leaves. Garnish & serve','After cooking the tomatoes, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, 1/2 teaspoon of Kashmiri red chili powder, and 1/2 teaspoon of salt and saute it on low flame for a minute. Next, add 1/2 cup of chopped fenugreek leaves and fry it on low flame for 2-3 minutes. After frying it, add the cooked toor dal and mix it well. Add 1/4 cup of water if required, to adjust the consistency of the dal. Cover it with a lid and simmer it for 5 minutes. After simmering the dal, take off the lid and give it a stir. Turn off the flame and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e98181dde86da3ab20984d1','5e26c2da057fd3f6fc80eed2',1,'AP1: Rinse & soak the rice','For Kerala Matta Rice, first, wash 1 cup of Kerela matta rice well with water. Then, soak it in 2 cups of water for 2 hours. While the rice is soaking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e981844c437aa13304ab0dc','5e26c2da057fd3f6fc80eed2',2,'M1: Pressure cook the rice','To make the Kerela Matta Rice, drain off the water from the soaked Kerala rice and add it to a pressure cooker. Add 2 cups of water into it and cover it with a lid. Pressure cook the rice over medium flame for 3-4 whistles. After that, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook it for another 8 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the rice is cooking, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e981873c437aa13304ab0dd','5e26c2da057fd3f6fc80eed2',3,'M2:  Add water & boil the rice. Rest & serve','After cooking the Kerela Matta Rice, remove the lid and gently mix it. Add about half a cup of water along with a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Then, bring it to a boil over high flame. As it comes to a boil, turn off the flame and drain off the excess water from the rice. Allow it to sit for another 5 minutes. Then, serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9818c4de86da3ab20984d2','5e26c527985ffca18ae8fab3',1,'P1: Prep the ingredients','For Kanda Poha, wash and finely chop 3/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 2 nos green chilies. Grate 2 tablespoons of fresh coconut using a coconut grater. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves. Wash and cut a lime into halves. Then, squeeze 2 teaspoons of lime juice using a lemon squeezer. Wash 8 nos curry leaves well with water.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9818f6d4c21142148b36e5','5e26c527985ffca18ae8fab3',2,'M1: Soak & rinse the poha','For Kanda Poha, first, add 1.5 cups of poha in a large mixing bowl and soak it in 2 cups of water for 2 minutes. After that, drain off the water from it. Next, add a teaspoon of sugar along with 3/4 teaspoon of salt and gently mix it.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e981923d4c21142148b36e6','5e26c527985ffca18ae8fab3',3,'M2: Roast the peanuts & fry the onions','To make the Kanda Poha, heat 2 tablespoons of cooking oil in a kadai over medium flame for a minute. Add 2 tablespoons of peanuts and roast it on low flame until it turns slightly golden brown. Then, take out the roasted peanuts in a bowl and set it aside. Next, temper the oil with 1 teaspoon of cumin seeds and 1/4 teaspoon of hing. Add 8 nos curry leaves and saute it for a minute. Next, add 3/4 cups of chopped onions followed by 2 nos chopped green chilies and saute it over medium flame for 3-4 minutes until it turns slightly golden.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e981943d4c21142148b36e7','5e26c527985ffca18ae8fab3',4,'M3: Simmer the poha','After frying the onions, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder and mix it well. Saute and continue to fry the onions over medium flame for another minute. Next, add the soaked poha along with the roasted peanuts and mix it gently. Keep stirring it with light hands until the yellow color of turmeric evenly sets on the poha. Then, cover it with a lid and simmer it on low flame for 5 minutes. While the poha is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e981974d4c21142148b36e8','5e26c527985ffca18ae8fab3',5,'M4: Add a dash of lime. Garnish & serve','After simmering the Kanda Poha, take off the lid and add 2 tablespoons of grated coconut along with 2 tablespoons of chopped coriander leaves. Add 2 teaspoons of lime juice and mix it well. Turn off the flame and take it out into a serving bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9819dcd4c21142148b36e9','5e26c97d057fd3f6fc80eed4',1,'AP1: Soak the black chickpeas','To make Kadala Curry, soak 1/2 cup of black chickpeas in 1.5 cups of water for 8 hours or overnight.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":480,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e981a2bd4c21142148b36ea','5e26c97d057fd3f6fc80eed4',2,'P1: Pressure cook the black chickpeas','To make Kadala Curry, cook 1/2 cup of soaked black chickpeas in a pressure cooker with 1/4 tsp of salt and 2 cups of water. Cook this on high flame for 1 whistle and then on low flame for 8 mins. Once this is cooked, allow the pressure to release naturally before you open the lid. While the chickpeas are cooking, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e981a6cc437aa13304ab0de','5e26c97d057fd3f6fc80eed4',3,'P2: Prep the ingredients','Next, Peel and roughly chop 3 shallots. Wash 12 curry leaves. Wash and slit 1 green chilli. Wash and roughly chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Wash and slice 1/4 cup of onions. Peel 1 clove of garlic. Peel and roughyl chop 1/2 inch of ginger.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e981a9cde86da3ab20984d3','5e26c97d057fd3f6fc80eed4',4,'M1: Make the masala paste','For Kadala Curry, in a pan heat 1 tsp of coconut oil and then add 1/2 inch of cinnamon, 1 green cardamom, 2 cloves, 1/2 tsp of fennel seeds, and let this splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 1/4 cup of sliced onions, 1 clove of garlic, 1/2 inch of chopped ginger, and saute for 2-3 mins. Once the onions are golden, add 1/4 cup of tomatoes and saute for 2 mins. Once the tomatoes are soft, add 1/4 cup of grated coconut, 6 curry leaves, and mix well. Next, add 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder, 1/4 tsp of red chili powder, 1/2 tsp of coriander powder, 1/4 tsp of garam masala, and mix well. Once the ingredients are combined well, let them cool down completely, and then blend them into a smooth paste with 1/4 cup of water. Once this is ready, set it aside, and move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e981ac9de86da3ab20984d4','5e26c97d057fd3f6fc80eed4',5,'M2: Simmer the kadala curry. Garnish & serve','Next, in a pan heat 1tsp of coconut oil and then add 1/2 tsp of mustard seeds, 1 broken dry red chili, 6 curry leaves, and let this splutter for a few seconds. Then, add 3 chopped shallots, 1 slit green chili, and saute this for 2 mins. After that, add the prepared vegetable paste and saute for 3 mins. Next, add 1/2 cup of cooked black chickpeas and 1/4 tsp of salt and mix well. Cover the pan with a lid and let the curry cook for 15 mins. After this, the curry will be ready to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e981b4cd4c21142148b36eb','5e26cebb4f28558c29df6441',1,'AP1: Soak the chickpeas','To make Falafel Salad, first, soak 1/2 cup of chickpeas in 1.5 cups of water for 12 hours.','prep_method','{"active_time":1,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":720,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e981b6dc437aa13304ab0df','5e26cebb4f28558c29df6441',2,'P1: Pressure cook the chickpeas','To make Falafel Salad, in a pressure cooker add 1/2 cup of soaked chickpeas, 1.25 cups of water, 1/4 tsp of salt, and 1/4 tsp of oil, give it a stir. Cook this on high flame for 1 whistle and then on low flame for 8 mins. Once this is done, allow the cooker to release pressure naturally before you open the lid. While the chickpeas are cooking move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e981b8cc437aa13304ab0e0','5e26cebb4f28558c29df6441',3,'P2: Chop & prep the ingredients','Next, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions and slice another 1/4 cup of onions.  Wash and half 1/4 cup of cherry tomatoes. Wash and roughly chop 1 cup of romaine lettuce. Wash and slice 1/4 cup of cucumber. Wash and slice 1/4 cup of red radish. Squeeze 2 tbsp of lime juice. Wash and roughly chop 1 cup of parsley. Peel and roughly chop 2 cloves of garlic.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e981bdac437aa13304ab0e1','5e26cebb4f28558c29df6441',4,'M1: Make the chickpea mixture & prepare the falafels','For Falafel Salad, in a large mixing bowl mash 1/2 cup of cooked chickpeas and then add 1/2 cup of chopped parsley, 1/4 cup of chopped onions, 2 cloves of chopped garlic, 3 tbsp of olive oil, 1 tbsp lime juice, 1/2 tbsp of cumin powder, and 1/2 tsp of salt. Combine all these ingredients for 5 mins, until it forms a dough. Once the dough is made, make small lemon sized balls from the dough and flatten it using your palms to make the falafels. Once all the dough is prepped, heat 1 tbsp of olive oil in a pan, and then place the falafels on top gently. Cook them on each side for 3-5 mins, until the falafels are evenly browned on both sides. Once the falafels are cooked, set them aside, and move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":14,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e981c09d4c21142148b36ec','5e5791425fc0995ffcc41409',1,'P1: Blanch Cauliflower','To blanch the cauliflower for Gobhi Sabzi, first, wash and cut 1.5 cups of cauliflower into small florets. Next, add 3 cups of water in a pan. Add half a teaspoon of salt followed by 1/4 teaspoon of salt into the water. Then, bring it to a boil over a high flame. As it comes to a rolling boil, add 1.5 cups of cauliflower florets and stir it well. Then, allow it to boil over medium flame for 2 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and drain off the water from it and set it aside. While the cauliflower florets are blanching, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":4}'),('5e981c26de86da3ab20984d5','5e26cebb4f28558c29df6441',5,'M2: Make the dressing & combine the salad. Garnish & serve','Next, in another large bowl, make the salad dressing, whisk 3 tbsp of tahini, 3 tbsp of warm water, 1 tbsp of olive oil, 1 tbsp of lime juice, and 1/2 tsp of salt. Once this is combined, reserve 1/2 the prepared salad dressing in a small bowl. Then, add 1 cup of romaine lettuce and 1/2 cup of chopped parsley, toss this in the dressing and then put it on a serving plate once it''s mixed well. Top the greens with 1/4 cup of chopped cucumber, 1/4 cup of cherry tomatoes, 1/4 cup of radishes, 1/4 cup of sliced onions, the prepared falafels, and the reserved salad dressing. The dish is ready to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e981c31de86da3ab20984d6','5e5791425fc0995ffcc41409',2,'P2: Prep Other Ingredients','For Gobhi Sabzi, first, soak 1/4 cup of green peas in 1 cup of water for 5 minutes. Next, peel, wash and finely chop half a cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes. Wash, peel and finely chop a half-inch piece of ginger. Wash and slit 2 nos green chilies. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves. Wash and cut a lemon into halves and squeeze 1 teaspoon of lime juice. Wash 7 nos curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e981c5dde86da3ab20984d7','5e5791425fc0995ffcc41409',3,'M1: Cook Spices and Onions','To make Gobhi Sabzi, heat 1.5 tablespoons of cooking oil in a kadai over medium flame for a minute. Add a half-inch piece of chopped ginger followed by 2 nos slit green chilies and 7 nos curry leaves. Saute and let it splutter over medium flame for a minute. Next, add half a cup of chopped onions and fry it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes, until translucent. Make sure not to brown the onions.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e981c88d4c21142148b36ed','5e5791425fc0995ffcc41409',4,'M2: Add Masala Powders','After frying the onions, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder followed by half a teaspoon of Kashmiri red chili powder and half a teaspoon of salt. Mix it well and fry the masala over low flame for 2-3 minutes. Then, add 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes and mix it well. Saute and cook the tomatoes over medium flame for 4-5 minutes until tender.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e981c9ec437aa13304ab0e2','5e26d0db985ffca18ae8fab5',1,'P1: Knead & prepare the dough','To make Akki Roti, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Peel and grate 1/4 cup of carrot. Peel and finely chop 1/2 inch of ginger. Wash and finely chop 1 green chilli. Wash and finely chop 1 tbsp of coriander leaves. Next, in a large mixing bowl combine 3/4 cup of rice flour, add 1/4 cup of onions, 1 green chili, 1 tbsp coriander leaves, 1/2 inch of ginger, 1/4 cup of carrots, 1/2 tsp of cumin powder, 1/2 tsp of salt, and mix well. Then, gradually add 1/2 cup of water to the flour to make a dough, knead it for 5 mins until you have a smooth and soft dough.','prep_method','{"active_time":11,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e981cd7d4c21142148b36ee','5e26d0db985ffca18ae8fab5',2,'M1: Roll the chapatis & cook. Serve','For Akki Roti, make a small lemon sized ball from the prepared dough, spread 1 tsp of oil on parchment paper and flatten this dough with wet hands until you have a circular shape.  Make 3 holes in the center of the roti and then heat a tawa with 1 tsp of oil for 1 min on medium flame. Place the raw roti on the tawa and roast on one side for 1 min. Next, flip the roti and drizzle 1 tsp of oil and cook on this side for another minute. Cook the roti until both sides have browned evenly and then place it on a plate. Repeat this process with the remaining dough until you have the desired number of roti. Enjoy.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e981d08c437aa13304ab0e3','5e5791425fc0995ffcc41409',5,'M3: Continue Cooking the Sabzi','After the tomatoes turn tender, add 1.5 cups of blanched cauliflower florets followed by 1/4 cup of frozen and soaked green peas. Then, gently mix it. Saute the vegetables with light hands for 1-2 minutes. Then, add 2 tablespoons of water and cover it with a lid. Allow it to simmer for 5 minutes. While the Gobhi Sabzi is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e981d25de86da3ab20984d8','5e5791425fc0995ffcc41409',6,'M4: Garnish','After simmering the Gobhi Sabzi, take off the lid and gently mix it. Add a teaspoon of lemon juice followed by 2 tablespoons of chopped coriander leaves and mix it well. Turn off the flame and take it out into a serving bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),
('5e981ee4d4c21142148b36f4','5e26ebe44f28558c29df6444',1,'P1: Soak the rice','For Palak Pulao, first, rinse 1 cup of basmati rice well with water and soak it into 2 cups of water for 30 minutes. While the rice is soaking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":30,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e981f25c437aa13304ab0e5','5e26ebe44f28558c29df6444',2,'P2: Chop & prep the ingredients','For Palak Puloa, wash a bunch of spinach leaves thoroughly with water to remove all the dirt. Then, cut off the stems and separate 3 cups of spinach leaves. Next, finely chop the spinach leaves. Peel, wash and finely chop half a cup of onions. Peel, wash and slice 1/4 cup onions into thin rings. Wash and slit 2 nos green chilies. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e981f51de86da3ab20984dc','5e26ebe44f28558c29df6444',3,'M1: Temper the oil with whole spices & fry onions','To make the Palak Pulao, heat 2 teaspoons of ghee in a pressure cooker over medium flame for a minute. Add 1 tablespoon of oil into it. Next, add half an inch piece of cinnamon stick, 3 nos green cardamoms, and 4 nos cloves followed by half a teaspoon of black peppercorns and 1 nos star anise. Add half a teaspoon of cumin seeds along with a bay leaf. Next, add half a cup of chopped onions and fry it over medium-high flame, until it turns slightly translucent. Add 2 nos slit green chilies and saute it for a minute.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e981f7ec437aa13304ab0e7','5e26ebe44f28558c29df6444',4,'M2: Stir-fry the spinach leaves with the masala','After frying the onions, add half a teaspoon of ginger-garlic paste and mix it well. Saute and continue to fry it for another 1-2 minutes over medium flame. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, 1 teaspoon of red chili powder, and 1 teaspoon of coriander powder followed by 1 teaspoon of cumin powder and half a teaspoon of garam masala and mix it well. Fry the masala over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Next, add 3 cups of chopped spinach leaves and mix it well with the masala. Add a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Stir and fry the spinach leaves for 2-3 minutes over medium flame until it slightly changes colour. Make sure not to overcook the spinach leaves, or it might turn dark.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e981fa7c437aa13304ab0e9','5e26ebe44f28558c29df6444',5,'M3: Pressure cook the pulao. Garnish & serve','After frying the spinach leaves with the masala, add 1 cup of soaked basmati rice and mix it gently. Add 2 cups of water into it and stir it well. Cover it with a lid and pressure cook it on high flame till one whistle. After the first whistle, reduce the flame to low, and continue to simmer it for another 8 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. After the pressure from the cooker is released, take off the lid and gently mix the pulao. Take it out into a serving bowl and garnish it with sliced onion rings and 2 tablespoons of chopped coriander leaves. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e982065de86da3ab20984de','5e26f24b985ffca18ae8fab7',1,'P1: Boil the eggs','In a saucepan, add 5 nos raw eggs. Add 4 cup water into it, enough to cover them, and let it come to a boil on high flame. Once it has come to a boil, further cook the eggs for 8 minutes on medium-high flame. While the eggs are boiling, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":4}'),('5e9820a1d4c21142148b36f6','5e5780f14e4267296216c92f',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Bhindi Peanut Masala, first, soak a teaspoon of tamarind in 1/4 cup of water for 10 minutes. Next, wash 1 cup of lady''s fingers well with water and spread it over a kitchen towel to wipe off the extra water. Allow it to dry completely and make sure there is no moisture left in the lady''s fingers. Then, cut it into 1-inch pieces. Next, peel, wash and chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and roughly chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. After soaking the tamarind, mash it and mix it well with water. Then, strain it to avoid any lumps.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9820d1c437aa13304ab0ea','5e5780f14e4267296216c92f',2,'P2: Fry Peanuts','To roast the peanuts for Bhindi Peanut Masala, Heat half a teaspoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Next, add 1/4 cup of peanuts followed by 1 nos dry red chili and a tablespoon of crushed coriander seeds and dry roast it over medium flame for 3-4 minutes, until it changes color. After that, add 3/4 teaspoon of poppy seeds and roast it over low flame for a minute. As the peanuts turn crunchy, turn off the flame and take it out into a blender jar. Allow it to cool down completely. While it is cooling down, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9820fbde86da3ab20984df','5e5780f14e4267296216c92f',3,'P3: Prepare a Masala Paste','To prepare the masala paste for Bhindi Peanut Masala, heat a teaspoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes and fry it over medium flame for 2 minutes. Next, add half a teaspoon of turmeric powder followed by 1/4 teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Next, add 3/4 teaspoon of ginger-garlic paste and mix it well. Saute and fry the masala over medium flame for 2-3 minutes, until tomatoes turn tender. Then turn off the flame and allow it cool down for some time. After that, transfer it to the blender jar with the peanuts and blend it together into a smooth paste.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e982121de86da3ab20984e0','5e5780f14e4267296216c92f',4,'M1: Fry Lady''s Finger','To fry the lady''s fingers for Bhindi Peanut Masala, heat a teaspoon of cooking oil in a kadai over medium flame for a minute. Add 1 cup of chopped ladies fingers and fry it over medium flame for 4-5 minutes, until tender-crisp. Then, turn off the flame and take it out into a bowl.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e982146d4c21142148b36f7','5e5780f14e4267296216c92f',5,'M2: Cook onions','To make Bhindi Peanut Masala, heat a teaspoon of cooking oil in a kadai over medium flame for a minute. Add 1/4 cup of chopped onions to it. Saute and fry the onions over medium flame for 3-4 minutes until it turns slightly translucent. Next, add the prepared peanut masala paste and mix it well. Saute and cook the masala over medium flame for 3-4 minutes until oil separates.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e98216fd4c21142148b36f8','5e5780f14e4267296216c92f',6,'M3: Cook Gravy','After cooking the masala, add about 1/4 cup of water, if required to adjust the consistency and mix it well. Add the prepared tamarind pulp and stit it well. Then, cover it with a lid and simmer it for 1-2 minutes. After that, take off the lid and add the fried ladies fingers. Mix it well and cover it with a lid. Continue to simmer the lady''s fingers for another 5 minutes. While it is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e98218fd4c21142148b36f9','5e5780f14e4267296216c92f',7,'M4: Garnish','After simmering the Bhindi Peanut Masala, take off the lid and mix it well. Turn off the flame and garnish it with a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('5e982228c437aa13304ab0eb','5e577fd74e4267296216c92e',1,'P1: Prepare the Milk','For Plain Naan, first, add half a cup of milk in a saucepan and heat it over medium flame for a minute. Then, turn off the flame and transfer it to a large bowl. Next, add 1 tablespoon of cooking oil into it. Next, add a teaspoon of powdered sugar followed by half a teaspoon of salt and half a teaspoon of baking powder. Mix it well to prepare a solution.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e98224ed4c21142148b36fa','5e577fd74e4267296216c92e',2,'P2: Make Dough','Next, add 1 cup of all-purpose flour into the prepared solution and knead it well into a soft dough. Then, cover it with a damp cloth and set it aside for 10 minutes. While the dough is resting, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e982275de86da3ab20984e1','5e577fd74e4267296216c92e',3,'M1: Rolling the Dough','To make the Plain Naan, divide the prepared dough into small equal-sized balls. Dust some flour over it and keep it covered with the damp cloth until use. Take a dough ball, dust some four over it and roll into a slightly thick round naan. Apply a tablespoon of water over it as shown.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e98229dde86da3ab20984e2','5e577fd74e4267296216c92e',4,'M2: Cook the Naan','Then, place it onto a hot tawa with the waterside on the bottom and cook it over medium flame for a minute. Then, hold and flip the tawa as shown and cook the other side of the naan over the direct flame until small brown spots appear on its surface. As it turns slightly golden and firm, put the Tawa back on the flame. Then, gently take it out onto a plate and brush half a teaspoon of butter over it. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9822f6de86da3ab20984e3','5e577f275fc0995ffcc41407',1,'P1: Make the Dough','To knead the dough for Tandoori Roti, in a large mixing bowl, add 1 cup of wheat flour followed by half a cup of all-purpose flour. Next, add half a teaspoon of salt, a teaspoon of powdered sugar and half a teaspoon of baking soda along with a teaspoon of cooking oil. Next, add half a cup of curd into the flour and mix it well.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e982314c437aa13304ab0ec','5e577f275fc0995ffcc41407',2,'P2: Make the Dough','After that, gradually, add about 1/4 cup of milk and knead it well into a smooth dough. Then apply half a teaspoon of cooking oil over it and grease it well. Cover the dough with a plate and set it aside for 20 minutes. While the dough is resting, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":20,"flame":0}'),('5e98232ec437aa13304ab0ed','5e577f275fc0995ffcc41407',3,'M1: Roll the Dough','To make Tandoori Roti, knead the prepared dough for again for a minute. Then, divide it into small equal-sized balls. Take a dough ball, dust some four over it and roll into a thin round roti. Apply a tablespoon of water over it as shown.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e982349d4c21142148b36fb','5e577f275fc0995ffcc41407',4,'M2: Cook the Roti','Then, place it onto a hot tawa with the waterside down and cook it over medium flame for a minute. Then, hold and flip the tawa as shown and cook the other side of the roti over the direct flame until small brown spots appear on its surface. As it turns slightly golden and firm, put the tawa back on the flame. Then, gently take it out onto a plate and brush half a teaspoon of butter over it. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9823a0d4c21142148b36fc','5e5777114e4267296216c92d',1,'P1: Make the Dough','To knead the dough for Makki Roti, in a large mixing bowl, add 1 cup of cornmeal along with 1/4 teaspoon of salt. Next, gradually add about 1/4 cup of water and knead it well into a slightly stiff dough. Then, divide the dough into small equal-sized dough balls.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9823b9c437aa13304ab0ee','5e5777114e4267296216c92d',2,'M1: Make Roti','To make the Makki Roti, dust some cornmeal over the rolling boards and place a prepared dough ball over it. Then, roll it into a thin roti while pressing it gently with palms in a circular motion as shown. Then, carefully place it onto the hot tawa and cook it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes until small brown spots start to appear on its surface. After that, gently flip it and cook the other side for 1-2 minutes. Then, cook the roti over the direct flame while flipping it in between. Cook the roti until both sides are evenly browned. After the roti puffs up, remove it from the flame and take it out onto a serving plate. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e982421c437aa13304ab0ef','5e577627f7851cecaf7c5094',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Methi Thepla, wash and finely chop 1/2 cup of fenugreek leaves. Wash, peel and grate a half-inch piece of ginger. Wash and finely chop 1 nos green chili.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e982556d4c21142148b36fd','5e577627f7851cecaf7c5094',2,'P2: Make Dough','To knead the dough for Methi Thepla, add 3/4 cup of wheat flour to a large mixing bowl. Next, add 1/4 cup of gram four, followed by 1/4 teaspoon of Kashmiri red chili powder, 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder and 1/4 teaspoon of sesame seeds. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of carom seeds along with 1/4 teaspoon of salt.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e982573c437aa13304ab0f0','5e577627f7851cecaf7c5094',3,'P3: Make Dough','Next, add 1 nos chopped green chili followed by a half-inch piece of chopped ginger and half a cup of chopped fenugreek leaves. Mix it well and add 1/4 cup of curd into it. Combine the curd well with the flour. Then, gradually add about 1/4 cup of water and knead it well into a smooth dough. Grease it well with half a teaspoon of cooking oil and allow it to rest for 20 minutes.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":20,"flame":0}'),('5e98259bd4c21142148b36fe','5e577627f7851cecaf7c5094',4,'M1: Make Roti','To make the Methi Thepla, first, divide the prepared into small equal-sized balls. Take a dough ball and dust some flour over it. Then, roll it into a thin round paratha. Make sure to roll out the edges thin. Then, place it onto a hot tawa and cook it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Flip and cook both sides evenly. Then apply half a teaspoon of cooking oil to each side and cook the paratha over medium flame for 2-3 minutes, until it is evenly browned on both the sides. Then, fold it into a triangle and take it out onto a plate. Serve. Make the rest of the parathas similarly.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e982639d4c21142148b36ff','5e5774e9f7851cecaf7c5093',1,'P1: Prep Ingredints','For Mint Chutney, wash and separate 3/4 cup of mint leaves. Wash and peel 5 cloves of garlic, Wash and peel a 1-inch piece of ginger. Wash and slit 1 nos green chili. Grate half a cup of fresh coconut using a grater. Wash 8 nos curry leaves well with water.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e98265ed4c21142148b3700','5e5774e9f7851cecaf7c5093',2,'M1: Cook Ingredients','To make the Mint Chutney, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Temper it with 1/4 teaspoon of urad dal and 1/4 teaspoon of cumin seeds. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 5 cloves of garlic followed by a 1-inch piece of ginger. Saute it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes, until garlic slightly changes color. After that, add 1 nos slit green chili along with 4 nos dry red chilies and saute it over medium flame for a minute. Add a teaspoon of tamarind and mix it well.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e982685c437aa13304ab0f1','5e5774e9f7851cecaf7c5093',3,'M2: Continue Cooking','Next,  add 3/4 cup of mint leaves and fry it over a low flame with the tempering for 2-3 minutes. Make sure not to fry the mint leaves for long, or it may turn dark. As the mint leaves start to shrivel up, add half a cup of grated coconut followed by 1 teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Then, turn off the flame and allow the mixture to cool down completely. While the chutney mixture is cooling down, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('5e9826cade86da3ab20984e4','5e5774e9f7851cecaf7c5093',4,'M3: Make Tadka','To make the Mint Chutney, after the prepared mint mixture cools down, transfer it to a blender jar. Add 1/4 cup of water and blend it well into a smooth chutney. Then take it out into a bowl and set it aside. To make the tempering for the chutney, heat a teaspoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add 1/4 teaspoon of urad dal, 1/4 teaspoon of mustard seeds and 1/4 teaspoon of cumin seeds followed by 1  dry red chili and 1/4 teaspoon of hing. Add 8 curry leaves and saute it over medium flame for a minute. Then, turn off the flame and add this tempering to the prepared chutney. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e98275361e059cac91f60d2','5e577353f7851cecaf7c5092',1,'M1: Cook Tamarind and Dates','To make Tamarind Chutney, in a kadai, add 1/4 cup of tamarind followed by 1/4 cup of dates and 1/4 cup of jaggery. Add 1.5 cups of water and mix it well. Allow it to cook over medium-high flame for 10 minutes until the syrup thickens and jaggery dissolves completely. While the tamarind syrup is cooking, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e982785502823b445d1236f','5e577353f7851cecaf7c5092',2,'M2: Add Spices, etc','After boiling the tamarind syrup for Tamarind Chutney, add 1/4 teaspoon of fennel powder, half a teaspoon of coriander powder, 1/4 teaspoon of cumin powder and half a teaspoon of Kashmiri red chili powder followed by 1/4 teaspoon of dry ginger powder and half a teaspoon of salt. Mix it well and mash the dates and tamarind with the spatula. Then, allow it to simmer for 2 minutes. Keep stirring in between. After simmering it, turn off the flame and allow it to cool down completely. While it is cooling down please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e9827aa502823b445d12370','5e577353f7851cecaf7c5092',3,'M3: Seive Chutney','After the prepared tamarind syrup for Tamarind Chutney cools down, transfer it into a sieve and strain it well into a bowl to remove the granules or any solid chunks. Then, keep it in an airtight jar until use.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e98295461e059cac91f60d3','5e576e5df7851cecaf7c508f',1,'P1: Chop Ingredients','For Beetroot Paratha, wash, peel and grate 3/4 cup of beetroot. Wash and slit 1 nos green chili. Wash and finely chop 1 nos green chili.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e98298e502823b445d12371','5e576e5df7851cecaf7c508f',2,'P2: Cook the Beetroot','For Beetroot Paratha, heat 1 tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add 1/4 teaspoon of ginger paste followed by 1 slit green chili and saute it for 1-2 minutes. Next, add 3/4 cup of grated beetroot along with 1/4 teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Saute and fry the beetroot over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Add 2 tablespoons of water into it. Then, cover it with a lid and allow it to simmer for 10 minutes until it is cooked completely. While the beetroot is simmering, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9829dade86da3ab20984e5','5e576e5df7851cecaf7c508f',3,'P3: Make a Beetroot Paste','After simmering the beetroot for Beetroot Paratha, take off the lid and give it a stir. Then, allow the mixture to cool down completely. After that, transfer it to a blender jar and blend it well into a smooth paste.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9829fede86da3ab20984e6','5e576e5df7851cecaf7c508f',4,'P4: Make Dough','To knead the dough for Beetroot Paratha, add 1 cup of wheat flour in a large mixing bowl. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of cumin powder, 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala and 1/4 teaspoon of dry mango powder followed by 1/4 teaspoon of carom seeds and 1/4 teaspoon of salt and mix it well.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e982a2561e059cac91f60d4','5e576e5df7851cecaf7c508f',5,'P5: Make Dough','Next, add the prepared beetroot paste followed by 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and mix it well. Then, gradually add about 1/4 cup of water and knead it well into a smooth dough. Apply half a teaspoon of cooking oil over the dough and grease it well. Then, cover it with a damp cloth and allow it to rest for 15 minutes. While the dough is resting, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e982a43de86da3ab20984e7','5e576e5df7851cecaf7c508f',6,'M1: Roll The Dough','To make the Beetroot Paratha, first, divide the prepared dough into small equal-sized balls. Next, take a dough ball and dust it into some flour. Then, gently press it and roll it into an 8-inch round paratha. Make sure to roll out the edges thin.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e982a65502823b445d12372','5e576e5df7851cecaf7c508f',7,'M2: Make the Paratha','To toast the Beetroot Paratha place the rolled paratha onto a hot tawa and cook it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Flip and cook both the sides of paratha until slightly golden. Then, apply half a teaspoon of cooking oil to each side of the paratha and continue to cook it for another 2-3 minutes, until it turns golden and crisp. After the paratha is evenly cooked from both the sides, gently fold it into a triangle and take it out onto a plate. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e982b2761e059cac91f60d5','5e576d805fc0995ffcc41403',1,'P1: Prepare the Dough','To prepare the dough for Pudina Laccha Paratha, first, wash and finely chop half a  cup of mint leaves. Next, add 1 cup of wheat flour in a large bowl. Add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, 1/4 teaspoon of Kashmiri red chili powder and 1/4 teaspoon of coriander powder followed by 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala and 1/4 teaspoon of chat masala.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e982b28de86da3ab20984e9','5e576d805fc0995ffcc41403',2,'P2: Prepare the Dough','Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of black pepper powder, half a teaspoon of cumin seeds, and 1/4 teaspoon of ginger paste. Next, add a teaspoon of cooking oil along with half a teaspoon of salt. Next, add half a cup of chopped mint leaves and mix it well. Then, gradually add half a cup of water and knead it well into a smooth dough.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e982b71502823b445d12373','5e576d805fc0995ffcc41403',3,'M1: Roll The Dough','To make Pudina Laccha Paratha, first, divide the prepared dough into small equal-sized balls. Next, take a dough ball and dust it into some flour. Then, gently press it and roll it into an 8-inch round paratha. Make sure to roll out the edges thin.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e982b92502823b445d12374','5e576d805fc0995ffcc41403',4,'M2: Fold the Dough','Next, apply a teaspoon of cooking oil over it and dust some wheat flour. Then, gently pleat it as shown. Stretch it lengthwise and roll it into a circle, securing the end tight. Make the rest of the pleated dough balls similarly. Dust the pleated dough ball into the wheat flour and pat it gently. Then, roll it into a 7-inch round paratha. Make sure to roll the edges thin.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e982bab502823b445d12375','5e576d805fc0995ffcc41403',5,'M3: Cook the Paratha','To toast the Pudina Laccha Paratha place the rolled laccha paratha onto a hot tawa and cook it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Flip and cook both the sides of paratha until slightly golden. Then, apply half a teaspoon of cooking oil to each side of the paratha and continue to cook it for another 2-3 minutes, until it turns golden and crisp. After the paratha is evenly cooked from both the sides, take it out onto a plate and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e983067ece7565dc3f1976e','5e576b7d4e4267296216c925',1,'P1: Blanch Spinach','To blanch the spinach leaves for Palak Paratha, first, wash and separate 1 cup of spinach leaves. Next, boil 3 cups of water in a saucepan over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. As the water comes to a rolling boil, add 1 cup of spinach leaves and boil it over medium-high flame for a minute. Then, turn off the flame and take it out of the hot water. Allow it to cool down completely. While it is cooling down, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e98308f9594ae7391cf4d10','5e576b7d4e4267296216c925',2,'P2: Make Spinach Puree','For Palak Paratha, wash and slit 1 nos green chili. Wash and peel a 1/4-inch piece of ginger. Next, to make the spinach puree, add 1 cup of blanched spinach leaves to a blender jar followed by a 1/4-inch piece of ginger and 1 nos slit green chili. Cover the jar with a lid and blend it well into a smooth puree.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9830c3ece7565dc3f1976f','5e576b7d4e4267296216c925',3,'P3: Make the Dough','To knead the dough for Palak Paratha, add 1 cup of whole wheat flour in a large mixing bowl. Add 1/4 teaspoon of carom seeds followed by half a teaspoon of salt and a teaspoon of cooking oil. Add the prepared spinach puree and mix it well. Next, gradually add about 1/4 cup of water and knead it well into a smooth dough. Grease the dough with half a teaspoon of cooking oil. Then, cover it with a damp cloth and allow it to rest for 30 minutes. While the dough is resting, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":30,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9830e89594ae7391cf4d11','5e576b7d4e4267296216c925',4,'M1: Make Paratha','To make the Palak Paratha, first, divide the prepared into small equal-sized balls. Take a dough ball and dust some flour over it. Then, roll it into a thin round paratha. Make sure to roll out the edges thin. Then, place it onto a hot tawa and cook it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Flip and cook both sides evenly. Then apply half a teaspoon of cooking oil to each side and cook the paratha over medium flame for 2-3 minutes, until it is evenly browned on both the sides. Then, fold it into a triangle and take it out onto a plate. Serve. Make the rest of the parathas similarly.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e9831585df8d42caf6f6b37','5e576a775fc0995ffcc41401',1,'P1: Make the Dough','To knead the dough for Mooli Paratha, first, add 1 cup of wheat flour in a large bowl. Add half a teaspoon of salt followed by half a teaspoon of cooking oil and mix it well. Then, gradually add half a cup of water and knead it well into a smooth dough. Apply a 1/4 teaspoon of cooking oil over it and grease it well. Cover the dough with a damp cloth and set it aside for 20 minutes. While the dough is resting, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":20,"flame":0}'),('5e9831cd9594ae7391cf4d12','5e576a775fc0995ffcc41401',2,'P2: Prep Filling','For Mooli Paratha, wash, peel and grate 3/4 cup of radish in a bowl using a grater. Next, add a teaspoon of salt into it and mix it well.  Adding salt to it will turn the radish moist, hence making it release all the water. Then, let it sit for 5-8 minutes. Meanwhile, wash, peel and finely chop a half-inch piece of ginger. Wash and finely chop 1 nos green chili. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. After the radish releases water, gently squeeze it between the palms as shown to squeeze out the excess water from it. Then, keep it in a separate bowl and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9831f05df8d42caf6f6b38','5e576a775fc0995ffcc41401',5,'P3: Cook Filling','To prepare the stuffing for Mooli Paratha, heat a teaspoon of cooking oil in a kadai over medium flame for a minute. Temper it with 1/4 teaspoon of cumin seeds and 1/4 teaspoon of carom seeds. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Next, add a half-inch piece of chopped ginger followed by 1 nos chopped green chili and saute it for a minute.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9832199594ae7391cf4d13','5e576a775fc0995ffcc41401',6,'P4: Cook Filling','Next, add 3/4 cup of grated radish and mix it well. Add half a teaspoon of red chili powder followed by 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala and 1/4 teaspoon of dry mango powder. Mix it well and fry it over medium-high flame for 4-5 minutes, until all the moisture is reduced. Then, turn off the flame and add a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and set it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e98324f5df8d42caf6f6b39','5e576a775fc0995ffcc41401',3,'M1: Roll & Stuff Dough','To make the Mooli Paratha, first, divide the prepared dough into small equal-sized balls. Take a dough ball and dust some flour over it. Then, roll it into a 5-inch circle. Place 2-3 tablespoons of the prepared radish stuffing over it and pleat it as shown to seal the stuffing inside. Remove the extra dough if any. Then, gently roll it into a slightly thick round paratha. Make sure to roll the paratha with light hands to prevent the stuffing from coming out of the dough.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9832719594ae7391cf4d14','5e576a775fc0995ffcc41401',4,'M2: Cook Paratha','To make the Mooli Paratha, place the rolled out paratha onto a hot tawa and cook it over medium flame for a minute. Flip and cook it evenly on both sides. Then, apply half a teaspoon of cooking oil to each side and cook it for another 2-3 minutes, until it is evenly browned on both sides. After that, take it out onto a plate and serve. Make the rest of the parathas similarly.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e98330e5df8d42caf6f6b3a','5e5769804e4267296216c924',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Besan Dhokla, wash and finely chop 1 nos green chili. Wash and slit 2 nos green chilies. Wash and finely chop a tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash 7 nos curry leaves well with water. Grate 1 tablespoon of coconut using a grater. Wash and cut a lemon into halves. Then, squeeze 1 tablespoon of lime juice. Next, grease the dhokla plate with a 1/4 teaspoon of cooking oil.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e983330ece7565dc3f19770','5e5769804e4267296216c924',2,'P2: Prepare Batter','To prepare the batter for Besan Dhokla, place a sieve over a large mixing bowl. Next, add half a cup of gram flour and a tablespoon of semolina to it. Sift the flour well to avoid any solid granules. Also, sifting the flour aerates it, allowing it to blend easily with the liquid ingredients.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e98334bece7565dc3f19771','5e5769804e4267296216c924',3,'P3: Make Batter','Next, add a 1/4 teaspoon of ginger paste, 1 nos chopped green chili, and 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder followed by 1/4 teaspoon of sugar and 1/4 teaspoon of hing. Add 1/4 teaspoon of salt along with a teaspoon of lemon juice and half a teaspoon of cooking oil. Add 1/4 cup of water and whisk it well using a whisk. Make sure to whisk the batter in a single direction only. Then, allow it to rest for 20 minutes. While the batter is resting, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9833909594ae7391cf4d15','5e5769804e4267296216c924',4,'M1: Cook the Batter','To make the Dhokla, first, prepare the steamer by adding 4 cups of water in a Kadai and let it boil over medium-high flame for 2-3 minutes. Next, add a 1/4 teaspoon of eno fruit salt to the prepared dhokla batter and mix it well. The batter will rise and turns frothy. Then, instantly pour the batter to the greased dhokla plate without further resting it. As resting the batter after adding the eno salt will reduce the rise and dhokla might not come out spongy. Next, carefully place the dhokla plate in the steamer and cover it with a lid. Allow it to steam for 20 minutes, until cooked through.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":20,"flame":3}'),
('5e9833da5df8d42caf6f6b3b','5e5769804e4267296216c924',5,'M2: Dhokla is ready','After steaming the Besan Dhokla, it will rise up. Then, remove the lid and check if it is cooked through by inserting a toothpick into it. The toothpick should come out clean without any batter sticking on it. Then, carefully take it out. Flip it and pat it gently to unmould the dhokla. Then, slice it into small cubes.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9833f7ece7565dc3f19772','5e5769804e4267296216c924',6,'M3: Make Tadka','To prepare the tempering for Besan Dhhokla, heat a teaspoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Temper it with 1/4 teaspoon of mustard seeds and 1/4 teaspoon of cumin seeds. Add 1/4 teaspoon of sesame seeds along with 1/4 teaspoon of hing and 7 nos curry leaves. Next, add 2 nos slit green chilies and saute it over medium flame for a minute.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e983413ece7565dc3f19773','5e5769804e4267296216c924',7,'M4: Final Touches','Next, add 1/4 cup of water followed by 1/4 teaspoon of sugar and 1/4 teaspoon of salt. Mix it well and bring it to a boil. Then, add 2 teaspoons of lime juice into it and mix it well. Turn off the flame and add the tempering over the prepared besan dhokla. Garnish it with a tablespoon of grated coconut and a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e983491ece7565dc3f19774','5e5768654e4267296216c923',1,'P1: Make the Dough','To knead the dough for Luchi, in a large mixing bowl, add 1 cup of all-purpose flour. Add 1/4 teaspoon of salt along with 2 teaspoons of ghee and mix it well. Next, gradually add about 1/4 cup of water and knead it well into a smooth dough. Apply half a teaspoon of cooking oil over it and allow it rest for 15 minutes. While the dough is resting, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":15,"flame":0}'),('5e9834b09594ae7391cf4d16','5e5768654e4267296216c923',2,'M1: Fry the Poori','To make the Luchi, first, add 1 cup of cooking oil in a kadai and let it heat over medium flame for 3-4 minutes. Meanwhile, divide the prepared dough into small lemon sized balls. Take a dough ball and grease it well with 1/4 teaspoon of cooking oil. Then, gently roll it into a small round luchi. Make sure to roll out the edges thin. Then, carefully drop it into the hot oil and fry it over medium-high flame, while gently pressing it with the turner so it puffs up. Keep splashing oil over it, in between and shallow fry it for 2-3 minutes, until it turns slightly golden. Make sure to flip and fry both the sides evenly. Then, take it out onto a kitchen napkin to remove the excess oil and serve. Make the rest of the luchis similarly.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e983a3d5df8d42caf6f6b3c','5e26f24b985ffca18ae8fab7',2,'P2: Prep the ingredients','Grate 1/2 cup dry coconut. Peel 6nos garlic cloves. Wash and finely chop 1/2 cup onion, 2nos green chilies and 2 tablespoon fresh coriander leaves','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e983a869594ae7391cf4d17','5e26f24b985ffca18ae8fab7',3,'P3: Pepare the mixture for masala paste','In a pan, add 1/2 cup grated dry coconut, 6 cloves garlic, 1-inch piece of cinnamon stick, 4 nos cloves, 1nos black cardamom, 5 nos black peppercorns, 1 teaspoon cumin seeds, 1 tablespoon coriander seeds, 1 tablespoon sesame seeds and 1/2 cup chopped onions and dry roast them without adding any oil for 4-5 minutes on medium flame until onion turns slightly brown, then turn off the heat and let this mixture cool down.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":4,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e983afa5df8d42caf6f6b3d','5e26f24b985ffca18ae8fab7',4,'P4: Prepare the masala paste','Once the mixture has cooled down, transfer it in a mixer grinder. Next add 2 nos chopped green chilies and 2 tablespoon chopped coriander leaves, 1/4 cup water and grind well to make a smooth paste.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e983b715df8d42caf6f6b3e','5e26f24b985ffca18ae8fab7',5,'P5: Peel the shell of the eggs','Once the eggs are completely boiled, take them out of the water and put them in cold water,it will allow the shell to come out easily. Peel 4 boiled eggs and make slits on the eggs with a knife. Grate 1 boiled egg using a grater.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e983bac5df8d42caf6f6b3f','5e26f24b985ffca18ae8fab7',6,'M1: Fry the eggs & cook the masala','In a pan, heat 1 tablespoon cooking oil on medium flame for a minute. Add 4 nos boiled and slit eggs into the oil along with 1/4 teaspoon red chili powder and 1/4 teaspoon turmeric powder and stir fry the eggs on medium heat for 3-4 minutes. Keep the fried eggs aside. To make the gravy, Heat 4 tablespoon cooking oil in a pan on medium heat for a minute. Add 1 teaspoon cumin seeds into the hot oil and let it crackle for a few seconds. Then add ground coconut paste into it and saute on medium heat for 4-5 minutes until oil separates. It is important for the oil to separate so please cook the masala till the oil separates.','cook_method','{"active_time":11,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":4,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e983be65df8d42caf6f6b40','5e26f24b985ffca18ae8fab7',7,'M2: Simmer the curry','Next, add 2 teaspoons Kashmiri red chili powder, 1/2 teaspoon turmeric powder, 1/2 teaspoon garam masala, and 1 tablespoon gram flour into the ground masala and fry for another 3-4 minutes on medium-low heat. While frying add about 1/4 cup water to the masala if it gets too dry and keeps stirring until everything is well combined.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e983c249594ae7391cf4d18','5e26f24b985ffca18ae8fab7',8,'M3: Simmer the eggs with gravy. Garnish & serve','Once the masala is well combined, add 1 nos boiled and grated egg into along with 1 teaspoon salt and 2 cup water. Give it a good stir and bring it to a boil. After the gravy comes to boil, add 4 nos boiled and fried eggs into the gravy and cook for 6-8 minutes on medium-low heat. In the end, add 1/2 tablespoon of lime juice, mix well and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e983cf09594ae7391cf4d19','5e27fb4c4f28558c29df6448',1,'P1: Simmer the oats','To make peanut butter banana oatmeal, in a pot boil 1.5 cups of water, 1/2 cup of milk, 1 cup of steel-cut oats, and 1 tsp of salt. Cover the pan with a lid and let this boil for 25 mins. Next, peel and mash 1 ripe banana. While the oats are cooking move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e983d2bece7565dc3f19775','5e27fb4c4f28558c29df6448',2,'M1: Combine the oats with banana & peanut butter. Garnish & serve','For Peanut Butter Banana Oatmeal, put the cooked oatmeal in a bowl, and then add 2 tbsp of peanut butter, 1 ripe banana, 1/2 tsp of chia seeds (optional) and mix them all together. Once the ingredients are combined well, the dish is ready to serve. If you prefer you may garnish the oatmeal with banana slices and a drizzle of peanut butter.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e983d9b5df8d42caf6f6b41','5e27fcd6985ffca18ae8fac4',1,'P1: Cook the oats with milk','To make apple cinnamon oatmeal, in an instant pot boil 1.5 cups of water, 1/2 cup of milk, 1 cup of steel-cut oats, and 1 tsp of salt. Cover the pan with a lid and let this boil for 25 mins. Next, wash and finely chop 1 apple and roughly chop 1 tbsp of almonds. While the oats are cooking move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":25,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e983dce5df8d42caf6f6b42','5e27fcd6985ffca18ae8fac4',2,'M1: Combine the oats with apples & cinnamon. Garnish & serve','For Apple Cinnamon Oatmeal, put the cooked oatmeal in a bowl, and then add 1 chopped apple, 1/2 tsp of cinnamon powder, 1 tbsp of maple syrup, 1 tbsp of almonds and then mix them all together. Once the ingredients are combined well, the dish is ready to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e983e5aece7565dc3f19776','5e27ff3d985ffca18ae8fac5',1,'P1: Cook the oats with milk','To make chocolate coconut oatmeal, in a pot boil 1.5 cups of water, 1/2 cup of milk, 1 cup of steel-cut oats, and 1 tsp of salt. Cover the pan with a lid and let this boil for 25 mins. While the oats are cooking move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":25,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e983e8cece7565dc3f19777','5e27ff3d985ffca18ae8fac5',2,'M1: Combine the oats with cocoa powder. Garnish & serve','For chocolate and coconut oatmeal, put the cooked oatmeal in a bowl, and then add 2 tsp of cocoa powder, 2 tbsp of coconut milk, 1 tbsp of maple syrup, 1/2 tsp of dry coconut, 1/2 tsp of chocolate chips, and mix them all together. Once the ingredients are combined well, the dish is ready to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e983ee35df8d42caf6f6b43','5e28015c4f28558c29df644a',1,'P1: Cook the oats with milk','To make maple and seat salt oatmeal, in a pot boil 1.5 cups of water, 1/2 cup of milk, 1 cup of steel-cut oats, and 1 tsp of salt. Cover the pan with a lid and let this boil for 25 mins. Next, roughly chop 1 tbsp of walnuts. While the oats are cooking move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":25,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e983f56ece7565dc3f19778','5e28015c4f28558c29df644a',2,'M1: Combine the oatmeal with  maple syrup & rock salt. Garnish & serve','For Maple and Sea Salt Oatmeal, put the cooked oatmeal in a bowl, and then add 1 tbsp of peanut butter, 1/2 tsp of vanilla essence, 2 tsp of maple syrup, 1 tsp of walnuts, 1/2 tsp of rock salt, 2 tsp of almond milk (optional) and mix them all together. Once the ingredients are combined well, the dish is ready to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e983fc65df8d42caf6f6b44','5e280513057fd3f6fc80eee4',1,'P1: Chop the vegetables','To make Sauteed Vegetables, wash and chop 1/2 cup of broccoli into small florets. Peel and roughly slice 1/4 cup of carrots. Wash and roughly chop 1/4 cup of yellow capsicum. Wash and roughly slice 1/4 cup of baby corn. Wash and roughly slice 1/2 cup of mushrooms. Peel and finely chop 1 tbsp of garlic.','prep_method','{"active_time":11,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e983ff29594ae7391cf4d1a','5e280513057fd3f6fc80eee4',2,'M1: Saute & season the vegetables','For Sauteed vegetables, heat 1 tbsp of butter in a pan on high flame and then add 1 tbsp of garlic. Saute this for 1 min and then add 1/2 cup of broccoli, 1/4 cup of carrots, 1/4 cup of capsicum, and 1/4 cup of baby corn. Saute this for 2 mins and then add1 tsp of salt, 1 tsp of pepper, and mix well. Next, add 1/2 cup of mushrooms and saute for 2 mins. Turn off the flame and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e993d975df8d42caf6f6b46','5e576790f7851cecaf7c508e',1,'AP1: Soak Sabudana','For Sabudana Khichdi, add 1 cup of sabudana in a large bowl and soak it in 2 cups of water for 3 hours. While the sabudana is soaking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":180,"advanced_prep_time":180,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e993e1dece7565dc3f19779','5e576790f7851cecaf7c508e',2,'P1: Cook the Potatoes','To boil the potato for Sabudana Khichdi, wash a medium-sized potato well with water and put it into a pressure cooker along with 1 cup of water. Cover it with a lid and pressure cook it over high flame until one whistle. After the first whistle, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook it for another 8 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the potato is boiling, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e993e56ece7565dc3f1977a','5e576790f7851cecaf7c508e',3,'P2: Prep Ingredients','For Sabudana Khichdi, first, drain off the water from the soaked sabudana and allow it to sit for another 15 minutes. Wash and slit 3 nos green chilies. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves. Crush a tablespoon of roasted peanuts coarsely. Wash and cut a lemon into halves. Then, squeeze a tablespoon of lemon juice using a squeezer. Next, after boiling the potato, take it out from the pressure cooker and gently peel off the skin. Then, cut it into medium cubes.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e993ecc5df8d42caf6f6b47','5e576790f7851cecaf7c508e',4,'M1: Cooking','To make Sabudana Khichdi, heat 2 tablespoons of ghee in a kadai over medium flame for a minute. Add a teaspoon of cumin seeds and let it splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 3 nos slit green chilies followed by 1/4 cup of boiled and cubed potato. Saute and fry the potatoes over medium flame for 2-3 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e993f399594ae7391cf4d1b','5e576790f7851cecaf7c508e',5,'M2: Cooking','After frying the potatoes, add the soaked sabudana along with a tablespoon of crushed peanuts. Next, add a teaspoon of sugar followed by half a teaspoon of salt and gently mix it. Then, cover it with a lid and simmer it for 3 minutes. While the sabudana khichdi is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e993f5b9594ae7391cf4d1c','5e576790f7851cecaf7c508e',6,'M3: Final Touches','After simmering the Sabudana Khichdi, remove the lid and gently mix it. Sabudana turns soft and slightly puffs up. Then, add 2 tablespoons of chopped coriander leaves and a tablespoon of lemon juice. Gently mix it to avoid the sabudana from sticking together. Turn off the flame and take it out into a serving bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9941049594ae7391cf4d1d','5e5763d05fc0995ffcc413ff',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Chicken Donne Biryani, first, wash and soak 1 cup of samba rice in 2 cups of water for 30 minutes. Meanwhile, wash 350 grams of chicken pieces thoroughly with water. Peel, wash and finely slice 3/4 cup of onion. Wash and slice half a cup of tomatoes. Wash, peel and finely slice a 1-inch piece of ginger. Peel, wash and finely slice 1 teaspoon of garlic. Wash and roughly chop 4 nos green chilies.  While the rice is soaking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":15,"flame":0}'),('5e99414a5df8d42caf6f6b48','5e5763d05fc0995ffcc413ff',2,'P2: Prepare Mint Coriander Paste','To prepare the mint coriander paste for Chicken Donnne Biryani, wash and roughly chop half a cup of mint leaves. Wash and roughly chop half a cup of coriander leaves. Next, to a blender jar add half a cup chopped mint leaves followed by half a cup of coriander leaves and 4 nos chopped green chilies. Then, cover the jar with a lid and blend it well into a smooth paste.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9941bd5df8d42caf6f6b49','5e5763d05fc0995ffcc413ff',3,'M1: Cook Spices and Onions','To make Chicken Donne Biryani, heat 2 tablespoons of ghee in a pressure cooker over medium flame for a minute. Add 1 tablespoon of oil, half-inch piece of cinnamon stick, 3 nos green cardamoms, half a teaspoon of stone flower and 2 bay leaves and saute it for a minute. Next, add 3/4 cup of sliced onions followed by a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Saute and fry the onions for 5-6 minutes over medium-low flame until it slightly changes color.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e99424a9594ae7391cf4d1e','5e5763d05fc0995ffcc413ff',4,'M2: Continue Cooking','After frying the onions, add a 1-inch piece of sliced ginger and 1 teaspoon of sliced garlic. Next, add 2 teaspoons of coriander powder, and a teaspoon of turmeric powder followed by 1 teaspoon of garam masala and mix it well. Then, fry the masala over medium-low flame for 2-3 minutes. After that, add half a cup of sliced tomatoes and mix it well. Saute and cook the tomatoes with the masala for 4-5 minutes, until oil separates.','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e99426f5df8d42caf6f6b4a','5e5763d05fc0995ffcc413ff',5,'M3: Add Chicken','As the masala releases oil, add 350 grams of chicken pieces and mix it well. Then, fry the chicken pieces with the masala over medium flame for 5-6 minutes, until it is no longer pink. Keep sauteing the chicken pieces to prevent it from getting burnt. After frying the chicken pieces, add 2 cups of water and stir it well. Then, bring it to a boil over high flame.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e9942a79594ae7391cf4d1f','5e5763d05fc0995ffcc413ff',6,'M4: Cook the Biryani','As the water comes to a boil, add the soaked samba rice and mix it well. Next, add 1/4 cup of curd and stir it continuously until it is well combined. Then, cover it with a lid and pressure cook it over medium flame for 12-14 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and set it aside for 30 minutes. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the Biryani is cooking, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":44,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":30,"flame":3}'),('5e9942cf5df8d42caf6f6b4b','5e5763d05fc0995ffcc413ff',7,'M5: Final Touches','After cooking the Chicken Donne Biryani, take off the lid and gently mix the rice with light hands. Then, take it out into a serving dish and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9944eb9594ae7391cf4d20','5e57600df7851cecaf7c508c',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Chili Paneer, cube 1 cup of paneer. Peel, wash and cut 1/4 cup of onions into petals. Wash and slice 1/4 cup of green capsicum. Peel, wash and finely chop 1 teaspoon of garlic. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of spring onion whites. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of spring onion greens. Wash and slit 1 nos green chili. Next, add a tablespoon of cornflour to a bowl. Add 1/4 cup of water and mix it well until smooth to make a slurry.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9945129594ae7391cf4d21','5e57600df7851cecaf7c508c',2,'P2: Prepare Batter','To prepare the batter for Chili Paneer, in a large bowl, add 1/4 cup of cornflour followed by 2 tablespoons of all-purpose flour. Add 1 teaspoon of ginger-garlic paste, half a teaspoon of black pepper powder, 1/4 teaspoon of Kashmiri red chili powder and 1/4 teaspoon of salt. Add 1/4 cup of water and mix it well to prepare the batter. Then, add 1 cup of cubed paneer pieces to the batter. Coat the paneer pieces well with the batter.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9945405df8d42caf6f6b4d','5e57600df7851cecaf7c508c',3,'M1: Fry Paneer','To fry the Paneer Pieces for Chili Paneer, heat 1 cup of cooking oil in a kadai over medium-high flame for 2-3 minutes. Once the oil is hot, carefully drop the coated paneer pieces one by one into the oil and fry it over medium flame for 5-6 minutes, until it turns crisp and golden brown. Then, take it out onto a paper napkin to wipe off the excess oil.','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e99456b5df8d42caf6f6b4e','5e57600df7851cecaf7c508c',4,'M2: Cook Ingredients','To make Chili Paneer, heat a tablespoon of cooking oil in a kadai over medium flame for a minute. Add 1 teaspoon of chopped garlic followed by 1 slit green chili and 2 tablespoons of spring onion whites. Saute and fry it over high flame for 1-2 minutes. Next, add 1/4 cup of onion petals along with 1/4 cup of sliced green capsicum and fry it over high flame for 2-3 minutes until tender-crisp.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9945969594ae7391cf4d22','5e57600df7851cecaf7c508c',5,'M3: Add Sauces and Masala Powders','After stir-frying the vegetables, add half a teaspoon of red chili sauce, 1.5 tablespoons of tomato ketchup and a tablespoon of vinegar followed by 1.5 tablespoons of soy sauce. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of Kashmiri red chili powder, 1/4 teaspoon of black pepper powder and 1/4 teaspoon of salt. Mix it well and stir fry the sauce over high flame for 1-2 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('5e9945bfece7565dc3f1977c','5e57600df7851cecaf7c508c',6,'M4: Continue Cooking','Next, add the prepared cornflour slurry and mix it well. Keep stirring it over a low flame until it is well combined to avoid any lumps. Cornflour slurry thickens the sauce giving it the desired consistency. Next, add the fried paneer cubes followed by 2 tablespoons of spring onion greens and mix it well. Coat the paneer pieces well with the sauce and saute it for a minute. Then, turn off the flame and take it out into a serving bowl. Garnish the chili paneer with a tablespoon of chopped spring onion greens. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e99473dfc2541d99b180f7d','5e575e0ff7851cecaf7c508b',1,'P1: Cook Rice','To cook the rice for Burnt Garlic Fried Rice, first, wash 1 cup of basmati rice well with water. Then add it to a pressure cooker along with 2 cups of water and 1/4 teaspoon of cooking oil. Cover it with a lid and pressure cook the rice over a high flame until one whistle. After the first whistle, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook it for another 8 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the rice is cooking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e99475b70b00f94066c5034','5e575e0ff7851cecaf7c508b',2,'P2: Prep Ingredients','For Burnt Garlic Fried Rice, peel, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of carrots. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of beans. Peel, wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of garlic. Wash and finely chop 1 nos green chili. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of spring onion whites. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of spring onion greens. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of green capsicum.','prep_method','{"active_time":18,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e994780498cf4279b6031ab','5e575e0ff7851cecaf7c508b',3,'M1: Cooking','To make Burnt Garlic Fried Rice, heat 1.5 tablespoons of cooking oil in a kadai over medium flame for a minute. Add 2 tablespoons of chopped garlic and saute it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes, until it turns aromatic and golden brown. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions followed by 2 tablespoons of chopped spring onion whites and 1 chopped green chili. Saute and fry the onions over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9947a4498cf4279b6031ac','5e575e0ff7851cecaf7c508b',4,'M2: Continue Cooking','After frying the onions, add 1/4 cup of chopped green capsicum along with 1/4 cup of chopped carrots and 1/4 cup of chopped beans. Stir and fry the vegetables over high flame for 1-2 minutes. Then, add 1.5 teaspoons of vinegar followed by 1.5 teaspoons of soy sauce and 3/4 teaspoons of red chili sauce. Mix it well and saute the vegetables with the sauce over high flame for 1-2 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":4}'),
('5e9947ddfc2541d99b180f7e','5e575e0ff7851cecaf7c508b',5,'M3: Continue Cooking','Next, add 1 cup of cooked basmati rice followed by 1/4 teaspoon of crushed black peppercorns and half a teaspoon of salt. Then, gently mix the rice and saute it with light hands over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and garnish it with a tablespoon of chopped spring onion greens. Take it out into a serving bowl and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9948d2498cf4279b6031ad','5e575cf9f7851cecaf7c508a',1,'P1: Blanch Drumstick Leaves','To blanch the Drumstick Leaves for Drumstick Leaves Poriyal, first, wash and finely chop 2.5 cups of drumstick leaves. Next, add  2 cups of water in a saucepan along with half a teaspoon of salt and bring it to rolling boil over a high flame. As the water comes to a boil, add 2.5 cups of chopped drumstick leaves and blanch it for 2-3 minutes over a high flame. Then, turn off the flame and drain off the water from it and rinse it well with cold water to prevent it from cooking further. While the drumstick leaves are blanching, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e99490770b00f94066c5035','5e575cf9f7851cecaf7c508a',2,'P2: Prep Ingredients','For Drumstick Leaves Poriyal, peel, wash and finely chop half a cup of onions. Peel, wash and finely chop 1 teaspoon of garlic. Wash and roughly chop 1 green chili.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e994989fc2541d99b180f7f','5e575cf9f7851cecaf7c508a',3,'M1: Cook Spices and Onions','To make the Drumstick Leaves Poriyal, heat 1 tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add a teaspoon of mustard seeds, 1 teaspoon of urad dal, 1 dry red chili and 1/4 teaspoon of cumin seeds. Saute it over medium flame for a minute. Next, add 1 teaspoon of chopped garlic followed by 1 nos chopped green chili and half a cup of chopped onions. Saute and fry the onions over medium flame for 2-3 minutes, until translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9949aefc2541d99b180f80','5e575cf9f7851cecaf7c508a',4,'M2: Continue Cooking','After frying the onions, add half a cup of desiccated coconut followed by half a teaspoon of salt and half a teaspoon of turmeric powder. Next, add a teaspoon of red chili powder and mix it well. Saute the masala over low flame for 1-2 minutes. After that, add the blanched drumstick leaves and mix it well. Saute and fry it over medium flame for 5-6 minutes to reduce the extra water. As the drumstick leaves shrivel up and turn slightly crisp. Turn off the flame and take it out into a bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e994a9a498cf4279b6031ae','5e575acc5fc0995ffcc413fd',1,'P1: Cook Dal','To cook the dal for Lemon Rasam, first, rinse half a cup of toor dal well with water. Then, add it to a pressure cooker along with 1/4 teaspoon of salt and 1 cup of water. Cover it with a lid and pressure cook the dal over a high flame until one whistle. After the first whistle, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook the dal for another 8 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the dal is cooking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e994abc498cf4279b6031af','5e575acc5fc0995ffcc413fd',2,'P2: Prep Ingredients','For Lemon Rasam, wash and roughly chop half a cup of tomatoes. Wash, peel and finely chop a half-inch piece of ginger. Wash and slit 1 nos green chili. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves. Wash and cut a lemon into halves. Then, squeeze 1 tablespoon of lemon juice. Wash 15 nos curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e994b1d498cf4279b6031b0','5e575acc5fc0995ffcc413fd',3,'M1: Cooking','To make the Lemon Rasam, add half a cup of chopped tomatoes in a kadai. Then, add a half-inch piece of chopped ginger followed by 1 slit green chili and 7 curry leaves. Next, add 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves along with 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder and 1.5 cups of water. Mix it well and allow it to boil over medium-high flame for 10 minutes until tomatoes turn tender. While the tomatoes are boiling, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e994b95fc2541d99b180f81','5e575acc5fc0995ffcc413fd',4,'M2: Continue Cooking','After boiling the tomatoes for Lemon Rasam, stir it well and mash half of the tomatoes using the turner. Next, add the cooked toor dal followed by half a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. If required, add about 1/4 cup of water to adjust the consistency of the rasam. Then, bring it to a boil over a high flame and continue to cook the rasam for another 2-3 minutes, while stirring in between. After that, turn off the flame and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e994bc7fc2541d99b180f82','5e575acc5fc0995ffcc413fd',5,'M3: Make Tadka','To make the tempering for Lemon Rasam, heat 2 teaspoons of ghee in a small tempering pan over medium flame for a minute. Add half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, 1/4 teaspoon of cumin seeds and 1 dry red chili followed by 7 nos curry leaves and 1/4 teaspoon of hing. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of crushed black peppercorns. Saute and let it splutter over medium flame for a minute. Then, turn off the flame and the tempering instantly over the prepared rasam. Mix it well and add a tablespoon of lemon juice and stir it well. Take it out into a serving bowl and garnish it with chopped coriander leaves. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e994da3fc2541d99b180f83','5e5758e0f7851cecaf7c5089',1,'P1: Prepare the Batter','To prepare the batter for Masala Paniyaram, in a large mixing bowl, add 3/4 cup of semolina followed by 1/4 cup of curd and 1/4 teaspoon salt. Add 3/4 cup of water and mix it well until smooth. Make sure to avoid any lumps in the batter. Then, set it aside and allow it to rest for 20 minutes. While the batter is resting, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e994e4f498cf4279b6031b1','5e5758e0f7851cecaf7c5089',2,'P2: Prep Ingredients','For Masala Paniyaram, peel, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash, peel and grate 1/4 cup of carrots. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of green capsicum. Wash and finely chop 1 nos green chili. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash 7 nos curry leaves well with water.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e994f00fc2541d99b180f84','5e5758e0f7851cecaf7c5089',3,'M1: Temper Spices','For Masala Paniyaram, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add 1/4 teaspoon of mustard seeds, 1/4 teaspoon of urad dal, 1/4 teaspoon of chana dal and 7 nos curry leaves. Saute it over medium flame for a minute. Next, add 1 nos green chili followed by 1/4 teaspoon of ginger paste and fry it for 1-2 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e994f22498cf4279b6031b2','5e5758e0f7851cecaf7c5089',4,'M2: Cook Vegetables','Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions and fry it over medium flame for 3-4 minutes until it turns slightly translucent. After frying the onions, add 1/4 cup of grated carrots followed by 1/4 cup of chopped green capsicum. Stir and fry the vegetables over medium-high flame for 2-3 minutes until tender-crisp. Next, add a tablespoon of desiccated coconut and mix it well. Saute it over low flame for a minute. Then, allow the mixture to cool down completely.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e994f45498cf4279b6031b3','5e5758e0f7851cecaf7c5089',5,'M3: Make the Batter','To make the Paniyaram Batter, add the prepared vegetable mixture to the prepared semolina batter. Add a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and mix it well. Next, add 2-3 tablespoons of water to the batter, to adjust the consistency and mix it well.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e994f6a70b00f94066c5036','5e5758e0f7851cecaf7c5089',6,'M4: Make Paniyarum','To make Masala Paniyaram, grease the appam pan with a teaspoon of cooking oil. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of Eno fruit salt to the batter and gently mix the batter. The batter will rise and turns slightly frothy. Then, instantly pour the prepared batter to the molds of the appam pan without further resting it. Resting the batter after adding the fruit salt will reduce the rise of the batter and paniyarams may not come out spongy. Then, cover it with a lid and simmer it for 2-3 minutes, until it turns golden and crisp. Flip and cook the other side evenly. Cook the paniyarams until both sides are evenly crisp and golden. Then, turn off the flame and take it out onto a plate. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e99507770b00f94066c5037','5e5757e94e4267296216c922',1,'P1: Soak Rice','For Paneer Pulao, first, rinse 1 cup of basmati rice well with water. Then, soak it in 2 cups of water for 20 minutes. While the rice is soaking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":20,"flame":0}'),('5e995096498cf4279b6031b4','5e5757e94e4267296216c922',2,'P2: Prep Ingredients','For Paneer Pulao, peel, wash and finely slice half a cup of onions. Wash, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of carrots. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of beans. Peel and wash 1/4 cup of green peas. Wash and slit 2 nos green chilies. Cut 1.5 cups of paneer into medium cubes. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of mint leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":18,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9950cc498cf4279b6031b5','5e5757e94e4267296216c922',3,'M1: Fry Paneer','To fry the paneer pieces for Paneer Pulao, heat 1.5 tablespoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Then, add 1.5 cups of cubed paneer pieces. Saute and fry the paneer pieces over medium-high flame for 5-6 minutes, until it is evenly browned on all the sides. As the paneer pieces turn crisp and golden, turn off the flame and carefully take it out onto a plate and set aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":4}'),('5e9950ec70b00f94066c5038','5e5757e94e4267296216c922',4,'M2: Temper Whole Spices','To make Paneer Pulao, heat 2 teaspoons of ghee in a pressure cooker over medium flame for a minute. Add 1.5 tablespoons of cooking oil into it and heat it for a few seconds. Next, add a half-inch piece of cinnamon stick, 3 nos cloves, 3 nos green cardamoms, 1 nos bay leaf and half a teaspoon of black peppercorns followed by half a teaspoon of cumin seeds. Saute the whole spices over low flame for a minute.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e995120498cf4279b6031b6','5e5757e94e4267296216c922',5,'M3: Cooking Vegetables','Next, add half a cup of sliced onions and fry it over medium flame for 3-4 minutes until it turns slightly translucent. Next, add 2 nos slit green chilies and saute it over medium flame for a minute. After that, add 1/4 cup of chopped carrots followed by 1/4 cup of chopped beans and 1/4 cup of green peans. Stir and fry the vegetables over high flame for 1-2 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e995154498cf4279b6031b7','5e5757e94e4267296216c922',6,'M4: Cooking the Masala Powders','After stir-frying the vegetables, add a teaspoon of salt followed by half a teaspoon of garam masala and mix it well. Saute and fry the vegetables over medium flame for another 2 minutes. Next, add 1.5 tablespoons of chopped coriander leaves and 2 tablespoons of chopped mint leaves followed by 1.5 cups of fried paneer pieces. Mix it well and fry the paneer pieces with the masala for 1-2 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e99517c498cf4279b6031b8','5e5757e94e4267296216c922',7,'M5: Cooking the Rice','Next, add 1 cup of soaked basmati rice and gently mix it with the masala. Stir it with light hands and fry it over medium flame for a minute. After that, add 2 cups of water and mix it well. Then, cover it with a lid and pressure cook the rice over a high flame until one whistle. After the first whistle, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook it for another 8 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the paneer pulao is cooking, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":12,"flame":3}'),('5e99519f498cf4279b6031b9','5e5757e94e4267296216c922',8,'M6: Final Touches','After simmering the paneer pulao, take off the lid and gently mix the rice with light hands. Then, take it out into a serving dish and garnish it with chopped coriander leaves. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9952f170b00f94066c5039','5e5756554e4267296216c921',1,'P1: Soak Moong Dal','For Methi Moong Dal Sabzi, first, rinse 1 cup of yellow moong dal well with water. Then, soak it in 2 cups of water for 20 minutes. While the dal is soaking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e99533070b00f94066c503a','5e5756554e4267296216c921',2,'P2: Prep Ingredients','For Methi Moong Dal Sabzi, wash half a bunch of fenugreek leaves thoroughly with water to remove all the dirt. Then, spread it over a kitchen towel to wipe off the extra water. Next, roughly chop 1.5 cups of the fenugreek leaves. Peel, wash and finely chop a teaspoon of garlic. Wash and finely chop 1 nos green chili. Wash and finely chop a tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash and roughly chop a medium-sized tomato, then add it to a blender jar and blend it into a smooth puree.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e99536c498cf4279b6031ba','5e5756554e4267296216c921',3,'M1: Temper Spices','To make Methi Moong Dal Sabzi, heat a tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Temper it with a 1/4 teaspoon of hing and half a teaspoon of cumin seeds. Next, add a teaspoon of chopped garlic along with 1 nos chopped green chili and saute it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e995391498cf4279b6031bb','5e5756554e4267296216c921',4,'M2: Cook Sabzi','Next, add 1 cup of soaked yellow moong dal and fry it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes. After that, add half a teaspoon of salt followed by half a teaspoon of turmeric powder and mix it well. Add 1/4 cup of water and bring it to a boil over a high flame. Then, reduce the flame to low and cover it with a lid. Simmer the dal for 7-8 minutes until tender. While the dal is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9953b9fc2541d99b180f85','5e5756554e4267296216c921',5,'M3: Continue to Cook Sabzi','After simmering the moong dal for Methi Moong Dal Sabzi, take off the lid and give it a stir. Then, saute and fry the dal over medium flame to reduce the extra water. Next, add 1/4 cup of the prepared tomato puree and mix it well. Cover it with a lid and continue to simmer the dal for another 4-5 minutes, until tomato puree is completely cooked.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9953d7498cf4279b6031bc','5e5756554e4267296216c921',6,'M4: Continue to Cook','After simmering the dal for Methi Moong Dal Sabzi, take off the lid and add 1.5 cups of chopped fenugreek leaves. Mix it well and saute it over medium flame for a minute. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of cumin powder followed by half a teaspoon of red chili powder and half a teaspoon of coriander powder. Mix it well and cover it with a lid. Then, simmer it for 5-6 minutes. While methi moong dal sabzi is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}');
INSERT INTO catalog_recipe_steps VALUES
('5e9953f2498cf4279b6031bd','5e5756554e4267296216c921',7,'M5: Garnish','After simmering the Methi Moong Dal Sabzi, take off the lid and stir it well. Then, turn off the flame and garnish it with a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves. Take it out into a serving bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e995572fc2541d99b180f86','5e5753e24e4267296216c920',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Godhuma Dosa, peel, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1 nos green chili. Wash, peel and finely chop a half-inch piece of ginger. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e99558e70b00f94066c503b','5e5753e24e4267296216c920',2,'P2: Prepare Batter','To prepare the batter for Godhuma Dosa, in a large mixing bowl, add half a cup of wheat flour followed by half a cup of rice flour and a tablespoon of semolina. Add a tablespoon of curd along with 1 cup of water and whisk it well until smooth, to avoid any lumps.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9955c2fc2541d99b180f87','5e5753e24e4267296216c920',3,'P3: Prepare Batter','Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions and a half-inch piece of ginger followed by 1 nos chopped green chili and 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves. Add 1 tablespoon of chopped curry leaves along with 1/4 teaspoon of cumin seeds and half a teaspoon of salt. Next, add about half a cup of water and mix it well. The batter should not be thick, instead, it should be runny as shown. Then, set the batter aside and allow it to rest for 20 minutes. While the batter is resting, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":20,"flame":0}'),('5e9955dafc2541d99b180f88','5e5753e24e4267296216c920',4,'M1: Make Dosa','To make Godhuma Dosa, after resting the prepared batter, mix it well and if required, add more water to adjust the consistency. Next, pour a ladle full of the prepared batter over a hot tawa and spread it across. Then, cook the dosa over low flame for 2-3 minutes until small bubbles start to appear on the surface and the bottom turns crisp and golden. As the dosa turns crisp and golden, carefully take it out while gently scraping the sides. Fold it into a triangle and serve. Make the rest of the dosas from the batter similarly.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e995661fc2541d99b180f89','5e57514b5fc0995ffcc413fb',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Curry Leaves Chutney, wash and separate half a cup of curry leaves. Peel and wash 2 cloves of garlic. Wash and peel a 1-inch piece of ginger. Wash and slit 1 nos green chili. Grate half a cup of fresh coconut using a grater.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e99568a70b00f94066c503c','5e57514b5fc0995ffcc413fb',2,'M1: Cooking','To make Curry Leaves Chutney, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add 2 cloves of garlic followed by a 1-inch piece of ginger and 1 slit green chili. Saute and fry it over low flame for a minute. Next, add half a cup of curry leaves and mix it well. Saute and fry the curry leaves over low flame for 2-3 minutes until it turns crisp and golden. As the curry leaves turn crisp, turn off the flame and allow this to cool down completely. While the curry leaves mixture is cooling down, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9956b270b00f94066c503d','5e57514b5fc0995ffcc413fb',3,'M2: Blend to Make Chutney','To make Curry Leaves Chutney, after the prepared curry leaves mixture cools down, transfer it to a blender jar. Add half a cup of grated coconut followed by 1 teaspoon of tamarind and 2 teaspoons of roasted peanuts. Add half a teaspoon of salt along with 1/4 cup of water and blend it well into a smooth chutney. Then, take it out into a bowl and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9956d2498cf4279b6031be','5e57514b5fc0995ffcc413fb',4,'M3: Make Tadka','To make the Tempering for Curry Leaves Chutney, heat a teaspoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, half a teaspoon of urad dal and 5 nos curry leaves. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Then, turn off the flame and the tempering to the prepared chutney. Mix it well and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e99576cfc2541d99b180f8a','5e574fcc5fc0995ffcc413fa',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Beans Poriyal, wash and finely chop 1 cup of beans. Peel, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and slit 2 nos green chilies. Wash 8 nos curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e99579270b00f94066c503e','5e574fcc5fc0995ffcc413fa',2,'M1: Cook Spices and Onions','To make Beans Poriyal, heat 1 tablespoon of cooking oil in a Kadai over medium flame for a minute. Add 1/4 teaspoon of chana dal, 1/4 teaspoon of urad dal and 1/4 teaspoon of mustard seeds followed by 1 dry red chili and 1/4 teaspoon of hing. Saute it over medium flame for a minute. Then, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions along with 2 nos slit green chilies and 8 nos curry leaves. Stir and fry the onions over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until it turns translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9957b0fc2541d99b180f8b','5e574fcc5fc0995ffcc413fa',3,'M2: Add Masala Powders','After frying the onions, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder and mix it well. Next, add 1 cup of chopped beans and mix it well. Stir and fry the beans over medium-high flame for 2-3 minutes. After that, add 2-3 tablespoons of water and stir it well. Then, cover it with a lid and simmer the beans for 2-3 minutes. While the beans are simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e9957e170b00f94066c503f','5e574fcc5fc0995ffcc413fa',4,'M3: Cook the Poriyal','After simmering the Beans Poriyal, take off the lid and season it with half a teaspoon of salt. Add 3 tablespoons of water and mix it well. Then, cover it with a lid and continue to simmer the beans for another 5-6 minutes, until it turns tender. While the beans are simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e995806fc2541d99b180f8c','5e574fcc5fc0995ffcc413fa',5,'M4: Final Touches','After simmering the Beans Poriyal, remove the lid and fry it over high flame for 2-3 minutes to reduce the extra water. Then, add 3 tablespoons of desiccated coconut and mix it well. Turn off the flame and take it out into a serving bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e99591e70b00f94066c5040','5e574deff7851cecaf7c5087',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Shahi Mushroom, first, soak 1/4 cup of cashews in 1 cup of water for 10 minutes. Meanwhile, wash 1.5 cups of button mushrooms thoroughly with water. Peel, wash and roughly chop half a cup of onions. Peel and wash 5 cloves of garlic. Wash and peel a half-inch piece of ginger. Wash and roughly chop 1 nos green chili. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves. Wash and cut a lime into halves and squeeze a tablespoon of lime juice.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e995943498cf4279b6031bf','5e574deff7851cecaf7c5087',2,'P2: Make Masala Paste','For Shahi Mushroom, first, add 1/4 cup of the soaked cashew nuts to a blender jar and blend it into a smooth puree. Then, take it out into a bowl and set it aside. Next, add half a cup of roughly chopped onions to a blender jar and blend it into a smooth paste. Next, to a mortar, add 5 cloves of garlic followed by a half-inch piece of ginger and 1 nos chopped green chili. Then, blend it coarsely into a paste.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e995983498cf4279b6031c0','5e574deff7851cecaf7c5087',3,'M1: Cook Mushrooms','To fry the mushrooms for Shahi Mushroom, heat a tablespoon of ghee in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add 1.5 cups of button mushrooms and saute it over medium flame. Saute and fry the mushrooms for 5-6 minutes until it turns slightly golden. Then, turn off the flame and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9959b2fc2541d99b180f8d','5e574deff7851cecaf7c5087',4,'M2: Temper Spices','To make Shahi Mushrooms, heat a tablespoon of ghee in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add 1 nos bay leaf along with half a teaspoon of cumin seeds and let it splutter for a few seconds. Next, add a tablespoon of the prepared ginger-garlic-green chili paste and saute it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e995a0470b00f94066c5041','5e574deff7851cecaf7c5087',5,'M3: Cook Vegetables','Next, add half a cup of the prepared onion paste and mix it well. Saute and fry the onion paste over medium flame for 5-6 minutes until it turns golden brown. Next, add 1/4 cup of tomato puree and mix it well. Saute and cook the gravy for 2-3 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e995a6170b00f94066c5042','5e574deff7851cecaf7c5087',6,'M4: Add Masala Powders','Next, add half a teaspoon of salt followed by half a teaspoon of turmeric powder and a teaspoon of Kashmiri red chili powder. Next, add half a teaspoon of cumin powder and mix it well. Add 1/4 cup of water and stir it well. Then, cover it with a lid and simmer the masala for 5-6 minutes, until oil separates. While the masala is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),
('5e995aa170b00f94066c5043','5e574deff7851cecaf7c5087',7,'M5: Continue Cooking','After simmering the masala for Shahi Mushroom, take off the lid and add 1/4 cup of the prepared cashew paste. Keep stirring it continuously over a low flame until the masala is well combined. Next, add half a teaspoon of shahi masala powder followed by 1/4 teaspoon of sugar and mix it well. Then, add 1.5 cups of fried button mushrooms and mix it well with the masala. Saute the mushrooms over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Then, cover it with a lid and cook it over low flame for 5 minutes. While the shahi mushroom is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('5e995ac570b00f94066c5044','5e574deff7851cecaf7c5087',8,'M6: Garnish','After simmering the Shahi Mushrooms, take off the lid and add a tablespoon of lime juice. Mix it well and garnish it with 2 tablespoons of chopped coriander leaves. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e995c08498cf4279b6031c1','5e2808cb4f28558c29df644f',1,'P1: Rinse the poha & prep the ingredients','To make mixed vegetable poha, rinse 1.5 cups of poha and then keep it aside. Peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Wash and dice 1/4 cup of potatoes. Peel and finely chop 1/4 cups of carrot. Wash and roughly chop 2 tbsp of coriander leaves. Squeeze 2 tsp of lime juice. Wash 7 curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":11,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e995c9870b00f94066c5045','5e2808cb4f28558c29df644f',2,'M1:  Cook the poha with vegetables','For mixed vegetable poha, heat 1 tbsp on a pan on medium flame and then add 1 tsp mustard seeds, 7 curry leaves let this splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 1/4 cup of onions and saute this for 2 mins. Once the onions become translucent, add 1/4 cup of tomatoes and saute for 2 mins. Next, add 1/4 cup of potatoes, 1/4 cup of carrots, and saute for 7-8 mins','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e995d48498cf4279b6031c2','5e280b9c057fd3f6fc80eee5',1,'P1: Pressure cook the rice','To make Vangi Bath, first, wash 1.5 cups of rice and then cook it in a pressure cooker with 3 cups of water. Cook the rice on high flame for 1 whistle and then on low flame for 6 mins. Once the rice is cooked, allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally before you open it. While the rice cooks please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":0,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e995d86498cf4279b6031c3','5e280b9c057fd3f6fc80eee5',2,'P2: Prep the ingredients','Next, Soak 1 tsp of tamarind in 1/4 cup of hot water and let it rest for 2 mins. Then, mash the tamarind and the water to make a tamarind extract. Wash and chop 1/2 cup of eggplant into wedges. Wash and slit 1 green chilli. Wash 6 curry leaves. Wash and roughly chop 1 tbsp of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e995de1498cf4279b6031c4','5e280b9c057fd3f6fc80eee5',3,'M1:  Prepare the vangi bath','For Vangi Bath, in a pan heat 1 tsp of cooking oil and then add 1 tsp mustard seeds, 1/2 tsp urad dal, 1/2 tsp of chana dal, 1 broken dry red chili, 6 curry leaves, and 1 slit green chili. Let this splutter for a few seconds and then add 1/2 cup of eggplant and 1 tbsp of peanuts. Let this cook for 4 mins, stirring frequently. Next, add the prepared tamarind extract, 1 tsp of vangi bath masala, 1/2 tsp of jaggery, 1 tsp of salt, 1/4 tsp of turmeric, and saute for 2 mins. Next, add 1.5 cups of cooked rice and gently combine all the ingredients. Once everything is mixed well, garnish with 1 tbsp of coriander leaves and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":4,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e995ea0498cf4279b6031c5','5e2819ae057fd3f6fc80eee7',1,'P1: Marinate the chicken','To make Honey Soy Sauce Grilled Chicken, first, clean 400 g of chicken and then place it is a bowl. To this, add 1 tsp of salt, 1.5 tsp of black pepper, 6 crushed pods of garlic, 4 tbsp of olive oil, and rub this marinade into the chicken. Let this rest for 30 mins. While the chicken is marinating make the soy sauce glaze, in a small bowl add, 1 tsp of soy sauce, 3 tsp of honey, and mix well.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":30,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e995ecafc2541d99b180f8e','5e2819ae057fd3f6fc80eee7',2,'M1: Grill the chicken. Garnish & serve','For Honey Soy Sauce Grilled Chicken, heat 2 tsp of butter on grilling pan on medium flame for 1 min. Next, gently place the marinated chicken on the pan and cook for 3 mins on high flame. Flip the chicken breasts and cook them for another 3 mins. Then, reduce the flame to medium and cook on each side for 5 mins. After that, coat each side of the chicken with the soy sauce glaze and cook on each side for another min on low flame. Take the chicken off the flame and place it on a serving dish and enjoy.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":16,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e995fff498cf4279b6031c7','5e294852057fd3f6fc80ef04',1,'P1: Prep the ingredients','To make Paneer Burji, first, grate 1 cup of paneer, peel and finely chop 3/4 cup of onions, wash and finely chop 3/4 cup of tomatoes, wash and chop 1 green chili, and wash and roughly chop 1 tbsp of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e996032fc2541d99b180f91','5e294852057fd3f6fc80ef04',2,'M1: Fry the onions','For Paneer Bhurji, heat 2 tsp of ghee in a pan on medium flame and then add 1/2 tsp of cumin seeds. Let them splutter for a few seconds and then add 3/4 cup of chopped onions. Saute them for 2-3 mins, until translucent. Next, add 1 tsp of ginger-garlic paste, 1 tsp of green chilli, and mix well. Then, add 1/2 tsp of red chilli powder, 1/4 tsp of garam masala, 1/2 tsp of salt, and mix well.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e99609b498cf4279b6031c8','5e294b86057fd3f6fc80ef06',1,'P1: Slice the eggplant & prep the ingredients','For Dahi Brinjal Curry, wash and slice 1.5 cups of eggplant as shown. Wash, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1.5 tablespoons of coriander leaves. Next, in a large mixing bowl, add 1/2 cup of curd and whisk it well using a whisk to avoid any lumps.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9960c0fc2541d99b180f92','5e294b86057fd3f6fc80ef06',2,'M1: Simmer the eggplant','To cook the eggplant for Dahi Brinjal Curry, heat, 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a pan on medium flame for a minute. Then, add 1.5 cups of sliced eggplant and fry it on medium-high flame for a minute. Then, cover it with a lid and cook it on low flame for 7-8 minutes. Keep stirring it occasionally. After cooking the eggplant, take off the lid and saute it on high flame for 1-2 minutes, until it turns slightly golden. Then, turn off the flame and take it out on a plate. While the eggplant is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e9960e6fc2541d99b180f93','5e294b86057fd3f6fc80ef06',3,'M2: Cook the masala','To make the Dahi Brinjal Curry, heat 1.5 teaspoons of cooking oil in a pan on medium flame for a minute. Add 1/2 teaspoon of cumin seeds, 1 nos bay leaf and 1/4 teaspoon of hing. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions and stir fry it on medium-high flame for 2-3 minutes, till it turns slightly translucent. After frying the onions, add 1/2 teaspoon of ginger garlic paste and saute it on medium flame for a minute. Next, add 1.5 teaspoons of gram flour and keep stirring it continuously on low flame for 5 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e99610efc2541d99b180f94','5e294b86057fd3f6fc80ef06',4,'M3: Add curd & simmer the curry.','After frying the gram flour well, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, 1/4 teaspoon of Kashmiri red chili powder, 1/4 teaspoon of coriander powder and 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala and saute it on low flame for 1-2 minutes. Next, add 1/4 cup of water along with 1/2 cup of curd and keep stirring it continuously on low flame for 2-3 minutes as it might curdle. Keep stirring it continuously till it is well combined. After stirring it well, add the cooked eggplant slices to it along with 1/2 teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Cover it with a lid and simmer it for 5 minutes. After 5 minutes, take off the lid and add 1/2 teaspoon of Kasuri methi and 1.5 tablespoons of coriander leaves. Mix it well and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('5e99627cfc2541d99b180f96','5e295132985ffca18ae8fae6',1,'P1: Prep the ingredients','For Tomato Soup, wash, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and roughly chop 1.5 cups of tomatoes. Wash, peel and cut 1/4 cup of carrot into 2 inch pieces. Peel 2 cloves of garlic. Crush 1 teaspoon of black peppercorns to a coarse powder using a pepper grinder.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9962a2498cf4279b6031cc','5e295132985ffca18ae8fae6',2,'M1: Simmer the tomatoes','To make Tomato Soup, heat 1 teaspoon of butter in a pan on low flame for a minute. Then, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions, 2 cloves of garlic and 1 nos bay leaf. Saute the onions for 2-3 minutes on medium-high flame till it turns slightly translucent. Next, add 1.5 cups of chopped tomatoes, 1/4 cup of chopped carrots and 1/4 teaspoon of salt and stir fry the tomatoes for a minute. Add 1/2 cup of water to the tomatoes, cover it with a lid and simmer it for 10 minutes, till the tomatoes are completely cooked.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e9962cbfc2541d99b180f97','5e295132985ffca18ae8fae6',3,'M2: Prepare tomato puree','After simmering the tomatoes, take off the lid and give it a stir. Take out the bay leaf from it and let the mixture cool down completely. After the mixture cools down, transfer it to a blender jar and blend it to a smooth puree.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9962ef498cf4279b6031cd','5e295132985ffca18ae8fae6',4,'M3: Simmer the soup. Garnish & serve','Next, place a sieve over the pan, pour the tomato puree in it and strain the puree to avoid any solid residue. Then, add 1/2 cup of water to the puree to adjust the consistency of the soup. Boil the soup for a minute on medium-high flame. Next, add 1 teaspoon of sugar and 1/2 teaspoon of crushed black pepper and stir it well. Reduce it to low flame, add 2 tablespoons of fresh cream to the soup and mix well. Turn off the flame and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e99634970b00f94066c5049','5e296b66057fd3f6fc80ef09',1,'P1: Prep the ingredients','For Methi Paratha, wash half a bunch of fenugreek leaves thoroughly with water to remove all the dirt. Then, spread it over a kitchen towel and pat it dry. Then, cut off the root ends and separate 1 cup of fenugreek leaves and finely chop it. Wash, peel and finely chop a 1/2-inch piece of ginger. Wash and finely chop 1 nos green chili.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e99636970b00f94066c504a','5e296b66057fd3f6fc80ef09',2,'P2: Knead the dough & rest','To knead the dough for Methi Paratha, in a large mixing bowl, add 1 cup of wheat flour. Add 1 cup of chopped fenugreek leaves, followed by half a teaspoon of salt. Next, add a 1/2-inch piece of chopped ginger, 1 nos chopped green chili, and half a teaspoon of carom seeds followed by half a teaspoon of red chili powder. Mix it well and add about half a cup of water and knead it well into a smooth dough. Then, cover it with a damp cloth and set it aside for 20 minutes. While the dough is resting, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e996385498cf4279b6031ce','5e296b66057fd3f6fc80ef09',3,'M1: Roll the paratha','To make the Methi Paratha, first, divide the prepared dough into equal-sized balls. Next, dust some flour over the rolling base and place the dough ball over it. Dust some flour over the dough ball and roll it into a 7-inch round paratha. Make sure to roll the edges thin.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9963a0fc2541d99b180f98','5e296b66057fd3f6fc80ef09',4,'M2: Cook the Paratha','To toast the Methi Paratha, place the rolled methi paratha onto a hot tawa and cook it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes until small brown spots start to appear. Flip and cook the other side similarly. Next, apply half a teaspoon of cooking oil to both the sides and continue to cook the paratha for another 2-3 minutes, until it turns slightly golden. Then, take it out onto a plate and serve. Make the rest of the parathas similarly.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e99644170b00f94066c504b','5e2972414f28558c29df6471',1,'P1: Pressure cook the rice','To cook rice for Peanut Rice, wash 1.5 cups of sona masuri rice well with water. Put the washed rice in a pressure cooker along with 3 cups of water. Cover it with a lid and pressure cook it on high flame till one whistle. After the first whistle, reduce it to low flame and continue to cook it for another 8 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the rice is cooking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e99647570b00f94066c504c','5e2972414f28558c29df6471',2,'P2: Make the masala powder','For the Peanut Rice, grate 2 tablespoons of fresh coconut using a grater. Wash 5 nos curry leaves. To make the masala powder, heat 1 teaspoon of cooking oil in a pan on medium flame for a minute. Add 2 tablespoons of roasted peanuts, 1 teaspoon of urad dal, 1 teaspoon of chana dal, 1/2 teaspoon of cumin seeds, 1 teaspoon of sesame seeds and 3 nos dry red chilies and saute it on medium-low flame for 2-3 minutes. Next, add 2 tablespoons of grated coconut and saute it for a minute. Then, turn off the flame and allow the mixture to cool down completely. After it cools down, transfer it to a blender jar and blend it to a fine powder.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":5,"flame":3}'),
('5e9964a5498cf4279b6031cf','5e2972414f28558c29df6471',3,'M1: Simmer the rice with masala. Garnish & serve','To make Peanut Rice, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil on medium flame for a minute. Add 1 teaspoon of mustard seeds, and 5 nos curry leaves. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 2 tablespoons of peanuts and saute it on medium-high flame for a minute. Then, add 2 cups of cooked rice along with the prepared masala and 1/2 teaspoon of salt. Mix it well. Then, cover it with a lid and simmer it for 5 minutes. After simmering the rice, take off the lid and give it a gentle stir. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e996c0270b00f94066c504d','5e2979354f28558c29df6475',1,'P1: Pressure cook the rice','To cook rice for Basil Fried Rice, wash 1.5 cups of basmati rice well with water. Next, add the washed rice to a pressure cooker with 3 cups of water. Cover it with a lid and pressure cook it on high flame until the first whistle. After the first whistle, reduce it to low flame and continue to cook the rice for another 8 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cook aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the rice is cooking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e996c3ffc2541d99b180f99','5e2979354f28558c29df6475',2,'P2: Chop & prep the ingredients','For Basil Fried Rice, wash, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions, 1/4 cup of carrot, 1/4 cup of pineapple,1- inch piece of ginger, and 1 teaspoon of garlic. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of green capsicum, 1/4 cup of red capsicum, 1/4 cup of spring onions, 1.5 tablespoons of basil leaves, and 1/4 cup of beans. Wash and make small slits in 3 nos Thai red chilies and 2 nos green chilies.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e996c72fc2541d99b180f9a','5e2979354f28558c29df6475',3,'M1: Fry the onions & ginger-garlic','To make Basil Fried Rice, heat 1 tablespoon of sesame oil in a pan on medium flame for a minute. Add 1 inch of chopped ginger, 1 teaspoon of chopped garlic, 3 nos slit thai red chilies, and 2 nos slit green chilies. Saute it on medium-high flame for 1-2 minutes, until the garlic turns slightly golden. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions and fry it on medium-high flame for 2-3 minutes, till it turns slightly translucent.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e996c78498cf4279b6031d0','5e566287f7851cecaf7c5086',1,'AP1: Soak Black-Eyed Peas','For Lobia Masala Curry, in a large mixing bowl, add 3/4 cups of black-eyed peas and soak it in 2 cups of water for 2 hours. While it is soaking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":120,"advanced_prep_time":120,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e996c92498cf4279b6031d1','5e2979354f28558c29df6475',4,'M2: Stir-fry the vegetables','After frying the onions, add 1/4 cup of chopped carrots, 1/4 cup of chopped beans, 1/4 cup of green capsicum, and 1/4 cup of red capsicum. Stir fry the vegetables on high flame for 1-2 minutes. Add 1/2 teaspoon of salt, 1/4 teaspoon of black pepper powder, and 1 teaspoon of soy sauce and mix it well. Next, add the cooked rice and gently mix it with the vegetables. Stir fry the rice on high flame for a minute.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":4}'),('5e996cc0498cf4279b6031d2','5e566287f7851cecaf7c5086',2,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Lobia Masala Curry, wash, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Next, finely slice 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Wash, and peel 1/2 inch piece of ginger. Crush and peel 2 cloves of garlic. Wash and finely chop 1.5 tablespoons of coriander leaves. Grate 2 tablespoons of fresh coconut using a grater.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e996ccd70b00f94066c504e','5e2979354f28558c29df6475',5,'M3: Add basil leaves & fry the rice','After frying the rice, add 1/4 cup of chopped pineapple, 1.5 tablespoons of chopped basil leaves, and 2 teaspoons of chili oil. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped spring onions and mix it well. Stir fry the rice on medium flame for a minute. Then, turn off the flame and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e996ceffc2541d99b180f9b','5e566287f7851cecaf7c5086',3,'P2: Make a Coconut Masala Paste','To make the coconut masala paste for Lobia Masala Curry, heat 1.5 teaspoons of oil in a pan on a medium flame for a minute. Add 2 cloves of crushed garlic and 1/2 inch piece of ginger. Saute it on a medium flame for 2-3 minutes, until it turns slightly golden. Next, add 1/4 cup of sliced onions and stir fry it on medium-high flame for 3-4 minutes until it turns slightly golden. After frying the onions, add 2 tablespoons of grated coconut and fry it on low flame for 1-2 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and let the mixture cool down completely. After it cools down, transfer it to a blender jar along with 2 tablespoons of water and blend it to a smooth paste.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e996d49498cf4279b6031d3','5e566287f7851cecaf7c5086',4,'M1: Cook Spice and Onions','To make the Lobia Masala Curry, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a pressure cooker on a medium flame for a minute. Add 1/4 teaspoon of mustard seeds, 1/2 teaspoon of cumin seeds and 1/4 teaspoon of hing. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions and saute it on medium-high flame for 3-4 minutes, till it turns slightly golden.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e996d87fc2541d99b180f9c','5e566287f7851cecaf7c5086',5,'M2: Add Masala Powders','After frying the onions, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, 1/2 teaspoon of Kashmiri red chili powder, 1/2 teaspoon of coriander powder, 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala and 1/2 teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Saute it on low flame for 1-2 minutes. After sauteing the spices, add 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes and fry it on medium-low flame for 2-3 minutes, till the tomatoes turn tender.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e996d9d498cf4279b6031d4','5e2988ec057fd3f6fc80ef14',1,'P1: Chop & prep the ingredients','To make broccoli and chicken stir fry, first, clean 400 g of chicken breast and then chop it into cubes. Next, wash and chop 1/4 cup of broccoli into small florets. Wash and roughly chop 1/4 cup of red capsicum. Peel and finely chop 1 tsp of garlic and 1/2 inch of ginger. In a small bowl make the stir-fry sauce, combine 3 tbsp of soy sauce, 3 tbsp of honey, 1 tsp of chopped garlic, 1/2 inch of chopped ginger, and 2 tsp of sesame seeds.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e996dd970b00f94066c504f','5e566287f7851cecaf7c5086',6,'M3: Continue Cooking the Curry','After cooking the tomatoes, add the prepared coconut paste and mix it well. Fry the masala on low flame for 3 minutes. Then, add the soaked black-eyed peas along with 1.5 cups of water and mix well. Cover it with a lid and pressure cook it on high flame until 4 whistles. After the fourth whistle, reduce it to low flame and continue to cook it for another 5 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. After the pressure has been released, take off the lid, and give it a stir. Mash a few black-eyed peas and mix it with the gravy to make its consistency slightly thicker. Garnish with 1.5 tablespoons of coriander leaves and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":20,"flame":2}'),('5e996e19498cf4279b6031d5','5e2988ec057fd3f6fc80ef14',2,'M1: Stir fry the chicken with broccoli. Season & serve','To make broccoli and chicken stir fry, heat 1 tbsp of oil in a pan and then add 400 g of diced chicken. Season it with 1/2 tsp of salt and 1/2 tsp of black pepper. Saute the chicken for 3 mins and then add the prepare stir-fry sauce, mix well. Next add 1/4 cup of broccoli and 1/4 cup of red capsicum, saute this for 3-4 mins and then turn off the flame. The dish is ready to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e996e98fc2541d99b180f9d','5e2ac0c2985ffca18ae8fb02',1,'P1: Chop & prep the ingredients','To make Matar Paneer, first, peel and slice 1/4 cup of onions. Chop 1 cup of paneer into cubes. Wash and peel 1/2 cup of green peas. Peel and roughly chop 1 tsp of garlic and1/2 inch of ginger. Wash and slice 3/4 cup of tomato. Wash and roughly chop 1 tbsp of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e996eca70b00f94066c5050','5e2ac0c2985ffca18ae8fb02',2,'M1:  Prepare the masala paste','For Matar Paneer, heat 1 tbsp of oil in a pan and then add 1/4 cup of sliced onions, 1 tsp of garlic, and 1/2 inch of ginger and saute this for 2-3 mins. Once the onions are translucent, add 3/4 cup of tomatoes, mix well, and then cover the pan with a lid and cook for 10 mins. After this let the mixture cool down before you blend it into a smooth puree.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e996f28498cf4279b6031d6','5e2ac0c2985ffca18ae8fb02',3,'M2: Cook the masala and simmer green peas in the gravy','Next, heat 1 tbsp of oil in the same pan on low flame and then add 1 bay leaf, 1/2 inch of cinnamon, 1 green cardamom, and 1/2 tsp of cumin seeds, 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder, 1/2 tsp of red chili powder, and 2 tsp of gram flour. Roast them for 1 min and then add the prepared vegetable puree. Stirring continuously for 2-3 mins cook the puree until it changes colour and becomes thicker. Next, add 1/4 tsp of cumin powder,1/2 tsp of coriander powder, 1/2 tsp of salt, and mix well. Then, add 1/2 cup of water and 1/2 cup of green peas and mix well. Cover the pan and boil the curry for 10 mins. Next, add 1 cup of cubed paneer, cover the pan, and simmer for another 10 mins. After this, garnish the dish with 1 tbsp of coriander leaves, 1/2 tsp of Kasuri methi, and 1/4 tsp of garam masala, mix well and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e99701afc2541d99b180fa0','5e2ac489985ffca18ae8fb07',1,'P1: Chop & prep the ingredients','To make ridge gourd chutney, first, peel 2 ridge gourds and save the skins in a bowl. Wash and slit 2 green chilies. wash and roughly chop 1/2 cup of tomatoes. peel 2 cloves of garlic. peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of carrots. peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. wash and roughly chop 2 tbsp of coriander leaves. Wash 6 curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":11,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e99705ffc2541d99b180fa1','5e2ac489985ffca18ae8fb07',2,'M1: Prepare the ridge gourd mixture & blend to a chutney','For Ridge gourd chutney, heat 1/2 tbsp in a pan and then add 1 cup of ridge gourd skins and saute for 1 min. Next, add 2 slit green chilies, 1/2 cup of tomato, and saute for 2 mins. Add 1/2 tsp of tamarind and  1/4 tsp of salt to this and mix well. Cover the pan with a lid and cook for 3 mins. After this, add 2 cloves of garlic and 1/2 tsp of cumin seeds, and mix well. Turn off the flame, allow the mixture to cool, and then blend it into a coarse paste with 3 tbsp of water.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9970fcfc2541d99b180fa2','5e2ac489985ffca18ae8fb07',3,'M2: Add tempering to the chutney','Next, add the blended chutney to a bowl and mix it with 1/4 cup of chopped carrots, 1/4 cup of chopped onions, and 2 tbsp of coriander leaves. Next, in a tempering pan, heat 1/2 tbsp of oil and then add 1/2 tsp of urad dal, 1/4 tsp of mustard seeds, 2 dry red chilies, 1/4 tsp of hing, and 6 curry leaves. Let this splutter for a few seconds and then pour it over the prepared chutney. The dish is ready to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e997154498cf4279b6031d7','5e2ac4f94f28558c29df647d',1,'P1: Pressure cook the potatoes','To make Dum Aloo, first, wash 6 baby potatoes and then place them in a pressure cooker with 1 cup of water and let it cook on high flame for 1 min and then on low flame for 5 mins. Once this is done, allow the cooker to release pressure naturally before you open the lid. While the potatoes are cooking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":7,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e99716a498cf4279b6031d8','5e565e515fc0995ffcc413f8',1,'P1: Marinate Chicken','To marinate the chicken for Andhra Chicken Curry, first, wash 400 grams of chicken thoroughly with water. Then, put the washed chicken pieces in a large bowl. Add half a teaspoon of salt followed by a teaspoon of red chili powder and half a teaspoon of turmeric powder, Mix it well and coat the chicken pieces well with the spices. Then, set it aside and allow it to marinate for 30 minutes. While the chicken is marinating, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":30,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":30,"flame":0}'),('5e99717370b00f94066c5054','5e2ac4f94f28558c29df647d',2,'P2: Prep the ingredients','Next, peel and slice 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and roughly chop 1/2 cup of tomatoes. Wash and roughly chop 1 tbsp of coriander leaves. Whisk 2 tbsp of curd ensuring to remove all lumps. Once the potatoes are cooked, peel the skins and using a fork poke the potatoes creating evenly distributed punctures.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e997198fc2541d99b180fa3','5e2ac4f94f28558c29df647d',3,'M1: Make the masala paste','For Dum Aloo, in a kadai heat 2 tbsp of cooking oil and then add 1/2 tsp of red chilli powder, 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder, and 6 peeled and cooked potatoes. Toss them in the masalas and oil for 1 min and then keep them aside. Next, in the same kadai, add 1/2 inch of cinnamon, 1 clove, 1 green cardamom, and saute for a few seconds. Then, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions and saute for 2 mins. Next, add 1/2 tsp of ginger-garlic paste and mix well. Add 1/2 cup of chopped tomatoes and 2 tbsp of cashew nuts to this and saute for 2-3 mins. Turn off the flame and allow this mixture to cool down completely. Once the onions and tomatoes are cool, blend them until they form a smooth paste.','cook_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9971db498cf4279b6031d9','5e2ac4f94f28558c29df647d',4,'M2: Simmer the gravy & add fried potatoes. Garnish & serve','Next, in the same kadai heat 1/2 tbsp of oil and then add 1/2 tsp of cumin seeds followed by the blended masala paste and let this cook for 5 mins, stirring occasionally. Then, add 1/2 tsp of Kashmiri red chili powder, 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder, 1/2 tsp of coriander powder, 1/4 tsp of cumin powder,1/2 tsp of salt, and mix well. Next, reduce the flame to low and then add 2 tbsp of whisked curd and combine with the other ingredients. Add 1/4 cup of water to this and cook for 2 mins. Next, add the fried potatoes, cover the kadai with a lid and let everything cook for 20 mins. After that, garnish the dish with 1/2 tsp of Kasuri methi, 1 tbsp of coriander leaves, and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":23,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('5e9971f6498cf4279b6031da','5e565e515fc0995ffcc413f8',2,'P2: Prep Ingredients','For Andhra Chicken Curry, peel, wash and finely chop 3/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop half a cup of tomatoes. Wash and roughly chop 2 nos green chilies. Wash 15 nos curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e99723670b00f94066c5055','5e2ac5ef057fd3f6fc80ef1b',1,'P1: Prep the ingredients','To make Kadhi Pakoda, first, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions and peel and slice another 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1 green chili. Wash and roughly chop 1 tbsp of coriander leaves. Wash 6 curry leaves. Whisk 1/2 cup of curd, ensure to remove all lumps. Crush 1 tsp of coriander seeds in a mortar and pestle. Once this is complete please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e997240fc2541d99b180fa4','5e565e515fc0995ffcc413f8',3,'P3: Make a Masala Powder','To make the masala powder for Andhra Chicken Curry, in a pan, add 2 teaspoons of coriander seeds, half a teaspoon of cumin seeds and half a teaspoon of fennel seeds followed by half a teaspoon of poppy seeds. Next, add 3 nos cloves, 2 nos green cardamoms and a 1-inch piece of cinnamon stick. Saute and dry roast the spices over low flame for 3-4 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and transfer it to a blender jar and grind it well into a fine powder.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e99727ffc2541d99b180fa5','5e2ac5ef057fd3f6fc80ef1b',2,'M1: Make batter & Fry the pakodas','For Kadhi Pakoda, in a large bowl, add 1/4 cup of sliced onions, 1/4 tsp of red chilli powder, 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder, 1/2 tsp of salt, 1 chopped green chilli, 2 tbsp of gram flour, and mix well. Once the ingredients are combined well, add 2 tbsp of water and mix everything into a thick batter. In a kadai heat, 1/2 cup of oil and then with wet hands make small balls out of the batter and drop them into the hot oil. Deep fry the pakodas for 2-3 mins stirring continuously until they are golden brown. Once they are golden, remove the pakodas and let them rest on a plate with a paper towel on it to absorb the oil.','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e99729f498cf4279b6031db','5e2ac5ef057fd3f6fc80ef1b',3,'M2: Prepare the curd mixture','Next, make a curd mixture, in a large bowl add 1/2 cup of curd, 2tbsp of gram flour, 1/2 tsp of red chili powder, 1/2 tsp of ginger-garlic paste, 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder, and 1/2 tsp of salt. Whisk these ingredients together well and then add 1/4 cup of water. Mix well and keep this aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9972cffc2541d99b180fa6','5e2ac5ef057fd3f6fc80ef1b',4,'M3: Simmer the kadhi & add the pakodas.','Next, in a pan heat 1 tbsp of oil and then add 1/2 tsp of mustard seeds, 1/4 tsp of cumin seeds, 1/4 tsp of fenugreek seeds, 1/4 tsp of crushed coriander seeds, 1 dry red chilli, 1/2 inch of cinnamon, and 6 curry leaves.Let this splutter for a few seconds and then add 1/4 cup of chopped onions and 1/2 tsp of ginger-garlic paste. Saute this for 2-3 mins and once the onions are translucent add the prepared curd mixture to the pan. Stirring continuously cook the kadhi for 15 mins. After this, adjust the consistency of the kadhi if required and then add the prepared pakodas. Garnish the dish with 1 tbsp of coriander leaves and then serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":20,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e9972e870b00f94066c5056','5e565e515fc0995ffcc413f8',4,'M1: Cooking','To make Andhra Chicken Curry, heat 3 tablespoons of cooking oil in a kadai over medium flame for a minute. Next, add 2 nos chopped green chili followed by 15 nos curry leaves and saute it for a minute. Next, add 3/4 cup of chopped onions and fry it over medium flame for 5-6 minutes, until it slightly changes color. Next, add 2 teaspoons of ginger-garlic paste and fry it with the onions for 1-2 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e99730870b00f94066c5057','5e565e515fc0995ffcc413f8',5,'M2: Cook Chicken','Next, add the marinated chicken pieces and mix it well. Then, saute and fry the chicken pieces over high flame for 2 minutes. After that, continue to fry the chicken over medium flame for 5 minutes. Next, add the ground masala powder and mix it well. Saute the chicken pieces with the masala for 2-3 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":4}'),('5e997338498cf4279b6031dc','5e2ac6554f28558c29df647f',1,'P1: Rinse the poha & prep the ingredients','To make Batata Poha, first, rinse 1.5 cups of poha with 2 cups of water. Peel and finely dice 1/4 cup of potatoes. Peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1 green chili. Wash and roughly chop 2 tbsp of coriander leaves. Squeeze 1 tbsp of lime juice. Wash 7 curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e99734370b00f94066c5058','5e565e515fc0995ffcc413f8',6,'M3: Cook Curry','Next, add 2-3 tablespoons of water while frying the chicken pieces to prevent it from sticking to the bottom of the pan. Add half a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Then, continue to fry the chicken over medium flame for another 5 minutes. After that, add half a cup of chopped tomatoes and mix it well. Then cover it with a lid and simmer it for 10 minutes until tomatoes turn tender. While the chicken is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),
('5e997384fc2541d99b180fa7','5e565e515fc0995ffcc413f8',7,'M4: Final Touches','After simmering the Andhra Chicken Curry, remove the lid, and add 1 cup of water. Stir it well and again cover it with a lid. Then, continue to simmer the chicken for another 10 minutes until it is cooked through. After that, take off the lid and turn off the flame. Take it out into a serving bowl and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('5e99741470b00f94066c5059','5e565824f7851cecaf7c5084',1,'M1: Boil Egg','To hard boil, the eggs, first, place 4 nos eggs in a saucepan. Then, add 3 cups of water into it. Make sure eggs are completely submerged in the water. Then, bring it to a rolling boil over a high flame. After that, continue to boil the eggs for another 10-12 minutes over medium-high flame. While the eggs are boiling, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":12,"flame":3}'),('5e99744670b00f94066c505a','5e565824f7851cecaf7c5084',2,'M2: Peel Shell','After hard boiling, the eggs, turn off the flame and carefully dip it in the ice bath. This will allow the shell to come off easily and prevents the eggs from cooking further. Then, gently peel off the shell and cut it into halves. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e997908fc2541d99b180fa9','5e53a54095b6c57e91021793',1,'P1: Make the Dough','To make the dough for Aloo Kulcha, in a large bowl, add 3/4 cup of all-purpose flour. Add half a teaspoon of sugar, half a teaspoon of baking powder and half a teaspoon of baking soda followed by half a teaspoon of salt and 2 tablespoons of curd. Add a teaspoon of cooking oil and mix it well. Then gradually add about 1/4 cup of water and knead it well into a smooth dough. Cover the dough with a damp cloth and allow it to rest for 1 hour. While the dough is resting, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":60,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e997939fc2541d99b180faa','5e53a54095b6c57e91021793',2,'P2: Cook the Potatoes','To boil the potatoes for Aloo Kulcha, first, wash 2 medium-sized potatoes well with water. Next, put the potatoes in a pressure cooker along with 2 cups of water. Cover it with a lid and pressure cook it over a high flame until one whistle. After the first whistle, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook it for another 8 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the potatoes are boiling, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e99795cfc2541d99b180fab','5e53a54095b6c57e91021793',3,'P3: Prep Ingredients','For Aloo Kulcha, wash and finely chop 2 nos green chilies. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves. Wash, peel and finely chop a 1-inch piece of ginger. Next, after boiling the potatoes take it out from the pressure cooker and gently peel off the skin.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e99797e70b00f94066c505c','5e53a54095b6c57e91021793',4,'P4: Make the Stuffing','To make the stuffing for Aloo Kulcha, add the boiled potatoes to a large mixing bowl and mash it well using a fork. Next, add 1 nos chopped green chili. a 1-inch piece of chopped ginger and 1/4 teaspoon of Kashmiri red chili powder followed by 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala and 1/4 teaspoon of dry mango powder. Add 1/4 teaspoon of carom seeds along with a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves. Season it with a teaspoon of salt and mix it well to prepare a potato stuffing.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9979d6fc2541d99b180fac','5e53a54095b6c57e91021793',5,'M1: Prep Dough','To make the Aloo Kulcha, first, divide the prepared dough into small equal-sized balls. Take a dough ball and roll it into a 5-inch circle. Take 3 tablespoons of the prepared potato mixture and shape it into a small lemon-sized ball. Place the stuffing ball over the rolled out kulcha and pleat it as shown to seal the stuffing inside. Next, sprinkle 1/4 teaspoon of sesame seeds and 1/4 teaspoon of chopped coriander leaves over the dough ball and press it gently. Then, flip it and place it over the rolling surface and roll it into an oval kulcha as shown. Next, brush some water over it using an oil brush.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9979f8fc2541d99b180fad','5e53a54095b6c57e91021793',6,'M2: Cook Kulcha','To make the Aloo Kulcha, place the prepared kulcha onto a hot tawa with waterside down and cook it over medium flame for a minute. Then, hold and flip the tawa as shown and cook the other side of the kulcha over the direct flame until small brown spots appear on its surface. As it turns slightly golden and firm, put the tawa back on the flame. Then, brush half a teaspoon of butter over it and gently take it out onto a plate and Serve. Make the rest of the aloo kulchas similarly.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e997d2dfc2541d99b180fb0','5e539bcb8bc0fbeacf45f184',1,'AP1: Soak Moth Beans','For Misal Pav, first, soak 1.5 cups of moth beans in 3 cups of water for 8 hours. While the moth beans are soaking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":480,"advanced_prep_time":480,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e997d5b498cf4279b6031e0','5e539bcb8bc0fbeacf45f184',2,'AP2: Make Sprouts','To make the moth beans sprouts for the Misal Pav, place a damp muslin cloth over a bowl, add the soaked moth beans to it and tie it well into a tight bundle. Set it aside for another 10 hours and make sure to sprinkle some water over the bundle to keep it moist. While the moth beans are resting, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":600,"advanced_prep_time":600,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e997dd3498cf4279b6031e1','5e539bcb8bc0fbeacf45f184',3,'P1: Pressure Cook Moth beans','To boil the moth beans sprout for Misal Pav, first, add the moth beans sprouts to a pressure cooker along with 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder and 1/4 teaspoon of salt. Add 1 cup of water into it and cover it with a lid. Pressure cook over a high flame until one whistle. After the first whistle, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker and allow it to cool down completely. After the pressure from the cooker is released, take off the lid and stir it well. While the moth beans sprouts are boiling, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e997f4c498cf4279b6031e2','5e539bcb8bc0fbeacf45f184',5,'P2: Prep Ingredients','For Misal Pav, peel, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash, peel and roughly chop a half-inch piece of ginger. Peel and wash 2 cloves of garlic. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Finely slice 2 tablespoons of coconut using a grater. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves. Wash and cut a lemon into wedges. Wash 8 nos curry leaves well with water.','cook_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e997f8b70b00f94066c505f','5e539bcb8bc0fbeacf45f184',4,'M1: Prepare Masala Paste','To prepare the masala paste for Misal Pav, first, heat 2 tablespoons of cooking oil in a Kadai over medium flame for a minute. Add a half-inch piece of chopped ginger followed by 2 cloves of garlic. Saute it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions and fry it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes, until it turns slightly golden. Then, add 2 tablespoons of sliced coconut and saute it over low flame for 3 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e997fbefc2541d99b180fb1','5e539bcb8bc0fbeacf45f184',6,'M2: Prepare Masala Paste','Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes and mix it well. Saute and cook the tomatoes for 3-4 minutes, until tender. After that turn off the flame and allow the mixture to cool down completely. Then, transfer it to a blender jar. Add 2 tablespoons of water into it and blend it well into a smooth paste.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('5e998090fc2541d99b180fb2','5e539bcb8bc0fbeacf45f184',7,'M3: Make the Gravy','To prepare the moth beans gravy for Misal Pav, heat 1.5 teaspoons of cooking oil in a kadai over medium flame for a minute. Temper it with half a teaspoon of mustard seeds and half a teaspoon of cumin seeds. Add 8 nos curry leaves and allow it to splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, half a teaspoon of Kashmiri red chili powder and half a teaspoon of coriander powder followed by a 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala and mix it well. Saute and fry the masala over low flame for 2-3 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9980d7fc2541d99b180fb3','5e539bcb8bc0fbeacf45f184',8,'M4: Make the Gravy','After frying the masala, add the prepared tomato-onion paste and mix it well. Saute and cook the masala over medium flame for 4-5 minutes until oil separates. As the masala releases the oil, add the boiled moth sprouts along with a teaspoon of jaggery along with half a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Add 1.5 cups of water into it and stir it well. Then, cover it with a lid and allow it to cook over medium flame for 10 minutes. While it is cooking, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e9980fc70b00f94066c5060','5e539bcb8bc0fbeacf45f184',9,'M5: Make Misal Pav','After simmering the moth beans gravy for Misal Pav, remove the lid and stir it well. Turn off the flame and take it out into a serving dish. Add 2 tablespoons of farsan mixture and a tablespoon of chopped onions over it. Garnish it with 2 tablespoons of chopped coriander leaves. Serve it alongside pav and lemon wedges.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e998170fc2541d99b180fb4','5e2ac6554f28558c29df647f',2,'M1: Fry the Potatoes','For Batata Poha, in a pan heat 2 tsp of cooking oil and then add 1/4 cup of chopped potatoes. Let them fry for 6-7 mins until they are a golden brown color. Once this is done, take the potatoes out of the pan and set them aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e99828170b00f94066c5061','5e5385878bc0fbeacf45f183',1,'P1: Cook the Pasta','To boil the pasta for Spinach & Chicken Pasta, first, add 3 cups of water to a saucepan along with a teaspoon of salt. Bring it to a boil over a high flame. As the water comes to a rolling boil, add 1 cup of penne pasta into it and stir it well. Then, boil the pasta over medium-high flame for 9 minutes, until it is firm to the bite. While the pasta is boiling, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e99829cfc2541d99b180fb5','5e5385878bc0fbeacf45f183',2,'P2: Prep Ingredients','For Spinach & Chicken Pasta, wash and roughly chop half a cup of spinach leaves. Wash 200 grams of boneless chicken pieces thoroughly with water. Grate 1/4 cup of parmesan cheese using a grater. Peel, wash and finely chop 1 teaspoon of garlic. Next, after boiling the pasta, turn off the flame and carefully drain off the water from it. Then, set it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9982ee498cf4279b6031e3','5e5385878bc0fbeacf45f183',3,'M1: Cook Chicken','To make Spinach & Chicken Pasta,  heat 1 tablespoons of olive oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Next, add the boneless chicken pieces followed by a teaspoon of black pepper powder and a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Then, sear the chicken over medium flame for 8-10 minutes, until it is cooked through and evenly browned on all the sides. After the chicken turns tender-crisp, take it out onto a plate and set aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e998332498cf4279b6031e4','5e5385878bc0fbeacf45f183',4,'M2: Cook Vegetables','Next, to the same pan, heat a tablespoon of olive oil over a medium flame a minute. Add a teaspoon of garlic followed by half a teaspoon of red chili flakes and saute it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Then, add 3/4 cup of tomato puree and mix it well. Stir and cook the tomato puree over medium flame for 2-3 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e998368fc2541d99b180fb6','5e5385878bc0fbeacf45f183',5,'M3: Continue Cooking','After cooking the tomato puree, reduce the flame to low and then add 1/4 cup of fresh cream into it. Mix it well, while continuously stirring it on low flame to prevent the cream from splitting. Once the cream is well combined with the tomato puree, add half a cup of chopped spinach leaves and mix it well. Stir and cook the spinach leaves with the sauce for 2-3 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e99838bfc2541d99b180fb7','5e5385878bc0fbeacf45f183',6,'M4:Garnish','Next, add the seared boneless chicken pieces and mix it well. After that, add the boiled pasta into it and coat it well with the sauce. Stir and cook the pasta over low flame for 2-3 minutes. Then, add 3 tablespoons of grated parmesan cheese and mix it well. Take it out into a serving bowl and garnish the pasta with a tablespoon of grated parmesan cheese. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e99864efc2541d99b180fb8','5e53761e4874a44a24b1f84c',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Roasted Eggplant Wedges, wash a medium-sized eggplant well with water. Then, slice off its both ends and place it horizontally over the chopping board. Slice it into halves and then cut into wedges. Peel, wash and finely chop 1 teaspoon of garlic. Rinse a spring of fresh thyme with water. Wash and cut a lemon into halves. Then, squeeze 1 tablespoon of lemon juice using a squeezer.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e99866efc2541d99b180fb9','5e53761e4874a44a24b1f84c',2,'P2: Make the Marinade','To prepare the marinade for Roasted Eggplant Wedges, in a small bowl, add 1 tablespoon of lime juice followed by 1 teaspoon of chopped garlic and half a teaspoon of paprika. Next, add a teaspoon of fresh thyme, 1/4 teaspoon of salt and 2 teaspoons of olive oil. Mix it well and prepare a marinade.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9986cd498cf4279b6031e5','5e53761e4874a44a24b1f84c',3,'M1: Bake Eggplant','To make the Roasted Eggplant Wedges, preheat the oven at 170°C, brush the prepared marinade over the eggplant wedges using an oil brush. Coat the wedges from all the sides well with the marinade. Next, line the baking tray with a sheet of parchment paper. Place the coated eggplant wedges onto the baking tray and arrange it. Then, place it in the oven and bake it for 25 minutes at 170°C, until it turns crisp and golden brown. While the eggplant wedges are baking, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":25,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":25,"flame":0}'),('5e9986e7fc2541d99b180fba','5e53761e4874a44a24b1f84c',4,'M2: Garnish','After roasting the eggplant wedges, carefully take it out of the oven. It should turn crisp and golden brown. Take it out onto a plate and garnish it with a sprig of fresh thyme and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e998781498cf4279b6031e6','5e53749395b6c57e91021791',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Maggi Noodles Soup, first, soak 1/4 cup of frozen green peas in 1 cup of water for 3 minutes. Next, peel, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of green capsicum. Wash, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of carrots. Wash and chop 1/4 cup of broccoli into small florets. Peel, wash and finely chop 1 teaspoon of garlic. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of spring onion whites. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of spring onion greens.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9987a7fc2541d99b180fbb','5e53749395b6c57e91021791',2,'M1: Saute Onions','To make Maggi Noodle Soup, heat 1.5 teaspoons of olive in a kadai over medium flame for a minute. Add 1 teaspoon of chopped garlic and saute it over medium flame for a minute. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions followed by 1 tablespoon of chopped spring onion whites. Saute and fry the onions over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9987cc70b00f94066c5062','5e53749395b6c57e91021791',3,'M2: Cook Vegetables','After frying the onions, add 1/4 cup of chopped green capsicum. 1/4 cup of chopped carrots and 1/4 cup of green peas followed by 1/4 cup of broccoli florets and 1/4 cup of sweet corn kernels. Season it with half a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Stir and fry the vegetables over high flame for1-2 minutes until tender-crisp. Then, add 2.5 cups of water and stir it well. Cover it with a lid and boil the vegetables over medium flame for 5 minutes. While the vegetables are boiling, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e9987ed498cf4279b6031e7','5e53749395b6c57e91021791',4,'M3: Cook Noodles','After boiling the vegetables for Maggi Noodles Soup, take off the lid and stir it well. Add one packet of Maggi tastemaker into it and mix it well. Next, add one packet of Maggi noodles, while roughly breaking it. Mix it well and allow it to cook for 2 minutes over medium-high flame. As the noodles are cooked and firm to the bite, add 1/4 teaspoon of black pepper powder followed by 1.5 teaspoons of soy sauce and half a teaspoon of vinegar. Next, add 1 tablespoon of chopped spring onion greens and mix it well. Turn off the flame and take it out into a bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9988f5fc2541d99b180fbc','5e5372208bc0fbeacf45f180',1,'P1: Cook the Potatoes','To boil the potatoes for Aloo Saagu, first, wash 2 nos medium-sized potatoes well with water. Next, put the potatoes in a pressure cooker along with 2 cups of water. Cover it with a lid and pressure cook it over high flame until one whistle. After the first whistle, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook it for another 8 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the potatoes are boiling, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":4}'),('5e998914498cf4279b6031e8','5e5372208bc0fbeacf45f180',2,'P2: Blanch Green Peas','To blanch the green peas for Aloo Saagu, first, soak 1/4 cup of frozen green peas in 1 cup of water for 2 minutes. Meanwhile, boil 1 cup of water in a saucepan over high flame for 1-2 minutes. Then add the soaked green peas into it and boil over medium-high flame for 4-5 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and drain off the excess water from it and set it aside. While the green peas are blanching, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e9989b3fc2541d99b180fbd','5e5372208bc0fbeacf45f180',3,'P3: Prep Ingredients','For Aloo Saagu, wash, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of carrots. Peel, wash and medium dice 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and slit 2 nos green chilies. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of curry leaves. Wash 10 nos curry leaves. Next, to make the gram flour slurry, in a small bowl add 2 tablespoons of gram flour. Add 1/4 cup of water to it and mix it well to avoid any lumps. Next, after boiling the potatoes, gently peel off the skin and mash it well using a potato masher or a fork.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9989e270b00f94066c5063','5e5372208bc0fbeacf45f180',4,'M1: Temper Spices and Onions','To make the Aloo Saagu, heat 1 tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Temper it with half a teaspoon of cumin seeds and half a teaspoon of mustard seeds. Next, add 2 nos green chilies followed by 1/4 cup of chopped onions and 10 nos curry leaves. Saute and fry it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until onions turn translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e998a03498cf4279b6031e9','5e5372208bc0fbeacf45f180',5,'M2: Continue Cooking','After frying the onions, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions along with 1/4 cup of blanched green peas. Stir and fry the vegetables over medium-high flame for 3-4 minutes until tender-crisp. Next, add half a teaspoon of turmeric powder and saute it for a minute. Then, add the prepared gram flour slurry into the vegetables and mix it well. Saute and cook the slurry over low flame for 2-3 minutes until it thickens.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e998a27498cf4279b6031ea','5e5372208bc0fbeacf45f180',6,'M3: Continue Cooking','After cooking the slurry with vegetables, add 1 cup of mashed potatoes and mix it well. Saute and cook it over low flame for 2-3 minutes. After that, add about 1/4 cup of water to adjust the consistency and stir it well. Add half a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Bring it to a boil and cook it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and garnish it with 2 tablespoons of chopped coriander leaves. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e998ac770b00f94066c5064','5e5370d395b6c57e91021790',1,'P1: Make Dough','To knead the dough for Poori, in a large bowl, add 1 cup of wheat flour along with 1 teaspoon of semolina. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of sugar followed by 1/4 teaspoon of salt and a teaspoon of cooking oil and mix it well. Then, gradually add about half a cup of water and knead it well into a smooth and stiff dough. Then, divide the dough into halves and roll it cylindrically. Cut it into small pieces and shape each piece into a small round dough ball.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e998ae2498cf4279b6031eb','5e5370d395b6c57e91021790',2,'M1: Make Poori','To make the Poori, first, heat 1 cup of cooking oil in a kadai over medium flame for 2-3 minutes. Meanwhile, take a prepared dough ball and apply 1/4 teaspoon of oil over it. Then pat it gently and roll it into a thin round poori. Make sure to roll out the edges thin. Then, carefully drop it into the hot oil and fry it over medium-high flame, while gently pressing it with the turner so it puffs up. Keep splashing oil over it, in between and shallow fry it for 2-3 minutes, until it turns slightly golden. Make sure to flip and fry both the sides evenly. Then, take it out onto a kitchen napkin to remove the excess oil and serve. Make the rest of the pooris similarly.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e998bfdfc2541d99b180fbe','5e536fcd4874a44a24b1f84b',1,'AP1: Soak Chana Dal','For Vada Curry, add 3/4 cup of chana dal in a bowl and soak it in 2 cups of water for 2 hours. While the chana dal is soaking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":120,"advanced_prep_time":120,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e998c26498cf4279b6031ec','5e536fcd4874a44a24b1f84b',2,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Vada Curry, peel, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Wash and slit 2 nos green chili. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of curry leaves. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of coriander leaves. Wash 6 nos curry leaves well with water.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e998c65498cf4279b6031ed','5e536fcd4874a44a24b1f84b',3,'P2: Prepare Vada Batter','To prepare the vada mixture for Vada Curry, first, add drain off the water from the soaked chana dal and add it to a blender jar. Next, add half a teaspoon of fennel seeds followed by 1 slit green chili and half a teaspoon of cumin seeds. Then, cover the jar with a lid and blend it into a slightly coarse paste. Then, transfer it to a bowl and add 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves along with a tablespoon of chopped curry leaves and a 1/4 teaspoon of salt. Mix it well and prepare the vada mixture.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e998cb7fc2541d99b180fbf','5e536fcd4874a44a24b1f84b',4,'P3: Cook the Vada','To prepare the vada for vada Curry, first, divide the prepared vada mixture into small portions and shape them into small lemon-sized balls. Then, gently press it to slightly flatten it as shown.  Next, heat 1 cup of cooking oil in a Kadai over high flame for 1-2 minutes. Then, carefully drop the prepared vadas one by one into the hot oil and deep fry it over medium flame for 3-4 minutes until it turns crisp and golden brown. After frying it, take it out onto a kitchen napkin and crumble the vadas into small pieces as shown.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e998cedfc2541d99b180fc0','5e536fcd4874a44a24b1f84b',5,'M1: Temper Whole Spices','To make the Vada Curry, heat 2 tablespoons of cooking oil in a kadai over medium flame for a minute. Add 1 nos bay leaf, a half-inch piece of cinnamon stick and 2 nos green cardamoms followed by 3 nos cloves and half a teaspoon of fennel seeds. Next, add a 1/4 teaspoon of hing and saute it over low flame for a minute. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions and fry it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until it turns translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e998d16fc2541d99b180fc1','5e536fcd4874a44a24b1f84b',6,'M2: Add Masalas','After frying the onions, add half a teaspoon of ginger-garlic paste followed by 1 nos slit green chili and 6 nos curry leaves. Saute it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. After that, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, and half a teaspoon of Kashmiri red chili powder along with half a teaspoon of coriander powder and a 1/4 teaspoon of salt. Mix it well and fry the masala over low flame for 1-2 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e998d3dfc2541d99b180fc2','5e536fcd4874a44a24b1f84b',7,'M3: Continue Making Curry','After frying the masala, add 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes and mix it well. Saute and cook the tomatoes for 3-4 minutes, until it turns tender. Then, add 3/4 cup of water followed by half a cup of coconut milk and mix it well. Keep stirring it continuously over low flame until it is well combined, as coconut milk can split easily. Once it is well combined, cover it with a lid and simmer it for 2 minutes. While the gravy is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e998d64fc2541d99b180fc3','5e536fcd4874a44a24b1f84b',8,'M4: Final Touches','After simmering the gravy for Vada Curry, take off the lid and stir it well. Next, add the crumbled chana dal vadas into it and mix it well. Cover it with a lid and continue to simmer it for 5 minutes. After that, remove the lid and turn off the flame. Add 2 tablespoons of chopped coriander leaves and mix it well. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e998f03fc2541d99b180fc4','5e536e2795b6c57e9102178e',1,'P1: Make Dough','For Gatte Ki Sabzi, in a large bowl, add half a cup of gram flour. Add 1/4 teaspoon of coriander seeds, 1/4 teaspoon of carom seeds, 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder and 1/4 teaspoon of Kashmiri red chili powder followed by 1/4 teaspoon of hing. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of salt along with a tablespoon of ghee and a tablespoon of curd and mix it well. Add some water and knead it well into a smooth dough.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e998f2f498cf4279b6031ef','5e536e2795b6c57e9102178e',2,'P2: Boil Dough','Next, divide the prepared dough into equal portions and roll it into thin cylinders as shown. Flatten the edges and prepare the gatta cylinders from the besan dough. Next, to cook the gattas, add 3 cups of water to a saucepan and bring it to a boil over high flame. As it comes to a boil, carefully add the prepared dough cylinders one by one into it. Make sure that it is completely dipped in water. Then, allow it to boil over medium flame for 10 minutes until it starts to float over the water. While it is boiling, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":10,"flame":3}'),('5e998f4c70b00f94066c5065','5e536e2795b6c57e9102178e',3,'P3: Prep Ingredients','For Gatte ki Sabzi, peel, wash and finely chop1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Next, add half a cup of curd in a bowl and whisk it until smooth using a whisk.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e998f7bfc2541d99b180fc5','5e536e2795b6c57e9102178e',4,'P4: Chop Cooked Dough','After boiling the dough cylinders for Gatte Ki Sabzi, it slightly changes color and starts to float in the water. Then, turn off the flame and carefully take it out onto a plate. Next, slice it into small round pieces as shown.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e998fb970b00f94066c5066','5e536e2795b6c57e9102178e',5,'M1: Temper Whole Spices','To make Gatte Ki Sabzi, heat a tablespoon of cooking oil in a kadai over medium flame for a minute. Add half a teaspoon of cumin seeds, half a teaspoon of kasuri methi and 1 nos bay leaf followed by 1/4 teaspoon of fennel seeds and 1/4 teaspoon of hing. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions and fry it over medium-high flame for 3-4 minutes until it turns golden brown.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e998fef70b00f94066c5067','5e536e2795b6c57e9102178e',6,'M2: Add Masalas','After frying the onions, add half a teaspoon of ginger-garlic paste and saute it for a minute. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, 1/4 teaspoon of Kashmiri red chili powder and 1/4 teaspoon of coriander powder followed by 1/4 teaspoon of cumin powder and mix it well. Fry the masala over low flame for 1-2 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e999015498cf4279b6031f0','5e536e2795b6c57e9102178e',7,'M3: Cook Curry','After frying the masala, reduce the flame to low and then add 1/4 cup of water followed by half a cup of curd and mix it well. Keep stirring it continuously on low flame until it is well combined, to prevent the curd from splitting. Next, add the prepared gattas followed by 1/4 teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Then, cover it with a lid and allow it to cook over medium flame for 10 minutes. While it is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":10,"flame":2}'),('5e999032498cf4279b6031f1','5e536e2795b6c57e9102178e',8,'M4: Garnish & Serve','After simmering the Gatte Ki Sabzi, remove the lid and stir it well. Add 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala and 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves. Mix it well and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e99955670b00f94066c506a','5e2ac71e057fd3f6fc80ef1f',1,'P1: Prep the ingredients','For Veg Manchurian, wash, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of carrot. Wash and finely shred 1/4 cup of cabbage. Wash and finely chop 3/4 cup of spring onion greens. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of spring onion whites. Wash, peel and finely chop a half-inch piece of ginger.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9995e2498cf4279b6031f2','5e2ac71e057fd3f6fc80ef1f',2,'P2: Prepare the cornflour slurry','Peel, wash and finely chop half a teaspoon of garlic. Wash and cut 1/4 cup of capsicum into medium dices. To make the cornflour slurry, add a teaspoon of cornflour in a bowl. Add 1/4 cup of water into it and mix it well to avoid any lumps.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e99962e70b00f94066c506b','5e2ac71e057fd3f6fc80ef1f',3,'P3: Prepare the vegetable mixture','To prepare the vegetable balls for Veg Manchurian, in a large mixing bowl, add 1/4 cup of chopped carrot, 1/4 cup of chopped cabbage and 1/4 cup of chopped spring onion greens. Next, add 1 teaspoon of soy sauce, 1 teaspoon of red chili sauce and 1 teaspoon of ginger-garlic paste followed by 1/4 teaspoon of black pepper powder. Mix it well while squeezing the vegetables to make the mixture moist.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e99966370b00f94066c506c','5e2ac71e057fd3f6fc80ef1f',4,'P4: Prepare the veg balls from the mixture','Next, add 2 tablespoons of all-purpose flour followed by 2 tablespoons of cornflour and mix it well to prepare a dough-like stiff mixture. Then, divide it into equal portions and shape it into small round balls.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e99978afc2541d99b180fc7','5e2ac71e057fd3f6fc80ef1f',5,'M1: Fry the veg balls','To fry the Veg Balls for Veg Manchurian, heat 3/4 cup of cooking oil in a kadai over medium-high flame for 2-3 minutes. Next, carefully drop the prepared veg balls one by one into the hot oil and deep fry it over medium flame for 5-6 minutes, until it turns crisp and golden brown. After frying the balls, carefully take it out onto a kitchen napkin to wipe off the excess oil.','cook_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9997bc70b00f94066c506e','5e2ac71e057fd3f6fc80ef1f',6,'M2: Stir& fry the vegetables','To make the Veg Manchurian, heat 1 tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Next, add a 1/2-inch piece of chopped ginger and half a teaspoon of chopped garlic and saute it for 1-2 minutes. Then, add 1/4 cup of chopped spring onions and fry it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until it slightly changes color. Add 1/4 cup of diced green capsicum and fry it over high flame for 1-2 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9997fdfc2541d99b180fc8','5e2ac71e057fd3f6fc80ef1f',7,'M3: Add the veg balls to the gravy. Garnish & serve','After frying the vegetables, add 1 teaspoon of red chili sauce and 2 teaspoons of soy sauce along with the prepared cornflour slurry. Mix it well and cook it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Add 1/4 cup of water and keep stirring it continuously, until it is well combined. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of black pepper powder and half a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Next, add the fried veg balls and coat it well with the sauce. Turn off the flame and take it out into a serving bowl. Garnish it with a tablespoon of chopped spring onion greens and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e99988e70b00f94066c506f','5e2ac8f24f28558c29df6483',1,'P1: Prepare the pancake batter','To make Peanut Butter Banana Pancakes, in a large mixing bowl, add 1 cup of all-purpose flour, 1/2 tsp of baking powder, 1/4 tsp of salt, and 1/4 tsp of baking soda and mix well. In another bowl mash 1 ripe banana with a fork and then add 1 egg, 1 tsp of vanilla essence, 2 tsp of oil, 1 tbsp of sugar, and 1.5 tbsp of peanut butter and whisk this together until combined well. To the banana mixture gradually add the flour mixture and 1/2 cup of milk and gently combine them together. Once this is done, move on the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9998b770b00f94066c5070','5e2ac8f24f28558c29df6483',2,'M1: Cook the pancakes. Garnish & serve','For Peanut butter Banana Pancakes, heat 1 tbsp of butter in a frying pan for 1 min and then, add 1/4 cup of pancake batter. Let this cook for 2 mins and once bubbles start to appear on top of the pancake flip it. Let it cook on the other side for 2 mins as well. Once the pancake is browned evenly on both sides, place it on a plate to serve. Continue this process with the remaining pancake batter. Garnish the pancakes with 1 tbsp of honey before serving.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e999907fc2541d99b180fc9','5e2ac9d54f28558c29df6485',1,'P1: Knead & rest the dough','To knead the dough for Gobhi Paratha, add 1.5 cups of wheat flour in a large mixing bowl. Add 1/4 teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Next, gradually add about half a cup of water and knead the flour for 4-5 minutes. Add a little more water, if required and knead it well into a smooth dough. Then, cover it with a damp cloth and allow it to rest for 20 minutes.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e99993efc2541d99b180fca','5e2ac9d54f28558c29df6485',2,'P2: Grate cauliflower & prep the ingredients','For Gobhi Paratha, wash a small cauliflower and remove the stem end. Next, grate 1 cup of cauliflower using a grater. Wash, peel and finely chop a 1/2-inch piece of ginger. Wash and finely chop 1 nos green chili.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e99998170b00f94066c5071','5e2ac9d54f28558c29df6485',3,'P3: Prepare the cauliflower stuffing','To make the stuffing for Gobhi Paratha, first, in a bowl, add 1 cup of grated cauliflower. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of salt into it and mix it well. Salt will draw out the moisture from the cauliflower. Then, squeeze out the extra water from the grated cauliflower and put it in a separate bowl. Next to this, add 1 nos chopped green chili, and a 1/2- inch piece of chopped ginger followed by 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Mix it well to prepare the stuffing.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9999b6fc2541d99b180fcb','5e2ac9d54f28558c29df6485',4,'M1: Stuff & roll out the dough ball','To make the Gobhi Paratha, first, divide the prepared dough into equal-sized balls. Next, take a dough ball and dust some flour over it. Then, roll it into a 5-inch circle. Next, place 1-2 tablespoons of the prepared cauliflower stuffing onto it and gently pack it inside the dough ball. Then, gently pat it and roll it into a 7-inch round paratha. Make sure to roll the edges thin.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9999f84590a0278779051d','5e2ac9d54f28558c29df6485',5,'M2: Toast the paratha','To toast the Gobhi Paratha, place the rolled out paratha over the hot tawa and cook it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes until small brown spots start to appear on it''s surface. Then, carefully flip the paratha and apply half a teaspoon of ghee to each of its sides and continue to cook the paratha over medium flame for 2-3 minutes, until it is evenly cooked from both the sides. As the paratha turns golden brown, turn off the flame and take it out onto a plate. Slice it into quarters and serve. Make the rest of the parathas similarly.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e999b4877c5bbfa41905eb2','5e2acb084f28558c29df6487',1,'P1: Prep the ingredients','For Akoori, wash, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1/2 cup of tomatoes. Wash, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of potatoes. Wash and finely chop 1 nos green chili. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Next, in a mixing bowl, crack 4 nos eggs and whisk it well using a whisk. Add 1/2 teaspoon of salt, 1 tablespoon of milk and whisk it well, once again.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e999b6d4590a02787790520','5e2acb084f28558c29df6487',2,'M1: Fry the potatoes','To make Akoori, heat 1.5 tablespoons of ghee in a pan on medium flame for a minute. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions and 1/4 cup of chopped potatoes. Saute and cook the potatoes on medium-low flame for 6-7 minutes until it is completely cooked. Stir the potatoes in between while it is cooking, to prevent it from sticking to the bottom of the pan. While the potatoes are cooking, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":4,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e999c0f4590a02787790521','5e2acb084f28558c29df6487',3,'M2: Stir in the beaten eggs into the vegetables & cook','After cooking the potatoes for Akoori, add 1 nos chopped green chili and 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes. Saute and cook the tomatoes on medium flame for a minute. Then, pour the prepared beaten egg mixture in portions and stir it continuously on low flame in a clockwise motion to make sure that the egg mixture is well combined with the vegetables. Saute and cook it on low flame only for 2-3 minutes to keep it moist. Ensure not to overcook it as it might turn dry. Keep stirring it as it cooks, to prevent it from sticking to the bottom of the pan. After the eggs are cooked turn off the flame. Garnish it with 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e999c7d84eb5c1cc4e90763','5e2acb6a057fd3f6fc80ef23',1,'P1: Prepare the kofta dough','For Lauki Kofta Curry, peel and grate 1 cup of bottle gourd. Next, in a bowl add the grated bottle gourd sprinkle 1/2 tsp of salt, mix well, and then squeeze out the excess water from the bottle gourd. In another bowl add the prepped bottle gourd, 1/4 cup of gram flour, 1/4 tsp of red chili powder, and 1/4 tsp of salt and mix well to make a kofta dough. Once the dough is ready, set it aside and move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e999c9b84eb5c1cc4e90764','5e2acb6a057fd3f6fc80ef23',2,'P2: Prep the ingredients','Next, wash and roughly chop 1 tbsp of coriander leaves. Peel and finely chop 1/2 cup of onions. Wash and roughly chop 1 cup of tomatoes. Blend this cup of tomatoes in a blending jar to make a tomato puree.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e999cd084eb5c1cc4e90765','5e2acb6a057fd3f6fc80ef23',3,'M1: Make the kofta balls','For Lauki Kofta Curry, heat 1/2 cup of oil in a pan for 3 mins. Next, make 12 small balls with the kofta dough and fry them in the hot oil for 2-3 mins until they turn golden brown. Once the kofta becomes golden take them out of the oil and place them on a plate with a kitchen towel on it to absorb excess oil. Once all the kofta dough has been fried, set them aside and move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e999cf94590a02787790522','5e2acb6a057fd3f6fc80ef23',4,'M2: Simmer the kofta balls in the gravy','Next, in a pan heat 1 tbsp of oil for 1 min and then add 1/2 cup of chopped onions. Saute this for 2-3 mins, until the onions are golden brown. Next, add 1 cup of the prepared tomato puree and saute for 1 min. Then, add 1/4 tsp of red chilli powder, 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder, 1.5 tsp of coriander powder, and 1/4 tsp of salt and mix well. Saute this for 1 min and then turn off the flame. In a serving dish add the fried kofta and then pour the prepared curry over it. Garnish the curry with 1 tbsp of coriander leaves and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e999d6c4590a02787790523','5e2acbc0985ffca18ae8fb0c',1,'P1: Cook the dal with vegetables','To make Vegetable Sambar, first, peel and chop 1/4 cup of radish and 1/4 cup of carrots into sticks. Wash and chop 1/4 cup of drumsticks into 2 inch long pieces. Next, wash 1/4 cup of toor dal and then cook it in a pressure cooker with 3/4 cup of water. Then, place a steel bowl in the cooker and put 1/4 cup of radish, 1/4 cup of carrot, and 1/4 cup of drumstick. Cook all this on high flame for 1 whistle and then on low flame for 8 mins. Once the dal is cooked , let the pressure release naturally before you open the cooker. While the dal is cooking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e999d8d4590a02787790524','5e2acbc0985ffca18ae8fb0c',2,'P2: Prep the ingredients','Next, in a small bowl, add 2 tsp of tamarind with1/4 cup of hot water. Let this soak for 2 mins and then mash the tamarind and water together to make a pulp. Wash and chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Peel and chop 1/4 cup of onions into petals. Wash and slit 1 green chilli. Wash 10 curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e999ddc84eb5c1cc4e90766','5e2acbc0985ffca18ae8fb0c',3,'M1: Simmer the sambar','For Vegetable Sambar, in a kadai, add the prepared tamarind pulp, 1/4 cup of tomatoes, 1 slit green chili, 5 curry leaves, 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder, 1/4 tsp of jaggery, and let this come to a boil. Once boiling, add 1/4 cup of onion petals, 1/4 tsp of salt, and let it boil for another 5 mins. Next, add the vegetables that were cooked in the pressure cooker - 1/4 cup of radish, 1/4 cup of carrot, 1/4 cup of drumsticks. Then, add 1/4 cup of cooked toor dal and mix well. Once the sambar comes to a boil add 1 tbsp of sambar powder, mix well, and then reduce the heat to low flame. While the sambar is simmering move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e999e0e77c5bbfa41905eb4','5e2acbc0985ffca18ae8fb0c',4,'M2: Add the tempering to the sambar','Next, in a tadka pan, heat 1 tbsp of coconut oil and then add 1/4 tsp of mustard seeds, 1/4 tsp of hing, 1 dry red chili, 5 curry leaves, and let this splutter for a few seconds. Next, pour the prepared tadka over the simmering sambar, give it a stir and then turn off the flame. The dish is ready to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e999eab77c5bbfa41905eb5','5e2acc1d057fd3f6fc80ef25',1,'P1: Prepare the pancake batter','To make Blueberry Pancakes, first, in a small bowl melt  1 tbsp of butter and wash 1/2 cup of blueberries. In a large mixing bowl add 1 cup of all-purpose flour, 1.5 tbsp of sugar, 1/2 tsp of baking powder, and 1/4 tsp of baking soda and mix well. Next, add 1/2 cup of milk, 1 tsp of vanilla essence, 1 tbsp of melted butter, 1/4 tsp of vinegar, 1 egg, and whisk all the ingredients together. Then, add 1/2 cup of blueberries and give it a final stir.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('5e999ecf84eb5c1cc4e90767','5e2acc1d057fd3f6fc80ef25',2,'M1: Make the pancakes','For blueberry pancakes, in a frying pan heat 1 tbsp of butter on medium heat. Next, pour 1/4 cup of the prepared pancake batter to the pan and let it cook for 2 mins. Once bubbles start to form on top of the pancake, flip it and cook for another 2 mins. When the pancake is evenly browned on both sides, put it on a plate to serve. Repeat this process with the remaining pancake batter to make more pancakes. Garnish your pancakes with 1 tbsp of honey before serving.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e999f2677c5bbfa41905eb6','5e2acdac4f28558c29df648a',1,'P1: Boil the pasta','To make veg alfredo pasta, start by boiling 2 cups of water in a pot. Once the water is boiling add 1 cup of penne pasta. Cook the pasta for 8-12 mins until it is 3/4th cooked or al dente. Once the pasta is cooked, drain the water, and set it aside. While the pasta cooks, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e999f5177c5bbfa41905eb7','5e2acdac4f28558c29df648a',2,'P2: Prep the ingredients','Next, peel and chop 1 tsp of garlic. peel and finely chop 1/2 cup of onions. wash and chop 1/4 cup of broccoli into small florets. wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of red capsicum, 1/4 cup of green capsicum, and 1/4 cup of yellow capsicum. Wash and slice 1/4 cup of mushrooms. Grate 1/4 cup of mozzarella cheese. Boil 1/2 cup of water and then add 1/4 cup of sweet corn kernels. Let them cook for 2 mins and then drain the water.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e999f8a4590a02787790525','5e2acdac4f28558c29df648a',3,'M1: Stir-fry the vegetables','For Alfredo Pasta, heat 1 tbsp of olive oil and 2 tsp of butter in a pan for 1 min. Next, add 1 tsp of garlic, saute for 1 min, and then add 1/2 cup of onions and saute for 2 mins. Next, add 1/4 cup of broccoli florets, 1/4 cup of red capsicum, 1/4 cup of green capsicum, 1/4 cup of yellow capsicum, 1/4 cup of sweet corn, and 4 chopped mushrooms. Season this with 1 tsp of Italian seasoning, 1/4 tsp of salt, and saute the vegetables for 2 mins.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e99a00977c5bbfa41905eb8','5e2acdac4f28558c29df648a',4,'M2: Add the all purpose flour & milk. Combine the pasta & serve','Next, to make the pasta sauce, add 1 tbsp of all-purpose flour and mix well. Next pour in 3/4 cup of milk and mix well. Once the flour and milk are combined without any lumps, add 2 tbsp of fresh cream, add mix well. Next, 1 cup of cooked pasta, and 1/4 cup of grated cheese. Mix all the ingredients well and then the dish is ready to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e99a07c84eb5c1cc4e90768','5e2acde4985ffca18ae8fb0e',1,'P1: Prep the ingredients','To make Pav Bhaji, first, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 3/4 cup of tomatoes. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of capsicum. Peel and chop 1/4 cup of potatoes into cubes. Wash and roughly chop 1 tbsp of coriander leaves. Wash and slice 1 piece of lime to use as garnish.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e99a0a577c5bbfa41905eb9','5e2acde4985ffca18ae8fb0e',2,'M1:  Pressure cook the vegetables with the masala','For Pav Bhaji, heat 1 tbsp of butter in a pressure cooker and then add 1/4 cup of onions and 1/2 tsp of ginger-garlic paste. Saute this for 2-3 mins and once the onions become translucent add 1/4 cup of capsicum and mix well. Next, add 3/4 cup of tomatoes and saute for 2-3 mins. Once the tomatoes are soft, add 1/4 cup of green peas and 1/4 cup of potatoes, saute for 1 min. Next, add1/2 tsp of red chili powder, 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder, 1 tsp of pav bhaji masala, and 1/2 tsp of salt, saute for 1 min. Then, add 3/4 cup of water, mix well, and then cook on high flame for 1 whistle and then on low flame for 8 mins. Once this is done allow the pressure to release naturally before you open the cooker. While the bhaji is cooking, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e99a0e084eb5c1cc4e90769','5e2acde4985ffca18ae8fb0e',3,'M2: Simmer the bhaji & serve with toasted pavs','Next, open the cooker and mash some of the vegetables in the bhaji to make the curry thicker. Then, add 1 tbsp of butter and 1 tbsp of coriander leaves, mix well, and the dish is ready to serve. Next, toast the pav on a tawa with 1 tsp of butter and 1/2 tsp of the prepared bhaji. Once the desired number of pav is toasted your Pav Bhaji is ready.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e99a1ac77c5bbfa41905eba','5e2ad66d4f28558c29df648c',1,'P1: Pressure cook the dal & rice','To make Palak Dal Khichdi, wash 1/2 cup of sona masuri and 1/2 cup of yellow moong dal. Cook both the rice and dal in a pressure cooker along with 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder and 2.5 cups of water on high flame for 1 whistle and then on low flame for another 8 mins. Once this is done, allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturallly before you take off the lid.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e99a1dc4590a02787790526','5e2ad66d4f28558c29df648c',2,'P2: Chop spinach leaves & prep the ingredients','Next, wash and roughly chop 1/2 cup of spinach leaves. Peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and slit 1 green chili. Wash and finely chop 1/2 cup of tomatoes. Blend the 1/2 cup of spinach leaves into a smooth puree.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e99a2154590a02787790527','5e2ad66d4f28558c29df648c',3,'M1: Temper the ghee with whole spices and fry onions','For Palak Dal Khichdi, in a pan heat 2 tsp of oil for 1 min. Then, add 1 tsp of cumin seeds, 2 green cardamoms, 1/2 inch of cinnamon, 1 bay leaf, 1 dry red chili, and let this splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions and fry them for 2 mins. Then, add 1/2 tsp of ginger-garlic paste and 1 slit green chili and saute this for another minute.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e99a2794590a02787790528','5e2adffb985ffca18ae8fb18',1,'P1: Prepare the mint paste','For Mint Raita, wash and separate 1/4 cup of mint leaves. Next, in a bowl, add 1 cup of curd and whisk it well using a whisk to avoid any lumps. Next, to make the mint paste, add 1/4 cup of mint leaves to a blender jar along with a tablespoon of curd and blend it well into a smooth paste.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e99a2a777c5bbfa41905ebb','5e2adffb985ffca18ae8fb18',2,'M1: Add the mint paste to the curd. Season & serve','To make the Mint Raita, in a large bowl, add the prepared mint paste followed by 1 cup of curd. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of Kashmiri red chili powder, half a teaspoon of cumin powder and 1/4 teaspoon of salt. Mix it well and transfer it into a serving bowl. Garnish the raita with a mint leaf and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e99a31884eb5c1cc4e9076a','5e2af2a5057fd3f6fc80ef2a',1,'P1: Prep the ingredients','For the Pomegranate Salad, peel and separate 1 cup of pomegranate seeds. Wash, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of capsicum. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e99a33b77c5bbfa41905ebc','5e2af2a5057fd3f6fc80ef2a',2,'P2: Chop & prep the ingredients','Next, wash and finely chop 1 nos green chili. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of mint leaves. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash and cut a lime into halves. Then, squeeze 1 tablespoon of lime juice. Crush 1/2 teaspoon of black peppercorns to a coarse powder using a pepper grinder.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e99a35b84eb5c1cc4e9076b','5e2af2a5057fd3f6fc80ef2a',3,'M1: Make the salad dressing','To make the dressing for the Pomegranate Salad, in a mixing bowl, add 1 tablespoon of lime juice, 1/4 teaspoon of salt and 1/4 teaspoon of crushed black pepper. Next, add 2 teaspoons of olive oil and mix it well.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e99a3884590a02787790529','5e2af2a5057fd3f6fc80ef2a',4,'M2: Combine the salad & dressing. Garnish & serve','To make the Pomegranate Salad, put 1 cup of peeled pomegranate seeds to a large mixing bowl. Add 1/4 cup of chopped onions, 1/4 cup of chopped capsicum, 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes and 1 nos chopped green chili. Next, add 1 tablespoon of chopped mint leaves and 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves to the salad. Next, pour the dressing over the salad and mix well. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9d31a484eb5c1cc4e9076c','5e536d004874a44a24b1f848',1,'P1: Cook Vermicelli','To boil the vermicelli for Shavige Bhath, first, add 4 cups of water in a saucepan along with half a teaspoon of cooking oil and half a teaspoon of salt. Mix it well and bring it to a boil over a high flame. As it comes to a boil, add 2 cups of thin rice vermicelli into it and dip it into the water completely. Then, allow it to boil for 2 minutes over medium-high flame. Keep stirring it in between to avoid it from sticking together. After boiling it, turn off the flame and drain off the excess water. Set aside and allow it to cool down completely. While the vermicelli is cooling down, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":10,"flame":4}'),('5e9d32744590a0278779052a','5e536d004874a44a24b1f848',2,'P2: Prep Ingredients','For Shavige Bhath, wash, peel and finely chop a 1-inch piece of ginger. Wash and finely chop 2 nos green chilies. Peel, wash and finely chop a 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and cut a lemon into halves. Then, squeeze 1 tablespoon of lime juice using a squeezer. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves. Wash 7 nos curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d32ff77c5bbfa41905ec6','5e536d004874a44a24b1f848',3,'M1: Roast Nuts','To make Shavige Bhath, first, heat 2 tablespoons of cooking oil in a Kadai over medium flame for a minute. Next, add 2 tablespoons of peanuts and roast it over low flame for 2-3 minutes until it turns slightly golden and crunchy. Add 8 nos cashew nuts and roast it over low flame for 2-3 minutes. As the cashew nuts slightly change color, turn off the flame and take it out into a bowl and set aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d33454590a0278779052b','5e536d004874a44a24b1f848',4,'M2: Temper Spices','Next, to the same oil, add 1 teaspoon of chana dal, 1 teaspoon of urad dal and 1 nos dry red chili followed by 7 nos curry leaves. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Next, add a 1-inch piece of chopped ginger along with 1 nos chopped green chili and fry it over medium flame for a minute. Then, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions and fry the onions over medium flame for 3-4 minutes until it turns slightly golden.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d337577c5bbfa41905ec7','5e536d004874a44a24b1f848',5,'M3: Add Turmeric and Simmer','After frying the onions, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder and mix it well. Next, add the boiled rice vermicelli and gently mix it until the yellow color of turmeric sets on it evenly. Then, cover it with a lid and simmer it for 2 minutes. While the vermicelli is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('5e9d341777c5bbfa41905ec8','5e536d004874a44a24b1f848',6,'M4: Final Touches','After simmering the Shavige Bhath, take off the lid and gently mix it. Next, add the fried peanuts and cashew nuts followed by 2 tablespoons of chopped coriander leaves. Add 1 tablespoon of lime juice and mix it well. Turn off the flame and take it out into a serving bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d34bd84eb5c1cc4e9076d','5e536ba195b6c57e9102178d',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Bhindi Raita, wash 3/4 cups of ladies'' fingers well with water and spread them over a kitchen towel to wipe off the excess water. Then, allow it to dry completely for some time. There should be no moisture left in the ladies'' fingers or it will stick together while cooking. After drying the ladies'' fingers completely, chop them into roundels. Next, wash and finely chop 1 nos green chili. Wash 5 nos curry leaves well with water. Next, in a bowl add 1 cup of curd using a whisk and whisk it well until smooth.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":5,"flame":0}'),('5e9d34ec77c5bbfa41905ec9','5e536ba195b6c57e9102178d',2,'M1: Fry Lady''s Finger','To fry the ladies fingers the Bhindi Raita, heat 1 tablespoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add 3/4 cups of chopped ladies fingers followed by 1 nos chopped green chili and fry it over medium-high flame until it turns crisp. Fry the lady''s fingers for 6-7 minutes while stirring in between. As it turns slightly dark in color and crisp, turn off the flame and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d351784eb5c1cc4e9076e','5e536ba195b6c57e9102178d',3,'M2: Make Raita','To make the Bhindi Raita, add 1 cup of whisked in a large mixing bowl. Add the fried ladies finger into the curd along with half a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Next, to make the tempering, heat 1 teaspoon of cooking oil in a small tempering pan over medium flame for a minute. Add 1/4 teaspoon of mustard seeds, followed by 1/4 teaspoon of cumin seeds and 1/4 teaspoon of hing. Add 5 nos curry leaves along with 1 dry red chili and allow it to splutter for a few seconds. Then turn off the flame and add the tempering to the prepared raita. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d37634590a0278779052d','5e53628795b6c57e9102178c',1,'P1: Prep Bitter Gourd','To prepare Bitter Gourd Sabzi, first, wash and slice 1 cup of bitter gourd, remove the seeds after slicing the gourd. Then transfer the sliced bitter gourd into a mixing bowl and add 1/4 tsp of salt and mix well. Next, pour in 1/2 cup of water and let them soak for 20 mins.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":20,"flame":0}'),
('5e9d37fd4590a0278779052e','5e53628795b6c57e9102178c',2,'P2: Prep the Other Ingredients','Next, peel and slice1/4 cup of onions. Wash and slit 1 green chilli. Wash and roughly chop 1 tbsp of coriander leaves. Wash 7 curry leaves and soak 1/2 tsp of tamarind in 1/4 cup of warm water.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d382077c5bbfa41905eca','5e53628795b6c57e9102178c',3,'M1: Temper Spices','For Bitter Gourd Sabzi, in a pan heat 2 tsp of oil on medium flame. Then add 1/4 tsp of cumin seeds, 1/4 tsp of fennel seeds, 7 curry leaves, and let them splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 1/4 cup of sliced onions and saute them for 2 mins. Once the onions become translucent, add 1/2 tsp of ginger-garlic paste, 1 slit green chill, and saute for 1 min. Next, add 1 cup of sliced bitter gourd squeezing out any excess water. Saute this for 1 min.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d384884eb5c1cc4e90771','5e53628795b6c57e9102178c',4,'M2: Continue Cooking Sabzi','Next, add 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder, 1/4 tsp of red chilli powder, 1/4 tsp of coriander powder, 1/4 tsp of garam masala, 1/4 tsp of salt, and saute on low flame for 1 min. After this, add the tamarind extract along with 1/2 tsp of jaggery. Cover the pan with a lid and let it simmer for 20 mins. After 20 mins, take off the lid and add 1 tbsp of chopped coriander leaves. Then, mix well and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":20,"flame":2}'),('5e9d3cb884eb5c1cc4e90772','5e5361608bc0fbeacf45f17d',1,'P1: Cook Dal','To make Rava Pongal, in a pressure cooker dry roast 1/4 cup of yellow moong dal for 2 mins. Then, add 1 cup of water along with 1 tsp of ghee in the cooker. Close the lid and let the dal cook on high flame for 1 whistle and then on low for 8 mins. Once this is complete, turn off the flame, set the cooker aside, and let the pressure release naturally before you open it. While the Dal is cooking please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d3d0477c5bbfa41905ecb','5e5361608bc0fbeacf45f17d',2,'P2: Prep Ingredients','Next, Wash 7 curry leaves. Crush 1 tsp of black peppercorns with a mortar and pestle. Wash and finely chop 1 inch of ginger. Wash and slit 1 green chilli.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9d3d8b4590a0278779052f','5e5361608bc0fbeacf45f17d',3,'M1: Cooking Pongal','For Rava Pongal, in a pan dry roast 1/2 cup of semolina for 2 min on low flame and then set it aside. In another pan, add the cooked dal along with 1 cup of water and 1/2 tsp of salt, mix well, and bring this to a boil. Once this is boiling, slowly add 1/2 cup of roasted semolina, stir continuously ensuring to remove all lumps. Once the consistency is smooth cover the pan with a lid and keep it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d3da977c5bbfa41905ecc','5e5361608bc0fbeacf45f17d',4,'M2: Make Tadka','Next, in a tadka pan heat 2.5 tbsp of ghee for 1 min. Once warm, add 1 tsp cumin seeds, 1 tsp of crushed peppercorns, 1 inch of chopped ginger, 1 slit green chilli, 10 cashew nuts, and saute for a few seconds. Then add 1/4 tsp of hing, 7 curry leaves, and let this splutter for a few seconds. Turn off the flame and then pour the tadka into the dal and semolina mixture. Mix everything well and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d3edf4590a02787790530','5e53606a8bc0fbeacf45f17c',1,'P1: Cook Dal','To make Dal Dhokli, first, wash 1/4 cup of toor dal and then place it in a pressure cooker along with 3/4 cups of water and 1 tsp of oil. Next, in a small steel bowl add 1 tbsp of peanuts and place it in the pressure cooker and close the lid. Cook the dal and peanuts in the cooker for 5 whistles on medium-low flame. Once this is complete allow the pressure to release naturally before you open the cooker. While the dal is cooking, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d3f114590a02787790531','5e53606a8bc0fbeacf45f17c',2,'P2: Make Wheat Flour Chapatis','Next, in a large bowl mix 1/2 cup of whole wheat flour, 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder, 1/4 tsp of red chilli powder, 1/4 tsp carom seeds, 1/4 tsp of salt, and 1 tsp of oil. Next, gradually add 1/4 cup of water as you knead the dough for 5 mins. Once the dough is smooth and soft make a lemon sized ball with it, place it on a rolling board, and dust it with flour. Begin rolling the ball of dough with a rolling pin into a disk shape, allowing it to remain slightly thick. Next, using a knife diagonally slice the chapati to create diamond shapes and set these aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d3f454590a02787790532','5e53606a8bc0fbeacf45f17c',3,'P3: Prep Other Ingredients','Next, wash and roughly chop 1 tbsp of coriander leaves. Squeeze 1/2 tsp of lime juice. Wash 7 curry leaves. Wash and roughly chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9d3f794590a02787790533','5e53606a8bc0fbeacf45f17c',4,'M1: Temper Spices','For Dal Dhokli, heat 1/2 tsp of ghee in a Kadai on medium flame. To this, add 1/2 tsp mustard seeds, 1/4 tsp of cumin seeds, 1 broken dry red chilli, 1/4 tsp of hing, 7 curry leaves, and let this splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes, 1/2 tsp of ginger-garlic paste, and saute for 2 mins. Then, take off the pressure cooker lid, set the peanuts aside, and whisk the cooked dal. Then, pour this into the kadai and add 3/4 C of water. Mix everything well.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d3fb484eb5c1cc4e90773','5e53606a8bc0fbeacf45f17c',5,'M2: Make Dal Dhokli','Next, add 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder, 1/2 tsp of red chilli powder, 1/4 tsp of cumin powder, 1/2 tsp of coriander powder, 1/4 tsp of garam masala, and mix well. Next, add the 1 tbsp of boiled peanuts and allow the dal to come to a boil. Once it''s boiling, add 1 tsp of jaggery, 1/2 tsp of salt, 1/2 tsp of lime juice, and give it a good stir. Then, add the diamond shape chapati pieces to the Kadai and gently stir it. Next, close the Kadai with a lid and let it boil for 10 mins. After this, garnish the dish with 1 tbsp of coriander leaves and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d41a64590a02787790534','5e535ecd8bc0fbeacf45f17b',1,'AP1: Soak Dal','To make Hesarubele Kosambari, first, soak 3/4 cup of yellow moong dal for 3 hours in 1 cup of water.','prep_method','{"active_time":1,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":180,"advanced_prep_time":180,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d42134590a02787790535','5e535ecd8bc0fbeacf45f17b',2,'P1: Prep Ingredients','To make Hesarubele Kosambari, grate 2 tbsp of fresh coconut, wash and chop 1 tbsp of coriander leaves, and peel and chop 1/2 cup of cucumber. Peel and grate 1/4 cup of carrot.  Wash and finely chopped 1 green chilli.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d423477c5bbfa41905ece','5e535ecd8bc0fbeacf45f17b',3,'M1: Mix Ingredients','For Hesarubele Kosambari, in a large mixing bowl combine 3/4 cup of yellow moong dal, 2 tbsp of grated coconuts, 1/4 cup of grated carrot, 1 chopped green chilli, 1 tbsp of chopped coriander leaves, 1/2 cup of chopped cucumber, 1/2 tsp of salt, and mix everything well.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9d424f4590a02787790536','5e535ecd8bc0fbeacf45f17b',4,'M2: Make Tadka','In a tadka pan, heat 1 tsp of oil and then add 1/4 tsp of mustard seeds, 1/4 tsp of cumin seeds, 1/4 tsp of hing, 1 broken dry red chilli, and pour this into the moong dal mixture. Combine all ingredients well and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d442e84eb5c1cc4e90775','5e4fc1a28bc0fbeacf45f178',1,'P1: Soak Rice','To make mushroom fried rice, first, wash then soak 1 cup of basmati rice in 2 cups of water for 30 minutes. While the rice is soaking, please move on to the next step..','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":30,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d445b84eb5c1cc4e90776','5e4fc1a28bc0fbeacf45f178',2,'P2: Cook Rice & Prep Ingredients','Next, to cook the rice, boil 3 cups of water in a deep bottom pan. Add in half a teaspoon of salt followed by the soaked rice and stir it well. Then, boil the rice over medium flame for 7-8 minutes until it is 3/4th cooked. While the rice is simmering, wash and slice 3/4 cup of mushrooms. Peel and finely chop 1 tsp of garlic, wash and finely chop 2 green chilies, and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and chop 1/4 cup of green capsicum.  After simmering the rice, carefully drain any excess water from the rice and set it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d447c77c5bbfa41905ed1','5e4fc1a28bc0fbeacf45f178',3,'M1: Cook Vegetables','For mushroom fried rice, heat 1.5 tbsp of oil in a pan on medium flame. To this add 1 tsp of chopped garlic, 2 chopped green chilies, 1/4 cup of chopped onions for 2-3 mins. Once the onions are slightly translucent add 1/4 cup of chopped capsicum saute this for 1 min and then add 3/4 cup of sliced mushroom. Saute this for 3 mins and then season with 1/2 tsp of salt, 1/2 tsp of pepper, and mix well.','cook_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d44b377c5bbfa41905ed2','5e4fc1a28bc0fbeacf45f178',4,'M2: Add Sauces and Rice','Next, add 2 tsp of vinegar, 2 tsp of soy sauce, 2 tbsp of schezwan sauce, mix this until everything is combined well. To this, add 1 cup of cooked basmati rice and gently mix. Once everything is mixed well, garnish the dish with 2 tbsp of chopped spring onions and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e9d455e4590a02787790537','5e4faf4795b6c57e91021785',1,'P1: Make Idli','To make Podi Idli, you will need 4 cooked idlis, if you have any leftover idlis you can use them or you can start by making 4 idlis. Begin by coating the molds with oil and then pour in 1/4 cup of idli batter. Allow the idlis to steam for 10 mins. Let them cool down before you take them out of the molds. While the idlis are steaming move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d455f84eb5c1cc4e90777','5e4faf4795b6c57e91021785',2,'P2: Make Gunpowder (Milagai Podi) (optional)','To make gunpowder, in a pan dry roast 1 tbsp of sesame seeds for 2 mins and then transfer it to a blending jar. Next, 1.5 tbsp of sesame oil and then roast 8 dry red chllies until they begin to puff up. To this add 7 curry leaves, saute this for 1 min and then transfer into the blending jar. In the same pan add 1 tbsp of sesame oil and then 2 tbsp of chana dal, 2 tbsp of urad dal and saute until golden on low flame. Then tansfer this to the blending jar. Add 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder, 1/4 tsp of hing, and 1 tsp of salt, and blend everything together until it forms a coarse powder.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d461784eb5c1cc4e90778','5e4faf4795b6c57e91021785',3,'M1: Make Podi Idli','For Podi Idli, heat 2 tsp of ghee in a pan for a few seconds. Next, add the 4 cooked idlis to the pan, add 1 tbsp of the prepared gun powder on top of the idlis and mix them well. Cook this for 1 min on the pan and take them off to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d47f977c5bbfa41905ed3','5e2e72e6057fd3f6fc80ef39',1,'P1: Prep the ingredients','For Dal Khichdi, rinse half a cup of yellow moong dal well with water. Next, rinse half a cup of rice well with water and set it aside. Peel, wash and finely chop half a cup of onions. Wash and finely chop half a cup of tomatoes. Wash, peel and finely chop a half-inch piece of ginger. Wash and finely chop 1 nos green chili. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Next, in a bowl, add half a cup of curd and whisk it until smooth.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d482877c5bbfa41905ed4','5e2e72e6057fd3f6fc80ef39',2,'M1: Fry the onions','To make the Dal Khichdi, heat a tablespoon of ghee in a pressure cooker over medium flame for a minute. Next, temper it with half a teaspoon of cumin seeds and 1/4 teaspoon of hing. Add a 1/2-inch piece of chopped ginger and 1 nos chopped green chili followed by half a cup of chopped onions. Saute and fry the onions over medium flame for 3-4 minutes until it turns slightly translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e9d48484590a02787790538','5e2e72e6057fd3f6fc80ef39',3,'M2: Cook the masala','After frying the onions, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, 1/4 teaspoon of black pepper powder and half a teaspoon of salt. Mix it well. Next, add half a cup of chopped tomatoes and mix it well with the masala. Saute and cook the tomatoes over medium flame for 4-5 minutes, until it turns tender. Then, fry the masala for 1-2 minutes, until oil separates.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d48694590a02787790539','5e2e72e6057fd3f6fc80ef39',4,'M3: Pressure cook the khichdi','As the oil separates from the masala, add half a cup of rinsed rice along with half a cup of rinsed moong dal and mix it well. Next, add 3 cups of water into it and stir well. Then, cover it with a lid and pressure cook it on high flame until 2 whistles. After that, reduce to low flame and continue to cook it for another 8 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. After the cooker cools down, remove the lid and take it out into a serving bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d48ef84eb5c1cc4e90779','5e2e7bf8057fd3f6fc80ef3c',1,'AP1: Soak Black chickpeas & moong beans','For the Kala Chana Salad, wash and soak 3/4 cup of black chana in 2 cups of water for 8-10 hours. Next, in another bowl, soak 1/2 cup of green moong beans in 2 cups of water for 8-10 hours. While the black chana and moong beans are soaking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":600,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d492377c5bbfa41905ed5','5e2e7bf8057fd3f6fc80ef3c',2,'AP2: Sprout the black chickpeas & moong beans','To make the sprouts for the Kala Chana Salad, take a bowl and place a damp muslin cloth over it. Then, add the soaked chana and tie it into a tight bundle and set it aside for another 10 hours. Make sure to wet the muslin cloth with water from time to time, as the moisture is important for the chana to sprout. Similarly, to make moong sprouts, place a damp muslin cloth over a bowl and add the soaked moong beans in it. Then, tie a knot to make it a tight bundle. Set it aside for 10 hours. Make sure to sprinkle some water over the bundle to keep it moist. While the black chana and moong beans are resting, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":600,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d495477c5bbfa41905ed6','5e2e7bf8057fd3f6fc80ef3c',3,'P1: Prep the ingredients','For the Kala Chana Salad, wash, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Wash and finely chop 2 nos green chilies. Wash, peel and finely chop 1.5 tablespoons of raw mango. Cut 3/4 cup of paneer into 1-inch cubes.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9d497b4590a0278779053b','5e2e7bf8057fd3f6fc80ef3c',4,'P2: Make roasted cumin powder','Next, finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash and cut a lemon into halves and squeeze 2 teaspoons of lime juice. Next, to make the roasted cumin powder, heat a pan on a medium flame for a minute. Then, add 1.5 teaspoons of cumin seeds to it. Dry roast it on medium-low flame for 2-3 minutes, till it turns aromatic. Then, transfer the roasted cumin seeds to a blender jar and grind it into a coarse powder.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d49b084eb5c1cc4e9077c','5e2e7bf8057fd3f6fc80ef3c',5,'M1: Add the sprouts to a bowl with vegetables','To make the Kala Chana Salad, in a large mixing bowl, add black chana sprouts and moong sprouts. Next, add 3/4 cup of cubed paneer, 1/4 cup of chopped onions, 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes and 2 teaspoons of chopped coriander leaves. Next, add 1.5 tablespoons of roasted peanuts, followed by a tablespoon of chopped raw mango.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d49da4590a0278779053c','5e2e7bf8057fd3f6fc80ef3c',6,'M2: Combine the salad. Season & serve','Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of black salt, 1 teaspoon of prepared roasted cumin powder, and 2 nos chopped green chilies along with 1/4 teaspoon of black pepper powder. Lastly, add 1/4 teaspoon of chat masala and 2 teaspoons of lime juice. Mix the salad well and garnish with 1 teaspoon of chopped coriander leaves. Finish the garnish with 2 teaspoons of chopped raw mangoes and 2 teaspoons of roasted peanuts and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d4a0a4590a0278779053d','5e4fa65e4874a44a24b1f844',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','To make Vegetable Stir-Fry, first, wash and chop 1/4 cup of broccoli into small florets. Wash and slice 3 baby corns and 1/4 cup of carrots. Wash and chop 6 beans into 1-inch pieces. Wash and roughly dice 1/4 cup of green capsicum, 1/4 cup of yellow capsicum, and 1/4 cup of red capsicum.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d4a2384eb5c1cc4e9077d','5e4fa65e4874a44a24b1f844',2,'P2: Prep Ingredients','Next, wash and roughly dice 1/4 cup of cabbage. Peel and chop 1/4 cup of onions into petals. Wash and roughly chop 3 tbsp of spring onions. Peel and finely chop 2 tsp of garlic. Wash, peel, and finely chop 1/2 inch piece of ginger. Wash and finely chop 1 green chilli. Squeeze 1 tbsp of lime juice.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9d4a504590a0278779053e','5e2e8cf4057fd3f6fc80ef45',1,'P1: Rinse & soak the horse grams','To make Horse gram dal, first, wash 1 cup of horse gram and then soak it in 1 cup of water for 30 mins. While the dal is soaking, wash 8 curry leaves, grate half a cup of coconut, peel 5 shallots, and peel 2 cloves of garlic.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":30,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d4a7584eb5c1cc4e9077e','5e2e8cf4057fd3f6fc80ef45',2,'M1: Pressure cook the soaked dal','For Horse gram dal, add 1 cup of soaked dal into a pressure cooker along with 2.5 cups of water, 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder, 1/2 tsp of red chili powder, 1/2 tsp of salt, and 4 curry leaves. Give it a stir and cook on high flame for 1 whistle and then on low flame for 8 mins. Once this is done, allow the pressure to release naturally before you open the cooker.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d4a864590a0278779053f','5e4fa65e4874a44a24b1f844',3,'P3: Blanch Vegetables','Next, blanch 1/4 cup of broccoli florets, 3 sliced baby corn, 6 chopped beans, and 1/4 cup of sliced carrots in hot water along with 1 tsp of salt for 2 mins. After this, transfer the vegetables into a cold bath to stop them from cooking further. In another pan, dry roast 1 tbsp of white sesame seeds for 1 min, set this aside and move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d4aa577c5bbfa41905ed7','5e2e8cf4057fd3f6fc80ef45',3,'M2: Simmer the dal with coconut paste','Next, in a blending jar add 1/2 cup of coconut, 5 shallots, 2 cloves of garlic, 1/4 tsp of cumin seeds, and blend into a coarse paste. Once the dal is cooked, open the cooker, and pour in the prepare coconut paste. Mix well and add 1/4 cup of water. Cook the dal on medium flame for 5 mins. Once this is done, garnish with 4 curry leaves and 1 tbsp of coconut oil. The dish is ready to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e9d4af54590a02787790540','5e4fa65e4874a44a24b1f844',4,'M1: Cooking','To make Vegetable Stir-Fry, heat 1 tbsp of sesame oil in a pan on medium flame. Once the oil is warm, add 2 tsp of chopped garlic and let this cook for a few seconds and then add 1/2 inch of chopped ginger, 1 chopped green chilli, and 1/4 cup of onion petals. Saute this for 2-3 min until the onions are translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e9d4b0e4590a02787790541','5e4fa65e4874a44a24b1f844',5,'M2: Cook Vegetables','Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped green, red, and yellow capsicum followed by 1/4 cup of chopped cabbage. Saute this for 2 mins and then add the blanched vegetables. Mix the vegetables well and then add 1/2 tsp of white pepper powder, 2 tsp of soy sauce, and 1/2 tsp of salt. Saute this for 2-3 mins.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d4b2b84eb5c1cc4e9077f','5e2fed154f28558c29df64c0',1,'P1: Grate paneer & prep the ingredients','For Paneer Sandwich, fist, In a pan boil 3/4 cups of water and then add 1/4 cup of sweet corn kernels. Let them boil for 5 mins and then drain the water. Next, grate 1 cup of paneer, peel and grate 1/4 cup of carrot, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of green capsicum, wash and chop 1/4 cup of coriander leaves, wash and roughly chop 1/4 cup of mint leaves, peel 1/2 inch of ginger, peel 2 cloves of garlic, and squeeze 1 tbsp of lime juice. Set them aside and move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":11,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d4b304590a02787790542','5e4fa65e4874a44a24b1f844',6,'M3: Final Touches','Next, add 1 tsp of green chilli sauce, 1 tbsp of lime juice, and mix this well. Then, add 3 tbsp of chopped spring onion greens and saute everything for 2 mins. Turn off the flame, transfer the vegetables to a serving plate and garnish with 1 tbsp of sesame seeds.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d4b5977c5bbfa41905ed8','5e2fed154f28558c29df64c0',2,'P2: Prepare the sandwich filling','Next, make the sandwich filling, in a large bowl add 1 cup of grated paneer, 2 tbsp of grated carrot, 1/4 cup of chopped capsicum, 2 tbsp of blanched sweet corn, 1 tbsp of coriander leaves, 1/4 tsp of red chili powder, 3/4 tsp of cumin powder, 1/4 tsp of salt, 2 tbsp of ketchup, and mix well. Once the ingredients are combined well, set them aside and move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d4b9084eb5c1cc4e90780','5e2fed154f28558c29df64c0',3,'P3: Make green chutney','Next, make green chutney, in a blending jar add 1/4 cup of mint leaves, 1/4 cup of coriander leaves, 2 cloves of garlic, 1/2 inch of ginger, 2 tbsp of roasted grams, 2 green chilies, 1/2 tsp of chaat masala, 1/2 tsp of salt, 1/2 tsp of cumin powder, 1/2 tsp of sugar, 1/4 tsp of hing, 1 tbsp of lemon juice, and blend into a smooth chutney. Once the chutney is ready, set it aside and move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9d4bba84eb5c1cc4e90781','5e2fed154f28558c29df64c0',4,'M1: Make the sandwich','To make a Paneer sandwich, on one slice of bread spread 1/2 tsp of the prepared green chutney and then 2 tbsp of the prepare paneer mixture. Spread another 1/2 tsp of chutney on the second slice of bread and close this sandwich. Turn on your sandwich maker and make a second sandwich following the same process. Put 1/2 tsp of butter on each side of the sandwich maker and then place the 2 prepared sandwiches ontop. Next, spread 1/2 tsp of butter on top of the sandwich, close the sandwich maker and grill the sandwiches for 1 min. Once they have a nice golden brown color on them take them out of the sandwich maker and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d4bd177c5bbfa41905ed9','5e4fbf174874a44a24b1f846',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Lemon Coriander Soup, wash, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Peel and finely chop 1 teaspoon of garlic. Wash, peel and finely chop 1/2 inch piece of ginger. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of cabbage.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d4bd284eb5c1cc4e90782','5e4fbf174874a44a24b1f846',2,'P2: Prep Ingredients','Next, wash a bunch of coriander leaves and remove the leaves from the stems. Then, roughly chop 1/4 cup of coriander stems. To make the cornflour slurry, in a bowl, add 1 teaspoon of cornflour and 1/4 cup of water. Mix the slurry well to avoid any lumps. Squeeze 1 tablespoon of lime juice.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d4c1c77c5bbfa41905eda','5e4fbf174874a44a24b1f846',3,'M1: Cook Spices and Onions','To make the Lemon Coriander Soup, heat 1 tablespoon of cooking oil in a deep bottom pan on a medium flame for a minute. Add 1 teaspoon of chopped garlic, 1/2 inch piece of chopped ginger and saute it for a minute on medium-high flame. Next, add 1/4 cup of finely chopped onions and saute it for 2-3 minutes, till the onions turn slightly translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d4c6284eb5c1cc4e90783','5e311d3b057fd3f6fc80ef56',1,'P1: Prep the pointed gourds','For Bharwa Parwal, wash 7 nos pointed gourds well with water. Then, cut the edges and gently scrape the skin off. Next, scoop out the seeds and pulp from within using the back of the spoon to make it hollow. Keep the scooped out portion in a bowl to be further used for the stuffing. Next, wash, peel and finely chop 1/2 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1/2 cup of tomatoes. Wash and finely chop 2 nos green chilies. Grate 1/2 cup of coconut using a grater. Wash and finely chop 1.5 tablespoons of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9d4c6f4590a02787790543','5e4fbf174874a44a24b1f846',4,'M2: Cook Vegetables','After frying the onions, add 1/4 cup of chopped cabbage and stir fry it for 1-2 minutes on high flame. Then, add 1.5 cups of water along with 1/4 cup of chopped coriander stems and stir well. Cover it with a lid and simmer the soup for 10 minutes on medium-low flame.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e9d4c9d77c5bbfa41905edb','5e4fbf174874a44a24b1f846',5,'M3: Continue Cooking to make Soup','After simmering the soup, take off the lid and remove all the coriander stems from the soup. Next, add 1/2 teaspoon of black pepper powder, 1/4 teaspoon of salt and 1.5 tablespoons of chopped coriander leaves. Mix it well and bring the soup to a boil on medium-high flame. Next, add 1 tablespoon of lime juice to the soup along with the prepared cornflour slurry and allow it to boil for another 1-2 minutes. Then, turn off the flame, garnish the soup with 1 teaspoon of chopped coriander leaves and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d4ca584eb5c1cc4e90784','5e311d3b057fd3f6fc80ef56',2,'P2: Stir-fry the pointed gourds','To prepare the pointed gourds for Bharwa Parwal, in a large mixing bowl, add the hollowed pointed gourds. Add 1/4 teaspoon of salt and 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder and mix it well. Next, heat 2 tablespoons of mustard oil in a pan on medium flame for a minute. Add the pointed gourds and fry it on medium-high flame for 4-5 minutes, till it turns slightly tender. Then, turn off the flame and carefully take it out on a kitchen towel to remove the extra oil.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d4cc94590a02787790544','5e311d3b057fd3f6fc80ef56',3,'P3: Make the mustard paste','To make the mustard paste for Bharwa Parwal, in a mixing bowl, add 2 tablespoons of mustard powder, 1/4 teaspoon of salt, and 2 nos chopped green chilies. Next, add 1 tablespoon of mustard oil along with 2 tablespoons of water and mix it well.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d4cf74590a02787790545','5e311d3b057fd3f6fc80ef56',4,'M1: Make the stuffing','To make the stuffing for Bharwa Parwal, heat 1 tablespoon of mustard oil in a pan on medium flame for a minute. Add the scooped-out pulp of pointed gourds and 1/2 cup of grated coconut. Saute it on medium flame for 4-5 minutes, till it turns slightly moist. Then, add the prepared mustard paste and 1/4 teaspoon of salt along with 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and mix it well. Saute and cook it on medium flame for another 2-3 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and take it out in a bowl.','cook_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e9d4d234590a02787790546','5e311d3b057fd3f6fc80ef56',5,'M2: Stuff the pointed gourds','To stuff the pointed gourds for Bharwa Parwal, take a fried pointed gourd and stuff it with 1 tablespoon of the prepared mixture. Gently press the stuffing inside, using fingers. Similarly, stuff the remaining fried pointed gourds with the prepared mixture.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d4d4977c5bbfa41905edc','5e311d3b057fd3f6fc80ef56',6,'M3: Prepare the gravy','To make the semi-gravy for Bharwa Parwal, heat 1 tablespoon of ghee in a pan on medium flame for a minute. Add 1/2 cup of chopped onions and fry it on medium flame for 2-3 minutes, till it turns slightly translucent. After frying the onions, add 1 teaspoon of ginger paste and 1 teaspoon of garlic paste and mix it well. Saute it on medium flame for 1-2 minutes, till the garlic turns aromatic.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d4d6f77c5bbfa41905edd','5e311d3b057fd3f6fc80ef56',7,'M4: Simmer the gravy','After frying the ginger-garlic paste for Bharwa Parwal, add 1 teaspoon of red chili powder, 1/2 teaspoon of turmeric powder and 1/2 teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Next, add 1/2 cup of chopped tomatoes. Saute and cook the tomatoes on medium-low flame for 4-5 minutes, till it turns tender. Keep stirring the tomatoes while cooking, to prevent it from sticking to the bottom of the pan. After cooking the tomatoes, add 1/4 cup of water and simmer it for 3 minutes. While the gravy is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e9d4dab4590a02787790547','5e311d3b057fd3f6fc80ef56',8,'M5: Simmer the stuffed gourds. Garnish & serve','After simmering the gravy for Bharwa Parwal, carefully add the stuffed pointed gourds one by one. Then, cover it with a lid and cook it on low flame for 5-6 minutes. After simmering the pointed gourds, take off the lid and turn off the flame. Garnish it with 2 teaspoons of chopped coriander leaves and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e9d4e1884eb5c1cc4e90785','5e4fa4a04874a44a24b1f843',1,'P1: Cook Noodles','To boil the noodles- Take 200 grams of egg noodles in a deep bottom pan. Add 2.5 cups of water along with 1 teaspoon salt and 1 teaspoon oil into it and bring it to a boil on high flame. It has come to boil, reduce the flame and continue to cook the noodles on medium-low flame for 7-8 minutes. Keep stirring in between to avoid the noodles from clumping. Meanwhile, take 5 nos Kashmiri red chilies and deseed them. Soak the Kashmiri red chilies in 1/4 cup of water and set aside for 10 minutes. While the noodles are boiling, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":10,"flame":3}'),
('5e9d4e504590a02787790548','5e4fa4a04874a44a24b1f843',2,'P2: Roasting Sesame and Peanuts','For the sesame peanut noodles- In a pan take 2 teaspoon sesame seeds and dry roast them without adding any oil on low flame for 1 min. Keep stirring them until the flavor comes out. After roasting them for 1-2 minutes, turn off the heat and take them out in a bowl and set aside. In the same pan, take 2 tablespoon peanuts and dry roast them on a medium flame for 2-3 minutes until they turn slightly brown. Turn off the heat and take them out in a bowl.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d4e8277c5bbfa41905ede','5e4fa4a04874a44a24b1f843',3,'P3: Make Chilli Paste','After boiling the noodles for 10 minutes, check if they are completely cooked, Once cooked, turn off the heat and drain off the excess water from the noodles and wash them with normal water or they will continue to cook further. Keep the noodles aside. To make the red chili paste, after soaking the red chilies in water for 10 minutes, take them out of the water, put them in a blender jar and blend smoothly to make a paste.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d4eb784eb5c1cc4e90786','5e4fa4a04874a44a24b1f843',4,'M1: Make Sesame Noodles','To make sesame peanut noodles- In a pan, heat 1 teaspoon peanut butter on medium flame. Add 1 tablespoon of sesame oil into the butter and mix them well. Then add 2 teaspoons of prepared Kashmiri red chili paste, 1 teaspoon soy sauce, 1 teaspoon vinegar into this and saute them together on medium-high flame for 1 minute. Next, add boiled noodles into the sauce and combine the noodles well with the sauce. Stir fry the noodles gently on high flame for 2 minutes with light hands. After 2 minutes, add 2 teaspoon roasted sesame seeds and 2 teaspoon roasted peanuts on top of the noodles and give it a gentle toss. Garnish the noodles with 2 tablespoons of finely chopped spring onion greens and Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d4f4784eb5c1cc4e90788','5e312fb44f28558c29df64ca',1,'P1: Peel the green peas','For Green Peas Fry, peel 1.5 cups of green peas. Wash and roughly chop 1 tbsp of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d4f8b4590a0278779054a','5e312fb44f28558c29df64ca',2,'M1: Fry the green peas & simmer. Garnish & serve','For Green Peas Fry, heat 1 tbsp of cooking oil on a pan for 1 min and then add 1/4 tsp of cumin seeds, 1/4 tsp of mustard seeds, 1/4 tsp of hing. Let this splutter for a few seconds, then add 1.5 cups of green peas, and saute for 2 mins. Next, add 1/4 tsp of salt, 1/2 tsp of red chili powder, 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder, 1/4 tsp of coriander powder, 1/4 tsp of cumin powder, 1/4 tsp of garam masala, and mix well. Then, add 1/4 cup of water, cover the pan with a lid, and simmer for 15 mins. Once this is done, garnish the sabzi with 1 tsp of lime juice and 1 tbsp of coriander leaves. The dish is ready to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e9d50174590a0278779054b','5e4f9f364874a44a24b1f842',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','To make Garlic Mushrooms, first, wash 2 cups of button mushrooms and then finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Next, peel and finely chop 2 tsp of garlic. Wash and finely chop 1/2 tsp of fresh thyme and 1 tbsp of fresh parsley.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d503584eb5c1cc4e9078b','5e4f9f364874a44a24b1f842',2,'M1: Cook Mushrooms','For Garlic Mushrooms, heat 1.5 tbsp of butter in medium-high flame for 1 min. Next, add 1/4 cup of onions and saute them for 2-3 mins. Once they are slightly translucent add 2 cups of button mushrooms and saute them for 2-3 mins. This next step is optional - add 1 tbsp of white wine to the pan.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d505d84eb5c1cc4e9078c','5e4f9f364874a44a24b1f842',3,'M2: Final Touches','Next, add 1/2 tsp of thyme and 1 tbsp of parsley and saute this for 1 min. To this, add 2 tsp of garlic and then season with 1/2 tsp of salt and 1/2 tsp of pepper. Saute this for 2 mins and then turn off the flame and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d506b4590a0278779054c','5e3137ea057fd3f6fc80ef5b',1,'P1: Soak the rice & prep the ingredients','To make Aloo Matar Tehri, wash 1 cup of basmati rice and soak it in 1.5 cups of water for 30 mins. While the rice is soaking, peel and thinly slice 1/4 cup of onions, peel and dice 1/2 cup of potatoes, wash and chop 1 green chili, and wash and roughly chop 1 tbsp of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":30,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d50a577c5bbfa41905ee2','5e3137ea057fd3f6fc80ef5b',2,'M1: Fry the onions & potatoes','For Aloo Matar Tehri, heat 2 tbsp of ghee in a pan for 1 min and then add 1-inch of cinnamon, 3 cloves, 2 green cardamoms, 1 tsp of cumin seeds, and let this splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 1/4 cup of sliced onions, 1 green chili, 1 tsp of ginger garlic paste, and saute for 2-3 mins. Once the onions have slightly browned, add 1/2 cup of chopped potatoes, 1 tsp coriander powder, 1/2 tsp red chili powder, 1 tsp turmeric powder, 1/4 tsp garam masala, and mix well.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e9d50c177c5bbfa41905ee3','5e4f9d0a4874a44a24b1f841',1,'Prep Ingredients','To make Scrambled Eggs, wash and roughly chop 1 tbsp of spring onion greens and move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d50e44590a0278779054d','5e3137ea057fd3f6fc80ef5b',3,'M2: Add the green peas & Simmer the rice','Next, add 1/4 cup of green peas, 1/2 tsp salt, 2 tsp of lime juice, 2 cups of water, and mix well. COver the pan with a lid and let the water come to a boil. Once the water is boiling, add 1 cup of soaked rice, combine all the ingredients, cover it once more, and let the tehri cook for 15-20 mins. Once the rice is cooked, put it in a serving dish, and enjoy.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d50ec84eb5c1cc4e9078d','5e4f9d0a4874a44a24b1f841',2,'M1: Cook Eggs','To make Scrambled Eggs, crack 4 eggs into a mixing bowl and whisk them until combined completely. Season the eggs with 1/4 tsp of salt and 1/4 tsp of pepper and set this aside. Next, heat 2 tbsp of butter in on medium-high flame for 1 min. Next, pour in the eggs and let that cook for 1 min. Once the edges of the egg begin to cook, using a spatula push the eggs towards the center from the outside in. When they look like they are almost ready, add another 1/2 tbsp of butter to the pan. Let this cook for 1 min and then take the eggs off the heat and onto a plate. Next, garnish the eggs with 1 tbsp of spring onion and grate 1 tbsp of parmesan cheese directly onto the eggs and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d51544590a0278779054e','5e314d59985ffca18ae8fb4a',1,'P1: Blanch the spinach leaves & puree','To make Aloo Palak, first, wash 1 cup of spinach leaves and then in a pot boil 2 cups of water. Blanch the spinach leaves in the hot water for 1 -2 mins. Then, transfer them to an ice bath to prevent further cooking. Next, squeeze out any excess water and blend the spinach leaves into a smooth puree. Once this is complete set the puree aside and move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d517c4590a0278779054f','5e314d59985ffca18ae8fb4a',2,'P2: Chop & prep the ingredients','Next, wash and quarter 3/4 cup of baby potatoes. Wash and chop 2 green chilies. Peel and finely chop 1/2 cup of onions. Peel and finely chop 1 inch of ginger. Peel and finely chop 1 tsp of garlic. wash and finely chop 1/2 cup of tomatoes.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9d51ad4590a02787790550','5e314d59985ffca18ae8fb4a',3,'M1: Simmer the potatoes with gravy','For Aloo Palak, in a pan heat 2 tsp of cooking oil on a medium flame for 1 min. Next, add 1 tsp of cumin seeds, 2 chopped green chilies, 1/2 cup of chopped onion, 1 inch of chopped ginger, 1 tsp of chopped garlic, and saute for 2-3 mins. Once the onions are translucent, add 1/2 cup of chopped tomatoes and saute for 1 min. Next, add 3/4 cup of quartered baby potatoes and mix well. Then, add 1/2 tsp of salt, mix well, cover the pan with a lid and cook for 2-3 mins.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e9d51dc84eb5c1cc4e9078e','5e314d59985ffca18ae8fb4a',4,'M2: Add the spinach puree & simmer the curry','Next, take the lid off and then add 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder, 1/2 tsp of red chili powder, 1/2 tsp of cumin powder, 1/2 tsp of coriander powder, 1/4 tsp of garam masala, and mix well. To this, add the prepare spinach puree along with 1/4 cup of water and mix well. Cover the pan with a lid and cook for 4-5 mins.  After 5 mins, take off the lid, give the curry a stir and pour it into a serving dish. Enjoy.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e9d51fa4590a02787790551','5e3cf790985ffca18ae8fbe7',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Aloo Parwal, wash 6-7 nos pointed gourds well with water. Then, slice off the ends and cut it vertically into halves, remove the seeds and finely slice 1 cup of pointed gourds into thin juliennes. Next, wash, peel and finely slice 1/2 a cup of potatoes into thin wedges. Wash, peel and finely slice 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and slit 2 nos green chilies. Peel, wash and finely chop 1 teaspoon of garlic.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d52434590a02787790552','5e3cf790985ffca18ae8fbe7',2,'M1: Cook Spices and Onions','To make Aloo Parwal, heat 2 tablespoons of cooking oil in a pan on a medium flame for a minute. Add 1 teaspoon of cumin seeds and 2 nos slit green chilies followed by a teaspoon of chopped garlic. Saute and fry the garlic on a medium flame for a minute. Next, add 1/4 cup of sliced onions and fry it on a medium flame for 3-4 minutes until it turns slightly golden.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d52b677c5bbfa41905ee4','5e3cf790985ffca18ae8fbe7',3,'M2: Cook Vegetable','After frying the onions, add 1/2 cup of sliced potato wedges and fry it on a medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Then, add 1 cup of the sliced pointed gourd and mix it well. Stir and fry the vegetables on a medium flame for 2-3 minutes. Next, add a quarter teaspoon of turmeric powder, half a teaspoon of red chili powder and half a teaspoon of salt. Mix it well and cover it with a lid. Reduce the flame to low and simmer the vegetables for 8-10 minutes. Keep stirring the vegetables occasionally to prevent it from sticking to the bottom of the pan. While it is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('5e9d52ed77c5bbfa41905ee5','5e3cf790985ffca18ae8fbe7',4,'M3: Final Touches','After simmering the Aloo Parwal, take off the lid and give it a stir. Again cover it with a lid and cook it on a medium flame for 2 minutes. Next, remove the lid and fry the vegetables on high flame for a minute until it turns tender and crisp. Then, turn off the flame and take it out onto a plate and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d530084eb5c1cc4e90790','5e31514d985ffca18ae8fb4f',1,'P1: Pressure cook the rice','To make Pudina Rice, first, wash 1 cup of sona-masuri and then cook it in a pressure cooker with 2 cups of water on high flame for 1 whistle and then on low flame for 8 mins. Once this is complete, allow the cooker to release pressure naturally before you open it. While the rice is cooking, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d532a77c5bbfa41905ee6','5e31514d985ffca18ae8fb4f',2,'P2: Chop & prep the ingredients','Next, peel and roughly chop 1/2 inch of ginger. Peel 4 cloves of garlic. Peel and chop 5 shallots. Wash and slit 2 green chilies. Wash and roughly chop 1 cup of mint leaves. Wash 7 curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d538e77c5bbfa41905ee7','5e31514d985ffca18ae8fb4f',3,'M1: Make the mint masala paste','For pudine rice, heat 1 tbsp of cooking oil in a pan for 1 min. Next, add 4 cloves of garlic, 1/2 inch of ginger, and saute for 1 min. Then, add 5 chopped shallots and 2 slit green chilies, saute for 2-3 mins. Once the onions are translucent, add 1 cup of mint leaves and saute them for 2-3 mins. Once the mint leaves have wilted, allow the mixture to cool before you blend it into a smooth paste along with 2 tbsp of water.','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d53c34590a02787790555','5e31514d985ffca18ae8fb4f',4,'M2: Cook the rice with the mint masala paste. Garnish & serve','Next, on the same pan, heat 1/2 tbsp of oil and then add 1/2 tsp of mustard seeds, 1/2 tsp of urad dal, and  1/2 tsp of chana dal, let this splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 5 cashew nuts, 1 dry red chili, 7 curry leaves, and saute for 1 min. Once the cashews are golden add the prepare mint leaf paste and mix well. Then, add 1/2 tsp of salt and saute the paste for 2 mins. After that, add 1 tsp of ghee, mix well, and then add 1 cup of cooked rice. Gently mix the rice and mint leaf paste together. Once everything is mixed well turn off the flame and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e9d54304590a02787790556','5e3154e2985ffca18ae8fb52',1,'AP1: Soak the peanuts','For Boiled Peanut Salad, wash and soak 3/4 cup of peanuts in 2 cups of water and set it aside for 10 hours. While the peanuts are soaking, please move the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":600,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d546177c5bbfa41905ee8','5e3154e2985ffca18ae8fb52',2,'P1: Boil the peanuts','To boil the peanuts for the Boiled Peanut Salad, add soaked peanuts to a pressure cooker with 2 cups of water and 1/4 teaspoon of salt. Cover it with a lid and pressure cook it on high flame for 3 whistles. After 3 whistles, reduce it to sim and continue to cook for another 8 minutes. Then turn off the flame, set the pressure cooker aside and let the pressure from the cooker release naturally. While the peanuts are boiling, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":18,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d548b84eb5c1cc4e90792','5e3154e2985ffca18ae8fb52',3,'P2: Chop & prep the ingredients','For Boiled Peanut Salad, wash, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onion. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Wash, peel and chop 1/4 cup of cucumber. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of carrot. Wash, peel and finely chop 2 tablespoons of raw mango. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Squeeze 1 tablespoon of lime juice.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d54c284eb5c1cc4e90793','5e3154e2985ffca18ae8fb52',4,'M1: Combine the vegetables with peanuts. Season the salad & garnish','To make Boiled Peanut Salad, add the boiled peanuts in a large mixing bowl. Add 1/4 cup of chopped onions, 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes, 2 tablespoons of chopped raw mango and 2 tablespoons of chopped carrot to it. Next, add 1/2 teaspoon of black pepper powder, 1/4 teaspoon of red chili powder and 1/4 teaspoon of salt to the salad and mix it well. Add 1 tablespoon of lemon juice to it and toss it well. Garnish it with 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d559f84eb5c1cc4e90794','5e3157a2057fd3f6fc80ef62',1,'AP1: Soak the moong dal','For Moong Dal Chilla, add 1 cup of yellow moong dal in a large bowl and soak it in 2 cups of water for 5 hours. While the dal is soaking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":180,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9d55d484eb5c1cc4e90795','5e3157a2057fd3f6fc80ef62',2,'P1: Blend the soaked dal to make a paste','For Moong Dal Chilla, first, wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves. Wash and peel a 1-inch piece of ginger. Wash and slit 1 nos green chili. Next, add the soaked moong dal to a blender jar, along with a slit green chili, 1-inch piece of ginger and a teaspoon of cumin seeds. Cover the jar with a lid and blend it well into a smooth paste.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d55f04590a02787790557','5e3157a2057fd3f6fc80ef62',3,'P2: Prepare the batter','To prepare the batter for Moong Dal Chilla, transfer the prepared moong dal paste to a large mixing bowl. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, 2 tablespoons of chopped coriander leaves and 1/4 teaspoon of hing. Add half a teaspoon of salt followed by 3 tablespoons of water and mix it well.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d561277c5bbfa41905ee9','5e3157a2057fd3f6fc80ef62',4,'M1: Make the Dal Chillas','To make the Besan Chilla, pour a ladle full of the prepared moong dal batter over the hot tawa and gently spread it into a slightly thick 7-inch circle. Add half a teaspoon of oil and cover it with a lid. Cook the chilla over medium flame for a minute. Then, take off the lid and carefully flip it and cook the other side for another 1-2 minutes. As it turns slightly golden, gently fold it and take it out onto a plate. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d567b84eb5c1cc4e90796','5e315a41057fd3f6fc80ef63',1,'P1: Shred the cabbage','For Cabbage Chutney, wash and finely chop 1 cup of cabbage. Wash 7 nos curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d56a54590a02787790558','5e315a41057fd3f6fc80ef63',2,'M1: Simmer & prepare the cabbage mixture','To make the Cabbage Chutney, heat 1 teaspoon of cooking in a kadai over medium flame for a minute. Add 1 tablespoon of urad dal along with 1/4 teaspoon of hing and saute it on low flame until it turns slightly golden. Next, add 1 cup of chopped cabbage and fry it over medium-low flame for 4-5 minutes. Add 1 nos dry red chili and saute it for a minute. Then, turn off the flame and allow this mixture to cool down completely. While the mixture is cooling down please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('5e9d56d94590a02787790559','5e315a41057fd3f6fc80ef63',3,'M2: Blend the cabbage mixture & make the chutney','To make the Cabbage Chutney, after the prepared cabbage mixture cools down, transfer it to a blender jar along with a teaspoon of tamarind and 1/4 teaspoon of salt. Add 1/4 cup of water and blend it well into a smooth chutney. Then, take it out into a bowl and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d56fe84eb5c1cc4e90797','5e315a41057fd3f6fc80ef63',4,'M3: Prepare & add the tempering to the chutney','To make the tempering for the Cabbage Chutney, heat 1 teaspoon of cooking oil in a small tempering pan over medium flame for a minute. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of mustard seeds and 7 nos curry leaves. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Then, turn off the flame and add this tempering instantly over the prepared chutney. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d57994590a0278779055a','5e315d6c057fd3f6fc80ef64',1,'P1: Knead & prepare the dough','To make Gehun Bajra Roti, first, peel and finely chop 1 inch of ginger, wash and finely chop 1 green chili, and wash and roughly chop 1 tbsp of coriander leaves. Next, in a large mixing bowl combine 1 cup of bajra flour, 1/2 cup of whole wheat flour, 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder, 1/4 tsp of black pepper powder, 1/2 tsp of salt, 1 inch of chopped ginger, 1 chopped green chilli, 1 tbsp of chopped coriander leaves, and 1 tsp of oil. Once the ingredients are mixed well, gradually add 1/4 cup of water and knead the dough. When your dough has begun to come together add 1 tsp of oil and continue kneading until you have a smooth and soft dough.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d57cf77c5bbfa41905eea','5e315d6c057fd3f6fc80ef64',2,'M1: Divide the dough into dough balls & roll','For gehun bajra roti, make small lemon sized balls from the dough. Take one of these dough balls, flatten it with your palm on a rolling board, and dust it with flour. Next, using a rolling pin roll the dough into a disk shape, allowing it to remain slightly thick. Repeat this process with the remaining dough and move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d57ff84eb5c1cc4e90798','5e315d6c057fd3f6fc80ef64',3,'M2: Make the rotis & serve','Next, heat a tawa on medium flame for 1 min. Then, drizzle 1/2 tbsp of oil on the tawa, then place a roti on top followed by another 1/2 tsp of oil. Let the roti cook on each side for 2-3 mins. Once both sides have browned evenly, take them off the tawa. Repeat this with the remaining raw rotis and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e9d596784eb5c1cc4e9079a','5e3180ee057fd3f6fc80ef67',1,'AP1: Soak the chickpeas','For the Chickpea Salad, soak 3/4 cup of chickpeas in 2 cups of water and set it aside for 8 hours.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":480,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d598b77c5bbfa41905eed','5e3180ee057fd3f6fc80ef67',2,'P1: Pressure cook the chickpeas','Cook the chickpeas in a pressure cooker with salt and 4 cups of water. Cook on high flame for 3 whistles and then cook on low flame for another 8 mins. Once this is done, turn off the flame to let the cooker cool down.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d59b177c5bbfa41905eee','5e3180ee057fd3f6fc80ef67',3,'P2: Chop & prep the ingredients','Finely chop onions, tomatoes, coriander, garlic and dice cucumbers. Squeeze 2 tsp of lime juice.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d59d777c5bbfa41905eef','5e3180ee057fd3f6fc80ef67',4,'M1: Make the salad dressing','In a bowl make the salad dressing, add garlic, lime juice, salt, black pepper, and olive oil. Mix it well','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d5a0877c5bbfa41905ef0','5e3180ee057fd3f6fc80ef67',5,'M2: Combine the salad & dressing. Garnish & serve','In a large mixing bowl, add cucumber, tomatoes, onions, chickpeas and pour in the salad dressing. Toss this together and mix it well. Garnish it with coriander leaves and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9d5c6677c5bbfa41905ef4','5e31856a4f28558c29df64d2',1,'P1: Chop the ingredients & grind the masala','To make Tambdi Bhaji, first, wash and roughly chop 2 cups of red amaranth leaves. Peel and slice 1/2 cup of onion. Peel 2 cloves of garlic. Next, in a blending jar blend 1 tbsp of fried gram dal, 1 tbsp of peanuts, 2 dry red chilies, 2 tsp of dry coconut, 2 cloves of garlic, and 1/2 tsp of salt into a coarse powder.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d5cac84eb5c1cc4e9079e','5e31856a4f28558c29df64d2',2,'M1: Simmer the amaranth leaves','For Tambdi Bhaji, heat 1 tbsp of cooking oil in a pan for 1 min. Next, add 1/4 tsp of cumin seeds, 1/4 tsp of mustard seeds, 1/2 tsp of urad dal, 1/2 tsp of chana dal, 1 dry red chili, and let them splutter for a few seconds. Add curry leaves and 1/4 cup of sliced onions, then saute them for 2-3 mins. Once the onions are translucent, add 2 cups of amaranth leaves, and mix well. Next, cover the pan with a lid and simmer for 5 mins. While it is simmering, please move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d5e2484eb5c1cc4e907a3','5e3187e14f28558c29df64d4',1,'P1: Knead & prepare the dough','To knead the dough for Jowar Roti, first, heat half a cup of water in a pan over medium flame for a minute. As it comes to a boil, turn off the flame and take it out into a cup and set it aside. Next, in a large mixing bowl, add 1 cup of jowar flour. Gradually add half a cup of hot water and mix it well. Knead the flour for 4-5 minutes until it comes together and forms a non-sticky and smooth dough.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d5e5b84eb5c1cc4e907a4','5e3187e14f28558c29df64d4',2,'M1: Divide the dough into dough balls. Roll & cook the rotis','To make Jowar Roti, first, divide the prepared dough into small equal-sized balls. Take a dough ball and gently press it between the palms to flatten it. Next, dust some jowar flour over the rolling surface and place the dough ball over it. Dust some flour over it and roll it into a thin roti while pressing it gently with palms in a circular motion as shown.  Then, carefully place it onto the hot tawa while dusting off the excess flour. Apply some water over it and cook it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. After that, gently flip it and cook the other side for 1-2 minutes. Cook the roti until both sides are evenly browned. After the roti slightly puffs up, remove it from the flame and take it out onto a serving plate. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d5ea984eb5c1cc4e907a5','5e318886985ffca18ae8fb5e',1,'P1: Soak the lentil & chop the spinach leaves','To make Palak and Moong Dal Sabzi, wash and then soak 1/2 cup of yellow moong dal in 1 cup of water for 30 mins. While the dal is soaking, wash and roughly chop 1 cup of spinach leaves. Squeeze 1/4 tsp of lime.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":30,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9d5ee94590a0278779055d','5e318886985ffca18ae8fb5e',2,'M1: Simmer the dal with spinach leaves. Garnish & serve','For Palak and Moong dal sabzi, heat a pan on medium flame and then add 1/2 cup of soaked moong dal along with 1/4 cup of water. Give this a sitr and cook it for 5 mins. After that, add 1 cup of chopped spinach leaves and mix well. Cover the pan with a lid and cook for 2 mins. Next, add 1/4 tsp of salt, 1/2 tsp of red chili powder, 2 tsp oil, and mix well. Cover with the lid and cook for another 2 mins on low flame. Next, garnish with 1/4 tsp of lime juice, mix once more, and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":11,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e9d5f3a77c5bbfa41905ef5','5e33d5c9057fd3f6fc80ef93',1,'AP1: Soak the chickpeas','For Hummus, in a bowl, add half a cup of chickpeas. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of baking soda and soak it in 2 cups of water for 10 hours. While the chickpeas are soaking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":600,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d5f6177c5bbfa41905ef6','5e33d5c9057fd3f6fc80ef93',2,'P1: Bake the chickpeas','To bake the Chickpeas for Hummus, spread half a cup of soaked chickpeas over a baking tray. Sprinkle 1/4 teaspoon of baking soda over it and mix it well. Then, set it in the microwave and allow it to bake at 200°C for 10 minutes. While the chickpeas are baking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d5f8784eb5c1cc4e907a6','5e33d5c9057fd3f6fc80ef93',3,'P2: Prep the ingredients','For Hummus, peel, wash and slice 3 cloves of garlic. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash and cut a lemon into halves. Then, squeeze out 2 teaspoons of lime juice.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d5fba84eb5c1cc4e907a7','5e33d5c9057fd3f6fc80ef93',4,'P3: Blanch the chickpeas','To blanch the Chickpeas for Hummus, take out the baked chickpeas from the microwave. Then, rinse it thoroughly with water to remove the skin. Next, add the rinsed chickpeas to a pan along with 1/4 teaspoon of baking soda. Add 3 cups of water and bring it to a rolling boil. Discard the skin of the chickpeas that come afloat in the water if any. Then, add 2 cloves of sliced garlic and mix it well. Allow the chickpeas to boil on a medium flame for 5-6 minutes until it is cooked through. After that, turn off the flame and drain off the water from it. While the chickpeas are boiling, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":4}'),
('5e9d5fe984eb5c1cc4e907a8','5e33d5c9057fd3f6fc80ef93',5,'M1: Blend the chickpeas with other ingredients & make the hummus','To make the Hummus, in a blender jar, add the blanched chickpeas. Add 2 tablespoons of tahini followed by half a teaspoon of salt and 1/4 teaspoon of cumin powder. Next, add 2 teaspoons of lemon juice and blend it to a smooth paste. Next, add 1 tablespoon of canola oil and 1 tablespoon of olive oil. Add 2 tablespoons of water, if required to get a creamy consistency and blend it well to make a smooth paste. Then, take it out in a bowl. Add 2 tablespoons of tahini and 2 teaspoons of olive oil to the hummus. Garnish it with 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and 1/4 teaspoon of paprika powder. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d608384eb5c1cc4e907a9','5e33dc714f28558c29df64f7',1,'P1: Wash & pressure cook the chicken','To cook the chicken for Broccoli Chicken Salad, wash 200 grams of chicken well with water. Then, add the washed chicken to a pressure cooker. Add 1/4 cup of water, 1 teaspoon of Italian seasoning along with 1/2 teaspoon chili flakes. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of salt and cover it with a lid. Pressure cook the chicken on high flame for 3 whistles. After 3 whistles, turn off the flame and allow the pressure to release naturally. While the chicken is cooking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d60ae4590a0278779055e','5e33dc714f28558c29df64f7',2,'P2: Blanch the broccoli florets','For the Broccoli Chicken Salad, wash and cut 1 cup of broccoli into small florets. To blanch the broccoli, boil 3 cups of water in a deep bottom pan on high flame for 2 minutes. Then, add 1 cup of broccoli florets to the boiling water, cover it with a lid and blanch it on medium-high flame for 1-2 minutes. After blanching the broccoli, turn off the flame, take off the lid and drain the water. Keep it aside to cool down to room temperature.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":4}'),('5e9d60e084eb5c1cc4e907aa','5e33dc714f28558c29df64f7',3,'P3: Prep the ingredients & toast the sliced almonds','For the Broccoli Chicken Salad, wash, peel and finely slice 1/2 cup of onions. Wash, peel, and grate 1/2 cup of carrot. Finely slice 3 tablespoons of almonds. To toast the almond slices, heat a pan on medium flame, add 3 tablespoons of almond slices to the pan and toast it on medium-low flame for 3-4 minutes without adding oil. Keep stirring the almonds continuously to prevent it from burning. After toasting the almond slices, it will turn slightly golden. Then, turn off the flame and take it out.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d611c77c5bbfa41905ef9','5e33dc714f28558c29df64f7',4,'P4: Flake the cooked chicken','For the Broccoli Chicken Salad, after the pressure from the cooker has been released, take off the lid and reduce the water from the chicken by stir-frying it on high flame for 1-2 minutes till the moisture from the chicken evaporates. Then, turn off the flame and let the chicken cool down completely. After the chicken cools down, shred it to small pieces as shown and discard all the bones.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9d613f4590a02787790561','5e33dc714f28558c29df64f7',5,'M1: Make the salad dressing','To make the dressing for Broccoli Chicken Salad, pour 3/4 cup of mayonnaise in a mixing bowl. Add 1.5 tablespoon apple cider vinegar, 1/4 teaspoon of salt and 1/4 teaspoon of crushed black pepper and mix it well.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d61734590a02787790562','5e33dc714f28558c29df64f7',6,'M2: Combine the salad & refrigerate. Garnish & serve','To make the Broccoli Chicken Salad, add blanched broccoli in another mixing bowl. Add shredded chicken pieces, 1/2 cup of grated carrot and 1/2 cup of sliced onions to it. Next, add 2 tablespoons of dried cranberries and 2.5 tablespoons of toasted almonds. Pour the prepared mayo dressing over the salad and mix it well using a spatula. Refrigerate the salad for 20 minutes. After refrigerating the salad, garnish it with 1.5 teaspoons of toasted almonds and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d62034590a02787790564','5e33dd91985ffca18ae8fb86',1,'M1: Roast the fox nuts','To make the Masala Makhana, heat 1 tablespoon of ghee in a pan on medium flame for a minute. Add 1.5 cups of fox nuts and roast it on medium flame for 6-7 minutes. Keep stirring it in between to prevent it from getting burnt. Roast the fox nuts until it turns slightly golden and crisp.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d623177c5bbfa41905efa','5e33dd91985ffca18ae8fb86',2,'M2: Add the spices & season the fox nuts. Serve','After roasting the fox nuts, add 1/4 teaspoon of salt, 1/4 teaspoon of black salt and 1 teaspoon of cumin powder. Next, add half a teaspoon of dry mango powder along with 1/4 teaspoon of red chili powder and mix it well. Stir and fry it on medium flame for 2-3 minutes. Add a teaspoon of ghee and mix it well. Then, turn off the flame and take it out in a bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d629284eb5c1cc4e907ac','5e33df5c4f28558c29df64f9',1,'P1: Slice the mushrooms & prep the ingredients','For Mushroom Soup, wash and finely slice half a cup of button mushrooms. Wash, peel, and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Peel and finely chop 1 teaspoon of garlic. Crush 1/2 teaspoon of black peppercorns to a coarse powder using a pepper grinder.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9d62b277c5bbfa41905efb','5e33df5c4f28558c29df64f9',2,'M1: Simmer the mushrooms','To make Mushroom Soup, heat 1 teaspoon of olive oil and 2 teaspoons of unsalted butter in a pan on medium flame for a minute. Add 1/4 cup of finely chopped onions and 1 teaspoon of chopped garlic to the pan. Saute the onions for 2-3 minutes on medium-high flame till onions turn slightly translucent. Next, add half a cup of sliced mushrooms and saute it for a minute. Then, reduce it to low flame and simmer the mushrooms for 5 minutes till it is completely cooked. While the mushrooms are simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e9d62ef4590a02787790565','5e33df5c4f28558c29df64f9',3,'M2: Add all purpose four & combine. Add the herbs & simmer the soup','After simmering the mushrooms, add 1/2 teaspoon of all purpose flour and keep stirring continuously for a minute on medium flame. Next, add 1.5 cups of water along with 1/4 teaspoon of crushed black pepper and 1/4 teaspoon of fresh thyme. Add 1/4 teaspoon of salt and stir it well. Boil the soup on medium-high flame for 5 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d632277c5bbfa41905efc','5e3bf01a057fd3f6fc80eff9',1,'P1: Cook Quinoa','To cook the quinoa for Quinoa Salad, first, rinse 3/4 cup of quinoa thoroughly with water. Next, add the rinsed quinoa in a saucepan and toast it on a medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Next, add half a teaspoon of olive oil and roast it for another 1-2 minutes. After roasting the quinoa, add 1.5 cups of water into it and mix it well. Then, bring it to a rolling boil on high flame. Add 1/4 teaspoon of salt and mix it well. As the water comes to a boil, cover it with a lid and allow it to simmer for 12-15 minutes or until the quinoa is cooked. While the quinoa is cooking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d632684eb5c1cc4e907ad','5e33df5c4f28558c29df64f9',4,'M3: Prepare the mushroom paste & add it to the soup. Garnish & serve','After 5 minutes, transfer 1 cup of mushroom broth with a few mushroom slices into a blender jar and blend it well to make a smooth paste. Add this prepared mushroom paste to the soup along with 2 tablespoons of fresh cream and mix it well. Simmer the soup for another 1 minute. Then turn off the flame. Garnish the soup with a pinch of crushed black pepper and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":1,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d635777c5bbfa41905efd','5e3bf01a057fd3f6fc80eff9',2,'P2: Prep Ingredients','For Quinoa Salad, wash, peel and grate 1/4 cup of carrot. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of parsley. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of mint leaves. Wash and finely dice 1/4 cup of red capsicum. Cut 1/4 cup of raisins into halves. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of spring onion greens. Squeeze 1 tablespoon of lime juice using a lemon squeezer.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9d639f77c5bbfa41905efe','5e3bf01a057fd3f6fc80eff9',3,'M1: Mix Ingredients','To make the Quinoa Salad, first, add the cooked quinoa to a large mixing bowl. Next, add 1/4 cup of grated carrot, 1/4 cup of chopped spring onion greens, and 1/4 cup of diced red capsicum. After that, add 1/4 cup of chopped parsley and mint leaves followed by 1/4 cup of chopped raisins and mix it well.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d63da77c5bbfa41905eff','5e3bf01a057fd3f6fc80eff9',4,'M2: Final Touches','Next, to the Quinoa Salad, add 2 teaspoons of honey and 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder. Season it with 1/4 teaspoon of salt and 1/4 teaspoon of black pepper powder. Mix it well and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d655b4590a02787790566','5e3bee744f28558c29df6568',1,'P1: Cook Potatoes','For Sweet Potato & Carrot Soup, wash a medium-sized sweet potato well with water. Then, put it into a pressure cooker with 2 cups of water and cover it with the lid. Pressure cook it on high flame till the first whistle. After that, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook it for another 8 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the sweet potato is boiling, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d659e77c5bbfa41905f00','5e3bee744f28558c29df6568',2,'P2: Prep Ingredients','For Sweet Potato & Carrot Soup, wash, peel and slice 1.5 cups of carrot into thick coins. Wash, peel and cube 3/4 cup of sweet potato. Wash, peel and finely chop 1/2 inch piece of ginger. Wash, peel and finely chop 1 nos green chilies.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d66b74590a02787790567','5e33e1a3985ffca18ae8fb8a',1,'P1: Chop & prep the ingredients','For Tomato Cucumber Salad, wash and cut half a cup of cucumber into medium dices. Wash and cut half a cup of cherry tomatoes into halves. Wash, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely 1 tablespoon of dill leaves. Wash and cut a lemon into halves and squeeze 1 tablespoon of lemon juice using a lemon squeezer.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9d66d84590a02787790568','5e33e1a3985ffca18ae8fb8a',2,'M1: Make the salad dressing','To make the dressing for Tomato Cucumber Salad, add 2 tablespoons of olive oil in a bowl. Next, add 1 tablespoon of lemon juice, 2 teaspoons of apple cider vinegar followed by half a teaspoon of sugar and 1/4 teaspoon of salt. Add 1/4 teaspoon of black pepper powder along with 1 tablespoon of chopped dill leaves and mix it well.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d670577c5bbfa41905f01','5e33e1a3985ffca18ae8fb8a',3,'M2: Combine the salad.  Garnish & serve','To make the Tomato Cucumber Salad, in a large mixing bowl, add half a cup of diced cucumber, half a cup of chopped cherry tomatoes and 1/4 cup of chopped onions. Next, pour the prepared dressing over the salad and mix it well. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d676b4590a02787790569','5e33e3db985ffca18ae8fb8b',1,'P1: Soak the foxtail millet & prep the ingredients','For Millet Upma, in a bowl, add half a cup of foxtail millet and soak it in 2 cups of water for 15 minutes. Meanwhile, wash, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 2 nos green chilies. Wash, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of carrot. Wash and finely chop 4 nos beans. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Wash and finely chop 1-inch piece of ginger. Wash 7 nos curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d679e84eb5c1cc4e907ae','5e33e3db985ffca18ae8fb8b',2,'M1: Temper the oil with cumin & mustard seeds. Fry the onions','To make the Millet Upma, heat 2 tablespoons of ghee in a kadai on medium flame for a minute. Add 1 teaspoon of chana dal, 1 teaspoon of urad dal, half a teaspoon of mustard seeds and half a teaspoon of cumin seeds. Saute and allow it to splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions, 2 nos chopped green chilies and 1-inch piece of chopped ginger followed by 7 nos curry leaves. Stir and fry it on medium flame for 2-3 minutes, until the onion turns translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d67d177c5bbfa41905f02','5e33e3db985ffca18ae8fb8b',3,'M2: Simmer the vegetables','After frying the onions, add 1/4 cup of chopped carrots along with 4 nos chopped beans. Mix it well and stir-fry the vegetables on medium-high flame for 2-3 minutes. Next, add 1/4 cup of green peas and mix it well. Add 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes and fry the vegetables on medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Then, add half a teaspoon of salt followed by 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder and mix it well. Next, add 1.5 cups of water and cover it with a lid. Allow it to simmer for 5 minutes. While the vegetables are simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('5e9d686584eb5c1cc4e907af','5e33e3db985ffca18ae8fb8b',4,'M3: Add the soaked foxtail millet & simmer the upma','After simmering the vegetables for Millet Upma, take off the lid and add the soaked foxtail millet. Mix it well. Then, cover it with a lid and cook it on low flame for 15 minutes. While the millet upma is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e9d689284eb5c1cc4e907b0','5e33e3db985ffca18ae8fb8b',5,'M4: Garnish & serve','After simmering the Millet Upma, take off the lid and mix it well. By this time the millet will absorb all the water and will be cooked through. Saute it on medium flame for a minute. Then, turn off the flame and transfer it on a plate. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d68fc4590a0278779056a','5e3bee744f28558c29df6568',3,'P3: Prep Potatoes','After boiling the sweet potato, remove the lid of the pressure cooker and take out the boiled sweet potato. Allow it cool down a bit then gently peel off the skin and cut it into small cubes.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d691c4590a0278779056b','5e33eccc057fd3f6fc80ef96',1,'P1: Preheat the oven & prep the ingredients','For Roasted Carrot and Pumpkin Soup, preheat the oven at 200 °C. Wash, peel and cube 3/4 cup of pumpkins. Wash, peel and cut 3/4 cup of carrots into thick slices. Wash, peel and slice 1/4 cup of onions. Peel 3 cloves of garlic. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d693d4590a0278779056c','5e33eccc057fd3f6fc80ef96',2,'M1: Bake the vegetables','To roast the vegetables for Roasted Carrot and Pumpkin Soup, in a mixing bowl, add 3/4 cup of cubed pumpkins, 3/4 cup of sliced carrots, 1/4 cup of sliced onions and 3 cloves of garlic. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of salt, 1/4 teaspoon of black pepper powder, 1/4 teaspoon of nutmeg powder and 2 tablespoons of olive oil. Mix it well. Transfer the seasoned vegetables to a baking tray and place it in the oven. Roast the vegetables 180 degrees C for 20 minutes. While the vegetables are roasting, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9d697177c5bbfa41905f03','5e33eccc057fd3f6fc80ef96',3,'M2: Boil the roasted vegetables & puree','To make Roasted Carrot and Pumpkin Soup, heat 1 tablespoon of butter in a pan on low flame for 30 seconds. Then, add the roasted vegetables and saute it on medium-high flame for 1-2 minutes. Next, add 1/2 cup of water and bring it to a boil. After it boils, turn off the flame and let it cool down completely. After the vegetables cool down, transfer it to a blender jar and blend it to a smooth puree.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d698a84eb5c1cc4e907b1','5e3bee744f28558c29df6568',4,'Temper Spices','For Sweet Potato & Carrot Soup, heat a small pan on a medium flame for a minute. Then, add 1/2 inch piece of chopped ginger followed by 1 nos chopped green chili and half a teaspoon of cumin seeds. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of coriander seeds and dry roast it on medium-low flame for 1-2 minutes, until fragrant. Then, turn off the flame and keep it aside for later use.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d699584eb5c1cc4e907b2','5e33eccc057fd3f6fc80ef96',4,'M3: Simmer the soup. Garnish & serve','Next, transfer the prepared puree to the same pan and cook it on medium-low flame for 1-2 minutes. Add 2 tablespoons of finely chopped coriander leaves to the soup and give it a stir. Next, add 1 tablespoon of fresh cream and mix well. Turn off the flame and garnish the soup with 1 tablespoon of fresh cream and a sprig of coriander leaves. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d6a014590a0278779056d','5e3bee744f28558c29df6568',5,'M2: Cook Vegetables','To make the Sweet Potato & Carrot Soup, in a stockpot, add 1.5 cups of carrot roundels and 3/4 cup of cubed sweet potato. Next, add the roasted spices and mix it well. Saute it on a medium flame for 1-2 minutes and allow all the flavors from the roasted spices to come together. Next, add 1.5 cups of water and cover it with a lid. Allow the vegetables to cook on a medium flame for another 20 minutes, until tender. After cooking the vegetables, turn off the flame and allow it to cool down completely. While it is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":30,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":30,"flame":3}'),('5e9d6a2584eb5c1cc4e907b3','5e3bee744f28558c29df6568',6,'M3: Blend Cooked Vegetables','To make the Sweet Potato & Carrot Soup, after the simmered vegetables cool down, transfer it to a blender jar and blend it into a smooth puree. Add a teaspoon of rock salt and blend it again. Then, transfer it to a bowl and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9d6a334590a0278779056e','5e33f3e9057fd3f6fc80ef98',1,'AP1: Soak the black chana','For Black Chana Chat, in a bowl, add 3/4 cup of black chana and soak it in 2 cups of water for 10 hours. While the black chana is soaking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":600,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d6a5a84eb5c1cc4e907b4','5e33f3e9057fd3f6fc80ef98',2,'P1: Pressure cook the soaked chana','To boil black chana for Black Chana Chat, put the soaked black chana in a pressure cooker with half a teaspoon of salt and 1.5 cups of water. Cover it with a lid and pressure cook it on high flame until 3 whistles. After the third whistle, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook it for another 8 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the black chana is cooking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":18,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d6a6c4590a0278779056f','5e3bee744f28558c29df6568',7,'M4: Garnish','To prepare the garnish for Sweet Potato & Carrot Soup, heat a small pan on a medium flame for a minute. Then, add 1/4 teaspoon of mustard seeds and 1/4 teaspoon of cumin seeds. Saute and dry roast the spices on a medium flame for 1-2 minutes until it turns fragrant. Then, add the boiled and cubed sweet potato and 1/4 teaspoon of salt and saute it for 1-2 minutes. Then turn off the flame and set it aside. Next, pour the prepared soup into a bowl and garnish it with a tablespoon of fresh cream. Add the dry roasted sweet potato cubes. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d6a9177c5bbfa41905f04','5e33f3e9057fd3f6fc80ef98',3,'P2: Boil the potatoes','To boil the potato for Black Chana Chat, wash a medium-sized potato well with water. Then, put it into a pressure cooker with 3 cups of water and pressure cook it on high flame till the first whistle. After the first whistle, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook it for another 8 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the potato is boiling, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d6b0a4590a02787790570','5e33f3e9057fd3f6fc80ef98',4,'P3: Prep the ingredients & make green chutney','For Black Chana Chat, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Wash, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1.5 tablespoons of coriander leaves. Wash and slit 1 nos green chili. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of mint leaves. To make the green chutney, open the packet of the ready-made chutney mix and rinse the chopped ingredients well with water. Then, put it into a blender jar and blend it into a smooth chutney.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9d6b2577c5bbfa41905f05','5e3bec4f4f28558c29df6566',1,'P1: Cook Potatoes','For Sukha Bhel, wash a medium-sized potato well with water. Then, add it to a pressure cooker with 2 cups of water and 1/4 teaspoon of salt. Cover it with a lid and pressure cook it on high flame till the first whistle. After that, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook it for another 8 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the potatoes are boiling, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d6b4077c5bbfa41905f06','5e33f3e9057fd3f6fc80ef98',5,'P4: Peel & cube the boiled potatoes','For Black Chana Chat, after boiling the potato, remove the lid of the pressure cooker, take out the potato and allow it cool down for some time. Then, gently peel off the skin and cut into small cubes. Next, after boiling the black chana, take off the lid and drain the water from it and set it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d6b5084eb5c1cc4e907b5','5e3bec4f4f28558c29df6566',2,'P2: Prep Ingredients','For Sukha Bhel, wash, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Wash and slit 1 nos green chili. Wash 1/4 cup of coriander leaves. Next, wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash 8 nos curry leaves. Next, to make the sukha chutney, in a blender jar, add 1/4 cup of coriander leaves, 1 slit green chili and 1 tablespoon of roasted chana dal. Cover the jar with the lid and blend it well to make a dry chutney.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d6b6877c5bbfa41905f07','5e33f3e9057fd3f6fc80ef98',6,'M1: Fry the boiled  black chana','To make the Black Chana Chat, heat 1 teaspoon of cooking oil in a kadai on medium flame for a minute. Add 1 nos slit green chili and saute it for a minute. Then, add the boiled black chana and mix it well. Saute and fry the chana on medium flame for 2 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d6b8e84eb5c1cc4e907b6','5e33f3e9057fd3f6fc80ef98',7,'M2: Add the spices & cook the chana','After frying the black chana, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, 1/4 teaspoon of Kashmiri red chili powder, 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala, 1/4 teaspoon of dry mango powder followed by 1/4 teaspoon of chat masala and 1/4 teaspoon of cumin powder. Add half a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Stir and fry the chana on low flame for 2-3 minutes. Mash a few black chana using the spatula and mix it well. After frying the chana, turn off the flame and take it out in a bowl.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e9d6b9477c5bbfa41905f08','5e3bec4f4f28558c29df6566',3,'P3: Prep Potatoes','After boiling the potato for Sukha Bhel, take off the lid and transfer the boiled potato to a plate. Allow it to cool down a bit, then gently peel off the skin. Next, cut the boiled potato into cubes.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d6bb177c5bbfa41905f09','5e33f3e9057fd3f6fc80ef98',8,'M3: Assemble the chat & serve','To make the Black Chana Chat, add 2 teaspoons of the prepared green chutney, to the fried chana. Add 2 teaspoons of tamarind chutney along with 1.5 tablespoons of curd and mix it well. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions, 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes, and 1/4 cup of the boiled and cubed potato. Next, add 1 tablespoon of mint leaves followed by 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves and mix it well. Take it out into a bowl and pour 1 teaspoon of curd over the chat. Garnish it with green chutney and tamarind chutney along with a tablespoon of sev and some chopped coriander leaves. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d6bbb84eb5c1cc4e907b7','5e3bec4f4f28558c29df6566',4,'M1: Roast Peanuts','To make the Sukha Bhel, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a kadai on a medium flame for a minute. Then, add 2 tablespoons of peanuts and roast it on a medium flame for 3-4 minutes until it turns slightly brown and crunchy. After that, add 2 tablespoons of roasted chana dal and fry it on low flame for 1-2 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d6bf584eb5c1cc4e907b8','5e3bec4f4f28558c29df6566',5,'M2: Continue to Cook - Add other Ingredients','After frying the peanuts and roasted chana dal, add 8 nos curry leaves, 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder and 1/4 teaspoon of kashmiri red chili powder. Season it with half a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Stir and fry it for another minute on low flame. After that, add 2 cups of puffed rice and mix it well. Saute it on a medium flame for 2-3 minutes or until the flavours combine well. Then, turn off the flame and take it out in a bowl.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d6c2c84eb5c1cc4e907b9','5e3bec4f4f28558c29df6566',6,'M3: Make Bhel','Next, crush 4 nos papdis into small pieces and add it to the fried puffed rice. Then, add the prepared sukha chutney and mix it well. Add 1/4 cup of chopped onions, 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes and 1/4 cup of boiled and cubed potatoes. Next, add half a teaspoon of chat masala along with 2 tablespoons of sev and mix it well. Take it out in a bowl and garnish it with some chopped onions, sev and a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9d6cc94590a02787790571','5e3be3234f28558c29df6565',1,'P1: Roast Flour','To dry roast the rice flour for Idiyappam, add half a cup of rice flour to a pan. Saute and dry roast the flour without adding oil, on low flame for 2 minutes. Keep stirring it continuously while roasting, as it might get burnt. Roasting the flour cooks out the raw taste making it more flavorful. After roasting it, turn off the flame and set it aside. Next, grease the idli plate with 1/4 teaspoon of cooking oil using an oil brush.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d6cec84eb5c1cc4e907ba','5e3be3234f28558c29df6565',2,'M1: Prepare the Dough','To prepare the dough for Idiyappam, add 3/4 cup of water in a kadai along with 1/4 teaspoon of salt and half a teaspoon of cooking oil. Mix it well and bring it to a rolling boil on high flame. As it comes to a boil, reduce the flame to low and add the roasted rice flour to it. Keep stirring the flour continuously on low flame until it is well combined with the water. After that, turn off the flame and cover it with the lid. Allow it to rest for 5 minutes. While it is resting, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d6d0b84eb5c1cc4e907bb','5e3be3234f28558c29df6565',3,'M2: Prepare the Dough','After resting the cooked rice flour for Idiyappam, take off the lid and knead it well into a smooth dough. Make sure to knead the dough while it is still hot or it might turn too stiff. Next, place the perforated circular disk to the bottom of the idiyappam maker and grease it well with 1/4 teaspoon of oil. Then, take a ball sized dough and shape it into a cylindrical shape and stuff it inside the idiyappam maker. Close it with the lid and press it gently over the greased idli plate and stuff the cavities with thin noodles. Next, place the idli plate inside the steamer and steam it for 10 minutes. While the idiyappam is steaming, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d6d304590a02787790572','5e3be3234f28558c29df6565',4,'M3: Serve','After cooking the idiyappams, remove the lid of the steamer and carefully take out the idli plate. Then, take out the prepared idiyappams on a plate and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d6dde84eb5c1cc4e907bc','5e3bdc98985ffca18ae8fbe5',1,'AP1: Soak Dal','For Langar Dal, in a bowl, add 1/2 cup of black urad dal and 2 tablespoons of chana dal. Add 2 cups of water and allow it to soak it for 4 hours. While the dal is soaking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":240,"advanced_prep_time":240,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9d6e0a4590a02787790573','5e3bdc98985ffca18ae8fbe5',2,'P1: Cook Dal','To cook the dal for Langar Dal, first, peel, wash and finely chop 1 teaspoon of garlic. Wash, peel and finely chop a 1-inch piece of ginger. Next, add the soaked urad dal to a pressure cooker. Add 1 teaspoon of chopped garlic and a 1-inch piece of chopped ginger. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder followed by half a teaspoon of cooking oil and 1/4 teaspoon of salt. Add 1.5 cups of water and cover it with a lid. Pressure cook the dal on high flame until three whistles. After that, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook it for another 5 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the dal is cooking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d6e494590a02787790574','5e3bdc98985ffca18ae8fbe5',3,'P2: Prep other Ingredients','For Langar Dal, wash, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Wash and finely chop 1 nos green chili. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. After the pressure from the cooker has been released, take off the lid and slightly mash the dal to make it a bit vicious consistency.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d6e6e4590a02787790575','5e3bdc98985ffca18ae8fbe5',4,'M1: Cook Spices and Onions','To make the Langar Dal, heat 1 tablespoon of ghee in a kadai on a medium flame for a minute. Then, add half a teaspoon of cumin seeds and 1 nos bay leaf. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions and fry it on a medium flame for 2-3 minutes till it turns slightly translucent. Next, add 1 teaspoon of ginger-garlic paste followed by 1 nos chopped green chili and fry it for another 2-3 minutes until the onions turn golden brown.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d6eac84eb5c1cc4e907bd','5e3bdc98985ffca18ae8fbe5',5,'M2: Continue Cooking the Dal','After frying the onions, add 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes. Season it with 1/4 teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Saute and cook the tomatoes on medium-low flame for 3-4 minutes until it turns tender. As the tomatoes turn soft and mashy, add the cooked dal to it and mix it well. Add half a cup of water to adjust the consistency of the dal. Then, cover it with a lid and simmer it for 10 minutes. While the dal is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e9d6ece4590a02787790576','5e3bdc98985ffca18ae8fbe5',6,'M3: Garnish','After simmering the Langar Dal, take off the lid and give it a stir. Add 1/4 teaspoon of salt and 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves. Mix it well and take it out in a bowl. Add a teaspoon of butter and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9d6f5f77c5bbfa41905f0a','5e3bdb1b057fd3f6fc80eff7',1,'AP1: Soak Idli Rice for Batter','For Vegetable Uttapam, add half a cup of idli rice to a bowl. Next, add 1/4 cup of urad dal followed by 1/4 teaspoon of fenugreek seeds. Add 2 cups of water and allow it to soak for 5 hours. While the rice is soaking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":300,"advanced_prep_time":300,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d6f934590a02787790577','5e3bdb1b057fd3f6fc80eff7',2,'AP2: Make Batter','To make the batter for Vegetable Uttapam, add the soaked idli rice and urad dal to a blender jar and blend it well to a smooth batter. Then, pour it in a large mixing bowl. Next, in a bowl, add 2 tablespoons of poha and rinse it well with half a cup of water. Then, transfer it to a blender jar and blend it to a fine paste. Add the poha paste to the prepared batter and mix it well. Then, allow the batter to ferment for 8 hours. While the batter is resting, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":480,"advanced_prep_time":480,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d6fb94590a02787790578','5e3bdb1b057fd3f6fc80eff7',3,'P1: Prep Ingredients for Uttapam','For Vegetable Uttapam, wash, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash, peel and grate 1/4 cup of carrot. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of green capsicum. Wash, peel and finely chop 1/2 inch piece of ginger. Wash and finely chop 1 nos green chili. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":16,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d6fd684eb5c1cc4e907be','5e3bdb1b057fd3f6fc80eff7',4,'P2: Make Vegetable Mixture','To make the vegetable mixture for Vegetable Uttapam, in a mixing bowl, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions, 1/4 cup of grated carrot, 1/4 cup of chopped capsicum followed by 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes and 1/2 inch piece of chopped ginger. Next, add 1 nos chopped green chili, 1 tablespoon of chopped curry leaves and 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves. Season it with 1/4 teaspoon of salt and mix it well.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d6ffb4590a02787790579','5e3bdb1b057fd3f6fc80eff7',5,'M1: Make Uttapam','To make Vegetable Uttapam, first, place a tawa on a medium-low flame and heat it for about a minute. Meanwhile, prepare the batter for uttapam, after fermenting the batter, gently mix it. Then, add 1/4 teaspoon of salt and mix it well. After that, pour a ladle full of batter over the hot tawa and spread it into a 6-inch circle. As soon as small bubbles start to appear over it, spread the prepared vegetable mixture over it and pat it gently over the uttapam. Add a teaspoon of cooking oil over it and cover it with a lid. Cook it on low flame for a minute.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":1,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e9d702277c5bbfa41905f0b','5e3bdb1b057fd3f6fc80eff7',6,'M2: Serve','After cooking the Vegetable Uttapam, carefully flip it, scraping the sides and press it gently. Continue to simmer it for another minute. Then, turn off the flame and carefully take it out on a plate and serve. Similarly, make the rest of the uttapams.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":1,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d72394590a0278779057e','5e3bd8194f28558c29df6563',1,'AP1: Soak Black Chana','For Black Chana Sundal, wash and soak 3/4 cup of black chana in 2 cups of water for 8-10 hours. While the black chana is soaking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":600,"advanced_prep_time":600,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d725984eb5c1cc4e907bf','5e3bd8194f28558c29df6563',2,'P1: Cook Black Chana','To boil the Black Chana for Black Chana Sundal, add 3/4 cup of soaked black chana to a pressure cooker along with 3 cups of water and 1/2 teaspoon of salt. Cover it with a lid and pressure cook it on high flame until three whistles. After the third whistle, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook it for another 8 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the black chana is boiling, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":18,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d72744590a0278779057f','5e3bd8194f28558c29df6563',3,'P2: Prep Ingredients','For Black Chana Sundal, wash and finely chop 2 nos green chillies. Grate 1/4 cup of fresh coconut using a grater. Wash 8 nos curry leaves well with water. Wash and cut a lime into two halves, then squeeze 2 teaspoons of lime juice using a lemon squeezer.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d729c84eb5c1cc4e907c0','5e3bd8194f28558c29df6563',4,'M1: Temper Spcies','To make the Black Chana Sundal, heat 1 tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan on a medium flame for a minute. Add half a teaspoon of urad dal followed by half a teaspoon of mustard seeds and allow it to crackle for a few seconds. Next, add 2 nos chopped green chillies, 1/4 teaspoon of hing and 8 nos curry leaves. Saute the tempering for a minute. Then, add the boiled black chana and mix it well.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e9d72be4590a02787790580','5e3bd8194f28558c29df6563',5,'M2: Final Touches','Next, add half a teaspoon of salt along with 1/4 cup of grated coconut and mix it well. Saute and fry it on a medium flame for 2-3 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and add 2 teaspoons of lime juice and mix it well. Take it out in a bowl and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d734977c5bbfa41905f0e','5e3bc0164f28558c29df6562',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Oats & Jaggery Bar, roughly chop 8 nos walnuts using a tapered blade knife. Roughly chop 8 nos dried dates. Roughly chop 8 nos cashew nuts. Next, grease a tray with 1/4 teaspoon of ghee using an oil brush and set it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d73704590a02787790581','5e3bc0164f28558c29df6562',2,'M1: Roast Nuts','To roast the nuts for the Oats & Jaggery Bar, heat 1 tablespoon of ghee in a pan on a medium flame for a minute. Add 8 nos chopped walnuts, 8 nos chopped cashew nuts, and 8 nos chopped dried dates. Saute and roast the nuts on a medium flame for 4-5 minutes until it is slightly brown and crunchy. Keep stirring the nuts to prevent it from getting burnt. Once the nuts start to turn slightly brown, add 1 teaspoon of sesame seeds and saute it for a minute.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d739e77c5bbfa41905f0f','5e3bc0164f28558c29df6562',3,'M2: Cook Jaggery','After roasting the nuts, add 1 cup of rolled oats and saute it on a medium flame for 4-5 minutes. Stir and roast the oats until it is slightly brown and crisp. After roasting it, add 1 cup of jaggery and mix it well with the nuts. Stir it briskly and break up the big chunks of jaggery into small pieces. Keep stirring it on low flame until the jaggery melts and is well dissolved with the oats and nuts. Ensure not to overcook the jaggery as it might turn brittle. After the jaggery melts and is well combined with the oats, turn off the flame and add 2 tablespoons of desiccated coconut and mix it well.','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d73d777c5bbfa41905f10','5e3bc0164f28558c29df6562',4,'M3: Make the Bars','To set the Oats & Jaggery Bar, transfer the prepared oats mixture to the greased tray and spread it to make a thick and even layer using a spatula. Then, allow it to sit for 20 minutes. After it is set, cut it into rectangular pieces and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":20,"flame":0}'),
('5e9d744d77c5bbfa41905f11','5e3bb835985ffca18ae8fbe3',1,'P1: Soak Dal','For Mor Kulambu, in a bowl, add 1 teaspoon of toor dal, half a teaspoon of cumin seeds and 1/4 teaspoon of rice. Next, add 1 teaspoon of coriander seeds and 1/4 cup of water, soak it for 30 minutes. While the lentil is soaking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":30,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":30,"flame":0}'),('5e9d747784eb5c1cc4e907c1','5e3bb835985ffca18ae8fbe3',2,'P2: Prep Ingredients','For Mor Kulambu, wash, peel, and cut 3/4 cup of ash gourd into 2 inch long pieces. Wash and slit 2 nos green chilies, grate 1/4 cup of fresh coconut using a grater. Next, add half a cup of curd in a bowl and whisk it well until smooth. Wash 8 nos curry leaves well with water.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d749684eb5c1cc4e907c2','5e3bb835985ffca18ae8fbe3',3,'P3: Make Coconut Paste','To make the coconut paste for Mor Kulambu, add the soaked spices and dal into a blender jar. Add 1/4 cup of grated coconut along with 2 nos slit green chilies and blend it well into a fine paste.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d74b877c5bbfa41905f12','5e3bb835985ffca18ae8fbe3',4,'M1: Cook Ash Gourd','To make Mor Kulambu, in a kadai, add 3/4 cup of chopped ash gourd followed by 1/4 cup of water and 1/4 teaspoon of salt. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder and cover it with a lid. Cook it on low flame for 10 minutes until tender. While the ash gourd is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e9d74e084eb5c1cc4e907c3','5e3bb835985ffca18ae8fbe3',5,'M2: Add Coconut Paste','After simmering the ash gourd for Mor Kulambu, take off the lid and give it a stir. Next, add the prepared coconut paste to it and reduce the flame to low. Then, add half a cup of whisked curd and keep stirring it continuously on low flame as the curd might split. Keep stirring until the curd is well combined with the masala. Add a little water if required, to adjust the consistency of the gravy. Then, continue to cook it on low flame for another 4-5 minutes until it turns a little frothy. Keep stirring in between. Turn off the flame and set it aside. While it is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('5e9d74fd4590a02787790582','5e3bb835985ffca18ae8fbe3',6,'M3: Make Tadka','To make the tempering for Mor Kulambu, heat 1 teaspoon of coconut oil in a small tempering pan. Add half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, 1/4 teaspoon of hing and 8 nos curry leaves. Saute and allow it to splutter for a few seconds. Then, turn off the flame and add this tempering instantly to the prepared Mor Kulambu. Mix it well, take it out in a bowl and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d75984590a02787790583','5e3bb62a4f28558c29df6561',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Indori Poha, first, peel and wash 1/4 cup of green peas. Next, add 1 cup of water to a pan and bring it to boil on high flame. Add 1/4 teaspoon of salt and bring the water to a rolling boil. Then, add 1/4 cup of green peas to the boiling water and boil it on high flame for 4-5 minutes. Meanwhile, wash, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash, peel and cut 1/4 cup of potatoes into small cubes. Wash and finely chop 2 nos green chilies. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. After boiling the green peas, turn off the flame and drain the water from the peas and set it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d75c64590a02787790584','5e3bb62a4f28558c29df6561',2,'P2: Prep Ingredients','For Indori Poha, place a sieve over a large bowl and add 1.5 cups of flattened rice into it. Then, rinse it with half a cup of water, and leave it damp for 5-6 minutes. Meanwhile, wash and cut the pomegranate into halves, then take one half and pat it gently using a spoon and peel 2 tablespoons of pomegranate seeds. Next, wash, peel and grate half a carrot. Cut a lemon into two halves and squeeze 1 tablespoon of lime juice using a lemon squeezer. Wash 7 nos curry leaves well with water.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d75ec77c5bbfa41905f13','5e3bb62a4f28558c29df6561',3,'M1: Cooking','To make Indori Poha, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a pan on a medium flame for a minute. Add half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, half a teaspoon of cumin seeds, and half a teaspoon of fennel seeds followed by 2 nos chopped green chillies and 7 nos curry leaves. Next, add 1/4 cup of onions and fry it on a medium flame for 2-3 minutes until it turns slightly translucent. Then, add 1/4 cup of chopped potatoes and saute it on low flame for 6-7 minutes, till the potatoes are cooked through.','cook_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d76084590a02787790585','5e3bb62a4f28558c29df6561',4,'M2: Cooking','After cooking the potatoes, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder and mix it well. Add 1.5 cups of soaked poha followed by half a teaspoon of salt and mix it gently. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala and half a teaspoon of sugar and mix it well. After that, add 1/4 cup of boiled green peas to the poha and mix it well. Stir and fry it on medium-high flame for 2-3 minutes. Then, cover it with a lid and simmer it for 2-3 minutes. While the poha is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e9d76284590a02787790586','5e3bb62a4f28558c29df6561',5,'M3: Final Touches','After simmering the Indori Poha, take off the lid and give it a stir. Turn off the flame and take it out in a plate. Sprinkle a pinch of jeerawan masala over it. Top it up with a tablespoon of ratlami sev followed by 2 tablespoons of grated carrot and a teaspoon of chopped onions. Garnish with a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves followed by a tablespoon of lime juice and 2 tablespoons of pomegranate seeds and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d791c84eb5c1cc4e907c4','5e3bacac4f28558c29df6560',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Energy Nuts Bar, first, wash and cut a lime into halves, then squeeze 2 teaspoons of lime juice using a lemon squeezer. Next, grease a baking mold with a teaspoon of cooking oil or with an oil spray.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d79464590a02787790587','5e3bacac4f28558c29df6560',2,'P2: Roast Nuts','To dry roast the nuts for the Energy Nuts Bar, first, in a pan, add 1/4 cup of almonds, 1/4 cup of pistachios, 1/4 cup of walnuts and 1/4 cup of cashews. Next, add 2 tablespoons of pumpkin seeds followed by 2 tablespoons of sesame seeds. Stir and dry roast the nuts without adding any oil on a medium flame for 5 minutes. Keep stirring the nuts until it is slightly brown. After dry roasting, the nuts, turn off the flame and set it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d796c4590a02787790588','5e3bacac4f28558c29df6560',3,'M1: Make a Sweet Syrup','To make the brown sugar and honey syrup for Energy Nuts Bar, add 3/4 cup of brown sugar in a saucepan followed by a quarter cup of honey. Next, add a pinch of salt and mix it well. Stir and cook it on low flame for 4-5 minutes until the sugar is completely dissolved. Then, add 2 teaspoons of lime juice into it and mix it well. Continue to simmer it for another 3-4 minutes. After that, take it down from the flame and set it aside. While the sugar syrup is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":4,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9d79974590a02787790589','5e3bacac4f28558c29df6560',4,'M2: Make Energy Bars','To make the Energy Nuts Bar, place the pan with the roasted nuts over low flame and pour the prepared brown sugar syrup over the nuts. Mix it well and coat the nuts with the sugar syrup. Stir and cook it on low flame for 2 minutes. Then, turn off the flame, and transfer the nuts into the greased mold. Level it evenly using the spatula and allow it to set in the refrigerator for 2 hours. While it is refrigerating, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":120,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9d79c884eb5c1cc4e907c5','5e3bacac4f28558c29df6560',5,'M3: Cut into Bars','For the Energy Nuts Bar, after the sugar-coated nuts set in the refrigerator, take it out and carefully remove the nut disk from the dish. Then, cut it into rectangular bars and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d7a5477c5bbfa41905f14','5e3ba9ae057fd3f6fc80eff4',1,'P1: Prepare the Flour Mixture','To prepare the flour crumb for the Puttu, in a large mixing bowl, add 1 cup of puttu flour along with a quarter teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Add 1/4 cup of water and mix it well. Do not to knead the flour, only crumble it. Add more water if required and keep mixing it well with flour. Add water in batches and keep crumbling the flour until it holds a ball like shape as shown. Once the flour is crumbled and moist, set it aside. Next, grate half a cup of fresh coconut using a grater.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d7a8d84eb5c1cc4e907c6','5e3ba9ae057fd3f6fc80eff4',2,'M1: Assemble Puttu','To make the Puttu, in a puttu steamer, set the layers of grated coconut and crumbled puttu flour. First, add about 2 tablespoons of grated coconut into the steamer and press it to the bottom. Next, add a thick layer of about 3 tablespoons of crumbled flour over it. Repeat the layers until the steamer is packed with grated coconut and crumbled puttu flour. Then, close it with the lid and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d7ab577c5bbfa41905f15','5e3ba9ae057fd3f6fc80eff4',3,'M2: Cook Puttu','To steam, the Puttu, place a roaster mesh over the burner. Place the steamer pot over it and fill it with water. Bring the water to a rolling boil on high flame. Then, place the puttu steamer on it and steam the puttu for 5 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and carefully take out the puttu from the steamer onto a plate. Cut it into halves and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":5,"flame":3}'),('5e9d7b4384eb5c1cc4e907c7','5e3ba74b057fd3f6fc80eff3',1,'P1: Melt Butter','For Sweet & Spicy Trail Mix, in a small glass bowl, add 2 teaspoons of butter and 1 teaspoon of brown sugar. Microwave it for 30 seconds to melt the butter, making it easier to dissolve the sugar in it. Then, mix it well using a spoon. Alternatively, you can melt the butter along with the brown sugar in a small pan on a low flame for 30-40 seconds.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9d7b6384eb5c1cc4e907c8','5e3ba74b057fd3f6fc80eff3',2,'M1: Prepare Nuts','To prepare the nuts for Sweet & Spicy Trail Mix, first, in a large mixing bowl, add 1/4 cup of cashew nuts, 1/4 cup of walnuts, and 1/4 cup of almonds followed by 2 tablespoons of pumpkin seeds. Next, add half a teaspoon of paprika powder. Season it with 1/4 teaspoon of black pepper powder and half a teaspoon of salt. Next, add the prepared butter and brown sugar solution and mix it well with the nuts.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9d7b844590a0278779058a','5e3ba74b057fd3f6fc80eff3',3,'M2: Bake Nuts','To make the Sweet & Spicy Trail Mix, line a baking tray with parchment paper and place the prepared nuts over it. Spread it evenly all over the tray and keep the tray inside the microwave. Roast the nuts for 5 minutes at 180° C. Then, carefully take it out from the microwave. Allow it cool down completely. Store the trail mix in an airtight container. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":5,"flame":0}'),('5e9e86a74590a0278779058f','5e3ba3c54f28558c29df655e',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Aloo Gobhi Dalna, wash and peel 1/2 cup of green peas. To boil the green peas, boil 2 cups of water in a saucepan on high flame for a minute. Add 1/4 teaspoon of salt and 1/2 cup of green peas and boil the peas on medium-high flame for 4-5 minutes. Meanwhile, wash and cut 1 cup of cauliflower into small florets. Wash, peel and cube 1/4 cup of potatoes. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Slit 3 nos green chilies lengthwise. After boiling the green peas, turn off the flame and drain the water from the boiled green peas. While the green peas are boiling, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":4}'),('5e9e86ff4590a02787790590','5e3ba3c54f28558c29df655e',2,'P2: Blanch Cauliflower','To blanch the cauliflower florets, boil 3 cups of water in a pan on high flame for 1-2 minutes. Add the cauliflower florets to the water and boil it on medium-high flame for 1-2 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and take out the blanched florets from the water.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":4}'),('5e9e874977c5bbfa41905f18','5e33f54d4f28558c29df64fc',1,'P1: Wash chicken & prep the ingredients','For Chicken Curry, first, wash 400 grams of chicken thoroughly with water. Then, put it into a bowl. Next, add half a cup of curd into a bowl and whisk it until smooth. Wash, peel and finely chop 1 cup of onions.','prep_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9e876a77c5bbfa41905f19','5e3ba3c54f28558c29df655e',3,'P3: Make Masala Mixture','For Aloo Gobhi Dalna, in a mixing bowl, add 1/2 teaspoon of red chili powder, 1 teaspoon of coriander powder, 1/2 teaspoon of cumin powder and 1/2 teaspoon of turmeric powder. Add 2 tablespoons of water and mix it well.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9e87fb4590a02787790592','5e33f54d4f28558c29df64fc',2,'P2: Marinate Chicken','To marinate the chicken for Chicken Curry, add 1 teaspoon of salt, and half a cup of whisked curd to the washed chicken. Next, add half a teaspoon of turmeric powder, 1 teaspoon of red chili powder, and 1 teaspoon of coriander powder along with half a teaspoon of cumin powder. Mix it well and coat the chicken pieces well with the marinade. Marination tenderizes the chicken while allowing it to absorb the flavors from the spices, hence making it more succulent and flavourful. Allow the chicken to marinate for 1 hour. While the chicken is marinating, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":60,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9e886d4590a02787790593','5e3ba3c54f28558c29df655e',4,'M1: Fry Potatoes','To fry the potatoes for Aloo Gobhi Dalna, heat 3 tablespoons of mustard oil in a pan on a medium flame for a minute. Add 1/4 cup of cubed potatoes and fry it on a medium flame for 4-5 minutes, till it turns slightly golden. After frying the potatoes, carefully take it out on a kitchen towel to remove excess oil.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9e88b684eb5c1cc4e907c9','5e3ba3c54f28558c29df655e',5,'M2: Fry Cauliflower','To fry the cauliflower florets for Aloo Gobhi Dalna, to the same pan, add the blanched cauliflower florets and fry it on medium-high flame for 3-4 minutes. After frying the cauliflower florets, carefully take it out on a kitchen towel to remove extra oil.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9e88bf84eb5c1cc4e907ca','5e33f54d4f28558c29df64fc',3,'M1: Fry onions','To make the chicken Curry, heat 3 tablespoons of cooking oil in a kadai on medium flame for a minute. Add 3 nos cloves followed by 3 nos green cardamoms and 1-inch piece of cinnamon stick, saute it on medium flame for a minute. Next, add 1 cup of chopped onions and fry it on medium flame for 4-5 minutes until it turns slightly golden.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e9e88dc84eb5c1cc4e907cb','5e3ba3c54f28558c29df655e',6,'M3: Temper Spices','To make the Aloo Gobhi Dalna, heat 1 tablespoon of mustard oil in a pan on a medium flame for a minute. Add 1/2 teaspoon of cumin seeds, 1/2 inch piece of cinnamon stick, 2 nos cloves, 1 nos green cardamom, 1 nos bay leaf, 2 nos slit green chilies and 1 teaspoon of ginger paste. Saute it on a medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Next, add the prepared mix of spices and saute it on medium flame for 1-2 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9e892a4590a02787790594','5e33f54d4f28558c29df64fc',4,'M2: Braise the chicken','After frying the onions, add 2 teaspoons of ginger-garlic paste and mix it well. Saute and continue to fry the masala on medium flame for 2-3 minutes until the onion turns golden brown. After that, add the marinated chicken pieces and mix it well. Fry the chicken on medium flame for 10 minutes, until it is no longer pink.','cook_method','{"active_time":13,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9e895077c5bbfa41905f1a','5e33f54d4f28558c29df64fc',5,'M3: Simmer the chicken curry','After frying the chicken, saute and cook the chicken on medium flame for 10 minutes, until the oil separates. As the oil separates from the masala, add 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala and mix it well. Next, add half a cup of water and mix it well. Then, cover the chicken with a lid and simmer it for 10 minutes. While the chicken is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e9e897484eb5c1cc4e907cc','5e33f54d4f28558c29df64fc',6,'M4: Garnish & serve','After simmering the chicken for Chicken Curry, take off the lid and stir it well. By this time the chicken will be cooked through. Turn off the flame and take it out into a bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9e8a4c4590a02787790596','5e33f831985ffca18ae8fb8f',1,'P1: Chop & prep the ingredients','For Rainbow Salad, wash, peel and cut 1/4 cup of carrot into juliennes. Wash, peel and finely slice 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and cut 1/4 cup of green capsicum into juliennes. Wash and cut 1/4 cup of yellow capsicum into juliennes. Wash, peel and cut 1/4 cup of cucumber into juliennes.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9e8a6f77c5bbfa41905f1e','5e33f831985ffca18ae8fb8f',2,'P2: Prep the ingredients','For Rainbow Salad, wash and cut a small tomato into halves then remove the seeds and cut it into juliennes. Squeeze 1 teaspoon of lime juice using a lemon squeezer. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash and finely chop 1 nos green chili.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9e8ad94590a02787790598','5e33f831985ffca18ae8fb8f',3,'M1: Combine the vegetables','To make Rainbow Salad, in a large mixing bowl, add 1/4 cup of carrot juliennes, 1/4 cup of cucumber juliennes, and 1/4 cup of sliced onions. Next, add 1/4 cup of green capsicum juliennes, 1/4 cup of tomato juliennes along with 1/4 cup of julienned yellow capsicum.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9e8aff4590a02787790599','5e33f831985ffca18ae8fb8f',4,'M2: Season the salad. Garnish & serve','Next, add 1 nos chopped green chili and 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves to the salad. Season it with 1/4 teaspoon of salt. Add 1/4 teaspoon of red chili powder and mix it well. Then, add 1 teaspoon of lime juice and mix it well. Transfer the Rainbow Salad in a bowl and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9e8b7977c5bbfa41905f1f','5e33f999057fd3f6fc80ef9b',1,'P1: Whisk the eggs & prep the ingredients','To make a Mixed Veg Omelette, wash and julienne 1/4 cup of green capsicum, 1/4 cup of red capsicum, and 1/4 cup of yellow capsicum. Peel and slice 1/4 cup of onion. Wash and slice 1/4 cup of mushroom. Grate 3 tbsp of mozzarella cheese. Wash and roughly chop 1 cup of spinach leaves. Whisk 4 eggs together in a bowl.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9e8ba077c5bbfa41905f20','5e33f999057fd3f6fc80ef9b',2,'M1: Saute the vegetables','For a Mixed Veg Omelette, heat 1 tbsp of cooking oil in a large pan for 1 min. Next add 1/4 cup of green capsicum, 1/4 cup of red capsicum, 1/4 cup of yellow capsicum, 1/4 cup of onions, and 1/4 cup of mushroom. Saute this occasionally for 5 mins. Then, add 1/4 tsp of salt and mix well. After this, put the vegetables on a plate and set them aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e9e8bc684eb5c1cc4e907d0','5e33f999057fd3f6fc80ef9b',3,'M2: Fry the spinach leaves','Next, in the same pan add 1 cup of spinach leaves and 1/4 tsp of salt, cook this for 2-3 mins on medium flame. Once the spinach has wilted, put it on the same plate with the other vegetables, and move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9e8c0a84eb5c1cc4e907d1','5e33f999057fd3f6fc80ef9b',4,'M3: Cook the whisked eggs with sauteed vegetables.','Next, in the same pan, heat 1 tbsp of oil and pour in the 2 whisked eggs, ensure it is spread evenly on the pan. Once the edges begin to cook add 1/4 cup of the cooked vegetable to one side of the omelette. Next, add the 3 tbsp of grated cheese on top of the vegetables, and let this cook for 2 mins. Next, close the omelette and let it cook for 1 min and then flip it to cook it on the other side for 1 min. Put your omlette on a plate and serve. Repeat this process for the remaining whisked eggs.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9e8c2977c5bbfa41905f21','5e3ba3c54f28558c29df655e',7,'M4: Cook Tomatoes','After frying the spices, add 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes. Saute and cook the tomatoes on medium-low flame for 1-2 minutes. Then, add the fried potatoes and mix it well. Cover it with a lid and simmer the potatoes for a minute. After simmering the potatoes, take off the lid and add 3/4 cup of water. Mix it well and cover it with a lid. Continue to simmer the potatoes for another 2-3 minutes on low flame. While the potatoes are simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":4,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e9e8c5a77c5bbfa41905f22','5e3ba3c54f28558c29df655e',8,'M5: Season the Dish','After simmering the potatoes, take off the lid and add 1/2 teaspoon of salt along with the fried cauliflower florets. Mix it well and cover it with a lid. Simmer the dalna for 6-7 minutes, until the florets are completely cooked. While it is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":7,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e9e8c7e77c5bbfa41905f23','5e3ba3c54f28558c29df655e',9,'M6: Final Touches','After simmering the Aloo Gobhi Dalna, take off the lid and add 1/2 cup of boiled green peas. Mix it well and cook it on low flame for 1-2 minutes, while stirring in between. Then, turn off the flame and garnish it with 1/2 teaspoon of ghee and 1 slit green chilies.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('5e9e8ca084eb5c1cc4e907d2','5e33fb384f28558c29df64ff',1,'P1: Marinate the fish fillets','To make masala grilled fish, clean 400 grams of rohu fish and cut the fish into slices. Wash and roughly chop 1 tbsp of coriander leaves. Wash and chop 1 tbsp of curry leaves. Next, in a large bowl marinate the 400 grams of fish with 1/2 tsp of turmeric powder, 2 tsp of red chili powder,1 tsp of coriander powder, 1/2 tsp of garam masala, 1 tsp of salt, 1 tbsp of ginger-garlic paste, 2 tsp of lime juice, 1 tbsp of chopped coriander, 1 tbsp of curry leaves, and 2 tbsp of oil. Mix all the ingredients well, cover the bowl, and let the fish marinate for 1 hour.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":60,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9e8cd477c5bbfa41905f24','5e33fb384f28558c29df64ff',2,'M1: Char & grill the fish.','For Masala Grilled Fish, heat 1 tbsp of cooking oil in a frying pan for 1 min. Next, place the marinated fish on the pan, let it cook for 3 min on medium flame and then for another 3 mins on low flame. Then, flip the pieces of fish, cook for 3 mins on medium flame, and then another 3 mins on low flame. Flip the fish again and cook on each side for 2 mins on low flame. Once this is done, turn off the flame, and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9e8d634590a0278779059a','5e33fc5c985ffca18ae8fb92',1,'P1: Chop the ladies fingers & prep the ingredients','To make Kerala Bhindi Stir-Fry, first, wash and dry 1 cup of lady''s finger. Allow the lady''s finger to dry completely before you begin chopping it. While they are drying, dry and slice 1/2 cup of shallots. Wash 7 curry leaves, wash and roughly chop 2 green chilies, grate 1 tbsp of coconut, and peel and finely chop 1 tsp of garlic. Once the lady''s finger has dried completely, trim the edges and slice them.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9e8e7384eb5c1cc4e907d3','5e33fc5c985ffca18ae8fb92',2,'M1: Simmer the ladies fingers. Garnish & serve','For Kerala Bhindi Stir-Fry, heat 1 tbsp of coconut oil in a kadai for 1 min. Next, add 1/4 tsp of urad dal, 1/4 tsp of mustard seeds, and let this splutter for a few seconds. Then, add 1/2 cup of sliced shallots, 7 curry leaves, 2 chopped green chilies, and saute for 2-3 mins. Once the onions are translucent, add 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder, 1 tsp of red chili powder, and mix well. Next, add 1 cup of sliced lady''s finger and saute for 2 mins. Then, add 1/2 tsp of salt and mix well. Next, cover the kadai with a lid and cook the sabzi for 15 mins on low flame. Once this is complete, add 1 tsp of chopped garlic, 1 tbsp of grated coconut, and mix well. Turn off the flame, and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9e8ed284eb5c1cc4e907d4','5e37cc26057fd3f6fc80efae',1,'P1: Prep the ingredients','To make Guava and Cucumber Chaat, first, wash and dice 2 guavas. Wash and dice 1/2 cup of cucumber. Peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and dice 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Wash and finely chop 1/4 tsp of green chili. Roughly chop 1 tbsp of cashew nuts. Wash and roughly chop 1 tbsp of coriander leaves. Squeeze 2 tsp of lemon juice.','prep_method','{"active_time":11,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9e8f1484eb5c1cc4e907d5','5e37cc26057fd3f6fc80efae',2,'M1: Combine the chat. Garnish & serve','For guava and cucumber chaat, in a large mixing bowl add 2 diced guavas, 1/2 cup of chopped cucumber, 1/4 cup of chopped onions, 1/4 cup of tomatoes, 1/4 tsp of green chili, 1/2 tsp of chaat masala, 2 tsp of lime juice, 1/2 tsp of salt, and mix well. Once the ingredients are combined well add1 tbsp cashew nuts and 1 tbsp of coriander leaves and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9e8f914590a0278779059b','5e37cd384f28558c29df6514',1,'P1: Pressure cook the dal','To cook the dal for Dal Palak, first, rinse half a cup of masoor dal well with water. Next, rinse half a cup of toor dal well with water. Next, to a pressure cooker add half a cup of masoor dal followed by half a cup of toor dal. Add 2 cups of water along with half a teaspoon of salt and a 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder. Cover the pressure cooker with a lid and pressure cook the dal on high flame till one whistle. After that, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook it for another 8 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow it cool down completely. While the dal is cooking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9e8fb24590a0278779059c','5e37cd384f28558c29df6514',2,'P2: Chop & prep the ingredients','For Dal Palak, Wash and chop 1.5 cups of spinach leaves. Peel, wash and finely chop half a cup of onions. Wash and finely chop half a cup of tomatoes. Wash, peel and finely chop a 1-inch piece of ginger. Wash, peel, and julienne a 1-inch of a piece of ginger. Peel, wash and finely chop 1 teaspoon of garlic. Wash and finely chop 1 nos green chili.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9e8fd24590a0278779059d','5e37cd384f28558c29df6514',3,'M1: Fry the onions','To make the Dal Palak, heat 2 teaspoons of ghee in a kadai over medium flame for a minute. Add 1/4 teaspoon of hing followed by 1 teaspoon of chopped garlic and a 1-inch piece of chopped ginger. Saute it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Then, add half a cup of chopped onions and fry it for 3-4 minutes until it turns translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9e8ff04590a0278779059e','5e37cd384f28558c29df6514',4,'M2: Cook the masala','After frying the onions, add 1 nos chopped green chili, 1 teaspoon of red chili powder and 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala followed by 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder and half a teaspoon of salt. Mix it well and fry the masala over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Next, add half a cup of chopped tomatoes and mix it well. Saute and cook the tomatoes for 4-5 minutes, until it turns tender. Make sure to cook the masala until oil separates.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e9e901f84eb5c1cc4e907d6','5e37cd384f28558c29df6514',5,'M3: Add spinach leaves & simmer the dal. Garnish & serve','As the oil separates from the masala, add 1.5 cups of chopped spinach leaves and mix it well. Saute and cook the spinach leaves with the masala over medium-low flame for 1-2 minutes. Make sure not to overcook the spinach leaves or it may turn dark. After frying the spinach leaves, add the prepared dal and mix it well. Cook the dal over medium-high flame and bring it to a boil. Then, turn off the flame and take it out into a serving bowl. Garnish it with chopped ginger juliennes and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e9e906077c5bbfa41905f25','5e3b9f03985ffca18ae8fbdf',1,'P1: Cook Pumpkin','To cook the pumpkin for Pumpkin Poriyal, first, wash, peel and cube 1 cup of pumpkin. Next, add the cubed pumpkin pieces to a pan along with 1/4 cup of water, just enough to cover the bottom of the pan. Season it with half a teaspoon of salt. Cover it with a lid and let it simmer for 12-15 minutes or until fork-tender. While the pumpkin is simmering, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e9e907e4590a0278779059f','5e3b9f03985ffca18ae8fbdf',2,'P2: Prep Ingredients','For Pumpkin Poriyal, wash, peel and finely slice 1/2 cup of shallots. Wash and chop 2 nos green chilies. Grate half a cup of fresh coconut using a grater. Wash 7 nos curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9e90a384eb5c1cc4e907d7','5e3b9f03985ffca18ae8fbdf',3,'P3: Make Coconut Paste','To make the coconut paste for Pumpkin Poriyal, in a blender jar, add half a cup of grated coconut, 2 nos chopped green chilies and 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder and blend it to a coarse paste. Add a little water to it and blend it again to a fine paste. Then, take it out into a bowl and set it aside. After simmering the pumpkins, take off the lid and check if it is cooked through. Then, turn off the flame and take it out into a bowl.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9e90cb77c5bbfa41905f26','5e3b9f03985ffca18ae8fbdf',4,'M1: Cook Spices and Shallots','To make the Pumpkin Poriyal, heat 1 tablespoon of coconut oil in a kadai on a medium flame for a minute. Add half a teaspoon of mustard seeds and half a teaspoon of cumin seeds, allow it to splutter for a few seconds. Next, add half a cup of sliced shallots followed by 7 nos curry leaves and saute it on a medium flame for 3-4 minutes, until it turns translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e9e90f777c5bbfa41905f27','5e3b9f03985ffca18ae8fbdf',5,'M2: Continue cooking to make Poriyal','After frying the shallots, add the cooked pumpkin and mix it well with the shallots. Next, add the prepared coconut paste and gently mix it. Stir fry on a medium flame for a minute. Season it with a quarter teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Stir and cook the pumpkin on medium-high flame for 3-4 minutes until the raw smell of the ground masala disappears. Then, turn off the flame and garnish it with a tablespoon of grated coconut and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e9e91bd84eb5c1cc4e907d8','5e3b9caf057fd3f6fc80eff2',1,'P1: Make Idli','To make Podi Idli, you will need 6 cooked idlis, if you have any leftover idlis you can use them or you can start by making 6 idlis. Begin by coating the molds with oil and then pour in 1/4 cup of idli batter. Allow the idlis to steam for 10 mins. Let them cool down before you take them out of the molds. While the idlis are steaming move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9e91e684eb5c1cc4e907d9','5e3b9caf057fd3f6fc80eff2',2,'P2: Prep Ingredients','For Idli Upma, wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Grate 2 tablespoons of fresh coconut using a grater. Wash 1 lime and cut it into halves, then squeeze 2 teaspoons of lime juice using a lemon squeezer. Wash 8 nos curry leaves well with water. Next, to crumble the idlis, first, in a large mixing bowl, add 6 nos leftover idlis. Then, crumble the idlis one by one into fine crumbs and set it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9e921477c5bbfa41905f28','5e3b9caf057fd3f6fc80eff2',3,'M1: Cooking','To make the Idli Upma, heat 1 tablespoon of coconut oil in a kadai on a medium flame for a minute. Add 1 teaspoon of mustard seeds, 1 teaspoon of urad dal, and 1 teaspoon of chana dal followed by 1 teaspoon of cumin seeds and 1 dry red chili. Next, add 8 nos curry leaves and 1 slit green chili. Saute and let the tempering splutter. Next, add the crumbled idlis along with half a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Add 2 tablespoons of grated coconut and cover it with a lid and allow it to simmer for 3 minutes. While the idli upma is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9e923484eb5c1cc4e907da','5e3b9caf057fd3f6fc80eff2',4,'M2: Final Touches','After simmering the Idli Upma, take off the lid and mix it well. Stir and saute it for a minute on medium flame. Then, turn off the flame and add 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves followed by 2 teaspoons of lime juice and mix it well. Take it out in a plate and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('5e9e930e4590a027877905a0','5e3a9a22057fd3f6fc80efe3',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Beetroot Soup, wash, peel and cube 1.5 cups of beetroot. Wash, peel and cut 2 nos pearl onions into halves. Wash, peel and cut 1/4 cup of carrots into cubes. Wash and chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Peel 2 cloves of garlic. Wash and peel a 1-inch piece of ginger. Wash 4 nos mint leaves. Crush 1 teaspoon of black peppercorns to a coarse powder using a pepper grinder.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9e933c84eb5c1cc4e907db','5e3a9a22057fd3f6fc80efe3',2,'M1: Cook Vegetables','To cook the vegetables for Beetroot Soup, heat 1 teaspoon of butter in a pressure cooker on low flame for 30 seconds. Add 1 nos bay leaf and saute it for a few seconds until aromatic. Next, add 2 cloves of garlic, 1-inch piece of ginger and 2 nos halved pearl onions, saute the onions on medium-high flame for 2 minutes. Next, add 1.5 cups of cubed beetroot, 1/4 cup of cubed carrots, 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes and stir fry the vegetables on high flame for 2 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9e935c84eb5c1cc4e907dc','5e3a9a22057fd3f6fc80efe3',3,'M2: Pressure Cook the Vegetables','After frying the vegetables, add 1/2 teaspoon of salt and 2 cups of water. Stir it well. Cover it with a lid and pressure cook the vegetables on high flame for 4 whistles. After 4 whistles, reduce to low flame and continue to cook it for another 5 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the vegetables are cooking, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9e93864590a027877905a1','5e3a9a22057fd3f6fc80efe3',4,'M3: Blend Vegetables into a Puree','For the Beetroot Soup, after the pressure from the cooker has been released, take off the lid and drain the water from the vegetables using a strainer. Set the beetroot water aside to be used further in the soup. Allow the cooked vegetables to cool down completely. Then, transfer the vegetables to a blender jar, remove the bay leaf and blend it to a smooth puree.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9e93ac4590a027877905a2','5e3a9a22057fd3f6fc80efe3',5,'M4: Final Touches','To make the Beetroot Soup, transfer the prepared beetroot puree to a saucepan. Add the beetroot water and stir it well. Add 1 teaspoon of crushed black pepper and bring it to a boil on high flame. After a boil, turn off the flame and garnish the soup with 1 teaspoon of fresh cream and mint leaves. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e9e945177c5bbfa41905f29','5e3a9871057fd3f6fc80efe1',1,'P1: Boil Eggs','To boil the eggs for Avocado Deviled Eggs, add 2 cups of water into a saucepan and bring it to a rolling boil on high flame. Then, add 1/4 teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Add 3 nos eggs to the boiling water and boil it on medium-high flame for 10-12 minutes. While the eggs are boiling, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":4}'),('5e9e947784eb5c1cc4e907dd','5e3a9871057fd3f6fc80efe1',2,'P2: Prep Ingredients','For Avocado Deviled Eggs, wash, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Wash and cut an avocado into two halves. Then, remove the seed and scoop out the pulp using a spoon. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of cilantro. Wash and cut a lemon into two halves. Then, squeeze out the juice using a lemon squeezer. Next, after boiling the eggs, turn off the flame and dip it in the cold water. This will help peel off the shell without any hassle. Then, gently peel off the shell.','prep_method','{"active_time":14,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9e94ef77c5bbfa41905f2a','5e3a9871057fd3f6fc80efe1',3,'M1: Prep Eggs','To make the stuffing for Avocado Deviled Eggs, first, cut the boiled eggs into two halves. Then, scoop out the yolk from it and keep it in a bowl. Keep the egg white halves aside for later use. Next, add the avocado pulp to the egg yolks, followed by 1 tablespoon of lime juice. Mash the avocado pulp and egg yolks using a spoon and mix it well. Next, add a teaspoon of salt and 1 tablespoon of chopped cilantro followed by 1/4 cup of chopped onions and 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes. Then, mix it well and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9e95144590a027877905a3','5e3a9871057fd3f6fc80efe1',4,'M2: Make the Deviled Eggs','To make the Avocado Deviled Eggs, take a tablespoon of the prepared avocado mixture and spoon it into the egg whites. Similarly, stuff the rest of the egg whites with the avocado mixture, as shown. Garnish the deviled eggs with 1/4 teaspoon of paprika and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9e96ba77c5bbfa41905f2b','5e3a9636985ffca18ae8fbd4',1,'P1: Boil Eggs','To boil the eggs for Egg Malai Masala, add 3 nos raw eggs in a deep bottom pan with 4 cups of water and bring it a boil on high flame. After a boil, continue to boil the eggs on medium-high flame for another 8 minutes. While the eggs are boiling, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":8,"flame":4}'),
('5e9e96f484eb5c1cc4e907de','5e3a9636985ffca18ae8fbd4',2,'P2: Prep Ingredients','For Egg Malai Masala, wash, peel and cut 2 nos small-sized onions into quarters. Wash 3 nos green chilies. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves. Crush 1/2 teaspoon of black peppercorns to a coarse powder using a pepper grinder.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9e971a84eb5c1cc4e907df','5e3a9636985ffca18ae8fbd4',3,'P3: Make Onion Paste','For Egg Malai Masala, to make the onion paste, in a blender jar, add 3/4 cups of chopped onions and 2 nos slit green chilies and blend it to a smooth paste. After boiling the eggs, turn off the flame, take out the boiled eggs and instantly put it in cold water, this will help peel off the shell easily.  Then, gently peel off the eggshells and cut it into halves.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9e97434590a027877905a4','5e3a9636985ffca18ae8fbd4',4,'M1: Temper Spices','To make the Egg Malai Masala, heat 3 tablespoons of cooking oil in a pan on a medium flame for a minute. Add 1 teaspoon of cumin seeds and let it splutter for a few seconds. Then, add the prepared onion paste and saute it on medium-low flame for 5-6 minutes, till the onion paste turns slightly golden.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9e97674590a027877905a5','5e3a9636985ffca18ae8fbd4',5,'M2: Continue Cooking','After frying the onion paste, add 1 teaspoon of ginger-garlic paste and saute it for 1-2 minutes on medium-high flame. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of crushed black peppercorns, 1/2 teaspoon of garam masala, 1 teaspoon of salt, and 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder along with 1/2 cup of water and mix it well. Add 3 nos halved boiled eggs and 1/2 cup of milk and stir it well. Allow the curry to cook on medium-low flame for 2-3 minutes. While the curry is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9e978677c5bbfa41905f2c','5e3a9636985ffca18ae8fbd4',6,'M3: Final Touches','After simmering the curry for Egg Malai Masala, turn off the flame and pour 3 tablespoons of fresh cream over it. Garnish it with 2 tablespoons of chopped coriander leaves. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('5e9e987877c5bbfa41905f2d','5e3a9562057fd3f6fc80efdf',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Brinji Rice, add 3/4 cup of basmati rice to a bowl and soak it in 1 cup of water. Next, wash, peel and finely slice 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Wash and slit 1 nos green chili. Wash and roughly chop 4 nos beans. Wash, peel and cube 1/4 cup of carrot. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of mint leaves. Wash, peel and cube 1/4 cup of potatoes. Wash and cut 1/4 cup of cauliflower into florets. Wash 8 nos curry leaves well with water.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9e98974590a027877905a6','5e3a9562057fd3f6fc80efdf',2,'P2: Make Mint Paste','To make the mint paste for Brinji Rice, first, rinse 1/4 cup of mint leaves well with water. Rinse 1/4 cup of coriander leaves well with water. Next, to a blender jar, add 1/4 cup of coriander leaves and 1/4 cup of mint leaves. Add 1 nos green cardamom and 2 nos cloves followed by 1/2 an inch piece of cinnamon stick and half a teaspoon of fennel seeds. Add 2 tablespoons of water and blend it well into a fine paste.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9e98c977c5bbfa41905f2e','5e3a9562057fd3f6fc80efdf',3,'M1: Cook Spices and Vegetables','To make Brinji Rice, heat 1.5 tablespoons of ghee in a pressure cooker. Add 2 nos bay leaves, 1 nos star anise and 1 nos green cardamom. Saute it on a medium flame for a minute. Next, add 1/4 cup of sliced onions and fry it on a medium flame for 2-3 minutes, until it turns slightly translucent. After that, add 1 teaspoon of ginger-garlic paste and fry it on a medium flame for a minute. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes and mix it well. Saute and cook the tomatoes on medium flame for 3-4 minutes until it turns tender.','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9e98e94590a027877905a7','5e3a9562057fd3f6fc80efdf',4,'M2: Add other Vegetables','After cooking the tomatoes, add 1/4 cup of chopped carrots, 1/4 cup of green peas and 1/4 cup of cubed potatoes followed by 1/4 cup of cauliflower florets and 4 nos chopped beans. Season it with a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Stir and fry the vegetables on a medium flame for a minute. Next, add the prepared mint paste along with 8 nos curry leaves and mix it well. Saute and cook the masala with the vegetables for another 2 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9e991a4590a027877905a8','5e3a9562057fd3f6fc80efdf',5,'M3: Pressure Cook Brinji Rice','After frying the vegetables with the masala, add half a cup of water followed by 3/4 cup of coconut milk and mix it well. Keep stirring it on low flame as the coconut milk might split. After it is well combined, bring it to a boil on high flame. As it comes to a boil, add the soaked basmati rice to it and mix it well. Add 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and mint leaves and mix it well. Cover it with a lid and pressure cook it on high flame until the first whistle. After that, reduce it to low flame and continue to cook it for another 8 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the Brinji Rice is cooking, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e9e99324590a027877905a9','5e3a9562057fd3f6fc80efdf',6,'M4: Serve','After cooking the Brinji Rice, take off the lid from the pressure cooker and gently mix it. Then, take it out in a bowl and serve','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9e9ed14590a027877905aa','5e37cf31985ffca18ae8fba9',1,'AP1: Soak the beans','To make a Brown Rice Burrito Bowl, soak 1/4 cup of kidney beans in 3/4 cup of water for 8 hours.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":480,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9e9efc77c5bbfa41905f2f','5e37cf31985ffca18ae8fba9',2,'P1: Pressure cook the kidney beans','To make a Brown Rice Burrito Bowl, first, cook 1/4 cup of soaked kidney beans in a pressure cooker with 3/4 cup of water, 1/2 tsp of salt, and 1/2 tsp of oil. Cook the beans on high flame for 3 whistles and then on low flame for 8 mins. Once this is complete wait for the pressure to release naturally from the cooker before you open it. While the beans are cooking please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9e9f234590a027877905ab','5e37cf31985ffca18ae8fba9',3,'P2: Simmer the rice','Next, wash 3/4 cup of rice well, cook it in a deep pan with 1.5 cups of water for 40 mins. While the rice is cooking move on the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":40,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e9e9f474590a027877905ac','5e37cf31985ffca18ae8fba9',4,'P3: Prep the ingredients','Next, peel and finely chop 1/2 cup of onion. Wash and roughly chop 1/2 cup of tomatoes. Wash and finely chop 1 green chili. Peel and deseed 1 avocado. Wash and roughly chop 1/4 cup of coriander leaves. Peel and finely chop 2 teaspoons of garlic. Squeeze 2 tbsp of lime juice.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9e9f784590a027877905ad','5e37cf31985ffca18ae8fba9',5,'M1: Make tomato salsa','For Brown Rice Burrito Bowl, make the tomato salsa, first in a mixing bowl, add 1/2 cup of chopped tomatoes, 2 tbsp of chopped coriander leaves, 2 tbsp of chopped onions, 1/2 a chopped green chili,  a teaspoon of chopped garlic, a tsp of lime juice, 1/2 tsp of salt, 1/4 tsp of black pepper powder, and mix well. Once this is done, set it aside and move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9e9f9f84eb5c1cc4e907e0','5e37cf31985ffca18ae8fba9',6,'M2: Make Guacomole','Next, prepare the guacamole, first in a blending jar, add 1 avocado, 2 tbsp of chopped onions, 1/2 a chopped green chili, 1 chopped clove of garlic, 2 tbsp of lime juice, 1/2 tsp of salt, 1/4 tsp of black pepper powder, 2 tbsp of coriander leaves, and blend this until you have a coarse paste. Once this is ready set it aside and move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9e9ffb84eb5c1cc4e907e1','5e37cf31985ffca18ae8fba9',7,'M3: Make Mexican Rice','Next, prepare the Mexican rice, in a saucepan heat 1 tbsp of coconut oil and then add 1/4 cup of chopped onions and 2 cloves of chopped garlic. Saute this for 3 mins and then add 1/2 tsp of paprika, 1/2 tsp of cumin powder, 1 tsp of coriander powder, 1/2 tsp of oregano, 1/2 tsp of red chili powder, and 1/4 tsp of cinnamon powder. Saute this for 1 min, you can add 2 tbsp of water if the pan is too dry. Next, add 1/4 cup of cooked kidney beans, 1/4 cup of sweet corn kernels, 1 tbsp of tomato puree, 2 tbsp of water, and mix well. Then, add 2 tbsp of lime juice, 3/4 cup of cooked rice, and mix well. Saute this for another minute and then turn off the flame and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9ea02177c5bbfa41905f30','5e37cf31985ffca18ae8fba9',8,'M4: Assemble the Burrtio Bowl','Next, assemble the burrito bowls. In a serving bowl add 1/4 cup of the Mexican rice, 2 tbsp the tomato salsa, 2 tbsp the guacamole, and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9ea1054590a027877905ae','5e37cfd7985ffca18ae8fbab',1,'P1: Prep the ingredients','To make Coconut Milk Fish Curry, first, wash and clean 400 grams of Seer fish fillets. Peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Peel and julienne 1 inch of ginger. Peel and slice 3 cloves of garlic. Wash and slit 2 green chilies. Wash and roughly chop 1/2 cup of tomatoes. Wash 10 curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9ea14d4590a027877905af','5e37cfd7985ffca18ae8fbab',2,'M1: Cook the masala','For Coconut milk fish curry, heat 1 tbsp of coconut oil in a kadai on medium flame. Next, add 1 tsp of mustard seeds and let it splutter for a few seconds. Then add 1/4 cup of chopped onions, 3 cloves of sliced garlic, 1 inch of julienned ginger, 2 slit green chilies, 5 curry leaves, and saute this for 2-3 mins. Once the onions are golden add 1/2 cup of chopped tomatoes and saute this for 2 mins until the tomatoes are soft. Then, add 1 tsp of rock salt, 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder, 1/2 ts of red chili powder, 1 tsp of coriander powder, 1/2 tsp of cumin powder, and mix well.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9ea19884eb5c1cc4e907e2','5e37cfd7985ffca18ae8fbab',3,'M2: Add coconut milk & simmer the fish curry','Next, add 1/2 cup of water, mix well, and once the water begins to boil gently add the 400 grams of seer fish fillet. Cover the kadai with a lid and let it simmer for 10 mins. After this is complete, flip the fish fillets and cook them for another 2 mins. Next, add 1.5 cups of coconut milk and gently stir the curry ensuring not to break any of the fish pieces. Next, add 5 curry leaves and cover the kadai again, let it simmer for another 5 mins. Once this is done, pour the curry into a serving bowl, and enjoy!','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":17,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e9ea3b984eb5c1cc4e907e7','5e37e881057fd3f6fc80efb1',1,'P1: Soak the soya chunks','To make soya chunk salad, soak 3/4 cup of soya chunks in 1 cup of hot water for 5 mins. Next, whisk 1/2 cup of curd and remove all lumps. After 5 mins squeeze out any excess water from the soya chunks and move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9ea3ec4590a027877905b2','5e37e881057fd3f6fc80efb1',2,'P2: Marinate the soaked soya chunks','Next, marinate the soya chunks in a bowl with 1/2 tsp of pink salt, 1/4 tsp of cumin powder, 1/2 tsp of pepper powder, 1 tsp of olive oil, 1/2 tsp of mixed herbs, 1/2 tsp of dry mint, and 1/2 cup of whisked curd. Mix all the ingredients together and let it marinate for 30 mins.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":30,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9ea42684eb5c1cc4e907e8','5e37e881057fd3f6fc80efb1',3,'P3: Prep the ingredients','Next, wash and roughly chop 1/4 cup of beans and 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Peel and roughly chop 1/4 cup of carrots. Wash and dice 1/4 cup of pumpkin. Grate 2 tbsp of fresh coconut.','prep_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9ea4744590a027877905b3','5e37e881057fd3f6fc80efb1',4,'M1: Blanch the vegetables & season','For soya chunk salad, heat 2 tbsp of water on a pan. Then add 1/4 cup of chopped beans, 1/4 cup of chopped carrot, and 1/4 cup of chopped pumpkin. Cover this with a lid and let it cook for 5 mins. After that, take off the lid and season it with 1/4 tsp of mixed herbs, 1/4 tsp of dry mint, 1/4 tsp pepper powder, 1/4 tsp of salt, and mix well. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped tomato and saute this for 1 min. After this turn off the flame and let the vegetables cool down.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9ea4a384eb5c1cc4e907e9','5e37e881057fd3f6fc80efb1',5,'M2: Combine the salad. Garnish & serve','Once the vegetables are cool add them to the marinated soya chunks and mix everything together. Garnish the salad with 2 tbsp of grated coconut and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9ea65777c5bbfa41905f31','5e37eab3985ffca18ae8fbae',1,'P1: Prep the ingredients','To make Grilled Fish, clean 2 fillets of Basa Fish and then season it with 1/2 tsp of salt and 1/2 a tsp of black pepper powder. After this, set the fish aside and in a blending jar blend 1/4 cup of onion into a puree. Wash and roughly chop 1 tbsp of parsley.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9ea6b584eb5c1cc4e907ea','5e37eab3985ffca18ae8fbae',2,'M1: Coat the fish fillet with refined flour & grill the fish','For Grilled Fish, sprinkle 1/4 cup of all purpose flour on a plate and coat the 2 fish fillets in flour. Next, heat 1 tbsp of cooking oil in a frying pan on medium flame and then add 1/4 cup of pureed onion and 1 tbsp of garlic paste. Saute this for 1 min, then add the basa fillets to the pan and cook it on each side for 3 mins. Once the fillets are golden brown, add 1 tbsp lime juice, 2 tbsp of water, and 1 tbsp of butter. Once the butter has melted, add 1 tbsp of chopped parsley and using a spoon pour the butter mixture on top of the fillets. Do this for 1 min on each side and then turn off the flame. Place both fillets on serving plates, pour 1 tsp of butter on each fillet, and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":11,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":4,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9ea88d84eb5c1cc4e907eb','5e37f0a44f28558c29df6521',1,'P1: Marinate the fish','To prepare Goan Fish Curry, start by washing 350 grams of Basa fillets. Marinate them for 1 hour with 1/2 tsp of salt.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":60,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9ea8b54590a027877905b6','5e37f0a44f28558c29df6521',2,'P2: Prep the ingredients','For Goan Fish Curry, peel 5 cloves of garlic and 1/2 inch piece of ginger. Soak 1/2 tsp of tamarind in 2 tbsp of warm water and let this rest for 1 min. Then mash the tamarind with the water to create a pulpy extract. Peel and finely chop 1/4 cups of onion. Wash and slit 2 green chilies.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9ea91184eb5c1cc4e907ec','5e37f0a44f28558c29df6521',3,'P3: Prepare the coconut paste','Next, in a blending jar add 1/4 cup of fresh coconut, 6 dry Kashmiri red chilies, 5 cloves of garlic, 1/2 inch piece of ginger, 1/2 tsp of cumin seeds, 3 black peppercorns, 1 tbsp of coriander seeds, 1/4 tsp turmeric powder, the prepared tamarind pulp, and 1/2 cup of water. Blend this into a smooth paste.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9ea9384590a027877905b7','5e37f0a44f28558c29df6521',4,'M1: Simmer the curry. Garnish & serve','For Goan Fish Curry, heat 1 tbsp of oil in a pan on medium flame. Once warm add 1/4 cup of chopped onions, 1/2 tsp of salt and 2 slit green chilies, and saute for 3 mins. After this, add the prepare masala paste and mix it well. Fry this for 2-3 mins on low flame. Next, add 1/4 cup of water, give it a stir, and then add 4 pieces of dry kokum to the curry. Bring this to a boil and then add the marinated fillets of fish. Cover the pan with a lid and let it cook on a medium flame for 5 mins. After this remove the lid and gently stir the curry so you do not break the fillets of fish. Let the curry boil for another 2 mins to thicken the curry. Next, turn off the flame, pour the curry into a serving dish, and enjoy.','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e9ea95e4590a027877905b8','5e3a940b4f28558c29df6546',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Pundi Undi, grate 2 tablespoons of fresh coconut using a grater. Wash 5 nos curry leaves. Break 1 nos dry red chili into small pieces.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9ea9994590a027877905b9','5e3a940b4f28558c29df6546',2,'M1: Roast Spices and Rava','To make Pundi Undi, heat 1.5 teaspoons of cooking oil in a pan on a medium flame for a minute. Add 1/4 teaspoon of mustard seeds, 1/4 teaspoon of urad dal, 1/4 teaspoon of fenugreek seeds, 1 dry red chili, and 5 curry leaves. Saute and let it splutter on a medium flame for a few seconds. Next, add 1/4 cup of semolina and roast it on low flame for 5 minutes, until it turns aromatic. Keep stirring it continuously to prevent it from getting burnt. Meanwhile, boil 1 cup of water in a saucepan on medium-high flame for 2-3 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e9ea9c94590a027877905ba','5e3a940b4f28558c29df6546',3,'M2: Make Dough','After roasting the semolina, add 2 tablespoons of grated coconut along with 1/2 teaspoon of salt and saute it for a minute. Then, add 1 cup of hot water and mix it well, ensure there are no lumps. Keep stirring it continuously on medium-low flame for 3-4 minutes, till it comes together, forms a smooth dough and separates from the pan. Then, turn off the flame and let it cool down a bit.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9ea9e777c5bbfa41905f34','5e3a940b4f28558c29df6546',4,'M3: Make Pundi Undi','For Pundi Undi, after the semolina mixture cools down, make 8 nos small lemon sized balls from the mixture with wet hands and make a small impression in the center of each ball as shown. Next, place these balls in the steamer, cover it with a lid and let it steam on medium-high flame for 15 minutes. After steaming the balls, take off the lid and turn off the heat. Take out the Pundi Undi on a plate and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":15,"flame":0}'),('5e9eaa6284eb5c1cc4e907ed','5e3a91e7985ffca18ae8fbd3',1,'P1: Cook Dal','For Mysore Rasam, soak 1 tablespoon of tamarind in 1/2 cup of water for 15 minutes. Next, to cook the dal, wash 1/2 cup of toor dal well with water. Add the washed dal in a pressure cooker with 1 cup of water. Cover it with a lid and pressure cook it on high flame till one whistle. After the first whistle, reduce it to low flame and continue to cook it for another 8 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside and allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the dal is cooking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9eaac777c5bbfa41905f39','5e3a91e7985ffca18ae8fbd3',2,'P2: Prep Ingredients','For Mysore Rasam, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Wash and slit 1 nos green chili lengthwise. Wash 10 nos curry leaves. Grate 2 tablespoons of fresh coconut using a grater. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves.  After soaking the tamarind, mash it well with water and strain it using a strainer to remove the residue from the tamarind water.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9eabdc84eb5c1cc4e907ef','5e3a91e7985ffca18ae8fbd3',3,'P3: Make Rasam Powder (Optional)','To make the rasam powder for Mysore Rasam, heat a pan on medium flame for a minute. Add 1 teaspoon of coriander seeds, 1/4 teaspoon of cumin seeds, 1 teaspoon of chana dal, 1/4 teaspoon of black peppercorns and 1 dry kashmiri red chili. Dry roast the spices on low flame without adding any oil for 2-3 minutes, till it turns aromatic. Next, add 2 tablespoons of grated coconut and fry it for another minute on low flame, then turn off the flame and let the mixture cool down completely. After it cools down, transfer it to a blender jar and blend it well to a fine powder.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e9eac4677c5bbfa41905f3a','5e3a91e7985ffca18ae8fbd3',4,'M1: Cook Tomatoes','To make Mysore Rasam, in a kadai, add 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes and 1/2 cup of prepared tamarind water. Next, add 5 nos curry leaves, 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, 1/4 teaspoon of salt and 1/4 teaspoon of jaggery. Cover it with a lid and simmer it for 15 minutes. While the rasam is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":15,"flame":3}'),('5e9eac7277c5bbfa41905f3b','5e3a91e7985ffca18ae8fbd3',5,'M2: Add the Cooked Dal','After simmering the rasam, take off the lid and add 1/2 cup of cooked toor dal to it. Mix it well. Next, add 1 cup of water to adjust the consistency of the rasam and stir it well. Let it boil on high flame for a minute. Then, add 2 teaspoons of the prepared rasam powder and mix it well. Continue to boil the rasam for 2 minutes on high flame. Then, turn off the flame.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9eac9b77c5bbfa41905f3c','5e3a91e7985ffca18ae8fbd3',6,'M3: Make Tadka','To make the tempering for Mysore Rasam, heat 1 teaspoon of cooking oil in a tadka pan on a medium flame for a minute. Add 1/2 teaspoon of mustard seeds, 1/4 teaspoon of hing, 1dry red chili, and 5 nos curry leaves. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Then, turn off the flame and pour this tempering instantly over the prepared rasam. Garnish with 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9ead544590a027877905bc','5e37f5784f28558c29df6525',1,'P1: Knead & prepare the dough','To make Bajara Roti, first, in a mixing bowl add 1.5 cups of banjara flour, 1/4 tsp of salt, and mix this well. Next, gradually add 1/2 a cup of warm water and knead the dough for 10 mins until the dough is soft and smooth. Once the dough is ready you can move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9ead8e4590a027877905bd','5e37f5784f28558c29df6525',2,'M1: Divide the dough into dough balls & roll out the rotis','To make Bajara Roti, make small lemon sized balls from the dough. Place 1 dough ball on a rolling board and dust it with flour. Using your hands first flatten the dough ball and then roll it as thin as possible with a rolling pin into a disk shape. Repeat this process with all the other dough balls.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}');
INSERT INTO catalog_recipe_steps VALUES
('5e9eadb64590a027877905be','5e37f5784f28558c29df6525',3,'M2: Cook the rotis & serve','Next, heat a tawa for 1 min and then place 1 raw roti on the tawa. Let it cook for 1 min on one side and while it is cooking coat the other side with 1 tsp of water. Flip the roti and cook the other side for another minute. Cook the roti until both sides have browned evenly and then place the cooked roti on a plate. Repeat this process for the remaining raw rotis until they are all cooked.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9eadd177c5bbfa41905f3f','5e3a8a60057fd3f6fc80efda',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Capsicum Chutney, wash, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Wash and cut half a cup of green capsicum into medium cubes. Peel, wash and chop 2 cloves of garlic. Wash 8 nos curry leaves well with water.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9eadf74590a027877905bf','5e3a8a60057fd3f6fc80efda',2,'M1: Cook Spices and Onions','To make the Capsicum Chutney, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a pan on a medium flame for a minute. Add half a teaspoon of urad dal and chana dal followed by 2 cloves of chopped garlic and 2 nos dry Kashmiri red chilies. Saute and fry it on a medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions and fry it on a medium flame for 2-3 minutes, until it turns translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9eae2577c5bbfa41905f40','5e3a8a60057fd3f6fc80efda',3,'M2: Continue Cooking','After frying the onions, add 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes and mix it well. Saute and cook the tomatoes on a medium flame for 3-4 minutes, until it turns tender. After that, add half a cup of cubed capsicum and fry it on a medium flame for 2-3 minutes until tender. Then, turn off the flame and allow the mixture to cool down completely. While it is cooling down, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9eae4b77c5bbfa41905f41','5e3a8a60057fd3f6fc80efda',4,'M3: Blend into a Chutney','To make the Capsicum Chutney, transfer the prepared vegetable mixture to a blender jar. Add half a teaspoon of salt and 1/4 cup of water. Blend it well into a smooth chutney. Then, take it out in a bowl and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9eae6777c5bbfa41905f42','5e3a8a60057fd3f6fc80efda',5,'M4: Make Tadka','To make the tempering for Capsicum Chutney, heat a teaspoon of cooking oil in a small tempering pan. Add 1/4 teaspoon of mustard seeds and 1/4 teaspoon of urad dal followed by 1/4 teaspoon of hing and 8 nos curry leaves. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Then, turn off the flame and add this tempering instantly over the prepared chutney. Mix it well and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9eae714590a027877905c0','5e37fe744f28558c29df6527',1,'M1: Peel  the cucumber & battonet','Wash, peel & cut the cucumber into rectangular sticks as shown.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9eaedf77c5bbfa41905f43','5e37fee5057fd3f6fc80efbc',1,'M1: Make the fruit bowl','Wash and cut the fruits. Then, add the chopped fruits to a bowl and combine. Serve','cook_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9eaf1b77c5bbfa41905f44','5e3a86eb985ffca18ae8fbca',1,'AP1: Soak Rice and Dal for Dosa Batter','For Onion Uttapam, soak 3/4 cup of rice with 1/2 teaspoon of fenugreek seeds in 2 cups of water. Set it aside and allow the rice to soak in water for 5 hours. In a separate bowl, soak 1/4 cup of urad dal in 1 cup of water for 3 hours. While the rice and dal are soaking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":300,"advanced_prep_time":180,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9eaf494590a027877905c1','5e3a86eb985ffca18ae8fbca',2,'AP2: Blend to Make Dosa Batter','To make the batter for the Onion Uttapam,  Add the soaked dal to a blender and blend it well into a smooth paste. Transfer the urad dal batter in a large mixing bowl. Transfer the soaked rice in a blender and blend it into a coarse batter. Then transfer the rice batter to the urad dal batter. Wash 1/2 cup of puffed rice with water and squeeze the extra water from it. Transfer it to the blender and blend it into a smooth paste. Add the puffed rice paste to the rice batter and combine it well. Allow the uttapam batter to rest and ferment for another 8 hours. While the batter is fermenting, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":480,"advanced_prep_time":480,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9eaf6e84eb5c1cc4e907f1','5e37ff41985ffca18ae8fbaf',1,'AP1: Soak Almonds','Soak the almonds in water for 2 hours. Then, gently peel off the skin and use it as required.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":120,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9eaf7884eb5c1cc4e907f2','5e3a86eb985ffca18ae8fbca',3,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For the Onion Uttapam, wash, peel and finely chop 1/2 cup of onions. Wash, peel and finely chop 1/2 inch piece of ginger. Wash and finely chop 1 nos green chili. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash and finely chop 5 nos curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9eafa64590a027877905c2','5e3a86eb985ffca18ae8fbca',4,'P2: Mixing prepped Ingredients','To make the topping for Onion Uttapam, in a large mixing bowl, add 1/2 cup of chopped onions. Add 1 chopped green chili, 1/2 inch piece of chopped ginger, 1 tablespoon of chopped curry leaves and 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves to the bowl. Next, add 1 teaspoon of salt and mix it well.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9eafc64590a027877905c3','5e3a86eb985ffca18ae8fbca',5,'M1: Make Uttapam','To make Onion Uttapam, after resting the uttapam batter for 8 hours, it will ferment and doubles in size. Give the batter a gentle mix. Heat a tawa on medium flame for a minute. Pour 1 ladle full of batter on the hot tawa and spread it evenly, ensure the layer of the batter is slightly thick. After small bubbles start to appear on its surface, add 3 tablespoons of onion topping over the uttapam and spread it evenly. Press the onion topping gently with hand on the uttapam. Add 1 teaspoon of oil on it and cover it with a lid. Cook the uttapam on low flame for a minute. After thet, take off the lid and carefully flip the uttapam and cook on the other side on low flame for 2 minutes. Once cooked, carefully take it out scraping the sides and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9eb07284eb5c1cc4e907f3','5e3a838e057fd3f6fc80efd8',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Sarson Ka Saag, first, wash a bunch of mustard leaves thoroughly with water to remove all the dirt. Then, pat it dry with a kitchen towel to get rid of the water. Then, slice off the core and separate the leaves. Make sure to slice off the stems from the leaves. Then, finely chop 1 cup of mustard leaves and keep it in a bowl. Next, wash half a bunch of spinach leaves thoroughly with water. Remove the stems and finely chop half a cup of spinach leaves and put it in the same bowl.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9eb0964590a027877905c4','5e3a838e057fd3f6fc80efd8',2,'P2: Prep Ingredients','Next, wash, peel and finely chop half a cup of onions. Wash and slice 2 teaspoons of garlic. Wash, peel and finely chop a 1.5-inch piece of ginger. Wash and slit 3 nos green chilies.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9eb0c677c5bbfa41905f45','5e3a838e057fd3f6fc80efd8',3,'M1: Cook the Greens','To boil the greens for Sarson Ka Saag, in a pressure cooker, add the chopped mustard and spinach leaves. Add 1 teaspoon of sliced garlic, 1-inch piece of chopped ginger, and 1/4 cup of chopped onion followed by 2 nos slit green chilies. Next, add half a teaspoon of salt along with 1 cup of water. Cover it with a lid and pressure cook it on high flame until three whistles. After that, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook it for another 5 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the greens are boiling, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":18,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9eb0f477c5bbfa41905f46','5e3a838e057fd3f6fc80efd8',4,'M2: Continue Cooking','After boiling the greens for Sarson Ka Saag, take off the lid and mash it well using a ladle until smooth. After that, add 1.5 tablespoons of cornmeal and mix it well. Keep stirring it on low flame to avoid any lumps. Stir and cook it on medium-low flame for 3-4 minutes until it thickens. Then, turn off the flame and set aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9eb12077c5bbfa41905f47','5e3a838e057fd3f6fc80efd8',5,'M3: Continue Cooking','To make Sarson Ka Saag, heat 1.5 tablespoons of ghee in a kadai on a medium flame for a minute. Add 1 teaspoon of chopped garlic and 1/2 inch piece of chopped ginger. Saute and fry it on a medium flame for 1-2 minutes until fragrant. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions followed by 1 nos slit green chili. Stir and fry the onions on medium-high flame for 3-4 minutes, until it turns golden brown.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9eb1404590a027877905c5','5e3a838e057fd3f6fc80efd8',6,'M4: Final Touches','After frying the onions, add the cooked saag followed by half a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Stir and cook it on a medium flame for 5 minutes. As it turns glossy and thick, turn off the flame and take it out in a bowl. Add a teaspoon of butter and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e9eb1ca4590a027877905c6','5e3a7c2a057fd3f6fc80efd7',1,'P1: Roast Poha','To roast the poha for Walnut Poha, in a kadai, add 1.5 cups of poha. Saute and dry roast it without adding any oil on a medium flame for 2-3 minutes. As it turns light and crisp, turn off the flame and set it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9eb1e577c5bbfa41905f48','5e3a7c2a057fd3f6fc80efd7',2,'P2: Prep Ingredients','For Walnut Poha, wash and finely chop 2 nos green chilies. Finely chop 1/4 cup of walnuts. Cut a lemon into halves and squeeze 1 teaspoon of lime juice using a lemon squeezer. Wash 10 nos curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9eb20677c5bbfa41905f49','5e3a7c2a057fd3f6fc80efd7',3,'M1: Temper Spices','To make the Walnut Poha, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a kadai on a medium flame for a minute. Add half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, followed by 2 nos chopped green chilies and 10 nos curry leaves. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Then, add 1/4 cup of chopped walnuts and fry it on a medium flame for 2-3 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9eb22b84eb5c1cc4e907f4','5e3a7c2a057fd3f6fc80efd7',4,'M2: Make Poha','After frying the walnuts, add 2 teaspoons of roasted chana dal and 1 teaspoon of sliced coconut and mix it well. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder followed by half a teaspoon of sugar and 1 teaspoon of salt. Add 1 teaspoon of lemon juice and mix it well. Stir and fry the masala on a medium flame for 1-2 minutes. After that, add 1.5 cups of roasted poha and mix it well with the masala. Saute and fry the poha on a medium flame for a minute. Then, turn off the flame and take it out in a bowl and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9eb2b54590a027877905c7','5e3a6fd8057fd3f6fc80efd6',1,'P1: Soak Soya Granules','To boil the soya chunks for Soya Keema, add 2 cups of water in a pan. Add half a teaspoon of salt to it and bring it to a boil. As it comes to a boil, add half a cup of soya chunks and allow it boil on medium-high flame for 10 minutes. While the soya chunks are boiling, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9eb2cd84eb5c1cc4e907f5','5e3a6fd8057fd3f6fc80efd6',2,'P2: Prep Ingredients','For Soya Keema, wash, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash, peel and finely chop 1 teaspoon of garlic. Wash and slit 1 nos green chili. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash and roughly chop 2 small tomatoes. Add 1/4 cup of curd to a bowl and whisk it well using a whisk to avoid any lumps.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9eb2eb84eb5c1cc4e907f6','5e3a6fd8057fd3f6fc80efd6',3,'P3: Make Tomato Puree','After boiling the soya chunks for Soya Keema, take it out from the water and soak it in cold water for 10 minutes. Meanwhile, to prepare the tomato paste, add the chopped tomatoes to a blender jar and blend it into a smooth puree. While the soya chunks are soaking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9eb2ec4590a027877905c8','5e3a6fd8057fd3f6fc80efd6',4,'P4: grind the soya chunks into granules','For Soya Keema, after soaking the soya chunks in cold water, squeeze the water from it and put it in a blender jar. Then, blend the soya chunks coarsely into fine granules.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9eb34384eb5c1cc4e907f7','5e3a6fd8057fd3f6fc80efd6',5,'M1: Cook Spices and Onions','To make the Soya Keema, heat 2 teaspoons of ghee in a kadai on a medium flame for a minute. Add half a teaspoon of cumin seeds, 1/2 inch cinnamon stick and 3 cloves followed by 1 nos green cardamom. Saute and let it splutter for a minute. Next, add 1 slit green chili along with 1 teaspoon of chopped garlic. Saute and fry it for 1-2 minutes, until the garlic turns slightly golden. After that, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions and fry it on a medium flame for 3-4 minutes until it turns slightly golden.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9eb35e4590a027877905c9','5e3a6fd8057fd3f6fc80efd6',6,'M2: Add Masalas','After frying the onions, add 1 teaspoon of ginger-garlic paste and fry it for a minute. Then, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, half a teaspoon of kashmiri red chili powder, half a teaspoon of coriander powder, and half a teaspoon of cumin powder followed by 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala. Saute and fry the masala on low flame for 2-3 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e9eb37577c5bbfa41905f4a','5e38003b985ffca18ae8fbb0',1,'P1: Prep the ingredients','For Spiced Buttermilk, wash and separate 1/4 cup of mint leaves. Wash and roughly chop 1/4 cup of coriander leaves. Wash and slit 1 nos green chili. Wash and peel a 1-inch piece of ginger.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9eb38284eb5c1cc4e907f8','5e3a6fd8057fd3f6fc80efd6',7,'M3: Add Tomato Puree','After frying the masala, add the prepared tomato puree and mix it well. Saute and cook the masala on a medium flame for 3-4 minutes until the oil separates. After cooking the masala, add the crumbled soya chunks followed by half a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Add 1/4 cup of water and cover it with a lid. Allow it to simmer for 10 minutes. While the soya chunks are simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e9eb39b4590a027877905ca','5e3a6fd8057fd3f6fc80efd6',8,'M4: Garnish','After simmering the Soya Keema, take off the lid and mix it well. Garnish it with a tablespoon of coriander leaves. Take it out in a bowl and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9eb3ba77c5bbfa41905f4b','5e38003b985ffca18ae8fbb0',2,'M1: Prepare the spiced buttermilk','To make the Spiced Buttermilk, In a blender jar, add 1/4 cup of mint leaves, 1/4 cup of chopped coriander leaves and 1 nos slit green chili followed by a 1-inch piece of ginger and 1 cup of thick yogurt. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of hing, half a teaspoon of salt, half a teaspoon of cumin powder and a tablespoon of lime juice. Add 1 cup of water and blend it well. Then, pour the buttermilk into a jug and some ice cubes to keep it chilled.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9eb3f84590a027877905cb','5e38003b985ffca18ae8fbb0',3,'M2: Add the tempering to the buttermilk & serve','To make the tempering for the Spiced Buttermilk, heat a teaspoon of ghee in a small tempering pan. Add half a teaspoon of cumin seeds followed by 7 nos curry leaves. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Then, turn off the flame and add the tempering to the prepared buttermilk. Mix it well and pour the buttermilk into the glasses. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5e9eb3ff77c5bbfa41905f4c','5e3919c3985ffca18ae8fbc7',1,'P1: Make Dough','To knead the dough for Ajwain Paratha, first, take 1.5 cups of wheat flour in a bowl. Add 1/4 teaspoon of salt to it. Next, crush half a teaspoon of carom seeds between the palms and add it to the four. Then, add a teaspoon of ghee and mix it well with the flour. Next, add about 3/4 cup of water slowly to the flour and knead it well into a smooth dough. Then, cover it with a damp cloth and allow it rest for 20 minutes. While the dough is resting, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":20,"flame":0}'),('5e9eb4164590a027877905cc','5e3919c3985ffca18ae8fbc7',2,'M1: Roll Dough','To make the Ajwain Paratha, first, divide the prepared dough into small equal sized balls. Then, take a ball and dust some flour on the rolling board. Place the dough ball on the rolling board and roll it into a small circle using a rolling pin. Then, apply 1/4 teaspoon of ghee over it and fold it into a triangle as shown. Next, dust some flour over it and flatten it with your hands and roll it into a 7-inch triangular paratha.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9eb43184eb5c1cc4e907f9','5e3919c3985ffca18ae8fbc7',3,'M2: Make Paratha','Next, place the paratha over a tawa and toast it on a medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Then, flip it and toast the other side for another 1-2 minutes, until small brown spots start to appear on the surface of the paratha. Then, apply half a teaspoon of cooking oil on both the sides and toast the paratha on a medium flame for 2-3 minutes, until it turns golden brown. As it turns slightly crisp and golden, take it out in a plate and serve. Similarly, make the rest of the parathas from the dough.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9eb48377c5bbfa41905f4d','5e3803cb985ffca18ae8fbb2',1,'M1: Slice the apples','Wash and slice the apples. Serve','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9eb4c74590a027877905cd','5e38046f985ffca18ae8fbb4',1,'M1: Peel  the orange','Wash and peel the orange. Serve','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9eb4c977c5bbfa41905f4e','5e38059d057fd3f6fc80efc2',1,'M1: Make Tea','To make Herbal Tea, boil 1 cup of water either on the stove or in a kettle. Once the water has boiled, pour it into a mug, and add 1 tea bag. Allow the tea to brew for 2 mins and remove the bag. The tea is ready to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9eb53977c5bbfa41905f4f','5e391779057fd3f6fc80efd4',1,'P1: Cook Pasta','To boil the pasta for Penne Arrabbiata, add 3 cups of water to a saucepan and bring it to a rolling boil on high flame. As it comes to a boil, add 1/4 teaspoon of salt followed by 1 cup of penne pasta. Boil and cook the pasta on medium-high flame for 8 minutes. Keep stirring the pasta in between. While the pasta is boiling, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":4,"idle_time":4,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9eb5524590a027877905ce','5e391779057fd3f6fc80efd4',2,'P2: Prep Ingredients','For Penne Arrabbiata, wash and cut 1/4 cup of yellow capsicum into medium cubes. Wash and cut 1/4 cup of red capsicum into medium cubes. Wash, peel and cube 1/4 cup of zucchini. Wash and cut 1/4 cup of broccoli into florets. Wash and chop 4 nos baby corns. Next, after boiling the pasta, turn off the flame and drain the hot water. Keep the pasta stock aside for later use. Then, rinse the pasta with normal water to prevent it from cooking further.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9eb56c4590a027877905cf','5e391779057fd3f6fc80efd4',3,'P3: Prep Ingredients','For Penne Arrabbiata, wash and finely chop 1 teaspoon of garlic. Wash, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Grate 1 tablespoon of cheddar cheese using a grater. Grate 2.5 tablespoons of parmesan cheese using a grater. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of basil leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5e9eb58a77c5bbfa41905f50','5e3804d9057fd3f6fc80efc0',1,'M1: Whisk the curd & serve','Add the curd to a bowl and whisk it well until smooth. Season it with either salt or sugar, or serve it plain.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9eb59284eb5c1cc4e907fa','5e391779057fd3f6fc80efd4',4,'M1: Cook Garlic and Onions','To make the Arrabbiata sauce for Penne Arrabbiata, heat 1 tablespoon of olive oil in a pan on a medium flame for a minute. Add 1 teaspoon of chopped garlic and saute it for a minute. Then, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions. Stir and fry the onions on a medium flame for 3-4 minutes, until it turns slightly golden. After frying the onions, add 3/4 cup of tomato puree and mix it well.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9eb5b784eb5c1cc4e907fb','5e391779057fd3f6fc80efd4',5,'M2: Cook Sauce','Next, add 1 teaspoon of Italian herbs and stir it well. Season the sauce with half a teaspoon of salt and 1/4 teaspoon of sugar. Add 1 tablespoon of cheddar cheese followed by 1/4 teaspoon of black pepper powder and mix it well. Add 1/4 cup of the preserved pasta stock to the sauce. The starch from the stock will thicken the sauce and make it more flavorful. Then, cover it with a lid and allow it to simmer for 15 minutes. While the sauce is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5e9eb5d94590a027877905d0','5e391779057fd3f6fc80efd4',6,'M3: Make Vegetable Stir-Fry','To make the vegetable stir fry for Penne Arrabbiata, heat a tablespoon of olive oil in a pan on a medium flame for a minute. Add 1/4 cup of broccoli florets followed by 1/4 cup of cubed zucchini and 4 nos sliced baby corns. Mix it well and fry the vegetables on high flame for a minute. Season it with half a teaspoon of salt and 1/4 teaspoon of black pepper powder and mix it well.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9eb5f34590a027877905d1','5e391779057fd3f6fc80efd4',7,'M4: Make Vegetable Stir-fry','Next, add 1/4 cup of diced red and yellow capsicum. Mix it well and fry it for 1-2 minutes. Then, cover it with a lid and simmer the vegetables for a minute. Then, take off the lid and add 1/4 cup of the preserved pasta stock to it. Cover it with a lid and continue to simmer it for a minute. After that, turn off the flame and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5e9eb61577c5bbfa41905f51','5e391779057fd3f6fc80efd4',8,'M5: Finish Making Sauce','After simmering the Arrabbiata sauce, take off the lid and add 2 tablespoons of parmesan cheese and mix it well. Add 1 tablespoon of chopped basil leaves and mix well. Cook the sauce on high flame for a minute. Then, turn off the flame and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5e9eb6444590a027877905d2','5e391779057fd3f6fc80efd4',9,'M6: Make Pasta','To make the Penne Arrabbiata, add the cooked penne pasta to the fried and simmered vegetables and mix it well. Next, add the prepared Arrabbiata sauce and coat the pasta well with the sauce. Then, turn off the flame and garnish with a teaspoon of grated parmesan cheese and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5ea68a2a4590a02787790630','5e21911e057fd3f6fc80eeab',1,'M1: Make the butter toast','Toast the bread slices and apply the butter. Serve with tea or coffee.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5ebe561123f2db2d2b66471b','5e3b9e1e4f28558c29df655b',1,'P1: Prep the ingredients','For Vendekkai Sambar, soak 1 tablespoon of tamarind in 1 cup of water for 15 minutes. Next, wash 1/2 cup of ladies fingers well with water and dab it on a kitchen towel to remove the water. Spread the ladies fingers on a kitchen towel and allow it dry for another 15 minutes. Make sure there is no moisture left in the ladies finger to prevent it from sticking together while cooking. While the ladies fingers are drying, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5ebe56512661f8c73feec97a','5e3b9e1e4f28558c29df655b',2,'P2: Pressure cook the dal','To cook the dal for Vendekkai Sambar, wash 3/4 cup of toor dal well with water. Next, put the washed dal into a pessure cooker with 1.5 cups of water. Cover it with a lid and pressure cook it on high flame till one whistle. After the first whistle, reduce it to low flame and continue to cook the dal for another 8 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the dal is cooking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5ebe56b02661f8c73feec97b','5e3b9e1e4f28558c29df655b',3,'P3: Prep the ingredients','For Vendekkai Samabar, wash and slit 2 nos green chilies lengthwise. Wash and finely chop 1.5 tablespoons of coriander leaves. Wash 10 curry leaves. After drying the ladies fingers completely, cut the cap and thin bottom part of each ladies finger using a knife, then cut it into 1/2 inch roundels. After soaking the tamarind, mash it and mix it well with the water. Then, strain it using a strainer to remove any extra residue from it.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5ebe57118eee55d98e8329f4','5e3b9e1e4f28558c29df655b',4,'M1: Simmer the ladies fingers','To make the Vendekkai Sambar, in a pan, add 1 cup of the prepared tamarind water, 2 nos slit green chilies, and 1 tablespoon of jaggery. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, 5 nos curry leaves, and 1/2 teaspoon of salt. Bring it to a boil on medium-high flame. After a boil, add 1/2 cup of chopped ladies fingers and stir it well. Then, cover it with a lid and cook it on medium flame for 10 minutes. While it is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5ebe573e23f2db2d2b66471c','5e3b9e1e4f28558c29df655b',5,'M2: Simmer the sambar','After simmering the ladies fingers for Vendekkai Sambar, take off the lid and give it a stir. Add 1 cup of cooked toor dal and mix it well. Next, if required add 1/4 cup of water, to adjust the consistency of the sambar. Continue to boil the sambar for another 3 minutes on medium flame. Then, turn off the flame.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5ebe57a323f2db2d2b66471d','5e3b9e1e4f28558c29df655b',6,'M3: Add the tempering','To make the tempering for the Vendekkai Sambar, heat 1.5 teaspoons of cooking oil in a tadka pan on medium flame for a minute. Add 1/2 teaspoon of mustard seeds, 1/2 teaspoon of urad dal, 1/4 teaspoon of hing, 1 nos dry red chili, and 5 nos curry leaves. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds on medium flame. Then, turn off the flame and pour this tempering instantly over the prepared sambar. Add 1.5 tablespoons of chopped coriander leaves and mix it well. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5ed7552868e46c823ccc70db','5ed752df361df09636e46ba6',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For the Egg Drop Soup, wash 100 grams of chicken well with water. Wash peel and roughly chop 1/4 cup of onions. Peel 2 cloves of garlic. Wash, peel, and roughly chop 1/4 cup of carrots. Wash and roughly chop 1 tablespoon of celery. Wash, peel and finely chop 1/2 inch piece of ginger. Wash and finely slice 1/4 cup of spring onion whites. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of spring onion greens.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5ed75583361df09636e46ba7','5ed752df361df09636e46ba6',2,'M1: Make Chicken Stock','To make the chicken stock for the Egg Drop Soup, add 100 grams of washed chicken to a deep bottom pot and stir-fry it for 2-3 minutes on a medium-high flame without adding any oil. Then, add 2 cloves of garlic, 1/4 cup of chopped onions, 1/4 cup of chopped carrots and 1 tablespoon of chopped celery.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5ed755e968e46c823ccc70dc','5ed752df361df09636e46ba6',3,'M2: Continue to make stock','Next, add 1 nos bay leaf, 1/2 teaspoon of black peppercorns and 1/2 teaspoon of rock salt and saute it for a minute on medium-high flame. Add 3 cups of water and bring it to a boil. As the water comes to a boil, reduce it to low flame, cover it with a lid and allow it to simmer for an hour. After an hour, turn off the flame, take off the lid and using a ladle remove the chicken pieces from the stock. Strain the chicken stock using a strainer and set it aside. This chicken stock can be stored in the refrigerator for 2 weeks and can be store in the freezer for 6 months. While the chicken stock is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":60,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":60,"flame":3}'),('5ed756c768e46c823ccc70dd','5ed752df361df09636e46ba6',4,'M3: Make Soup','To make the Egg Drop Soup, pour the prepared chicken stock into a deep bottom pot. Add 1/2 inch piece of chopped ginger, 1/4 cup of sliced spring onion whites and 2 teaspoons of soy sauce. Give it a stir on a medium-low flame and bring it to a boil. Meanwhile, crack 3 nos eggs in a bowl and whisk it well using a fork or a whisk.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5ed75726361df09636e46ba8','5ed752df361df09636e46ba6',5,'M4: Add Eggs','After the soup has come to a boil, add the whisked eggs to the soup while stirring it continuously using a fork or a ladle clockwise. Make sure to stir the soup only in one direction while adding the eggs. The eggs will automatically crumble in the soup. Then, add 1 tablespoon of spring onion greens and turn off the flame. Add 1/4 teaspoon of black pepper powder and 1/4 teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Let it sit for a minute to make sure the eggs are completely cooked. After a minute, garnish the soup with 1 tablespoon of chopped spring onion greens and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":1,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5ed75e9e68e46c823ccc70de','5ed75a1f1079d47c33077105',1,'P1: Parboil Noodles','To parboil the noodles for Veg Manchow Soup, boil 2 cups of water in a deep bottom pan on high flame for 1-2 minutes. Add 1/2 teaspoon of salt and 1/4 teaspoon of cooking oil and stir it well. Then, add 1/2 cup of noodles to the boiling water. Boil the noodles on medium-high flame for 4-5 minutes. Make sure not to cook the noodles completely. Keep stirring the noodles in between, to prevent them from sticking together. After boiling the noodles, turn off the flame and drain the water from it. In a bowl add cold water, transfer the boiled noodles to it and set it aside for 2-3 minutes. Using a seive drain the cold water and set the noodles aside. While the noodles are boiling, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":7,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5ed75f73361df09636e46ba9','5ed75a1f1079d47c33077105',2,'P2: Chop Ingredients','For the Veg Manchow Soup, wash, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of spring onion greens. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of spring onion whites. Wash, peel and finely chop 1 teaspoon of garlic. Wash, peel and finely chop a 1-inch piece of ginger. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of cabbage.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5ed75fe768e46c823ccc70df','5ed75a1f1079d47c33077105',3,'P3: Chop Ingredients','Next, wash, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of carrots. Wash and finely chop 4 nos beans. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of green capsicum. Crush 1/2 teaspoon of black peppercorns to a coarse powder using a pepper grinder. To make the cornflour slurry, add 2 teaspoons of cornflour and 1/4 cup of water in a bowl. Mix it well to avoid any lumps.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5ed7603f361df09636e46baa','5ed75a1f1079d47c33077105',4,'P4: Fry Noodles','To fry the noodles, heat 1/4 cup of cooking oil in a pan on high flame for 1-2 minutes. Next, carefully add the boiled noodles to the pan as the noodles might splutter in the oil. Shallow fry the noodles on medium-high flame for 4-5 minutes, until it turns crisp and slightly golden. After frying the noodles, take it out on a kitchen towel to remove excess oil.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5ed7619a68e46c823ccc70e0','5ed75a1f1079d47c33077105',5,'M1: Cook Onions','To make Veg Manchow Soup, heat 1 teaspoon of cooking oil in a pan on a medium flame for a minute. Add 2 tablespoons of spring onion whites and 1/4 cup of chopped onions and stir fry the onions for 1-2 minutes on high flame. Next, add 1 teaspoon of chopped garlic and a 1-inch piece of chopped ginger, fry it for 1-2 minutes till the garlic turns aromatic.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5ed761d01079d47c33077106','5ed75a1f1079d47c33077105',6,'M2: Cook remaining Vegetables','Then, add 1/4 cup of chopped cabbage, 1/4 cup of chopped carrots, 4 nos chopped beans, and 1/4 cup of chopped capsicum. Saute the vegetables on high flame for 1-2 minutes. Next, add 1.5 cups of water and stir it well. Boil the vegetables on medium-high flame for 5 minutes. While it is boiling, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5ed7630e68e46c823ccc70e1','5ed75a1f1079d47c33077105',7,'M3: Added Sauces and Slurry','After boiling the soup, add 1/4 teaspoon of salt and 1 teaspoon of red chili sauce and stir it well. Continue to boil the soup on medium-high flame for another 2 minutes. After that, add 1 teaspoon of vinegar, 1 teaspoon of soy sauce, and 1/4 cup of the prepared cornflour slurry. Stir it well and bring it to a boil. Next, add 1 tablespoon of chopped spring onion greens and 1/4 teaspoon of crushed black pepper to the soup and mix it well. Garnish the soup with 1/2 cup of fried noodles and 1 tablespoon of chopped spring onion greens. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('5ed76a2068e46c823ccc70e2','5ed7698d361df09636e46bab',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Caesar Salad, take 2 nos bread slices, stack it together, cut out the brown edges of the bread slices. Then, cut the slices into small cubes as shown. Peel and finely chop 4 teaspoons of garlic. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of parsley. Grate 1/4 cup of parmesan cheese using a grater. Wash and remove the leaves of the romaine lettuce from it''s center stock. Then, roughly chop 3/4 cup of lettuce leaves as shown. Crush 1 teaspoon of black peppercorns using a pepper grinder to a coarse powder.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5ed76aac1079d47c33077107','5ed7698d361df09636e46bab',2,'M1: Make Croutons','To make the croutons for Caesar Salad, heat 2 teaspoons of olive oil in a pan on a medium flame for a minute. Then, add 2 teaspoons of chopped garlic along with bread cubes to the oil. Toast the bread cubes on low flame for 5-6 minutes till it turns crisp and golden. Keep tossing the bread cubes in between, to prevent it from burning. After the croutons turn crisp and golden, add 1 teaspoon of chopped parsley and 1/4 teaspoon of crushed black pepper. Add 1 tablespoon of grated parmesan cheese to the croutons. Turn off the flame, give it a light toss and take it out in a bowl.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5ed76b4d68e46c823ccc70e3','5ed7698d361df09636e46bab',3,'M2: Make Salad Dressing','To make the dressing for the Caesar Salad, in a mixing bowl, add 1/2 cup of veg mayonnaise. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of salt, 1/4 teaspoon of crushed black pepper, 2 teaspoons of chopped parsley, and 2 teaspoons of chopped garlic. Then, add 2 tablespoons of grated parmesan cheese along with 1 tablespoon of chilled water and mix it well. It is important to use chilled water in the dressing to get a thin and flowy consistency.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5ed76ba168e46c823ccc70e4','5ed7698d361df09636e46bab',4,'M3: Toss Salad','To make Caesar Salad, put the prepared bread croutons in a large mixing bowl. Add 3/4 cup of chopped lettuce leaves and 1 tablespoon of grated parmesan cheese and mix it well. Pour the prepared Caesar dressing over the salad and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5ed7710d68e46c823ccc70e5','5ed77017361df09636e46bac',1,'P1: Chop Ingredients','For the Thai Salad, first, roughly chop 2 cups of romaine lettuce. Next, you have to wash and dry the lettuce leaves. Fill a large vessel with water and wash the chopped lettuce well, drain and set aside to dry. If you have a salad spinner use it to dry the lettuce leaves completely. The leaves should have any water on it else the dressing will not stick to it. Wash and finely slice 1 cup of red cabbage. Next, wash, peel and finely chop 1 tablespoon of garlic. Then, wash and finely chop a 1-inch piece of ginger.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5ed771be1079d47c33077108','5ed77017361df09636e46bac',2,'P2: Chop Ingredients','Next, wash, peel, and cut 1/2 a cup of carrot into thin julienne pieces. After that, wash and finely slice 1/2 a cup of red bell pepper into strips as shown and set aside. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of the green portion of spring onions and set this aside. Next, wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves and 2 tablespoons of mint leaves. Squeeze 2 tablespoons of lime juice and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5ed77424361df09636e46bad','5ed77017361df09636e46bac',3,'M1: Make Salad Dressing','To make Thai Salad Dressing, in a blender jar, add 4 tablespoons of peanut butter, 2 tablespoons of lemon juice, 2 tablespoons of honey and 2 tablespoons of soy sauce. Next, add 1/2 a teaspoon of sesame oil and 1 teaspoon Sriracha sauce. Then, add a 1-inch piece of chopped ginger, half a tablespoon of chopped garlic, and 1 tablespoon of water into the jar and blend well to make a smooth dressing and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5ed774ce1079d47c33077109','5ed77017361df09636e46bac',4,'M2: Toss Salad','For Thai Salad, in a large mixing bowl and add 2 cups of the chopped romaine lettuce. Next, add half a cup of carrot juliennes, one cup of chopped red cabbage, half a cup of sliced red bell pepper. Next, add 3 tablespoons of chopped spring onions, 2 tablespoons of chopped mint, and 2 tablespoons of chopped coriander leaves. Next, pour in the prepared salad dressing and toss all the ingredients together. Once this is combined well, garnish it with 2 tablespoons of crushed peanuts and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5ed77b3b361df09636e46baf','5ed77a9f361df09636e46bae',1,'P1: Cook Pasta','To boil the Shell Pasta for the Salad, add 4 cups of water in a saucepan and bring it to a rolling boil on high flame. As it comes to a boil, add 1 teaspoon of oil and 3/4 teaspoon of salt. Next, add 1 cup of Shell Pasta to it and boil it on medium-low flame for another 8 minutes, until it is completely cooked. Keep stirring it in between to prevent it from sticking together. While the macaroni is boiling, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":8,"flame":3}'),('5ed78062361df09636e46bb0','5ed77a9f361df09636e46bae',2,'P2: Chop Ingredients','For the Pasta Salad, wash, peel and finely slice 1/4 cup of onion. Wash and cut 1/4 cup of capsicum into juliennes. Wash, peel and cut 1/4 cup of carrot into juliennes. Wash and cut 5 nos cherry tomatoes into halves. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of spring onion greens. Wash and finely chop 1 teaspoon of dill leaves. Crush 1 teaspoon of black peppercorns to a coarse powder using a pepper grinder.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5ed780a3361df09636e46bb1','5ed77a9f361df09636e46bae',3,'P3: Drain Pasta','After boiling the pasta for Pasta Salad,  turn off the flame and drain off the water from it. Then, instantly rinse the boiled macaroni with cold water to prevent it from cooking further.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5ed780f368e46c823ccc70e6','5ed77a9f361df09636e46bae',4,'M1: Make Salad Dressing','To make the dressing for the Pasta Salad, in a large mixing bowl, add 4 teaspoons of eggless mayonnaise. Add 1/2 teaspoon of crushed black pepper, 1/4 teaspoon of salt, and 1 teaspoon of lime juice and mix it well.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5ed7811e1079d47c3307710a','5ed77a9f361df09636e46bae',5,'M2: Toss Salad','To make the Pasta Salad, add 1/2 cup of sliced onion to the prepared dressing. Next, add 1/4 cup of carrot juliennes, 1/4 cup of capsicum juliennes, 5 nos of halved cherry tomatoes, and 2 tablespoons of chopped spring onion greens. Then, add the boiled macaroni and gently mix it. Garnish the salad with 1 teaspoon of chopped dill leaves and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5ed8c4c332b322986fd38d16','5ed8c456d5a1765f7fd14dad',1,'P1: Cook the Potatoes','To boil the potatoes for the Potato Mayo Salad, wash 1.5 cups of baby potatoes well with water. Add the washed baby potatoes to a pressure cooker. Add 3 cups of water along with 1/2 teaspoon of salt. Cover it with a lid and pressure cook it on high flame till the first whistle. After the first whistle, reduce it to low flame and continue to cook the potatoes for another 8 minutes. Then turn off the flame, and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the potatoes are boiling, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5ed8c54d32b322986fd38d17','5ed8c456d5a1765f7fd14dad',2,'P2: Chop Ingredents','For the Potato Mayo Salad, wash, peel, and finely chop 1/2 cup of onions. Squeeze 2 teaspoons of lime juice. Wash and finely chop 1 teaspoon of dill leaves. Crush 1/2 teaspoon of black peppercorns to a coarse powder using a pepper grinder. After the pressure from the cooker has been released, take off the lid and take out the boiled baby potatoes. Next, cut it into halves without peeling it.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5ed8c5d532b322986fd38d18','5ed8c456d5a1765f7fd14dad',3,'M1: Make the Salad','To make the Potato Mayo Salad, add the boiled halved baby potatoes in a large mixing bowl. Add 1/2 teaspoon of salt, 1/2 teaspoon of paprika powder, 1/4 teaspoon of crushed black pepper, 1/2 cup of chopped onions, and 2 teaspoons of lime juice to the potatoes. Next, add 1/2 teaspoon of dijon mustard and 2 tablespoons of mayonnaise and mix it well. Garnish the salad with 1 teaspoon of chopped dill leaves and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5ed9d87232b322986fd38d19','5ed9d70b42d8139ca2497c36',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Raw Papaya Salad, first, soak 1 teaspoon of tamarind in 3 tablespoons of hot water and set it aside for 10 minutes. Meanwhile, wash, peel and then julienne 2 cups of raw papaya. Wash and finely slice 1/4 cup of spring onions. Peel and grate 1/4 cup of carrots. Wash and cut 1/4 cup of cherry tomatoes into halves.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5ed9d8d242d8139ca2497c37','5ed9d70b42d8139ca2497c36',2,'P2: Prep Other Ingredients','Next, wash and roughly chop 2 fresh red chillies. Peel 5 cloves of garlic. Wash and cut a lime into halves and squeeze 1 tablespoon of lime juice. Next, after soaking the tamarind mash it well with water strain it to make the tamarind juice','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5ed9da78d5a1765f7fd14dae','5ed9d70b42d8139ca2497c36',3,'M1: Make Salad Dressing','To make the salad dressing for Raw Papaya Salad, first, in a mortar and pestle add 2 roughly chopped red chilies, 5 cloves of garlic, 2 tablespoons of roasted peanuts, and 1 teaspoon of brown sugar and crush it until it is coarse. Then, take it out in a small bowl. Next, add a tablespoon of lime juice, a teaspoon of soy sauce followed by the prepared tamarind pulp, and mix it well to prepare the dressing.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5ed9fe30e6eee2576f694836','5ed9e3cd5a2e75247c04c1d5',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Walnut Salad, wash 1/4 cup of romaine lettuce and remove the leaves from it''s center stock. Wash 1/4 cup of mizuna leaves and remove the stems. Wash and cut 6 nos cherry tomatoes into halves. Wash and cut 3 nos figs into quarters. Wash 8 nos red grapes. Squeeze 2 tablespoons of lime juice. Crush 1/2 teaspoon of black peppercorns to a coarse powder using a pepper grinder.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5ed9ff10679a700c00831f06','5ed9e3cd5a2e75247c04c1d5',2,'M1: Make Savoury Walnuts','To make savoury nuts for the Walnut Salad, heat 2 teaspoons of butter in a pan on low flame for a minute. Add 1 cup of walnuts to the pan on low flame and roast the nuts for 1 minute. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, 1/2 teaspoon red chilli powder, 1/4 teaspoon cumin powder, 1/2 teaspoon salt, and combine well. After that, turn off the flame and set them aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5ed9ff83679a700c00831f07','5ed9e3cd5a2e75247c04c1d5',3,'M2: Make Sweet Walnuts','To make honey glazed walnuts for the Walnut Salad, heat 2 teaspoons of butter in a pan on low flame for a minute. Add 1/2 cup of walnuts to the pan and roast the walnuts on a medium flame for 2 minutes. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of cinnamon powder and 1/4 teaspoon of salt and gently toss the walnuts on low flame for 2-3 minutes. Then, add 1/4 cup of honey and keep stirring the walnuts on low flame for 2-3 minutes, until the walnuts are well coated with honey. After that, turn off the flame and keep it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5eda03915a2e75247c04c1d6','5ed9e3cd5a2e75247c04c1d5',4,'M3: Make Salad Dressing','To make the dressing for Walnut Salad, in a mixing bowl, add 2 tablespoons of lime juice and 2 teaspoons of olive oil. Next, add 1 tablespoon of honey, 1/4 teaspoon of salt and 1/4 teaspoon of crushed black pepper and mix it well.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5eda058fe6eee2576f694837','5ed9e3cd5a2e75247c04c1d5',5,'M4: Make Salad','To make Walnut Salad, spread 1/4 cup of romaine lettuce onto a platter. Add 1/4 cup of mizuna greens over the romaine lettuce. Next, add 6 nos halved cherry tomatoes, 3 nos quartered figs, and 8 red grapes to it. Next, add the prepared roasted savory and honey glazed walnuts to the salad and pour the prepared dressing over it. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5eda0f21679a700c00831f13','5eda0e78679a700c00831f0f',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For the Persian Salad, wash and cut 1 medium-sized cucumber into halves, then scoop out the seeds using a spoon and chop it into small cubes. Wash and chop 1/2 cup of tomatoes. Wash, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of parsley. Squeeze 2 tablespoons of lime juice. Crumble 2 tablespoons of feta cheese using a fork.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5eda0f705a2e75247c04c1e1','5eda0e78679a700c00831f0f',2,'M1: Make Salad Dressing','To make the dressing for Persian Salad, in a mixing bowl, add 2 tablespoons of lemon juice, 1 teaspoon of olive oil, and 1/4 teaspoon of black pepper. Mix it well and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5eda0febe6eee2576f694844','5eda0e78679a700c00831f0f',3,'M2: Make Salad','To make the Persian Salad, in a large mixing bowl, add 1 chopped cucumber. Add 1/2 cup of chopped tomatoes, 1/4 cup of chopped onions, and 1.5 tablespoons of chopped parsley. Next, add 2 tablespoons of crumbled feta cheese to the salad and mix well. Then, pour the prepared dressing over the salad and mix well. Garnish it with 1 teaspoon of crumbled feta cheese and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5eda16a5e6eee2576f694845','5eda13ca679a700c00831f18',1,'P1: Marinate Chicken','To marinate the chicken for BBQ Chicken Salad, wash 200 grams of the boneless chicken breast well with water. Next, in a large mixing bowl, add 1 tablespoons of olive oil, 1/2 teaspoon of salt, 1/4 teaspoon of black pepper powder, and 1/2 cup of barbeque sauce and mix it well. Next, place the chicken breast in the bowl and coat it well with the marinade. Cover it with a plastic wrap and refrigerate it for an hour. While the chicken is marinating, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":60,"advanced_prep_time":60,"timer":60,"flame":0}'),('5eda16f2e6eee2576f694846','5eda13ca679a700c00831f18',2,'P2: Blanch Sweet Corn','To boil the sweet corn kernels for BBQ Chicken Salad, boil 1.5 cups of water in a deep bottom pan on high flame for 1-2 minutes. Add 1/2 cup of sweet corn kernels to the boiling water and continue to boil it for another 4-5 minutes. After 5 minutes, turn off the flame and take out the boiled corn kernels from the water and keep it aside. While the sweet corn kernels are boiling, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5eda179e5a2e75247c04c1e5','5eda13ca679a700c00831f18',3,'P3: Chop Ingredients','For BBQ Chicken Salad, wash and roughly chop 1/4 cup of iceberg lettuce. Wash and finely slice 1/4 cup of onions. Wash 1/4 cup of cherry tomatoes and cut into halves. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of green capsicum. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5eda17f05a2e75247c04c1e6','5eda13ca679a700c00831f18',4,'M1: Cook Chicken','To cook the chicken breast for BBQ Chicken Salad, drizzle 1 tablespoon of olive oil over a grill pan and heat it on a medium flame for a minute. Then, place the marinated chicken breast onto the pan and cook it on medium-low flame for 7-8 minutes, until it turns golden brown. After cooking it from one side, carefully flip it on the other side and similarly cook it on a medium flame for 6-7 minutes. After cooking the chicken, turn off the flame and take it out. Then, roughly cut it into medium-sized cubes. While the chicken is cooking, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5eda18435a2e75247c04c1e7','5eda13ca679a700c00831f18',5,'M2: Toss Vegetables','For BBQ Chicken Salad, in a large mixing bowl, add 1/2 cup of sliced onions, 1/4 cup of chopped capsicum, 1/4 cup of halved cherry tomatoes, and 1/2 cup of boiled sweet corn kernels. Next, add 2 tablespoons of chopped coriander leaves, 2 tablespoons of barbeque sauce, and 2 tablespoons of ranch dressing and mix it well. Add 1/4 teaspoon of salt and 1/4 teaspoon of white pepper powder and mix it well.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5eda187a679a700c00831f19','5eda13ca679a700c00831f18',6,'M3: Add cooked chicken','To make the BBQ Chicken Salad, first, in a bowl, add 1/4 cup of chopped iceberg lettuce. Add 1/4 cup of ranch dressing and mix it well. Next, spread the dressed lettuce over a plate. Then, add the prepared barbeque dressed vegetables. Next, add the chopped grill chicken pieces over it and garnish it with 2 tablespoons of ranch dressing. Ensure to assemble the salad right before serving, as resting it for too long may turn the vegetables soggy. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5ef454a1f6b45f7d97855d7d','5ef45213be79f3ae1c8521b2',1,'P1: Marinate the Chicken','For Chicken and Avocado Salad, first, wash and clean the boneless chicken fillets thoroughly with water. Next, peel and finely chop 2 teaspoons of garlic. Wash and finely chop 1 green chilli. Wash and cut 2 limes into halves and then squeeze 4 tablespoons of lime juice. Next, to marinate the chicken, in a medium bowl add 1 tablespoon of olive oil, a teaspoon of salt, and 2 teaspoons of chopped garlic followed by 1 chopped green chilli and half a teaspoon of red chilli powder. Next, add a tablespoon of honey along with 2 tablespoons of lime juice and mix it well. Then, add 200 grams of boneless chicken fillets and coat them well with the marinade. Then let the chicken marinate for 1 hour. While the chicken marinates, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":60,"advanced_prep_time":60,"timer":60,"flame":0}'),('5ef45508f6b45f7d97855d7e','5ef45213be79f3ae1c8521b2',2,'P2: Prep the Lettuce','For Chicken & Avocado Salad, Wash and remove the leaves of the romaine lettuce from it''s center stock. Then, roughly slice 1 cup of lettuce leaves as shown and dip the sliced shreds in cold water until use. Make sure to dry off the lettuce leaves completely before use. If you have a salad spinner use that to dry the lettuce or spread it on a plate with some kitchen towel and let it air dry.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5ef4557af6b45f7d97855d7f','5ef45213be79f3ae1c8521b2',3,'P3: Prep Remaining Ingredients','Next, wash and slice half a cup of cherry tomatoes into halves. Peel, wash, and finely slice 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and cut an avocado into halves and remove the seed and using a spoon. Then, scoop out the avocado pulp and roughly dice it.','prep_method','{"active_time":11,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5ef455c8f6b45f7d97855d80','5ef45213be79f3ae1c8521b2',4,'M1: Cook the Chicken','To sear the chicken fillets for chicken and avocado salad, heat 1 tablespoon of olive oil in a pan for a min. Then, add the marinated chicken fillets to the pan and let them cook on each side for  5-6 minutes over medium flame, until evenly browned. Keep flipping the fillets occasionally to cook them evenly. As the fillets turn golden and are cooked through, turn off the flame and carefully take them out onto a plate. Then, roughly slice the fillets into small pieces ans set aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5ef456faf6b45f7d97855d81','5ef45213be79f3ae1c8521b2',5,'M2: Make Salad Dressing','To prepare the dressing for Chicken and Avocado Salad, in a small bowl add 3 tablespoons of olive oil, half a teaspoon of salt, half a tsp of black pepper powder, 2 tbsp of honey, and 2 tbsps of lime juice. Mix this well with a fork and then set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5ef457628b78ddeebde85a9c','5ef45213be79f3ae1c8521b2',6,'M3: Toss the Salad','To make Chicken and Avocado Salad, in a large mixing bowl add 1 cup of chopped romaine lettuce, half a cup of halved cherry tomatoes, half a cup of chopped avocado and 1/4 cup of chopped onions. Next, add the boneless shredded chicken and pour the prepared salad dressing over the vegetables. Mix and combine the salad using 2 large spoons. Then, take it out into a serving bowl and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5ef4604bf6b45f7d97855d83','5ef45b02f6b45f7d97855d82',1,'AP1: Soak the Chickpeas','For this roasted chickpea salad, soak 1 cup of chickpeas in 2 cups of water for 8 hours or overnight.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":480,"advanced_prep_time":480,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5ef460d1f6b45f7d97855d84','5ef45b02f6b45f7d97855d82',2,'P1: Pressure Cook Chickpeas','To boil the chickpeas for the Roasted chickpea salad, first, add 1 cup of soaked chickpeas to a pressure cooker along with half a teaspoon of salt. Add 3 cups of water and cover it with a lid. Then, pressure cooks it over a high flame until three whistles. After that, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook the chickpeas for another 8 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally.  While the chickpeas are boiling, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5ef476a3be79f3ae1c8521b4','5ef45b02f6b45f7d97855d82',3,'P2: Prep the Lettuce','For Roasted Chickpea Salad, wash and separate the leaves of iceberg lettuce. Then, roughly chop 1/4 cup of the lettuce leaves. Remove the lettuce leaves from its center stock. Then, slice 1/4 cup of romaine lettuce into small bite-size pieces. Then wash the lettuce thoroughly with water and dry it completely before using it in the salad. If you have a salad spinner use that to dry the lettuce or air dry them on a plate with a kitchen towel on top.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5ef47718be79f3ae1c8521b5','5ef45b02f6b45f7d97855d82',4,'P3: Prep Vegetables','Next, wash and dice 1/4 cup of cucumber. Wash and slice half a cup of cherry tomatoes into halves. Wash and cut an avocado into halves and remove the seed. Then scoop out the flesh and roughly dice it. Wash and cut 1 lime into halves and squeeze 2 tbsp of lime juice.','prep_method','{"active_time":11,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5ef4781ebe79f3ae1c8521b6','5ef45b02f6b45f7d97855d82',5,'P4: Bake Chickpeas','After boiling the chickpeas for Roasted Chickpea Salad, remove the lid of the pressure cooker and drain off the water from the chickpeas. Then, add the chickpeas to a mixing bowl along with 2 tablespoons of olive oil, a teaspoon of paprika and a teaspoon of garlic powder followed by half a teaspoon of salt. Mix it well and then spread the chickpeas on a baking tray and bake them in the oven at 200 degrees Celcius for 25-30 mins. While the chickpeas are roasting, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":30,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":30,"flame":0}'),('5ef478998b78ddeebde85a9d','5ef45b02f6b45f7d97855d82',6,'M1: Make Salad','To make roasted chickpea salad, in a large mixing bowl add the washed and dried lettuce, 1/4 cup of cucumber, 1/2 cup of cherry tomatoes, 1 chopped avocado, 1 cup of roasted chickpeas, 2 tablespoons olive oil, 2 tablespoons of lime juice, 1/2 teaspoon of salt, and 1/2 teaspoon of black pepper powder. Toss the ingredients together with 2 large spoons and once the this is combined well, the salad is ready to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5ef47c96be79f3ae1c8521b7','5ef47c598b78ddeebde85a9e',1,'P1: Prep the Lettuce','For Orange and Basil salad, first, remove the leaves of romaine lettuce from its center stock and wash it thoroughly with water. Then, Allow the lettuce leaves to dry completely before use. If you have a salad spinner use that to dry the lettuce or spread it on a plate and pat dry with a kitchen towel and let it air dry. Then, roughly chop 1 cup of lettuce leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5ef47cfdf6b45f7d97855d85','5ef47c598b78ddeebde85a9e',2,'P2: Prep Other Ingredients','Next, peel, wash, and slice 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of basil leaves. Peel and separate 1 orange into wedges. Crumble 3 tablespoons of feta cheese.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5ef47d60f6b45f7d97855d86','5ef47c598b78ddeebde85a9e',3,'M1: Make the Salad Dressing','To prepare the balsamic vinaigrette dressing for Orange and Basil Salad,  in a small bowl add 1.5 tablespoons of balsamic vinegar, 1.5 tablespoons of honey, 3 tablespoons of olive oil and half a tsp of salt followed by half a teaspoon of black pepper powder. Mix it well using a whisk and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5ef47d92be79f3ae1c8521b8','5ef47c598b78ddeebde85a9e',4,'M2: Make Salad','To make Orange and Basil Salad,  in a large mixing bowl add 1 cup of chopped lettuce and 1/4 cup of sliced onions. Next, add 2 tablespoons of chopped basil leaves, wedges of 1 orange, and 3 tablespoons of feta cheese. Next, pour the prepared dressing over the salad and mix it well using 2 large spoons until it is well combined. Then, take it out into a serving bowl and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5ef488318b78ddeebde85a9f','5ef487f8f6b45f7d97855d87',1,'P1: Prep Lettuce','For Orange and Walnut Salad, first, remove the leaves of romaine lettuce from its center stock and wash it thoroughly with water. Then, Allow the lettuce leaves to dry completely before use. If you have a salad spinner use that to dry the lettuce or spread it on a plate and pat dry with a kitchen towel and let it air dry. Then, roughly chop 1 cup of lettuce leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5ef488768b78ddeebde85aa0','5ef487f8f6b45f7d97855d87',2,'P2: Toast Walnuts','To toast the walnuts for Orange & Walnut Salad, heat a pan over medium flame for a min. Then, add half a cup of walnuts to the pan and toast them for 3-4 mins stirring occasionally. Once the walnuts turn slightly brown, turn off the flame and set them aside','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5ef488cdbe79f3ae1c8521b9','5ef487f8f6b45f7d97855d87',3,'P3: Prep Ingredients','For Orange and Walnut Salad, wash and peel an orange with a knife. Cut off the ends of the orange and then slice the peel off the sides. Then, gently slice the orange pieces in between 2 membranes. Slice the oranges over a bowl so any juice that falls can be used in the dressing later. Wash and cut 1 lime into halves and squeeze 1 tablespoon of lime juice.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5ef489168b78ddeebde85aa1','5ef487f8f6b45f7d97855d87',4,'M1: Make Salad Dressing','To prepare the dressing for Orange & Walnut salad, in a small bowl add 3 tablespoons of orange juice. Next, add 1 tablespoon of lime juice, 1 tablespoon of olive oil, 1 tablespoon of water, 2 teaspoons of sugar, and 1 teaspoon of salt. Mix it well using a whisk and set the dressing aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5ef4894df6b45f7d97855d88','5ef487f8f6b45f7d97855d87',5,'M2: Make Salad','To make Orange and Walnut Salad, in a large bowl, add 1 cup of chopped lettuce. Add the chopped orange wedges and half a cup of toasted walnuts. Next, pour the prepared salad dressing over the salad and mix it well using two large spoons to combine the salad. Then, take it out into a serving bowl and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5ef48b23be79f3ae1c8521ba','5ef48aeef6b45f7d97855d89',1,'P1: Marinate the Chicken','For the chicken and pear salad, first, wash the boneless chicken cubes thoroughly with water. Next, to marinate the chicken, in a medium bowl add the boneless chicken cubes along with half a teaspoon of salt, half a teaspoon of black pepper powder, and a 1/4 teaspoon of paprika. Mix it well and allow it to sit for 15-20 minutes. While the chicken marinates, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5ef48b548b78ddeebde85aa2','5ef48aeef6b45f7d97855d89',2,'P2: Prep Lettuce','For Chicken & Pear Salad, separate the lettuce leaves from its center stock and remove the core. Then wash it thoroughly with water. Allow the lettuce leaves to dry completely before use. If you have a salad spinner use that to dry the lettuce or spread it on a kitchen towel and let it air dry. Next, gather the lettuce leaves together and chop 1 cup of green lettuce crosswise into bite-sized pieces.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5ef48b86be79f3ae1c8521bb','5ef48aeef6b45f7d97855d89',3,'P3: Chop Pear and Walnuts','For Chicken and Pear Salad, wash 1 medium-sized pear and cut it into halves. Then deseed the fruit, and finely slice half a cup of pear. Next, roughly chop 2 tablespoons of walnuts.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5ef48baaf6b45f7d97855d8a','5ef48aeef6b45f7d97855d89',4,'M1: Cook Chicken','To cook the chicken for Chicken and Pear Salad, heat a tablespoon of olive oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Next, add the marinated chicken to the pan and cook it over medium flame for 7-8 minutes. Keep flipping the chicken cubes occasionally to make sure they are evenly browned on all sides. Once the chicken pieces are through, turn off the flame and take them out into a bowl.','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5ef48bdcbe79f3ae1c8521bc','5ef48aeef6b45f7d97855d89',5,'M2: Make Salad Dressing','To make the salad dressing for Chicken and Pear Salad, in a small bowl add 2 tablespoons of olive oil, 2 tablespoons of apple cider vinegar, 1 teaspoon of honey, 1/2 teaspoon of mustard sauce, 1/4 teaspoon of salt, and 1/4 teaspoon of black pepper powder. Mix it well using a whisk and set the dressing aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5ef590a6be79f3ae1c8521c1','5ef48d75be79f3ae1c8521bd',1,'P1: Prep Ingredietns','For Gyro Chicken Salad, first, wash and clean 200 grams of boneless chicken thoroughly with water. Then, cut it into medium cubes. Next, wash and cut 1 lime into halves and squeeze 2 tablespoons of lime juice. Peel and finely chop 2 teaspoons of garlic.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5ef59178be79f3ae1c8521c2','5ef48d75be79f3ae1c8521bd',2,'P2: Marinate the Chicken','For Gyro Chicken Salad, in a small bowl, add the boneless chicken cubes. Add 1 tablespoon of lime juice, 1 tablespoon of olive oil, 1 tablespoon of oregano, 1 teaspoon of minced garlic, 1/2 teaspoon of salt, and 1/2 teaspoon of black pepper powder. Mix it well and allow the chicken to sit for 10-15 minutes. While the chicken marinates, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5ef591c98b78ddeebde85aa3','5ef48d75be79f3ae1c8521bd',3,'P3: Prep Lettuce','For the Gyro Chicken Salad, first, separate the lettuce leaves from it''s center stock and remove the core. Then wash it thoroughly with water. Allow the lettuce leaves to dry completely before use. If you have a salad spinner use that to dry the lettuce or spread it on a kitchen towel and let it air dry. Then, gather the leaves together and chop 1 cup of green lettuce crosswise into bite-sized pieces.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5ef5926dbe79f3ae1c8521c3','5ef48d75be79f3ae1c8521bd',4,'P4: Prep Remaining Ingredients','For Gyro Chicken Salad, wash, peel and grate 1/4 cup of cucumber. Next, finely dice 1/4 cup of cucumber. Wash 1/2 cup of cherry tomatoes and then cut them into halves. Peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Crush 1/2 cup of crackers into a bowl either with your hands or roughly chop them with a knife. Wash and cut a lime into halves and then squeeze 1 tablespoon of lime juice.','prep_method','{"active_time":11,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5ef593dcbe79f3ae1c8521c4','5ef48d75be79f3ae1c8521bd',5,'M1: Cook Chicken','For Gyro Chicken Salad, heat a tablespoon of olive oil in a pan over medium flame. Next, add the marinated chicken to the pan and cook it over medium flame for 6-7 mins until it is evenly browned on all the sides. Once the chicken pieces are tender and crisp, turn off the flame and take them out into a bowl.','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5ef5941c8b78ddeebde85aa4','5ef48d75be79f3ae1c8521bd',6,'M2: Make Salad Dressing','To make the salad dressing for gyro chicken salad, in a small bowl add 1 cup of greek yogurt, 1/4 cup of grated cucumber, and a tablespoon of lime juice followed by a tablespoon of olive oil. Add half a teaspoon of salt, and half a teaspoon of black pepper powder and whisk this together until combined well and then set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5ef59a1ef6b45f7d97855d8c','5ed9d70b42d8139ca2497c36',4,'M2: Make Salad','To make Raw Papaya Salad, in a large bowl, add 2 cups of shredded papaya, 1/4 cup of sliced spring onions, 1/4 cup of grated carrots, and 1/4 cup of cherry tomatoes. Next, add 2 tablespoons of roasted peanuts, and pour the prepared salad dressing over the vegetables. Mix the salad using 2 large spoons and toss it together until well combined. Then, take it out into a serving bowl and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5ef5a651f6b45f7d97855d8d','5ef48aeef6b45f7d97855d89',6,'M3: Toss the Salad','To make Chicken and Pear Salad, in a large bowl add 1 cup of chopped lettuce. Add half a cup of sliced pears, 2 tablespoons of chopped walnuts, and 2 tablespoons of dried cranberries. Next, and the cooked chicken pieces and pour the prepared salad dressing over the salad. Mix it well using 2 large spoons and toss the salad together until it is well combined. Then, take it out into a serving bowl and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5ef5cdeabe79f3ae1c8521fc','5ef48d75be79f3ae1c8521bd',7,'M3: Toss Salad','To make the Gyro Chicken Salad, in a large bowl add 1 cup of chopped green lettuce. Add 1/2 cup of chopped cherry tomatoes, 1/4 cup of diced cucumber, and 1/4 cup of chopped onions. Next, add 1/2 cup of crushed crackers, and the cooked boneless chicken cubes. Next, pour the prepared salad dressing over the salad and then toss the ingredients together with 2 large spoons to mix it well. Then, take it out into a serving bowl and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5ef99afabe79f3ae1c85220a','5e60a757a342c0f170bd9a3c',6,'M4: Final Touches','After simmering the Rajasthani Dal, take off the lid and give it a stir. Turn off the flame and garnish it with a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f06e768556f1d370234cd85','5f06e2d8556f1d370234cd4d',1,'P1: Marinate the Chicken','For Chilli Chicken, first, wash 250 grams of boneless chicken cubes thoroughly with water and clean them well. Next, to marinate the chicken, add the chicken cubes to a large mixing bowl. Add half a teaspoon of ginger-garlic paste, 1/4 teaspoon of black pepper powder, and half a teaspoon of vinegar. Next, crack an egg into this and add 2 tablespoons of all-purpose flour followed by 2 tablespoons of cornflour. Add half a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Coat the chicken cubes well with the marinade and allow it to rest for 30 minutes. While the chicken marinates, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":30,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":30,"flame":0}'),
('5f06e7bdfc298c2ba9ed07af','5f06e2d8556f1d370234cd4d',2,'P2: Chop Vegetables','To prep, the ingredients for Chilli Chicken, peel, wash, and roughly dice 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and chop 1/4 cup of green capsicum into medium pieces. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of spring onion whites. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of spring onion greens.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f06e821fc298c2ba9ed07b0','5f06e2d8556f1d370234cd4d',3,'P3: Chop Ingredients and Prepare Slurry','Next, wash and finely chop 2 nos green chilies. Peel, wash and finely chop 2 teaspoons of garlic. Wash, peel and finely chop a half-inch piece of ginger. Next, to prepare the cornflour slurry, in a small bowl, add a teaspoon of cornflour followed by 1/4 cup of water and mix it well to prepare a thin slurry.','prep_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f06e86c556f1d370234cd86','5f06e2d8556f1d370234cd4d',4,'M1: Fry Marinated Chicken','To fry the chicken cubes for chilli chicken, first heat 1 cup of cooking oil in a Kadai over medium flame for 2-3 minutes. Once the oil is hot, carefully drop the marinated chicken cubes into it one by one. Then, deep fry them over medium flame for 6-7 minutes until golden and crisp. Once the chicken cubes are cooked through and turn golden-crisp, turn off the flame and take them out onto a plate.','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f06e8bf59142db0285ef32f','5f06e2d8556f1d370234cd4d',5,'M2: Cook the Vegetables','To make Chilli Chicken, heat 2 tablespoons of butter in a pan over low flame. Add 2 teaspoons of chopped garlic followed by a 1/2-inch piece of chopped ginger and 2 nos chopped green chilies. Saute and fry it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Next, add 2 tablespoons of chopped spring onion whites, 1/4 cup of diced onions along with 1/4 cup of diced capsicum. Stir and fry the vegetables over high flame for 2-3 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":4}'),('5f06e912fc298c2ba9ed07b1','5f06e2d8556f1d370234cd4d',6,'M3: Add Sauces','Next, add a tablespoon of red chili sauce, 2 tablespoons of tomato ketchup, and 2 tablespoons of schezwan sauce followed by a tablespoon of soy sauce. Mix it well and cook the sauces with the vegetables over high flame for 1-2 minutes. Next, add the prepared cornflour slurry to the sauce and mix it well. Keep stirring it continuously over medium flame until the slurry is well combined with the sauce.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('5f06e964fc298c2ba9ed07b2','5f06e2d8556f1d370234cd4d',7,'M4: Add Fried Chicken','Next, season the sauce with half a teaspoon of salt and 1/4 teaspoon of black pepper powder. Mix it well and cook it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes until the sauce thickens. Then, add the fried chicken cubes and mix them well with the sauce. After that, cover it with a lid and simmer the chicken over low flame for 5 minutes. While the chicken is simmering, please move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":5,"flame":1}'),('5f06e98e59142db0285ef330','5f06e2d8556f1d370234cd4d',8,'M5: Garnish','After simmering the chilli chicken, remove the lid and stir it with light hands. Then, turn off the flame and take it out into a serving bowl. Garnish it with 2 tablespoons of chopped spring onion greens and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f06ed31556f1d370234cd88','5f06ec2a556f1d370234cd87',1,'P1: Marinate the Chicken','For Sweet & Sour Chicken, first, wash 250 grams of boneless chicken cubes thoroughly with water and clean them well. Next, add the chicken cubes to a large mixing bowl. Next, crack an egg into this and mix it well. Then, add a tablespoon of cornflour, a tablespoon of refined flour, and half a teaspoon of salt followed by 1/4 teaspoon of black pepper powder. Mix it well and coat the chicken pieces evenly with the marinade. After that, allow it to rest for 15 minutes. While the chicken marinates, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":15,"flame":0}'),('5f06ed8959142db0285ef331','5f06ec2a556f1d370234cd87',2,'P2: Chop Vegetables and Prepare the Slurry','For Sweet & Sour Chicken, peel, wash, and finely chop 1/4 cup of spring onion bulbs. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of spring onion greens. Peel, wash and finely chop 2 teaspoons of garlic. Wash, peel and finely chop a half-inch piece of ginger. Next, to prepare the cornflour slurry, in a small bowl, add a teaspoon of cornflour followed by 1/4 cup of water and mix it well to prepare a thin slurry.','prep_method','{"active_time":14,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f06edcb556f1d370234cd89','5f06ec2a556f1d370234cd87',3,'M1: Fry the Marinated Chicken','To fry the chicken cubes for Sweet & Sour Chicken, first heat 1 cup of cooking oil in a Kadai over medium flame for 2-3 minutes. Once the oil is hot, carefully drop the marinated chicken cubes into it, one by one. Then, deep fry them over medium flame for 6-7 minutes until golden and crisp. Once the chicken cubes are cooked through and turn golden-crisp, turn off the flame and take them out onto a kitchen napkin to dab off the excess oil.','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5f06ee08556f1d370234cd8a','5f06ec2a556f1d370234cd87',4,'M2: Temper the Ginger and Garlic','To make Sweet & Sour Chicken, heat a tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add 2 teaspoons of chopped garlic followed by a 1/2-inch piece of chopped ginger and 1/4 cup of chopped spring onions. Stir and fry it over medium-high flame for 2-3 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f06ee8d556f1d370234cd8b','5f06ec2a556f1d370234cd87',5,'M3: Add Sauce and Seasoning','After frying the onions, add a tablespoon of tomato ketchup and mix it well. Next, add a teaspoon of soy sauce along with 3/4 cup of chicken stock and stir it well. If the chicken stock is not available water can be used as a substitute. Then, bring it to a boil over a high flame. As it comes to a boil, add half a teaspoon of sugar, half a teaspoon of salt and a 1/4 teaspoon of black pepper powder. Next, add the prepared cornflour slurry and keep stirring it continuously over medium until it is well combined. Then, continue to cook it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes until the sauce slightly thickens.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5f06eec5fc298c2ba9ed07b3','5f06ec2a556f1d370234cd87',6,'M4: Final Touches','Next, add a tablespoon of vinegar followed by the fried chicken cubes and mix it well. Stir and cook the chicken with the sauce over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and garnish it with a tablespoon of chopped spring onion greens. Take it out into a serving bowl and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5f06f0f1fc298c2ba9ed07b4','5f06f082556f1d370234cd8c',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Garlic Chicken, wash 250 grams of boneless chicken cubes thoroughly with water and clean them well. Peel, wash, and cut half a cup of onions into petals. Peel and finely chop 2 teaspoons of garlic. wash and slit 2 green chilies. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of spring onion greens. Next, to prepare the cornflour slurry, in a small bowl, add a teaspoon of cornflour followed by 1/4 cup of water and mix it well to prepare a thin slurry.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f06f1d859142db0285ef332','5f06f082556f1d370234cd8c',2,'M1: Cook Chicken','To make Garlic Chicken, heat 3 tablespoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add 2 teaspoons of minced garlic and fry it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes until golden. Next, add 250 grams of boneless chicken cubes to this and fry it over medium flame for 5-6 minutes till it is no longer pink. Then, cover it with a lid and cook the chicken over low flame for 7-8 minutes until it is cooked through. While the chicken is simmering, please move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5f06f24cfc298c2ba9ed07b5','5f06f082556f1d370234cd8c',3,'M2: Cook Vegetables','After simmering the chicken for Garlic Chicken, take off the lid and fry it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Then, add half a cup of chopped onions and fry it with the chicken cubes over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Next, add half a teaspoon of salt, 1/4 teaspoon of black pepper powder, a tablespoon of soy sauce, and 2 teaspoons of vinegar. Add 2 tablespoons of chili garlic sauce followed by 3/4 teaspoons of sugar and mix it well. Then, cook it over high flame for 2 minutes while stirring it continuously.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f06f50559142db0285ef333','5f06f082556f1d370234cd8c',4,'M3: Add Stock and Slurry','Next, add 3/4 cup of chicken stock to the chicken and mix it well. If the chicken stock is not available water can be used as a substitute. Then, bring it to a boil over a high flame. As it comes to a boil, add the prepared cornflour slurry and stir it continuously over medium flame until the slurry is well combined. Then, continue to cook it over medium flame for another 1-2 minutes until the sauce slightly thickens. Make sure to keep the consistency of the dish slightly runny. Avoid cooking the sauce for too long after adding the cornflour slurry as this will make the gravy too thick.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f06f5a0556f1d370234cd8d','5f06f082556f1d370234cd8c',5,'M4: Garnish','After reaching the gravy-like consistency for garlic chicken, add 2 slit green chilies and mix it well. Stir it over medium flame for a minute. Then, turn off the flame and garnish it with a tablespoon of chopped spring onion greens. Take it out into a serving bowl and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('5f07f7affc298c2ba9ed07b8','5f07f75559142db0285ef336',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Sesame Chicken, wash 350 grams of chicken breast with water. Then, place it onto a cutting board and slice it crosswise across the grain into thin long strips using a sharp knife. Then, keep the chicken strips in a bowl. Next, peel and finely chop 2 teaspoons of garlic. Wash and finely chop 2 fresh red chilies. Next, in a small bowl, crack an egg and lightly beat it using a spoon or a fork.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f07f81d556f1d370234cd90','5f07f75559142db0285ef336',2,'P2: Marinate the Chicken','To marinate the chicken for Sesame Chicken, add 350 grams of sliced chicken strips to a large bowl. Add 2 teaspoons of chopped garlic, half a teaspoon of salt, and half a teaspoon of black pepper powder. Next, add 2 teaspoons of soy sauce, 1 tablespoon of cornflour, and 1 chopped fresh red chili followed by 1 beaten egg. Mix it well and coat the chicken pieces evenly with the marinade. Then, cover it with a plate and allow it to rest for 1 hour. While the chicken marinates, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":60,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":60,"flame":0}'),
('5f07f8a6556f1d370234cd91','5f07f75559142db0285ef336',3,'P3: Prepare the Sauce','To prepare the sauce mix for Sesame Chicken, first, in a bowl, add 1.5 tablespoons of tomato ketchup, 1.5 tablespoons of soy sauce, 1.5 tablespoons of honey, and 1.5 tablespoons of brown sugar. Mix it well and prepare a mix of the sauce. Next, to make the cornflour slurry, add 3 tablespoons of cornflour in a small bowl along with 1/4 cup of water and mix it well to avoid any lumps.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f07f8f459142db0285ef337','5f07f75559142db0285ef336',4,'P4: Toast Sesame Seeds','For Sesame Chicken, add a tablespoon of white sesame seeds to a small pan and lightly toast them over medium-low flame for 2-3 minutes until fragrant. Then, turn off the flame and take it out into a small bowl.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f07f942556f1d370234cd92','5f07f75559142db0285ef336',5,'M1: Fry the Chicken','To fry the chicken strips for Sesame Chicken, first, heat 1 cup of cooking oil in a Kadai over medium flame for 2-3 minutes. Once the oil is hot, carefully drop the marinated chicken strips into it, one by one. Then, deep fry them over medium flame for 5-6 minutes until golden and crisp. Once the chicken cubes are tender-crisp, turn off the flame and take them out onto a plate and set aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f07fcdd59142db0285ef338','5f07f75559142db0285ef336',6,'M2: Cook the Sauce','To cook the sauce for Sesame Chicken, add the prepared mix of sauce to a pan followed by 1/4 cup of water and mix it well. Then, cook the sauce over medium flame for 2 minutes, while stirring in between. Next, add the prepared cornflour slurry to the sauce and keep stirring it continuously over a low flame until it has combined well with the sauce. Then, continue to cook the sauce over medium flame for 3-4 minutes until it turns glossy and color changes to dark brown. Keep stirring the sauce using a whisk to avoid any lumps.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f07fd1959142db0285ef33a','5f07f75559142db0285ef336',7,'M3: Garnish','As the sauce turns slightly thick and has a nice glaze, add the fried chicken strips and mix it well. Then, reduce the flame to low and simmer the chicken with the sauce for 2 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and garnish it with a tablespoon of chopped spring onion greens and chopped red chilies. Finish it off with a tablespoon of toasted sesame seeds and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),
('5f07ffbcfc298c2ba9ed07b9','5f07fee459142db0285ef33b',1,'P1: Chopping','For Hyderabadi green chicken curry, first, wash and clean 400 grams of chicken thoroughly with water. Next, peel, wash, and finely slice 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and prick 1/4 cup of mint leaves. Wash and roughly chop half a cup of coriander leaves. Peel 5 cloves of garlic. Wash, peel, and roughly chop a 1-inch piece of ginger. Wash and slit 4 nos green chilies.','prep_method','{"active_time":14,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f08003d556f1d370234cd93','5f07fee459142db0285ef33b',2,'P2: Fry Onions','To make the Birista for Hyderabadi green chicken curry, heat 2 tablespoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Next, add 1/4 cup of sliced onions and fry them over medium flame for 7-8 minutes until onions are crisp and golden brown. Then, turn off the flame and take out the brown onions onto a kitchen napkin to dab off the excess oil.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f0801a8556f1d370234cd95','5f07fee459142db0285ef33b',3,'P3: Prepare Mint & Coriander Paste','To prepare the mint-coriander paste for Hyderabadi Green Chicken Curry, in a blender jar, add half a cup of coriander leaves, 5 cloves of garlic, and a 1-inch piece of ginger followed by 4 green chilies. Feel free to add less or more chilies as per taste. Next, add 1/4 cup of mint leaves along with 1/4 cup of the prepared birista and 5 nos cashews. Then, cover the jar with a lid and blend it well into a fine paste.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f080238fc298c2ba9ed07c0','5f07fee459142db0285ef33b',4,'P4: Marinate Chicken','To marinate the chicken for Hyderabadi green chicken curry, first, add 400 grams of chicken to a large bowl. Next, add half a teaspoon of salt, half a teaspoon of black pepper powder, 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, and half a cup of curd. Next, add the prepared mint-coriander paste to this and mix it well. Coat the chicken pieces well with the marinade and allow it to rest for 1 hour. While the chicken marinates, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":60,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":60,"flame":0}'),('5f0802ca59142db0285ef340','5f07fee459142db0285ef33b',5,'M1: Cook Chicken','To make Hyderabadi Chicken Curry, heat 2 tablespoons of cooking oil in a deep bottom pan over medium flame for a minute. Next, add the marinated chicken pieces to the pan along with the marinade and mix it well. Then, cover it with a lid and cook the chicken over low flame for 20 minutes. Keep stirring it occasionally. While the chicken is simmering, please move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":20,"flame":3}'),
('5f08030559142db0285ef341','5f07fee459142db0285ef33b',6,'M2: Continue Simmering the Curry','After simmering the Hyderabadi green chicken curry, take off the lid and stir it gently. Then, again cover it with a lid and continue to simmer it over medium flame for 10 minutes until the chicken is tender and cooked through. While the chicken is simmering, please move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":10,"flame":2}'),('5f08037d556f1d370234cd96','5f07fee459142db0285ef33b',7,'M3: Garnish','After simmering the Hyderabadi green chicken curry, take off the lid and add 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala. Mix it well and cover it with a lid. Continue to simmer the chicken for another 2 minutes so it gains the flavour from garam masala. Then, turn off the flame and take it out in a serving bowl. Garnish it with a small sprig of mint leaves and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('5f080d2c556f1d370234cd99','5f080cc5556f1d370234cd98',1,'P1: Soak Chicken','For Gongura Chicken, first, wash and clean 400 grams of chicken thoroughly with water and keep it in a large bowl. Add 2 cups of water and a teaspoon of salt into it. Then, soak it in salt water for 1 hour. While the chicken is soaking, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":60,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":60,"flame":0}'),('5f080d9c556f1d370234cd9a','5f080cc5556f1d370234cd98',2,'P2: Prep Ingredients','For Gongura Chicken, wash half a bunch of sorrel leaves thoroughly with water to remove all the dirt. Then, separate 1 cup of sorrel leaves. Peel, wash and finely chop half a  cup of onions. Wash and finely chop half a cup of tomatoes. Wash and slit 2 nos green chilies. Wash 10 nos curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":14,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f080e59556f1d370234cd9b','5f080cc5556f1d370234cd98',3,'M1: Fry Chillies and Onions','To make Gongura Chicken, heat 1/4 cup of cooking oil in a Kadai over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Next, add 10 nos curry leaves, 2 nos slit green chilies, and 1 dry red chili followed by 1/2 cup of onions and half a teaspoon of salt. Saute and fry the onions over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5f080ec2556f1d370234cd9c','5f080cc5556f1d370234cd98',4,'M2: Add Tomatoes etc.','After frying the onions, add 2 teaspoons of ginger-garlic paste and fry it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until the raw smell of garlic fades away. Next, add half a teaspoon of turmeric powder and mix it well. Add half a cup of chopped tomatoes and mix it well. Then, cook the tomatoes over medium flame for 4-5 minutes until tender.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5f081206556f1d370234cd9d','5f080cc5556f1d370234cd98',5,'M3: Add Masala Powders','After cooking the tomatoes, add a teaspoon of red chili powder followed by a teaspoon of coriander powder. Mix it well and cook the masala over low flame for 1-2 minutes until oil separates. After that, add 1 cup of chopped sorrel leaves and mix them well with the masala. Then, fry the sorrel leaves over low flame for 2-3 minutes. Make sure to cook the leaves over low flame only, as when exposed to heat for long the leaves will lose all the moisture.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5f0812a6556f1d370234cd9e','5f080cc5556f1d370234cd98',6,'M4: Add Chicken','As the sorrel leaves slightly shrivels, add 400 grams of chicken and mix it well. Then, fry the chicken pieces with the masala over medium flame for 3-4 minutes. After that, add 1/4 cup of water and mix it well. Then, cover it with a lid and cook the chicken over low flame for 20 minutes until it is tender and cooked through. Keep stirring the chicken occasionally. Also, while cooking the chicken if the masala gets too dry then add some water as required. While the chicken is simmering, please move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":20,"flame":2}'),('5f0812fc59142db0285ef344','5f080cc5556f1d370234cd98',7,'M5: Final Touches','After simmering the Gongura Chicken, take off the lid and mix it well. By this time masala should release the oil.  Add 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala and mix it well. Then, turn off the flame and take it out into a serving bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('5f081ff2fc298c2ba9ed07c3','5f081f6e556f1d370234cda3',1,'P1: Chop Ingredients','For Butter Garlic Prawns, peel and finely chop 1.5 tablespoons of garlic. Wash and finely chop 2 green chilies. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of spring onion greens. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash and cut a lime into halves. Then, squeeze the lime juice in a small bowl using a squeezer.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5f08203259142db0285ef349','5f081f6e556f1d370234cda3',2,'P2: Prep Prawns','For Butter Garlic Prawns, rinse 300 grams of prawns in cold water and discard any discolored or slimy ones. Then, hold the prawn with one hand and firmly twist off the head using your other hand. Then, pull off the tail, peel away the outer shell, and pull off the legs from the underside of the shell. Similarly, clean all the prawns and keep them in a bowl. If using the deveined prawns, then just rinse them under cold water and clean them. Next, add a tablespoon of cornflour and coat the prawns well with it.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f0820f059142db0285ef34b','5f081f6e556f1d370234cda3',3,'M1: Cook Prawns','To make Butter Garlic Prawns, heat a tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Next, add the prawns and stir-fry them over high flame for 1-2 minutes. Keep flipping the prawns so they are evenly browned on all sides. Prawns should be semi-cooked at this stage. Make sure not to cook them through. As the prawns turn slightly golden-crisp, turn off the flame and take them out onto a plate.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":4}'),('5f08213959142db0285ef34c','5f081f6e556f1d370234cda3',4,'M2: Make the Sauce','Next, to the same pan, add a teaspoon of cooking oil followed by a tablespoon of salted butter. Mix it well and heat it over medium flame. Next, add 1.5 tablespoons of chopped garlic and fry it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes until fragrant. After that, add 2 nos chopped green chilies followed by 1 tablespoon of chopped spring onions and 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves. Stir and fry it over medium flame for a minute.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f0821a359142db0285ef34d','5f081f6e556f1d370234cda3',5,'M3: Combine Sauce and Prawns','Next, add the fried prawns along with half a teaspoon of black pepper powder and 1/4 teaspoon of salt. Be careful while adding the salt as the butter used in the dish is already salted. Next, add half a teaspoon of chili flakes and mix it well. Stir-fry the prawns over medium-high flame for 2-3 minutes until it has a nice sear on each side and turn tender-crisp. Prawns should be slightly overcooked at this stage. Then, add a teaspoon of butter and finish it off with 2 teaspoons of lime juice. Stir-fry the prawns with light hands to mix the butter and lime juice. Then, turn off the flame and take them out into a serving bowl. Garnish with a tablespoon of spring onions and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5f0827c059142db0285ef351','5f08262359142db0285ef350',1,'P1: Soak Mustard Seeds','For Steamed Mustard Prawns, in a small bowl, add 2 tablespoons of yellow mustard seeds and 1 tablespoon of black mustard seeds. Make sure to add more yellow mustard in the paste than black to get a nice yellow colored paste. Next, add a tablespoon of poppy seeds and mix them well. Then, soak it in 1/4 cup of water for 1 hour. While the mustard is soaking please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":60,"advanced_prep_time":60,"timer":60,"flame":0}'),
('5f082805fc298c2ba9ed07c7','5f08262359142db0285ef350',2,'P2: Prep Prawns','For Steamed Mustard Prawns, first, rinse the 12 nos deveined prawns in the cold water and clean them thoroughly. If using shelled prawns, hold the prawn with one hand and firmly twist off the head using your other hand. Then, pull off the tail, peel away the outer shell, and pull off the legs from the underside of the shell. Similarly, clean the rest of the prawns. Next, wash and slit 2 nos green chilies.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f0828ac59142db0285ef353','5f08262359142db0285ef350',3,'P3: Make Mustard Paste','To prepare the mustard paste for Steamed Mustard Prawns, add 2 tablespoons of desiccated coconut to the soaked mustard seeds. Next, add 1 green chili followed by 1/4 teaspoon of salt and add this to a blender jar. Then, blend it well into a thick paste and take it out in a steel container that has a lid.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f082929556f1d370234cda5','5f08262359142db0285ef350',4,'P4: Make Mustard Paste','Next, add 1 tablespoon of turmeric powder and 2 tablespoons of thick curd to the prepared mustard paste. The curd used in the marinade should be thick, not runny. You can also use hung curd in the marinade. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of salt along with half a teaspoon of sugar and mix it well. Then, add the cleaned prawns and coat them well with the marinade. Next, cover it with a lid and allow the prawns to sit in the marinade for 1 hour. While the prawns are marinating, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":60,"advanced_prep_time":60,"timer":60,"flame":0}'),('5f082a07fc298c2ba9ed07c9','5f08262359142db0285ef350',5,'M1: Steam Prawns','To make the steamed mustard prawns, first, add 6 cups of water to a deep bottom pan or a steamer. Then, bring it to a rolling boil. While the water boils, add 2 nos slit green chilies to the marinated prawns followed by 3 tablespoons of mustard oil and mix it well. It''s important to use mustard oil in the dish as it''s pungent character and mildly bitter taste is the key flavour of this dish. Then, mix it well and cover the steel box with the lid and carefully place the box in the boiling water pan or steamer. Cover the steamer and allow it to steam over medium flame for 15 minutes. While the prawns are steaming, please move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":15,"flame":3}'),('5f082a3ffc298c2ba9ed07ca','5f08262359142db0285ef350',6,'M2: Remove from steamer','After steaming the mustard prawns, carefully take out the steel box from the steamer and allow it to cool down for some time. Then, remove the lid and take out the steamed prawns in a serving bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":15,"flame":2}'),
('5f082e37fc298c2ba9ed07cc','5f082da5fc298c2ba9ed07cb',1,'P1: Marinate Chicken','To marinate the chicken for Roasted Chicken & Potatoes, first, wash and clean 350 grams of chicken thoroughly with water. Next, in a large bowl, add 2 tablespoons of olive oil, half a salt, half a teaspoon of black pepper powder, and half a teaspoon of garlic powder. Next, add a teaspoon of paprika, half a teaspoon of cumin powder, half a teaspoon of oregano followed by half a teaspoon of dried thyme and mix it well.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f082e8459142db0285ef355','5f082da5fc298c2ba9ed07cb',2,'P2: Marinate the Chicken','Next, add the chicken pieces to the marinade and mix it well until chicken pieces are well coated with the marinade. Then, cover it with a plastic wrap or a plate and let it rest for at least 1 hour. While the chicken marinates, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":60,"advanced_prep_time":60,"timer":60,"flame":0}'),('5f082f02556f1d370234cda7','5f082da5fc298c2ba9ed07cb',3,'P3: Prep Vegetables','For Roasted Chicken & Potatoes, wash 2 medium-sized potatoes well with water and cut them into quarters. If the skin of the potatoes is too thick then, remove the skin otherwise leave the potato skins on. Next, peel, wash, and finely slice 1/4 cup of onions. Peel and wash 4 cloves of garlic.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f082f83556f1d370234cda8','5f082da5fc298c2ba9ed07cb',4,'M1: Season Potaotes','For Roasted Chicken & Potatoes, add 1 cup of quartered potatoes in a large bowl. Add half a teaspoon of fresh rosemary and 1/4 teaspoon of salt followed by a tablespoon of olive oil. Toss the potatoes with the seasoning and mix it well. Then, transfer the potatoes to a baking tray along with the marinated chicken pieces and arrange them on the tray.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f082fbf556f1d370234cda9','5f082da5fc298c2ba9ed07cb',5,'M2: Bake the Potatoes and Chicken','Next, add 1/4 cup of sliced onions followed by half a teaspoon of fresh rosemary and carefully place the baking tray in the oven. Then bake the chicken and potatoes at 220°C for 50-60 minutes until the chicken is cooked through and potatoes are tender-crisp. While the chicken and potatoes are baking, please move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":60,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5f082fe3556f1d370234cdaa','5f082da5fc298c2ba9ed07cb',6,'M3: Ready to Serve','After roasting the chicken and potatoes, carefully take them out of the oven. Transfer the dish to a serving plate and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f0c029dfc298c2ba9ed07ce','5f0c00db59142db0285ef35f',1,'P1: Prep Poha and Defrost Peas','For Tomato Poha, first, place a sieve over a large bowl and add 1.5 cups of thick poha into it. Then, sieve the poha well. Next, sprinkle about 2-3 tablespoons of water in the poha and toss it gently with hands or a spoon to moisten the poha. Then, set it aside for 15 minutes. Next, thaw 1/4 cup of frozen green peas and soak it in 1 cup of water for 10 minutes. While the poha and peas are soaking, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":15,"flame":0}'),('5f0c035059142db0285ef360','5f0c00db59142db0285ef35f',2,'P2:  Chop Ingredients','For Tomato Poha, peel, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 3/4 cup of tomatoes.  Peel and finely chop a half-inch piece of ginger. Wash and slit 2 nos green chilies. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves. Grate 3 tablespoons of fresh coconut. Wash and cut a lime into halves and squeeze 1 teaspoon of lime juice in a small bowl. Wash 8 nos curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f0c03a9fc298c2ba9ed07cf','5f0c00db59142db0285ef35f',3,'M1: Temper Spices and Onions','To make Tomato Poha, heat 2 tablespoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add half a teaspoon of mustard seeds followed by half a teaspoon of cumin seeds and let it splutter for a few seconds. Next, add a half-inch piece of chopped ginger and fry it over medium flame for a minute. After that, add  2 nos slit green chilies followed by 1/4 cup of chopped onions and fry the onions over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f0c03f659142db0285ef361','5f0c00db59142db0285ef35f',4,'M2: Add Peas and Tomatoes','After frying the onions, add 1/4 cup of green peas and stir fry the peas with the onions for 1-2 minutes. Next, add 3/4 cup of chopped tomatoes followed by half a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Then, cover it with a lid and cook it over low flame for 10 minutes until peas and tomatoes turn tender. While it is simmering, please move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":10,"flame":2}'),
('5f0c0474556f1d370234cdaf','5f0c00db59142db0285ef35f',5,'M3: Garnish','After simmering the peas for Tomato Poha, take off the lid and fry the masala over medium flame for a minute. Then, add 1.5 cups of soaked poha and gently mix it with the masala. Next, add 3/4 teaspoon of sambar powder followed by 2 tablespoons of chopped coriander leaves and a teaspoon of lime juice. Gently mix it and then, add 3 tablespoons of grated fresh coconut and stir it gently. Turn off the flame and take it out into a serving bowl and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('5f0c079d59142db0285ef362','5f0c075f556f1d370234cdb0',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Andhra Chilli Chicken, first, wash and clean 400 grams of chicken thoroughly with water. Wash and slit 10 nos green chilies. Next, to prepare the cornflour slurry, in a small bowl, add 2 teaspoons of cornflour followed by 1/4 cup of water and mix it well to prepare a thin slurry.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f0c08e5fc298c2ba9ed07d0','5f0c075f556f1d370234cdb0',2,'M1: Cook Chicken','To cook the chicken for Andhra Chilli Chicken, heat 1.5 tablespoons of ghee in a pressure cooker over medium flame for a minute. Next, add 10 nos slit green chilies and fry them over medium flame for a minute. Then, add 400 grams of chicken pieces and fry them over medium flame for 4-5 minutes until it''s pink color slightly fades away.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f0c094959142db0285ef363','5f0c075f556f1d370234cdb0',3,'M2: Close the Pressure Cooker','Next, add a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Then, add 1.5 cups of water and bring it to a boil. As it comes to a boil, cover it with a lid and pressure cook the chicken over a high flame until two whistles. After that, simmer it for 5 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the chicken is cooking, please move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":12,"flame":2}'),('5f0c0a1b556f1d370234cdb1','5f0c075f556f1d370234cdb0',4,'M3: Make the Curry','To make Andhra Chilli Chicken, heat 2 tablespoons of ghee in a kadai over medium flame. Next, carefully add the cooked chicken pieces to the hot ghee and fry them over medium flame for 3-4 minutes. After that, add the chicken broth and mix it well. Then, allow it to boil over medium flame for 2-3 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5f0c0ad6fc298c2ba9ed07d1','5f0c075f556f1d370234cdb0',5,'M4: Season the Curry','Next, add a tablespoon of soy sauce followed by 2 teaspoons of lime juice and the prepared cornflour slurry. Mix it well and keep stirring it continuously over medium flame until the slurry is well combined with the broth. Then, cook it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until the broth slightly thickens. Keep stirring in between to avoid any lumps. Then, turn off the flame and take it out in a serving bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5f0c1049fc298c2ba9ed07d2','5f0c0fbb59142db0285ef364',1,'P1: Prepare the Manchurian Batter','To prepare the chicken mince mixture for Chicken Manchurian, add 250 grams of minced chicken to a large bowl. Next, add half a teaspoon of salt, half a teaspoon of black pepper powder and half a teaspoon of ginger-garlic paste. Add a teaspoon of cornflour along with 2 teaspoons of all-purpose flour and crack an egg into this. Then, mix it well using a whisk and let it sit for 15 minutes. While the mixture marinates, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":15,"flame":0}'),('5f0c10f6fc298c2ba9ed07d3','5f0c0fbb59142db0285ef364',2,'P2: Prep Ingredients','For Chicken Manchurian, peel, wash and finely chop half a cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of green capsicum. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup red capsicum. Wash, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of spring onions. Wash, peel and finely chop a 1-inch piece of ginger. Peel and finely chop 2 teaspoons of garlic. Next, to prepare the cornflour slurry, in a small bowl, add 2 teaspoons of cornflour followed by 1/4 cup of water and mix it well to prepare a thin slurry.','prep_method','{"active_time":18,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f0c113dfc298c2ba9ed07d4','5f0c0fbb59142db0285ef364',3,'M1: Fry the Chicken Manchurian','To fry the chicken balls for Chicken Manchurian, first, heat 3/4 cup of cooking oil in a kadai over medium flame for 2-3 minutes. Once the oil is hot, take a small lemon sized portion of the prepared chicken mince mixture and shape it into a small ball. Then, carefully drop it into the hot oil. Similarly, make the rest of the balls from the mixture and drop them into the oil, one by one. Then, shallow fry them over medium flame for 5-6 minutes until golden and crisp. Once the chicken balls are crisp and evenly browned, turn off the flame and take them out onto a plate and set aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f0c1186fc298c2ba9ed07d5','5f0c0fbb59142db0285ef364',4,'M2: Prepare the Gravy','To make the gravy for Chicken Manchurian, heat a tablespoon of sesame oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Next, add half a cup of chopped onions followed by a 1-inch piece of chopped of ginger and 2 teaspoons of chopped garlic. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped green capsicum and mix it well. Then, stir-fry the vegetables over high flame for 2-3 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5f0c11f7556f1d370234cdb2','5f0c0fbb59142db0285ef364',5,'M3: Add Sauces','Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped red capsicum and fry it for a minute over medium flame. After that add 1/4 cup of chopped spring onions both whites and greens and saute the vegetables over high flame for 1-2 minutes. Next, add 2 teaspoons of vinegar, 2 teaspoons of soy sauce, and 1 tablespoon of red chili sauce followed by 2 teaspoons of tomato ketchup and mix it well. Then cook the sauces over high flame for a minute.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5f0c1236fc298c2ba9ed07d6','5f0c0fbb59142db0285ef364',6,'M4: Add the Slurry','Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of black pepper powder and mix it well. After that, add the prepared cornflour slurry followed by 1/4 cup of water. Mix it well and keep stirring it continuously over medium flame until the slurry is well combined with the sauce. Cook it over medium-low flame for 1-2 minutes until the sauce thickens. Season it with a 1/4 teaspoon of salt and mix it well.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5f0c126659142db0285ef365','5f0c0fbb59142db0285ef364',7,'M5: Add the Manchurian','Next, add the fried chicken balls to the Manchurian gravy and coat them well with the sauce. Then, allow it to simmer in the sauce for 1-2 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and take out the ready chicken Manchurian in a serving bowl. Garnish it with a tablespoon of spring onion greens and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('5f0c1d0859142db0285ef366','5f0c1c75fc298c2ba9ed07d7',1,'P1: Marinate the Chicken','For Dragon Chicken, first, rinse 250 grams of boneless chicken in the water and clean it thoroughly. Next, add the chicken pieces to a large bowl. Add 1/4 teaspoon of salt, 1/4 teaspoon of black pepper powder, and 2 teaspoons of soy sauce. Next, crack an egg into this and add a tablespoon of cornflour. Then, mix it well and coat the chicken pieces well with the marinade. Then, allow it to sit in the marinade for 30 minutes. While the chicken marinates, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":30,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":30,"flame":0}'),('5f0c1d8b556f1d370234cdb3','5f0c1c75fc298c2ba9ed07d7',2,'P2: Chop Vegetables','For Dragon Chicken, wash and finely slice 1/4 cup of green capsicum. Wash and finely slice 1/4 cup of spring onion whites. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of spring onion greens. Wash, peel and finely chop a half-inch piece of ginger.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5f0c1e56556f1d370234cdb4','5f0c1c75fc298c2ba9ed07d7',3,'P3: Prep Ingredients','Next, wash, peel and finely chop a teaspoon of garlic. Coarsely crush 1/4 cup of cashew nuts in a mortar & pestle or roughly chop them. Next, to prepare the cornflour slurry, in a small bowl, add 2 teaspoons of cornflour followed by 1/4 cup of water and mix it well to prepare a thin slurry.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f0c1ea2fc298c2ba9ed07d8','5f0c1c75fc298c2ba9ed07d7',4,'M1: Fry Chicken','To fry the chicken cubes for Dragon Chicken, first, heat 1 cup of cooking oil in a kadai over medium flame for 2-3 minutes. Once the oil is hot, carefully drop the marinated chicken pieces into it one by one. Then, deep fry them over medium flame for 6-7 minutes until golden and crisp. Once the chicken pieces are crisp and evenly browned, turn off the flame and take them out onto a plate and set aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f0c20b6fc298c2ba9ed07d9','5f0c1c75fc298c2ba9ed07d7',5,'M2: Temper Ingredients','To make Dragon Chicken, heat 2 tablespoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped cashew nuts and fry them over medium flame for 2-3 minutes. As the cashews turn slightly golden, add a half-inch piece of chopped ginger followed by a teaspoon of chopped garlic and fry it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes until fragrant.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f0c216859142db0285ef367','5f0c1c75fc298c2ba9ed07d7',6,'M3: add Vegetables and Sauces','Next, add a teaspoon of chili flakes and saute it over low flame for a few seconds. Add 1/4 cup of sliced spring onion whites along with 1/4 cup of sliced capsicum and stir-fry them over high flame for 2-3 minutes. After that, add 2 teaspoons of soy sauce, 1 tablespoon of red chili sauce followed by 2 tablespoons of tomato ketchup, and mix it well.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5f0c2197556f1d370234cdb6','5f0c1c75fc298c2ba9ed07d7',7,'M4: Add the Slurry','Next, add half a teaspoon of sugar and mix it well. Then, cook the sauces over medium-high flame for 1-2 minutes. Next, add about half a cup of water and stir it well. Then, bring it to a boil over medium flame. As it comes to a boil, reduce the flame to low and add the prepared cornflour slurry while stirring it continuously over medium flame until the slurry is well combined with the sauce. Then, cook it over medium-low flame for 1-2 minutes until the sauce slightly thickens.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5f0c2216fc298c2ba9ed07da','5f0c1c75fc298c2ba9ed07d7',8,'M5: Season and Garnish','As the sauce thickens, season it with a 1/4 teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Be careful while adding the salt, as we have added soy sauce to the dish which is salty. Next, add the fried chicken pieces and coat them well with the sauce. Then, let the chicken cook with the sauce over low flame for 5 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and finish it off by adding 2 tablespoons of chopped spring onion greens. Take it out in a serving bowl. Garnish it with some white sesame seeds and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":5,"flame":2}'),('5f0e9597556f1d370234cdf2','5f0d99a9556f1d370234cdf0',1,'P1: Marinate the Chicken','For Orange Chicken, rinse the boneless chicken breasts in the water and clean them well. Next, place the chicken breast on a cutting board and slice into bite-size cubes. Then, add the chicken cubes to a large bowl and crack an egg into this. Next, add a teaspoon of cornflour followed by 2 teaspoons of all-purpose flour. Next,  add 1/4 teaspoon of salt along with  1/4 teaspoon of black pepper powder and mix it well. Coat the chicken pieces evenly with the marinade and allow this to sit for 10 minutes. While the chicken marinates, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":10,"flame":0}'),('5f0e960bfc298c2ba9ed0826','5f0d99a9556f1d370234cdf0',2,'P2: Prep Ingredients','For Orange Chicken, wash, peel and finely chop a half-inch piece of ginger. Wash, peel and finely chop a teaspoon of garlic. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of spring onion greens. Wash a small orange and zest a teaspoon of orange zest. Next, to prepare the cornflour slurry, in a small bowl, add 2 teaspoons of cornflour followed by 1/4 cup of water and mix it well to prepare a thin slurry.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f0e971b556f1d370234cdf3','5f0d99a9556f1d370234cdf0',3,'M1: Fry the Chicken','To fry the chicken for Orange Chicken, first, heat 1 cup of cooking oil in a kadai over medium flame for 2-3 minutes. Once the oil is hot, carefully drop the marinated chicken cubes into it one by one. Then, deep fry them over medium flame for 4-5 minutes until golden and crisp. Fry the chicken pieces in small batches so they don''t stick together. Once the chicken pieces are crisp and evenly browned, turn off the flame and take them out on a kitchen napkin to dab off the excess oil.','cook_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f0e9763fc298c2ba9ed0827','5f0d99a9556f1d370234cdf0',4,'M2: Saute Ginger & Garlic','To make the Orange Chicken, heat a tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame. Next, add a half-inch piece of chopped ginger followed by a teaspoon of chopped garlic. Saute and fry the ginger-garlic over medium flame for 1-2 minutes until fragrant.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5f0e97d5fc298c2ba9ed0828','5f0d99a9556f1d370234cdf0',5,'M3: Add Sauces','Next, add 3/4 cup of orange juice followed by 2 teaspoons of soy sauce and 2 teaspoons of rice wine vinegar. Rice wine vinegar is optional in the dish so if you don''t have it you can skip adding it. Next, add 2 teaspoons of brown sugar followed by a teaspoon of orange zest and mix it well. Then, bring it to a boil over medium flame.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5f0e985bfc298c2ba9ed0829','5f0d99a9556f1d370234cdf0',6,'M4: Add the Slurry and Fried Chicken','As it comes to a rolling boil, add the prepared cornflour slurry and keep stirring it continuously over medium flame until the slurry is well combined. Then, stir and cook it over medium flame until the sauce thickens. After that, add the fried chicken cubes to the sauce, then toss them well until the chicken is well coated with the sauce. Then, turn off the flame and take it out in a serving bowl. Garnish it with a tablespoon of chopped spring onion greens and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5f0e9d06556f1d370234cdf5','5f0e9cc7556f1d370234cdf4',1,'P1: Cook Pasta','To boil the spaghetti For Keema Spaghetti, first, boil 6 cups of water in a deep bottom pan over medium flame. Add half a teaspoon of cooking oil and 1/4 teaspoon of salt into the water and bring it to a rolling boil. As it comes to a boil, add 150 grams of spaghetti and dip it completely in the water. Then, boil the spaghetti over medium-high flame for 8-10 minutes until it is firm to the bite. While the spaghetti is boiling, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":10,"flame":3}'),('5f0e9e9d556f1d370234cdf6','5f0e9cc7556f1d370234cdf4',2,'P2: Chop Ingredients','For Keema Spaghetti, first, rinse 200 grams of chicken mince in the water and clean it thoroughly. Next, wash, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash, peel and finely chop a half-inch piece of ginger. Peel and finely chop a teaspoon of garlic. Wash and finely chop 2 fresh red chilies. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f0e9fa8556f1d370234cdf7','5f0e9cc7556f1d370234cdf4',3,'P3: Finish Cooking the Pasta','After boiling the spaghetti for Keema Spaghetti, turn off the flame and drain off the water. Then, rinse the spaghetti under cold water to prevent it from cooking further and sticking together. Then, set it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5f0ea02d556f1d370234cdf8','5f0e9cc7556f1d370234cdf4',4,'M1: Saute Ginger & Garlic','To make Keema Spaghetti, heat 2 tablespoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame. Next, add a half-inch piece of chopped ginger and a teaspoon of chopped garlic. Saute and fry the ginger-garlic over medium flame for 1-2 minutes until fragrant. After that, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions and fry it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f0ea0abfc298c2ba9ed082a','5f0e9cc7556f1d370234cdf4',5,'M2: Add Chicken and Season it','After frying the onions, add 200 grams of chicken mince and stir it briskly, breaking up the mince into granules. Then, cook the chicken for 5-6 minutes over a medium flame while stirring it continuously to keep it from sticking together and forming lumps. Next, add half a teaspoon of salt followed by 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder and half a teaspoon of black pepper powder. Mix it well and saute the chicken over medium flame for 2-3 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5f0ea0e559142db0285ef3bc','5f0e9cc7556f1d370234cdf4',6,'M3: Add Tomatoes','Next, add 2 nos chopped fresh red chilies and saute it for a minute. Add 3/4 cup of tomato puree to the mince and mix it well. Then, allow it to simmer over low flame for 5-7 minutes until the chicken mince is cooked through. While the keema is simmering, please move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":7,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":7,"flame":2}'),('5f0ea10b556f1d370234cdf9','5f0e9cc7556f1d370234cdf4',7,'M4: Garnish','After simmering the chicken mince for keema spaghetti, give it a final stir and turn off the flame. Next, to plate the dish, take out the boiled spaghetti in a serving plate. Add the prepared keema on top. Garnish it with a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('5f0ea77b556f1d370234cdfb','5f0ea722556f1d370234cdfa',1,'P1: Prepare the Dough','To prepare the dough for Keema Paratha, in a large mixing bowl, add 1.5 cups of wheat flour followed by  1/4 teaspoon of carom seeds and half a teaspoon of salt. Next, add 2 teaspoons of ghee and gradually add about half a cup of water. Mix it well and knead it into a smooth dough. Next, cover it with a damp cloth and allow it to rest for 15 minutes. While the dough is resting, please move on to the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":15,"flame":0}'),
('5f0ea7fefc298c2ba9ed082c','5f0ea722556f1d370234cdfa',3,'P2: Prep Ingredients for Filling','For Keema Paratha, peel, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Peel, wash, and slice 1/4 cup of onions into thin rings. Next, wash, peel, and finely chop a half-inch piece of ginger. Peel and finely chop a teaspoon of garlic. Wash and finely chop 2 green chilies. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of mint leaves. Wash and cut a lime into halves and squeeze 2 teaspoons of lime juice in a small bowl.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f0ea8cafc298c2ba9ed082d','5f0ea722556f1d370234cdfa',2,'M1: Saute Ginger, Garlic, & Onions','To cook prepare the keema stuffing for keema paratha, heat 2 tablespoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add a half-inch piece of chopped ginger followed by a teaspoon of chopped garlic and 1/4 cup of chopped onions. Saute and fry the onions over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until translucent.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f0ea924fc298c2ba9ed082e','5f0ea722556f1d370234cdfa',4,'M2: Add Chicken','After frying the onions, add 2 chopped green chilies and saute it for a minute. Next, add 200 grams of chicken mince and stir it briskly to break up the mince into granules. Then, cook the chicken for 6-8 minutes over a medium flame while stirring it in between to keep it from sticking together and forming lumps. Saute and cook the mince until it is tender and cooked through.','prep_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5f0eaa07556f1d370234cdfc','5f0ea722556f1d370234cdfa',5,'M3: Season the Filling','After cooking the chicken mince, add half a teaspoon of salt, 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, a teaspoon of red chili powder, a teaspoon of coriander powder, and half a teaspoon of cumin powder, followed by a teaspoon of chicken masala. Mix it well and cook the mince with the masala over low flame for 1-2 minutes. Next, add a teaspoon of ghee and mix it well. Then, add 2 tablespoons of chopped coriander leaves along with 2 tablespoons of chopped mint leaves. Add 2 teaspoons of lime juice and mix it well. Then, turn off the flame and allow the chicken stuffing to cool down completely.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":10,"flame":2}'),('5f0eaae1556f1d370234cdfd','5f0ea722556f1d370234cdfa',6,'M4: Prepare the Dough','To make the Keema Paratha, first, divide the prepared dough into small equal-sized balls. Next, take a dough ball and dust some flour. Then, gently press it and roll it into a round paratha as shown and keep it aside. Similarly, take another dough ball and roll it out into a thin round paratha. Next, add and spread about 2-3 tablespoons of the prepared keema stuffing onto the rolled out paratha. Then, cover it with another rolled out paratha and seal edges across the circumference of the paratha as shown. Then, dust some flour and gently roll it spread the stuffing evenly inside the paratha.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5f0eab1afc298c2ba9ed082f','5f0ea722556f1d370234cdfa',7,'M5: Cook the Paratha','Next, place the stuffed paratha onto a hot Tawa and cook it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Flip and cook both the sides of paratha until slightly golden. Then, apply half a teaspoon of cooking oil to each side of the paratha and continue to cook it for another 2-3 minutes, until it turns golden and crisp. After the paratha is evenly cooked from both the sides, slice it into quarters and take it out onto a plate.  Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f0eaeb059142db0285ef3be','5f0eae48556f1d370234cdfe',1,'P1: Chop Ingredients','For Chilli Cheese Toast, peel, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of green capsicum. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of red capsicum. Wash and finely chop 2 nos green chilies. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves. Peel and finely chop a teaspoon of garlic.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f0eaf5afc298c2ba9ed0830','5f0eae48556f1d370234cdfe',2,'P2: Prep Other Ingredients','Next, wash, peel, and grate 1/4 cup of carrot. Grate 1/4 cup of processed cheese in a bowl using a grater. Next, roughly tear 2 yellow cheese slices into small pieces. Next, to make the garlic butter, add 2 tablespoons of butter in a small bowl followed by a teaspoon of chopped garlic and mix it well using a spoon.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f0eafbd59142db0285ef3bf','5f0eae48556f1d370234cdfe',3,'M1: Prep the Slices of Bread','To make Chilii Cheese Toast, first, apply a thin layer of prepared garlic butter to the bread slices. Next, take a bread slice and spread about 1-2 tablespoons of grated processed cheese over it. Next, add a few small pieces of the yellow cheese slice on top of the grated cheese. After that, sprinkle a teaspoon of chopped onions followed by a teaspoon of chopped green and red capsicum.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f0eafea59142db0285ef3c0','5f0eae48556f1d370234cdfe',4,'M2: Add the Toppings','Next, add half a teaspoon of chopped green chilies followed by a teaspoon of chopped coriander leaves and a teaspoon of grated carrots. Season the toast with a pinch of salt and finish it off with some extra cheese on top of it. Prepare the rest of the cheese toasts similarly.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5f0eb042556f1d370234ce00','5f0eae48556f1d370234cdfe',5,'M3: Make the Toast','Next, to toast the Chilli Cheese Toast, carefully lift the prepared toast and place it onto a Tawa. Then, cover it with a lid and cook it over the lowest flame possible until the cheese melts. Make sure to cook the toast only at the low flame as it will take some time for the upper layer of cheese to melt and if the flame is medium or high then the bread will start getting burnt from the bottom. Cook the toast for about 4-5 minutes and keep checking it. Once the cheese melts, take off the lid and take it out onto a serving plate. Slice it into triangles and serve. Make the rest of the chili cheese toasts similarly.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":5,"flame":2}'),('5f0eb333fc298c2ba9ed0831','5f0eb2a1556f1d370234ce01',1,'Prep Ingredients','For Garlic Bread, take the bread loaf and slice it into half an inch thick slices using a bread knife as shown. Next, peel, wash and finely chop a teaspoon of garlic. To make the garlic butter for add 2 tablespoons of butter to a small bowl. Next, add a teaspoon of chopped garlic and mix it well.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f0eb41afc298c2ba9ed0832','5f0eb2a1556f1d370234ce01',2,'M1: Make Garlic Bread','To make Garlic Bread, first, take a bread slice and apply a teaspoon of butter to its one side. Similarly, apply a thin layer of butter to each of the bread slices. Then, heat a pan over medium flame. Once the pan is medium-hot, place the bread slices onto the Tawa keeping the butter-side down. Make sure the pan should not be too hot before you start placing the bread slices on it. Then, toast the bread slices over medium flame until it is crisp and evenly browned. To get the perfect crisp garlic bread, make sure to toast the slices over medium flame for long. Once the bread slices are golden-crisp from one side, carefully flip them and toast the other side similarly. Once the bread slices are evenly browned on all the sides, turn off the flame and take them out onto a serving plate. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f0eb610fc298c2ba9ed0834','5f0eb5c2fc298c2ba9ed0833',1,'P1: Cook Potatoes','To boil the potatoes for Bread Pakora, first, wash 2 nos medium-sized potatoes well with water. Next, put the potatoes in a pressure cooker along with 2 cups of water. Cover it with a lid and pressure cook it over a high flame until one whistle. After the first whistle, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook it for another 8 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the potatoes are boiling, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":10,"flame":3}'),('5f0eb666556f1d370234ce02','5f0eb5c2fc298c2ba9ed0833',2,'P2: Prep Ingredients','For Bread Pakora, wash and finely chop 1 nos green chili. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves. Wash, peel and finely chop a half-inch piece of ginger. Next, after boiling the potatoes, take them out of the pressure cooker and allow it cool for some time. Then, gently peel off the skin and mash them using a potato masher.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5f0eb6d6556f1d370234ce03','5f0eb5c2fc298c2ba9ed0833',3,'P3: Prepare the Stuffing','To prepare the stuffing for Bread Pakoda, add 1 cup of boiled and mashed potatoes to a large bowl. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of cumin seeds, a half-inch piece of chopped ginger, 1 nos chopped green chili, and a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves. Next, add half a teaspoon of red chili powder followed by half a teaspoon of salt and mix it well to prepare the stuffing.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f0eb733fc298c2ba9ed0835','5f0eb5c2fc298c2ba9ed0833',4,'P4: Assemble the Pakoras','Next, take a bread slice and spread a thick layer of the prepared potato stuffing to it. Spread the stuffing evenly, from the center till the edges of the bread slice. Then, cover it with a bread slice and press it gently. Prepare the rest of the stuffed bread pakoras similarly.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f0eb7a059142db0285ef3c1','5f0eb5c2fc298c2ba9ed0833',5,'P5: Prepare the Batter','To prepare the batter for Bread Pakora, add 3/4 cup of gram flour in a large bowl. Add 1/4 teaspoon of salt, 1/4 teaspoon of carom seeds, 1/4 teaspoon of red chili powder followed by a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves, and 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder. Next, add 3/4 cup of water and mix it well. The ratio of the gram flour and water in the batter is 1:1. Keep the quantities of both gram flour and water exactly the same in the batter. Next, mix it well using a whisk to avoid any lumps and prepare the batter.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f0eb841556f1d370234ce04','5f0eb5c2fc298c2ba9ed0833',6,'M1: Fry the Pakora','To make the bread pakora, first, add a tablespoon of cooking oil to a Tawa and let it heat over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. while the Tawa is heating, take the prepared stuffed bread and carefully dip it in the gram flour batter to coat it well on all the sides. Then, place it onto the hot Tawa and cook it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes. Next, carefully flip the bread pakora and cook the other side until it is golden and crisp. After that, hold the pakora with a tong and cook the edges as shown. Once the bread pakora is evenly browned on all sides, take it out onto a plate and slice it into halves. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f0eca8559142db0285ef3e6','5f0eca15fc298c2ba9ed085e',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Dry Fruit Banana Smoothie, first, add half a cup of water in a pan and heat it over medium flame for a minute. Do not boil the water, just warm it. Then, turn off the flame and take it out in a cup. Next, in a bowl, add 5 nos seedless dates, 5 nos almonds, and 5 nos cashews followed by a teaspoon of raisins. Add half a cup of warm water into it and soak the nuts for 15 minutes. While the nuts are soaking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":15,"flame":0}'),
('5f0ecac4fc298c2ba9ed085f','5f0eca15fc298c2ba9ed085e',2,'M1: Make Smoothie','To make the Dry Fruit Banana Smoothie, first, peel and roughly slice 1 nos ripe banana. Next, in a blender jar, add the soaked nuts along with 1 nos sliced banana. Add a tablespoon of honey followed by 1 cup of chilled milk and blend it smooth. Pour the prepared smoothie into glasses and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f15355d1d24e89e57859528','5f15351e1d24e89e57859527',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Grilled Mushroom Sandwich, wash the button mushrooms thoroughly with water to remove all the dirt. Then, finely slice 2 cups of mushrooms. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f15359a1969dae2fbbff449','5f15351e1d24e89e57859527',2,'M1: Saute Mushrooms','To make the stuffing for Grilled Mushroom Sandwich, first, heat 2 tablespoons of butter in a pan. Next, add 2 cups of sliced mushrooms. Then, stir-fry them over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until mushrooms are slightly golden. After that, add 2 teaspoons of garlic paste and mix it well. Then, cook the mushrooms over medium flame for 2-3 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f1535e11d24e89e57859529','5f15351e1d24e89e57859527',3,'M2: Season the Mushrooms','Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of salt followed by 1/4 teaspoon of black pepper powder and mix it well. Stir and fry the mushrooms over high flame for 1-2 minutes. Once the mushrooms are evenly browned, add a tablespoon chopped coriander leaves and mix it well. Then, turn off the flame and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5f1536451969dae2fbbff44a','5f15351e1d24e89e57859527',4,'M3: Toast the Bread','To toast the bread slices for Grilled Mushroom Sandwich, heat 2 teaspoons fo butter on a tawa over medium flame. Next, place the bread slices onto the hot tawa and toast them over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until the slices are slightly browned on one side. After that, take them out onto a plate. Toast the rest of the bread slices similarly.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5f1536c817e1bc857e91efe9','5f15351e1d24e89e57859527',5,'M4: Make Sandwich','To make the Grilled Mushroom Sandwich, take a toasted bread slice and place it onto a plate, toasted side down. Then, add the prepared mushroom stuffing onto it and spread it across evenly. Next, add a slice of provolone cheese and cover the sandwich with another toasted bread slice. Then, carefully place it inside a sandwich grill and grill the sandwich until the red light blinks or the grill beeps. After that, take the sandwich out of the grill and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f153c4d1969dae2fbbff44b','5f153be21d24e89e5785952a',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Mayo Cheese sandwich, wash, peel and grate 1/4 cup of carrots. Wash and finely shred 1/4 cup of cabbage. Peel, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of green capsicum. Grate 1/4 cup of cheddar cheese in a bowl.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f153cb617e1bc857e91efea','5f153be21d24e89e5785952a',2,'P2: Prep Ingredients to make Green Chutney','For Green Chutney, rinse 1 cup of coriander leaves well with water and remove the root ends. Wash and separate 1/4 cup of mint leaves. Peel and wash 3 cloves of garlic. Wash, and peel a 1-inch piece of ginger. Wash and slit 3 nos green chilies. Wash and cut a lemon into halves. Then, squeeze 1 tablespoon lime juice.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f153d3a1d24e89e5785952b','5f153be21d24e89e5785952a',3,'P3: Blend Ingredients to Make Chutney','To make the Green Chutney, in a blender jar, add 1 cup of coriander leaves and 1/4 cup of mint leaves. Next, add 3 cloves of garlic, a 1-inch piece of ginger and 3 nos slit green chilies followed by 2 tablespoons of roasted gram dal and half a teaspoon of cumin powder. Next, add half a teaspoon of chat masala, half a teaspoon of sugar and half a teaspoon of salt along with 1/4 teaspoon of hing and 3 tablespoons of water. Blend it well into a smooth chutney. Take it out into a bowl and add a tablespoon of lime juice. Mix it well and serve.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f153df11d24e89e5785952c','5f153be21d24e89e5785952a',4,'P4: Prepare Filling','To prepare the stuffing for Mayo Cheese Sandwich, in a large bowl, add 1/4 cup of grated carrots, 1/4 cup of chopped cabbage, 1/4 cup of chopped green capsicum, and 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes followed by 1/4 cup of chopped onions. Next, add half a teaspoon of black pepper powder along with 1/4 teaspoon of salt. Add half a cup of mayonnaise and mix it well to prepare the sandiwch stuffing.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5f153e6017e1bc857e91efeb','5f153be21d24e89e5785952a',5,'M1: Assemble the Sandwich','To make the Mayo Cheese Sandwich, first, apply a thin layer of butter to one side of the bread slices. Then, spread a teaspoon of the prepared green chutney to both the bread slices. Next, add a tablespoon of the prepared mayonnaise stuffing to each of the bread slices and spread it evenly. Add a teaspoon of tomato ketchup followed by a tablespoon of grated cheddar cheese.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f153eaa1d24e89e5785952d','5f153be21d24e89e5785952a',6,'M2: Make the Sandwiches','Next, carefully lift a bread slice and layer it onto the other bread slice as shown. Next, apply a teaspoon of butter to another bread slice followed by a teaspoon of green chutney. Then, cover the sandwich with this slice, while keeping the butter-side down and gently press the sandwich. Then, apply a thin layer of butter to the upper layer of the sandwich and carefully place it in a sandwich grill and grill the sandwich until golden. After that, take it out of the sandwich grill and slice it diagonally. Plate the sandwich, finish it off with some grated cheese followed by chili flakes and serve. Make another sandwich similarly.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f15412317e1bc857e91efec','5f1540b01969dae2fbbff44c',1,'AP1: Make Hung Curd','To make the hung curd for Dahi Sandwich, place a sieve over a large mixing bowl and cover it with a muslin cloth as shown. Next, pour 1 cup of fresh curd into the muslin cloth and tie it tightly, tucking the curd inside. Then, carefully place the tied curd over the sieve and refrigerate the bowl for 2 hours. This will allow the excess water to drain off from the curd, leaving the hung curd thick and creamy. While the curd is refrigerating, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":120,"advanced_prep_time":120,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f1541c317e1bc857e91efed','5f1540b01969dae2fbbff44c',2,'P1: Blanch Sweet Corn','To boil the sweet corn kernels for Dahi Sandwich, boil 2 cups of water in a saucepan over a high flame. As the water comes to a boil, add 1/4 cup of sweet corn kernels to the boiling water and continue to boil it for another 4-5 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and drain off water from the boiled corn kernels and keep it aside. While the sweet corn kernels are boiling, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":5,"flame":3}'),('5f1542491d24e89e5785952e','5f1540b01969dae2fbbff44c',3,'P2: Prep Ingredients','For the Dahi Sandwich, wash, peel and grate 1/4 cup of carrot using a grater. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of cabbage. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of capsicum. Next, stack the bread slices and trim the brown edges using a bread knife as shown.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5f1542b61d24e89e5785952f','5f1540b01969dae2fbbff44c',4,'P3: Make the Filling','To prepare the stuffing for Dahi Sandwich, after refrigerating the curd, carefully untie the bundle and take it out in a large mixing bowl. Then, whisk it well using a whisk until smooth. Next, add 1/4 cup of grated carrot, 1/4 cup of chopped cabbage, and 1/4 cup of chopped capsicum followed by 1/4 cup of blanched sweet corn kernels. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of black pepper powder along with 1/4 teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Keep the sandwich stuffing in the refrigerator until use.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f1542f91d24e89e57859530','5f1540b01969dae2fbbff44c',5,'M1: Make Sandwich','To make the Dahi Sandwich, take a bread slice and spread 2 tablespoons of the prepared sandwich filling onto it evenly. Then, cover it with another bread slice and press it gently. Then, slice it into halves and plate the sandwich. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f1546591d24e89e57859531','5f1545d21969dae2fbbff44d',1,'P1: Chop Ingredients','For Bread Omelette, peel, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of green capsicum. Wash and finely chop 2 nos green chilies.  Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f1546da17e1bc857e91efee','5f1545d21969dae2fbbff44d',2,'M1: Make Egg Mixture','For Bread Omelette, first, crack 4 nos eggs in a bowl and beat them well using a fork or a whisk. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions, 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes, and 1/4 cup of chopped capsicum followed by 2 chopped green chilies and 2 tablespoons of chopped coriander leaves. Next, add half a teaspoon of red chili powder, half a teaspoon of black pepper powder followed by half a teaspoon of salt and mix it well.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f1547221969dae2fbbff44e','5f1545d21969dae2fbbff44d',3,'M2: Cook Eggs','To make the Bread Omelette, add 2 teaspoons of cooking oil to a tawa and spread it across evenly. Then, heat it over medium flame for a minute. Next, carefully pour half of the prepared omlette batter and spread it across the tawa. Hold the tawa and slightly shake it to spread the liquid batter across the tawa uniformly. Then, cook it over medium flame for 10-20 seconds.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5f1547941969dae2fbbff44f','5f1545d21969dae2fbbff44d',4,'M3: Continue Cooking to make Bread Omelette','As the omelette starts to get slightly stiff from the bottom, place a bread slice onto it in the center and press it gently. Then, carefully fold the sides of the omelette as shown using a spatula and gently press it so the omlette sides stick to the bread slice. Then, cook it over medium flame 1-2 minutes. Next, carefully flip it and cook the other side for 1-2 minutes until golden. Then, turn off the flame and take it out onto a plate. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f154d6c1d24e89e57859534','5f154c851d24e89e57859532',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Creamy Mushroom Chicken, first, rinse the chicken breasts in water and clean them well. Then, slice them into halves. Next, wash the mushrooms thoroughly with water to remove all the dirt. Then, finely slice half a cup of mushrooms. Peel and finely chop a teaspoon of garlic. Peel, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Grate half a cup of cheddar cheese in a bowl. Wash and finely chop a teaspoon of parsley.','prep_method','{"active_time":17,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f154e151d24e89e57859535','5f154c851d24e89e57859532',2,'M1: Season and Cook the Chicken','To make Creamy Mushroom Chicken, first, season both the sides of chicken breasts with 1/4 teaspoon of salt and half a teaspoon of black pepper powder. Next, heat 2 tablespoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame. Then, add in the seasoned chicken and fry it over medium flame for 4-5 minutes until it is no longer pink and is evenly browned on all sides. Make sure to flip and cook the chicken on all sides until tender-crisp. Then, take it out onto a plate and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f154eb517e1bc857e91efef','5f154c851d24e89e57859532',3,'M2: Add Onions and Garlic','Next, to the same pan, add a teaspoon of chopped garlic followed by 1/4 cup of chopped onions and half a cup of sliced mushrooms. Saute and fry the mushrooms over medium flame for 2-3 minutes or until they begin to change color.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5f154fa417e1bc857e91eff0','5f154c851d24e89e57859532',4,'M3: Add Cream and Stock Water','As the mushrooms turn slightly brown, pour in half a cup of chicken stock followed by half a cup of heavy cream. If you don''t have the chicken stock, add water instead. Then, keep stirring it over a low flame until the cream is well combined with the stock. Make sure to stir the cream at low flame continuously as it might split. Once the sauce is well combined, bring it to a boil over a high flame.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('5f15515417e1bc857e91eff7','5f154c851d24e89e57859532',5,'M4: Add the Cheese','After the sauce comes to a boil, add half a cup of grated cheddar cheese and stir it over medium flame until it melts. Next, add the fried chicken back in and let it simmer for 4 to 5 minutes over a low flame, allowing the sauce to thicken, while spooning some sauce over it. After that, turn off the flame and plate the chicken, spoon the sauce over, and garnish it with a teaspoon of chopped parsley.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('5f15643c1969dae2fbbff451','5f1563a41969dae2fbbff450',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Honey Garlic Butter Chicken, wash and clean the chicken thighs thoroughly with water. Next, season it with 1/4 teaspoon of salt and half a teaspoon of black pepper powder on both sides. Peel and finely chop a teaspoon of garlic. Wash and finely chop a tablespoon of spring onion greens','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f1564d81d24e89e57859540','5f1563a41969dae2fbbff450',2,'M1: Cook Chicken','To make Honey Garlic Butter Chicken, heat a tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame. Place the seasoned chicken in, and fry it over medium flame for 6-7 minutes on each side until it is cooked through and turns slightly golden brown. After that, turn off the flame and take it out onto a plate and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":14,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f15659a17e1bc857e91eff9','5f1563a41969dae2fbbff450',3,'M2: Temper Garlic with Seasonings','Next, to the same, add a tablespoon of butter and allow it to melt over low flame. Add a teaspoon of chopped garlic followed by half a teaspoon of chili flakes and fry the garlic over medium flame until fragrant. After that, add 1/4 cup of honey and 2 teaspoons of dijon mustard. Mix it well and bring it to a boil over medium-high flame.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5f1565f917e1bc857e91effa','5f1563a41969dae2fbbff450',4,'M3: Final Touches','Next, add the fried chicken back in and allow it to simmer for 2-3 minutes while spooning the sauce over it. Cook the chicken until the sauce thickens. After that, turn off the flame and plate the chicken and garnish it with a tablespoon of chopped spring onion greens. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),
('5f1569151d24e89e57859544','5f1568171d24e89e57859542',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Kale Smoothie, first, rinse thoroughly a bunch of kale in water. Then, stack and fold the leaves in half with the topside of the greens folded inward and cut alongside the stems and discard the stems. It''s okay to keep a few stems as it''s going to be pureed. Next, roughly shred 2 cups of kale and keep it in a bowl. Wash, peel, and slice 2 nos ripe bananas.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f1569571d24e89e57859545','5f1568171d24e89e57859542',2,'M1: Make Smoothie','To make the Kale Smoothie, first, add in 2 cups of the chopped kale to a blender jar. Next, add 2 chopped bananas, followed by a tablespoon of whey protein powder and half a teaspoon of peanut butter. Add a tablespoon of chia seeds and pour in 1 cup of water. Cover the jar with a lid and blend it well until smooth. Then, pour the smoothie right away into the serving glasses or mason jar and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f156bfa1969dae2fbbff455','5f156ba71969dae2fbbff454',1,'AP1: Freeze Bananas','For Banana Romaine Smoothie, peel and roughly slice 2 ripe bananas. Then, place them in a plastic ziplock bag and set them in the freezer for 2-3 hours. While the bananas are freezing, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":180,"advanced_prep_time":180,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f156c3a1969dae2fbbff456','5f156ba71969dae2fbbff454',2,'P1: Prep Lettuce','For Banana Romaine Smoothie, wash and remove the leaves of the romaine lettuce from its center stock. Then, roughly shred 2 cups of lettuce leaves as shown and dip the sliced shreds in cold water until use.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f156c901d24e89e57859549','5f156ba71969dae2fbbff454',3,'M1: Make Smoothie','To make Banana Romaine Smoothie, first, add 2 cups of chopped romaine lettuce in a blender jar. Add 2 sliced frozen bananas, a teaspoon of vanilla extract and a teaspoon of sugar. Next, pour in 1 cup of coconut water followed by some ice cubes. Cover the jar with a lid and blend it well until smooth. Then, pour the refreshing smoothie right away into the serving glasses and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5f16849d1969dae2fbbff481','5f16845917e1bc857e91f018',1,'AP1: Freeze the Banana','For Mango Spinach Smoothie, peel and roughly slice 1 ripe banana. Then, place it in a plastic ziplock bag and set it in the freezer for 2-3 hours. While the banana is freezing, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":180,"advanced_prep_time":180,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f1684f81d24e89e57859563','5f16845917e1bc857e91f018',2,'P1: Prep Mangoes and Spinach','For Mango Spinach Smoothie, wash, peel and cube half a cup of mangoes. Wash the spinach leaves thoroughly with water to remove all the dirt. Then, cut off the stem ends and roughly chop 1 cup of spinach leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f1685d31d24e89e57859564','5f16845917e1bc857e91f018',3,'M1: Blend and Make Smoothie','To make Mango Spinach Smoothie, in a blender jar, add 1 sliced frozen banana, followed by half a cup of chopped mangoes and 1 cup of chopped spinach leaves. Next, add a teaspoon of chia seeds and pour in 1 cup of almond milk. Add some ice cubes along with a tablespoon of honey and blend it well until smooth. Pour in the smoothie to the serving glasses and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f1689231969dae2fbbff482','5f16884017e1bc857e91f019',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Cucumber Mint Smoothie, wash, peel and roughly dice 2 cups of cucumber. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of mint leaves. Wash and roughly chop 1 cup of spinach leaves. Wash and cut a lemon into halves and squeeze 2 teaspoons of lime juice in a bowl.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f1689b51969dae2fbbff483','5f16884017e1bc857e91f019',2,'M1: Blend and Make Smoothie','To make Cucumber Mint Smoothie, first, add 2 cups of diced cucumber in a blender jar followed by some ice cubes and 2 teaspoons of lime juice. Add 1/4 cup of chopped mint leaves, 1/4 cup of almonds and 1 cup of chopped spinach leaves. Next, cover the jar with a lid and blend it well until smooth. Pour the smoothie into the serving glasses and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5f168dde1d24e89e57859566','5f168daa1d24e89e57859565',1,'AP1: Freeze Bananas','For Orange Goji Berry Smoothie, peel and roughly slice 1 ripe banana. Then, place it in a plastic ziplock bag and set it in the freezer for 2-3 hours. While the banana is freezing, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":180,"advanced_prep_time":180,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f168f141d24e89e57859567','5f168daa1d24e89e57859565',2,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Orange Goji Berry Smoothie, rinse 2 oranges in the water. Then, using a sharp knife, carefully slice off the top and bottom of the orange and slice the skin away from the flesh and discard. Then, cut between the membranes to segment the orange, removing the seeds. Keep the segmented oranges in a bowl. Next, wash and cut a lime into halves. Then, squeeze 1/4 cup of lime juice in a bowl using a squeezer.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f168faa17e1bc857e91f01a','5f168daa1d24e89e57859565',3,'M1: Blend and Make Smoothie','To make the Goji Berry Smoothie, first, add in 2 peeled & deseeded oranges to a blender jar. Add 1 sliced frozen banana, 2 tablespoons of chia seeds, and 1/4 cup of lime juice. Next, add half a cup of water followed by 1/4 cup of dried goji berries. Then, cover the blender jar with a lid and blend all the ingredients together. Add in some ice cubes and blend the smoothie until frosty. Then, pour the smoothie into the serving glasses right away and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f1693c217e1bc857e91f01c','5f16935217e1bc857e91f01b',1,'P1: Freeze Bananas','For Orange Banana Oats Smoothie, peel and roughly slice 2 ripe bananas. Then, place them in a plastic ziplock bag and set them in the freezer for 2-3 hours. While the bananas are freezing, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":180,"advanced_prep_time":180,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f1694591d24e89e57859568','5f16935217e1bc857e91f01b',2,'M1: Blend and Make Smoothie','To make the Banana Oats Smoothie, first, add 3/4 cup of rolled oats in a blender jar followed by 2 frozen bananas. Next, add 1/4 cup of whey protein powder, a teaspoon of honey and some ice cubes along with 1.5 cups of water. Then, cover the jar with a lid and blend all the ingredients well until smooth. Pour the refreshing smoothie into the serving glasses and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5f1697941969dae2fbbff485','5f16973e1d24e89e57859569',1,'P1: Roast the Beetroot','For Beetroot Smoothie, wash 2 small beetroots under cold running water and pat dry with kitchen paper. Cutaway the leaves, making sure you leave at least 1 inch of the stalk. Then, place the beetroots on a baking tray and drizzle a teaspoon of oil on top. Then, set the tray inside an oven and roast the beets in the preheated oven at 200 C for 40 minutes until tender. While the beetroots are roasting, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":40,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":40,"flame":0}'),('5f1698051d24e89e5785956a','5f16973e1d24e89e57859569',2,'P2: Prep Ingredients','For Beetroot Smoothie, rinse 2 oranges in the water. Then, using a sharp knife, carefully slice off the top and bottom of the orange and slice the skin away from the flesh and discard. Then, cut between the membranes to segment the orange, removing the seeds. Keep the segmented oranges in a bowl. Next, after roasting the beetroots, let them cool down for some time. Then, gently peel away the skin and roughly dice the beetroots.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f1698691969dae2fbbff486','5f16973e1d24e89e57859569',3,'M1: Blend and Make Smoothie','To make the Beetroot Smoothie, in a blender jar, add 1 cup of diced beetroots followed by 2 peeled & deseeded oranges. Add 1 cup of almond milk, a tablespoon of honey, and some ice cubes. Then, cover the jar with a lid and blend it well until smooth. Pour the smoothie into the serving glasses and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f169e7417e1bc857e91f01e','5f169e151d24e89e5785956b',1,'P1: Marinate the Chicken','For Chicken Ghee Roast, first, wash and clean 400 grams of chicken thoroughly with water. Next, to marinate the chicken, add the chicken to a large bowl. Add half a cup of curd, followed by half a teaspoon of turmeric powder and half a teaspoon of salt. Mix it well and coat the chicken pieces with the marinade. Then, cover it with a plate and allow it to marinate for 1 hour. While the chicken marinates, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":60,"advanced_prep_time":60,"timer":60,"flame":0}'),('5f169fc217e1bc857e91f01f','5f169e151d24e89e5785956b',2,'P2: Make Ghee Roast Masala','For Chicken Ghee roast masala, heat a pan over medium flame. Once the pan is medium hot, add a tablespoon of coriander seeds followed by half a teaspoon of black peppercorns, 1 teaspoon of cumin seeds, and 1/4 teaspoon of fenugreek seeds. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of fennel seeds, 3 cloves, and 5 dry Kashmiri red chilies. Then, saute and dry roast the spices over low flame for 2-3 minutes. Avoid roasting the spices for long, just lightly roast them as the spices are going to be ground later, and grinding itself will further heat up the spices.  Make sure to stir the spices continuously. Once the whole spices are fragrant, turn off the flame and transfer them to a blender jar. Allow the spices to cool down for some time.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5f16a04b1d24e89e5785956c','5f169e151d24e89e5785956b',3,'P3: Make a Masala Paste','For Chicken Ghee Roast, peel and wash 5 cloves of garlic. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash 16 curry leaves. Next, to make the masala paste, add 5 cloves of garlic to the roasted spices followed by a tablespoon of tamarind pulp and 1/4 cup of water. Then, cover the jar with a lid and blend it well into a smooth paste. The masala paste should be of semi-thick consistency.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f16a0df1d24e89e5785956d','5f169e151d24e89e5785956b',4,'M1: Cook the Marinated Chicken','To make Chicken Ghee Roast, heat 1/4 cup of ghee in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add 8 curry leaves and let it splutter for a few seconds. Next, add the marinated chicken and fry it over medium flame for 7-8 minutes until it is no longer pink. Make sure not to cook it through.','cook_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f16a1651d24e89e5785956e','5f169e151d24e89e5785956b',5,'M2: Add the Masala Paste','After frying the chicken, add the prepared masala paste and mix it well. Then, fry the chicken with the masala over medium flame for 2-3 minutes. After that, add half a teaspoon of salt followed by 8 curry leaves and mix it well. Then, cover it with a lid and reduce the flame to low, and allow the chicken to simmer with the masala for 15 minutes. Avoid adding water while simmering the chicken, as the consistency of the masala should be thick. Simmer the chicken until it is tender and cooked through. While the chicken is simmering, please move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":15,"flame":1}'),('5f16a1901969dae2fbbff487','5f169e151d24e89e5785956b',6,'M3: Final Touches','After simmering the Chicken Ghee Roast, take off the lid and give it a stir. By this time the masala should have released the oil. Then, turn off the flame and plate the chicken in a serving bowl. Garnish it with a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('5f16b1161969dae2fbbff488','5f16b0ac17e1bc857e91f020',1,'P1: Pressure Cook the Dals','To cook the lentils for Chicken Dhansak, in a pressure cooker, add 2 tablespoons of chana dal, 2 tablespoons of toor dal and 2 tablespoons of urad dal followed by 2 tablespoons of yellow moong dal. Then, add water to rinse well the lentils and drain off the water. Next, to the rinsed lentils, add in 2 cups of water along with half a teaspoon of salt and cover it with a lid. Then, pressure cook the lentils over high flame until one whistle. After that, reduce the flame to low and continue to simmer it for another 8 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the lentils are boiling, please move on the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5f16b1c71d24e89e5785956f','5f16b0ac17e1bc857e91f020',2,'P2: Make a Masala Powder','To make the masala powder for Chicken Dhansak, heat a pan over medium flame for 30 seconds. Add 1/4 teaspoon of black peppercorns, 2 nos cloves, 1 nos green cardamom, a half-inch piece of cinnamon stick, a teaspoon of mace, and 1 nos bay leaf. Next, add 1 nos star anise, half a teaspoon of cumin seeds, half a teaspoon of coriander seeds, 1/4 teaspoon of fenugreek seeds, and 1/4 teaspoon of sesame seeds followed by 2 nos dry Kashmiri red chilies.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f16b2371d24e89e57859570','5f16b0ac17e1bc857e91f020',3,'P3: Dry Roast Spices and then Blend','Then, saute and dry roast the spices over low flame for 2-3 minutes. Avoid roasting the spices for long, just lightly roast them as the spices are going to be ground later, and grinding itself will further heat up the spices.  Make sure to stir the spices continuously. Once the whole spices are fragrant, turn off the flame and transfer allow the spices to cool down for some time. Next, add the roasted spices to a blender jar along with 1/4 teaspoon of nutmeg powder and 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder. Then, cover the jar with a lid and grind the spices into a slightly coarse powder.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f16b2ea1d24e89e57859571','5f16b0ac17e1bc857e91f020',4,'P4: Prep Ingredients','For Chicken Dhansak, Wash and clean 250 grams of chicken thoroughly with water. Peel, wash and finely chop 1 cup of onions. Wash a bunch of fenugreek leaves thoroughly with water to remove all the dirt. Then, spread them over a kitchen towel to dry them off. After that, finely chop half a cup of fenugreek leaves. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of mint leaves. Wash and finely chop 2 nos green chilies. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f16b3391d24e89e57859572','5f16b0ac17e1bc857e91f020',5,'P5: Make a Puree with the Green Vegetables','For Chicken Dhansak, heat 1 tablespoons of ghee in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped coriander leaves followed by half a cup of chopped fenugreek leaves and 1/4 cup of chopped mint leaves. Then, stir and fry the greens over medium flame for 2-3 minutes, until the greens slightly shrivel up. After that, turn off the flame and allow it to cool down for some time. Then, transfer the fried greens to a blender jar along with 1/4 cup of water and blend them well into a smooth puree.','prep_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f16b3aa1969dae2fbbff489','5f16b0ac17e1bc857e91f020',6,'M1: Cook Onions','To make Chicken Dhansak, heat 1.5 tablespoons of ghee in a kadai over medium flame for a minute. Next, add 1 cup of chopped onions and fry them over medium flame until translucent. Add a tablespoon of ginger-garlic paste and fry it with the onions over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until the onions are slightly golden.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5f16b3ec17e1bc857e91f021','5f16b0ac17e1bc857e91f020',7,'M2: Add the Prepared Masala Powder','After frying the onions, add the roasted masala powder followed by half a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Then, fry the masala over medium-low flame for 2-3 minutes. Next, add 1/4 cup of water and stir it well. Continue to cook the masala over medium flame for a minute. After that, add 250 grams of chicken and mix it well. Fry the chicken with the masala over medium flame for 6-7 minutes, until the water from the masala is completely reduced.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5f16b43617e1bc857e91f022','5f16b0ac17e1bc857e91f020',8,'M3: Let the Curry Simmer','After frying the chicken, add 2 nos chopped green chilies and mix it well. Next, add the cooked lentils followed by the prepared coriander paste and a tablespoon of tamarind paste. Then, mix it well and add 1 cup of water to this. Stir and bring it to a boil over medium flame. Then, cover it with a lid and cook the chicken over low flame for 15 minutes until fork-tender. While the chicken is simmering, please move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":15,"flame":2}'),('5f16b45f17e1bc857e91f023','5f16b0ac17e1bc857e91f020',9,'M4: Serve','After simmering the Chicken Dhansak, take off the lid and stir it well. Turn off the flame and plate the chicken, spoon over the gravy, and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f17dec517e1bc857e91f027','5f17d88317e1bc857e91f026',1,'P1:Make the Chicken Marinate','For Chicken Vindaloo, wash and clean 400 grams of chicken thoroughly with water. Peel and wash 4 cloves of garlic. Wash, peel, and roughly chop a half-inch piece of ginger. Next, to prepare the marinade, in a blender jar, add 3 cloves, 1/4 teaspoon of black peppercorns, a half-inch piece of ginger, and a half-inch piece of cinnamon stick. Add 4 cloves of garlic, a teaspoon of cumin seeds, 4 nos dry kashmiri red chilies, and half a teaspoon od turmeric powder followed by half a teaspoon salt and 1/4 cup of vinegar. Then, cover the jar with a lid and blend it well into a smooth paste.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f17df1417e1bc857e91f028','5f17d88317e1bc857e91f026',2,'P2: Marinate the Chicken','To marinate the chicken for Chicken Vindaloo, first, add the prepared marinade to a large bowl. Next, add in 400 grams of chicken and mix it well. Coat the chicken pieces evenly with the marinade. Then, cover it with a plate and allow it to sit for an hour. While the chicken marinates, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":60,"advanced_prep_time":60,"timer":60,"flame":0}'),
('5f17df971d24e89e57859577','5f17d88317e1bc857e91f026',3,'P3: Chop Ingredients','For Chicken Vindaloo, peel, wash, and finely chop 3/4 cup of onions. Peel and finely chop 1 teaspoon of garlic. Wash and finely chop a tablespoon of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f17e00b1d24e89e57859578','5f17d88317e1bc857e91f026',4,'M1: Fry Onions','To make Chicken Vindaloo, heat 2 tablespoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add a teaspoon of chopped garlic and fry it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes until it is fragrant and turns slightly golden. After that, add 3/4 cup of chopped onions. Saute and fry the onions over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until translucent. Next, add 1/4 cup of water and braise the onions over medium-low flame for 4-5 minutes until onions are tender and mushy.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f17e1001d24e89e57859579','5f17d88317e1bc857e91f026',5,'M2: Add Chicken','After braising the onions, fry them over medium-high flame for a minute to reduce the excess water. Next, add the marinated chicken along with the marinade and mix it well. Stir and fry the chicken over medium flame for 6-7 minutes until oil separates. Make sure to stir the chicken continuously to avoid it from sticking to the bottom of the pan. After the masala releases the oil, add 1 cup of water and stir it well. Then, bring it to a boil over medium flame. As it comes to a boil, cover it with a lid and cook the chicken over low flame for 15-20 minutes until it is cooked through. While the chicken is simmering, please move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":20,"flame":2}'),('5f17e1b41969dae2fbbff495','5f17d88317e1bc857e91f026',6,'M3: Simmer the Curry','After simmering the Chicken Vindaloo, take off the lid and gently stir it. Turn off the flame and garnish it with a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves. Plate the chicken in a serving bowl and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f17e64b1d24e89e5785957a','5f17e5ce1969dae2fbbff496',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Chicken Keema Palak, rinse and clean 250 grams of chicken in water. Wash a bunch of spinach leaves thoroughly with water to remove all the dirt. Then, cut off the stem ends and finely chop 2 cups of spinach leaves. Peel, wash and finely chop 3/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 2 nos green chilies. Wash and finely chop a tablespoon of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5f17e96817e1bc857e91f029','5f17e5ce1969dae2fbbff496',2,'M1: Temper the Spices','To make Chicken Keema Palak, heat 1 tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add 1 nos bay leaf, 1/4 teaspoon of black peppercorns, 3 nos cloves, and half an inch piece of cinnamon stick. Then saute the whole sices over low flame for a min. Next, add 3/4 cup of chopped onions and fry them over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until translucent.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f17e9db1d24e89e5785957b','5f17e5ce1969dae2fbbff496',3,'M2: Add Masala Powders','After frying the onions, add 2 nos chopped green chilies and continue to fry the onions for another 2-3 minutes. Next, add a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Add a teaspoon of cumin powder, a teaspoon of red chili powder, half a teaspoon of turmeric powder along with a teaspoon of coriander powder and mix it well. Saute and cook the masala over low flame. Add 2 tablespoons of water to the masala if it gets too dry and cook the masala for 3-4 minutes until oil separates.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5f17ea1617e1bc857e91f02a','5f17e5ce1969dae2fbbff496',4,'M3: Cook the Chicken','After cooking the masala, add 250 grams of chicken mince and stir it briskly to break up the mince into granules. Then, cook the chicken for 5-6 minutes over a medium flame while stirring it in between to keep it from sticking together and forming lumps. Saute and cook the mince until it is slightly tender and no longer pink.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5f17eae417e1bc857e91f02b','5f17e5ce1969dae2fbbff496',5,'M4: Add the Spinach','Next, add 2 cups of chopped spinach leaves and mix it well. Then, continue to stir and cook the mince over medium flame for 6-7 minutes until the water is reduced and mince dries up. After that, add half a cup of water and mix it well. Then, cover it with a lid and simmer the mince for 5 minutes until it is cooked through. While the chicken keema is simmering, please move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5f17eb7a17e1bc857e91f02c','5f17e5ce1969dae2fbbff496',6,'M5: Final Touches','After simmering the Chicken Keema Palak, take off the lid and add half a teaspoon of garam masala. Mix it well and turn off the flame. Garnish the chicken keema with a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),
('5f17fd2b1d24e89e5785957d','5f17ee751d24e89e5785957c',1,'P1: Soak Cashews and Melon Seeds','To soak the cashews for Curry Base, first, add half a cup of water to a saucepan and heat it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Once the water is medium-hot, turn off the flame and set it aside. Next, add 2 tablespoons of cashews in a bowl followed by 2 tablespoons of melon seeds. Add half a cup of hot water and soak in the cashews and melon seeds for 15 minutes. While the cashews are soaking, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":15,"flame":0}'),('5f1804e41d24e89e5785957e','5f17ee751d24e89e5785957c',2,'P2: Chop Ingredients','For Curry Base, peel, wash, and slice 1.5 cups of onions. Wash and roughly slice 2.5 cups of tomatoes. Wash, peel, and roughly chop 2 tablespoons of ginger. Peel, and crush 2 tablespoons of garlic.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f1805531969dae2fbbff497','5f17ee751d24e89e5785957c',3,'M1: Temper Spices','To make the Curry Base, heat 1/4 cup of cooking oil in a kadai over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Next, add a half inch-piece of cinnamon stick, half a teaspoon of green cardamom, half a teaspoon of cloves, and 1 nos bay leaf followed by half a teaspoon of cumin seeds. Saute the whole spices over low flame for a minute.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f1805e91d24e89e5785957f','5f17ee751d24e89e5785957c',4,'M2: Cook Onions and Tomatoes','Next, add 1.5 cups of sliced onions and fry them over medium flame for 3-4 minutes until onions are slightly translucent. After that, add 2 tablespoons of crushed garlic along with 2 tablespoons of chopped ginger. Add half a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Then, saute and cook the onions over medium flame for another 2-3 minutes until it slightly changes color. Next, add 2.5 cups of sliced tomatoes and mix it well. Then, cover it with a lid and cook the tomatoes over medium flame for 15 minutes until tender. While the tomatoes are simmering, please move on to the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5f18060c17e1bc857e91f02e','5f17ee751d24e89e5785957c',5,'M3: Make Cashew Paste','To prepare the cashew paste for Curry Base, add the soaked cashews and melon seeds to a blender jar and blend them well into a smooth paste.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5f18065f1d24e89e57859580','5f17ee751d24e89e5785957c',6,'M4: Blend the onions and tomatoes','After simmering the tomatoes for Curry Base, remove the lid and turn off the flame. Then, set it aside and allow the mixture to cool down completely. Next, to prepare the masala paste, after the prepared tomato mixture cools down, add it to a blender jar and blend it well into a smooth puree.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f1806c61969dae2fbbff498','5f17ee751d24e89e5785957c',7,'M5: Cook Masala Powders','To make the Curry Base, heat 2 tablespoons of cooking oil in a kadai over medium flame for a minute. Add half a teaspoon of turmeric powder, 1 tablespoon of red chili powder, 1.5 tablespoons of coriander powder, half a teaspoon of cumin powder and half a teaspoon of garam masala. Saute and cook the masala over low flame for 1-2 minutes until fragrant.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f1806ff17e1bc857e91f02f','5f17ee751d24e89e5785957c',8,'M6: Add the Prepared Vegetable Puree','After cooking the dry spices, add the prepared tomato-onion paste and mix it well. Then, cover it with a lid and cook the masala over low flame for 20 minutes until oil separates. While the masala is simmering, please move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":20,"flame":0}'),('5f18074c1d24e89e57859581','5f17ee751d24e89e5785957c',9,'M7: Add the Cashew Paste','After cooking the masala for Curry Base, take off the lid and mix it well. The masala should release the oil by this time. Then, add the prepared cashew paste and mix it well with the masala until it is well combined. Keep stirring it over a low flame to avoid any lumps. Then, continue to cook the masala over medium flame for 4-5 minutes while stirring continuously. Make sure to cook the masala until oil separates. As the masala releases the oil, turn off the flame and let it cool down. Then, transfer it to an airtight jar or box and keep it in the refrigerator until use.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5f193733c47ac639e61dab99','5f1936aea2ea097a286f12ee',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Jhinge Aloo Posto, first, add in 3 tablespoons of poppy seeds to a small bowl. Then, add 1/4 cup of water and soak the poppy seeds for 30 minutes. Next, wash, peel, and cube 1 cup of potatoes. Wash, peel, and cube 1 cup of ridge gourd. Wash and slit 2 green chilies. While the poppy seeds are soaking, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":30,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":30,"flame":0}'),
('5f193790a2ea097a286f12ef','5f1936aea2ea097a286f12ee',2,'M1: Fry the Potatoes','To make Jhinge Aloo Posto, heat 1 tablespoons of mustard oil in a kadai over medium-high flame for 1-2 minutes until it releases light smoke. Make sure to heat the oil to the point till it lightly fumes to remove the pungency from it. Next, add 1 cup of cubed potatoes and fry them over medium flame for 3-4 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f1937d6a2ea097a286f12f0','5f1936aea2ea097a286f12ee',3,'M2: Add Masala Powders','Next, add half a 1/4 teaspoon of salt followed by 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder and mix it well. Then, continue to fry the potatoes over medium flame for another 1-2 minutes. After that, add 1 cup of cubed ridge gourd and mix it well. Then, fry the ridge gourd with the potatoes over medium flame for 3-4 minutes until potatoes are slightly golden.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f193867c47ac639e61dab9a','5f1936aea2ea097a286f12ee',4,'M3: Boil Vegetables','Next, add 1 cup of water and stir it well. Add half a teaspoon of salt along with 1/4 teaspoon of sugar and mix it well. Then, bring it to a boil over a high flame. As it comes to a boil, cover it with a lid and continue to boil the vegetables over high flame for another 5-6 minutes, until the water is reduced to half and potatoes are tender. While the vegetables are boiling, prepare the poppy seed paste, for this, add the soaked poppy seeds to a blender jar along with 2 tablespoons of water and blend it well into a slightly coarse paste.','cook_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f1939a1c47ac639e61dab9b','5f1936aea2ea097a286f12ee',5,'M4: Temper Spices','After boiling the vegetables for Jhinge Aloo Posto, take off the lid and stir the vegetables. Then, continue to cook it over high flame for another 1-2 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and set the boiled vegetables aside. Next, heat 1 tablespoon of mustard oil over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Then, temper the oil with 1 nos dry red chili and half a teaspoon of black cumin seeds. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Next, add the prepared poppy seeds paste and saute it over medium flame. Stir and cook the masala for 1-2 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5f1939dea2ea097a286f12f1','5f1936aea2ea097a286f12ee',6,'M5: Final Touches','After that, add the boiled potatoes and ridge gourd along with the stock and mix it well. Then, cook the vegetables with the masala over medium-high flame for 4-5 minutes until the stock is reduced completely and the gravy masala is thickened. The consistency of the masala should be rich and thick. After the masala thickens, add 2 slit green chilies and mix it well. Then, turn off the flame and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5f193ddf1ffca33b0ecea2fb','5f193d48c47ac639e61dab9c',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Grilled Chicken Patty, first, rinse and clean 400 grams of minced chicken with water. Then, pat the mince dry with a kitchen towel to wipe off the water and keep it in a bowl. Next, peel, wash and finely chop half a cup of onions. Peel and finely chop 2 teaspoons of garlic. Wash and finely chop a tablespoon of mint leaves. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves. Wash and zest a 1/4 teaspoon of lemon using a grater or a zester.','prep_method','{"active_time":18,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f193e38a2ea097a286f12f2','5f193d48c47ac639e61dab9c',2,'P2: Saute Onions and Garlic','For Grilled Chicken Patty, heat a tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame. Add half a cup of chopped onion and fry it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until translucent. Next, add 2 teaspoons of chopped garlic and fry it with the onions over medium for 2-3 minutes until onions turn slightly golden brown. After that, turn off the flame and set it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f193ecc1ffca33b0ecea2fc','5f193d48c47ac639e61dab9c',3,'P3: Make the Patty Mixture','To prepare the mixture for Grilled Chicken Patty, add the minced chicken to a large bowl. Next, add the fried onions and garlic to the mince followed by a tablespoon of chopped mint leaves, and 2 tablespoons of chopped coriander leaves. Next, crack an egg into this and add a teaspoon of cumin powder, half a teaspoon of pepper powder, half a teaspoon of chili flakes, and a teaspoon of salt. Add 1/4 teaspoon of lemon zest and combine it well to prepare the patty mixture.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f193f47c47ac639e61dab9d','5f193d48c47ac639e61dab9c',4,'P4: Make the Patties','To prepare the patties for Grilled Chicken Patty, apply some oil to the palms, then take a small ball-sized portion of the prepared mince mixture and shape it into a round ball. Then, gently press it to flatten it, and shape it into a round flat patty. Make the rest of the patties from the mixture similarly.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f193f9c1ffca33b0ecea2fd','5f193d48c47ac639e61dab9c',5,'M1: Cook Patties','To make the Grilled Chicken Patty, heat a grill pan and grease it with a tablespoon of cooking oil. Once the pan is medium-hot, carefully place the prepared chicken patties and cook them over medium flame for 5-6 minutes on each side. Flip and cook the patties until they are evenly browned on both sides and the mince is cooked through. After grilling the patties, turn off the flame and carefully take them out onto the serving plate and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5f1e73f57eb177afc92f702d','5f1e733ce2eb13885b32e31e',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Lauki Coconut Milk Curry, wash, peel, and cube 1.5 cups of bottle gourd. Wash and slit 2 nos green chilies. Peel and crush 2 cloves of garlic. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves. Wash 8 nos curry leaves well with water. Next, in a large bowl, add half a cup of curd. Add in 1 cup of water and whisk it well using a whisk until smooth.','cook_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f1e74f27eb177afc92f702e','5f1e733ce2eb13885b32e31e',2,'M1: Cook Bottle Gourd','To make Lauki Coconut Milk Curry, first, add the prepared buttermilk to a pan. Next, add 1.5 cups of cubed bottle gourd followed by 2 nos slit green chilies and half a teaspoon of salt. Mix it well. Then, cover it with a lid and cook it over medium flame for 5-6 minutes until the bottle gourd is half-cooked. While the bottle gourd is simmering, please move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":6,"flame":2}'),('5f1e756e7eb177afc92f702f','5f1e733ce2eb13885b32e31e',3,'M2: Add the Coconut Milk','After simmering the bottle gourd for lauki coconut milk curry, take off the lid and give it a stir. Next, reduce the flame to low and add 1 cup of coconut milk while stirring it, to avoid it from splitting. Then, again cover it with a lid and continue to simmer the curry over medium-low flame for 5-6 minutes until the bottle gourd is tender and cooked. While the curry is simmering, please move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":6,"flame":2}'),('5f1e7605e2eb13885b32e31f','5f1e733ce2eb13885b32e31e',4,'M3: Make Tadka','After simmering the Lauki Coconut Milk Curry, turn off the flame and set it aside. Next, to make the tempering, heat a tablespoon of coconut oil in a small tempering pan. Then, temper it with half a teaspoon of mustard seeds and half a teaspoon of cumin seeds. Next, add 2 cloves of crushed garlic followed by 2 nos dry red chilies and 8 nos curry leaves. Then, saute it over medium flame until garlic is slightly golden. After that, turn off the flame and add the tempering to the curry. Add 2 tablespoons of chopped coriander leaves and mix it well. Then, plate it in a serving bowl, garnish it with some coriander leaves and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5f2106b5e2eb13885b32e32d','5f2105f3b287d4a9eb97c78c',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For South Indian Lauki Sabzi, first, add 3 tablespoons of chana dal in a small bowl and soak it in 1/4 cup of water for 20 minutes. Next, wash, peel, and cube 2 cups of bottle gourd. Wash and roughly chop 2 nos green chilies. Peel and wash 4 cloves of garlic. Roughly chop 1/4 cup of coconut. Wash 16 nos curry leaves well with water. Wash and cut a lime into halves. Then squeeze a tablespoon of lime juice in a bowl. While the chana dal is soaking, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5f2106fbe2eb13885b32e32e','5f2105f3b287d4a9eb97c78c',2,'P2: Roast Peanuts','To dry roast, the peanuts for Soth Indian Lauki Sabzi, heat a pan over medium flame for a few seconds. Next, add 3 tablespoons of peanuts and dry roast them without adding any oil over low flame for 3-4 minutes. Keep stirring the peanuts while roasting. As the peanuts turn slightly brown and crisp, turn off the flame and take them out into a bowl.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f210773e2eb13885b32e32f','5f2105f3b287d4a9eb97c78c',3,'P3: Cook Ingredients for a Masala Paste','For South Indian Lauki Sabzi, heat a tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add 2 nos chopped green chilies followed by 8 nos curry leaves and let them splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 2 tablespoons of soaked chana dal along with 4 cloves of garlic and saute it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes until the garlic is fragrant. After that, add 1/4 cup of chopped coconut and saute it for a minute. Next, add 3 tablespoons of roasted peanuts and mix it well. Saute and fry it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and allow this to cool down completely. While it cools, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f2107a17eb177afc92f7035','5f2105f3b287d4a9eb97c78c',4,'P4: Blend to make Masala Paste','To prepare the masala paste for South Indian Lauki Sabzi, after the prepared mixture of peanuts cools down, transfer it to a blender jar and blend it well into a fine paste. Add some water, if the paste gets too thick and dry while blending.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f21081f7eb177afc92f7036','5f2105f3b287d4a9eb97c78c',5,'M1: Cook Bottle Gourd','To make the South Indian Lauki Sabzi, heat a tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Next, temper it with half a teaspoon of mustard seeds and 8 nos curry leaves and let them splutter for a few seconds. Add 2 cups of cubed bottle gourd and fry it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Next, add half a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Then, cover it with a lid and cook it over medium flame for 5-6 minutes until the bottle gourd is half cooked. While the bottle gourd is simmering, please move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":6,"flame":3}'),('5f210865e2eb13885b32e330','5f2105f3b287d4a9eb97c78c',6,'M2: Add the Prepared Masala Paste','After simmering the bottle gourd for South Indian Lauki Sabzi, take off the lid and add the prepared coconut masala paste into this, followed by half a cup of water. Then, mix it well and allow it to cook over medium flame for 3-4 minutes until the bottle groud is tender and gravy has slightly thickened. After that, turn off the flame and finish it off with a tablespoon of lime juice. Mix it well and plate it in a serving bowl. Garnish it with a fresh sprig of curry leaves and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":4,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":4,"flame":2}'),
('5f21135ab287d4a9eb97c78e','5f210ff8b287d4a9eb97c78d',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Chicken and Basil Soup, rinse and clean 200 grams of chicken breast well with water. Next, peel, wash and roughly chop 3/4 cup of onions. Peel and wash 3 cloves of garlic. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of basil leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f2113bb7eb177afc92f7037','5f210ff8b287d4a9eb97c78d',2,'M1: Pressure Cook the Chicken','To cook the chicken for Chicken and Basil Soup, first, add in 4 cups of water to a pressure cooker. Next, add 2 nos bay leaves followed by 3 cloves of garlic and 3/4 cup of chopped onions. Add half a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Add 200 grams of the chicken breast and cover it with a lid and pressure cook the chicken over a high flame until two whistles. Then, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook it for another 5 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the chicken is cooking, please move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5f2114027eb177afc92f7038','5f210ff8b287d4a9eb97c78d',3,'M2: Shred the Cooked Chicken','After pressure cooking, the chicken for Chicken and Basil Soup, remove the lid of the pressure cooker and carefully strain the chicken stock in a large bowl using a strainer and set it aside for later use. Next, shred the cooked chicken breast into small pieces as shown.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f21158c7eb177afc92f7039','5f210ff8b287d4a9eb97c78d',4,'M3: Make a Roux (Butter and Flour Mixture)','To make the Chicken and Basil Soup, heat a tablespoon of butter in a stockpot or any deep bottom pan over low flame. Add 2 tablespoons of all-purpose flour to the butter and keep stirring it continuously over low flame for 1-2 minutes. Keep stirring the flour until it is well combined with the butter or it will form lumps. Next, gradually add 3/4 cup of milk while stirring it continuously over a low flame to avoid any lumps. Stir and cook the sauce over low flame for 2-3 minutes until it comes together.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f2116a97eb177afc92f703a','5f210ff8b287d4a9eb97c78d',5,'M4: Boil the Soup','After cooking the sauce, add in the saved chicken stock and mix it well. Then, allow it to boil over a medium flame for a minute. Season the soup with half a teaspoon of black pepper powder and half a teaspoon of salt. Mix it well and add the shredded chicken into the soup. Boil the soup over medium flame for 2-3 minutes. After that, add 2 tablespoons of chopped basil leaves and mix well. Turn off the flame and add 1/4 cup of fresh cream. Mix it well and divide the soup among bowls. Garnish it with a pinch of black pepper powder and some fresh basil leaves. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('5f211ea8b287d4a9eb97c793','5f211e6a7eb177afc92f703b',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Dhaba Mutton, wash and clean 400 grams of mutton thoroughly with water. Peel, wash and finely chop half a cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1 cup of tomatoes. Wash and finely chop a tablespoon of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f211f2ee2eb13885b32e332','5f211e6a7eb177afc92f703b',2,'M1: Temper Whole Spices','To make Dhaba Mutton, heat 2 tablespoons of ghee in a pressure cooker over medium flame for a minute. Add a half-inch piece of cinnamon stick, 1 bay leaf, 2 green cardamoms, 1 black cardamom, and 3 cloves followed by 2 dry red chilies and saute the whole spices over low flame for a minute. Next, add half a cup of chopped onions and fry them over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f211fb4b287d4a9eb97c794','5f211e6a7eb177afc92f703b',3,'M2: Add Tomatoes and Masala Powders','Next, add a tablespoon of ginger-garlic paste and fry it with the onions over medium flame for 1-2 minutes until onions turn slightly golden. After that, add 1 cup of chopped of tomatoes and mix it well. Saute and cook the tomatoes over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Next, add a teaspoon of coriander powder, half a teaspoon of cumin powder, half a teaspoon of red chili powder along with half a teaspoon of garam masala and mix it well. Add half a teaspoon of turmeric powder and mix well. Saute and cook the masala over low flame for 2-3 minutes, until tomatoes are tender.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5f211fe7e2eb13885b32e333','5f211e6a7eb177afc92f703b',4,'M3: Add Curd','After cooking the masala, add half a cup of curd and mix it well. Make sure to reduce the flame to low while adding the curd to avoid it from splitting and keep stirring the masala until the curd is well combined. Then, cook the masala over medium-low flame for another 3-4 minutes until oil separates.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('5f2124d6b287d4a9eb97c795','5f211e6a7eb177afc92f703b',5,'M4: Close the Pressure Cooker','After the oil separates from the masala, add 1 cup of water and stir it well. Add a teaspoon of salt and mix well. Next, add 400 grams of mutton and mix it well with the masala. Then, stir and fry the mutton with the masala over medium flame for 2-3 minutes. Then, cover the pressure cooker with a lid and cook the mutton over a high flame until two whistles. After the 2nd whistle, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook it for another 15-20 minutes until the mutton is cooked through. Then, turn off the flame and allow the pressure cooker to cool down naturally. While the mutton is simmering, please move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":25,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5f21254c7eb177afc92f703c','5f211e6a7eb177afc92f703b',6,'M5: Final Touches','After simmering the Dhaba Mutton, remove the lid of the pressure cooker and plate the mutton in a serving dish. Spoon over the gravy and garnish it with a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5f2128a0b287d4a9eb97c796','5f212849e2eb13885b32e334',1,'AP1: Make Hung Curd','To make the hung curd for Dal Gosht, place a sieve over a large mixing bowl and cover it with a muslin cloth as shown. Next, pour half a cup of fresh curd into the muslin cloth and tie it tightly, tucking the curd inside. Then, carefully place the tied curd over the sieve and refrigerate it for 2 hours. This will allow the excess water to drain off from the curd, leaving the hung curd thick and creamy. While the curd is refrigerating, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":120,"advanced_prep_time":120,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f212924b287d4a9eb97c797','5f212849e2eb13885b32e334',2,'AP2: Prep Ingredients to make Marinade','For Dal Gosht, wash and clean 400 grams of mutton thoroughly with water. Peel, wash and roughly chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and roughly chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Next, to prepare the marinade,  in a blender jar, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions followed by 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes. Add half a teaspoon of turmeric powder, 1 teaspoon of cumin powder, half a teaspoon of red chili powder, and 1 teaspoon of coriander powder. Next, add a tablespoon of ginger-garlic paste along with 2 tablespoons of hung curd and cover the jar with a lid. Then,  blend it well into a smooth paste.','prep_method','{"active_time":16,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f2129617eb177afc92f703d','5f212849e2eb13885b32e334',3,'AP3: Marinate the Mutton','To marinate the mutton for Dal Gosht, add 400 grams of mutton in a large bowl. Next, add the prepared marinade and mix it well. Coat the mutton pieces well with the marinade and cover it with a plate. Then, allow the mutton to marinate for 2 hours. While the mutton marinates, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":120,"advanced_prep_time":120,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f2129c4e2eb13885b32e335','5f212849e2eb13885b32e334',4,'P1: Prep Ingredients for Dal Gosht','To soak the lentils for Dal Gosht, add 1/4 cup of chana dal and 1/4 cup of toor dal in a bowl and soak the lentils in 1 cup of water for 20 minutes. Meanwhile, wash and finely chop a tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash and slit 1 nos fresh red chili. While the lentils are soaking, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":20,"flame":0}'),
('5f212c53b287d4a9eb97c798','5f212849e2eb13885b32e334',5,'M1: Temper Spices and Cook Mutton','To make Dal Gosht, heat 1 tablespoon of ghee in a pressure cooker over low flame for a minute. Add  1 nos bay leaf, a half-inch piece of cinnamon stick, cloves, half a teaspoon of black peppercorns, 1 nos black cardamom, and 2 nos green cardamoms. Saute the whole spices over low flame for a minute. Next, add the marinated mutton along with the marinade and fry it over medium flame for 4-5 minutes until it slightly changes color.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f212cd87eb177afc92f703e','5f212849e2eb13885b32e334',6,'M2: Add the Soaked Dal and Cook','After frying the mutton, add the soaked lentils, half a teaspoon of red chili powder, and half a teaspoon of garam masala followed by 1 teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Add 1 cup of water and stir it well. Then, cover the pressure cooker with a lid and cook the mutton over a high flame until two whistles. After the 2nd whistle, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook it for another 15 minutes until the mutton is cooked through. Then, turn off the flame and allow the pressure cooker to cool down naturally. While the mutton is simmering, please move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5f212d0ae2eb13885b32e336','5f212849e2eb13885b32e334',7,'M3: Final Touches','After simmering the Dal Gosht, remove the lid of the pressure cooker and plate the mutton in a serving dish. Spoon over the gravy and garnish it with a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and a slit red chili. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f2130457eb177afc92f703f','5f212fdfe2eb13885b32e339',2,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Grilled Lamb Chops, wash and clean 4 nos lamb chops thoroughly with water. Peel, wash and slice 1/4 cup of onion into thin round slices and separate them into rings. Wash and finely chop a tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash and cut a lime into halves. Then, squeeze a tablespoon of lime juice in a small bowl.','cook_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f213d527eb177afc92f7044','5f212fdfe2eb13885b32e339',1,'P2: Marinate the Lamb Chops','To marinate the lamb chops for Grilled Lamb Chops, in a large bowl, add 2 teaspoons of ginger-garlic paste, half a teaspoon of turmeric powder, half a teaspoon of red chili powder, half a teaspoon of coriander powder, half a teaspoon of cumin powder, half a teaspoon of garam masala. Next, add a teaspoon of salt followed by a tablespoon of lime juice and mix it well. Add 4 nos lamb chops into this and coat the them well with the marinade. Then, cover it with a plate and allow the chops to sit in the marinade for 30 minutes. While the lamb chops marinates, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":30,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":30,"flame":0}'),
('5f213daa7eb177afc92f7045','5f212fdfe2eb13885b32e339',3,'M1: Grill Lamb Chops in the Oven','To grill the Lamb Chops, first, grease the grill rack of the oven with a teaspoon of oil using an oil brush. Then, carefully place the marinated lamb chops onto the grill and place it inside the oven. Next, grill the lamb chops at 200°C for 20 minutes until the lamb is browned and cooked through. While the lamb chops are grilling, please move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":20,"flame":0}'),('5f213dcde2eb13885b32e33c','5f212fdfe2eb13885b32e339',4,'M2: Garnish','After grilling the lamb chops, carefully take them out of the oven and place them onto a serving plate. Garnish the lamb chops with some chopped coriander leaves and onion rings. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f22644fe2eb13885b32e340','5f214552b287d4a9eb97c79a',1,'P1: Prep Mutton','For Mutton Stew, first, wash and clean 200 grams of mutton thoroughly with water. Then, put the mutton in a large bowl. Next, add half a teaspoon of garlic powder, half a teaspoon of ginger powder, and half a teaspoon of salt. Add 2 tablespoons of all-purpose flour and mix it well. Coat the mutton pieces evenly with the flour.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f22679bb287d4a9eb97c79f','5f214552b287d4a9eb97c79a',2,'P2: Grill the Mutton','Next, to grill the mutton, apply a teaspoon of olive oil to the baking plate and grease it well using an oil brush. Then, place and arrange the mutton pieces onto the greased plate and set it inside the oven. Grill the mutton at 180°C for 15 minutes until it''s browned and half cooked. Do not cook it through as the mutton is going to be stewed later. While the mutton is grilling, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":15,"flame":0}'),('5f2268297eb177afc92f7080','5f214552b287d4a9eb97c79a',3,'P3: Chop Vegetables','For Mutton Stew, peel, wash and roughly dice 3/4 cup of onions. Peel and finely chop 2 teaspoons of garlic. Wash, peel, and dice 1/4 cup of carrots. Wash and cut 1/4 cup of baby potatoes into halves. Wash and roughly dice 1/4 cup of mushrooms. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of parsley. After grilling the mutton, carefully take it out of the oven and set it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":18,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5f2268b8e2eb13885b32e341','5f214552b287d4a9eb97c79a',4,'M1: Temper Spices','To make the Mutton Stew, heat 2 tablespoons of olive in a pressure cooker over medium flame. Add 2 nos bay leaves, a half-inch piece of cinnamon stick, and 1 nos star anise.  Saute the whole spices over low flame for a minute. Next, add 2 teaspoons of garlic followed by 3/4 cup of diced onions and fry them over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until onion is translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f2269b87eb177afc92f7081','5f214552b287d4a9eb97c79a',5,'M2: Cook the Vegetables','After frying the onions, add 1 teaspoon of red chili paste and fry it with the onions for a few seconds. Next, add a teaspoon of dried thyme followed by 1/4 cup of diced carrots, 1/4 cup of chopped mushrooms, and 1/4 cup of halved baby potatoes. Add half a teaspoon of red chili powder, half a teaspoon of black pepper powder, and half a teaspoon of salt. Deglaze with a teaspoon of white wine vinegar and mix it well. Stir and fry the vegetables over high flame for 1-2 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5f226a9ce2eb13885b32e342','5f214552b287d4a9eb97c79a',6,'M3: Close the Lid and Cook','After frying the vegetables, add the grilled mutton followed by 1.5 cups of mutton stock. If the mutton stock is not available, water can be used instead of stock. Then, stir it well and cover the cooker with the lid. Pressure cook the mutton over medium flame until one whistle. After the first whistle, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook it for another 10 minutes until the mutton is cooked through. Then, turn off the flame and allow the pressure cooker to cool down naturally. While the mutton stew is simmering, please move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5f226ac9e2eb13885b32e343','5f214552b287d4a9eb97c79a',7,'M4: Garnish','After simmering the Mutton Stew, remove the lid of the pressure cooker and ladle the stew into serving bowls. Garnish it with some chopped fresh parsley and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f226fcb7eb177afc92f7083','5f226dfd7eb177afc92f7082',1,'P1: Soak Rice','For Hyderabadi Khichdi, first, wash and soak 1 cup of basmati rice in 2 cups of water for 20 minutes. Next, in a separate bowl, soak half a cup of masoor dal in 1 cup of water for 20 minutes. While the rice and dal are soaking, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":20,"flame":0}'),
('5f227028b287d4a9eb97c7a0','5f226dfd7eb177afc92f7082',2,'P2: Chop Ingredients','For Hyderabadi Khichdi, peel, wash, and finely slice half a cup of onions. Wash and slit 2 nos green chilies. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of mint leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f2270a67eb177afc92f7086','5f226dfd7eb177afc92f7082',3,'M1: Temper Spices','To make Hyderabadi Khichdi, first, heat 2 tablespoons of ghee in a pressure cooker over medium flame for a minute. Next, add 2 nos bay leaves, 1-inch piece of cinnamon, 3 nos green cardamom, and 3 nos cloves followed by 1/4 teaspoon of black peppercorns. Saute the whole spices over low flame for a minute. Next, add 2 nos slit green chilies and half a cup of sliced onions. Stir and fry the onions over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until translucent. Next, add a teaspoon of ginger-garlic paste and fry it with the onions for another minute.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5f2270f6e2eb13885b32e344','5f226dfd7eb177afc92f7082',4,'M2: Close the Lid and Cook Khichdi','After frying the onions, add half a teaspoon of turmeric powder along with a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Next, add 1 cup of soaked basmati rice and half a cup of soaked masoor dal into this and mix it well. Stir in 3 cups of water followed by 2 tablespoons of chopped coriander leaves and 2 tablespoons of chopped mint leaves. Mix it well and cover it with a lid. Then, pressure cook the khichdi on high flame until 2 whistles. After that, reduce to low flame and continue to cook it for another 8 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5f227122e2eb13885b32e345','5f226dfd7eb177afc92f7082',5,'M3: Garnish','After simmering the Hyderabadi Khichdi, remove the lid and plate the khichdi in a serving plate. Garnish it with a sprig of fresh coriander leaves and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f2274e77eb177afc92f7088','5f22737db287d4a9eb97c7a3',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Grilled Koliwada Prawns, first, rinse 250 grams of deveined prawns in the cold water and clean them thoroughly. If using shelled prawns, hold the prawn with one hand and firmly twist off the head using your other hand. Then, pull off the tail, peel away the outer shell, and pull off the legs from the underside of the shell. Similarly, clean the rest of the prawns. Next, wash and cut a lime into halves and squeeze 2 tablespoons of lime juice in a small bowl. Wash and finely chop 1 teaspoon of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5f22755eb287d4a9eb97c7a4','5f22737db287d4a9eb97c7a3',2,'M1: Season the Prawns','To make Grilled Koliwada Prawns, first, add the deveined prawns in a large bowl. Next, a teaspoon of coriander, a teaspoon of cumin powder, half a teaspoon of red chili powder, and 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder. Add a teaspoon of salt, and a teaspoon of garlic paste followed by 2 tablespoons of lime juice. Mix it well and coat the prawns evenly with the masala.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f2275ae7eb177afc92f708a','5f22737db287d4a9eb97c7a3',3,'M2: Grill Prawns','To Grill, the Koliwada Prawns, heat a grill pan over medium flame and grease it with 2 teaspoons of cooking oil. Next, add the prawns and grill them over medium-high flame for 6-7 minutes. Keep flipping the prawns often so they are evenly browned on all sides. After the prawns are crisp and browned, turn off the flame and plate them onto a serving plate and serve. Alternatively, prawns can also be grilled in the oven, for that first, grease the grill rack with a teaspoon of cooking oil using an oil brush. Then, thread the prawns onto the skewers and place them onto the grill rack. Drizzle over a teaspoon of olive oil and set it inside the oven. Grill the prawns at 200°C for 10-12 minutes until they are tender-crisp. After that, carefully take out the prawns from the oven and garnish them with some coriander leaves and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":10,"flame":0}'),('5f2287ce7eb177afc92f709a','5d7d2eb739613718ed7d853d',3,'M2: Simmer the chicken','Saute this for 2 mins and then add 1/2 cup of chopped tomatoes, saute for another 2 mins. Next, add the 400 g of chicken, mix well, and then add 3/4 cup of water. Cover the kadai with a lid and let the curry cook for 10 mins. After this, add 2 cups of spinach leaves, saute for 3 mins. Once the spinach has cooked, garnish with 1 tbsp of coriander leaves, and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5f27c30eb287d4a9eb97c7ba','5e1977f04f28558c29df63f5',5,'M2:  Simmer the dal, add fresh cream. Garnish & serve','Next, add 1/2 inch of chopped ginger, 1/4 tsp of garam masala, and cook for another 2 mins. Next add the cooked dal to the pan, 2 tbsp of fresh cream, 1 tbsp of butter, and mix well. Cook this for 2 mins and then garnish with 1 tbsp of coriander leaves and 1 tsp of fresh cream. The dish is ready to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5f3f651ab287d4a9eb97c88c','5f3f6488e2eb13885b32e481',1,'P1: Prep Onions','For Prawn Malai Curry, first, peel, wash and roughly slice 1 cup of onions. Next, to boil the onions, add in the sliced onions to a saucepan followed by 2 cups of water. Mix it well and boil the onions over medium flame for 8-10 minutes, while stirring occasionally. Cook the onions until they turn slightly off-white and translucent. Make sure to stir the onions in between to prevent them from sticking to the bottom of the pan. While the onions are boiling, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":10,"flame":3}'),
('5f3f655de2eb13885b32e482','5f3f6488e2eb13885b32e481',2,'P2:  Prep the Prawns','For Prawn Malai Curry, first, rinse the 12 nos deveined prawns in the cold water and clean them thoroughly. If using shelled prawns, hold the prawn with one hand and firmly twist off the head using your other hand. Then, pull off the tail, peel away the outer shell, and pull off the legs from the underside of the shell. Similarly, clean the rest of the prawns.  Wash and finely chop a tablespoon of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f3f65cce2eb13885b32e483','5f3f6488e2eb13885b32e481',3,'P3: Make Onion Paste','To prepare the boiled onion paste for Prawn Malai Curry, after boiling the onions, turn off the flame and transfer them to a large bowl. Soak the boiled onions in 2 cups of water for 2-3 minutes until it cools down. After that, strain the onions and discard the water. Add the boiled onions to a blender jar and blend it well into a smooth paste.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f3f66a8e2eb13885b32e484','5f3f6488e2eb13885b32e481',4,'M1: Season and Cook Prawns','For Prawn Malai Curry, add 12 nos shelled and deveined prawns in a large bowl. Season the prawns with 1/4 teaspoon of salt and 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, and mix it well. Next, to fry the prawns, heat 2 tablespoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame. Add in the seasoned prawns and fry them over medium flame for 3-4 minutes. Flip and fry the prawns evenly on both sides until they are slightly golden. Then, turn off the flame and take them out onto a plate.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f3f6744b287d4a9eb97c88d','5f3f6488e2eb13885b32e481',5,'M2: Add Whole Spices','To make Prawn Malai Curry, add 1 tablespoon of cooking oil to the same pan and heat it over medium flame for a minute. Add 3 nos green cardamoms, 3 nos cloves, 1 nos bay leaf, and a half-inch piece of cinnamon stick. Next, add the prepared boiled onion paste followed by a tablespoon of ginger-garlic paste and fry it over medium flame for 4-5 minutes until it turns slightly golden brown.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5f3f677c7eb177afc92f7167','5f3f6488e2eb13885b32e481',6,'M3: Add Masala Powders','After cooking the masala, add 1 teaspoon of red chilli powder followed by 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder and mix it well. Add 1/4 cup of water and cook the masala over low flame for another 2-3 minutes until oil separates. Next, add the fried prawns back in and coat them well with the masala. Add 1 cup of fresh cream and keep stirring it continuously over a low flame until it is well combined. Then, simmer the prawns with the gravy for 2-3 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and plate the prawns in the serving bowl spooning over the gravy. Garnish it with a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5f4cc2abfba58f6f2a229040','5d0a1fcc828e55e31ee1151d',4,'Add the tempering to Pongal. Garnish & Serve','To make Kara Pongal, heat 1 tablespoon of ghee in a kadai over medium flame for a minute. Add a teaspoon of cumin seeds followed by half a teaspoon of crushed black peppercorns and a 1-inch piece of chopped ginger. Next, add 2 nos slit green chilies, 10 nos cashew nuts along with 7 nos curry leaves and 1/4 teaspoon of hing. Saute it over low flame for 3-4 minutes until cashews turn slightly golden. Then, turn off the flame and this tempering instantly over the prepared Pongal. Mix it well and take it out into a serving bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f58845dfba58f6f2a22906c','5e19695c4f28558c29df63e9',3,'M2: Add spices. Garnish and serve','Then, add 1/2 inch of ginger, 1 tsp of gram flour, 1/4 tsp of coriander powder, mix well, and then cover the pan again and simmer it for 5 mins. Next add 1/4 tsp of crushed black pepper and mix well. Once the ingredients are combined well, the dish is ready to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":5,"flame":3}'),('5f5b23a33a5ec6d73102e0a6','5f5b217aae3cb6df54f6d437',1,'P1: Cook the Sweet Potatoes','To prepare Sweet Potato Stir-Fry, start by cooking 2 medium-sized sweet potatoes in a pressure cooker along with 1 cup of water. Cook the sweet potatoes on high flame for 1 whistle and then reduce the flame to low and cook for 5 minutes. Once this is done, allow the pressure cooker to cool down completely before you take the lid off. While the potatoes are cooking please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f5b2423fba58f6f2a229079','5f5b217aae3cb6df54f6d437',2,'P2: Prep Ingredients','For Sweet Potato Stir-Fry, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash, peel, and finely chop 1/4 inch of ginger. Wash and finely chop 2 green chillies. Grate 3 tablespoons of fresh coconut. Wash 6 curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f5b24b9ae3cb6df54f6d438','5f5b217aae3cb6df54f6d437',3,'P3: Prep Sweet Potatoes','For Sweet Potato Stir-Fry, once the sweet potatoes are done cooking in the pressure cooker, allow it to cool down completely and then take the lid off. Next, peel the sweet potatoes and dice them into even cubes.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5f5b256efba58f6f2a22907b','5f5b217aae3cb6df54f6d437',4,'M1: Temper Spices','To cook Sweet Potato Stir-Fry, in a Kadai heat 2 teaspoons of coconut oil for about 1 minute. Once warm, add 1/2 teaspoon of mustard seeds, 1/4 teaspoon of cumin seeds, tear 2 dry red chillies with your hands, and add them to the oil. Next, add 1/4 inch of finely chopped ginger, 2 finely chopped green chillies, 1/4 cup of finely chopped onions, 1/2 tsp of salt, and tear 6 curry leaves with your hands and add them to the Kadai. Saute this for 3-4 mins.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5f5b2601ae3cb6df54f6d439','5f5b217aae3cb6df54f6d437',5,'M2: Add sweet potatoes and coconut','Once the onions have started to brown, add 1/2 a teaspoon of turmeric powder, 1/4 a teaspoon of black pepper powder, and mix well. Then, add the cooked sweet potato and saute for 3-4 mins. Once the sweet potatoes are coated in the masala, add 3 tablespoons of grated coconut. Mix this well and the dish is ready to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f5b28a9ae3cb6df54f6d43a','5f5b28443a5ec6d73102e0a7',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','To prepare Sweet Potato Fried Rice, first, peel 2 large sweet potatoes and then grate them using a box grater. The sweet potato needs to have a rice-like consistency. Next, peel and finely chop 1/2 cup of onions. Then, crack 2 eggs into a small bowl and whisk it well. Blanch 1/4 cup of green peas','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f5b290d3a5ec6d73102e0a8','5f5b28443a5ec6d73102e0a7',2,'M1: Cook Onions','For Sweet Potato Fried Rice, heat 2 teaspoons of olive oil in a frying pan for a mintue. Once warm add 1/2 cup of finely chopped onions and saute for 2-3 minutes until translucent. Next, add 1.5 cups of grated sweet potato, 1/2 teaspoon of salt, 1/2 a teaspoon of black pepper powder, and saute them for 3-4 mintues.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f5b296f3a5ec6d73102e0a9','5f5b28443a5ec6d73102e0a7',3,'M2: Add Eggs','Next, build a cavity in the center of the pan and pour in the whisked eggs and begin to scramble them. Once the eggs have cooked combine them with the onions and sweet potato, saute this for 3-4 minutes. Then, add 1/4 cup of green peas, 1 tablespoon of soy sauce, and mix well. Once the ingredients have combined well, the dish is ready to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('5f5efe7bae3cb6df54f6d43e','5f5efe2afba58f6f2a22908a',1,'P1: Cook Sweet Potato','To prepare Sweet Potato Paratha, start by cooking 1 medium-sized sweet potatoes in a pressure cooker along with 1 cup of water. Cook the sweet potatoes on high flame for 1 whistle and then reduce the flame to low and cook for 5 mintues. Once this is done, allow the pressure cooker to cool down completely before you take the lid off. While the potatoes are cooking please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f5efed23a5ec6d73102e0af','5f5efe2afba58f6f2a22908a',2,'P2: Chop Ingredients','For Sweet Potato Paratha, wash and finely chop 1 green chilli. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f5f032dae3cb6df54f6d43f','5f5efe2afba58f6f2a22908a',3,'P3: Make Dough','For Sweet Potato Stir-Fry, once the sweet potatoes are done cooking in the pressure cooker, allow it to cool down completely and then take the lid off. Next, peel the sweet potatoes and then in a large bowl mash them with a fork or a masher until smooth. Next, add 1 cup whole wheat flour, a 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, a 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala, 1/4 teaspoon of dry mango powder, 1/4 teaspoon of carom seeds, 1 finely chopped green chilli, 1/4 teaspoon of ginger paste, 1/2 teaspoon of Kasuri methi, 1/4 teaspoon of salt, and 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves. Mix these dry ingredients together until they are combined well. Then, add 1/4 cup of water gradually until the dough combines and then knead it for 5 mins. Once the dough is soft, let it rest for 20 mins. While the dough is rest please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":20,"flame":0}'),('5f5f03a0ae3cb6df54f6d440','5f5efe2afba58f6f2a22908a',4,'M1: Make the Parathas','To make Sweet Potato Paratha, make small lemon-sized balls from the prepared dough. Take a dough ball and dust some flour over it. Then, roll it into a thin round paratha. Make sure to roll out the edges thin. Then, place it onto a hot Tawa and cook it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Flip and cook both sides evenly. Then apply half a teaspoon of cooking oil to each side and cook the paratha over medium flame for 2-3 minutes, until it is evenly browned on both the sides. Then, fold it into a triangle and take it out onto a plate. Serve. Make the rest of the parathas similarly.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f5f080cfba58f6f2a22908b','5f5f07adae3cb6df54f6d441',1,'P1: Prep Ingredietns','To prepare Mirch ka Salan, first, wash, peel, and roughly chop 1/2 an inch of ginger. Peel 1 clove of garlic. Wash 5 green chilies, slit them on one side and deseed them. Peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5f5f08c5fba58f6f2a22908c','5f5f07adae3cb6df54f6d441',2,'P2: Dry Roast Spices','For Mirchi Ka Salan, heat a frying pan for 1 min on a low flame and then add 2 tablespoons of raw peanuts, 1.5 tablespoons of sesame seeds, 1/2 teaspoon of poppy seeds, and 1 tablespoon of dry coconut. Saute this for 2-3 minutes, once it becomes aromatic, remove it from the flame and allow it to cool for 5 minutes.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f5f098cfba58f6f2a22908d','5f5f07adae3cb6df54f6d441',3,'P3: Blend to Make Masala Paste','For Mirchi ka Salan, add the dry roasted ingredients to a blender along with 1/2 inch of chopped ginger, 1 peeled garlic clove, 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala, 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, 1/2 teaspoon of red chili powder, 1/4 tsp of fenugreek seeds, and 1/4 cup of water. Blend these ingredients together to make a masala paste for the Salan.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f5f09d43a5ec6d73102e0b0','5f5f07adae3cb6df54f6d441',4,'M1: Fry Green Chilies','To make Mirchi Ka Salan, heat 2.5 teaspoons of cooking oil in a pan for 1 minute. Once warm, add the slit green chilies to the oil and fry them for 2-3 minutes. Once the chilies begin to blister take them off the heat and set them aside on a plate.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f5f0a8aae3cb6df54f6d442','5f5f07adae3cb6df54f6d441',5,'M2: Temper Spices','Next, in the same pan temper 1/4 teaspoon of cumin seeds and 8 curry leaves. Once aromatic, add 1/4 cup of onions and saute them until they are golden brown. Then add the prepared masala paste and saute for 1 minute. Then add 1/4 cup of tamarind pulp, 1/2 teaspoon of jaggery, 1/2 teaspoon of salt, and mix well. Next, add 1 cup of water to the pan, mix well, and then cover the pan with a lid. Let the Salan simmer for 30 minutes. While this is simmering please move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":30,"flame":3}'),('5f5f0acbfba58f6f2a22908e','5f5f07adae3cb6df54f6d441',6,'M3: Final Touches','Once the Salan is done simmering, take the lid off and then add the fried green chillies and 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves to the pan.  Cover the pan with the lid once more and let the Salan simmer for 5 mins. Once this is complete the dish is ready to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":5,"flame":2}'),
('5f5f0d8ffba58f6f2a22908f','5f5f0d4bae3cb6df54f6d443',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','To prepare Broccoli and Zucchini Soup, first, wash and chop 1 cup of broccoli into small florets. Wash and roughly dice 1/2 cup of Zucchini. Squeeze 2 tablespoons of lime juice.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f5f0e453a5ec6d73102e0b1','5f5f0d4bae3cb6df54f6d443',2,'M1: Cook the Vegetables','To make Broccoli and Zucchini Soup, in a pot heat 1 tablespoon of olive oil for 1 minute. Once warm add 1/2 teaspoon of ginger paste, 1/2 teaspoon of garlic paste, 1/4 teaspoon of coriander seeds, and 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder. Saute this for 1 minute until combined well. Next, add 1 vegetable stock cube to the pan along with 2 cups of water, if you do not have stock water or stock cubes feel free to use just water.  Allow the water to come to a boil, then add 1 cup of broccoli florets, 1/2 cup of diced Zucchini, and 1/2 teaspoon of salt. Give this a stir, cover the pot with a lid, and let the soup simmer for 15-20 minutes. While the soup is simmering please move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":20,"flame":3}'),('5f5f0ee13a5ec6d73102e0b2','5f5f0d4bae3cb6df54f6d443',3,'M2: Blend to Make Soup','For Broccoli and Zucchini Soup, once the soup is done simmering turn off the flame and let the soup cool down for around 5 minutes. Then, transfer the contents of the pot into a blender and blend until smooth. Adjust the consistency of the soup with some water if necessary. Once this is done your soup is ready to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f5f119a3a5ec6d73102e0b3','5f5f1109ae3cb6df54f6d444',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','To prepare this Creamy Zucchini Soup, peel and finely chop 2 teaspoons of garlic. Peel and finely chop 1/2 cup of onions. Wash and roughly dice 1 cup of zucchini.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f5f1229ae3cb6df54f6d445','5f5f1109ae3cb6df54f6d444',2,'M1: Cook Vegetables','To make Creamy Zucchini Soup, in a pot heat 1/2 tablespoon of olive oil for 1 minute. Once warm, add 1/2 cup of chopped onions and 2 teaspoons of chopped garlic. Saute this for 2-3 minutes until the onions are tender. Next, add 1 cup of chopped zucchini, 1 vegetable stock cube, and 2 cups of water. If you do not have a stock cube or stock water, feel free to use just water. Give this a nice stir and then cover the pot with a lid. Allow the soup to simmer for 20 minutes. While the soup is simmering please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":20,"flame":3}'),
('5f5f12c6ae3cb6df54f6d446','5f5f1109ae3cb6df54f6d444',3,'M2: Blend and Make Soup','For Creamy Zucchini Soup, turn off the flame on the simmering soup and allow it to cool down for 5 minutes. Then pour the contents of the pot into a blender and blend into a smooth paste. Once blended, pour the soup back into the pot and set the flame to low. Next, add 1/4 cup of fresh cream, 1/2 teaspoon of salt, and 1/4 teaspoon of pepper powder. Stir the soup and once everything is combined the dish is ready to serve. Garnish the soup with 1/2 teaspoon of parmesan cheese and 1/4 teaspoon of black pepper powder.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":5,"flame":2}'),('5f5f152afba58f6f2a229090','5f5f14f8ae3cb6df54f6d449',1,'AP1: Soak Chickpeas','For Chickpea Tofu Curry, first, soak 3/4 cup of chickpeas in a large bowl with 2 cups of water for 8 hours or overnight. While the chickpeas are soaking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":480,"advanced_prep_time":480,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f5f157cae3cb6df54f6d44a','5f5f14f8ae3cb6df54f6d449',2,'P1: Cook Chickpeas','To prepare this Chickpea Tofu Curry, in a pressure cooker add 3/4 cup of soaked chickpeas along with 1.5 cups of water. Cook this on high flame for 4 whistles. After that, reduce the flame to low and cook for 5 minutes. Once the chickpeas are done cooking, turn off the flame and allow the pressure to release naturally before you take off the lid. Set the cooked chickpeas aside. While the chickpeas are boiling, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":18,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f5f1608fba58f6f2a229091','5f5f14f8ae3cb6df54f6d449',3,'P2: Marinate the Tofu and Chop Ingredients','For Chickpea Tofu Curry, dice 1 cups of tofu and then place it in a medium-sized bowl. Next, add 1 tablespoon of rice flour, 1/2 teaspoon of salt, and 1/2 teaspoon of black pepper to the bowl. Mix this well until the tofu is evenly coated in flour, then set this aside. Next, wash and finely chop 2 green chillies. Peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f5f1698fba58f6f2a229092','5f5f14f8ae3cb6df54f6d449',4,'M1: Fry Tofu','To make Chickpea Tofu Curry, heat 1 tablespoon of olive oil in a pan and then add the flour-coated tofu to the pan. Let them cook on each side for about 2-3 minute each. Once they have a nice light brown colour on them, take them off the heat and onto a plate. Set this aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5f5f1749ae3cb6df54f6d44b','5f5f14f8ae3cb6df54f6d449',5,'M2: Cook Onions','For Chickpea Tofu Curry, to the same pan add another tablespoon of olive oil, then add 2 teaspoons of garlic paste, 2 teaspoons of ginger paste, 2 chopped green chillies, 1/4 cup of chopped onions, and saute this for 2-3 mins. Once the onions are golden brown,  add 1/2 cup of tomato puree, 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, 1/2 teaspoon of cumin powder, 1/2 teaspoon of coriander powder, and 1/2 teaspoon of salt. Mix this well, then cover the pan with a lip and let the mixture simmer for 5 minutes. While this is simmering please move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f5f1798fba58f6f2a229093','5f5f14f8ae3cb6df54f6d449',6,'M3: Add Cooked Chickpeas and Tofu','For Chickpea Tofu Curry, once the vegetables are done simmering, take the lid off, and then add 3/4 cup of cooked chickpeas, 3/4 cup of water, and give it a stir. Once everything is combined well, close the pan with a lid once more and let the curry simmer for another 5 minutes. After that, add the cooked tofu, 1/2 cup of coconut milk, and 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves. Mix this well, once the ingredients have combined well, the dish is ready to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5f5f1a473a5ec6d73102e0b4','5f5f1a18ae3cb6df54f6d44c',1,'AP1: Soak Green Chickpeas','For Green Chana Paneer Masala, first, soak 3/4 cup of green chana in a large bowl with 2 cups of water for 8 hours or overnight. While the chana is soaking please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":480,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f5f1a9e3a5ec6d73102e0b5','5f5f1a18ae3cb6df54f6d44c',2,'P1: Cook Green Chickpeas','To prepare this green chana paneer masala, in a pressure cooker add 3/4 cup of soaked chickpeas along with 1 teaspoon of salt, 1 black cardamom, 1-inch cinnamon stick, and 1.5 cups of water. Cook this on high flame for 3 whistles. After that, reduce the flame to low and cook for 5 minutes. Once the chickpeas are done cooking, turn off the flame and allow the pressure to release naturally before you take off the lid. Set the cooked chickpeas aside. While the chickpeas are boiling, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5f5f1b673a5ec6d73102e0b6','5f5f1a18ae3cb6df54f6d44c',3,'P2: Marinate Paneer and Chop Ingredients','For Green Chana Paneer Masala, wash and finely chop 2 green chilies. Peel and roughly chop 1/4 cup of onions and then place them in a blender to make a smooth onion paste. Dice 3/4 cup of paneer into even cubes and place them in a large bowl. In this bowl add 1 tablespoon of ginger paste, 1 tablespoon of garlic paste, 1/2 teaspoon of salt, 1 chopped green chili, 1/2 teaspoon of cumin powder, 1/2 teaspoon of coriander powder, and 1/2 teaspoon of fennel powder. Mix this well and once the paneer is coated well with the masala set it aside for 20 minutes.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5f5f1cb7ae3cb6df54f6d44d','5f5f1a18ae3cb6df54f6d44c',4,'M1: Fry the Paneer','For Green Chana Paneer Masala, heat 2 tablespoons of butter in a pan, and once warm add the marinated paneer. Let them cook on each side for about 2-3 minutes each. Once they have a nice light brown color on them, take them off the heat and onto a plate. Set this aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f5f1d53fba58f6f2a229094','5f5f1a18ae3cb6df54f6d44c',5,'M2: Cook Vegetables','For Green Chana Paneer Masala, in a pan heat 1 tablespoon of cooking oil for 1 minute. Once warm, add the prepared onion paste and saute for 2-3 minutes. Then, add 1 tablespoon of garlic paste and 1 tablespoon of ginger paste, saute this for another 2-3 minutes. Next, add 1/2 cup of tomato puree and mix well. Once the ingredients are combined well, add 1 chopped green chili, 1/2 teaspoon of salt, 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, 1/2 teaspoon of paprika, 1/2 teaspoon of cumin powder, 1/2 teaspoon of coriander powder, 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala, and mix well. Then, cook the masala over medium flame until oil separates.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f5f1d8c3a5ec6d73102e0b7','5f5f1a18ae3cb6df54f6d44c',6,'M3: Add Cooked Chickpeas and Paneer','Next, add the cooked green chana to the pan and mix everything really well. Then add the fried paneer pieces and combine everything well. Once combined, the curry is ready to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5f5f1fc63a5ec6d73102e0b9','5f5f1f6bae3cb6df54f6d44e',1,'AP1: Prep the Chicken Legs','To make Yogurt Ghee Roast, first, wash and clean 450 grams of chicken legs. With your knife make about 4 slits along the fleshy part of the leg and then sprinkle 1 teaspoon of salt, 1 teaspoon of black pepper, and 1 tablespoon of lime juice on all the chicken legs. Rub this seasoning into the chicken with your hands. Once this is complete, allow the chicken to rest for 10-15 minutes. While the chicken is rest please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":15,"flame":0}'),('5f5f2029ae3cb6df54f6d44f','5f5f1f6bae3cb6df54f6d44e',2,'AP2: Prep ingredients for the Marinade','For Yogurt Ghee Roast, peel and finely chop 1 tablespoon of garlic, wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves, and zest 1 lemon with a grater or microblade to get 1/2 a teaspoon of lemon zest. Then cut the lemon in half and squeeze 1 tablespoon of lemon juice.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5f5f20a83a5ec6d73102e0ba','5f5f1f6bae3cb6df54f6d44e',3,'AP3: Marinate the Chicken','Then prepare the yogurt marinade for Yogurt Chicken Roast, in a large bowl, add 1 cup of yogurt, 1 tablespoon of chopped garlic, 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves, 1/2 teaspoon of lemon zest, 1 teaspoon of chilli flakes, 1 tablespoon of lemon juice, 1 teaspoon of mixed herbs, 1/2 teaspoon of salt, 1/2 teaspoon of black pepper powder, and mix well. Next, add the seasoned chicken legs to the bowl and drizzle 1 teaspoon of olive oil. Mix this well, cover the bowl, refrigerate it, and allow it to marinate for 3 hours.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":180,"advanced_prep_time":180,"timer":180,"flame":0}'),('5f5f2117fba58f6f2a229095','5f5f1f6bae3cb6df54f6d44e',4,'M1: Cook Chicken in the Oven','For Yogurt Ghee Roast, preheat the oven at 180 degrees for at least 10 minutes. While the oven is preheating, coat your oven tray with 1 teaspoon of olive oil and spread this with a pastry brush. Next, place the marinated chicken on the tray and pour any remaining marinade over the chicken legs with a spoon. Then drizzle the chicken legs in another teaspoon of olive oil. Place the tray in the oven and let it cook for 30 minutes. While the chicken is cooking please move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":35,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":30,"flame":0}'),('5f5f21493a5ec6d73102e0bb','5f5f1f6bae3cb6df54f6d44e',5,'M2: Take the Chicken out of the Oven','For Yogurt Ghee Roast, once the chicken is cooked remove it from the oven carefully. Place the cooked pieces onto a serving plate and enjoy!','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f6321413a5ec6d73102e0d8','5f6320e4ae3cb6df54f6d46d',1,'P1: Marinate the Chicken','Next, marinate the chicken for Chicken Fajita Pasta, wash and clean 1 cup of boneless chicken. Chop the chicken into cubes and place it in a medium-sized bowl. Then, add squeeze 2 tablespoons of lime juice, 1/2 teaspoon of salt, and 1/2 a teaspoon of black pepper powder. Mix this well and let it rest for 30 minutes. While the chicken is marinating please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":30,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":30,"flame":0}'),('5f6321793a5ec6d73102e0d9','5f6320e4ae3cb6df54f6d46d',2,'P2: Cook the Pasta','Boil the pasta for Chicken Fajita Pasta, first, add 3 cups of water to a saucepan along with a teaspoon of salt. Bring it to a boil over a high flame. As the water comes to a rolling boil, add 1 cup of penne pasta into it and stir it well. Then, boil the pasta over medium-high flame for 9 minutes, until it is firm to the bite. While the pasta is boiling, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":10,"flame":4}'),
('5f6321e53a5ec6d73102e0da','5f6320e4ae3cb6df54f6d46d',3,'P3: Prep Ingredients','For Chicken Fajita Pasta, peel and slice 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and julienne 1/4 cup of yellow capsicum and 1/4 cup of green capsicum. Wash and roughly dice 1/2 cup of tomato. Peel and finely chop 1 tablespoon of garlic. Next, using a box grater, grate 1/2 cup of cheddar cheese.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f632255fba58f6f2a2290a8','5f6320e4ae3cb6df54f6d46d',4,'P4: Make the Fajita Seasoning','To prepare Chicken Fajita Pasta, prepare a fajita seasoning, in a small bowl add 1/2 teaspoon of paprika, 1/2 teaspoon of cumin, 1/2 teaspoon of black pepper powder, 1 teaspoon of red chili powder, 1/2 teaspoon of garlic powder, and 1 teaspoon of salt. Mix this well and set it aside. If you do not have any paprika then it can be replaced with Deji Mirchi Powder.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f6322973a5ec6d73102e0db','5f6320e4ae3cb6df54f6d46d',5,'M1: Cook Chicken','To make Chicken Fajita Pasta, in a pan heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil. Once the oil is hot add the marinated chicken pieces. Cook the chicken on each side for 7-10 mintues until it becomes a light brown colour. Once the chicken has gained colour, take it off the pan and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f63233f3a5ec6d73102e0dc','5f6320e4ae3cb6df54f6d46d',6,'M2: Cook the  Vegetables','Next, for Chicken Fajita Pasta, in the same pan heat 1 teaspoon of cooking oil. Once its hot, add 1/4 cup of chopped yellow capsicum, 1/4 cup of green capsicum, and 1/4 cup of onions. Saute this for 2-3 minutes, then add 1 tablespoon of chopped garlic, and mix well. To this, add 1 tablespoon of the fajita seasoning and mix well. Allow the vegetables to cook for another 2 minutes and once they are tender set them aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":2,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f6323ad3a5ec6d73102e0dd','5f6320e4ae3cb6df54f6d46d',7,'M3: Make the Pasta Sauce','For Chicken Fajita Pasta, in a pot heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil for 1 minute. Once warm, add 1/2 cup of diced tomatoes and saute for 2-3 minutes. Once the tomatoes are tender add 1 tablespoon of the fajita seasoning and mix well. To this, add the cooked chicken, give it a good mix, then add the cooked pasta and cooked vegetables, mix it well. Once everything is combined well, add 1 cup of fresh cream, 1/2 cup of grated cheddar cheese, and 1 teaspoon of mixed herbs. Mix everything well and your dish is ready to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5f632579fba58f6f2a2290aa','5f63253cae3cb6df54f6d46e',1,'P1: Cook the Pasta','Boil the pasta for Pasta with Mint Sauce, first, add 3 cups of water to a saucepan along with a teaspoon of salt. Bring it to a boil over a high flame. As the water comes to a rolling boil, add 1 cup of penne pasta into it and stir it well. Then, boil the pasta over medium-high flame for 9 minutes, until it is firm to the bite. While the pasta is boiling, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":4}'),('5f6325c7fba58f6f2a2290ab','5f63253cae3cb6df54f6d46e',2,'P2: Make Spinach Puree','For Pasta with Mint Sauce, Prep the Spinach Leaves. In a pot boil 1.5 cups of water over a high flame. Next, wash 1/2 cup of spinach leaves, and then when the water starts boiling add 1/2 cup of spinach leaves. Let this cook for 3-4 minutes. Once the spinach leaves have wilted and become deeper in colour, turn off the flame and drain the water. Allow the leaves to cool for 5 minutes and then place them in a blender and make a smooth spinach puree.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":9,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f6326473a5ec6d73102e0df','5f63253cae3cb6df54f6d46e',3,'P3: Make Mint Mixture','Next, for Pasta with Mint Sauce, once the pasta has cooked, drain the water, and set the pasta aside. Then prepare the mint sauce, wash 1/4 cup of mint leaves. Wash 1/4 cup of coriander leaves. Peel 1/2 an inch of ginger. Wash 2 green chilies. Cut 1 lime in half and squeeze 1 tablespoon of lime juice. Then, in a blending jar, add 1/4 cup of mint leaves, 1/4 cup of coriander leaves, 2 green chillies, 1/2 an inch of ginger, 1/2 teaspoon of salt, 1/2 teaspoon of cumin powder, 1 tablespoon of lime juice, and 2 tablespoons of water. Blend this until you have a smooth Mint Mixture. Once this is done, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f6326b0ae3cb6df54f6d46f','5f63253cae3cb6df54f6d46e',4,'P4: Prep Ingredients','Next, Prep the Vegetables for Pasta with Mint Sauce, peel, and finely chop 1 tablespoon of garlic. Peel and slice 1/4 cup of onions. Peel and julienne 1/4 cup of carrots. Then, wash and julienne 1/4 cup of green capsicum, 1/4 cup of yellow capsicum, and 1/4 cup of red capsicum. Wash and chop 1/4 cup of broccoli into small florets.','prep_method','{"active_time":14,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f6326e8fba58f6f2a2290ad','5f63253cae3cb6df54f6d46e',5,'M1: Cook Vegetables','To make Pasta with Mint Sauce, in a pot heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil for 1 minute. Once warm, add 1 tablespoon of chopped garlic and 1/4 cup of sliced onions, saute this for 2-3 minutes until slightly golden. Then, add 1/4 cup of carrots, 1/4 cup of green capsicum, 1/4 cup of red capsicum, 1/4 cup of yellow capsicum, and 1/4 cup of broccoli florets. Mix this well and saute for 3-4 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5f632738ae3cb6df54f6d470','5f63253cae3cb6df54f6d46e',6,'M2: Add Mint Sauce','Next, to make Pasta with Mint Sauce, add 1/2 cup of the prepared spinach puree and mix well. Once this is combined add the cooked pasta and gently combine all the ingredients. Next, pour the prepared mint sauce into the pot and mix it well. Season this with 1 teaspoon of salt and 1 teaspoon of black pepper powder. Combine everything well and the dish is ready to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5f644a7cfba58f6f2a2290b3','5f644994fba58f6f2a2290b2',1,'P1: Marinate Paneer','For Paneer Pasta Masala, first, chop 1/2 cup of paneer into even cubes. Peel and roughly dice 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and roughly dice 1/4 cup of green capsicum, 1/4 cup of red capsicum, and 1/4 cup of yellow capsicum. Cut 1 lime in half and then squeeze 1 tablespoon of lime juice. Then, in a large bowl, add 1/2 cup of cubed paneer, 1/4 cup of onions, 1/4 cup of green capsicum, 1/4 cup of red capsicum, 1/4 cup of yellow capsicum, 1 tablespoon of ginger paste, 1 tablespoon of garlic paste, 1/2 cup of curd, 1 teaspoon of paprika, 1 teaspoon of tandoori masala, 1 teaspoon of salt, and 1 tablespoon of lime juice. Combine all these ingredients well and then let the paneer marinate for 1 hour. While the paneer is marinating please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":60,"advanced_prep_time":60,"timer":60,"flame":0}'),('5f644aed3a5ec6d73102e0e4','5f644994fba58f6f2a2290b2',2,'P2: Cook the Pasta','Next, cook the pasta for Paneer Pasta Masala, add 3 cups of water to a saucepan along with a teaspoon of salt. Bring it to a boil over a high flame. As the water comes to a rolling boil, add 1 cup of fusilli pasta into it and stir it well. Then, boil the pasta over medium-high flame for 9 minutes, until it is firm to the bite. While the pasta is boiling, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":4}'),('5f644bd3fba58f6f2a2290b4','5f644994fba58f6f2a2290b2',3,'P3: Make Blanched Tomato Puree','Next, prepare a Tomato Puree for Paneer Pasta Masala, in a saucepan heat 3 cups of water over a high flame. Once boiling, add 3 - 4 medium-sized tomatoes to the water. Boil them for 2-3 minutes, until the skin starts to peel black. Then, remove them from the water using a spoon and let them cool down for 5 minutes. Once cool, transfer them to a blending jar and blend into a smooth puree. Once the tomato puree is ready, set it aside, and move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f644c2fae3cb6df54f6d473','5f644994fba58f6f2a2290b2',4,'P4: Prep Ingredients','For Paneer Pasta Masala, peel and finely chop 1 tablespoon of garlic. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of green chilli. Grate 2 teaspoons of cheese using a box grater. Once the pasta is done cooking, drain the water, and set the pasta aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5f644ced3a5ec6d73102e0e5','5f644994fba58f6f2a2290b2',5,'M1: Bake Paneer','To make Paneer Pasta Masala, preheat the oven at 180°C for 5 minutes. Then place the marinated paneer on a baking tray and bake in the oven for 20 - 25 mins. While the Paneer is baking please move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":25,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":20,"flame":0}'),('5f644d83fba58f6f2a2290b5','5f644994fba58f6f2a2290b2',6,'M2: Temper Spices','Next, to make Paneer Pasta Masala, in a large pan heat 2 teaspoons of butter for 1 minute. Once warm add 1 tablespoon of chopped garlic and saute this for 1 minute, until the garlic is golden. Then add 1 bay leaf, 1 tablespoon of chopped green chilli, and 1/2 a cup of the prepared tomato puree. Mix this well until all the ingredients are incorporated well.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f644e42fba58f6f2a2290b6','5f644994fba58f6f2a2290b2',7,'M3: Add Seasoning to make the Pasta Sauce','Then, to make Paneer Pasta Masala, add 1/4 cup of pasta sauce and mix well. Next, add 1/2 teaspoon of tandoori masala, 1/2 teaspoon of red chilli powder, 1/2 teaspoon of salt, and mix well. Then, add 1/4 cup of cheese spread and 1/2 cup of fresh cream, gently mix this into the sauce. Once incorporated well, add 1 tablespoon of oregano and add the baked paneer, mix it well. Then, add the cooked pasta and gently fold it into the sauce. Once everything is mixed well the dish is ready to serve. Garnish the pasta with 2 teaspoons of grated cheese.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5f645592fba58f6f2a2290b7','5f64553dae3cb6df54f6d474',1,'P1: Cook Pasta','Boil the pasta for Keema Pasta, first, add 3 cups of water to a saucepan along with a teaspoon of salt and 1 tablespoon of cooking oil. Bring it to a boil over a high flame. As the water comes to a rolling boil, add 1 cup of penne pasta into it and stir it well. Then, boil the pasta over medium-high flame for 9 minutes, until it is firm to the bite. While the pasta is boiling, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f645680ae3cb6df54f6d475','5f64553dae3cb6df54f6d474',2,'P2: Prep Ingredients','Next, for Keema pasta, peel and finely chop 1 teaspoon of garlic. Peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onion. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of green capsicum. Wash and finely chop 1/2 cup of tomato. Once the pasta is done cooking, drain the water, and set the pasta aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5f6456e3fba58f6f2a2290b8','5f64553dae3cb6df54f6d474',3,'M1: Cook Chicken Mince','To make Keema Pasta, in a pan heat 1 tablespoon of cooking oil for 1 minute. Once it''s warm, add 1 teaspoon of chopped garlic and 1/4 cup of chopped onions, saute this for 2-3 minutes. Once the onions have browned slightly, add 1 cup of minced chicken, break up the chicken and mix it with the onions and garlic well. Saute this for 7-10 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":14,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f64575c3a5ec6d73102e0e6','5f64553dae3cb6df54f6d474',4,'M2: Add Vegetables','Next, to make keema pasta, add 1/4 cup of chopped capsicum to the pan and mix it well. Then, add 1/2 cup of chopped tomatoes and gently fold all the ingredients together. Next, add 1 teaspoon of salt, 1/2 teaspoon of cumin powder, 1 teaspoon of oregano, 1 teaspoon of chilli flakes, 1/2 teaspoon of sugar, and mix well. Once combined, add the cooked pasta and gently incorporate it with the other ingredients. Then, add 1/4 cup of tomato ketchup and mix well. Once this is combined, the dish is ready to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5f645a5b3a5ec6d73102e0e7','5f6459dbfba58f6f2a2290b9',1,'P1: Season Chicken','For Creamy Chicken and Garlic Pasta, clean 1 cup if chicken breast and then chop then into cubes. Place them in a medium-sized bowl and season it with 1/2 teaspoon of salt, 1 teaspoon of garlic powder, 1/4 teaspoon of black pepper powder, and 1/2 teaspoon of Italian seasoning. Mix this well and let the chicken marinate for 30 minutes. While the chicken is rest, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":30,"advanced_prep_time":30,"timer":30,"flame":0}'),('5f645cbb3a5ec6d73102e0e8','5f6459dbfba58f6f2a2290b9',2,'P2: Cook Pasta','Boil the pasta for Creamy Chicken and Garlic Pasta, add 3 cups of water to a saucepan along with 1/4 teaspoon of salt, and 1/2 teaspoon of oil. Bring it to a boil over a high flame. As the water comes to a rolling boil, add 1 cup of penne pasta into it and stir it well. Then, boil the pasta over medium-high flame for 9 minutes, until it is firm to the bite. While the pasta is boiling, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":4}'),('5f645d13fba58f6f2a2290ba','5f6459dbfba58f6f2a2290b9',3,'P3: Prep Ingredients','For Creamy Chicken and Garlic Pasta, peel and finely chop 1.5 tablespoons of garlic. Grate 1 cup of parmesan cheese with a box grater, preserve 1/4 cup of the grated cheese for the garnish. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of Italian basil. Once the pasta has finished cooking, drain the water, and set it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5f645d8afba58f6f2a2290bb','5f6459dbfba58f6f2a2290b9',4,'M1: Cook Chicken','To make Creamy Chicken and Garlic Pasta, in a pan heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil for 1 minute. Once warm, add the marinated chicken pieces and cook them for 10 - 15 minutes until they become golden brown. Once this is done, set the chicken aside, and move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":10,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f645e96ae3cb6df54f6d476','5f6459dbfba58f6f2a2290b9',5,'M2: Make Creamy Sauce','Next, to make Creamy Chicken and Garlic Pasta, heat 2 tablespoons of butter in a pan on a medium flame for 1 minute or until its melts. Then, add 1 tablespoon of chopped garlic and saute for 2 - 3 minutes. Once the garlic is golden add 1 tablespoon of all-purpose flour and mix well. Next, reduce the flame to low and add 1/2 cup of fresh cream, 1/2 teaspoon of salt, 1/4 teaspoon of black pepper powder, and 1/2 cup of parmesan cheese. Mix this well.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5f645ec53a5ec6d73102e0e9','5f6459dbfba58f6f2a2290b9',6,'M3: Add Cooked Pasta','For Creamy Chicken and Garlic Pasta, once the ingredients have been mixed well, add the cooked chicken and saute this for 3-4 minutes. Then, add the cooked pasta and gently fold it into the creamy sauce. Once combined the dish is ready to serve. Garnish the dish with 2 tablespoons of parmesan cheese and 1/2 tablespoon of chopped basil.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5f646268fba58f6f2a2290bc','5f6461e43a5ec6d73102e0ea',1,'P1: Cook Pasta','Boil the pasta for Pasta in Pumpkin Sauce, first, add 3 cups of water to a saucepan along with a teaspoon of salt. Bring it to a boil over a high flame. As the water comes to a rolling boil, add 1 cup of penne pasta into it and stir it well. Then, boil the pasta over medium-high flame for 9 minutes, until it is firm to the bite. While the pasta is boiling, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":4}'),('5f6462b4ae3cb6df54f6d477','5f6461e43a5ec6d73102e0ea',2,'P2: Prep Ingredients','Next, for Pasta in Pumpkin Sauce, peel 15 cloves of garlic and finely chop 3 cloves to make 1 tablespoon of chopped garlic. Peel and roughly dice 1 cups of pumpkin. Wash and roughly dice 1/4 cup of red capsicum, 1/4 cup of green capsicum, and 1/4 cup of yellow capsicum.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('5f6462efae3cb6df54f6d478','5f6461e43a5ec6d73102e0ea',3,'P3: Prep Ingredients','Next, for Pasta in Pumpkin Sauce, Peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Grate 1.5 tablespoons of processed cheese using a box grater. Grate 1/4 cup of mozzarella cheese with a box grater. Once the pasta is cooked, drain the water, and set it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f6463a8ae3cb6df54f6d479','5f6461e43a5ec6d73102e0ea',4,'M1: Cook Onions and Pumpkin','To make the Pumpkin Sauce, in a pan heat on medium flame, then pour 2 tablespoons of olive oil and add 12 cloves of peeled garlic. Saute this for 1 minute and add 1/4 cup of chopped onions. Cook the onions until they become translucent and slightly brown. Then add 1/2 teaspoon fo salt, 2 teaspoons of all-purpose flour, and mix well. Next, add 1 cups of chopped pumpkin and 1/2 a cup of water. Mix this well and then cover the pan with a lid and let it cook for 15 minutes on a medium flame. While the pumpkin is simmering please move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":15,"flame":3}'),('5f6464273a5ec6d73102e0ec','5f6461e43a5ec6d73102e0ea',5,'M2: Continue Cooking the Pumpkin Sauce','Next, to make Pasta with Pumpkin Sauce, take the lid off the pan and add 1 cup of curd, 1/2 teaspoon red chili powder, 1/2 teaspoon garam masala, 1/2 teaspoon turmeric, 1/2 teaspoon coriander powder, and 1 tablespoon ginger garlic paste. Mix this well, cover the pan with a lid once more, and cook for 5 minutes on a medium flame. While the sauce is simmering please move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":5,"flame":2}'),('5f64646cae3cb6df54f6d47a','5f6461e43a5ec6d73102e0ea',6,'M3: Blend Pumpkin Mixture to Make Sauce','Next, to make Pasta with Pumpkin Sauce, take the lid off the pan and add 1/2 a cup of milk and mix it well. Then, turn off the flame and allow the sauce to cool for about 5 minutes and then transfer it to a blender jar and blend it into a smooth sauce.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f6464c23a5ec6d73102e0ed','5f6461e43a5ec6d73102e0ea',7,'M4: Cook Capsicum','Next, to make Pasta with Pumpkin Sauce, in a pan heat 1 tablespoon of olive oil on a medium flame and add 1 tablespoon of chopped garlic. Saute this for 1 minute, once the garlic has browned add  1/4 cup of red capsicum, 1/4 cup of green capsicum, and 1/4 cup of yellow capsicum. Saute this for 5 - 7 minutes and then add 1/2 teaspoon of salt and the prepared pumkin sauce. Mix this well.','cook_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5f646518fba58f6f2a2290bd','5f6461e43a5ec6d73102e0ea',8,'M5: Final Touches','Then, to make Pasta with Pumpkin Sauce, add 1 teaspoon of dried basil, 1 tablespoon of pasta seasoning, 1.5 tablespoons of precessed cheese, and 1/4 cup of mozzarella cheese. Mix this well and once these ingredients have incorporated well add the cooked pasta. Gently mix this and cook for 4 -5 minutes. After this, the dish is ready to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5f64676bae3cb6df54f6d47c','5f64671cae3cb6df54f6d47b',1,'P1: Cook Pasta','Boil the pasta for Shrimp and Spinach Pasta, first, add 3 cups of water to a saucepan along with 1/2 a teaspoon of salt and 1 teaspoon of oil. Bring it to a boil over a high flame. As the water comes to a rolling boil, add 1 cup of fettuccini pasta into it and stir it well. Then, boil the pasta over medium-high flame for 9 minutes, until it is firm to the bite. While the pasta is boiling, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":4}'),('5f64679bae3cb6df54f6d47d','5f64671cae3cb6df54f6d47b',2,'P2: Prep Shrimp','Next, clean 1 cup of shrimp for Shrimp and Spinach Pasta, First, wash the shrimp in a sieve with cold water and discard any discolored or slimy ones. Then, if your cooking with whole shrimp, pinch the head at the point where it meets the body, and twist and pull the head off. Next, turn the shrimp so that the belly faces you, grab the legs, and pull them up and towards the tail. Remove any legs that may have been left behind. Then, begin to peel off the shell with your hands or a small knife. Next, remove the tail, with a small knife slice the underside of the tail, and then remove it. After that, you need to devein the shrimp, along the back ridge you should see a dark vein. Using a small knife cut into the shrimp along the ridge until you reach the vein and pull it out. Once the vein is out, gently pull until the entire vein is removed. Make sure that no part of the vein is still in the shrimp. Be careful while you do this as shrimp can be quite small. Clean all the shrimp similarly and place them in a bowl.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f6467dfae3cb6df54f6d47e','5f64671cae3cb6df54f6d47b',3,'P3: Prep Other Ingredients','Next, for Shrimp and Spinach Pasta, wash and roughly dice 1/2 cup of tomatoes. Wash and roughly chop 1 cup of spinach leaves. Cut 1 lime in half and then squeeze 1 tablespoon of lime juice. Grate 1/2 cup of parmesan cheese using a box grater. Once the pasta is done cooking, drain the water, and set it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f64681fae3cb6df54f6d47f','5f64671cae3cb6df54f6d47b',4,'M1: Cook Shrimp','To make Shrimp and Spinach Pasta, heat 2 tablespoons of butter in a pan on a medium flame. Then add 1 cup of cleaned shrimp, season them with 1/4 teaspoon of salt, and cook them on each side for 1 - 2 minutes until they are golden brown. Shrimp cook quickly so keep an eye on them. Once they are cooked place them on a plate with an absorbent paper and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5f64726dae3cb6df54f6d483','5e2263124f28558c29df642f',4,'M2: Pressure cook the sambar. Garnish & serve','Next, add 1 tbsp of sambar powder, mix well. Next, add 1/4 cup of tomatoes, 1/2 tsp of salt, 1/2 cup of water, and mix well. To this, add the prepared coconut paste, mix well, and then add 1/2 cup of water. Once the saaru comes to a boil close the lid of the cooker and cook this on high flame for 1 min and then on low flame for 5 mins. Once this is done, allow the pressure to release naturally before you take off the lid. After the saaru has cooked, garnish it with 1 tbsp of coriander leaves and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f6473e7ae3cb6df54f6d484','5f64671cae3cb6df54f6d47b',5,'M2: Cook Garlic and Tomatoes','Next, to make Shrimp and Spinach Pasta, heat 1 tablespoon of olive oil and 2 tablespoons of butter in a pan on medium flame. Once warm, add 1 teaspoon of garlic paste and saute for 1 minute. Next, add 1/2 cup of chopped tomatoes and cook for 5 - 7 minutes on medium heat, stirring occasionally.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":5,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f647576fba58f6f2a2290c1','5f64671cae3cb6df54f6d47b',6,'M3: Cook Spinach Leaves','Next, to make Shrimp and Spinach Pasta, once the tomatoes are tender add 1 cup of chopped spinach leaves and mix well. Cook this for 3 - 5 minutes on a medium flame, stirring occasionally. Then, add 1/2 teaspoon of salt, 1/2 teaspoon 0f black pepper powder, 1/2 teaspoon of chilli flakes, and mix well. Next, add the cooked shrimp and mix it in. Then add the cooked pasta and gently mix everything together. Cook this on a medium flame for 3 - 5 minutes, stirring occasionally.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":6,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5f6475fffba58f6f2a2290c2','5f64671cae3cb6df54f6d47b',7,'M4: Final Touches','For Shrimp and Spinach Pasta, add 1 tablespoon of lime juice and 1/2 cup of grated parmesan cheese. Mix this well and cook for 3 - 5 minutes on a medium flame, stirring occasionally. Once this is done, the dish is ready to serve. Garnish this pasta with 1 tablespoon of parmesan cheese.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":3,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f647cdbae3cb6df54f6d488','5e2554b4057fd3f6fc80eec2',4,'M2: Simmer the vegetables with masala. Garnish & Serve','Then add, 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder, 1/2 tsp of salt, and saute for 1 min. Next, add 1/2 cup of boiled potatoes, 1/2 cup of boiled cauliflower, 1/4 cup of green peas and mix well. To this, add 1 tsp of red chili powder, 1 tsp of coriander powder, 1 tsp of dry mango powder, 1 tsp of cumin powder, and mix well. Let this cook for 10 mins, stirring occasionally. Once this is done, garnish with 1 tbsp of coriander leaves and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5f68470d3a5ec6d73102e0f7','5f6846e23a5ec6d73102e0f6',1,'P1: Cook Pasta','Boil the pasta for Spaghetti with Chicken Meatballs, first, add 3 cups of water to a saucepan along with a teaspoon of salt. Bring it to a boil over a high flame. As the water comes to a rolling boil, add 1 cup of spaghetti pasta into it and stir it well. Then, boil the pasta over medium-high flame for 9 minutes, until it is firm to the bite. While the pasta is boiling, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":4}'),('5f684896ae3cb6df54f6d48b','5f6846e23a5ec6d73102e0f6',2,'P2: Prepare Chicken Meatball Mixture','For Spaghetti with Chicken Meatballs, wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves and 1 tablespoon of green chilli. Next, in a large bowl add 1 cup of minced chicken, 1 tablespoon of ginger paste, 1 tablespoon of garlic paste, 1 teaspoon of salt, 1 teaspoon of red chilli powder, 1/2 teaspoon of cayenne powder, 1 teaspoon of garlic powder, 1 teaspoon of onion powder, 1/4 teaspoon of black pepper powder, 1/2 teaspoon of coriander powder, 1/2 teaspoon of cumin powder, 1 tablespoon of chopped green chillies, 1/4 cup of bread crumbs, and 2 tablespoons of chopped coriander leaves. Combine these ingredients well until it has a dough-like consistency. Once this is ready set it aside and move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f6848c7ae3cb6df54f6d48c','5f6846e23a5ec6d73102e0f6',3,'P3: Chop Ingredients','For Spaghetti with Chicken Meatballs, peel and finely chop 4 tablespoons of garlic and 1/4 cup of onions. Once the pasta is done cooking, drain the water, and set it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f68491ffba58f6f2a2290cc','5f6846e23a5ec6d73102e0f6',4,'M1: Fry Meatballs','Fry the Meatballs for Spaghetti with Chicken Meatballs, in a Kadai heat 1.5 cups of cooking oil on a medium flame. While the oil is heating, shape the meatballs with your hands from the prepared chicken mince mixture, making lemon-sized balls. Once the meatballs are shaped, gently drop them in the hot oil and allow them to fry for 4 -6 minutes, until golden brown. Once they are golden, take them out of the oil and place them on a plate with an absorbent paper. Once all the meatballs are fried set them aside and move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":6,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f684972ae3cb6df54f6d48d','5f6846e23a5ec6d73102e0f6',5,'M2: Cook Garlic and Onions','Next, for Spaghetti with Chicken Meatballs, in a pan heat 2 tablespoons of butter on a medium flame and then add 2 tablespoons of chopped garlic. Saute this for 1 -2 minutes, once the garlic is brown add 1/4 cup of chopped onion. Saute this for 2 -3 minutes, until the onions are translucent. Then, add 1/2 cup of tomato puree, mix well, and cook this for 5 - 7 minutes, stirring occasionally.','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}');
INSERT INTO catalog_recipe_steps VALUES
('5f684a62fba58f6f2a2290cd','5f6846e23a5ec6d73102e0f6',6,'M3: Add Seasonings','Next, for Spaghetti with Chicken Meatballs, add, 1/2 teaspoon of salt, 1/2 teaspoon of paprika, 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, and mix well. Then, add 3 tablespoons of tomato ketchup, 1 teaspoon of oregano, and mix well. Cook this for 3-5 minutes on a medium flame, stirring occasionally. Next, add the cooked meatballs to the sauce and cook this for another 3-5 minutes on a medium flame, stirring occasionally. Once this is done, turn off the flame, and set the sauce aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5f684adf3a5ec6d73102e0f8','5f6846e23a5ec6d73102e0f6',7,'M4: Cook the Pasta in Seasoning','For Spaghetti with Chicken Meatballs, heat 2 tablespoons of butter in a fresh pan and then add 2 tablespoons of chopped garlic. Saute this for 1 -2 minutes until the garlic is golden. Then, add the cooked pasta along with 1 teaspoon of salt, 1 teaspoon of chilli flakes, 1 teaspoon of pasta seasoning, 1 teaspoon of oregano, and 1/2 teaspoon of dried basil. Gently mix these ingredients together coating the spaghetti in all the seasonings. Cook this for 3 -5 minutes on a medium flame. Once this is done, on a serving plate, place the seasoned spaghetti and pour the prepare meatball sauce over it and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f684d1bfba58f6f2a2290ce','5f684cd93a5ec6d73102e0f9',1,'P1: Cook Pasta','Boil the pasta for Chicken Pesto Pasta, first, add 3 cups of water to a saucepan along with a teaspoon of salt. Bring it to a boil over a high flame. As the water comes to a rolling boil, add 1 cup of farfalle pasta into it and stir it well. Then, boil the pasta over medium-high flame for 9 minutes, until it is firm to the bite. While the pasta is boiling, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":4}'),('5f684dc5ae3cb6df54f6d48e','5f684cd93a5ec6d73102e0f9',2,'P2: Prep ingredients','To prepare Chicken and Pesto Pasta, clean 1 cup of boneless chicken and chop it into cubes. Wash and chop 3/4 cups of cherry tomatoes into halves. Wash and pick one cup of fresh basil leaves. Peel 4 cloves of garlic. Next, to make the pesto sauce, in a blender jar, add 1 cup of fresh basil leaves, followed by 2 tablespoons of walnuts, 4 cloves of garlic, 1 tablespoon of olive oil, a teaspoon of salt, and half a teaspoon of black pepper powder. Then, blend it into a smooth paste and set it aside. Once the pasta is done cooking, drain the water, and set it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f684fd5ae3cb6df54f6d48f','5f684cd93a5ec6d73102e0f9',3,'M1: Cook the Chicken','To make Chicken Pesto Pasta, heat 2 tablespoons of oil in a pan on a medium flame. Once warm, add 1/2 teaspoon of garlic paste, saute this for 1 minute and then add 1 cup of chicken. Cook the chicken for 5 - 7 minutes until it''s golden brown on each side. Next, add 3/4 cup of chopped cherry tomatoes and gently mix. Cook this for 3 - 5 minutes, until the tomatoes are tender. Once this is done turn off the flame and set the chicken aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5f68503aae3cb6df54f6d490','5f684cd93a5ec6d73102e0f9',4,'M2: Mix Pasta and Sauce','To make Chicken Pesto Pasta, in a large bowl add the cooked pasta, the cooked chicken and tomatoes, and the pesto sauce as required. Gently mix these ingredients together and once it''s combined well the dish is ready to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f685770ae3cb6df54f6d491','5f6853043a5ec6d73102e0fa',1,'P1: Marinate Chicken','For Butter Chicken Pasta, clean 1 cup of chicken breast and then chop it into cubes. Cut a lime in half and squeeze 2 tablespoons of lime juice. Next, in a large bowl, add the chopped chicken, 1/2 cup of yogurt, 1 tablespoon of ginger-garlic paste, 1/2 teaspoon of red chilli powder, 1/2 teaspoon of cumin powder, 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala, 1/2 teaspoon of salt, and 2 tablespoons of lime juice. Mix these ingredients well and let the chicken marinate for 30 minutes. While the chicken is marinating please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":30,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":30,"flame":0}'),('5f685853ae3cb6df54f6d492','5f6853043a5ec6d73102e0fa',2,'P2: Cook the Pasta','Boil the pasta for Butter Chicken Pasta, first, add 3 cups of water to a saucepan along with 1/4 a teaspoon of salt and 1/4 teaspoon of oil. Bring it to a boil over a high flame. As the water comes to a rolling boil, add 1 cup of penne pasta into it and stir it well. Then, boil the pasta over medium-high flame for 9 minutes, until it is firm to the bite. While the pasta is boiling, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":4}'),('5f685886fba58f6f2a2290d0','5f6853043a5ec6d73102e0fa',3,'P3: Chop Ingredients','For Butter Chicken Pasta, wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Once the pasta is done cooking, drain the water, and set the pasta aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('5f6858bfae3cb6df54f6d493','5f6853043a5ec6d73102e0fa',4,'M1: Cook Chicken','To make Butter Chicken Pasta, heat 2 tablespoons of cooking oil in a pan on a medium flame. Then, add the marinated chicken and cook this for 5 - 7 minutes until the chicken is golden brown. Once cooked, set the chicken aside, and move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":5,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('5f68592a3a5ec6d73102e0fb','5f6853043a5ec6d73102e0fa',5,'M2: Cook Onions','Next, to make Butter Chicken Pasta, heat 2 tablespoons of butter in a pan on medium flame. Then, add 1 tablespoon of ginger-garlic paste and 1/4 cup of chopped onions. Saute this for 3 - 5 minutes until the onions are translucent. Next, pour in 1/2 cup of tomato puree, mix it well, and cook this for 5 - 7 minutes on medium flame and stir occasionally.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":7,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f6859893a5ec6d73102e0fc','5f6853043a5ec6d73102e0fa',6,'M3: Add seasonings to the Sauce','To make Butter Chicken Pasta, add 1/2 teaspoon of salt, 1/2 teaspoon of red chilli powder, and 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala to the pan. Mix this well and then add 1/2 cup of water. Saute this and allow it to come to a boil. Then, add the cooked chicken and gently mix the sauce and the chicken. Once combined, add 1/4 cup of fresh cream and mix well. Next, add the cooked pasta and gently fold it into the sauce. Cook this for 3 - 5 minutes on medium flame. After this, the dish is ready to serve, garnish each plate with 1/2 tablespoon of coriander leaves.','cook_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f6b1ca6fba58f6f2a2290e4','5e2808cb4f28558c29df644f',3,'M2: Simmer the poha with vegetables. Garnish & Serve','Then, add 1/2 tsp of turmeric powder, 1.5 cups of poha, 1/4 cup of sweet corn, 1/4 cup of green peas, 3 tbsp of water, and and gently mix all the ingredients together. Next, 1 tsp of salt and mix well, then garnish the poha with 2 tbsp of coriander leaves and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5f6c6b70ae3cb6df54f6d4c7','5e294852057fd3f6fc80ef04',3,'M2: Fry the grated paneer with the masala. Garnish & Serve','Next, add 3/4 cup of tomatoes, 1 cup of grated paneer, and mix well. Saute this for 2 mins on low flame and then garnish with 1 tbsp of coriander leaves. The dish is ready to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5f73040aae3cb6df54f6d4e0','5e2ac0c2985ffca18ae8fb02',4,'M3: Simmer the panner in the gravy. Garnish & Serve','Next, add 1 cup of cubed paneer, cover the pan, and simmer for another 10 mins. After this, garnish the dish with 1 tbsp of corinader leaves, 1/2 tsp of kasuri methi, and 1/4 tsp of garam masala, mix well, and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('5f7452ddfba58f6f2a229108','5e2ac6554f28558c29df647f',3,'M2:  Fry the poha with the potatoes. Garnish& Serve','Next, add 1/4 tsp of mustard seeds, 1/2 tsp of cumin seeds, 1/4 tsp of hing,  7 curry leaves, and let this splutter for a few seconds, Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions and saute this for 2-3 mins. Then, add 1 tbsp of roasted peanuts, and saute for 1 min. Next, season this with 1/2 tsp of salt, and then add 1/4 cup of fried potatoes, mix well. To this, add 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder, 1.5 cups of poha, and gently combine all the ingredients. Once the ingredients are combined well, garnish with 1 tbsp of lime juice and 2 tbsp of coriander leaves, give it a final mix, put the poha in a serving dish and enjoy.','cook_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('5f7d83d8ae3cb6df54f6d518','5e2ad66d4f28558c29df648c',4,'M2: Simmer the khichdi with spinach. Garnish & Serve','Next, 1/2 cup of tomatoes, and saute for 3-4 mins. After that, add the prepared spinach puree and mix well. Allow this to cook for 4 mins and then add the cooked rice and dal along with 1/2 cup of water and 1/2 tsp of salt. Combine all the ingredients well and adjust the consistency if necessary. Let the khichdi simmer for 5 mins and then it is ready to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('5f8944463a5ec6d73102e1b8','5e31856a4f28558c29df64d2',3,'M2:  Add the masala powder. Garnish & Serve','After simmering the tambdi bhaji, take off the lid and add the prepared masala powder. Mix it well and saute the bhaji for 2 mins. Once the ingredients are combined well, put the bhaji in a serving dish and enjoy.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6040a568fba58f6f2a229482','6040a4f1cf76b8674a2e9e50',1,'ap1-Soak the Chana','To soak the chana for make Bengalgram salad, first, take a bowl and 2 cups of water in it, then soak half a cup of whole black Bengal gram in the water for 8 hrs. While the chana is soaking, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":480,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6040a601cf76b8674a2e9e51','6040a4f1cf76b8674a2e9e50',2,'p1-Boil the Chana','To boil the chana for Bengalgram salad, add the soaked chana to a pressure cooker along with 2 cups of water. Add half a tsp of salt and cover the cooker with the lid. Then, pressure cook the chana over a high flame until three whistles. After the third whistle, reduce the flame to low and allow it to cook for another 5 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the chana is boiling, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":18,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('6040a684cf76b8674a2e9e52','6040a4f1cf76b8674a2e9e50',3,'p2-Prep the Ingredients','To prep, the ingredients for Bengalgram salad, wash and finely chop 0.5 cups of tomatoes. Wash, peel, and finely chop 1/4 cup English cucumber. Wash and finely chop 1 tbsp coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6040a721fba58f6f2a229483','6040a4f1cf76b8674a2e9e50',4,'M1- Assemble the salad. Garnish & Serve','To make Bengalgram salad, first, strain the boiled chana after the pressure cooker cools down, and add it to a mixing bowl. Next, add half a cup of chopped tomatoes, 1/4 cup of chopped cucumber, and half a teaspoon of red chili powder. Season the salad with half a teaspoon of salt. Add 0.5 tbsp finely chopped coriander leaves, followed by 1 teaspoon of lemon juice, and give it a good mix. Garnish the salad with 0.5 tbsp chopped coriander leaves and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6040afc63a5ec6d73102e554','6040a808fba58f6f2a229484',1,'ap1- Prepare the peri-peri marinade for the chicken','To prepare the marinade for Peri-Peri chicken salad, first, wash, peel and roughly chop a 1-inch piece of ginger. Peel 2 cloves of garlic and roughly chop it. Next, to prepare the peri masala, in a blender jar, add a 1-inch piece of chopped ginger followed by 2 cloves of chopped garlic. Next, add half a teaspoon of turmeric powder, half a teaspoon of white wine vinegar,  half a teaspoon of oregano, half a teaspoon of black pepper powder, half a teaspoon of cumin powder, 2 nos green cardamom, and 2 nos cloves. Add half a teaspoon of cinnamon powder, half a teaspoon of coriander seeds, a teaspoon of cooking oil, and 2 nos dry red chilies. Then, cover the jar with a lid and blend it well into a smooth paste.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6040b46acf76b8674a2e9e53','6040a808fba58f6f2a229484',2,'ap2-Marinate the chicken','To marinate the chicken for Peri Peri Chicken Salad, first, rinse and clean 200 grams of the boneless chicken breast with water. Next, add the prepared peri- peri marinade to the chicken along with a teaspoon of oil and rub it well on both sides of the chicken breast. Then, allow it to refrigerate for 8 hours. While the chicken marinates, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6040b4de3a5ec6d73102e555','6040a808fba58f6f2a229484',3,'p1-boil the sweet potato','For Peri Peri Chicken Salad, first, rinse half a cup of black masoor dal with water and soak it in 2 cups of water for 15 minutes. Next, to boil the sweet potato, wash a medium-sized sweet potato well with water and add it to a pressure cooker along with 2 cups of water. Cover the cooker with a lid and pressure cook it over high flame until one whistle. After that, reduce the flame to low and allow it to cook for another 5 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the sweet potato is boiling and dal is soaking please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('6040b5773a5ec6d73102e556','6040a808fba58f6f2a229484',4,'p2- Prep the igredients','To prep, the ingredients for Peri Peri Chicken Salad, wash, peel and dice half a cup of mangoes. Wash, and dice half a cup of English cucumber into triangles. Wash and cut 1/4 cup of cherry tomatoes into halves. Roughly slice a tablespoon of black pitted olives. into halves. Peel and finely chop 2 cloves of garlic. Wash and pick a tablespoon of mint leaves. Wash and finely chop a tablespoon of parsley. Next, after boiling the sweet potato, remove it on a plate and carefully peel off the skin. Then, roughly dice it and add it to a blender jar and blend it well into a smooth puree.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6040b5f03a5ec6d73102e557','6040a808fba58f6f2a229484',5,'p3- Boil the dal','To boil the dal for Peri Peri Chicken Salad, add in 3 cups water to a deep bottom pan followed by a 1/4 teaspoon of salt. Mix it well and bring the water to a boil. Then, add half a cup of soaked masoor dal and cover it with a lid. Simmer the dal over medium flame for 8-10 minutes until tender. Make sure to cook the dal only till it is firm to the bite, avoid overcooking it. After that, turn off the flame and strain the boiled dal into a bowl and set it aside. While the dal is boiling, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6040b6863a5ec6d73102e558','6040a808fba58f6f2a229484',6,'p4- Prep the greens and dry roast the cashews','For Peri Peri Chicken Salad, wash and pat dry 1/4 cup of iceberg lettuce and then roughly tear it. Next, wash and pat dry 1/4 cup of leaf lettuce. Then, roughly shred the lettuce. Wash and pat dry 1/4 cup of lolo roso and roughly shred it. Wash, pat dry and roughly shred 1/4 cup of red cabbage. Next, to roast the cashew nuts, heat up a pan over medium flame for a minute. Then, add a tablespoon of cashew nuts and dry roast it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until it turns crisp and golden brown. After that, turn off the flame and take it out in a bowl, and set it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6040b6eefba58f6f2a229485','6040a808fba58f6f2a229484',7,'m1- grill the chicken','To grill the chicken for Peri Peri Chicken Salad, add a teaspoon of cooking oil over a grill pan and heat it for a minute. Next, place the marinated chicken breast onto the pan and cook it for 2-3 minutes on each side. Flip and cook the chicken until it is evenly cooked and browned on both sides. Then, turn off the flame and remove it on a plate. Allow the chicken to cool for some time then cut it into dices.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6040b7adcf76b8674a2e9e54','6040a808fba58f6f2a229484',8,'m2- prepare the dressing','To prepare the chili-lime dressing for the Peri Peri Chicken Salad, in a blender jar, add a tablespoon of salad oil, a teaspoon of dijon mustard, 2 cloves of chopped garlic, half a teaspoon of white wine vinegar, and a tablespoon of lime juice. Next, add in 1/4 cup of the prepared sweet potato paste followed by 2 tablespoons of water and blend it well into a smooth paste. Then, pour the dressing into a bowl. Add a teaspoon of oregano followed by half a teaspoon of salt and half a teaspoon of black pepper powder. Add a tablespoon of chopped parsley along with 2 nos chopped red chilies and mix it well.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('6040b846fba58f6f2a229486','6040a808fba58f6f2a229484',9,'m3- Assemble the salad. Garnish & Serve','To assemble the Peri Peri Chicken Salad, first, in a mixing bowl add 1/4 cup of diced cucumber, 1/4 cup of cherry tomatoes, 1/4 cup of red cabbage, 2 teaspoons of chopped jalapeno, and mix it well. Next, over a salad plate, lay out 1/4 cup of shredded lolo roso, iceberg, and leaf lettuce. Top it up with the boiled masoor dal and the mixed vegetables.  Add half a cup of diced mangoes followed by the diced grilled chicken. Pour the prepared dressing on top and garnish it with a tablespoon of roasted cashews and mint leaves. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6040e13b3a5ec6d73102e55a','6040df9b3a5ec6d73102e559',1,'ap1- prep the ingredients & marinate paneer','For peri peri paneer salad, Cut 1 cup of paneer into medium cubes. Then, peel 2 cloves of garlic and finely chop them. To prepare the peri peri marinade,in a blender jar, add a 1-inch piece of chopped ginger followed by 2 cloves of chopped garlic. Next, add half a teaspoon of turmeric powder, half a teaspoon of white wine vinegar,  half a teaspoon of oregano, half a teaspoon of black pepper powder, half a teaspoon of cumin powder, 2 nos green cardamom, and 2 nos cloves. Add half a teaspoon of cinnamon powder, half a teaspoon of coriander seeds, a teaspoon of cooking oil, and 2 nos dry red chilies. Then, cover the jar with a lid and blend it well into a smooth paste. Next, in a bowl, add 1 cup of cubed paneer. Add in the prepared marinade followed by a 1/4 teaspoon of salt and half a teaspoon of oil and coat the paneer slices well with the marinade then refrigerate it for 8hrs. While the paneer marinates, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6040e1dfcf76b8674a2e9e55','6040df9b3a5ec6d73102e559',2,'p1- soak masoor dal & boil sweet potato','For Peri Peri Paneer Salad, first, rinse half a cup of black masoor dal with water and soak it in 2 cups of water for 15 minutes. Next, to boil the sweet potato, wash a medium sized sweet potato well with water and add it to a pressure cooker along with 2 cups of water. Cover the cooker with a lid and pressure cook it over high flame until one whistle. After that, reduce the flame to low and allow it to cook for another 5 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the sweet potato is boiling and dal is soaking please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6040e261cf76b8674a2e9e56','6040df9b3a5ec6d73102e559',3,'p2- prep the ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Peri Peri Paneer Salad, wash, peel and dice half a cup of mangoes. Wash, and dice half a cup of english cucumber into triangles. Wash and cut 1/4 cup of cherry tomatoes into halves. Roughly slice a tablespoon of black pitted olives. into halves. Peel and finely chop 2 cloves of garlic. Wash and pick a tablespoon of mint leaves. Wash and finely chop a tablespoon of parsley. Next, after boiling the sweet potato, remove it on a plate and carefully peel off the skin. Then, roughly dice it and add it to a blender jar and blend it well into a smooth puree.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6040e2983a5ec6d73102e55b','6040df9b3a5ec6d73102e559',4,'p3- boil the dal','To boil the dal for Peri Peri Paneer Salad, add in 3 cups water to a deep bottom pan followed by a 1/4 teaspoon of salt. Mix it well and bring the water to a boil. Then, add half a cup of soaked masoor dal and cover it with a lid. Simmer the dal over medium flame for 8-10 minutes until tender. Make sure to cook the dal only till it is firm to the bite, avoid overcooking it. After that, turn off the flame and strain the boiled dal into a bowl and set it aside. While the dal is boiling, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('6040e2fbcf76b8674a2e9e57','6040df9b3a5ec6d73102e559',5,'p4- prep the greens','For Peri Peri Paneer Salad, wash and pat dry 1/4 cup of iceberg lettuce and then roughly tear it. Next, wash and pat dry 1/4 cup of leaf lettuce. Then, roughly shred the lettuce. Wash and pat dry 1/4 cup of lolo roso and roughly shred it. Wash, pat dry and roughly shred 1/4 cup of red cabbage. Next, to roast the cashew nuts, heat up a pan over medium flame for a minute. Then, add a tablespoon of cashew nuts and dry roast it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until it turns crisp and golden brown. After that, turn off the flame and take it out in a bowl and set it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6040e33b3a5ec6d73102e55c','6040df9b3a5ec6d73102e559',6,'m1- grill the paneer','To grill the paneer for Peri Peri Paneer Salad, add a teaspoon of cooking oil over a grill pan and heat it for a minute. Next, place the marinated paneer onto the pan and cook it for 2-3 minutes on each side. Flip and cook the panner until it is evenly browned on all sides. Then, turn off the flame and remove it on a plate. Allow the paneer to cool for some time then cut it into dices.','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6040e3cdcf76b8674a2e9e58','6040df9b3a5ec6d73102e559',7,'m2- prepare the dressing','To prepare the chili-lime dressing for the Peri Peri Paneer Salad, in a blender jar, add a tablespoon of salad oil, a teaspoon of dijon mustard, 2 cloves of chopped garlic, half a teaspoon of white wine vinegar, and a tablespoon of lime juice. Next, add in 1/4 cup of the prepared sweet potato paste followed by 2 tablespoons of water and blend it well into a smooth paste. Then, pour the dressing into a bowl. Add a teaspoon of oregano followed by half a teaspoon of salt and half a teaspoon of black pepper powder. Add a tablespoon of chopped parsley along with 2 nos chopped red chilies and mix it well.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6040e4123a5ec6d73102e55d','6040df9b3a5ec6d73102e559',8,'m3- assemble the salad. Garnish & serve','To assemble the Peri Peri Paneer Salad, first, in a mixing bowl add 1/4 cup of diced cucumber, 1/4 cup of cherry tomatoes, 1/4 cup of red cabbage, 2 teaspoons of chopped jalapeno, and mix it well. Next, over a salad plate, layout 1/4 cup of shredded lolo roso, iceberg, and leaf lettuce. Top it up with the boiled masoor dal and the mixed vegetables.  Add half a cup of diced mangoes followed by the diced grilled paneer. Pour the prepared dressing on top and garnish it with a tablespoon of roasted cashews and mint leaves. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6041be3dfba58f6f2a229487','6041bde6cf76b8674a2e9e5a',1,'ap1- soak the rajma & chana','For Chickpea patty & green beans salad, in a bowl add 1/4 cup of Kashmiri rajma and soak it in 2 cups of water for 8 hours. Next, in a separate bowl, add 1/4 cup of black chana and soak it in 2 cups of water for 8 hours. While the beans and chana are soaking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":360,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('6041be77fba58f6f2a229488','6041bde6cf76b8674a2e9e5a',2,'ap2- Make the hung curd','To make the hung curd for Chickpea patty & green beans salad, place a sieve over a large mixing bowl and cover it with a muslin cloth as shown. Next, pour 1 cup of fresh curd into the muslin cloth and tie it tightly, tucking the curd inside. Then, carefully place the tied curd over the sieve and refrigerate it for 2 hours. This will allow the excess water to drain off from the curd, leaving the hung curd thick and creamy. While the curd is refrigerating, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":120,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6041beaf3a5ec6d73102e55e','6041bde6cf76b8674a2e9e5a',3,'p1- boil the kidney beans','To boil the kidney beans for Chickpea patty & green beans salad, add 1/4 cup of soaked kidney beans to a pressure cooker along with 1/4 teaspoon of salt and 2 cups of water. Cover it with a lid and pressure cook the beans over a high flame until three whistles. After that, allow it to cook over low flame for 8 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and strain the boiled rajma in a bowl. Then, mash it well and set it aside. While the kidney beans are boiling, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":18,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6041bef43a5ec6d73102e55f','6041bde6cf76b8674a2e9e5a',4,'p2- boil the black grams','To boil the black grams for Chickpea patty & green beans salad, add 1/4 cup of soaked black chana to a pressure cooker along with 1/4 teaspoon of salt and 2 cups of water. Cover it with a lid and pressure cook the beans over a high flame until three whistles. After that, allow it to cook over low flame for 5 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and strain the boiled chana in a bowl. Then, mash it well and set it aside. While the chana is boiling, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6041bf3dcf76b8674a2e9e5b','6041bde6cf76b8674a2e9e5a',5,'p3- blanch the beans','To blanch the beans for Chickpea patty & green beans salad, first, wash and cut 3/4 cup of haricot beans into 2-inch long pieces. Next, boil 2 cups of water with 1/4 teaspoon of salt in a pan over medium flame. As the water comes to a boil, add 3/4 cup of chopped haricot beans and let it boil for 3-4 minutes over medium flame. Then, turn off the flame and drain off the water from the blanched beans and soak them in an ice bath for 2 minutes. After that, strain the beans in a bowl and set them aside. While the beans are blanching, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6041bf793a5ec6d73102e560','6041bde6cf76b8674a2e9e5a',6,'p4- boil the sweet potato','To boil the sweet potato for Chickpea patty & green beans salad, wash a medium sized sweet potato well with water and add it to a pressure cooker along with 2 cups of water. Cover the cooker with a lid and pressure cook it over high flame until one whistle. After that, reduce the flame to low and allow it to cook for another 5 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. After that, take out the boiled sweet potato from the cooker and gently peel off the skin and mash it well using a fork. While the sweet potato is boiling please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('6041bfd6cf76b8674a2e9e5c','6041bde6cf76b8674a2e9e5a',7,'p5- roast the beans','To roast the beans for Chickpea patty & green beans salad, add the blanched beans to a glass dish or bowl. Add 1/4 teaspoon of salt, 1/4 teaspoon of black pepper powder, and half a teaspoon of cooking oil to the beans and mix it well. Then, set it inside the oven and roast the beans at 160 degrees C for 7 minutes. While the beans are roasting, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":7,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6041c0693a5ec6d73102e561','6041bde6cf76b8674a2e9e5a',8,'p6- prep the ingredients','For Chickpea patty & green beans salad, wash and finely chop a tablespoon of mint leaves. Wash and finely chop a tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash and finely chop a tablespoon of parsley. Wash, pat dry and roughly shred 1/4 cup of iceberg lettuce. Wash, pat dry and roughly shred 1/4 cup of leaf lettuce. Wash, pat dry and roughly shred 1/4 cup of lolo roso lettuce. Wash and dice 1/4 cup of green capsicum. Wash and dice 1/4 cup of yellow bell pepper. Wash and dice 1/4 cup of red bell pepper. Next, add in the chopped mixed bell peppers to a mixing bowl and season it with a 1/4 teaspoon of salt and 1/4 teaspoon of black pepper powder. Mix it well and set it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6041c11cfba58f6f2a229489','6041bde6cf76b8674a2e9e5a',9,'p7- prepare the patty mixture & shape the patties','To prepare the patty mixture for Chickpea patty & green beans salad, in a large bowl, add the mashed boiled rajma followed by mashed boiled black chana and 1/4 cup of mashed boiled sweet potato. Add half a teaspoon of paprika, a teaspoon of cumin powder, half a teaspoon of salt, and a teaspoon of coconut oil. Add a teaspoon of chopped mint leaves and a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves. Mix it well and prepare a dough-like mixture. Then, divide it into equal portions and shape them into round flat patties as shown.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6041c15fcf76b8674a2e9e5d','6041bde6cf76b8674a2e9e5a',10,'m1- Grill the chickpea patties','To make the chickpea patties for Chickpea patty & green beans salad, grease the grill pan with a tablespoon of cooking oil and heat it up for a minute. Then, place the prepared patties onto the pan and grill them on each side for 2-3 minutes until evenly browned. After that, turn off the flame and remove the patties onto a plate.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6041c1c8fba58f6f2a22948a','6041bde6cf76b8674a2e9e5a',11,'m2- make the tahina sauce','To make the Tahina sauce for Chickpea patty & green beans salad, add 1/4 cup of hung curd to a bowl. Add in 1/4 teaspoon of black pepper powder, 1/4 teaspoon of salt, and a tablespoon of chopped parsley followed by 2 teaspoons of chopped mint leaves. Add 2 teaspoons of tahini along with 2 tablespoons of water and mix it well. Add half a teaspoon of garlic paste and mix it well to prepare the sauce.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('6041c234fba58f6f2a22948b','6041bde6cf76b8674a2e9e5a',12,'m3- Assemble the salad. Garnish & Serve','To assemble the Chickpea patty & green beans salad, layer the salad bowl with 1/4 cup of chopped iceberg, lollo rosso, and green lettuce. Top it with the marinated bell peppers, roasted beans, and chickpea patties. Garnish the salad with roasted peanuts, pumpkin seeds, sunflower seeds and sesame seeds. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6041c5a43a5ec6d73102e562','6041c54acf76b8674a2e9e5e',1,'ap1- soak sun dried tomatoes','For Feta Cheese Greek Salad, in a bowl, add 1 cup of water and soak 0.25 sun-dried tomatoes in the water. Then allow it to refrigerate for 8hrs. While it is soaking, please move to th next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":480,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6041c6183a5ec6d73102e563','6041c54acf76b8674a2e9e5e',2,'p1- knead dough for wheat chips','To knead the dough for Feta Cheese Greek Salad,  in a large bowl, add 0.5 cup wheat flour, 0.5 tsp salt, 1 tsp curd,  1/4 cup of water, 1 tsp oil and knead it into a smooth dough. Divide the whole wheat Chips dough into lemon-sized balls. cover it and keep it aside','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6041c688cf76b8674a2e9e5f','6041c54acf76b8674a2e9e5e',3,'p2- prep the ingredients for mirepoix','For Feta Cheese Greek Salad, peel and finely chop 0.25 cup onion; peel and finely chop 1 clove garlic; wash and finely chop 1 stalk leek; wash and finely chop 1 stalk celery; wash, peel and finely chop 0.5 cup carrot.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6041c6fd3a5ec6d73102e564','6041c54acf76b8674a2e9e5e',4,'p3- prep the ingredients','For Feta Cheese Greek Salad, wash and cut 0.25 cup English cucumber into triangles; wash and cut 0.25 cup red bell pepper into half, remove the seeds and cut the bell pepper into triangles; wash and cut 0.25 cups yellow bell pepper into half, remove the seeds and cut the bell pepper into triangles; cut 1 tbsp green pitted olives into half; cut 1 tbsp black pitted olives into half and keep aside','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('6041c7543a5ec6d73102e565','6041c54acf76b8674a2e9e5e',5,'p4- prep the greens','For Feta Cheese Greek Salad, wash and cut 0.5 cup Iceberg lettuces and pat dry using a kitchen towel or a lettuce dryer; wash 0.5 cup leaf lettuce and pat dry using a kitchen towel; wash 0.5 cup lolo roso lettuce and pat dry using a kitchen towel; wash 1/4 cup rocket lettuce and pat dry using a kitchen towel. Now roughly tear the different types of lettuce and keep them aside. Wash and pluck 1 tbsp mint leaves','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6041c7b1fba58f6f2a22948c','6041c54acf76b8674a2e9e5e',6,'m1- make whole wheat chips','To make the whole wheat chips, heat a tawa on low flame. Next, take the prepared dough ball and with the help of a rolling pin, flatten the dough ball and roll it into a round shape, place it on the hot tawa and cook on both sides for 1 min or until brown spots appear on them. After that, remove these wheat chips to a sandwich griller and grill it for a min on medium heat or until it becomes crisp. Then break them into small pieces and keep aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6041c826fba58f6f2a22948d','6041c54acf76b8674a2e9e5e',7,'m2- boil & puree sweet potato','To make feta cheese greek salad, in a pan heat 3 cups water and add a medium sized of sweet potato. Boil the potatoes on a medium flame for 8mins or until soft. then roughly chop them and add them in a blender jar, and blitz it into a puree. While the water is boiling, move towards the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6041c8a6fba58f6f2a22948e','6041c54acf76b8674a2e9e5e',8,'m3- Make the mirepoix','To make the mirepoix, heat 1 tsp of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Next, add 0.5 cups chopped onion, saute it on a medium flame for a min until translucent. Then, add 1 clove chopped garlic, add 1 stalk chopped celery, add 0.5 stalk chopped leeks, add 0.5 cups chopped carrot and 0.5 tsp thyme and saute it for 2-3 mins over medium flame until the vegetables are tender-crisp. Then, turn off the flame and remove the mirepoix in a bowl and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6041c956cf76b8674a2e9e60','6041c54acf76b8674a2e9e5e',9,'m4- make lemon couscous','To prepare the lemon couscous for the salad, take a pan and heat 3/4 cup of water in it, and allow it to boil. While the water is boiling- add the prepared mirepoix, add 0.5 tsp pepper powder, add 0.5 tsp salt, 0.5 tsp lemon zest, add 1 tablespoon couscous and mix it well. Then add the hot water, cover it with a lid and keep aside for 5mins, while the couscous is resting move towards the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('6041c9b13a5ec6d73102e566','6041c54acf76b8674a2e9e5e',10,'m5- Make the dressing','To make the vinaigrette, take a blender jar and add 2 tbsp salad oil, add 0.5 tsp salt, add 0.5 tsp pepper powder, add 0.5 tsp oregano herbs, add 1 clove minced garlic, add 1 tsp lemon juice, and the boiled sweet potato puree along with 2 tbsp water. Now blitz it into a fine paste and keep aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6041ca43fba58f6f2a22948f','6041c54acf76b8674a2e9e5e',11,'m6- Assemble the salad. Garnish & serve','To assemble the salad, take a salad bowl and place the roughly torn lettuce mix to form the base, then add lemon couscous and top it with English cucumber triangles, red bell pepper triangles, yellow bell pepper triangles, green pitted olives, black pitted olives. Garnish it with whole wheat chips, soaked sun-dried tomatoes, 4 tsp feta cheese, 1 tsp sunflower seeds, and mint leaves. Serve along with the prepared dressing','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6041cd45fba58f6f2a229491','6041cc9dfba58f6f2a229490',1,'p1- marinate & roast the chicken','For Roasted pepper and sliced grilled chicken salad, peel and finely chop 1 teaspoon of garlic; wash and grate lemon to get 0.5 tsp lemon zest. Next, to marinate the chicken, rinse and clean 200 gms of chicken breast and place it in a glass dish. Then add 0.5 tsp salt; add 0.5 tsp pepper powder, add 0.5 tsp thyme, add 1 tsp dijon mustard paste, add 0.5 tsp lime zest, add a teaspoon of minced garlic and rub it well on the meat such that it is evenly coated with the marinade. Then, set it inside the oven and bake it at 160 degrees C for 6 minutes. While the chicken is baking, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6041cddfcf76b8674a2e9e61','6041cc9dfba58f6f2a229490',2,'p2- marinate the roast the bell peppers','For Roasted pepper and sliced grilled chicken salad, wash 1/4 cup red bell pepper, and cut it into half, remove the seeds and cut the bell pepper into triangles, wash 1/4 cup yellow bell peppers and cut it into half, remove the seeds and cut the bell peppers into triangles; wash 1/4 cup green capsicum, cut the capsicum into half and remove the seeds, cut the capsicum into triangles. Take a mixing bowl and add the bell pepper triangles, add 0.5 tsp salt, add 0.5 tsp pepper powder, add 0.5 tsp oregano herbs and mix it well. Then arrange the marinated peppers and roast them for 20mins at 180 degrees celsius. While the peppers are being roasted, move towards the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6041cebf3a5ec6d73102e567','6041cc9dfba58f6f2a229490',3,'p3- prep the ingredients','For roasted pepper and sliced grilled chicken salad, wash 0.5 cup English cucumber and cut them into triangles; wash and cut 1 /4 cup of cherry tomatoes into half; wash and finely chop 1 tbsp parsley leaves. Wash and pat dry 1/4 cup iceberg lettuce using a kitchen towel or a lettuce dryer; wash and pat dry 1/4 cup leaf lettuce; wash and pat dry 1/4 cup lolo roso lettuce; wash and pat dry 1/4 cup of rocket lettuce. Make sure the lettuce leaves are completely dry or the dressing will not stick to the lettuce leaves','prep_method','{"active_time":16,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('6041d01ccf76b8674a2e9e62','6041cc9dfba58f6f2a229490',4,'p4- boil & puree sweet potato','For roasted pepper and sliced grilled chicken salad, take a heavy bottom pan and add 3 glasses of water in it, 0.5 tsp salt, and 1/4 cup sweet potato and allow it to boil on a medium flame for 6mins or until it is soft. Then turn off the flame and allow it to slightly cool. Then peel off the skin, add it to the blender, and blitz it into a smooth puree. While the sweet potato is boiling, Take a pan and add 2 tsp flax seeds, and dry roast it on a medium flame for 2 mins until it turns golden brown. Turn off the flame and keep aside','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":4,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6041d0e03a5ec6d73102e568','6041cc9dfba58f6f2a229490',5,'m1-grill the chicken','For roasted pepper and sliced grilled chicken salad, heat a grill pan and grease it with oil, then place the marinated chicken and cook it on both sides on a medium flame for 2mins each or until it turns golden brown. Allow the chicken to slightly cool and then cut them into slices.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6041d157cf76b8674a2e9e63','6041cc9dfba58f6f2a229490',6,'m2- prepare the dressing','To prepare the dressing for roasted pepper and sliced grilled chicken salad, take a blender and add 1 tsp salad oil, add 1 tsp white wine vinegar, add 0.5 tsp salt, add 0.5 tsp pepper powder, add 0.5 tsp dijon mustard paste, add 0.5 tsp chopped parsley, add the sweet potato puree, add 0.5 tsp oregano powder, and blitz it into a smooth paste.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6041d19ecf76b8674a2e9e64','6041cc9dfba58f6f2a229490',7,'m3- Assemble the salad. Garnish & Serve','To assemble the salad, take a salad bowl and place the lettuce mix, then arrange English cucumber triangles, add the roasted bell peppers, add the cut cherry tomatoes. Then arrange the sliced grilled chicken, garnish the salad with 2 tsp feta cheese and 2 tsp roasted flax seeds and rocket leaves.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6041e44bcf76b8674a2e9e65','6041d3f13a5ec6d73102e569',1,'ap1- soak the broken wheat','For American Garden Salad, take a bowl and add 2 cups of water, add1/4 cup broken wheat, and allow it to soak for 8hrs. While it is soaking, please move on to the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":480,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('6041e4befba58f6f2a229493','6041d3f13a5ec6d73102e569',2,'ap2- roast the pineapple','For American Garden Salad, peel 1/3 cup pineapple and cut them into thick slices., or use 1/3 cup of diced pineapple chunks. Then take a baking tray, place the thick pineapple slices and roast them in the oven at 80 degrees celsius for 1hr 20mins. While the pineapple is baking, please move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":80,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6041e53e3a5ec6d73102e56a','6041d3f13a5ec6d73102e569',3,'p1- roast the tomatoes','For American Garden Salad, wash 3/4 cup of tomatoes and cut them into thick wedges, slice 2 cloves garlic, chop 0.5 tsp thyme. Then take a mixing bowl and add the tomato wedges, the sliced garlic, chopped thyme, and mix it well. then take a baking tray and arrange the seasoned tomato wedges with the cut side up and roast it at 180 degrees for 25mins till lightly charred. While the tomatoes are roasting, please move towards the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":25,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6041e5f2fba58f6f2a229494','6041d3f13a5ec6d73102e569',4,'p2- prep the ingredients','For American Garden Salad, wash 1/4 cup green zucchini and cut them into dices; wash 1/4 cup yellow zucchini and cut them into dices; wash 1/3 cup peeled baby corn and cut them into medium size cubes; wash 1/4 cup tomatoes, remove the seeds, and cut them into dices.  wash 1/4 cup red bell pepper and cut it in half, remove the seeds and cut the bell pepper into medium size dices; wash 1/4 cup yellow bell pepper cut it into half, remove the seeds and cut the bell pepper into medium size dices; wash 1/4 cup green capsicum, cut it into half remove the seeds and cut them into medium size dices. Keep aside','prep_method','{"active_time":17,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6041e683fba58f6f2a229495','6041d3f13a5ec6d73102e569',5,'p3- blanch baby corns & prep the greens','To blanch the baby corn for American Green Salad, take a bowl and fill it with 2 cups of cold water, then take a heavy bottom pan and add 2 cups of water in it and bring to boil on medium flame. Next,  add 1/3 cup cut baby corn pieces to the boiling water and remove it within a minute. Then transfer it to the cold water bowl to stop the cooking process and strain it. Next, wash, pat dry, and roughly tear 1/4 cup of  iceberg lettuce; wash, pat dry, and roughly tear 1/4 cup of lolo roso lettuce','prep_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6041e703fba58f6f2a229496','6041d3f13a5ec6d73102e569',6,'m1- cook the broken wheat','For American Garden Salad, take a heavy bottom pan and heat 1 cup of water, add 0.5 tsp turmeric powder, add 0.5 tsp salt, add 0.5 tsp aromat powder, and bring to boil for 4mins then add 0.5 tsp chopped parsley and 1/4 cup of soaked broken wheat. Cover the lid and allow it to cook for 20mins on medium flame. Stir it occasionally to prevent it from sticking to the bottom and burning, While the broken wheat is cooking, Move towards the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('6041e77bfba58f6f2a229497','6041d3f13a5ec6d73102e569',7,'m2- grill the zucchini & baby corns','For American Garden Salad, take a bowl and add the diced yellow zucchini, add the diced green zucchini, add the blanched baby corn, then for the marination add 1 tsp oil, add 0.5 tsp salt, add 0.5 tsp pepper powder and mix it well. Heat a grill pan and add the marinated zucchini and baby corn and place on the grill for 10mins or until slightly charred. After that, remove the vegetables on a plate and set them aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6041e80fcf76b8674a2e9e66','6041d3f13a5ec6d73102e569',8,'m3- season & roast the bell peppers','For American Garden Salad, heat a pan and add medium diced mixed bell pepper, then season it with 0.5 tsp salt, add 0.5 tsp pepper powder, add 0.5 tsp oregano herbs and saute it on a medium flame for 2 mins.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6041e80ffba58f6f2a229498','6041d3f13a5ec6d73102e569',9,'m4- prepare the dressing','For American Garden Salad, take a blender jar and add the roasted tomatoes, add 1 tsp oil, add 2 tsp water, add 1 tsp lemon juice, wash and add 1 tbsp basil leaves and blitz it into a fine paste and keep aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6041e8e2cf76b8674a2e9e67','6041d3f13a5ec6d73102e569',10,'m5- Assemble the salad. Garnish & serve','To assemble the salad, take a salad bowl and place the roughly torn lettuce mix, then add the cooked broken wheat, diced deseeded tomatoes, add the sauteed bell peppers, add grilled zucchini, and baby corn. Then top it with sliced oven-roasted pineapple, and garnish with 1 tsp sunflower seeds and 1 tsp pumpkin seeds. Serve it along with the dressing.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6041ec0efba58f6f2a229499','6041ebd2cf76b8674a2e9e68',1,'ap1- soak the chickpeas','For Fattoush Salad Falafel, add half a cup of chickpeas in a bowl and soak them in 2 cups of water for 8 hours. While the chickpeas are soaking, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":480,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('6041ec52cf76b8674a2e9e69','6041ebd2cf76b8674a2e9e68',2,'p1-boil the chickpeas','To boil the chickpeas for Fattoush Salad Falafel, in a pressure cooker, add the soaked chickpeas along with 3 cups of water and 1/4 teaspoon of salt. Cover the cooker with a lid and pressure cook it until 4 whistles over low flame. After the fourth whistle, reduce the flame to low, and simmer it for another 8mins. Then, Turn off the flame and allow the pressure cooker to release the pressure naturally. After that, remove the lid of the pressure cooker and strain the boiled chickpeas. While the chickpeas are boiling, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6041ece23a5ec6d73102e56b','6041ebd2cf76b8674a2e9e68',3,'p2- boil the sweet potato','To boil the sweet potato for Fattoush Salad Falafel, wash a medium-sized sweet potato and add it to pressure along with 2 cups of water. Cover the cooker with a lid and pressure cook it over a high flame until one whistle. After the first whistle, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook it for another 5 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside to depressurize it naturally. After that, remove the boiled sweet potato on a plate and gently peel off the skin. Then, roughly slice it. While the sweet potato boils, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6041ed84cf76b8674a2e9e6a','6041ebd2cf76b8674a2e9e68',4,'p3- prep the ingredients','For Fattoush Salad Falafel, wash and dice 1/4 cup of green capsicum into triangles, Wash and cut 1/4 cup red bell pepper into a triangle. Wash and cut 1/4 cup yellow bell pepper into triangles. Wash and cut 1/4 cup of cherry tomatoes into halves. Peel and finely chop 2 teaspoons of garlic. Wash and finely chop half a cup of coriander leaves. Wash and finely chop half a of cup mint leaves. Wash and finely chop 1 green chili. Wash and roughly chop half a cup of parsley. Wash and finely chop a teaspoon of basil leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":20,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6041edf63a5ec6d73102e56c','6041ebd2cf76b8674a2e9e68',5,'p4- prep the greens','For Fattoush Salad Falafel, wash and cut half a cup of English cucumber into triangles. Roughly slice 2 tablespoons of black pitted olives into halves. Wash and pat dry 1/4 cup of iceberg lettuce using a kitchen towel or a lettuce dryer. Then roughly shred it. Wash, pat dry and roughly slice 1/4 cup of leaf lettuce. Wash, pat dry and roughly tear 1/4 cup lollo roso lettuce.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6041ee64cf76b8674a2e9e6b','6041ebd2cf76b8674a2e9e68',8,'p5- make the falafel mixture','To prepare the falafel mixture for Fattoush Salad Falafel, add the boiled chickpeas to a blender jar followed by half a cup of chopped parsley,1 chopped green chili, and a teaspoon of chopped garlic. Next, add half a teaspoon of salt, half a teaspoon of cumin powder, half a cup of chopped coriander leaves, half a cup of chopped mint leaves, and half a teaspoon of lime zest. Then, cover the jar with the lid blend it into a coarse paste.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('6041f186cf76b8674a2e9e6c','6041ebd2cf76b8674a2e9e68',6,'m1- make the croutons','To make the croutons for fattoush salad falafel, first, slice off the brown edges of 4 slices of sandwich bread, then cut the slices into 5mm dices. Next, heat a teaspoon of cooking oil in a pan over a medium flame. Then, add the bread dices and season it with half a teaspoon of black pepper powder. Add in a teaspoon of chopped garlic and toss it over medium flame for 3-4 mins until the bread becomes golden brown and crisp. Then, add half a teaspoon of chopped basil leaves and toss it for another 30 secs. After that, turn off the flame and keep the croutons aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6041f3b5fba58f6f2a22949a','6041ebd2cf76b8674a2e9e68',7,'m2- make the dressing','To make the zatar dressing for fattoush salad falafel, in a blender and add the sweet potato paste, add 1 tsp lemon juice, add 1 tsp dijon mustard paste, add 1 tsp honey, add 1 tsp salad oil, add 1 tsp salt, add 0.5 tsp pepper powder, add 1 tsp zatar powder , and blend it well into a smooth paste.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6041f3f6cf76b8674a2e9e6d','6041ebd2cf76b8674a2e9e68',9,'m3- make the falafels','To make the falafels for Falafel Salad Fattoush, divide the prepared falafel mixture into equal lemon-sized balls and roll them between your palms, then slightly flatten them to prepare the equal sized patties. Then heat a nonstick pan and grease it with 1 tsp oil in it and place the flattened falafel tikkis and sear on each side for 2 minutes or until it becomes slightly brown. Then, turn off the flame and remove the falafels onto a plate.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6041f441cf76b8674a2e9e6e','6041ebd2cf76b8674a2e9e68',10,'m4- Assemble the salad. Garnish & Serve','To assemble the fattoush salad falafel, take a mixing bowl and arrange the mixed lettuce leaves to form the base, then place the English cucumber triangles, add bell pepper triangles, add the halved cherry tomatoes and black pitted olives. Top it with croutons, 8 tsp feta cheese, and the falafel. Serve it along with the zatar dressing','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6041f6aa3a5ec6d73102e56d','6041f60dcf76b8674a2e9e6f',1,'p1- soak the dal & prep the ingredients','For Cucumber Bellpepper and Lentil Salad, first, add half a cup of black masoor dal to a bowl and soak it in 2 cups of water for 15 minutes. While the dal is soaking, wash and dice half a cup of English cucumber. Wash and cut the green capsicum into halves. Then, remove the seeds and finely chop 1/4 cup of the green capsicum. Wash the yellow bell pepper and cut it in half. Remove the seeds and finely chop 1/4 cup of the bell pepper into small dices. Wash and slice red bell pepper it in half, remove the seeds and finely chop 1/4 cup of the bell pepper into small dices. Wash and finely chop 2 green chilies. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of cup coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":18,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('6041f6e5cf76b8674a2e9e70','6041f60dcf76b8674a2e9e6f',2,'p2- boil the dal','To boil the dal for Cucumber Bellpepper and Lentil Salad, add in 3 cups water to a deep bottom pan followed by a 1/4 teaspoon of salt. Mix it well and bring the water to a boil. Then, add half a cup of soaked masoor dal and cover it with a lid. Simmer the dal over medium flame for 8-10 minutes until tender. Make sure to cook the dal only till it is firm to the bite, avoid overcooking it. After that, turn off the flame and strain the boiled dal into a bowl and set it aside. While the dal is boiling, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6041f74efba58f6f2a22949b','6041f60dcf76b8674a2e9e6f',3,'m1- Combine the salad. Garnish & Serve','To make Cucumber Bellpepper and Lentil Salad, first, add in half a cup of diced cucumber to a large mixing bowl. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped red, yellow, and green bell peppers followed by a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and 2 nos green chilies. Add the boiled masoor dal along with half a teaspoon of salt, half a teaspoon of chat masala, half a teaspoon of cumin powder, and half a teaspoon of Kashmiri red chili powder. Next, add a teaspoon of lemon juice, and mix it well. Then, plate the salad in a serving bowl. Garnish it with a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6041fe5acf76b8674a2e9e72','6041fbb0cf76b8674a2e9e71',1,'p1- boil the sweet potato','To boil the sweet potato for Vietnamese veg salad, wash a medium-sized sweet potato and add it to pressure along with 2 cups of water. Cover the cooker with a lid and pressure cook it over a high flame until one whistle. After the first whistle, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook it for another 5 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside to depressurize it naturally. After that, remove the boiled sweet potato on a plate and gently peel off the skin. Then, roughly slice it. While the sweet potato boils, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6041fea53a5ec6d73102e56e','6041fbb0cf76b8674a2e9e71',2,'p2- prep the ingredients','To prep, the ingredients for Vietnamese veg salad, first, cut half a cup of tofu into thick rectangular slices. Then, wash, peel and finely chop 2-inch piece of galangal. Peel, wash, and finely slice half a cup of onions. Peel and finely chop 1 tablespoon of garlic. Wash and finely chop 8 kafir lime leaves. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of lemongrass. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash, pick and finely chop 1 tablespoon of mint leaves. Wash and finely chop 2 fresh red chilies.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6041fef3cf76b8674a2e9e73','6041fbb0cf76b8674a2e9e71',3,'p3- marinate the tofu','To marinate the tofu for Vietnamese veg salad, in a large mixing bowl, add a tablespoon of salad oil followed by a tablespoon of kaffir lime leaves, 1-inch piece of galangal, 2 teaspoons of garlic, and 1 chopped fresh red chili. Next, add in half a teaspoon of salt, a teaspoon of coconut milk powder, 1/4 cup of sliced onions, a teaspoon of aromat powder, a tablespoon of chopped lemongrass, and a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves. Mix it well and add in half a cup of sliced tofu. Coat the tofu slices well with the marinade and set it aside for 15 minutes. While the tofu is marinating, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('6041ff5f3a5ec6d73102e56f','6041fbb0cf76b8674a2e9e71',4,'p4- blanch the beans','To blanch the beans for Vietnamese veg salad, first, wash and cut 10 beans into juliennes. Next, add 2 cups of water to a saucepan along with 1/4 teaspoon of salt and bring it to a rolling boil. Then, add the sliced beans and boil them over medium flame for a minute. After that, turn off the flame and transfer the blanched beans to the cold water to prevent them from cooking further. Soak the beans in cold water for a minute, then remove them in a separate bowl and set them aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6041ffac3a5ec6d73102e570','6041fbb0cf76b8674a2e9e71',5,'p5- prep the ingredients','For Vietnamese veg salad, wash and slice 1/4 cup of cherry tomatoes into halves. Wash and cut 1/2 cup yellow bell pepper into half and remove the seeds, then cut the bell pepper into juliennes. Wash,  peel and cut 1/4 cup of raw mango into juliennes. Peel, wash, and cut 1/4 cup of carrot into juliennes. Wash and cut 1/4 cup of English cucumber into juliennes.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('604200053a5ec6d73102e571','6041fbb0cf76b8674a2e9e71',6,'m1- grill the tofu','To grill the tofu for Vietnamese veg salad, first, heat up a grill pan and grease it with 2 teaspoons of cooking oil. Then, place the marinated tofu onto the pan and cook it evenly on both sides for 1 min. Then, turn off the flame and remove the tofu onto a baking tray. Set it inside the oven and grill the tofu at 180 degrees celsius for 6 mins. While the tofu is being grilled, please move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('604200803a5ec6d73102e572','6041fbb0cf76b8674a2e9e71',7,'m2- make the birista','To make the birista for Vietnamese Veg salad, place 1/4 cup of sliced onions onto a baking tray and drizzle a teaspoon of cooking oil over it. Then, set it inside the oven and roast the onions at 180 degree celsius for 5-6 minutes or until it becomes golden brown and crisp. Alternatively to make the birista on pan, heat a tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan and add the sliced onions. Then, fry the onions over medium-low flame for 6-7 minutes until golden brown and crisp. After that, take it out in a bowl and set aside. While the onions are in the oven, please move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('604200b43a5ec6d73102e573','6041fbb0cf76b8674a2e9e71',8,'m3- make the dressing','To make the Vietnamese dressing for the Vietnamese veg salad, in a blender jar and a teaspoon of chopped garlic, 1 chopped fresh red chili, 2 teaspoons of white vinegar, 2 teaspoons of jaggery, a teaspoon of cooking oil, and 1/4 cup of boiled diced sweet potato. Next, add in half a teaspoon of salt and 1/4 cup of water. Cover the jar with a lid and blend it well into a smooth paste. Transfer the prepared dressing to a bowl and set it aside','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('604200f1fba58f6f2a22949c','6041fbb0cf76b8674a2e9e71',9,'m4- Assemble the salad. Garnish & Serve','To assemble the Vietnamese Veg Salad, in a salad bowl, add 1/4 cup of carrot juliennes, followed by 1/4 cup of julienned cucumber, 1/4 cup of yellow bell pepper juliennes, and 1/4 cup of red bell pepper juliennes. Next, add 1/4 cup of raw mango juliennes, a tablespoon of chopped mint leaves, and the blanched haricot beans. Then, add the prepared Vietnamese dressing and mix it well. Plate the dressed vegetables on a salad platter. Place the sliced grilled tofu on top and garnish it with brown onions and sliced cherry tomatoes. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6045a8bb3a5ec6d73102e57b','6045a8553a5ec6d73102e57a',1,'ap1- roast the apple slices','For Country Garden Salad, first, wash and cut 1 cup Shimla apple into very thin slices. Next, arrange the apple slices onto a baking tray and set it inside the oven. Then, roast them at 180 degrees celsius for 35 mins or until the apple loses all the water and becomes crisp. Then store it in an air-tight container until next use. While the apple slices roast, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":35,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6045a925cf76b8674a2e9e78','6045a8553a5ec6d73102e57a',2,'p1- char the bell peppers','To char, the bell peppers for the country garden salad, wash 1 small red bell pepper and wash 1 small yellow bell pepper. Next, put the roast grill or mesh onto the gas stove and turn on the flame. Then, place the whole bell peppers onto it and allow it to char over direct medium flame for 5-6 mins or until it has a layer of black skin formed around it. Keep rotating the bell peppers for evenly charring. Then, turn off the flame and allow it to cool down for some time. While the bell peppers are being charred and are cooling please move on to the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":7,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6045b8b13a5ec6d73102e57c','6045a8553a5ec6d73102e57a',3,'p2- blanch the beans','To blanch the beans for Country Garden Salad, first, wash and cut 1/4 cup of haricot beans into juliennes. Next, add 2 cups of water to a saucepan along with 1/4 teaspoon of salt and bring it to a rolling boil. Then, add the sliced beans and boil them over medium flame for 3-4 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and transfer the blanched beans to the cold water to prevent them from cooking further. Soak the beans in cold water for a minute, then remove them in a separate bowl and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6045b937cf76b8674a2e9e79','6045a8553a5ec6d73102e57a',4,'p3- prep the ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Country Garden Salad, wash and slice 1/4 cup English cucumber into rondelles. Wash and finely chop a teaspoon of coriander leaves. Wash and cut 1/4 cup of cherry tomatoes into halves. Wash, pat dry and roughly shred 1/4 cup iceberg lettuce. Wash, pat dry and roughly shred 1/4 cup of green lettuce. Wash, pat dry, and roughly tear 1/4 cup of lolo roso lettuce. Wash, pat dry and shred 1/4 cup of  of rocket lettuce.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('6045b9ddcf76b8674a2e9e7a','6045a8553a5ec6d73102e57a',5,'p4- marinate the bell peppers','To marinate the bell peppers for Country Garden Salad, first, peel off the black layer of skin off the charred bell peppers by dipping it in water for easy peeling of the skin. Then, cut them into long strips. Next, add the charred bell pepper slices to a mixing bowl and season them with half a teaspoon of salt. Add 2 teaspoons of apple cider vinegar followed by a teaspoon of honey and mix it well. Then, set marinated peppers inside the refrigerator until use.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6045ba4afba58f6f2a22949f','6045a8553a5ec6d73102e57a',6,'p5- toast the seeds','To toast the seeds for Country Garden salad, heat up a pan over medium flame and add a teaspoon of pumpkin seeds to it. Then, lightly toast them for 1-2 min over medium flame or until it becomes slightly brown. After that, remove them in a bowl and keep aside. Next, in the same pan add a teaspoon of sunflower seeds and lightly toast them over medium flame for a min or until it becomes slightly brown. Then, turn off the flame and set the toasted seeds aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6045ba9fcf76b8674a2e9e7b','6045a8553a5ec6d73102e57a',7,'m1- make the dressing','To prepare the dressing for Country Graden Salad, in a mixing bowl, add 3 tablespoons of curd followed by a teaspoon of Tobasco sauce and half a teaspoon of black pepper powder. Next, add in half a teaspoon of salt, half a teaspoon of paprika, a teaspoon of water, and a teaspoon of chopped coriander leaves. Mix it well using a whisk to avoid any lumps and prepare the dressing.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6045bd623a5ec6d73102e57d','6045a8553a5ec6d73102e57a',8,'m2- Assemble the salad. Garnish & Serve','To assemble the Country Garden salad, in a mixing bowl add 1/4 cup of roughly shredded iceberg lettuce, green lettuce and lolo rosso lettuce. Add a tablespoon of rocket lettuce followed by 1/4 cup of sliced cucumbers and the oven dried apple slices, and mix it well. Then, transfer the lettuce mix to a salad bowl and place it as the base for the salad. Next, layer it with the marinated bell pepper strips and 1/4 cup of blanched beans. Top it with 1 teaspoon of toasted pumpkin seeds and sunflower seeds. Add in the prepared buttermilk dressing followed by 1/4 cup of sliced cherry tomatoes and a tablespoon of black olives. Garnish the salad with the oven dried apple slice and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6045bf40fba58f6f2a2294a0','6045bf0fcf76b8674a2e9e7c',1,'p1- marinate the chicken','To marinate the chicken for Chicken Country salad, peel and finely chop a teaspoon of garlic. Next, rinse and clean 200 grams of boneless chicken breast and place it in a glass dish or mixing bowl. Then, add half a teaspoon of salt, half a teaspoon of black pepper powder, a teaspoon of chopped garlic, and a teaspoon of dijon mustard. Next, add a sprig of rosemary and rub the marinade well on both the sides of the chicken breast. Then, allow it to marinate for 20 minutes. While the chicken marinates, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('6045bf99cf76b8674a2e9e7d','6045bf0fcf76b8674a2e9e7c',2,'p2- char the bell peppers','To char the bell peppers for Chicken country garden salad, wash 1 small red bell pepper and wash 1 small yellow bell pepper. Next, put the roast grill or mesh onto the gas stove and turn on the flame. Then, place the whole bell peppers onto it and allow it to char over direct medium flame for 5-6 mins or until it has a layer of black skin formed around it. Keep rotating the bell peppers for evenly charring. Then, turn off the flame and allow it to cool down for some time. While the bell peppers are being charred and are cooling please move on to the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":7,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6045bfd63a5ec6d73102e57e','6045bf0fcf76b8674a2e9e7c',3,'p3- blanch the beans','To blanch the beans for Chicken Country Garden Salad, first, wash and cut 1/4 cup of haricot beans into juliennes. Next, add 2 cups of water to a saucepan along with 1/4 teaspoon of salt and bring it to a rolling boil. Then, add the sliced beans and boil them over medium flame for a minute. After that, turn off the flame and transfer the blanched beans to the cold water to prevent them from cooking further. Soak the beans in cold water for a minute, then remove them in a separate bowl and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6045c0053a5ec6d73102e57f','6045bf0fcf76b8674a2e9e7c',4,'p4- prep the ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Chicken Country Garden Salad, wash and slice 1/4 cup English cucumber into rondelles. Wash and finely chop a teaspoon of coriander leaves. Wash and cut 1/4 cup of cherry tomatoes into halves. Wash, pat dry and roughly shred 1/4 cup iceberg lettuce. Wash, pat dry and roughly shred 1/4 cup of green lettuce. Wash, pat dry, and roughly tear 1/4 cup of lolo roso lettuce. Wash, pat dry and shred 1 tbsp of rocket lettuce.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6045c076cf76b8674a2e9e7e','6045bf0fcf76b8674a2e9e7c',5,'p5- marinate the bell peppers','To marinate the bell peppers for Chicken Country Garden Salad, first, peel off the black layer of skin off the charred bell peppers by dipping it in water for easy peeling of the skin. Then, cut them into long strips. Next, add the charred bell pepper slices to a mixing bowl and season them with half a teaspoon of salt. Add 2 teaspoons of apple cider vinegar followed by a teaspoon of honey and mix it well. Then, set marinated peppers inside the refrigerator until use.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6045c0bdcf76b8674a2e9e7f','6045bf0fcf76b8674a2e9e7c',6,'p6- toast the seeds','To toast the seeds for Chicken Country Garden salad, heat up a pan over medium flame and add a teaspoon of pumpkin seeds to it. Then, lightly toast them for 1-2 min over medium flame or until it becomes slightly brown. After that, remove them in a bowl and keep them aside. Next, in the same pan add a teaspoon of sunflower seeds and lightly toast them over medium flame for a min or until it becomes slightly brown. Then, turn off the flame and set the toasted seeds aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('6045c0f83a5ec6d73102e580','6045bf0fcf76b8674a2e9e7c',7,'m1- grill the chicken','To grill the chicken for Chicken Country Garden Salad, grease the grill pan with a teaspoon of cooking oil and place the marinated chicken breast onto it. Then, cook the chicken over medium flame for 3-4 minutes on each side until it is evenly browned on both sides. After that, turn off the flame and remove the chicken in a bowl. Then, using a fork, hold the cooked chicken breast and with the help of another fork tear the marinated chicken into shreds and keep it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6045c1583a5ec6d73102e581','6045bf0fcf76b8674a2e9e7c',8,'m2- make the dressing','To prepare the dressing for Chicken Country Graden Salad, in a mixing bowl, add 3 tablespoons of curd followed by a teaspoon of Tobasco sauce and half a teaspoon of black pepper powder. Next, add in half a teaspoon of salt, half a teaspoon of paprika, a teaspoon of water, and a teaspoon of chopped coriander leaves. Mix it well using a whisk to avoid any lumps and prepare the dressing.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6045c18fcf76b8674a2e9e80','6045bf0fcf76b8674a2e9e7c',9,'m3- Assemble the salad. Garnish & Serve','To assemble the Chicken Country Garden salad, in a mixing bowl add 1/4 cup of roughly shredded iceberg lettuce, green lettuce, and lolo rosso lettuce. Add a tablespoon of rocket lettuce followed by 1/4 cup of sliced cucumbers and the oven-dried apple slices, and mix it well. Then, transfer the lettuce mix to a salad bowl and place it as the base for the salad. Next, layer it with the marinated bell pepper strips and 1/4 cup of blanched beans. Top it with 1 teaspoon of toasted pumpkin seeds and sunflower seeds. Add in the prepared buttermilk dressing followed by the grilled chicken shreds. Top it up with 1/4 cup of sliced cherry tomatoes and a tablespoon of black olives. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6045c5ed3a5ec6d73102e584','6045c57b3a5ec6d73102e583',1,'ap1- soak the paneer in salt water','For the roasted tomato penne and bell pepper salad, first, cut half a cup of paneer into medium cubes. Next, add 2 cups of water in a mixing bowl along with half a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Then, add the paneer cubes to the saltwater and soak it in the water for 2 hours. After that, pat dry the paneer pieces and set them aside. While the paneer soaks, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":120,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6045c7ca3a5ec6d73102e585','6045c57b3a5ec6d73102e583',2,'p1- prep the bell peppers','For Roasted Tomato Penne and Bell Pepper Salad, wash and cut 1/4 cup of red bell pepper into triangles. Wash and cut 1/4 cup of green capsicum into triangles. Wash and cut 1/4 cup yellow bell pepper into triangles. Next, add the tri-colored bell pepper triangles to a mixing bowl and season them with half a teaspoon of salt, half a tsp of black pepper powder, and half a tsp of oregano herbs. Add a teaspoon of cooking oil and mix it well. Next, in a separate bowl add a tablespoon of almonds followed by a teaspoon of honey and mix it well.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('6045c8603a5ec6d73102e586','6045c57b3a5ec6d73102e583',3,'p2- marinate the tomatoes & roast the vegetables','For Roasted Tomato penne and bell pepper salad, wash 1 and cut 1 cup of tomatoes and into wedges. Peel and finely chop 2 teaspoons of garlic. Next, to marinate the tomatoes, add the tomato wedges to a mixing bowl followed by half a teaspoon of black pepper powder, a teaspoon of cooking oil, half a teaspoon of garlic, and half a teaspoon of salt. Next, add 2 teaspoons of balsamic vinegar and mix it well. Then, arrange the tomato wedges onto a baking tray along with the marinated bell peppers and the honey glazed almonds. Make sure the 3 items are spaced out well. Then, set the baking tray inside the oven and roast it at 180 degrees celsius for 20 mins. While it is roasting, please on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6045c89acf76b8674a2e9e82','6045c57b3a5ec6d73102e583',4,'p3- boil the pasta','To boil the pasta for Roasted Tomato Penne and Bell Pepper Salad, add 3 cups of water in a saucepan along with a 1 tsp of cooking oil and 0.5 tsp salt. Mix it well and bring the water to a rolling boil. After that, add 3/4 cup of whole wheat penne pasta and allow it to cook for 8-10 mins until the pasta is tender and firm to the bite. Then, turn off the flame and strain the pasta and rinse it under cold water to prevent the pasta from sticking and cooking further. While the pasta is boiling move towards the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6045c92ffba58f6f2a2294a1','6045c57b3a5ec6d73102e583',5,'p4- prep the ingredients','For Roasted Tomato and Bellpepper Salad, wash half a cup of broccoli and cut them into florets. Wash 1/4 cup English cucumber and then cut them into triangles. Wash and finely chop 1 tbsp parsley, Slice 2 teaspoons of pitted green olives. Wash 1/4 cup lolo rosso lettuce, wash 1/4 leaf lettuce, and pat dry using a kitchen towel and roughly tear them. Roughly dice a tablespoon of walnuts. Wash and chop half a cup of basil leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6045c9aefba58f6f2a2294a2','6045c57b3a5ec6d73102e583',6,'p5- blanch the broccoli','To blanch the broccoli, take a bowl and fill it with cold water, now take a pot and add 500ml water in it and bring to boil on a medium flame for 6mins. When the water starts boiling add the broccoli florets and remove them within 1-2mins and transfer them to the cold water bowl to stop the cooking process. Keep Aside','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6045c9fdcf76b8674a2e9e83','6045c57b3a5ec6d73102e583',7,'m1- make the pesto sauce','To make the pesto sauce, take a mixy jar and add 0.5 cup basil, 1tbsp diced walnuts, 2 tbsp water, 0.5 tsp garlic, 1 tsp olive oil, 0.5 tsp salt, 0.5 tsp pepper powder, and blitz it into a smooth paste. Keep Aside','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('6045ca863a5ec6d73102e587','6045c57b3a5ec6d73102e583',8,'m2- make the dressing','To make the dressing, take a bowl and add 0.5 tbsp dijon mustard, 1 tbsp chopped parsley. 0.5 tsp oregano herbs, 1 tsp lemon juice, 2 tsp salad oil, 2 tbsp water, 2 tsp white wine vinegar, 0.5 tsp chopped garlic and mix it well using a whisk and keep aside','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6045caedcf76b8674a2e9e84','6045c57b3a5ec6d73102e583',9,'m3- fry the paneer cubes','To sear the paneer for roasted tomato penne and bell pepper salad, take a pan and add 0.5 tsp oil and pan sear the paneer cubes for 2 mins or until crisp and golden brown, in the same pan add 1 tsp pumpkin seeds and dry roast it on a medium flame for 1 min until it becomes golden brown and then turn off the flame.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6045cb4dcf76b8674a2e9e85','6045c57b3a5ec6d73102e583',10,'m4- Assemble the salad. Garnish & Salad','To assemble the salad, first, In a mixing bowl, add the boiled penne pasta, blanched broccoli, and english cucumber, add the pesto sauce and mix it well such that the pasta and blanched vegetables are evenly coated with the sauce;   take a plate and place the washed and dried lettuce leaves to form the base, then add the boiled penne and blanched broccoli and cucumber coated in pesto sauce. then add roasted tomato, roasted bell peppers, sliced green olives, 4 teaspoons feta cheese, Honey roasted almonds, toasted pumpkin seeds, then pour some dressing on top and add the pan-seared paneer cubes.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6045e809cf76b8674a2e9e86','6045e371fba58f6f2a2294a3',1,'p1- prep the bell peppers','For Roasted Tomato Penne and chicken Salad, wash and cut 1/4 cup of red bell pepper into triangles. Wash and cut 1/4 cup of green capsicum into triangles. Wash and cut 1/4 cup yellow bell pepper into triangles. Next, add the tri-colored bell pepper triangles to a mixing bowl and season them with half a teaspoon of salt, half a tsp of black pepper powder, and half a tsp of oregano herbs. Add a teaspoon of cooking oil and mix it well. Next, in a separate bowl add a tablespoon of almonds followed by a teaspoon of honey and mix it well.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6045e8bdcf76b8674a2e9e87','6045e371fba58f6f2a2294a3',2,'p2- marinate the  tomatoes & roast the vegetables','For Roasted Tomato penne and chicken salad, wash and cut 1 cup of tomatoes and into wedges. Peel and finely chop 2 teaspoons of garlic. Next, to marinate the tomatoes, add the tomato wedges to a mixing bowl followed by half a teaspoon of black pepper powder, a teaspoon of cooking oil, half a teaspoon of garlic, and half a teaspoon of salt. Next, add 2 teaspoons of balsamic vinegar and mix it well. Then, arrange the tomato wedges onto a baking tray along with the marinated bell peppers and the honey glazed almonds. Make sure the 3 items are spaced out well. Then, set the baking tray inside the oven and roast it at 180 degrees celsius for 20 mins. While it is roasting, please on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('6045e941cf76b8674a2e9e88','6045e371fba58f6f2a2294a3',3,'p3- boil the pasta','To boil the pasta for Roasted Tomato Penne and chicken Salad, add 3 cups of water in a saucepan along with 1 tsp of cooking oil and 0.5 tsp salt. Mix it well and bring the water to a rolling boil. After that, add 3/4 cup of whole wheat penne pasta and allow it to cook for 8-10 mins until the pasta is tender and firm to the bite. Then, turn off the flame and strain the pasta and rinse it under cold water to prevent the pasta from sticking and cooking further. While the pasta is boiling move towards the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6045e9cdcf76b8674a2e9e89','6045e371fba58f6f2a2294a3',4,'p4- marinate the chicken','To marinate the chicken for Roasted Tomato Penne and Chicken Salad, first, zest half a teaspoon of lemon zest using a zester or grater. Rinse and clean 200 grams of boneless chicken breast. Next, place the chicken in a dish or mixing bowl. Then, add half a teaspoon of salt, half a teaspoon of black pepper powder, a teaspoon of cooking oil, and half a teaspoon of lemon zest. Next, add a teaspoon of chopped garlic, followed by half a teaspoon of thyme and half a teaspoon of dijon mustard. Then, rub the marinade well on each side of the chicken and allow it to marinate for 15 minutes. While the chicken marinates, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6045ea4b3a5ec6d73102e588','6045e371fba58f6f2a2294a3',5,'p5- prep the ingredients','For Roasted Tomato penne and chicken salad, wash half a cup of broccoli and cut them into florets. Wash 1/4 cup English cucumber and then cut them into triangles. Wash and finely chop 1 tbsp parsley, Slice 2 teaspoons of pitted green olives. Wash 1/4 cup lolo rosso lettuce, wash 1/4 leaf lettuce, and pat dry using a kitchen towel and roughly tear them. Roughly dice a tablespoon of walnuts. Wash and chop half a cup of basil leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6045ea8d3a5ec6d73102e589','6045e371fba58f6f2a2294a3',6,'p6- blanch the broccoli','To blanch the broccoli for roasted tomato penne and chicken salad, take a bowl and fill it with cold water, now take a pot and add 500ml water in it and bring to boil on a medium flame for 6mins. When the water starts boiling add the broccoli florets and remove it within 1-2mins and transfer it to the cold water bowl to stop the cooking process. Keep Aside','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6045eacacf76b8674a2e9e8a','6045e371fba58f6f2a2294a3',7,'m1- grill the chicken','To grill the chicken for roasted tomato penne and chicken salad, grease a grill pan with a teaspoon of cooking oil. Then, place the marinated chicken and cook it for 2-3 mins on each side or until it is evenly cooked and browned on all sides. After that, turn off the flame and remove it on a plate. Then allow it to slightly cool and shred it into slices.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('6045eb793a5ec6d73102e58a','6045e371fba58f6f2a2294a3',8,'m2- make the pesto sauce','To make the pesto sauce for roasted tomato penne and chicken salad, in a blender jar, add 0.5 cup basil, 1tbsp diced walnuts, 2 tbsp water, 0.5 tsp garlic, 1 tsp olive oil, 0.5 tsp salt, 0.5 tsp pepper powder, and blend it into a smooth paste. Keep Aside','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6045ec2cfba58f6f2a2294a4','6045e371fba58f6f2a2294a3',9,'m3- make the dressing','To make the dressing for roasted tomato penne and chicken salad, in a mixing bowl, add in a half a teaspoon of chopped garlic followed by half a teaspoon of dijon mustard, half a teaspoon of oregano, and 2 teaspoons of white wine vinegar. Next, add 2 teaspoons of salad oil, a teaspoon of lime juice, along 2 tablespoons of water, and a tablespoon of chopped parsley. Mix it well using a whisk and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6045ec673a5ec6d73102e58b','6045e371fba58f6f2a2294a3',10,'m4- Assemble the Salad. Garnish & Serve','To assemble the roasted tomato penne and chicken salad, first, add the boiled penne pasta to a large mixing bowl followed by 1/4 cup of cucumber and 1/4 cup of blanched broccoli. Add in the prepared pesto sauce and mix it well. Next, in a separate bowl, add 1/4 cup of iceberg lettuce, 1/4 cup of green lettuce, and 1/4 cup of lolo rosso lettuce followed by the pesto tossed penne. Add roasted tomato wedges, roasted bell peppers, 2 teaspoons of sliced olives, 4 teaspoons of crumbled feta cheese, a tablespoon of honey roasted almonds, and a teaspoon of pumpkin seeds, followed by the prepared salad dressing and mix it well. Next, add the grilled chicken into the salad and top it up with some pesto sauce. Mix Serve','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6045f0c03a5ec6d73102e58d','6045eff4fba58f6f2a2294a5',1,'ap1- marinate the chicken','To marinate the chicken for chicken and orange salad, peel and finely chop a teaspoon of garlic. Next, rinse and clean the 200 grams of boneless chicken breast. Then place it in a bowl and add 0.5 tsp salt, 0.5 tsp pepper powder, 2 cloves chopped garlic,  0.5 tsp thyme, 0.5 tsp dijon mustard paste and rub it on the chicken such that it coats the meat evenly. Now allow the chicken to marinate in the refrigerator overnight. While the chicken marinates, please move on to the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":480,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6045f14b3a5ec6d73102e58e','6045eff4fba58f6f2a2294a5',2,'ap2- soak cranberry & almonds','For chicken and orange salad, first, add 2 cups of water in a pan and heat it over medium flame for a minute. Then, turn off the flame and set the warm water aside. Next, take a bowl and fill it with 1 cup of warm water and soak 1 tbsp cranberry, then take another bowl and fill it with 1 cup of warm water and soak 1 tbsp almonds and allow it to soak for 30mins. While the almonds and cranberry are soaking, please move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":30,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('6045f1e1cf76b8674a2e9e8b','6045eff4fba58f6f2a2294a5',3,'p1- marinate & roast the carrots','For Chicken and Orange Salad, peel and wash and slice half a cup of carrot it into a diamond shape, then take a bowl and add the diamond cut carrot pieces and add 1 tsp oil, 0.5 tsp salt, 0.5 tsp pepper powder, 1 tsp honey, 0.5 tsp turmeric powder, 0.5 tsp cumin powder, 0.5 tsp coriander powder and toss it well. Then, place the marinated carrots onto a baking tray and roast it at 180 degrees celsius for 10mins or until it starts browning. While the carrots are being roasted move towards the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6045f283fba58f6f2a2294a6','6045eff4fba58f6f2a2294a5',4,'p2- blanch the beans','For Chicken and Orange Salad wash and cut half a cup of haricot beans into medium-long pieces. To blanch the beans, take the bowl and fill it with cold water. Then take a pot and heat 2 cups of water in it, bring to boil for 3-4 mins on medium flame and then when water starts boiling add the cut beans and remove it within 1 minute, and transfer the beans in cold water to stop the cooking process.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6045f2d73a5ec6d73102e58f','6045eff4fba58f6f2a2294a5',5,'p3- prepare the corn flour slurry','To prepare the cornflour slurry, Take a bowl and add 0.5 tsp cornflour and 1 tsp water and mix it well to make cornflour slurry, now take a pan and add the cornflour slurry in it and cook it on a medium flame for 30secs or until it starts to thicken and then stir vigorously and turn off the flame. Allow it to cool','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('6045f3e43a5ec6d73102e590','6045eff4fba58f6f2a2294a5',6,'p4- prep the ingredients','For Chicken and Orange Salad, Wash and pat dry 1/4 cup iceberg lettuce, wash and pat dry 1/4 cup leaf lettuce, wash and pat dry 1/4 cup Lolo Rosso lettuce; peel the soaked almonds. Wash and cut 1/4 cup cherry tomatoes into half; peel 1 no orange and cut them into wedges and store in the refrigerator until you assemble the salad.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6045f433fba58f6f2a2294a7','6045eff4fba58f6f2a2294a5',7,'m1- grill the chicken','To grill the marinated chicken, take a grill pan and grease it with 0.5 tsp oil, and grill the marinated chicken on a medium flame for 30secs on each side or until it becomes slightly brown. Then place the grilled chicken on the baking tray and roast at 160 degrees celsius for 6 mins.  Allow it to cool','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('6045f4a23a5ec6d73102e591','6045eff4fba58f6f2a2294a5',8,'m2- make the dressing','To make the dressing, take a blender and add 0.5 tsp dijon mustard paste, 1 tsp water, 1 tablespoon black currant, 1 tsp lemon juice, 1 tbsp salad oil, 0.5 tsp salt, 0.5 tsp pepper powder 1 tsp cranberry juice, and the cornflour slurry and blitz it into a fine paste.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6045f541cf76b8674a2e9e8c','6045eff4fba58f6f2a2294a5',9,'m3- Assemble the salad. Garnish & Serve','To assemble the salad, take a salad bowl and place the mixed lettuce leaves as the base, then layer the roasted carrots and lanched haricot beans, cherry tomato, then place the sliced grilled chicken and orange wedges. Garnish the salad with peeled almonds, 4 tsp feta cheese, 2 tablespoons pomegranate seeds, and serve it with the dressing','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('608a9bc86aa4baac08ff6eb4','608a9b05cfe25b2dcca7587c',1,'ap1- marinate tofu overnight','For Carrot Ribbon and Tofu salad, slice 3/4 cup tofu, peel and finely chop 1 teaspoon of garlic, wash a lemon and grate 0.5tsp lime zest. Now to marinate the tofu slices, take a mixing bowl and add 80gms sliced tofu, a teaspoon of chopped garlic, 0.5 tsp dijon mustard paste,0.5 tsp thyme, 0.5 tsp lime zest, 0.5 tsp pepper powder, 0.5 tsp salt, and rub it well such that the tofu slices are evenly coated then refrigerate it overnight. While the tofu marinates, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":480,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('608a9c6b6aa4baac08ff6eb5','608a9b05cfe25b2dcca7587c',2,'p1- prep and roast bell peppers','To prepare the roasted bell peppers for Carrot Ribbon Tofu salad, wash and cut 1/4 cup of yellow bell pepper into triangles. Wash and cut 1/4 cup of red bell pepper into triangles. Wash and cut 1/4 cup of green capsicum into triangles. Next, add the chopped bell peppers to a mixing bowl. Add half a tsp of salt, half a tsp of black pepper powder, half a tsp of oregano herbs, and 2 tsp of cooking oil. Then, toss it well and arrange the marinated bell peppers onto a baking tray and roast them at 180 degrees for 20 mins. While the bell peppers are roasting, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('608a9ce5867a6ad4a82a9a2f','608a9b05cfe25b2dcca7587c',3,'p2- slice the carrot into ribbons and roast it','To prepare the roasted carrot ribbons for Carrot Ribbon and tofu salad, first, wash, peel and slice 3/4 cup of carrot into thin ribbons. Next, add in the carrot ribbons to a mixing bowl. Add 1 tablespoon of jaggery, followed by half a teaspoon of salt, half a teaspoon of black pepper powder, a teaspoon of paprika mix it well. Then, transfer the marinated carrots to a baking glass dish and set it inside the oven. Roast the carrots at 160 degrees for 20 minutes. While the carrot is roasting, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('608a9d396aa4baac08ff6eb6','608a9b05cfe25b2dcca7587c',4,'p3- boil the sweet potato','To boil the sweet potato for Carrot ribbon tofu salad, wash a medium-sized sweet potato and add it to pressure along with 2 cups of water. Cover the cooker with a lid and pressure cook it over a high flame until one whistle. After the first whistle, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook it for another 5 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside to depressurize it naturally. After that, remove the boiled sweet potato on a plate and gently peel off the skin. Then, roughly slice it or mash it using a fork. While the sweet potato boils, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('608a9d966aa4baac08ff6eb7','608a9b05cfe25b2dcca7587c',5,'p4- Grill the tofu','To grill the tofu for Carrot Ribbon Tofu Salad, heat up a grill pan and grease it with a teaspoon of cooking oil. Next, place the marinated tofu slices onto it and grill them for a minute on each side. Then, turn off the flame and remove the grilled tofu onto a baking tray and set it inside the oven to roast the tofu at 160 degrees C for 6 minutes. While it roasts, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('608a9de7cfe25b2dcca7587d','608a9b05cfe25b2dcca7587c',6,'p5-blanch the beans','To blanch the beans for Carrot Ribbon Tofu Salad, first, wash and cut 1/4 cup of haricot beans into juliennes. Next, add 2 cups of water to a saucepan along with 1/4 teaspoon of salt and bring it to a rolling boil. Then, add the sliced beans and boil them over medium flame for 3-4 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and transfer the blanched beans to the cold water to prevent them from cooking further. Soak the beans in cold water for a minute, then remove them in a separate bowl and set them aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('608a9ea5cfe25b2dcca7587e','608a9b05cfe25b2dcca7587c',7,'p6-prep the ingredients and marinate zucchini','For carrot ribbon and tofu salad, first, soak a tablespoon of cashew nut in 1 cup of water for 15 minutes. Next, wash and cut 1/4 cup of green zucchini into triangles. Wash and cut 1/4 cup of yellow zucchini into triangles. Wash, pat dry and roughly shred 1/4 cup of leaf lettuce. Wash, pat dry and roughly shred 1/4 cup of Lolo Rosso lettuce. Wash, pat dry and roughly shred 1/4 cup of iceberg lettuce. Next, to marinate the zucchini, add 1/4 cup of sliced yellow zucchini and 1/4 cup of green zucchini triangles to a mixing bowl. Add half a teaspoon of oregano herbs, half a teaspoon of black pepper powder, half a teaspoon of salt, and half a teaspoon of cooking oil. Then, mix it well and set it aside','prep_method','{"active_time":18,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('608a9ef6cfe25b2dcca7587f','608a9b05cfe25b2dcca7587c',8,'m1- char the marinated zucchini','To char the zucchini for Carrot ribbon tofu salad, heat a grill pan and grease it half a teaspoon of oil, place the marinated zucchini and allow it to cook on medium flame for 2 mins or until the char marks appear. Then remove it in a bowl, allow it to slightly cool and refrigerate until you assemble the salad.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('608a9fb26aa4baac08ff6eb8','608a9b05cfe25b2dcca7587c',9,'m2- prepare the dressing','To make the cashew mayo dressing for carrot ribbon tofu salad, in a blender jar add a tablespoon of soaked cashew nuts followed by 1 tsp dijon mustard paste,1 tsp lemon juice, a teaspoon of chopped garlic, 0.5 tsp of salt, half a teaspoon of paprika, a teaspoon of honey, 3 tablespoons of curd and 1/4 cup of boiled sweet potato. Add in 2 tablespoons of water and blend it well into a smooth dressing.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('608a9ffd867a6ad4a82a9a30','608a9b05cfe25b2dcca7587c',10,'m3- Assemble the salad. Garnish & Serve','To assemble the salad, take a mixing bowl and place the iceberg lettuce, lolo rosso lettuce, leaf lettuce to form the base of the salad, then top it with grilled zucchini and blanched beans, then add the roasted bell pepper triangles and carrot slices, top it with grilled tofu pieces and garnish it with black olives, green olives, diced sundried tomatoes, and serve it with the dressing','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('608bdd8bcfe25b2dcca75884','608bda226aa4baac08ff6ebe',1,'ap1- marinate the chicken overnight','For Carrot Ribbon and chicken salad, rinse and clean 200 grams of chicken breast. Peel and finely chop 1 teaspoon of garlic, wash a lemon and grate 0.5tsp lime zest. Now to marinate the chicken, place the chicken onto a mixing glass dish. Add a teaspoon of chopped garlic, 0.5 tsp dijon mustard paste,0.5 tsp thyme, 0.5 tsp lime zest, 0.5 tsp pepper powder, 0.5 tsp salt, and rub the marinade well on each side of the chicken breast, then refrigerate it overnight. While the chicken marinates, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":480,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('608bde2d867a6ad4a82a9a39','608bda226aa4baac08ff6ebe',2,'p1- prep and roast the bell peppers','To prepare the roasted bell peppers for Carrot Ribbon chicken salad, wash and cut 1/4 cup of yellow bell pepper into triangles. Wash and cut 1/4 cup of red bell pepper into triangles. Wash and cut 1/4 cup of green capsicum into triangles. Next,  add the chopped bell peppers to a mixing bowl. Add half a tsp of salt, half a tsp of black pepper powder, half a tsp of oregano herbs, and 2 tsp of cooking oil. Then, toss it well and arrange the marinated bell peppers onto a baking tray and roast them at 180 degrees for 20 mins. While the bell peppers are roasting, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('608bdec1cfe25b2dcca75885','608bda226aa4baac08ff6ebe',3,'p2- slice the carrot into ribbons. Marinate and oven roast it','To prepare the roasted carrot ribbons for Carrot Ribbon and chicken salad, first, wash, peel and slice 3/4 cup of carrot into thin ribbons. Next, add the carrot ribbons to a mixing bowl. Add 1 tablespoon of jaggery, followed by half a teaspoon of salt, half a teaspoon of black pepper powder, a teaspoon of paprika mix it well. Then, transfer the marinated carrots to a baking glass dish and set it inside the oven. Roast the carrots at 160 degrees for 20 minutes. While the carrot is roasting, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":20,"flame":0}'),
('608bdf17cfe25b2dcca75886','608bda226aa4baac08ff6ebe',4,'p3- boil the sweet potato','To boil the sweet potato for Carrot ribbon chicken salad, wash a medium-sized sweet potato and add it to pressure along with 2 cups of water. Cover the cooker with a lid and pressure cook it over a high flame until one whistle. After the first whistle, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook it for another 5 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside to depressurize it naturally. After that, remove the boiled sweet potato on a plate and gently peel off the skin. Then, roughly slice it. While the sweet potato boils, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('608bdf57867a6ad4a82a9a3a','608bda226aa4baac08ff6ebe',5,'p4- grill the marinated chicken','To grill the chicken for Carrot Ribbon chicken Salad, heat up a grill pan and grease it with a teaspoon of cooking oil. Next, place the marinated chicken breast onto it and grill it for a minute on each side. Then, turn off the flame and remove the grilled chicken onto a baking tray and set it inside the oven to roast the chicken at 160 degrees C for 6 minutes. After that, shred the grilled chicken into rectangular pieces. While it roasts, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('608bdf97cfe25b2dcca75887','608bda226aa4baac08ff6ebe',6,'p5- blanch the beans','To blanch the beans for Carrot Ribbon chicken Salad, first, wash and cut 1/4 cup of haricot beans into juliennes. Next, add 2 cups of water to a saucepan along with 1/4 teaspoon of salt and bring it to a rolling boil. Then, add the sliced beans and boil them over medium flame for 3-4 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and transfer the blanched beans to the cold water to prevent them from cooking further. Soak the beans in cold water for a minute, then remove them in a separate bowl and set them aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":4}'),('608be04d6aa4baac08ff6ebf','608bda226aa4baac08ff6ebe',7,'p6- prep the greens and other ingredients','For carrot ribbon and chicken salad, first, soak a tablespoon of cashew nut in 1 cup of water for 15 minutes. Next, wash and cut 1/4 cup of green zucchini into triangles. Wash and cut 1/4 cup of yellow zucchini into triangles. Wash, pat dry and roughly shred 1/4 cup of leaf lettuce. Wash, pat dry and roughly shred 1/4 cup of lolo rosso lettuce. Wash, pat dry and roughly shred 1/4 cup of iceberg lettuce. Next, to marinate the zucchini, add 1/4 cup of sliced yellow zucchini and 1/4 cup of green zucchini triangles to a mixing bowl. Add half a teaspoon of oregano herbs, half a teaspoon of black pepper powder, half a teaspoon of salt, and half a teaspoon of cooking oil. Then, mix it well and set it aside','prep_method','{"active_time":18,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('608be08f867a6ad4a82a9a3b','608bda226aa4baac08ff6ebe',8,'m1- char the zucchini','To char the zucchini for Carrot ribbon tofu salad, heat a grill pan and grease it with some oil, place the marinated zucchini and allow it to cook on medium flame for 2 mins or until the char marks appear. Then remove it in a bowl, allow it to slightly cool and refrigerate until you assemble the salad.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":4}'),
('608be10d6aa4baac08ff6ec0','608bda226aa4baac08ff6ebe',9,'m2- prepare the dressing','To make the cashew mayo dressing for carrot ribbon chicken salad, in a blender jar add a tablespoon of soaked cashew nuts followed by 1 tsp dijon mustard paste,1 tsp lemon juice, a teaspoon of chopped garlic, 0.5 tsp of salt, half a teaspoon of paprika, a teaspoon of honey, 3 tablespoons of curd and 1/4 cup of boiled sweet potato. Add in 2 tablespoons of water and blend it well into a smooth dressing.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('608be149867a6ad4a82a9a3c','608bda226aa4baac08ff6ebe',10,'m3- Assemble the salad. Garnish & Serve','To assemble the Carrot Ribbon and Chicken salad, in a mixing bowl lay out 1/4 cup of shredded lolo rosso lettuce, green lettuce, and iceberg lettuce. Next, top it up with the roasted bell peppers, grilled zucchini, 1/4 cup of blanched beans, and roasted carrot ribbons. Add in the grilled chicken and garnish it with black olives, green olives, and diced sundried tomatoes. Serve it alongside the prepared dressing.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('608fe154cfe25b2dcca7588e','608fe11bcfe25b2dcca7588d',1,'ap1- soak the broken wheat','For Mango Burst Chicken salad, soak 1/4 cup of broken wheat in 1 cup of water for 8 hours. While it soaks, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":480,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('608fe1e2867a6ad4a82a9a45','608fe11bcfe25b2dcca7588d',2,'ap2- marinate the chicken','To marinate the chicken for Mango Burst Chicken Salad, rinse and clean 200 grams of boneless chicken breast. Peel and finely chop a teaspoon of garlic. Wash a lime and zest half a teaspoon of lime zest using a zester. Next, place the chicken in a dish or mixing bowl. Then, add a teaspoon of chopped garlic,  half a teaspoon of lemon zest, half a teaspoon of salt, and half a teaspoon of black pepper powder. Next, add in half a teaspoon of thyme and half a teaspoon of dijon mustard. Then, rub the marinade well on each side of the chicken and allow it to marinate for 8 hours. While the chicken marinates, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('608fe2a06aa4baac08ff6ec9','608fe11bcfe25b2dcca7588d',3,'p1- prep and roast the bell peppers','To prepare the roasted bell peppers, wash and cut 1/4 cup of yellow bell pepper into triangles. Wash and cut 1/4 cup of red bell pepper into triangles. Wash and cut 1/4 cup of green capsicum into triangles. Next, add in the chopped bell peppers to a mixing bowl. Marinate it with 0.5 tsp salt, 0.5 tsp pepper powder, 0.5 tsp oregano herbs,2 tsp oil, mix it well and transfer it to a glass dish. Then, set it inside the oven and roast the bell peppers at 180 degrees for 20 minutes. While the bell peppers are being grilled, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('608fe30f867a6ad4a82a9a46','608fe11bcfe25b2dcca7588d',4,'p2- simmer the broken wheat','To cook the broken wheat for Mango Burst Chicken Salad, add 1.5 cups of water to a pan and bring it to a boil over medium flame. Next, add half a teaspoon of turmeric powder, half a teaspoon of salt, and half a teaspoon of aromat powder, followed by the soaked broken wheat, and mix it well. Then, cover it with a lid and cook the Dalia over low flame for 8-10 minutes. After that, remove the lid and add a teaspoon of chopped parsley,5 and set the cooked broken wheat aside. While the broken wheat is being cooked, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('608fe354867a6ad4a82a9a47','608fe11bcfe25b2dcca7588d',5,'p3- boil the sweet potato','To boil the sweet potato for Mango Burst chicken salad, wash a medium-sized sweet potato and add it to pressure along with 2 cups of water. Cover the cooker with a lid and pressure cook it over a high flame until one whistle. After the first whistle, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook it for another 5 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside to depressurize it naturally. After that, remove the boiled sweet potato on a plate and gently peel off the skin. Then, roughly slice it or mash it using a fork. While the sweet potato boils, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('608fe3db6aa4baac08ff6eca','608fe11bcfe25b2dcca7588d',6,'p4- prepare the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Mango Burst Chicken salad, peel and finely chop 1 cup of onion; wash and finely chop 1/2 cup of celery stalk; wash and finely chop half a cup of leek stalk; peel, wash and dice half a cup of carrot; Then wash 1/4 cup of leaf lettuce and pat dry using a kitchen towel; wash 1/4 cup of iceberg lettuce and pat dry it using a kitchen towel; wash 1/4 cup of lolo roso lettuce and pat dry using a kitchen towel; wash and pluck 1 tbsp mint leaves and keep aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":17,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('608fe44c6aa4baac08ff6ecb','608fe11bcfe25b2dcca7588d',7,'p5- dice mango and prepare other ingredients','Next, wash English cucumber and cut it into half, remove the seeds and cut 1/4 cup of English cucumber into triangles; wash and peel 3/4 cup of Mallika mango and cut them into dices. Then wash 0.5 cups of red cabbage and finely shred them. Wash and finely chop 1 fresh red chili. Wash and finely chop a tablespoon of parsley. Wash and finely chop a teaspoon of garlic','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('608fe4976aa4baac08ff6ecc','608fe11bcfe25b2dcca7588d',8,'m1- grill the marinated chicken','To grill the chicken for Mango Burst Chicken Salad, heat a grill pan and grease it with 1 tsp oil. Then, place the marinated chicken onto it and grill the chicken for 1-2 mins on each side on medium flame. Then, turn off the flame and remove it onto a baking tray and further grill it inside the oven at 160 degrees for 6mins, then allow it to cool and shred the chicken into slices. While the chicken is being grilled, please move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('608fe4eb867a6ad4a82a9a48','608fe11bcfe25b2dcca7588d',9,'m2- prepare the mirepoix','To prepare the mirepoix for Mango Burst Chicken Salad, Take pan and heat 1 tsp oil in it, and after it becomes hot add 1 cup of chopped onion, half a cup of chopped carrots, and saute it for a minute on medium flame until translucent. Then add the 1/2 cup of chopped celery, followed by half a cup chopped leek, half a teaspoon of chopped garlic, and half a teaspoon of thyme. Mix it well and saute it over medium flame for 4-5 mins or until the vegetables are tender-crisp. Then turn off the flame and keep it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('608fe574cfe25b2dcca7588f','608fe11bcfe25b2dcca7588d',10,'m3- prepare the dressing','To make the dressing for Mango Burst Salad, take a blender jar and add the sweet potato paste, 1 tsp dijon mustard paste,  a teaspoon of chopped garlic, 1 tsp lemon juice,1 tsp white wine vinegar,  2 tbsp salad oil, 1 tsp water and blend it into a smooth paste. Then transfer the dressing to a bowl and,  0.5 tsp salt, 0.5 tsp pepper powder, add 0.5 tsp oregano herbs, 1 finely chopped red chili, and 1 tbsp chopped parsley. Mix it well and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('608fe5bdcfe25b2dcca75890','608fe11bcfe25b2dcca7588d',11,'m4- Assemble the salad. Garnish & Serve','To assemble the Mango Burst salad, take a salad bowl and lay out the shredded iceberg, lolo roso, and green lettuce. Next, add in the cooked broken wheat followed by 1/4 cup of diced cucumber, roasted bell peppers, and 1/4 cup of shredded red cabbage. Top it up with 3/4 cup of diced mangoes, and sliced grill chicken. Garnish it with mint leaves and roasted cashew, serve it along with the chili lime dressing and mirepoix','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('609120e3cfe25b2dcca75896','609120a2867a6ad4a82a9a52',1,'p1- blanch the corn','To prepare the Corn salad, cut the American corn in half so it cooks faster. Take a heavy bottom vessel and add 3 cups of water, 0.5 tsp salt, cut American corn and bring to boil over medium flame for 10mins or until the corn is cooked and soft. While the corn is boiling, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('609121436aa4baac08ff6ed5','609120a2867a6ad4a82a9a52',2,'p2- prep the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Corn Salad, wash and finely chop 1 unit green chili; wash 0.5 cup green capsicum in half, remove the seeds and cut the green capsicum into small dices; wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves; wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of spring onion greens.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('6091219e6aa4baac08ff6ed6','609120a2867a6ad4a82a9a52',3,'p3- slice off the corn kernels and remove the cob','After boiling the corn for corn salad, turn off the flame and remove the boiled corn onto a pate. Then, use a knife to cut off all the cooked kernels and remove the cob. Keep the kernels aside and allow them to dry.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('609121e76aa4baac08ff6ed7','609120a2867a6ad4a82a9a52',4,'m1- Mix all the ingredients & Prepare the salad. Serve','To make the Corn Salad, Take a mixing bowl and add cooked corn kernels, followed by 1/4 cup of chopped spring onion greens, 1 tbsp chopped coriander leaves, 1 chopped green chili, and half a cup of diced capsicum. Add in 2 tsp of lime lemon juice and half a teaspoon of salt. Mix it well and plate the salad in a serving bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60924bd16aa4baac08ff6ed9','60924b70cfe25b2dcca7589a',1,'Dice the tomatoes and prep other ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Tomato Feta Salad, wash and cut 1 cup of tomatoes into dices; wash 1 tbsp mint leaves and finely chop; wash 2 tbsp parsley and finely chop. Wash and cut a lime into half, then squeeze 2 teaspoons of lime juice into a bowl. Roughly dice 1/4 cup of feta cheese into small cubes, or crumble it as shown','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60924c1a6aa4baac08ff6eda','60924b70cfe25b2dcca7589a',2,'m1- Combine the ingredients and prepare the salad','To make the Tomato Feta Salad, in a mixing bowl, add 1 cup of diced tomatoes followed by 2 tablespoons of chopped parsley, a tablespoon of chopped mint leaves, and  1/4 cup of diced feta cheese. Next, add in 2 teaspoons of sunflower seeds, 2 teaspoons of lemon juice, half a teaspoon of salt, and a teaspoon of black pepper powder. Mix it well and plate the salad into a serving bowl and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('609390d66aa4baac08ff6ede','60939091867a6ad4a82a9a56',1,'ap1- soak the lentil','Soak 1/4 cup of yellow moong dal in 2 cups of water for 2 hours. While the dal is soaking, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":120,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('609391276aa4baac08ff6edf','60939091867a6ad4a82a9a56',2,'p1- slice the cucumber & prep other ingredients','For cucumber mint salad, wash 1 cup English cucumber and cut them into juliennes; wash and finely chop 2 tbsp mint leaves;','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('609391ad867a6ad4a82a9a57','60939091867a6ad4a82a9a56',3,'p2- toast the seeds','To make the garnish for Cucumber Mint Salad, heat a pan and add a tablespoon of peanuts, add a tablespoon of white sesame seeds, add a tablespoon of pumpkin seeds, add 2 tsp sunflower seeds, and dry roast it on a medium flame for 1 min until it turns slightly brown, then turn off the flame and keep it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('609392186aa4baac08ff6ee2','60939091867a6ad4a82a9a56',4,'m1- Combine the ingredients. Garnish & Serve','To assemble the cucumber mint salad, take a mixing bowl and add 1 cup cucumber julienne, followed by the prepared seed mix and 1/4 cup of soaked moong dal. Next, add in 2 tablespoons of chopped mint leaves, 2 teaspoons of  lemon juice, and half a teaspoon of salt. Mix it well and serve','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6093b5e56aa4baac08ff6ee3','6093b5b1cfe25b2dcca758a0',1,'ap1- soak the whole moong beans','Soak 3/4 cup of whole green moong beans in 2 cups of water for 8 hours. While the dal soaks, please move on to the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":480,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6093b61e6aa4baac08ff6ee4','6093b5b1cfe25b2dcca758a0',2,'ap2- sprout the moong beans','To sprout the moong beans for Sprouts Pomegranate Salad,  take a muslin cloth and slightly wet it, place the soaked moong beans in a moist cloth and tie it. Allow it to sprout for 6-8 hours. While the moong beans sprouts, please move on to the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":480,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('6093b68b867a6ad4a82a9a59','6093b5b1cfe25b2dcca758a0',3,'p1- prep the ingredients','For sprouts pomegranate salad, wash 0.25 cup yellow bell pepper, cut it into half, remove the seeds and finely chop the yellow bell pepper. Wash 0.25 cup green capsicum, cut it into half, remove the seeds and finely chop green capsicum; wash 0.25 cup red bell pepper and cut it into half, remove the seeds and finely chop the red bell pepper. Wash and finely chop 1 tbsp coriander leaves; wash peel and finely dice 0.5 cup beetroot.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6093b6bdcfe25b2dcca758a1','6093b5b1cfe25b2dcca758a0',4,'p2- blanch the beetroot','To blanch the beetroots for Sprouts Pomegranate Salad, add 2 cups of water in a saucepan and bring it to a boil over high flame. Next, add in 1/4 teaspoon of salt followed by half a cup of diced beetroots and mix it well. Then, boil the beetroots for 2 minutes over medium flame. Then, turn off the flame and remove the blanched beetroots into a bowl, and set them aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6093b7196aa4baac08ff6ee5','6093b5b1cfe25b2dcca758a0',5,'m1- Combine the ingredients and prepare the salad','To make sprouts pomegranate salad, take a mixing bowl and add the prepared moong beans sprouts. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped red bell peppers, 1/4 cup of chopped yellow bell peppers, 1/4 cup of diced green capsicum, and 1/4 cup of pomegranate seeds followed by 1 tsp lemon juice and half a cup of blanched beetroots. Next, add 0.5 tsp chat masala, 0.5 tsp salt, 0.5 tsp chili powder, and mix it well. Garnish it with chopped coriander leaves and serve','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6094e8cf6aa4baac08ff6ee9','6094e8886aa4baac08ff6ee8',1,'p1- prepare the ingredients','For Asian Cucumber salad, wash 1 cup English cucumber, remove the seeds and cut them into juliennes; wash and cut 1 cup red bell pepper into half and remove the seeds, then cut the red bell pepper into juliennes','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6094ebc2867a6ad4a82a9a5f','6094e8886aa4baac08ff6ee8',2,'p2- sweat the vegetables','For Asian Cucumber salad, take a mixing bowl and add 1 cup of bell pepper juliennes and 1 cup of cucumber juliennes. Next, add 0.5 tsp salt and allow it to sweat for 30mins until it leaves out all the water. Then strain the water and keep it aside. While it''s resting, please move on to the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":30,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('6094ec11867a6ad4a82a9a60','6094e8886aa4baac08ff6ee8',3,'m1- prepare the salad and refrigerate. Serve chilled.','To make Asian cucumber salad, take a mixing bowl and add the sweated bell peppers and English cucumber. Next, add 1 tsp honey, 1 tsp sesame oil, and give it a good mix. Store it in the refrigerator until use. Serve Chilled.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":30,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('609518b06aa4baac08ff6eea','6095184a867a6ad4a82a9a61',1,'ap1-marinate the chicken breast','To marinate the chicken for Teriyaki Chicken Salad with Asian Dressing, first, rinse and clean 200 gms of boneless chicken breast chicken then place it in a mixing dish. Next, add 1.5 tablespoons of teriyaki sauce, add 0.5 tsp salt, add 0.5 tsp pepper powder and rub it well such that the meat is evenly coated with the marinade. Then, set it inside the refrigerator and allow it to marinate overnight or for 8 hrs. While the chicken marinates, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":480,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('609518fb867a6ad4a82a9a62','6095184a867a6ad4a82a9a61',2,'p1- prep and roast the bell peppers','To prepare the roasted bell peppers for Teriyaki Chicken Salad with Asian Dressing,  wash 1/4 cup green bell pepper, and cut it into half, remove the seeds and cut the bell pepper into dices, wash 1/4 cup yellow bell peppers and cut it into dices, remove the seeds and cut the bell peppers into dices; wash 1/4 cup red capsicum, cut the capsicum into half and remove the seeds, cut the capsicum into dices. Next, add the mixed bell peppers to a baking glass dish followed by half a teaspoon of salt, a teaspoon of teriyaki sauce, and a teaspoon of cooking oil. Mix it well and roast them for 20mins at 180 degrees celsius. While the peppers are being roasted, move towards the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6095194c6aa4baac08ff6eeb','6095184a867a6ad4a82a9a61',3,'p2- boil the sweet potato','To boil the sweet potato for Teriyaki Chicken with asian dressing, wash a medium sized sweet potato well with water and add it to a pressure cooker along with 2 cups of water. Cover the cooker with a lid and pressure cook it over high flame until one whistle. After that, reduce the flame to low and allow it to cook for another 5 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. After that, take out the boiled sweet potato from the cooker and gently peel off the skin and mash it well using a fork. While the sweet potato is boiling please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60951ae0867a6ad4a82a9a64','6095184a867a6ad4a82a9a61',4,'p3- blanch the beans','To blanch the beans for Teriyaki Chicken salad, first, wash and cut half a cup of haricot beans into 2-inch long pieces. Next, boil 2 cups of water with 1/4 teaspoon of salt in a pan over medium flame. As the water comes to a boil, add the chopped haricot beans and let it boil for 3-4 minutes over medium flame. Then, turn off the flame and drain off the water from the blanched beans and soak them in an ice bath for 2 minutes. After that, strain the beans in a bowl and set them aside. While the beans are blanching, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":4}'),
('60951b646aa4baac08ff6eec','6095184a867a6ad4a82a9a61',5,'p4- cut the tomato in wedges and roast the wedges in the oven','To prepare the roasted tomato wedges for Teriyaki Chicken Salad with Asian Dressing, first, wash and cut half a cup of tomato into wedges. Next, arrange the tomato wedges onto a baking tray. Add a teaspoon of teriyaki sauce and half a teaspoon of oil.  Mix it well and evenly coat the wedges in the sauce. Then, set it inside the oven and roast the wedges at 180 degrees Celcius for 10 minutes or until tomatoes wedges are slightly charred. While the tomato wedges are being charred, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60951baa6aa4baac08ff6eed','6095184a867a6ad4a82a9a61',6,'p5- prepare the ingredients','To prep, the ingredients for teriyaki chicken salad with Asian dressing, wash and cut 1/4 cup English cucumber, dessed them and cut them into triangles, wash and finely shred 1/4 cup of red cabbage. Wash peel and finely chop a teaspoon of garlic. Wash and finely chop 1 fresh red chili, Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of spring onion greens. Wash and cut a lemon into halves. Then, squeeze a teaspoon of lime juice in a bowl.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":4}'),('60951bfbcfe25b2dcca758a5','6095184a867a6ad4a82a9a61',7,'p6- blanch the broccoli florets','To blanch the broccoli for Teriyaki Chicken salad with Asian dressing, first, wash and cut half a cup of broccoli into small florets. Next, boil 3 cups of water in a pan over a high flame. When the water starts boiling add the broccoli florets and remove them within 1-2 mins and transfer them to the cold water bowl to stop the cooking process. Keep Aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":4}'),('60951f21867a6ad4a82a9a65','6095184a867a6ad4a82a9a61',8,'p7- toast the nuts','For Teriyaki Chicken Salad with Asian Dressing, heat up a pan over medium flame and add a tablespoon of cashew nuts to it. Then, dry roast the cashews over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until it turns slightly golden. Then, remove the cashews in a bowl and set them aside. Next, add a teaspoon of peanuts to the same pan and dry roast them over medium flame for 2-3 minutes. After that, remove the peanuts in a bowl and set them aside. Next, add a teaspoon of white sesame seeds to the same pan and lightly toast them over medium flame for a minute. Then, turn off the flame and take it out in a bowl.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60951f616aa4baac08ff6eee','6095184a867a6ad4a82a9a61',9,'m1- grill the marinated chicken','To grill the chicken for Teriyaki Chicken Salad with Asian Dressing, heat up a grill pan and grease it with half a teaspoon of cooking oil. Then, place the marinated chicken breast onto the grill pan and grill it over medium flame for 2 minutes on each side. Then, remove it on a baking tray and set it inside the oven and allow it to grill for 20 mins at 160 degrees celsius until the chicken is tender-crisp. After that, remove it from the oven and slice the chicken into shreds. While the chicken is being grilled, please move onto the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('60951fd7867a6ad4a82a9a66','6095184a867a6ad4a82a9a61',10,'m2- prepare the dressing','To prepare the dressing for Teriyaki Chicken Salad with Asian Dressing, in a blender jar, add 1 tsp of dark soy sauce, 1 chopped fresh red chili, a teaspoon of jaggery and a teaspoon of lime juice followed by a teaspoon of sesame oil and 1/4 cup of prepared boiled sweet potato paste. Next, add a teaspoon of olive oil, 1 tablespoon of light soy sauce, and a tablespoon of water. Then, cover the jar with a lid and blitz it into a smooth sauce. Remove the dressing in a bowl and add a teaspoon of chopped garlic and a tablespoon of chopped spring onion greens. Mix it well and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60952020cfe25b2dcca758a6','6095184a867a6ad4a82a9a61',11,'m3- Assemble the salad.  Garnish and Serve','To assemble the salad, take a salad bowl and add the blanched broccoli and haricot beans, add the English cucumber triangles, add roasted bell peppers, roasted tomato wedges, add the shredded red cabbage, add the toasted peanuts, and cashew nuts and toss it together. Plate the salad and top it with sliced grilled chicken and the prepared dressing. Garnish the salad with toasted sesame seeds and chopped spring onion greens. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6098f8376aa4baac08ff6ef8','6098f7dc6aa4baac08ff6ef7',1,'ap1- prepare the hung curd','To make the hung curd for Chicken patty & green beans salad, place a sieve over a large mixing bowl and cover it with a muslin cloth as shown. Next, pour 1 cup of fresh curd into the muslin cloth and tie it tightly, tucking the curd inside. Then, carefully place the tied curd over the sieve and refrigerate it for 2 hours. This will allow the excess water to drain off from the curd, leaving the hung curd thick and creamy. While the curd is refrigerating, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":120,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6098f880867a6ad4a82a9a70','6098f7dc6aa4baac08ff6ef7',2,'p1- blanch the haricot beans','To blanch the beans for Chicken patty & green beans salad, first, wash and cut 3/4 cup of haricot beans into 2-inch long pieces. Next, boil 2 cups of water with 1/4 teaspoon of salt in a pan over medium flame. As the water comes to a boil, add 3/4 cup of chopped haricot beans and let it boil for 3-4 minutes over medium flame. Then, turn off the flame and drain off the water from the blanched beans and soak them in an ice bath for 2 minutes. After that, strain the beans in a bowl and set them aside. While the beans are blanching, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6098f8dfcfe25b2dcca758b0','6098f7dc6aa4baac08ff6ef7',3,'p2- boil the sweet potato','To boil the sweet potato for Chicken patty & green beans salad, wash a medium sized sweet potato well with water and add it to a pressure cooker along with 2 cups of water. Cover the cooker with a lid and pressure cook it over a high flame until one whistle. After that, reduce the flame to low and allow it to cook for another 5 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. After that, take out the boiled sweet potato from the cooker and gently peel off the skin and mash it well using a fork. While the sweet potato is boiling please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('6098f9376aa4baac08ff6ef9','6098f7dc6aa4baac08ff6ef7',4,'p3- roast the beans','To roast the beans for Chicken patty & green beans salad, add the blanched beans to a glass dish or bowl. Add 1/4 teaspoon of salt, 1/4 teaspoon of black pepper powder, and half a teaspoon of cooking oil to the beans and mix it well. Then, set it inside the oven and roast the beans at 160 degrees C for 7 minutes. While the beans are roasting, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":7,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6098f9d5cfe25b2dcca758b1','6098f7dc6aa4baac08ff6ef7',5,'p4- prepare the ingredients','For Chicken patty & green beans salad, wash and finely chop a tablespoon of mint leaves. Wash and finely chop a tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash and finely chop a tablespoon of parsley. Wash, pat dry and roughly shred 1/4 cup of iceberg lettuce. Wash, pat dry and roughly shred 1/4 cup of leaf lettuce. Wash, pat dry and roughly shred 1/4 cup of lolo roso lettuce. Wash and dice 1/4 cup of green capsicum. Wash and dice 1/4 cup of yellow bell pepper. Wash and dice 1/4 cup of red bell pepper. Next, add in the chopped mixed bell peppers to a mixing bowl and season it with a 1/4 teaspoon of salt and 1/4 teaspoon of black pepper powder. Mix it well and set it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6098fa536aa4baac08ff6efa','6098f7dc6aa4baac08ff6ef7',6,'p5- clean the chicken and prepare the ingredients for mirepoix','For Chicken patty & green beans salad, peel, wash, and finely chop half a cup of onions. Peel, wash, and finely chop half a cup of carrots. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of leek. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of celery. Peel and finely chop a teaspoon of garlic. Rinse and clean 200 grams of chicken mince.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6098fa9ecfe25b2dcca758b2','6098f7dc6aa4baac08ff6ef7',7,'p6- prepare the mirepoix','To prepare the Mirepoix for Chicken Patty and Green Beans Salad, heat a tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add a teaspoon of chopped garlic, 1/4 cup of chopped celery, and 1/4 cup of chopped leek. Next, add half a cup of chopped carrots followed by half a cup of chopped onions. Add half a teaspoon of thyme and mix it well. Stir and fry the vegetables over medium flame for 3-4 minutes until tender-crisp. Then, turn off the and remove it in a bowl and set it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6098fb4f867a6ad4a82a9a71','6098f7dc6aa4baac08ff6ef7',8,'p7- prepare the patty mixture','To prepare the patty mixture for Chicken patty & green beans salad, in a large bowl, add the prepared mirepoix followed by 200 grams of minced chicken and 1/4 cup of mashed boiled sweet potato. Add half a teaspoon of salt, half a teaspoon of pepper powder, half a teaspoon of aromat powder, and half a teaspoon of cumin powder. Add half a teaspoon of red chili powder, half a teaspoon of lime juice, a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves, and a teaspoon of oil. Mix it well and prepare a dough-like mixture. Then, divide it into equal portions and shape them into round flat patties as shown.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('6098fbc76aa4baac08ff6efb','6098f7dc6aa4baac08ff6ef7',9,'m1- cook the chicken patties','To make the chicken patties for Chicken patty & green beans salad, grease the grill pan with a tablespoon of cooking oil and heat it up for a minute. Then, place the prepared patties onto the pan and grill them on each side for 2-3 minutes until evenly browned. After that, turn off the flame and remove the patties onto a plate.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6098fc29867a6ad4a82a9a72','6098f7dc6aa4baac08ff6ef7',10,'m2- make the tahini sauce','To make the Tahini sauce for Chicken patty & green beans salad, add 1/4 cup of hung curd to a bowl. Add in 1/4 teaspoon of black pepper powder, 1/4 teaspoon of salt, and a tablespoon of chopped parsley followed by 2 teaspoons of chopped mint leaves. Add 2 teaspoons of tahini along with 2 tablespoons of water and mix it well. Add half a teaspoon of garlic paste and mix it well to prepare the sauce.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6098fcae867a6ad4a82a9a73','6098f7dc6aa4baac08ff6ef7',11,'m3- Assemble the Salad. Garnish & Serve','To assemble the Chicken patty & green beans salad, layer the salad bowl with 1/4 cup of chopped iceberg, lollo rosso, and green lettuce. Top it with the marinated bell peppers, roasted beans, and chickpea patties. Garnish the salad with roasted peanuts, pumpkin seeds, sunflower seeds, and sesame seeds. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('609a2c78cfe25b2dcca758bd','609a2b64cfe25b2dcca758bc',1,'p1- slice cucumber and prepare the other ingredients','For cucumber ginger and fennel salad, wash and cut a medium-sized English cucumber lengthwise into halves. Then, finely slice half a cup of cucumber. Wash, peel, and slice half a cup of carrots. wash and pluck 5 curry leaves. Wash, peel, and finely chop a 1-inch piece of ginger. Wash and finely chop 1 green chili. Wash and finely chop a tablespoon of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('609a2ced6aa4baac08ff6f00','609a2b64cfe25b2dcca758bc',2,'m1- combine the ingredients and prepare the salad','To make cucumber ginger and fennel salad, take a mixing bowl and add half a cup of sliced cucumber followed by half a cup of sliced carrot. Next, add in 1-inch piece of chopped ginger, 1 chopped green chili, half a teaspoon of black salt 0.5 tsp salt, 0.5 tsp fennel powder, half a teaspoon of cumin powder, and half a teaspoon of chat masala. Add 1/4 teaspoon of salt, half a teaspoon of dry ginger powder, and 1 tsp lemon juice along with a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves. Mix it well and transfer it to a serving bowl.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('609a2d506aa4baac08ff6f01','609a2b64cfe25b2dcca758bc',3,'m2- Add the tempering. Garnish and Serve','To make the tempering for cucumber ginger and fennel salad, heat a tempering pan and add 1 tsp oil, allow it to become hot, and then add half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, 0.5 tsp chana dal. 1 dry red chili, a pinch of asafoetida and curry leaves. Then, allow it to splutter for a few seconds. After that, Turn off the flame and add the tempering to the prepared salad. Serve','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('609b7ab776deac86bca5cdb6','609b7a456aa4baac08ff6f0b',1,'p1- prep the ingredients','For cucumber kachumber salad, wash 1 cup English cucumber, remove the seeds and cut the cucumber into medium size dices. Wash and finely chop half a cup of tomatoes. Wash and finely chop a tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash and finely chop 1 green chili.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('609b7bfa6aa4baac08ff6f0c','609b7a456aa4baac08ff6f0b',2,'m1- combine the ingredients and serve the salad','To make cucumber kachumber salad, in a mixing bowl, add 1 cup of diced cucumber followed by half a cup of diced tomatoes. Next, add 1 nos chopped green chili, add 0.5 tsp salt, add 0.5 tsp cumin powder, 0.5 tsp chili powder, add 0.5 tsp chaat masala, add 1 tsp lemon juice, add a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves. Mix it well and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('609b8dc46aa4baac08ff6f10','609b8d696aa4baac08ff6f0f',1,'p1- boil the sweet potato','To boil the sweet potato for Chicken Fattoush Salad with Zatar Dressing, wash a medium-sized sweet potato and add it to pressure along with 2 cups of water. Cover the cooker with a lid and pressure cook it over a high flame until one whistle. After the first whistle, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook it for another 5 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside to depressurize it naturally. After that, remove the boiled sweet potato on a plate and gently peel off the skin. Then, mash it well using a fork. While the sweet potato boils, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('609b8e3976deac86bca5cdbb','609b8d696aa4baac08ff6f0f',2,'p2- marinate the chicken','To marinate the chicken for chicken fattoush salad with zaatar dressing, first, peel and finely chop 2 teaspoons of garlic, Wash a lemon and zest half a teaspoon of lemon zest. Rinse and clean 200 grams of boneless chicken breast. Next, to marinate the chicken, place the chicken breast in a mixing dish. Add 0.5 tsp salt, add 0.5 tsp pepper powder, add 0.5 tsp mustard paste, a teaspoon of chopped garlic, half a teaspoon of thyme, and  1 tsp of sumac powder. Rub the marinade on each side of the chicken such that the meat is evenly coated with the marinade. Then, set it aside and let it marinate for 20 minutes. While the chicken marinates, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('609b8e976aa4baac08ff6f11','609b8d696aa4baac08ff6f0f',3,'p3- prepare the ingredients','For chicken fattoush salad with zaatar dressing, wash and slice 1/4 cup of red bell pepper. Wash and slice 1/4 cup of yellow bell pepper. Wash and slice 1/4 cup of green capsicum. Wash and cut 1/4 cup of English cucumber into triangles. Wash and cut 1/4 cup of cherry tomatoes into halves.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('609b8f1a76deac86bca5cdbc','609b8d696aa4baac08ff6f0f',4,'p4- prep the greens','For chicken fattoush salad with zaatar dressing, wash and pat dry 1/4 cup ice berg lettuce with a kitchen towel or a lettuce dryer; wash and pat dry 1/4 cup leaf lettuce; wash and pat dry 1/4 cup lolo roso lettuce, wash and finely chop a tablespoon of fresh basil leaves. Roughly slice or crumble 2 tablespoons of feta cheese. Wash and cut a lemon into halves and squeeze a tablespoon of lime juice in a bowl.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('609b8f566aa4baac08ff6f12','609b8d696aa4baac08ff6f0f',5,'m1- grill the marinated chicken','To grill the chicken for chicken fattoush salad with zaatar dressing, heat up a grill pan and grease it with a teaspoon of cooking oil. Then, place the marinated chicken breast onto the grill pan and grill it over medium flame for 2 minutes on each side. Then, remove it on a baking tray and set it inside the oven and allow it to grill for 6-8 mins at 180 degrees celsius until the chicken is tender-crisp. After that, remove it from the oven and slice the chicken into shreds.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('609b8fd076deac86bca5cdbd','609b8d696aa4baac08ff6f0f',6,'m2- make the bread croutons','To make the croutons for Chicken fattoush salad with zatar dressing, first, slice off the brown edges of 2 slices of sandwich bread, then cut the slices into 5mm dices. Next, heat a teaspoon of cooking oil in a pan over a medium flame. Then, add the bread dices followed by half a teaspoon of chopped garlic. Season it with half a teaspoon of black pepper powder. Add in a tablespoon of chopped basil and toss it over medium flame for 3-4 mins until the bread becomes golden brown and crisp.  After that, turn off the flame and keep the croutons aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('609b909d6aa4baac08ff6f13','609b8d696aa4baac08ff6f0f',7,'m3- make the zatar dressing','To make the dressing for Chicken Fattoush Salad with Zatar Dressing, take a blender jar and add 1/4 cup of the prepared sweet potato paste followed by a tablespoon of lime juice and a teaspoon of mustard paste. Next add 2 teaspoons of honey, a teaspoon of olive oil, half a teaspoon of salt, half a teaspoon of black pepper powder, 2 teaspoons of zatar powder, and 2 tablespoons of water. Cover the jar with the lid and blitz it into a fine sauce.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('609b912039154e5888e26e1c','609b8d696aa4baac08ff6f0f',8,'m4- Assemble the salad. Garnish & Serve','To assemble the Chicken Fattoush Salad with Zatar Dressing, in a mixing bowl add 1/4 cup of sliced mixed bell peppers, 1/4 cup of cucumber triangles, and 1/4 cup of sliced cherry tomatoes. Add a tablespoon of green pitted olives and toss the vegetables together. Next, lay out the mixed lettuce over the serving platter. Add the tossed vegetable mix and grilled sumac chicken. Garnish the salad with bread croutons and feta cheese. Serve it along with the prepared zatar dressing.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('609cf4e376deac86bca5cdc4','609cf47b76deac86bca5cdc3',1,'ap1- soak the foxtail millet','For Jamaican Tofu Salad, add half a cup of foxtail millet in a bowl and soak it in 2 cups of water for 6 hours. While the millet is cooking, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('609cf5466aa4baac08ff6f19','609cf47b76deac86bca5cdc3',2,'p1- simmer the soaked foxtail millet','To prepare the foxtail millet for Jamaican Tofu Salad, boil 2.5 cups of water in a deep bottom pan over a high flame. As the water comes to a boil, add the soaked foxtail millet along with half a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Then, cover it with a lid and allow it to cook over medium flame for 8 minutes until all the water is completely absorbed. Then, turn off the flame and set it aside. While the millet is simmering, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('609cf5c876deac86bca5cdc5','609cf47b76deac86bca5cdc3',3,'p2- prep and roast the sweet potato','To make the roasted sweet potato, first, peel, wash, and dice 1/4 cup of sweet potato into small cubes. Then, place it in a baking dish. Add 1/4 teaspoon of salt, 1/2 teaspoon of black pepper powder, half a teaspoon of rosemary, and half a teaspoon of cooking oil. Mix it well and coat the sweet potato evenly with the marinate. Then, set it inside the oven and bake it at 160 degrees Celcius for 15-20 minutes. While the sweet potato is being roasted, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('609cf65139154e5888e26e25','609cf47b76deac86bca5cdc3',4,'p3- prepare the ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Jamaican Tofu Salad, peel, wash and finely chop half a cup of onions. Peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of carrot. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of celery. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of leek. Peel and finely chop 2 teaspoons of garlic. wash, peel and finely chop a 1-inch piece of ginger. Wash and finely chop 1 fresh red chili. Cut 1 cup of tofu into thick slices','prep_method','{"active_time":17,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('609cf6e36aa4baac08ff6f1a','609cf47b76deac86bca5cdc3',5,'p4- prep the mirepoix for jamaican marinade','For the Jamaican Marinade, heat a tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Next, add half a cup of chopped onions followed by 1/4 cup of chopped carrots and 1/4 cup of chopped celery. Add 1/4 cup of chopped leek and saute the vegetables over medium flame for 3-4 minutes until it turns slightly translucent. Then, turn off the flame and remove it in a bowl.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('609cf7e639154e5888e26e26','609cf47b76deac86bca5cdc3',6,'p5- marinate the tofu','To marinate the tofu, first prepare the Jamaican marinade, for this, in a blender jar, add half a teaspoon of black pepper powder, half a teaspoon of red chili powder, half a teaspoon of cumin powder, half a teaspoon of cinnamon powder, and half a teaspoon of star anise powder. Next, add a teaspoon of chopped garlic followed by a 1-inch piece of chopped ginger, half a teaspoon of dark soy sauce and sauteed vegetables. Add 1 chopped fresh red chili along with a teaspoon of cooking oil, and blend it well into a smooth marinade. Next, add the sliced tofu to a mixing dish and season it with half a teaspoon of salt. Then, add the prepared marinade to the sliced tofu and coat it well on each side with the marinade and set it aside for 15 minutes','prep_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('609cf88076deac86bca5cdc6','609cf47b76deac86bca5cdc3',7,'p6- prep the greens and other ingredients','For Jamaican Tofu Salad, wash and cut 1/4 cup of English cucumber into triangles. Wash and cut 1/4 cup of cherry tomatoes into halves. Wash, pat dry and roughly shred 1/4 cup of leaf lettuce. Wash, pat dry and roughly shred 1/4 cup of rocket lettuce. Wash and dice 1/4 cup of yellow zucchini. Wash and cut the pomegranate into halves and peel 1/4 cup of pomegranate seeds. Wash and finely chop a tablespoon of mint leaves','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('609cf8bf76deac86bca5cdc7','609cf47b76deac86bca5cdc3',8,'m1- grill the tofu','To grill, the tofu for Jamaican tofu salad, heat up a grill pan and grease it with 0.5 tsp oil and place the marinated tofu, and grill it on a medium flame for 2-3 minutes on each side or until the tofu becomes golden brown. Turn off the flame and then cut them into dices. and keep aside','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('609cf9256aa4baac08ff6f1b','609cf47b76deac86bca5cdc3',9,'m2- char the zucchini','To make the roasted Zucchini for Jamaican Tofu salad, heat a pan and add 0.5 tsp oil and allow it to become hot, then add a teaspoon of chopped garlic followed by 1/4 cup of the zucchini triangles Next, add 0.5 tsp salt, add 0.5 tsp pepper powder, 0.5 tsp thyme and saute it for over medium flame for 3-4 minutes until it becomes slightly golden brown. After that, Turn off the flame and keep aside','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('609cf9b039154e5888e26e27','609cf47b76deac86bca5cdc3',10,'m3- prepare the  dressing','To prepare the dressing for Jamaican Tofu Salad, take a bowl and add 1 tsp cornflour and 2 tsp water and whisk it well into a smooth paste. Then take a blender jar and add 2 tbsp balsamic vinegar, add 2 tsp honey, add 1 tsp dijon mustard paste, add 2 tsp salad oil, add the cornflour slurry, add 0.5 tsp salt, add 0.5 tsp pepper powder, add 2 tablespoons water and blitz it into a smooth sauce. Keep aside','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('609cfa0e76deac86bca5cdc8','609cf47b76deac86bca5cdc3',11,'m4- Assemble the salad and serve','To assemble the Jamaican Tofu Salad, In a salad bowl lay out the rocket and leaf lettuce as the base. Then, top it with 1/4 cup of cherry tomatoes and cooked foxtail millet. Next, add 1/4 cup of cucumber triangles, roasted sweet potatoes, and sauteed zucchini. Then mix it together. Add the sliced Jamaican tofu. Garnish it with 1 tsp sunflower seeds, add 1 tsp pumpkin seeds, pomegranate seeds, and mint leaves. Serve it along with the prepared dressing','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60a23a3a39154e5888e26e2f','60a239eb76deac86bca5cdd4',1,'ap1- soak the paneer in brine','For the roasted vegetable salad, first, cut 1 cup of paneer into thick slices. Next, add 2 cups of water in a bowl with 1/4 tsp of salt and mix it well. Then, add the sliced paneer and allow it to soak for 2 hrs. While the paneer is soaking, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":120,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60a23a9d6aa4baac08ff6f55','60a239eb76deac86bca5cdd4',2,'ap2- soak the Aubergines','For the roasted vegetable salad, wash and slice 1/4 cup of aubergines into rondelles. Then, add them to a large bowl. Add 2 cups of water and 1/4 tsp of salt and allow it to soak in salt water for 30 mins. While it soaks, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":30,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60a23b276aa4baac08ff6f56','60a239eb76deac86bca5cdd4',3,'p1- slice and roast the shallots','To prepare the balsamic roasted onions for roasted vegetable salad, peel and slice 1/2 cup of shallots. Then, arrange the shallots in a baking dish. Add  1/4 tsp salt, add 1/4 tsp pepper powder, 1/4 tsp thyme, 2 teaspoons of balsamic vinegar, and a teaspoon of cooking oil. Mix it well and set it inside the oven and bake it at 160 degrees Celcius for 45 minutes. While the onions are being roasted, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":45,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('60a23b8f76deac86bca5cdd5','60a239eb76deac86bca5cdd4',4,'p2- slice and roast the carrots','To make the roasted carrots for Roasted Vegetable Salad, first, wash, peel and cut half a cup of carrots into diamonds. Next, add the carrots to a baking dish. Add 1/4 teaspoon of paprika powder, 1/4 teaspoon of fennel powder, 1/4 teaspoon of salt, and half a teaspoon of cooking oil. Mix it well and set it inside the oven and roast the carrots at 180 degrees Celcius for 20 minutes. While the carrots are roasting, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60a23bd76aa4baac08ff6f57','60a239eb76deac86bca5cdd4',5,'p3- boil the sweet potato','To boil the sweet potato for Roasted Vegetable salad, wash a medium sized sweet potato well with water and add it to a pressure cooker along with 2 cups of water. Cover the cooker with a lid and pressure cook it over a high flame until one whistle. After that, reduce the flame to low and allow it to cook for another 5 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. After that, take out the boiled sweet potato from the cooker and gently peel off the skin and mash it well using a fork. While the sweet potato is boiling please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60a23c526aa4baac08ff6f58','60a239eb76deac86bca5cdd4',6,'p4- prep the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Roasted vegetable salad, wash, pat dry, and roughly shred 1/4 cup of leaf lettuce. Wash, pat dry and roughly shred 1/4 cup of rocket lettuce. Wash, pat dry and roughly shred 1/4 cup of lolo roso lettuce. Make sure to dry off the lettuce leaves completely before you shred it or the dressing won''t stick to it. Peel and chop 2 teaspoons of garlic. Wash 1/4 cup of cherry tomatoes. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of parsley','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60a23cc76aa4baac08ff6f59','60a239eb76deac86bca5cdd4',7,'m1- prepare the couscous','To prepare the couscous for Roasted vegetable salad, first, boil 2 cups of water in a saucepan over high fame for 2-3 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the hot water aside. Next, add 1/4 cup of couscous to a deep bottom pan. Add half a teaspoon of salt, 1/4 teaspoon of black pepper powder, a tablespoon of chopped parsley, and a teaspoon of cooking oil. Mix it well and add 2 cups of boiled hot water. Stir it well and cover it with a lid and allow the couscous to soak in hot water for 15 minutes or until it fluffs up and has absorbed all the water. While it soaks, please move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60a23d1e76deac86bca5cdd6','60a239eb76deac86bca5cdd4',8,'m2- grill the aubergines','To grill the aubergines for roasted vegetable salad, heat up a grill pan and add 0.5 tsp oil, allow it to become hot, and then add the soaked aubergine slices, followed by 1/4 tsp of salt and 1/4 tsp of black pepper powder and saute for 2-3 mins or until they are slightly charred. Then, turn off the flame and remove it in a bowl, and set it aside','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('60a23d7439154e5888e26e30','60a239eb76deac86bca5cdd4',9,'m3- grill the paneer','To grill the paneer for Roasted Vegetable Salad, heat up a grill pan with a teaspoon of cooking oil. Add the brined paneer slices and cook it for 2 mins on each side or until the grill marks appear. Then, turn off the flame and cut them into slices.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60a23dd776deac86bca5cdd7','60a239eb76deac86bca5cdd4',10,'m4- make the blistered tomatoes','To make the blistered tomatoes for Roasted Vegetable Salad, heat a teaspoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add 1/4 cup of cherry tomatoes followed by 1/4 teaspoon of salt, 1/4 teaspoon of black pepper powder, a teaspoon of chopped garlic, and 1/4 teaspoon of oregano. Next, add a teaspoon of balsamic vinegar and saute the tomatoes over medium-high flame for 3-4 minutes until the tomatoes are slightly charred. Then, turn off the flame and remove them in a bowl.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60a23e7876deac86bca5cdd8','60a239eb76deac86bca5cdd4',11,'m5- prepare the dressing','To prepare the dressing for Roasted Vegetable Salad, in a bowl, add a tablespoon of balsamic vinegar, followed by a teaspoon of apple cider vinegar and a tablespoon of date syrup. Next, add 2 tablespoons of water and mix it well. Add 1/4 teaspoon of salt, 1/4 teaspoon of black pepper powder, and a teaspoon of mustard sauce followed by 1/4 cup of boiled sweet potato paste and a tablespoon of olive oil. Mix it well using a whisk and prepare the dressing.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60a23eb876deac86bca5cdd9','60a239eb76deac86bca5cdd4',12,'m6- assemble the salad and serve','To assemble the Roasted Vegetable Salad, in a salad bowl, lay out the shredded leaf, and lolo roso lettuce to form the base. Next, top it with the cooked couscous, roasted carrots, roasted onions, grilled aubergines, and salted cottage cheese slices. Next, add the blistered tomatoes and rocket lettuce. Pour the prepared dressing and garnish the salad with pumpkin seeds. Serve','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60a2442639154e5888e26e37','60a243af76deac86bca5cde4',1,'p1- slice and blanch the carrots','For carrot pineapple and pomegranate salad, peel, wash and cut 3/4 cup of carrots into diamonds. Next, to blanch the carrots, first, take a bowl and fill it with cold water, and set it aside. Then, boil 2 cups of water in a pot with a pinch of salt over medium-high flame. As the water comes to a boil, add 3/4 cup of sliced carrots and remove it within 1-2 minutes. Transfer it to the cold water bowl to stop the cooking process. Then, strain the carrots and set them aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('60a2448439154e5888e26e38','60a243af76deac86bca5cde4',2,'p2- prepare the ingredients','For carrot pineapple and pomegranate salad, peel 0.5 cup pineapple and cut them into half, remove the core and cut the pineapple into small cubes; Wash and cut the pomegranate into halves, then peel 1/4 cup of pomegranate seeds into a bowl. wash and pluck 5 mint leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60a244e839154e5888e26e39','60a243af76deac86bca5cde4',3,'m1- Assemble the Salad. Refrigerate and Serve.','To make carrot pineapple and pomegranate salad, in a mixing bowl add half a cup of diced pineapple followed by 3/4 cup of blanched carrots and 1/4 cup of pomegranate seeds. Next, add 2 teaspoons of honey, a teaspoon of black salt, half a teaspoon of chili flakes, a teaspoon of lime juice, 5 mint leaves, and mix it well. After that, refrigerate the salad for 30 minutes. Then, plate the salad in a serving bowl and serve chilled.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":30,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60a3994639154e5888e26e3d','60a398a539154e5888e26e3c',1,'p1- marinate the chicken','To marinate the chicken for Mediterranean balsamic chicken salad, first, peel and finely chop 2 teaspoons of garlic. Next, rinse and clean 200 grams of boneless chicken breast and place it in a mixing glass dish. Then, add 1/4 tsp salt, add 1/4 tsp pepper powder, 0.5 tsp dijon mustard paste, 1/4 tsp thyme, a teaspoon of chopped garlic, and 1 tablespoon of balsamic vinegar.  Then, rub the marinade well on each side of the chicken and allow it to marinate for 20 minutes. While the chicken marinates, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60a399d376deac86bca5cde6','60a398a539154e5888e26e3c',2,'p2- marinate and roast the bell peppers','To prepare the roasted bell peppers for Mediterranean balsamic chicken salad, wash and cut 1/4 cup of red bell pepper into triangles. Wash and cut 1/4 cup of green bell pepper into triangles. Wash and cut 1/4 cup of yellow capsicum into triangles. Next, add in the chopped bell peppers to the baking dish. Marinate it with add 1/4 tsp salt, add 1/4 tsp pepper powder, add 1/4 tsp oregano herbs, add 1 tsp oil and toss it well. Then, set it inside the oven and roast the bell peppers at 180 degrees for 20 minutes. While the bell peppers are being grilled, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60a39a696aa4baac08ff6f68','60a398a539154e5888e26e3c',3,'p3- slice and roast the tomato wedges','To prepare the roasted tomato wedges for Mediterranean balsamic chicken salad, first, wash and cut half a cup of tomato into wedges. Next, arrange the tomato wedges onto a baking tray. Add half a teaspoon of salt, 1/4 teaspoon of black pepper powder, a teaspoon of chopped garlic, 1/4 teaspoon of oregano, 1 tablespoon of balsamic vinegar, and a teaspoon of oil. Mix it well and evenly coat the wedges in the marinade. Then, set it inside the oven and roast the wedges at 180 degrees Celcius for 20 minutes or until tomato wedges are slightly charred. While the tomato wedges are being charred, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('60a39aaa39154e5888e26e3e','60a398a539154e5888e26e3c',4,'p4- blanch broccoli','To blanch the broccoli for Mediterranean balsamic chicken salad, first, wash and cut half a cup of broccoli into small florets. Next, boil 3 cups of water in a pan over a high flame. When the water starts boiling add the broccoli florets and remove them within 1-2 mins and transfer them to the cold water bowl to stop the cooking process. Keep Aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60a39ae539154e5888e26e3f','60a398a539154e5888e26e3c',5,'p5- blanch the beans','To blanch the beans for Mediterranean Balsamic Chicken Salad, first, wash and cut 1/4 cup of haricot beans into 2-inch long pieces. Next, add 2 cups of water to a saucepan along with 1/4 teaspoon of salt and bring it to a rolling boil. Then, add the sliced beans and boil them over medium flame for 3-4 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and transfer the blanched beans to the cold water to prevent them from cooking further. Soak the beans in cold water for a minute, then remove them in a separate bowl and set them aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60a39b7f39154e5888e26e40','60a398a539154e5888e26e3c',6,'p6- Prepare the ingredients and caramalise the walnuts','To prep, the ingredients for Mediterranean Balsamic Chicken Salad, wash, pat dry, and roughly shred 1/4 cup of leaf lettuce. Wash, pat dry and roughly shred 1/4 cup of rocket lettuce. Wash, pat dry and roughly shred 1/4 cup of iceberg lettuce. Wash and finely chop a tablespoon of basil leaves. Next, to caramelize the walnuts, take a pan and heat 2 tablespoons of honey, then add 1 tbsp walnut and allow it to caramelize on a medium flame for 3 mins or until it becomes dry and sticky. Then take it off the flame and keep it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60a39be739154e5888e26e41','60a398a539154e5888e26e3c',7,'p7- prepare the cornflour slurry','To prepare the cornflour slurry for Mediterranean Balsamic Chicken Salad, Take a bowl and add 2 teaspoons of cornflour and 1/4 cup of water and mix it well to make cornflour slurry, now take a pan and add the cornflour slurry in it and cook it on a medium flame for 30 secs or until it starts to thicken and then stir vigorously and turn off the flame. Allow it to cool and set it aside','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60a39c286aa4baac08ff6f69','60a398a539154e5888e26e3c',8,'m1- grill the chicken','To grill the chicken for Mediterranean Balsamic Chicken Salad, heat up a grill pan and grease it with half a teaspoon of cooking oil. Then, place the marinated chicken breast onto the grill pan and grill it over medium flame for 2 minutes on each side. Then, remove it on a baking tray and set it inside the oven and allow it to grill for 6 mins at 160 degrees celsius until the chicken is tender-crisp. After that, remove it from the oven and slice the chicken into shreds.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('60a39ca26aa4baac08ff6f6a','60a398a539154e5888e26e3c',9,'m2- prepare the dressing','To prepare the dressing for Mediterranean Balsamic Chicken Salad, in a blender jar, add 2 tablespoons of balsamic vinegar, 2 tsp honey, 1 tsp dijon mustard paste, 2 tsp salad oil, cornflour slurry, 1/4 tsp salt, add 1/4 tsp pepper powder and 3 tbsp water. Cover the jar with the lid and blitz it into a smooth dressing.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60a39cda76deac86bca5cde7','60a398a539154e5888e26e3c',10,'m3- Assemble the salad. Garnish & Serve','To assemble the Mediterranean Balsamic Chicken Salad, in a mixing bowl, add the blanched beans, roasted tomato wedges, blanched broccoli, and roasted bell peppers. Mix it well. Then, place the lettuce mix onto a serving platter as a base, add the vegetable mix, Then top it with diced grilled chicken and garnish it with caramelized walnuts and basil leaves. Serve it along with the dressing.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60a3a6b376deac86bca5cdf3','60a3a64a39154e5888e26e47',1,'ap1- Shred the cabbage and grate raw papaya','For cabbage and raw papaya salad, peel and wash and cut half a cup of carrots into juliennes. Wash, peel, and grate 1/4 cup of raw papaya. Wash 0.5 cup green cabbage and cut them into fine shreds.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60a3a71976deac86bca5cdf4','60a3a64a39154e5888e26e47',2,'ap2- marinate the vegetables and leave them to sweat','For cabbage and raw papaya salad, take a mixing bowl and add and half a cup of shredded cabbage, half a cup of carrot juliennes, and 1/4 cup of grated raw papaya. Next, add in 2 teaspoons of vinegar, a teaspoon of jaggery, and half a teaspoon of salt. Mix it well and allow it to marinate for 1 hour. While the vegetables marinate, please move on to the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":60,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60a3a78739154e5888e26e48','60a3a64a39154e5888e26e47',3,'p1- prep the ingredients','For cabbage and raw papaya salad, wash 5 nos curry leaves well with water. Wash and finely chop 1 tbsp of coriander leaves. Next, squeeze out the water from the marinated vegetables and strain them.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('60a3a7f96aa4baac08ff6f72','60a3a64a39154e5888e26e47',4,'m1- combine the ingredients and prepare the salad','To make Cabbage and Raw Papaya Salad, add the marinated vegetables to a mixing bowl. Next, add in half a teaspoon of black salt, 1/4 teaspoon of Kashmiri red chili powder, and half a teaspoon of cumin powder. Mix it well and transfer the salad to a serving bowl.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60a3a86039154e5888e26e49','60a3a64a39154e5888e26e47',5,'m2- add the tempering to the salad and serve','To make the tempering for cabbage and raw papaya salad, heat a pan and add 1 tsp oil, allow it to become hot, and then add a pinch of hing, add 0.5 tsp mustard seeds, and 5 curry leaves. Saute and allow it to splutter for a few seconds. Then, turn off the flame and the tempering instantly to the prepared salad. Garnish it with chopped coriander leaves and serve','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60a4eb7b39154e5888e26e4b','60a4eb4f76deac86bca5cdfa',1,'ap1- soak the rajma','For Caribbean chicken and corn salad, soak 1/4 cup of rajma in 2 cups of water for 8-10 hours. While the rajma soaks, please move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":480,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60a4eba876deac86bca5cdfb','60a4eb4f76deac86bca5cdfa',2,'p1- boil the rajma','To boil the kidney beans for Caribbean Chicken and Corn Salad, add 1/4 cup of soaked kidney beans to a pressure cooker along with 1/4 teaspoon of salt and 2 cups of water. Cover it with a lid and pressure cook the beans over high flame until three whistles. After that, allow it to cook over low flame for 8 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and strain the boiled rajma in a bowl. Then, mash it well and set it aside. While the kidney beans are boiling, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":18,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60a4ebe639154e5888e26e4c','60a4eb4f76deac86bca5cdfa',3,'p2- prepare the pumpkin puree','To prepare the pumpkin puree for Caribbean Chicken and Corn Salad, first, peel, wash and roughly dice 1/4 cup of pumpkin. Take a heavy bottom vessel and boil 2 cups of water, add 1/4 tsp salt, and bring to boil. When the water is boiling add the cubed pumpkin and allow to boil for 5 mins or until soft. Strain the boiled pumpkin pieces. Then take a blender jar, add the boiled pumpkin and blitz it into a smooth puree.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('60a4ec1e76deac86bca5cdfc','60a4eb4f76deac86bca5cdfa',4,'p3- prepare the batter for corn bread','To prepare the batter for corn bread for Caribbean Chicken and Corn Salad, in a mixing bowl, add 3/4 cup of maize flour followed by 1/4 cup of whole wheat flour. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of baking powder, 1/4 teaspoon of salt, 1/4 teaspoon of cinnamon powder, 1/4 teaspoon of thyme, and 1/4 teaspoon of cayenne pepper and mix it well. Next, in a separate bowl, add 1/4 cup of pumpkin puree, 3 tablespoons of soya milk, 1 tsp of coconut oil, and a teaspoon of honey. Mix it well using a whisk and add the flour mix to it. Then, combine the batter well using a whisk to avoid any lumps and prepare a semi-thick batter','prep_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60a4ec5676deac86bca5cdfd','60a4eb4f76deac86bca5cdfa',5,'p4- bake the corn bread','To bake the corn bread, first, grease a baking mold with a teaspoon of oil. Then, line it with parchment paper. Then, pour in the prepared corn bread batter and level it in the mold using a spatula. Then, set it inside the oven and bake the bread at 180 degrees Celcius for 20-25 minutes. While it is baking, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":25,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60a4ec8376deac86bca5cdfe','60a4eb4f76deac86bca5cdfa',6,'p5- marinate the chicken','To marinate the chicken for Caribbean Chicken and Corn Salad, first, rinse and clean 100 grams of boneless chicken cubes well with water. Then, place them in a mixing bowl and add a teaspoon of jamaican all spice powder. Mix it well and coat the chicken pieces well with the seasoning. Then allow it to marinate for 20 minutes. While the chicken marinates, please move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60a4ecc276deac86bca5cdff','60a4eb4f76deac86bca5cdfa',7,'p6- blanch the sweet corn kernels','To blanch the sweet corn kernels for Caribbean Chicken and corn salad, first, boil 2 cups of water in a pan over high flame for 1-2 minutes. Then, add 3/4 cup of corn kernels and boil them over medium flame for 3-4 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and strain the blanched corns in a bowl, and set them aside. While the corns are blanching, please move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":4,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60a4ecec6aa4baac08ff6f78','60a4eb4f76deac86bca5cdfa',8,'p7- prepare the ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Caribbean Chicken and Corn Salad, peel and finely chop 2 teaspoons of garlic. Wash and finely chop 3 nos green chilies. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of celery. Wash, peel, and finely chop 1/4 cup of carrot. Wash and dice half a cup of tomatoes. Wash and finely chop a tablespoon of mint leaves','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('60a4ed1e6aa4baac08ff6f79','60a4eb4f76deac86bca5cdfa',9,'p8- prepare the ingredients','Next, wash and finely chop 1/2 cup of green bell pepper. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of green zucchini. Wash and finely chop a tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of spring onion greens. Next, after baking the cornbread, carefully take it out from the oven and allow it to slightly cool down. Then, remove the bread from the mold and slice it into rectangular pieces as shown','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60a4ed6276deac86bca5ce00','60a4eb4f76deac86bca5cdfa',10,'m1- make the caribbean chili','To make the Caribbean Chili for Caribbean Chicken and Corn Salad, heat a tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Then, add 2 teaspoons of chopped garlic followed by 2 chopped green chilies and saute it over medium flame for a minute. Next, add 2 tablespoons of chopped celery, 1/4 cup of chopped carrot, 1/4 cup of chopped green capsicum and 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes. Add 1/4 cup of chopped green zucchini and fry the vegetables over medium-high flame for 2-3 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60a4ed9b6aa4baac08ff6f7a','60a4eb4f76deac86bca5cdfa',11,'m2- add the chicken, boiled rajma and simmer','Next, add half a  teaspoon of red chili powder, 1 teaspoon of cumin powder, 1/2 teaspoon of black pepper powder, half a teaspoon of salt, and 1/4 teaspoon of aromat powder. Mix it well and fry the vegetables for another 1-2 minutes. Next, add the marinated chicken and fry it with the vegetables for 2-3 minutes. Then, add 3/4 cup of water followed by the boiled rajma and mix it well. Simmer the chicken for 6-8 minutes, until it is cooked through. Then, turn off the flame and garnish it with a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves. While the chicken is simmering, please move onto the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60a4edc976deac86bca5ce01','60a4eb4f76deac86bca5cdfa',12,'m3- Make the corn salad','To make the corn salad for Caribbean Chicken and Corn Salad, 3/4 cup of blanched corn kernels to a mixing bowl. Add 2 tablespoons of spring onion greens, 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves, 1/4 cup of chopped green bell pepper followed by 1 chopped green chili, half a teaspoon of salt, and 1 teaspoon of lime juice. Mix it well and set it aside','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60a4edfb39154e5888e26e4d','60a4eb4f76deac86bca5cdfa',13,'m4- Make the tomato feta salad','To make Tomato feta salad for Caribbean Chicken and Corn salad, add 1/4 cup of diced tomatoes to a mixing bowl. Add a tablespoon of chopped mint and parsley followed by 1/4 teaspoon of black pepper powder and a teaspoon of peanuts, white sesame seeds, sunflower, and pumpkin seeds. Add a teaspoon of lime juice, 1/4 teaspoon of salt and mix it well.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('60a4ee3939154e5888e26e4e','60a4eb4f76deac86bca5cdfa',14,'m5- Assemble the salad and serve','To assemble the Caribbean Chicken and Corn Salad, plate the Caribbean chili chicken in a serving bowl. Plate the prepared corn salad and serve it along with the prepared cornbread and tomato feta salad.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60a4f3f176deac86bca5ce0b','60a4f3c46aa4baac08ff6f7d',1,'ap1- soak the peanuts','For moongfali salad, take a bowl fill it with 2 cups of water and soak 3/4 cup of peanuts and allow it to soak for 8-10 hrs . While it soaks, please move on to the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":600,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60a4f44d6aa4baac08ff6f7e','60a4f3c46aa4baac08ff6f7d',2,'p1- prep the ingredients','For Moongfali salad, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup tomatoes; wash 0.5 cup English cucumber and cut them into triangles, wash and finely chop 1 tbsp coriander leaves','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60a4f49c76deac86bca5ce0c','60a4f3c46aa4baac08ff6f7d',3,'m1- combine the salad and serve','For moongfali salad, take a mixing bowl and add soaked peanuts, followed by half a cup of diced cucumber and 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes. Next, add 0.5 tsp chat masala, 0.5 tsp salt, 0.5 tsp black salt, 1 tsp lemon juice, add  Mix it well and garnish it with chopped coriander leaves.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60a61e236aa4baac08ff6f82','60a61dd139154e5888e26e59',1,'p1- soak the masoor dal and boil the sweet potato','For Mediterranean Balsamic Veg Salad, first, rinse half a cup of black masoor dal with water and soak it in 2 cups of water for 15 minutes. Next, to boil the sweet potato, wash a medium-sized sweet potato well with water and add it to a pressure cooker along with 2 cups of water. Cover the cooker with a lid and pressure cook it over a high flame until one whistle. After that, reduce the flame to low and allow it to cook for another 5 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the sweet potato is boiling and dal is soaking please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('60a6216676deac86bca5ce12','60a61dd139154e5888e26e59',2,'p2- prep the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Mediterranean Balsamic Veg Salad, first, wash and cut 1/4 cup of yellow bell pepper into juliennes. Wash and cut 1/4 cup of red bell pepper into juliennes. Wash, peel and cut 1/4  cup of carrot into diamonds. Wash and finely slice 1/4 cup of yellow zucchini. Wash and finely slice 1/4 cup of green zucchini. Wash and cut 1/4 cup of haricot beans into 2-inch pieces. Slice 1/4 cup of baby corns','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60a6268e6aa4baac08ff6f83','60a61dd139154e5888e26e59',3,'p3- boil the masoor dal','To boil the dal for Mediterranean Balsamic Veg Salad, add in 3 cups water to a deep bottom pan followed by a 1/4 teaspoon of salt. Mix it well and bring the water to a boil. Then, add half a cup of soaked masoor dal and cover it with a lid. Simmer the dal over medium flame for 8-10 minutes until tender. Make sure to cook the dal only till it is firm to the bite, avoid overcooking it. After that, turn off the flame and strain the boiled dal into a bowl and set it aside. While the dal is boiling, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60a626e66aa4baac08ff6f84','60a61dd139154e5888e26e59',4,'p4- blanch the beans and baby corns','To blanch the beans and baby corns for Mediterranean Balsamic Veg Salad, add 3 cups of water to a saucepan along with 1/4 teaspoon of salt and bring it to a rolling boil. Then, add the sliced beans and baby corns and boil them over medium flame for 3-4 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and transfer the blanched beans and baby corns to the cold water to prevent them from cooking further. Soak them in cold water for about a minute, then remove them in a separate bowl and set them aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60a6276f76deac86bca5ce13','60a61dd139154e5888e26e59',5,'p5- roast the vegetables','To roast the vegetables for Mediterranean Balsamic Veg Salad, in a baking dish, add 1/4 cup of carrot diamonds, 1/4 cup of sliced yellow bell pepper, 1/4 cup of sliced red bell pepper, 1/4 cup of sliced green zucchini, 1/4 cup of sliced yellow zucchini, 1/4 cup of blanched beans and baby corns. Next, add half a teaspoon of salt, half a teaspoon of pepper powder, half a teaspoon of paprika powder, and a teaspoon of balsamic vinegar followed by 1/2 teaspoon of rosemary. Mix it well and set the vegetable inside the oven to roast them at 180 degrees Celcius for 20 minutes. While the vegetables are being roasted, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60a627c676deac86bca5ce14','60a61dd139154e5888e26e59',6,'p6- boil the quinoa','To boil the quinoa for Mediterranean Balsamic Veg Salad, first, rinse 1/4 cup of quinoa well with water. Then, boil 3/4 cup of water in a pan with 1/4 teaspoon of salt. Then, add the rinsed quinoa and stir it well. Cover the pan with a lid and allow it to cook over medium-low flame for 10-12 minutes until the quinoa has absorbed all the water. Then, turn off the flame and set it aside. While the quinoa is simmering, please move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('60a628696aa4baac08ff6f85','60a61dd139154e5888e26e59',7,'p7- prep the greens','To prepare the ingredients for Mediterranean Balsamic Veg Salad, wash and dice 1/4 cup of English cucumber into triangles. Wash and dice 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of basil leaves. Wash, pat dry and roughly shred 1/4 cup of leaf lettuce. Wash, pat dry and roughly shred 1/4 cup of Lolo lettuce. Wash, pat dry and roughly shred 1/4 cup of iceberg lettuce. Wash and cut a lemon into halves. Then, squeeze 2 teaspoons of lime juice in a bowl. Wash and finely chop a teaspoon of parsley','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60a637be76deac86bca5ce15','60a61dd139154e5888e26e59',8,'m1- prepare the dressing','To prepare the dressing Mediterranean Balsamic Veg Salad, take a blender jar and add 2 teaspoons of chopped garlic, 1 tsp white wine vinegar, 2 tsp lemon juice,1 tsp dijon mustard paste, 1/4 cup of boiled sweet potato paste, 1 tbsp salad oil, and 3 tablespoons of water. Then, cover the jar with a lid and blend it well into a smooth dressing. Next, remove it in a bowl and add 1/4 teaspoon of oregano herbs and a teaspoon of chopped parsley. Mix it well and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60a637ef39154e5888e26e5a','60a61dd139154e5888e26e59',9,'m2- Assemble the salad & serve','To assemble the Mediterranean Balsamic Veg Salad, take a salad bowl and add the lettuce mix as a base, then add the boiled quinoa followed by the boiled masoor dal, and 1/4 cup of cucumber triangles. Next, add the balsamic roasted vegetables. Garnish the salad with black olives, curry leaves, a teaspoon of sunflower seeds, and diced tomatoes. Serve it along with the greek vinaigrette','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60a651ee39154e5888e26e62','60a651aa39154e5888e26e61',1,'p1- blanch the sweet corn kernels','To blanch the sweet corn kernels for Makai Shimla Mirch Salad, first, boil 2 cups of water in a pan over medium-high flame for 1-2 minutes. As the water comes to a boil, add 1 cup of sweet corn kernels and boil them over medium flame for 4-5 minutes until tender. Then, turn off the flame and remove the blanched corn kernels in a bowl and set them aside. While the corn kernels are being blanched, please move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60a6526576deac86bca5ce20','60a651aa39154e5888e26e61',2,'p2- prep the ingredients','To prep the ingredients for makai and Shimla Mirch salad, wash 1/4 cup green capsicum, cut it into half, remove the seeds and dice the capsicum; wash 1/4 cup red bell pepper, cut it into half, remove the seeds and dice the red bell pepper; wash 1/4 cup yellow bell pepper, cut it into half, remove the seeds and dice the yellow bell pepper. Wash and dice 1/4 cup of English cucumber. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of spring onion greens. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('60a652d476deac86bca5ce21','60a651aa39154e5888e26e61',3,'m1- Combine the ingredients and prepare the salad','To make the Makai Shimla Mirch Salad, add 1 cup of blanched sweet corn kernels to a mixing bowl followed by 1/4 cup of diced English cucumber, and 1/4 cup of diced yellow bell pepper. Next, add 1/4 cup of diced red bell pepper, 1/4 cup of diced green capsicum, and 2 tablespoons of chopped spring onion greens. Add 0.5 tsp salt, 0.5 tsp chat masala, 0.5 tsp cumin powder, add 0.5 tsp chili powder, and 1 tablespoon of lemon juice. Mix it well. Garnish with chopped coriander leaves and serve chilled.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60a6d11039154e5888e26e6f','60a6d0ba39154e5888e26e6e',1,'p1- slice and roast the garlic','To prepare the burnt garlic for Bhuna lehsan and Haricot Beans salad, first, preheat the oven to150 degrees celsius. Next, peel and slice 3 tablespoons of garlic. Then, add the sliced garlic to a baking dish and drizzle a teaspoon of cooking oil onto it. Then, set it inside the oven and roast the garlic at 150 degrees for 30 mins in the preheated oven until the garlic turns crisp and golden brown. While the garlic is being roasted move towards the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":30,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60a6d15d39154e5888e26e70','60a6d0ba39154e5888e26e6e',2,'p2- blanch the beans','To blanch the beans for Buna lesan and Haricot Beans Salad, first, wash and slice off the ends of 1 cup of haricot beans. Next, boil 3 cups of water with 1/4 teaspoon of salt in a pan over medium flame. As the water comes to a boil, add 3/4 cup of chopped haricot beans and let it boil for 3-4 minutes over medium flame. Then, turn off the flame and drain off the water from the blanched beans and soak them in an ice bath for 2 minutes. After that, strain the beans in a bowl and set them aside. While the beans are blanching, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60a6d1b576deac86bca5ce24','60a6d0ba39154e5888e26e6e',3,'p3- prepare the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Bhuna Lesan and Haricot Beans Salad, wash and cut 1/4 cup of yellow bell pepper into juliennes. Wash and cut 1/4 cup of red bell pepper into juliennes. Wash and chop 1 fresh green chili. Wash and finely chop a tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash and cut a lemon into halves and squeeze a tablespoon of lime juice in a bowl.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60a6d20539154e5888e26e71','60a6d0ba39154e5888e26e6e',4,'m1- Prepare the salad and serve','To make the Bhuna Lesan and Haricot Beans Salad, add the blanched beans to a mixing bowl. Next, add 1/4 cup of red yellow, and red bell pepper juliennes followed by the prepared burnt garlic. Add half a teaspoon of black peppercorns, 1 chopped green chili, a tablespoon of lime juice, half a teaspoon of cumin powder, and half a teaspoon of black salt. Next, add 3 tablespoons of curd, and a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves. Mix it well and plate the salad in a serving bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('60a6d57739154e5888e26e75','60a6d5066aa4baac08ff6f91',1,'p1- prep the ingredients','For Rocket Apple and Raw Mango Slad, wash, peel and cut half a cup of raw mango into juliennes. Wash and remove the core of a medium-sized apple and cut 3/4 cup of apple into juliennes. Then, soak the sliced apples in lime water until use, to avoid it from turning brown. Wash, pat dry and finely shred 1/4 cup of red cabbage. Wash and finely chop 2 green chilies.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60a6d5f039154e5888e26e76','60a6d5066aa4baac08ff6f91',2,'p2- prep the greens','Next, wash, pat dry, and finely chop 1/4 cup of rocket lettuce. Wash and finely shred 1/4 cup of green cabbage. Wash and finely chop 1 tbsp of mint leaves. Wash and cut a lime into halves. Then, squeeze 1 tablespoon of lime juice into a bowl.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60a6d66739154e5888e26e77','60a6d5066aa4baac08ff6f91',3,'m1- prepare the salad and serve','To make Rocket Apple and Raw Manago Salad, add half a cup of raw mango juliennes to a mixing bowl, followed by 3/4 cup of sliced apple and 1/4 cup of shredded red cabbage. Next, add 1/4 cup of shredded green cabbage. Add 0.5 tsp black salt, add  0.5 tsp cumin powder, 0.5 tsp red chili powder, 2 tsp honey, add 2 tsp vinegar.  0.5 tsp salt, 2 chopped green chilies, and a tablespoon of chopped mint leaves. Mix it well and garnish it with chopped rocket lettuce and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60ab7b2c6aa4baac08ff6f93','60ab7af576deac86bca5ce2a',1,'p1- boil the sweet potato','To boil the sweet potato for Sweet Potato Salad, wash 2 small-sized sweet potatoes and add them to pressure along with 2 cups of water. Cover the cooker with a lid and pressure cook the sweet potatoes over high flame until one whistle. After the first whistle, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook it for another 5 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside to depressurize it naturally. While the sweet potato boils, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60ab7b826aa4baac08ff6f94','60ab7af576deac86bca5ce2a',2,'p2- prep the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for sweet potato salad, wash and dice 0.5 cup of english cucumber. Wash and dice 0.5 cup tomatoes. Wash and finely chop 1 tbsp coriander leaves. Wash and cut a lemon into halves and squeeze 2 teaspoons of lime juice into a bowl. Next, after boiling the sweet potato, open the lid of the pressure cooker and remove the boiled sweet potatoes on a plate. Then, gently peel off the skin and cut the sweet potato into medium dices.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('60ab7bcc6aa4baac08ff6f95','60ab7af576deac86bca5ce2a',3,'m1- Assemble the salad and serve','To make the Sweet potato salad, take a mixing bowl and add 3/4 cup of diced boiled sweet potato. Next, add half a cup of diced cucumber, and half a cup of diced tomato, followed by 1 tsp salt, 0.5 tsp cumin powder, 0.5 tsp red chili powder, add 2 tsp lemon juice, and mix it well. Garnish it with chopped coriander leaves and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60ab868839154e5888e26e7c','60ab86316aa4baac08ff6f99',1,'p1- boil the sweet potato','For berry broccoli veg salad, first, soak 1 tablespoon of cashew nuts in half a cup of water for 20 minutes. Next, to boil the sweet potato, wash a medium-sized sweet potato well with water and add it to a pressure cooker along with 2 cups of water. Cover the cooker with a lid and pressure cook it over a high flame until one whistle. After that, reduce the flame to low and allow it to cook for another 5 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. After that, take out the boiled sweet potato from the cooker and gently peel off the skin and mash it well using a fork. While the sweet potato is boiling please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60ab86f376deac86bca5ce2c','60ab86316aa4baac08ff6f99',2,'p2- roast the pumpkin','To prepare the roasted pumpkin for Berry Broccoli Veg Salad, wash, peel and dice 0.5 cups pumpkin. Next, arrange the pumpkin cubes onto a baking dish. Add 1/4 tsp salt, add 1/4 tsp pepper powder, add 1/4 tsp paprika powder, and half a teaspoon of cooking oil. Mix it well and set it inside the oven to roast the pumpkin at 180 degrees Celcius for 10 minutes. While the pumpkin is being roasted, please move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60ab875276deac86bca5ce2d','60ab86316aa4baac08ff6f99',3,'p3- blanch broccoli','To blanch the broccoli for Berry Broccoli Veg Salad, first, wash and cut half a cup of broccoli into small florets. Next, take a bowl and fill it with cold water. Next, in a pot, add 3 cups of water and bring to boil over high flame. When the water starts boiling add the broccoli florets and remove them within 1-2 mins and transfer it to the cold water bowl to stop the cooking process. Keep Aside','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60ab87b76aa4baac08ff6f9a','60ab86316aa4baac08ff6f99',4,'p4- prep the greens','To prep the ingredients for Berry Broccoli Veg Salad, wash, pat dry, and roughly shred 1/4 cup of iceberg lettuce. wash, pat dry and roughly shred 1/4 cup of leaf lettuce. wash, pat dry and roughly shred 1/4 cup of lolo roso lettuce. Wash and dice 1/4 cup of English cucumber. Grate 2 tablespoons of parmesan cheese in a bowl.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('60ab881b76deac86bca5ce2e','60ab86316aa4baac08ff6f99',5,'m1- prepare the cashew mayo','To prepare the dressing for Berry Broccoli Veg Salad, in a blender jar, add a tablespoon of soaked cashew nuts followed by a teaspoon of dijon mustard, a teaspoon of lime juice, and 2 teaspoons of garlic paste. Add half a teaspoon of salt, 2 tablespoons of water, and 1/4 cup of boiled sweet potato paste and blend it well into a fine paste and prepare the cashew mayo.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60ab88ab39154e5888e26e7d','60ab86316aa4baac08ff6f99',6,'m2- prepare the dressing','Next, to this cashew mayo, add 3 tablespoons of curd, 2.5 teaspoons of poppy seeds, 1/4 teaspoon of salt, 1/4 teaspoon of black pepper powder, a teaspoon of lime juice. Then, cover the jar with a lid and again blend it well into a smooth dressing.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60ab898a6aa4baac08ff6f9b','60ab86316aa4baac08ff6f99',7,'m3- Assemble the salad. Garnish & Serve','To assemble the Berry Broccoli veg Salad, take a salad bowl and place the lettuce mix, then add the blanched broccoli, roasted pumpkin, and 1/4 cup of diced English cucumber. Garnish the salad with roasted almonds, cranberries, and grated parmesan cheese. Serve it along with the poppy seed dressing','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60ae214b76deac86bca5ce36','60ae20cc76deac86bca5ce35',1,'p1- prepare the ingredients','To prepare the ingredient for badanekayi gojju, first, soak a teaspoon of tamarind in 1/4 cup of water for 10 minutes. Next, wash 4 small white brinjals and cut the crown and the bottom of the brinjals, then cut the white brinjal into quarters, remove in a bowl and set aside; wash and slit 2 green chillies. Wash and pluck 7 nos curry leaves, remove all in a bowl and set aside. Next, after soaking the tamarind, mash it well with the water and strain the pulp in a bowl.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60ae218e39154e5888e26e83','60ae20cc76deac86bca5ce35',2,'p2- boil the brinjals','To boil the brinjals for Badanekayi Gojju, in a deep bottom pan add the quartered brinjal, add 1 cup of water along with a pinch of salt and allow the brinjal to boil for 7-8mins or until the brinjal becomes soft and shrinks in size. To check for softness, strain a piece of brinjal and press the back of the spoon against it and it should be easily pressed. Next, strain the remaining brinjal and allow it to slightly cool. After it cools, gently peel the skin of the brinjal, and mash the cooked brinjal using a masher until it becomes pulpy, then set aside. While the brinjals are boiling, please move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('60ae220e39154e5888e26e84','60ae20cc76deac86bca5ce35',3,'m1- add the seasonings and chopped ingredients to mashed brinjal','To make the Badanekayi Gojju, in a mixing bowl add the mashed brinjal followed by the prepared tamarind water, 1 tbsp of jaggery powder, and 2 slit green chilies. Next, add 1 tsp of salt and mix it well using a spoon. Then, add 2 tbsp of water, or add water as per desired consistency and mix well.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60ae22886aa4baac08ff6fa2','60ae20cc76deac86bca5ce35',4,'m2- add the tempering to the curry and serve','To make the tempering for badanekayi gojju, heat a tempering pan on low flame and add 2 tsp of coconut oil and allow it to become hot, then add 1/4 tsp of white lentil and allow it to crackle, then add half a tsp of mustard seeds and allow it to splutter, then add 7 nos of curry leaves followed by 1/4 tsp of hing and mix it well and allow the tempering to splutter, then turn off the flame and pour the tempering instantly over the prepared badanekayi gojju. Mix it well and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60ae264c76deac86bca5ce38','60ae260c6aa4baac08ff6fa3',1,'p1- boil the potatoes','To boil the potatoes for Aloo Raita, wash 2 medium-sized potatoes and add them to a pressure cooker along with 1 cup of water. Cover it with a lid and pressure cook the potatoes over a high flame until 1 whistle. Then, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook the potatoes for another 8 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally.  While the potatoes are boiling, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60ae26b439154e5888e26e87','60ae260c6aa4baac08ff6fa3',2,'p2- prepare the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Aloo Raita, in a mixing bowl add 1 cup of curd and continuously beat the curd using a hand whisk or a hand blender for 2 mins or until it becomes of pourable consistency, remove in a bowl and set aside, then wash and pluck 7 nos curry leaves. Wash, peel, and grate a half-inch piece of ginger. Wash and finely chop 2 green chilies.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60ae26f039154e5888e26e88','60ae260c6aa4baac08ff6fa3',3,'p3- peel and mash the boiled potatoes','After boiling the potatoes for Aloo Raita, strain the boiled potatoes and allow them to slightly cool. Then, gently peel off the skin and transfer the boiled potatoes to a mixing bowl and mash the potatoes into a crumbly texture as shown using a masher.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('60ae272776deac86bca5ce39','60ae260c6aa4baac08ff6fa3',4,'m1- prepare the raita','To make the Aloo Raita, in a mixing bowl add 1 cup of mashed potatoes, followed by 1 cup of whisked curd and a teaspoon of salt. Mix it well and set it aside. It should have a thick and creamy consistency at this stage','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60ae27976aa4baac08ff6fa4','60ae260c6aa4baac08ff6fa3',5,'m2- add the tempering to the raita and serve','Next, to make the tempering for Aloo Raita, heat a tempering pan and add 2 tsp of oil and allow it to become hot, then add 1/2 tsp of mustard seedsand allow it to splutter, then add 1/2 tsp of urad dal and allow it to crackle, then add 7 nos curry leaves, 2 chopped green chillies and1/2-inch piece of chopped ginger, followed by 1/4 tsp of hing and saute it well on low flame until the tempering has spluttered. Then, add 2 curd chillies and saute for a few seconds until the chillies crinkle, then turn off the flame and pour the tempering over the raita and mix it well. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60ae29c96aa4baac08ff6fa7','60ae298e6aa4baac08ff6fa6',1,'p1- boil the potatoes','To boil the potato for Potato Rasam, wash a medium-sized potato and add it to a pressure cooker along with 1 cup of water. Cover it with a lid and pressure cook the potato over a high flame until 1 whistle. Then, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook the potato for another 8 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally.  While the potato is boiling, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60ae2a336aa4baac08ff6fa8','60ae298e6aa4baac08ff6fa6',2,'p2- prepare the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for the potato rasam, wash and slit 2 green chilies then wash and pluck 7 nos curry leaves. Remove in a bowl and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60ae2a6e76deac86bca5ce3a','60ae298e6aa4baac08ff6fa6',3,'p3- peel and mash the boiled potatoes','After boiling the potato for Potato Rasam, strain the boiled potato and allow it to slightly cool. Then gently peel off the skin and mash the potato well into a crumbly texture leaving behind some small chunks using your hands, remove in a bowl, and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('60ae2aa26aa4baac08ff6fa9','60ae298e6aa4baac08ff6fa6',4,'m1- simmer the rasam','To make the potato rasam, in a deep bottom pan, add the crumbled potato, followed by 2 slit green chilies and half a teaspoon of salt. Next, add 2 cups of water and mix it well. Then, turn on the flame and allow the rasam to boil over medium flame for 5 minutes until it slightly thickens. Then, turn off the flame and set it aside. While the rasam is boiling move towards the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60ae2af676deac86bca5ce3b','60ae298e6aa4baac08ff6fa6',5,'m2- add the tempering to the rasam and serve','To make the tempering for potato rasam, in a tempering pan heat a tablespoon of cooking oil and allow it to become hot, then add 1/2 a tsp of mustard seeds and allow it to crackle, then add 1 tsp of curry leaves and allow it to crackle. Next, add 2 dried red chilies followed by 1/4 tsp of hing. Saute the tempering over low flame and allow the ingredients to splutter. Make sure to keep the flame low to prevent the ingredients from burning. Then, turn off the flame and add the tempering to the prepared potato rasam. Mix it well and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60af924739154e5888e26e8b','60af84fe39154e5888e26e8a',1,'p1- roast and grind the urad dal into fine powder','To prepare the urad dal for urad dal curry, heat a pan and add 1/4 cup of urad dal, and dry roast it over low flame for 3-4 mins until it is slightly brown and crisp. Then turn off the flame and allow it to slightly cool. Then, transfer it to a blender jar and blitz it into a very fine powder, remove it in a bowl, and set it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60af92946aa4baac08ff6fab','60af84fe39154e5888e26e8a',2,'p2- prepare the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for urad dal curry, wash and finely chop 2 green chilies. Wash, peel, and finely chop a 1-inch piece of ginger. Next, wash and finely chop a tablespoon of curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60af92e039154e5888e26e8c','60af84fe39154e5888e26e8a',3,'m1- combine urad dal powder and curd to prepare the curry','To make the urad dal curry, in a mixing bowl add the powdered urad dal along with 1 cup of sour curd and mix it well using a spoon to avoid any lumps. Then, add 1/2 a cup of water and mix it well until well combined. The consistency of the mixture should be semi-thick.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('60af934876deac86bca5ce3c','60af84fe39154e5888e26e8a',4,'m2- add the tempering to the curry & serve','To make the tempering for urad dal curry, heat a pan on low flame and add 2 tsp of coconut oil and allow it to become hot, then add 1/2 a tsp of mustard seeds and allow it to crackle, then add 1/2 a tsp of white lentils and allow it to crackle. Next add 1 tbsp of chopped curry leaves, 1-inch piece of grated ginger, 2 chopped green chilies, and 1/4 tsp of hing followed by 2 curd chilies. Saute it over low flame for a few seconds. Then, turn off the flame and add the tempering to the prepared urad dal batter. Mix it well and add a teaspoon of salt. You can add more curd or water if required to adjust the consistency. Mix it well and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60af961976deac86bca5ce3e','60af95b976deac86bca5ce3d',1,'p1- chop the spinach and prep other ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for palak Tambuli, in a strainer add 1 cup of spinach leaves and thoroughly wash the leaves twice or thrice until you get rid of the mud. Then, place the washed spinach on the chopping board and chop off the roots, then transfer the cleaned spinach in a bowl and set aside. Grate 1/4 cup of coconut using a grater and set aside. Next, wash 7 nos curry leaves. Wash and roughly chop 1 green chili.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60af967e76deac86bca5ce3f','60af95b976deac86bca5ce3d',2,'m1- Fry the spinach leaves','To make Palak Tambuli, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame. Next, add 1/2 a tsp of cumin seeds and saute it on low flame for a few seconds. Then, add 1 cup of spinach leaves followed by 1 tsp of oil and saute it over low flame for 1-2 minutes along with the cumin seeds until the palak leaves wilt. Do not fry the spinach leaves over a high flame as they get burnt easily. Then, turn off the flame and allow the mixture to slightly cool.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('60af96ca76deac86bca5ce40','60af95b976deac86bca5ce3d',3,'m2- puree the fried spinach & add it to the buttermilk','To blend the spinach mixture for Palak Tambuli, after the spinach mixture cools, transfer it to a blender jar along with 1/4 cup of grated coconut, 1 green chili, add 1/2 a tsp of salt. Add 1/4 cup of water, and blend it into a fine puree. Remove it to a bowl and add half a cup of buttermilk to it. Mix it well and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60af975239154e5888e26e8e','60af95b976deac86bca5ce3d',4,'m3- add the tempering to the tambuli & serve','To make the tempering for Palak Tambuli,  heat a tempering pan and add 1 tsp of ghee and allow it to melt, then add 1/2 a tsp of mustard seeds and allow it to splutter, then add 1 dry red chili, and 7 nos curry leaves. Then, allow it to splutter over low flame for a few seconds. Then, turn off the flame and pour the tempering over the prepared palak Tambuli. Mix it well and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('60af99676aa4baac08ff6fac','60af992439154e5888e26e8f',1,'ap1- soak the foxtail millet','For millet masala dosa, in a mixing bowl add 3/4 cup of foxtail millet followed by 3 tablespoons of urad dal add half a tsp of fenugreek seeds, and add 3 cups of water and rinse twice and then discard the water. Then soak it in 2 cups of water for 4 hours. While the millets soak, please move towards the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":240,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60af99aa39154e5888e26e90','60af992439154e5888e26e8f',2,'ap2- prepare and ferment the batter','To prepare the batter for Millet Masala Dosa, first, rinse 3 tablespoons of poha well with water. Next, add the soaked millet and urad dal to a blender jar followed by the rinsed poha and blend it well into a smooth batter. Then, remove the batter in a bowl and allow it to ferment for 8-10 hours. While the batter ferments, please move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":600,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60af99e376deac86bca5ce41','60af992439154e5888e26e8f',3,'p1- boil the potatoes','To boil the potatoes for Millet Masala Dosa, wash 2 medium-sized potatoes and add them to a pressure cooker along with 1 cup of water. Cover it with a lid and pressure cook the potatoes over a high flame until 1 whistle. Then, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook the potatoes for another 8 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally.  While the potatoes are boiling, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60af9a9f39154e5888e26e91','60af992439154e5888e26e8f',4,'p2- prep the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Millet Masala Dosa, peel, wash, and finely slice 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and slit 2 nos green chilies. Wash, peel, and grate a 1-inch piece of ginger. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash and pluck 7 nos curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60af9ad239154e5888e26e92','60af992439154e5888e26e8f',5,'p3- peel and mash the potatoes','After boiling the potatoes for Millet Masala Dosa, remove the lid of the pressure cooker and carefully remove the boiled potatoes onto a plate. Then, allow them to slightly cool and gently peel off the skin. Then, mash the potatoes well using a fork or a potato masher.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('60af9b496aa4baac08ff6fad','60af992439154e5888e26e8f',6,'m1- make the aloo masala stuffing for dosa','To make the aloo masala for Millet Masala Dosa, heat a tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Then add 1/2 a tsp of mustard seeds, 1/2 a tsp of urad dal, 1/2 tsp of chana dal, followed by 7 curry leaves, and saute it for a few seconds over medium flame and allow it to splutter. Then, add 1/4 cup of sliced onions, 2 slit green chilies, and a 1-inch piece of grated ginger, followed by 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder. Mix it well and fry the onions over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60af9b9276deac86bca5ce42','60af992439154e5888e26e8f',7,'m2- season the stuffing and garnish','Next, add 1/2 a tsp of salt, followed by mashed potatoes and 1/4 cup of water, and mix it well until the potatoes are well combined with the masala. Saute and cook the potatoes over medium flame for 2-3 minutes. Next, add 1/4 tsp of lemon juice followed by a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and mix it well. Turn off the flame and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60af9c066aa4baac08ff6fae','60af992439154e5888e26e8f',8,'m3- make the dosa with the batter and serve','To make the Millet Masala Dosa, add 1/2 a tsp of salt to the fermented batter and mix it well. Next, heat an iron griddle and allow it to become hot, then add a ladle full of the dosa batter and move the ladle in a circular motion to form a thin dosa, then pour 1/2 a tsp of oil on the edges of the dosa to ensure easy removal, then cover the pan with a lid and allow the dosa to cook on medium flame 1-2 minutes. Next, add a spoonful of the prepared aloo masala to the dosa and spread it in the center as shown. Then, fold the dosa from both ends and remove it onto a serving plate. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60b5201a6aa4baac08ff6fb0','60b51fd539154e5888e26e97',1,'ap1- soak the sabudana','To soak the sabudana for sabudana idli, In a bowl add 1/4 cup of sabudana along with 1.5 cups of water and thoroughly rinse the sabudana twice or thrice and discard the water. Then soak the sabudana in 3/4 cup of water for 3-5 hours. While the sabudana is soaking move towards the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":300,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60b520786aa4baac08ff6fb1','60b51fd539154e5888e26e97',2,'p1- roast the rava','To roast the rava for sabudana idli, heat a pan and add 1/2 a cup of medium rava and dry roast it on medium low flame for 3 mins or until the rava becomes slightly brown, keep stirring the rava to prevent it from burning. Then, turn off the flame and transfer it in a bowl, and set it aside. Next, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of dill leaves and grease the idli plate with a teaspoon of cooking oil using an oil brush.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('60b520d06aa4baac08ff6fb2','60b51fd539154e5888e26e97',3,'p2- prepare the idli batter','To prepare the batter for Sabudana Idli, first, squeeze out the extra water from the soaked sabudana as shown. Next, add the sabudana to a mixing bowl followed by 1/2 a cup of roasted rava, and half a cup of curd. Mix it well into a smooth batter. There should be no lumps in the batter and it should be semi-thick in consistency. Next, cover the batter with a lid and allow it to rest for 30 mins. While the batter rests, please move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":30,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60b5212276deac86bca5ce4a','60b51fd539154e5888e26e97',4,'m1- steam the idlis and serve','To make the Sabudana Idli, first, to set up the steamer for idli, add 2 cups of water in the steamer and allow it to boil over medium flame for 2-3 minutes. Next, add about 1/4 cup of water to the prepared batter to adjust the consistency since the rava has absorbed the water. Add half a teaspoon of salt, 1/4 cup of chopped of dill leaves, and 1/4 teaspoon of baking soda. Mix it well and pour the batter instantly into the molds of the greased idli plate without resting it any further. Then, set it inside the steamer and steam the idlis over medium flame for 10-12 minutes. After that, carefully remove the idli plate from the steamer and demould the idlis from the plate. Plate the idlis onto a serving plate and serve','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60b5245939154e5888e26e99','60b523fd39154e5888e26e98',2,'p2- prepare the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Saouthekayi Huli, wash and cut the Mangalore cucumber into half, and scoop out the seeds, then cut 1 cup of cucumber into medium-sized chunks, remove in a bowl, and set aside. Wash and pluck 7 nos curry leaves. Grate 1/2 cup of coconut using a grater. Next, after soaking the tamarind, mash it well with water and strain the pulp in a bowl.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60b5245976deac86bca5ce4c','60b523fd39154e5888e26e98',1,'p1- pressure cook the toor dal','For Sothekayi Huli, first, soak a teaspoon of tamarind in 1/4 cup of water for 15 minutes. Next, to boil the toor dal, rinse half a cup of toor dal well with water. Then, add it to a pressure cooker along with 1 cup of water and half a teaspoon of salt. Then cover it with a lid and pressure cook the dal over a high flame until 1 whistle. Then, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook it for another 8 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and allow the pressure cooker to release the pressure naturally. While the dal simmers, please move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60b525336aa4baac08ff6fb3','60b523fd39154e5888e26e98',3,'m1- simmer the mangalore cucumber','To make the Southekayi Huli, heat a deep bottom pan add 1 cup of diced Mangalore cucumber along with1 a cup of water. Next, add the prepared tamarind pulp, a teaspoon of salt, 1 tbsp of jaggery powder, and 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder. Mix it well and cover it with a lid.  Allow the curry to cook on a medium flame for 10-12 mins or until the mangalore cucumber is tender. While the curry simmers, please move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('60b525a376deac86bca5ce4d','60b523fd39154e5888e26e98',4,'m2- make the coconut masala paste','To make the masala paste for Sothekayi Huli, heat a tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add 2 teaspoons of urad dal, a tablespoon of coriander seeds, a teaspoon of cumin seeds, 1/4 teaspoon of fenugreek seeds, 2 dry red chilies, and 7 curry leaves. Saute the masalas over low flame for 1-2 minutes until fragrant. Then, turn off the flame and allow them to slightly cool. Next, add the masalas to a blender jar along with half a cup of grated fresh coconut and 1/4 cup of water. Cover the jar with a lid and blend it well into a smooth paste.','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60b525db6aa4baac08ff6fb4','60b523fd39154e5888e26e98',5,'m3- add the masala paste and toor dal to the curry and boil','After simmering the Sothekayi Huli, carefully remove the lid and check if the Mangalore cucumbers are cooked through. Next, add the ground masala paste into the curry followed by the cooked toor dal and 1/4 cup of water. Mix it well and cook the curry over medium flame for 2-3 minutes and bring it to boil. Then, turn off the flame and set it aside','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60b526ad6aa4baac08ff6fb5','60b523fd39154e5888e26e98',6,'m4- add the tempering to the curry & serve','To make the tempering for sothekayi huli, heat a tempering pan and add 2 tsp of coconut oil and allow it to become hot, then add 1/2 a tsp of mustard seeds, add 1/2 a tsp of white lentils, then add 1 dried red chili followed by a tsp of curry leaves and allow it to splutter then turn off the flame and pour it over the sothekayi huli and mix well. The curry is now ready to serve','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60b52b9739154e5888e26e9a','60b52b3676deac86bca5ce4e',1,'p1- boil the drumstick','To prepare the ingredients for drumstick curry, first, soak a teaspoon of tamarind in 1/4 cup of water for 15 minutes. Next, to boil the drumsticks, wash 1/2 a cup of drumstick and cut it into 2 inch long pieces. Then, boil the drumsticks over medium flame for 7-8 minutes until half-tender. While the drumstick is boiling, please move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60b52c2339154e5888e26e9b','60b52b3676deac86bca5ce4e',2,'p2- prepare the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Drumstick Curry, wash white brinjals, cut the crown of the brinjal, then cut half a cup of brinjals into medium-sized chunks and immerse it in the water until further use, this prevents the brinjal from turning black. Next, grate 3/4 cup of fresh coconut using a grater. Wash and slit 3 green chilies. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Next, after soaking the tamarind, mash it well with water and strain the pulp in a bowl.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('60b52cb076deac86bca5ce4f','60b52b3676deac86bca5ce4e',3,'m1- add the brinjals to the boiled drumsticks & simmer','To make the drumstick curry, add half a cup of diced brinjals to the boiled drumsticks followed by 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder, 2 slit green chilies, and the prepared tamarind pulp. Next, add 1 tsp of salt and mix the curry well. Cover the curry with a lid and allow it to cook on a medium flame for 7-8 mins or until the vegetables are tender and cooked through. While the curry simmers, please move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('60b52cfa39154e5888e26e9c','60b52b3676deac86bca5ce4e',4,'m2- prepare the coconut masala paste','To make the coconut masala paste for drumstick curry, in a blender jar add 3/4 cup of grated coconut, 1 green chilli, 2 tsp of coriander seeds, 1 tsp of mustard seeds, and 1/4 cup of water. Cover the jar with a lid and blend it into a smooth paste. Then, transfer it in a bowl and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60b52d3476deac86bca5ce50','60b52b3676deac86bca5ce4e',5,'m3- add the coconut paste and boil the curry. Garnish & serve','After simmering the Drumstick Curry, add the prepared coconut paste to it and mix it well. Then, bring the curry to boil over medium flame for a few minutes until the gravy slightly thickens. Then, turn off the flame and garnish it with 1 tbsp of chopped coriander leaves and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60b88b3c76deac86bca5ce51','60b88ad66aa4baac08ff6fb7',1,'p1- prepare the dough','To prepare the dough for Bili Holige, in a mixing bowl add 1 cup of maida, add 1/4 cup of rava, add 1 tsp of salt, and mix the dry ingredients well using your hands, Then add 1/2 a cup of water, and combine all the ingredients to mix well, add some more water if required and knead into a soft and loose dough. Then add 2 tsp of oil and knead the dough again, then cover the dough with a damp cloth and allow it to rest for 20mins. While the dough rests, move towards the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60b88b824679878674289c2e','60b88ad66aa4baac08ff6fb7',2,'p2- prepare the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for bili holige, wash and finely chop 2 nos of green chili, wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves. Remove all in a bowl and set aside','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('60b88c3a6aa4baac08ff6fb8','60b88ad66aa4baac08ff6fb7',3,'p3- prepare the rice flour stuffing','To prepare the stuffing for Bili Holige, add 2 cups of water to a pan along with half a tsp of salt, and 1/2 a tsp of cumin seeds. Add 2 nos chopped green chilies followed by a tbsp of coriander leaves and mix it well. Then, bring it to boil over medium flame. When the water starts boiling add 1 cup of rice flour while simultaneously stirring it, to prevent the formation of lumps. Mix the dough and allow it to cook over medium flame for 2-3 minutes. Keep stirring the flour until it is well combined and turns into a soft dough-like stuffing. Then turn off the flame and transfer it to a plate.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60b88d804679878674289c2f','60b88ad66aa4baac08ff6fb7',4,'m1- prepare the rice flour stuffed dough balls','To make Bili Holige, first, knead the prepared rice flour stuffing for a minute with greased hands. Then, divide the stuffing into small equal portions. Next, divide the prepared maida dough into equal parts and roll them between your palms to form a round ball. Then, stuff the dough balls with the prepared rice flour stuffing as shown. Prepare the rest of the stuffed dough balls similarly from the stuffing.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60b88dfd6aa4baac08ff6fb9','60b88ad66aa4baac08ff6fb7',5,'m2- roll out the stuffed dough balls and roast the bili holige','Next, place the stuffed dough ball onto the rolling board and gently roll it into a slightly thick round chapati. Next, gently transfer the rolled-out bili holige onto the hot pan and allow it to cook over medium flame for a minute. Once you see the small bubbles forming on the dough, pour 1/2 a tsp of oil around the edges and in the center and flip the bili holige on the other side and roast it for another 1-2 minutes until small brown dots appear and the holige puffs up a little, then lift it with a spatula and serve hot. Repeat the same for the remaining dough','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60b890db76deac86bca5ce52','60b890734679878674289c31',1,'p1- prepare the brinjals & other ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Brinjal Masala, first, soak 1 teaspoon of tamarind in 1/4 cup of water for 10 minutes. Next, wash 6 nos baby brinjals and cut the crown off, then cut the brinjal into medium-sized cubes and immerse the brinjal cubes in water until later use, to prevent it from turning black and set it aside. Peel, wash, and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash 7 nos curry leaves. Next, after soaking the tamarind, mash it well with water and strain the pulp in a bowl','prep_method','{"active_time":14,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60b8915d4679878674289c32','60b890734679878674289c31',2,'p2- roast and grind the peanuts','To roast the peanuts for Brinjal Masala, heat up a pan and 3 tablespoons of peanuts and dry roast the peanuts over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until they are crisp and slightly golden brown. Then turn off the flame and remove the peanuts to a blender jar. Allow the peanuts to cool for some time. Then, cover the jar with a lid and pulse grind it into a coarse powder, do not over blend the peanuts as it will start leaving out oil, remove the crushed peanuts in a bowl and set aside','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('60b891b276deac86bca5ce53','60b890734679878674289c31',3,'m1- temper the oil and fry the onions','To make Brinjal Masala, heat 1 tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Then, add 1/2 tsp of mustard seeds followed by 7 curry leaves and saute it over low flame for a few seconds or until it splutters. Then, add 1/4 teaspoon of hingh and saute it for a few seconds. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions and fry the onions over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60b891f176deac86bca5ce54','60b890734679878674289c31',4,'m2- add the brinjals and simmer the curry','Next, add 2 cups of cubed brinjal and fry it with the onions over medium flame for 2 minutes. After that, season the brinjal with 1 tsp of salt followed by 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder and mix it well.  Then, cover the pan with a lid and allow it to cook for 5-7 mins or until the brinjal becomes tender. While the brinjals simmer, please move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('60b892934679878674289c33','60b890734679878674289c31',5,'m3- Simmer the curry with peanut powder & spices. Garnish & serve','After simmering the Brinjal Masala, remove the lid and add the prepared tamarind pulp followed by 1/2 a tsp of red chili powder and 1/4 tsp of garam masala, and 1/2 tsp of jaggery powder. Mix it well and add 1/4 cup of water. Then, bring it to a boil over medium flame. Then, add the prepared peanut powder and mix it well. Cover the pan with a lid and allow it to cook again over low flame for 3 mins. After that, turn off the flame. Plate the brinjal masala in a serving dish. Garnish it with some chopped coriander leaves and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60b894e74679878674289c34','60b894736aa4baac08ff6fbb',1,'p1- dice the pumpkin & prep other ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Kumbalekayi Palya, first, wash a sweet pumpkin, then cut it in half and scoop out the seeds using a spoon and discard them. Then, peel the pumpkin and cut 1.5 cups of pumpkin into cubes, and set it aside. Then, wash and finely chop 2  green chilies. Wash and finely chop 1 tbsp of coriander leaves. wash and pluck 7 nos curry leaves. Grate 1 tbsp of fresh coconut.','prep_method','{"active_time":17,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60b8958d4679878674289c35','60b894736aa4baac08ff6fbb',2,'m1- Temper the pumpkin and simmer','To make the Kumbalekayi Palya, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Next, add 1/4 tsp of mustard seeds, 7 nos curry leaves, and saute it over low flame for a few seconds or until it splutters. Then, add 2 chopped green chilies followed by 1/4 teaspoon of hing and half a teaspoon of turmeric powder and saute it over low flame for a few seconds. Then, add 1.5 cups of diced sweet pumpkin and mix it well.  Sprinkle some water and cover the pan with a lid and cook it on a medium flame for 10-12 mins or until the sweet pumpkin is cooked through. While palya is simmering, please move onto the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('60b895e44679878674289c36','60b894736aa4baac08ff6fbb',3,'m2- Fry the pumpkin. Finish it off with lime juice & coriander leaves','After simmering the Kumbalekayi Palya, carefully remove the lid and add 1 tablespoon of grated fresh coconut followed by 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves, and 2 teaspoons of lime juice. Mix it well and fry the palya over medium flame for another 2-3 mins. Then turn off the flame and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60bd129776deac86bca5ce56','60bd122f76deac86bca5ce55',1,'ap1- soak the peas','To soak the peas for Tondekayi Curry, in a bowl add 1/2 cup of peas, add 1 cup of water and rinse the peas well. Then strain the peas and discard the water. Then add 1.5 cups of fresh water and allow the peas to soak for 30mins. While the peas soak, move towards the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":120,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60bd12e676deac86bca5ce57','60bd122f76deac86bca5ce55',2,'p1- boil the green peas','To boil the peas for Tondekayi Curry,  add the soaked peas in a pressure cooker along with 1 cup of water and a pinch of salt and cover the lid, then pressure cook the soaked peas until 2 whistles on high flame and continue to cook the peas on low flame for another 5 mins and then allow the cooker to release the pressure naturally. Then open the lid and strain the peas. Remove the strained peas in a bowl and set it aside. While the peas are boiling, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":14,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60bd134076deac86bca5ce58','60bd122f76deac86bca5ce55',3,'p2- prepare the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Tondekayi Curry, first, soak a teaspoon of tamarind in 1/4 cup of water for 10 minutes. Next, wash and quarter 1 cup of ivy gourds. Grate 1/2 a cup of coconut, remove it in a bowl, and set aside. After soaking the tamarind, mash it well with water and strain the pulp in a bowl.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60bd138b6aa4baac08ff6fc1','60bd122f76deac86bca5ce55',4,'m1- simmer the ivy gourds','To make Tondekayi Curry, heat a deep bottom on low flame and transfer the cut ivy gourds into the pan along with 1 cup of water, then add 1/2 a tsp of salt, add 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder, and mix well, then partially cover the pan with a lid and allow it to cook over medium flame for 8-10 mins. While the ivy gourd cooks, move towards the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('60bd141976deac86bca5ce59','60bd122f76deac86bca5ce55',5,'m2- prepare the masala paste','To prepare the masala paste for Tondekayi Curry, heat up a pan and add 2 teaspoons of urad dal, and roast it on a medium flame for a few seconds or until the dal becomes golden brown, then turn off the flame. Next in a blender jar add 1/2 a cup of grated coconut, followed by roasted urad dal, 1/2 tsp of coriander seeds, 1 tsp of cumin seeds, 2 dried red chilies, 1-inch piece of cinnamon stick, 2 cloves, and 1/4 cup of water. Then, cover the jar with a lid and blend it well into a smooth paste. Remove in a bowl and set aside','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60bd14e86aa4baac08ff6fc2','60bd122f76deac86bca5ce55',6,'m3-add the boiled peas and masala paste to the curry & cook','After simmering the ivy gourds for Tondekayi Curry, add the cooked peas and mix it well. Add the tamarind pulp followed by 1/2 a tsp of jaggery, mix the curry well, and allow the curry to cook over low flame for another 1-2 mins or until the jaggery melts and the vegetables become tender. Then, add the prepared masala paste to the curry and mix it well. Season it with 1 tsp of salt and adjust the consistency of the curry by adding water as per requirement and allow the curry to boil over low flame for 3-5 mins. Then, turn off the flame and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60bd15596aa4baac08ff6fc3','60bd122f76deac86bca5ce55',7,'m4- add the tempering to the curry & serve','To make the tempering for Tondekayi Curry, heat a tempering pan and add 1 tsp of oil and allow it to become hot, then add 1/4 tsp of urad dal and allow it to crackle, then add 1/4 tsp of mustard seeds and allow it to splutter. Next, add 1/2 dried red chili followed by 7 curry leaves. Saute it over low flame for a few seconds and allow the tempering to splutter. Then, turn off the flame and pour the tempering over the prepared curry and mix it well. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60bd188c4679878674289c3a','60bd17f86aa4baac08ff6fc4',1,'p1- prepare the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for coriander leaves Tambuli, in a strainer add 1 cup of coriander leaves and thoroughly wash the coriander leaves until you get rid of the mud. Next, grate 1/4 cup of coconut and set aside. Wash 7 nos curry leaves. Wash and roughly chop 1 green chili.  Then in a mixing bowl add 1/2 cup of fresh curd and 1/4 cup of water. Whisk it until it reaches a pourable consistency and set it aside','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60bd18de4679878674289c3b','60bd17f86aa4baac08ff6fc4',2,'m1- Temper the oil and fry the coriander leaves','To make coriander leaves Tambuli, heat a pan and add 2 tsp of oil and allow it to become hot, then add 1/2 a tsp of cumin seeds, 1 green chili and saute it on low flame for a few seconds and then add 1 cup of washed coriander leaves. Stir and fry the coriander leaves over low flame for a few seconds until the coriander leaves wilt. Do not fry the coriander leaves over high flame. Then, turn off the flame and allow it cool for sometime','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('60bd192c6aa4baac08ff6fc5','60bd17f86aa4baac08ff6fc4',3,'m2- Puree the coriander leaves & add the buttermilk','After the coriander leaves for Tambuli cools, transfer it in a blender jar along with 1/4 cup of grated coconut, 1/2 a tsp of salt, add 1/2 cup of water and blend it into a fine puree. Remove it in a bowl. Then, add the prepared buttermilk and mix it well.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60bd197c6aa4baac08ff6fc6','60bd17f86aa4baac08ff6fc4',4,'m3- add the tempering to the tambuli & serve','To make the tempering for Coriander Leaves Tambuli, heat a tempering pan and add 1/2 tsp of ghee and allow it to melt, then add 1/2 a tsp of mustard seeds and allow it to splutter, then add 1/2 tsp of urad dal, add 7 curry leaves, add 1 dried red chilli and mix well using the spoon, allow the ingredients to splutter, then turn off the flame and pour the tempering over the prepared Tambuli and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('60bd1c644679878674289c3c','60bd1bf86aa4baac08ff6fc8',1,'p1- soak tamarind & boil the toor dal','For Heerekayi Palya, first, soak a teaspoon of tamarind in 1/4 cup of water for 10 minutes. Next, to boil the dal, rinse and clean 1/4 cup of toor dal well and add it to a deep bottom pan along with 1 cup of water. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, 1 tsp of oil, and mix it well. Then, bring it to a boil over medium flame. As it comes to a boil, reduce the flame to low and cover the pan with a lid. Then, allow the dal to simmer for 10 minutes until it is cooked and tender. Do not overcook the dal as it should not be mashy. Then, turn off the flame and set it aside. While the dal simmers, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60bd1cd46aa4baac08ff6fc9','60bd1bf86aa4baac08ff6fc8',2,'p2- prepare the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Heerekayi Palya, wash and peel 2 medium-sized ridge gourds. Then cut 1.5 cups of ridge gourd into small cubes. Peel, wash, and finely chop 1/4 cup of onion. Peel and crush 1 tsp of garlic. Wash and pluck 7 nos curry leaves. Wash and finely chop 2 nos green chilies. Next, after soaking the tamarind, mash it well in water and strain the pulp in a bowl.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60bd1d314679878674289c3d','60bd1bf86aa4baac08ff6fc8',3,'m1- temper the oil and fry the onions','To make the Heerekayi Palya, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Next, add 1/4 tsp of mustard seeds,1/4 tsp of cumin seeds, 7 curry leaves, and 1 tsp of crushed garlic, followed by 1/4 cup of chopped onions. Stir and fry the onions over medium flame for 2-3 mins until the onions are translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('60bd1d9c76deac86bca5ce5a','60bd1bf86aa4baac08ff6fc8',4,'m2- simmer the ridge gourd','Next, add 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder, 2 chopped green chilies, and 1/4 teaspoon of hing. Saute it over low flame for a minute. After that, add 1.5 cups of diced ridge gourd, and mix it well. Add 1/4 cup of water and boil it over medium flame for a minute. Then, cover the pan with a lid and allow the ridge gourd to cook over low flame for 12-15 minutes until it is cooked through. Keep stirring it at regular intervals. While the curry is simmering, please move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('60bd1e0d6aa4baac08ff6fca','60bd1bf86aa4baac08ff6fc8',5,'m3- add the boiled toor dal & simmer the curry.  Serve','After simmering the Heerakayi Palya, remove the lid and add the boiled toor dal followed by the prepared tamarind pulp and 1 tsp of jaggery. Add 1 tsp of salt and mix it well. Next, add 1 tsp of uchellu powder(ramtil powder) and mix it well. Then, cover the pan with a lid and allow it to simmer over low flame for another 2-3mins. After that, turn off the flame and remove the curry into a serving bowl and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60beefdb76deac86bca5ce5b','60beef5b4679878674289c3f',1,'p1- prepare the inngredients','To prepare the ingredients for Ashgourd Majjige Huli, first, soak 2 tablespoons of chana dal in 1/4 cup of water for 15 minutes. Next, wash, peel and cube 3/4 cup of ash gourd. Grate half a cup of coconut in a bowl. Wash and slit 2 green chilies. Wash, peel, and slice 1/4 inch piece of ginger. wash and pluck 7 nos curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":17,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60bef04676deac86bca5ce5c','60beef5b4679878674289c3f',2,'m1- simmer the ash gourd','To make the Ash Gourd Majjige Huli, add 3/4 cup of chopped ash gourd to a deep bottom pan along with 1 cup of water. Add half a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Then, allow it to boil over medium flame for 10-12 mins or until the ash gourd becomes soft and tender. While the ash gourd is boiling, move towards the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60bef09e76deac86bca5ce5d','60beef5b4679878674289c3f',3,'m2- prepare the masala paste','To prepare the masala paste for Ashgourd Majjige Huli, in a blender jar add half a cup of grated fresh coconut, followed by add 2 slit green chili, 1/4 inch piece of sliced ginger, and 2 tablespoons of soaked chana dal. Next, add 1 tsp of cumin seeds,1/4 tsp of turmeric powder, and 1/4 cup of water. Cover the jar with a lid and blend it well into a fine paste.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('60bef11076deac86bca5ce5e','60beef5b4679878674289c3f',4,'m3- Add the masala paste & curd  to the curry & simmer','After simmering the Ash gourd for Majige Huli, add the prepared masala paste and mix it well. Then season the curry with half a teaspoon of salt. Next, reduce the flame to low and then add 1/2 a cup of curd while stirring it continuously until it is well combined. Do not add the curd over the high flame as it might split and make sure to stir the curry until the curd is well combined. Then, cook it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and set it aside','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('60bef18576deac86bca5ce5f','60beef5b4679878674289c3f',5,'m4- add the tempering to  the curry & serve','To make the tempering for Ash gourd Majjige Huli, heat a tempering pan and add 2 teaspoons of oil, add 1/2 a tsp of urad dal, add 1/2 tsp of mustard seeds, add 1 dried red chilli, and 7 curry leaves, mix it well and allow it to splutter. Then, turn off the flame and add the tempering to the prepared Majjige Huli, mix well and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60bef4e84679878674289c40','60bef49a76deac86bca5ce60',1,'p1- boil the potatoes','To boil the potato for Tomato Potato Gojju, wash 2 medium-sized potatoes and add it to a pressure cooker along with 1 cup of water. Cover it with a lid and pressure cook the potatoes over a high flame until 1 whistle. Then, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook the potatoes for another 8 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally.  While the potatoes are boiling, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60bef5446aa4baac08ff6fcc','60bef49a76deac86bca5ce60',2,'p2- boil the tomatoes','To boil the tomatoes for Tomato Potato Gojju, wash and add 2 medium-sized tomatoes to a deep bottom pan along with 3 cups of water and 1/4 teaspoon of salt. Then, allow it to boil over medium flame for 6-7 mins or until you see the skin of the tomato start peeling off. Then, turn off the flame, and remove the tomatoes to a bowl. Allow them to slightly cool. Then, gently peel off the skin and mash them well using a masher.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":7,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60bef58f76deac86bca5ce61','60bef49a76deac86bca5ce60',3,'p3- prepare the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Tomato Potato Gojju, wash and slit 2 green chilies. Wash and pluck 7 curry leaves. Wash and finely chop 1 tbsp of coriander leaves. Next, after boiling the potatoes, open the lid of the pressure cooker and carefully remove the boiled potatoes onto a plate. Then, gently peel off the skin and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('60bef6126aa4baac08ff6fcd','60bef49a76deac86bca5ce60',4,'m1- Combine the boiled potatoes with mashed tomatoes & curd','To make the Tomato Potato Gojju, add the prepared tomato puree to a mixing bowl followed by the boiled potatoes. Then, mash the potatoes well using a masher and combine it well with the tomato puree. Next, add 1/2 a tsp of salt followed by 2 slit green chilies and 1/4 teaspoon of hing. Mix it well and add about 1/4 cup of water to adjust the consistency. Next, add 1/2 a cup of curd and mix it well.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60bef6716aa4baac08ff6fce','60bef49a76deac86bca5ce60',5,'m2- add the tempering to the gojju & serve','To make the tempering for Tomato Potato Gojju, heat a tempering pan and add 2 tsp of coconut oil, after it becomes hot add 1/2 a tsp of mustard seeds followed by 7 nos curry leaves and 1/4 teaspoon high, saute for a few seconds and allow the tempering to splutter over medium flame. Then, turn off the flame and add the tempering to the prepared gojju. Mix it well and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('60bf007276deac86bca5ce62','60beffd94679878674289c41',1,'p1- dice the snake gourd & prepare other ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Snake Gourd Tambuli, wash, peel and cut one small snake gourd in half and scoop out the seeds. Then, dice half a cup of snake gourd into small cubes.  Grate 1/4 cup of coconut. Wash and slit 1 green chili. Wash and pluck 7 nos curry leaves. Next, add half a cup of curd to the mixing bowl and whisk it well using a whisk until smooth.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60bf010d76deac86bca5ce63','60beffd94679878674289c41',2,'m1- boil the snake gourd','To cook the snake gourd for the Snake Gourd Tambuli, add 3/4 cup of diced snake gourd to a deep bottom pan along with 1 cup of water. Add half a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Then, cover it with a lid and allow it to boil over medium flame for 10-12 mins until the snake gourd is cooked completely. Then, turn off the flame and allow it cool for some time. While the snake gourd is boiling, move towards the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60bf01936aa4baac08ff6fcf','60beffd94679878674289c41',3,'m2- puree the boiled snake gourd & add it to the whisked curd','To prepare the Snakegourd Tambuli, in a blender jar add 1/4 cup of grated coconut, followed by 1 slit green chili, add 1/2 a tsp of cumin seeds, and 1/2 a tsp of salt. Cover the jar with a lid and blend it well into a fine paste. Next, open the lid of the jar and add the boiled snake gourd and blend it again into a fine puree. Remove it in a bowl and add half a cup of whisked curd. Mix it well and add some water if required to adjust the consistency of the Tambuli.','cook_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('60bf02046aa4baac08ff6fd0','60beffd94679878674289c41',4,'m3- add the tempering to the tambuli & serve','To make the tempering for Snake gourd Tambuli, heat 2 teaspoons of oil in a tempering pan. Next, add 1/2 a tsp of mustard seeds followed by 1/2 a tsp of urad dal, 1 broken red dried red chili, and 7 curry leaves. Then, saute for a few seconds and allow the tempering to splutter. Turn off the flame and pour the tempering over the prepared snake gourd tambuli and mix well. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60bf04716aa4baac08ff6fd1','60bf04134679878674289c42',1,'ap1- soak the horse gram and rice in water','To soak the horse gram dal for Horse Gram Dosa, in a mixing bowl add 1/4 cup of horse gram, along with 2 cups of water and rinse the horse gram dal, then strain the horse gram and discard the water. Then to dal add 1 cup of fresh water and allow it to soak for 6 hours. Next, rinse and add 1 cup of rice to another bowl and soak it in 2 cups of water for 6 hours. While the dal and rice are soaking, move towards the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":360,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60bf04b84679878674289c43','60bf04134679878674289c42',2,'ap2- prepare the batter and allow it to ferment','To make the batter for horse gram dosa, in the blender jar, strain and add the soaked horse gram dal along with half a cup of water, and blend it into a smooth paste. Transfer it to a mixing bowl and set aside. Next, strain and add the soaked rice to the same blender jar along with 1/4 cup of water and blend it well into a smooth paste. Then, add it to the prepared horse gram batter and mix it well. Cover the batter with a plate and allow it to ferment for 8-10 hours. While the batter ferments, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":600,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60bf053d76deac86bca5ce65','60bf04134679878674289c42',3,'m1- prepare the dosa from the fermented batter & serve','To make the Horse Gram Dosa, add 1/2 a tsp of salt to the fermented batter and mix it well. Next, heat the tawa over medium flame. Next, pour a ladle full of the dosa batter to the center of the tawa and spread it into a thin round dosa as shown. Add 1/2 a tsp of oil on the edges of the dosa to ensure easy removal, then cover the pan with a lid and allow the dosa to cook on a medium flame for a minute. After that, carefully flip the dosa and cook the other side over medium flame for 1-2 minutes until the dosa is crisp and golden brown. Then, turn off the flame, fold the dosa and remove it onto a serving plate. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60c047a74679878674289c44','60c045e976deac86bca5ce67',1,'p1- cut the beans and prepare other ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Alasande Palya, first, soak a teaspoon of tamarind in 1/4 cup of water for 10 minutes. Next, wash and trim the end of the long beans and finely chop 1.5 cups of long beans. Grate 1/4 cup of coconut, remove in a bowl, and set aside. Then, wash and slit 2 green chilies. Wash and pluck 7 nos curry leaves. Next, after soaking the tamarind, mash it well in water and strain the pulp in a bowl.','prep_method','{"active_time":17,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('60c0481b76deac86bca5ce69','60c045e976deac86bca5ce67',2,'m1- simmer the beans','To make Alasande Palya, heat a tablespoon of coconut oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Next, add 1/2 a tsp of mustard seed, followed by 1/2 a tsp of urad dal, 1 dried red chili, and 7 curry leaves. Then, saute it over low flame for a few seconds. Next, add 1.5 cups of chopped long beans and fry them over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Add 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder followed by 1 tsp of salt, and 1/4 cup of water. Mix it well and cover it with a lid and allow it to cook for 5-6 minutes over medium flame. While the beans cook, move towards the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('60c048634679878674289c45','60c045e976deac86bca5ce67',3,'m2- prepare the coconut masala paste','To make the coconut masala paste for Alasande Palya, in a blender jar, add 1/4 cup of grated coconut, 1 dried red chili followed by 1/2 a tsp of cumin seeds, and grind it well into a coarse mixture. Then, remove it in a bowl and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60c048ab6aa4baac08ff6fd3','60c045e976deac86bca5ce67',4,'m3- cook the beans with the masala paste and serve','After simmering the long beans for Alasande Palya, carefully remove the lid and add the prepared tamarind pulp along with 1 tsp of jaggery powder and 2 slit green chilies. Mix it well. Then cover the pan with a lid and allow it to cook for another 5 mins over medium flame or until the beans are tender. After that, add the prepared coconut masala paste into the pan and mix it well. Fry the palya over medium-high flame 1-2 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and remove it in a serving bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60c0715a76deac86bca5ce6a','60c070716aa4baac08ff6fd5',1,'p1- boil the dal','To boil the toor dal for Malabar Spinach Curry, first, rinse and clean 1/4 cup of toor dal well with water and add it to a pressure cooker along with half a cup of water. Then, cover it with a lid and pressure cook the dal over high flame until 1 whistle. Then, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook the dal for another 8 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the dal is boiling, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60c071d14679878674289c46','60c070716aa4baac08ff6fd5',2,'p2- prepare the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Malabar Spinach Curry, first, soak a teaspoon of tamarind in 1/4 cup of water for 10 minutes. Next, rinse and clean a bunch of Malabar spinach with water thoroughly to remove all the mud. Next, discard the root ends and finely chop 2 cups of spinach leaves including the tender stems. Peel, wash, and finely slice half a cup of onions. Grate half a cup of coconut using a grater. Wash 7 curry leaves well with water. Next, after soaking the tamarind, mash it well with water and strain the pulp in a bowl.','prep_method','{"active_time":17,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('60c072214679878674289c47','60c070716aa4baac08ff6fd5',3,'m1- simmer the spinach','To make Malabar Spinach Spinach Curry, add 2 cups of chopped Malabar spinach leaves to a deep bottom pan along with 1/4 cup of sliced onions and 1/4 cup of water. Mix it well and cover the pan with a lid. Next, add 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder, add 1 teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Then, allow it to cook over medium flame for 7-8 mins or until the spinach leaves wilt. While the spinach simmers, please move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('60c072706aa4baac08ff6fd6','60c070716aa4baac08ff6fd5',4,'m2- prepare the masala paste','To make the coconut masala paste for Malabar Spinach Curry, first, heat a teaspoon of cooking oil in a pan and add 1 dry red chili. Fry the chili over low flame for a few seconds. Then, turn off the flame and remove it in a blender jar. Next, add in half a cup of grated fresh coconut, followed by the soaked tamarind pulp and 1/4 cup of water. Then, cover the jar with a lid and blend it well into a smooth paste.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('60c072c16aa4baac08ff6fd7','60c070716aa4baac08ff6fd5',5,'m3- add boiled toor dal, & masala paste to the curry & simmer','After simmering the Malabar spinach, add the cooked toor dal and mix it well. Allow it to cook over medium flame for 2 mins. Then, add the prepared masala paste to the curry and mix it well. Add 1 tsp of jaggery and bring the curry to boil over low flame. Then, turn off the flame and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('60c0730a4679878674289c48','60c070716aa4baac08ff6fd5',6,'m4- add the tempering to the curry & serve','To make the tempering for Malabar Spinach Curry, heat a pan and add 2 tsp of oil and allow it to become hot, then add 1/2 a tsp of mustard seeds, along with 7 curry leaves, and saute on low flame for a few seconds or until the tempering splutters. Then, add 1/4 cup of sliced onions and fry it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until it turns translucent. After that, turn off the flame and add the tempering to the prepared Malabar spinach curry. Remove it in a serving bowl and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60c0756b4679878674289c4b','60c0750a4679878674289c4a',1,'p1- par-boil the toor dal','To boil the toor dal for Dill leaves stir fry, first, rinse and clean 1/4 cup of toor dal well with water and add it to a deep bottom pan along with 1 cup of water. Add 1/4 teaspoon of salt, and a tsp of cooking oil and bring it to a boil over high flame. Then, reduce the flame to medium and allow it to boil for another 6-8 minutes until the toor dal is half-cooked. To check if the toor dal is half-cooked, strain a toor dal from the boiling water and press it between your fingers, the dal should just break and not become mushy. After it is half cooked, turn off the flame, strain the half-cooked dal, and set it aside. While the dal is boiling, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('60c075c36aa4baac08ff6fd8','60c0750a4679878674289c4a',2,'p2- chop the dill leaves & prepare other ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Dill Leaves Stir Fry, rinse a bunch of dill leaves thoroughly with water. Next, slice off the root ends and finely chop 1.5 cups of dill leaves. Then, peel and finely chop 1/2 a cup of onion. Peel and crush 3 cloves of garlic. Wash and pluck 7 nos of curry leaves. Wash and slit 2 green chilies.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60c076166aa4baac08ff6fd9','60c0750a4679878674289c4a',3,'m1- temper the oil & fry the onions','To make the dill leaves stir fry, heat a tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Next, add 1/2 a tsp of mustard seeds, 1/2 a tsp of urad dal, 7 curry leaves, and saute it on low flame for a few seconds or until it splutters. Next, add 3 cloves of crushed garlic, followed by 1/2 a cup of chopped onions and 2 slit green chilies. Then, fry the onions over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60c076584679878674289c4c','60c0750a4679878674289c4a',4,'m2- simmer the dill leaves','After frying the onions, add 1.5 cups of chopped dill leaves, and saute it for 2-3 mins over medium-low flame until the greens wilt. Then season it with 1 tsp of salt and mix it well. Next, cover the pan with a lid and allow it to cook over low flame for 4-5 mins while stirring in between, to prevent the dill leaves from burning. While the dill leaves simmer, please move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60c0768976deac86bca5ce6b','60c0750a4679878674289c4a',5,'m3- add the boiled toor dal & cook.','After simmering the dill leaves, carefully remove the lid and add in the boiled toor dal. Mix it well and fry the sabzi over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Then, cover the pan with a lid and allow it to simmer for another minute. Then, turn off the flame and plate the sabzi into a serving dish. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":1,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60c704076aa4baac08ff6fde','60c703b06aa4baac08ff6fdd',1,'p1- soak the tamarind & pressure cook the rice','For Kayi Sasive Chitranna, first, soak a teaspoon of tamarind in 1/4 cup of water for 15 minutes. Next, to boil the rice, rinse 1 cup of sona masuri rice well with water. Then, add it to a pressure cooker along with 2 cups of water. Then, cover it with a lid and pressure cook the rice over a high flame until 1 whistle. Then, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook the rice for another 8 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the rice is cooking, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('60c7049a76deac86bca5ce6f','60c703b06aa4baac08ff6fdd',2,'p2- prepare the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Kayi Sasive Chitranna, Grate 1/4 cup of coconut using a grater. Wash and slit 1 green chili. Wash 7 curry leaves. Next, to prepare the masala paste, add 1/4 cup of grated coconut to a blender jar followed by 1/2 a tsp of mustard seeds and 2 dry red chilies. Do not add any water, cover the blender with a lid and blend it into a coarse mixture. Next, after soaking the tamarind, mash it well with water and strain the pulp in a bowl.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60c705294679878674289c4e','60c703b06aa4baac08ff6fdd',3,'m1- Temper the oil and roast the peanuts','To make Kayi Sasive Chitranna, heat a tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame. Next, add 1/2 a tsp of mustard seeds, 1/2 a tsp of urad dal, 1 tsp of chana dal, and 7 curry leaves. Saute it over low flame for a few seconds until the tempering splutters. Next, add 1 dried red chili along with 2 tablespoons of peanuts. Stir and fry the peanuts over medium flame for 1-2 minutes until it is slightly golden.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60c705ca76deac86bca5ce70','60c703b06aa4baac08ff6fdd',4,'m2- cook the masala paste and add the boiled rice.','Next, add in the prepared tamarind water, followed by 1 slit green chili and 1 tbsp of jaggery powder. Mix it well. Then, add 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder and a tsp of salt to it. Stir and cook it over low flame for a minute or until the jaggery melts and the tempering slightly thickens. After that, add the prepared masala paste and cook it over medium flame for a minute. Then, add the boiled rice and gently mix it with the masala. Stir and fry it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and plate the rice. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60c7086f6aa4baac08ff6fdf','60c708024679878674289c50',1,'p1- slice and marinate the bitter gourds','For Bittergourd Gojju, first, soak 2 teaspoons of tamarind in half a cup of water for 15 minutes. Next, wash and cut 3/4 cup of bitter gourd in thin round slices as shown. Then, add the sliced bitter gourd to a mixing bowl followed by a teaspoon of salt and 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder. Rub the salt well onto the bitter gourd and allow it to sweat for 20 minutes. Do not skip this step as it is important to prep the bitter gourd before making the curry. Salt will draw out the bitterness from the bitter gourd. While the bitter gourds sweat, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60c708dc6aa4baac08ff6fe0','60c708024679878674289c50',2,'p2- dry roast the sesame seeds and prepare other ingredients','To dry roast the sesame seeds for Bittergourd Gojju, heat up a pan over medium and add 2 tbsp of black sesame seeds to it. Then, dry roast the sesame seeds over low flame for 2 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and remove it in a bowl. Next, grate 1/4 cup of fresh coconut using a grater. Wash and pluck 12 curry leaves. Next, after soaking the tamarind, mash it well with water and strain the pulp in a bowl.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('60c7096476deac86bca5ce71','60c708024679878674289c50',3,'p3- prepare the masala paste','To prepare the masala paste for Bitter Gourd Gojju, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Next, add 1 tablespoon of urad dal followed by 1/2 a tespoon of chana dal, 2 dried red chilies 7 nos curry leaves, and 1/4 tsp of fenugreek seeds. Then, roast the whole spices over low flame for 1-2 minutes until the spices are fragrant and slightly brown in color. Then, turn off the flame and remove the roasted spices in a blender jar. Add the roasted black sesame seeds followed by 1/4 cup of grated coconut and 1/4 cup of water. Then, cover the jar with a lid and blend it well into a fine paste. Next, after sweating the bitter gourds, rinse them well with water to remove the salt and set it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60c70a154679878674289c51','60c708024679878674289c50',4,'m1- simmer the bitter gourds','To make Bittergourd Gojju, heat 1 tablespoon of cooking oil in a kadai over medium flame for a minute. Then, add 1/4 tsp of mustard seeds, 1/4 tsp of urad dal, 5 curry leaves, and saute it over low flame for a few seconds until the ingredients splutter. Then, add the prepared bitter gourd and fry it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes. Next, add half a cup of prepared tamarind water followed by 1/4 cup of jaggery and 1 teaspoon of salt. Mix it well and add 1/4 cup of water. Then, cover the pan with a lid and allow it to simmer over low flame for 5-6 minutes until the bitter gourds are tender. While it simmers, please move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('60c70a656aa4baac08ff6fe1','60c708024679878674289c50',5,'m2- cook the bitter gourds with masala paste and serve','After simmering the bitter Gourd Gojju, carefully remove the lid and add the prepared masala paste. Mix it well. Then, add about 1/4 cup of water to adjust the consistency of the gojju. Then, cook it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until the gravy thickens. After that, turn off the flame and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60c70d4a4679878674289c53','60c70d034679878674289c52',1,'p1- boil the toor dal','For Amarantha Leaes Curry, first, soak a teaspoon of tamarind in 1/4 cup of water for 15 minutes. Next, to boil the toor dal, rinse and clean 1/2 cup of toor dal well with water and add it to a pressure cooker along with 1 cup of water. Then, cover it with a lid and pressure cook the dal over high flame until 1 whistle. Then, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook the dal for another 8 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the dal is boiling, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60c70de24679878674289c54','60c70d034679878674289c52',2,'p2- prep the greens & other ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Amarantha Leaves Curry, rinse a bunch of amaranth leaves thoroughly with water and dab it with a kitchen towel to dry off the water. Then, trim the stems and finely chop 1.5 cups of amaranth leaves. Wash and slit 1 nos green chili. Wash and pluck 7 nos curry leaves. Next, after soaking the tamarind, mash it well with water and strain the pulp in a bowl.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('60c70e3876deac86bca5ce73','60c70d034679878674289c52',3,'m1- simmer the amaranth leaves','To make the Amaranth Leaves Curry, add 1.5 cups of chopped amaranth leaves to a deep bottom pan. Next, add the prepared tamarind pulp followed by 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder, 1 tsp of salt, 1 slit green chili, and 1 tsp of jaggery.  Mix it well and add 1/4 cup of water. Then, cover the pan with a lid and cook it over medium flame for 6 minutes. While it simmers, please move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('60c70e7776deac86bca5ce74','60c70d034679878674289c52',4,'m2- add the boiled toor dal to the curry & simmer','After simmering the Amaranth Leaves Curry, carefully remove the lid and add 2 teaspoons of sambar powder. Mix it well and add half a cup of water followed by half cup of cooked toor dal. Mix it well and bring the curry to boil over medium flame. Then, allow it to cook over low flame for 2-3 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set it aside. While the curry simmers, please move onto the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('60c70ed376deac86bca5ce75','60c70d034679878674289c52',5,'m3- add the tempering to the curry & serve','To prepare the tempering for Amaranth Leaves Curry, heat 1 tsp of cooking oil in a tempering pan. Next, add 1/2 a tsp of mustard seeds, add 1/2 a tsp of urad dal, 7 curry leaves, and 1/4 teaspoon of hing. Then, saute it for a few seconds over low flame until the tempering splutters. Then, turn off the flame and add the tempering to the prepared curry. Mix it well and remove it in a serving bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('60c85fc64679878674289c78','60c85f7076deac86bca5ce76',1,'p1- slice the bitter gourds and soak the tamarind','To prepare the ingredients for Bitter Gourd Fry, first, soak a teaspoon of tamarind in 1/4 cup of water for 10 minutes. Next, wash and slice 1 cup of bitter gourds and remove the thick seeds off the slices if any. Next, after soaking the tamarind, mash it well with water and strain the pulp in a bowl.','prep_method','{"active_time":14,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60c8604176deac86bca5ce77','60c85f7076deac86bca5ce76',2,'p2- coat the bitter gourds in the flour mixture','To prepare the Bitter Gourds for Bittergourd Fry, add the sliced bitter gourds to a mixing bowl followed by 2 tablespoons of rice flour and a tablespoon of cornflour. Add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, a teaspoon of salt, 2 tablespoons of sambar powder, and the tamarind pulp. Mix it well and coat the bitter gourd slices evenly with the flour mix. Sprinkle some water and mix it well.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('60c8608a4679878674289c79','60c85f7076deac86bca5ce76',3,'m1- fry the bitter gourds and serve','To fry the bitter gourds for Bittergourd Fry, first, heat 1 cup of cooking oil in kadai over medium flame for 2-3 minutes. Next,  drop in the coated bitter gourd slices in small batches to the hot oil and fry them over medium flame for 4-5 minutes, until the bitter gourds turn crisp and golden brown. Then, turn off the flame and remove the fried bitter gourds onto a kitchen napkin to dab off the excess oil. Then, plate the fried bitter gourds and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60c887df70dcb78de45cf7dd','60c8866876deac86bca5ce79',1,'p1- prep the greens and other ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Drumstick Leaves Soup, first, rinse and clean a bunch of drumstick leaves thoroughly with water. Then, remove the stems and pick 1 cup of drumstick leaves. Next rinse and clean 2 tbsp of yellow moong dal well with water. Wash and roughly chop 1/2 a cup of tomatoes. Wash and cut a lemon into halves. Then, squeeze 2 teaspoons of lemon juice into a bowl.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60c88a0076deac86bca5ce7a','60c8866876deac86bca5ce79',2,'m1- boil the drumstick leaves','To make the Drumstick Leaves Soup, add 1 cup of drumstick leaves to a pressure cooker followed by 2 tablespoons of yellow moong dal and 1/2 a cup of chopped tomatoes. Next, add 2 cups of water and cover it with a lid. Then, pressure cooks it over a high flame until 2 whistles. After the second whistle, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook it for another 5 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and allow the pressure cooker to release air naturally. While the drumstick leaves are boiling, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":14,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60c88ae976deac86bca5ce7b','60c8866876deac86bca5ce79',3,'m2- Season the soup and boil. Garnish & serve','After boiling the drumstick leaves for Drumstick leaves soup, remove the lid of the pressure cooker and strain the leaves using a strainer as shown. Mash the puree using a spatula into the strainer by pressing it in a downwards motion to strain the fibers. Then, add this stock back into the pan. Season it with half a teaspoon of salt and half a teaspoon of black pepper powder. Mix it well and boil the soup over medium flame for 2-3 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and add 2 teaspoons of lemon juice. Mix it well and divide the soup among bowls. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60cadbed76deac86bca5ce80','60cadb8070dcb78de45cf7e0',1,'p1- soak the lentil and prep the other ingredients','For Moong Dal Rasam, first, rinse and soak half a cup of yellow mong dal in 1 cup of water for 15 minutes. Next, peel, and finely chop a teaspoon of garlic. Wash and finely chop a tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash and pluck 7 curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":7,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('60cadcce4679878674289c7b','60cadb8070dcb78de45cf7e0',2,'p2- roast and pound the spices into a coarse powder','To roast the spices for Moong Dal Rasam,  heat 1 tsp of ghee in a pan over medium flame. Then, add 1 tsp of cumin seeds followed by half a teaspoon of black peppercorns and roast it over low flame for 1-2 minutes until the spices are fragrant. Then, then turn off the flame and transfer the roasted spices into a mortar and pound it using a pestle as shown into a slightly coarse powder.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('60cadd0f76deac86bca5ce81','60cadb8070dcb78de45cf7e0',3,'p3- boil the soaked moong dal','To boil the dal for Moong Dal Rasam, add the soaked dal to a pressure cooker along with 1 cup of water. Then, cover it with a lid and pressure cook the dal over high flame until 1 whistle. Then, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook the dal for another 8 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the dal is boiling, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60cae05e4679878674289c7c','60cadb8070dcb78de45cf7e0',4,'m1- Boil the rasam with ground spices','To make Moong Dal Rasam, add the boiled dal to a deep bottom pan. Next, add the ground spices followed by 1 tsp of salt and 7 curry leaves. Mix it well and allow the sambar to come to boil over medium flame. Then, turn off the flame and add 2 teaspoons of lemon juice. Mix it well and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60cae0b44679878674289c7d','60cadb8070dcb78de45cf7e0',5,'m2- add the tempering to the sambar & serve','To make the tempering for Moong Dal Rasam, heat 2 teaspoons of ghee in a pan over medium flame. Next, add 1 teaspoon of chopped garlic and fry it over low flame for 2-3 minutes until it turns slightly brown. Then turn off the flame and add the tempering to the prepared rasam. Garnish it with a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and serve.\','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60cae3fc76deac86bca5ce83','60cae3bc70dcb78de45cf7e1',1,'p1- roast and grind the poha into fine powder','To prepare the poha for poha balls, first, add 1 cup of flattened rice to a pan and dry roast it over medium flame for 3-4 minutes until the poha is slightly golden brown and crisp. Keep stirring the poha while roasting it. Then, turn off the flame and transfer the roasted poha to a blender jar. Allow it to slightly cool. Then, cover the jar with a lid and pulse grind it into a fine powder. Remove it in a bowl and set it aside','prep_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('60cae42876deac86bca5ce84','60cae3bc70dcb78de45cf7e1',2,'p2- roast the rava','To roast the rava for Poha Balls, add 1/2 a cup of rava to a pan and dry roast it over medium flame for 3-4 minutes until it is slightly golden brown. Then, turn off the flame and set it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60cae4874679878674289c7e','60cae3bc70dcb78de45cf7e1',3,'p3- prepare the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Poha Balls, wash and peel a medium-sized carrot, and grate 2 tablespoons of carrot using a grater. Next, wash and finely chop 1 green chili. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of curry leaves. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves. Grate 3 tbsp of fresh coconut using a grater.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60cae50670dcb78de45cf7e2','60cae3bc70dcb78de45cf7e1',4,'m1- prepare the dough and make the poha balls','To make the dough for poha balls, add the ground poha powder to a mixing bowl followed by the roasted rava.  Next, add 1/2 a tsp of salt, 1 chopped green chilies, 1 tbsp of chopped curry leaves, 2 tablespoons of grated carrot, and add 2 tablespoons of chopped coriander leaves. Mix it well using a spoon. Then, add 1/4 cup of water gradually to it, as and when required, and knead it well into a smooth dough. Then, divide the dough into equal portions and shape them into small round balls as shown.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60cae52f76deac86bca5ce85','60cae3bc70dcb78de45cf7e1',5,'m2- steam the poha balls','To steam the poha balls, set up the steamer, add 2 cups of water to the steamer and allow it to boil. Meanwhile grease the plate of the steamer and arrange the poha balls onto it. Then, carefully place it inside the steamer and cover it with a lid. Steam the poha balls over medium flame for 5 mins. After that, turn off the flame and set it aside. While the poha balls cook, please move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":5,"flame":3}'),('60cae5a476deac86bca5ce86','60cae3bc70dcb78de45cf7e1',6,'m3-  coat the poha balls in tempering and serve','To make the tempering for poha balls, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame. Then, add 1/2 a tsp of mustard seeds, add 1/2 a tsp of cumin seeds, 5 curry leaves, and saute it on low flame for a few seconds. Then, add the steamed poha balls to the tempering followed by 3 tablespoons of grated coconut, and toss them together in the pan to coat the balls evenly with the tempering. Then, turn off the flame and plate the poha balls onto a serving plate. Serve','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('60cb0aba70dcb78de45cf7e5','60cb09ff70dcb78de45cf7e4',1,'p1- prepare the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Pepper Rasam, first, soak a tablespoon of tamarind in 1/4 cup of water for 10 minutes. Next,  peel and finely chop 2 tsp of garlic. Wash, peel, and roughly chop a 1-inch piece of ginger. Wash and pluck 7 nos curry leaves. Next, add 1 teaspoon of cumin seeds to a mortar along with 1 teaspoon of black peppercorns and pound it into a coarse powder. Next, after soaking the tamarind, mash it well with water and strain the pulp in a bowl.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60cb0b3376deac86bca5ce87','60cb09ff70dcb78de45cf7e4',2,'m1- boil the rasam with the ground masala powder','To make the Pepper Rasam, add 1/4 cup of the tamarind water to a pan followed by a 1-inch piece of chopped ginger and 1 tbsp of jaggery. Next, add 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder and bring the rasam to boil over medium flame. Stir and boil the rasam until the jaggery melts. Then, add 1.5 cups of water, 1 tsp of salt, and the freshly ground cumin and pepper powder. Mix it well and allow it to boil over medium flame for 6-8 mins. Then, turn off the flame and set it aside. While the rasam boils, please move onto the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60cb0b9b4679878674289c7f','60cb09ff70dcb78de45cf7e4',3,'m2- add the tempering to the rasam and serve','To make the tempering for pepper rasam, heat 2 tsp of ghee in a tempering pan over medium flame. Next, add 2 tsp of chopped garlic, and7 curry leaves. Saute and fry the garlic over medium flame for 1-2 minutes until fragrant. Then, turn off the flame and add the tempering to the prepared rasam and mix it well. Divide the rasam among bowls and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60cc3eed70dcb78de45cf7e8','60cc3e9c70dcb78de45cf7e7',1,'p1- prep the spinach leaves and other ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Soppu Palya,  wash a bunch of spinach thoroughly with water to remove all the mud. Then, slice off the stem ends and finely chop 1.5 cups of spinach. Peel and finely chop 1/2 a cup of onions. Wash and pluck 7 nos curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60cc3f6470dcb78de45cf7e9','60cc3e9c70dcb78de45cf7e7',2,'m1- stir-fry the spinach leaves and simmer','To make the Soppu Palya, heat 2 teaspoons of ghee in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Then, add 1/2 a tsp of cumin seeds, 7 curry leaves, and 1/2 a cup of chopped onions. Stir and fry the onions over medium flame for 3-4 minutes until translucent. Next, add 1.5 cups of chopped spinach and fry it over low flame for 2 minutes. Season it with 3/4 tsp of salt and half a tsp of pepper powder and mix it well. Then, cover the pan with a lid and allow it to cook over medium-low flame for 5-6 mins. Then, turn off the flame and remove it in a serving bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('60d588344679878674289c91','60d586e07a06e422f7cfba95',1,'p1- peel and dice the banana stem','To prepare the ingredients for Banana Stem Fry, wash one piece of banana stem and peel the thick layer around the stem, then cut the stem into roundels and peel the fibre. Next, cut 1cup of banana stem slices into small cubes. Then, immerse the banana stem cubes into the water until later use. Next, grate 1/4 cup of coconut using a grater. Wash and pluck 7 nos curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":17,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60d588977a06e422f7cfba96','60d586e07a06e422f7cfba95',2,'p2- prepare the masala paste','To prepare the coconut masala for Banana Stem Fry, add 1/4 cup of grated coconut to a blender jar followed by add 1/2 a tsp of mustard seeds, and 1 dried red chili. Cover the jar with a lid and grind it well into a coarse mixture.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60d589c27a06e422f7cfba97','60d586e07a06e422f7cfba95',3,'m1- Fry the banana stem and simmer','To make the banana stem stir fry, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Then, add half a tsp of mustard seeds, 1/2 a tsp of urad dal, 7 curry leaves, and 2 dried red chilies. Saute it over low flame for a few seconds until the tempering splutters. Next, add 1 cup of cubed banana stem and fry it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Add a teaspoon of jaggery along with a teaspoon of salt. Sprinkle about 2 tablespoons of water and stir it well. Then, cover it with a lid and allow it to cook over medium-low flame for 6-8 minutes until the banana stem is tender. While it simmers, please move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60d58a3876deac86bca5cea9','60d586e07a06e422f7cfba95',4,'m2- add the masala paste','After simmering the banana stem, carefully remove the lid and the prepared coconut masala to it followed by 1/2 a tsp of turmeric powder. Mix it well. Then, saute and cook it over medium flame for another 3 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60d599aa7a06e422f7cfba98','60d5997076deac86bca5ceab',1,'ap1- soak the chickpeas','For Chana Usli, rinse and soak 1 cup of white chickpeas in 2 cups of water for 8-10 hours. While the chickpeas are soaking, please move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":600,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('60d59a047a06e422f7cfba99','60d5997076deac86bca5ceab',2,'p1- boil the soaked chickpeas','To boil the chickpeas for Chana Usli, add the soaked chickpeas to a pressure cooker along with 1 cup of water and 1 tsp of salt. Mix it well and cover the cooker with a lid. Then, pressure cook the chickpeas over a high flame until 3 whistles. Then, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook the chickpeas for another 5 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the chickpeas are boiling, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":18,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60d59a537a06e422f7cfba9a','60d5997076deac86bca5ceab',3,'p2- prep the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Chana Usli, grate 1/4 cup of coconut using a grater in a bowl. Wash and slit 1 green chili. Wash and pluck 7 nos curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60d59ade7a06e422f7cfba9b','60d5997076deac86bca5ceab',4,'m1- temper the chickpeas and simmer','To make Chana Usli, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Then, add 1/2 a tsp of mustard seeds,1/2 a tsp of cumin seeds, 1/2 a tsp of urad dal, 2 dried red chilies, and 7 nos curry leaves. Saute it over low flame for a few seconds until the ingredients splutter. Next, add 1 slit of green chili and saute it for a few seconds. After that, add in the boiled chickpeas and mix it well. Then, cover the pan with a lid and cook it over medium flame for 5 minutes. While the chana usli simmers, please move onto the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('60d59b307a06e422f7cfba9c','60d5997076deac86bca5ceab',5,'m2- fry the chickpeas and garnish the usli with grated coconut','After simmering the Chana Usli, carefully remove the lid and fry the chickpeas over medium-high flame for 1-2 minutes. Then, add 1/4 cup of grated coconut and mix it well. After that turn off the flame and remove it in a serving bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60d5a01c76deac86bca5cead','60d59fee76deac86bca5ceac',1,'ap1- soak the kokum','To soak the kokum for kokum rasam, in a mixing bowl add 1/4 cup of kokum and soak it in 1 cup of water for 1 hour. While the kokum soaks, please move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('60d5a08a76deac86bca5ceae','60d59fee76deac86bca5ceac',2,'p1- prep the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Kokum Rasam, wash and slit 1 green chili. Wash peel and finely slice 1-inch piece of ginger. Peel and crush 1 tsp of garlic. Wash and pluck 7 curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60d5a87876deac86bca5ceaf','60d59fee76deac86bca5ceac',3,'m1- simmer the rasam','To make the Kokum Rasam, place a strainer over a deep bottom pan as shown and add the soaked kokum along with the water. Mash the kokum into the strainer to extract the juice in the pan. Then, add 1 slit green chili followed by a 1-inch piece of sliced ginger, 1 teaspoon of jaggery, 1 teaspoon of salt, and 7 nos curry leaves. Mix it well and bring the rasam to boil over medium flame. As it comes to a rolling boil, reduce the flame to low and add 1 cup of coconut milk. Keep stirring it continuously over low flame until it is well combined. Make sure to add the coconut milk at low flame only to avoid it from splitting. Then, allow it to boil over medium flame for a minute. Turn off the flame and set it aside','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('60d5a8d94679878674289c92','60d59fee76deac86bca5ceac',4,'m2- add the tempering to the rasam and serve','To make the tempering for kokum rasam, heat a tempering pan and add 2 tsp of ghee and allow it to become hot, then add 1/2 a tsp of cumin seeds, add 1 tsp of crushed garlic, 7 curry leaves along with 1/4 tsp of hing. Saute it over low flame for a few seconds until it splutters. Then, turn off the flame add the tempering to the prepared rasam. Divide the rasam among bowls and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60d9ac214679878674289c94','60d9ac0aeaf3f9f340a58855',1,'p1- dry roast the rava','To roast the rava for Sajjige Bajil, heat a pan and add 1 cup of rava to it. Then, dry roast it over medium flame for 3-4 minutes until it turns slightly golden brown. Keep stirring the rava continuously. Then, turn off the flame and remove it in a bowl.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60d9ac3e4679878674289c95','60d9ac0aeaf3f9f340a58855',2,'p2- prep the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Sajjige Bajil, grate 3/4 cup of fresh coconut using a grater. Wash peel and finely chop a 1-inch piece of ginger. Wash and finely chop 1 teaspoon of green chilies. Wash and pluck 16 nos curry leaves. Then, wash and finely chop 1 tbsp of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('60d9ac624679878674289c96','60d9ac0aeaf3f9f340a58855',3,'m1- temper the oil with spices for Sajige','To make Sajige for Sajjige Bajil, heat 3 tablespoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Then, temper it with 1 tsp of mustard seeds, 1 tsp of cumin seeds, 1 tsp of urad dal, 1 tsp of chana dal, and 7 curry leaves. Saute it over low flame for a few seconds until the tempering splutters. Add a 1-inch piece of chopped ginger, followed by 1 teaspoon of chopped green chilies, and saute it for a few seconds. Next, add 3 cups of water along with 1 teaspoon of salt, and 1 teaspoon of sugar. Mix it well and bring it to a boil over medium flame.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60d9ac84eaf3f9f340a58856','60d9ac0aeaf3f9f340a58855',4,'m2- add the roasted rava and simmer','As the water comes to a rolling boil, reduce the flame to low and add 1 cup of roasted Rava to the boiling water and mix it well while continuously stirring it over a low flame to avoid any lumps. Then, cover the pan with a lid and allow the upma to cook over low flame for 4-5 minutes until the Rava absorbs all the water. While the upma simmers, please move onto the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('60d9ac9f4679878674289c97','60d9ac0aeaf3f9f340a58855',5,'m3- prepare the masala paste for Bajil','To make the masala for Bajil, add 1 tablespoon of coriander seeds to a blender jar followed by half a teaspoon of cumin seeds and 1 dry red chili. Then, cover the jar with a lid and grind it well into a slightly coarse powder.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60d9acb87a06e422f7cfba9f','60d9ac0aeaf3f9f340a58855',6,'m4- Garnish the sajige with coriander leaves and dessicated coconut','After simmering the Sajige for Sajige Bajil, carefully open the lid and give it a stir. Rava has absorbed all the water. Then, add 2 teaspoons of lemon juice, 2 tablespoons of grated fresh coconut along a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves. Mix it well and turn off the flame. Remove the upma in a serving bowl and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('60d9acf2eaf3f9f340a58857','60d9ac0aeaf3f9f340a58855',7,'m5- Cook the masala for Bajil','To make the Bajil, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Next, add 1 tsp of urad dal, 1 dry red chili, and 8 nos curry leaves. Saute it for a few seconds over low flame until it splutters. Then, add the prepared Bajil masala powder to the tempering and saute it over low flame for a minute. Next, add half a cup of grated coconut and mix it well. Stir and fry it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and take it off the flame.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('60d9ad2deaf3f9f340a58858','60d9ac0aeaf3f9f340a58855',8,'m6- prepare the Bajil and serve it along Sajige','Next, add half a teaspoon of salt followed by 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder and 1 tablespoon of jaggery. Mix it well.  Then, add 1 cup of thin rice flakes and mix it well using your hands while breaking the jaggery into small granules. Combine the rice flakes well with the prepared mixture. Then, remove it on a serving plate and serve it along with the prepared sajige.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60d9c6484679878674289c98','60d9c5e1eaf3f9f340a5885a',1,'p1- prep the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Vegetable Saagu, peel, wash, and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Peel, wash, and cut half a cup of potatoes into small dices. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of beans. Wash, peel, and finely chop 1/4 cup of carrot.','prep_method','{"active_time":16,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60d9c6ba7a06e422f7cfbaa0','60d9c5e1eaf3f9f340a5885a',2,'p2- grate coconut and prep other ingredients','Next, grate 1/2 a cup of coconut in a bowl using a grater. Wash and slit 1 green chili. Wash, peel, and roughly chop a 1-inch piece of ginger. Wash and roughly chop 1/4 cup of coriander leaves. wash and pluck 7 curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60d9c72deaf3f9f340a5885b','60d9c5e1eaf3f9f340a5885a',3,'m1- temper the oil and fry the onions','To make Vegetable saagu, heat 1 tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Then, add 1 tsp of mustard seeds, followed by 1 tsp of urad dal, 2 dried red chilies, 7 curry leaves, and 1/4 tsp of hing. Saute it over low flame for a few seconds until the tempering splutters. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions and fry it over medium flame for a minute. Then, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder and mix it well. Then, continue to fry the onions over medium flame for 2-3 minutes, until translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60d9c76eeaf3f9f340a5885c','60d9c5e1eaf3f9f340a5885a',4,'m2- add vegetables and simmer the curry','Next, add 1/4 a cup of chopped tomatoes, and cook them over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until tomatoes are tender. Then, add 1/4 cup of chopped carrot followed by 1/4 cup of chopped beans and half a cup of cubed potatoes. Mix it well and fry the vegetables over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Then, add 3/4 cup of water along with a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Then, cover the pan with a lid and allow the vegetables to cook over low flame for 5-6 minutes, until tender. While the vegetables are simmering, please move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('60d9c817eaf3f9f340a5885d','60d9c5e1eaf3f9f340a5885a',5,'m3- prepare the masala paste','To make the masala paste for vegetable saagu, add 1/2 a cup of grated coconut to a blender jar followed by a 1-inch piece of cinnamon stick, 1/4 tsp of black peppercorns, 2 green cardamoms, and 2 cloves. Next, add 1 green chili, 1-inch piece of ginger, 1 tbsp of coriander seeds, 1/4 tsp of cumin seeds, 1 tbsp of a roasted gram, and 1/4 cup of coriander leaves along with 1/4 cup of water. Then, cover the jar with a lid and blend it well into a smooth paste.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60d9c8517a06e422f7cfbaa1','60d9c5e1eaf3f9f340a5885a',6,'m4- add the masala paste and boil the curry','After simmering the Vegetable Saagu, carefully remove the lid and add the prepared masala paste to the cooked vegetables. Mix it well and bring it to a boil over medium flame. Then, turn off the flame, transfer the curry to a serving bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60dd81d2eaf3f9f340a58860','60dd816c4679878674289c9e',1,'p1- prep the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Bendekayi Majjige Huli, wash and pat dry the lady''s fingers using a kitchen towel. Then, trim the ends of the lady''s finger and roughly chop 1 cup of ladies finger. Grate 3/4 cup of fresh coconut. Wash and slit 2 green chilies. Wash and pluck 7 nos curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":2,"flame":0}'),('60dd82307a06e422f7cfbaa3','60dd816c4679878674289c9e',2,'m1- fry the ladies  fingers','To fry the ladies finger for Bendekayi Majjige Huli, heat a tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Next,  add 1 cup of chopped lady''s finger and fry them over medium-high flame for 3-4 minutes until tender-crisp. Then, turn off the flame and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60dd8274eaf3f9f340a58861','60dd816c4679878674289c9e',3,'m2- add the buttermilk and simmer the curry','To make Bendekayi Majige Huli, add 1 cup of buttermilk to a deep bottom pan and cook it over medium-low flame for 2-3 minutes while stirring it continuously to avoid the buttermilk from splitting. Next, add the sauteed ladies finger to the buttermilk and mix it well. Then, cover the pan with a lid and allow it to cook over low flame for 4-5 minutes until the ladies fingers are cooked completely. While the curry simmers, please move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('60dd82b0eaf3f9f340a58862','60dd816c4679878674289c9e',4,'m3- make the coconut masala paste','To make the masala paste for Bendekayi Majjige Huli, in a blender jar add 3/4 cup of grated coconut, followed by 2 green chilies, 1 tbsp of rice, and 1/4 cup of water. Cover the jar with a lid and blend it well into a fine paste.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60dd82f04679878674289c9f','60dd816c4679878674289c9e',5,'m4- add the masala paste to the curry & cook','After simmering the Bendekayi Majjige Huli, carefully open the lid and give it a stir. Then, add a teaspoon of salt along with 7 curry leaves and mix it well. Next, add the prepared masala paste and continue to cook it over medium flame for another 2-3 minutes, until the curry slightly thickens. Then, turn off the flame and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60dd8356eaf3f9f340a58863','60dd816c4679878674289c9e',6,'m5- add the tempering to the curry & serve','To make the tempering for Bendekayi Majige Huli, heat 2 teaspoons of ghee in a tempering pan over medium flame. Then, add 1/2 a tsp of mustard seeds, 1/2 a tsp of cumin seeds, 1/4 tsp of fenugreek seeds, 7 curry leaves, and 1 dried red chili. Saute it over low flame for a few seconds until the tempering splutters. Then, turn off the flame and add the tempering to the prepared majige huli. Mix it well and remove it into a serving bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('60dd85187a06e422f7cfbaa4','60dd84e4eaf3f9f340a58865',1,'ap1- soak the rava & lnetils','For Pumpkin Idli, In a mixing bowl add 1 cup of idli rava followed by 3 cups of water and rinse it well. Then, strain the Rava and drain the water. Next, soak the Rava in 3/4 cup of water for 1 hour. Next, to a separate bowl, add in a tablespoon of yellow moong dal and a tablespoon of chana dal. Then, soak the lentils in 1/4 cup of water for 30 minutes. While the Rava and lentils soak, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":60,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60dd85777a06e422f7cfbaa5','60dd84e4eaf3f9f340a58865',2,'p1- grate the pumpkin and prep other ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Pumpkin Idli, wash and peel half a pumpkin, and scoop out the seeds. Then, grate 3/4 cup of the pumpkin using a grater and remove it in a bowl. Next, grate 1/4 cup of fresh coconut. wash and finely chop 1 green chili. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Next, grease the idli plate with a teaspoon of oil using an oil brush.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('60dd85dc4679878674289ca0','60dd84e4eaf3f9f340a58865',3,'p2- prepare and rest the idli batter','To prepare the batter for Pumpkin Idli, add 3/4 cup of grated pumpkin to the soaked rava followed by the soaked lentils and 1/4 cup of grated coconut. Next, add 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves, half a teaspoon of cumin seeds, half a teaspoon of black pepper powder, and 1 teaspoon of salt. Mix it well and allow it to rest for 10 minutes. While the batter is resting, move on to the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60dd86187a06e422f7cfbaa6','60dd84e4eaf3f9f340a58865',4,'m1- steam the Idly and serve','To make the Pumpkin Idli, first, set up the steamer for the Idlis. Add the required water in the steamer and allow it to boil over medium flame. Next, portion an equal amount of batter, add it into the idli molds as shown. Then, carefully place the idli plate inside the steamer and cover it with a lid. Allow the idli to steam over medium flame for 12 minutes. Then, turn off the flame, demould the idli, and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60dd98467a06e422f7cfbaa7','60dd8844eaf3f9f340a58867',1,'ap1- soak the moth beans','To soak the beans for Moth Beans Curry, add 1.5 cups of moth beans to a bowl and soak them in 2 cups of water for 6 hours. While the beans are soaking, please move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":360,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60dd98d67a06e422f7cfbaa8','60dd8844eaf3f9f340a58867',2,'p1- prepare the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Moth Beans Curry, first, soak a teaspoon of tamarind in 1/4 cup of water for 10 minutes. Next, peel, wash and finely chop half a cup of onions. Grate a tablespoon of fresh coconut using a grater. Peel and crush 6 cloves of garlic. Wash, peel, and roughly chop 1/4 inch piece of ginger. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash and pluck 7 curry leaves. Next, after soaking the tamarind, mash it well with water and strain the tamarind water in a bowl.','prep_method','{"active_time":17,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60dd99324679878674289ca1','60dd8844eaf3f9f340a58867',3,'m1- fry the onions','To make Moth Beans Curry, in a pan, heat 1 tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Then, temper the oil with half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, half a teaspoon of cumin seeds, and 7 curry leaves. Then, allow it to splutter over low flame. Next, add half a cup of chopped onions followed by 6 cloves of crushed garlic and fry it over medium flame for 3-4 minutes until onions are translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}');
INSERT INTO catalog_recipe_steps VALUES
('60dd99947a06e422f7cfbaa9','60dd8844eaf3f9f340a58867',4,'m2- add the moth beans & simmer the curry','Next, add half a teaspoon of garam masala, followed by half a teaspoon red chili powder, and 1 teaspoon salt. Mix it well and fry the masala over low flame for a minute. Then, add the soaked moth beans and mix it well. Next, add 1/4 cup of water and cover the pan with a lid. Cook the moth beans over low flame for 7-8 minutes until they are tender. While the beans simmer, please move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('60dd99efeaf3f9f340a58868','60dd8844eaf3f9f340a58867',5,'m3- Garnish & serve','After simmering Moth Beans Curry, remove the lid and add half a teaspoon of teaspoon jaggery followed by the prepared tamarind water, and 1 teaspoon of niger seeds powder. Mix it well and add additional water if required. Then, stir and cook it over medium flame for another 2 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and remove the curry in a serving bowl. Garnish it with a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and serve','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60deae0a4679878674289ca3','60deadb67a06e422f7cfbaab',1,'p1- prep the ingredients','For Carom leaves Tambuli, wash, clean, and pat dry 20 carom leaves. Grate 1/4 cup of fresh coconut using a grater. Wash, clean, and separate 7 nos curry leaves from the stem. Next, add 1/4  cup of fresh curd to a mixing bowl along with 1/4 cup of water and whisk it well until smooth','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60deaf754679878674289ca4','60deadb67a06e422f7cfbaab',2,'m1- fry the carom leaves','To make Carrot Leaves Tambuli, heat 1 teaspoon of ghee in a pan over medium flame. Then, add 1/4 teaspoon of black peppercorns, and half a teaspoon of cumin seeds and allow it to splutter for a few seconds. Next, add the cleaned carom leaves and fry them over medium-low flame for 2-3 minutes until the leaves wilt and turn slightly pale in color. Next, add 1/4 cup of grated coconut and saute it over low flame for a few seconds. Then, turn off the flame and allow the mixture to cool for some time.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60deafb5eaf3f9f340a58869','60deadb67a06e422f7cfbaab',3,'m2- puree the carom leaves and add buttermilk','To make the carom leaves puree for the Tambuli, transfer the prepared carom leaves mixture to a blender jar along with half a teaspoon of salt and 1/4 cup of water and blend it well into a smooth paste. Then, remove the puree into a mixing bowl and add half a cup of prepared buttermilk to it. Mix it well and prepare the tambuli.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('60deb00c4679878674289ca5','60deadb67a06e422f7cfbaab',4,'m3- add the tempering to the tambuli & serve','To make the tempering for Carom Leaves Tambuli, heat 1 teaspoon of ghee in a tempering pan over medium flame. Then,  add 1/2 a teaspoon of cumin seeds, 1/2 a teaspoon mustard seeds, 7 curry leaves and1 dry red chili. Saute it over low flame for a few seconds and allow it to splutter. Then, turn off the flame and add the tempering to the prepared tambuli. Divide among bowls and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60deb77e7a06e422f7cfbaac','60deb74a4679878674289ca6',1,'p1- boil the vermicelli','To boil the vermicelli for Bagala Bath, boil 2 cups water in a deep bottom pan over medium-high flame. Next, add 1 cup of vermicelli to the boiling water and stir it well. Then, allow the vermicelli to cook over medium-low flame for 5-6 minutes until it is cooked completely. Keep stirring the vermicelli at regular intervals. Then, turn off the flame and set it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60deb7ec7a06e422f7cfbaad','60deb74a4679878674289ca6',2,'p2- prep the ingredients','For Bagala Bath, wash and chop 1 green chili. Wash, peel, and grate a 1/2 inch piece of ginger. Break 1 tablespoon of cashew nuts into halves. Wash and finely chop a tablespoon of curry leaves. Wash, clean and separate 7 curry leaves from its stem.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60deb8407a06e422f7cfbaae','60deb74a4679878674289ca6',3,'m1- add curd to the boiled vermicelli & season it','To make Bagala Bath, transfer the boiled vermicelli to a mixing bowl.  Add half a cup of curd and half a cup of milk to it mix it well. Then, add a teaspoon of salt and mix it well.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60deb8bf4679878674289ca7','60deb74a4679878674289ca6',4,'m2- add the tempering to the prepared vermicelli & serve','To make the tempering for Bagala Bath, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a tempering pan over medium flame. Next, add half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, half a teaspoon of urad dal, half a teaspoon of chana dal, and saute it over low flame until brown. Then, add 7 curry leaves, followed by a 1/2 inch piece of grated ginger, add 1 dry red chili and saute it for a few seconds. Next, add 1 chopped green chili along with a tablespoon of cashew nuts and saute it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and add the tempering to the prepared bath. Mix it well and garnish it with a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('60debbf34679878674289ca9','60debb794679878674289ca8',1,'p1- rinse & puree the finger millet and rest','For Ragi Porridge, in a large bowl, add 3/4 cup of finger millet, and 1/4 cup of whole wheat grains. Add water as required and rinse the grains well. Drain the water from the cleaned grains and transfer them to a blender jar along with 3/4 cup of water. Then cover the jar with a lid and blend it well into a smooth puree. Next, place a strainer over a large bowl and sieve the puree. Then, again add the leftover mixture from the sieve to the blender jar along with 1/4 cup of water and blend. Then, strain the mixture. Repeat the process 3 times and discard the grinds after the third process.  Then, allow the mixture to rest for 1 hour. While it rests, please move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":60,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":10,"flame":0}'),('60debc6aeaf3f9f340a5886c','60debb794679878674289ca8',2,'p2- spread the ragi mixture onto a cotton cloth and let it dry','After resting the prepared Ragi batter for Ragi Porridge, the thick mixture will settle at the bottom. Then, carefully discard the thin water above the thick mixture as shown. Next, layer 2 pieces of cotton cloth on a baking tray and pour in the thick ragi mixture on the cloth as shown. Spread the mixture evenly and allow it to dry for 10 -15 minutes. Meanwhile, please move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60debd53eaf3f9f340a5886d','60debb794679878674289ca8',3,'p3- sun dry the ragi biscuits','For Ragi Porridge, once the ragi mixture has settled and dried off, scrape off the thick mixture from the cloth as shown and shape it into bite-sized balls. Flatten the balls and arrange them on a tray. Then, sun dry the ragi biscuits for 1-2 days until they are completely dry. There should not be any moisture left in the biscuits or they won''t last long. After sun drying the biscuits, transfer them to an airtight container and store them until use.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":600,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60debdac4679878674289caa','60debb794679878674289ca8',4,'m1- prepare the ragi porridge from the ragi biscuits','To make Ragi Porridge, in a bowl, crush 2 prepared ragi biscuits. Add half a cup of water and mix it well until it dissolves completely. Then, transfer the mixture to a pan add 1/4 cup of milk followed by 1/4 cup of water and a teaspoon of jaggery. Mix it well and bring it to a boil over the medium flame while stirring continuously. Cook it for 2-3 minutes, until the mixture thickens. Then, turn off the flame and transfer the cooked ragi porridge to a bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('60e29fdd7a06e422f7cfbab5','60e29f847a06e422f7cfbab4',1,'p1- prepare the batter','To prepare the batter for Banana Appma, first, peel 3 ripe banans and roughly slice them. Then, add the banana slices to a mixing bowl and mash them well using a masher. Next, add 1/4 cup of jaggery half a teaspoon of cardamom powder, 1/8 teaspoon of salt, and mix it well. Then, add 1 cup of whole wheat flour and combine it well into a semi-thick dough-like batter.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('60e2a01feaf3f9f340a58871','60e29f847a06e422f7cfbab4',2,'m1- deep fry the appam & serve','To make Banana Appam, heat 1 cup of cooking oil in a kadai over medium flame for 2-3 minutes for deep frying.  Once the oil is hot, prepare the small lemon-sized balls from the appam dough and carefully drop them one by one into the hot oil. Then, deep fry the balls over medium-low flame for 4-5 minutes, until the appams are crisp and golden brown. Fry the appam in small batches to make them crisp. Then, turn off the flame remove the appams onto a kitchen napkin to dab off the extra oil, and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60e2a27beaf3f9f340a58873','60e2a2337a06e422f7cfbab6',1,'p1- boil the toor dal','To boil the dal for Pineapple Rasam, first, rinse and clean half a cup of toor dal. Then, add it to a pressure cooker along with 1 cup of water. Then, cover it with a lid and pressure cook the dal over a high flame until 1 whistle. Then, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook the dal for another 8 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the dal is boiling, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60e2a2f3eaf3f9f340a58874','60e2a2337a06e422f7cfbab6',2,'p2- dice the pineapple & prep the other ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Pineapple Rasam, peel and dice 1.25 cups pineapple. Next, wash and chop half a cup of tomatoes. Wash and finely chop a tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash and separate 7 curry leaves from its stem. Next, add 1 cup of diced pineapple to a blender jar and blend it well into a smooth puree','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60e2a3657a06e422f7cfbab7','60e2a2337a06e422f7cfbab6',3,'p3- prepare the masala paste','To grind the masala paste for Pineapple Rasam, in a blender jar, add half a teaspoon cumin seeds,  half a teaspoon black peppercorns, and 1 green chili. Then, cover the jar with a lid and blend it into a coarse paste. Transfer the paste to a bowl and set it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60e2a3c54679878674289caf','60e2a2337a06e422f7cfbab6',4,'m1- boil the rasam','To make Pineapple Rasam, first, add the prepared pineapple puree to a large bowl. Then, add the ground paste, followed by 1/4 cup of chopped tomato, and mix it well. Next, transfer this mixture to a deep bottom pan and add 1 cup of water. Mix it well and bring it to a rolling boil over a high flame. After that allow the rasam to boil over medium flame for 5-6 minutes. While the rasam is boiling, please move onto the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('60e2a42eeaf3f9f340a58875','60e2a2337a06e422f7cfbab6',5,'m2- add the tempering to the rasam','To make the tempering for Pineapple Rasam, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame. Then, add half a teaspoon cumin seeds, half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, 1/4 teaspoon of asafoetida, and 7 curry leaves. Saute and allow it to splutter for a few seconds. Then,  add 1/4 cup of diced pineapple along with 1/4 cup of diced tomatoes and fry it with the tempering over medium flame for 2-3 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and add the tempering to the prepared rasam and mix it well.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60e2a47a7a06e422f7cfbab8','60e2a2337a06e422f7cfbab6',6,'m3- Add the boiled dal to the rasam and boil.  Garnish & serve','Next, add a teaspoon of salt and allow the rasam to cook over low flame for 2-3 minutes. Then, add the boiled toor dal and stir it well. Then, boil the rasam over medium flame for 2-3 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and garnish it with a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves. Remove the rasam in a serving bowl and serve','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60e2a6d67a06e422f7cfbaba','60e2a675eaf3f9f340a58876',1,'p1- prepare the ingredients','For snake gourd stir fry, wash, deseed and dice 1.5 cups of snake gourd. Grate 1/4 cup of fresh coconut using a grater. Wash and slit 1 green chili. Wash, clean and separate 1 sprig of curry leaves from its stem.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60e2a74ceaf3f9f340a58877','60e2a675eaf3f9f340a58876',2,'m1- simmer the curry','To make snake gourd stir fry, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a kadai over medium flame for a minute. Then,  add 1/2 a teaspoon of mustard seeds, 1/4 teaspoon of urad dal, and 7 curry leaves. Saute and allow it to splutter over medium flame for a few seconds. Next, add in 1.5 cups of diced snake gourd and fry it over medium flame for a minute. Then, add 1/4 cup of water and stir it well. Add half a teaspoon of jaggery followed by half a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Then, cover the pan with a lid and cook it over on a medium-low flame for 6-7 minutes until it is completely cooked. While it simmers, please move onto the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":7,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('60e2a7867a06e422f7cfbabb','60e2a675eaf3f9f340a58876',3,'m2- prepare the masala paste','To make the coconut paste for snake gourd stir fry, in a blender jar, add 0.25 cup of grated coconut, followed by 1 green chili, half a teaspoon of cumin seeds, and cover the jar with a lid. Then, blend it into a coarse paste. Transfer it to a bowl and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('60e2a7c7eaf3f9f340a58878','60e2a675eaf3f9f340a58876',4,'m3- add the masala paste to the curry & cook','After simmering the Snakegourd Stir-Fry, carefully remove the lid and add the prepared coconut paste to the Kadai. Then, gently mix it and continue to cook it over medium flame for another 2 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and plate the dish in a bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60e3ff15eaf3f9f340a5887c','60e3fe9feaf3f9f340a5887b',1,'p1- soak the tamarind and prep the ingredients','For Thili Saaru, first, soak a teaspoon of tamarind in 1/4 cup of water for 10 minutes. Next, wash and roughly dice 1 cup of tomatoes. Wash, clean and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander Leaves. Wash and slit 1 green chili in half. Wash, clean and separate 1 sprig curry leaves from its stem.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60e3ff6ceaf3f9f340a5887d','60e3fe9feaf3f9f340a5887b',2,'p2- pound the whole spices','For Thilli Saaru, add a teaspoon of cumin seeds to a mortar followed by half a teaspoon of black peppercorns and pound it using a pestle into a coarse powder. Next, after soaking the tamarind, mash it well in water and strain the juice in a bowl.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60e3ffcb4679878674289cb0','60e3fe9feaf3f9f340a5887b',3,'m1- mash the tomatoes','To make Thili Saaru, first, add 1 cup of diced tomatoes to a mixing bowl. Next, add a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves, followed by the pounded spice powder, and a teaspoon of salt. Then, mix it well and squeeze the tomatoes well as shown until tomatoes are slightly mushy.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60e4000f7a06e422f7cfbabc','60e3fe9feaf3f9f340a5887b',4,'m2- simmer the rasam','Next, add the prepared tamarind juice to a deep bottom pan. Add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, 1 slit green chili, 1 teaspoon of jaggery, and 1 cup of water. Mix it well and bring it to a boil over medium-high flame. Then, add the mashed tomatoes to the boiling tamarind water and mix it well. Cover it with a lid and boil the rasam over a medium flame for 3-5 minutes. While the rasam is boiling, please move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('60e4004deaf3f9f340a5887e','60e3fe9feaf3f9f340a5887b',5,'m3- add the rasam powder and boil the rasam','After boiling the Thili Saaru, remove the lid and give it a stir. Then, add 2 teaspoons of rasam powder and mix it well. Add about half a cup of more water if the rasam is not thin and runny. Then, mix it well and boil it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60e400cdeaf3f9f340a5887f','60e3fe9feaf3f9f340a5887b',6,'m4- add the tempering to the rasam & serve','After boiling the Thili Saaru, remove the lid and give it stir. Then, add 2 teaspoons of rasam powder and mix it well. Add about half a cup of more water if the rasam is not thin and runny. Then, mix it well and boil it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60e403767a06e422f7cfbabd','60e40341eaf3f9f340a58881',1,'ap1- soak the black chickpeas','For Chickpeas Yam Curry, soak 3/4 cup of black chickpeas in 2 cups of water for 8-10 hours. While the chickpeas are soaking, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":600,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60e403c34679878674289cb1','60e40341eaf3f9f340a58881',2,'p1- boil the chickpeas','To boil the chickpeas for Chickpeas Yam Curry, rinse and add the soaked black chickpeas to a pressure cooker along with 1.5 cups of water. Then, cover it with a lid and pressure cook the chickpeas over a high flame until 3 whistles. Then, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook the chickpeas over low flame for another 8 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and allow the cooker to release the pressure naturally. While the chickpeas are boiling, please move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":18,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60e4041a4679878674289cb2','60e40341eaf3f9f340a58881',3,'p2- dice the yam and prep other ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Chickpeas Yam Curry, wash, peel and dice 3/4 cup of yam. Place the diced yam soaked in water until later use. Grate 1/4 cup of fresh coconut. Wash and remove 7 curry leaves from its stem.','prep_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('60e404504679878674289cb3','60e40341eaf3f9f340a58881',4,'p3- boil the yam','To boil the yam for Chickpeas Yam Curry, add 3/4 cup of diced yam to a deep bottom pan along with half a cup of water. Then, cover the pan with a lid and allow it to cook over medium-low flame for 10-12 minutes until tender. While the yam is boiling, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60e404f57a06e422f7cfbabe','60e40341eaf3f9f340a58881',5,'p4- prepare the masala paste','To prepare the masala paste for  Chickpeas Yam Curry, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Then, add 1 teaspoon of urad dal followed by 2 teaspoons of coriander seeds, and 1 dry red chili. Saute and roast the whole spices over low flame for 1-2 minutes until fragrant. Then, turn off the flame and remove the spices in a blender jar. Next, add 1/4 cup of grated coconut, a teaspoon of tamarind, and 1/4 cup of water. Then, cover the jar with a lid and blend it well into a smooth paste.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60e4056eeaf3f9f340a58882','60e40341eaf3f9f340a58881',6,'m1- simmer the curry','To make the Chickpeas Yam Curry, after boiling the yam, carefully remove the lid and add the boiled black chickpeas to it. Next, add half a teaspoon of jaggery along with a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Then, bring it to a boil over medium flame. After that, add the prepared masala paste and mix it well. Then, continue to cook the curry over medium flame for another 2-3 minutes until the gravy slightly thickens. Then, turn off the flame and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60e405c0eaf3f9f340a58883','60e40341eaf3f9f340a58881',7,'m2- add the tempering to the curry & serve','To make the tempering for Chickpeas Yam Curry, heat 1 teaspoon of cooking oil in a tempering pan over medium flame. Then, add half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, 7 curry leaves, and allow it to splutter over low flame for a few seconds. Then, turn off the flame and add the tempering to the prepared curry. Mix it well and remove the curry in a serving bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60e40b08eaf3f9f340a58884','60e40a707a06e422f7cfbac0',1,'p1- prepare the coconut masala paste','To prepare the coconut masala paste for Masala Rava Roti, first, grate half a cup of coconut using a grater. Next, add the grated coconut to a blender jar followed by 1 tablespoon of tamarind, 2 dry red chilies, 1 teaspoon of jaggery, and 2 teaspoons of coriander seeds. Add 1 teaspoon cumin seeds along with 0.25 cup of water and blend it well into a smooth paste. Transfer it to a bowl and set it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('60e40b68eaf3f9f340a58885','60e40a707a06e422f7cfbac0',2,'p2- prepare the batter','To prepare the batter for Masala Rava Rotti, add 1 cup of semolina to a large mixing bowl. Next, add 1 cup of water and combine it well. Then, add the prepared coconut masala paste followed by 1 teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Add additional water if required to adjust the consistency of the batter. The batter should be thick inconsistency.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60e40bb94679878674289cb4','60e40a707a06e422f7cfbac0',3,'m1- make the rava rotis and serve','To make Masala Rava Roti, heat up a tava over medium flame and grease it with half a teaspoon of cooking oil. Then, pour one ladle full of the prepared batter and spread it into a slightly thick round roti as shown. Drizzle half a teaspoon of cooking oil and cover it with a lid. Then, cook the roti over medium flame for 2 minutes until it is crisp and golden brown. Then, remove the lid and carefully flip the rava roti and cook it over medium flame for another minute. Then, turn off the flame and remove it onto a serving plate. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60e56ca84679878674289cb7','60e56c294679878674289cb6',1,'p1- slice and prep the bitter gourds','To prepare the bitter gourds for Udupi Bittergourd Curry, wash and slice the bitter gourd in half lengthwise and remove the seeds. Then, finely slice 3/4 cup of the bitter gourds and remove it in a bowl. Next, add a teaspoon of salt along with half a teaspoon of turmeric powder and rub the salt well onto the bitter gourds. Then, allow it to sweat for 20 minutes. Do not skip this step as it is important to prep the bitter gourd before making the curry. Salt will draw out the bitterness from the bitter gourds. Then, rinse the bitter gourds with water and set them aside. While the bitter gourds sweat, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60e56cf1eaf3f9f340a58886','60e56c294679878674289cb6',2,'p2- soak the tamarind & prep other ingredients','For Udupi Bittergourd Curry, first, soak a teaspoon of tamarind in 1/4 cup of water for 10 minutes.  Wash and finely chop a tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash and separate 7 curry leaves from its stem. While the tamarind soaks, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60e56e10eaf3f9f340a58887','60e56c294679878674289cb6',3,'p3- prepare the masala powder','To prepare the masala powder for Udupi Bittergourd Curry, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Next, add half a teaspoon of chana dal, 2 teaspoons of coriander seeds, half a teaspoon of cumin seeds, 1/4 teaspoon of fenugreek seeds, and 2 dry red chilies. Saute the whole spices over low flame for 1-2 minutes until fragrant. Then, turn off the flame and remove the roasted spices in a blender jar. Cover the jar with a lid and blend it into a fine powder. Next, after soaking the tamarind, mash the pulp with water and strain the juice in a bowl.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('60e56e7e4679878674289cb8','60e56c294679878674289cb6',4,'m1- simmer the bitter gourds','To make Udupi Bittergourd Curry, heat 1.5 tablespoons of coconut oil in a pan over medium flame. Then,  add half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, half a teaspoon of urad dal, 7 curry leaves. Saute and allow it to splutter over low flame. Next, add the prepared bitter gourds and fry them over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Then, cover the pan with a lid and cook the bitter gourd over low flame for 5 minutes. Keep stirring the bitter gourds in between. While the bitter gourds simmer, please move onto the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('60e56efaeaf3f9f340a58888','60e56c294679878674289cb6',5,'m2- Add the masala powder to the curry & simmer. Garnish & serve','After simmering the Udupi Bitter gourd Curry, carefully remove the lid and add the prepared tamarind juice, half a teaspoon of salt, and half a teaspoon of jaggery. Mix it well and continue to cook the curry over medium flame for another 3-5 minutes until the bitter gourds are tender. Then, add the prepared spice powder and mix it well. Add about half a cup of water and 1/4 teaspoon of asafoetida and stir it well. Then, bring the curry to boil over medium flame and cook it until it slightly thickens. Then, turn off the flame and remove the curry in a serving bowl. Garnish it with a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and serve','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60e5723a4679878674289cba','60e571baeaf3f9f340a58889',1,'p1- prep the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Vermicelli Pulao, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onion. Wash, peel and cut 1/4 cup of carrots into julienne. Wash, string, and dice 1/4 cup of haricot beans. Peel and wash 1/4 cup of green peas. Wash and pick 1/4 cup of mint leaves. Wash and roughly chop 3 tablespoons of coriander leaves. Wash and peel 3 cloves of garlic. Wash, peel, and roughly chop 1/4 inch piece of ginger.','prep_method','{"active_time":17,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60e572887a06e422f7cfbac1','60e571baeaf3f9f340a58889',2,'p2- prepare the mint masala paste','To prepare the mint paste for Vermicelli Pulao, add 1/4 cup of mint leaves to a blender jar. Add 3 tablespoons of coriander leaves, 2 green chilies, 3 cloves of garlic, 1/4 inch piece of ginger, and a 1/2 inch piece of cinnamon stick. Next, add 2 cloves along with 1/4 cup of water and blend it well into a smooth puree.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60e572cbeaf3f9f340a5888a','60e571baeaf3f9f340a58889',3,'p3- roast the vermicelli','To roast the Vermicelli for Vermicelli Upma, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame. Next, add 1.5 cups of vermicelli and roast it over medium flame for 3-4 minutes until it turns slightly golden. Then, turn off the flame and remove the roasted vermicelli onto a plate, and set it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('60e573827a06e422f7cfbac2','60e571baeaf3f9f340a58889',4,'m1- temper the oil with whole spices and cook the masala paste','To make Vermicelli Pulao, heat 2 teaspoons of ghee in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Next, add a half-inch piece of cinnamon stick, 1 green cardamom, 2 bay leaves, and saute it over low flame for a few seconds. Then add 1/4 cup of chopped onions and fry them over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until the onions are slightly translucent. Then, add the prepared mint paste and cook it over medium flame for 3-4 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60e573cceaf3f9f340a5888b','60e571baeaf3f9f340a58889',5,'m2- add the vegetables and simmer the vermicelli','Next, add 1/4 cup of sliced carrots, followed by 1/4 cup of diced haricot beans, 1/4 cup of peeled green peas, and mix it well. Then, stir-fry the vegetables over high flame for 2-3 minutes. Next, add 1 teaspoon salt along with 1.5 cups of water and bring it to a boil. Then, add the roasted vermicelli and mix it well. Cover the pan with a lid and allow the vermicelli to cook over low flame for 3-5 minutes until it has absorbed all the water. While the vermicelli simmers, please move onto the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('60e574057a06e422f7cfbac3','60e571baeaf3f9f340a58889',6,'m3- add the lime juice & serve','After simmering the Vermicelli Pulao, remove the lid and give it a stir. Vermicelli has absorbed the water. Then, add 2 teaspoons of lime juice to the pulao. Then, gently mix it with light hands. Turn off the flame and plate the vermicelli.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60e575d0eaf3f9f340a5888d','60e5759c4679878674289cbb',1,'ap1- soak the lentil','For Carrot Kosambari, first, rinse and clean half a cup of chana dal well with water. Then, add it to a bowl and soak the dal in 1 cup of water for 2 hours. While the dal is soaking, please move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":120,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60e576454679878674289cbc','60e5759c4679878674289cbb',2,'p1- prep the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Carrot Kosambari, wash, peel and grate 1 cup of carrot. Wash, peel, and grate 2 tablespoons of raw mango. Wash, peel, and grate a half-inch piece of ginger. Wash and finely chop 1 green chili. Grate 2 tablespoons of fresh coconut in a bowl using a grater. Wash and finely chop a tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash and pluck 7 curry leaves.','cook_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('60e5768a4679878674289cbd','60e5759c4679878674289cbb',3,'m1- Combine the ingredients and prepare the kosambari','To make Carrot Kosambari, in a large bowl, add half a cup of soaked chana dal along with 1 cup of grated carrot. Next,1 finely chopped green chili, 2 tablespoons of grated raw mango, add 2 tablespoons of grated coconut, and a half-inch piece of grated ginger. Add half a teaspoon of salt, 1/4 teaspoon of hing and mix it well.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60e576d94679878674289cbe','60e5759c4679878674289cbb',4,'m2- add the tempering and serve','To prepare the tempering for Carrot Kosambari, heat a teaspoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame. Then, add 1/4 teaspoon of mustard seeds, 1/4 teaspoon white lentils, 7 curry leaves, and allow it to splutter over low flame. Then, turn off the flame and add the tempering to the prepared kosambari. Mix it well and serve','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60e697b37a06e422f7cfbac6','60e697507a06e422f7cfbac5',1,'p1- chop the ginger & prep the other ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Ginger Tambuli, wash, peel and roughly chop 2-inch ginger. Grate half a cup of fresh coconut in a bowl using a grater. Wash, clean and separate 7 curry leaves from its stem and set them aside. Next, add half a cup of fresh curd to a bowl. Add 1/4 cup of water and mix it well using a whisk to prepare the buttermilk.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60e6982deaf3f9f340a5888e','60e697507a06e422f7cfbac5',2,'m1- puree the ginger & coconut mixture','To make Ginger Tambuli, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame. Next, half a teaspoon of cumin seeds, chopped ginger, and 1 dry red chili Then, saute it and allow it to splutter over low flame until fragrant. Then, turn off the flame and remove it in a blender jar. Add half a cup of grated coconut, half a teaspoon of salt, and 1/4 cup of water. Cover the jar with a lid and blend it well into a smooth puree.','cook_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60e698b74679878674289cbf','60e697507a06e422f7cfbac5',3,'m2- add the buttermilk and temper the raita','To make Ginger Tambuli, transfer the prepared ginger and coconut puree to a mixing bowl. Add in the prepared buttermilk and mix it well. Next, to prepare the tempering, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a tadka pan over medium flame. Then, add half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, half a teaspoon of urad dal, 1 dry red chili, and 7 curry leaves. Saute and allow it to splutter for a few seconds. Then, turn off the flame and add the tempering to the prepared tambuli. Mix it well and serve','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('60e6b4f54679878674289cc0','60e6b48c7a06e422f7cfbac8',1,'p1- dice the tomatoes & prep other ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Tomato Kurma, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1.5 cups of tomatoes. Grate 1/4 cup of fresh coconut in a bowl using a grater. Wash and slit 1 green chili. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60e6b5a54679878674289cc1','60e6b48c7a06e422f7cfbac8',2,'p2- prepare the masala paste','To prepare the masala paste for Tomato Kurma, in a blender jar, add 1/4 cup of grated coconut, followed by 1 tablespoon of roasted grams, 1 green chili, 5 cashew nuts, and 1 teaspoon of fennel seeds. Add 1 teaspoon coriander seeds along with 1/4 cup of water. Cover the jar with a lid and blend it well into a smooth paste','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60e6b5fa4679878674289cc2','60e6b48c7a06e422f7cfbac8',3,'m1- fry the onions & simmer the tomatoes','To make Tomato Kurma, heat a tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Then, add 1 bay leaf, 1-inch piece of cinnamon stick, and saute it over low flame for a few seconds. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions and fry them over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until translucent. Then, add 1.5 cups of diced tomatoes and mix it well. Cover the pan with a lid and cook the tomatoes over low flame for 5 minutes until tomatoes are cooked and tender. While it simmers, please move onto the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60e6b655eaf3f9f340a58890','60e6b48c7a06e422f7cfbac8',4,'m2- Add the masala paste & simmer. Garnish & serve','After simmering the Tomato Kurma, remove the lid and stir the tomatoes. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, half a teaspoon of sugar, half a teaspoon of red chili powder, and 1 teaspoon salt. Mix it well and cook the masala over medium flame for 2 minutes. Then, add the prepared masala paste followed by half a cup of water. Mix it well and bring it to a boil. Then, cover it with a lid and cook the kurma over low flame for another 5 minutes, until it slightly thickens. Then, turn off the flame and garnish it with some chopped coriander leaves. Remove it in a serving bowl and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60e6b8daeaf3f9f340a58891','60e6b8a14679878674289cc3',1,'p1- boil the potatoes','To boil the potatoes for Batata Song, wash 2 medium-sized potatoes and add them to a pressure cooker along with 1 cup of water. Cover it with a lid and pressure cook the potatoes over high flame until 1 whistle. Then, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook the potatoes for another 8 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the potatoes are boiling, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('60e6b936eaf3f9f340a58892','60e6b8a14679878674289cc3',2,'p2- prep the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Batata Song, peel, wash, and roughly dice half a cup of onions. Then, separate the diced onion layers and set them aside. Grate 1/4 cup of fresh coconut using a grater. Wash, clean and separate 1 sprig of curry leaves from its stem.','prep_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60e6b99e4679878674289cc4','60e6b8a14679878674289cc3',3,'p3- prepare the masala paste','To prepare the masala paste for Batata Song, heat a teaspoon of coconut oil in a pan over medium flame. Then, add 2 dry red chilies and roast them over low flame for a minute. Then, turn off the flame and set it aside. Next, add 1/4 cup of grated coconut to a blender jar followed by the roasted dry red chilies and 1/4 cup of water. Then, cover the jar with a lid and blend it well into a smooth paste. Next, after boiling the potatoes, remove them onto a plate and gently peel off the skin. Then, dice the potatoes into medium cubes.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60e6b9f04679878674289cc5','60e6b8a14679878674289cc3',4,'m1- fry the onions','To make Batata Song, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame. Then, add half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, 7 curry leaves, and allow it to splutter for a few seconds. Next, add half a cup of diced onion and fry it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60e6ba367a06e422f7cfbaca','60e6b8a14679878674289cc3',5,'m2- cook the potatoes with masala paste & serve','After frying the onions, add the boiled potatoes along with a teaspoon of salt and fry them over medium flame for a minute. Next, add the prepared masala paste and mix it well until the potatoes are evenly coated. Then, saute and cook the potatoes with the masala over medium flame for 5 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and plate the potatoes. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60e7e9c94679878674289cc8','60e7e9834679878674289cc7',1,'ap1- soak the lentils','To soak the lentils for Nuchin Unde, first, add 3/4 cup of toor dal and 1/4 cup of chana dal to a bowl. Then, rinse and clean the lentils well with water. Next, add 2 cups of water to the lentils and let them soak in water for 3 hours. While the lentils soak, please move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":180,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('60e7ea997a06e422f7cfbacc','60e7e9834679878674289cc7',2,'p1- prep the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Nuchin Unde, wash and finely chop half a cup of dill leaves. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of coriander leaves. Grate 2 tablespoons of fresh coconut. Wash and finely chop 1 green chili. Wash, peel, and finely chop a 1-inch piece of ginger. Wash and chop  curry leaves','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60e7ebad4679878674289cc9','60e7e9834679878674289cc7',3,'p2- prepare the lentil batter','To prepare the mixture for Nuchin Unde, first, drain the soaked lentils and add them to a blender jar. Do not add any water to the lentils. Then, cover the jar with a lid and blend it well into a slightly coarse paste. Remove the paste to a large bowl and add 1 chopped green chili, 1-inch piece of chopped ginger, half a cup of chopped dill leaves followed by 1/4 cup of chopped coriander leaves, 7 curry leaves, 2 tablespoons of grated coconut, combine it well. Next, add a teaspoon of salt along with 1/4 teaspoon of hing and mix  it well to form a dough-like mixture.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60e7ee817a06e422f7cfbacd','60e7e9834679878674289cc7',4,'m1- steam the dumplings & serve','To make Nuchin Unde, first, add water to the steamer and let it boil over medium-high flame for 2-3 minutes. Next, divide the prepared lentil mixture into equal portions and shape them each into small cylindrical dumplings as shown. Then, carefully place them in the steamer. Cover it with a lid and steam the dumplings over medium for 10 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and carefully remove the steamed dumplings onto a serving plate. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60e7f641eaf3f9f340a58893','60e7f5d34679878674289cca',1,'ap1- soak the green peas','For Potatoes Peas Kurma, add half a cup of green peas to a bowl and soak them in 1 cup of water for 4 hours. While the peas are soaking please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":240,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60e7f6804679878674289ccb','60e7f5d34679878674289cca',2,'p1- boil the soaked green peas','To boil the green peas for Potato Peas Kurma, add the soaked green peas to a pressure cooker along with 1 cup of water and half a teaspoon of salt. Then, cover the cooker with a lid and pressure cook the peas over high flame until three whistles. Then, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook the peas for another 5 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and allow the cooker to release the pressure naturally. While the peas are boiling, please move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":14,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('60e7f72eeaf3f9f340a58894','60e7f5d34679878674289cca',3,'p2- prep the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Potato Peas Kurma, peel, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Peel, wash, and dice 1 cup of potatoes. Wash, clean, and finely chop a tablespoon of coriander leaves. Grate 1/4 cup of coconut in a bowl using a grater.','prep_method','{"active_time":14,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60e7f78b7a06e422f7cfbacf','60e7f5d34679878674289cca',4,'m1- simmer the potatoes','To make Potato Peas Kurma, heat a tablespoon of cooking oil in a Kadai over medium flame for a minute. Then, add half a teaspoon of cumin seeds, and 2 bay leaves to the oil and allow it to splutter over low flame. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions fry them over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until onions are translucent. Next,  add 1 cup of diced potatoes followed by half a cup of water and stir it well.  Then, cover the pan with a lid and cook the potatoes over medium-low flame for 5-6 minutes until potatoes are tender. While the potatoes simmer, please move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('60e7f8444679878674289ccc','60e7f5d34679878674289cca',5,'m2- add the boiled peas & spices, cook the curry & serve','After simmering the potatoes for Potato Peas Kurma, carefully remove the lid and add the boiled green peas. Mix it well and add about 1/4 cup of water. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, 1 teaspoon of coriander powder, half teaspoon red chili powder, 1.5 teaspoon jaggery, and 1/4 cup grated coconut. Mix it well and cook the curry over medium flame for another 3-4 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and garnish it with a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves. Remove the curry to a serving bowl and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":14,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60e7fdf2eaf3f9f340a58897','60e7fa11eaf3f9f340a58896',1,'p1- soak the rice & prep the ingredients','For Beetroot Pulao, first, wash and soak 1 cup basmati rice in 2 cups of water for 20 minutes. Next, wash, peel and dice 3/4 cup of beetroot into medium cubes. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Wash, peel, and finely chop a 1-inch piece of ginger. Wash and slit 2 nos green chilies. Wash and finely chop a tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash and cut a lime into halves and squeeze a teaspoon of lime juice into a bowl.','prep_method','{"active_time":16,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":4,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60e7fe6f7a06e422f7cfbad0','60e7fa11eaf3f9f340a58896',2,'m1- fry the onions and cook the tomatoes','To make Beetroot Pulao, heat 2 tablespoons of cooking oil in a pressure cooker over medium flame for a minute. Next, add 2 bay leaves, 3 cloves, 1-inch piece of cinnamon stick, 2 green cardamoms, followed by 1/4 teaspoon of black peppercorns, 2 tablespoons of cashew nuts, 1-inch piece of chopped ginger, and 2 slit green chilies. Then, saute it over low flame for 1-2 minutes until cashews turn slightly golden. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes and mix it well. Then, saute and cook the tomatoes over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until the tomatoes are tender.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('60e7fefd4679878674289ccd','60e7fa11eaf3f9f340a58896',3,'m2-  add beetroot & soaked rice & pressure cook the pulao','Next, add 3/4 cup of diced beetroot and fry it over medium flame for a minute. Then, add 1 cup of soaked rice to it and gently mix it. Next, add a teaspoon salt, followed by half a teaspoon of red chili powder, and 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala and mix it well. Then, add 2 cups of water and stir it well. Add 1/4 cup of green peas along with a teaspoon of lemon juice and mix it well. Then, cover it with a lid and pressure cook the pulao over a high flame until 2 whistles. After the second whistle, reduce the flame to low and cook it for another 5 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. After that, open the lid of the pressure cooker and gently mix the pulao. Plate the pulao and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60ebe64ceaf3f9f340a58a01','60ebe4dd4dd3fbdb6b4c2d07',1,'ap1- soak the rice','For Methi Leaves Dosa, in a bowl, add 1.5 cups of sona masuri rice and a teaspoon of fenugreek seeds. Then, add water and rinse the rice well. Then, drain the rice and soak it in 2 cups of water for 2 hours. While the rice is soaking please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":120,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60ebf4501e8237eb6e973489','60ebe4dd4dd3fbdb6b4c2d07',2,'p1- chop the fenugreek leaves and prep other ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Methi Leaves Dosa, first, soak a teaspoon of tamarind in 1/4 cup of water for 10 minutes. Next, wash and clean a bunch of fenugreek leaves thoroughly with water. Remove the root ends and hard stems. Then, finely chop 1 cup of fenugreek leaves. Grate half a cup of fresh coconut using a grater.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60ebf4d41e8237eb6e97348a','60ebe4dd4dd3fbdb6b4c2d07',3,'p2- prepare the coconut paste','To prepare the batter for Methi Leaves Dosa, add half a cup of grated coconut to a blender jar followed by a tablespoon of coriander seeds, a teaspoon of cumin seeds, and 2 nos dry red chilies. Next, mix the soaked tamarind in water and squeeze out the juice in the blender jar as shown. Add 2 tablespoons of jaggery and cover the jar with a lid and blend it well into a smooth paste.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60ebf52deaf3f9f340a58a02','60ebe4dd4dd3fbdb6b4c2d07',4,'p3- prepare the batter','Next, add the soaked rice to the prepared masala paste along with a teaspoon of salt. Add about 1/4 cup of water and blend it again into a smooth batter. Then, remove the batter into a large mixing bowl and add 1 cup of chopped fenugreek leaves. Mix it well and add more water if required to adjust the consistency of the batter. The batter should not be too runny either too thick.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('60ebf58e1e8237eb6e97348b','60ebe4dd4dd3fbdb6b4c2d07',5,'m1- make the dosa from the batter & serve','To Make Methi Leaves Dosa, heat up a tawa over medium flame for a minute and grease it with a teaspoon of cooking oil. Then, add one ladleful of the prepared batter onto the hot tawa and spread it into a thin round dosa as shown. Then, cover it with a lid and allow it to cook over medium flame for 1-2 minutes until it is crisp and brown. Then, take off the lid and carefully remove the dosa onto a serving plate and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60ebf82a4dd3fbdb6b4c2d09','60ebf7ee4dd3fbdb6b4c2d08',1,'ap1- soak the rice','To soak the rice for Pineapple Dosa, first, add 1 cup of sona masuri to a bowl along with half a teaspoon of fenugreek seeds. Add water and rinse the rice well. Then, soak the rice in 2 cups of water for 3 hours. While the rice is soaking, please move on to the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":180,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60ebf87e4dd3fbdb6b4c2d0a','60ebf7ee4dd3fbdb6b4c2d08',2,'ap2- soak the poha & dice the pineapple','To prepare the ingredients for Pineapple Dosa, first, soak half a cup of poha in 3/4 cup of water for 10 minutes. Next, peel and roughly dice 1 cup of pineapple. Grate half a cup of coconut using a grater.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60ebf8fa1e8237eb6e97348d','60ebf7ee4dd3fbdb6b4c2d08',3,'ap3- prepare the batter & rest','To prepare the batter for pineapple dosa, first, add 1 cup of diced pineapple to a blender jar followed by half a cup of grated coconut. Then, cover the jar with a lid and blend it well into a smooth puree. Next, add to the same blender, add in the soaked rice along with the soaked rice flakes and blend it well into a smooth batter. Then, transfer the batter to a large bowl and add a teaspoon of salt. Mix it well and cover it with a plate. Then, allow it to ferment for 8-10 hours. While the batter ferments, please move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":600,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60ebf9814dd3fbdb6b4c2d0b','60ebf7ee4dd3fbdb6b4c2d08',4,'m1-make the dosa & serve','To make Pineapple Dosa, heat up a tawa over medium flame for a minute and grease it with a teaspoon of cooking oil. Then, pour one ladleful of the prepared batter onto the hot tawa and spread it evenly into a thin circle as shown. Then, cover the pan with a lid and cook the dosa over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until it is crisp and golden brown. After that, carefully remove the dosa onto a serving plate and serve. Make the rest of the dosas from the batter similarly.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('60ec1abd4dd3fbdb6b4c2d14','60ec0c664dd3fbdb6b4c2d13',1,'p1- prep the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Stuffed Ridge Gourd Curry, first, soak a teaspoon of tamarind in 1/4 cup of water for 10 minutes. Next, wash and peel 2 medium ridge gourds. Then, cut the ridge gourd into 1 inch thick cylindrical pieces and cross slit the cubes as shown. Next, peel, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash, peel and roughly chop a half-inch piece of ginger. Peel and crush 4 cloves of garlic. Wash and roughly chop 1/4 cup of coriander leaves. Grate 3/4 cup of fresh coconut using a grater. Wash and pluck 7 curry leaves','prep_method','{"active_time":17,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60ec1b2eeaf3f9f340a58a05','60ec0c664dd3fbdb6b4c2d13',2,'p2- prepare the peanut powder','To prepare the masala paste for Stuffed Ridge Curry, heat up a pan and add 1/4 cup of peanuts to it. Then, dry roast the peanuts over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Next, add a tablespoon of white sesame seeds and roast it with the peanuts over low flame for 1-2 minutes until it turns slightly golden. Then, turn off the flame and remove it to a blender jar. Cover the jar with a lid and grind it well into a slightly coarse powder. Remove it in a bowl and set it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60ec1bb0eaf3f9f340a58a06','60ec0c664dd3fbdb6b4c2d13',3,'p3- prepare the masala & stuff the ridge gourds','Next, add 3/4 cup of grated coconut to the same blender jar followed by a teaspoon of cumin seeds, a half-inch piece of ginger, 2 green chilies, 1/4 cup of coriander leaves, and 1/4 cup of water. Then, cover the jar with a lid and blend it well into a smooth paste. Transfer this paste to the prepared roasted peanuts powder along with 1/4 cup of chopped onions. Next, squeeze out the pulp from the soaked tamarind and add it to the mixture. Then, add 2 teaspoons of jaggery, 2 teaspoons of sambar powder, 1 teaspoon of salt, and mix it well. Then, stuff the ridge gourd pieces with the prepared masala as shown.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60ec1c29eaf3f9f340a58a07','60ec0c664dd3fbdb6b4c2d13',4,'m1- temper the oil  with whole spices & garlic','To make Stuffed Ridge Gourd Curry, heat 1 tablespoon of cooking oil in a kadai over medium flame for a minute. Then, add half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, 7 curry leaves, and 4 cloves of crushed garlic and saute it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes until garlic turns slightly golden and fragrant.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60ec1c671e8237eb6e973495','60ec0c664dd3fbdb6b4c2d13',5,'m2- add the stuffed ridge gourds & simmer','Next, carefully add the stuffed ridge gourds one by one to the pan and gently saute them. Then, add the remaining masala paste to the pan followed by half a cup of water and gently stir it. Cover the pan with a lid and cook the ridge gourds over a low flame for 6-7 minutes while stirring occasionally. Then, turn off the flame and remove the curry in a serving dish. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('60ed2c57eaf3f9f340a58a16','60ed2bf1eaf3f9f340a58a15',1,'p1- prep the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Curry Leaves Tambuli, wash, clean, and separate half a cup of curry leaves from its stem. Pat dry the curry leaves. Then, grate 2 tablespoons of fresh coconut using a grater. Wash and slit 1 green chili. Next, to prepare the buttermilk, add half a cup of curd to a bowl followed by half a cup of water. Then, mix it well using a whisk to avoid any lumps.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60ed2cf3eaf3f9f340a58a17','60ed2bf1eaf3f9f340a58a15',2,'m1- temper the oil & fry the curry leaves','To make Curry Leaves Tambuli, heat 2 teaspoons of coconut oil in a pan over medium flame. Then, add 1/4 teaspoon of cumin seeds, followed by half a cup of curry leaves, and 1 green chili. Then, stir and fry the curry leaves over low flame for 2-3 minutes until the curry leaves turn crisp. Do not fry the curry leaves over high flame. Once the curry leaves are crisp and slightly wilted, turn off the flame and allow the mixture to cool for some time. While it cools, please move onto the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('60ed2d5ee157b3e11c2ca934','60ed2bf1eaf3f9f340a58a15',3,'m2- blend the curry leaves mixture & add buttermilk','To make the Curry Leaves Tambuli, add the prepared curry leaves mixture to a blender jar. Add 2 tablespoons of grated coconut, along with half a teaspoon of salt and 1/4 cup of water. Then, cover the jar with a lid and blend it well into a smooth puree. Remove the puree into a mixing bowl and add the prepared buttermilk to it. Mix it well and prepare the tambuli','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60ed2dae1e8237eb6e9734aa','60ed2bf1eaf3f9f340a58a15',4,'m3- add the tempering & serve','To make the tempering for Curry Leaves Tambuli, heat 1 teaspoon of coconut oil in a tempering pan over medium flame. Then, temper it with half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, half a teaspoon of white lentils, 1 dry red chili, and a few curry leaves. Then, allow it to splutter over low flame for a few seconds. Then, turn off the flame and add the tempering to the prepared tambuli and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60ed377de157b3e11c2ca950','60ed3066eaf3f9f340a58a18',1,'p1- dice the vegetables','To prepare the ingredients for Konkani Curry, wash, peel and dice half a cup of Mangalore cucumber. Wash, peel, and dice half a cup of ash gourd. Wash, clean, and cut 1/4 cup of ivy gourds into julienne. Wash, peel, and dice 1/4 cup of sweet pumpkin.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('60ed37e41e8237eb6e9734ab','60ed3066eaf3f9f340a58a18',2,'p2- prep the ingredients','Next, wash, peel and dice 1/4 cup of sweet potato. Grate 3/4 cup of fresh coconut using a grater. Wash and slit 3 green chilies. Wash and remove 7 curry leaves from its stem. Next, to make the flour slurry, add a tablespoon of refined flour to a bowl along with 1/4 cup of water and mix it well to prepare a lump-free slurry','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60ed45ece157b3e11c2ca951','60ed3066eaf3f9f340a58a18',3,'m1- partially boil the vegetables','To boil the vegetables for Konkani Curry, first, add half a cup of diced Mangalore cucumber to a deep bottom pan. Next, add half a cup of diced ash gourd and 1/4 cup of sliced ivy gourds. Add 1 cup of water and cover the pan with a lid. Then, allow the vegetables to boil over medium flame for 5-6 minutes until half-cooked. While the vegetables simmer, please move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60ed462be157b3e11c2ca952','60ed3066eaf3f9f340a58a18',4,'m2- prepare the coconut milk','To make the coconut milk for Konkani Curry, add the grated coconut to a blender jar along with 1/4 cup of water and blend it well into a smooth paste. Then, remove the coconut paste into a strainer and strain the thick coconut milk in a bowl as shown. Next, add the remaining coconut back into the blender jar along with 1/4 cup of water and blend it into a smooth paste. Then, strain the thin coconut milk in a bowl similarly.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60ed467de157b3e11c2ca953','60ed3066eaf3f9f340a58a18',5,'m3- simmer the curry','After simmering the vegetables for Konkani Curry, carefully remove the lid and add 1/4 cup of diced sweet pumpkin followed by 1/4 cup of diced sweet potato, 2 tablespoons of cashew nuts, and 1/4 cup of water. Mix it well and cover the pan again with a lid. Then, continue to simmer the vegetables over medium flame for another 5 minutes until they are tender and cooked through. While the curry simmers, please move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('60ed46e0eaf3f9f340a58a1a','60ed3066eaf3f9f340a58a18',6,'m4- add the coconut milk & simmer','After simmering the Konkani Curry, remove the lid and add 2 slit green chilies, a teaspoon of salt, and the prepared refined flour slurry. Stir and cook the curry over medium flame for 2 minutes until it thickens. Then, reduce the flame to low and add the prepared thin coconut milk to the curry. Allow the curry to cook over low flame for another 2 minutes while stirring it continuously. Then, add the prepared thick coconut milk and mix it well. Bring the curry to a rolling boil over medium flame. Then, turn off the flame and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('60ed4731eaf3f9f340a58a1b','60ed3066eaf3f9f340a58a18',7,'m5- add the tempering & serve','To make the tempering for Konkani Curry, heat 2 teaspoons of ghee in a tempering pan over medium flame. Then, add half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, half a teaspoon of cumin seeds, 7 curry leaves, and allow it to splutter over low flame. Then, turn off the flame and add the tempering to the prepared curry. Remove the curry in a serving bowl and serve','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60ed62ddeaf3f9f340a58a1c','60ed5a62e157b3e11c2ca955',1,'p1- boil the dal','To boil the dal for Bendekayi Sambar, first, rinse and clean half a cup of toor dal well with water. Next, add the rinsed dal to a pressure cooker along with 1 cup of water. Then, cover it with a lid and pressure cook the dal over a high flame until 1 whistle. Then, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook the dal for another 8 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the dal is boiling, please move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60ed636de157b3e11c2ca956','60ed5a62e157b3e11c2ca955',2,'p2- prep the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Bendekayi Sambar, first, soak 2 teaspoons of tamarind in 1/4 cup of water for 10 minutes. Next, wash and pat dry the ladies fingers using a kitchen towel. Then, roughly slice 1 cup of ladies fingers into 1-inch pieces. Wash and slit 2 green chilies. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash and separate 14 curry leaves from its stem','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60ed63d7eaf3f9f340a58a1d','60ed5a62e157b3e11c2ca955',3,'m1- simmer the sambar','To make Bendekayi Sambar, first, squeeze out the extract from the soaked tamarind and add it to a deep bottom pan. Next, add 1 cup of water followed by 2 slit green chilies, 1 tablespoon of jaggery, 7 curry leaves, and 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder. Mix it well and bring it to a boil over medium flame. Then, add 1 cup of sliced ladies fingers along with a teaspoon of salt. Stir it well and cover the pan with a lid. Then, allow the ladies finger to cook over low flame for 8 minutes. While the sambar is simmering, please move onto the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60ed6411e157b3e11c2ca957','60ed5a62e157b3e11c2ca955',4,'m2- add the cooked toor dal & boil','After simmering the Bendekayi Sambar, remove the lid and add the boiled toor dal. Mix it well and boil the sambar over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('60ed64671e8237eb6e9734ac','60ed5a62e157b3e11c2ca955',5,'m3- add the tempering & serve','To make the tempering for Bendekayi Sambar, heat 2 teaspoons of coconut oil in a tempering pan over medium flame. Then, add half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, followed by half a teaspoon of urad dal, 1 dry red chili, and 7 curry leaves. Saute and let it splutter over low flame for a few seconds. Then, turn off the flame and add the tempering to the prepared sambar. Remove the sambar into a serving bowl and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60ee9ac8e157b3e11c2ca95b','60ee9a8deaf3f9f340a58a1f',1,'ap1- soak the black eyed peas','For Black Eyed Peas Curry, add 3/4 cup of black-eyed peas in a bowl and soak them in 2 cups of water for 4-5 hours. While the peas are soaking, please move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":300,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60ee9b1eeaf3f9f340a58a20','60ee9a8deaf3f9f340a58a1f',2,'p1- boil the soaked black-eyed peas','To boil the black-eyed peas for Black Eyed Peas Curry, add the soaked peas to a deep bottom pan along with 1 cup of water and a teaspoon of salt. Mix it well and cover the pan with a lid. Then, allow it to boil over medium flame for 7-8 minutes. While the peas are boiling, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60ee9b861e8237eb6e9734ad','60ee9a8deaf3f9f340a58a1f',3,'p2- prepare the ingredients','For Black Eyed Peas Curry, first, soak a teaspoon of tamarind in 1/4 cup of water for 10 minutes. Next, peel, wash, and dice 3/4 cup of potatoes into medium cubes. Grate half a cup of fresh coconut using a grater. Wash and pluck 7 curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60ee9bd3e157b3e11c2ca95c','60ee9a8deaf3f9f340a58a1f',4,'m1- add the potatoes & simmer the curry','After boiling the Black Eyed Peas for the curry, remove the lid and add the 3/4 cup of diced potatoes to the curry along with 1/4 cup of water. Then, cover it with a lid and continue to cook it over low flame for 7-8 minutes until the potatoes are tender. While the curry is simmering please move onto the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('60ee9ce41e8237eb6e9734ae','60ee9a8deaf3f9f340a58a1f',5,'m2- prepare the masala paste','To make the masala paste for Black-eyed peas curry, heat half a teaspoon of coconut oil in a tempering flame over medium flame. Then, add a teaspoon of urad dal and roast it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes until it turns slightly golden. Then, turn off the flame and set it aside. Next, add half a cup of grated fresh coconut to a blender jar followed by a teaspoon of coriander seeds, a teaspoon of cumin seeds, roasted urad dal, and 1 dry red chili. Add 1/4 cup of water and blend it well into a smooth paste.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60ee9d69eaf3f9f340a58a21','60ee9a8deaf3f9f340a58a1f',6,'m3- add the masala paste & simmer the curry','After simmering the Black Eyed Peas Curry, remove the lid and squeeze out the extract from the soaked tamarind and add it to the curry. Add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder and mix it well. Then, bring the curry to a boil over medium flame. Next, add the prepared masala paste to the curry and mix it well. Stir and cook the curry over medium flame for another 2-3 minutes until it slightly thickens. Then, turn off the flame and set it aside','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60ee9f69eaf3f9f340a58a22','60ee9a8deaf3f9f340a58a1f',7,'m4- add the tempering & serve','To make the tempering for Black Eyed Peas Curry, heat a teaspoon of coconut oil in a tempering pan over medium flame. Then, temper it with half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, half a teaspoon of urad dal, 1 dry red chili, and 7 curry leaves. Saute and let it splutter over low flame for a few seconds. Then, turn off the flame and add the tempering to the prepared curry. Remove it in a serving bowl and serve','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60eea9d1eaf3f9f340a58a23','60eea311e157b3e11c2ca95d',1,'p1- prep the ingredients','For pineapple raita, wash, peel and finely chop half a cup of pineapple. Wash, clean, and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash, clean and separate 4 mint leaves from its stem.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60eeaa07e157b3e11c2ca95e','60eea311e157b3e11c2ca95d',2,'p2- blanch the pineapple','To blanch the pineapple for Pineapple Raita, add half a cup of water to a saucepan and bring it to a boil over medium-high flame. Then, add half a cup of diced pineapple and boil them over medium flame for a minute. Then, turn off the flame and remove the blanched pineapple chunks into a strainer. Drain off the extra water and set them aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('60eeaa7ceaf3f9f340a58a24','60eea311e157b3e11c2ca95d',3,'m1- prepare the raita & serve','To make Pineapple Raita, add 1 cup of fresh curd in a mixing bowl and whisk it well using a whisk until smooth. Next, add half a teaspoon of cumin powder, half a teaspoon of black salt, half a teaspoon of sugar. Add 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and mix it well. Next, add in the blanched pineapples and mix it well. Then, remove the raita in a serving bowl and garnish it with some mint leaves. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60eeacf9eaf3f9f340a58a27','60eeac86eaf3f9f340a58a26',1,'p1- soak the tamarind & prep other ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Zunka, add 1 teaspoon of tamarind in a bowl and soak it in 1/4 cup of water. Next, peel, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Grate 1 tablespoon of fresh coconut using a grater. Wash and finely chop 2 green chilies. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash and pluck 7 curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60eead631e8237eb6e9734b0','60eeac86eaf3f9f340a58a26',2,'p2- toast the sesame seeds & prepare the batter','To toast the sesame seeds for Zunka, add a teaspoon of white sesame seeds to a pan and lightly toast them over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and remove them in a bowl. Then, grease a glass mold or any dish with half a teaspoon of oil and sprinkle the toasted sesame seeds into the mold as shown. Next, to prepare the gram flour batter, add half a cup of gram flour to a bowl followed by half a teaspoon of salt,  3/4 cup of water, and mix it well until smooth. There should be no lumps in the batter.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('60eeadd0eaf3f9f340a58a28','60eeac86eaf3f9f340a58a26',3,'m1- fry the onions','To make zunka, heat 1 tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium for a minute. Then, add 1 teaspoon of cumin seeds, 7 curry leaves and allow it to splutter for a few seconds. Next,  add 1/4 cup of chopped onions and fry the onions over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until translucent. Next, add 2 chopped green chilies followed by 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder and fry it over medium flame for another minute. Then, squeeze out the extract from the soaked tamarind and add it to the pan. Mix it well and bring it to a boil over medium flame.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60eeaebaeaf3f9f340a58a29','60eeac86eaf3f9f340a58a26',4,'m2- cook the mixture &  set  in greased mold','Next, reduce the flame to low and then add the prepared gram flour batter to the pan while stirring it continuously. Keep stirring the batter over low flame and cook it for 2-3 minutes until it thickens and starts to come together. The mixture should turn into a semi-thick dough-like consistency. Then, add a tablespoon of grated coconut and mix it well. Turn off the flame and carefully remove the mixture into the greased mold. Level the mixture into the mold using a spatula. Then, allow it to cool and set in the mold for 10 minutes. After that, slice it into bite-size squares and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('60eeb140e157b3e11c2ca95f','60eeb10d1e8237eb6e9734b1',1,'ap1- soak the rice','For Cucumber Neer Dosa, in a bowl, add 1 cup of sona masuri and rinse it well with water. Then, soak the rice in 2 cups of water for 4-5 hours. While the rice is soaking, please move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":300,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60eeb187e157b3e11c2ca960','60eeb10d1e8237eb6e9734b1',2,'p1- dice the cucumber','To prepare the ingredients for Cucumber Neer Dosa, wash and cut off the ends of the cucumber. Then, roughly dice half a cup of cucumber. Next, grate 1/4 cup of fresh coconut using a grater.','prep_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60eeb1d0eaf3f9f340a58a2b','60eeb10d1e8237eb6e9734b1',3,'p2- prepare the batter','To prepare the batter for Cucumber Neer Dosa, add the soaked rice to a blender jar followed by 1/4 cup of grated coconut and half a cup of diced cucumber. Add 1/4 cup of water and cover the jar with a lid. Then, blend it well into a smooth batter. Remove the batter into a large mixing bowl. Add half a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Add more water to the batter if required. The batter should be thin and flowy.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60eeb23ee157b3e11c2ca961','60eeb10d1e8237eb6e9734b1',4,'m1- make the dosa & serve','To make Cucumber Neer Dosa, heat up a tawa over medium flame and grease it with a teaspoon of cooking oil. Then, pour a ladle full of the prepared batter onto the hot tawa and spread it across as shown. Then, cover and cook the dosa over medium flame for 2 minutes until it is crisp and slightly golden. After that, remove the lid and carefully fold the dosa as shown. Remove it onto a serving plate and serve. Similarly, make the rest of the dosas from the batter.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60eeb4d71e8237eb6e9734b2','60eeb49ae157b3e11c2ca962',1,'ap1- soak the rice & fenugreek seeds','For Fenugreek Dosa, first, add 1.5 cups of sona masuri  to a bowl and rinse it well with water. Then, soak the rice in 2 cups of water for 6 hours. Next, in a separate bowl add 1.5 tablespoons of fenugreek seeds and soak it in 1/4 cup of water for 6 hours. While the rice and fenugreek seeds soak, please move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":360,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('60eeb53ae157b3e11c2ca963','60eeb49ae157b3e11c2ca962',2,'ap2- prepare & set the batter to ferment','To prepare the batter for Fenugreek Dosa, add the soaked fenugreek seeds to a blender jar along with 1/4 cup of water and blend it well into a smooth paste. Then, add the soaked rice to the same blender jar followed by half a cup of water and blend it again into a smooth batter. Next, remove the batter into a large bowl and cover it with a plate. Then, allow it to ferment for 8-10 hours. While the batter ferments, please move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":600,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60eeb59f1e8237eb6e9734b3','60eeb49ae157b3e11c2ca962',3,'m1- make the dosa & serve','To make Fenugreek Dosa, add a teaspoon of salt to the fermented batter. Add about 1/4 cup of water to adjust the consistency of the batter and mix it well. Next, heat up a tawa over medium flame and grease it with a teaspoon of cooking oil. Wipe off the extra oil with a tissue and add a ladleful of the prepared batter to the tawa. Then, spread it evenly into a slightly thick round circle using the ladle as shown. Next, cover it with a lid and cook the dosa over medium-low flame for 3 minutes until slightly golden. Then, remove the lid and carefully remove the dosa onto a serving plate. Make the rest of the dosas similarly to the batter and serve','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60eebbde1e8237eb6e9734b4','60eeba32eaf3f9f340a58a2d',1,'p1- prep the ingredients','For Pineapple Curry, wash, peel and cut 1 cup of pineapple into cubes. Grate 1/4 cup of fresh coconut using a garter. Wash and pluck 14 curry leaves. Next, to roast the sesame seeds, heat up a pan and add 2 tablespoons of black sesame seeds to it. Then, dry roast the seeds over medium-low flame for 1-2 mins. After that, turn off the flame and remove it in a bowl.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('60eec23fe157b3e11c2ca965','60eeba32eaf3f9f340a58a2d',2,'m1- simmer the pineapples','To make Pineapple Curry, add 1 cup of diced pineapple to a deep bottom pan. Next,  add in 1 cup of water followed by 2 tablespoons of peanuts, 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, and a teaspoon of salt. Add 2 tablespoons of jaggery along with 7 curry leaves and mix it well. Then, cover the pan with a lid and cook it over low flame for 10 minutes until the pineapples are tender. While the curry simmers, please move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60eec345e157b3e11c2ca966','60eeba32eaf3f9f340a58a2d',3,'m2- prepare the masala paste','To prepare the masala paste for Pineapple Curry, heat a tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame. Add 2 teaspoons of urad dal followed by a teaspoon of chana dal, 1/4 teaspoon of fenugreek seeds, 1 dry red chili, and 7 curry leaves. Roast the lentils over medium flame for 1-2 minutes until they are golden brown. Then, turn off the flame and remove the roasted lentils into a blender jar. Add 2 tablespoons of roasted sesame seeds along with 1/4 cup of grated coconut and blend it well into a smooth paste','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('60eec380e157b3e11c2ca967','60eeba32eaf3f9f340a58a2d',4,'m3- add the masala paste & cook the curry','After simmering the Pineapple Curry, carefully remove the lid and add the prepared masala paste. Mix it well. Add about half a cup of water to adjust the consistency. Then, bring it to a boil over medium flame. After that turn off the flame and remove it in a serving bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60eec9461e8237eb6e9734b6','60eec906eaf3f9f340a58a2e',1,'p1- boil the rice','To boil the rice for Mango Rice, first, rinse and clean half a cup of basmati rice thoroughly with water. Next, boil 1.25 cups of water in a deep bottom pan and add the rinsed rice. Stir it well. Then, cover the pan with a lid and allow it to boil over medium flame for 8-10 minutes or until the rice is cooked through. Then, turn off the flame and set it aside. Alternatively, you can also cook the rice in a pressure cooker. While the rice is boiling, please move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60eec9cb1e8237eb6e9734b7','60eec906eaf3f9f340a58a2e',2,'p2- prep the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Mango Rice, wash, peel and grate 1/4 cup of raw mango. Separate 1 tablespoon of grated raw mango for garnish. Wash, peel, and finely chop a half-inch piece of ginger. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Grate 2 tablespoons of fresh coconut. Wash and pluck 7 curry leaves','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60eeca00eaf3f9f340a58a2f','60eec906eaf3f9f340a58a2e',3,'p3- prepare the raw mango masala paste','To prepare the raw mango paste for Mango Rice, add 1/4 cup of grated raw mango to a blender jar followed by 2 green chilies, and 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder. Cover the jar with a lid and blend it well into a smooth paste.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60eeca8deaf3f9f340a58a30','60eec906eaf3f9f340a58a2e',4,'m1- fry the peanuts & cashews','To make Mango Rice, heat 1.5 tablespoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame. Then, add half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, half a teaspoon of urad dal, half a teaspoon cumin seeds, and half a teaspoon of chana dal and 7curry leaves. Saute and allow it to splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 1.5 tablespoons of peanuts and roast them over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Then, add half-inch piece of chopped ginger along with 1 tablespoon of cashew nuts and fry them over medium flame for another minute.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('60eecad91e8237eb6e9734b8','60eec906eaf3f9f340a58a2e',5,'m2- cook the rice with the masala & serve','Next, add the prepared raw mango paste and cook it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes.  Add a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. After that, add the boiled rice and gently mix it with the masala. Then, add 2 tablespoons of grated coconut, 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves, and 1 tablespoon of grated raw mango. Mix it well with light hands without breaking the rice. Then, turn off the flame and plate the rice. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60eed19eeaf3f9f340a58a32','60eed110e157b3e11c2ca968',1,'p1- dry roast the rava  & dice cucumber','To prepare the ingredients for Cucumber Rawa Idli, first, add 1 cup of rava to a pan and dry roast it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and remove it in a bowl. Next, wash and clean 1 cucumber. Then, cut off the ends and finely chop 3/4 cup of cucumber. Next, grate 1/4 cup of fresh coconut. Wash and slit 1 green chili. Cut the banana leaf into squares as shown','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60eed1df1e8237eb6e9734b9','60eed110e157b3e11c2ca968',2,'p2- prepare the coconut paste','To prepare the coconut paste for Cucumber Rava Idli, add 1/4 cup of grated coconut to a blender jar along with 1 green chili and a teaspoon of cumin seeds. Add 1/4 cup of water and blend it well into a smooth paste.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60eed2211e8237eb6e9734ba','60eed110e157b3e11c2ca968',3,'m1- make the batter','To make the batter of Cucumber Rava Idli, add the roasted rawa to a mixing bowl. Add the prepared coconut paste followed by 3/4 cup of chopped cucumber and a teaspoon of salt. Mix it well. Then, add about 1/4 cup of water and prepare a loose dough-like batter.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60eed251eaf3f9f340a58a33','60eed110e157b3e11c2ca968',4,'m2- steam the idli & serve','To make the Cucumber Rawa Idli, divide the idli batter into equal portions and place each onto the banana leaf as shown. Then, gently pat it and spread the batter on the leaf. Fold the leaf in half as shown Prepare the rest of the idlis similarly and place them into the steamer one by one. Then, cover the steamer and steam the idli over medium flame for 15 mins. After that, turn off the flame and remove the idlis onto a serving plate. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('60efd8571e8237eb6e9734bc','60efd7fceaf3f9f340a58a34',1,'p1- rinse & boil the dal','For Tovve Dal, first, rinse and clean 3/4 cup of toor dal thoroughly with water. Next, to boil the dal, add the boiled dal to a deep bottom pan followed by 1.5 cups of water and 1/8 teaspoon of turmeric powder. Mix it well and let the dal boil over medium-low flame for 10 minutes. Keep stirring the dal occasionally and cook it until tender. While the dal is boiling, please move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60efd8bdeaf3f9f340a58a35','60efd7fceaf3f9f340a58a34',2,'p2- prep the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Tovve dal, wash, peel and chop 1-inch ginger into juliennes. Wash and slit 2 green chilies. Wash, clean and separate 7 curry leaves from its stem. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Cut and squeeze 1 teaspoon of lime juice into a bowl.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60efd9101e8237eb6e9734bd','60efd7fceaf3f9f340a58a34',3,'m1- add salt & cook the dal','To make Tovve dal, after boiling the toor dal, stir it well and slightly mash the dal using the ladle as shown. Then, add 1/8 teaspoon of turmeric powder followed by a teaspoon of salt and 2 slit green chilies. Mix it well and bring it to a boil over medium flame. Then,  turn off the flame and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60efd9be1e8237eb6e9734be','60efd7fceaf3f9f340a58a34',4,'m2- add the tempering & serve','To make the tempering for Tovve Dal, heat 1 teaspoon of ghee and 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a tempering pan. Then, add 1 teaspoon of cumin seeds, 1/4 teaspoon of hing, 7 curry leaves, and 1-inch ginger juliennes. Saute the tempering over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and add the tempering to the prepared dal, Mix it well and let the dal boil over medium flame for 2 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and add 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves followed by a teaspoon of lime juice. Mix it well and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('60efdd63eaf3f9f340a58a36','60efdd22e157b3e11c2ca96a',1,'p1- soak the rice flakes','For Huli Avalakki, soak 2 teaspoons of tamarind in 1/4 cup of water for 10 minutes. Next, add 1.5 cups of rice flakes to a bowl and soak them in 2 cups of water for 10 minutes. While the tamarind and rice flakes soak, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('60efdde1eaf3f9f340a58a37','60efdd22e157b3e11c2ca96a',2,'p2- prepare the masala paste','To prepare the ingredients for Huli Avalakki, grate half a cup of fresh coconut using a grater. Wash and pluck 7 curry leaves from the stem.  Next, to prepare the masala paste, add half a cup of grated coconut to a blender jar followed by 2 dry red chilies and 1/4 teaspoon of mustard seeds. Cover the jar with a lid and blend it into a slightly coarse paste. Next, after soaking the rice flakes, drain the water and set them aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60efdff31e8237eb6e9734c0','60efdd22e157b3e11c2ca96a',3,'m1- temper the oil & roast the peanuts','To make Huli Avalakki, heat 2 teaspoons of coconut oil in a pan over medium flame. Then, add 1/4 teaspoon of mustard seeds, half a teaspoon of urad dal, and 7 curry leaves. Saute and allow it to splutter for a few seconds. Then, add 2 tablespoons of peanuts and saute over medium flame for 1-2 minutes until peanuts turn crisp and brown','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60efe06be157b3e11c2ca96b','60efdd22e157b3e11c2ca96a',4,'m2- cook the rice flakes with the masala paste & serve','Next, mash the soaked tamarind in water as shown and strain the juice into the pan. Mix it well and add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder followed by 1 teaspoon of jaggery powder, and 1 teaspoon of salt. Stir and bring it to boil over medium flame. Then, add the prepared coconut masala and cook it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes. Next, add the soaked rice flakes and gently mix it until coated evenly with the masala. Stir and cook over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and plate the avlakkai. Serve','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60f003aaeaf3f9f340a58a39','60efe5f7eaf3f9f340a58a38',1,'p1- prep the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for the Yogurt Dip, grate 2.5 tablespoons of fresh coconut using a grater. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of coriander leaves. Wash and slit 1 green chili. Next, add half a cup of curd to a mixing bowl and whisk it well until smooth.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60f004fc1e8237eb6e9734c1','60efe5f7eaf3f9f340a58a38',2,'m1- make the coconut masala','To make the masala paste for Yogurt Dip, heat up a frying pan over medium flame. Then, add half a teaspoon mustard seeds, followed by half a teaspoon of fenugreek seeds, and dry roast them over low flame for a minute until fragrant. Next, add 2.5 tablespoons of grated coconut, 1/4 cup of chopped coriander leaves, and 1 green chili. Stir and fry the mixture over medium-low flame for 1-2 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and remove it in a blender jar. Cover the jar with a lid and blend it well into a slightly coarse paste.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('60f0059fe157b3e11c2ca96d','60efe5f7eaf3f9f340a58a38',3,'m2- prepare the dip & serve','To make the Yogurt Dip, add half a cup of whisked to a mixing bowl along with half a cup of water and mix it well using a whisk. Next, add the prepared powdered spices followed by half a teaspoon of salt and 1/4 teaspoon of hing. Mix it well and remove the dip in a serving bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60f01733e157b3e11c2ca96f','60f009eceaf3f9f340a58a3a',1,'p1- slit the brinjals & prep other ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Stuffed Brinjal Curry, first, soak a tablespoon of tamarind in 1/4 cup of water for 15 minutes. Next, wash and clean 6 small brinjals. Then, cross-slit the brinjals as shown while retaining the stem. Next, soak the slit brinjals in water until later use. Next, peel, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Peel 8 cloves of garlic. Wash and roughly chop 2 green chilies. Wash and roughly chop 1/4 cup of coriander leaves. Grate half a cup of coconut using a grater. Wash and pluck 7 curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":17,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60f01eb4eaf3f9f340a58a3b','60f009eceaf3f9f340a58a3a',2,'p2- prepare the masala paste','To prepare the coconut masala paste for Stuffed Brinjal Curry, add half a cup of grated coconut to a blender jar followed by 2 chopped green chilies, half a teaspoon of cumin seeds, and 4 cloves of garlic. Add 1/4 cup of water and cover the jar with a lid. Then, blend it well into a smooth paste.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60f01f27e157b3e11c2ca970','60f009eceaf3f9f340a58a3a',3,'p3- prepare the roasted peanut powder','To prepare the peanut mixture for Stuffed Brinjals, heat up a pan over medium flame and add 1/4 cup of peanuts to it. Then, dry roast the peanuts over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until they are slightly golden. Next, add 2 tablespoons of white sesame seeds and roast the seeds with the peanuts for another minute. Then, turn off the flame and remove it into a blender jar. Cover the jar with a lid and blend it well into a slightly coarse powder.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60f01f9ee157b3e11c2ca971','60f009eceaf3f9f340a58a3a',4,'p4- prepare the stuffing & stuff the brinjals','To prepare the stuffing for Stuffed Brinjal Curry, add the prepared peanut mixture to a mixing bowl along with 1/4 cup of chopped onions. Next, mash the soaked tamarind in water and strain the pulp as shown, and add it to the mixture. Next, add half a teaspoon of turmeric powder, 2 teaspoons sambar powder, 2 teaspoons of jaggery, and the prepared coconut masala paste. Add 1 teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Then, stuff the masala into the slits of the brinjals as shown and prepare the stuffed brinjals.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('60f01fe91e8237eb6e9734c2','60f009eceaf3f9f340a58a3a',5,'m1- simmer the stuffed brinjals','To make Stuffed Brinjal Curry, heat 2 tablespoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame. Then, add half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, 7 curry leaves, and 4 cloves of garlic. Saute it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes until garlic is fragrant. Then, add the stuffed brinjals one by one to the pan. Cover the pan with a lid and cook the brinjals over low flame for 10 minutes while stirring the brinjals occasionally. While the brinjals simmer, please move onto the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('60f0201aeaf3f9f340a58a3c','60f009eceaf3f9f340a58a3a',6,'m2- add the leftover masala paste & simmer','After simmering the brinjals for Stuffed Brinjal Curry, remove the lid and the leftover masala paste. Add 1/4 cup of water and gently stir it. Then, cover the pan with a lid and continue to simmer the curry for another 5-6 minutes until the oil separates from the masala and the masala is cooked completely. After that, turn off the flame and plate the stuffed brinjal curry into a serving dish. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('60f022b8eaf3f9f340a58a3d','60f02277e157b3e11c2ca973',1,'p1- boil the horse gram lentil','To boil the dal for Horsegram Rasam, first, rinse and clean half a cup of horse gram lentil thoroughly with water. Next, add the rinsed dal to a pressure cooker along with 1.25 cups of water and cover it with a lid. Then, pressure cook the dal over a high flame until three whistles. After that, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook the dal for another 5 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and allow the cooker to release the pressure naturally. While the dal is boiling, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60f02335eaf3f9f340a58a3e','60f02277e157b3e11c2ca973',2,'p2- prep the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Horsegram Rasam, first, soak a tablespoon of tamarind in half a cup of water for 10 minutes. Next, grate 2 tablespoons of fresh coconut using a garter, Peel, and finely chop 1 tablespoon of garlic. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash and pluck 12 curry leaves','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60f0237b1e8237eb6e9734c3','60f02277e157b3e11c2ca973',3,'m1- boil the rasam','To make the Horsegram Rasam, place a strainer over a deep bottom pan and strain the boiled horse gram dal as shown. Keep the boiled dal aside. Next, mash the soaked tamarind in water and strain the juice into the pan as shown. Then, add a teaspoon of jaggery and 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder and mix it well. Then, allow the rasam to boil over medium flame for 6-8 minutes. While the rasam boils, please move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('60f023f7e157b3e11c2ca974','60f02277e157b3e11c2ca973',4,'m2- prepare the masala paste','To prepare the rasam powder for Horsegram Rasam, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame. Add 2 teaspoons of coriander seeds followed by a teaspoon of cumin seeds, 1/4 teaspoon of fenugreek seeds, and 1 dry red chili and 7 curry leaves. Saute and roast the spices over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until the spices are fragrant. Then, turn off the flame and remove the spices into a blender jar. Next, add 2 tablespoons of grated coconut and 1/4 cup of boiled horse gram dal. Add 1/4 cup of water and blend it well into a smooth paste.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60f0242e1e8237eb6e9734c4','60f02277e157b3e11c2ca973',5,'m3- add the masala paste & boil the rasam','After boiling the Horse gram Rasam, add the prepared masala paste and mix it well. Then, add about 3/4 cup of water to adjust the consistency of the rasam.  Add 1 teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Then, stir and boil the rasam over medium flame for 2-3 minutes. After that add a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60f024691e8237eb6e9734c5','60f02277e157b3e11c2ca973',6,'m4- add the tempering & serve','To make the tempering for Horsegram Rasam, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a tempering pan over medium flame. Next,  add half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, 5 curry leaves, and a tablespoon of chopped garlic. Saute the tempering over medium flame for 1-2 minutes until garlic is fragrant. Then, turn off the flame and add the tempering to the rasam. Remove it in a serving bowl and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60f02717eaf3f9f340a58a40','60f026dceaf3f9f340a58a3f',1,'p1- boil the dal','To boil the toor dal for Udupi Tomato Rasam, first, rinse and clean 3/4 cup of toor dal thoroughly with water. Then, add it to a pressure cooker along with 1.5 cups of water. Mix it well and cover it with a lid. Pressure cook the dal over high flame until one whistle. Then, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook it for another 8 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and allow the pressure cooker to release the pressure naturally. While the dal simmers, please move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60f027761e8237eb6e9734c6','60f026dceaf3f9f340a58a3f',2,'p2- prep the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Udupi Tomato Rasam, first, soak 1 tablespoon of tamarind in half a cup of water for 10 minutes. Next, wash and roughly dice 1 cup of tomatoes. Wash and slit 1 green chili. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash and pluck 7 curry leaves.  Next, after soaking the tamarind, mash and mix it well with water. Then, strain the juice in a bowl.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('60f027bf1e8237eb6e9734c7','60f026dceaf3f9f340a58a3f',3,'m1- simmer the rasam','To make Udupi Tomato Rasam, add 1 cup of diced tomatoes to a deep bottom pan followed by half a cup of prepared tamarind juice. Next, add 1 cup of water, 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, 7 curry leaves, 1 slit green chili, and 1 teaspoon of jaggery. Mix it well and cover the pan with a lid. Then, cook it over medium-low flame for 5 minutes until the tomatoes are tender. While the rasam simmers, please move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60f0280f1e8237eb6e9734c8','60f026dceaf3f9f340a58a3f',4,'m2- add the boiled dal & boil the rasam','After simmering the Udupi Tomato Rasam, carefully take off the lid and stir it well. Then, add a tablespoon of rasam powder and bring it to a boil. Next, add the prepared toor dal followed by 1 cup of water, 1 teaspoon of salt, and 1/4 teaspoon of hing. Add a teaspoon of rasam and mix it well. Boil the rasam over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and remove it in a serving bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60f02a5de157b3e11c2ca977','60f02a081e8237eb6e9734c9',1,'p1- soak the saffron & chop the cashew nuts','For Kesari Bath, first, soak 2 strands of saffron in 2 tablespoons of water for 10 minutes. Next, roughly chop 2 tablespoons of cashew nuts. While the saffron soaks, please move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":7,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60f02a9eeaf3f9f340a58a41','60f02a081e8237eb6e9734c9',2,'m1- roast the nuts','To roast the nuts Kesari Bath, heat 2 teaspoons of ghee in a pan over medium flame. Then,  add 2 tablespoons of chopped cashew nuts and roast them over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until cashews are slightly golden. Then, remove the roasted cashews in a bowl and set them aside. Next, add 1 tablespoon of raisins to the same pan and roast them over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and remove the raisins in a bowl.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60f02b091e8237eb6e9734ca','60f02a081e8237eb6e9734c9',3,'m2- roast the semolina','To make Kesari Bath, first, add 1 cup of water to a saucepan and bring it to boil over medium-high flame. Then, turn off the flame and set it aside. Next, add half a cup of fine semolina to the pan or kadai and roast it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes until fragrant. Then, reduce the flame to low and add 1 cup of hot water to the pan. Keep stirring it continuously over low flame for 2-3 minutes or until well combined.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('60f02b871e8237eb6e9734cb','60f02a081e8237eb6e9734c9',4,'m3- add sugar,  ghee and cook','Next, add 1/4 cup of sugar followed by soaked saffron and a teaspoon of cardamom powder and mix it well. Stir and cook it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until the sugar dissolves. Next, add 1/4 cup of desi ghee and cook it for another minute. Add the roasted nuts and mix it well. Then, turn off the flame and remove it in a serving bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60f02e25eaf3f9f340a58a43','60f02dcae157b3e11c2ca978',1,'p1- prep the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Bende Mosaru Gojju, first, rinse and clean 1 cup of ladies fingers thoroughly with water. Then, spread them on a kitchen towel and pat dry the ladies fingers. Make sure to dry off the ladies finger completely before slicing and cooking or they will stick together. Next, remove the ends and cut 1 cup of ladies fingers into round slices. Grate half a cup of fresh coconut using a grater. Wash and slit 1 green chili. Wash and pluck 7 curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60f02e74eaf3f9f340a58a44','60f02dcae157b3e11c2ca978',2,'p2- prepare the masala paste','To prepare the masala paste for Bende Mosaru Gojju, add half a cup of grated coconut to a blender jar followed by 1 teaspoon of cumin seeds, 1 green chili, and half a teaspoon of salt. Add 1/4 cup of water and cover the jar with a lid. Then, blend it well into a fine paste.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60f02ee7eaf3f9f340a58a45','60f02dcae157b3e11c2ca978',3,'m1- fry the ladies fingers','To fry the ladies fingers for Bende Mosaru Gojju, heat 1 tablespoon of cooking oil in a frying pan over medium flame for a minute. Then, add 1 cup of sliced ladies fingers and fry them over medium-high flame for 5-6 minutes until they are tender-crisp. Then, turn off the flame and remove them in a bowl.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60f02f27e157b3e11c2ca979','60f02dcae157b3e11c2ca978',4,'m2- add curd & masala paste','To make the Bende Mosaru Gojju, add the prepared masala paste to a mixing bowl. Add half a cup of fresh curd and mix it well until smooth. Then, add the fried ladies fingers and mix it well.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('60f02fa0eaf3f9f340a58a46','60f02dcae157b3e11c2ca978',5,'m3- add the tempering & serve','To make the tempering for Bende Mosaru Gojju, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a tempering pan over medium flame. Then, add half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, half a teaspoon of urad dal, 1 dry red chili, and 7 curry leaves. Saute and let it splutter over low flame for a few seconds. Then, turn off the flame and add the tempering to the prepared curry. Mix it well and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60fe86ba69a0e1cc4cab0fb5','60fe866c69a0e1cc4cab0fb4',1,'p1- boil the dal','To boil the toor dal for Mysore Kootu, first, rinse 1/4 cup of toor dal thoroughly with water. Then, add it to a pressure cooker along with half a cup of water, 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder, and 1 teaspoon of cooking oil. Mix it well and cover it with a lid. Pressure cook the dal over high flame until one whistle. Then, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook it for another 8 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and allow the pressure cooker to release the pressure naturally. While the dal simmers, please move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60fe872ddcf1124d0dd76c00','60fe866c69a0e1cc4cab0fb4',2,'p2- dice the vegetables','To prepare the ingredients for Mysore Kootu, wash 1/4 cup of sweet pumpkin and cut them into cubes along with the skin. Wash peel and cut 1/4 cup of carrot into cubes. Wash and cut 1/4 cup of beans into 1 inch long pieces. Wash, peel, and dice 1/4 cup of potatoes. Grate half a cup of fresh coconut using a grater. Wash and pluck 7 nos curry leaves','prep_method','{"active_time":17,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('60fe880f69a0e1cc4cab0fb6','60fe866c69a0e1cc4cab0fb4',3,'p3- prepare the masala paste','To prepare the masala powder for Mysore Kootu, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Next, add 1 tsp of urad dal, 1 tsp of chana dal, 1 tsp of coriander seeds, 1/2 tsp of cumin seeds, 1/2 tsp of black peppercorns, 2 dried red chilies, and a 1-inch piece of cinnamon stick. Saute the whole spices over medium flame until it turns aromatic. Then, add 1/2 a cup of grated coconut and mix it well. Then, fry it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until the coconut is slightly brown. Then, turn off the flame and allow the mixture to slightly cool. After that, transfer it to a blender jar and blend it into a coarse powder, remove it in a bowl, and set it aside','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('60fe886469a0e1cc4cab0fb7','60fe866c69a0e1cc4cab0fb4',4,'m1- simmer the vegetables','To make Mysore Kootu, heat  2 cups of water in a deep bottom pan over medium flame for a minute. Next, add 1/4 cup of diced beans, potatoes, carrots, and pumpkin along with 2 tbsp of peanuts. Mix it well. Add a teaspoon of salt and stir it well. Then, allow the vegetables to cook over low flame for 6 to 7 minutes until the vegetables are tender. While the vegetables are cooking, please move onto the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":7,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('60fe889d69a0e1cc4cab0fb8','60fe866c69a0e1cc4cab0fb4',5,'m2- add the toor dal & masala paste','After simmering the vegetables for Mysore Kootu, add the prepared kootu masala powder followed by the cooked toor dal and mix it well. Gently mash the dal using the ladle to add thickness to the gravy. Do not mash the vegetables. Then, stir and cook the kootu over medium flame for 2-3 minutes and bring it to a rolling boil. After that turn off the flame and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('60fe88eedcf1124d0dd76c01','60fe866c69a0e1cc4cab0fb4',6,'m3- add the tempering & serve','To make the tempering for Mysore Kootu, heat a tempering pan and add 1 tsp of oil, after it becomes hot add 1/2 a tsp of mustard seeds, add 7 nos curry leaves, and allow it to splutter on low flame, then turn off the flame and add the tempering to the prepared kootu. Mix it well and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('611a2bac5b3783aa411a3129','611a2639c757b57058a8ae09',1,'p1- chop the vegetables','For Veg Stew, wash, peel, and finely slice 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and roughly chop 5 nos beans. Wash, peel and cut 1/4 cup of carrot into 2-inch pieces. Wash, peel, and cube 1/4 cup of potatoes. Peel and wash 1/4 cup of green peas. Wash and cut 1/4 cup of cauliflower into florets. Wash and slit 2 nos green chilies. Wash and cut 1/2 inch piece of ginger into juliennes. Wash 7 nos curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":18,"semi_active_time":1,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('611a2c13c757b57058a8ae0a','611a2639c757b57058a8ae09',2,'m1- fry the onions','To make Veg Stew, heat 1 teaspoon of coconut oil in a kadai on a medium flame for a minute. Add 2 nos cloves, half an inch piece of cinnamon stick, and 2 nos green cardamoms. Saute it on a medium flame for a minute. Next, add 1/4 cup of sliced onions and fry it for 2-3 minutes, until it turns slightly translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('611a2c5acffdac1d2c01981c','611a2639c757b57058a8ae09',3,'m2- simmer the vegetables','After frying the onions, add 5 nos chopped beans, 1/4 cup of chopped carrots, 1/4 cup of cubed potatoes, and 1/4 cup of green peas followed by 1/4 cup of cauliflower florets. Next, add 2 nos slit green chilies along with 1/2 inch piece of ginger juliennes and mix it well. Add 3/4 cup of water followed by half a teaspoon of salt and 7 nos curry leaves. Mix it well and cover it with a lid. Cook the vegetables on medium-high flame for 5 minutes. Make sure not to cook the vegetables completely. While the vegetables are cooking, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":1,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('611a2c9b5b3783aa411a312a','611a2639c757b57058a8ae09',4,'m3- add coconut milk & simmer the gravy','After simmering the vegetables for Veg Stew, take off the lid and reduce the flame to low. Then, add 1/4 cup of coconut milk and mix it well. Be careful while adding the coconut milk as it might split, so keep stirring until it is well combined with the vegetables. Then, boil it on a medium flame for 6-7 minutes. Keep stirring it in between. While it is boiling, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":7,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('611a2cf0cffdac1d2c01981d','611a2639c757b57058a8ae09',5,'m4- Garnish & serve','After cooking the Veg Stew, give it a stir. Add 1/4 cup of thick coconut milk along with half a teaspoon of coconut oil and mix it well. Then, turn off the flame and take it out into a bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('611a45a2c757b57058a8ae0e','611a452bc757b57058a8ae0d',1,'p1- knead the dough','To knead the dough for Phulka, first, add 1.5 cups of whole wheat flour in a large mixing bowl. Add 1/4 teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Next, gradually add about half a cup of water and knead it well into a smooth dough. Then, cover it with a cloth and allow it to rest for 20 minutes. While the dough is resting, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('611a45d7cffdac1d2c019836','611a452bc757b57058a8ae0d',2,'m1- divide the dough and roll out the phulka','To make the Phulka, first, divide the prepared dough into small equal-sized balls. Then, take a dough ball and dust it in some flour. Press it gently to slightly flatten it and roll it into a 7-inch thin circle. Make sure to roll out the edges thin.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('611a460ccffdac1d2c019837','611a452bc757b57058a8ae0d',3,'m2- cook the phulka and serve','Next, carefully place the rolled-out roti onto the hot tawa and cook it over medium flame for a minute. Then, gently flip it and cook the other side for 1-2 minutes, until small brown spots start to appear on its surface. Then, cook the roti over the direct flame while flipping it in between. Cook the roti until both sides are evenly browned. After the roti puffs up, remove it from the flame and take it out onto a serving plate. Serve. Make the rest of the rotis similarly.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('611a57e5c757b57058a8ae3e','611a5773c757b57058a8ae3d',1,'p1- prep the ingredients','For Sweet Corn Soup, peel and finely chop 1 teaspoon of garlic. Wash, peel, and finely chop a 1-inch piece of ginger. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of spring onion whites. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of spring onion greens. Wash, peel, and finely chop 1/4 cup of carrots. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of beans.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('611a582bc757b57058a8ae3f','611a5773c757b57058a8ae3d',2,'p2- prepare the sweet corn paste','To make the corn paste for the Sweet Corn Soup, add 1/2 cup of sweet corn kernels to a blender jar along with 2 tablespoons of water and blend it well to make a smooth paste. Next, to make the cornflour slurry, add 1 teaspoon of cornflour to a bowl along with 1/4 cup of water. Mix it well to avoid any lumps.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('611a586ec757b57058a8ae40','611a5773c757b57058a8ae3d',3,'m1- saute the spring onions with ginger & garlic','To make the Sweet Corn Soup, heat 1 tablespoon of olive oil in a deep bottom pan on a medium flame for a minute. Add 1 teaspoon of chopped garlic, 1-inch piece of chopped ginger, and saute it for 1-2 minutes on medium-high flame. Next, add 2 tablespoons of spring onion whites and saute it for another 2-3 minutes, until it turns slightly translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('611a58aecffdac1d2c01984d','611a5773c757b57058a8ae3d',4,'m2- stir-fry the vegetables','After frying the spring onions, add 1/4 cup of sweet corn kernels, 1/4 cup of finely chopped carrots, 1/4 cup of finely chopped beans, and stir fry the vegetables on high flame for 2 minutes. Then, add the prepared sweet corn paste to the pan and saute it for 2-3 minutes on medium-low flame till the paste comes together. Keep stirring the paste continuously to prevent it from sticking to the bottom of the pan.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('611a5909cffdac1d2c01984e','611a5773c757b57058a8ae3d',5,'m3- simmer the soup & serve','After frying the sweet corn paste, add 3 cups of water along with 3/4 teaspoon of salt. Stir it well. Cover it with a lid and allow the soup to boil for 15 minutes on medium-low flame. After 15 minutes, take off the lid, and add the prepared cornflour slurry to the soup. Stir well and boil it until the soup thickens. Next, add 1/2 teaspoon of black pepper powder, 1 teaspoon of vinegar, and 2 tablespoons of spring onion greens to the soup, stir it well, and turn off the flame. Garnish it with 1/4 teaspoon of black pepper powder and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('611a5b725b3783aa411a3140','611a5b1ac757b57058a8ae50',1,'m1- Crack the egg onto the greased pan, season & cook','To make Sunny Side Up Eggs, first, crack an egg into a bowl. Next, heat a pan over medium flame and add half a teaspoon of butter into it. Twirl the pan slightly to spread the butter across it. Then, gently add the cracked egg into it without breaking up the yolk. Then, cook it over medium-low flame for 4-5 minutes. Season it with 1/4 teaspoon of salt and 1/4 teaspoon of black pepper powder. As the sides of the egg start to get slightly crisp and golden brown. Carefully take it out onto a plate and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('611a5f395b3783aa411a3142','611a5ea0c757b57058a8ae53',1,'p1- prepare the marinade','To prepare the marinade for the Lemon Coriander Chicken, first, wash and roughly chop 3 tablespoons of coriander leaves. Peel and wash 3 cloves of garlic. Squeeze 2 teaspoons of lime juice using a lemon squeezer. Next, to a blender jar, add 3 cloves of garlic followed by a teaspoon of chili flakes and oregano. Next, add 1 teaspoon of black pepper powder along with half a teaspoon of salt and brown sugar. Add 2 teaspoons of lime juice followed by 3 tablespoons of coriander leaves. Then, add 3 tablespoons of olive oil and blend it into a smooth paste.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('611a5f73c757b57058a8ae54','611a5ea0c757b57058a8ae53',2,'p2- marinate the chicken','To marinate the chicken breast for Lemon Coriander Chicken, first, wash the chicken fillets thoroughly with water. Next, keep it in a dish and pour the prepared marinade over it. Rub the marinade over the chicken fillets and coat it well. Marination tenderizes the chicken while allowing it to absorb the flavors from the spices, hence making it more succulent and flavourful. Allow the chicken to marinate for 30 minutes. While it is marinating, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":30,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('611a5fc05b3783aa411a3143','611a5ea0c757b57058a8ae53',3,'m1- sear the marinated chicken','To make the Lemon Coriander Chicken, add 1 tablespoon of olive oil to a grill pan and spread over the pan using an oil brush. Heat the oil for a minute on medium flame. Then, place the marinated chicken fillets over the hot pan. Pour the leftover marinade over it and grill the fillets on high flame for 3 minutes. While the chicken fillets are roasting, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('611a6008c757b57058a8ae55','611a5ea0c757b57058a8ae53',4,'m2- cook the chicken on all sides','After grilling the chicken fillets for Lemon Coriander Chicken from one side, carefully flip it and continue to grill it for another 3 minutes on high flame. Brush the chicken fillets with the oil in the pan to keep it moist while cooking. After that, reduce the flame to medium and continue to flip and cook the chicken fillets from both sides for another 3-4 minutes, until it is cooked through. While the chicken is cooking, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('611a6037cffdac1d2c019852','611a5ea0c757b57058a8ae53',5,'m3- char the fillets & serve','Once the Lemon Coriander Chicken fillets are cooked through and are evenly browned on both sides, turn off the flame and take it out onto a plate and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('611a6320c757b57058a8ae5a','611a61f4cffdac1d2c019854',1,'p1- grate the cucumber','For Cucumber Raita, wash, peel and grate 3/4 cup of cucumber. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('611a63925b3783aa411a3145','611a61f4cffdac1d2c019854',2,'m1-Combine the ingredients to make raita. Garnish & serve','To make Cucumber Raita, in a large mixing bowl, add 3/4 cup of grated cucumber. Next, add 1 cup of curd followed by 1/4 teaspoon of red chili powder and half a teaspoon of cumin powder. Add half a teaspoon of salt along with 2 tablespoons of chopped coriander leaves and mix it well. Take it out into a serving bowl and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('611a6685cffdac1d2c019858','611a6604cffdac1d2c019856',1,'p1- pressure cook rice','Wash 1 cup Basmati rice with water. To cook the rice, put 1 cup washed rice into a pressure cooker, add 2 cups water and 1/2 teaspoon salt into this, and pressure cook on high flame till the first whistle. After the first whistle simmers and cook on low flame for the next 8 minutes and turn off the flame. Keep the cooker aside and let the pressure release naturally. While the rice is cooking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('611a66c75b3783aa411a3148','611a6604cffdac1d2c019856',2,'p2- prep the ingredients','Wash 10 nos curry leaves, Wash and slit 2 nos green chilies lengthwise, and finely chop 2 tablespoon coriander leaves. Keep this aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('611a66f9cffdac1d2c019859','611a6604cffdac1d2c019856',3,'p3- dry roast peanuts','In a pan, dry roast 1/4 cup peanuts and 7 nos cashews without adding any oil on medium-low flame for 2-3 minutes and set this aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":2,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('611a67b9cffdac1d2c01985b','611a6604cffdac1d2c019856',4,'m1- temper the oil and fry the cashew nuts','In a pan heat 2 tablespoon sesame oil, add 1/2 teaspoon mustard seeds, 1 teaspoon urad dal, 1 teaspoon chana dal into it, and let it sputter. Into this, add 2 nos slit green chilies, 3-4 nos dried red chilies, 10-12 nos curry leaves, 1/4 teaspoon hing, saute it  for 10 seconds. Next add dry roasted 1/4 cup peanuts, 7 nos cashew nuts along with 1/2 teaspoon turmeric and 1/4 teaspoon salt and give it a good mix.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('611a67edcffdac1d2c01985d','611a6604cffdac1d2c019856',5,'m2- garnish & serve','Now add cooked basmati rice and 2 tablespoons of lemon juice and gently combine everything together till the yellow color sets on the rice. Garnish the lemon rice with 2 tablespoons chopped coriander leaves and serve','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('611b57ee5b3783aa411a315a','611b57945b3783aa411a3159',1,'p1- prep the ingredients','Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup onion, 1/4 cup tomato, 1 teaspoon green chili, and 2 tablespoon fresh coriander leaves. In a bowl take 1.5 cups curd, whisk it until it is smooth and lump-free.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('611b583b5b3783aa411a315b','611b57945b3783aa411a3159',2,'m1- make the raita & serve','To make the raita, to the whisked curd, add 1/4 cup finely chopped onion, 1/4 cup finely chopped tomatoes, 2 nos chopped green chilies, and 2 tablespoon fresh coriander leaves. Now add 1/2 teaspoon cumin powder and 1/2 teaspoon salt into the curd and give it a good mix and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('611b644b5b3783aa411a315f','611b63becffdac1d2c01986e',1,'p1- prep the ingredients','For the Tomato Rice, wash and finely chop 1/2 cup onion,1 cup tomatoes,1 teaspoon garlic, and 2 tablespoons of fresh coriander leaves. Grate a 1-inch piece of ginger and slit 3 nos green chilies lengthwise. Wash 1 cup rice well with water and keep it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('611b652b5b3783aa411a3160','611b63becffdac1d2c01986e',2,'m1- cook the tomatoes','To make the Tomato Rice, heat 1 tablespoon ghee in a pan on medium flame. Into the hot ghee, add 1/2 teaspoon mustard seeds and 1/2 teaspoon cumin seeds, give it a quick saute and let them crackle for a few seconds. Then, add 3 nos cloves, 1-inch piece of cinnamon stick, 3 nos black peppercorns, and saute on medium flame. Next, add 1/2 cup finely chopped onion into this and saute it for 3-4 minutes on medium-high flame until it turns slightly golden. Next, add 1 teaspoon chopped garlic, 1-inch piece of grated ginger to the onions and saute them together for another 1 minute. Add 1 cup chopped tomatoes into this, give it a quick stir and add 3 nos slit green chilies to it. Saute and cook the tomatoes on medium-low flame for 4 minutes until they turn tender.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":2,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('611b66a95b3783aa411a3161','611b63becffdac1d2c01986e',3,'m2- add rice & simmer','After cooking the tomatoes, add 1/2 teaspoon turmeric powder,1/2 teaspoon red chili powder,1/2 teaspoon cumin powder and 1/2 teaspoon garam masala into the tomatoes. Then, mix and saute everything together on medium-low flame for 2 minutes. Next, add 1 cup washed rice along with 2 cups of water into this, give it a good stir and add 1 teaspoon salt. Stir well, cover the rice with a lid and cook on low flame for 12 minutes until rice absorbs all the water and is completely cooked. If cooking the rice in a pressure cooker, after adding water to rice, pressure cook it on high flame till the first whistle, after the first whistle, reduce to low flame and continue to cook for another 8 minutes. Then, turn off the heat and allow the pressure to release naturally. After cooking the rice remove the lid, give the rice a gentle stir and garnish with 2 tablespoons of chopped coriander leaves. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('611b715fcffdac1d2c019870','611b70c2c757b57058a8ae7d',1,'p1- prep the ingredients','To make Egg Burji, first, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onion, 1 tsp of garlic, and 1/2 tsp of ginger. Wash and finely chop 1 green chili, 1/4 cup of tomatoes, and 2 tbsp of coriander leaves. Whisk 4 eggs together in a bowl and season it with 1/2 tsp of salt and 1/2 tsp of black pepper. Squeeze 1 tbsp of lime juice.','prep_method','{"active_time":11,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('611b71f3c757b57058a8ae7e','611b70c2c757b57058a8ae7d',2,'m1- cook the masala','For Egg Burji, heat 1/2 tbsp of butter in a frying pan and then add 1/4 cup of onions, saute for 2-3 mins. Once the onions are translucent, add 1/2 tsp of ginger, 1 tsp of garlic, and 1 chopped green chili, mix well. Next, add 1/4 cup of tomatoes, cook for 1 min, and then add 1/2 tsp of coriander powder, 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder, 1 tsp of pav bhaji masala, 1/4 tsp of red chili powder, and 1/2 tsp of salt. Saute and cook the masala over low flame for 1-2 mins.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('611b7226c757b57058a8ae7f','611b70c2c757b57058a8ae7d',3,'m2- add the whisked eggs and cook','then reduce the heat to low and add the whisked eggs to the pan. Once the edges of the egg begin to cook, using a spatula push the eggs towards the center from the outside in gently mixing the eggs and masala together. Cook this for 4-5 mins or until desired, then garnish the dish with 2 tbsp of coriander leaves and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('611b7653cffdac1d2c019873','611b75decffdac1d2c019872',1,'p1- dice the vegetables','For ABC Juice, wash and roughly slice 1.5 cups of apples. Wash and roughly cut 3/4 cup of beetroot into quarters. Wash and roughly slice 3/4 cup of carrot. Wash and roughly chop 2 tablespoons of mint leaves. Wash and peel a half-inch piece of ginger. Wash and cut a lime into halves and squeeze 2 teaspoons of lime juice using a lemon squeezer.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('611b7693c757b57058a8ae81','611b75decffdac1d2c019872',2,'m1- make the juice & serve','To make the ABC juice, in a juicer add 1.5 cups of sliced apples, 3/4 cup of chopped beetroot, and 3/4 cup of sliced carrots. Next, add 2 tablespoons of mint leaves followed by a half-inch piece of ginger and blend it well to make the juice. Add 2 teaspoons of lime juice into the juice and mix it well. Pour the prepared juice into the glasses and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('611ba4565b3783aa411a3169','611ba4035b3783aa411a3168',1,'p1- pressure cook the dal','To cook the dal for Garlic Dal Tadka, wash 1 cup of toor dal well with water. Next, add the toor dal to a pressure cooker along with 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder and a teaspoon of salt. Add 2 cups of water and cover the cooker with a lid. Pressure cook the dal over high flame until one whistle. Then, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook it for another 8 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the dal is cooking please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('611ba4b75b3783aa411a316a','611ba4035b3783aa411a3168',2,'p2- prep the ingredients','For Garlic Dal Tadka, peel, wash and finely chop 1 teaspoon of garlic. Peel, wash, and finely slice 1 teaspoon of garlic. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves. Wash and cut a lime into halves. Then, squeeze 1 teaspoon of lime juice using a squeezer.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('611ba510cffdac1d2c019875','611ba4035b3783aa411a3168',3,'m1- prepare the tempering','To make Garlic Dal Tadka, after the pressure from the dal cooker is released, take off the lid and mash the dal well using a whisk. Next, heat a tablespoon of ghee in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Temper it with a teaspoon of cumin seeds and a 1/4 teaspoon of hing. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 1 teaspoon of chopped garlic followed by 1 no slit green chili and half a teaspoon of ginger paste. Mix it well and fry it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('611ba563c757b57058a8aeb7','611ba4035b3783aa411a3168',4,'m2- simmer the dal','After frying the garlic, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder along with half a teaspoon of kashmiri red chili powder and saute it over low flame for 1-2 minutes. Next, add the prepared toor dal and mix it well. Add some water, if required to adjust the consistency of dal. Then, allow it to simmer for 2 minutes. Keep stirring in between. After that, turn off the flame, and add 2 tablespoons of chopped coriander leaves. Add 1 teaspoon of lime juice and mix it well.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('611ba5bdc757b57058a8aeb8','611ba4035b3783aa411a3168',5,'m3- Add the tempering. Garnish & serve','To make the tempering for Garlic Dal Tadka, heat 1 tablespoon of ghee in a small tempering pan over medium flame for a minute. Add 1 teaspoon of finely sliced garlic followed by 1 nos dry red chili. Saute it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes, until garlic turns aromatic. Add a 1/4 teaspoon of Kashmiri red chili powder and mix it well. Turn off the flame and add the tempering to the prepared garlic dal. Mix it well and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('611ba7fb5b3783aa411a316c','611b6c27c757b57058a8ae7c',1,'p1- prep the ingredients','Wash, peel, and finely chop 1/2 cup onion. Peel and grate 1-inch piece ginger. Wash and finely chop 2 nos green chilies,1/4 cup carrot, and 2 tablespoon fresh coriander leaves. Peel and wash 1/4 cup green peas. Wash 10 nos curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('611ba83fcffdac1d2c019879','611b6c27c757b57058a8ae7c',2,'m1- roast the semolina','In a pan heat 1 teaspoon ghee on a medium flame for 1 minute, add 1 cup fine rava into the hot ghee, and roast the rava by constantly stirring it on medium-low flame for 4-5 minutes until it turns slightly brown in color. After roasting the rava for 4-5 minutes. Then, turn off the heat and take out the roasted rava on a plate.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('611ba8b4c757b57058a8aebd','611b6c27c757b57058a8ae7c',3,'m2- fry the onions','In a pan heat 1 tablespoon ghee on medium flame for 1 minute. Add 1 teaspoon mustard seeds,10 nos curry leaves,1 teaspoon urad daal,1 teaspoon chana daal,10 nos cashew nuts into the hot ghee and stir fry them together on medium flame for 2-3 minutes until cashews turn slightly golden. Into the fried cashews, Next add 1/2 cup chopped onion, 3 nos chopped green chilies and 1-inch piece grated ginger and saute everything together on high flame for another 2-3 minutes until onion turns slightly golden. Meanwhile, put 2.5 cup water in a deep bottom pan and allow it to boil on high flame for 3 minutes. While the water is boiling, keep frying the onions by stirring in between. After boiling the water for 3 minutes, turn off the flame and keep it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":2,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('611ba8f95b3783aa411a316d','611b6c27c757b57058a8ae7c',4,'m3- simmer the upma & serve','After stir-frying the onions for 2-3 minutes, add 1/4 cup chopped carrot and 1/4 cup green peas into it and give it a quick toss. Next, add 2.5 cups hot water into this along with 1 teaspoon salt and 1 teaspoon sugar. Give it a good stir and bring it to a boil. Once it has come to a boil, add 1 cup roasted rava into it and continue to stir on medium-low flame for 1-2 minutes. Then cover it with a lid and cook on low flame for 3-4 minutes. After cooking the upma for 3-4 minutes, take off the lid, add 1 tablespoon lemon juice into it and give it a gentle mix. Turn off the heat and let it rest for another 3-4 minutes. Garnish the upma with 2 tablespoon fresh coriander leaves and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('611ca490c757b57058a8aeee','611ca43fc757b57058a8aeed',1,'p1- prep the ingredients','For Tomato Onion Chutney,  wash and roughly chop 1/2 a cup of tomatoes. Peel, wash, and roughly chop 1/2 a cup of onions. Wash, peel, and roughly chop 1 teaspoon of garlic. Wash 8 nos curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('611ca4dbc757b57058a8aeef','611ca43fc757b57058a8aeed',2,'m1- fry the onions & garlic','To make the Tomato Onion Chutney, first, heat  2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a pan on a medium flame for a minute. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of hing and 2 nos dry red chilies followed by a teaspoon of chopped garlic. Saute and fry the garlic on a medium flame for a minute. Next, add 1/2 a cup of chopped onions and stir-fry it on medium-high flame for 3-4 minutes, until it turns slightly translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('611ca518cffdac1d2c01988e','611ca43fc757b57058a8aeed',3,'m2- cook the tomatoes','After frying the onions, add 1/2 a cup of chopped tomatoes along with 1/2 a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Stir and cook the tomatoes on medium flame for 5-6 minutes, until it turns tender. After that, turn off the flame and allow the mixture to cool completely. While the mixture is cooling down, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('611ca575cffdac1d2c01988f','611ca43fc757b57058a8aeed',4,'m3- puree the mixture and prepare the chutney','To make the Tomato Onion Chutney, after the prepared tomato-onion mixture cools down, carefully transfer it to a blender jar and blend it well to a smooth chutney. Take out the prepared chutney into a bowl and set it aside. Next, to make the tempering, heat a teaspoon of cooking oil in small fry pan. Add 1/4 teaspoon of mustard seeds and 1/4 teaspoon of urad dal followed by 8 nos curry leaves. Saute and let it temper for a few seconds. Then, turn off the flame and add this tempering over the prepared chutney. Mix it well and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('611ca7f3c757b57058a8aef2','611ca7633a4d5fc6fdfa16fe',1,'ap1- soak the lentils','For Mallige Idli, add 1/4 cup of urad dal in a bowl along with 1/4 cup of poha, and soak it in 2 cups of water for 4 hours. Next, in a separate bowl, add 1/4 cup of sona masuri rice and soak it in 2 cups of water for 4 hours. While the dal and rice are soaking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":240,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('611ca83fc757b57058a8aef3','611ca7633a4d5fc6fdfa16fe',2,'ap2- blend the soaked lentils & let the batter ferment','To prepare the batter for Mallige Idli. add the soaked urad dal and poha to a blender jar and blend it well into a smooth batter. Then, transfer it into a large mixing bowl. Next, add the soaked rice to the blender jar and blend it into a slightly coarse batter. Then, add the rice batter to the prepared urad dal batter and mix it well. Cover it with a lid and allow it to ferment for 10 hours. While the batter is fermenting, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":600,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('611ca8863a4d5fc6fdfa16ff','611ca7633a4d5fc6fdfa16fe',3,'p1- prepare the idly batter & grease the idli plate','For Mallige Idli, after fermenting the prepared idli batter, add half a teaspoon of salt and gently mix it and set it aside. Next, grease an idli plate with 2 teaspoons of cooking oil using an oil brush. Greasing will prevent the idli from sticking to the base of the idli plate, and idlis will come off easily.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('611ca8d5c757b57058a8aef4','611ca7633a4d5fc6fdfa16fe',4,'m1- steam the idly and serve','To make the Mallige Idli, pour the prepared idli batter into the cavities of the greased idli plate. Next, carefully place it inside the steamer and cover it with a lid. Allow the idlis to steam for 12 minutes. After steaming the idlis, remove the lid of the steamer and carefully take out the idli plate. Gently, take out the idlis from the plate and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":12,"flame":3}'),
('611cac31c757b57058a8aef8','611cabfe3a4d5fc6fdfa1704',1,'p1- marinate the chicken','To marinate the chicken for Chicken Chettinad, wash 500 grams of chicken well with water. Next, put the washed chicken in a large mixing bowl. Add 1/2 teaspoon of salt, 1 teaspoon of red chili powder, and 1/2 teaspoon of turmeric powder. Next, add 1 tablespoon of ginger-garlic paste along with 2 teaspoons of lime juice and mix it well. Set it aside and allow it to marinate for 20 minutes. Marination tenderizes the chicken while allowing it to absorb the flavors from the spices, hence making it more succulent and flavourful. While the chicken is marinating, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('611cac59cffdac1d2c019891','611cabfe3a4d5fc6fdfa1704',2,'p2- prep the ingredients','For Chicken Chettinad, wash and finely chop 1/2 cup of tomatoes. Wash, peel, and finely chop 1/2 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves. Wash 5 nos curry leaves. Grate 1/2 cup of coconut using a grater. Wash and slice 1 nos lemon and remove the seeds. Then, cut it into wedges. Squeeze 2 teaspoons of lime juice.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('611cac95cffdac1d2c019892','611cabfe3a4d5fc6fdfa1704',3,'p3- dry roast the spices for coconut paste','To make the coconut paste for Chicken Chettinad, heat a pan on low flame for a minute. Add 3 nos dry red chilies, 3 nos green cardamoms, 1 nos star anise, 1/2 teaspoon of black peppercorns, and a 1-inch piece of cinnamon stick. Next, add 1/2 teaspoon of coriander seeds, 3 nos cloves, 1/2 teaspoon of fennel seeds, and 1 teaspoon of poppy seeds. Saute and dry roast the spices without adding any oil, on low flame for 2-3 minutes until it turns aromatic. Keep stirring the spices continuously while roasting, to prevent it from getting burnt.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('611cacc5c757b57058a8aef9','611cabfe3a4d5fc6fdfa1704',4,'p4- prepare the coconut paste','As the spices turn aromatic, add 1/2 cup of grated coconut and saute it on low flame for a minute. Then, turn off the flame and allow it to cool down for some time. Next, add the roasted spices to a blender jar along with 2 tablespoons of water and blend it to a coarse paste. Take it out in a bowl and set it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('611cacf6cffdac1d2c019893','611cabfe3a4d5fc6fdfa1704',5,'m1- fry the onions','To make the Chicken Chettinad, heat 2 tablespoons of ghee in a deep bottom pan on medium flame for a minute. Add 1/2 cup of chopped onions and fry it on medium flame for 2-3 minutes, till it turns slightly translucent. Add 5 nos curry leaves and saute it for a minute.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('611cad3ec757b57058a8aefa','611cabfe3a4d5fc6fdfa1704',6,'m2- sear the marinated chicken and simmer','Next, add the marinated chicken and mix it well. Saute and cook the chicken on medium flame for 10-12 minutes. Keep stirring the chicken while cooking it, to prevent it from sticking to the bottom of the pan. After frying the chicken, add 1/2 cup of chopped tomatoes and mix it well. Cover it with a lid and simmer it for 4-5 minutes. While the chicken is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":14,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('611cad6a3a4d5fc6fdfa1705','611cabfe3a4d5fc6fdfa1704',7,'m3- add the coconut paste & simmer the curry','After simmering the chicken for Chicken Chettinad, take off the lid and add the prepared coconut paste. Mix it well and fry the chicken on medium-high flame for 2-3 minutes. Next, add 3/4 cup of water and mix it well. Cover it with a lid and cook it on low flame for 20-25 minutes. While the chicken is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":25,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('611cad953a4d5fc6fdfa1706','611cabfe3a4d5fc6fdfa1704',8,'m4- garnish & serve','After simmering the chicken for Chicken Chettinad, take off the lid and give it a stir. Turn off the flame and take it out in a serving bowl. Garnish it with 2 tablespoons of chopped coriander leaves and lime wedges. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('611cb3733a4d5fc6fdfa170e','611cb31f3a4d5fc6fdfa170d',1,'p1- clean the chicken & prep other ingredients','To make Pepper Chicken Gravy, first, clean 400 g of chicken and then peel and finely chop 1 cup of onions. Wash 8 curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('611cb3dccffdac1d2c019896','611cb31f3a4d5fc6fdfa170d',2,'m1- fry the onions','For Pepper Chicken Gravy, heat 1 tbsp of sesame oil in a pan, then add 1 cup of chopped onions, and saute them for 3 mins. Once the onions are translucent, add 1/2 tsp of ginger-garlic paste and fry it with the onions for another minute.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('611cb44a3a4d5fc6fdfa170f','611cb31f3a4d5fc6fdfa170d',3,'m2- add the spices & simmer the curry','Next, add 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder, 1 tsp of red chili powder, 1/2 tsp of coriander powder, and 1/2 tsp of cumin powder and mix well. Saute and cook the masala over low flame for 1-2 minutes. Next, add 400 g of chicken, 1/2 tsp of salt, and 2 tsp of black pepper powder and gently mix all the ingredients together. Stir and fry the chicken over medium flame for 4-5 minutes. Then, add 3/4 cup of water, cover the pan with a lid, and cook for 12-15 mins. While the chicken simmers, please move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('611cb4813a4d5fc6fdfa1710','611cb31f3a4d5fc6fdfa170d',4,'m3- garnish & serve','After this, add 8 curry leaves and 1 tsp of black pepper, gently mix, and fry the chicken with the masala for another 2-3 minutes. Then turn off the flame. This dish is ready to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('611cb7b13a4d5fc6fdfa1712','611cb782c757b57058a8aeff',1,'p1- roast the peanuts','To roast the peanuts for Peanut Chutney, add half a cup of peanuts to a pan and dry roast it over medium flame for 3-4 minutes. Keep stirring it continuously while roasting it, as it may get burnt easily when exposed to heat for long. Roast the peanuts until the skin starts to come off and it turns crisp and slightly golden. After roasting the peanuts, turn off the flame and remove the skin. Then, set it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('611cb7e33a4d5fc6fdfa1713','611cb782c757b57058a8aeff',2,'p2- prep the ingredients','For Peanut Chutney, peel and wash 1 clove of garlic. Wash and roughly chop 1 nos green chili.  Wash 6 nos curry leaves well with water.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('611cb817cffdac1d2c01989a','611cb782c757b57058a8aeff',3,'m1- blend the chutney','To make the Peanut Chutney, first, add half a cup of roasted peanuts to a blender jar. Next, heat a teaspoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Temper it with half a teaspoon of urad dal and half a teaspoon of chana dal. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 1 nos chopped green chili followed by a clove of garlic and saute it over low flame for 2-3 minutes until garlic turns slightly golden. Then, turn off the flame and transfer it to the blender jar. Add 1 teaspoon of tamarind followed by a teaspoon of salt and 1/4 cup of water. Blend it well into a smooth chutney. Then, take it out into a bowl.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('611cb846cffdac1d2c01989b','611cb782c757b57058a8aeff',4,'m2- add the tempering & serve','To make the tempering for Peanut Chutney, heat a teaspoon of cooking oil in a small tempering pan over medium flame for a minute. Add half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, followed by half a teaspoon of urad dal and 1/4 teaspoon of hing. Add 1 nos dry red chili along with 6 nos curry leaves. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds, Then, turn off the flame and add this tempering instantly over the prepared peanut chutney. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('611cbca7c757b57058a8af02','611cbc6ccffdac1d2c01989f',1,'ap1- soak the lentil','For Moong Dal Dosa, in a large mixing bowl, add 1/2 cup of moong dal and 2 teaspoons of chana dal and soak it in 3 cups of water for 10 hours.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":600,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('611cbd223a4d5fc6fdfa1715','611cbc6ccffdac1d2c01989f',2,'p1- blend the soaked lentils','For the Moong Dal Dosa, wash, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1 nos green chili. Wash, peel, and finely chop 1/4 inch piece of ginger. Next, drain the water from the soaked moong dal and chana dal, transfer it to a blender jar and blend it well into a smooth batter. If required add a little amount of water.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('611cbd5d3a4d5fc6fdfa1716','611cbc6ccffdac1d2c01989f',3,'m1- prepare the batter','To make the batter for the Moong Dal Dosa, transfer the prepared moong dal batter to a large mixing bowl. Add 1 teaspoon of rice flour along with 1/4 teaspoon of salt and 2-3 tablespoons of water and mix it well to avoid any lumps. Make sure to keep the consistency of the batter slightly thick.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('611cbd93c757b57058a8af03','611cbc6ccffdac1d2c01989f',4,'m2- make the dosa & serve','To make Moong Dal Dosa, heat a tawa on medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Then, pour a ladleful of the prepared dosa batter on the hot tawa and spread it into a 9 inch thin circle as shown. Next, sprinkle some cumin seeds, chopped onions and chopped green chili over the dosa. Drizzle 1 teaspoon of oil over it and press it gently with a spatula. Cook the dosa on medium-high flame for 1-2 minutes. Then, mark a triangle over the dosa using the spatula. Carefully scrape the sides and fold the dosa, making a triangle, as shown. Take it out on a plate and serve. Similarly, make the rest of the dosas from the batter.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('611dff26cffdac1d2c0198af','611dfef43a4d5fc6fdfa177d',1,'p1- pressure cook the dal','For Udupi Sambar, soak 1/4 teaspoon of tamarind in 1/4 cup of water for 15 minutes. To cook the dal, wash 1/2 cup of toor dal well with water. Transfer the washed toor dal in a pressure cooker with 1 cup of water and cover it with a lid. Pressure cook it on high flame till one whistle. After the first whistle, reduce it to low flame and continue to cook the dal for another 8 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('611e04253a4d5fc6fdfa177e','611dfef43a4d5fc6fdfa177d',2,'p2- prep the ingredients','For Udupi Sambar, wash, peel and cube 1/4 cup of potatoes. Wash, peel and cut 1/4 cup of onions into petals. Grate 1/4 cup of fresh coconut using a grater. Wash 10 nos curry leaves. Next, after soaking the tamarind, mash it well with water and strain it using a strainer to remove any extra residue from it. Squeeze the pulp to extract more flavor.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('611e0495c757b57058a8af32','611dfef43a4d5fc6fdfa177d',3,'p3- prepare the coconut paste','To make the coconut paste for Udupi Sambar, heat 1 teaspoon of cooking oil in a pan on medium flame for a minute. Then, add 1 teaspoon of coriander seeds, 1/4 teaspoon of cumin seeds, 1/2 teaspoon of urad dal, 1/4 teaspoon of fenugreek seeds, and 2 nos dry red chilies and saute it on medium-low flame for 1-2 minutes, till it turns aromatic. Then, turn off the flame and transfer the roasted spices to a blender jar along with 1/4 cup of fresh coconut and 2 tablespoons of water. Blend it well to a smooth paste.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('611e04c9cffdac1d2c0198b0','611dfef43a4d5fc6fdfa177d',4,'m1- simmer the potatoes','To make the Udupi Sambar, in a deep bottom pan, add 1/4 cup of cubed potatoes and 1/4 cup of onion petals along with 1 cup of water. Cover it with a lid and simmer it for 15 minutes, till the potatoes are completely cooked. While the potatoes are simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('611e051ecffdac1d2c0198b1','611dfef43a4d5fc6fdfa177d',5,'m2- add coconut paste & simmer the sambar','After simmering the potatoes, take off the lid and add 1/4 cup of the prepared tamarind water. Next, add 5 nos curry leaves, 1/2 teaspoon of jaggery, 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, and 1/2 teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Let it boil on medium-high flame for 5 minutes. Then, add the cooked toor dal along with the prepared coconut paste and mix it well. Simmer it for another 5 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('611e0576cffdac1d2c0198b5','611dfef43a4d5fc6fdfa177d',6,'m3- add the tempering & serve','To make the tempering for Udupi Sambar, heat 1 teaspoon of cooking oil in a tadka pan on medium flame for a minute. Add 1/4 teaspoon of mustard seeds, 1/4 teaspoon of urad dal, 1 nos dry red chili, and 5 nos curry leaves to it. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Then turn off the flame and pour this tempering instantly over the prepared Udupi Sambar and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('611e0aa7cffdac1d2c0198b9','611e08dacffdac1d2c0198b8',1,'p1- boil the noodles','For Veg Hakka Noodles, first, boil 3 cups of water in a pot, once the water is boiling reduce the flame to low and then add 200 grams of rice noodles. Cook them for 8-12 mins and drain the water once noodles have cooked completely. Set them aside and move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":12,"flame":3}'),('611e0ba13a4d5fc6fdfa1783','611e08dacffdac1d2c0198b8',2,'p2- prep the ingredients','Next, peel and finely chop 1 tsp of garlic. peel and finely chop 1 inch of ginger. Wash and roughly chop 1/4 cup of spring onions. Peel and finely slice 1/4 cup of carrots. wash and finely slice 1/4 cup of cabbage. wash and finely slice 1/4 cup of green capsicum. Crush 1/2 tsp of black pepper powder in a mortar and pestle.','prep_method','{"active_time":11,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('611e0c36c757b57058a8af35','611e08dacffdac1d2c0198b8',3,'m1- toss the noodles in vegetables & serve','For Veg Hakka Noodles, in a pan heat 2 tsp of oil and then add 1 tsp of chopped garlic and 1 inch of chopped ginger and saute for 1 min. Next add 1/4 cup of chopped onions, 1/4 cup of chopped spring onions, 1/4 cup of chopped cabbage, 1/4 cup of chopped capsicum and saute on high flame for 2-3 mins. Next, add 1/4 tsp of salt, 1 tbsp of soy sauce, 1 tbsp of vinegar, 1 tbsp of chilli sauce, and mix well. Then, add 200 grams of cooked rice noodles, 1/2 tsp of crushed black peppercorns, 1/4 cup of bean shoots, and gently mix all the ingredients together. Once everything is combined well, put it in a serving dish and enjoy.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('611e135e3a4d5fc6fdfa1785','611e12f8cffdac1d2c0198bb',1,'p1- mash the bananas','For Banana Pancakes, Peel 2 nos ripe bananas and keep them in a bowl. Mash the bananas well using a fork. Add 1 teaspoon of vanilla essence and 1/2 cup of milk into the mashed bananas. Next, add 1 teaspoon of vinegar into it and mix them well','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('611e13d2c757b57058a8af38','611e12f8cffdac1d2c0198bb',2,'p2- prepare the batter','To make the pancake batter, place a sieve over an empty bowl, add 1 cup of all-purpose flour, 1/2 cup of powdered sugar, 1 teaspoon of baking powder, 1/4 teaspoon of baking soda, 1/2 teaspoon of cinnamon powder, and 1/4 teaspoon of salt into the sieve and sieve all the dry ingredients together to avoid any clusters. Pour the banana milk mixture into this and combine them well using a hand blender. Whisk it well to lump-free and smooth consistency.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('611e14003a4d5fc6fdfa1786','611e12f8cffdac1d2c0198bb',3,'m1- make the pancakes & serve','To make Banana Pancakes, heat 1 teaspoon of butter on a nonstick tawa on medium flame for 30 seconds. Pour 1/2 cup of the batter onto the tawa and cook it on medium flame for 1-2 minutes till small bubbles start to appear on the surface of the pancake. Then flip the pancake and cook the other side on medium flame for 1-2 minutes. After cooking both sides of the pancake evenly, take it out and serve. Make the rest of the pancakes similarly.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('611e1674c757b57058a8af3b','611e1616c757b57058a8af3a',1,'p1- grate carrot & prep other ingredients','For Carrot Raita, wash, peel and grate half a cup of carrot. Wash and finely chop 1 nos green chili. Wash and slit 1 nos green chili. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash 8 nos curry leaves. Next, add 1 cup of curd in a bowl and whisk it well until smooth.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('611e1c26c757b57058a8af3c','611e1616c757b57058a8af3a',2,'m1- combine the chopped ingredients & prepare the raita','To make the Carrot Raita, add 1 cup of whisked curd to a large mixing bowl. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of chat masala, 1 nos chopped green chili, 1/4 teaspoon of black salt and 1/4 teaspoon of sugar. Add 1/4 teaspoon of salt and mix it well using a whisk. Next, add half a cup of grated carrot along with 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and mix it well.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('611e1c70cffdac1d2c0198bc','611e1616c757b57058a8af3a',3,'m2- add the tempering & serve','To make the tempering for Carrot Raita, heat1 teaspoon of cooking oil in a small pan over medium flame for a minute. Add 1/4 teaspoon of mustard seeds, 1/4 teaspoons of cumin seeds, 8 nos curry leaves, and 1 nos slit green chili. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Then turn off the flame and pour this tempering instantly over the prepared raita. Mix it well and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('611e1f56c757b57058a8af3d','611e1e943a4d5fc6fdfa1789',1,'p1- slice the cucumber','To make Cucumber Salad, first, wash and slice 1 cucumber. Wash and roughly chop 1 tbsp of coriander leaves. Crush 2 tsp of coriander seeds with a mortar and pestle. In a mixing bowl combine 1.5 tbsp of rice vinegar, 1 tbsp of olive oil, 1/4 tsp of chili flakes, 1/4 tsp of salt, 1/4 tsp of sugar, 2 tsp of crushed coriander seeds, with a whisk.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('611e1f7dcffdac1d2c0198bf','611e1e943a4d5fc6fdfa1789',2,'m1- prepare the salad & serve','For cucumber salad, in a large bowl add 1 chopped cucumber, 1 tbsp of coriander leaves, 2 tsp of crushed coriander seeds, and mix all the ingredients well. Once this is combined, the salad is ready to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('611e22503a4d5fc6fdfa178b','611e21d8cffdac1d2c0198c1',1,'p1- rinse & simmer the dal','To make Moong Masoor Dal, wash 1/4 cup of moong dal and 3/4 cup of pink masoor dal. Wash and chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. In a pan, add 1 cup of the washed moong and masoor dal along with 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes, 1/4 tsp of salt, and 1.5 cups of water. Let this cook for 15 mins on medium heat. While the dal is boiling, wash and slit 1 green chili. Wash and roughly chop 1 tbsp of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('611e22bbc757b57058a8af3f','611e21d8cffdac1d2c0198c1',2,'m1- add the tempering to the dal & serve','For Moong Masoor Dal, in a tempering pan heat 2 tsp of oil and then add 1 broken dry red chili, 1 bay leaf, 1 slit green chili, 1/2 tsp of panch phoran, 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder, and let this splutter for a few seconds. Once this is done pour it into the dal and then add 1/4 tsp of sugar. Cover the pan with a lid and let the dal cook for 2 mins on medium flame. Next, add 1 tbsp of chopped coriander and give the dal a quick stir. Pour the dal into a serving dish and enjoy.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('611f5a74c757b57058a8af41','611f59da3a4d5fc6fdfa178d',1,'p1- add gram flour & spices to a mixing bowl','To knead the dough for Besan Phulka, in a large mixing bowl, add 1 cup of whole wheat flour followed by half a cup of gram flour. Next, add half a teaspoon of turmeric powder, half a teaspoon of red chili powder, 1 teaspoon of coriander powder, and half a teaspoon of cumin powder along with half a teaspoon of dry mango powder.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('611f5aa63a4d5fc6fdfa178e','611f59da3a4d5fc6fdfa178d',2,'p2- knead the dough','Next, add 2 nos chopped green chilies followed by half a teaspoon of salt. Gradually, add about half a cup of water and knead it well into a smooth dough. Add a teaspoon of cooking oil and knead it again for a minute. Then, cover the dough with a damp cloth and allow it to rest for 20 minutes. While the dough is resting, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('611f5aeac757b57058a8af42','611f59da3a4d5fc6fdfa178d',3,'m1- divide the dough and prepare the phulkas','To make the Besan Phulka, divide the prepared dough into small equal-sized balls. Then, take a dough ball and dust some four over it. Then, roll it into a thin 7-inch circle. Make sure to roll out the edges thin. Then, place the rolled-out roti over a hot tawa and cook it over medium flame for 1-2 until both sides are evenly browned. Add half a teaspoon of ghee to each side and cook it until it turns slightly golden. Then, take it out onto a plate and serve. Make the rest of the phulkas similarly.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('611f5fbfcffdac1d2c0198c5','611f5f463a4d5fc6fdfa1791',1,'P1: Soak the soya chunks & prep the ingredients','To make Soya Chunk Pulao, first, soak 3/4 cups of soya chunks in 1.5 cups of hot water for 15 mins. While the soya chunks are soaking, peel and finely chop 1/2 cup of onions, wash and finely chop 2 green chilies, wash and finely chop 1/2 cup of tomatoes, and wash and roughly chop 1 tbsp of mint leaves and 1 tbsp of coriander leaves. Whisk 1/4 cup of fresh curd, ensuring to remove all lumps.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('611f61a03a4d5fc6fdfa1792','611f5f463a4d5fc6fdfa1791',2,'P2: Marinate the soya chunks','Next, squeeze out the water from the soaking soya chunks, place them in a large mixing bowl, and let them cool down slightly. Then, add 1/4 cup of whisked curd, 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder, 1 tsp of red chili powder, 1/2 tsp of salt, and mix well. Let the soya chunks marinate for 20mins. Next, wash 1 cup of basmati rice and then soak it in 2 cups of water for 20 mins. While the rice and soya chunks are soaking please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('611f622ecffdac1d2c0198c6','611f5f463a4d5fc6fdfa1791',3,'M1: Cook the masala','For Soya Chunks Pulao, in a pressure cooker heat 1.5 tbsp of ghee on medium flame. Next, add 1/2 inch piece of cinnamon, 3 cloves, 1 green cardamom, 1 bay leaf, 1/2 tsp of cumin seeds, and let them splitter for a few seconds. Then, add 1/2 cup of chopped onions and saute this for 2-3 mins. Next, add 2 chopped green chilies,1 tsp of ginger-garlic paste, and mix well. Then, add 1/2 cup of chopped tomatoes and saute for 3-4 mins.','cook_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('611f6281c757b57058a8af45','611f5f463a4d5fc6fdfa1791',4,'M2: Pressure cook the pulao','Next, add 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder, 1 tsp of red chili powder, 1/2 tsp of garam masala, and saute for 1 min. Then, add 3/4 cup of marinated soya chunks, mix well, and cook for 5 mins. After this, add 1 tbsp of mint leaves, 1 tbsp of coriander leaves, 1/2 tsp of salt, and mix well. Next, add 1 cup of soaked basmati rice, and gently mix all the ingredients together. To this, add 2 cups of water, clove the pressure cookers, and let the pulao cook on high flame for 1 whistle and then on low flame for 8 mins. Once this is done, allow the pressure to release naturally before you open the cooker. Next, put the rice in a serving dish and enjoy.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('611f6795c757b57058a8af47','611f66c7cffdac1d2c0198ca',1,'P1: Pressure cook the dal & soak the tamarind','Soak 2 tsp tamarind in 3/4 cup of warm water for 15 mins. Cook toor dal in a pressure cooker with 1.5 cups of water on high flame for 1 whistle and then on low flame for 8 mins. Once this is done set the cooker aside to cool before you take the lid off.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('611f681fc757b57058a8af48','611f66c7cffdac1d2c0198ca',2,'P2: Chop & prep the ingredients','Peel and half shallots, chop tomatoes, slit green chili, peel garlic, and wash curry leaves. Mash and mix the tamarind and water, remove the pulp, and set the tamarind extract aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('611f68cb3a4d5fc6fdfa1796','611f66c7cffdac1d2c0198ca',3,'P3: Make sambhar powder','Heat coconut oil in a pan, saute fenugreek seeds for a few seconds and then add coriander seeds, cumin seeds, urad dal, and chana dal, saute together for 2-3 mins, stirring continuously. Next, add dry red chili and curry leaves and saute for 1-2 mins. Let this spice mixture cool completely before transferring it to a blending jar. Turn it into a coarse powder. (If you wish you can also purchase a ready-made sambar powder and skip this step.)','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":4,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('611f692fcffdac1d2c0198cb','611f66c7cffdac1d2c0198ca',4,'M1: Fry the shallots with garlic & green chili','Heat cooking oil in a pan, then add shallots, garlic, and green chili, saute this for 2-3 mins on high flame. Once translucent, add turmeric powder and salt, saute this for 1 min on medium-high flame.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('611f69613a4d5fc6fdfa1797','611f66c7cffdac1d2c0198ca',5,'M2: Simmer the tomatoes','Next, add tomatoes, saute for 1-2 mins on medium flame, pour in the tamarind extract and 1 cup of water, cover it and simmer for 10 mins.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('611f6994c757b57058a8af49','611f66c7cffdac1d2c0198ca',6,'M3: Add the cooked dal & simmer the sambar','After 10 mins, add the cooked toor dal and mix it well. Boil on high flame for 2 mins stirring occasionally. Next, add sambar powder, jaggery, and stir well. Simmer for 1-2 mins.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('611f6a00cffdac1d2c0198cc','611f66c7cffdac1d2c0198ca',7,'M4: Prepare & add the tempering to sambar. Garnish & serve','To make the tempering for the Onion Sambar, heat 1 teaspoon of cooking oil in a tadka pan on medium flame for a minute. Add 1/2 teaspoon of mustard seeds, 1/4 teaspoon of fenugreek seeds and 1/4 teaspoon of hing. Next, add 2 nos dry red chilies into it and let it splutter for a few seconds, then turn off the flame and add this tempering instantly over the onion sambar. Add 2 tablespoons of chopped coriander leaves and give it a final stir. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('611f6df03a4d5fc6fdfa179f','611f6da73a4d5fc6fdfa179e',1,'AP1: Soak the lentil','To make Green moong dal, first, wash and soak 3/4 cup of green moong dal for 8 hour.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":480,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('611f6e703a4d5fc6fdfa17a0','611f6da73a4d5fc6fdfa179e',2,'P1: Chop & prep the ingredients','Next, peel and chop 1/4 cup of onions, wash and peel 1/4 cup of tomatoes, peel and finely chop 1 tsp of garlic, peel and finely chop 1 inch of ginger, wash and chop 1 green chili, and wash and roughly chop 1 tbsp of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('611f6eb4cffdac1d2c0198d3','611f6da73a4d5fc6fdfa179e',3,'M1: Pressure cook the dal','For green moong dal, in a pressure cooker add 3/4 cup of soaked moon dal, 1.5 cups of water, 1/4 tsp of salt, and 1/4 tsp turmeric powder. Cook this on high flame for 1 min and then on low flame for 5 mins. Once this is done, allow the cooker to release pressure naturally before you open the lid. While the dal is cooking please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('611f6f29cffdac1d2c0198d4','611f6da73a4d5fc6fdfa179e',4,'M2: Cook the masala & add it to the dal. Garnish & serve','Next, in a pan heat 1 tbsp of cooking oil for 1 min. Then add 1/4 tsp of hing, 1 tsp cumin seeds, 1 tsp of chopped garlic, 1 inch chopped ginger, and saute for 1 min. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions and saute for 2-3 mins. Once the onions are translucent, 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes, 1/4 tsp of red chili powder, 1 chopped green chili, 1/2 tsp coriander powder, 1/4 tsp turmeric powder, and saute for 2-3 mins. Once the tomatoes are soft pour the cooked vegetables into the pressure cooker with the dal and give it a stir. Next, add 1 tbsp of coriander leaves, pour the dal into a serving dish, and enjoy.','cook_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('611f76413a4d5fc6fdfa17a2','611f75e3cffdac1d2c0198d8',1,'p1- rinse the rice','For Brown Rice, in a bowl, add 1 cup of brown rice and rinse it well with water.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('611f768acffdac1d2c0198d9','611f75e3cffdac1d2c0198d8',2,'m1- pressure cook the rice & serve','To make the Brown Rice, add 1 cup of rinsed brown rice to a pressure cooker along with 2 cups of water. Add 1/4 teaspoon of salt and cover it with a lid. Pressure cook the rice on high flame until 2 whistles. Then, reduce it to low flame and continue to cook it for another 8 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. After the pressure from the cooker has been released, take off the lid and mix it gently. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('611f7a6e3a4d5fc6fdfa17a5','611f7a2fcffdac1d2c0198db',1,'P1: Pressure cook the dal','To make Masoor Palak Dal, start by washing 1 cup of pink masoor dal. Next, cook the dal in a pressure cooker with 2 cups of water. Cook the dal on high flame for 1 whistle and then on low flame for 8 mins. Once this is done, let the cooker release pressure naturally before you take off the lid. While the dal is cooking please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('611f7aebcffdac1d2c0198dc','611f7a2fcffdac1d2c0198db',2,'P2: Prep the ingredients','Next, wash and roughly chop 1.5 cups of spinach leaves. Peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1 green chilli. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomato. Peel and finely chop 1-inch piece of ginger. Wash and roughly chop 1 tbsp of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('611f7b513a4d5fc6fdfa17a6','611f7a2fcffdac1d2c0198db',3,'M1: Cook the masala','For Masoor Palak Dal, in a kadai heat 1 tbsp of ghee for 1 min. Next, add 1/2 tsp of cumin seeds, 1/4 tsp of hing and let this splutter for a few seconds. To this add 1/4 cup of chopped onions, 1 chopped green chili, 1 inch of chopped ginger, and saute this for 2-3 mins on high flame. Once the onions are translucent, add 1/2 tsp of red chili powder, 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder, 1 tsp of coriander powder, and mix well.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('611f7b80c757b57058a8af51','611f7a2fcffdac1d2c0198db',4,'M2: Simmer the dal with spinach & masala','Next, add 1 cup of cooked masoor dal, mix well, and then add 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes and 1/2 tsp of salt.  Bring the dal to a boil and then add 1.5 cups of spinach leaves.  Cook the dal for another 2 mins on high flame. Once this is done, turn off the flame, pour the dal into a serving bowl, and enjoy.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61234af63ca3bf7c22a8d8ba','61234ab53ca3bf7c22a8d8b9',1,'p1- pressure cook the dalia','To prepare Dalia Salad, cook 1/2 cup of dalia in a pressure cooker with 1 cup of water. Cook the dalia on a medium flame for 2 whistles, once this is done let the pressure release naturally before you open the pressure cooker. While the dalia is cooking please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61234b593ca3bf7c22a8d8bb','61234ab53ca3bf7c22a8d8b9',2,'p2- prep the ingredients','next, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of green capsicum, 1/4 cup of tomatoes, and 1/4 cup of cucumber. Peel and finely dice 1/4 cup of carrot. Dice 1/4 cup of paneer. Squeeze 1 tbsp of lime juice.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('61234b8c3a4d5fc6fdfa17d7','61234ab53ca3bf7c22a8d8b9',3,'m1- simmer the dalia with vegetables','For dalia salad, in a pan heat 1 tsp of olive oil on medium flame. To this, add 1/2 tsp of cumin seeds and let them splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped capsicum, 1/4 cup of chopped carrot, 1/4 cup of black gram sprouts, 1/4 cup of paneer, and saute for 1 min. Then, add 1/4 tsp of black pepper powder, 1/2 tsp of salt, 1/4 tsp of mixed herbs, and mix well. Next, add 1/2 cup of cooked dalia and cover the pan and let everything cook for 2-3 mins.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('61234bce3ca3bf7c22a8d8bc','61234ab53ca3bf7c22a8d8b9',4,'m2- prepare the salad & serve','Next, in a large mixing bowl combine 1/4 cup of chopped cucumber, 1/4 cup of chopped tomato, 1/4 tsp of chili flakes, 1 tbsp of lemon juice, and mix it well. To this, add the cooked vegetables and dalia and mix all ingredients well. Transfer the salad to a serving bowl and enjoy.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6123547a3ca3bf7c22a8d8bf','61235361003d0c069277c36c',1,'P1: Prepare & rest the idli batter','To make ragi idli, start by dry roasting 1/2 cup of semolina on a pan for 2 mins on low flame. Allow this to cool down completely. Next, in a mixing bowl combine 1/2 cup of roasted semolina, 1/2 cup of ragi flour, 1/4 tsp of salt, 1/4 cup of curd, and 1/4 cup of water. Mix these ingredients well and let the batter rest for 30 mins.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":35,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('612354e23a4d5fc6fdfa17da','61235361003d0c069277c36c',2,'M1: Steam the idlis & serve','For ragi idli, once the batter has rested coat the idli mold in 1 tsp of oil. Next, add 1/4 tsp of baking soda to the idli batter and mix well. Pour 1/4 cup of batter into each mold and allow the idlis to steam for 10 mins. After that is complete, remove the idlis from their mold and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61235a1a3ca3bf7c22a8d8c2','612359443ca3bf7c22a8d8c1',1,'P1: Chop & prep the ingredients','To make bhindi stir-fry, start by washing and completely drying 1.5 cups of lady''s finger. Allow the lady''s finger to dry for 10 mins before you begin chopping it. Once the lady''s finger is dry, slice it into 1/2 inch pieces. Wash and slit 2 green chilies.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('61235b6a003d0c069277c36e','612359443ca3bf7c22a8d8c1',2,'M1: Stir-fry the ladies fingers & serve','For Bhindi Stir-fry, heat 2 tsp of cooking oil in a pan on medium flame. To this, add 1/2 tsp of mustard seeds, 1/4 tsp of hing, 1/2 tsp of turmeric powder, 2 slit green chilies, and let this splutter for a few seconds. Then, add 1.5 cups of chopped lady''s finger and mix well. Next, reduce the flame to low and let the lady''s finger cook for 10 mins stirring occasionally. Once the lady''s finger has browned nicely add 1/2 tsp of salt, mix well, turn off the flame, and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('612360d23a4d5fc6fdfa17de','61235f4a3a4d5fc6fdfa17dd',1,'AP1: Soak the moong beans','For the Moong Sprout Salad, wash and soak 1 cup of green moong beans in 2 cups of water for 8-10 hours. While the moong beans are soaking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":300,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('612361843a4d5fc6fdfa17df','61235f4a3a4d5fc6fdfa17dd',2,'AP2: Sprout the moong beans','To make the moong sprouts for the Moong Sprout Salad, place a damp muslin cloth over a bowl, add the soaked moong beans to it and tie it well into a tight bundle. Set it aside for another 10 hours and make sure to sprinkle some water over the bundle to keep it moist. While the moong beans are resting, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('612361f33a4d5fc6fdfa17e0','61235f4a3a4d5fc6fdfa17dd',3,'P1: Blanch the moong sprouts','To blanch the moong sprouts for the Moong Sprout Salad, boil 3 cups of water in a saucepan on medium-high flame for 3 minutes. Transfer the moong sprouts to a large mixing bowl and soak them in the hot water for 5 minutes. After blanching the moong sprouts, drain off the water and keep it aside. While the moong sprouts are soaking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('612364bc3a4d5fc6fdfa17e1','61235f4a3a4d5fc6fdfa17dd',4,'P2: Prep the ingredients','For the Moong Sprout Salad, wash, peel and dice 1/4 cup of cucumber. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Wash, peel, and grate 1/4 cup of carrot using a grater. Wash and chop 1/4 cup of green capsicum. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of spring onion greens.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('612366363ca3bf7c22a8d8c4','61235f4a3a4d5fc6fdfa17dd',5,'P3: Crush the peanuts','Next, wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of mint leaves. Wash and finely chop 1 nos green chili. Squeeze 1 teaspoon of lime juice. Next, to crush the peanuts, put 2 tablespoons of roasted peanuts in a mortar and crush it coarsely using a pestle.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('612388613ca3bf7c22a8d8c5','61235f4a3a4d5fc6fdfa17dd',6,'M1: Add the spices to the blanched moong sprouts','To make the Moong Sprout Salad, add the blanched moong sprouts in a large mixing bowl. Add 1/2 teaspoon of cumin powder, 1/4 teaspoon of Kashmiri red chili powder, 1/2 teaspoon of dry mango powder, and 1/4 teaspoon of salt and mix it well.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('612388e83a4d5fc6fdfa17e2','61235f4a3a4d5fc6fdfa17dd',7,'M2: Add the vegetables & combine the salad','Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped cucumber, 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes, 1/4 cup of grated carrot, and 1/4 cup of chopped capsicum to the moong beans. Next, add 2 tablespoons of chopped spring onion greens, 2 tablespoons of chopped coriander leaves, 2 tablespoons of chopped mint leaves, 1 nos chopped green chili, and 1 teaspoon of lime juice to the salad and mix well. Garnish the salad with 2 tablespoons of crushed peanuts and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61238d2c003d0c069277c375','61238cce3a4d5fc6fdfa17e6',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Beetroot Sabzi, wash, peel and grate 1 cup of beetroot. Grate 2 tablespoons of fresh coconut using a grater. Wash and roughly chop 1 nos green chili. Break 1 nos dry red chili into half. Wash 10 nos curry leaves well with water.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61238dc83ca3bf7c22a8d8c9','61238cce3a4d5fc6fdfa17e6',2,'M1: Temper Spices','To make Beetroot Sabzi, heat 1 tablespoon of cooking oil in a kadai. Add 1/4 teaspoon of mustard seeds, half a teaspoon of chana dal, half a teaspoon of urad dal, and 1 no broken dry red chili. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, 1/4 teaspoon of hing, and 1 nos chopped green chili along with 10 nos curry leaves. Saute it on a medium flame for a minute.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('61238e2f3ca3bf7c22a8d8ca','61238cce3a4d5fc6fdfa17e6',3,'M2: Cook Poriyal','Next, add 1 cup of grated beetroot and mix it well. Stir and fry it on high flame for 1-2 minutes. Then, add half a teaspoon of salt along with 1/4 cup of water and mix it well. Cover it with a lid and allow it to simmer for 5-6 minutes. While the beetroot is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61238e683a4d5fc6fdfa17e7','61238cce3a4d5fc6fdfa17e6',4,'M3: Add Coconut','After simmering the Beetroot Sabzi, take off the lid and add 2 tablespoons of grated coconut. Mix it well and turn off the flame. Take it out into a bowl and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6123983c003d0c069277c377','6123980a3ca3bf7c22a8d8cf',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Veg Dalma, first, take 3/4 cup of toor dal in a bowl and rinse it well with water and set it aside. Next, wash, peel and cut 1/4 cup raw banana in thick roundels. Wash and roughly chop 5 nos beans. Wash, peel and cube 1/4 cup of carrot. Wash and roughly cut 1/4 cup of eggplant into big cubes. Wash, peel and cube 1/4 cup of pumpkin.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('612398653a4d5fc6fdfa17ea','6123980a3ca3bf7c22a8d8cf',2,'P2: Prep Ingredients','Next, wash, peel and cube 1/4 cup of yam. Wash, peel, and cube 1/4 cup of radish. Wash, peel, and cube 1/4 cup of potatoes. Wash a tomato well with water. Wash and slit 1 nos green chili. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61239892003d0c069277c378','6123980a3ca3bf7c22a8d8cf',3,'M1: Cook Dal and Vegetables','To cook the vegetables for Veg Dalma, in a pressure cooker, add 3/4 cup of rinsed toor dal. Next, add 5 nos chopped beans, 1/4 cup of cubed potatoes, 1 nos tomato, 1/4 cup of cubed carrot and 1/4 cup of cubed eggplant. Next, add 1/4 cup of cubed pumpkins, 1/4 cup of cubed radish, 1/4 cup of raw banana roundels and 1/4 cup of cubed yam. Then, add 2 cups of water followed by half a teaspoon of salt. Cover it with a lid and pressure cook the vegetables on high flame until three whistles. Reduce the flame to low and continue to simmer the vegetables for another 5 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the vegetables are cooking, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":18,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('612398c93ca3bf7c22a8d8d0','6123980a3ca3bf7c22a8d8cf',4,'M2: Cook the masala','To make the Veg Dalma, heat 1 tablespoon of ghee in a kadai on a medium flame for a minute. Add a 1/4 teaspoon of hing, 1 nos bay leaf, and 1 nos dry red chili along with 1 teaspoon of ginger paste. Stir and saute the ginger paste on a medium flame for a minute. After that, add a quarter teaspoon of turmeric powder followed by 1 teaspoon of red chili powder, and 1 teaspoon of sabzi masala. Mix it well and fry the masala on a medium flame for a minute.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('612398f7003d0c069277c379','6123980a3ca3bf7c22a8d8cf',5,'M3: Continue Cooking to make Dalma','After frying the masala, add the cooked tomato and mash it well with the spatula. Then, stir it with the masala. Add 1 slit green chili. Saute and cook the masala on a medium flame for 3-4 minutes or until the oil separates. Then, add the pressure-cooked vegetables and dal to the masala and mix it well. Simmer the dalma for 6-7 minutes. While the dalma is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":7,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61239934003d0c069277c37a','6123980a3ca3bf7c22a8d8cf',6,'M4: Garnish & serve','After simmering the dalma, give it a stir and add a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves. Add a pinch of red chili powder followed by a quarter teaspoon of roasted cumin powder and mix it well. Turn off the flame and take it out in a serving bowl. Garnish it with some chopped coriander leaves and a teaspoon of ghee. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6123a5c63a4d5fc6fdfa17ef','6123a4d23a4d5fc6fdfa17ee',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Masala Toast, wash, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Wash, peel, and grate 1/4 cup of carrot. Wash and finely shred 1/4 cup of cabbage. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of green capsicum.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6123a63b3ca3bf7c22a8d8d3','6123a4d23a4d5fc6fdfa17ee',2,'P2: Prep Ingredients','Wash and finely chop 1 nos green chili. Wash, peel and finely chop a 1-inch piece of ginger. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('6123a68d003d0c069277c37e','6123a4d23a4d5fc6fdfa17ee',3,'M1: Make Stuffing','To make the stuffing for Masala Toast, heat 1 teaspoon of cooking oil in a kadai on a medium flame for a minute. Add half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, 1/4 teaspoon of cumin seeds, and 1 no chopped green chili followed by 1/2 inch piece of chopped ginger. Saute and let the tempering splutter for a minute. Then, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions and fry it on a medium flame for 2-3 minutes, till it turns slightly translucent. Then, add 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes and mix it well. Saute and cook the tomatoes on medium flame for 4-5 minutes until it turns tender.','cook_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6123a7253ca3bf7c22a8d8d4','6123a4d23a4d5fc6fdfa17ee',4,'M2: Make Stuffing','After cooking the tomatoes, add 1/4 cup of grated carrot, 1/4 cup of shredded cabbage, and 1/4 cup of chopped green capsicum and mix it well. Stir and fry the vegetables on high flame for 2-3 minutes until tender-crisp. Then, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, 1/4 teaspoon of Kashmiri red chili powder, and 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala followed by 1/4 teaspoon of cumin powder and 1/4 teaspoon of chat masala. Season the vegetables with 1/4 teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Fry the vegetables on medium-high flame for another 2 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6123a76c003d0c069277c37f','6123a4d23a4d5fc6fdfa17ee',5,'M3: Make Stuffing','After frying the vegetables, add 1 tablespoon of tomato ketchup and mix it well. Fry it for another 1-2 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and add 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves. Mix it well and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6123a7c33ca3bf7c22a8d8d5','6123a4d23a4d5fc6fdfa17ee',6,'M4: Make Masala Toast','To make the Masala Toast, take a bread slice and cut it diagonally. Then apply 1/4 teaspoon of butter to both halves. Place the bread slices onto a tawa and toast it on medium flame. Apply the butter to the other side of the bread slices as well. Toast the slices for 2-3 minutes until it turns golden brown. Then, flip the slices one by one, and spread 1 tablespoon of the prepared masala stuffing over each slice. Continue to toast it for another 2 minutes until it turns crisp and golden. Then, turn off the flame and take it out onto a plate. Make the rest of the masala toasts similarly. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61247dd63a4d5fc6fdfa17f4','61247daf3a4d5fc6fdfa17f3',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Khara Bhath, wash, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Wash, peel, and finely chop a 1-inch piece of ginger. Wash and finely chop 1 nos green chili. Wash and chop 5 nos beans. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of carrot.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('61247e393a4d5fc6fdfa17f5','61247daf3a4d5fc6fdfa17f3',2,'P2: Prep Ingredients','Next, peel and wash 1/4 cup of green peas. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves. Grate 2 tablespoons of fresh coconut using a grater. Squeeze 1 teaspoon of lime juice using a lemon squeezer.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61247e713a4d5fc6fdfa17f6','61247daf3a4d5fc6fdfa17f3',3,'P3: Roast Semolina','To roast the rava for Khara Bhath, add half a cup of rava to a pan and dry roast it without adding any oil on low flame for 3-4 minutes until it turns slightly golden. Keep stirring to prevent it from getting burnt. After roasting the rava, turn off the flame and set it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61247ece3a4d5fc6fdfa17f7','61247daf3a4d5fc6fdfa17f3',4,'M1: Temper Spices','To make Khara Bhath, heat 2 tablespoons of ghee in a kadai on a medium flame for a minute. Add 1 teaspoon of mustard seeds, 1 teaspoon urad dal and 1 teaspoon of chana dal followed by 10 nos cashew nuts and 8 nos curry leaves. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions along with a 1-inch piece of chopped ginger and 1 nos chopped green chili. Stir and fry the onions on medium flame for 2-3 minutes, till it slightly turns translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61247f06003d0c069277c382','61247daf3a4d5fc6fdfa17f3',5,'M2: Cook Vegetables','After frying the onions, add 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes and mix it well. Saute and cook the tomatoes on medium-low flame for 3-4 minutes until it turns tender. Keep stirring the tomatoes, to prevent it from sticking to the bottom of the pan. After cooking the tomatoes, add 1/4 cup of chopped capsicum, 5 nos chopped beans, 1/4 cup of chopped carrot and 1/4 cup of green peas. Season it with a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Stir and fry the vegetables on medium flame for 2-3 minutes until it turns tender.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61247f463ca3bf7c22a8d8d8','61247daf3a4d5fc6fdfa17f3',6,'M3: Continue Cooking Khara Bath','After frying the vegetables, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder followed by 1 teaspoon of vangi bhath masala and mix it well. Fry and cook the masala for 1-2 minutes. After that, add 1.5 cups of water and mix it well. Then, bring it to a rolling boil on high flame. As it comes to a boil, start adding half a cup of roasted rava slowly and keep stirring it in a clockwise motion to avoid any lumps. Once it is well combined with the masala, cover it with a lid and simmer it for 5 minutes. While the rava bhath is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('61247f6e3a4d5fc6fdfa17f8','61247daf3a4d5fc6fdfa17f3',7,'M4: Garnish & Serve','After simmering the Khara Bhath, take off the lid and mix it well. By this time, the rava will absorb all the water. Saute it on a medium flame for 1-2 minutes until it leaves the pan completely. Then, add 2 tablespoons of grated coconut and 2 tablespoons of chopped coriander leaves. Add 1 teaspoon of lime juice and mix it well. Turn off the flame, take it out in a bowl and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('612487c63a4d5fc6fdfa17fd','612486bd3ca3bf7c22a8d8e2',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','To make Beans and Potato Sabzi, first, wash and chop 1 cup of beans into 1-inch pieces. Next, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Peel and dice 1/2 a cup of potatoes. Wash and roughly chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Wash and finely chop 1 tbsp of coriander leaves. Wash and slit 1 green chilli.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('612488003ca3bf7c22a8d8e3','612486bd3ca3bf7c22a8d8e2',2,'M1: Cook Vegetables','To make Beans and Potato Sabzi, heat 1 tbsp of cooking oil in a kadai on high-medium flame for 1 min. To this, add 1 tsp of cumin seeds and let them splutter for a few seconds and then add 1 tsp of finely chopped garlic followed by 1/4 cup of finely chopped onions. Saute this for 2-3 mins until the onions are translucent. Next, add 1 slit green chilli followed by 1/2 cup of diced potatoes and saute this for 1 min. To this, add 1 cup of chopped beans and combine all the ingredients well.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6124885d3ca3bf7c22a8d8e4','612486bd3ca3bf7c22a8d8e2',3,'M2: Continue Cooking to make Sabzi','Next, season the dish with 1/2 tsp of salt, 1/2 tsp of red chilli powder, 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder, 1 tsp of coriander powder, 1/4 tsp of dry mango powder, and mix it well. Cover the kadai with a lid and let the vegetables cook for 6 mins on low-medium flame. After this, take off the lid and add 1/4 cup of roughly chopped tomatoes, saute this for 1 min, and then cover the kadai once more for 2 mins. Next, take off the lid, add 1/4 tsp of garam masala and 1 tbsp of coriander leaves. Mix well and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6126035f3a4d5fc6fdfa17ff','6126030c3ca3bf7c22a8d8ec',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','To make Garlic Chutney, soak 5 dry red chilies in water for 10 mins. Peel 12 cloves of garlic and peel and roughly chop 2 shallots. Wash 7 curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":10,"flame":0}'),
('612603a83a4d5fc6fdfa1800','6126030c3ca3bf7c22a8d8ec',2,'M1: Cook Shallots and Blend Ingredients','To make garlic chutney, in a pan heat 2 tsp of oil on a medium flame for 1 min. Next, add 12 cloves of garlic along with 2 diced shallots. Saute this for 2-3 mins until golden brown and then allow this to cool down before you transfer it to a blender. In this blender along with the shallots and garlic add the 5 soaked red chilies, 1 tsp of tamarind, 1/2 tsp of salt, and blend it into a smooth paste.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61260403003d0c069277c386','6126030c3ca3bf7c22a8d8ec',3,'M2: Add the tempering & serve','Next, in a pan heat 1 tsp of oil on a medium flame for 1 min. To this add, 1/2 tsp of mustard seeds, 1/2 tsp of urad dal, 1/4 tsp of hing, and 7 curry leaves. Let this splutter for a few seconds and then pour in the paste from the blender. Cook the chutney for 1 min and once the oil has separated transfer it to a serving bowl.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('612606d3003d0c069277c38a','6126064f003d0c069277c389',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','To make Masala Khichdi, first, wash 1/2 cup of rice and 1/2 cup of yellow moong dal and set them aside. Next, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onion and 1/4 cup of carrot. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomato and 1/4 cup of capsicum. Wash and slit 1 green chilli. Wash and roughly chop1 tbsp of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6126077c003d0c069277c38b','6126064f003d0c069277c389',2,'M1: Saute vegetables','For Masala Khichdi, heat 1 tbsp of ghee in a pressure cooker on medium flame. Next, add 1 bay leaf, 1/2 inch cinnamon stick, 2 green cardamoms, 3 cloves, 1 tsp of cumin seeds, 1/4 tsp of hing, and let this splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions, saute them for 2 min, and then add 1 slit green chili and 1 tsp of ginger-garlic paste. Mix this well and then add 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Saute them for 1 min and add 1/4 cup of green peas, 1/4 cup of chopped carrot, and 1/4 cup of chopped green capsicum. Saute for another minute, add 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder, 1/2 tsp of red chili powder, 1/4 tsp of garam masala, 1/2 tsp of salt, and mix everything well.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('612607bc3a4d5fc6fdfa1804','6126064f003d0c069277c389',3,'M2: Pressure cook the khichdi & serve','Next, add 1/2 a cup of washed raw rice and 1/2 cup of washed yellow moong dal. Combine all the ingredients, then add 3.5 cups of water and 1 tbsp of chopped coriander leaves, mix well, and then close the lid of the pressure cooker. Cook the khichdi on high flame for 2 whistles and then on low flame for another 8 mins. Once this is done turn off the flame and allow the pressure to release naturally before you open the cooker. After you open the cooker, give the khichdi a good mix, adjust the consistency if necessary, then transfer it into a serving dish, and enjoy.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('612616463a4d5fc6fdfa1807','6126158c3a4d5fc6fdfa1806',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','To make oats poha, first, rinse 1.5 cups of oats with 3 tsp of water. Next, slice 1/4 cup of onions, wash and finely chop 1 green chilli, wash and finely chop 5 beans, peel and finely chop 1/4 cups of carrot, and wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of green and yellow capsicum. Wash 7 curry leaves and thaw 1/4 cup of frozen green peas. Wash and chop 1 tbsp of coriander leaves. Peel and finely dice 1/4 cup of potatoes. Squeeze 2 tsp of lime juice.','prep_method','{"active_time":16,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('612616b0003d0c069277c38e','6126158c3a4d5fc6fdfa1806',2,'M1: Cook Spices and Vegetables','For Oats Poha, in a kadai heat 1 tablespoon of oil and roast 3 tbsp of peanuts for 2 mins, once the nuts are roasted take them out of the kadai and set it aside. Add 1/2 tsp of mustard seeds, 1/2 tsp of cumin seeds, 7 curry leaves, 1 chopped green chili, and let this splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 1/4 cup of sliced onions and saute this for 2-3 mins. Then, add 1/4 cup of green peas followed by 1/4 cup of chopped potato and saute this for 2-3 mins. After that, add 5 chopped beans, 1/4 cup of chopped carrot, and saute for 1 min.','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('612616fa3a4d5fc6fdfa1808','6126158c3a4d5fc6fdfa1806',3,'M2: Continue Cooking to make Poha','Next, add 1/4 cup of yellow capsicum, 1/4 cup of green capsicum, saute for 1 min. Then close the kadai with a lid and let everything cook for 3-4 mins. After this, add 1/4 tsp of turmeric powder, 1/2 tsp of salt and mix well. Next, add 1.5 cups of rolled oats, mix well and then add 2 tsp of lime juice and 1/2 tsp of chaat masala. Sprinkle 2 tbsp of water on top, mix everything well, and cover the kadai with a lid and let it cook for 2-3 mins. Next, add 3 tbsp of roasted peanuts, 1 tbsp of coriander leaves, mix well, and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":7,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6126196f3a4d5fc6fdfa180b','6126192d3a4d5fc6fdfa180a',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Cheese Omelette, wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves. Grate 2 tablespoons of processed cheese. Grate 2 tablespoons of mozzarella cheese.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('612619e1003d0c069277c392','6126192d3a4d5fc6fdfa180a',2,'M1: Whisk Eggs','To make the Cheese Omelette, first, crack 4 nos eggs in a bowl and whisk it well using a whisk. Add 2 tablespoons of fresh cream and mix it well. Next, add half a teaspoon of black pepper powder followed by half a teaspoon of salt and mix it well.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('61261a12003d0c069277c393','6126192d3a4d5fc6fdfa180a',3,'M2: Cook Omelette','To make the Cheese Omelette, heat a tablespoon of butter in a pan over medium flame. Twirl the pan slightly to spread the butter across. Then, pour half of the prepared egg mixture into the pan and spread it across evenly. Cook it over medium-low flame for 1-2 minutes. As the omelette starts to get slightly stiff from the bottom, gently stir it with the spatula as shown, spreading the liquid batter over the pan to cook it evenly. Cook the omelette over medium flame for another 2-3 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61261a6f3ca3bf7c22a8d8f3','6126192d3a4d5fc6fdfa180a',4,'M3: Add cheese & serve','Next, spread a tablespoon of grated mozzarella cheese and a tablespoon of grated processed cheese over it. Spread the cheese to one half of the omelette as shown. Next, sprinkle a pinch of black pepper powder over it followed by 1/4 teaspoon of chili flakes and a 1/4 teaspoon of mixed herbs. Add a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves. Then gently fold the omelette and cook it over medium flame for another 1-2 minutes, until it turns slightly golden. Then, turn off the flame and take it out onto a plate. Serve.  Make the other omelette from the mixture similarly.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61261cff3ca3bf7c22a8d8f6','61261cac3ca3bf7c22a8d8f5',1,'P1: Prepare the Dough','To knead the dough for Matar Paratha, first, in a large mixing bowl, add 3/4 cup of wheat flour and 1/4 cup of all-purpose flour. Add 1/4 teaspoon of salt followed by 1/4 teaspoon of cooking oil. Then, gradually add about half a cup of water and knead it well into a smooth dough. Cover the dough with a damp cloth and allow it to rest for 30 minutes. While the dough is resting, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":30,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61261d533a4d5fc6fdfa180f','61261cac3ca3bf7c22a8d8f5',2,'P2: Prep Ingredients','For Matar Paratha, wash and peel 3/4 cup of green peas. Wash, peel and finely chop a half-inch piece of ginger. Wash and finely chop 1 nos green chili. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61261df13a4d5fc6fdfa1810','61261cac3ca3bf7c22a8d8f5',3,'P3:  Prepare the stuffing','To make the stuffing for Matar Paratha, first, add 3/4 cups of green peas to a blender jar and blend it into a slightly coarse paste. Then, take it out in a mixing bowl. Next, add a half-inch piece of chopped ginger followed by 1 nos chopped green chili and a tablespoon of coriander leaves. Add half a teaspoon of coriander powder, 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala, and half a teaspoon of dried pomegranate seeds followed by 1/4 teaspoon of salt. Mix it well and prepare a stuffing.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('61261e253a4d5fc6fdfa1811','61261cac3ca3bf7c22a8d8f5',4,'M1: Divide the dough and roll out the paratha','To make the Matar Paratha,  first, divide the prepared dough into small equal-sized balls. Take a dough ball and dust some flour over it. Then, gently roll it using fingers while making a small cavity as shown. Place 2-3 tablespoons of the prepared green peas stuffing into it and pleat it as shown to seal the stuffing inside. Then, gently roll it into a slightly thick round paratha. Make sure to roll the paratha with light hands to prevent the stuffing from coming out of the dough.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61261e653a4d5fc6fdfa1812','61261cac3ca3bf7c22a8d8f5',5,'M2: Roast the paratha and serve','To make the Matar Paratha, place the rolled out matar paratha onto a hot tawa and cook it over medium flame for a minute. Flip and cook it evenly on both sides. Then, apply half a teaspoon of cooking oil to each side and cook it for another 2-3 minutes, until it is evenly browned on both sides. After that, take it out onto a plate and serve. Make the rest of the parathas similarly.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6126215d3ca3bf7c22a8d8fa','612621273a4d5fc6fdfa1817',1,'P1: Soak Dal','For Chana Dal, soak 3/4 cup of chana dal in 2 cups of water for 30 minutes. While the dal is soaking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":30,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('612621d33a4d5fc6fdfa1818','612621273a4d5fc6fdfa1817',2,'P2: Prep Ingredients','For Chana Dal, peel, wash and finely chop half a cup of onions. Wash and finely chop half a cup of tomatoes. Peel, wash, and finely chop 1 teaspoon of garlic. Wash and finely chop 2 nos green chilies. Wash, peel, and finely chop a 1-inch piece of ginger. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves. Wash 8 nos curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6126224b3a4d5fc6fdfa1819','612621273a4d5fc6fdfa1817',3,'M1: Temper the oil with whole spices','To make Chana Dal, heat 1 tablespoon of cooking oil in a pressure cooker over medium flame for a minute. Add 3/4 teaspoons of mustard seeds, half a teaspoon of cumin seeds, 1 dry red chili, 1/4 teaspoon of hing and 8 nos curry leaves. Saute it over medium flame for a minute. Next, add a 1-inch piece of chopped ginger followed by 1 teaspoon of chopped garlic and 2 nos chopped green chilies. Saute it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('612622a93a4d5fc6fdfa181a','612621273a4d5fc6fdfa1817',4,'M2: fry the onions & cook the masala','Next, add half a cup of chopped onions and fry it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until translucent. Add half a cup of chopped tomatoes and mix it well. Saute and cook the tomatoes over medium flame for 4-5 minutes until tender. Next, add half a teaspoon of Kashmiri red chili powder followed by 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder and half a teaspoon of coriander powder. Add 1/4 teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Saute and cook the masala for 1-2 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('612622de003d0c069277c398','612621273a4d5fc6fdfa1817',5,'M3: Simmer the dal','Next, add the soaked chana dal and mix it well. Add 1.5 cups of water and stir it well. Then, cover it with a lid and pressure cook the dal over a high flame until two whistles. After that, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook it for another 5 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the dal is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('612623123a4d5fc6fdfa181b','612621273a4d5fc6fdfa1817',6,'M4: Garnish & serve','After cooking the dal, take off the lid and stir it well. Garnish it with 2 tablespoons of chopped coriander leaves and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('6127687744613cc23f0a73e2','612767dd312d2963f71466b3',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Quinoa Upa, first, rinse half a cup of quinoa well with water. Soak 1/4 cup of frozen green peas in half a cup of water for 5 minutes. Then, drain off the water and set aside. Next, peel, wash and finely slice half a cup of onions. Wash, peel and finely chop half a cup of carrots. Wash, peel and finely chop a 1-inch piece of ginger. Wash and finely chop 2 nos green chilies. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash 8 nos curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6127692390169a0ec9a837e6','612767dd312d2963f71466b3',2,'M1: Temper Spices','To make the Quinoa Upma, heat 2 tablespoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, and half a teaspoon of cumin seeds followed by half a teaspoon of chana dal and half a teaspoon of urad dal. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 8 nos curry leaves along with 2 nos chopped green chilies and a 1-inch piece of chopped ginger and fry it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('6127695944613cc23f0a73e3','612767dd312d2963f71466b3',3,'M2: Cook Vegetables','Next, add half a cup of sliced onions. Saute and fry the onions over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until translucent. Then, add 1/4 cup of frozen green peas followed by half a cup of chopped carrots and mix it well. Stir and fry the vegetables over medium-high flame for 1-2 minutes. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder and mix it well.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6127699844613cc23f0a73e4','612767dd312d2963f71466b3',4,'M3: Cook Quinoa','Add 3/4 cup of water and let it boil. Add half a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Then, boil the water over high flame for a minute. As the water comes to a rolling boil, add half a cup of rinsed quinoa and mix it well. Then, cover it with a lid and cook the quinoa over low flame for 10-12 minutes, until it fluffs up and is cooked through. While the quinoa upma is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('612769c544613cc23f0a73e5','612767dd312d2963f71466b3',5,'M4: Garnish & Serve','After simmering the Quinoa Upma, take off the lid and add a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves. Gently mix the upma with light hands. Take it out into a bowl and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61276cfc312d2963f71466b6','61276c7944613cc23f0a73eb',1,'P1:  Whisk eggs','To prepare the batter for French Toast, crack 2 nos eggs in a shallow dish. Whisk the eggs well using a fork. Next, add 1/4 cup of milk followed by 1 teaspoon of sugar and 1/4 teaspoon of cinnamon powder. Add 1/4 teaspoon of salt along with half a teaspoon of vanilla essence and mix it well until well combined.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61276d52312d2963f71466b7','61276c7944613cc23f0a73eb',2,'M1: Make French Toast','To make French Toast, heat 1/4 teaspoon of canola oil in a frying pan over medium flame for a minute. Add 1/4 teaspoon of butter and spread it across the pan. Then, gently dip a bread slice in the prepared egg mixture and coat it well. Place the bread slice onto the pan and toast it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes. Flip and toast the other side for 1-2 minutes. Toast the bread slice until it is evenly browned on both sides. Then, take it out onto a plate and garnish the french toast with a teaspoon of maple syrup. Make the rest of the toasts similarly.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('61276f8244613cc23f0a73ee','61276f3a44613cc23f0a73ed',1,'P1: Knead the Dough','To knead the dough for Cabbage Paratha, add 1 cup of wheat flour in a large mixing bowl. Add 1/4 teaspoon of salt followed by 1/4 teaspoon of cooking oil and mix it well. Then, gradually add about half a cup of water and knead it well into a smooth dough. Then, grease the dough with 1/4 teaspoon of cooking oil and cover it with a damp cloth. Allow the dough to rest for 20 minutes. While the dough is resting, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6127700690169a0ec9a837ea','61276f3a44613cc23f0a73ed',2,'P2: Prepare the Cabbage Stuffing','For Cabbage Paratha, wash and finely chop 3/4 cup of cabbage. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves. Next, to prepare the stuffing for the paratha, heat a tablespoon of cooking oil in a kadai over medium flame for a minute. Temper it with a 1/4 teaspoon of crushed coriander seeds and a 1/4 teaspoon of carom seeds. Saute it over low flame for a minute. Next, add 3/4 cup of chopped cabbage and mix it well. Stir and fry the cabbage over medium flame for 1-2 minutes.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6127707e312d2963f71466ba','61276f3a44613cc23f0a73ed',3,'P3:  Add spices to the stuffing','After stir-frying the cabbage, add 1/4 teaspoon of ginger paste, 1/4 teaspoon of Kashmiri red chili powder and 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder followed by 1/4 teaspoon of cumin powder and 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of dry mango powder and 1/4 teaspoon of salt. Mix it well and fry the cabbage with the masala for 2-3 minutes. Stir and fry the cabbage over a high flame to reduce the moisture. Then, turn off the flame and add a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves. Mix it well and set it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('612770c990169a0ec9a837eb','61276f3a44613cc23f0a73ed',4,'M1: Stuff the dough balls & roll out the paratha','To make the Cabbage Paratha, first, divide the prepared dough into small equal-sized balls. Take a dough ball and dust some flour over it. Then, roll it into a 5-inch circle. Place 2-3 tablespoons of the prepared cabbage stuffing over it and pleat it as shown to seal the stuffing inside. Remove the extra dough if any. Then, gently roll it into a slightly thick round paratha. Make sure to roll the paratha with light hands to prevent the stuffing from coming out of the dough.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6127710e44613cc23f0a73ef','61276f3a44613cc23f0a73ed',5,'M2: Cook the Parathas & Serve','To make the Cabbage Paratha, place the rolled-out cabbage paratha onto a hot tawa and cook it over medium flame for a minute. Flip and cook it evenly on both sides. Then, apply half a teaspoon of cooking oil to each side and cook it for another 2-3 minutes, until it is evenly browned on both sides. After that, take it out onto a plate and serve. Make the rest of the parathas similarly.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('61277606312d2963f71466be','612775c490169a0ec9a837f0',1,'P1: Knead the Dough','In a large bowl, add wheat flour and salt. Then gradually add 3/4 cup of water and mix well. Mix and knead this until you create a smooth dough. Cover it with a damp cloth and let it rest for 25 mins.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":25,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61277672312d2963f71466bf','612775c490169a0ec9a837f0',2,'P2: Prep Ingredients','Wash and chop coriander leaves. Into a large bowl, crack 3 eggs then add salt, turmeric, red chili powder, garam masala, and the coriander leaves. Mix this well with a whisk.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('612776b244613cc23f0a73f5','612775c490169a0ec9a837f0',3,'M1: Divide the dough & roll out the paratha','Once the dough has rested, take it out and knead it once again. Then divide it into 4 equal portions and roll them into balls. Turn 1 ball into a 7-inch thick circle with a rolling pin. Spread ghee and sprinkle flour over the circle and fold it in half and sprinkle ghee and flour once more. Fold it one more time, into a triangle shape and sprinkle some flour on top. Next, roll it into a 7-inch thick paratha.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('612776f644613cc23f0a73f6','612775c490169a0ec9a837f0',4,'M2: Prepare the paratha & serve','On a heated tawa, place the paratha and cook until some browning occurs and repeat the same for the other side. Then with a fork open one of the layers in the paratha and pour some egg mixture in. Then add ghee and cook on both sides. Cook this for 2-3 mins and once it is golden brown take it off the heat. Repeat this process for the rest of the dough to prepare parathas.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61289e8c312d2963f71466cf','61289e2744613cc23f0a73fe',1,'P1: Prep Ingredients','For Dahi Bhindi, wash 1 cup of lady''s fingers well with water and spread it over a kitchen towel to wipe off the extra water. Allow it to dry completely and make sure there is no moisture left in the lady''s fingers. Then, cut it into 1-inch pieces. Peel, wash and finely slice 1/4 cup of onions. Peel and rough chop a half-inch piece of ginger. Peel and wash 1 clove of garlic. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash 7 nos curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('61289ec790169a0ec9a837f8','61289e2744613cc23f0a73fe',2,'P2: Prepare Onion Paste','For Dahi Bhindi, heat a tablespoon of cooking oil in a kadai over medium flame for a minute. Add 1/4 cup of sliced onions followed by a half-inch piece of chopped ginger and a clove of garlic. Saute and fry the onions over medium flame until it turns slightly golden. Then, turn off the flame and allow the mixture to cool down completely. While it is cooling down, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61289f05312d2963f71466d0','61289e2744613cc23f0a73fe',3,'P3: Fry Ladies finger','To fry the lady''s fingers for Dahi Bhindi,  heat a tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add 1 cup of chopped lady''s fingers to it. Stir and fry the ladies fingers over medium flame for 4-5 minutes until it turns slightly dark and tender-crisp. Then, turn off the flame and set it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61289f4f312d2963f71466d1','61289e2744613cc23f0a73fe',4,'P4: Blend the onion mixture to prepare the masala paste','To prepare the onion paste for Dahi Bhindi, after the prepared onion mixture cools down, transfer it to a blender jar. Cover the jar with a lid and blend it well into a smooth paste.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61289fd390169a0ec9a837f9','61289e2744613cc23f0a73fe',5,'M1: Temper the oil with spices','To make Dahi Bhindi, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a kadai over medium flame for a minute. Add half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, half a teaspoon of cumin seeds followed by a 1/4 teaspoon of fenugreek seeds, and 1/4 teaspoon of hing. Next, add 7 nos curry leaves and saute it over medium flame for a minute. Add the prepared onion paste and mix it well. Saute and fry over medium flame for 2-3 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6128a1c390169a0ec9a837fa','61289e2744613cc23f0a73fe',6,'M2: Add Masala Powders','After frying the masala, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, 1 teaspoon of Kashmiri red chili powder and 1/4 teaspoon of coriander powder followed by half a teaspoon of salt. Mix it well and fry the masala over low flame for another 1-2 minutes. Add about 1/4 cup of water, if the masala gets too dry and mix it well.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('6128a20d312d2963f71466d2','61289e2744613cc23f0a73fe',7,'M3: Add curd & simmer the curry','Then, reduce the flame to low and add half a cup of curd to the masala. Keep stirring it continuously over a low flame until it is well combined, to prevent the curd from splitting. Once the gravy comes together, add 1 cup of the fried lady''s fingers and gently mix it with the masala. Then, cover it with a lid and allow it to simmer for 5 minutes. While the Dahi bhindi is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('6128a23e312d2963f71466d3','61289e2744613cc23f0a73fe',8,'M4: Garnish & serve','After simmering the Dahi Bhindi, take off the lid and add 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves followed by a 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala. Mix it well and take it out into a serving bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('6128a59a312d2963f71466d7','6128a56b90169a0ec9a83802',1,'P1: Boil Potatoes','To boil the potatoes for Gobhi Aloo Matar Sabzi, first, wash 2 nos medium-sized potatoes well with water. Next, put the potatoes in a pressure cooker along with 2 cups of water. Cover it with a lid and pressure cook it over high flame until one whistle. After the first whistle, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook it for another 8 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the potatoes are boiling, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6128a5da90169a0ec9a83803','6128a56b90169a0ec9a83802',2,'P2: Blanch Green Peas','To blanch the green peas for Gobhi Aloo Matar Sabzi, first, soak 1/4 cup of frozen green peas in 1 cup of water for 2 minutes. Meanwhile, boil 1 cup of water in a saucepan over high flame for 1-2 minutes. Then add the soaked green peas into it and boil over medium-high flame for 4-5 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and drain off the excess water from it and set it aside. While the green peas are blanching, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6128a64944613cc23f0a7407','6128a56b90169a0ec9a83802',3,'P3: Blanch Cauliflower','To blanch the cauliflower florets for Gobhi Aloo Matar Sabzi, first, wash and cut half a cup of cauliflower into small florets. Then, boil 2 cups of water in a pan over a high flame. As it comes to a rolling boil, add half a teaspoon of salt followed by half a cup of cauliflower florets and stir it well. Then, allow it to boil over medium flame for 2-3 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and drain off the water form it and rinse the blanched cauliflower florets with cold water to prevent it from cooking further. While the cauliflower florets are blanching, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('6128a6bc312d2963f71466d8','6128a56b90169a0ec9a83802',4,'P4: Prep other Ingredients','For Gobhi Aloo Matar Sabzi, peel, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of chopped onions. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes. Wash and finely chop 1 nos green chili. Wash, peel, and julienne a half-inch piece of ginger. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves. After boiling the potatoes, take it out from the pressure cooker and gently peel off the skin. Then, cut it into medium pieces.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6128a7db44613cc23f0a7408','6128a56b90169a0ec9a83802',5,'M1: Temper Spices','To make Aloo Gobhi Matar Sabzi, heat 1.5 tablespoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add 1 nos bay leaf followed by half a teaspoon of cumin seeds and allow it to splutter for a few seconds. Then, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions and fry it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes, until it turns translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6128a83844613cc23f0a7409','6128a56b90169a0ec9a83802',6,'M2: Cook the masala','After frying the onions, add a teaspoon of ginger-garlic paste and mix it well. Add 1 nos chopped green chili and saute it over medium flame for a minute. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes and mix it well. Saute and cook the tomatoes over medium-low flame until it turns tender. Then, add 1/4 cup of tomato puree and mix it well. Saute and cook the masala over medium flame for another 3-4 minutes, until oil separates.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6128a89090169a0ec9a83804','6128a56b90169a0ec9a83802',7,'M3: Add Masala Powders','After cooking the masala, add 1 teaspoon of red chili powder followed by 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder and half a teaspoon of coriander powder. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of chat masala along with 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala and mix it well. Saute and fry the masala over low flame for 2-3 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6128a8c790169a0ec9a83805','6128a56b90169a0ec9a83802',8,'M4: Continue Cooking the Sabzi','After frying the masala well, add half a teaspoon of Kasuri methi and mix it well.  Add half a cup of water and stir it well. Then, bring it to a boil while stirring in between. Next, add 2 tablespoons of chopped coriander leaves and stir it well. Add 1/4 cup of boiled and cubed potatoes and mix it well. Next, add half a cup of blanched cauliflower florets followed by 1/4 cup of blanched green peas and mix it well. Add a teaspoon of salt and stir it well. Then, cover it with a lid and allow it to simmer for 5-6 minutes. While it is simmering, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('6128a8fc44613cc23f0a740a','6128a56b90169a0ec9a83802',9,'M5: Garnish & serve','After simmering the Aloo Gobhi Sabzi, take off the lid and mix it well. Add a half-inch piece of sliced ginger to it and mix it well. Then, turn off the flame and take it out into a serving bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6128b0f490169a0ec9a83810','6128b0c244613cc23f0a740f',1,'P1: Soak Rice','For Methi Pulao, wash and soak 1 cup of basmati rice in 2 cups of water for 30 minutes. While the rice is soaking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":30,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6128b18990169a0ec9a83811','6128b0c244613cc23f0a740f',2,'P2: Prep Ingredients','For Methi Pulao, wash and roughly chop 1 cup of fenugreek leaves. Peel, wash and finely slice half a cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Wash and chop 2 tablespoons of mint leaves. Wash and peel a 1-inch piece of ginger. Wash and peel 5 cloves of garlic. Wash and slit 2 nos green chillis. Next, to make ginger garlic-paste, in a blender jar add 5 cloves of garlic along with a one-inch piece of ginger and 2 nos slit green chilies and blend it well into a smooth paste.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6128b20790169a0ec9a83812','6128b0c244613cc23f0a740f',3,'M1: Temper the oil with whole spices','To make Methi Pulao, heat 2 teaspoons of ghee along with 1 tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Add half an inch piece of cinnamon stick, 4 nos cloves, 2 nos green cardamoms, 1 nos star anise, and 1 nos bay leaf and saute it over low flame for a minute. Next, add half a cup of sliced onions and fry it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6128b258312d2963f71466e1','6128b0c244613cc23f0a740f',4,'M2: Fry the fenugreek leaves','After frying the onions, add the prepared ginger-garlic-green chili paste and saute it over medium flame for a minute. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes and mix it well. Saute and cook the tomatoes over medium flame for 4-5 minutes until tender. Next, add 1 cup of chopped fenugreek leaves and saute it over low flame for 2-3 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('6128b2a090169a0ec9a83813','6128b0c244613cc23f0a740f',5,'M3: Add rice & pressure cook the pulao','Next, add a teaspoon of salt followed by 2 teaspoons of red chili powder and mix it well. Next, add 1 cup of soaked basmati rice and mix it well with the masala. Saute it over medium flame for a minute. Then, add 2 tablespoons of chopped mint leaves along with 2 cups of water and stir it well. Then, cover it with a lid and pressure cook the rice over a high flame until one whistle. After that, reduce the flame to low and continue to simmer it for another 8 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the rice is cooking, please move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('612cb2d944613cc23f0a7413','612cb16544613cc23f0a7412',1,'P1- Prepare the tea mix','To prepare the spice mix for the digestive tea, in a blender jar add 1 tbsp fenugreek seeds, add 1 tbsp fennel seeds, add 1 tbsp black peppercorns then cover it with a lid and blitz it into a dry coarse mixture. Store the prepared mix in an air-tight container until further use.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('612cb32144613cc23f0a7414','612cb16544613cc23f0a7412',2,'M1- Boil the tea mix & serve the tea','To make the digestive tea, first, add 2 cups of water to a saucepan and bring it to a boil over high flame. As the water begins to boil, add 2 teaspoons of the prepared tea mix and bring it to a rolling boil, then allow it to simmer over low flame for 1-2 minutes to let the spices infuse the flavor completely in the water. Then, turn off the flame, and strain the tea into a kettle. Pour the tea into the serving cups and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('612cb4b090169a0ec9a83850','612cb47990169a0ec9a8384f',1,'AP1- Soak the cashews','To soak the cashews for no egg mayonnaise, rinse 3/4 cup cashew nuts well in water. Then, add them to a bowl and soak the cashew nuts in 1.5 cups of water for 30 minutes. While the cashew nuts are soaking move towards the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":30,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('612cb4ee44613cc23f0a7416','612cb47990169a0ec9a8384f',2,'P1- Prep the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for no egg mayonnaise, peel 3 cloves garlic; wash a lime and cut it into half, remove the seeds and squeeze about 1 tablespoon lemon juice and keep aside; strain the soaked cashew nuts and keep aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('612cb531312d2963f71466ee','612cb47990169a0ec9a8384f',3,'M1- Prepare the mayonnaise & serve','To make the no egg mayonnaise, take a blender jar and add the soaked cashew nuts followed by 3 garlic cloves, 2 teaspoons of oil, half a teaspoon of salt, 1 tbsp of water, 1 tbsp of lemon juice, and then blitz it into a fine paste. Remove it in a bowl and it is ready to use.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('612e0929312d2963f71466f2','612e0895312d2963f71466f1',1,'p1- prep the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Mango salsa, wash, peel and finely chop 1 cup of ripe mango. Then wash green capsicum in half, remove the seeds and finely chop 1/4 cup green capsicum. Peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onion. Wash and finely chop 1 tbsp of coriander leaves. Wash and finely chop 1 green chili.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('612e099e44613cc23f0a7419','612e0895312d2963f71466f1',2,'m1- combine the diced ingredients & prepare the salsa','To make the mango salsa, in a mixing bowl add 1/4 cup of chopped onions, followed by 1 cup of chopped ripe mangoes, and 1/4 cup of chopped green capsicum. Next, add 1 chopped green chill and a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves. Season the salsa with 0.5 tsp of pepper powder and 0.5 tsp of black salt. Add 2 teaspoons of olive oil, followed by a tablespoon of lemon juice, and mix it well. Remove the salsa in a serving bowl and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('612e0e7e312d2963f71466f3','612e0e4b90169a0ec9a83853',1,'p1- pre-heat the pressure cooker','For the Pressure Cooker Pund Cake, to pre-heat the pressure cooker, add 2 cups of salt to a pressure cooker and spread it to the base of the cooker using a spatula to form the base for keeping the cake mould, then place a stand, cover the cooker with a lid, and allow the cooker to pre-heat over low flame for about 20 mins. Make sure to remove the gasket and whistle from the lid. Next, to line the cake mould grease it with half a teaspoon of cooking oil, then dust some wheat flour on top and to the sides of the mould, then tap the cake mould to get rid of the extra flour and set it aside. While the pressure cooker pre-heats, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('612e0ef0312d2963f71466f4','612e0e4b90169a0ec9a83853',2,'m1- whisk the eggs and add milk','To make the pressure cooker pound cake, first, crack 2 eggs in a large mixing bowl, and whisk them well using a whisk until the eggs turn frothy and light yellow in color. Next, add in half a cup of milk followed by 2 tablespoons of curd and mix it well to prepare the liquid mix.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('612e0f5544613cc23f0a741b','612e0e4b90169a0ec9a83853',3,'m2- prepare the batter','Next, to prepare the flour mix, add 1 cup of whole wheat flour to another mixing bowl, followed by a teaspoon of baking powder, 1/4 teaspoon of baking soda, 1/4 teaspoon of salt, and half a cup of jaggery powder. Then, mix it well. Next, add in the flour mixture to the whisked eggs and fold in the dry ingredients with spatula part by part to prepare the batter. Mix until everything is well combined and do not over mix the batter.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('612e0fa390169a0ec9a83854','612e0e4b90169a0ec9a83853',4,'m3- bake the cake in the pressure cooker','To bake the pressure cooker pound cake, transfer the prepared cake batter into the greased mould immediately without resting it. Then, tap the mould to level the batter in. Then, carefully place the cake mould onto the stand in the pre-heated pressure cooker. Cover it with a lid and allow it the cake to cook over medium flame for 30 mins or until the top of the cake becomes slightly brown and the cake is cooked through. Make sure to remove the gasket and whistle from the lid. While the cake is baking in the cooker, please move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":30,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('612e1007312d2963f71466f5','612e0e4b90169a0ec9a83853',5,'m4- slice the cake & serve','After simmering the pressure cooker pound cake, check if the cake is cooked through by inserting a toothpick in the center of the cake. If it comes out clean the cake is well cooked and is ready. If the toothpick does not come out clean with wet batter stuck to it, then allow it to cook for another 3-4 mins. After that, turn off the flame and carefully remove the cake mold from the cooker and allow it to cool. After the cake cools, carefully remove the cake from the mold. Slice it and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('612f2efc312d2963f71466f7','612f2eaf312d2963f71466f6',1,'p1- simmer the milk','To prepare the saffron milk for Angoori Rasmalai, heat a heavy bottom vessel and add 250 ml of milk in it and bring to boil on medium flame, then lower the flame and continue to simmer the milk for 25 mins over low flame until it thickens, keep stirring the milk at regular intervals. While the milk is simmering move towards the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":25,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('612f2f4a44613cc23f0a741e','612f2eaf312d2963f71466f6',2,'p2- prepare the chenna','To prepare the Chena for Angoori Rasmalai, add 500 ml of milk to a heavy botoom vessel and bring it to boil over medium flame. Keep stirring the milk at regular intervals as it boils. Then, turn off the flame and add 1/4 cup of cold water to reduce the temperature of the milk and allow it to sit for a min. Then, add a tablespoon of lemon juice and stir it slowly as shown until the milk curdles. Then, drain the water from the chenna using a large strainer. Then hold the strainer with chenna under running water to get rid of the taste of lemon juice. Next, allow the chenna to rest in the strainer for 5 minutes to let the extra water drain off. Meanwhile, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('612f2fa390169a0ec9a83856','612f2eaf312d2963f71466f6',3,'p3- prepare the chenna balls','For Angoori Rasmalai, soak 2 strands of saffrons in 1/4 cup of water for 10 minutes. Next, finely slice 1 tablespoon of pistachios for the garnish. Next, to prepare the chenna balls, first, squeeze out the extra water from the chenna as shown and remove it in a large bowl. Add half a teaspoon of cornflour and mix it well. Then, mash and knead the dough by rubbing it with the end of your palm against the flat surface to form a soft dough. Continue to knead the dough for about 10 minutes until the chenna turns smooth. Then, divide it into equal portions and shape them into small-sized balls as shown.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('612f2fff312d2963f71466f8','612f2eaf312d2963f71466f6',4,'p4- prepare the saffron milk','After simmering the saffron milk for Angoori Rasmalai, the milk has thickened and reached the desired consistency. Then, add 2 soaked saffron strands, 1/4 tsp of cardamom powder followed by 1/4 cup of jaggery powder, and mix it well until the jaggery is completely dissolved in the milk. Then, add a tablespoon of chopped pistachios and mix it well. Turn off the flame and keep it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('612f307d44613cc23f0a741f','612f2eaf312d2963f71466f6',5,'m1- simmer the chenna balls in jaggery syrup','To make the Jaggery Syrup for Angoori Rasmalai, add half a cup of jaggery to a pan followed by 2 cups of water and bring to boil over the medium flame while stirring it continuously. Once the jaggery syrup slightly thickens and starts to boil, add in the prepared chenna balls one by one and allow it to simmer in the jaggery syrup over low flame for 8-10 minutes until the chenna balls fluff up and start to float in the syrup. While the chenna balls simmer, please move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('612f30e0312d2963f71466f9','612f2eaf312d2963f71466f6',6,'m2- soak the chenna balls in saffron milk & serve','After simmering the chenna balls in the jaggery syrup, turn off the flame and carefully remove the balls in a bowl filled with half a cup of water. Next, to assemble the rasmalai, transfer the prepared saffron milk to a bowl. Then, gently squeeze the soaked chenna balls one by one as shown and add them to the saffron milk. Then, refrigerate the rasmalai for 2-3 hours. After that, remove the rasmalai in a serving bowl and garnish it with chopped pistachios. Serve','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":3,"flame":0}'),('612f34bd312d2963f71466fa','612f343b44613cc23f0a7421',1,'p1- prepare the dal mixture','For leftover dal ka parantha, Wash, peel and finely chop 1/2 inch piece of ginger; wash and finely chop 1 tbsp coriander leaves. Wash and finely chop 1 green chilli and set aside. Next heat a pan with a teaspoon of cookin oil and temper it wth 1/2 teaspoon of cumin seeds. Add 1/2 inch piece of chopped ginger, 1 green chili and saute ot for a few seconds. Next, add the leftover cooked dal and season it with salt as per taste. Then allow the dal to cook on medium-low flame for 4-5 minutes. until it becomes thick in consistency, keep stirring the dal at regular intervals to prevent it from sticking to the bottom of the pan. After the dal reaches a thick consistency, turn off the flame and allow it to cool for some time.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('612f34f944613cc23f0a7422','612f343b44613cc23f0a7421',2,'p2- knead the dough','To prepare the dough for leftover dal ka parantha, in a mixing bowl add the cooked dal, add 1 cup wheat flour, and chopped coriander leaves and knead it well into a soft dough. Cover the dough with a damp cloth and allow it to rest for 10 mins. While the dough rests, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('612f354290169a0ec9a83857','612f343b44613cc23f0a7421',3,'m1- prepare the parathas & serve','To make the leftover dal parantha, heat up a tawa on low flame for 1-2 minutes. While the tawa is heating up, divide the dough into equal dough balls and slightly flatten the dough ball between your palms and roll it out into a round shape using the rolling pin. Then, tranfer the rolled paratha onto the hot tawa and cook it over medium flame for a minute. Then, add a teasoon of oil on each side and roast the paratha over medium flame for 1-2 minutes until it is evenly evenly cooked on both sides. Then, remove it onto a serving plate and serve','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6130836690169a0ec9a83858','61308308312d2963f71466fd',1,'p1- prep the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Shahi Paneer, first, in a bowl, soak 1 tablespoon of cashew nuts and 1 tablespoon of almonds in 1/4 cup of water for 15 minutes. Next, peel, wash, and finely slice half a cup of onion. Wash and finely chop half a cup of tomatoes. Wash and finely chop 1 green chili. Then, cut 1 cup paneer into cubes and keep aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":16,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('613083e5312d2963f71466fe','61308308312d2963f71466fd',2,'p2- prepare the masala mixture','To prepare the masala paste for shahi paneer, heat a pan and add 2 tablespoons of cooking oil and allow it to become hot, then add the sliced onions and saute it on a medium flame for 2-3 minutes until it turns slightly golden. Next, add the soaked cashew nuts and almonds followed by 1/4 tsp cumin seeds, 1 clove, 1/2 inch piece of cinnamon stick, and 1 chopped green chili. Saute and cook the onions over medium flame for another 1-2 minutes until they turn golden brown.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61308511312d2963f71466ff','61308308312d2963f71466fd',3,'p3- blend the masala mixture to prepare the paste','Next, add half a cup of chopped tomatoes and mix it well. Stir and cook the tomatoes over medium flame for 3-4 minutes until tender. Then, turn off the flame and allow the mixture to cool down for some time. After the mixture has cooled, transfer the prepared mixture to a blender jar and blend it well into a smooth paste. Remove it in a bowl and keep it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('6130882d44613cc23f0a7423','61308308312d2963f71466fd',4,'m1- cook the masala','To cook the gravy for shahi paneer, heat a pan and add 1 tablespoon of cooking oil and allow it to become hot, then add a teaspoon of ginger garlic paste and saute for a minute until the raw smell fades away. Then, 1/2 tsp chili powder, 1/4 tsp turmeric powder, and 1/4 tsp garam masala. Mix it well and cook the masala over low flame for 1-2 minutes until oil separates. Next, add the prepared masala paste and mix it well. Stir and cook the masala over medium for 2-3 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('613088f5312d2963f7146700','61308308312d2963f71466fd',5,'m2-  add paneer & simmer the curry','After the raw smell goes and the onion-tomato paste looks cooked, reduce the flame to low, and then add half a cup of milk, followed by half a teaspoon of green cardamom powder, 2 strands of saffron, and half a teaspoon of salt. Mix it well. Stir and cook the gravy over low flame for 2-3 minutes until the gravy is slightly thickened. Keep stirring occasionally to prevent the gravy from sticking to the bottom and burning. Next, add 1 cup of cubed paneer and mix it well. Simmer the panner with the gravy for 3-4 minutes. Then, add 1/2 tsp of crushed Kasuri methi and mix it well. Turn off the flame and take out the paneer in a serving bowl. Garnish it with some cashew nuts and sliced almonds. Serve','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61309652312d2963f7146701','61308b9444613cc23f0a7424',1,'p1- prepare the jaggery base','For apple outside down cake, to prepare the base, in a bowl add 1/4 cup jaggery powder, add 1 tbsp cooking oil and 3/4 tsp of cinnamon powder and mix well to form a crumbly mixture. Then, take a baking tin and grease it well by brushing some oil on the base of the tin. Then evenly spread the prepared jaggery mixture on the greased cake tin and keep aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6130968d312d2963f7146702','61308b9444613cc23f0a7424',2,'p2- slice the apple','For apple upside-down cake, to slice the apple, wash 1 medium-sized apple and remove the core, then cut the apple into half and finely slice it as shown. Next, in a bowl add 1.5 cups of water and soak the sliced apple until further use to prevent it from decoloring.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61309717312d2963f7146703','61308b9444613cc23f0a7424',3,'m1- pre-heat the oven & prepare the batter','For Apple Upside Down cake, first, set the oven to pre-heat at 180 degrees celsius for 7 mins. Next, to prepare the batter, in a mixing bowl, add 1 cup of whole wheat flour, followed by add 1 tsp of baking powder, 1/4 tsp of baking soda, half a teaspoon of cinnamon powder, and 1/4 teaspoon of salt. Then, mix it well and combine the dry ingredients using a spatula.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('6130977b312d2963f7146704','61308b9444613cc23f0a7424',4,'m2- set the cake in the oven to bake','Next, in another bowl, add half a cup of jaggery powder followed by half a cup of milk and a tablespoon of cooking oil. Then, mix it well using a whisk until the jaggery dissolves.  After that, combine the dry ingredients part by part with the wet ingredients and mix them well to form a smooth lump-free batter. The batter should be of pourable consistency. Next, arrange the apple slices in the greased cake mold covering the base as shown and pour in the prepared batter.  Level the cake batter by patting the cake tin, this will also break the air bubbles if any.  Then, set it inside the pre-heated oven and allow the cake to bake at 180 degrees Celcius for 25-30 minutes. While the cake is in the oven, please move onto the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":30,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":30,"flame":0}'),('613097b1312d2963f7146705','61308b9444613cc23f0a7424',5,'m3- slice the cake & serve','After baking the Apple Upside-Down Cake, check if the cake is done by inserting a toothpick in the center, and if the toothpick comes out clean then the cake is done, if the toothpick comes out with uncooked batter stuck to it allow the cake to bake for another 2 mins. After that, remove the cake from the oven and allow the cake to completely cool. Next, to unmold the cake, place an inverted plate on the top of the cake tin, and hold the plate from the base and flip the cake tin over on the plate. The sliced apple should be facing the top. Slice the cake pieces and serve warm','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('613f6a6fb9ce8a38e88410b1','613f69fceb89ec14c5d7a855',1,'p1-peel & dice the jackfruit','For Jackfruit Halwa, first, apply some oil to the palms and grease the knife with some oil. Then peel, and slit the jackfruit in half, and remove the seeds. Applying oil to the palms before cutting the jackruit is important since it tends to stick to the palms and knife making it difficult to make the clean cuts. Also, make sure to use a sharp knife for cutting the jackfruit. Then, using the greased sharp knife, finely chop 2 cups of the jackfruit and set it aside','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('613f6c93eb89ec14c5d7a856','613f69fceb89ec14c5d7a855',2,'p2- toast the nuts','To toast the nuts for Jackfruit Halwa, heat a teaspoon of ghee in a pan for a minute. Then, add a tablespoon of cashews followed by a tablespoon of raisins and toast the nuts over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until the nuts are slightly golden. Then, turn off the flame and remove the toasted nuts in a bowl','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('613f6dc5467b552b4ec7bd94','613f69fceb89ec14c5d7a855',3,'m1- simmer the halwa','To make jackfruit halwa, add 1/4 cup of jaggery to a pan followed by 2 cups of chopped jackfruit and mix it well. Stir and cook it over low flame for 3-4 minutes until the jaggery dissolves. Then, add 3/4 cup of milk, and 2 green cardamom pods and mix it well. Then, cover it with a lid and allow it to simmer for 8-10 minutes until the jackfruit is tender and mushy and milk is reduced completely. Keep stirring it at regular intervals to prevent the halwa from burning. While the halwa simmers, please move on to the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('613f6e23467b552b4ec7bd95','613f69fceb89ec14c5d7a855',4,'m2- cook the halwa & serve','After simmering the jackfruit halwa, take off the lid and stir it well. Halwa has absorbed the milk and has thickened. Next, add half a teaspoon of cardamom powder followed by the toasted nuts and mix it well. Stir and cook the halwa over medium flame for another 2-3 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and remove the halwa in the serving bowls. Garnish it with some toasted nuts and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('613f989d467b552b4ec7bd97','613f9829eb89ec14c5d7a857',1,'p1- prepare the ingredients','For pumpkin risotto, thoroughly rinse 1 cup of arborio rice, drain the water and keep the washed rice aside. Then peel and finely chop half a cup of onion. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of leeks; Wash peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of carrot. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of celery. Peel and finely chop 1 tablespoon of garlic. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of parsley','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('613f990cb9ce8a38e88410b3','613f9829eb89ec14c5d7a857',2,'p2- dice the pumpkin & toast the pumpkin seeds','For pumpkin Rissoto, peel and wash the pumpkin, cut it into half and remove the seeds, then cut 3/4 cup pumpkin into dice. Then, grate 1/4 cup of parmesan cheese and remove it in a bowl. To toast the pumpkin seeds, heat a pan and dry roast 1 tbsp of pumpkin seeds on a medium flame for 1 min or until they become slightly golden brown, store it in an airtight container and keep it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('613f9994467b552b4ec7bd98','613f9829eb89ec14c5d7a857',3,'m1- simmer the pumpkin','To cook the pumpkin, heat 1 teaspoon of olive oil in a frying pan over medium flame for a minute. Next, add a teaspoon of sliced garlic, followed by 3/4 cup of diced pumpkin, and saute it on a medium flame for a minute. Then, add 1/4 cup of water allow the pumpkin to cook over medium flame for 2-3 minutes. Then, season it with 1 tsp salt and 1/4 tsp pepper powder. Mix it well and add half a cup of water. Then, continue to cook the pumpkin over low fame for 5-6 minutes until it is tender. After that, add a tablespoon of chopped parsley and set it aside. While the pumpkin simmers, please move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('613f9a15eb89ec14c5d7a858','613f9829eb89ec14c5d7a857',4,'m2- fry the vegetables & add rice','To make the risotto, heat a pan and add 2 tsp of olive oil, allow it to become hot, and then add 2 tablespoons of finely chopped celery, 1/4 cup of chopped carrots, 1/4 cup f chopped leeks, 1/2 cup of chopped onions, and 2 teaspoons of chopped garlic. Stir and fry the vegetables over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until translucent. Then add 1 cup of rinsed arborio rice and saute it well until toasted. The rice grains should not change their color, next add 1 tsp thyme and mix it well, then add 1 tsp apple cider vinegar and mix it well.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('613f9a52eb89ec14c5d7a859','613f9829eb89ec14c5d7a857',5,'m3- simmer the rice','Next, add the vegetable stock to the rice in 3 parts, water can be used in place of vegetable stock. After every addition of 1 cup of vegetable stock gently mix the rice to prevent from damaging the rice grains and cook it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes. After the last addition of vegetable stock, cover it with the lid and allow the rice grains to cook on medium-low flame for 7-8 minutes until it has absorbed most of the water and the rice is cooked through. While the rice simmers, please move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('613f9acdb9ce8a38e88410b4','613f9829eb89ec14c5d7a857',6,'m4- Garnish & serve','After simmering the risotto, add 1/2 teaspoon of black pepper powder, half a teaspoon of salt, and 1/4 cup of grated parmesan cheese. Mix it well and cook it for another minute. Next, add 1 tablespoon of chopped parsley and mix it, add in the sauteed pumpkin dices and combine it well. Then, turn off the flame and plate the pumpkin risotto onto a serving plate. Garnish it with toasted pumpkin seeds and chopped parsley. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('61dea0e3725519e05259e4eb','61dea07b725519e05259e4ea',1,'P1- Prepare the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Ragi Ambli, first, wash and finely chop 1 green chili. Wash, peel, and grate a half-inch piece of ginger. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash and pick 7 curry leaves. Next, to make the ragi slurry, add 2 tablespoons of finger millet flour to a bowl followed by half a cup of water and mix it well until smooth.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61dea12f03bacf9265243281','61dea07b725519e05259e4ea',2,'M1- Simmer the ragi slurry with buttermilk','To make the Ragi Ambli, add 1.5 cups of water to a saucepan and bring it to a rolling boil over high flame. As the water comes to a boil, add the prepared finger millet flour slurry and keep stirring it continuously as shown to avoid any lumps. Then, allow it to cook over medium flame for a minute. Next, add 3/4 teaspoon of salt and bring it to a boil. Then, reduce the flame to low and add in half a cup of buttermilk. Stir and cook the ambli over medium flame for 1-2 minutes and bring it to a boil. Then, turn off the flame and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61deaab3725519e05259e4ec','61dea07b725519e05259e4ea',3,'M2- Add the tempering to the Ambli & serve','To make the tempering for Ragi Ambli, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame. Then, add 1/4 teaspoon of mustard seeds followed by 7 curry leaves, 1/4 teaspoon of hing, 1 chopped green chili, and a half-inch piece of grated ginger. Saute and let it splutter over medium flame for a few seconds. Then, turn off the flame and add the tempering to the prepared ambli. Mix it well  and garnish it with a tablespoon of coriander leaves and serve','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('61deaf2e03bacf9265243282','61deaecc725519e05259e4ee',1,'P1- Grate coconut','To prepare the ingredients for Flax Seeds Chutney Powder, finely slice 2 tablespoons of dry coconut. Wash and pick 15 curry leaves','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61deaf6d56901577ca528ddb','61deaecc725519e05259e4ee',2,'M1- Dry roast the flax seeds & urad dal','To make the Flax Seeds Chutney Powder, first, add half a cup of flax seeds to a pan and dry roast them over medium flame for 2-3 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and remove the roasted seeds in a bowl or a plate. Next, add 1/4 cup of urad dal to the same pan and dry roast it over medium flame for 3-4 minutes until it is slightly golden in color. Then, turn off the flame and remove the roasted lentil on the same plate.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('61deb07703bacf9265243283','61deaecc725519e05259e4ee',3,'M2- Grind the roasted flax seeds with the spices & lentils','Next, to the same pan, add 2 tablespoons of sliced coconut, 15 nos curry leaves, a tablespoon of tamarind. Saute and roast them over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Then, remove them on the same plate. After that, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in the same pan over medium flame. Add 7 dry red chilies and roast them over low flame for 2-3 minutes until the chilies fluff up as shown. Then, turn off the flame and remove the chilies on the same plate with all the other roasted ingredients. Next, add a teaspoon of salt, 1 teaspoon of cumin powder, along with a teaspoon of jaggery, and transfer the roasted ingredients to a blender jar. Cover the jar with a lid and grind it well into a fine powder. Remove the chutney powder in an air-tight container and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('61dec1a6725519e05259e4f0','61dec13f56901577ca528ddc',1,'AP1- Soak the rice and urad dal','For Banana Lead Idli, first, add 3/4 cup of urad dal to a bowl and rinse it well in water. Then, soak it in 2 cups of water for 2 hours. Next, add 1.5 cups of idli rice to another bowl and rinse it well. Then, soak the rice in 3 cups of water for 2 hours. While the dal and rice soak, please move on to the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":120,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61dec778725519e05259e4f1','61dec13f56901577ca528ddc',2,'AP2-  Blend the soaked dal & rice to prepare the batter','To prepare the batter for Banana Leaf Idli, add the soaked urad dal to a blender jar and blend it well into a smooth paste. Then, remove the urad dal paste into a deep vessel. Next, add the soaked rice to the blender jar and blend it into a slightly coarse batter. Remove the rice batter to the same vessel and mix it well. Combine the urad dal and rice batter properly and make sure to keep the batter in a large vessel to make sure there is enough space for the batter to rise. Then, cover it with a lid and allow the batter to ferment for 8-10 hours. While the batter ferments, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":480,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('61dec7cf03bacf9265243285','61dec13f56901577ca528ddc',3,'P1- Prepare the banana leaf molds','To prepare the banana leaf molds for the Banana leaf Idli, first, wash the banana leaves well with water and wipe them off with a kitchen towel. Then, put the banana leaf over the direct low flame as shown and slightly heat it on each side evenly. This will soften the banana leaf making it easier to shape it into molds. Heat the banana leaf until its color is slightly changed. Then, carefully split the leaf in two as shown and discard the stem. Next, roll the leaf over a long glass and tie it together using a thread as shown. Cut the extra thread and trim the extra leaf. Then, carefully remove the glass and fix the ends using the toothpick. Make the rest of the banana leaf cups similarly.','prep_method','{"active_time":17,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('61dec80603bacf9265243286','61dec13f56901577ca528ddc',4,'M1- Steam the idlis and serve','To make the Banana leaf idli, add a teaspoon of salt to the fermented batter and mix it well. Add some water and adjust the consistency of the batter if it is too thick. Then, set up the steamer and place the banana leaf cups into the steamer as shown. Then, carefully pour the batter into the banana leaf cups. Cover it with a lid and steam cook the idlis over medium-high flame for 30 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and carefully the idlis onto a plate. Gently remove the banana leaf and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":30,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61decc14725519e05259e4f3','61decbb156901577ca528ddd',1,'P1- Prepare the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Chayote Chutney, wash and peel 2 medium-sized chayotes as shown and keep the peels slightly thick. Next, wash and slit 1 green chili. Wash, and pick 15 curry leaves. Grate 1/4 cup of coconut in a bowl.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61decc4503bacf9265243287','61decbb156901577ca528ddd',2,'M1- Fry the chayote peels','To make the Chayote Chutney, heat a teaspoon of ghee in a pan over medium flame. Add 3/4 cup of chayote peels and fry them over medium-low flame for 2-3 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and remove them onto a plate.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61deccd9725519e05259e4f4','61decbb156901577ca528ddd',3,'M2-  Prepare the chutney','To make the Chayote Chutney, heat a teaspoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame. Next, add a tablespoon of urad dal followed by 2 dry red chilies, 1 slit green chili, and 7 curry leaves. Saute it over low flame for a minute until the urad dal is slightly golden. Then, turn off the flame and remove the tempering on a plate. Next, add the prepared tempering to a blender jar along with 3/4 cup of roasted chayote peels. Add 1/4 cup of grated coconut, a teaspoon of tamarind, a teaspoon of salt along with 1/4 cup of water. Cover the jar with a lid and blend it well into a smooth chutney. Remove it in a bowl and set it aside','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('61decd1d56901577ca528dde','61decbb156901577ca528ddd',4,'M3- Add the tempering to the chutney & serve','To make the tempering for Chayote Chutney, heat a teaspoon of cooking oil in a small tempering pan over medium flame. Next, add half a teaspoon of mustard seeds followed by 8 curry leaves and let it splutter for a few seconds. Then, turn off the flame and add the tempering to the chutney. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61e002329658247a5c977be1','61e000c0e4038b7cb9b3522a',1,'p1- dice the chayote','To prepare the ingredients for Chayote Palya, first, wash, peel and dice 1.5 cups of chayote into small cubes. Next, wash and slit 1 green chili. Wash and pick 7 curry leaves. Grate 1/4 cup of coconut using a grater.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61e0055d56901577ca528de1','61e000c0e4038b7cb9b3522a',2,'m1- Simmer the palya','To make Chayote Palya, heat a teaspoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Next, add half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, half a teaspoon of urad dal, and 7 curry leaves. Add 1 dry red chili and let it splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 1.5 cups of diced chayote and mix it well. Add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, followed by a teaspoon of salt, and mix it well. Then, add half a cup of water and cover it with a lid. Allow it to simmer over low flame for 5-7 minutes until tender. While the palya simmers, please move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":7,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('61e005be56901577ca528de2','61e000c0e4038b7cb9b3522a',3,'m2- make the masala powder','To make the coconut masala powder for Chayote Palya, add 1/4 cup of grated coconut to a blender jar along with 1 dry red chili, 1 slit green chili, and half a teaspoon of cumin seeds. Cover the jar with a lid and grind it well into a slightly coarse masala powder','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61e0060fe4038b7cb9b3522b','61e000c0e4038b7cb9b3522a',4,'m3- add the coconut masala powder & fry the palya','After simmering the Chayote Palya, carefully remove the lid, add 1 tsp of jaggery and add the prepared coconut masala powder. Mix it well and cook it over medium flame for a minute. Then, turn off the flame and remove the palya in a serving bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('61e00c60e4038b7cb9b3522c','61e00ad456901577ca528de3',1,'p1- prepare  the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Tuppada Avalakkai, first, peel, wash and finely chop half a cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 2 green chilies. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of curry leaves. Grate 1/4 cup of fresh coconut using a grater in a bowl.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61e00ce79658247a5c977be3','61e00ad456901577ca528de3',2,'m1- roast the cashews and peanuts','To roast the nuts for Tuppada Avalakkai, heat a tablespoon of ghee in a pan over medium flame. Then, add a tablespoon of peanuts and roast them over medium fame for 1-2 minutes. Next, add a tablespoon of cashews and roast them over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until peanuts and cashews turn slightly golden. Then, turn off the flame and remove the nuts in a bowl.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61e00d7e56901577ca528de4','61e00ad456901577ca528de3',3,'m2- fry the onions','To make the Tuppada Avalakkai, add a tablespoon of ghee to the same pan and heat it over medium flame. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of mustard seeds and 1/4 teaspoon of cumin seeds. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Then, add half a cup of chopped onions followed by a tablespoon of chopped curry leaves, and 2 chopped green chilies. Saute and fry the onions over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until it is translucent. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of sugar, half a teaspoon of salt, and mix it well. Saute the onions for another minute. Then, turn off the flame and remove it in a mixing bowl.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61e00e2c56901577ca528de5','61e00ad456901577ca528de3',4,'m3- make the chivda and serve','To make the Tuppada Avalakkai, add 1.5 cups of thin rice flakes to the prepared onion tempering followed by 1/4 cup of grated fresh coconut and mix it well. Next, add a tablespoon of lime juice along with the roasted peanuts and cashews. Mix it well and garnish it with a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves. Plate the avalakkai and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61e011d9e4038b7cb9b3522e','61e0112fe4038b7cb9b3522d',1,'p1- Grate coconut and prepare other ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Turmeric Leaves Dumpling, first, rinse and clean 5 turmeric leaves and wipe off the water with a kitchen towel. Grate 1.25 cups of fresh coconut using a grater. Next, add half a cup of grated coconut to a blender jar along with 1/4 cup of water and blend it well into a coarse paste.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":1,"flame":0}'),
('61e01437e4038b7cb9b3522f','61e0112fe4038b7cb9b3522d',2,'p2- Roast the rava','To roast the rava for Turmeric Leaves Dumpling, add 1 cup of rava to a pan and dry roast it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes. Keep stirring the Rava continuously. Roast the Rava until it slightly changes color. Then, turn off the flame and remove it in a bowl.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":1,"flame":3}'),('61e014cee4038b7cb9b35230','61e0112fe4038b7cb9b3522d',3,'p3- Prepare the batter','To prepare the rava batter for Turmeric Leaves Dumpling, add 1 cup of roasted rava to a mixing bowl. Next, add the prepared coconut paste and combine it well. Add about 1/4 cup of water and mix it well. Season it with half a teaspoon of salt and combine it well to prepare a loose dough as shown.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":1,"flame":0}'),('61e0150d56901577ca528de7','61e0112fe4038b7cb9b3522d',4,'m1- Make the jaggery syrup','To make the jaggery coconut mixture for Turmeric Leaves Dumpling, first, add 3/4 cup of jaggery to a pan followed by 2 tablespoons of water. Mix it well and cook it over medium flame for 5-6 minutes until jaggery melts and dissolves completely in water. Then, turn off the flame and strain the syrup in a bowl.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61e01552e4038b7cb9b35231','61e0112fe4038b7cb9b3522d',5,'m2- make the jaggery & coconut stuffing','Next, add the jaggery syrup back into the same pan and cook it over medium flame for a minute. Then, add 3/4 cup of grated fresh coconut and mix it well. Stir and cook it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until it slightly thickens. Next, add half a teaspoon of cardamom powder and a teaspoon of poppy seeds. Mix it well and cook the mixture for another minute. Then, turn off the flame and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61e015a79658247a5c977be5','61e0112fe4038b7cb9b3522d',6,'m3- Steam the dumplings & serve','To make the Turmeric Leaves Dumpling, spread a thin layer of the prepared Rava batter onto the turmeric leaf as shown. Next, spread a thin layer of the prepared jaggery coconut stuffing onto it and gently fold the leaf as shown. Prepare the rest of the dumplings similarly. Then, carefully place them inside the steamer. Cover it with a lid and steam cook the dumplings over medium for 15 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and carefully remove the dumplings onto a plate. Gently remove the leaves and plate the dumplings. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('61e01d60e4038b7cb9b35234','61e01ccce4038b7cb9b35233',1,'p1- prepare the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Ladies Finger Fry, first, soak a teaspoon of tamarind in 1/4 cup of water for 10 minutes. Next, rinse and clean the ladies finger thoroughly with water. Then, spread them on a kitchen towel and dry them off completely before slicing. Wipe off the extra moisture from the ladies fingers and make sure they are completely dry. Then, remove the cap and thin bottom part and slice 2 cups of ladies fingers into rondelles as shown. Next, grate 1/4 cup of fresh coconut using a grater. Wash and pick 7 curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61e01e089658247a5c977be6','61e01ccce4038b7cb9b35233',2,'m1- simmer the ladies fingers','To make the ladies fingers fry, heat a tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame. Add 1/2 a teaspoon of mustard seeds followed by half a teaspoon of urad dal and let it splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 7 curry leaves and saute them for a few seconds. Then, add 2 cups of sliced ladies fingers to the tempering and fry them over medium flame for a minute. Add a teaspoon of jaggery followed by the soaked tamarind. Mash the tamarind in water and add strain the pulp in the pan as shown. Next, add a teaspoon of salt along with 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder and mix it well. Then, cover it with a lid and allow the ladies finger to simmer over low flame for 7-8 minutes until tender. Keep stirring in between. While it simmers, please move on to the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61e01ed7e4038b7cb9b35235','61e01ccce4038b7cb9b35233',3,'m2- make coconut masala powder','To make the coconut masala powder for Ladies Finger Fry, add 1/4 cup of grated coconut to a blender jar followed by 2 dry red chilies and half a teaspoon of mustard seeds. Then, cover the jar with a lid and grind it into a coarse powder without adding any water.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61e0205356901577ca528de8','61e01ccce4038b7cb9b35233',4,'m3- fry the ladies fingers with masala powder & serve','After simmering the ladies fingers for Ladies Finger Fry carefully remove the lid and add the prepared coconut masala powder. Then, gently mix it well and stir-fry the ladies fingers over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and remove the sabzi in a serving bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61e68ccd5f33d3b52575a325','61e68c71596d96fe725430a1',1,'p1- prep the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Raw Mango Rasam, first, wash, peel and dice 1 medium-sized raw mango into small cubes. Wash and slit 1 green chili. Wash and pick 7 curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('61e68d132725bf1a655c5f24','61e68c71596d96fe725430a1',2,'m1- simmer the raw mangoes','To make the Raw Mango Rasam, add 3/4 cup of diced raw mango to a deep bottom pan along with 1 cup of water. Then, boil the raw mango over medium flame for 5-6 minutes until turns soft and mashy. While it simmers, please move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('61e68dc45f33d3b52575a326','61e68c71596d96fe725430a1',3,'m2- add the spices & boil the rasam','After boiling the raw mango for Raw Mango Rasam, turn off the flame and mash it well using a masher as shown. Next, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame. Add half a teaspoon of cumin seeds, half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, 1 dry red chili, and 1/4 teaspoon of hing. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 7 curry leaves along with 1 slit green chili and saute it for another few seconds. After that, add 2 cups of water followed by 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, 1 tablespoon of jaggery, and 1 teaspoon of salt. Mix it well and bring it to a rolling boil. Then, add the mashed raw mangoes and mix it well. Boil the rasam for a minute over medium flame. Then, turn off the flame and serve','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61e690c1596d96fe725430a2','61e690745f33d3b52575a328',1,'p1- peel and steam-cook the raw bananas','For Balekayi Palya, wash and peel 2 medium-sized raw bananas. Then, add 1 cup of water to a pressure cooker. Carefully place a cooking stand inside it and place a steel plate over the stand. Next, place the peeled raw bananas on the plate and cover the cooker with a lid. Then, pressure cook the raw bananas over medium flame for 6 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and let the pressure from the cooker release naturally. While the bananas are steam-cooking, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61e696545f33d3b52575a329','61e690745f33d3b52575a328',2,'p2- grate the steamed bananas and prep other ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Balekayi Palya, wash and finely chop 1 green chili. Grate 2 tablespoons of fresh coconut using a grater. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash and pick 7 curry leaves. Next, after steam-cooking the bananas, carefully remove them from the pressure cooker and gently peel off the upper layer as shown. Then, grate the bananas using a grater.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61e6973b5f33d3b52575a32a','61e690745f33d3b52575a328',3,'m1- Fry the grated bananas with spices & serve','To make Balekayi Palya, heat 2 tablespoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame. Then, temper it with half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, half a teaspoon of urad dal, half a teaspoon of chana dal, and 7 curry leaves. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 1 chopped green chili followed by the steamed grated bananas and mix it well. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powfer and mix it well. Then add a teaspoon of salt and sprinkle about 2 tablespoons of water. Mix it well and cover it with a lid. Then, allow it to simmer for 1-2 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and add 2 tablespoons of grated coconut, 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves, and a tablespoon of lime juice. Mix it well and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('61e69b665f33d3b52575a32b','61e69b312725bf1a655c5f26',1,'ap1- Soak the chickpeas','For Chickpeas Cabbage Palya, soak half a cup of chickpeas in 2 cups of water for 8 hours. While the chickpeas are soaking, please move on to the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":480,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61e69bad2725bf1a655c5f27','61e69b312725bf1a655c5f26',2,'p1- Boil the chickpeas','To boil the chickpeas for Chickpeas Cabbage Palya, add the soaked chickpeas to a pressure cooker along with 1 cup of water. Then, cover the cooker with a lid and pressure cook it over a high flame until three whistles. After that, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook it for another 10 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally.  While the chickpeas are boiling, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":18,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61e69c112725bf1a655c5f28','61e69b312725bf1a655c5f26',3,'p2- Shred cabbage and prep other ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Chickpeas Cabbage Palya, wash and finely shred 1.5 cups of cabbage. Grate 1/4 cup of fresh coconut using a grater. Wash and pick 7 curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61e69ca0596d96fe725430a3','61e69b312725bf1a655c5f26',4,'m1- Simmer the cabbage','To make Chickpeas Cabbage Palya, heat a tablespoon of cooking in a pan over medium flame. Then, add half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, half a teaspoon of urad dal, 7 curry leaves, and 1 dry red chili. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 1.5 cups of chopped cabbage and mix it well. Add half a teaspoon of salt along with 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder and mix it well. Sprinkle about 2 tablespoons of water and cover it with a lid. Then, allow it to cook over medium flame for 5-7 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":7,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('61e69d285f33d3b52575a32c','61e69b312725bf1a655c5f26',5,'m2- Make the coconut masala powder','To make the masala powder for Chickpeas Cabbage Palya, add 1/4 cup of grated coconut to a blender jar followed by half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, half a teaspoon of cumin seeds, 1 dry red chili, and 1 teaspoon of tamarind. Cover the jar with a lid and grind it into a coarse masala powder.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('61e69d992725bf1a655c5f29','61e69b312725bf1a655c5f26',6,'m3- Add the boiled chickpeas and  ground masala powder.  Simmer & serve','After simmering the cabbage for Chickpeas Cabbage Palya, remove the lid and add the boiled chickpeas. Mix it well and add the ground masala powder. Combine it well and fry the palya for a few seconds. Then, cover it with a lid and simmer it for another 2 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and serve','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61e6a1912725bf1a655c5f2a','61e6a0215f33d3b52575a32e',1,'p1- boil the toor dal','For Rajagiri Soppina Muddi Palya, first, soak 2 teaspoons of tamarind in 1/4 cup of water for 15 minutes. Next, to boil the dal, add 1/4 cup of toor dal to a bowl followed by 1 tablespoon of chana dal and rinse it well in water. Then, add the lentils to a pressure cooker along with 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder and half a cup of water. Cover the lid and pressure cooker the dal over high flame until two whistles. Then, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook the dal for another 5 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and let the cooker release the pressure naturally. While the dal simmers, please move on to the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61e6a2515f33d3b52575a32f','61e6a0215f33d3b52575a32e',2,'p2- chop the amaranth leaves & prepare the masala paste','To prepare the ingredients for Rajagiri Soppina Muddi Palya,  first, rinse and clean a bunch of amaranth leaves thoroughly with water. Then, pat dry the greens and remove the thick stems.  Next, finely chop 2.5 cups of the amaranth leaves. Wash and slit 2 green chilies. Wash and roughly chop 1/4 cup of coriander leaves. Wash and pick 7 curry leaves. Next, to make the masala paste, add 2 green chilies to a blender jar followed by half a teaspoon of cumin seeds, 1 teaspoon of coriander seeds, 3-4 fenugreek seeds, 1/4 teaspoon of hing, and 1/4 cup of coriander leaves. Then, cover the jar with a lid and blend it well into a fine paste.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61e6ab155f33d3b52575a330','61e6a0215f33d3b52575a32e',3,'m1- stir & fry the amaranth leaves','To make Rajagiri Soppina Muddi Palya, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame. Then, temper it with half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, half a teaspoon of cumin seeds, 7 curry leaves, and 1/4 teaspoon of hing. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 2.5 cups of chopped amaranth leaves followed by 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder and 3/4 teaspoon of salt. Mix it well and saute the palya over low flame for 5 minutes until the leaves start to wilt as shown.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":1,"flame":3}'),('61e6ab7e2725bf1a655c5f2b','61e6a0215f33d3b52575a32e',4,'m2- simmer the palya & serve','Next, add the prepared masala paste and mix it well. Saute and cook the amaranth leaves with the masala over medium flame for 3 minutes. Next, mash the soaked tamarind in water and add the pulp in the palya followed by half a teaspoon of red chili powder and half a teaspoon of jaggery. After that, add the boiled dal followed by a tablespoon of peanuts, and mix it well. Add about half a cup of water and give it a sir. Cover the pan with a lid and allow it to simmer for 5 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and garnish it with some chopped coriander leaves. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('61e7ec5e5f33d3b52575a346','61e7ec0b79acbd5abef140a4',1,'p1- Boil the barley','To boil the barley for Barley Ganji, first, add 3/4 cup of barley to a steel bowl and rinse it well. Then, drain the extra water and place the steel bowl inside the pressure cooker as shown. Next, add 2 cups of water to the barley and cover the bowl with a steel plate.  Cover pressure cooker with a lid and pressure cook the barley over a high flame until 3 whistles. Then, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook it for another 10 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and let the cooker release the pressure naturally. While the barley simmers, please move on to the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":14,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":3,"flame":3}'),('61e7ed075f33d3b52575a347','61e7ec0b79acbd5abef140a4',2,'p2- Prep the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Barley Ganji, peel, wash, and grate a half-inch piece of ginger. Wash and finely chop 1 green chili. Wash and pick 7 curry leaves. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61e7edf94af638932b6590cc','61e7ec0b79acbd5abef140a4',3,'m1- Combine curd and boiled barley','To make the Barley Ganji, after pressure cooking the barley, remove the lid off the pressure cooker and carefully take out the steel bowl. Then, strain the barley using a strainer as shown. Save the barley stock for later use. Next, add the boiled barley to a blender jar and blend it into a coarse paste. Next, transfer the barley paste to the same bowl with barley stock. Add half a cup of curd, followed by half a teaspoon of salt, and mix it well.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61e7ee825f33d3b52575a349','61e7ec0b79acbd5abef140a4',4,'m2- Add the tempering to Ganji and serve','To make the tempering for Barley Ganji, heat 1 tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame. Add a teaspoon of mustard seeds, a teaspoon of cumin seeds, 7 curry leaves, half-inch piece of grated ginger, and 1 chopped green chili. Saute and let the tempering splutter for a few seconds. Then, turn off the flame and add it to the prepared Ganji. Mix it well and garnish it with a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61e7f17279acbd5abef140a7','61e7f1115f33d3b52575a34a',1,'p1- prep the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Raw Banana Palya, first, soak 1 tablespoon of tamarind in 1/4 cup of water for 10 minutes. Next, peel 2 medium-sized raw bananas and dice them into small cubes. Grate 1/4 cup of fresh coconut. Wash and slit 1 green chili. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves. Wash and pick 10 curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}');
INSERT INTO catalog_recipe_steps VALUES
('61e7f22079acbd5abef140a8','61e7f1115f33d3b52575a34a',2,'m1- simmer the raw bananas','To make Raw Banana Palya, heat 1 tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame. Then, temper it with a teaspoon of mustard seeds, a teaspoon of urad dal, 10 curry leaves, and 2 dry red chilies. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 1 slit of green chili and saute it for a few seconds. After that, add 2 cups of diced raw banana and fry it for a minute. Add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder followed by a teaspoon of jaggery, a teaspoon of salt, and the soaked tamarind. Mash the tamarind and add the pulp to the palya. Mix it well and add about 1/4 cup of water. Then, cover it with a lid and allow it to cook over low flame for 7-8 minutes. While the palya simmers, please  move on to the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":7,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61e7f2af79acbd5abef140a9','61e7f1115f33d3b52575a34a',3,'m2- grind the masala powder','To make the masala powder for Raw Banana Palya, add 2 tablespoons of grated coconut to a pan and dry roast it over low flame for 1-2 minutes. Then, remove it into a blender jar. Next, to the same pan, add a tablespoon of chana dal followed by a tablespoon of urad dal and roast them over medium flame for 2-3 minutes. Add a tablespoon of coriander seeds and roast it for another 1-2 minutes. Then, remove the roasted spices to the same blender jar. Next, to the same pan add 4 dry red chilies along with 2 teaspoons of cooking oil and roast them over low flame for 1-2 minutes. Then, turn off the flame add the chilies to the blender jar, and grind it well into a fine powder.','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('61e7f2ea4af638932b6590cf','61e7f1115f33d3b52575a34a',4,'m3- fry the palya with the masala powder & serve','After simmering, the Raw Banana Palya, remove the lid, and give it a stir. Next, add 2 teaspoons of the prepared masala powder followed by 2 tablespoons of grated coconut and mix it well. Saute and fry the palya over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and remove it in a serving bowl. Garnish it with some chopped coriander leaves and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61e7fb7e5f33d3b52575a34e','61e7f84579acbd5abef140ab',1,'p1- boil the dalia','For Broken Wheat Bisi Bele Bath, first, soak a tablespoon of tamarind in 1/4 cup of water for 15 minutes. Next, to boil the Dalia, rinse and clean 1 cup of Dalia thoroughly with water and add it to a pressure cooker along with 3 cups of water. Then, cover the cooker with a lid and pressure cook it over a high flame until two whistles. After that, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook it for another 8 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally.  While the dalia is boiling, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61e7fbeb5f33d3b52575a34f','61e7f84579acbd5abef140ab',2,'p2- bol the dal','To boil the dal for Broken Wheat Bisi Bele Bath, first, rinse and clean 1/4 cup of toor dal well with water and add it to a pressure cooker along with 1 cup of water and 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder. Then, cover it with a lid and pressure cook the dal over a high flame until one whistle. After that, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook it for another 8 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and let the pressure from the cooker release naturally. While the dal is boiling, please move on to the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('61e7fca64af638932b6590d1','61e7f84579acbd5abef140ab',3,'p3- prep the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for  Broken Wheat Bisi Bele Bath, wash and cut 1/4 cup of beans into 1 inch long pieces. Wash, peel, and dice 1/4 cup of carrots. Peel and wash 1/4 cup of green peas. Wash and pick 7 curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61e7fcfc5f33d3b52575a350','61e7f84579acbd5abef140ab',4,'m1- simmer the vegetables','To make  Broken Wheat Bisi Bele Bath, add 1 cup of water to a deep bottom pan followed by 1/4 cup of chopped beans, 1/4 cup of chopped carrots, and 1/4 cup of green peas. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder along with half a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Then, allow the vegetables to cook over medium-low flame for 5-6 minutes. While the vegetables simmer, please move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61e7fe6479acbd5abef140ac','61e7f84579acbd5abef140ab',5,'m2- add the boiled dal & dalia','After simmering the vegetables for Broken Wheat Bisi Bele Bath, mash the soaked tamarind in the water and add the pulp to the vegetables. Next, add a teaspoon of jaggery followed by 2 teaspoons of bisi bele bath. Mix it well and continue to cook the vegetables for another 2-3 minutes until tender. Then, add the boiled dal along with 1/4 teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Next, add the boiled dalia and combine it well with the vegetables. Simmer the bath for 2 minutes while stirring in between. Then, turn off the flame and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61e7fedd4af638932b6590d2','61e7f84579acbd5abef140ab',6,'m3- add the tempering & serve','To make the tempering for Broken Wheat Bisi Bele Bath, heat 2 teaspoons of ghee in a small tempering pan. Add half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, half a teaspoon of urad dal, 7 curry leaves, and 1 dry red chili. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Next, add a tablespoon of cashew nuts and saute it for another minute. Then, turn off the flame and add the tempering to the prepared bisi bele bath. Mix it well and remove it in a serving bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61ea9813710b3b894d728345','61ea976c710b3b894d728344',1,'p1- prep the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Bread Upma, first, peel, wash, and finely chop half a cup of onions. Wash and finely chop half a cup of tomatoes. Peel and cut half-inch piece of ginger  into juliennes. Wash and slit 1 green chili.  Wash and finely chop a tablespoon of coriander leaves. Wash and cut a lime into halves and squeeze a tablespoon of lime juice into a bowl. Wash and pick 7 curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('61ea997ed5a8fe92761c9514','61ea976c710b3b894d728344',2,'p2- toast the bread slices','To toast the bread slices for bread upma, first, heat a tablespoon of butter in a pan over low flame. Spread the butter across the pan and place the bread slices. Then, toast them over medium-low flame for 3-4 minutes until they are crisp and evenly browned on all sides. Similarly, toast all the 6 bread slices and remove them on a cutting board. Then, cut the bread slices into small pieces as shown.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61ea99d9d5a8fe92761c9515','61ea976c710b3b894d728344',3,'m1- fry the onions and simmer the tomatoes','To make Bread Upma, heat 2 tablespoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame. Then, temper it with 1/4 teaspoon of mustard seeds, and 7 curry leaves. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Next, add half a cup of chopped onions followed by a half-inch piece of grated ginger and 2 slit green chilies. Saute and fry the onions over medium flame for 3-4 minutes until translucent. After that, add half a cup of chopped tomatoes and mix it well. Then, cover it with a lid and cook the tomatoes over low flame for 2-3 minutes until tender.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61ea9a5fd5a8fe92761c9516','61ea976c710b3b894d728344',4,'m2- add the roasted bread cubes and spices','After cooking the tomatoes for Bread Upma, remove the lid and add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder followed by half a teaspoon of red chili powder, half a teaspoon of salt, and a teaspoon of sugar. Mix it well and add 2 tablespoons of water. Saute and cook the masala over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. After that, add the toasted bread pieces and gently coat them with the masala. Add a tablespoon of lime juice and mix it well. Turn off the flame and garnish it with a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves. Plate the bread upma and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61eaa079710b3b894d72836c','61eaa00b710b3b894d72836b',1,'p1- cut the raw mangoes and grate coconut','To prepare the ingredients for Raw Mango Curry, first, wash 2 medium-sized raw mangoes and cut them into wedges without peeling. Next, grate half a cup of fresh coconut using a grater. Wash and pick 7 curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61eaa0d0710b3b894d72836d','61eaa00b710b3b894d72836b',2,'m1- simmer the raw mangoes','To make the Raw Mango Curry, add 1.5 cups of raw mango wedges to a deep bottom pan followed by 1 cup of water. Next, add 2 tablespoons of jaggery, and a teaspoon of salt. Mix it well and cover it with a lid. Then, allow it to cook over low flame for 7-8 minutes until the raw mangoes are tender. While the raw mangoes simmer, please move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('61eaa12f710b3b894d72836e','61eaa00b710b3b894d72836b',3,'m2- make the coconut masala paste','To make the coconut masala paste for Raw Mango Curry, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame. Next, add 2 teaspoons of urad dal, 2 teaspoons of coriander seeds, 1/2 teaspoon of fenugreek seeds and 2 dry red chilies. Saute and roast the spices over low flame for 2-3 minutes until the lentils turn golden brown in color. Then, turn off the flame and remove the roasted spices into a blender jar. Add half a cup of grated coconut along with half a cup of water and blend it well into a smooth paste.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61eaa1b761a09c469f1262ca','61eaa00b710b3b894d72836b',4,'m3- add the masala paste and cook the curry','After simmering the Raw Mango Curry, remove the lid and add the prepared masala paste. Mix it well and bring it to a boil over medium flame. Then, turn off the flame and set it aside. Next, to make the tempering, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a small tempering pan. Add half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, half a teaspoon of urad dal, 1 dry red chili, and 7 curry leaves. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Then, turn off the flame and add the tempering to the curry. Mix it well and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61eaa68fd5a8fe92761c951a','61eaa451710b3b894d728371',1,'ap1- soak the moth beans','For Matki Usal, add 3/4 cup of moth beans to a bowl and soak them in 2 cups of water for 8-10 hours. While the beans are soaking, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":480,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61eaa6f1d5a8fe92761c951b','61eaa451710b3b894d728371',2,'ap2- sprout the soaked moth beans','To sprout the moth beans for Matki Usal, after soaking the moth beans, drain off the water and transfer the soaked beans to a cotton cloth as shown. Then, tie the moth beans into a tight bundle and keep it inside a bowl. Sprinkle some water on the bundle and cover the bowl with a lid. Then, let the moth beans sprout for 8-10 hours. While the beans sprout, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":480,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61eaa77661a09c469f1262cb','61eaa451710b3b894d728371',3,'p1- prep the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Matki Usal, peel, wash, and finely chop half a cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Wash, peel, and roughly chop a half-inch piece of ginger. Wash and slit 2 green chilies. Peel 4 cloves of garlic. Wash and chop 1/4 cup of coriander leaves. Wash and pick 7 curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('61eaa8d0d5a8fe92761c951c','61eaa451710b3b894d728371',4,'p2- prepare the ginger garlic and green chili paste','To prepare the ginger garlic paste for Matki Usal, add 2 green chilies to a blender jar followed by 4 cloves of garlic and a half-inch piece of chopped ginger. Add 3 tablespoons of coriander leaves along with 1/4 teaspoon of salt. Then, cover the jar with a lid and blend it into a fine paste.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61eaa92061a09c469f1262cc','61eaa451710b3b894d728371',5,'m1- fry the onions','To make Matki Usal, heat a tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame. Then, add 1/4 teaspoon of mustard seeds and let it splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of cumin seeds and 7 curry leaves. Saute and let them splutter. Next, add half a cup of chopped onions and fry them over medium flame for 2-3 minutes, until translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61eaa994710b3b894d728372','61eaa451710b3b894d728371',6,'m2- cook the moth beans with the masala & serve','After frying the onions, add 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes and cook them for 2-3 minutes until tomatoes are slightly tender. Add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder followed by the prepared ginger garlic paste, and mix it well. Saute and cook the masala for 1-2 minutes until the raw smell of garlic fades away. Then, add the prepared moth beans sprouts and mix them well. Add about 2-3 tablespoons of water and cover it with a lid. Allow the moth beans to cook over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Then remove the lid and add 2 teaspoons of niger seeds powder. Mix it well and turn off the flame. Remove the matki usal in the serving bowl. Garnish it with some chopped coriander leaves and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61eaafe561a09c469f1262ce','61eaafa061a09c469f1262cd',1,'ap1- soak the chana dal','For Cluster Beans Matodi Palya, first, add half a cup of chana dal to a bowl and rinse it well with water. Then, soak it in 1 cup of water for 3 hours. While the lentil is soaking, please move on to the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":180,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61eab0ced5a8fe92761c951d','61eaafa061a09c469f1262cd',2,'p1- chop the ingredients and prepare other ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Cluster Beans Matodi Palya, first, rinse and clean cluster beans well with water. Then, trim the ends remove the threads from the edges as shown, and finely chop 2 cups of the cluster beans. Next, grate half a cup of fresh coconut. Wash and slit 2 green chilies. Wash and pick 7 curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('61eab13961a09c469f1262cf','61eaafa061a09c469f1262cd',3,'m1- simmer the cluster beans','To make Cluster Beans Matodi Palya, heat 2 tablespoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame. Then, temper it with half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, 7 curry leaves, 1/4 teaspoon of hing, and 1 dry red chili. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 2 cups of chopped cluster beans followed by a teaspoon of salt and half a teaspoon of turmeric powder. Mix it well and add about 1/4 cup of water. Then, cover the pan with a lid and allow it to simmer over low flame for 7-8 minutes until tender. While it simmers, please move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('61eab189710b3b894d728374','61eaafa061a09c469f1262cd',4,'m2- make the masala paste','To make the coconut paste for Cluster Beans Mtodi Palya, add half a cup of grated coconut to a blender jar. Next, drain the water from the soaked chana dal and add it to the blender jar along with 2 slit chillies. Cove the jar with a lid and blend it well into a coarse paste.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61eab1cfd5a8fe92761c951e','61eaafa061a09c469f1262cd',5,'m3- add the masala paste and simmer the palya','After simmering the Cluster Beans Matodi Palya, carefully remove the lid and fry them over medium flame for a minute to reduce the moisture. Next, add the prepared coconut paste and spread it evenly on the palya as shown. Then, cover the pan with a lid and allow it to cook over medium flame for 5 minutes. While it simmers, please move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('61eab20bd5a8fe92761c951f','61eaafa061a09c469f1262cd',6,'m4- fry the palya and serve','After simmering the Cluster Beans Matodi Palya, remove the lid and give it a stir. Coconut and lentil paste is steam cooked perfectly. Stir and fry the palya over medium flame for another 2-3 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and remove it in a serving bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61eab502710b3b894d728375','61eab4abd5a8fe92761c9520',1,'p1- pressure cook the dal','For Soppu Saaru, first, soak 1 tablespoon of tamarind in 1/4 cup of water for 15 minutes. Next, rinse 3/4 cup of toor dal with water and add it to a pressure cooker along with 1.25 cups of water. Then, cover it with a lid and pressure cook the dal over a high flame until one whistle. After that, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook the dal over low flame for another 8 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and let the cooker release the pressure naturally. While the dal is boiling, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('61eab55b710b3b894d728376','61eab4abd5a8fe92761c9520',2,'p2- prep the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for soppu saaru, first, rinse and clean a bunch of amaranth leaves thoroughly with water. Then, pat dry the greens and finely chop 1 cup of the amaranth leaves. Next, grate 1/4 cup of fresh coconut using a grater. Wash and pick 7 curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61eab596d5a8fe92761c9521','61eab4abd5a8fe92761c9520',3,'m1- simmer the amaranth leaves','To make Soppu Saaru, add 1 cup of chopped amaranth leaves to a deep bottom pan along with 3/4  cup of water. Then, cover it with a lid and allow it cook over medium-low flame for 7 minutes until the leaves turn dark in color. While the greens simmer, please move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":7,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61eab5d461a09c469f1262d0','61eab4abd5a8fe92761c9520',4,'m2- make the masala paste','To make the masala paste for Soppu Saaru, add 1/4 cup of grated coconut to a blender jar followed by 1 tablespoon of sambar powder and 1/4 cup of water. Cover the jar with a lid and blend it well into a smooth paste','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61eab641d5a8fe92761c9522','61eab4abd5a8fe92761c9520',5,'m3- simmer the sambar','After simmering the amaranth leaves for Soppu Saaru, remove the lid and give it a stir. Then, squeeze and add the tamarind pulp followed by a teaspoon of jaggery and half a teaspoon of salt. Mix it well and let it boil over medium flame for 5 minutes. While sambar boils, please move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61eab6a5710b3b894d728377','61eab4abd5a8fe92761c9520',6,'m4- add the tadka to the sambhar and serve','After boiling the amaranth leaves for Soppu Saaru, add the ground coconut masala paste followed by the boiled toor dal. Mix it well and bring it to a boil over medium flame. Then, turn off the flame and set it aside. Next, to prepare the tempering for Saaru, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a small tempering pan over medium flame. Add half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, 7 curry leaves, and 1/4 teaspoon of hing. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Then, turn off the flame and add the tempering to the prepared saaru. Mix it well and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('61eab8e761a09c469f1262d1','61eab882d5a8fe92761c9523',1,'p1- cut the brinjals','To prepare the ingredients for Badanekayi Palya, first, soak a tablespoon of tamarind in 1/4 cup of water for 15 minutes. Next, wash 3 small green brinjals well with water. Then, remove the crown part and cut the brinjals into wedges as shown. Soak the sliced wedges into the water until used to prevent them from browning. Next, wash and pick 7 curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61eab96f61a09c469f1262d2','61eab882d5a8fe92761c9523',2,'m1- simmer the brinjals','To make Badanekayi Palya, heat 2.5 tablespoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame. Then, add half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, half a teaspoon of urad dal, and 7 curry leaves. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Next, add the sliced brinjal followed by 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, a tablespoon of jaggery, 3/4 teaspoon of salt, and mix it well. Then, cover it with a lid and cook it over low flame for 8-10 minutes, while stirring in between. Cook the brinjals until tender. While the brinjals simmer, please move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('61eab9b561a09c469f1262d3','61eab882d5a8fe92761c9523',3,'m2-  add the masla powders and cook the palya','After simmering the Badanekayi Palya, carefully remove the lid and add 1.5 tablespoons of rasam powder. Mix it well and saute the palya over medium flame for a minute. Next, add the soaked tamarind juice and mix it well. Turn off the flame and remove the palya in a serving bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61ee6f43d5a8fe92761c9571','61ee6ebed5a8fe92761c9570',1,'p1- prepare the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Cucumber Curry, first, wash and finely chop 2 medium-sized cucumbers. Next, grate half a cup of fresh coconut using a grater in a bowl. Wash and slit 2 green chilies. Wash and pick 7 curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61ee6f92c61f719bb3eb1250','61ee6ebed5a8fe92761c9570',2,'p2- grind the coconut masala paste','To prepare the coconut masala paste for Cucumber Curry, add half a cup of grated coconut to a blender jar followed by 2 green chilies, and 1 teaspoon white sesame seeds. Add half a cup of water and cover the jar with a lid. Then, blend it well into a smooth paste.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('61ee6ff2c61f719bb3eb1251','61ee6ebed5a8fe92761c9570',3,'m1- fry the diced cucumber','To make Cucumber Curry, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame. Add half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, followed by half a teaspoon of urad dal, and 7 curry leaves. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Next, add a teaspoon of sesame seeds and saute it over low flame for a minute. After that, add 1.5 cups of chopped cucumber and mix it well. Saute and fry the cucumber over medium flame for 2 minutes until it turns pale. Then, turn off the flame and remove it in a mixing bowl.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61ee7036d5a8fe92761c9572','61ee6ebed5a8fe92761c9570',4,'m2- add the masala paste and curd. Cook the curry & serve','Next, to the sauteed cucumber, add the prepared coconut masala paste followed by half a cup of curd. Season it with 3/4 teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Remove the curry into a serving bowl and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61ee7a6d159d3ae2a6bf3701','61ee7a10c61f719bb3eb1252',1,'p1- dice the cucumber & grate coconut','To prepare the ingredients for Southekayi Gojju, wash and finely chop 2 medium-sized cucumbers. Grate half a cup of fresh coconut using a grater. Wash and pick 7 curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61ee7ac6159d3ae2a6bf3702','61ee7a10c61f719bb3eb1252',2,'p2- prepare the masala paste','To make the masala paste for Southekayi Gojju, add half a cup of grated coconut to a blender jar followed by half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, 1 dry red chili, and 1 tablespoon of tamarind. Add 1/4 cup of water and cover the jar with a lid. Then, blend it well into a smooth paste.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61ee7b33159d3ae2a6bf3703','61ee7a10c61f719bb3eb1252',3,'m1- prepare the curry & serve','To make Southekayi Gojju, add the ground masala paste to a mixing bowl. Next, add 1.5 cups of chopped cucumber followed by 3/4 teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Next, to make the tempering, heat 2 teaspoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame. Add half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, half a teaspoon of urad dal, 1 dry red chili, and 7 curry leaves. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Then, turn off the flame and add the tempering to the gojju. Mix it well and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('61ee8553159d3ae2a6bf3705','61ee8443159d3ae2a6bf3704',1,'p1- rinse & clean the lentil and broken wheat','To prepare the ingredients for Dalia Pongal, first, rinse and clean 1/4 cup of yellow moong dal with water. Next, rinse and clean half a cup of broken wheat with water. Grate 1 tablespoon of fresh coconut using a grater. Wash,  Wash and pick 7 curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61ee90cbc61f719bb3eb1253','61ee8443159d3ae2a6bf3704',2,'m1- pressure cook the dalia','To make Dalia Pongal, add 1/4 cup of yellow moong dal to a pan and dry roast it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and transfer it to a pressure cooker. Next, add half a cup of dalia along with 2 cups of water. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, 3/4 teaspoon of salt, and mix it well. Then, cover it with a lid and pressure cook it over high flame until 3 whistles. Then, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook it for another 5 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the dalia is cooking, please move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61ee9139c61f719bb3eb1254','61ee8443159d3ae2a6bf3704',3,'m2- add the tempering to the pongal & serve','To make the tempering for Dalia Pongal, heat 2.5 tablespoons of ghee in a pan over medium flame. Add a teaspoon of cumin seeds, a teaspoon of crushed black peppercorns, 7 curry leaves, a half-inch piece of grated ginger, and a tablespoon of cashew nuts. Saute and let it splutter. Next, add the boiled dalia along with 1/4 cup of water and mix it well. Adjust the salt as per taste and bring it to a boil over medium flame. Then, turn off the flame, garnish with 1 tablespoon of grated coconut and Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61ee9477159d3ae2a6bf3706','61ee9408d5a8fe92761c9573',1,'p1- knead the dough','To prepare the dough for Rava Roti, add 1.25 cups of water to a saucepan followed by half a teaspoon of salt. Stir it well and a teaspoon of cooking oil. Then, bring it to a boil over high flame. After that, reduce the flame to low and add 1 cup of rava to the boiling water while stirring it continuously. Keep stirring it over low flame for 5 minutes until the rava comes together and forms a dough. Then, turn off the flame and remove it onto plate. Let it slightly cool down, then knead it well into a soft dough. Make sure to knead the dough while it is still warm. Then, cover it with a cloth and set it aside','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61ee94bb159d3ae2a6bf3707','61ee9408d5a8fe92761c9573',2,'m1- divide the dough and roll the roti','To make Rava Roti, divide the prepared rava dough into small equal-sized dough balls. Then, take a dough ball and dust some flour on it. Place it onto a rolling board and gently roll it into a thin round roti. You can use a round bowl to remove the uneven edges and cut them into a perfect round shape as shown. Then, gently roll it again to smoothen out the edges','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('61ee94f0d5a8fe92761c9574','61ee9408d5a8fe92761c9573',3,'m2- cook the roti and serve','Next, place the roti onto a hot Tava and cook it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes on each side until the small brown spots start to appear and the roti puffs up as shown. Then, remove the roti onto a serving plate and serve. Make the rest of the rotis similarly','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61ee97bdc61f719bb3eb1256','61ee9697c61f719bb3eb1255',1,'p1- soak the sabudana','For Sabudana Kheer, first, add 1/4 cup of sabudana to a bowl and soak it in half a cup of water for 30 minutes. Next, to soak the saffron, add in 2 tablespoons of milk to a small bowl and soak 2 strands of saffron in the milk for 10 minutes. While the sabudana and saffron soak, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":25,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61ee9821159d3ae2a6bf3708','61ee9697c61f719bb3eb1255',2,'p2- roast the nuts','To roast the nuts for Sabudana Kheer, heat a tablespoon of ghee in a small pan over medium flame. Next, add 1 tablespoon of raisins and roast them over medium-low flame for 1-2 minutes until the raisins puff up. Then, remove them in a bowl. Next, to the same pan, add a tablespoon of cashew nuts and roast them over medium flame for 2-3 minutes. After that, turn off the flame, remove the cashews in the same bowl, and set it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61ee9866159d3ae2a6bf3709','61ee9697c61f719bb3eb1255',3,'m1- simmer the kheer','To make Sabudana Kheer, add 2 cups of milk to a pan and bring it to a boil over high flame. Next, add the soaked sabudana and stir it well. Then, cover it with a lid and allow it to cook over low flame for 5 minutes. While the kheer simmers, please move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('61ee98add5a8fe92761c9575','61ee9697c61f719bb3eb1255',4,'m2- add sugar and continue to simmer the kheer','After simmering the Sabudana Kheer, remove the lid and give it a stir. Add 1/4 cup of sugar and mix it well. Next, cover the pan with a lid and continue to simmer it for another 10 minutes until it thickens. While the kheer simmers, please move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('61ee9a31c61f719bb3eb1257','61ee9697c61f719bb3eb1255',5,'m3- add the soaked saffron and serve the kheer','After simmering the Sabudana Kheer, carefully remove the lid and add the soaked saffron milk followed by 1/4 teaspoon of cardamom powder and the roasted nuts. Mix it well and turn off the flame. Divide the kheer among bowls and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61ee9deed5a8fe92761c9576','61ee9dc0c61f719bb3eb1258',1,'ap1- soak the lentil','For Curd Vada, add 3/4 cup of urad dal to a bowl and rinse it thoroughly with water. Then, soak it in 2 cups of water for 2 hours. While the lentil soaks, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":120,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61ee9e59d5a8fe92761c9577','61ee9dc0c61f719bb3eb1258',2,'p1- prepare the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Curd Vada, first, wash and finely chop 1 green chili. wash, peel and finely chop a half-inch piece of ginger. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves. Cut 1 tablespoon of coconut into small dice. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61ee9ead159d3ae2a6bf370a','61ee9dc0c61f719bb3eb1258',3,'p2- prepare the batter','To prepare the batter for Curd Vada, add the soaked urad dal to a blender jar along with 3 tablespoons of water and blend it well into a smooth batter. Then, remove it into a mixing bowl. Next, add 1 chopped green chili, 1 tablespoon of chopped curry leaves, a half-inch piece of chopped ginger, 2 teaspoons of Rava, 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves, and 3/4 teaspoon of salt. Add a tablespoon of chopped coconut and mix it well. Whisk the batter using a spoon for a minute and set it aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61ee9ef5d5a8fe92761c9578','61ee9dc0c61f719bb3eb1258',4,'m1- fry the vadas and soak in water','To fry the vada for Curd Vada, first, heat 1 cup of cooking oil in a kadai over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Once the oil is hot, apply some water to the fingers as shown and shape the prepared batter into the small vadas as shown. Then, carefully drop the vadas one by one into the hot oil and deep fry them over medium flame for 2-3 minutes. Fry the vadas until they are crisp and golden brown. Then, turn off the flame and remove them onto a kitchen napkin. Next, boil 2 cups of water in a saucepan and remove it in a large bowl. Then, soak the fried vadas in the hot water for 10 minutes. While the vadas soak in water, please move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('61ee9f61d5a8fe92761c9579','61ee9dc0c61f719bb3eb1258',5,'m2- squeeze the soaked vadas & add curd','To make Curd Vada, add 2 cups of curd to a mixing bowl followed by 3/4 teaspoon of salt, 3/4 teaspoon of sugar, and 1/4 cup of water. Mix it well until smooth. Next, squeeze out the water from the soaked vada and arrange them into a serving dish. Then, pour in the prepared curd over the vadas and add a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61ee9fa6d5a8fe92761c957a','61ee9dc0c61f719bb3eb1258',6,'m3- add the tempering and refrigerate the curd vada','To make the tempering for Curd Vada, heat a tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame. Next, temper it with half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, half a teaspoon of urad dal, and a tablespoon of curry leaves. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Then, turn off the flame and add the tempering to the prepared vadas. Allow the curd vadas to refrigerate for 30 minutes. Then, plate the curd vadas and garnish them with some boondi and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":30,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61efedb799421ad3f444f268','61efed03c61f719bb3eb1284',1,'p1- prepare the ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Soppina Majige Huli,first, soak 2 tablespoons of chana dal in 1/4 cup of water for 20 minutes. Next, wash and clean a bunch of green amaranth leaves thoroughly with water. Then, remove thick stems and finely chop 2 cups of amaranth leaves. Next, grate half a cup of fresh coconut using a grater. Wash and slit 3 green chilies. Wash, peel and roughly chop a half inch piece of ginger. Wash and roughly chop 1/4 cup of coriander leaves. Wash and pick 7 curry leaves. Next, add half a cup of curd to a bowl and whisk it well until smooth.','prep_method','{"active_time":20,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61efee47c61f719bb3eb1285','61efed03c61f719bb3eb1284',2,'m1- simmer the amaranth leaves','To make Soppina Majige Huli, heat a teaspoon of cooking oil in a deep bottom pan over medium flame. Next, add 2 cups of chopped amaranth leaves and fry them over low flame for a minute. Then, add 1 cup of water followed by half a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Cover it with a lid and allow it cook over low flame for 7-8 minutes. While it simmers, please move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61eff290c61f719bb3eb1286','61efed03c61f719bb3eb1284',3,'m2- grind the masala paste','To prepare the masala paste for Soppina Majige Huli, add 2 tablespoons of soaked chana dal to a blender jar followed by half a cup of grated coconut, 3 green chilies and a tablespoon of coriander seeds. Next, add a teaspoon of cumin seeds, half inch piece of ginger, 1/4 cup of chopped coriander leaves, and half a cup of water. Cover the jar with a lid and blend it well into a smooth paste.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('61eff399159d3ae2a6bf371e','61efed03c61f719bb3eb1284',4,'m3- add the masala paste and simmer the curry','After simmering the amaranth leaves for Soppina Majige Huli, remove the lid and give it a stir. Then, add the prepared coconut masala paste and mix it well. Stir and bring it to a boil over medium flame. After that, reduce the flame to low and add half a cup of whisked curd. Mix it well and add some water if required. Stir and cook it for a minute. Then, turn off the flame and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('61eff409159d3ae2a6bf371f','61efed03c61f719bb3eb1284',5,'m4- add the tempering & serve','To make the tempering for Soppina Majige Hili, heat 2 teaspoons of ghee in a small tempering pan over medium flame. Then, add half a teaspoon of cumin seeds, 7 curry leaves, and 1 dry red chili. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Then, turn off the flame and add the tempering to the prepared curry. Mix it well and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61eff8d899421ad3f444f26a','61eff84f99421ad3f444f269',1,'p1- dry roast and grind the flax seeds','To prepare the flax seeds powder for Flax Seeds Chapati, add 2 tablespoons of flax seeds to a pan and dry roast them over medium-low flame for 2-3 minutes. Keep stirring continuously and roast the seeds until they start popping up as shown. Next, turn off the flame and allow the roasted seeds to cool down for some time. Then, remove them in a blender jar and grind them into a fine powder','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('61eff945c61f719bb3eb1288','61eff84f99421ad3f444f269',2,'p2- knead the dough','To prepare the dough for Flax Seeds Chapati, add 1 cup of whole wheat flour to a large bowl followed by half a teaspoon of salt, 1/4 teaspoon of flax seeds and a teaspoon of cooking oil. Next, add the prepared flax seeds powder and mix it well. Then, about 3/4 cup of water and knead it well into a smooth dough. Cover it with a damp cloth and allow it to rest for 20 minutes. While the dough rests, please move on to the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61eff993159d3ae2a6bf3720','61eff84f99421ad3f444f269',3,'m1- cook the chapati and serve','To make the Flax Seeds Chapati, first, divide the prepared dough into equal-sized dough balls. Then, dust a dough ball in the flour and gently roll it into a thin round chapati. Next, place the rolled out chapati onto a hot tawa and cook it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until small brown spots appear on both the sides of chapati. Add half a teaspoon of ghee and remove it onto a serving plate. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('61effc3499421ad3f444f26b','61effbac159d3ae2a6bf3721',1,'p1- dice the bottle gourd and puree','To prepare the ingredients for Bottle Gourd Dosa, wash, peel and cube 1 cup of bottle gourd. Peel, wash and finely chop half a cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 2 green chilies. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of curry leaves. Wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves. Next, to make the bottle gourd puree, add the diced bottle gourd to a blender jar and blend it well into a smooth puree.','prep_method','{"active_time":18,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61effc97c61f719bb3eb1289','61effbac159d3ae2a6bf3721',2,'p2- prepare the batter','To prepare the batter for Bottle Gourd Dosa, transfer the prepared bottle gourd puree to a mixing bowl. Next, add 1 cup of rice flour followed by half a cup of semolina and mix it well. Add 2 cups of water and mix it well. Adjust water as per the requirement. The consistency of the batter should be slightly thin and flowy. Next, a teaspoon of salt, half a cup of chopped onions, 2 tablespoons of chopped curry leaves, 2 chopped green chilies, 2 tablespoons of chopped coriander leaves and a teaspoon of cumin seeds. Mix it well and cover it with a lid. Allow the batter to rest for 20 minutes. While the batter rests, please move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('61effceec61f719bb3eb128a','61effbac159d3ae2a6bf3721',3,'m1- make the dosa & serve','To make the Bottle Gourd Dosa, heat up a tawa over medium-high flame for 1-2 minutes. Once the tawa is hot grease it with half a teaspoon of cooking oil. Then, pour a ladlefull of the prepared batter on the tawa and spread it evenly as shown. Then, add a teaspoon of cooking oil and cover it with a lid. Cook the dosa over medium flame for 2-3 minutes. Then, remove the lid and gently fold the dosa. Remove it onto a serving plate and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('625553ae77eed6f6962bfb7e','62554f4945bb8da240aa3308',1,'P1: Prep the Ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Sev Tamatar Sabzi, first, wash and finely chop 1.25 cups of fresh tomatoes. Next, peel, wash and grate a half-inch piece of ginger. Wash and finely chop a tablespoon of fresh coriander leaves. Next, to prepare the tomato puree, add 3/4 cup of chopped tomatoes to a blender jar along with 1/4 cup of water and blend it well into a smooth puree.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('625554f677eed6f6962bfb7f','62554f4945bb8da240aa3308',2,'P2: Prepare the Gramflour Batter','To prepare the gram flour batter for Sev Tamatar Sabzi, add half a cup of gram flour to a large bowl followed by 1/4 teaspoon of salt, 1/4 teaspoon of red chili powder, 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder and 1 teaspoon of cooking oil. Mix it well and add about 1/4 cup of water. Then, knead it well into a slightly stiff dough.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('625555615bead4f59cb0b211','62554f4945bb8da240aa3308',3,'P3: Fry the Sev','To prepare the sev for Sev Tamatar Sabzi, heat 1 cup of cooking oil in a kadai over medium-high flame for 2-3 minutes. Once the oil is hot, take a small portion of the prepared besan dough and  press it over the perforated turner as shown. Then, deep fry the sev over medium flame for 3-4 minutes until they are crisp and golden brown. After that, remove the sev on a kitchen napkin to dab off the excess oil.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('6255572545bb8da240aa3309','62554f4945bb8da240aa3308',4,'M1: Prepare the tempering','To make Sev Tamatar Sabzi, heat a tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Next, temper it with half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, half a teaspoon of cumin seeds, 1/4 teaspoon of hing, and a half-inch piece of grated ginger. Next, add half a teaspoon of red chili powder, 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, half a teaspoon of coriander powder, and half a teaspoon of salt. Saute and cook the masala over low flame for a minute. Next, add in the prepared tomato puree and stir it well. Add about 1/4 cup of water and bring it to a boil. Next, add half a cup of chopped tomatoes and cover it with a lid. Then, allow it cook over low flame for 5-6 minutes until the tomatoes are tender. While the curry simmers, please move on to the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":5,"flame":1}'),('625558045bead4f59cb0b212','62554f4945bb8da240aa3308',5,'M2: Add the Sev and Simmer the Curry','After simmering the curry for Sev Tamatar Sabzi, remove the lid and add about 1/4 cup of water. Next, add half a teaspoon of sugar followed by 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala and mix it well. After that, add in the prepared besan sev and mix it well. Then, cover the pan with a lid and simmer the curry for another 2 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and garnish it with a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves. Serve','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":2,"flame":2}'),('6255647977eed6f6962bfb84','6255628e77eed6f6962bfb82',1,'P1: Stir fry the Wadi and Prep the ingredients','To roast the Wadiyan for Aloo Wadiyan, first heat a pan and add 2 teaspoons of cooking oil and allow it to become hot . After the oil becomes hot, add 1/4 cup of Amritsari Wadiyan and stir fry on medium low flame for 3 minutes or until it becomes slightly brown and crisp. Remove in a bowl and set aside. Next to prep the ingredients, wash and roughly chop 1 cup of tomatoes and add it to a blender jar. Blend it well to make a smooth puree. Remove in a bowl and set aside. Then peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onion; wash, peel and cut 2 cups of potatoes into medium sized wedges; wash, peel and grate 1 teaspoon of ginger, wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":18,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('625565615bead4f59cb0b214','6255628e77eed6f6962bfb82',2,'M1: Prepare the Tempering','To make Aloo Wadiyan, heat a pan and add 2 teaspoons of cooking oil and allow it to become hot. Next add half a teaspoon of cumin seeds, stir fry on low flame for a few seconds and allow it to splutter. Then add 1 teaspoon of grated ginger followed by 1/4 cup of chopped onion and saute on medium low flame for a minute until the onions become translucent. Then add the prepared tomato puree and mix it well with the tempering. Cover it with a lid and allow it to simmer on low flame for 5 minutes. While the puree is simmering move onto the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":5,"flame":2}'),
('6255681e5bead4f59cb0b215','6255628e77eed6f6962bfb82',3,'M2: Prepare the curry','After the tomato puree is cooked, open the lid and give it a mix. The puree would have become thick in consistency now. Next, add a teaspoon of coriander powder, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, add half a teaspoon of red chilli powder, add 1 teaspoon of salt followed by 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala and mix it well with the puree. Then add 2 cups of potato wedges and mix it well with the masala, next, add the roasted amritsari wadiyan and mix it with the potatoes. Add half a cup of water and mix again, cover the pan with a lid and allow the potatoes to cook on low flame for 12 mins or until the potatoes become soft. After the potatoes have cooked, open the lid and adjust the salt, then add 1/4 teaspoon of amchur powder and mix again. Now turn off the flame and transfer the curry in a bowl. Garnish with 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":12,"flame":1}'),('62558f6477eed6f6962bfb87','62558d3277eed6f6962bfb85',1,'P1: Prepare and Rest the dough','To prepare the dough for Stuffed Potato Kulcha, in a mixing bowl add 2 cups of all purpose flour, add 1 teaspoon of sugar, add 1/2 teaspoon of salt, add 1/2 a teaspoon of baking powder, add 1/4 teaspoon of baking soda, add 2 teaspoons of oil followed by 1/4 cup of yogurt . Now combine the ingredients well using your fingers and add warm water at regular intervals as and when required. Please be careful with the quantity of water you add, as you don''t want the dough to become watery and loose. Knead the dough for 5 minutes until it results in a soft dough. Next cover the dough with a damp cloth and allow it to rest for one hour. While the dough is resting please move to the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":60,"advanced_prep_time":60,"timer":60,"flame":0}'),('62558fed5bead4f59cb0b216','62558d3277eed6f6962bfb85',2,'P2:  Boil the potatoes','To boil the potatoes for Stuffed Potato Kulcha, first, wash 2 medium-sized potatoes well with water. Next, put the potatoes in a pressure cooker along with 2 cups of water. Cover it with a lid and pressure cook it over a high flame until one whistle. After the first whistle, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook it for another 8 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the potato is boiling move to the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":12,"flame":2}'),('6255910677eed6f6962bfb88','62558d3277eed6f6962bfb85',3,'P3: Prep the ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Stuffed Potato Kulcha, transfer the boiled potatoes in a bowl and allow it to cool. While the potatoes cool, wash and finely chop 2 teaspoons of coriander leaves, wash, peel and finely chop 1 teaspoon of ginger, wash and finely chop 1 teaspoon of green chillies.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":3,"flame":0}'),('625591e35bead4f59cb0b217','62558d3277eed6f6962bfb85',4,'P4: Prepare the potato stuffing','To prepare the stuffing for Stuffed Potato Kulcha, add the boiled potatoes to a large mixing bowl and mash it well using a masher. Next, add 1 teaspoon of chopped green chilli, add 1 teaspoon of chopped ginger, add 1 teaspoon of salt, add 1 teaspoon of red chilli powder, add 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala, add 1/4 teaspoon of dry mango powder, add 1/4 teaspoon of carom seeds and mix it well to form a stuffing','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('625592985bead4f59cb0b218','62558d3277eed6f6962bfb85',5,'M1 : Roll the Kulcha','To make the Stuffed Potato Kulcha, first divide and shape the prepared dough into a big lemon sized ball using your palms. Then place it on a rolling surface and flatten it using your finger as shown. Next, roll out the dough into a 5-inch disc using the rolling pin. Now, divide the potato stuffing and shape into a lemon sized ball and place it in the center of the rolled Kulcha dough and bring the edges together and pleat it as shown to seal the stuffing inside the dough. Next, sprinkle a teaspoon of black sesame seeds and gently press on the rolled kulcha such that it sticks to the surface, similarly spread a teaspoon of chopped coriander leaves on the dough and gently press on the kulcha and ensure it sticks. Then flip the kulcha on the rolling surface roll it into an oval kulcha as shown. Please ensure that the rolled kulcha remains slightly thick. Next, dip your fingers in a bowl of water and evenly spread the water over the back of the rolled kulcha.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6255930777eed6f6962bfb89','62558d3277eed6f6962bfb85',6,'M2 : Roast the Kulcha','To make Stuffed Potato Kulcha, heat a tawa and allow it to become hot. Then place the prepared kulcha onto the tawa with the coriander and sesame seeds facing the top and roast it over medium flame for a minute. Then, turn the tawa upside down as shown and cook the other side of the kulcha over the direct flame until small brown spots appear on its surface. As it turns slightly golden and firm, put the tawa back on the flame. Then, smear some butter on top and gently take it out onto a plate and Serve. Make the rest of the stuffed potato kulchas similarly.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('62564eb945bb8da240aa330e','6255983c45bb8da240aa330c',1,'P1: Prep the Ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Maharashtrian Poha, peel, wash, and finely chop half a cup of onions. Grate 3/4 cup of fresh coconut using a grater. Wash and pick 7 curry leaves. Wash and cut a lime into halves. Squeeze a tablespoon of lime juice in a bowl.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('62564f8677eed6f6962bfb8b','6255983c45bb8da240aa330c',2,'M1: Dampen and mix the Poha','To make Maharashtrian Poha, first, add 2 cups of thin flattened rice flakes to a bowl, and sprinkle about 1/4 cup of water. Mix it well and set it aside. Next, add half a cup of chopped onions to a separate mixing bowl followed by 3/4 cup of fresh coconut and half a teaspoon of salt. Add a tablespoon of lime juice and mix it well.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('625653b85bead4f59cb0b21a','6255983c45bb8da240aa330c',3,'M2: Temper and prepare the poha','Next, to make the tempering for Maharashtrian Poha, heat a tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame. Add half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, half a teaspoon of cumin seeds, 7 curry leaves, and 1/4 teaspoon of hingh. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder followed by 1/4 cup of peanuts and mix it well. Stir and fry the peanuts over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and remove the tempering into the same bowl. Mix it well and add the moistened rice flakes. Then, mix the rice flakes well with the masala and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('625659f05bead4f59cb0b21c','625658bb77eed6f6962bfb8c',1,'P1: Prepare the Dough','To prepare the dough for Chawal Ki Roti, first, add 1 cup of water to a pan followed by half a teaspoon of salt and bring to a rolling boil over high flame. As the water comes to a boil, reduce the flame to low and add in 1 cup of rice flour to it. Then, Stir it briskly and mix the flour well with water until it crumbles. After that, turn off the flame and sprinkle about 2 tablespoons of water. Next, remove it into a bowl and let it slightly cool. Then, knead it well into a smooth dough.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6256625645bb8da240aa3311','625658bb77eed6f6962bfb8c',2,'M1: Roll and Roast the Roti','To make Chawal ki Roti, first, divide the dough into equal sized dough balls. Next, take a dough ball and dust some flour onto it. Then, gently roll it into a thin round roti. After that, place the roti onto a medium hot tawa and cook it on each side over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until roti puffs up and little brown spots start to appear on it. Then, turn off the flame and remove the roti onto a serving plate. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('62566ce077eed6f6962bfb91','625667f577eed6f6962bfb8f',1,'P1: Prep the Ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Lauki Bharta, first, wash and peel a medium sized bottle gourd. Cut it into halves and remove the seeds as shown. Then, grate 2 cups of bottle gourd in a bowl. Next, wash and finely chop 1 cup of tomatoes. Wash and finely chop 2 green chilies. Wash, peel, and grate a half-inch piece of ginger. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":17,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('62566e0377eed6f6962bfb92','625667f577eed6f6962bfb8f',2,'M1: Prepare the tempering','To make Lauki Bharta, heat a tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Next, temper the oil with half a teaspoon of cumin seeds, 1/4 teaspoon of hing and 1 dry red chili. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. After that, add in 1 cup of chopped tomatoes and saute them over medium flame for a minute. Add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder followed by 2 chopped green chilies and a teaspoon of salt. Mix it well and cover the pan with a lid. Then, cook the tomatoes over low flame for 3-4 minutes until tender. While the tomatoes simmer, please move on to the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":4,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":4,"flame":1}'),('625678c277eed6f6962bfb93','625667f577eed6f6962bfb8f',3,'M2 : Simmer the Bharta','After simmering the tomatoes for Lauki Bharta, remove the lid and give it a stir. Next, add in the grated bottle gourd along with a half-inch piece of grated ginger and mix it well. Then, cover the pan again with and lid and simmer the bharta over low flame for 5 minutes. While the bharta simmers, please move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),
('625679e662c2596eb82b16f4','625667f577eed6f6962bfb8f',4,'M3: Season and Serve','After simmering the Lauki ka Bharta, remove the lid and mash the bharta slightly with the spatula as shown. Then, add half a teaspoon of red chili powder followed by a teaspoon of sugar and 2 teaspoons of lime juice. Mix it well and turn off the flame. Garnish it with a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('62569ad062c2596eb82b16f7','62569a3c62c2596eb82b16f6',1,'P1:  Prep the Ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Dudhi Muthiya, first, wash, peel and grate 3/4 cup of bottle gourd. Next, wash and finely chop 1 green chili. Wash, peel, and finely chop 1/2 inch piece of ginger. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('62569c2a45bb8da240aa3312','62569a3c62c2596eb82b16f6',2,'P2: Prepare the Dough','To prepare the dough for Dudhi Muthiya, add 3/4 cup of whole wheat flour to a large bowl followed by 1/4 cup of semolina, and 1/4 cup of besan. Next, add a half-inch piece of chopped ginger, half a teaspoon of salt, 1 chopped green chili, 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, half a teaspoon of coriander powder, 1/8 teaspoon of baking soda, half a teaspoon of red chili powder, 1 tablespoon of cooking oil, and 1 tablespoon of yogurt. Mix it well and then add 3/4 cup of bottle gourd. Combine it well and prepare a soft dough as shown without adding any water. Next, divide the dough into two or three equal parts and shape each of them into thick cylinders as shown.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('62569cd35bead4f59cb0b21f','62569a3c62c2596eb82b16f6',3,'M1: Steam the Muthiya','To make Dudhi Muthiya, first, add water to a steamer and bring it to a boil. Next, carefully place the prepared dudhi cylinders into the steamer and cover it with a lid. Then, allow it to steam-cook over medium flame for 10 minutes. Meanwhile, please move on to the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":10,"flame":2}'),('6256a2c55bead4f59cb0b220','62569a3c62c2596eb82b16f6',4,'M2: Slice the Muthiya','After steaming the Dudhi Muthiya, remove the lid of the steamer and insert a toothpick into the steamed muthiya to check if they are cooked through. If the toothpick comes out clean then the muthiyas are perfectly cooked. Then, carefully remove the streamed muthiya onto a chopping board and slice them into thick round slices as shown.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('6256a40545bb8da240aa3313','62569a3c62c2596eb82b16f6',5,'M3 : Stir fry the Muthiya','To stir fry the Dudhi Muthiya,  heat 2 tablespoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame for a minute. Then, temper it with half a mustard seeds, half a teaspoon of cumin seeds, half a teaspoon of white sesame seeds, and 7 curry leaves. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Next, add half a teaspoon of dry mango powder, followed by half a teaspoon of coriander powder, and half a teaspoon of red chili powder. Saute and cook the masala over low fame for a few seconds. Next, add the muthiya slices and mix it well. Stir and dry the muthiyas over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and garnish it with a tablespoon of coriander leaves. Serve','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('6256c1ce45bb8da240aa3316','6256c0d35bead4f59cb0b222',1,'P1: Boil the Cowpeas','To boil the red cowpeas for Pumpkin Errissery, first, rinse and clean 1/4 cup of red cowpeas thoroughly with water. Then, transfer them to a pressure cooker along with 1 cup of water and 1/4 teaspoon of salt. Cover the cooker with a lid and pressure cook the peas over high flame until 3 whistles. Then, turn off the flame and allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the cowpeas boil, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":12,"flame":2}'),('6256c26962c2596eb82b16f8','6256c0d35bead4f59cb0b222',2,'P2: Prep the Ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Pumpkin Errissery, first, wash, peel, and cube 2 cup of pumpkin. Next, grate 3/4 cup of fresh coconut using a grater. Wash and slit 1 green chili. Wash and pick 7 curry leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6256c2f85bead4f59cb0b223','6256c0d35bead4f59cb0b222',3,'M1: Cook the pumpkin','To make Pumpkin Errisery, add 2 cups of diced pumpkin to a deep bottom pan followed by 3/4 cup of water, 3/4 teaspoon of salt, and 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder. Mix it well and cover it with a lid. Then, let it cook over medium flame for 7-8 minutes. While the pumpkin simmers, please move on to the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":8,"flame":2}'),('6256c3915bead4f59cb0b224','6256c0d35bead4f59cb0b222',4,'M2: Prepare the Masala','To make the masala paste for Pumpkin Errisery, add half a cup of fresh coconut to a blender jar followed by 1 green chili, half a teaspoon of cumin seeds, and 1/4 cup of water. Then, cover the jar with a lid and blend it well into a smooth paste.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('6256c48245bb8da240aa3317','6256c0d35bead4f59cb0b222',5,'M3: Prepare the Curry','After simmering the pumpkin for Pumpkin Errissery, take off the lid and add the boiled cowpeas followed by the prepared coconut masala paste. Mix it well and cook the curry over medium flame for 2-3 minutes. Bring the curry to a boil and then turn off the flame. To make the tempering, heat 2 teaspoons of coconut oil in a tempering pan over medium flame. Next, add half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, half a teaspoon of urad dal, 1 dry red chili and 7 curry leaves. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Then, turn off the flame and add the tempering to the curry. Mix it well and serve','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('6257a06d62c2596eb82b16f9','6256d4fa45bb8da240aa3319',1,'P1: Prepare the Dough','To prepare the dough for Besan Pyaz Paratha, first, add 1.5 cups of whole wheat flour to a large bowl followed by half a teaspoon of salt. Mix it well and gradually add about 3/4 cup of water. Combine it well and knead it into a smooth dough. Then, cover it with a damp cloth and allow it to rest for 20 minutes. While the dough rests, please move on to the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":20,"flame":0}'),('6257a11545bb8da240aa331b','6256d4fa45bb8da240aa3319',2,'P2:  Prep the Ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Besan Pyaz Paratha, first, peel, wash, and finely chop 3/4 cup of onions. Wash and finely chop 1 green chili. Peel and finely chop 1 teaspoon of garlic. Peel and finely chop a half-inch piece of ginger.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6257a6925bead4f59cb0b227','6256d4fa45bb8da240aa3319',3,'P3: Prepare the Stuffing','To prepare the stuffing for Besan Pyaz Paratha, heat 1.5 tablespoons of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame. Next, add 1 teaspoon of cumin seeds, half a teaspoon of carom seeds, 1 teaspoon of chopped garlic , and 1/4 teaspoon of hing. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Then, add 3/4 cup of chopped onions and fry them over medium flame for 3-4 minutes until translucent. Add 1 chopped green chili followed by half-inch piece of chopped ginger and saute it for another minute.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('6257a7ef5bead4f59cb0b228','6256d4fa45bb8da240aa3319',4,'P4: Continue preparing the Stuffing','Next, add 1/4 cup of gram flour and mix it well. Then, saute and roast it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until fragrant. Then, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, half a teaspoon of salt, half a teaspoon of red chili powder, and half a teaspoon of coriander powder. Mix it well and fry the stuffing over medium flame for another 1-2 minutes. After that, add a teaspoon of dry mint leaves and mix it well. Turn off the flame and set it aside','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('6257a86b5bead4f59cb0b229','6256d4fa45bb8da240aa3319',5,'M1: Roll and Roast the Paratha','To make the Besan Pyaz Paratha, first, divide the prepared dough into equal sized dough balls. Then, dust a dough ball into flour and roll it using a rolling pin into a small 5-inch circle. Place 1.5 tablespoonss of the prepared stuffing and seal it inside as shown. Then, dust some flour and gently roll into a slightly thick round paratha. Next, place it onto a hot tawa and cook it over medium flame for a minute on each side. Then, add a teaspoon of ghee and cook the paratha until it is evenly browned on all sides. After that, remove it onto a serving plate and serve. Make the rest of the parathas similarly','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('6257b09045bb8da240aa331c','6257af2e5bead4f59cb0b22c',1,'P1: Soak the Rice','To soak the rice for Masala Bhat, first wash 1 cup of sona masuri rice and soak it in 2 cups of water for 20 mins. While the rice is soaking please move to the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":20,"flame":0}'),('6257b17445bb8da240aa331d','6257af2e5bead4f59cb0b22c',2,'P2: Prep the Ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Masala Bhat, first grate 1/4 cup of dry coconut. Then heat a pan and allow it to become hot. Next add the grated dry coconut and stir fry on low flame until it turns slightly brown. After it turns slightly brown, transfer it in a wide plate and allow it to cool. While the roasted coconut cools, wash, peel and cut 1/4 cup of potatoes into medium sized cubes. Wash, clean and cut 1/4 cup of cauliflower into florets. Wash, deseed and dice 1/4 cup of green capsicum. Wash, peel and grate 1.5 teaspoon of ginger using a grater. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":17,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('6257b61962c2596eb82b16fa','6257af2e5bead4f59cb0b22c',3,'P3: Roast the Spices for the Masala','To prepare the Masala for Masala Bhat, heat a pan, add 1 teaspoon of sesame seeds, 1 teaspoon of coriander seeds, 1 teaspoon of shahi jeera, 1 bayleaf, 2 inch cinnamon stick, 3 cloves, 1 star anise, 2 cardamoms, 4 black peppercorns and dry roast it on low flame for a few seconds or until the spices turn aromatic and golden brown. Turn off the flame and transfer the roasted spices in the plate and allow it to slightly cool. While the roasted spices cool, please move to the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":2,"flame":1}'),('6257b68245bb8da240aa331e','6257af2e5bead4f59cb0b22c',4,'P4: Roast the Cashews and grind the masala','To roast the cashewnuts for Masala Bhat, heat a pan and add 1 teaspoon of ghee and allow it to become hot. Then add 1 tablespoon of cashewnuts and roast on medium low flame for a few seconds or until it becomes slightly brown. Turn off the flame, transfer the roasted cashewnuts in a bowl and set aside. Then add the spices roasted for the masala in a mixy jar and blitz it into a fine powder. Keep aside','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('6257bbfd45bb8da240aa331f','6257af2e5bead4f59cb0b22c',5,'M1: Cook the Vegetables','To prepare Masala Bhat, heat a deep bottom pan and add 2 tablespoons of cooking oil and allow it to become hot. Then add 1 teaspoon of cumin seeds, add 1/2 a teaspoon of mustard seeds and allow it to splutter. Then add half a cup of cubed potatoes and saute it for a few minutes on medium low flame, then add 1/4 cup of cauliflower florets and saute for a few seconds. Next add 1/4 cup of diced green capsicum and continue sauteing for a few seconds. Then add 1.5 teaspoon of grated ginger, 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes and saute for a few minutes until the vegetables become soft.','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('6257bcd85bead4f59cb0b22f','6257af2e5bead4f59cb0b22c',6,'M2: Cook the Masala Bhat','Next drain the water from the soaked rice using a colander, and add 1 cup of strained rice to the pan. Add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, add 1/2 teaspoon of red chilli powder, add the ground masala powder and combine it well with the vegetables and rice. Then add 2 cups of water, 1.5 teaspoon of salt and bring to boil on medium low flame. Then cover the pan with a lid and cook on low flame for 18mins. Then turn off the flame and gently mix the rice. Garnish the Masala bhat with roasted cashewnuts and chopped coriander leaves, serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":20,"flame":2}'),('6257c4a7cd63c5902673b129','6257c3441f9c5c940d3184b8',1,'P1: Boil the Potatoes','To boil the potatoes for Bhel Puri, wash a medium-sized potato well with water. Then, add it to a pressure cooker with 2 cups of water and 1/4 teaspoon of salt. Cover it with a lid and pressure cook it on high flame till the first whistle. After that, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook it for another 8 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the potatoes are boiling, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":12,"flame":2}'),('6257c8fe1f9c5c940d3184b9','6257c3441f9c5c940d3184b8',2,'P2: Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredinets for Bhel Puri, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onion, wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of tomato, wash and grate 2 tablespoons of raw mango using a grater. Wash 1/2 a cup of coriander leaves to prepare the chutney, remove the root ends. Then finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves to garnish the Bhel. Wash and separate 1/4 cup of mint leaves. Peel and wash 3 cloves of garlic. Wash, and peel a 1/2 inch piece of ginger. Wash and slit 2 nos green chilies. Wash and cut a lemon into halves. Then, squeeze 1 tablespoon lime juice.','prep_method','{"active_time":18,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6257ca6e0a6b8e64dc3156f9','6257c3441f9c5c940d3184b8',3,'P3: Prepare the Mint Chutney','After boiling the potato for Bhel Puri, take off the lid and transfer the boiled potato to a plate. Allow it to cool down a bit. While the potatoes cool, prepare the mint chutney. Take a blender jar and add 1/2 a cup of coriander leaves ,1/4 cup of mint leaves, 2 cloves of garlic, 1/2 -inch piece of ginger and 2 nos slit green chilies followed by 1 tablespoons of roasted gram dal and 1/4 teaspoon of cumin powder. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of chat masala, 1/4 teaspoon of sugar and 1/4 teaspoon of salt along with a pinch of hing and 1.5 tablespoons of water. Blend it well into a smooth chutney. Take it out into a bowl and add a tablespoon of lime juice, remove in a bowl and set aside. Next, cut the boiled potato into small cubes.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('6257cba01f9c5c940d3184ba','6257c3441f9c5c940d3184b8',4,'M1: Prepare the Bhel','To make Bhel Puri, in a mixing bowl add 2.5 cups of puffed rice, add 1/4 cup of chopped onion, add 1/4 cup of cubed potatoes, then crush 3 nos papdis into small pieces and add it to the mix, add 1/4 cup of mixture, add 2 tablespoons of roasted peanuts, add 2 tablespoons of chopped tomatoes, add 2 tablespoons of grated raw mango or substitute it with 1 tablespoon of lemon juice. Then add 1/4 teaspoon of red chilli powder, add 1/4 a tsp of salt, add 1/2 a teaspoon of chaat masala, add 3 tablespoons of tamarind chutney, add 1 tablespoon of green chutney and mix well. Then add 1/4 cup of nylon sev and mix again. Serve the Bhel Puri in a plate and garnish it with some more sev and chopped coriander leaves.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6257d13dcd63c5902673b12b','6257d0420a6b8e64dc3156fa',1,'P1: Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Khatta Meetha Kaddu first soak a tablespoon of tamarind and in half a cup of water for 15 minutes. While the tamarind is soaking, wash, peel and cut 2.5 cups of pumpkin into medium sized cubes. Then wash, peel and grate 1-inch of ginger and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":12,"flame":0}'),('6257d2671f9c5c940d3184bd','6257d0420a6b8e64dc3156fa',2,'M1: Prepare the Tempering','To prepare the tempering for Khatta Meetha Kaddu, heat a pan and add 1.5 tablespoon of cooking oil and allow it to become hot. Then add 1/4 teaspoon of fenugreek seeds, add 1 teaspoon of cumin seeds, add 1 teaspoon of fennel seeds, break 2 dried red chillies into half and add to the pan. Then saute the spices for a few seconds on low flame and allow it to splutter. Next add 1-inch of grated ginger, add 1 teaspoon of red chilli powder and saute well with the spices. Then add, 2.5 cups of cubed pumpkin and mix well with the tadka. Add 1/4 cup of water and mix again. Cover the pan with a lid and cook on medium low flame for 8 mins until the pumpkin is half cooked. While it is simmering please move onto the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":8,"flame":2}'),('6257d32a1f9c5c940d3184be','6257d0420a6b8e64dc3156fa',3,'M2: Season and cook the Curry','After simmering the Khatta Meetha Kaddu, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, add 1 teaspoon of salt, add 1 teaspoon of jaggery powder. Then mash the soaked tamarind using your fingers and squeeze 1/4 cup of the tamarind pulp to the mix using your hands. Please ensure the fibres and seeds are strained between your fingers. Next, mix well and cover the lid and allow it to cook on medium low flame for another 2 mins. Then turn off the flame and serve the Khatta Meetha Kaddu with chapathi or poori.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('6257d9f21f9c5c940d3184bf','6257d928cd63c5902673b12d',1,'P1: Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Rava Toast, first peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onion, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomato, wash, peel and grate 2 tablespoon of carrot wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('6257e3e31f9c5c940d3184c0','6257d928cd63c5902673b12d',2,'P2: Prepare the Rava Mixture','To prepare the Rava mixture for Rava Toast, in a mixing bowl add half a cup of rawa followed by half a cup of yogurt and mix well using a spoon. Then add 1/4 cup of water and mix until well combined without any lumps. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions, add 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes, add 2 tablespoons of grated carrot, add 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves, add 1 teaspoon of salt, add 1 teaspoon of sugar, and mix well. Then add 1/2 a teaspoon of red chilli powder and mix again.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6257e4ef1f9c5c940d3184c1','6257d928cd63c5902673b12d',3,'M1: Roast the Rava Toast','To roast the Rava Toast, heat a tawa and allow it to become hot on medium low flame. Then place a bread slice on a board and take a tablespoon of the prepared Rava Mixture and spread a thick layer of the mixture evenly on the bread. After the tawa is hot, flip and place the bread slice such that the plain side is facing on top. Next, evenly spread a teaspoon of butter on top and flip the bread slice using a spatula and allow it to cook on the other side for a few seconds. Once the bread turns slightly golden brown, flip again as show and cook for a minute. Turn off the flame, and transfer the Rava Toast on a serving plate and cut it diagonally using a cutter, into 2 halves resulting in triangles. Serve hot with ketchup or mint chutney. Repeat the same for the remaining slices','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('6257f2f61f9c5c940d3184c3','6257f1b90a6b8e64dc3156fc',1,'AP1: Soak the Chickpeas','To soak the chickpeas for Chickepea Veggie Burger, in a bowl add 1.5 cups of chickpea along with 2.5 cups of water and allow it to soak overnight. While the Chickepea is soaking move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":480,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6257f4130a6b8e64dc3156fd','6257f1b90a6b8e64dc3156fc',2,'P1: Boil the Chickpeas','To boil the chickpeas for Chickepea Veg Burger, first wash and peel half an inch of ginger and thinly slice them into a teaspoon of juliennes. Next, drain the water from the soaked chickepeas and transfer the the chickpeas in a pressure cooker along with 2 cups of water. Add a bay leaf, followed by 1 teaspoon of ginger juliennes and a teaspoon of salt. add the soaked chickpeas to a pressure cooker along with 1 cup of water and 1 tsp of salt. Mix it well and cover the cooker with a lid. Then, pressure cook the chickpeas over a high flame until 3 whistles. Then, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook the chickpeas for another 5 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the chickpeas are boiling, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":15,"flame":2}'),('6257f4e51f9c5c940d3184c4','6257f1b90a6b8e64dc3156fc',3,'P2:  Boil the Potatoes','To boil the potatoes for the Chickepea Veg Burger, first, wash 2 medium-sized potatoes well with water. Next, put the potatoes in a pressure cooker along with 2 cups of water. Cover it with a lid and pressure cook it over a high flame until one whistle. After the first whistle, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook it for another 8 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the potato is boiling move to the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":12,"flame":2}'),
('6257f6721f9c5c940d3184c5','6257f1b90a6b8e64dc3156fc',4,'P3: Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Chickpea Veg Burger, first, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onion; and slice 1/2 cup of onion, wash and slice 1/2 a cup of tomatoes, wash and finely chop 2 teaspoons of green chilli, wash and finely chop 2.5 tablespoons of coriander leaves, wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of mint leaves and then grate 1/4 cup of paneer using a grater.','prep_method','{"active_time":20,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6257f6f5cd63c5902673b130','6257f1b90a6b8e64dc3156fc',5,'P4: Mash the potatoes and chickpeas','To prepare the dough for the chickpea patty, take off the lid of the pressure cooker, remove the bay leaf and check if the chickpeas are cooked. To check if they are cooked press the chickpea between your fingers, the chickpea should be easily mashed at this stage. If the chickpeas are still hard, close the lid and allow it to pressure cook on medium low flame for another 2 whistles. Then drain the water from the boiled chickpeas and transfer the chickpeas in a mixing bowl and mash it well using a masher. Similarly, transfer the boiled potatoes in a mixing bowl and mash it well using a masher and add it to the mashed chcikpeas.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6257f8471f9c5c940d3184c6','6257f1b90a6b8e64dc3156fc',6,'P5: Prepare the Patty Dough','After mashing the chickpea and potatoes, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions, add 2 teaspoons of ginger and garlic paste, add 2 teaspoons of chopped green chillies, add half a tablespoon of red chilli powder, add 1 teaspoon of coriander powder, add 1 teaspoon of dry mango powder, add 1/4 teaspoon of cumin powder, add 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala, add 1 tablespoon of kasuri methi, add 2 tablespoons of chopped coriander leaves add 2 tablespoons of chopped mint leaves, add 1/4 cup of grated paneer, add half a teaspoon of salt. Next combine the ingredients well and form a soft dough.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('625a2cab0a6b8e64dc315703','6257f1b90a6b8e64dc3156fc',7,'P6: Shape the Patty','To shape the chickpea patty for Chickpea Veg Burger, first take a lemon sized ball of the chickpea dough and shape it into a ball, then gently flatten it between your palms and shape it like a patty as shown in the video. Next, to make the corn flour slurry, in a mixing bowl add 1/4 cup of corn flour along with 1/4 cup of water and mix it well using a spoon in a thin consistency. Please break the lumps if any.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('625a2d51328879d6e1e609a9','6257f1b90a6b8e64dc3156fc',8,'M1: Shallow fry the patty','To shallow fry the chickpea patty, heat a wide pan and add 1 cup of cooking oil to shallow fry the patty, allow it to become hot on medium high flame for 3 minutes. Meanwhile, in wide plate, add a 1 cup of bread crumbs and spread it across the plate. Next, carefully dip the patty in the prepared corn flour slurry as shown and place it in the bread crumbs mix and evenly coat it with the bread crumbs, ensuring it is coated on all sides. Now carefully place the coated patty in the hot oil and shallow fry until it turns brown, then flip the patty using a spoon and spatula and allow it to fry and turn golden brown on the other side. Then turn off the flame, and transfer the patty onto a plate.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":3,"flame":2}'),
('625a2eb9cd63c5902673b133','6257f1b90a6b8e64dc3156fc',9,'M2: Saute the vegetables','To prepare the sauted vegetables for Chickpea Veg Burger, heat a pan and add 2 teaspoons of oil and allow it to become hot on medium low flame. Then add 1 teaspoon of cumin seeds, add half a cup of sliced onions, add half a cup of sliced tomatoes, and saute on medium low flame for 3 mins until the onions become translucent and the tomatoes become soft. Then add half a teaspoon of salt, add 1/4 teaspoon of red chilli powder, and saute for another 3 mins. Then turn off the flame and add half a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and mix well. Set aside','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('625a2fab0a6b8e64dc315704','6257f1b90a6b8e64dc3156fc',10,'M3: Roast the Buns','To roast the burger buns for Chickpea Veg Burger, heat a pan and add 1 tablespoon of butter and allow it to slightly melt, then add 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and and mix well. Then place the burger buns and gently press them as shown to absorb the coriander butter and allow it to roast on medium flame until it turns brown. Then turn off the flame and set the toasted buns aside','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('625a3007cd63c5902673b134','6257f1b90a6b8e64dc3156fc',11,'M4: Assemble the Burger','To assemble the Chickpea Veg Burger, take the flat bottom bun, add a tablespoon of ketchup on it and evenly spread on the bun. Then add a tablespoon of the stir fried vegetables and spread a layer of it, then place the chickpea patty in the center and add spread another tablespoon of the stir fried veggies. Place the fluffed burger bun on top and serve warm with ketchup.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('625a394e0a6b8e64dc315706','625a3733328879d6e1e609aa',1,'P1: Boil the Potatoes','To boil the sweet potatoes for Dabeli Sandwich, wash 2 medium-sized sweet potatoes well with water. Then, add it to a pressure cooker with 2 cups of water and 1/4 teaspoon of salt. Cover it with a lid and pressure cook it on high flame till the first whistle. After that, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook it for another 8 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the potatoes are boiling, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":12,"flame":2}'),('625a3c610a6b8e64dc315707','625a3733328879d6e1e609aa',2,'P2:  Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Dabeli Sandwich, peel and finely chop half a cup of onions, wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves and set aside. Next, to prepare the spice mix heat a pan and add half a tablespoon of coriander seeds, add half a tablespoon of cumin seeds, add 2 inch of cinnamon stick followed by 2 dried red chillies. Now dry roast these spices on low flame for 2 minutes until they turn aromatic. Then turn off the flame and transfer the roasted spices in a mixy jar and blend into a fine powder. Remove in a bowl and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('625a3d4f328879d6e1e609ab','625a3733328879d6e1e609aa',3,'P3: Mash the Potatoes','After the sweet potatoes have boiled, open the lid of the pressure cooker, transfer the potatoes onto a wide plate and allow them to slightly cool. While the potatoes cool, place the slices of bread on a chopping board and trim the brown edges. Discard the edges and set the slices aside. After the potatoes have cooled, gently peel off the skin and transfer the potatoes in a mixing bowl. Now, mash the potatoes using your hands and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('625a40b2328879d6e1e609ac','625a3733328879d6e1e609aa',4,'P4: Prepare the Stuffing','To prepare the stuffing for Dabeli Sandwich, heat a pan and add 2 teaspoons of ghee and allow it to become hot. Then add half a cup of chopped onions and saute it on medium flame for a minute until it becomes soft. Then add 2 tablespoons of tamarind chutney and saute it for another minute. Next add 2 teaspoons of the prepared spice powder and mix it well. Next add 1.5 cups of the mashed sweet potato followed by one teaspoon of salt and mix well with the masala. Then add a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and mix well. Now turn off the flame and set the stuffing aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('625a412acd63c5902673b136','625a3733328879d6e1e609aa',5,'M1: Assemble the Sandwich','To assemble the Dabeli Sandwich, place a slice of bread and evenly spread a tablespoon of the tamarind chutney, then scoop 3 tablespoons of the potato stuffing and spread evenly to form a thick layer. Then sprinkle a few roasted peanuts on top of the stuffing followed by a few pomegranate seeds. Then cover the sandwich with another slice of bread on top.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('625a4193cd63c5902673b137','625a3733328879d6e1e609aa',6,'M2: Roast the Sandwich','To roast the sandwich, heat a pan and add 1 tablespoon of butter and allow it to become hot, then place the prepared sandwich and allow it to roast on medium flame for a minute until it becomes golden brown, then flip the sandwich and cook on the other side and allow it to become brown. Then turn off the flame and place the roasted sandwich on a plate and cut it diagonally into half using a cutter resulting in 2 traingles. Next, place 1/4 cup of sev in a wide plate and pat the sandwich on the sev as shown. Serve warm.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('625a508d328879d6e1e609af','625a4c9c328879d6e1e609ae',1,'P1: Soak the Tamarind','To prep the ingredients for Sindhi Kadhi first soak a tablespoon of tamarind and in half a cup of water for 15 minutes. While the tamarind is soaking, wash, clean and cut half a cup of lady''s finger into medium length pieces. Then wash and string 1/4 cup of broad beans and tear them into half; wash and pluck a sprig of curry leaves, wash and slit 2 green chillies, wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('625a51e70a6b8e64dc315709','625a4c9c328879d6e1e609ae',2,'P2: Chop the vegetables','Next for the Sindhi Kadhi, wash, peel and cut 1/2 a cup of carrot into medium length pieces; wash, peel and cut half a cup of potatoes into medium length pieces; peel and finely chop half a tablespoon of ginger. Then wash and chop half a cup of tomatoes, wash and string half a cup of cluster beans and then cut them into medium length pieces.','prep_method','{"active_time":20,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('625a55c9328879d6e1e609b0','625a4c9c328879d6e1e609ae',3,'M1: Prepare the Tempering','To temper the Sindhi Kadhi, heat a deep bottom pan and add 1 tablespoon of cooking oil and allow it to become hot. Then add 1 teaspoon of cumin seeds, add 1 teaspoon of mustard seeds, add the curry leaves, add 1/4 teaspoon of asafoeitida, add 1/4 teaspoon of fenugreek seeds and saute it on low flame for a few seconds until the spices splutter. Then add half a tablespoon of chopped ginger, add 3 tablespoons of gram flour and roast it on low flame. Stir the flour continuously to prevent it from burning. Continue roasting the flour until it becomes slightly brown. The flour will result in a crumbly texture. Add 2 cups of water at this stage and give it a good mix, then bring to boil on medium low flame. While the kadhi is simmering move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('625a5691cd63c5902673b138','625a4c9c328879d6e1e609ae',4,'M2: Cook the Vegetables','After the Sindhi Kadhi has come to a boil, add half a cup of chopped tomatoes, then add half a cup of cut carrot followed by 1/4 cup of cut broad beans along with half a cup of cut cluster beans. Then add half a cup of cut potato along with 1 teaspoon of salt. Next, add 1/8 teaspoon of turmeric powder and mix well. Cover the pan with a lid and allow the vegetables to cook on medium flame for 8 minutes. Stir the kadhi occasionally to prevent the gram flour mixture from settling at the bottom of the pan. While the vegetables are cooking, move onto the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":8,"flame":2}'),('625a572dcd63c5902673b139','625a4c9c328879d6e1e609ae',5,'M3: Stir Fry the Ladys'' Finger','To stir fry the ladies finger for Sindhi Kadhi, heat a pan and add 2 teaspoons of cooking oil and allow it to become hot, then add the cut lady''s finger and saute it on medium low flame for 2 minutes until cooks and becomes soft. Avoid stirring it continuously to prevent it from sticking.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":2,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":2,"flame":2}'),('625a59300a6b8e64dc31570a','625a4c9c328879d6e1e609ae',6,'M4: Cook the Kadhi','After cooking the vegetables for Sindhi Kadhi, open the lid give it a good mix and then add half a cup of water followed 2 slit green chillies along with half a teaspoon of red chilli powder. Then mix it well and add the stir fried lady''s finger. Mix the kadhi again and adjust the consistency by adding required amount of water and allow it to cook on medium flame for another minute. The Kadhi should be slightly thick. While the kadhi is simmering, mash the soaked tamarind using your fingers and squeeze 1 tablespoon of the tamarind pulp to the kadhi using your hands and then mix well. Please ensure the fibres and seeds are strained between your fingers and don''t fall in the kadhi. Allow the sindhi kadhi to boil on high flame for a minute. Then turn off the flame and garnish it with chopped coriander leaves, mix well transfer in a serving bowl and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('625a7d77cd63c5902673b13b','625a6830328879d6e1e609b3',1,'P1: Prepare the Idli','To prepare the Idli for Idli Chat, first grease an idli plate with 2 teaspoons of cooking oil using an oil brush. Greasing will prevent the idli from sticking to the base of the idli plate, and idlis will come off easily. Next, pour the prepared idli batter into 8 cavities of the greased idli plate and carefully place it inside the steamer and cover it with a lid. Allow the idlis to steam for 12 minutes. After steaming the idlis, remove the lid of the steamer and carefully take out the idli plate. Gently, take out the idlis from the plate and allow it to slightly cool. While the Idlis are steaming please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":15,"flame":2}'),('625a7e61cd63c5902673b13c','625a6830328879d6e1e609b3',2,'P2: Prep the Ingreidients','To prep the ingredients for Idli Chat, peel and finely chop 4 tablespoons of onion, wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of tomatoes, wash and clean half a cup of coriander leaves and remove the root ends, wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of mint leaves, wash and clean 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves and then wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of curry leaves. Next, to prepare the yogurt mix for Idli Chaat, in a mixing bowl add 1 cup of curds, add half a teaspoon of black salt, add half a teaspoon of cumin powder, add 1.5 tablespoon of powdered sugar, and whip it well using a whisk. Then add half a cup of water and mix well, the curd should achieve a flowy consistency.','prep_method','{"active_time":20,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('625a7ff3cd63c5902673b13d','625a6830328879d6e1e609b3',3,'P3: Prepare the Green Chutney','To prepare green chutney for Idli Chat, in a blender jar, add half a cup of washed coriander leaves, one tablespoon of mint leaves.  2 cloves of garlic, half an inch ginger and 3 slit green chilies followed by 1 tablespoon of roasted gram dal and 1/4 teaspoon of cumin powder. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of chat masala, 1/4 teaspoon of sugar and 1/4 teaspoon of salt along with a pinch of hing and 1.5 tablespoons of water. Blend it well into a smooth chutney. Take it out into a bowl and add half a tablespoon of lime juice. Mix it well and set aside','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('625a8267cd63c5902673b13e','625a6830328879d6e1e609b3',4,'M1: Temper the Idlis','To temper the Idlis for Idli Chat, first place the cooled idlis on a chopping board and cut them into medium sized pieces. Next, heat a pan and add 2 tablespoons of oil and allow it to become hot. Then add half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, half a teaspoon of white lentils, add half a teaspoon of chana dal and saute it on low flame until the spices splutter. Then add 1/4 teaspoon of hingh, add 1 tablespoon of curry leaves and saute for a few seconds on medium low flame. Next, add 2 teaspoons of red chilli powder, and mix well with the tempering. Then add the cut idli pieces to the pan and combine well. Ensure the idlis are evenly coated with the masala.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('625a831b328879d6e1e609b5','625a6830328879d6e1e609b3',5,'M2: Assemble the Idli  Chat','To assemble the Idli Chat, in a serving plate place the roasted idlis, now pour 2 tablespoons of the whisked curd, then sprinkle a pinch of cumin powder on top followed by a pinch of chat masala. Then drizzle two tablespoons of sweet chutney along with 1 tablespoon of green chutney on top. Next, garnish the chat with 2 tablespoons of chopped onion, 1 tablespoon of chopped tomato, and 2 tablespoons of nylon sev follwed by 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves. The idli chaat is ready to serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('625a8c57328879d6e1e609b6','625a87abcd63c5902673b140',1,'P1: Prepare the Dough','To prepare the dough for Methi Thepla, first wash and finely chop one cup of methi leaves. Then, in a mixing bowl add 2 cups of wheat flour , add 1 cup of gram flour, add half a teaspoon of turmeric powder, add 1 teaspoon of salt, half a teaspoon of red chilli powder followed by 1 teaspoon of coriander powder and 1 teaspoon of garam masala. Next, combine the ingredients well using your fingers, then add 1 cup of chopped methi leaves along with 2 tablespoons of yogurt and mix well with the dry ingredients. Then add required amount of water and mix well, gradually add water at regular intervals and knead into a soft dough. Please be careful with the quantity of water as excess water will result in a sticky and loose dough. After kneading a soft dough, add a teaspoon of oil and smear it on the dough, then cover the mixing bowl with a lid and allow the dough to rest for 15 mins. While the dough is resting move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":15,"flame":0}'),('625a8cdf328879d6e1e609b7','625a87abcd63c5902673b140',2,'M1: Roll and roast the thepla','To roast the Methi Thepla, first take off the lid and knead the dough again for a few seconds. Then equally portion the dough into lemon sized balls by shaping it between your palms. Then place the ball on a rolling surface and dust it with a teaspoon of flour. This will prevent it from sticking on the surface. Now flatten the dough gently with your fingers, and start rolling it evenly using a rolling pin into a thin disc as shown. Then heat a tawa and allow it to become hot, after it becomes hot gently place the rolled thepla add drizzle a teaspoon of ghee or oil and evenly spread it. Allow the thepla to roast on medium low flame for a minute or until the bubble appear, then flip it on the other side and drizzle a teaspoon of oil or ghee and roast until the brown spots appear. Flip it again on the other side to ensure it has cooked evenly. Tranfer the thepla on a serving plate and serve hot with curds and pickle. Repeat the same for the remaining dough.','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('6272122ceeb80cd182c6bb0a','625a5d62328879d6e1e609b2',1,'AP1: Soak the Green Peas','To soak the green peas for Masala Poori, wash and soak 1.5 cups of green peas along with 3 cups of water. Allow it to soak overnight. While the green peas are soaking move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":480,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6272132733a45f94759170aa','625a5d62328879d6e1e609b2',2,'P1: Boil the Green Peas','To boil the green peas for Masala Poori, drain the water from the soaked peas and transfer the soaked green peas in a pressure cooker. Then add 3 cups of water along with half a teaspoon of salt. Cover it with a lid and pressure cook on high flame for 3 whistles, then allow it to simmer for another 5 minutes on low flame. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the green peas are boiling, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":15,"flame":2}'),('6272140c0c136c6c53067739','625a5d62328879d6e1e609b2',3,'P2: Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Masala Poori, first grate 1/4 cup of coconut, then peel and finely chop 2 tablespoons of onion, wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of tomatoes and set aside. Then wash and pluck 2 tablespoons of mint leaves, wash half a cup of coriander leaves and remove the root ends. Peel and wash 2 cloves of garlic. Wash, and peel a 1/2-inch piece of ginger. Wash and slit 4 nos green chilies. Wash and cut a lemon into halves. Then, squeeze half a tablespoon lime juice. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":18,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('6272153133a45f94759170ab','625a5d62328879d6e1e609b2',4,'P3: Prepare the Masala','To prepare the masala for Masala Poori, heat a pan and add 2 teaspoons of cooking oil. After it becomes hot add 2 teaspoons of coriander seeds, add 1.5 teaspoon of cumin seeds, add 1/4 teaspoon of black peppercons, add 5 cloves followed by 2 inch cinnamon and 1 star anise. Then add a small piece of nutmegalong with a green chilli. Roast the spices on low flame for 2 minutes until they smell aromatic. Then add 15 mint leaves along with 1/4 cup of grated coconut and roast on low flame for another 3 minutes until the coconut turns slighlty brown and the mint leaves shrink. Then turn off the flame and transfer it in a wide plate, allow it to slightly cool. Then add the roasted spices in a blender jar and blend it into a smooth paste and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('6272163e0c136c6c5306773a','625a5d62328879d6e1e609b2',5,'P4: Prepare the Green Chutney','To prepare green chutney for Masala Poori, in a blender jar, add half a cup of washed coriander leaves, one tablespoon of mint leaves.  2 cloves of garlic, half an inch ginger and 3 slit green chilies followed by 1 tablespoon of roasted gram dal and 1/4 teaspoon of cumin powder. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of chat masala, 1/4 teaspoon of sugar and 1/4 teaspoon of salt along with a pinch of hing and 1.5 tablespoons of water. Blend it well into a smooth chutney. Take it out into a bowl and add half a tablespoon of lime juice. Mix it well and set aside','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('62721a0e33a45f94759170ac','625a5d62328879d6e1e609b2',6,'M1: Prepare the Green Peas Gravy','After the pressure cooker has cooled, remove the lid of the pressure cooker and check if the green peas have cooked. To check if they are cooked, take a boiled green pea and gently press between your fingers. They should be soft and mushy at this stage, if they are still hard cover the lid and pressure cook them on low flame for another 5 minutes. Then transfer them in a deep bottom pan and allow to simmer on low flame. Then remove half a cup of boiled green peas in a bowl from the pan and in a blender jar and blend it into a fine puree. Now add the prepared spice masala to the green peas in the deep bottom pan, add the pureed green peas and give it a good mix. Next, add 1 teaspoon of salt and bring to boil on medium flame. While the masala is boiling, please move onto the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":7,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":7,"flame":2}'),('62721cc233a45f94759170ad','625a5d62328879d6e1e609b2',7,'M2: Assemble the Masala Poori','To assemble the Masala Poori, take a serving plate and crush 5 pooris then pour a ladle of the prepared masala, drizzle a teaspoon of the prepared green chutney on top, then add a teaspoon of tamarind chutney, followed by one tablespoon of chopped onion and 1 tablespoon of chopped tomato. Garnish it with a tablespoon of nylon sev along with chopped coriander leaves and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('62753fb60c136c6c5306773e','62753ed20c136c6c5306773c',1,'P1: Prep the Ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Drumstick Leaves Paratha, wash a bunch of drumstick leaves thoroughly with water and pat dry it using a kitchen towel. Next, pick the leaves and finely chop 1 cup of the greens. Peel, wash, and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Wash, peel, and grate a half inch piece of ginger. Wash and finely chop 1 green chili.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('6275434435e977e17d921453','62753ed20c136c6c5306773c',2,'P2: Prepare the Dough','To prepare the dough for Drumstick Leaves Paratha, add 1.5 cup of whole wheat flour to a large mixing bowl followed by 1 cup of chopped drumstick leaves, and 1/4 cup of gram flour. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions, 1 chopped green chili, a half inch piece of grated ginger, 1 teaspoon of coriander powder, 1 teaspoon of cumin powder, 1 teaspoon of salt, and 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder. Mix it well and gradually add about 3/4 cup of water. Then, knead it well into a smooth dough. Add a teaspoon of cooking oil and knead it again for a minute. Then, cover the dough with a damp cloth and set it aside for 20 minutes. While the dough rests, please move on to the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":20,"flame":0}'),('6275442835e977e17d921454','62753ed20c136c6c5306773c',3,'M1: Roll the Dough','To make the Drumstick Leaves Paratha, divide the prepared dough into equal sized dough balls. Then, place a dough ball onto a rolling board and gently roll it into a small 5 inch circle. Add half a teaspoon of ghee and spread evenly. Then, sprinkle some flour and fold it as shown. Dust some flour and gently roll it again into a slightly thick paratha.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6275449aeeb80cd182c6bb13','62753ed20c136c6c5306773c',4,'M2: Roast the Paratha','Next, heat up a tawa over medium flame and gently place the rolled out paratha. Add half a teaspoon of ghee and cook the paratha over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Then flip the paratha over and add some ghee to the other side. Next, cook the paratha until it is evenly browned on each side over medium flame. Then, turn off the flame and remove it onto a serving plate. Make the rest of the parathas similarly and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('62754d0d35e977e17d921457','62754b7735e977e17d921455',1,'AP1: Soak the Chana','For Chana Chili, soak 1 cup of chickpeas in 2 cups of water for 8-10 hours. Please move on to the next step while the chickpeas soak.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":480,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('62754d800c136c6c53067741','62754b7735e977e17d921455',2,'P1: Boil the Chickpeas','To boil the chickpeas for Chana Chili, transfer the soaked chickpeas to a pressure cooker followed by half a cup of water and half a teaspoon of salt. Mix it well and cover the cooker with a lid. Then, allow it cook over high flame until 3 whistles. After that, reduce the flame to low and continue to boil the chickpeas for another 5 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and allow the pressure from the cooker release naturally. While the chickpeas boil, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":15,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":15,"flame":2}'),
('62754ed3eeb80cd182c6bb16','62754b7735e977e17d921455',3,'P2: Prep the Ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Chana Chili, wash, peel, and grate a half inch piece of ginger. Peel and finely chop 2 teaspoons of garlic. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of the white part of spring onions. Next, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of spring onion greens. Wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of green bell pepper. Wash and slit 2 green chilies. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Next, to make the corn flour slurry, add a teaspoon of corn flour to a bowl and stir in 1/4 cup of water. Mix it well to avoid any lumps','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('62754f6f0c136c6c53067742','62754b7735e977e17d921455',4,'P3: Prep the boiled Chickpeas','After boiling the chickpeas for Chana Chili, carefully remove the lid off the pressure cooker and remove the boiled chickpeas into a strainer. Discard the water and transfer the chickpeas to a large bowl. Next, add in 1/4 cup of corn flour and gently shake the bowl while tossing the chickpeas in the corn flour. Make sure that chickpeas are evenly coated in the corn flour.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('62754fed35e977e17d921458','62754b7735e977e17d921455',5,'M1: Fry the Chickpeas','To fry the chickpeas for Chana Chili, heat 1 cup of cooking oil in a kadai over medium-high flame for 2-3 minutes. Once the oil is medium-hot, carefully drop in the coated chickpeas one by one to the oil and deep fry them over medium flame for 3 minutes until the chickpeas are crisp and golden brown. After that, turn off the flame and remove them on a kitchen napkin to dab off the excess oil.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('6275523935e977e17d921459','62754b7735e977e17d921455',6,'M2:  Prepare the Chana Chili','To make Chana Chili, heat a tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium oil. Next, add 2 teaspoons of chopped garlic followed by a half inch piece of ginger, and 1/4 cup of chopped spring onions. Saute and fry the onions over high flame for 1-2 minutes. Next, add in 1/4 cup of chopped green bell pepper along with 2 slit green chilies and fry them over for 1-2 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('627554c00c136c6c53067743','62754b7735e977e17d921455',7,'M3:  Season the Chana Chili','Next, add 1 tablespoon of soy sauce, 1 tablespoon of white vinegar, 2 tablespoons of red chilli sauce, and 2 tablespoons of tomato ketchup. Mix it well and cook it for a minute. Next, add in the prepared corn flour slurry and mix it well while stirring continously to avoid any lumps. Add about 2-3 tablespoons of water and cook the sauce until it slightly thickens. Next, season it with half a teaspoon of salt and half a teaspoon of black pepper powder. After that, add the fried chickpeas and coat them evenly in the sauce. Then, turn off the flame and garnish it with 1/4 cup of chopped spring onion greens and 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves. Mix it well and plate the chickpeas. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('62760a6235e977e17d921460','6276069535e977e17d92145b',1,'P1: Prep the Ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Besan Pitla, first, add 2 tablespoons of gram flour to a sieve and sift the flour to break up the fine lumps. Next, peel, wash, and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Peel 4 cloves of garlic. Wash and slit 2 green chilies. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Next, cut a lemon into half and squeeze 1 tablespoon of juice in a bowl. Wash and pick 7 curry leaves.  Next, add 2 green chilies to a mortar followed by 7 cloves of garlic, and 1/4 a teaspoon of salt. Then, crush it well using a pestle to prepare a coarse paste.','prep_method','{"active_time":17,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('62760b8d35e977e17d921462','6276069535e977e17d92145b',2,'M1: Prepare the Tempering','To make the Besan Pitla, heat a tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame. Next, add half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, and half a teaspoon of cumin seeds. Saute and let it splutter for a few seconds. Add 7 curry leaves followed by 1/4 teaspoon of hing and saute it for a few seconds. After that, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions and fry them over medium flame for 3-4 minutes until translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('62760e9deeb80cd182c6bb1c','6276069535e977e17d92145b',3,'M2: Bring the water to boil and add gram flour','Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, half a teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Stir and fry the onions for another minute. Then, add 1.5 cup of water and bring it to a rolling boil over high flame. As the water comes to a boil, reduce the flame to low and gradually add 2 tablespoons of gram flour into it while stirring continuously to avoid any lumps. Keep stirring it over low flame for 3-4 minutes until it is well combined. Then, cover it with a lid and cook it over low flame for 5 minutes until it thickens. While it simmers, please move on to the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":5,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":5,"flame":2}'),('62760ff80c136c6c53067748','6276069535e977e17d92145b',4,'M3: Cook and season the Pitla','After simmering the besan pitla, remove the lid and give it a stir. Pitla has thickened and reached the right consistency. Turn off the flame and add a tablespoon of lime juice followed  by a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves. Mix it well and serve','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('62761f50eeb80cd182c6bb20','627619d0eeb80cd182c6bb1e',1,'P1: Prep the Karela','To prepare the bitter gourds for Bharwa Karela, first, wash 5 medium-small bittergourds and trim the ends as shown. Then, slit the bitter gourds vertically and remove all the seeds. Transfer the hollowed bittergourds to a bowl and sprinkle a teaspoon of salt. Rub the salt on the bitter gourds as shown, and leave them for 30 minutes. Salt will reduce the bitterness so always make sure to coat the bitter gourds in salt before cooking. please move on to the next step while the bitter gourds rest.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":30,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":30,"flame":0}'),
('6276203aeeb80cd182c6bb21','627619d0eeb80cd182c6bb1e',2,'P2: Prep the Ingredients','To prepare the ingredients for Bharwa Karela, soak a tablespoon of tamarind in 1/4 cup of water for 10 minutes. Next, peel, wash, and finely chop 3/4 cup of onions.  Grate 1/4 cup of fresh coconut using a grater. Next, to prepare the peanut powder, first, add 1/4 cup of peanuts to a pan and dry roast them over medium flame for 2-3 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and remove the peanuts in a blender jar. Allow them to slightly cool down before grinding. Then, grind the roasted peanuts into a fine powder.','prep_method','{"active_time":20,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('6276233b0c136c6c5306774b','627619d0eeb80cd182c6bb1e',3,'M1: Prepare the Stuffing','To make the stuffing for Bharwa Karla, first, heat a tablespoon of cooking oil in a pan over medium flame. Next, add 3/4 cup of chopped onions followed by half a teaspoon of turmeric powder and mix it well. Saute and fry the onions over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until translucent. Next, add half a teaspoon of red chili powder, and a teaspoon of coriander powder. Mix it well and fry the onions with the masala for another 1-2 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('627624460c136c6c5306774c','627619d0eeb80cd182c6bb1e',4,'M2: Continue preparing the stuffing','After that, add 1/4 cup of grated coconut along with 1/4 cup of roasted peanut powder and mix it well.  Next, add half a teaspoon of salt, half a teaspoon of fennel seeds, soaked tamarind pulp, and a teaspoon of jaggery. Mix it well and cook the stuffing for 1-2 minutes. Then, remove it in a bowl and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('627628ac0c136c6c5306774d','627619d0eeb80cd182c6bb1e',5,'M3: Stuff the Bittergourd','To make Bharwa Karela, first, wash the seasoned bitter gourds thoroughly with water to remove the salt. Then, stuff the bitter gourds with the prepared stuffing as shown. Next, heat 2 tablespoons of cooking oil in a pan and add the stuffed bitter gourds. Flip and cook the bitter gourds over medium flame on all sides. Cover the pan with a lid and simmer the bitter gourds for 5-6 minutes until tender and keep flipping them at regular intervals.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('62762988eeb80cd182c6bb26','627619d0eeb80cd182c6bb1e',6,'M4: Cook the Bittergourd','After simmering the Bharwa Karela, remove the lid and add the leftover stuffing. Sprinkle some water and cover the pan with a lid. Simmer it for another 1-2 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and plate the bitter gourds. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('628eff6e70bb2dbf00da1b7d','628efdc670bb2dbf00da1b7b',1,'P1: Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Amla Breakfast Smoothie, wash and deseed 3 Amlas and cut them in sections as shown. Then peel and roughly chop 1 banana. You can freeze the banana for a thicker smoothie. Next, deseed 2 dates.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('628f0272c53a466dcc3644af','628efdc670bb2dbf00da1b7b',2,'M1: Prepare the Smoothie','To make Amla Breakfast Smoothie, in a blender jar add 3 chopped amlas, add 5 cashew nuts for a creamy texture. Then, add 1 chopped banana, add 1/8 teaspoon of turmeric powder, add 1/8 teaspoon of black pepper powder, add 1/4 teaspoon of dry mango powder, add 1/2 cinnamon powder, add 2 deseeded dates for sweetness, add 1 tablespoon of flax seeds. Then, cover the jar with a lid and blend it well until smooth. Pour the smoothie into the serving glasses and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('628f16cae2a38341ff97adee','628f1023c53a466dcc3644b0',1,'P1: Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Apple Fennel Smoothie, wash and clean the fennel bulb, and dice half a cup of fennel bulb; wash, peel and core the pineapple and cut half a cup of pineapple into dices; wash, core and dice half a cup of green apple into dices; wash and pat dry 1/4 cup of baby spinach using a kitchen towel','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('628f17a6e2a38341ff97adef','628f1023c53a466dcc3644b0',2,'M1: Prepare the Smoothie','To prepare Apple Fennel Smoothie, in a blender jar add 1 cup of coconut water, add 1/4 cup of washed and cleaned baby spinach, add half a cup of diced fennel bulb, add 1/2 a cup of diced pineapple, add half a cup of diced green apple , add 1/2 a tablespoon of lemon juice, then cover the jar with a lid and blend it well until smooth. Pour the smoothie into the serving glasses and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('628f1baee2a38341ff97adf2','628f1b32e2a38341ff97adf0',1,'P1: Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Blueberry Banana Smoothie, wash and freeze 2 cups of blueberry; peel and roughly chop 1 banana, transfer the chopped banana in a bowl, cover the bowl with a lid and allow it to freeze for 30 minutes. While the fruits are being chilled move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":30,"advanced_prep_time":1800,"timer":30,"flame":0}'),
('628f1c5ae2a38341ff97adf3','628f1b32e2a38341ff97adf0',2,'M1: Prepare the Smoothie','To make blueberry banana smoothie, in a blender jar add 2 cups of coconut water, add 2 cups of frozen blueberry, add 1 chopped and frozen banana, add 1/2 a cup of yogurt, add 1 tablespoon of flax seeds, then cover the jar with a lid and blend it well until smooth. Pour the smoothie into the serving glasses and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('628f3bdfe2a38341ff97adf7','628f3356a7f58edc8b730bac',1,'P1: Prepare the green tea and prep the ingredients','To prepare green tea for Cucumber Kiwi Smoothie, first in a deep bottom pan add 3/4 cup of water and bring to a rolling boil. Meanwhile, place a green tea bag in a cup. After the water starts boiling, turn off the flame and pour the hot water over the tea bad and allow the tea bag to sit in for 3 minutes. Then remove the tea bag allow the green tea to cool. Refrigerate and chill the green tea for an hour. Meanwhile, wash, deseed and dice 1 cup of cucumber with the peel on; wash and pat dry 1 cup of baby spinach using a kitchen towel; wash, peel and dice 2 green kiwis. While the green tea is chilling move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":18,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":45,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":45,"flame":2}'),('628f3c5ee2a38341ff97adf8','628f3356a7f58edc8b730bac',2,'M1: Prepare the Smoothie','To make Cucumber Kiwi Smoothie, in a blender jar add 1/2 a cup of green tea, add 1 cup of diced cucumber, add 1 cup of baby spinach, add 2 diced kiwis along with 1 tablespoon of honey, then cover the jar with a lid and blend it well until smooth. Pour the smoothie into the serving glasses and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('628f465de2a38341ff97adfe','628f45f8a7f58edc8b730bb3',1,'P1: Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Ginger Shot, thoroughly wash 1/4 cup of ginger to get rid of all the mud. Next, roughly chop the ginger with it''s peel on. Then, cut 2 lemons into half, deseed them and squeeze 2 tablespoons of lemon juice.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('628f46df6c7b69e5885f51ac','628f45f8a7f58edc8b730bb3',2,'M1: Prepare the shot','To make Ginger Shot, in a blender jar add 1/4 cup of chopped ginger, add 2 tablespoons of lemon juice, add 1/4 cup of coconut water, add a pinch of cayenne pepper and blend it well until smooth. Then place a fine mesh strainer on the serving glass and pour the ginger shot over it to strain all the fiber, press with the back of the spoon to extract all the juices and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('628f4e667d7209a9389bac8c','628f4b2da0b61f97c08e0ce7',1,'P1: Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Grape Broccoli Smoothie, wash and pluck 1 cup of grapes; peel and roughly chop 1 medium sized banana, thoroughly wash a broccoli and cut them into 1 cup florets.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('628f503c0e2100caa4990214','628f4b2da0b61f97c08e0ce7',2,'M1: Prepare the Smoothie','To make Grape Broccoli Smoothie, in a blender jar add 3/4 cup of almond milk, add 1 cup of washed green grapes, add 1 roughly chopped banana, add 1 cup of broccoli florets, then cover the jar with a lid and blend it well until smooth. Pour the smoothie into the serving glasses and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('628f5d16a0b61f97c08e0cec','628f5c40a0b61f97c08e0cea',1,'P1: Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Green Juice, wash and cut 2 limes into half, deseed them and squeeze 2 tablespoons of lime juice, wash a medium sized cucumber and slice them into roundels with the skin on; wash and roughly chop 3 stalks of celery; thoroughly wash and chop 1/2 an inch of ginger; thoroughly wash 1/4 cup of kale; wash and core an apple and roughly chop 1/2 a cup of apple.','prep_method','{"active_time":18,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('628f5dc77d7209a9389bac8e','628f5c40a0b61f97c08e0cea',2,'M1: Prepare the Smoothie','To make Green Juice, in a blender jar add 2 tablespoons of lime juice, add 1/2 a cup of sliced cucumber, add half an inch of chopped ginger, add 3 roughly chopped celery, add 1/2 a cup of sliced apple, add 1/4 cup of kale leaves, add 1/2 a cup of water for easy blending. Then cover the jar with a lid and blend it well until smooth. Push down the ingredients using a tall spoon for easy blending. Then place a strainer on top of a mixing bowl and strain the smoothie to strain the fiber content or directly pour the smoothie into the serving glasses and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('628f63cb0e2100caa4990219','628f632fa0b61f97c08e0cee',1,'P1: Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Pineapple Paradise Smoothie, wash and pat dry 1 cup of baby spinach using a kitchen towel. Then peel and roughly chop 1 banana, wash, peel and dice 3/4 cup of pineapple, wash, peel and grate1/2 a teaspoon of ginger.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('628f64797d7209a9389bac91','628f632fa0b61f97c08e0cee',2,'M1: Prepare the Smoothie','To make Pineapple Paradise Smoothie, in a blender jar add 3/4 cup of unsweetened almond milk, add 1/4 cup of coconut milk, add 1 cup of washed and dried baby spinach, add 1 chopped banana, add 3/4 cup of chopped pineapple, add 1/2 a teaspoon of grated ginger; then cover the jar with a lid and blend it well until smooth. Pour the smoothie into the serving glasses and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('628f68d4a0b61f97c08e0cf1','628f67c50e2100caa499021b',1,'P1: Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Spirulina Pineapple Smoothie, first wash and peel a pineapple and core it, then cut 2 cups of pineapple into cubes, then wash and cut a small cucumber into half a cup of roundels with the skin on. Next, wash and pat dry 1/4 cup of kale, wash and peel 1/2 an inch of ginger, cut a lime into half and squeeze for lime juice.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('628f695f7d7209a9389bac95','628f67c50e2100caa499021b',2,'M1: Prepare the Smoothie','To make Spirulina Pineapple Smoothie, in a blender jar add 2 cups of cubed pineapple, add 1/2 a cup of sliced cucumber, add 1/4 cup of washed kale, add 1/2 an inch of peeled ginger, squeeze half a lime, add 1 teaspoon of spirulina powder followed by 1/2 a cup of water, then cover the jar with a lid and blend it well until smooth. Pour the smoothie into the serving glasses and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('628f6ccea0b61f97c08e0cf4','628f6c587d7209a9389bac97',1,'P1: Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Mango Tropical Smoothie, wash, peel and chop 2 cups of ripe mango, wash and pat dry 1/4 cup of baby spinach using a kitchen towel, wash and deseed an avocado and cut it into half.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('628f6d4d7d7209a9389bac99','628f6c587d7209a9389bac97',2,'M1: Prepare the Smoothie','To make Mango Tropical Smoothie, in a blender jar add 2 cups of chopped mango, add 1/4 cup of washed baby spinach, add half an avocado, add 1 teaspoon of spirulina, add 1 cup of coconut water, then cover the jar with a lid and blend it well until smooth. Alter the amount of coconut water in the smoothie to achieve the desired consistency. Pour the smoothie into the serving glasses and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('6298f6236d06336922956b21','6298f4a187f2fdb6b4ac1dca',1,'P1: Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Aloo Capsicum, peel and finely chop half a cup of onion, wash and finely chop half a cup of tomato; wash, a medium sized green bell pepper, cut it in the center and deseed it, then cut half a cup of bell pepper into dices. Wash, peel and cut half a cup of potatoes into cubes and set aside','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('6298f7b187f2fdb6b4ac1dce','6298f4a187f2fdb6b4ac1dca',2,'M1: Prepare the tempering and cook the potatoes','To prepare Aloo Capsicum, heat a pan on medium flame and add 1.5 tablespoons of cooking oil and allow it to become hot, then add a pinch of asafoeitida followed by half a teaspoon of cumin seeds and allow them to crackle. Next add half a cup of chopped onions along with half a teaspoon of ginger garlic paste and saute it on medium flame for 2 mins till the onions become translucent. Then add one cup of cubed potatoes and mix well with the tempering. Then cover the pan with a lid and cook the potatoes on medium low flame for 12 minutes until the potatoes cook and becomes soft. You can add a little water at this stage to fasten the cooking process. While the potatoes are cooking, move onto the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":12,"flame":2}'),('6298f849dc761ec6d976bcfe','6298f4a187f2fdb6b4ac1dca',3,'M2: Add the masalas and cook the tomato','After the potatoes have cooked for Aloo Capsicum, take off the lid and give it a good mix. Then add half a teaspoon of coriander powder, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, add half a teaspoon of Kashmiri Red Chili Powder followed by 1 teaspoon of salt to taste, then mix the masalas with the tempering until well combined. Next add half a cup of chopped tomatoes, mix it well and cook on medium flame for 4 minutes until the tomatoes become soft and mushy. While the tomatoes are cooking, move onto the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":1,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":4,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":4,"flame":2}'),('6298f8ef6d06336922956b22','6298f4a187f2fdb6b4ac1dca',4,'M3: Cook the sabzi','After the tomatoes have become soft for the Aloo Capsicum, add half a cup of diced capsicum and mix it well. Now cover the pan with a lid and allow the capsicum to cook for 8 minutes on medium low flame. Stir the sabzi occasionally to prevent the vegetables from burning or sticking to the bottom. After the capsicum has cooked, take off the lid and give it a mix, then add half a teaspoon of dry mango powder and mix well. Turn off the flame and garnish the sabzi with chopped coriander leaves and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":8,"flame":2}'),('629906b5dc761ec6d976bd01','629902eb6d06336922956b26',1,'P1: Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Meethi Keema, first wash and thoroughly clean 1 cup of fenugreek leaves under running water to ensure the roots are free from mud and dirt. Then roughly chop the leaves and set aside. Next, peel and finely chop half a cup of onion, wash and slit 1 green chili, cut a lemon into half and squeeze to collect lime juice, filter the seeds and set the lime juice aside. Then take a mixing bowl and add 1/4 cup of yogurt in it, whisk it well using a whisk until it reaches a pourable consistency and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('629908c36d06336922956b2a','629902eb6d06336922956b26',2,'M1: Prepare the Tempering','To prepare Meethi Keema, heat a pressure cooker pan without the lid on medium flame and add 2 tablespoons of mustard oil, allow it to become hot. Then add 1 black cardamom followed by 1 green cardamom and half an inch of cinnamon stick, saute it on medium flame for a few seconds and allow it to crackle. Then add half a cup of chopped onion and saute it with a spices for 3-4 mins or until it becomes translucent. Then add 1 teaspoon of ginger garlic paste and fry it with onions for another 4 mins until the onion turns golden brown.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('6299099f6d06336922956b2b','629902eb6d06336922956b26',3,'M2: Add the Masalas and Meat','To prepare the Meethi Keema, next add 1.5 cups of mutton mince along with one slit green chili and saute it with the onion masala on high flame for 5 to 6 minutes until the mince is cooked and becomes brown. Next, add 1 teaspoon of coriander powder, 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, 1 teaspoon of Kashmiri laal mirch powder, 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala and 1 teaspoon of salt and mix it well ensuring the masalas are well combined.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":4}'),('62990b136d06336922956b2c','629902eb6d06336922956b26',4,'M3: Pressure cook the meat','Next, to prepare Methi Keema, lower the flame and add 1/4 cup of whisked curd to it and mix it well with the mutton mince and cook on low flame for a minute. Then add 1/4 cup of water and mix again. Now cover the pan with the lid and pressure cook the mutton mince on high flame until one whistle, then lower the flame and allow it to cook for another 10minutes. Then turn off the flame and allow the pressure cooker to cool and release air naturally. While the mutton mince is cooking, move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":15,"flame":3}'),('62990bd187f2fdb6b4ac1dd0','629902eb6d06336922956b26',5,'M4: Add meethi leaves and cook the curry','To prepare Meethi Keema, after the pressure cooker has released air, carefully take off the lid and give it a good mix, then add 1 cup of roughly chopped fenugreek leaves along with 1 teaspoon of lemon juice and saute it on medium flame for 5 to 6 minutes until the meethi leaves are well combined and cooked. Next, adjust the salt s per taste, and add a little water at this stage if the curry is very thick. Allow the curry to simmer on low flame for 2 minutes, then turn off th flame and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('629994d2dc761ec6d976bd03','6299942287f2fdb6b4ac1dd3',1,'P1: Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Gajar Methi, first, wash and peel 1.5 cups of carrot and cut them into 1/4th inch cubes. Then wash and thoroughly clean 1 cup of fenugreek leaves under running water to ensure the roots are free from mud and dirt. Then finely chop the leaves and set aside.. Next, wash, peel and grate half an inch of ginger, peel and finely chop 2 teaspoons of garlic.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('6299959d239293e15044855e','6299942287f2fdb6b4ac1dd3',2,'M1: Prepare the tempering','To make Gajar Methi, heat a pan on medium flame and add 2 tablespoons of cooking oil and allow it to become hot. Then add 1/4 teaspoon of asefoeitida along with half a teaspoon of cumin seeds and saute it for a few seconds until they crackle. Then add a teaspoon of grated ginger, followed by 2 teaspoons of chopped garlic and saute it on low flame for a few seconds. Next, add 1.5 cups of cubed carrot and mix it well with the tempering. Allow it to cook for a minute.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('6299968d87f2fdb6b4ac1dd6','6299942287f2fdb6b4ac1dd3',3,'M2: Add the Masalas and cook the carrot','After the carrots have become tender, add 1 tablespoon of coriander powder, add 1/2 a teaspoon of turmeric powder, add 1 teaspoon of Kashmiri lal mirch powder, add 1/2 a teaspoon of garam masala, add some salt to taste and give it a good mix. Then cover the pan with a lid and allow the carrots to cook on low flame for 10minutes or until they become soft. Sprinkle some water at this stage to fasten the cooking process and prevent the masala from burning. While the carrots are cooking, move onto the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":10,"flame":1}'),('6299974bdc761ec6d976bd04','6299942287f2fdb6b4ac1dd3',4,'M3: Season and Garnish','After the carrots are cooked for Gajar Methi, take off the lid and give it a mix, then add 1 cup of chopped Methi leaves and combine it well with the carrots and masala. Allow it to cook on medium flame for 3-4 minutes until it shrinks. Keep stirring it occasionally to prevent it from burning. Then check and adjust the salt as per taste, turn off the flame and serve hot','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":4,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":4,"flame":2}'),('629bc0ca85551318bcdc4fc4','629bbed785551318bcdc4fc2',1,'P1: Cook the Noodles','To cook the noodles for Garlic Noodles, in a deep bottom pan add 3 cups of water along with 1 tablespoon of salt and bring to a rolling boil. When the water starts boiling add 200gms of egg noodles and allow it to cook for 6 to 8 minutes until they are 90% cooked. While the noodles are boiling, please move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":15,"flame":3}'),('629bc15085551318bcdc4fc5','629bbed785551318bcdc4fc2',2,'P2: Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Garlic Noodles, peel and finely chop 2 tablespoons of garlic, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of spring onion greens; peel and chop 1/2 a cup of onions into dices and set aside. After the noodles are 90% cooked, turn off the flame and carefully strain the noodles as shown using a colander, discard the water and set the cooked noodles aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('629bc23385551318bcdc4fc6','629bbed785551318bcdc4fc2',3,'M1: Prepare the Garlic Noodles','To prepare the Garlic Noodles, heat a pan on medium flame and add 2 tablespoons of sesame oil and allow it to become hot. Then add 2 tablespoons of chopped garlic and saute it on medium flame for a minute until it becomes golden brown. Then add half a cup of cubed onion followed by 4 dried red chilies and saute it with the browned garlic for a minute. Then add the boiled egg noodles along with some salt and toss it well such that the noodles are evenly coated with the oil and garlic mix. Cook the noodles on high flame for 2 minutes and then garnish it with chopped spring onions and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('629c4443e7e5902eb9ac37d9','629c43a3af0117ae76ffd130',1,'AP 1: Soak the Chickpeas','To soak the chickpeas for Himachali Chana Madra, in a mixing bowl add 1 cup of chickpeas along with 2 cups of water and allow it to soak for 8-10 hours. Please move on to the next step while the chickpeas soak.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":480,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('629c44e1e7e5902eb9ac37da','629c43a3af0117ae76ffd130',2,'P1: Boil the Chickpeas','To boil the chickpeas for Himachali Chana Madra, transfer the soaked chickpeas to a pressure cooker followed by 2 cups of water and half a teaspoon of salt. Mix it well and cover the cooker with a lid. Then, allow it cook over high flame until 3 whistles. After that, reduce the flame to low and continue to boil the chickpeas for another 5 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and allow the pressure from the cooker release naturally. While the chickpeas boil, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":15,"flame":2}'),('629c489daf0117ae76ffd132','629c43a3af0117ae76ffd130',3,'P2: Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Himachali Chana Madra, cut 1.5 cups of paneer into 1 inch cubes, wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves and set aside. In a mixing bowl add 2 cups of curds followed by 2 teaspoons of Maida, 2 teaspoons of coriander powder, 1/2 a teaspoon of cumin powder, 1/2 a teaspoon of turmeric powder, 2 teaspoons of kashmiri lal mirch powder, and whisk well until the masalas are well combined.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('629c49b985551318bcdc4fc8','629c43a3af0117ae76ffd130',4,'M1: Prepare the Tempering','To prepare the tempering for Himachali Chana Madra, heat a pan on medium flame and add 3 tablespoons of ghee and allow it to become hot. Then add 1/4 teaspoon of hingh followed by 1 teaspoon of cumin seeds and saute it on medium flame for a few seconds until they crackle. Then add 1 bay leaf, add 3 cloves, add 2 black cardamoms, one inch cinnamon and 2 dried red chillies and saute it for a few seconds until the aromas of the spices release. Next, lower the flame and add the whisked spice and curd mixture into the pan, mix it well with the tempering and allow it to cook on low flame for 2-3 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":3,"flame":2}'),
('629c4a67af0117ae76ffd133','629c43a3af0117ae76ffd130',5,'M2: Cook the Curry','Wile the curd mixture starts to boil for Himachali Chana Madra, add the boiled chana followed by 1.5 cups of cubed paneer, 10 cashewnuts and 10 raisins and then mix well. Allow the curry to simmer for a minute and then season it with a teaspoon of salt and 1/2 a teaspoon of sugar and allow the curry to cook on low flame for another 5 minutes. Then turn off the flame, garnish the curry with chopped coriander leaves and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('629c56ae85551318bcdc4fcc','629c5071e7e5902eb9ac37de',1,'P1:  Cook the Rice','To boil the rice for Tawa Pulao, first, rinse and clean half a cup of sona masuri rice thoroughly with water, then trasnfer the rice in a mixing bowl and add 2 cups of water and allow it to soak for 10minutes. While the rice is soaking, add 3 cups of water in a deep bottom pan with a teaspoon of oil and a teaspoon of salt and bring to a boil. Stir it well. When the water comes to a rolling boil, add the soaked rice, give it a stir, then cover the pan with a lid and allow it boil over medium flame for 8-10 minutes or until the rice is cooked through. Then, turn off the flame and strain the rice using a colander and set aside. Alternatively you can also cook the rice in a pressure cooker. While the rice is boiling, please move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":12,"flame":2}'),('629c5770e7e5902eb9ac37e0','629c5071e7e5902eb9ac37de',2,'P2: Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Tawa Pulao, wash and cut a medium sized green bell pepper into half, deseed it and chop 1/4 cup of green bell pepper; wash and chop 1/2 a cup of tomatoes; peel and finely chop half a cup of onions; peel, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of carrots; wash, string and finely chop 1/4 cup of beans and set aside.  Cut a lemon into half, squeeze the lemon juice in a bowl, filter and discard the seeds.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('629c5ceae7e5902eb9ac37e1','629c5071e7e5902eb9ac37de',3,'P3: Cook the vegetables','To cook the carrots and peas for Tawa Pulao, heat a deep bottom pan and add 2 cups of water with half a teaspoon of salt and bring to a boil. When the water reaches a rolling boil add 1/4 cup of peas and 1/4 cup of chopped carrots and 1/4 cup of chopped beans and allow it to cook for 8minutes or until they are cooked and become soft. While the evegetables are boiling,wash, peel and grate 2 teaspoons of ginger; wash and finely chop 1 teaspoon of green chilli; peel and finely chop 2 teaspoons of garlic; wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":10,"flame":2}'),('629c5dbe85551318bcdc4fcd','629c5071e7e5902eb9ac37de',4,'M1: Prepare the Tempering','To prepare Tawa Pulao, heat a frying pan and add 2 tablespoons of butter and allow it to melt to medium low flame, then add 1 teaspoon of cumin seeds and allow it to crackle. Next, add half a cup of chopped onion, add 2 teaspoons of grated ginger, add 2 teaspoons of chopped garlic, add 1 teaspoon of chopped green chilli and saute it on medium low flame for a minute until it becomes translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('629c5f4285551318bcdc4fce','629c5071e7e5902eb9ac37de',5,'M2: Cook the vegetables','To prepare Tawa Pulao, next add half a cup of chopped tomatoes followed by 1/4 cup of chopped capsicum and saute it on medium flame for 2 minutes until the tomatoes become soft. Then add 1/2 a teaspoon of turmeric powder, 1/2 a teaspoon of red chilli powder, 2 tablespoons of pav bhaji masala, and 1 teaspoon of salt, and mix it well with the tempering. Saute it for 2 minutes until when combined, add a little water at this stage to prevent the masala from burning. Slightly mash the masala using the back of the ladle and mix it well','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('629c5fdfaf0117ae76ffd136','629c5071e7e5902eb9ac37de',6,'M3: Prepare the Pulao','To prepare the Tawa Pulao, next add the boiled carrots, peas and beans followed by the cooked rice and combine it well with the masala. Break the rice lumps, and mash and mix with the masala as shown, ensure that the rice is well coated with the vegetables and masala. Then, add 2 teaspoons of lemon juice and mix it again. Garnish the pulao with chopped coriander leaves and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('629c67d5e7e5902eb9ac37e4','629c649d85551318bcdc4fd0',1,'P1: Clean the prawns','To clean the prawns for Drumstick Raw Mango Prawns, rinse 1 cup of prawns in cold water and discard any discolored or slimy ones. Then, hold the prawn with one hand and firmly twist off the head using your other hand. Then, pull off the tail, peel away the outer shell. Next, to devein the prawns take a sharp knife and make a slit on the backline of the prawns and remove the slimy greenish vein and discard the same. Similarly do so for the remaining prawns and rinse them again with cold water, remove in a bowl and set aside. If using the deveined prawns, then just rinse them under cold water and clean them.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('629c6dc2e7e5902eb9ac37e5','629c649d85551318bcdc4fd0',2,'P2: Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Drumstick Raw Mango Prawns, first, grate 1/4 cup of fresh coconut, then peel and finely chop 1 cup of onion, peel and thinly slice 5 shallots, wash and cut 0.5 cup raw mango into wedges. Then, wash and cut 1 drumstick into medium length pieces; wash, peel and roughly slice 1 inch ginger ; wash and pluck 10 curry leaves, wash 3 green chilies and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('629c6f6a85551318bcdc4fd3','629c649d85551318bcdc4fd0',3,'P3: Blend the Masala','To prepare the masala for Drumstick Raw Mango Prawns, in a mixy jar add 1 cup of chopped onions, add 1/4 of grated coconut, add 3 green chilies, add 1 inch of roughly sliced ginger and blend it into a smooth paste.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('629c71c1e7e5902eb9ac37e6','629c649d85551318bcdc4fd0',4,'M1: Cook the vegetables in masala','To cook the masala for Drumstick Raw Mango Prawns, heat a pan and add 2 tablespoons of coconut oil in it and allow it to become hot. Then add 1 teaspoon of mustard seeds followed by 10 curry leaves and allow it to splutter on medium low flame. Then add the blended masala paste and saute it on medium flame for 3-4 minutes until the masala is cooked. Then add 1/2 a cup of raw mango wedges along with 1/2 a cup of cut drumstick pieces followed by 1 teaspoon turmeric powder, 2 teaspoons of red chilli powder and 1 teaspoon of salt and mix it until well combined. Then add 1/4 cup of water and mix again. Then, cover the pan with a lid and allow the vegetables to cook in the masala for 8 minutes or until the vegetables become tender. While the vegetables are cooking, move onto the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":8,"flame":2}'),('629c7292e7e5902eb9ac37e7','629c649d85551318bcdc4fd0',5,'M2: Cook the prawns in masala and temper the Curry','After the vegetables have cooked for Drumstick Raw Mango Prawns, add 1 cup of deveined prawns along with 1/4 cup of water and allow the prawns to cook on medium flame for 5 to 6 minutes. While the prawns are simmering, heat a tadka pan on high flame and add half a tablespoon of coconut oil and allow it to become hot, then add 0.5 teaspoon of mustard seeds, add 5 curry leaves, add 3 dried red chilli followed by 5 sliced shallots and saute it on medium flame until the shallots become golden brown. Then turn off the flame, pour the tempering over the curry after the prawns have cooked, mix well and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":6,"flame":0}'),('629c7e9ee7e5902eb9ac37eb','629c7dfe85551318bcdc4fd5',1,'P1: Blanch the Spinach','To blanch the spinach for Palak Corn, wash a bunch of spinach leaves well with water. Remove the stems of 1 cup of spinach leaves. To blanch the spinach leaves, boil 2 cups of water in a deep bottom pan on high flame for 1-2 minutes. Then, add 1 cup of washed spinach leaves along with 1/2 teaspoon of salt to the boiling water and let it boil on medium flame for 2-3 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and drain the excess water from the spinach leaves. Then, wash the blanched spinach leaves under cold running water to prevent it from cooking further and set aside. While the spinach leaves are boiling, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":5,"flame":4}'),('629c7f0faf0117ae76ffd13a','629c7dfe85551318bcdc4fd5',2,'P2: Boil the Corn','To cook the corn for Palak Corn, first, boil 2 cups of water in a pan over medium-high flame for 1-2 minutes. As the water comes to a boil, add 1 cup of sweet corn kernels and boil them over medium flame for 4-5 minutes until tender. Then, turn off the flame and remove the blanched corn kernels in a bowl and set them aside. While the corn kernels are boiling, move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":10,"flame":3}'),('629c8189af0117ae76ffd13c','629c7dfe85551318bcdc4fd5',3,'P3: Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Palak Corn, peel and finely chop 1/2 cup of onions, peel and finely chop 3 cloves of garlic, wash and finely chop 1/2 cup of tomato, wash and finely chop 2 green chilies. Next, to prepare the palak puree in a mixy jar add the blanched palak, add 3 green chilies and blend it into a smooth puree.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('629c820485551318bcdc4fd7','629c7dfe85551318bcdc4fd5',4,'M1: Prepare the tempering','To prepare the tempering for Palak Corn, heat a pan and add 2 tablespoons of oil and allow it to become hot, then add 1/2 a teaspoon of cumin seeds along with 2 dried red chilli and saute it for a few seconds on medium low flame until it crackles. Next, add 1/2 a cup of chopped onion, add 3 cloves of chopped garlic and saute it for 3 minutes until the onion becomes translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('629c82c8e7e5902eb9ac37ec','629c7dfe85551318bcdc4fd5',5,'M2: Prepare the curry','To prepare Palak Corn, next add 1/2 a cup of chopped tomatoes and saute it on medium flame for 2 minutes until the tomatoes become slightly mushy, then add 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala and saute for another minute. Then, add the prepared palak puree and saute it on high flame for a minute until the puree is cooked and becomes dark green. Then add the boiled corn kernels followed by a teaspoon of salt and mix well. Then add half a cup of water, mix again and bring the curry to boil. Next, lower the flame and add 1 teaspoon of lemon juice, add 1 T of fresh cream and mix well. Turn off the flame and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('629c873de7e5902eb9ac37f0','629c86b0af0117ae76ffd13e',1,'P1: Clean the Bajra','To clean the husk for Bajra Khichdi, first wash 1/2 a cup whole Bajra with water a few times and then add then transfer the washed bajra in a mixy jar add pulse grind it to form a coarse powder. Do not over grind the Bajra, as we are grinding it only to remove the husk. Next, transfer the coarse powder in a bowl and add 2 cups of water and allow it to rest for a minute. The husk will float on top of the water, drain the water along with the husk as shown. Then, add 2 more cups of water to the bowl and wait for the husk to float on top, repeat the process until the bajra is clean and free of husk.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('629c87fe85551318bcdc4fda','629c86b0af0117ae76ffd13e',2,'P2: Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Bajra Khichdi, in a mixing bowl add half a cup of yellow moong dal and thoroughly rinse it with water, set aside. Then add 1/4 cup of Sona masuri rice in a mixing bowl and wash it well. Next, wash, peel and grate 1 teaspoon of ginger; wash and finely chop 2 teaspoons of green chilli.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('629c8908af0117ae76ffd140','629c86b0af0117ae76ffd13e',3,'M1: Prepare the Khichdi','To make Bajra Khichdi heat a bottom pan of the pressure cooker on high flame and add 1/2 a cup of washed and cleaned Bajra, add 1/2 a cup of washed yellow moong dal, add 1/4 cup of washed rice, followed by 1/4 teaspoon of hingh, 1/2 teaspoon of cumin seeds, 1 teaspoon of grated ginger and 2 teaspoons of chopped green chilli. Add 1 teaspoon of salt and mix the masalas well with the pulses. Next, add 7 cups of water and mix again. Then cover the pressure cooker with a lid and cook on high flame for 1 whistle, then lower the flame and allow it to simmer on low flame flame 10-12 minutes. Then turn off the flame and allow the pressure cooker to release the pressure naturally. While the khichdi is cooking, move onto the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":18,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),
('629c8949e7e5902eb9ac37f1','629c86b0af0117ae76ffd13e',4,'M2: Mix and serve hot','After the pressure cooker has cooled for Bajra Khichdi, gently take off the lid and mix the Khichdi nicely in a circular motion as shown, using a wooden or wire whisk. Add some water and adjust the consistency if the Khichdi looks too dry, cook the khichdi for another minute if you have added the water. Top it by pouring a tablespoon of ghee on top and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('629c94e685551318bcdc4fe1','629c943085551318bcdc4fdf',1,'P1: Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Pomegranate Raita, wash, peel and seprate half a cup of pomegranate seeds. Wash and finely chop 1 teaspoon of coriander leaves; wash and finely chop half a teaspoon of green chillies.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('629c95ae85551318bcdc4fe2','629c943085551318bcdc4fdf',2,'M1: Make the Raita','To make the Pomegranate Raita, in a mixing bowl add 1 cup of yogurt and beat it well using a whisk until it becomes smooth and creamy. Then add 1/4 cup of pomegranate juice followed by some salt to taste, 1/2 a teaspoon of sugar, 1/4 teaspoon of roasted cumin powder, 1/4 teaspoon of red chilli powder ,1 teaspoon of chopped coriander leaves and 1/2 a teaspoon of chopped green chillies. Mix well using a whisk, then add 1/2 a cup of pomegranate seeds and mix again. Refrigerate the pomegranate raita for an hour and serve chilled.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":60,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":60,"flame":0}'),('629c9a72af0117ae76ffd14a','629c9944e7e5902eb9ac37f8',1,'P1: Prepare the besan Mixture','To prepare the chickpea flour mixture, in a mixing bowl add 1/4 cup of chickpea flour along half a cup of water and mix well. Add the remaining 2 cups of water gradually to ensure the mixture is lump free. Break the lumps if any and mix well, set aside. Next, wash and pluck 8 curry leaves and then wash, peel and cube 1/4 cup of raw mangoes','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('629cb2a9e7e5902eb9ac37fa','629c9944e7e5902eb9ac37f8',2,'M1: Cook the mangoes','To prepare the tempering for Green mango Kadhi, heat a pan and add 1 tablespoon of cooking oil and allow it to become hot. Then add 1/2 a teaspoon of mustard seeds, add 1/4 teaspoon of fenugreek seeds, add 1/2 a teaspoon of cumin seeds, add 1/4 teaspoon of asafoetida followed by 8 curry leaves and 2 dried red chillies. Saute it on medium flame for a minute until the spices crackle, then add 1/4 cup of peeled and cubed raw mango and saute it with the tempering for a minute. Next, reduce the flame to low and cover the pan with a lid and allow the mangoes to cook for 3 minutes until they cook and become soft. Add a little water at this stage to prevent the tempering from burning.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":3,"flame":2}'),
('629cb37285551318bcdc4fe8','629c9944e7e5902eb9ac37f8',3,'M2: Cook the chickpea flour mixture','After the mangoes have cooked for Green Mango Kadhi, take off the lid and stir the cooked mangoes. Next, add the prepared besan mixture to the pan, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, add 1/4 teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Then, allow the kadhi to boil on medium flame for 10 to 12 minutes until the besan has cooked and the Green Mango Kadhi thickens. Stir the kadhi at regular intervals to prevent the besan from settling at the bottom and burning. After the besan has cooked, adjust the kadhi by adding water if the kadhi is too thick. The kadhi should be slightly runny and flowy in consistency. While the kadhi is boiling please move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":10,"flame":2}'),('629cb40c85551318bcdc4fe9','629c9944e7e5902eb9ac37f8',4,'M3: Add the Tadka','To prepare the tadka for kadhi, heat a tadka pan on medium flame and add 1/2 a tablespoon of ghee and allow it to become hot, then add 8 curry leaves and allow it to crackle. Then turn off the flame and add 1 teaspoon of  Kashmiri Red Chilli powder and mix well. Pour the prepared tempering over the kadhi and mix well. Serve hot','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('629ccdd1af0117ae76ffd14f','629cca54af0117ae76ffd14c',1,'AP1: Prepare Sour Curd','To prepare sour curd for Ripe Mango Kadhi, remove half a cup of curds in a bowl, cover it with a lid and allow it to rest in a warm place for 4 to 6 hours until it becomes sour. To use sour curd instantly for the Kadhi, simply squeeze a few drops of lime to the curds while adding it to the Kadhi.','prep_method','{"active_time":1,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":60,"advanced_prep_time":360,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('629cd753e7e5902eb9ac37fd','629cca54af0117ae76ffd14c',2,'P1: Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Ripe Mango Kadhi, first wash, peel and roughly chop 1/2 an inch ginger; wash a green chilli; wash and pluck 8 curry leaves. Next, to prepare the besan mixture, in a blender jar add 1/4 tablespoon of chickpea flour along with 1/2 a cup of sour curd followed by half an inch of ginger and 1 green chilli. Blend it into a smooth lump free watery mixture and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('629cd95de7e5902eb9ac37fe','629cca54af0117ae76ffd14c',3,'P2: Prepare mango Puree','To prepare the mango puree for Ripe Mango Kadhi, wash, peel and chop 1 mango. Then in a blender jar, add the chopped mango along with 1/4 cup of water and blend it into a smooth puree. Then in a wide mixing bowl add half a cup of water then wash and massage the mango pit to collect the remaining pulp sticking on it. mix the collected pulp with the puree and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('629cdaeeaf0117ae76ffd150','629cca54af0117ae76ffd14c',4,'M1: Prepare the Tempering','To prepare Ripe Mango Kadhi,first, heat a pan on medium flame and add 1 tablespoon of cooking oil and allow it to become hot. Then add 1/2 a teaspoon of fenugreek seeds, add 1/4 a teaspoon of mustard seeds, add 1/4 a teaspoon of cumin seeds followed by a pinch of asafoetida, 1 dry red chilli and 7 curry leaves. Reduce the flame and saute the tempering for a few seconds and allow them to crackle.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('629ce0c785551318bcdc4fec','629cca54af0117ae76ffd14c',5,'M2: Cook the puree and chickpea mixture','After the tempering has crackled for Ripe Mango Kadhi, add the prepared besan mixture along with 1/4 cup of water. Then add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, add half a teaspoon of salt, add half a cup of prepared mango puree and mix well. Then allow the kadhi to simmer on medium flame for 15minutes. Keep stirring the kadhi at regular interval to prevent the chickpea flour from settling down and burning. While the kadhi is simmering move onto the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":15,"flame":2}'),('629ce170af0117ae76ffd151','629cca54af0117ae76ffd14c',6,'M3: Top it with Tadka','To prepare the tadka for Ripe mango kadhi, heat a pan on medium flame and add 1 tablespoon of ghee and allow it to become hot. Then add 1/4 teaspoon of fenugreek seeds, add 1/4 teaspoon of mustard seeds, add 1/4 teaspoon of cumin seeds and 1 dried red chilli. Mix well and allow the tempering to crackle. Then, turn off the flame and add 1/4 teaspoon of red chilli powder . Mix again and pour the tempering over the ripe mango kadhi and serve hot','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('629d83c93c7f2023640b5f93','629d822b3c7f2023640b5f92',1,'P1: Prep the Noodles','To soak the noodles for Pad Thai Noodles, heat a sauce pan and add 200 ml of water and simmer the water until it becomes lukewarm. Do not boil the water. Then, in a mixing bowl add 150gms of flat rice noodles and pour the lukewarm water on top, ensure that the noodles are evenly soaked in the water. Allow the rice noodles to soak for 15 minutes until they become soft. Do not overcook the noodles. Next, after 15minutes, drain the water, seperate the noodles and add few drops of cooking oil to the strained noodles, toss the noodles well and set aside. While the noodles are soaking move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('629d84fbaf0117ae76ffd159','629d822b3c7f2023640b5f92',2,'P2: Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Pad Thai Noodles, peel and finely chop 1 teaspoon of garlic, wash and finely chop half a teaspoon of thai red chilli, peel and slice 1/4 cup of onion, wash cut and deseed half a red bell pepper and slice 2 tablespoons of red bell pepper, wash cut and deseed half a yellow bell pepper and slice 2 tablespoons of yellow bell pepper. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of cilantro. Next, in a blender jar add 2 tablespoons of roasted peanuts and pulse grind to break the peanuts into smaller pieces as shown. Do not pulse grind it into a powder','prep_method','{"active_time":18,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('629d863329fb46b3cfbc50f3','629d822b3c7f2023640b5f92',3,'M1: Prepare the Sauce','To prepare the sauce for pad Thai noodles, heat a deep bottom pan and add 1/4 vegetable stock cube along with half a cup of water and mix well, then add 1.5 tablespoon of soy sauce, add add 1.5 tablespoon of brown sugar, add 1/2 a teaspoon of tamarind paste, add 1/2 a teaspoon of red chilli paste, add half a teaspoon of salt along with 1/4 cup of water. Mash the pastes using the back of the ladle and mix well. Bring the sauce to a boil on high flame and then reduce the flame to medium and allow it to simmer for 3 minutes. While the sauce is cooking move onto the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('629d8b7b3c7f2023640b5f94','629d822b3c7f2023640b5f92',4,'M2: Cook the vegetables','To prepare Pad Thai Noodles, heat a pan on high flame and add 1 tablespoon of sesame oil and allow it to become hot. Then add 1 teaspoon of chopped garlic, add 1/2 a teaspoon of chopped Thai red chilli and saute it for a few seconds until the garlic becomes golden brown. Then add 1/4 cup of sliced onions followed by 2 tablespoons of sliced red bell pepper, 2 tablespoons of sliced yellow bell pepper and 2 tablespoons of bean sprouts. Mix and saute well on medium flame for a minute until the vegetables become tender.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('629d8c29af0117ae76ffd15a','629d822b3c7f2023640b5f92',5,'M3: Prepare the Noodles','Next, to prepare the Pad Thai Noodles add the cooked rice noodles followed by the prepared Pad Thai Noodles sauce and toss it well using kitchen tongs. Ensure that the noodles are well coated with the sauce. Allow it to simmer on medium low flame for 2-3 minutes until the sauce has slightly thickened. Then, turn off the flame and garnish with 2 tablespoons of chopped peanuts and 1 tablespoon of chopped cilantro and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('629da847af0117ae76ffd161','629da6683c7f2023640b5f99',1,'P1: Cook the Noodles','For Shrimp Mei Fun, first, boil 3 cups of water in a pot, once the water is boiling reduce the flame to low and then add 200 grams of rice noodles. Cook them for 8-12 mins on high flame until cooked through, then turn off the flame and drain the water using a colander. Wash the cooked noodles under cold running water to prevent it from cooking further and turning mushy. Next, add one teaspoon of cooking oil along with one teaspoon of dark soy sauce and toss the noodles well using tongs. The noodles should be evenly coated with the sauce. While the noodles are boiling move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":12,"flame":5}'),('629da8c53c7f2023640b5f9d','629da6683c7f2023640b5f99',2,'P2: Clean the Shrimp','To prep the shrimp for Shrimp Mei Fun, rinse 100 grams of prawns in cold water and discard any discolored or slimy ones. Then, hold the shrimp with one hand and firmly twist off the head using your other hand. Then, pull off the tail, peel away the outer shell. Next, to devein the shrimps take a sharp knife and make a slit on the backline of the shrimps and remove the slimy greenish vein and discard the same. Similarly do so for the remaining shrimps and rinse them again with cold water, remove in a bowl and set aside. If using the deveined shrimps, then just rinse them under cold water and clean them.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('629da9db29fb46b3cfbc50fc','629da6683c7f2023640b5f99',3,'P3: Marinate the Shrimps','To marinate the shrimps for Shrimp Mei Fun, in a mixing bowl add 100 grams of cleaned shrimps, then add 1 teaspoon of corn starch, add 1/2 a tablespoon of oyster sauce, add 1/2 a tablespoon of white wine vinegar, add 1/4 teaspoon of white pepper powder along with half a teaspoon of cooking oil and mix well. The shrimps should be well coated with the marinade. Allow the shrimps to marinate for 20 minutes. While the shrimps are marinating move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('629dab253c7f2023640b5f9e','629da6683c7f2023640b5f99',4,'P4: Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Shrimp Mei Fun, wash peel and julienne 1 tablespoon of ginger; peel, wash and slice 2 shallots; wash, peel and julienne 1/4 cup of carrot; wash and finely slice 1/2 a cup of cabbage; wash and cut 1 spring onion green into medium length pieces','prep_method','{"active_time":18,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('629dac6caf0117ae76ffd162','629da6683c7f2023640b5f99',5,'M1: Stir Fry the vegetables and shrimp','To prepare Shrimp Mei Fun, first keep the chopped veggies and the marinated shrimp ready as they all need to be cooked on high flame one after the other. Heat a wok on high flame and allow it to become hot, then add 1.5 tablespoon of vegetable oil and allow it to become hot. Next add, 1 tablespoon of julienned ginger followed by 2 sliced shallots and stir fry on high flame for a few seconds. Then add the marinated shrimp and allow it to cook for 3 minutes until it turns slightly pink and is cooked. Keep stirring the shrimps while cooking to prevent it from burning.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":5}'),('629dad2929fb46b3cfbc50fe','629da6683c7f2023640b5f99',6,'M2: Add the noodles and season it','After the shrimps have cooked for Shrimp Mei Fun, add 1/4 cup of julienned carrot followed by 1/2 a cup of sliced cabbage, then 1 Tablespoon of chopped spring onion greens and stir fry on high flame for a minute. Next, to season the vegetables add half a tablespoon of dark soy sauce, add 1/4 teaspoon of sesame oil, add 1/4 teaspoon of white pepper powder, add 1/2 a teaspoon of salt and mix everything well. Then add the boiled noodles and toss them well with the shrimp and vegetables. Check for seasoning and sauces and alter as per taste. Then mix well and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":4}'),('629e3c5daf0117ae76ffd16b','629de13caf0117ae76ffd168',1,'AP1: Soak the Sabudana','To soak the sago for Sabudana Thalipeeth, first rinse half a cup sago twice, do not rinse it too much as it would wash away the starch. The starch in the sago will help bind the dough. Next, in a mixing bowl add the washed sago along with 1 cup of water and allow it to soak for 8 hours. The sago pearls should become soft enough to be mashed, if the pearls are still hard from the center add some more water and allow it to soak for another hour. Then, drain the water and set the soaked sago aside. While the sago is soaking move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":480,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('629e3ce0af0117ae76ffd16c','629de13caf0117ae76ffd168',2,'P1: Boil the potatoes','To boil the potatoes for Sabudana Thalipeeth, wash 1 medium-small sized potatoes and add it to a pressure cooker along with 1 cup of water. Cover it with a lid and pressure cook the potatoes over high flame until 1 whistle. Then, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook the potato for another 8 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. Then take off the lid, and allow the potatoes to cool While the potatoes are boiling, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":12,"flame":2}'),('629e3d923c7f2023640b5fa4','629de13caf0117ae76ffd168',3,'P2: Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Sabudana Thalipeeth, wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves, wash and finely chop 1 teaspoon of green chillies. Next, in a blender jar add 2 tablespoons of roasted peanuts and blitz it into a coarse powder. After the potatoes have cooled, gently peel the potatoes, transfer the peeled potatoes in a mixing bowl and mash them until soft using a masher.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('629e4005af0117ae76ffd16d','629de13caf0117ae76ffd168',4,'P3: Prepare the Dough','To prepare the dough for Sabudana Thalipeeth, in a mixing bowl add 1/2 a cup of soaked sago, add 1/4 cup of boiled and mashed potato, add 2 tablespoons of chopped coriander leaves, add 1/4 teaspoon of salt, add 1 teaspoon of chopped green chillies, add 2 tablespoons of coarsely crushed roasted peanuts, add 1 teaspoon of lime juice, add 1 teaspoon of sugar and 2 tablespoons of amaranth flour followed by 1/2 a teaspoon of cumin seeds and mix well, using your hands. Knead well mashing all the ingredients as shown, to make a soft and sticky dough. If the dough feels dry, wet your hands and continue to knead the dough.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('629e40e9af0117ae76ffd16e','629de13caf0117ae76ffd168',5,'M1: Shape the Thalipeeth','To make Sabudana Thalipeeth, heat a tawa on medium heat and allow it to become hot. Meanwhile, place a parchment paper on the counter and drizzle some oil on the paper and grease it well with oil. Next wet your hands with water, this will prevent the dough from sticking to you hands. Then, take a lemon sized ball of the prepared dough, and shape it into a ball. Then gently flatten it between your palms, then place the flattened dough on the parchment paper and flatten it further by gently patting it as shown, ensure that the sides are thinner than the center. After flattening it into a 5 inch disc, shape it from the sides as shown. Next, make a hole in the center of the flattened dough, using your finger.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('629e4132af0117ae76ffd16f','629de13caf0117ae76ffd168',6,'M2: Roast the Thalipeeth','Next, to roast the Sabudana Thalipeeth, lift the parchment paper and place it upside down with the thalipeeth onto the hot griddle. Now, gently peel off the thalipeeth and drizzle half a teaspoon of oil in the center of the hole, and drizzle a teaspoon of oil circling the sides of the thalipeeth. Roast it on medium low flame until the bottom starts to brown and becomes crisps, then flip the thalipeeth and drizzle some oil in the center and on the sides. Allow to cook on the other side for 3 minutes, until it becomes brown. Do the same for the remaining dough and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('629e47b729fb46b3cfbc510c','629e462a29fb46b3cfbc510a',1,'P1: Poach and Shred the Chicken','To poach the Chicken for Chicken Sweet Potato Soup, heat a deep bottom pan and add 100 gms of skinless chicken breasts along with 2 cups of water or until it is 2 inches above the breast, then add 1 teaspoon of salt and mix well. Allow the chicken to cook on medium high flame for 12-15 minutes until the chicken is cooked through. The chicken will turn white with a foam formation on top, remove the foam at regular intervals. Do not overcook the chicken as it will become chewy. If the chicken breast is thin, reduce the cooking time. After the chicken breast has cooked, turn off the flame place the cooked breast on a chopping board and shred the chicken using 2 forks as shown. While the chicken breast is cooking, move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":15,"flame":3}'),('629e48db3c7f2023640b5fa9','629e462a29fb46b3cfbc510a',2,'P2: Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Chicken Sweet Potato Soup, peel and finely chop 2 tablespoons of onion; wash, peel and cube 1/4 cup of carrot, wash and finely chop 1/4 celery; peel and finely chop 1/2 teaspoon of garlic. Next, wash and trim the mushroom stems, then slice 1/4 cup of mushrooms; wash and thoroughly clean 1/4 cup of spinach to get rid of the mud, then finely chop the spinach. Wash, peel and cube 1/4 cup of sweet potato.','prep_method','{"active_time":20,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('629e499e3c7f2023640b5faa','629e462a29fb46b3cfbc510a',3,'M1: Stir fry the vegetables','To prepare Chicken Sweet Potato Soup, heat a deep bottom pan on medium flame and add 1 tablespoon of olive oil and allow it to become hot. Then add 2 tablespoons of chopped onion, add 1/4 cup of cubed carrot, add 1/4 chopped celery and saute it for 3 minutes until the vegetables become tender. Next, add 1 teaspoon of finely chopped garlic followed by 1/4 cup of cubed sweet potato and saute it on medium flame for 5-7 minutes. Keep stirring at regular interval to prevent the vegetables from sticking to the bottom and burning.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":5,"flame":2}'),('629e4a5b29fb46b3cfbc510d','629e462a29fb46b3cfbc510a',4,'M2: Season and boil the stock','Next, to prepare the Chicken Sweet Potato Soup, add 1/8 teaspoon of cayenne pepper, add 1/2 a teaspoon of dried oregano, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, add 1/4 teaspoon of black pepper powder and mix well. Next add 2.5 cups of water along with one chicken stock cube, and mix it well. Then, cover the Pan with a lid, reduce the flame to low and allow it to simmer on low flame for 12 minutes. While the soup is simmering move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":1,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":12,"flame":2}'),('629e4b1129fb46b3cfbc510e','629e462a29fb46b3cfbc510a',5,'M3: Cook the vegetables and prepare the soup','After the stock has boiled for the Chicken Sweet Potato soup, add 1/4 cup of sliced mushroom, add the shredded chicken, and mix well. Cover the pan with a lid and allow to simmer on medium low flame for 8 minutes until the sweet potatoes become soft. After 8 minutes, insert a fork in the potato to check if they are cooked through. Next, turn off the flame and add 1/4 cup of chopped spinach and mix it well until the leaves shrink. Then, add 1 tablespoon of heavy cream, followed by 1/4 tablespoon of lemon juice, then mix well and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":8,"flame":2}'),
('629ef13477df44ca9ebc0d6c','629ee8aa41c0a73ad905c141',1,'P1: Prepare the first marination','To prepare the first marination for Tandoori Chicken, wash and pat dry 1kg chicken legs using a kitchen towel. Then, using a sharp knife make 4 diagonal slits on the chicken legs on each side of the leg. This will help absorb the marination. Next, in a mixing bowl add 1 teaspoon of salt, add 3 teaspoons of lemon juice, add 2 teaspoons of ginger garlic paste, add 2 teaspoons of Kashmiri red chilli powder and mix well. Next, add the slit chicken legs in the marinade and toss it well. Ensure that the chicken legs are evenly marinated. Cover the bowl with a lid and refrigerate for an hour. While the chicken is marinating, move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":60,"advanced_prep_time":60,"timer":60,"flame":0}'),('629ef26277df44ca9ebc0d6d','629ee8aa41c0a73ad905c141',2,'P2: Prepare the second marination','To prepare the second marination for the Tandoori Chicken, remove the marinated chicken from the refrigerator then, add 2 tablespoons of thick yogurt, add 1 teaspoon of ginger garlic paste, add 1 teaspoon of Kashmiri red chilli powder, add 1/2 a teaspoon of black pepper powder, add 1/2 a teaspoon of turmeric powder, add 1/2 a teaspoon of cumin powder, add 1/2 a teaspoon of garam masala, add 1 teaspoon of coriander powder, add 2 tablespoons of mustard oil, add 1 teaspoon of lime juice, add 2 tablespoons of heavy cream, add 1 tablespoon of kasuri methi and then mix it well using your fingers. Rub the marinade on the chicken and coat it evenly, then cover the bowl with a foil and refrigerate it for 8 hours.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":480,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":480,"flame":0}'),('629ef35f7e07b1f43c93032b','629ee8aa41c0a73ad905c141',3,'M1: Pan sear the Chicken','To grill the Tandoori Chicken, heat a grill pan on medium flame and allow it to become hot. Then place the marinated chicken piece on the grill pan using tongs. Then drizzle one tablespoon of mustard oil evenly on the chicken piece, then cover the pan with a lid and cook on medium flame for 8 minutes until the chicken is cooked and charred. Then take off the lid and flip the chicken on the other side, cover with a lid and cook again for another 8 minutes until the chicken is cooked and charred.  While the chicken is cooking, move onto the next stop','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":16,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":16,"flame":3}'),('629ef3bb7e07b1f43c93032c','629ee8aa41c0a73ad905c141',4,'M2: Roast the Chicken on open flame','After the chicken is cooked for Tandoori Chicken, increase the flame to high, take off the lid and allow the marinated juices to evaporate. Then turn off the flame. Next, place a wire rack on direct flame on high heat, and place the grilled chicken on top, continue flipping and roasting over direct flame until the chicken is charred. Then turn off the flame, transfer the Tandoori Chicken onto a plate, garnish with a pinch of chaat masala and serve hot with onion rings and lemon wedges.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":4}'),('629efcfe7e07b1f43c930335','629ef84e611512d32b3a73ac',1,'P1: Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Daliya Khichdi, first wash, peel and cube 1/4 cup of carrot, wash, peel and cube 1/4 cup of potatoes, add the cubed potatoes in a bowl of water until use to prevent it from turning black. Then, wash, string and chop 1/4 cup of green beans; wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves; wash, peel and finely chop 1 teaspoon of ginger. Next, thoroughly wash 1/4 cauliflower with warm water and ensure there are no worms, then cut 1/4 cup of florets and set aside. Then, rinse 1/4 cup of broken wheat, and rinse 1/4 cup of split yellow lentils.','prep_method','{"active_time":25,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('629f01b5611512d32b3a73b5','629ef84e611512d32b3a73ac',2,'M1: Saute the vegetables','To prepare the tempering for Daliya Khichdi, heat a pressure cooker pan and add 1 tablespoon of ghee and allow it to become hot, then add 1/2 a teaspoon of cumin seeds, add a pinch of hingh and saute it for a few seconds on low flame until the spices crackle. Next, add 2 dry red chillies, add 2 slit green chillies, add 1 teaspoon of chopped ginger and saute it on medium low flame for a few seconds. Next, add 1/4 cup of cubed caroot, add 1/4 cup of chopped beans, add 1/4 cup of cubed potatoes, add 1/4 cup of cauliflower florets, and saute them on medium high flame for a minute.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":3,"flame":3}'),('629f0f25611512d32b3a73b6','629ef84e611512d32b3a73ac',3,'M2: Cook the Khichdi','Next, to prepare Daliya Khichdi, add 1/4 cup of rinsed broken wheat and add 1/4 cup of rinsed moong dal. Then add 1.5 cups of water followed by 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder and some salt to taste. Mix it well with the vegetables and dal, then cover the cooker with a lid and pressure cook the khichdi on high flame for one whistle, then reduce the flame to low and continue to cook the khichdi for another 8 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. After the pressure has released, take off the lid and garnish with 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and 1/2 a tablespoon of lime juice and mix well. Serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":5,"flame":2}'),('629f187d7e07b1f43c930338','629f1780611512d32b3a73b7',1,'P1: Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Clear Chicken Soup, peel and finely chop 2 tablespoons of onion; wash, peel and chop 2 tablespoons of carrot; peel and smash 3 garlic cloves, wash and chop; wash and chop 1 spring onion green. Next, in a mortar and pestle add 10 to 12 whole black peppercorns and pound it into a fine powder.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('629f1adb77df44ca9ebc0d77','629f1780611512d32b3a73b7',2,'P2: Prepare the Chicken Stock','To prepare chicken stock for Clear Chicken Soup, first thoroughly wash 150 gms of chicken. Then heat a cooker''s bottom pan  and add the washed chicken with bones, add 2 tablespoons of chopped onion, add 3 smashed garlic cloves, add 2 tablespoons of chopped carrots, add 1 bay leaf, add 1 sprig of thyme followed by 2 cups of water, 1/2 a teaspoon of salt and 1/4 teaspoon of crushed black pepper powder. Mix well, and cover the cooker with a lid and cook on high flame until one whistle, and then reduce the flame and allow it to simmer on low flame for 8 to 10minutes. After that, turn off the flame and allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the chicken is cooking, move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":15,"flame":3}'),('629f1c257e07b1f43c930339','629f1780611512d32b3a73b7',3,'M1: Assemble the Soup','To prepare Clear Chicken Soup, place a deep bottom mixing bowl and then place a strainer on top. Next, take off the lid of the pressure cooker and strain the vegetables and chicken bones, collect the stock water and set aside. Next, discard the vegetables and transfer the chicken pieces onto a plate and shred them using your hands or fork as shown. Then, add a ladle of the chicken stock in a serving bowl, add the shredded chicken, garnish it with a teaspoon of chopped spring onion greens and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('629f50de5511d9e71bcc7d9f','629f5021408a7678b46618ff',1,'AP1: Freeze the Fruits','To prep the ingredients for Strawberry Kiwi Smoothie, wash, peel and chop 2 kiwis; wash and hull (remove the green leaves) of 12 strawberries and thinky slice them, peel and slice 1 banana. In a mixing bowl add the sliced kiwi, sliced strawberries and sliced banana, place it in the chiller and allow it to freeze for 5 hours. While the fruits are being chilled, move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":300,"advanced_prep_time":300,"timer":300,"flame":0}'),('629f512c408a7678b4661901','629f5021408a7678b46618ff',2,'P1: Thaw the Fruits','To thaw the fruits for Strawberry Kiwi Smoothie, thaw them under running water for a few seconds or allow it to sit in a warm place for 10 minutes to become slightly soft. While the fruits are thawing move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":1,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":10,"flame":0}'),('629f51eb5e33e0a4df83145b','629f5021408a7678b46618ff',3,'M1: Prepare the Smoothie','To prepare the Strawberry Kiwi Smoothie, in a blender jar, add 2 chopped kiwis, add 12 sliced strawberries, add 1 sliced banana followed by half a cup of milk. Then add 1 teaspoon of Chia seeds, add 2 teaspoons of honey and blend it into a smooth puree. Add some milk at this point if the smoothie is too thick. Transfer the Strawberry Kiwi Smoothie into a serving glass and garnish it with chia seeds, chopped fruits or mint leaf. Serve chilled','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('62a035a1408a7678b4661909','62a023015511d9e71bcc7da0',1,'AP1: Freeze the Fruits','To prep the ingredients for Muskmelon Smoothie, peel and slice 1/2 a cup of banana and transfer it in a bowl, cover it with a lid and place it in the chiller. Allow it to freeze for 4 hours. While the banana is in the chiller, move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":240,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('62a0360c5e33e0a4df831469','62a023015511d9e71bcc7da0',2,'P1: Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Muskmelon Smoothie, wash, peel and cut the muskmelon into half and then using a spoon scoop out the seeds and discard them. Then, chop the deseeded muskmelon and set aside. If not using canned orange juice, wash and peel an orange and deseed them, then transfer the deseeded orange juice in a blender jar and blend it into a fine juice.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('62a03682408a7678b466190a','62a023015511d9e71bcc7da0',3,'M1: Prepare the Smoothie','To prepare Muskmelon Smoothie, in a blender jar add 1 cup of peeled and chopped muskmelon, add ½ a cup of peeled, sliced and frozen banana, add 2 tablespoons of curd, and ¼ cup of orange juice and blend into a smooth puree. Add some milk at this point if the smoothie is too thick. Transfer the Muskmelon Smoothie into a serving glass and serve chilled or as it is.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('62a041f45e33e0a4df83146f','62a041275e33e0a4df83146c',1,'AP1: Freeze the Fruits','To prep the ingredients for Watermelon Smoothie, first wash a watermelon and cut it into half. Then, cut them into smaller slices and deseed them, now cut one and a half cup of watermelon into cubes. Next, wash and hull (remove the green leaves) half a cup of strawberries and roughly chop them. In a mixing bowl, add the cubed watermelon and chopped strawberries and cover it with a lid. Place the bowl in the chiller and allow it to freeze for 4 hours. While the fruits are being chilled move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":300,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('62a042515e33e0a4df831470','62a041275e33e0a4df83146c',2,'P1: Thaw the Fruits','To thaw the fruits for Watermelon Smoothie, thaw them under running water for a few seconds or allow it to sit in a warm place for 5 minutes to become slightly soft. Then, wash and pluck 1 tablespoon of mint leaves. While the fruits are thawing move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":1,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":5,"flame":0}'),('62a042f5408a7678b466190d','62a041275e33e0a4df83146c',3,'M1: Prepare the Smoothie','To make Watermelon Smoothie, in a blender jar add 1.5 cups of frozen cubed watermelon, add half a cup of frozen strawberry, add 1/4 cup of thick vanilla yogurt, add 1/4 tablespoon of honey, add 1/4 cup of milk, add 1 tablespoon of washed and plucked mint leaves and blend it into a fine puree. Add some milk at this point if the smoothie is too thick. Transfer the Watermelon Smoothie into a serving glass and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('62a06ecf408a7678b4661911','62a06e4a257bc51176277de5',1,'AP1: Freeze the Fruits','To prep the ingredients for Green Apple Spinach Smoothie, first, peel and slice 1 cup of Banana. Transfer it in a bowl and place it in a chiller. Allow it to freeze for 4 hours. While the Banana is being chilled, move towards the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":1,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":300,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('62a06f51408a7678b4661914','62a06e4a257bc51176277de5',2,'P1: Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Green Apple Spinach Smoothie, thoroughly rinse 1 cup of spinach and pat dry using a kitchen towel. Next, wash and core 1 green smith apple and roughly chop with the skin on, transfer the chopped green apple in a bowl filled with water to prevent it from turning black. Then, in a mortar and pestle add 1 teaspoon of flax seeds and pound it into a fine powder.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('62a06fdee5a130569204d421','62a06e4a257bc51176277de5',3,'M1: Prepare the Smoothie','To prepare Green Apple Spinach Smoothie, in a blender jar add 1 cup of spinach, add 1 chopped green smith apple, add 1 cup of sliced and frozen banana, add 1 teaspoon of ground flax seeds, add 1 cup of water, add 1/2 a cup of plain yogurt and blend it into a smooth puree. Add some water or curds at this point if the smoothie is too thick. Transfer the Green Apple Spinach Smoothie into a serving glass and serve chilled.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('62a183574fef9acdfc16379f','62a17b577bd3bfc140191968',1,'P1: Freeze the watermelon','To freeze the watermelon for Watermelon Feta Salad, first wash a watermelon and cut it into half. Then, cut them into smaller slices and deseed them, now cut 3 cups of watermelon into medium sized cubes. Transfer the deseeded watermelon cubes into a bowl, cover it with a lid and allow to chill in the refrigerator for an hour. While the watermelon is being chilled, move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":60,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":60,"flame":0}'),('62a183f855140e9b2409a4c5','62a17b577bd3bfc140191968',2,'P2: Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Watermelon Feta Salad, first crumble half a cup of feta cheese and set aside. Next, take a lemon and gently grate 1/4 teaspoon of lemon using a zester or a peeler to make lemon zest. Then, wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of mint leaves; in a mortar and pestle add 10 black peppercorns and ground them into a fine powder.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('62a184b67bd3bfc14019196b','62a17b577bd3bfc140191968',3,'M1: Prepare the dressing and assemble the salad','To prepare the dressing for Watermelon Feta Salad, in a mixing bowl add 2 tablespoons of olive oil, add half a tablespoon of lime juice, add 1/4 teaspoon of lemon zest, add 1/4 teaspoon of salt to taste, add 1/8 teaspoon of black pepper powder , add chopped mint leaves and mix well. Then in a mixing bowl add chilled and cubed watermelon, pour the dressing over the watermelon cubes and toss it well. Transfer the salad to a serving plate and then top it with crumbled feta cheese and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('62a1955a4fef9acdfc1637a4','62a18fec4fef9acdfc1637a2',1,'P1: Prepare the Dressing','To prepare the dressing for Strawberry Walnut Salad, wash and hull (remove the green leaves) half a cup of strawberry and roughly chop them, Then, in a blender jar add half a cup of roughly chopped strawberry, add 1 tablespoon of olive oil, add 1 tablespoon of honey, add half a tablespoon of balsamic vinegar, add 1/4 teaspoon of salt, add 1/4 teaspoon of black pepper powder, and blend it into a smooth paste.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('62a195f855140e9b2409a4c9','62a18fec4fef9acdfc1637a2',2,'P2: Toast the Walnuts','To toast the walnuts for Strawberry Walnut Salad, preheat a microwave oven at 180 degrees C for 3 to 5 minutes. Meanwhile, take a baking tray and spread 1/4 cup of walnuts in the tray in a single layer. Then place the baking tray in the oven and bake at 180 degree celsius for 4 minutes until the walnuts become crisp and slightly brown. Then, carefully take out the tray and allow it to cool for 5 minutes. After the walnuts cool, chop them into small pieces and set aside. While the walnuts are baking and cooling, move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":10,"flame":0}'),('62a197e055140e9b2409a4ca','62a18fec4fef9acdfc1637a2',3,'P3: Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Strawberry Walnut Salad, first wash and hull (remove the green leaves) one cup of strawberry and slice them. Next, thoroughly wash half a cup of spinach to get rid of the mud and then pat dry using a kitchen towel. Then, peel and thinly slice 2 tablespoons of onion; crumble 1 tablespoon of feta cheese and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('62a1982b7bd3bfc140191977','62a18fec4fef9acdfc1637a2',4,'M1: Assemble the Salad','To assemble the Strawberry Walnut Salad, take a serving plate and spread a layer of washed spinach leaves, arranger the sliced strawberries on top, then layer it with a handful of sliced onions, and top it with crumbled feta cheese. Garnish the salad with toasted and chopped walnuts, drizzle a tablespoon of the prepared dressing , toss the salad and serve','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('62a1dead55140e9b2409a4cf','62a1de034fef9acdfc1637a5',1,'P1: Chill the Watermelon','To chill the watermelon for Thai Watermelon Salad, first wash a watermelon and cut it into half. Then, cut them into smaller slices and deseed them, now cut 2 cups of watermelon into medium sized cubes. Transfer the deseeded watermelon cubes into a bowl, cover it with a lid and allow to chill in the refrigerator for an hour. While the watermelon is being chilled, move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":60,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":60,"flame":0}'),
('62a1e4f855140e9b2409a4d0','62a1de034fef9acdfc1637a5',2,'P2: Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Thai Watermelon Salad, wash and slice 1/4 cup of cucumber, peel and thinly slice 1/4 cup of onion, peel and grate 1/4 teaspoon of ginger .Then, in a blender jar or mortar and pestle add 1 tablespoon of roasted peanuts and pound them into a coarse powder. Wash and pluck 1 tablespoon of mint leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('62a1e7e055140e9b2409a4d1','62a1de034fef9acdfc1637a5',3,'P3: Prepare the Dressing','To prepare the dressing for Thai Watermelon Salad, in a mixing bowl add half a tablespoon of lime juice, add half a tablespoon of rice vinegar, add 1/4 teaspoon of grated ginger, add 1/2 a teaspoon of brown sugar, add some salt to taste, add 1/8 teaspoon of pepper powder, then mix well.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('62a1e9667bd3bfc14019197e','62a1de034fef9acdfc1637a5',4,'M1: Assemble The Salad','To assemble the salad, in a mixing bowl add 2 cups of cubed watermelon, add 1/4 cup of sliced cucumber, add 1 tablespoon of sliced onion and mix well. Then, add the prepared dressing and toss the salad well. Then, add 1 tablespoon of crushed and roasted peanuts followed by 1 tablespoon of mint leaves, mix well and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('62a247df55140e9b2409a4db','62a1f8ae4fef9acdfc1637a7',1,'AP1: Marinate the Mutton','To marinate the Mutton for Kosha Mangsho, first, wash and clean 200 grams of mutton thoroughly with water. Then, in a mixing bowl add 200 grams of washed mutton, add 1/4 cup of thick yogurt, add add 1/2 a tablespoon of mustard oil, add 1 teaspoon of ginger garlic paste, and mix everything well using your fingers. Ensure that the mutton pieces are evenly coated with the marinade. Next, cover the bowl with a lid and refrigerate for 4 hours. While the mutton is marinating, move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":240,"advanced_prep_time":240,"timer":240,"flame":0}'),('62a24adb55140e9b2409a4dc','62a1f8ae4fef9acdfc1637a7',2,'P1: Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Kosha Mangsho, peel and slice 3/4 cup of onion; wash, peel and chop 1/2 a teaspoon of ginger, peel and chop 1/2 a teaspoon of garlic; wash and chop 1/4 cup of tomato; wash, peel and cut 1 potato into cubes; wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Then, in a mortar and pestle add 1 black cardamom, add 1.5 green cardamom, add 1/2 an inch of cinnamon stick, add 1 clove, and pound it lightly until it breaks into small pieces.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('62a24e2e7bd3bfc140191984','62a1f8ae4fef9acdfc1637a7',3,'M1: Brown the Onions','To prepare the onion base for Kosha Mangsho, heat a heavy bottom pan on medium high flame and add 2 tablespoons of mustard oil and allow it to become hot. Then add the crushed spices and allow  followed by 1.5 dry red chilli ,1 bay leaf, and 1/2 a teaspoon of sugar. Then saute it for a few seconds and allow it to splutter. Then add 3/4 cup of sliced onions, and fry it for 6 minutes until they turn brown. Keep stirring at regular intervals to prevent it from sticking to the bottom.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":5,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":5,"flame":2}'),('62a2525a7bd3bfc140191985','62a1f8ae4fef9acdfc1637a7',4,'M2: Cook the masala','After the onions have browned for Kosha Mangsho, add 1/2 a teaspoon of chopped ginger, add 1/2 a teaspoon of chopped garlic, and saute the onions for another 3-5 minutes until they turn further brown. Then add, 1/4 cup of chopped tomato, add saute it for 2 minutes until they become soft and mushy. Next, add the marinated mutton pieces and mix well. Then add the potato halves and mix with the masala. Stir fry the marinated mutton and potatoes on high flame for 5 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":4}'),('62a253204fef9acdfc1637aa','62a1f8ae4fef9acdfc1637a7',5,'M3: Cook the Mutton','After stir frying the mutton and potatoes for Kosha Mangsho, add 1 teaspoon of coriander powder, add 1/2 a teaspoon of turmeric powder, add 1 teaspoon of kashmiri red chilli powder, add 1/2 a teaspoon of cumin powder, add 1/2 a teaspoon of salt to taste. Mix well and cook for 2 to 3 minutes. Then add half a cup of water and mix well. Then, cover the pan with a lid and cook on low flame for 1.5 hour until the mutton becomes tender. Keep stirring at regular intervals to prevent the mutton from burning. Scrape from the sides and the center of the pan to mix the brown bits with the curry, this will help develop a rich colour and flavour. Add a splash of water when required to prevent the masala from burning. The consistency of the curry is to remain thick.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":90,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":90,"flame":1}'),('62a253c24fef9acdfc1637ab','62a1f8ae4fef9acdfc1637a7',6,'M4: Garnish and Serve','After the mutton and potatoes are cooked in the masala, add 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala, add 1/2 a tablespoon of lime juice and mix well. Allow the curry to simmer on low flame for 3 to 4 minutes until it becomes slightly thick. Garnish it with chopped coriander leaves and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":4,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":4,"flame":1}'),('62a2592955140e9b2409a4e1','62a257e755140e9b2409a4df',1,'P1: Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Laal Maas, peel, wash and slice 1 cup of onions, peel 5 cloves of garlic, wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves; cut a lemon into half and deseed them, then squeeze 1/2  a teaspoon of lemon juice. To crush the spices, in a mortar and pestle add 1 clove, add 3 black peppercorns, add 1 black cardamom, add 1 green cardamom, add half an inch of cinnamon and gently crush them. Next, in a  mixing bowl add 1/4 cup of plain yogurt and whisk it well until it reached a flowy consistency.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('62a259fc4fef9acdfc1637ae','62a257e755140e9b2409a4df',2,'M1: Brown the Onions','To prepare Laal Maas, heat a pressure cooker on medium high flame and add 3 tablespoons of mustard oil and allow it to become hot. Then add the crushed spices along with 1 bay leaf, then saute it for a few seconds until the spices turn aromatic. Then add 1 cup of sliced onions and saute it for 8 minutes until they become brown. Keep stirring it at regular intervals to prevent it from sticking to the bottom.','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('62a25b1b7bd3bfc140191988','62a257e755140e9b2409a4df',3,'M2: Cook the Mutton','After the onions have browned for Laal Maas, add 5 peeled garlic cloves, add 2 teaspoons of ginger garlic paste, and fry on medium flame for another 6 minutes until the raw smell of the paste goes. Then add 200 grams of mutton and saute it on high flame for 4-5 minutes. Next, add 1/4 cup of whisked curd, mix and allow to cook for 3 mins. Then add 2 teaspoons of kashmiri red chilli powder, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, add 1 teaspoon of coriander powder, add 1/4 teaspoon of cumin powder, add 1/4 teaspoon of salt and mix it well and cook for 2 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":3,"flame":3}'),('62a25bc755140e9b2409a4e2','62a257e755140e9b2409a4df',4,'M3: Pressure cook the mutton, garnish and serve','After the Masala is cooked for Laal Maas, add 3/4 cup of water, then cover the pressure cooker with a lid and pressure cook the mutton on high flame for one whistle, then reduce the flame to low and allow it to summer for another 20 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. After the pressure cooker has released air, gently take off the lid, check for salt and spice and adjust accordingly. Garnish it with chopped coriander leaves and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":25,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":25,"flame":2}'),('62ae0c503713337949bd7446','6128b0c244613cc23f0a740f',6,'M4: Garnish and Serve','After cooking the Methi Pulao, take off the lid and gently mix the pulao with light hands. Take it out into a serving bowl. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":1,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63ae7814f3ff15e9647a80d5','63ae76f14aa654d9b6ff050f',1,'P1 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Basil Ground Chicken, first wash and pat dry 250 gms of skinless and boneless chicken using a kitchen towel, and cut them into bite sized chunks. Next, wash and cut 1/4 cup of spring onion greens, peel and finely chop 2 garlic cloves, deseed and finely chop 1 Thai birds eye chilli and wash and pluck 1 cup of Thai basil leaves and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('63ae7913fd297ac6481f1f9a','63ae76f14aa654d9b6ff050f',2,'P2 Prepare the Sauce','To prepare the sauce for Basil Ground Chicken, in a mixing bowl add 2 teaspoons of oyster sauce, 1 teaspoon of light soy sauce, 1 teaspoon of dark soy sauce, 1 teaspoon of sugar and 2 tablespoons of water and mix it well using a whisk until the sugar has dissolved and is well combined.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63ae7ac2f3ff15e9647a80d7','63ae76f14aa654d9b6ff050f',3,'M1 Stir Fry the chicken','To prepare Basil Ground Chicken, first heat a wok on high flame, then add 1.5 tablespoons of peanut oil and allow it to become hot. Then reduce the flame to medium low and 2 chopped garlic cloves followed by 1 chopped thai birds eye chilli and saute it until the garlic becomes slightly brown. Next, add 250 gms of chicken chunks and half of 1/4 cup of cut spring onion and stir fry it for 2 to 3 minutes until the chicken is cooked.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":1,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":4}'),('63ae7b7cfd297ac6481f1f9b','63ae76f14aa654d9b6ff050f',4,'M2  Cook the chicken with Sauce','After the chicken is cooked for Basil Ground Chicken, pour in the prepared sauce and saute the chicken for 2 minutes on medium flame. Next, add the remaining cut green onions and mix again. Then add 1 cup of washed thai basil leaves and mix with the chicken until the green wilt. Then turn off the flame, and serve hot on top of steamed jasmine rice.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('63ae8451f3ff15e9647a80db','63ae81694aa654d9b6ff0518',1,'P1 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Kadai Paneer, wash, deseed and cut 1/2 a cup of green bell peppers into cubes; peel and cut 1/2 a cup of onions into cubes and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions. Next, wash and slit a green chilli into half, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes. Then, cut 200 gms of paneer into medium sized cubes, wash and cut a lemon into half, remove the seeds and squeeze 1/2 a tablespoon of lemon juice and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63ae861ffd297ac6481f1f9f','63ae81694aa654d9b6ff0518',2,'P2 Roast the spices and prepare the masala','To prepare the masala for Kadai Paneer, heat a pan and allow it to become hot on medium flame, then add 1 tablespoon of coriander seeds, add 2 kashmiri red chillies, add 1/2 a teaspoon of fennel seeds, add 4 black pepper cons, add 1 black cardamom, add 1 clove and 1/2 an inch of cinnamon and roast the spices on medium flame for 3-4 minutes until they turn slightly brown and fragrant. Then turn off the flame, allow the spices to slightly cool. Next, transfer them in a blender jar and grind it into a fine powder.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('63ae87064aa654d9b6ff051e','63ae81694aa654d9b6ff0518',3,'M1 Saute the Vegetables','To saute the vegetables for Kadai Paneer, heat a pan and add 1/2 a tablespoon of cooking oil and allow it to become hot over high flame, then add half a cup of cubed green bell peppers followed by 1/2 a cup of cubed onions and saute it on high flame for three to four minutes until the onions are slightly charred. Then turn off the flame, transfer the charred vegetables in a bowl and set aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63ae87aaf3ff15e9647a80dc','63ae81694aa654d9b6ff0518',4,'M2 Prepare the Gravy','To prepare the gravy for Kadai Paneer, heat a pan and add 1.5 tablespoons of oil and allow it to become hot on medium flame, then add 1/4 cup of finely chopped onion and saute it for 2-3 minutes until then become golden brown. Then, add 1 teaspoon of ginger garlic paste followed by 1 slit green chilli and saute it along with the onion for another 3 minutes until the raw smell of the ginger garlic paste goes.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63ae8965fd297ac6481f1fa0','63ae81694aa654d9b6ff0518',5,'M3 Simmer the tomato puree','After the ginger garlic paste is cooked for Kadai Paneer, next add 1/4 cup of finely chopped tomato followed by 1/4 cup of tomato puree and mix well and allow it to cook on low flame for 3 minutes. Ensure to stir fry occasionally to prevent it from sticking to the bottom and burning.','cook_method','{"active_time":1,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('63ae8a15f3ff15e9647a80dd','63ae81694aa654d9b6ff0518',6,'M4 Cook the gravy with masalas','After the tomato puree has cooked, add the prepared kadai masala, followed by 1/2 a teaspoon of salt, 1/4 teaspoon of kashmiri red chilli powder, 1/2 a teaspoon of garam masala and mix it well. Then add 1/4 cup of water and mix again, allow the gravy to cook on low flame for 2-3 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":1,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('63ae8b4ffd297ac6481f1fa1','63ae81694aa654d9b6ff0518',7,'M5 Toss the vegetables and cook the curry','After the gravy has cooked for Kadai Paneer, add the sauted green bell peppers and onions followed by 200 gms of cubed paneer and toss it well in the gravy such that the vegetables are evenly coated . If required, add 1/4 cup of water at this point to adjust the consistency, then allow the curry to cook on medium low flame for 2 minutes until the oil starts to seprate. Then add 1/2 a tablespoon of ghee followed by 1/2 a tablespoon of lemon juice and mix well. Then turn off the flame and serve hot with tandoori roti or paratha.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":2,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('63b1c979fd297ac6481f1faf','63b1c8c9f3ff15e9647a80f4',1,'P1 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Coconut Chutney, grate 1/2 a cup of coconut; wash and peel 1/2 an inch of ginger; wash and pluck 3 curry leaves; wash 1 green chilli and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63b1ca7df3ff15e9647a80f6','63b1c8c9f3ff15e9647a80f4',2,'M1 Prepare the chutney','To prepare the coconut chutney, in a blender jar add 1/2 a cup of grated coconut, add 2 tablespoons of chana dal, add 1 green chilli, add a pinch of tamarind, add 1/2 an inch of ginger followed by 1/4 teaspoon of salt and 2 tablespoons of water. Then close the lid and blend it into a fine chutney. Transfer it into a serving bowl and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63b1cb25fd297ac6481f1fb0','63b1c8c9f3ff15e9647a80f4',3,'M2 Prepare the tempering','To prepare the tempering for Coconut chutney, heat a tadka pan and add 2 teaspoons of oil and allow it to become hot on medium flame. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of mustard seeds, add 1/4 teaspoon of urad dal, add half dry red chilli followed by 3 curry leaves and saute it on low flame until the spices splutter. Then turn off the flame and pour the tempering over the prepared chutney, mix well and it is ready to be served.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63b1cf67fd297ac6481f1fb5','63b1cde3f3ff15e9647a80f8',1,'P1 Prep The Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Chicken Stew, wash and pat dry 400gms of chicken pieces; wash, peel and dice 1/2 a cup of potatoes; wash, peel and dice 1/2 a cup of carrot; wash, peel and slice 1/2 a tablespoon of ginger; peel and slice 1/2 a tablespoon of garlic; wash and slit two green chillies; peel and slice 1 cup of onion; wash and pluck 7 curry leaves and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":18,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63b1d04f82e228f7a7a57e58','63b1cde3f3ff15e9647a80f8',2,'M1 Roast the Spices','To prepare the base for Chicken Stew, heat a deep bottom pan and add 2 tablespoons of coconut oil and allow it to become hot on high flame. Then add 1.5 inch of Cinnamon, followed by 3 cardamoms and 3 Cloves and stir fry it for a few seconds until the spices splutter and become fragrant. Then lower the flame to medium low and add 1/2 a tablespoon of sliced ginger and saute it for a few seconds until it changes color. Next, add sliced 1/2 a tablespoon of sliced garlic followed by 2 slit green chilli and saute it for a minute until the garlic turns golden brown.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('63b1d0fcf3ff15e9647a80fc','63b1cde3f3ff15e9647a80f8',3,'M2 Prepare the base','After the garlic has turned golden brown, add 1 cup of sliced onions and saute it on medium flame for two to three minutes until they become translucent. Then, add 1/2 a teaspoon of salt and saute it for another minute. Next, add a bay leaf and mix again, then add 1/4 teaspoon of pepper powder, followed by 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala and mix until well combined.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63b1d1e282e228f7a7a57e59','63b1cde3f3ff15e9647a80f8',4,'M3 Cook the meat and vegetables','After cooking the masalas, add 400 gms of chicken and stir fry with the tempering on low flame for 3 to 4 minutes until the chicken is cooked and turns white. Next, add 1/2 a cup of diced potatoes followed by 1/2 a cup of carrots and mix it well. Allow the vegetables to cook for two minutes until they become slightly soft. While the vegetables cook, move onto the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":2,"flame":1}'),('63b1d357fd297ac6481f1fb6','63b1cde3f3ff15e9647a80f8',5,'M4 Simmer the stew','After the vegetables have cooked for the Chicken Stew, add 7 curry leaves and give it a good mix, then add salt as per taste and mix again. Then lower the flame and add half a cup of coconut milk along with half a cup of water and allow it to come to boil on low flame. Once the coconut milk starts boiling, close the lid and allow the stew to cook for 6 minutes on low flame. Keep stirring it occasionally to prevent it from sticking to the bottom and burning. While the stew is simmering, move onto the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":8,"flame":1}'),('63b1d42582e228f7a7a57e5a','63b1cde3f3ff15e9647a80f8',6,'M5 Season the stew','After simmering the stew, open the lid and give it a mix. Close the lid again and allow it to cook on medium low flame for another 10 minutes. Then open the lid, and add 1/4 teaspoon of pepper powder along with 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala and mix again. Then lower the flame and add half a cup of coconut milk and mix until well combined. Then turn off the flame, and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":10,"flame":1}'),('63b1e14afd297ac6481f1fbb','63b1e07cfd297ac6481f1fb8',1,'P1 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Palak Paneer, wash and clean 100 gms of spinach and ensure the greens are free from mud. Then cut 100 gms of paneer into medium sized cubes, peel and finely chop 1/2 a cup of onion, wash and finely chop 1/2 a cup of tomato, peel and crush 3 cloves of garlic; wash 1 green chilli and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":14,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('63b1e1a0f3ff15e9647a80ff','63b1e07cfd297ac6481f1fb8',2,'P2 Blanch the Spinach','To blanch the spinach for Palak Paneer, heat a deep bottom pan, add 2 cups of water and bring to boil on high flame. Then add 100 gms of spinach leaves along with 1/2 a teaspoon of salt and allow it to boil on medium flame for 2 to 3 minutes. Then, turn off the flame, drain the excess water and wash the spinach leaves under running water to prevent it from cooking further. While the spinach leaves are boiling, move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":4,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":4,"flame":3}'),('63b1e202fd297ac6481f1fbc','63b1e07cfd297ac6481f1fb8',3,'P3 Blend into a puree','To prepare the spinach puree for Palak Paneer, in a mixy jar add the blanched palak leaves along with one green chilli. Then close the lid and blend it into a smooth puree and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63b1e2f9f3ff15e9647a8100','63b1e07cfd297ac6481f1fb8',4,'M1 Prepare The Tempering','To prepare palak Paneer, heat a deep bottom pan and add 2 tablespoons of oil and allow it to become hot on high flame. Then add half a teaspoon of cumin seeds, add 2 dried red chillies and saute them for a few seconds until they splutter. Next, add half a cup of chopped onion followed by 3 crushed cloves, and saute them on medium flame for 2 minutes until the onions become translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63b1e3e3f3ff15e9647a8101','63b1e07cfd297ac6481f1fb8',5,'M2 Cook the Spinach Puree','After the onions have become translucent for Palak Paneer, add half a cup of chopped tomato, saute and allow it to cook for three minutes until they become mushy.  Next, add 1 teaspoon of coriander powder, 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala powder and saute it for another minute until well combined. Then add the prepared spinach puree and saute it on high flame for a minute.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":3,"flame":0}'),('63b1e451fd297ac6481f1fbd','63b1e07cfd297ac6481f1fb8',6,'M3 Add the paneer and simmer the curry','After cooking the spinach puree, add 100 gms of cubed paneer, add one teaspoon of salt along with 1/4 cup of water and bring the curry to boil on low flame. When the curry starts to boil, add 1 teaspoon of lemon juice followed by 1 tablespoon of fresh cream and mix well. Then turn off the flame and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":1,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":2,"flame":1}'),
('63b245dc82e228f7a7a57e64','63b1e70e82e228f7a7a57e5e',1,'P1 Soak and squeeze Boondi','To soak the boondi for Boondi Raita, heat 1/4 cup of water until luke warm and then turn off the flame. In a mixing bowl, add 1/2 a cup of boondi along with 1/4 cup of warm water and allow it to soak for 30 seconds. Then squeeze the soaked boondi to get rid of excess water and keep the squeezed boondi aside.Then, wash and finely chop 1/2 a teaspoon of green chillies.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":1,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":1,"flame":0}'),('63b24721fd297ac6481f1fc4','63b1e70e82e228f7a7a57e5e',2,'M1 Prepare the Raita','To prepare the Boondi Raita, in a mixing bowl add 1/2 a cup of yogurt, and whisk it well until it becomes smooth and creamy.  Then add 1/4 cup of cold milk followed by the squeezed boondi and 1/2 a teaspoon of salt. Next add half a teaspoon of chopped green chillies, add 1/4 teaspoon of roasted cumin powder, add 1/4 teaspoon of mint powder, add 1/4 teaspoon of fennel powder, add 1/4 teaspoon of red chilli powder and whisk it well until well combined. Refrigerate the boondi raita for 30mins and serve chilled.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":30,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":30,"flame":0}'),('63b2513afd297ac6481f1fc9','63b2504b82e228f7a7a57e65',1,'P1 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Baked Ghiya Kofta, wash, peel and cut a bottle gourd into half, scoop out the seeds and grate 100gms of bottle gourd; wash, peel and grate 1 teaspoon of ginger; wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves; peel and finely chop 1 teaspoon of garlic; wash and roughly chop two tomatoes and blend it into a fine puree, remove in a bowl and set aside. Next, peel and roughly chop one onion and blend it into a smooth puree and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":14,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63b251da82e228f7a7a57e67','63b2504b82e228f7a7a57e65',2,'M1 Prepare the Kofta Dough','To prepare the kofta dough for Baked Ghiya Kofta, in a mixing bowl add 100 gms of bottle gourd and hand squeeze the grated gourd and drain the excess water, add 2 tablespoons of chickpea flour, add 1 teaspoon of red chilli powder followed by 1/2 a teaspoon of turmeric powder and 1/2 a teaspoon of salt. Then mix well using your hands until the ingredients are well combined and form into a dough. Then, gently pinch and roll them into equal lemon sized balls and set aside. You can grease your palms with oil to prevent the dough from sticking to your palms.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63b2525382e228f7a7a57e68','63b2504b82e228f7a7a57e65',3,'M2 Bake the Kofta','To bake the kofta for Baked Ghiya Kofta, take a microwave safe bowl and grease it with half a teaspoon of oil and place the rolled kofta balls and brush them with a teaspoon of oil. Then microwave the kofta balls for five to eight minutes. While the kofta balls are getting baked, move onto the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":7,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":7,"flame":0}'),
('63b2537cfd297ac6481f1fca','63b2504b82e228f7a7a57e65',4,'M3 Prepare the gravy','To prepare the masala for Baked Ghiya Kofta, in another microwave safe bowl, add a teaspoon of oil followed by 1/2 a teaspoon of cumin seeds, the prepared onion puree, 1 teaspoon of chopped garlic, one teaspoon of grated ginger and mix it well. Next, microwave it for 5 minutes. While the masala is getting cooked, move onto the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":5,"flame":0}'),('63b256c282e228f7a7a57e69','63b2504b82e228f7a7a57e65',5,'M4 Cook the gravy','After the onion paste is cooked for Baked Ghiya Kofta, in the same bowl add the prepared tomato puree to the cooked onion mix, followed by 1 teaspoon of coriander powder, 1 teaspoon of red chilli powder, 1/2 teaspoon of garam masala and salt and mix it well until well combined, then microwave it for another 10 minutes until the puree is cooked. While the tomato puree is cooking move onto the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":10,"flame":0}'),('63b2574ff3ff15e9647a810a','63b2504b82e228f7a7a57e65',6,'M5 Cook the kofta with the gravy','After the tomato puree is cooked for Baked Ghiya Kofta, add half a cup of water and mix it well with the masala and puree, then place the baked ghiya kofta on top and microwave it for another 15minutes until it reaches a gravy consistency. Then garnish the baked kofta curry with 1 tablespoon of fresh cream and 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and serve hot. While the kofta curry is cooking, move onto the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":15,"flame":0}'),('63b282bcf3ff15e9647a8114','63b281b4f3ff15e9647a8112',1,'AP1 Soak the Chickpeas','To soak the chickpeas for Chana Masala, rinse 1/2 a cup of chickpeas well and in a mixing bowl add add the washed chickpeas along with 1.5 cups of water, cover it with a lid and allow it to soak overnight. While the chickpeas are soaking, move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":480,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63b2839ffd297ac6481f1fd3','63b281b4f3ff15e9647a8112',2,'P1 Pressure Cook the Chickpeas','To pressure cook the chickpeas for Chana Masala, in a pressure cooker add half a cup of soaked chickpeas, add the tea bag, add 2 cups of water along with half a teaspoon of salt followed by half an inch of cinnamon, 1 clove, 1 black cardamom, and 1/8 teaspoon of baking soda. Next, close the lid and allow the chickpeas to pressure cook on high flame for 5 whistles and then lower the flame and continue to cook on low flame for another 10 minutes. Then turn off the flame, take off the pressure cooker and allow it to naturally cool. While the chickpeas are cooking, move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":20,"flame":3}'),
('63b28429f3ff15e9647a8116','63b281b4f3ff15e9647a8112',3,'P2 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Chana Masala, peel and finely chop 1 cup of onions; wash and slit 2 green chillies, wash, peel and julienne 1 tablespoon of ginger and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63b284ab82e228f7a7a57e82','63b281b4f3ff15e9647a8112',4,'M1 Fry the onions','To prepare the gravy for Chana Masala, heat a pan and add 1.5 tablespoons of ghee followed by 1 tablespoon of oil and 1/4 teaspoon of hingh and allow it to become hot on high flame. Then, add 1 cup of finely chopped onion and saute it on medium low flame for three minutes until they become slightly brown. Then, add two teaspoons of ginger and garlic paste and stir fry for another minute until it is cooked and the raw smell goes.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('63b2856ffd297ac6481f1fd4','63b281b4f3ff15e9647a8112',5,'M2 Add the masalas and cook until oil seperates','After the ginger garlic paste has cooked for Chana Masala, add one tablespoon of coriander powder, add 2 teaspoons of Kashmiri red chilli powder, add 1/2 a teaspoon of turmeric powder, add half a teaspoon of roasted cumin powder, add half a teaspoon of ginger powder followed by half a teaspoon of garam masala, and one tablespoon of dried pomegranate seeds powder and mix it well on medium low flame until the masalas cook and the oil separates from the sides. Add 1/4 cup of water if the masala becomes too dry.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63b285f482e228f7a7a57e83','63b281b4f3ff15e9647a8112',6,'M3 Cook the gravy and chickpeas','After the masala is cooked for Chana Masala, add 1/4 cup of curd, add 1/4 cup of tomato puree and mix and cook on low flame for two to three minutes until well combined and slightly creamy. When the gravy starts to simmer, transfer the boiled chickpeas and mix it well along with the gravy, and slightly mash a few chickpeas using the back of the ladle. Add some water at this point if the chole are too dry.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":2,"flame":2}'),('63b2866dfd297ac6481f1fd6','63b281b4f3ff15e9647a8112',7,'M4 Simmer the curry and garnish','After adding some water for Chana Masala,  allow it to simmer on low flame for two to three minutes and then add one tablespoon of kasuri methi, add 2 slit green chillies, add one tablespoon of julienned ginger and mix well. Then allow it to simmer for another minute, turn off the flame and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":1,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":4,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":4,"flame":1}'),
('63b28aec82e228f7a7a57e86','63b28a2ef3ff15e9647a811b',1,'P1 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredIents for Aloo Methi, wash and peel 400 gms of baby potatoes, wash and thoroughly clean 200 gms of methi leaves to ensure it it free from dirt and mud. Next, finely chop 200 gms of methi leaves, peel and finely chop 1 teaspoon of garlic, wash and slit 1.5 numbers of green chillies and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":18,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63b28b94fd297ac6481f1fe0','63b28a2ef3ff15e9647a811b',2,'M1 Prepare the Tempering','To saute the spices for Aloo Methi, heat a deep bottom pan add one tablespoon of mustard oil, add 1/4 teaspoon of cumin seeds, add 1/8 teaspoon of asefoetida followed by 1 teaspoon of chopped garlic, 1.5 numbers of slit green chillies and 1 dried red chilli and saute it on medium low flame for 30 seconds until the spices splutter and become fragrant.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63b28ca482e228f7a7a57e89','63b28a2ef3ff15e9647a811b',3,'M2 Cook the potatoes','After the spices have spluttered for Aloo Methi, add 1 teaspoon of coriander powder, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, add 1/2  a teaspoon of kashmiri red chilli powder, and some salt to taste. Then saute the masalas well for a few seconds on low flame until they are well combined. Next, add 400 gms of peeled potatoes and mix it well such that it is evenly coated i the masalas and tempering. Then, allow the potatoes to cook on medium low flame for 5 minutes. Keep stirring it occasionally to prevent it from burning. While the potatoes cook, move onto the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":5,"flame":2}'),('63b28d17f3ff15e9647a811d','63b28a2ef3ff15e9647a811b',4,'M3 Continue to cook the potatoes','After the potatoes are half cooked for Aloo Methi, give it a mix again and add three tablespoons of water and give it a mix. Then, cover the lid with a pan and allow the potatoes to cook on low flame for 18 minutes until they are cooked and become tender. Keep stirring them occasionally to prevent it from burning. While the potatoes cook, move onto the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":1,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":18,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":18,"flame":1}'),('63b28dd0fd297ac6481f1fe1','63b28a2ef3ff15e9647a811b',5,'M4 Cook the Methi Leaves','After the potatoes have cooked for Aloo Methi, open the lid and add 200 gms of chopped methi leaves and mix it well along with the potatoes and tempering. Then, cover the pan with a lid and allow the methi leaves to cook on medium low flame for two to three minutes until they are cooked and start to wilt. While the methi leaves are cooking, move onto the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":1,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":3,"flame":1}'),
('63b28e3ef3ff15e9647a811e','63b28a2ef3ff15e9647a811b',6,'M5 Season the curry and serve','After the methi leaves have cooked for Aloo Methi, add 1/4 teaspoon of dry mango powder, add 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala powder and mix well. Then turn off the flame, adjust the seasoning and serve hot with roti or parathas.','cook_method','{"active_time":1,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('63b2a408fd297ac6481f1fe6','63b29080fd297ac6481f1fe3',1,'P1 Prep the ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Bhindi Pyaz Fry, wash and pat dry the ladies finger using a kitchen towel and get rid of the stickiness. Next, cut 1.5 cups of the ladies finger into roundels, peel and slice 0.5 cups of onion; wash and slit one green chilli, wash and finely chop 1 cup of tomatoes and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63b2a532f3ff15e9647a8120','63b29080fd297ac6481f1fe3',2,'M1 Fry the Ladies Finger','To prepare Bhindi Pyaz Fry, heat a pan and add 1 tablespoon of cooking oil and allow it to become hot on medium flame, then add 1.5 cups of ladies finger roundels and saute it until it is evenly coated in oil. Spread the cut ladies finger over the pan to ensure even heat and allow it to become slightly crisp. Occasionally stir the ladies finger to prevent it from sticking to the bottom and burning. Spread the ladies finger again and allow it to cook on medium low flame for another two minutes until it becomes golden brown. While the ladies finger is cooking move onto the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":3,"flame":2}'),('63b2a5f7f3ff15e9647a8121','63b29080fd297ac6481f1fe3',3,'M2 Cook the masalas','After the ladies finger have become golden brown for Bhindi Pyaz Fry, remove the fried ladies finger and set them aside. Then, in the same pan add 1 teaspoon of oil and allow it to become hot. Then, add 1/2 a teaspoon of cumin seeds, and 1/8 teaspoon of asafoeitida and stir fry it on medium low flame until the spices splutter. Then, add 0.5 cups of sliced onion and saute it on medium flame for a minute until it becomes translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63b2a6f9f3ff15e9647a8122','63b29080fd297ac6481f1fe3',4,'M3 Cook the tomatoes','After the onions become translucent for Bhindi Pyaz Fry, add 3/4 teaspoon of ginger garlic paste followed by 1 slit green chilli and give it a good mix. Next, add 1 cup of chopped tomatoes, and saute it on medium flame for two to three minutes until it becomes soft and mushy. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, add 1/4 teaspoon of kashmiri red chilli powder, add 1/2 a teaspoon of coriander powder, add 1/2 a teaspoon of dried mango powder followed by 1/4 teaspoon of roasted cumin powder and salt to taste and saute it on low flame until the masalas are well combined','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),
('63b2a8dcf3ff15e9647a8129','63b29080fd297ac6481f1fe3',5,'M4 Simmer the curry and serve','Next, for Bhindi Pyaz Fry, after the masalas are mixed add the fried ladies finger and gently combine with the masala and tempering. Then cover the pan with a lid and allow it to simmer for three minutes on low flame. After simmering the ladies finger, add 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala, add 3/4 teaspoon of kasuri methi and mix again. Then turn off the flame, remove in a serving bowl and serve hot with roti.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":3,"flame":2}'),('63b2b25ef3ff15e9647a812c','63b2af01f3ff15e9647a812b',1,'P1 Soak the Tamarind','To soak the tamarind for Tomato Onion Chutney, in a mixing bowl add a lemon sized ball of tamarind along with 1/4 cup of water and allow it to soak for 15minutes. While the tamarind is soaking, move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":1,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":15,"flame":0}'),('63b2b4cdfd297ac6481f1ffc','63b2af01f3ff15e9647a812b',2,'P2 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Tomato Onion Chutney, wash and roughly chop 1 cup of tomatoes, peel and roughly chop 1/2 a cup of onion; wash and peel half an inch of ginger, peel 1.5 cloves of garlic, wash and pluck 5 curry leaves; wash and green chilli and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63b2b6e9fd297ac6481f1ffd','63b2af01f3ff15e9647a812b',3,'M1 Roast the spices','To prepare Tomato Onion chutney, heat a pan and add 1 teaspoon of cooking oil and allow it to become hot, then add 1/8 teaspoon of asafoetida and saute it on low flame for a few seconds. Next add half a tablespoon of split black gram dal and saute it for two minutes on medium low flame until it becomes golden brown. Then, add half a teaspoon of mustard seeds, add half a teaspoon of cumin seeds, and saute it for a minute on medium low flame until the spices become golden brown.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63b2b7befd297ac6481f1ffe','63b2af01f3ff15e9647a812b',4,'M2 Roast the Onions','After the spices have become golden brown for Tomato Onion Chutney, add 1 dried red chilli followed by 5 curry leaves, 1.5 cloves of garlic and 1/2 an inch of ginger, and saute it for a minute on medium low flame. Next, add half a cup of chopped onion, add half green chilli and saute it for two to three minutes until the onions become translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('63b2b81082e228f7a7a57e8f','63b2af01f3ff15e9647a812b',5,'M3 Cook the Tomatoes','After the onions have become translucent for Tomato Onion Chutney, add one cup of roughly chopped tomatoes and saute it three minutes until the tomatoes become soft, then cover the pan with a lid cook the tomatoes on medium low flame until they become mushy.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":2,"flame":2}'),('63b2b887fd297ac6481f1fff','63b2af01f3ff15e9647a812b',6,'M4 Blend the chutney and serve','After the tomatoes have become mushy, open the lid and squeeze half a tablespoon of soaked tamarind using your fingers, ensure to filter the fibres and seeds if any. Mix well and add half a teaspoon of salt and mix again. Then turn off the flame and allow the mixture to cool. Next, transfer the mixture in a mixer jar and blend it into a smooth paste.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":3,"flame":0}'),('63b2be77fd297ac6481f2002','63b2bd5482e228f7a7a57e90',1,'P1 Prep the ingredients and marinate the chicken','To prep the ingredients for Chicken Chettinad, peel and finely chop 1/2 a cup of onion and grate 1/4 cup of coconut. Next, To marinate the chicken , wash and pat dry 300 gms of chicken thighs and place them on a chopping board and score them using a sharp knife, flip the thigh on the other side and score them on the other side as well. Repeat the same for the remaining chicken thighs. Next, to marinate the chicken, in a mixing bowl place the scored chicken thighs, add half a tablespoon of lemon juice along with half a teaspoon of turmeric powder, 1/4 teaspoon of salt and mix it well using your hands and ensure that the chicken thighs are evenly marinated.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63b2bf3082e228f7a7a57e92','63b2bd5482e228f7a7a57e90',2,'P2 Prepare the masala','To roast the spices for Chettinad Chicken, heat a pan and add 3 kashmiri red chillies, add 1/4 tablespoon of cumin seeds, add 1/4 tablespoon of coriander seeds, add 1/2 a tablespoon of black peppercons, followed by 1/4 tablespoon of fennel seeds, 1 inch of cinnamon sticks, and half a star anise. Dry roast it on medium flame for two minutes until the spices become fragrant and slightly golden brown. Then allow the dry roasted spices to slightly cool, transfer it in a blender jar and pulse grind it into a coarse powder.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('63b2bfbdfd297ac6481f2003','63b2bd5482e228f7a7a57e90',3,'P3 Continue preparing the masala','After pulse grinding the masala  for Chettinad Chicken, add 1/4 cup of grated coconut along with two tablespoons of water and blend it into a coarse paste. Then open the lid and add another tablespoon of water and blend it into a smooth puree. Continue to add water and blend until it reaches a wet paste consistency.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('63b2c0bafd297ac6481f2004','63b2bd5482e228f7a7a57e90',4,'M1 Prepare the tempering','After preparing the masala for Chettinad Chicken, heat a pan and add one tablespoon of coconut oil and allow it to become hot and melt. Then add half a cup of chopped onion and saute it for a minute on medium low flame until it becomes translucent. Next, add 1/2 a teaspoon of mustard seeds followed by 1/4 cup of curry leaves and saute it for a minute along with the tempering.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63b2c17f82e228f7a7a57e93','63b2bd5482e228f7a7a57e90',5,'M2  Cook the Chicken','Next, for Chettinad Chicken add 1 tablespoon of ginger garlic paste and saute for a minute on medium low flame until it is cooked and the raw smell goes. Then add the prepared masala and saute it on medium low flame until it is cooked. Then, add the marinated chicken pieces, half a teaspoon of salt and 1/4 cup of water and give it a good mix. Then, cover the pan with a lid and allow the chicken to cook on low flame for 15 minutes. Keep stirring the chicken occasionally to prevent it from sticking to the pan and burning. While the chicken is cooking, move onto the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":15,"flame":2}'),('63b2c1fc82e228f7a7a57e94','63b2bd5482e228f7a7a57e90',6,'M3 Simmer the curry','After the chicken is cooked for Chicken Chettinad, open the lid and allow the gravy to simmer on low flame for two minutes until it becomes slightly thick. Next, add one tablespoon of tomato paste and mix it well. Turn off the flame, and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":2,"flame":1}'),('63b2cf1afd297ac6481f2008','63b2cddcfd297ac6481f2006',1,'P1 Prep the Ingreidients','To prep the ingredients for Paneer Bhurji, crumble 3/4 cup of paneer, wash, peel and finely chop 1/2 a teaspoon of ginger, peel and finely chop 1/2 a teaspoon of garlic, wash and finely chop 1/2 a cup of tomatoes, peel and finely chop 1/2 a cup of onions, wash and cut a green bell pepper into half, remove the seeds and finely chop 1/4 cup of green bell peppers, wash and finely chop 1 teaspoon of green chillies, wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":18,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63b2d05ef3ff15e9647a8131','63b2cddcfd297ac6481f2006',2,'M1 Prepare the Tempering','To prepare the tempering for Paneer Bhurji, heat a pan and add 1 tablespoon of ghee and allow it to become hot and melt on medium low flame. Next, add 1/2 a teaspoon of cumin seeds followed by 1/8 teaspoon of asafoeitida and saute them for a few seconds until the spices splutter. Then, add 1/2 a cup of chopped onion followed by 1/2 a teaspoon of chopped ginger and half a teaspoon of chopped garlic and saute the onion on medium low flame for 8 minutes until they becomes slightly brown.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":6,"flame":2}'),
('63b2d10ffd297ac6481f2009','63b2cddcfd297ac6481f2006',3,'M2 Cook the masalas','After the onions have been browned for Paneer Bhurji, next add 1/2 a cup of chopped tomatoes along with 1 teaspoon of chopped green chillies, add 1/4 cup of chopped green bell peppers, and saute it on medium low flame for one minute until the vegetables are cooked. Next, add 1/2 a teaspoon of coriander powder, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, add 1 teaspoon of pav bhaji masala, followed by 1/2 a teaspoon of red chilli powder and then mix the masalas until well combined and allow it to cook for one to two minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63b2d21182e228f7a7a57e98','63b2cddcfd297ac6481f2006',4,'M3 Add the paneer and cook the bhurji','After the masalas are cooked for Paneer Bhurji, add 3/4 cup of crumbled paneer followed by some salt to taste, 1/4 teaspoon of cumin powder, add 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala, add 1 tablespoon of lime juice, and then mix everything well, and allow it to cook for two to three minutes. Then top it with 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves, turn off the flame and serve hot with paratha.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":3,"flame":2}'),('63b3fb982783738d69824784','63b3fad3fd297ac6481f2027',1,'P1 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Methi Paratha, thoroughly wash and clean the methi leaves and get rid of the mud from the roots. Next, finely chop 3/4 cup of methi leaves. Wash, peel and grate 1/2 a teaspoon of ginger; peel and finely chop 1/2 a teaspoon of garlic.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63b3ff9a27eb4d18be5b0107','63b3fad3fd297ac6481f2027',2,'P2 Prepare the Dough','To prepare the dough for Methi Paratha, in a mixing bowl add 3/4 cup of whole wheat flour, add 3/4 cup of chopped methi leaves, add 1/2 a teaspoon of salt, add 1/4 teaspoon of carom seeds, add 1/2 a teaspoon of cumin seeds, add 1/2 a teaspoon of red chilli powder followed by 1/2 a teaspoon of grated ginger, 1/2 a teaspoon of finely chopped garlic, and 1 tablespoon of cooking oil and mix it well using your hands such that the ingredients are well combined. Then allow the mixture to rest for 10 minutes allowing the methi leaves to leave out water. While the mixture is set aside, move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":10,"flame":0}'),('63b3fffd27eb4d18be5b0108','63b3fad3fd297ac6481f2027',3,'P3 Knead and Rest the Dough','After the methi leaves has left out water for Methi Paratha, add required amount of water and mix well. Do not add water more than required as it will result in a sticky dough. Knead a soft dough using your hands, and then cover the bowl with a cloth and allow it to rest for another 10 minutes. While the dough rests, move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":10,"flame":0}'),
('63b401192783738d69824785','63b3fad3fd297ac6481f2027',4,'M1 Roll the parathas','After the dough has rested for Methi Paratha, slightly knead the dough again and divide the dough into 6 equal lemon sized balls. Then dust the dough ball with some wheat flour and place it on the rolling board, now slightly flatten the dough ball and evenly roll it out into a 4 inch disc using a rolling pin. Then grease it with some oil on top and gather the rolled dough into a circle as shown, and roll it into a ball again, then dust the ball with wheat flour and flatten it a bit. Roll it into a five inch paratha using a rolling pin. Continue the same for the remaining dough balls and set aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":18,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63b401af2783738d69824786','63b3fad3fd297ac6481f2027',5,'M2 Roast the Parathas','Next, to roast the Methi Paratha, heat a griddle and transfer the rolled paratha onto the hot griddle and allow it to cook on medium low flame until the brown spots and bubbles appear on the lower side. Then, flip the rolled paratha apply some oil on both the sides and cook until the brown spots appear on the other side and the paratha is crispy. Repeat the same for the remaining parathas and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63b406a3fd297ac6481f202b','63b4052c2783738d69824788',1,'P1 Cook the Rice','To cook rice for Basil Fried Rice, wash 1.5 cups of rice well with water. Next, add the washed rice to a pressure cooker with 3 cups of water. Cover it with a lid and pressure cook it on high flame until two whistles. Then, reduce it to low flame and continue to cook the rice for another 8 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cook aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. While the rice is cooking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":18,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":18,"flame":0}'),('63b4085ffd297ac6481f202c','63b4052c2783738d69824788',2,'P2 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Basil Fried Rice, wash and cut a red bell pepper into half and remove the seeds, then slice 1/4 cup of red bell peppers. Next, cut 250 gms of tofu into medium size dices, wash and pat dry three to four ice berg lettuce leaves and roughly tear them into pieces; wash and finely chop 3 teaspoons of Birds eye chilli, peel and slice 1 large onion, wash and peel half an inch of ginger, peel and finely chop 4 Cloves of garlic and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":18,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63b40a4d27eb4d18be5b010b','63b4052c2783738d69824788',3,'P3 Marinate the Tofu','To marinate the tofu for Basil Fried Rice, in a mixing bowl add 3 tablespoons of soy sauce, add 1 teaspoon of chopped bird eye chilli, add half a teaspoon of chilli sauce, and mix well using a spoon until ingredients are well combined. Next, add 250 gms of diced tofu pieces and mix it well such that the tofu pieces are evenly coated with the marinade. Cover the bowl with a lid and allow it to marinate for 15 minutes. While the tofu is marinating, move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":15,"flame":0}'),
('63b40acbfd297ac6481f202e','63b4052c2783738d69824788',4,'P4 Prepare the paste','To prepare the paste for Basil Fried Rice, in a mortar and pestle, add 1 teaspoon of chopped bird eye chillies, followed by 3 cloves of chopped garlic, add half an inch of ginger, and crush it using a pestle. Do not form it into a paste, slightly crush it such that it results in a coarse mixture.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63b40baf27eb4d18be5b010c','63b4052c2783738d69824788',5,'M1 Cook the vegetables','To prepare the Basil Fried Rice, heat a wok and add 3 tablespoons of oil and allow it to become hot on high flame. Next, add 1 sliced onion, and saute it for 2-3 minutes until it becomes slightly golden brown, then lower the flame and add the marinated tofu pieces and saute it along with the onions for a minute. Then, add the prepared coarse mixture and 1/4 cup of sliced bell pepper and saute it for 3-4 minutes on medium flame until the bell pepper slightly shrink. Add 1/2 a teaspoon of salt and mix well.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63b40c64fd297ac6481f202f','63b4052c2783738d69824788',6,'M2 Mix and cook the rice','Next, for Basil Fried Rice add the remaining marinade of soy sauce and chilli sauce used for the tofu, and mix well. Then add 1/4 cup of torn ice berg lettuce leaves and mix well. Next, add the cooked rice and gently toss it with the cooked vegetables and seasoning. Top it with 1 tablespoon of soy sauce, and mix again. Then add 1 tablespoon of washed basil leaves and mix again. Then adjust the seasoning, turn off the flame and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63b42b8427eb4d18be5b010f','63b42adf2783738d6982478b',1,'P1 Prepare the Dough','To prepare the dough for Cauliflower Paratha, in a mixing bowl add 1 cup of wheat flour, add some salt to taste along with 1/4 cup of water and mix well and knead it into a smooth dough using your hands. Continue to add water little by little as and when required and continue to knead for another 5 minutes until the dough becomes non-sticky and soft. Then, add half a teaspoon of oil on top and grease the dough ball. Next, cover the dough with a moist cloth and allow it to rest for 20 minutes. While the dough is set aside, move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":20,"flame":0}'),('63b42c8127eb4d18be5b0110','63b42adf2783738d6982478b',2,'P2 Prepare the Stuffing','To prepare the stuffing for Cauliflower Paratha, wash and clean the cauliflower and then grate 3/4 cup of cauliflower; wash, peel and grate half an inch of ginger; wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves and set aside. Next, heat a pan and add 3/4 teaspoon of oil and allow it to become hot. Next, add 1/2 an inch of grated ginger and saute it on medium low flame for a few seconds until the raw smell goes. Then, add 3/4 cup of grated cauliflower and saute it on medium flame for 3 minutes until they are cooked and shrink in size. While the cauliflower cooks, move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":11,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":3,"flame":2}'),
('63b42ddbfd297ac6481f2032','63b42adf2783738d6982478b',3,'P3 Continue preparing the stuffing','After the cauliflower has cooked for Cauliflower Paratha, add 1/2 a teaspoon of turmeric powder, followed by 1/4 teaspoon of kashmiri red chilli powder, 1/4 teaspoon of coriander powder, 1/4 teaspoon of cumin powder, 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala, 1/4 teaspoon of dry mango powder and 1 teaspoon of salt and saute it well until the masalas are well combined. Then turn off the flame and add 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and mix again.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63b42e5afd297ac6481f2033','63b42adf2783738d6982478b',4,'M1 Roll the stuffed paratha','To roll the Cauliflower Paratha, divide the dough into equally portioned lemon size balls and place the dough ball on a rolling board and dust it with some wheat flour. Then, slightly flatten the dough and roll it into a 5 inch disc using a rolling pin. Next, place one tablespoon of the prepared cauliflower stuffing in the center and gather the paratha from the sides and start pleating it and bring to the center as shown. Pinch the excess dough off, and slightly flatten the stuffed ball. Dust it with some wheat flour, and gently roll it into a 5 inch disc. Ensure the stuffing is evenly distributed on all sides. Repeat the same for the remaining dough balls and stuffing','cook_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63b430b62783738d6982478d','63b42adf2783738d6982478b',5,'M2 Roast the stuffed paratha','To roast the Cauliflower Paratha, heat a tawa and allow it to become hot. Then transfer the rolled paratha onto the tawa and allow it to roast on medium low flame for half a minute until the brown spots and bubbles appear, then flip the paratha on the other side and apply a teaspoon of ghee and evenly spread it over the paratha. Then flip the paratha again and apply ghee on the other side, and continue to flip at regular intervals until the paratha is roasted evenly on both the sides. Repeat the same for the remaining parathas and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63b43c1a27eb4d18be5b0113','63b43b1bfd297ac6481f2035',1,'P1 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Akuri, in a mixing bowl, crack 3 large eggs and discard the shell. Then whisk the eggs well using the whisk until the eggs become fluffy and creamy, and then set the whisked eggs aside. Next, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onion, peel and finely chop 1 teaspoon of garlic, wash and finely chop 1/2 a teaspoon of green chillies, wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63b43cc72783738d6982478f','63b43b1bfd297ac6481f2035',2,'M1 Prepare the tempering','To prepare Akuri, heat a pan and add 1 tablespoon of oil and allow it to become hot .Then, add 1/4 teaspoon of cumin seeds and saute it over medium flame for a few seconds until it splutters. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped onion and saute it on medium low flame for two minutes until it becomes slightly brown in colour. Then, add 1 teaspoon of chopped garlic followed by 1/2 a teaspoon of chopped green chillies and saute it until the onions are nicely browned.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('63b43d9427eb4d18be5b0114','63b43b1bfd297ac6481f2035',3,'M3 Scramble the eggs','After the onions are browned for Akuri, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder and saute it for a few seconds until well combined with the tempering. Next, reduce the heat to low flame and add in the whisked eggs followed by one tablespoon of milk (You can replace the milk with fresh cream for a creamy Akuri) , 1/4 teaspoon of salt and using a spatula rapidly stir saute the eggs until they are slightly cooked. Scrape the sifes and bottom of the pan at regular intervals while scrambling the eggs to prevent it from sticking and burning. Once the eggs have become soft, creamy and slightly runny take the pan off the heat and continue scrambling it until it reaches the desired consistency. Do not overcook the eggs. Garnish the Akuri with a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and serve hot with toasted bread.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('63b440fb2783738d69824794','63b44039fd297ac6481f2038',1,'P1 Soak the Dal and Rice','To soak the dal and rice for Dal Khichdi, thoroughly rinse 1/2 a cup of rice under water and transfer the washed rice in a mixing bowl along with 1.5 cups of water and allow it to soak for 20 minutes. Next, rinse 1/2 a cup of moong dal under water and transfer the washed moong dal in another mixing bowl along with 1.5 cups of water and allow it to soak for 20 minutes. While the rice and dal are soaking, move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":20,"flame":0}'),('63b4420e27eb4d18be5b0117','63b44039fd297ac6481f2038',2,'P2 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Dal Khichdi, peel and finely chop 1/2 a cup of onions; wash and finely chop 1/2 a cup of tomatoes; wash and slit 1 green chilli; wash and finely chop two tablespoons of coriander leaves and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63b442c82783738d69824795','63b44039fd297ac6481f2038',3,'M1 Prepare the Tempering','To prepare Dal Khichdi, heat pressure cooker pan and add one tablespoon of ghee and allow it to become hot and melt. Then, add 1 teaspoon of cumin seeds, add 1 bay leaf followed by 1/8 teaspoon of hingh and saute it on medium low flame until the spices crackle and become fragrant. Next, add 1/2 a cup of chopped onion and saute it on medium low flame for two minutes until they become translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('63b4435ffd297ac6481f2039','63b44039fd297ac6481f2038',4,'M2  Cook the tomatoes','After the onions become translucent for Dal Khichdi, add 1 teaspoon of ginger garlic paste, followed by 1 slit green chilli and saute it well for a few seconds until the raw smell of the ginger garlic paste goes. Next, add 1/2 a cup of chopped tomatoes and saute it well on medium flame for three minutes until the tomatoes become soft and mushy.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('63b444022783738d69824796','63b44039fd297ac6481f2038',5,'M3 Pressure cook the Dal Khichdi','After the tomatoes become mushy for Dal Khichdi, add 1/2 a teaspoon of turmeric powder, add 3/4 teaspoon of salt, and saute it on low flame until the masalas are well combined. Next, add half a cup of soaked rice followed by half a cup of soaked moong dal and saute it for a minute until it is well combined with the tempering. Then, add 3.5 cups of water and give it a good mix. Next, cover the pressure cooker with a lid and allow it to pressure cook on high flame until 4 whistles and then reduce the flame and allow it to cook on low flame for another 8 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and allow the pressure cooker to release air naturally. While the dal khichdi is cooking, move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":22,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":22,"flame":3}'),('63b44710fd297ac6481f203a','63b44039fd297ac6481f2038',6,'M4 Garnish and Serve','After the pressure cooker has cooled for Dal Khichdi, carefully open the lid and gently mix the khichdi, do not mash at this point. Next, garnish it with two tablespoons of chopped coriander leaves and mix well. Remove in a serving plate and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63b51257fd297ac6481f203d','63b44a002783738d69824798',1,'P1 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Bharwa Parwal, thoroughly wash 7 pointed gourds, peel a thin layer of the outer skin and cut both the ends. Then make a slit in the center and scoop out the seeds and pulp. Repeat the same for all the gourds. Next, wash and finely chop 2 green chillies, wash, peel and grate half an inch of ginger, peel and finely chop 1/2 a cup of onion, wash and finely chop 1.5 tablespoons of coriander leaves and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63b512f6fd297ac6481f203e','63b44a002783738d69824798',2,'P2 Prepare the Stuffing','To prepare the stuffing for Bharwa Parwal, heat a pan and add 1 tablespoon of mustard oil and allow it to become hot. Then, add 1/2 a cup of chopped onion and saute it on medium low flame for two minutes until it becomes golden brown. Then, add half an inch of grated ginger, and saute it for a minute until the raw smell goes. Then, add the scooped parwal seeds followed by 2 chopped green chillies and  1/2 a teaspoon of turmeric powder and saute it on medium low flame for two minutes until the masalas are well combined and cooked','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63b51382fd297ac6481f203f','63b44a002783738d69824798',3,'P3 Continue preparing the stuffing','Next, for Bharwa Parwal, add 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala, add 1/4 teaspoon of black pepper powder, add 1/4 teaspoon of fennel powder, add 1 teaspoon of salt followed by 1 tablespoon of water and mix on medium low flame for a minute until the masalas are well combined. Then cover the pan with a lid and allow the stuffing to cook for two minutes on low flame. Then turn off the flame, open the lid and add 1.5 tablespoons of chopped coriander leaves and mix again. Remove in a bowl and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":2,"flame":1}'),
('63b513d3fd297ac6481f2040','63b44a002783738d69824798',4,'M1 Stuff the gourds','To stuff the pointed gourd for Bharwa Parwal, slightly open the slit pointed gourds without breaking them and fill in 1 tablespoons of the prepared stuffing as shown and press the pointed gourd to close. Ensure not to over stuff the pointed gourd to prevent it from breaking. Repeat the same for the remaining gourds and stuffing.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63b514402783738d698247a0','63b44a002783738d69824798',5,'M2 Cook the gourds','Next, to cook the Bharwa Parwal , heat a pan and add 2 tablespoons of mustard oil and allow it to become hot. Then, arrange the stuffed gourds on the pan, cover the pan with a lid and allow it to cook for three minutes on medium low flame. While the gourds are cooking, move onto the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":3,"flame":2}'),('63b514c527eb4d18be5b011f','63b44a002783738d69824798',6,'M3 Continue cooking the gourds','Then for Bharwa Parwal, open the lid and sprinkle salt over the gourds and flip the gourds on the other side and allow them to shallow fry until it becomes golden brown. Continue to cover the lid and flip and cook the gourds every two minutes until it is evenly browned on all sides. Then, turn off the flame and serve hot with rice or roti.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":6,"flame":2}'),('63b522662783738d698247a4','63b51f11fd297ac6481f2041',1,'P1 Prep the ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Aloo Gobi Dalna, to clean the cauliflower, thoroughly wash a cauliflower head and cut them into medium sized florets. Next, to clean the florets heat a stock pot and add 1 cup of water, add a teaspoon of salt and bring to a rolling boil. Then, add the cauliflower florets and allow it to boil for 2 minutes. Then turn off the flame, strain the cauliflower and set aside. Next, wash, peel and cut 1/2 a cup of potatoes into medium sized chunks and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":2,"flame":2}'),('63b522db27eb4d18be5b0122','63b51f11fd297ac6481f2041',2,'P2 Prepare the spice mix','To prepare the spice paste, in a mixing bowl add 1/2 a teaspoon of cumin powder, add 1/2 a teaspoon of coriander powder followed by 1/4 teaspoon of red chilli powder and 2 tablespoons of water and mix it well and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":1,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('63b52383fd297ac6481f2043','63b51f11fd297ac6481f2041',3,'M1 Fry the cauliflower','To fry the cauliflower for Aloo Gobi Dalna, heat a pan and add 1 tablespoon of cooking oil and allow it to become hot. Then, add 1 cup of cauliflower florets, add 1/4 teaspoon of salt, followed by 1/4 teaspoon of sugar and 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder and give it a good mix. Then cover the pan with a lid and cook the cauliflower for 7 to 8 minutes until it becomes tender. While the cauliflower is cooking, move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":8,"flame":2}'),('63b527202783738d698247a5','63b51f11fd297ac6481f2041',4,'M2 Fry the potatoes','To fry the potatoes for Aloo Gobi Dalna, heat a pan and add 1 tablespoon of cooking oil and allow it to become hot. Then, add 1 teaspoon of panch phoron, 2 bay leaves, 4 cloves and 3 cardamoms and saute it for a few seconds on medium flame until the spices splutter. Next, add 1/2 a cup of potato chunks followed by 1/2 a teaspoon of salt and 1/2 a teaspoon of turmeric powder and mix well. Then cover the pan with a lid and allow the potatoes to cook for 6 minutes until they are cooked and become slightly tender. While the potatoes are cooking, move onto the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":6,"flame":2}'),('63b527a327eb4d18be5b0123','63b51f11fd297ac6481f2041',5,'M3 Cook the vegetables','After the potatoes have cooked for Aloo Gobi Dalna, open the lid and give it a good mix. Then, pour the prepared spice paste and mix again. Next, add the fried cauliflower and mix it with the potatoes on medium flame. Saute the vegetables on medium flame for 2 to 3 minutes until they turn golden brown. Then add 1.5 cups of water followed by half a teaspoon of salt and cover the pan with a lid and cook for another 5 minutes on low flame until the vegetables become tender and cooked. While the vegetables are cooking move onto the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63b527fe27eb4d18be5b0124','63b51f11fd297ac6481f2041',6,'M4 Simmer and serve','After the vegetables have cooked for Aloo Gobi Dalna, carefully open the lid, insert a fork into the potato and check if it is well cooked. Then, add 1/4 cup of green peas and saute it and cook for a minute. Then turn off the flame and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63b552ad27eb4d18be5b0129','63b5517bfd297ac6481f2044',1,'P1 Boil the Corn','To boil the corn for Barbecue Chicken Salad, first, boil 1 cup of water in a pan over medium-high flame for 1-2 minutes. As the water comes to a boil, add 1/4 cup of sweet corn kernels and boil them over medium flame for 4-5 minutes until tender. Then, turn off the flame and remove the boiled corn kernels in a bowl and set them aside. While the corn kernels are boiling, move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":5,"flame":2}'),
('63b553b127eb4d18be5b012a','63b5517bfd297ac6481f2044',2,'P2 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Barbeque Chicken Salad, wash, peel and cut 1/4 cup of carrot into thin strips; wash and cut a green bell pepper into half and remove the seeds, then cut 1/4 cup of green bell pepper into slices, peel and slice 1/4 cup of onion; wash and cut 1/4 cup of English cucumber into thin strips; wash and cut 1/4 cup of tomato into slices; wash and shred half a cup of cabbage. Next, finely chop 2 tablespoons of jalapenos, and finely chop 2 tablespoons of black olives. Then, wash and pat dry 500 gms of boneless chicken and cut them into medium width strips and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":20,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63b5597d27eb4d18be5b012b','63b5517bfd297ac6481f2044',3,'M1 Cook The Chicken','To cook the chicken for Barbecue Chicken Salad, heat a pan and add 2 tablespoons of oil and allow it to become hot. Then add 500 gms of chicken strips and stir fry it on medium flame for a minute. Next, add 1 teaspoon of ginger garlic paste and mix it well with the chicken. Next, add 1/2 a teaspoon of salt followed by 1/2 a teaspoon of black pepper powder and 1/2 a teaspoon of red chilli powder and mix welluntil well combined.  Add 2 teaspoons of water if the chicken feels dry. Next, add 2 teaspoons of soy sauce, and saute and cook the chicken for 10 to 12 minutes on medium flame until the skin becomes slightly white and it is cooked. While the chicken is cooking, move onto the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":12,"flame":2}'),('63b55b132783738d698247a9','63b5517bfd297ac6481f2044',4,'M2 Assemble the Salad','To assemble the Barbecue Chicken Salad, in a mixing bowl add 1/4 cup of carrot strips, add 1/4 cup of slice green bell peppers, add 1/4 cup of slices onion, 1/4 cup of sliced english cucumber, add 1/4 cup of sliced tomato, add 1/2 a cup of cabbage shreds and toss the vegetables until well combined. Next, add the stir fried chicken and toss it with the vegetables. Then add 1/4 cup of boiled sweet corn, add 2 tablespoons of chopped jalapenos, add 2 tablespoons of chopped olives, add 2 tablespoons of BBQ sauce, add 2 tablespoons of ketchup, then add 1 tablespoon of mustard sauce, add 1 tablespoon of lemon juice followed by 2 teaspoons of vinegar and 1 tablespoon of honey. Toss the salad well, adjust the seasoning, garnish with sesame seeds and serve','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63b55ff62783738d698247ab','63b55e9cfd297ac6481f2047',1,'P1 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Aviyal, first in a mixing bowl add a lemon sized ball of tamarind along with 1/4 cup of water and allow it to soak for 15 minutes. While the tamarind is soaking, grease your hands with a little oil and then peel and cut 1/4 cup of yam into 1 inch batons; wash and cut 10 long beans into medium size long pieces,  grate 1/2 a cup of coconut, wash 2 green chillies, wash and pluck 10 curry leaves, wash and cut 1/4 cup of Managalore cucumber into medium sized chunks and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":20,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63b5607f2783738d698247ac','63b55e9cfd297ac6481f2047',2,'P2 Prepare the Coconut paste','To prepare the coconut paste for Aviyal, in a mixy jar add 1/2 a cup of grated coconut, add 1/2 a teaspoon of cumin seeds, add 2 green chillies, add 1/4 cup of water and blend it into a smooth paste . Next, in a mixing bowl add 1/4 cup of yogurt and whisk it well until it becomes flowy in consistency.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('63b56159fd297ac6481f2048','63b55e9cfd297ac6481f2047',3,'M1 Cook the vegetables','To cook the vegetables for Aviyal, heat a stock pot add 1/4 cup of yam, add 10 cut beans, add 1/4 cup of managalore cucumber chunks, add 1/4 cup of green peas along with 2 cups of water. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder followed by 1 teaspoon of salt, and mix it well. Then, allow it to cook for 10 to 12 minutes on medium low flame until the vegetables become tender and are cooked.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":12,"flame":2}'),('63b561b327eb4d18be5b012e','63b55e9cfd297ac6481f2047',4,'M2 Simmer the aviyal','After the vegetables becomes tender and are cooked for Aviyal, squeeze the soaked tamarind using your hands and add 1 tablespoon of tamarind pulp to the vegetables followed by the prepared coconut paste and gently mix until well combined. Then, allow the aviyal to simmer on low flame for 5 minutes. Next, lower the flame and add 1/4 cup of whisked curds and mix again. Then, bring to boil. While the Aviyal comes to a boil, move onto the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":8,"flame":1}'),('63b5624327eb4d18be5b012f','63b55e9cfd297ac6481f2047',5,'M3 Prepare the tempering','To prepare the tempering for Aviyal, heat a tempering pan and add 2 teaspoons of coconut oil and allow it to become hot on medium flame. Then, add 1/2 a teaspoon of mustard seeds and allow it to crackle. Next, add 10 washed curry leaves, and allow it to splutter. Then turn off the flame and pour the tempering over the boiling Aviyal. Then, turn off the flame and serve hot with rice.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63b5676f2783738d698247ae','63b566672783738d698247ad',1,'AP1 Soak the Kidney Beans','To soak the kidney beans for Kidney Beans Salad, first, soak 1/2 cup of kidney beans in 3/4 cup of water for 12 hours or overnight. While the kidney beans are soaking move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":720,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63b56830fd297ac6481f204a','63b566672783738d698247ad',2,'P1 Pressure Cook the Kidney Beans','To pressure cook the kidney beans for Kidney Beans Salad, in a pressure cooker add 1/2 a cup of soaked kidney beans, along with 2 cups of water and 1/4 tsp of salt, and 1/4 tsp of oil. Cook this on high flame for 4 whistles and then on low flame for 8 mins. Once this is done, allow the pressure to release naturally. While the kidney beans are cooking, move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":20,"flame":4}'),
('63b5693927eb4d18be5b0132','63b566672783738d698247ad',3,'P2 Boil the Corn','To boil the corn for Kidney Beans salad, first, boil 1 cup of water in a pan over medium-high flame for 1-2 minutes. As the water comes to a boil, add 1/2 a cup of sweet corn kernels and boil them over medium flame for 4-5 minutes until tender. Then, turn off the flame and remove the boiled corn kernels in a bowl and set them aside. While the corn kernels are boiling, move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":1,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":7,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":7,"flame":3}'),('63b569c327eb4d18be5b0133','63b566672783738d698247ad',4,'P3 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Kidney Beans Salad, wash and dice 1/4 cup of English cucumber, wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of parsley, wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of spring onions; wash and cut a lemon into half and squeeze the lemon to collect 3 tablespoons of lemon juice; crumble half a cup of feta cheese and set aside','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63b56bc4fd297ac6481f204b','63b566672783738d698247ad',5,'P4 Prepare the Dressing','Next, to prepare the dressing for Kidney Beans Salad in a mixing bowl add 3 tablespoons of lime juice, add 2 tablespoons of olive oil, add 3 teaspoons of mustard paste, add 2 teaspoons of cumin powder, add 3/4 teaspoon of oregano powder and 1 tablespoon of honey followed by half a teaspoon of peeper powder and 1/2 a teaspoon of salt and mix it well using a spoon or whisk until it is well combined','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63b56c8227eb4d18be5b0134','63b566672783738d698247ad',6,'M1 Toss the salad','To prepare the Kidney Beans Salad, in a mixing bowl add 1/2 a cup of boiled kidney beans, add 1/2 a cup of boiled corn, add 1/4 cup of diced English cucumber, add 2 tablespoons of parsley, add 2 tablespoons of chopped spring onion and pour the prepared dressing followed by half a cup of crumbled feta cheese and mix it well until well combined. Serve warm or chilled','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63b572b72783738d698247b1','63b571252783738d698247af',1,'P1 Prep the ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Persian Chicken, peel and finely chop 1 cup of onions and wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of parsley, wash and pat dry 500 gms of chicken legs. Next, to season the chicken legs , in a mixing bowl add 500 gms of chicken, and sprinkle 1 teaspoon of salt followed by 1 teaspoon of black pepper powder and mix it well using your hands until the chicken legs are evenly coated .','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('63b5738427eb4d18be5b0136','63b571252783738d698247af',2,'P2 Prepare the Pomegranate Molasses','To make pomegranate molasses for Persian Chicken, heat a deep bottom pan on medium flame and add 1 cup of pomegranate juice. Next, add 1 tablespoon of lemon juice and 3 tablespoons of sugar to the juice and stir it well. Keep stirring it continuously on medium flame until the sugar dissolves completely. Continue to boil the syrup on medium flame for another 10-12 minutes until the syrup is reduced to 1/4 cup. While the molasses is cooking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":12,"flame":2}'),('63b5743efd297ac6481f204d','63b571252783738d698247af',3,'P3 Sear the Chicken Legs','To sear the chicken legs, heat a heavy bottom skillet, add 1 tablespoon of olive oil and allow it to become hot on high heat. Then place the seasoned chicken legs with the skin side down and cook for 2 minutes until it becomes nicely brown. Then, flip the chicken legs and allow it to cook on the other side for 2 to 3 minutes until nicely browned. Then turn off the flame, transfer the browned chicken legs and set them aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":6,"flame":3}'),('63b574c627eb4d18be5b0137','63b571252783738d698247af',4,'P4 Prepare the walnut powder','To prepare the walnut powder for Persian Chicken, in a blender jar add 3/4 cup of walnuts and pulse grind it into a coarse powder. Ensure not to continuously grind the walnuts as it will leave out oil and become sticky. Next, heat a pan and transfer the coarse walnut powder onto it and dry roast them on medium flame for a minute until it becomes golden brown.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":2,"flame":2}'),('63b575e12783738d698247b2','63b571252783738d698247af',5,'M1 Prepare the sauce','To prepare the sauce for Persian Chicken, heat a stock pot and add 1 tablespoon of olive oil and allow it to become hot. Then, add 1 cup of chopped onion and saute it on medium flame for 2 to 3 minutes until the onions become golden brown. Then, add 1 teaspoon of turmeric powder, add 1/4 teaspoon of cinnamon powder, add 1/8 teaspoon of nutmeg powder and mix it well and cook for a minute.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('63b5766027eb4d18be5b0138','63b571252783738d698247af',6,'M2 Simmer the sauce','After the spices have cooked for Persian Chicken, add 6 cups of water and add 1.5 cubes of chicken broth cube, add 1/4 cup of honey, add 1/4 cup of the prepared pomegranate mollasses and mix it well until well combined. Allow it to cook on high flame until it comes to a rolling boil. While the stock comes to a boil move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":1,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":6,"flame":4}'),
('63b576f72783738d698247b3','63b571252783738d698247af',7,'M3 Cook the chicken in the sauce','After the stock has come to a boil for Persian Chicken, add the toasted walnut powder and mix it well. Next, reduce the heat to low flame and add the seared chicken pieces. Then allow the Persian Chicken to simmer on low flame for an hour until the gravy thickens and the chicken becomes tender and cooked. Keep stirring the curry occasionally to prevent it from sticking to the bottom and burning. While the curry is simmering, move onto the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":60,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":60,"flame":1}'),('63b5775927eb4d18be5b0139','63b571252783738d698247af',8,'M4 Garnish and Serve','After the sauce has thickened for Persian Chicken, garnish it with a tablespoon of chopped parsley, some chopped walnuts and 1 tablespoon of fresh pomegranate seeds and serve hot on a bed of cooked rice.','cook_method','{"active_time":1,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63b5813efd297ac6481f204f','63b580b327eb4d18be5b013a',1,'AP1 Chill the water and ice cubes','For Cinnamon Cold Coffee, fill an ice tray with drinking water and allow it to chill in the freezer overnight. Next, fill a jug with 250 ml of water and allow it to chill in the refrigerator overnight. Meanwhile, move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":480,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63b581c12783738d698247b7','63b580b327eb4d18be5b013a',2,'P1 Prepare the coffee mixture','To prepare Cinnamon Cold Coffee, in a mixing bowl or a jar add 1 tablespoon of instant coffee powder, add 250 ml of water, add 6 cubes of ice followed by 1/8 teaspoon of cinnamon and 1 tablespoon of brown sugar and mix it using a hand blender for 3-5 minutes until it foams up .','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63b5820127eb4d18be5b013c','63b580b327eb4d18be5b013a',3,'M1 Layer the Cinnamon Cold Coffee','To make Cinnamon Cold Coffee, in a serving glass add 2 ice cubes and pour 1/4 glass of full fat milk, then take a tablespoon and place it diagonally inside the glass touching its wall as shown. Next pour in the foamed coffee mixture in the glass until the rim such that it forms a layer on the milk and top the foam with some brown sugar and cinnamon powder. Repeat the same for the other glass and serve chilled','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('63b697e76f5a113faead2320','63b6968bf2d4a37dfeaa3da5',1,'AP1 Chill the water and ice cubes','For Vanilla Cold Coffee, fill an ice tray with drinking water and allow it to chill in the freezer overnight. While the ice cubes form, move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":480,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63b6987dc883dac33572c2b6','63b6968bf2d4a37dfeaa3da5',2,'P1 Prepare the coffee mixture','To prepare the coffee mixture for Vanilla Cold Coffee, in a small pan heat 1/4 cup of water and allow it to simmer for 2 minutes. Then turn off the flame and set aside. Next, in a mixing bowl or jar add 2 teaspoons of instant coffee, add 2 teaspoons of brown sugar, add 2 tablespoons of hot water and blend it using a milk frother for 3 minutes until the mixture foams up.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":2,"flame":1}'),('63b698b36f5a113faead2321','63b6968bf2d4a37dfeaa3da5',3,'M1 Layer the Vanilla Cold Coffee','To layer the Vanilla Cold Coffee, in a serving glass add 2 ice cubes, pour the prepared the coffee mixture until it reaches half a glass and pour 1/4 cup of milk on top. Then add 2 scoops of vanilla ice cream and serve chilled. You could top it with a few drops of vanilla essence (optional)','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63b6a12e6f5a113faead2324','63b6a0a6f2d4a37dfeaa3da7',1,'P1 Prep the ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Tindora Fry, wash 250 gms of ivy gourd and cut both the ends, then cut the ivy gourd into quarters. Then, wash and slit 2 green chillies, grate 1/2 a cup of Coconut and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63b6a4fbc883dac33572c2b7','63b6a0a6f2d4a37dfeaa3da7',2,'M1  Prepare the tempering','To prepare Tindora Fry, heat a pan and add 1 tablespoon of oil and allow it to become hot. Next, add 1/2 a teaspoon of mustard seeds, add  1 teaspoon of urad dal, break and add 2 dried red chillies, add 2 slit green chillies, add 10 curry leaves and saute it on medium low flame for a few seconds until the spices crackle and the dal becomes slightly brown.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),
('63b6a6206f5a113faead2325','63b6a0a6f2d4a37dfeaa3da7',3,'M2 Cook the ivy gourd','Next, for Tindora Fry add 250 gms of cut ivy gourd to the tempering and mix and saute the ivy gourd for 2 to 3 minutes on medium flame until the ivy gourd is cooked and becomes tender. Then add 3/4 teaspoon of salt, add 1/2 a teaspoon of turmeric powder, add 1 teaspoon of jaggery followed by 1/2 a cup of water and mix it until well combined. Next, cover the pan with a lid and allow the ivy gourd to cook on low flame for 15minutes. Stir the ivy gourd occasionally to prevent it from sticking to the pan and burning. Add a few tablespoons of water if you think the curry has become dry. While the ivy gourd is cooking, move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":15,"flame":1}'),('63b6a6bff2d4a37dfeaa3da9','63b6a0a6f2d4a37dfeaa3da7',4,'M3 Add the coconut and serve','After the ivy gourd is cooked well for the tindora fry, carefully open the lid and add 1/2 a cup of grated coconut and mix it well. Then cover the pan with a lid and cook for another minute on low flame. Then turn off the flame, and serve hot with roti or rice','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('63b6b57bf2d4a37dfeaa3dac','63b6ab416f5a113faead2326',1,'AP 1 Soak the ingredients for dosa batter','To prepare the dosa batter, in a mixing bowl add 1.5 cup of raw rice followed by 1/2 a cup of urad dal, add 1 tsp of fenugreek seeds, and add 3 cups of water and rinse twice and then discard the water. Then soak it in 3 cups of water for 3 hours. In another mixing bowl add 1/2 a cup of thin flattened rice flakes and add 1 cup of water and allow it to soak for 10 minutes. While the rice mixture and flattened rice are soaking move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63b6b5ff6f5a113faead2327','63b6ab416f5a113faead2326',2,'AP2 Blend and ferment the batter','Next, to prepare the dosa batter, in a mixy jar add the soaked rice mixture along with 1/2 a cup of soaked flattened rice flakes, close the lid and blend it into a fine batter. After preparing the batter, transfer it into a mixing bowl, cover the bowl with a lid and allow it to ferment for 8-10 hours. While the batter ferments, move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":600,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63b6b661f2d4a37dfeaa3dad','63b6ab416f5a113faead2326',3,'P1 Boil the Potatoes','To boil the potatoes for Masala Dosa, wash 2 medium-sized potatoes and add them to a pressure cooker along with 1 cup of water. Cover it with a lid and pressure cook the potatoes over a high flame until 1 whistle. Then, reduce the flame to low and continue to cook the potatoes for another 8 minutes. After that, turn off the flame and allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally.  While the potatoes are boiling, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":18,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":18,"flame":4}'),
('63b6c3896f5a113faead2328','63b6ab416f5a113faead2326',4,'P2 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Masala Dosa, remove the lid of the pressure cooker and carefully remove the boiled potatoes onto a plate. Then, allow them to slightly cool. While the potatoes cool, peel and slice 1/2 a cup of onions, wash 1 tablespoon of curry leaves, wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves, wash and slit 2 green chillies, wash, peel and finely chop 1.5 teaspoons of ginger. Then, gently peel off the skin of the potatoes, transfer it into a mixing bowl and mash the potatoes well using a fork or a potato masher.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63b6c4e26f5a113faead2329','63b6ab416f5a113faead2326',5,'M1 Prepare the tempering','To prepare the tempering for Masala Dosa, heat a pan and add 3 teaspoons of oil and allow it to become hot. Then, add 1/2 a teaspoon of mustard seeds, add 1/2 a teaspoon of split black gram, add 1 teaspoon of bengal gram, add 1/2 a teaspoon of cumin seeds, and saute it on medium low flame for a few seconds until the spices splutter and the dals become slightly brown.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63b6d2faf2d4a37dfeaa3dae','63b6ab416f5a113faead2326',6,'M2 Cook the onions','Next, after the spices have spluttered for Masala Dosa, add 1 tablespoon of curry leaves followed by 1/2 a cup of sliced onions, 1.5 teaspoon of chopped ginger and 2 slit green chillies and saute it on medium flame for 2 minutes until the onions become translucent.  Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, add 1 teaspoon of salt and continue mixing it until its well combined','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63b6d832f2d4a37dfeaa3daf','63b6ab416f5a113faead2326',7,'M3 Cook the potatoes','Next, for Masala Dosa, add in 1 cup of mashed potatoes, add 1/4 cup of water, and mix it well along with the tempering. Then, add 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves, squeeze 1 teaspoon of lemon juice and mix it well. Then turn off the flame, remove the prepared masala in a bowl and set aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63b6d9106f5a113faead232a','63b6ab416f5a113faead2326',8,'M4 Prepare the Masala Dosa','To make the Masala Dosa, to the fermented batter add 1/2 a tsp of salt, add 1 tablespoon of rice flour, add 1 teaspoon of sugar and mix it well. Next, heat an iron griddle and allow it to become hot, then add a ladle full of the dosa batter and move the ladle in a circular motion to form a thin dosa, then pour 1/2 a tsp of oil on the edges of the dosa to ensure easy removal, then cover the pan with a lid and allow the dosa to cook on medium flame 2-3 minutes. Next, add a spoonful of the prepared masala to the dosa and spread it in the center as shown. Then, fold the dosa from both ends and remove it onto a serving plate. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":7,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":7,"flame":0}'),
('63b7b5f1c883dac33572c2ba','63b7b53872bac7300481469a',1,'AP1 Form ice cubes','For Chocolate Cold Coffee, fill an ice tray with drinking water and allow it to chill in the freezer overnight. While the ice cubes form, move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":480,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63b7b6c2f2d4a37dfeaa3dbc','63b7b53872bac7300481469a',2,'M1 Prepare the coffee mixture','To prepare Chocolate Cold Coffee, in a mixing bowl add 1 tablespoon of instant coffee powder, add 1 tablespoon of cocoa powder, add 2 tablespoons of water and mix it using a spoon until well combined. Next, in a mixy jar add the prepared cocoa coffee decoction along with 1 cup of milk followed by 1 scoop of vanilla ice cream and 2 tablespoons of chocolate sauce. Next, add 1 tablespoon of sugar and 6 ice cubes. Then, close the mixy jar with a lid and blend it into a frothy mix.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63b7b705c883dac33572c2bc','63b7b53872bac7300481469a',3,'M2 Assemble and serve the Chocolate Cold Coffee','To serve the Chocolate Cold Coffee, line the inside of a serving glass with chocolate sauce starting from the top with as shown and allow the chocolate sauce to drip till the bottom of the glass. Next, pour in the prepared chocolate cold coffee into the glass and serve chilled.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63b7cce9f2d4a37dfeaa3dbf','63b7c93df2d4a37dfeaa3dbd',1,'P1 Prep the ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Pepper Chicken Gravy, peel and finely chop 1 cup of onion, wash and chop 2 green chillies, wash and pat dry 500 gms of chicken. Next, in a mixing bowl add 1/4 cup of yoghurt and whisk it well using a whisk until flowy and creamy.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63b7cfdf72bac730048146a3','63b7c93df2d4a37dfeaa3dbd',2,'P2 Simmer the onion','To prepare the onion puree for Pepper Chicken Gravy, in a stock pot add 200 ml of water and bring to boil on high flame. Next, when the water starts boiling add 1 cup of chopped onions, add 12 cashewnuts followed by 2 chopped green chillies and mix it well. Allow the onions to simmer for 5 minutes on medium flame until the raw smell is gone. While the onions are simmering, move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":5,"flame":2}'),
('63b7d01af2d4a37dfeaa3dc0','63b7c93df2d4a37dfeaa3dbd',3,'P3 Blend the gravy','After the onions have simmered for Pepper Chicken Gravy, turn off the flame and strain the onions mix. Then transfer the cooked onions, cashewnuts and chillies into a mixy jar along with 1/4 cup of water and bliend it into a smooth puree.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63b7d42972bac730048146a4','63b7c93df2d4a37dfeaa3dbd',4,'M1 Prepare the gravy','To prepare the gravy for Pepper Chicken Gravy, heat a pan and add 3 tablespoons of cooking oil and allow it to become hot. Then, add 3 cloves, add 3 cardamoms, half an inch of cinnamon stick and saute it on medium flame for a few seconds until the spices bloat up and release an aroma. Next, add the prepared onion paste and mix it well along with the spices. Then, mix the gravy well and allow the onion puree to cook on low flame for 8 minutes until the puree is cooked and the oil starts leaving from the sides. Scrape the bottom of the pan occasionally, and stir the onion puree to prevent it from burning. While the onion puree is being cooked, move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":8,"flame":2}'),('63b7d4def2d4a37dfeaa3dc1','63b7c93df2d4a37dfeaa3dbd',5,'M2 Continue preparing the gravy','After the onion puree is cooked for Pepper Chicken Gravy, add 2 teaspoons of ginger garlic paste, and saute it for 2 minutes until the raw smell goes. Then, add 500 gms of chicken curry cut and increase the flame to high and stir fry the chicken on high flame for 3 to 4 minutes until it becomes slightly brown from all sides. Next, add 1/4 cup of whisked curd to it and mix it well until the chicken is evenly coated.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63b7d5b7c883dac33572c2be','63b7c93df2d4a37dfeaa3dbd',6,'M3 Cook the chicken','Next, for Pepper Chicken Gravy, to the cooked chicken add 2 teaspoons of coriander powder, add 1/2 a teaspoon of cumin powder and 1/2 a teaspoon of salt to taste and mix it well. Allow the chicken to cook for 3 to 4 minutes on medium low flame along with the masala. While the chicken is cooking, move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":1,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":4,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63b7d64b72bac730048146a5','63b7c93df2d4a37dfeaa3dbd',7,'M4 Cook the chicken with the masala','After the chicken is cooked with the masala for Pepper Chicken Gravy, add 1/2 a cup of water to the pan along with 1 teaspoon of black pepper powder and mix it well. Then allow the curry to cook for another 3 to 4 minutes until the oil starts to seprate from the sides. After 4 minutes, cover the pan with a lid and allow the chicken to cook on low flame for 30minutes until the chicken is well cooked. While the chicken is cooking, move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":2,"idle_time":30,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":30,"flame":1}'),
('63b7d6c7c883dac33572c2bf','63b7c93df2d4a37dfeaa3dbd',8,'M5 Season the curry and serve','After the chicken is thoroughly cooked for Pepper Chicken Gravy, open the lid and add 1 tablespoon of lemon juice, add 1 teaspoon of honey, add 1 tablespoon of kasuri methi, add 1 tablespoon of black pepper powder, and mix everything until well combined. Next, lower the flame add 1/4 cup of fresh cream to it and mix again. Allow it to cook for a minute and then turn off the flame and serve hot along with an Indian flatbread.','cook_method','{"active_time":1,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":1,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":1,"flame":1}'),('63b7e3ccc883dac33572c2c2','63b7e294c883dac33572c2c0',1,'P1 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Gobi Aloo Masala, to clean the cauliflower, thoroughly wash a cauliflower head and cut 1/2 a cup into medium sized florets. Next, to clean the florets heat a stock pot and add 1 cup of water, add a teaspoon of salt and bring to a rolling boil. Then, add the cauliflower florets and allow it to boil for 2 minutes. Then turn off the flame, strain the cauliflower and set aside. Next, wash, peel and cube 1/2 a cup of potatoes, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions, wash, peel and finely chop 1 teaspoon of ginger, wash and slit 3 green chillies, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":3,"flame":0}'),('63b7e515f2d4a37dfeaa3dc8','63b7e294c883dac33572c2c0',2,'M1 Prepare the Tempering','To prepare the tempering for Gobi Aloo Masala, heat a pan and add 2 tablespoons of mustard oil and allow it to become hot. Then, add 1 cup of cleaned cauliflower, add 1/2 a cup of cubed potatoes, and stir fry on medium flame for 6 minutes until it turns golden brown. Then turn off the flame and transfer the stir fried vegetables onto a plate and set aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63b7e5e5c883dac33572c2c3','63b7e294c883dac33572c2c0',3,'M2 Cook the masala','Next, for Gobi Aloo Masala, in the same pan add 1/2 a teaspoon of cumin seeds, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions, and saute it on medium low flame until it becomes brown. Next, add 1 teaspoon of chopped ginger, add 3 slit green chillies and saute it for a minute. Then add 1 teaspoon of coriander powder, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, add 1 teaspoon of kashmiri red chilli powder, add 1/4 teaspoon of garam masala and 1/2 a teaspoon of salt and mix the masalas for a minute until well combined.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63b7e66072bac730048146a7','63b7e294c883dac33572c2c0',4,'M3 Cook the vegetables','After the masalas are cooked for Gobi Aloo Masala, add 1/4 cup of water and mix it well. Then, add 1/4 cup of chopped tomato and saute it on medium flame for 3 minutes until they become soft and mushy. Next, add the stir fried cauliflower and potatoes and mix them well. Then, cover the pan with a lid and cook on low flame for 7 minutes until the potates are cooked through. While the potatoes are cooking, move onto the next step.m','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":7,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":7,"flame":2}'),
('63b7e6c172bac730048146a8','63b7e294c883dac33572c2c0',5,'M4 Garnish and Serve','After the potatoes are cooked for Gobi Aloo Masala, add 1/2 a tablespoon of lemon juice, add 1 tablespoon of kasuri methi and mix well. Then turn off the flame, remove the prepared curry in a serving bowl and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":1,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63bac32e938f7a3f91ff5117','63bac23d938f7a3f91ff5114',1,'AP1 Pickle the Onions','To pickle the onions for Paneer Kathi Roll, first peel and slice 1/2 a cup of onions and wash and chop 1 green chilli. Next, in a mixing bowl add 1/4 cup of vinegar, add 3/4 cup of water, add 1 chopped green chilli and mix it well. Then add 1/2 a cup of slices onions and allow it to soak in the solution for 2 hours. While the onion pickles, move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":120,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63bac39b938f7a3f91ff5118','63bac23d938f7a3f91ff5114',2,'P1 Prepare Hung Curd','To prepare hung curd for Paneer Kathi Roll, spread a muslin cloth add 1/2 a cup of curds and tie the muslin cloth into a bundle and gently squeeze the curd to drain the water. Hang the bundled curd for 30 minutes to allow the remaining water to drain. While the excess water drains, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":30,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":30,"flame":0}'),('63bac5155154f6cb0ff78a9e','63bac23d938f7a3f91ff5114',3,'P2 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Paneer Kathi Roll, dice 200 gms of paneer, wash and cut a red bellpepper into half, remove the seeds and cut 1/4 cup of red bellpepper into triangles, then wash a green bellpepper and cut it into half, remove the seeds and cut 1/4 cup of green bellpeppers into triangles. Wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves and wash 1/4 cup of coriander leaves. Next, peel and cut 1/2 a cup of onion into petals and slice 1/4 cup of onion , wash and slit 1 green chilli , wash and peel half an inch of ginger, peel 2 cloves of garlic and wash 1/4 cup of mint leaves and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":22,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63bac5c4154462897ad1a4cb','63bac23d938f7a3f91ff5114',4,'P3 Prepare the Green Chutney','To prepare the green chutney for Paneer Kathi Roll, in a blending jar add, 1/4 cup of mint leaves, 1/4 cup of coriander leaves, 1 green chili, 2 cloves of garlic, 1/2 inch of ginger, 1/2 tsp of lime juice, 1/4 tsp of cumin seeds, 2 tsp of curd, 1/4 tsp of black salt. Blend this and make a smooth chutney. Once this is ready, set it aside, and move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('63bac7085154f6cb0ff78a9f','63bac23d938f7a3f91ff5114',5,'P5 Prepare the Dough','To prepare the dough for Paneer Kathi Roll, in a mixing bowl add 2 cups of wheat flour, add 1/4 cup of all purpose flour, add 2 tablespoons of curd, add 1/2 a teaspoon of salt, and mix the ingredients until well combined. Gradually add water as and when needed and continue to knead the dough for 5minutes until it becomes soft and non-sticky. Then, add a teaspoon of oil and evenly grease the dough with oil. Now, cover the dough with a wet cloth and allow it to rest the dough for 10 minutes. While the dough rests, please move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":10,"flame":0}'),('63bac8675154f6cb0ff78aa0','63bac23d938f7a3f91ff5114',6,'M1 Prepare the Marinade','To prepare the marinade for Paneer Kathi Roll, heat a pan add 1 tablespoon of mustard oil and allow it to become hot. Then add 2 tablespoons of gram flour and continuously stir it in a circular motion on low flame for 3 minutes until it is well cooked and becomes liquidy in consistency. Then turn off the flame and set it aside. Next, in a mixing bowl add 1/4 cup of hung curd, add the prepared gram flour paste, add 1 teaspoon of red chilli powder, add 1/2 a teaspoon of turmeric powder, add 1 teaspoon of ginger and garlic paste, add 1/2 a teaspoon of salt, squeeze and add 1/2 a tablespoon of lemon juice and mix it well using a whisk until it is smooth and creamy.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('63bac942154462897ad1a4cc','63bac23d938f7a3f91ff5114',7,'M2 Marinate the vegetables','Next, for Paneer Kathi Roll, add the diced paneer to the prepared marinade and mix it well until the paneer is evenly coated. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped red bell pepper triangles, add 1/4 cup of chopped green bell pepper triangles, add 1/2 a cup of onion petals into the marinade and mix it well until the vegetables are evenly coated. Allow the vegetables to marinate for 10 mins, while the vegetables marinate, move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":10,"flame":0}'),('63bad28c154462897ad1a4cd','63bac23d938f7a3f91ff5114',8,'M3 Cook the marinated vegetables','To cook the marinated vegetables, heat a pan and add 1 teaspoon of oil and allow it to become hot. Then add 1 teaspoon of cumin seeds and allow it to crackle on low flame. Then, add 1/4 cup of sliced onion, and saute it on medium flame for a minute until it turns slightly brown. Then, add 1 teaspoon of ginger garlic paste, and saute it for a minute until it is cooked and the raw smell goes. Next, add 1/4 cup of tomato puree, and mix it well. Then, add 1 teaspoon of red chilli powder, add 1/2 a teaspoon of turmeric powder, add 1/2 a teaspoon of garam masala followed by 1/2 a teaspoon of salt and a pinch of sugar and mix it well.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63bad7a5154462897ad1a4ce','63bac23d938f7a3f91ff5114',9,'M4 Cook the paneer','After the masalas are cooked for Paneer Kathi Roll, next add the marinated paneer and vegetables and gently mix the vegetables to prevent it from breaking. Allow the marinated vegetables to cook on medium low flame for 2 minutes. Then, turn off the flame garnish it with 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and set aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('63bad808154462897ad1a4cf','63bac23d938f7a3f91ff5114',10,'M5 Prepare the roti','To prepare the roti for Paneer Kathi Roll, pinch the rested dough, and make equal sized balls from it. Flatten them slightly with your palms, dush them in flour, and with a rolling pin roll them into large circular shapes. Then, spread a teaspoon of oil on it and dust it with some flour and fold it into a fan fold as shown. Then roll the roti inwards like a cinnamon roll, such that it forms layers. Then, slightly flatten the dough and dust it with some flour again and roll it into a 6 inch disc. Repeat the same for the remaining dough.','cook_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63bad84a938f7a3f91ff5119','63bac23d938f7a3f91ff5114',11,'M6 Roast the Roti','To roast the roti for Paneer Kathi Roll, heat a tawa and once hot place the rolled chapati on it. Let it cook on each side for 2 mins, then coat both sides in 1/4 tsp of ghee each, and cook them for another 2 mins on each side. Once the chapati has browned evenly on both sides take it off the tawa and set it aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63bad899154462897ad1a4d0','63bac23d938f7a3f91ff5114',12,'M7 Assemble the Kathi Roll','To assemble the kathi roll , place the roti and spread 2 tsp of green chutney, arrange 2 tablespoons of the marinated vegetables stuffing and align it in the center as shown, then top the paneer with some pickled onions, drizzle some mayonnaise (optional) and garnish it with a pinch of chaat masala. Then roll the paneer kathi roll as shown and serve warm. Repeat the same for the remaining dough and marinated vegetables.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63badc33938f7a3f91ff511c','63badbb6938f7a3f91ff511a',1,'P1 Soak the rice','To soak the basmati rice for Palak Pulao, thoroughly rinse 1 cup of basmati rice, then transfer it in a mixing bowl along with 2 cups of water and allow it to soak for 15 minutes. While the basmati rice soaks move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":15,"flame":0}'),('63bade5f5154f6cb0ff78aa2','63badbb6938f7a3f91ff511a',2,'P2 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Palak Pulao, thoroughly wash 3 cups of spinach with water to get rid of the mud and trim the roots. Then finely chop 3 cups of spinach, peel and slice 1 cup of onions, wash and cut a green bell pepper into half, remove the seeds and cut the 1/4 cup of green bell pepper into dices; wash and peel and cut 1/4 cup of potatoes into cubes. Next, crack ans slice 1/4 cup of coconut into slices, wash 1 tablespoon of mint leaves, peel 3 cloves of garlic, wash and finely chop 2 green chillies and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":22,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}');
INSERT INTO catalog_recipe_steps VALUES
('63badf21154462897ad1a4d2','63badbb6938f7a3f91ff511a',3,'P3 Dry Roast the Spices','To dry roast the spices for Palak Pulao, In a pan add 6 cloves of garlic along with 1 inch of ginger, Then, add 2 chopped green chillies, add 3 green cardamoms, add 1/2 an inch of cinnamon, add 4 cloves, add 1/2 a teaspoon of fennel seeds, add 1/2 a teaspoon of cumin seeds, add 1 teaspoon of coriander seeds, and dry roast the spices on medium flame for 2 to 3 minutes until the spices splutter and the spices turn slightly golden brown.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63bae01a5154f6cb0ff78aa3','63badbb6938f7a3f91ff511a',4,'P4 Blend the masala','After roasting the spices for Palak Pulao, to the same pan add 1 tablespoon of mint leaves, add 1/4 cup of sliced coconut, and dry roast it for another minute. Then, turn off the flame and transfer the roasted spices onto a plate and allow it to slightly cool. Then, add the roasted spices into a mixy jar and blend it into a smooth paste.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":3,"flame":0}'),('63bae0a7154462897ad1a4d3','63badbb6938f7a3f91ff511a',5,'M1 Prepare the tempering','To prepare the tempering for Palak Pulao, heat a pressure cooker pan and allow it to become hot. Then, add 2 tablespoons of ghee and allow it to melt. Then add 2 tablespoons of oil and allow it to become hot. Next, add 1 bay leaf and 1 star anise and saute it on medium low flame for a few seconds until the spices splutter and release an aroma. Then, add 1 cup of slices onions, followed by 1/4 cup of diced green bell peppers and saute it on medium flame for 2 minutes until the onions become translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63bae1395154f6cb0ff78aa4','63badbb6938f7a3f91ff511a',6,'M2 Cook the spinach leaves','After the onions become translucent for Palak Pulao, add 1/4 cup of potato cubes followed by the blended masala and saute it on medium low flame for 2 minutes until the masala is cooked and the raw smell goes. At this stage, add 3 cups of chopped spinach leaves, add 1/2 a teaspoon if turmeric powder, add 1/8 teaspoon of rock salt and saute it well for a few seconds on high flame until the spinach leaves start to wilt.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63bae294938f7a3f91ff511d','63badbb6938f7a3f91ff511a',7,'M3 Pressure cook and serve','Next, for Palak Pulao, add 1 cup of soaked basmati rice and  saute it with the masala on medium flame for 2 minutes. Then add 2 cups of water followed by 1 tablespoon of yogurt and mix it well. Then, cover the pan with the pressure cooker lid and pressure cook it on high flame for one whistle. After the first whistle, reduce the flame to low and continue to simmer the rice for another 8 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":18,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":18,"flame":4}'),
('63baf63b938f7a3f91ff511f','63baf1e0154462897ad1a4d4',1,'P1 Prep the Ingredients','To cook the ridge gourd for Ridge Gourd Chutney, wash and peel 1 ridge gourd, then chop them into medium sized slices. Next, heat a pan and add 1.5 cups of water along with 1 teaspoon of salt and add the chopped ridge gourds to it. Next, add 1 teaspoon of tamarind and allow it to simmer on medium low flame for 8 minutes until the ridge gourd is cooked and becomes soft. While the ridge gourd cooks, grate 1/2 a cup of coconut and wash and pluck 10 curry leaves and set aside','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":8,"flame":1}'),('63bafa66938f7a3f91ff5120','63baf1e0154462897ad1a4d4',2,'M1 Blend the Chutney','To prepare Ridge Gourd Chutney, heat a pan and add 2 teaspoons of oil, add 2 teaspoons of white lentil, add 10 curry leaves followed by 2 dried red chillies and roast it on medium low flame for 3 minutes until they become slightly golden brown. Then allow it to cool, and transfer the roasted spices into a mixy jar and along with half a cup of grated coconut and blend it into a fine paste. Next, add the cooked ridge gourd pieces, along with 1/4 teaspoon of asefoeitida, and blend it into a smooth chutney','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63bafb00938f7a3f91ff5121','63baf1e0154462897ad1a4d4',3,'M2 Prepare the tempering and serve','To prepare the tempering for Ridge Gourd Chutney, heat a tempering pan and add 1 teaspoon of oil, add 1/2 a teaspoon of mustard seeds, add 1/2 a teaspoon of white lentils, add 1 dried red chilli broken into half, add 4 curry leaves and allow the spices to splutter on medium low flame. Then, tuen off the flame and pour the tempering over the prepared chutney and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('63bafeba5154f6cb0ff78aa7','63bafd50938f7a3f91ff5122',1,'P1 Rinse and season the poha','For Batata Poha, add 1.5 cups thick beaten rice flakes in a colander and set it aside for 5 minutes until the excess water drains out. After the water drains out add 1 teaspoon of sugar, add 1/2 a teaspoon of turmeric powder, add 1.5 teaspoons of salt, and mix it until well combined. Next, add 1 teaspoon of lemon juice and mix again and set aside. While the poha is set aside for the excess water to drain out, move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":5,"flame":0}'),('63baff61938f7a3f91ff5123','63bafd50938f7a3f91ff5122',2,'P2 Prep the ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Batata Poha, peel and finely chop 1 onion; wash, peel and dice 1 potato; wash 6 curry leaves, wash and finely chop 1 green chilli; wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('63bb00af938f7a3f91ff5124','63bafd50938f7a3f91ff5122',3,'M1 Prepare the tempering','Next, to prepare the tempering for Batata Poha, heat a pan and add 1 tablespoon of oil and allow it to become hot. Then, add 1 tablespoon of peanuts and fry it for a few seconds on medium flame until it becomes brown and then strain the fried peanuts, remove it in a bowl and set aside. Then, in the same oil add 1/2 a teaspoon of mustard seeds, add 1 chopped chilli, add 1 diced potato, and saute it for two minutes until the potatoes are slightly cooked.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63bb016c938f7a3f91ff5125','63bafd50938f7a3f91ff5122',4,'M2 Cook and serve the poha','After the potatoes are slightly cooked for Batata Poha, add 1 chopped onion and saute it on medium low flame for 2 minutes until it becomes translucent. Next, add the fried peanuts and and saute it along with the tempering. Then add the rinsed poha mixed with spices and mix it well. Then cover the pan with a lid and allow the poha to cook for 3 minutes on low flame. After the poha is cooked, turn off the flame and garnish the poha with 1 tablespoon of pomegranate seeds, 1 tablespoon of sev and 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":3,"flame":1}'),('63bb93305154f6cb0ff78aa9','63bb043f938f7a3f91ff5126',1,'P1 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Pomegranate Salad, wash and finely chop 1/2 a cup of English cucumber, wash and cut a red bell pepper into half, remove the seeds and finely chop 1/4 cup of red bell peppers, wash, peel and thinly slice 1/4 cup of red radish, wash and roughly chop 2 tablespoons of parsley, wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of mint leaves, cut the pomegranate open into half and tap and remove the seeds.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63bb9ded5154f6cb0ff78aaa','63bb043f938f7a3f91ff5126',2,'P2 Prepare the Dressing','To prepare the dressing for pomegranate salad, in a mixing bowl or jar add 2 tablespoons of olive oil, add 1 tablespoon of lemon juice, add 1 teaspoon of black pepper powder, add 1 teaspoon of salt, add 1 tablespoon of honey and mix it well using a whisk or a frother until well combined','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63bb9e475154f6cb0ff78aab','63bb043f938f7a3f91ff5126',3,'P3 Roast the Almonds','To toast the almonds for Pomegranate salad, first cut 2 tablespoons of almonds into half. Then heat a pan and add the almond halves and dry roast it on medium low flame for 2 minutes until they become slightly brown. Then turn off the flame and set the toasted almonds aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('63bb9ec8938f7a3f91ff512d','63bb043f938f7a3f91ff5126',4,'M1 Assemble the Salad','To assemble the pomegranate salad, in a mixing bowl add 1/2 a cup of chopped english cucumber, add 1/4 cup of chopped red bell peppers, add 1/4 cup of sliced red radish, add 2 tablespoons of chopped parsley, add 2 tablespoons of chopped mint leaves, add 2 tablespoons of roasted almonds, add 400 gms of pomegranate seeds and pour the prepared dressing over the top. Toss the salad until well combined and serve cold.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63bbaffb3f41871d2334bfd7','63bbad983f41871d2334bfd4',1,'AP 1  Soak the Chickpeas','To soak the chickpea for Chickpea Salad, first rinse 3/4 cup of chickpeas and transfer in in a mixing bowl along with 2 cups of water and allow it to soak for 8 hours. While the chickpeas soak, move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":480,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63bbb05fede384519839393b','63bbad983f41871d2334bfd4',2,'P1 Boil the Chickpeas','To boil the chickpeas for Chickpea Salad, transfer the soaked chickpeas to a pressure cooker followed by half a cup of water and half a teaspoon of salt. Mix it well and cover the cooker with a lid. Then, allow it cook over high flame until 3 whistles. After that, reduce the flame to low and continue to boil the chickpeas for another 5 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and allow the pressure from the cooker release naturally. While the chickpeas boil, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('63bbb0f3ede384519839393e','63bbad983f41871d2334bfd4',3,'P2 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Chickpea Salad, wash and cut 1 cup of cucumber into dices; wash and cut a red bell pepper into half, remove the seeds and cut 1 cup of red bell pepper into dices; wash and cut 1 cup of tomato into dices; peel and finely chop 1/2 a cup of onion; wash and finely chop 1/2 a cup of parsley.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63bbb1a43f41871d2334bfdc','63bbad983f41871d2334bfd4',4,'P3 Prepare the Dressing','To prepare the salad dressing, in a mixing bowl add 3 tablespoons of olive oil, add 2 tablespoons of lemon juice, add 1 tablespoon of maple syrup, add 1/2 a teaspoon of salt, add 1/2 a teaspoon of pepper powder, and mix it until well combined.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('63bbb283ad4ff98b5d931925','63bbad983f41871d2334bfd4',5,'M1 Temper the Chickpeas','To prepare Chickpea Salad, heat a pan and add 1 tablespoon of cooking oil and allow it to become hot. Then add 3/4 cup of pressure cooked chickpeas, add 1/4 teaspoon of salt, add 2 teaspoons of paprika powder, add 1 teaspoon of chopped garlic, add 1 teaspoon of cumin powder, add 1 teaspoon of oregano powder, add 1/8 teaspoon of cayenne pepper powder and mix it well. Saute it on medium flame for 3 minutes until the chickpeas are coated well with spices. Scrape the spice powder stuck to the pan to prevent it from burning.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63bbb311ad4ff98b5d931926','63bbad983f41871d2334bfd4',6,'M2 Assemble the Salad','To assemble the Chickpea Salad, in a mixing bowl add 1 cup of diced cucumbers, add 1 cup of red bell pepper dices, add 1 cup of diced tomato, add 1/2 a cup of chopped onion, add 1/2 a cup of grated carrot, then pour in the salad dressing, add the stir fried chickpeas, add 1/2 a cup of finely chopped parsley, add 1/2 a teaspoon of pepper powder, and mix it until its well combined and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63bbd9c5ad4ff98b5d93192c','63bbd9453f41871d2334bfdd',1,'P1 Soak the Soya Chunks','To soak the soya chunks for Soya Chunk Pulao, heat a saucepan and add 2 cups of water and bring to a rolling boil on high flame. Then, add 3/4 cup of soya chunks, and allow it to simmer on medium low flame for 3 to 4 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and drain the water. While the soya chunks are simmering, move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":6,"flame":2}'),('63bbda13ad4ff98b5d93192d','63bbd9453f41871d2334bfdd',2,'P2 Soak the Rice','To soak the rice for Soya Chunks Pulao, thoroughly rinse 1 cup of rice and transfer the washed rice in a mixing bowl along with 2 cups of water and allow it to soak for 20 minutes. While the rice is soaking move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":20,"flame":0}'),('63bbdaa0ad4ff98b5d93192e','63bbd9453f41871d2334bfdd',3,'P3 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Soya Chunks Pulao, peel and slice 1/2 a cup of onions, wash and finely chop 1 cup of tomatoes, wash, peel and cube 1/2 a cup of potatoes, wash and finely chop 1 green chilli, wash and roughly chop 1/4 cup of coriander leaves and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('63bbdb4bede384519839393f','63bbd9453f41871d2334bfdd',4,'M1 Prepare the Tempering','To prepare the tempering for Soya Chunks Pulao, heat a pan and add 2 tablespoons of oil and allow it to become hot. Next, add the boiled soya chunks and shallow fry them on medium flame for 3 minutes. Then, transfer it onto a plate and set aside. Next, in the same pan add 2 teaspoons of oil along with 2 tablespoons of ghee and allow it to become hot. Then add 1 bay leaf, add 5 peppercorns, 2 cloves, and 1/2 a cup of sliced onions and saute it on medium flame for 3 minutes until the onions become slightly brown.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63bbdc09ede3845198393940','63bbd9453f41871d2334bfdd',5,'M2 Cook the vegetables','After the onions are cooked for Soya Chunks Pulao, add 1/2 a cup of cubed potato, and saute it for 3 minutes on medium flame until it is slightly cooked. Then add 1 chopped green chilli, add 1 teaspoon of ginger garlic paste and saute it for a few seconds until cooked. Next, add 1 cup of chopped tomatoes, and saute it for 4 minutes until the tomatoes are cooked and become mushy.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63bbe501ede3845198393943','63bbd9453f41871d2334bfdd',6,'M3 Add the masalas','After the tomatoes are cooked for Soya Chunks Pulao, add 1/4 cup of peas and mix it until well combined. Then, add 1 tablespoon of salt, add 1 teaspoon of coriander powder, add 1 teaspoon of cumin powder, add 1/2 a teaspoon of red chilli powder, add 1 tablespoon of pulao masala, add 1 tablespoon of biryani masala and mix it well along with the vegetables until well combined. Then, add 1/4 cup of roughly chopped coriander leaves and mix again.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63bbe59e3f41871d2334bfdf','63bbd9453f41871d2334bfdd',7,'M4 Cook the soya chunks and rice','Next, for Soya Chunks Pulao, add 3/4 cup of shallow fried soya chunks along with 1 cup of soaked rice and 2 cups of water and mix well. Allow it to come to a rolling boil on low flame. Then cover the deep bottom pan with a lid and allow it to cook on low flame for 10 minutes. While the rice is cooking move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":1,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":14,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":14,"flame":0}'),('63bbe64bad4ff98b5d93192f','63bbd9453f41871d2334bfdd',8,'M5 Continue to cook the rice and serve','After the rice is partially cooked for Soya Chunks Pulao, gently take off the lid and give it a mix again. Then allow the rice to further cook for 10 minutes on medium low flame. Gently stir the rice at regular intervals to prevent it from sticking to the bottom and burning. After the water has evaporated, cover the pan with a lid and cook the rice on low flame for another 3 minutes. Then turn off the flame, remove the cooked pulao in a serving plate and serve hot with raita.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":13,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":13,"flame":2}'),
('63bbecc7ede3845198393945','63bbec16ede3845198393944',1,'P1 Pressure Cook the Chicken','To cook the chicken for Broccoli & Chicken Salad, wash and pat dry 200 gms of chicken and transfer it in a pressure cooker along with 1/4 cup of water and 1/4 teaspoon of salt and cover it with a lid. Pressure cook the chicken on high flame for 3 whistles. After 3 whistles, turn off the flame and allow the pressure to release naturally. While the chicken is cooking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":15,"flame":3}'),('63bbed1f3f41871d2334bfe0','63bbec16ede3845198393944',2,'P2 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Broccoli & Chicken Salad, thoroughly wash and cut 4 cups of broccoli into florets, peel and finely chop 1/2 a cup of  onions, cut 2 tablespoons of cheddar into small bite sized pieces. Next, gently take off the lid of the pressure cooker, place the cooked chicken on a chopping board and cut them into bite sized pieces.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63bbf1c0ede3845198393946','63bbec16ede3845198393944',3,'P3 Stir Fry the Chicken','To stir fry the chicken for Broccoli & Chicken Salad, heat a pan and add 1 tablespoon of olive oil allow it to become hot. Then add 200 gms of cut chicken and stir fry it on medium low flame for 3 minutes  until it is slightly brown. Then turn off the flame, season the chicken with 1/2 a teaspoon of black pepper powder and a pinch of salt and mix it well and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63bbf25cede3845198393947','63bbec16ede3845198393944',4,'P4 Prepare the dressing','To prepare the dressing for Broccoli & Chicken Salad, in a mixing bowl add 1/4 cup of thick yogurt (you can use low fat greek yogurt for a healthy option), add 1/2 a cup of light mayonnaise, add 2 tablespoons of apple cider vinegar, add 1/2 a teaspoon of powdered sugar, add 1/2 a teaspoon of black pepper powder and mix it using a whisk until the ingredients are well combined.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63bbf2cfede3845198393948','63bbec16ede3845198393944',5,'M1 Assemble the salad','To assemble the Broccoli & Chicken Salad, in a mixing bowl add 4 cups of broccoli florets, add 1/2 cup of chopped onion, add 200 gms of cooked chicken pieces, add 2 tablespoons of chopped cheddar cheese, and pour the prepared dressing on top of the salad. Next, toss the salad using two spoons and mix it well until it is evenly coated in the dressing . Remove in a mixing bowl and serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('63bc01613f41871d2334bfe2','63bbf67f3f41871d2334bfe1',1,'P1 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Kerala Bhindi Stir-Fry, first, wash and pat dry 200 gms of lady''s finger. Allow the lady''s finger to dry completely before you begin chopping it. While they are drying, peel and finely chop 1/2 a cup of onions, peel and slice 3 cloves of garlic, wash and pluck 7 curry leaves and grate 3 tablespoons of coconut and set aside. After the lady''s finger have dried, cut 200gms of ladies finger into medium sized roundels.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63bc0f7cad4ff98b5d931930','63bbf67f3f41871d2334bfe1',2,'M1 Prepare the tempering','To prepare the tempering for Kerala Bhindi Stir Fry, heat a pan and add 1.5 T of coconut oil and allow it to become hot. Then, add 1/2 a teaspoon of mustard seeds and allow it to splutter on medium flame. Next, add 1/2 a teaspoon of split chickpea lentils along with 1/2 a teaspoon of cumin seeds, then lower the flame and add 2 dried red chillies and stir fry it for a few seconds until the split chickpeas becomes slightly brown. Next, add 2 cloves of sliced garlic and saute it on medium flame for a few seconds until it becomes golden brown. Then, add 1/2 a cup of chopped onions and saute it for 2 minutes until they are cooked and become translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63bc10143f41871d2334bfe3','63bbf67f3f41871d2334bfe1',3,'M2 Add the ladies finger and masalas','After the onions are cooked for Kerala Bhindi Stir Fry, add 7 curry leaves and saute it for a few seconds until they start to wilt. Next, add 200 gms of chopped ladies finger stir fry it along with the tempering for 2 minutes on medium low flame. Then, reduce the flame and add 1 teaspoon salt, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, add 1/4 teaspoon of red chilli powder, and mix it until well combined.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63bc1077ad4ff98b5d931931','63bbf67f3f41871d2334bfe1',4,'M3 Cook the ladies finger and serve','Next for Kerala Bhindi Stir Fry, add 3 tablespoons of grated coconut and mix again. Then allow the curry to cook for 3 minutes on low flame, then cover the pan with a lid and continue to cook on low flame for 12 minutes until the ladies finger is thoroughly cooked. Then, turn off the flame, adjust the seasoning, add a pinch of garam masala and mix again, then remove in a serving bowl and serve hot with roti.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":15,"flame":1}'),('63bcdb29524b9a351ee815f3','63bc142dad4ff98b5d931932',1,'P1 Marinate the Fish','To marinate the fish for Coconut Milk Fish Curry, first thoroughly wash and pat dry 400 gms of fish and cut them into 1/2 inch thick pieces. Then, in a mixing bowl add 400 gms of fish pieces, add 1/2 a teaspoon of turmeric powder, add 2 teaspoons of lemon juice, add 1/2 a teaspoon of black pepper powder, add 1/2 a teaspoon of salt, and mix it well until the fish pieces are evenly coated in the marinade. Allow the fish to marinate for 30 minutes, while the fish marinates move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":30,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":30,"flame":2}'),
('63bcdb7a5080e23b965f709d','63bc142dad4ff98b5d931932',2,'P2 Soak the Tamarind','To soak the tamarind for Coconut milk fish curry, in a mixing bowl add a lemon sized bowl of tamarind along with 1/4 cup of water and allow it to soak for 15 minutes. While the tamarind soak, move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":1,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":15,"flame":0}'),('63bcdc115080e23b965f709e','63bc142dad4ff98b5d931932',3,'P3 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Coconut milk fish curry, peel and slice 1/2 a cup of onions, wash and finely chop 1/2 a cup of tomatoes, wash and slit 2 green chillies, wash, peel and grate 1 inch of ginger, wash and pluck 10 curry leaves, peel and chop 3 cloves of garlic and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63bcdcf8524b9a351ee815f4','63bc142dad4ff98b5d931932',4,'M1 Fry the fish','To prepare the tempering for Coconut Milk Fish Curry, heat a pan and add 2 tablespoons of coconut oil and allow it to become hot. Then, arrange 400 gms of marinated fish pieces and allow them to cook on medium low flame for 3 minutes, next flip the pieces on the other side and allow them to cook for 3 minutes until they turn slightly brown. Then, remove the pieces from the plan and transfer it onto a plate and set aside. While the fish pieces are cooking move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":6,"flame":2}'),('63bcde0ccf7118db8864b17a','63bc142dad4ff98b5d931932',5,'M2 Prepare the Tempering','After the fish pieces have cooked for Coconut Milk Fish Curry, in the same pan add 1 teaspoon of mustard seeds, add 10 curry leaves, add 2 slit green chillies and stir fry it for a few seconds until the spices start to splutter. Next, add 1/2 a cup of sliced onion, and saute it on medium flame for 2 minutes until they become cooked and translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63bcdefbcf7118db8864b17b','63bc142dad4ff98b5d931932',6,'M3 Cook the tomatoes and masala','After cooking the onions for Coconut Milk Fish Curry, add 1 inch of grated ginger, and 3 cloves of chopped garlic and saute it for another minute until the onions turn slightly pink. Then, add 1/2 a cup of chopped tomatoes and saute it for 2 minutes on medium flame until it is cooked and becomes mushy. Next, add 1/2 a teaspoon of turmeric powder, add 1 teaspoon of salt, add 1/2 a teaspoon of black pepper powder, add 1 teaspoon of red chilli powder and mix it until well combined and allow it to cook for a minute.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('63bcdf935080e23b965f709f','63bc142dad4ff98b5d931932',7,'M4 Simmer the Curry','After cooking the masalas for Coconut Milk Fish Curry, lower the flame and add 1/2 a cup of water along with 1/2 a cup of coconut milk and and mix it well and bring the curry to boil on low flame. Next, add the shallow fried fish pieces and mix again. Then allow the curry to cook on medium low flame for 10 minutes. While the curry is simmering, move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":13,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":13,"flame":2}'),('63bce006524b9a351ee815f5','63bc142dad4ff98b5d931932',8,'M5 Continue to cook the curry and serve','After simmering the gravy for Coconut Milk Fish Curry, lower the flame and add 1 cup of thick coconut milk and squeeze 1 tablespoon of soaked tamarind using your fingers and allow the curry to cook for a minute on medium low flame. Continue to cook the curry on low flame until it comes to a gentle simmer. Then, turn off the flame, adjust the seasoning and serve hot with steamed rice.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":4,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":4,"flame":1}'),('63bd6181cf7118db8864b17e','63bcf871cf7118db8864b17c',1,'P1 Soak the rice','To soak rice for Mushroom Fried Rice, first, wash 1 cup of rice and transfer it in a mixing bowl along with 2 cups of water. Then, cover it with a lid and allow it to soak for 30 minutes. While the rice is soaking, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":30,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":30,"flame":0}'),('63bd6275524b9a351ee815f6','63bcf871cf7118db8864b17c',2,'P2 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Mushroom Fried Rice, wash 225 gms of mushrooms, trim the stems and cut them into medium sized slices; peel and finely chop 1/2 a cup of onions, wash, peel and finely chop 1 teaspoon of ginger, peel and finely chop 1 teaspoon of garlic. Then, wash a green bell pepper into half, remove the seeds and finely chop 1/4 cup of green bell pepper, wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of spring onions, wash and finely chop 0.5 tablespoon of celery and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63bd6b35cf7118db8864b17f','63bcf871cf7118db8864b17c',3,'P3 Cook the Rice','Next, to cook the rice for Mushroom Fried Rice, in a deep bottom pan add 3 cups of water and allow it to come to a rolling boil on high flame. When the water starts boiling add half a teaspoon of salt followed by 1 cup of soaked rice and stir it well. Then, then allow the rice to simmer and cook on medium flame for 7-8 minutes until it is 3/4th cooked. While the rice is cooking, move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":1,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":4}'),
('63bd6be4524b9a351ee815f7','63bcf871cf7118db8864b17c',4,'M1 Prepare the Tempering and stir fry the mushrooms','To prepare Mushroom fried rice, heat a wok and add 1 tablespoon of olive oil and allow it to become hot on high flame. Next, add 1 teaspoon of chopped garlic, add 1 teaspoon of chopped ginger, and saute it for a few seconds until the garlic turns brown. Then, add 1/2 a cup of chopped onions, and saute it on high flame for a few seconds until they turn slightly brown. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped green bell pepper followed by 225 gms of sliced mushrooms and continuously stir fry it for 2 minutes on high flame until the water from the mushrooms starts leaving out and evaporates.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":4}'),('63bd6ce4524b9a351ee815f8','63bcf871cf7118db8864b17c',5,'M2 Add the rice, season and serve','After the mushrooms are cooked for Mushroom Fried Rice, add the cooked rice into wok, add 1 teaspoon of soy sauce, add 1/2 a teaspoon of white vinegar, add 1/2 a teaspoon of black pepper powder, add 1/4 teaspoon of salt and mix it well on medium flame until the rice is evenly coated with soy sauce.  Then, add 0.5 tablespoon of finely chopped celery, add 1 tablespoon of finely chopped spring onions and mix again. Then, adjust the seasoning as per taste, turn off the flame, remove the fried rice in a serving bowl and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63bd7530524b9a351ee815fa','63bd7004524b9a351ee815f9',1,'P1 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Shahi mushroom, thoroughly wash 1.5 cups of mushrooms and trim the stem. Next, peel and finely slice 1/2 a cup of onions; wash and finely chop 1 cup of tomatoes, wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63bd75f25080e23b965f70a3','63bd7004524b9a351ee815f9',2,'P2 Saute the ingredients for the gravy','To prepare the gravy for Shahi Mushroom, heat a pan and add 1 tablespoon of oil and allow it to become hot. Then, add 0.5 cup of sliced onion and saute it on medium flame for 3 minutes until its cooked and golden brown. Next, break and add 3 kashmiri red chillies and saute it for a few seconds along with the onions. Then, add 1 tablespoon of cashew nuts and saute it for a minute until it becomes slightly golden brown. Then, turn off the flame, transfer the sauted mixture onto a plate and allow it to cool. While the sauted mixture cools, move onto the next step','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":3,"flame":2}'),('63bd77875080e23b965f70a4','63bd7004524b9a351ee815f9',3,'M1 Blend the gravy and prepare the tempering','Next, to prepare the gravy for Shahi Mushroom, in a mixy jar transfer the sauted mixture and leave out a tablespoon of the mixture for later use. Then close the lid of the mixy jar and blend it into a smooth puree. Next, to prepare the tempering, heat a pan and add 1 bay leaf, add 1/2 an inch of cinnamon, add 1 green cardamom pod, add 1 black cardamom pod, add 1 star anise and 3 black pepper corns. Then, add the prepared onion puree along with 1 tablespoon of ginger garlic paste and saute it on medium low flame for 2 minutes until the ginger garlic paste is cooked and the ingredients are well combined','cook_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),
('63bd78a4cf7118db8864b181','63bd7004524b9a351ee815f9',4,'M2 Cook the masalas','After cooking the masala for Shahi Mushroom, lower the flame and in the same pan add 1/2 a teaspoon of red chilli powder, add 1/2 a teaspoon of cumin powder, add 1/2 a teaspoon of garam masala, add 1/2 a teaspoon of turmeric powder followed by 1 cup of chopped tomatoes and saute it for 2 to 3 minutes on medium flame until the tomatoes are cooked and become mushy. Then, add a pinch of salt along with 1/2 a cup of water and mix it well. When the water starts to simmer, cover the pan with a lid allow it to simmer for 3 minutes on medium low flame.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":5,"flame":2}'),('63bd797fcf7118db8864b182','63bd7004524b9a351ee815f9',5,'M3 Cook the mushrooms','After simmering the gravy for Shahi Mushroom, gently open the lid and squish the tomatoes using the back of the ladle. Next, lower the flame and add 1/4 cup of coconut milk and mix it well. Then, turn off the flame and arrange 1.5 cups of whole mushrooms on the gravy, then turn on the flame on low, cover the pan with a lid and allow it to cook for 5 minutes. Stir the mushrooms occasionally with the gravy, to prevent it from sticking to the bottom and burning. While the mushrooms cook, move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":5,"flame":1}'),('63bd79ed524b9a351ee81600','63bd7004524b9a351ee815f9',6,'M4 Garnish and Serve','After the mushrooms have cooked for Shahi Mushroom, turn off the flame. Then, gently open the lid, garnish it with 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and the reserved onions and cashews and serve hot with steamed rice or paratha.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63bd7c9f5080e23b965f70a5','63bd7487cf7118db8864b180',1,'P1 Prep the ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Beans Poriyal, wash the beans, remove the fibres and finely chop 2 cups of beans; wash and slit 2 green chillies, wash and pluck 7 curry leaves, grate 2 tablespoons of coconut, thoroughly was 2 tablespoons of split chickpeas and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":13,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63bd7de4cf7118db8864b183','63bd7487cf7118db8864b180',2,'M1 Prepare the tempering','To prepare the tempering for Beans Poriyal, heat a pan and add 2 teaspoons of oil and allow it to become hot. Then, add 1/2 a teaspoon of mustard seeds, add 1/2 a teaspoon of cumin seeds, add 1/2 a teaspoon of white lentils followed by 7 curry leaves and 1 broken red chilli and saute it on medium low flame for half a minute until the spices crackle.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('63bd7f5e524b9a351ee81601','63bd7487cf7118db8864b180',3,'M2 Cook the beans','Next, for Beans Poriyal, add 2 cups of chopped beans to the tempering and and stir fry it for 2 minutes on medium flame. Then, add 2 tablespoons of washed split chickpeas and mix it well along with the beans and tempering. Next, add 2 slit green chillies and mix again. Then add 1 teaspoon of jaggery, add 1 teaspoon of salt, and mix well. Add 1/4 cup of water, and cover the pan with a lid and allow the beans to cook on low flame for 6 minutes. While the beans are cooking move onto the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":6,"flame":1}'),('63bd80e6524b9a351ee81602','63bd7487cf7118db8864b180',4,'M3 Season and serve','After the beans are cooked for Beans Poriyal, gently take off the lid and add 1/2 a teaspoon of turmeric powder, add 2 tablespoons of grated coconut and mix again. Then, squeeze half a teaspoon of lime and mix well. Turn off the flame, remove the cooked Beans Poriyal in a serving plate and serve hot with roti.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('63bd95accf7118db8864b185','63bd92f9cf7118db8864b184',1,'P1 Soak the Rice','To soak the rice for Paneer Pulao, first thoroughly wash 1 cup of basmati rice and transfer the washed rice into a mixing bowl along with 1.5 cups of water and allow it to soak for 20minutes. While the rice is soaking, move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":20,"flame":0}'),('63bd96f9cf7118db8864b186','63bd92f9cf7118db8864b184',2,'P2 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Paneer Pulao, cut 1 cup of paneer into medium sized cubes, then crumble 1/4 cup of paneer using your hands. Next, peel and slice 1/2 a cup of onions; wash and finely chop 1/2 a cup of tomatoes; wash, peel and finely chop 1 inch of ginger; peel and finely chop 2 cloves of garlic; wash and slit 1 green chilli; wash, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of carrots; wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":18,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63bd98a2524b9a351ee81603','63bd92f9cf7118db8864b184',3,'M1 Cook the rice','To cook the rice for paneer pulao, heat a deep bottom pan and add 4 cups of water in it along with 1 bay leaf, a teaspoon of salt, and a teaspoon of oil and bring to boil on high flame. Then, add 1 cup of soaked basmati rice and allow it to cook on medium flame for 12 to 15 minutes until the basmati rice is completely cooked. Then strain the rice using a colander, drain the water and set the cooked rice aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":18,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":18,"flame":0}'),
('63bd990e5080e23b965f70a7','63bd92f9cf7118db8864b184',4,'M2 Stir fry the paneer','Next, for Paneer Pulao, heat a pan and add 1 tablespoon of ghee and allow it to melt. Then, add 1 cup of medium chunks of paneer and stir fry it on medium flame for 4 minutes or until it becomes evenly brown from all sides. Then, take remove the browned paneer in a bowl and set aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63bd99accf7118db8864b187','63bd92f9cf7118db8864b184',5,'M3 Prepare the tempering','To prepare the tempering for Paneer Pulao, in the same pan add 1/2 a teaspoon of cumin seeds, add 1/2 an inch of cinnamon, add 3 cloves, add 1/2 a teaspoon of black peppercorns, and saute it on medium flame for a few seconds until it turns aromatic. Then, add 1/2 a cup of sliced onion, and saute it on medium low flame for 2 minutes until the onions are cooked and become translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63bd9a61cf7118db8864b188','63bd92f9cf7118db8864b184',6,'M4 Cook the vegetables','After the onions have cooked for Paneer Pulao, add 1 inch of chopped ginger, add 2 cloves of chopped garlic, add 1 slit green chilli and saute it for a minute on medium flame until the ginger and garlic are cooked and the raw smell goes. Then, add 1/2 a cup of chopped tomatoes, and saute it for 3 minutes on medium flame until it becomes soft and mushy. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped carrot, add 1/4 cup of peas, and saute it for a minute.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63bd9aed524b9a351ee81604','63bd92f9cf7118db8864b184',7,'M5 Prepare the pulao and serve','Next, for Paneer Pulao, to the vegetables add 1/2 a teaspoon of kashmiri red chilli powder, add 1/2 a teaspoon of garam masala, add 1 teaspoon of salt, and mix it well. Then, add 1/4 cup of crumbled paneer  and mix it well along with the vegetables. Then, add the cooked rice, and gently mix it with the vegetables and tempering. Next, top the rice with shallow fried paneer pieces, cover the pan with a lid, lower the flame and allow the rice to cook for another 5 minutes. The, turn off the flame, open the lid and remove the Paneer Pulao in a serving bowl, garnish it with 2 tablespoons of chopped coriander leaves and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":5,"flame":1}'),('63bda1d75080e23b965f70a9','63bda1585080e23b965f70a8',1,'P1 Prep the ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Phudina Chutney, wash and pluck half a bunch of mint leaves, peel 3 cloves of garlic.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('63bda2925080e23b965f70aa','63bda1585080e23b965f70a8',2,'M1 Saute the ingredients and blend the chutney','To prepare Phudina Chutney, heat a pan and add 1 tablespoon of oil and allow it to become hot.  Then, add 1/2 a tablespoon of chana dal, add half a tablespoon of white lentils, break and add 3 dried red chillies, add 3 peeled garlic cloves, and saute it on medium flame for a minute until the lentils become slightly golden brown. Next, add half a bunch of plucked mint leaves, add 1 teaspoon of tamarind, add 1/2 a teaspoon of salt, and saute it for 2 minutes on low flame until the mint leaves wilt and become cooked. Do not saute this on high flame as it can burn the mint leaves. Then turn off the flame, and allow the mixture to slightly cool. After the mixture has cooled, transfer it in a blender jar and blend it into a smooth chutney and serve with dosa.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":2,"flame":1}'),('63be25555a67b60f6d26f134','63be24bb524b9a351ee81605',1,'P1 Prep the ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Radish Paratha, first wash, peel and grate 3/4 cup of Radish using a grater. Then, in a mixing bowl add the grated radish along with 1/4 teaspoon of salt and set it aside for 10 minutes and allow the radish to leave out water. While the radish is set aside, wash and finely chop 1 green chilli; wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":10,"flame":0}'),('63be25facf7118db8864b18a','63be24bb524b9a351ee81605',2,'P2 Prepare the dough','To prepare the dough for Radish Paratha, in a mixing bowl add 1 cup of wheat flour, add 1/4 a teaspoon of salt, add 1/2 a teaspoon of carom seeds, add 1/2 a tablespoon of ghee, and gradually start to add water as and when required. Combine all the ingredients and knead the dough for 5 to 7 minutes until it becomes soft and non-sticky. Ensure not to add excess water, as the dough will become sticky. After kneading the dough, pour 1/2 a teaspoon of oil on top and grease it with your hands. Next, cover the dough with a cloth and allow it to rest for 15 minutes. While the dough rests, move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":15,"flame":0}'),('63be277ecf7118db8864b18b','63be24bb524b9a351ee81605',3,'P3 Prepare the Stuffing','To prepare the stuffing for Radish Paratha, first take the grated radish in batches and squeeze the radish between your palms to remove the excess water. Drain the water and transfer the squeezed radish in a mixing bowl. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of salt, add 1/2 a teaspoon of chilli powder, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, add 1 teaspoon of chilli flakes, add 1 teaspoon of cumin powder, add 1/2 a tablespoon of coriander powder add 1 chopped green chilli, add 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and mix it until well combined.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63be27c75a67b60f6d26f135','63be24bb524b9a351ee81605',4,'M1 Roll the parathas','To prepare the Radish Paratha, first, divide the prepared dough into small equal-sized balls. Next, take a dough ball and dust some flour over it. Then, roll it into a 3-inch circle. Place 1 tablespoon of the prepared radish stuffing and spread it across the rolled dough. Then, roll out another 3-inch circle and place it on top of the stuffing as shown, then gently seal the paratha using your fingers and continue rolling the stuffed paratha using a rolling pin and roll it out into a 6-inch disc. Ensure that the stuffing is evenly spread. Repeat the same for the remaining dough and stuffing.','cook_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('63be2819cf7118db8864b18c','63be24bb524b9a351ee81605',5,'M2 Roast the parathas','To roast the Radish Paratha, heat a tawa and transfer the rolled out paratha onto the tawa and cook it over medium flame for a minute. Next, flip the paratha on the other side and cook it until brown spots appear. Then, apply half a teaspoon of ghee on each side of the paratha and cook it for another 2-3 minutes, until it is evenly browned on both sides. After that, take it out onto a plate and serve. Repeat the same for the remaining parathas.','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63beec29ae1f412ac9428f3f','63be8b6dcf7118db8864b18e',1,'AP1 Soak the Dal','To soak the dal for Medu Vada, thoroughly rinse 3/4 cup of Urad Dal and transfer it into a mixing bowl along with 2 cups of water. Allow it to soak for 4 hours. While the dal is soaking, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":240,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63beedd3ae1f412ac9428f40','63be8b6dcf7118db8864b18e',2,'P1 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Medu Vada , wash and finely chop 1 teaspoon of green chillies, wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of curry leaves, wash peel and finely chop 3/4 tablespoon of ginger,  wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves, finely chop 1.5 tablespoons of coconut and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63beee6f4c40981f8958b5f7','63be8b6dcf7118db8864b18e',3,'M1 Prepare the Batter','To prepare the batter for Medu Vada, first, rinse the soaked urad dal well with water. Then, add it to a blender jar along with 1/4 cup of water, close the lid and blend it well into a smooth and thick batter. Transfer it into a mixing bowl, add 1 teaspoon of chopped green chilli, add 1 tablespoon of chopped curry leaves, add 3/4 tablespoon of chopped ginger, add 3/4 tablespoon of semolina, add 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves, add 1 teaspoon of salt, add 1.5 tablespoons of chopped coconut, and mix it until the ingredients are well combined.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63beeec1ae1f412ac9428f41','63be8b6dcf7118db8864b18e',4,'M2 Fry the Vadas','To fry the Medu Vadas, heat 1.5 cups of cooking oil in a Kadai over medium-high flame for 2-3 minutes. Next, slightly wet your palms and fingers, pull out a lemon sized ball and make a hole in the center using your thumb as shown, then shape it like a vada. Next, carefully drop it into the hot oil and deep fry it over medium flame for 4-5 minutes until it turns golden and crips. Then, take it out onto a plate and serve. Fry the remaining batter similarly.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":8,"flame":3}'),
('63bef07d4c40981f8958b5f8','63be8eca5a67b60f6d26f13a',1,'P1 Soak the Rice and prepare the paste','To soak the rice for Methi Pulao, thoroughly wash a cup of rice and transfer the washed rice in a mixing bowl along with 2 cups of water and allow it to soak for 20 minutes. While the rice is soaking, prepare the paste for the pulao. For that, peel 5 cloves of garlic, wash and peel 1 inch of ginger, peel and roughly chop 1 tablespoon of onions. Then in a mixy jar add 5 cloves of garlic, add 1 inch of ginger, add 2 green chillies, add 1 tablespoon of chopped onions, add 1/4 cup of water, and then close the lid of the mixy jar and blend it into a smooth paste.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":20,"flame":0}'),('63bef143ae1f412ac9428f42','63be8eca5a67b60f6d26f13a',2,'P2 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Methi Pulao, thorough wash fenugreek leaves, and finely chop 1.5 cups of fenugreek leaves ; the peel and slice 1 cup of onions; wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes; wash 1/2 a cup of green peas, and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":13,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63bef1f24c40981f8958b5fe','63be8eca5a67b60f6d26f13a',3,'M1 Prepare the Tempering','Next, to prepare Methi Pulao, in a pressure cooker pan add 1 tablespoon of ghee add 1/2 a tablespoon of oil, add 2 bay leaves, add 1/2 an inch of cinnamon, add 4 cloves, add 2 cardamoms, add 1 star anise and saute it well for a minute on medium flame until it crackles. Then add 1/2 a cup of sliced onions, and saute it on medium flame for 3 minutes until they become translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63bef2844c40981f8958b5ff','63be8eca5a67b60f6d26f13a',4,'M2 Cook the methi leaves','After cooking the onions for Methi Pulao, add 1/4 cup of chopped tomatoes and saute it for 2 minutes on medium flame until they become soft and mushy. Then add the prepared ginger chilly paste and mix it well. Next, add 1.5 cups of chopped methi leaves and stir fry it on high flame for 2 minutes until they are cooked and start to wilt. Then add 1/2 a cup of green peas and saute it for 2 minutes on medium flame until they become slightly soft.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63bef3104c40981f8958b600','63be8eca5a67b60f6d26f13a',5,'M3 Pressure cook the pulao and serve','After cooking the green peas for Methi Pulao, to the cooked vegetables add 1 teaspoon of red chilli powder, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, add 1.5 teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Next, add 1 cup of washed rice, and mix it well. Then add 1 tablespoon of mint leaves along with 2 cups of water , cover it with a lid and pressure cook the rice over a high flame until one whistle. After that, reduce the flame to low and continue to simmer it for another 8 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and set the pressure cooker aside. Allow the pressure from the cooker to release naturally. After the pressure cooker has released air, take off the lid, and gently mix the rice and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":16,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":16,"flame":3}'),
('63bef42e0a34f617d59f3a0f','63be9e91524b9a351ee81611',1,'AP1 Marinate the Chicken','To marinate the chicken for Butter Chicken, in a mixing bowl add 300 gms of chicken breasts, add 2 tablespoons of yogurt, add 1/2 a teaspoon of coriander powder, add 1 teaspoon of kashmiri chilli powder, add 1 teaspoon of ginger garlic paste, add 1/2 a teaspoon of garam masala powder, add 1 tablespoon of lemon juice, add 1/2 a teaspoon of salt and mix well using your fingers such that the chicken pieces are evenly coated in the marinade. Then allow the chicken to marinate in the refrigerator for three hours. While the chicken is marinating, move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":180,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63bef4970a34f617d59f3a10','63be9e91524b9a351ee81611',2,'P1 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Butter Chicken, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions; wash and finely chop 1/2 a cup of tomatoes; crumble 1 tablespoon of khoya; grate 2 tablespoons of processed cheese and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63bef4e94c40981f8958b601','63be9e91524b9a351ee81611',3,'M1 Grill the chicken','To grill the marinated Chicken for Butter Chicken, preheat the oven at 200 degrees C and line the baking tray with aluminuim foil. Then, arrange the marinated chicken on the baking tray and place the tray in the oven, and roast the chicken for 25 to 30 minutes until the chicken has become tender and is nicely browned. While the chicken is on roast in the oven, move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":30,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":30,"flame":0}'),('63bef591ae1f412ac9428f43','63be9e91524b9a351ee81611',4,'M2 Prepare the tempering','To prepare the gravy for Butter Chicken, in a deep bottom pan add 3 cups of water and allow it to come to a simmer on high flame, then add 10 cashewnuts, followed by 1/2 a cup of chopped tomatoes, 1/4 cup of chopped onions, 1 green cardamom, 1 black cardamom, 1/2 an inch of cinnamon stick, 1 clove, and 2 black peppercons and allow it to cook for 8 minutes on medium flame. While the tomato-onion mixture is simmering, move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":8,"flame":2}'),('63bef5ecae1f412ac9428f44','63be9e91524b9a351ee81611',5,'M3 Blend and sieve the puree','After the tomato onion mixture has simmered for Butter Chicken, drain the water and transfer the boiled ingredients into a mixy jar along with 1/4 cup of water and blend it into a smooth puree. Then, place a fine-mesh on top a mixing bowl and pass it through the mesh by pressing it with the back of the spoon. Discard the collected fibres and residue, and set the strained puree aside.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('63bef6540a34f617d59f3a11','63be9e91524b9a351ee81611',6,'M4 Cook the Gravy','Next to cook the gravy for Butter Chicken, heat a pan and add 1 tablespoon of butter on medium flame, add 1 teaspoon of kashmiri red chilli powder and saute it for a few seconds on low flame. Then, add the prepared puree and mix it well. Add 1/4 cup of water and mix again. Then, allow it to cook for 5 minutes on low flame. While the gravy is cooking, move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":5,"flame":2}'),('63bef6f04c40981f8958b602','63be9e91524b9a351ee81611',7,'M5 Simmer the gravy','After the gravy has cooked for Butter Chicken, add 1/4 teaspoon of salt, add 1 tablespoon of ketchup, add 1 tablespoon of crumbled khoya, add 2 tablespoons of grated cheese, add 2 tablespoons of heavy cream add 1 teaspoon of kasuri methi, add 1 tablespoon of honey add 1 tablespoon of lime juice and mix it well and allow it to cook for 3 minutes on low flame. While the gravy simmers, move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":3,"flame":1}'),('63bef7370a34f617d59f3a12','63be9e91524b9a351ee81611',8,'M6 Cook the chicken with the gravy','After the gravy has simmered for Butter Chicken, transfer the grilled chicken into the gravy and mix it well. Adjust the consistency of the gravy by adding water if needed, season with salt if required and continue to cook the chicken with gravy for 3 minutes on medium flame. Then, turn off the flame, transfer into a serving bowl and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":1,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":3,"flame":2}'),('63bef8b5ae1f412ac9428f45','63bea10d524b9a351ee81612',1,'P1 Marinate The Paneer','To marinate the paneer for Tawa Paneer, first cut 200 gms of paneer into medium sized chunks. Then, in a mixing bowl add 1/2 a cup of whisked curd, add 1 teaspoon of coriander powder, add 1/2 a teaspoon of turmeric powder, add 1 teaspoon of Kasmiri red chilli powder, add 1/2 a teaspoon of garam masala, add 1 teaspoon of ginger garlic paste, add 1 tablespoon of kasuri methi, add 1 teaspoon of salt and mix it well. Then add 1/2 a teaspoon of black pepper powder and mix again. Next, add 200 gms of paneer chunks and allow it to marinate for 20 minutes. While the paneer is marinating, move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":20,"flame":0}'),('63bef9050a34f617d59f3a13','63bea10d524b9a351ee81612',2,'P2 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Tawa Paneer, peel and finely chop 1/2 a cup of onions; wash and cut a green bell pepper into half remove the seeds and cut  1/2 a cup of green bell pepper into dices; wash and finely chop 1 green chilli and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('63bef95c0a34f617d59f3a14','63bea10d524b9a351ee81612',3,'M1 Cook the paneer','Next, for Tawa Paneer, heat a tawa and arrange the marinated paneer pieces, then lower the flame and pour the marinade on top of the arranged paneer pieces. Then continue flipping the paneer pieces every 3 minutes and allow it to cook on low flame for 15 minutes until it is evenly cooked from all sides. Keep scarping the marinade from the bottom of the pan to prevent it from burning. Then, turn off the flame, transfer the cooked paneer onto a plate and set aside. While the paneer is cooking, move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":15,"flame":1}'),('63bef9fc4c40981f8958b603','63bea10d524b9a351ee81612',4,'M2  Prepare the Tempering','To prepare the tempering for Tawa Paneer, heat a pan and add 1 tablespoon of oil and allow it to become hot. Then, add 1/2 a teaspoon of cumin seeds and allow it to crackle on medium flame. Then, add 1/2 a cup of chopped onion, and saute it on medium flame for a minute until it becomes translucent. Next, add 1 tablespoon of butter and allow it to melt, then add 1 chopped green chilli, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, add 1/4 teaspoon of Kashmiri red chilli powder and mix well.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63befa604c40981f8958b604','63bea10d524b9a351ee81612',5,'M3 Cook the paneer in the masala and serve','After cooking the masalas for for Tawa Paneer, add 1/2 a cup of green bell pepper dices, and saute it with the tempering for a minute on medium flame until it is slightly cooked. Do not overcook the green bell peppers as they should remain crunchy. Next, add 1/2 a teaspoon of cumin powder, add 1/4 teaspoon of salt and mix again. Now, add the pan fried paneer and mix it well with the tempering and saute it for a minute. Then, turn off the flame and serve hot as it is or with paratha.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63bfdb710a34f617d59f3a15','63bea403cf7118db8864b195',1,'P1 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Paneer Butter Masala, cut 250 gms of paneer into 1 inch cubes; peel and finely chop 1/2 a cup of onions; wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of tomatoes; wash, peel and finely chop 1/2 an inch of ginger; peel and finely chop 2 cloves of garlic; wash and slit one green chilli and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63bfdc024b5234e61d334999','63bea403cf7118db8864b195',2,'M1 Prepare the Tempering','To prepare the tempering for Paneer Butter Masala, heat a pan and add 1/4 tablespoon of vegetable oil and allow it to become hot. Then, add 1/2 a tablespoon of butter and allow it to melt on medium flame. Next, add 1 clove, add 1 black cardamom, add 1 green cardamom, and saute it for a few seconds on medium flame until the spices crackle. Next, add 1/2 a cup of chopped onions and saute it for 3 minutes until they become translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('63bfdc934b5234e61d33499a','63bea403cf7118db8864b195',3,'M2 Cook the tomatoes','Next for Paneer Butter Masala, add cup of chopped tomatoes, add 1/2 an inch of ginger, add 2 cloves of garlic, add 1 slit green chilli and saute it on medium flame for 3 minutes until the tomatoes become soft and mushy.  Then add 10 cashewnuts and saute and cook for another minute until the cashewnuts become slightly soft. Then, turn off the flame, set the mixture aside and allow it to cool.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":3,"flame":0}'),('63bfdd5f0a34f617d59f3a16','63bea403cf7118db8864b195',4,'M3 Prepare the gravy','After the mixture has cooled for Paneer Butter Masala, transfer it in a mixy jar, close the lid and blend it into a smooth puree. Then heat a pan and add 1/2 a tablespoon of butter, add the prepared puree, and saute it for a minute on medium flame. Next, add 1 teaspoon of coriander powder, add 1/2 a teaspoon of turmeric powder, add 1/2 a teaspoon of Kashmiri Red Chilli powder, add 1/4 cup of tomato puree, add 1/4 tablespoon of tomato ketchup, add 1/2 a teaspoon of salt and mix it until well combined. If the gravy feels very thick add 1/4 cup of water and adjust the consistency.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63bfddbfae1f412ac9428f46','63bea403cf7118db8864b195',5,'M4 Cook the paneer','Next, for Paneer Butter Masala, to the gravy add 250 gms of medium sized paneer chunks, and mix it well with the gravy such that the paneer pieces are evenly coated with the gravy and allow it to cook for 4 minutes on low flame. While the paneer cooks with the gravy, move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":1,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":4,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":4,"flame":1}'),('63bfde2a4b5234e61d33499b','63bea403cf7118db8864b195',6,'M5 Garnish and serve','When the gravy starts to simmer for Paneer Butter Masala, add 1/2 a teaspoon of garam masala, add 1 tablespoon of heavy cream, add 1 teaspoon of honey and 1 tablespoon of kasuri methi and mix again and cook for another minute on medium flame. Then turn off the flame, transfer the curry in a serving bowl and serve hot with jeera rice or paratha.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63c04d23f32103ff66f30812','63c01b5e0a34f617d59f3a1d',1,'P1 Prepare the tamarind pulp','To make tamarind pulp for Tomato Rasam, in a mixing bowl add 2 tablespoons of tamarind along with 1/2 a cup of water and allow it to soak for 15 minutes. After the tamarind soaks, transfer the soaked tamarind along with the water in a mixy jar, cover it with a lid and blend it into a smooth pulp. Then place a sieve on top of a mixing bowl and pass the soaked tamarind pulp through the sieve, and filter the fibres and seeds. Collect the filtered tamarind pulp and set aside. While the tamarind is soaking, move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":15,"flame":0}'),
('63c04dacf32103ff66f30813','63c01b5e0a34f617d59f3a1d',2,'P2 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Tomato Rasam, wash and roughly chop 250 gms of tomatoes, wash, peel and finely chop 1 inch of ginger, wash and finely chop 2 green chillies, wash and pluck 5 curry leaves and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63c04e4432db537915112b0a','63c01b5e0a34f617d59f3a1d',3,'M1 Cook the tomatoes','To prepare Tomato Rasam, heat a deep bottom pan and add 250 gms of roughly chopped tomatoes, add 2 cups of water, add the filtered tamarind pulp, and bring it to a rolling boil on medium flame. While the rasam is simmering add 2 chopped green chillies, add 1 inch of chopped ginger, 2 tablespoons of chopped coriander leaves, add 1 teaspoon of black salt and mix it well. Then add 5 curry leaves, cover the pan with a lid and allow it to cook for 10 minutes on low flame. While the tomatoes are cooking, move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":13,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":13,"flame":1}'),('63c04ec24b5234e61d3349a3','63c01b5e0a34f617d59f3a1d',4,'M2 Cook the tomato puree','After the tomatoes are cooked for Tomato Rasam, turn off the flame and allow the tomato mixture to slightly cool. After the tomatoes cool, transfer the cooked tomatoes into the blender jar, close the lid and blend it into a smooth puree. Next, transfer the prepared tomato puree into a deep bottom pan and add 2 cups of water and mix it well. Allow the rasam to simmer and come to a rolling boil on medium flame. Then add 1.5 tablespoons of rasam powder, and allow it to cook on low flame for 10 minutes. While the rasam is boiling move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":15,"flame":1}'),('63c04f6832db537915112b0b','63c01b5e0a34f617d59f3a1d',5,'M3 Add the tempering and serve','To prepare the tempering for Tomato Rasam, heat a tadka pan and add 1 tablespoon of oil and allow it to become hot. Then add 2 dried red chillies, add 5 curry leaves, add 1/4 teaspoon of asefoeitida, add 1 teaspoon of mustard seeds and allow the spices to crackle on medium flame. Then turn off the flame, and pour the tempering over the boiling rasam. Then turn off the flame, remove the rasam in a serving bowl and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63c05060f32103ff66f30814','63c00f8cae1f412ac9428f4b',1,'P1 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Onion Rava Dosa, wash and finely chop 1/4 teaspoon of chopped green chillies, wash, peel and grate 1/2 an inch of ginger, wash and finely chop 8 curry leaves, wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves, peel and finely chop 1/4 cup of onions and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('63c050fc4b5234e61d3349a4','63c00f8cae1f412ac9428f4b',2,'P2 Prepare the batter','To prepare the batter for Onion Rava Dosa, in a mixing bowl add 1/2 a cup of semolina, add 1 tablespoon of rice flour, add 1 tablespoon of all purpose flour, add 1/2 a teaspoon of salt, add 1/4 teaspoon of cumin seeds add 1/4 teaspoon of crushed black peppercorns, and mix it well using a whisk. Next, add 2 cups of water and mix it again.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63c051734b5234e61d3349a5','63c00f8cae1f412ac9428f4b',3,'P3 Rest the batter','After mixing the flour for Onion Rava Dosa, in the same bowl add 1/4 teaspoon of chopped green chillies, add 1/2 an inch of grated ginger, add 8 chopped curry leaves, add 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves, add 1/4 cup of chopped onions, and mix it well. If the batter seems too thick, add in 1/2 a cup of water to achieve a flowing consistency. Next, allow it to rest for 15mins. While the batter is resting, move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":5,"flame":0}'),('63c051be4b5234e61d3349a6','63c00f8cae1f412ac9428f4b',4,'M1 Prepare the Dosas','To prepare Onion Rava Dosa, heat a tawa and grease it with a teaspoon of oil. Next, pour a ladle full of the batter over the hot Tawa as shown, and pour a teaspoon of oil on top. Then, cover the pan with a lid and cook it over medium flame for 2-3 minutes until it turns golden and crisp. Then, open the lid and start to scrape the dosa from the sides and fold the dosa and transfer it onto a plate. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63c0525632db537915112b0c','63bffe8dae1f412ac9428f49',1,'AP1 Soak the peanuts','To prepare Groundnut Sundal, in a mixing bowl add 2 cups of peanuts along with 2 cups of water and rinse it well, then drain the water. Next, cover the pan with a lid and allow it to rest overnight. While the peanuts are soaking, move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":480,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63c052b04b5234e61d3349a7','63bffe8dae1f412ac9428f49',2,'P1 Pressure cook the peanuts','To pressure cook the peanuts for Groundnut Sundal, heat a pressure cooker and add 2 cups of soaked peanuts and water if necessary. Then, cover the pressure cooker with a lid and pressure cook the peanuts for 4 whistles on high flame, then reduce the flame to low and allow it to simmer on low flame for another 5 minutes. Then turn off the flame, and allow the pressure to release naturally and cool.  While the peanuts are cooking move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":20,"flame":4}'),
('63c0530bf32103ff66f30815','63bffe8dae1f412ac9428f49',3,'P2 Prep the ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Groundnut Sundal, grate 4 tablespoons of coconut, wash and finely chop 12 curry leaves, after the pressure cooker has cooled, drain the water and set the boiled peanuts aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63c0539df32103ff66f30816','63bffe8dae1f412ac9428f49',4,'M1 Prepare the Sundal','To make Groundnut Sundal, heat a pan and add 1 tablespoon of oil and allow it to become hot. Then, add 1 teaspoon of mustard seeds and allow it to splutter, next, break and add 3 red chillies, 1/2 a teaspoon of hingh, add the boiled peanuts, add 1 teaspoon of salt, and saute it for 2 minutes on medium flame. Then, lower the flame and add 4 tablespoons of grated coconut add 12 chopped curry leaves, and mix again. Then, turn off the flame, remove the Groundnut sundal in a serving bowl and serve','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63c0a49932db537915112b0d','63bffbfc0a34f617d59f3a1b',1,'AP1 Soak the Green Peas','To soak the dry green peas for Green Peas Sundal , in a mixing bowl add 1 cup of dry green peas along with 2 cups of water and and rinse it well, then discard the water. Add 2 cups of fresh water to the dried green peas and allow it to soak overnight. While the peas are soaking, move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":480,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63c0a51df32103ff66f3081c','63bffbfc0a34f617d59f3a1b',2,'P1 Pressure Cook the Green Peas and prep the Ingredients','To pressure cook the green peas for Green Peas Sundal, trasnfer the soaked green peas in a pressure cooker along with 2 cups of water, then cover the pressure cooker with a lid and pressure cook the green peas for 4 whistles on high flame, then reduce the flame to low and allow it to simmer on low flame for another 5 minutes. Then turn off the flame, and allow the pressure to release naturally and cool.  While the green peas are cooking, grate 2 tablespoons of coconut, wash and slit 1 green chilli, wash and pluck, 5 curry leaves and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":20,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":20,"flame":4}'),('63c0a5c732db537915112b0e','63bffbfc0a34f617d59f3a1b',3,'M1 Prepare the Tempering','To prepare the tempering for Green Peas Sundal, heat a pan and add 1/2 a tablespoon of oil and allow it to become hot. Next, add 1/4 teaspoon of mustard seeds, add 1/4 teaspoon of cumin seeds, add 1 slit green chilli, break and add 1 dried red chilli and saute it for a few seconds on medium flame until the spices crackle. Then add 5 curry leaves and allow it to splutter. Next, add the boiled green peas and mix it along with the tempering. Then add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, add 1/2 a teaspoon of salt and mix it well.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('63c0a6754b5234e61d3349a8','63bffbfc0a34f617d59f3a1b',4,'M2 Cook the green peas and serve','Next, for Green Peas Sundal, cover the pan with a lid and allow the green peas to cook on low flame for 2 minutes. After 2 minutes, open the lid add 1 tablespoon of lemon juice, add 2 tablespoons of grated coconut and mix it until well combined.  Saute it for a minute, then turn off the flame and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":2,"flame":2}'),('63c0a7a632db537915112b0f','63bff97b4b5234e61d33499d',1,'P1 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Coriander Chutney, thoroughly wash and roughly chop 1 cup of coriander leaves; peel and wash 4 pearl onions, wash 4 green chillies, wash and peel half an inch of ginger, peel 3 cloves of garlic, wash 5 curry leaves, grate 1/4 cup of coconut and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":16,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63c0a858f32103ff66f3081d','63bff97b4b5234e61d33499d',2,'M1 Saute the coriander leaves','To prepare the Coriander Chutney, heat a kadai and add 1 tablespoon of oil and allow it to become hot. Then, add 1 1/4 teaspoon of cumin seeds, add 1.5 teaspoon of urad dal, add 4 chopped shallots, and stir fry it on medium flame for half a minute until it becomes slightly golden brown. Then lower the flame and add 4 green chillies, add 6 cloves of garlic, add 1/2 an inch of ginger and saute it for 2 to 3 minutes until they are cooked and the raw smell goes.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63c0a8daf32103ff66f3081e','63bff97b4b5234e61d33499d',3,'M2 Blend into a chutney','Next, for Coriander Chutney after the ginger and garlic is cooked, add 5 curry leaves, add 1 teaspoon of tamarind, add 1/2 a cup of grated coconut and mix it well. Next, add 1 cup of chopped coriander leaves, and mix it well on low flame until the coriander leaves wilt. Then add 1/4 teaspoon of salt and mix again. Then allow it to slightly cool. After the mixture cools, transfer it into a blender jar and blend it into a smooth chutney.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":3,"flame":0}'),('63c0a9c74b5234e61d3349a9','63bff655ae1f412ac9428f47',1,'AP1 Soak the dals and Rice','To prepare the batter for Adai, in a mixing bowl add 1/2 a cup of raw rice, add 1/4 cup of toor dal, add 1/4 cup of chana dal, add 1/4 cup of urad dal, add 1/4 cup of moong dal and add 3 cups of water and rinse it well and drain the water. Then, add 3 cups of fresh water, cover the bowl with a lid and allow it to soak for 2 hours. While the lentils are soaking, move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":120,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('63c0a9f9f32103ff66f3081f','63bff655ae1f412ac9428f47',2,'P1 Prep the Ingredients and blend the dals','To prep the ingredients for Adai, wash 1 green chilli, grate 1/4 cup of coconut, wash and finely chop 1/4 cup of coriander leaves. Next, to blend the batter for Adai, transfer the soaked rice and lentils to a mixy jar along with 1/4 cup of water and blend it into a grainy paste. Do not add excess water as we want the batter to be slightly thick. Then transfer the blended batter into a mixing bowl and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63c0ab5532db537915112b10','63bff655ae1f412ac9428f47',3,'P2 Prepare the Batter','Next, to prepare the chilli paste for Adai, in a mixy jar add 2 dried red chillies, add 1 green chilli, add 1/2 a teaspoon of black peppercorns and blend it into a coarse powder and add it to the batter. Next, to the batter add 1/4 cup of grated coconut, add 1/4 cup of chopped coriander leaves, add 1/4 teaspoon of asefoeitida, add 1/4 teaspoon of cumin seeds, add 1/4 teaspoon of salt and mix it until the ingredients are well combined. If the batter feels too thick, add 3 tablespoons of water and mix well.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63c0ac2cf32103ff66f30820','63bff655ae1f412ac9428f47',4,'M1 Cook the Adai','To make Adai, pour a ladle full of the prepared adai batter over a hot tawa and spread it into a thick round circle. Add a teaspoon of cooking oil and cover the dosa with a lid and cook it over medium flame for 2minutes. Then, remove the lid and flip the adai on the other side and cook for another minute until it slightly turns golden brown. Then, carefully take it out onto a plate. Serve.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63c4ae4f4b5234e61d3349b4','63c4a23a47f2302e2ba964ad',1,'P1 Soak the rice','To soak rice for Schezwan Egg Fried Rice, first, wash 1 cup of basmati rice and transfer it in a mixing bowl along with 2 cups of water. Then, cover it with a lid and allow it to soak for 30 minutes. While the rice is soaking, please move on to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":30,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":30,"flame":0}'),('63c4af0b47f2302e2ba964ae','63c4a23a47f2302e2ba964ad',2,'P2 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Schezwan Egg Fried Rice, peel and slice two cloves of garlic, wash and slit one green chilli, peel and slice 1 cup of onion, wash and cut a red bell pepper into half, remove the seeds and slice 1/2 a cup of red bell peppers; wash and cut a green bell pepper into half, remove the seeds and slice 1/2 a cup of green bell peppers ; wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of spring onions, wash and slice 1/4 cup of cabbage and set aside. Then, in a mixing bowl, crack 2 eggs and whisk it using a fork or until it becomes light and fluffy.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('63c4af634b5234e61d3349b5','63c4a23a47f2302e2ba964ad',3,'P3 Cook the Rice','Next, to cook the rice for Schezwan Egg Fried Rice, in a deep bottom pan add 3 cups of water and allow it to come to a rolling boil on high flame. When the water starts boiling add half a teaspoon of salt followed by 1 cup of soaked rice and stir it well. Then, then allow the rice to simmer and cook on medium flame for 7-8 minutes until it is 3/4th cooked. While the rice is cooking, move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":1,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":13,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":13,"flame":3}'),('63c4afc947f2302e2ba964af','63c4a23a47f2302e2ba964ad',4,'M1 Prepare the tempering','To prepare Schezwan Egg Fried Rice, heat a pan and add 1/2 a tablespoon of oil and allow it to become hot. Then, add two cloves of sliced garlic, and saute it on medium flame for a few seconds. Next, add 2 slit green chilies, add 1 cup of sliced onion, add 1 schezwan peppercorn, and saute the onions on medium flame for 2 minutes until the onions becomes translucent.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63c4b08f4b5234e61d3349b6','63c4a23a47f2302e2ba964ad',5,'M2 Cook the vegetables','Next, for Schezwan Egg Fried Rice, add 3/4 teaspoon of vinegar, add 3/4 teaspoon of red chilli paste and mix it well. Next, add 1 teaspoon of soy sauce, add 1/2 a teaspoon of brown sugar and mix again. Then add 1 tablespoon of chopped spring onions, add 1/2 a cup of sliced red bell pepper, add  1/2 a cup of sliced green bell pepper, add 1/4 cup of shredded cabbage and saute it well on medium flame for 3 to 4 minutes until they are slightly cooked.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('63c4b10c4b5234e61d3349b7','63c4a23a47f2302e2ba964ad',6,'M3 Cook the rice with vegetables','After the vegetables are cooked for Schezwan Egg Fried Rice, pour the beaten egg and saute it well until it gets scrambled and cooked. Then add 1 cup of cooked basmati rice, add 1 teaspoon of salt, add 1/2 a teaspoon of black pepper powder, and stir fry the vegetables and rice for 2 minutes until well combined with the seasoning. Then, turn off the flame, transfer the Schezwan Egg Fried Rice into a serving bowl and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":3}'),('63c4b20247f2302e2ba964b0','63c4a48d9104c067b04761dd',1,'P1 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Egg Drop Soup, wash and finely chop 1 green chilli; then in a small jar crack 1 egg, and beat it well and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('63c4b2a047f2302e2ba964b1','63c4a48d9104c067b04761dd',2,'M1 Prepare the Stock','To prepare the stock for Egg Drop Soup, in a deep bottom pan add 2 cups of water, add 1 chicken stock cube, add 3/4 teaspoon of soy sauce, add 3/4 teaspoon of tomato puree, add 3/4 teaspoon of garlic paste, add 1 teaspoon of ginger paste add 2 teaspoons of salt and mix it until well combined. Then allow the stock to simmer for 5minutes on medium low flame and allow it come to a rolling boil.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":7,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":7,"flame":1}'),('63c4b2f747f2302e2ba964b2','63c4a48d9104c067b04761dd',3,'M2 Simmer the Soup','To prepare the corn flour slurry for Egg Drop Soup, in a mixing bowl add 1.5 tablespoon of corn flour, add 2 tablespoons of water, and mix it well using a spoon. Ensure there are no lumps, break the lumps with the back of the spoon if any. Then, pour the corn flour slurry into the boiling stock and allow it to cook for 5 minutes until the soup slightly thickens. While the soup is boiling move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":1,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":5,"flame":0}'),('63c4b35b47f2302e2ba964b3','63c4a48d9104c067b04761dd',4,'M3 Pour the egg and simmer again','Next, when the Egg Drop soup is boiling, pour the whisked egg from top and continue stirring the soup with a ladle to form egg threads. Do not pour the entire beaten egg mix at once, gradually pour the mix in intervals and continue to stir the soup with the ladle. Then season the soup with 1/2 a teaspoon of pepper powder, and continue to simmer the soup on medium flame for 5 minutes. Then turn off the flame, transfer the Egg Drop Soup into a serving bowl. Top it with 1 teaspoon of chopped green chillies and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":5,"flame":3}'),('63c4b3f39104c067b04761df','63c4a8064b5234e61d3349b2',1,'P1 Boil the potatoes','To boil the potatoes for Potato Mayo Salad, peel, wash and cut 4 potatoes into medium sized chunks. Ensure to keep the size of the potato cubes same so they cook evenly. Next, to boil the potatoes in a deep bottom pan, add 3 cups of water and transfer the potato cubes along with 2 teaspoons of salt and cook it on medium low flame for 10 minutes until it comes to a rolling boil on low medium heat. After the potatoes have boiled, turn off the flame insert a fork in one of the potatoes and check if they are cooked. Then, drain the water and allow the boiled potatoes to completely cool. While the potatoes are boiling move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":10,"flame":2}'),('63c4b46a47f2302e2ba964b4','63c4a8064b5234e61d3349b2',2,'P2 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Potato Mayo Salad, wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of spring onions, wash and finely chop 2 teaspoons of parsley, wash and finely chop 1 teaspoon of dill leaves and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('63c4b4ea4b5234e61d3349b8','63c4a8064b5234e61d3349b2',3,'M1 Assemble the salad','To prepare the Potato Mayo Salad, after the potatoes have completely cooled, transfer them in a large mixing bowl, then add 1 tablespoon of chopped spring onions, add 2 teaspoons of chopped parsley, add 1 teaspoon of black pepper powder, add 1/4 cup of mayonnaise, and toss the salad until all the ingredients are mixed well. Then garnish the salad with 1 teaspoon of dill leaves and serve chilled.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63c4b59647f2302e2ba964b5','63c4ab184b5234e61d3349b3',1,'P1 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Chicken Manchurian in a mixing bowl add 1 tablespoon of corn flour along with 2 tablespoons of water and mix well to form a slurry. Next, wash and finely chop spring 3/4 cup of spring onion, wash, peel and finely chop 2 teaspoons ginger; wash and finely 1 chop green chilli.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63c4b64e9104c067b04761e0','63c4ab184b5234e61d3349b3',2,'P2 Prepare the Dough','To prepare the dough for Chicken Manchurian, in a mixing bowl add 300 gms of minced chicken, add 1/4 cup of chopped spring onion greens, add 1/2 a teaspoon of salt, add 1/2 a teaspoon of pepper powder, add 2 teaspoons of chilli paste, add 1 teaspoon of Soy sauce, add 1 teaspoon of ginger garlic paste, add 2 tablespoons of corn flour, add 2 tablespoons of all purpose flour, and mix all the ingredients well using your hands.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63c4b6dd47f2302e2ba964b6','63c4ab184b5234e61d3349b3',3,'P3 Fry the Shaped Balls','To fry the balls for Chicken Manchurian, in a kadai add 1 cup of oil and allow it to become hot on medium flame for 3 minutes. While the oil becomes hot, grease your palms and hands with a teaspoon of oil and portion the dough into equal lemon sized balls. Then, drop the balls into hot oil and fry them for 8 minutes until they becomes crisp and slightly golden brown.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":12,"flame":3}'),('63c4b75847f2302e2ba964b7','63c4ab184b5234e61d3349b3',4,'M1 Prepare the Gravy','To prepare the gravy for Chicken Manchuruan, heat a pan and add 2 teaspoons of oil, add 2 teaspoons of chopped ginger, and saute it over medium flame for a minute. Then add 1.5 tablespoons of chopped garlic and saute it for another minute. Next, add 1 tablespoon of chopped spring onions, add 1 teaspoon of chopped green chillies, and saute it for a minute on medium low flame.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),
('63c4b7eb4b5234e61d3349b9','63c4ab184b5234e61d3349b3',5,'M2 Simmer the Gravy','Next, for Chicken Manchurian, in the same pan add 1.5 teaspoons of chilli paste, add 1 tablespoon of soy sauce, add 1.5 teaspoons of vinegar, add 400 ml of water, and mix it well with the sauces and ingredients. Then add 1 teaspoon of salt, add 1/4 teaspoon of pepper powder, add the prepared corn flour slurry and mix well. Then, allow the gravy to simmer on medium low flame for 4 minutes until it starts boiling and it becomes slightly thick. While the gravy is simmering move onto the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":4,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":4,"flame":2}'),('63c4b81e4b5234e61d3349ba','63c4ab184b5234e61d3349b3',6,'M3 Cook the Chicken balls in the Gravy','After the gravy has come to a boil, add the fried manchurian balls and cook it for another 7 minutes on low flame. Then turn off the flame, mix the manchurian, transfer it into a mixing bowl and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":1,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":7,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":7,"flame":1}'),('63c4b9399104c067b04761e1','63c4ade89104c067b04761de',1,'P1 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Dragon Chicken, wash and pat dry 250 gms of chicken. Place the chicken breast on a chopping board and cut them into medium length strips. Then in a mixing bowl crack 1 egg and whisk it until well combined. Next, peel and finely chop 1 tablespoon of garlic cloves, wash and finely slice 1/4 cup of spring onion whites, wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of spring onion greens. Next, wash and cut a red bell pepper into half, remove the seeds and slice 1/4 a cup of green bell peppers; wash and cut a red bell pepper into half, remove the seeds and slice 1/2 a cup of red bell peppers; wash and cut a yellow bell pepper into half, remove the seeds and slice 1/4 cup of yellow bell peppers.','prep_method','{"active_time":20,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63c4b9e89104c067b04761e2','63c4ade89104c067b04761de',2,'P2 Marinate the Chicken','To marinate the chicken for Dragon Chicken, in a mixing bowl add 250 gms of chicken strips, add 1 tablespoon of ginger garlic paste, add 1/2 a teaspoon of salt, add 1 teaspoon of black pepper powder, add 1/2 a tablespoon of soy sauce, add 1 teaspoon of vinegar, add 1 whisked egg and mix it until well combined with other ingredients. Then, add 1 tablespoon of corn flour, add 1.5 tablespoon of all purpose flour, and mix again until the chicken strips are evenly coated with the marinade.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63c4ba304b5234e61d3349bb','63c4ade89104c067b04761de',3,'P3 Fry the Marinated Chicken','To fry the marinated chicken, heat a frying pan and add 1/2 a cup of oil and allow it to become hot on high flame. Then, lower the flame and carefully place the marinated chicken strips one by one without crowding the pan. Then fry the chicken strips for 3 minutes until it is cooked and becomes golden brown. Strain the fried chicken using a skimmer and set aside. Repeat the same for the remaining strips','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":3,"flame":3}'),
('63c4ba9e47f2302e2ba964b8','63c4ade89104c067b04761de',4,'M1 Prepare the Tempering','To prepare Dragon Chicken, heat 2 tablespoons of oil and allow it to become hot. Then, add 10 cashewnuts, add 3-4 dried red chillies, and saute it on medium flame for a few seconds until the chillies crackle and the cashews become slightly golden brown. Next, add 1 tablespoon of chopped garlic cloves and saute it for a minute until it becomes brown.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63c4bb3e9104c067b04761e3','63c4ade89104c067b04761de',5,'M2 Add the vegetables and cook the sauces','Next, for Dragon Chicken, add 1/4 cup of sliced spring onion whites, add 1/2 a cup of sliced green capsicum, add 1/4 cup of sliced red capsicum, add 1/4 cup of sliced yellow capsicum, and saute it on medium flame until it becomes translucent and cooked. Do not overcook the vegetables as they need to be slightly crunchy. Then, add 1 tablespoon of soy sauce, add 2 tablespoons of of tomato kethchup, add 1 tablespoon of chilli sauce, and mix it well along with the vegetables.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63c4bb929104c067b04761e4','63c4ade89104c067b04761de',6,'M3 Toss the fried chicken with the vegetables and sauces','Then for Dragon Chicken, add 3 tablespoons of water, add 1/2 a teaspoon of pepper powder, add 1/2 a teaspoon of sugar, add some salt to taste and mix it well. Next, add the fried chicken strips, and stir fry it with the vegetables and sauce for 2 minutes on medium flame until it is evenly coated. Then turn off the flame, garnish it with a tablespoon of chopped spring onion greens and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63db50d51dd878ea6301a0ab','63db50020e9d976b9be59476',1,'P1 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Pumpkin Poriyal, wash and pluck 7 curry leaves, wash and slit one green chilli; wash and peel the pumpkin and remove the seeds. Then cut 250 grams of yellow pumpkin into medium sized cubes; wash and grate 2 tablespoons of coconut; wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63db51c4db77c073468a83c3','63db50020e9d976b9be59476',2,'M1 Prepare the tempering','To prepare the tempering for Pumpkin Poriyal, heat a pan and add 1 tablespoon of cooking oil and allow it to become hot. Then, add 1 teaspoon of mustard seeds followed by 1/2 a teaspoon of urad dal and allow it to crackle on low flame. Then add 7 curry leaves and 1/4 teaspoon of asafoetida, saute it and allow it to crackle. Next, add 1 broken red red chilli, add 1 slit green chilli and saute it on low flame along with the tempering.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),
('63db53181dd878ea6301a0ac','63db50020e9d976b9be59476',3,'M2 Cook the pumpkin','Next, for Pumpkin Poriyal, to the tempering add 250 gms of pumpkin cubes, add 1/2 a teaspoon of turmeric powder, add 1/2 a teaspoon of red chilli powder and saute it on medium flame until well combined. Next add 1/4 cup of water, cover the pan with a lid and allow it to cook on low flame for ten minutes until it becomes tender. Keep stirring the pumpkins occasionally to prevent it from sticking to the pan and burning.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":10,"flame":1}'),('63db53851dd878ea6301a0ad','63db50020e9d976b9be59476',4,'M3 Add the coconut and serve','After the pumpkin is cooked for Pumpkin Poriyal, add 2 tablespoons of grated coconut and mix well. Then add 1/2 a teaspoon of jaggery and mix until well combined. Then turn off the flame, garnish it with chopped coriander leaves and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63db6bb40e9d976b9be5947b','63db601ddb77c073468a83c5',1,'P1 Prep the ingredients and combine the dough','To prep the ingredients for Cabbage Thepla, wash grate 1 cup of cabbage; wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves; wash and finely chop 1/2 a teaspoon of green chilli; wash, peel and grate 1 teaspoon of ginger and set aside. To prepare the dough for Cabbage Thepla, in a mixing bowl add 2 cups of wheat flour, 1/2 a teaspoon of turmeric powder, add 1/2 a teaspoon of red chilli powder, add 1/2 a teaspoon of garam masala, add 1 teaspoon of cumin powder, add 1/2 a teaspoon of coriander powder, add 1/2 a teaspoon of green chilli, add 1 teaspoon of grated ginger, add 1 teaspoon of cumin seeds, add salt to taste, add 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves, add 1/8 teaspoon of asafoetida, 2 teaspoons of oil and mix it well using your hands until well combined.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63db737b0e9d976b9be5947c','63db601ddb77c073468a83c5',2,'P2 Knead and rest the dough','After the flour and spices are well combined for Cabbage Thepla, add 1 cup of grated cabbage and combine mix well with the combined ingredients, The dough will result in a dry and crumbly mixture. Add required amount of water at this point and knead for 5 minutes into a soft dough. Then grease your hands with 1 teaspoon of oil and knead again. Then cover the bowl with a lid and allow the dough to rest for 10 minutes. While the dough rests move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":10,"flame":0}'),('63db740ddb77c073468a83c7','63db601ddb77c073468a83c5',3,'M1 Roll out the Theplas','After resting the dough for Cabbage Thepla, dust some wheat flour on the dough and knead it again. Then pinch small lemon sized balls from the dough and roll them into a round ball. Next, take a rolled dough ball, slightLy flatten it with your palm on a rolling board, and dust it with flour. Then, using a rolling pin evenly roll the dough into a disk shape, allowing it to remain slightly thick. Repeat this process with the remaining dough and move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('63db745f0e9d976b9be5947d','63db601ddb77c073468a83c5',4,'M2 Roast the Theplas','To roast the Cabbage Thepla, heat a tawa on medium flame for 1 min. Transfer the rolled thepla onto a tawa and allow it to cook on medium low flame until brown spots appear, then spread 1/2 a teaspoon of oil and flip it on the other side, spread another 1/2 teaspoon of oil and allow it to cook on medium flame until it turns golden brown. Continue to flip the paratha and cook until it is evenly browned. Once it is evenly cooked on both sides , take them off the tawa and serve hot. Repeat this with the remaining dough balls.','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63db8b900e9d976b9be5947f','63db8ac31dd878ea6301a0b2',1,'P1 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Carrot Soup, wash, peel and cut 4 carrots; peel and slice 1 onion; peel 3 garlic cloves; wash, peel and grate 2 teaspoons of ginger; wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of ginger and set aside','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63db8cfb1dd878ea6301a0b4','63db8ac31dd878ea6301a0b2',2,'M1 Saute the vegetables','To prepare Carrot Soup, heat a deep bottom pan and add 1 tablespoon of cooking oil and allow it to become hot. Then, add 1 sliced onion, 4 chopped carrots and saute it for 6 minutes on medium low flame until the onions become translucent. Then, add 3 garlic cloves along with 2 teaspoons of chopped ginger and saute it for 2 minutes.','cook_method','{"active_time":9,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),('63db8dc41dd878ea6301a0b5','63db8ac31dd878ea6301a0b2',3,'M2 Blend, simmer and season the soup','Next, for Carrot Soup, add 2 cups of water along with 1.5 packets of vegetable stock and allow the cube to dissolve, then add 1 cup of water, 1 teaspoon of salt followed by 1/2 a teaspoon of black pepper powder. Then, close the pan with a lid and allow it to cook for 30 minutes on medium low flame until the carrot is cooked and turns soft. Next, allow the cooked vegetables to slightly cool. Then, using a hand blender, blend the cooked vegetables into a smooth puree. Then, heat the soup, add water as per desired consistency, add 1 tablespoon of apple cider vinegar and mix well. Allow the soup to simmer for 2 minutes, then turn off the flame, garnish it with a tablespoon of cream and 1 teaspoon of pumpkin seeds and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":32,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":32,"flame":2}'),('63db95b31dd878ea6301a0be','63db92280e9d976b9be59483',1,'P1 Clean the Cauliflower','To clean the cauliflower for Gobi Matar Sabzi, first in a deep bottom pan add 3 cups of water along with 1 teaspoon of salt and allow it to come to a rolling boil. While the water boils, wash and cut a small cauliflower into florets, then drop them in the boiling water and allow it to cook for 2 minutes. Then turn off the flame and strain the cleaned and cooked cauliflower using a colander and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":5,"flame":2}'),
('63db96680e9d976b9be59486','63db92280e9d976b9be59483',2,'P2 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Gobi Matar Sabzi, peel and slice 1/2 a cup onions; wash and finely chop 1 cup of tomatoes; thoroughly wash and finely chop 1/2 a cup of fenugreek leaves; wash 1/4 cup of green peas; wash, peel and cut 1/4 cup of potatoes into medium sized cubes.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63db97310e9d976b9be59487','63db92280e9d976b9be59483',3,'M1 Prepare the Tempering','To prepare the tempering for Gobi Matar Sabzi, heat a pan and add 1 tablespoon of cooking oil and allow it to become hot. Then add 1 teaspoon of cumin seeds, saute it on low flame and allow it to crackle. Next, add 1/2 a cup of sliced onions and saute it on medium flame for 2 minutes until it becomes slightly golden brown. Then add 1/2 a tablespoon of ginger garlic paste, and mix it well with the onions until the raw smell goes. Next, add 1 cup of chopped tomatoes and saute it for 3 minutes on medium flame until it becomes soft and mushy.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63db981c1dd878ea6301a0bf','63db92280e9d976b9be59483',4,'M2 Add the masalas','After the tomatoes have cooked and become mushy for Gobi Matar Sabzi, add 1 teaspoon of red chilli powder, add 1 teaspoon of coriander powder, add 1 teaspoon of cumin powder, add 1/2 a teaspoon of garam masala powder and mix it until well combined. Then, add 1/2 a teaspoon of turmeric powder, add 1/8 teaspoon of asafoetida, add 1/2 a teaspoon of salt and mix it well.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63db98fa0e9d976b9be59488','63db92280e9d976b9be59483',5,'M3 Add the vegetables and allow them to cook','Next, for Gobi Matar Sabzi, add 1/2 a cup of chopped fenugreek leaves, and mix it with the onion and tomato mixture, Then add 1/4 cup of green peas and mix it well. Next add 1/4 cup of water and mix again. Then add 1/4 cup of chopped potatoes and mix with the vegetables, add 1/2 a teaspoon of raw mango powder and mix again. Then cover the pan with a lid and allow the curry to simmer on medium flame for 5 minutes until the vegetables are cooked. After 5 minutes, open the lid and give it a good stir, continue to cook the vegetables for another 3 minutes on low heat. While the vegetables are cooking, move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":8,"flame":1}'),('63db996fdb77c073468a83cd','63db92280e9d976b9be59483',6,'M4 Continue cooking the vegetables and serve','After the vegetables have cooked for Gobi Matar Sabzi, add 1 cup of boiled cauliflower florets and mix again. Then , cover the pan with a lid and allow the cauliflower to cook in the gravy for another 5 minutes on medium flame. Give it a good mix after 5 minutes, and continue to cook on low flame for another 3 minutes. Then turn off the flame, remove in a serving bowl and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":8,"flame":0}'),
('63dbc85c0e9d976b9be5948a','63dbb683db77c073468a83ce',1,'P1 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Mixed Vegetable Poha, peel and finely chop 1/2 a cup of onions; wash, peel and dice 1/2 a cup of potatoes; wash, peel and dice 1/4 cup of carrots; wash 2 tablespoons of green peas; wash and finely chop 1 teaspoon of green chillies; wash and finely chop 1/2 a tablespoon of coriander leaves; wash and pluck 7 curry leaves and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63dbc8e51dd878ea6301a0c7','63dbb683db77c073468a83ce',2,'P2 Prep the Poha','To prep the poha for Mixed vegetable poha, sieve 1/2 a cup of thick poha to get rid of dust and particles. Then place the sieved poha in a mixing bowl, add 1.5 cups of water to it and gently swirl the poha with your hand for remaining dust particles to float on top, then strain the poha and discard the water. Next, to the washed and cleaned poha add 3/4 cup of water and allow it to soak for 4 minutes only. After that drain the water and allow the poha to release excess water if any. While the poha is soaking move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":4,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":4,"flame":0}'),('63dbca61db77c073468a83d1','63dbb683db77c073468a83ce',3,'M1 Prepare the seasoning and stir fry the vegetables','To prepare Mixed Vegetable Poha, heat a pan and add 1.5 tablespoons of oil and allow it to become hot. Then, add 1/2 a teaspoon of mustard seeds, add a few curry leaves, add 1/4 teaspoon of asafoeitida and allow the spices to crackle. Next, add1/2 a cup of chopped onions, and saute it for two minutes on medium flame until it becomes translucent. Then, add 1/2 a cup of diced potatoes and stir fry it for 2 minutes until it becomes slightly tender. Then add a pinch of salt followed by 1/4 cup of diced carrots and saute it for for 2 minutes until they becomes slightly tender','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63dbcb741dd878ea6301a0c8','63dbb683db77c073468a83ce',4,'M2 Add the masalas and cook the vegetables','Next, for mixed vegetable poha add 2 tablespoons of washed green peas and stir fry it for 2 minutes on medium flame. Then add 1 teaspoon of chopped green chillies followed by 10 raisins and saute it for 2 minutes. Then, add 1/2 a teaspoon of turmeric powder, add 1/2 a teaspoon of kashmiri red chilli powder, add 1/2 a teaspoon of coriander powder, add 1/2 a teaspoon of cumin powder, add 1 teaspoon of sugar add a pinch of salt and mix well until the masalas are well combined. Then, cover the pan with a lid and allow the vegetables to cook on low flame for 6 minutes until they are cooked. While the vegetables cook move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":6,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":6,"flame":2}'),('63dbe34e1dd878ea6301a0c9','63dbb683db77c073468a83ce',5,'M3 Season the poha and serve hot','After the vegetables have cooked for Mixed Vegetable Poha, gently open the lid and give it a good mix. Check if the vegetables have cooked through. Then, add the washed and cleaned poha, add 1/2 a tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves, add 1/2 a tablespoon of lemon juice and gently mix until the vegetables and poha are well combined. Then, add 1/2 a teaspoon of garam masala powder and mix well. Adjust the seasoning, then cover the pan with a lid allow it to cook for another minute on low flame. Turn off the flame, garnish it with chopped coriander leaves and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":1,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":1,"flame":1}'),
('63dcad4e4b12131919c8b008','63dc02e70e9d976b9be5948b',1,'P1 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Lauki Kofta, wash, peel and cut the bottle gourd in half, remove the seeds and grate 1 cup of bottle gourd; wash, peel and grate 1 teaspoon of ginger; wash and finely chop 1/2 a teaspoon of green chillies; wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves; peel and chop 2 onions into medium chunks; peel 3 cloves of garlic; wash and peel half an inch of ginger ; wash and finely chop 1 cup of tomatoes.','prep_method','{"active_time":18,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63dcade8db77c073468a83d6','63dc02e70e9d976b9be5948b',2,'P2 Prepare the Kofta Dough','To prepare the Kofta dough for Lauki Kofta, take a mixing bowl, place a muslin cloth on top and add 1 cup of grated bottle gourd, gather the cloth into a potli and squeeze the grated bottle gourd until it releases all the water out. Set aside the water for later use. Then, in a mixing bowl add the grated bottle gourd, add 1 tablespoon of grated ginger, add 1/2 a teaspoon of chopped green chillies, add 1/2 a teaspoon of garam masala, add 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves, add 1/2 a teaspoon of salt, add 1/4 cup of besan, and combine the ingredients well using your hands.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63dcb2834b12131919c8b009','63dc02e70e9d976b9be5948b',3,'P3 Shape and Fry the Kofta Dough','Next to shape and fry the koftas, grease your hands with oil and pinch lemon sized balls and shape the kofta into smooth balls and slightly flatten it. Then, heat two tablespoons of cooking oil in a pan and place the flattened Koftas at a distance from on and other. Allow it to cook on medium low flame for 2 minutes until it becomes slightly golden brown. Then, flip the Koftas and allow it to cook on the other side for 2 minutes until it becomes golden brown. Then, remove the shallow fried koftas and transfer them onto a kitchen towel to soak in the excess oil.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":4,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":4,"flame":2}'),('63dcb39c1dd878ea6301a0d1','63dc02e70e9d976b9be5948b',4,'P4 Prepare the Gravy','To prepare the gravy for Lauki Kofta, heat a pan and add 2 roughly chopped onions and saute it for 2 minutes on medium flame until they become translucent. Then, add 2 garlic cloves, add 1/2 an inch of ginger, add 1/4 cup of cashew nuts, add 1/2 a tablespoon of almonds, add 1/2 a tablespoon of melon seeds, add 1 innch of cinnamon, add 3 cloves, add 1 star anise, add 3 green cardamoms and saute it for 2 minutes on medium flame. Then, add 1 bay leaf followed by 1 cup of chopped tomatoes and saute it for 5 minutes until it is well cooked. Then turn off the flame and allow the mixture to slightly cool. After it cools, transfer the cooked mixture into a mixy jar and blend it into a fine puree.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63dcb57d1dd878ea6301a0d2','63dc02e70e9d976b9be5948b',5,'M1 Add the Masalas and Cook the Gravy','To cook the gravy for Lauki Kofta, heat a pan and add 1 tablespoon of oil and allow it to become hot. Next, add the prepared onion tomato puree and saute it on medium low flame for 1 minute until it is slightly cooked and slightly changes colour. Then, add 1/2 a teaspoon of salt, add 1/2 a teaspoon of red chilli powder, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, add 1/2 a teaspoon of cumin powder, add 1/2 a teaspoon of coriander powder, add 1/2 a teaspoon of garam masala and mix well. Then, cover the pan with a lid and allow it to cook on low flame for 2 minutes. Keep stirring the gravy to prevent it from sticking and burning.','cook_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":2,"flame":2}'),
('63dcb5e54b12131919c8b00a','63dc02e70e9d976b9be5948b',6,'M2 Simmer the Gravy and Serve Hot','After cooking the masalas for Lauki Kofta Curry, heat a pan and 2 cups of water, add the bottle gourd water and mix it well. Then, cover the pan with a lid and cook again on low flame for 10 to 15 minutes. Next, add the shallow fried koftas, and gently pour the gravy on top and coat the koftas as shown. Then add 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and allow it to simmer on low flame for 2 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":14,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":14,"flame":1}'),('63dcfbb3157369dc938f65ce','63dce44a1dd878ea6301a0d5',1,'P1 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for ABC juice, wash and core 3 apples and cut them into slices. Next, wash, peel and cut 1 beetroot into medium sized chunks; wash, peel and cut 2 medium sized carrots into halves; wash and peel half an inch of ginger; cut a lemon into half, deseed it and squeeze 1/2 a tablespoon of lemon juice and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63dcfc9cb69e17b37e566268','63dce44a1dd878ea6301a0d5',2,'M1 Prepare the Juice','To prepare the ABC juice, in a mixer jar add 3 sliced apples, add 1 roughly chopped beetroot, 2 carrots cut into half as well as 1/2 an inch of ginger and blend it into a smooth mix. Then, squeeze 1/2 a tablespoon of lemon juice and mix well.  Add water to adjust as per desired consistency. Then, add 3 ice cubes in a serving glass and pour the prepared juice over it and serve chilled.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63dcfe93b60cd30ede2908aa','63dcef1d1dd878ea6301a0d7',1,'P1 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Aloo Palak, peel and finely chop 1 tablespoon of garlic cloves, wash, peel and chop 1 teaspoon of ginger, peel and finely chop 1 onion, wash, peel and dice 3 potatoes and transfer it in a mixing bowl filled with water to prevent it from turning black. Then, wash and finely chop 350 grams of spinach leaves and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63dcff57b60cd30ede2908ab','63dcef1d1dd878ea6301a0d7',2,'M1 Prepare the Tempering','To prepare the tempering for Aloo Palak, heat a kadai and add 2 tablespoons of mustard oil and allow it to become hot on high flame. Once the oil is smokes, reduce the flame to low and add 1/2 a teaspoon of turmeric powder, add 1 teaspoon of cumin seeds, add 1 dry red chilli and saute it on low flame and allow the spices to crackle.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),
('63dcffcab69e17b37e56626a','63dcef1d1dd878ea6301a0d7',3,'M2 Saute the onions','After the spices have crackled for Aloo Palak, add 1 tablespoon of chopped garlic followed by 1 teaspoon of chopped ginger  and saute it on medium low flame for 2 minutes until they slightly become brown. Next, add 1 chopped onion and saute it on medium flame for 3 minutes until the onions become translucent and slightly cooked.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63dd0092b69e17b37e56626b','63dcef1d1dd878ea6301a0d7',4,'M3 Cook the Potato','After the onions cook for Aloo Palak, add 3 cubed potatoes, and saute it with the tempering for 2 minutes. Then, cover the kadai with a lid and allow the potatoes to cook on medium flame for 4 minutes. If you feel the tadka is become dry, sprinkle a few drops of water to prevent it from burning. Occasionally stir the cubed potatoes to prevent it from sticking to the kadai. While the potatoes are cooking, move on to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":4,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":4,"flame":2}'),('63dd0146b69e17b37e56626c','63dcef1d1dd878ea6301a0d7',5,'M4 Cook the Spinach Leaves','After the potatoes have cooked for Aloo Palak, add 1 teaspoon of coriander powder, add 1/2 a teaspoon of red chilli powder, add 350 grams of chopped spinach leaves and give it a stir. Then, cover the kadai with a lid and cook it on medium flame for 3 minutes until the spinach leaves are cooked and start to wilt. While the spinach leaves are cooking move onto the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":3,"flame":2}'),('63dd02dcb69e17b37e56626d','63dcef1d1dd878ea6301a0d7',6,'M5 Cook the Sabzi and serve','Now, gently open the lid and mix the palak along with the tempering. Then, add salt as per taste, and 1/2 a teaspoon of sugar and mix well. Now saute it for a minute and allow it to cook on low flame for 2 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":1,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":2,"flame":1}'),('63dd04acb69e17b37e56626e','63dcf997b60cd30ede2908a7',1,'P1 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Besan Phulka, in a mortar and pestle add 1/2 a tablespoon of coriander seeds and pound it into a coarse powder, then peel and finely chop 1 teaspoon of garlic cloves, peel and finely chop 2 tablespoons of onion, wash and finely chop 1 teaspoon of green chilli, wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('63dd05bdb60cd30ede2908ac','63dcf997b60cd30ede2908a7',2,'P2 Prepare the Dough','To prepare the dough for Besan Phulka, in a mixing bowl, add 1/2 a cup of wheat flour, add 1 cup of besan, add 1/2 a teaspoon of red chilli powder, add 1/2 a teaspoon of ajwain, add 1/2 a teaspoon of cumin seeds, add 1/2 a teaspoon of coarse coriander powder, add a pinch of salt, add 1 teaspoon of chopped garlic, add 2 tablespoons of chopped onion, add 1 teaspoon of chopped green chilli, add 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves followed by 2 tablespoons of cooking oil and combine the ingredients well using your hands. Gradually add water as required and knead it for 3 minutes into a soft dough.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63dd061db69e17b37e56626f','63dcf997b60cd30ede2908a7',3,'M1 Roll Out the Phulka','To roll out the Besan Phulka, first divide the prepared dough into small lemon-sized balls. Then slighlty flatter it between your palms and dust it in flour. Then, place it over a rolling board and roll it into a thin 7-inch circle. Make sure to roll out the edges thin. Repeat the same for the remaining dough balls.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63dd067db60cd30ede2908ad','63dcf997b60cd30ede2908a7',4,'M2 Roast the Phulka','Next, to roast the Besan Phulka, heat a tawa and transfer the rolled phulka onto it and allow it to cook on medium flame for 2 minutes, then pour half a teaspoon of cooking oil on top and spread it evenly. Once the brown spots appear, flip the phulka on the other side and repeat the same. Continue to flip and roast the phulka, until brown spots appear. Then turn off the flame and serve hot. Roast the other phulkas similarly.','cook_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63dffeb1b201c6c6b95f6674','63dd0c8db69e17b37e566270',1,'P1 Prepare the Dough','To prepare the dough for Ajwain Paratha, in a mixing bowl add 1.5 cups of whole wheat flour, then add 1/2 a teaspoon of salt into it. Next, take a teaspoon of carom seeds in your hand and crush it between your palms as shown and add to the flour and mix it well. Next, add 1 tablespoon of ghee and crumble it well with the flour using your fingers. Next, gradually add water in batches as and when required and knead it for 5 minutes to form a soft dough. Grease it with some more ghee and knead again. Then, cover the dough with a lid and allow it to rest for 15 minutes. While the dough rests, move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":15,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":15,"flame":0}'),('63dffef81ee35e4189d6a7f0','63dd0c8db69e17b37e566270',2,'M1 Roll the Parathas','To make the Ajwain Paratha, first, divide the prepared dough into equal lemon sized balls and slightly flatten it between your palms. Then, take a ball and dust some flour on the rolling board. Place the dough ball on the rolling board and roll it into a small circle using a rolling pin. Next, apply 1/4 teaspoon of ghee over it and spread it evenly using your fingers and sprinkle a pinch of flour over it as shown. Then fold it into half, and reapply the ghee and flour on top. Now fold it into a triangle, dust it with flour and evenly roll it into a 6-inch triangular paratha. Ensure that it is not too thick and even from all sides. Continue to roll other parathas similarly.','cook_method','{"active_time":18,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('63dfff53b201c6c6b95f6675','63dd0c8db69e17b37e566270',3,'M2 Roast the Parathas','Next, to roast the Ajwain Paratha, heat a tawa and transfer the rolled paratha onto the plate and roast it on a medium flame for 1-2 minutes until the brown spots appear. Then, flip it and toast the other side for another 1-2 minutes. Then, apply half a teaspoon of ghee on both the sides and roast the paratha on a medium flame for 2-3 minutes, until it turns golden brown. As it turns slightly crisp and golden, turn off the flame and transfer the parathas onto a plate. Similarly, roast the remaining parathas and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63e001da1ee35e4189d6a7f3','63df129fb201c6c6b95f6667',1,'P1 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Egg Malai Masala, peel and finely chop 1 cup of onions, peel 6 cloves of garlic, wash and peel 1 inch of ginger, wash and julienne 1 teaspoon of ginger, wash and finely chop 1 teaspoon of green chillies, wash 2 green chillies, wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves. Then, in a mixing bowl add 1/4 cup of curds and whisk it into creamy consistency.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63e0025174545a20c46f00a4','63df129fb201c6c6b95f6667',2,'P2 Boil the Eggs','To boil the eggs for Egg Malai Masala, heat a deep bottom pan and add 3 cups  of water along with a teaspoon of salt and allow it to come to a rolling boil on high flame. Then, add 4 raw eggs and allow it to cook for 8 mins on low flame. Then turn off the flame, and strain the egg using a slotted spoon to prevent it from further cooking. Next, gently rub the egg on the kitchen counter for easy deshelling and remove the shell and discard. Repeat the same for the remaining eggs. While the eggs are boiling, please move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":4,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":11,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":11,"flame":1}'),('63e002fdb201c6c6b95f6676','63df129fb201c6c6b95f6667',3,'P3 Prepare the Gravy','To prepare the gravy for Egg Malai Masala, heat a pan and add 2 tablespoons of oil and allow it to become hot. Next, add 1 cup of roughly chopped onion, and saute it on medium flame for 1 minute until it becomes translucent and soft. Then, add 6 cloves of garlic, 1 inch of ginger, 2 slit green chillies, and 2 tablespoons of cashew nuts and stir fry it on medium flame for 3 minutes until they become golden brown. Next, add 1/4 cup of water and mix again, then cover the pan with a lid and allow it to cook on medium low flame for 8 minutes. While the onions cook, move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":8,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":8,"flame":2}'),('63e003a7b201c6c6b95f6677','63df129fb201c6c6b95f6667',4,'M1 Cook the Gravy','After cooking the onions for Egg Malai Masala, transfer the cooked onions onto a plate and allow it to slightly cool. Next, transfer them into a blender jar and blend it into a smooth puree. To fry the gravy, heat a pan and add 1 tablespoon of oil and allow it to become hot. Next, add 1/2 a teaspoon of cumin seeds and allow it to splutter. Next, add the prepared cashewnut-onion puree and saute it well on medium flame and allow the oil to seprate.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":2,"flame":2}'),
('63e0059bb201c6c6b95f6678','63df129fb201c6c6b95f6667',5,'M2 Cook the masalas','After the oil has seprated for Egg Malai Masala, lower the flame and add 1/4 cup of whisked curd to it and mix it well with the masalas for 2 minutes. Then increase the flame to medium low, and add 1/2 a teaspoon of black pepper powder, add 1/2 a teaspoon of garam masala, add 1 teaspoon of crushed kasuri methi, as salt as required, then add 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and mix well. Next, adjust the consistency of the gravy by adding water if required.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63e005fa1ee35e4189d6a7f4','63df129fb201c6c6b95f6667',6,'M3 Simmer and serve','Next, for Egg Malai Masala, add 1/4 cup of fresh cream, and quickly mix it and simmer for a minute on low flame. Ensure not to cook for too long. Now, add the boiled eggs, add 1 teaspoon of chopped green chillies, add 1 tablespoon of julienned ginger and mix it well. Then, cover the pan with a lid and allow it to cook on medium flame for 10 to 12 minutes. Then, turn off the flame and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":13,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":13,"flame":2}'),('63e006bd1ee35e4189d6a7f5','63df2ef674545a20c46f009f',1,'P1 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Indori Poha, first add 1.5 cups of poha in a mixing bowl, along with 3 cups of water and let it rest for 30 seconds, the dust particles will float on top. Next, strain the poha using a colander and discard the water. Then, peel and finely chop 1/2 a cup of onion, wash and pluck 7 curry leaves, wash and finely chop 1 green chilli, wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63e007dab201c6c6b95f667a','63df2ef674545a20c46f009f',2,'M1 Prepare the Tempering','To prepare the tempering for Indori Poha, heat a pan and add 1 tablespoon of oil and allow it to become hot. Next, add 1/2 a teaspoon of mustard seeds and allow it to splutter. Then, add 1/2 a teaspoon of coriander seeds followed by 1/2 a teaspoon of cumin seeds, add 1/2 a teaspoon of fennel seeds, add 1/4 cup of chopped onion, add 7 washed curry leaves, add 1 chopped green chilli, and saute it on medium flame for 2 minutes until the onion becomes golden brown.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63e008a61ee35e4189d6a7f7','63df2ef674545a20c46f009f',3,'M2 Cook the poha, garnish and serve','After the onions have cooked for Indori Poha, next add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder, add 1/2 tablespoon of sugar, add 2 tablespoons of water and saute it on medium flame for 2 minutes until the sugar dissolves. Then, add salt as per taste and mix again. Next, reduce the flame to low and add the soaked poha and gently mix it with the tempering and allow it to cook on low flame for 2 minutes. Then turn off the flame, garnish the poha with 1 tablespoon of chopped coriander leaves and remove in a serving plate. Further garnish it with 1 tablespoon of pomegranate seeds, 1 tablespoon of ratlami sev and 1/2 a tablespoon of chopped onions and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),
('63e0095c1ee35e4189d6a7f8','63dff017b201c6c6b95f666f',1,'P1 Prep the ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Achari Bhindi, cut the ends of the ladies finger, wash and thoroughly pat dry the ladies finger, and then cut 250 grams of ladies finger into medium sized pieces. Next, peel and finely chop 1 onion, wash, peel and finely chop 1 inch of ginger, peel and finely chop 1 tablespoon of garlic, wash and finely chop 1 teaspoon of green chillies, wash and finely chop 1 tablespoon of coriander leaves and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":15,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63e009ef74545a20c46f00a6','63dff017b201c6c6b95f666f',2,'P2 Roast the Masala','To roast the ingredients for Achari Bhindi, heat a pan and add 1 teaspoon of cumin seeds, add 1 teaspoon of fennel seeds, add 1 teaspoon of mustard seeds, add 1 teaspoon of coriander seeds, add 1/2 a teaspoon of fenugreek seeds, add 1/2 a teaspoon of onion seeds, add 2 dried red chilli and dry roast it on medium flame for 2 minutes until the spices become aromatic. Then, turn off the flame and transfer the roasted spices onto a plate and allow it to slightly cool. Next, transfer the cooled spices in a mixer grinder and grind it into a coarse mixture.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":2,"flame":2}'),('63e00a5174545a20c46f00a7','63dff017b201c6c6b95f666f',3,'M1 Stir Fry the bhindi','To stir fry the bhindi for Achari Bhindi, heat a pan and add 1 tablespoon of mustard oil and allow it to become hot. Next, add 250 gms of cut bhindi pieces and stir fry it on medium flame for five minutes until it becomes slightly tender and slightly cooked.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63e00b0db201c6c6b95f667b','63dff017b201c6c6b95f666f',4,'M2 Prepare the tempering','After the bhindi is cooked for Achari Bhindi, heat a pan and add 2 tablespoons of oil and allow it to become hot, then add 1/4 teaspoon of hingh, add 1 teaspoon of cumin seeds, add 1 dried red chilli, add 1 inch of chopped ginger, add 1 tablespoon of chopped garlic, add 1 teaspoon of chopped green chillies, and saute it on medium low flame for a few seconds until it becomes golden brown.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63e00ba774545a20c46f00a8','63dff017b201c6c6b95f666f',5,'M3 Cook the onion and tomatoes','Next, for Achari Bhindi, after sauteing the spices add 1 chopped onion, and saute it on medium flame for 2 minutes until the onions become translucent. Then, add 1/2 a teaspoon of salt, add 3/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder and mix it well. Then add the ground coarse mixture, and mix it well with the onions. Then, add 1 cup of tomato puree and saute it with the onions on medium low flame until it is slightly cooked. Next, cover the pan with a lid and allow it to cook for five minutes on low flame. While the puree is cooking move onto the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":5,"flame":2}'),
('63e00c3174545a20c46f00a9','63dff017b201c6c6b95f666f',6,'M4 Cook the bhindi with the masala and serve','After the puree is cooked for Achari Bhindi, add 1/2 a teaspoon of red chilli powder, add mix well. Then, add the fried bhindi, and mix well with the masala. Then, cover the lid with a pan and allow it to cook for 2 minutes on low flame. Then, turn off the flame, gently open the lid garnish the Achari Bhindi with chopped coriander leaves, and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":1,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":2,"flame":1}'),('63ec40f6e75ef39cf076ff4b','63eb5444137bf03f315567fe',1,'P1 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Vegetables in Hot Garlic Sauce, peel and chop 1/2 a tablespoon of garlic; peel, wash and cube 1/4 cup of onion; wash, peel and chop 1/2 a teaspoon of ginger. Next, wash, cut and deseed a green bell pepper and cut 1 tablespoon of green bell pepper into dices; wash, cut and deseed a red bell pepper and cut 1 tablespoon of red bell pepper into dices; wash, cut and deseed a yellow bell pepper and cut 1 tablespoon of yellow bell pepper into dices.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63ec41a2f0ee55bfbd932609','63eb5444137bf03f315567fe',2,'P2 Continue prepping the Ingredients','To continue prepping the ingredients for Vegetables in Hot Garlic Sauce, thoroughly rinse the broccoli twice and cut 1/4 cup of florets; thoroughly rinse the cauliflower twice and cut 1/4 cup of florets. Then, wash and trim the mushroom stems and cut 1/4 cup of trimmed mushrooms into halves; wash, peel and slice 2 tablespoons of carrot; wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of spring onion and set aside','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63ec42a7f0ee55bfbd93260a','63eb5444137bf03f315567fe',3,'M1 Cook the vegetables','To prepare Vegetables in Hot Garlic Sauce, heat a pan and add 1/2 a tablespoon of sesame oil and allow it to become hot. Then, add 1/2 a tablespoon of chopped garlic, and saute it on medium low flame for a minute, until it becomes slightly golden brown. Then, add 1/4 cup of cubed onion, add 1/2 a teaspoon of chopped ginger and saute it for a few seconds until the raw smell of the ginger goes. Next, add 1/4 cup of halved mushrooms, add 1/4 cup of broccoli florets, add 1/4 cup of cauliflower florets, add 1/4 cup of sliced carrots, add 3 tablespoons of mixed bell pepper dices and saute it for 2 minutes on medium flame until the vegetables become slightly tender. Next, add 1 cup of water until it covers the vegetables and then bring to boil. While the vegetables are cooking move onto the next step','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":5,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":5,"flame":2}'),('63ec43e1f0ee55bfbd93260b','63eb5444137bf03f315567fe',4,'M2 Prepare the sauce','To prepare the corn flour slurry for Vegetables in Hot Garlic Sauce, in a small bowl add 3/4 tablespoon of corn starch along with 1.5 tablespoon of water and mix it well. Prepare a lump free slurry. Then, after the water has come to boil for , add 1/2 a tablespoon of soy sauce, add 1/2 a tablespoon of red chilli sauce, add 1/4 tablespoon of vinegar, add 1/2 a teaspoon of brown sugar, add 1/2 a teaspoon of tomato ketchup, add 1/4 tablespoon of red chilli paste and mix it well. Then add 1/4 teaspoon of red chilli flakes along with some salt to taste and mix well again. Next, add the prepared corn flour slurry and mix it well, allow it to cook for 3 to 4 minutes on medium flame until the gravy becomes slightly thick. Then turn off the flame, garnish it with chopped spring onions and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":3,"flame":2}'),
('63ec44eb53e26817c2f440de','63eb6328494592ff53d252a4',1,'P1 Prep the ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Sweet and Sour Chicken, wash and pat dry 300 grams of boneless chicken and then cut them into medium sized chunks. Then transfer the chicken chunks into a mixing bowl, add 1/2 a teaspoon of salt and mix it well, and set aside for 15 minutes. While the chicken is resting, prepare the sauce in a mixing bowl add 5 tablespoons of tomato ketchup, add 5 tablespoons of sugar, add 5 tablespoons of white vinegar, add 1 teaspoon of dark soy sauce, and mix well until well combined.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":12,"flame":0}'),('63ec473ef0ee55bfbd93260c','63eb6328494592ff53d252a4',2,'P2 Continue prepping the ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Sweet and Sour Chicken, peel and cut 1 medium sized onion into petals, wash and cut a red bell pepper into half, remove the seeds, and cut 1 cup of red capsicum into half inch squares; wash and cut a green capsicum into half remove the seeds, and cut 1 cup of green capsicum into half inch squares.','prep_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63ec47e4f0ee55bfbd93260d','63eb6328494592ff53d252a4',3,'P3 Prepare the batter','To prepare the batter for Sweet and Sour Chicken, in a mixing bowl add, 4 tablespoons of all purpose flour, add 3 teaspoons of corn starch, add 1/4 teaspoon of baking powder, add 1/4 teaspoon of salt, add 1 egg, add 5 tablespoons of water and whisk it well for 2 minutes until it is well combines and results in a smooth and flowy batter. Then pour the prepared batter over the salted chicken pieces and combine it well until the pieces are submerged in the batter.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63ec4843f0ee55bfbd93260e','63eb6328494592ff53d252a4',4,'P4 Fry the Chicken','To fry the chicken for Sweet and Sour Chicken, first heat 1 cup of cooking oil in a Kadai over medium flame for 2-3 minutes. Once the oil is hot, carefully drop the marinated chicken pieces into it, one by one. Then, deep fry them over medium flame for 6-7 minutes by flipping them at regular intervals until golden and crisp. Once the chicken cubes are cooked through and turn golden-crisp, turn off the flame and take them out onto a kitchen napkin to dab off the excess oil.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":10,"flame":3}'),('63ec495af0ee55bfbd93260f','63eb6328494592ff53d252a4',5,'M1 Prepare the sweet and Sour Chicken','To prepare Sweet and Sour Chicken, heat a pan and add 3 tablespoons of oil and allow it to become hot, then add 1/2 a cup of onion petals, and saute it on high flame for for a minute. Next, add 1 cup of red bell pepper and 1 cup of green capsicum and saute it on high flame for another 15 seconds. Do not overcook them, as the capsicum should remain slightly crunchy. Next, add the prepared sweet and sour sauce and stir fry it with the vegetables for half a minute. Then allow the sauce to simmer on low flame for a minute. Next, add the fried chicken pieces and stir fry it with the sauce until it is evenly coated. Then, turn off the flame and serve hot','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":2,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":2,"flame":4}'),
('63ec49e4e75ef39cf076ff4c','63eb7556494592ff53d252aa',1,'P1 Prep the ingredients','To prep the Ingredients for Kheema Paratha, peel and chop 1 cup of onions, wash and cut a green capsicum into half, remove the seeds and finely chop 1/4 cup of green capsicum. Next, in a mixing break an egg and whisk it until well combined.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63ec4a59f0ee55bfbd932610','63eb7556494592ff53d252aa',2,'P2 Prepare the Dough','To prepare the dough for Kheema Paratha, in a large mixing bowl, add 1 cup of all purpose flour, add 1/2 a cup of wheat flour, followed by 1 teaspoon of salt and combine it well with your hands. Then, add a teaspoon of cooking oil, and mix it well. Then, gradually add water as required and combine the ingredients well. Knead the dough for five minutes until it is well combined and becomes soft. Next, grease the dough a teaspoon of oil, cover the bowl with a lid and allow it to rest for 30 minutes. While the dough rests, move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":30,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":30,"flame":0}'),('63ec4bb9e75ef39cf076ff4d','63eb7556494592ff53d252aa',3,'P3 Prepare the Stuffing','To prepare the stuffing for Kheema Paratha, heat 1 tablespoon of oil in a pan and allow it to become hot. Then, add 1 cup of chopped onions, and saute it for a minute on medium flame until it becomes translucent. Then, add 1 teaspoon of ginger garlic paste, and saute it well. Next, add 1/4 cup of chopped green capsicum, and saute it on medium flame until it becomes slightly tender. Then, add 250 gms of mutton keema and saute it for 2 to 3 minutes until it changes colour.','prep_method','{"active_time":7,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63ec4c4b53e26817c2f440df','63eb7556494592ff53d252aa',4,'P4 Cook the Stuffing','Next, for Kheema Paratha, add 1/2 a teaspoon of turmeric powder, add 2 teaspoons of red chilli powder, add 1 teaspoon of coriander powder, add 1 teaspoon of garam masala, and mix it until well combined. Next, add a teaspoon of salt, and mix again. Then add 1/2 a cup of water and mix again. Next, cover the pan with a lid and allow it to cook for 12 minutes on low flame until the keema cooks and water evaporates. Then, gently open the lid and give it a good mix and keep aside. While the keema is cooking, move to the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":12,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":12,"flame":1}'),('63ec4c98f0ee55bfbd932611','63eb7556494592ff53d252aa',5,'M1 Roll the paratha and add pack the stuffing','To make the Kheema Paratha, first, divide the prepared dough into small equal-sized balls. Next, take a dough ball and dust some flour. Then, gently press it and roll it into a round paratha. Ensure it is slightly thin and even in thickness from all sides. Next, add and evenly spread about 2-3 tablespoons of the prepared keema stuffing onto the rolled out paratha. Then, pour a 1 tablespoon of whisked egg on top of the keema. Now, pack the paratha into a square parcel as shown and seal it ones all the sides are gathered in the center. Repeat the same for the remaining dough and stuffing.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),
('63ec4d05f0ee55bfbd932612','63eb7556494592ff53d252aa',6,'M2 Roast the Kheema paratha','Next, to roast the Kheema Paratha, heat a tawa and add 1 teaspoon of oil and allow it to become hot, then place the stuffed paratha onto the tawa cook it over medium flame for 1-2 minutes. Flip and cook both the sides of paratha until it turns golden and crisp. Then hold the paratha using tongs and cook the sides of the paratha as shown.  After the paratha is evenly cooked from all the sides, slice it into half, transfer it onto a serving plate and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":6,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}'),('63ec4d80e75ef39cf076ff4e','63eb7e68494592ff53d252b3',1,'P1 Prep the Prawns','To prep and marinate the prawns for Prawn Malai Curry, first, rinse 500 gms deveined prawns in the cold water and clean them thoroughly. If using shelled prawns, hold the prawn with one hand and firmly twist off the head using your other hand. Then, pull off the tail, peel away the outer shell. Then, make a slit in the center and remove the vein. Similarly, clean the rest of the prawns. Then, in a mixing bowl add the cleaned prawns, add 1/4 teaspoon of salt, add 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder and mix it well and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":10,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63ec4e36f0ee55bfbd932613','63eb7e68494592ff53d252b3',2,'P2 Prepare the spice mix','To prepare the spice mix for Prawn Malai Curry, in a mixing bowl add 1 teaspoon of turmeric powder, add 1 teaspoon of cumin powder, add 1 teaspoon of garam masala, add half a teaspoon of kashmiri chilli powder, add half a teaspoon of sugar, add 1/4 teaspoon of salt, add 1 tablespoon of water and mix it well using a spoon. Then, peel and slice 1/2 a cup of onions and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63ec4f96f0ee55bfbd932614','63eb7e68494592ff53d252b3',3,'M1 Fry the prawns','To fry the prawns for Prawn Malai Curry, heat a pan and add 2 tablespoons of oil and allow it to become hot. Then, place the marinated prawns and fry it on medium low flame for 2 minutes until it is evenly cooked on both sides. Keep stirring them in between to prevent it from sticking to the pan. Then, remove the shallow fried prawns, remove in a plate and set aside. In the same pan, add 3 cardamom, 1 cinnamon and 4 clove pieces and saute it for a few seconds.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":3,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":3,"flame":2}'),('63ec5045f0ee55bfbd932616','63eb7e68494592ff53d252b3',4,'M2 Cook the masala','Next, for Prawn Malai Curry, after sauteing the spices, add 1/2 a cup of sliced onion and saute it on medium low flame for two minutes until it becomes golden brown. Next, add 1 teaspoon of ginger garlic paste, add the prepared spice mix and mix it well. Then cover the pan with a lid and allow it to cook on medium flame for 3 to 4 minutes. Then, gently open the lid and give it a good mix. When the masala is cooking move to the next step.','cook_method','{"active_time":3,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":4,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":4,"flame":3}'),
('63ec513af0ee55bfbd932617','63eb7e68494592ff53d252b3',5,'M3 Cook the prawns in the masala','After the masala has cooked for Prawn Malai Curry, add 1/4 cup of water and mix again. Next, add the fried prawns and mix it again with the masala. Then, cover the pan with a lid and allow it to cook on low flame for 5 minutes. Next, add 1 cup of coconut milk and mix with the prawns and masala and cover the pan with a lid and allow it to cook on low flame for 2 minutes. Once it starts simmering, add 1/2 a teaspoon of garam masala and mix well. Then, turn off the flame, remove in a serving bowl and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":2,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":7,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":7,"flame":1}'),('63ec539281aa1ac1606590b2','63eb831ce75ef39cf076ff47',1,'P1 Prep the Ingredients','To prep the ingredients for Anda Paratha, wash and finely chop 1 green chilli ; wash and finely chop 2 tablespoons of coriander leaves; in a mixing bowl crack 3 eggs and discard the shell. Then, add 1/2 a teaspoon of salt followed by 1 teaspoon of black pepper powder and 1/2 a teaspoon of red chilli powder, then whisk the eggs until fluffy and well combined. Next, add 1 finely chopped green chilli followed by 2 tablespoons of chopped coriander leaves and mix again and set aside.','prep_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63ec544a81aa1ac1606590b3','63eb831ce75ef39cf076ff47',2,'P2 Prepare the Dough','To prepare the dough for Anda Paratha, in a mixing bowl add 2 cups of all purpose flour, add 1/2 a teaspoon of salt to taste, add 1 cup of warm water, and mix it well using your hands and mix the ingredients well using your fingers. Then, knead the dough for 5 to 7 minutes until it is well combined, soft and not sticking to the bowl anymore. Then apply 1/2 a teaspoon of oil and spread it evenly on the dough. Next, cover the dough with a cloth and allow it to rest for 10 minutes. While the dough is set aside, move onto the next step.','prep_method','{"active_time":8,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":10,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":10,"flame":0}'),('63ec54a081aa1ac1606590b4','63eb831ce75ef39cf076ff47',3,'M1 Roll the dough into layers','After resting the dough for Anda Paratha, dust the rolling surface with some flour and place the dough on top and knead it again. Then, portion the dough into equal lemon sized balls and roll them into a soft ball. Then, dust the portioned ball and place it on the rolling surface, and evenly roll it into a 7 inch thin disc. Then brush some melted ghee evenly over the rolled paratha. Then sprinkle some flour on the melted ghee and evenly sprinkle 1/4 teaspoon of kalonji on the dusted flour. Next, roll it into a cigar as shown, and gently flatten the cigar using your finger , again brush some ghee on the flattened dough and dust some flour on top and roll it again as shown. Repeat the same for the remaining dough.','cook_method','{"active_time":18,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":0}'),('63ec54e8f0ee55bfbd932618','63eb831ce75ef39cf076ff47',4,'M2 Roll and roast the paratha','To roll the Anda Paratha, dust the rolling surface with some flour, and roll out the prepared ball into a slightly thick 5 inch disc using a rolling pin, such that the layers are visible. Next, heat a tawa on low flame and allow it to become hot, then transfer the rolled paratha onto it and allow it to cook on low flame for one minute until the brown spots appear. Then, flip the paratha on the other side and allow it to cook for another minute until it is cooked and take it off the flame.','cook_method','{"active_time":5,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":1}'),
('63ec553981aa1ac1606590b5','63eb831ce75ef39cf076ff47',5,'M3 Roast the paratha with the egg','Next, to prepare the Anda Paratha, grease the hot tawa with half a teaspoon of oil and pour half a cup of the prepared egg batter and place the cooked paratha on top of the egg batter. Brush some oil on the top side of the paratha and flip the paratha on the other side as shown. Now continue flipping, gently pressing and roasting the paratha at regular intervals until it becomes crisp and golden brown. Repeat the same for the remaining dough and egg batter, and serve hot.','cook_method','{"active_time":12,"semi_active_time":0,"idle_time":0,"advanced_prep_time":0,"timer":0,"flame":2}');
